OFFLINE_LIBRARY.push(...[{"id":"igopx-reading-9565","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 An early cultural tourist","book":"阅读真题集 22","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test1","part":1,"description":"阅读真题集 22 · Test1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"9565:68282:1","type":"choice","text":"Cyriacus was unable to research his journeys before he left.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：We prepare for such trips by reading about what we are going to see, set out on the journey with a good idea of how we will get there and where we will stay, and have a sense of what we will encounter on location. Cyriacus of Ancona (1391-1452), the first cultural tourist since antiquity, lacked these advantages when, in the first half of the 15th century, he sailed around the Mediterranean in search of the remains of Greek and Roman civilisations.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题干询问Cyriacus在出发前是否能够研究他的旅程，关键词为“unable to research his journeys before he left”。\n定位关键信息：由人名“Cyriacus”和“before he left”定位到A段最后一句，该句指出他缺乏现代旅行者出发前查阅资料、规划行程等优势。\n解题思路：原文明确说明Cyriacus缺乏现代旅行者出发前阅读、规划等优势，因此他无法在出发前研究旅程，与题干一致，故TRUE。FALSE选项与原文矛盾，因为原文直接指出他缺乏这些能力；NOT GIVEN不成立，因为原文提供了明确信息而非未提及。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68282","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"9565:68283:2","type":"choice","text":"The Roman Emperor Trajan built the city of Ancona.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Cyriacus first became fascinated by ancient monuments while walking in his home city Ancona and looking at the marble arch, erected in AD 115, to the Roman Emperor Trajan.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题干问罗马皇帝图拉真是否建造了安科纳城，需要判断原文是否提供此信息。\n定位关键信息：用题干中“Roman Emperor Trajan”和“Ancona”定位，原文B段提及图拉真和安科纳。\n解题思路：原文只提到安科纳是Cyriacus的家乡，并有一座为图拉真建造的拱门，但未提图拉真建造了城市本身，故信息未给出；TRUE无依据，FALSE亦无否定证据，选NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68283","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"9565:68284:3","type":"choice","text":"Respect for ancient architecture was widespread in the 15th century.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Not many people of Cyriacus’s time were interested in historical travel; they generally ignored old buildings and structures, or worse, dismantled them for their building materials.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题干判断15世纪对古建筑的尊重是否普遍，关键词为widespread respect, 15th century, ancient architecture。\n定位关键信息：根据15th century定位至B段末句，该句描述当时人们的态度。\n解题思路：原文明确当时多数人忽视甚至破坏古建筑，与“尊重普遍”相反，故答案为FALSE；TRUE与原文矛盾；NOT GIVEN原文已明确提及，不成立。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68284","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"9565:68285:4","type":"choice","text":"Cyriacus’s experience as a merchant gave him skills he needed to investigate the ancient world.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：His training as a merchant did not prepare him for this vocation; he did not know ancient languages, history or art.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：判断Cyriacus的商人经验是否给了他研究古代世界所需的技能。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的“experience as a merchant”和“skills he needed to investigate”定位到C段“His training as a merchant did not prepare him for this vocation”。\n解题思路：原文明确说商人训练“did not prepare him”，即没有提供技能，与题干“gave him skills”相反，故选FALSE。TRUE与原文矛盾；NOT GIVEN不成立，因为原文直接明确提及此信息。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68285","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"9565:68286:5","type":"choice","text":"Before leaving on his journey, Cyriacus studied ancient languages.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He set out to solve these failings, first by learning Latin at the age of 30 and then adding ancient Greek. Having done this, he then set off on voyages around the Mediterranean to find, investigate and understand ancient cultures from their buildings, sculptures and inscriptions.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：判断Cyriacus在出发旅行前是否学习了古代语言，关键词“before leaving”“studied ancient languages”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干“ancient languages”和“studied”定位到C段“first by learning Latin ... adding ancient Greek ... Having done this, he then set off”。\n解题思路：原文明确说明他先学习拉丁语和古希腊语，然后才出发旅行，与题干一致，故选TRUE。FALSE错误因原文有直接肯定信息；NOT GIVEN错误因原文明确提及该信息。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68286","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"9565:68287:6","type":"choice","text":"Travelling by sea in the 15th century was easier than travelling on land.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Overland journeys by foot or mule along bad roads, under constant threat from bandits, were bad; voyages by sea were even worse.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：判断题问15世纪海上旅行是否比陆地旅行更容易，关键词“easier than travelling on land”。\n定位关键信息：通过题干关键词“15th century”、“sea”、“travelling on land”定位到D段关于旅行困难的描述。\n解题思路：原文明确说陆路旅行“bad”，但海上旅行“even worse”，即更困难，与题干“easier”相反，因此选FALSE；TRUE与原文冲突；NOT GIVEN不成立，因为原文直接比较了难易程度。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68287","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"9565:68288:7","type":"choice","text":"Cyriacus tried to make his fellow sea travellers more comfortable.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Remarkably, Cyriacus never complained about the miseries of travel. Optimistic by nature, he endured such hardships unafraid and saw opportunities where other people saw setbacks.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题干问Cyriacus是否试图让同船的海上旅行者更舒适，关键词是“fellow sea travellers”和“more comfortable”。\n定位关键信息：在原文D段搜索与同船旅行者或改善舒适度相关的描述，发现该段主要描述航海艰难及Cyriacus个人态度，未提及对他人舒适度的关注。\n解题思路：原文仅说明Cyriacus自己乐观忍受航海艰辛，未说他有任何试图让同船旅客更舒适的行为或言论，故答案选NOT GIVEN；选项TRUE无依据，选项FALSE也无相反证据。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68288","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"9565:68289:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"commerce","acceptedAnswers":["commerce"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Among many of the important records made by Cyriacus was his crucial documenting, in 1431, of the remains of Cyzicus, an ancient Roman city that had relied on commerce for its financial success.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问Cyzicus城市的财富来自什么，关键词wealth和Cyzicus。\n定位关键信息：用wealth和Cyzicus定位到E段中描述城市依靠commerce for its financial success。\n解题思路：原文“relied on commerce for its financial success”表明财富来源于commerce，与答案一致。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68289","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answer in boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"9565:68289:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"guidebook","acceptedAnswers":["guidebook"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He hired a local person to take him to the site and then had to work out for himself the significance of the ruins he was looking at because there was no guidebook on ancient architecture to help him.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问在Cyriacus访问Cyzicus古城遗址时，什么（guidebook）是不可用的。\n定位关键信息：根据题干关键词“not available”和“Cyzicus”，定位到E段最后一句中“no guidebook”。\n解题思路：原文明确说“there was no guidebook”，与答案“guidebook”对应，表明当时缺乏旅行指南。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68289","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answer in boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"9565:68289:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"earthquake","acceptedAnswers":["earthquake"],"explanation":"原文答案句：in AD 123 the city was so devastated by a major earthquake\n对应段落：F段\n审题：问Cyzicus在公元123年被什么强大的东西摧毁；关键词是destroyed、AD 123。\n定位关键信息：用AD 123定位到F段，找到“in AD 123 the city was so devastated by a major earthquake”。\n解题思路：原文“devastated by a major earthquake”与题目“destroyed by a powerful ____”对应，earthquake即答案。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68289","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answer in boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"9565:68289:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"campaign","acceptedAnswers":["campaign"],"explanation":"原文答案句：when the Roman Emperor Hadrian visited it the following year, he was so saddened that he decided to subsidise a campaign to reconstruct Cyzicus.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问哈德良皇帝支持了什么来重建城市，填入一个词。\n定位关键信息：用“the following year”（即AD 124）和“supported a ... to rebuild”定位到F段原文subsidise a campaign to reconstruct。\n解题思路：原文中subsidise与题目supported同义，campaign与题目所需名词对应，因此答案为campaign。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68289","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answer in boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"9565:68289:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"doorway","acceptedAnswers":["doorway"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He sketched the great doorway adorned with carved foliage and mythological characters.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问Cyriacus发现部分神庙，并画了神庙的什么及其装饰雕刻；关键词为drawings、temple、decorative carvings。\n定位关键信息：用“Cyriacus found part of the temple”和“made drawings”定位到F段后半部分。\n解题思路：原文sketched对应made drawings，great doorway即为画的对象，且后面adorned with carved foliage对应decorative carvings，故答案为doorway。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68289","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answer in boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"9565:68289:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"war","acceptedAnswers":["war"],"explanation":"原文答案句：when Cyriacus arrived at the site of Delphi, however, he found war, earthquakes and avalanches had all but obliterated its ruins.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问德尔斐在15世纪几乎消失的原因，包括自然灾害和另一个因素，需填入一个词。\n定位关键信息：通过地名“Delphi”和“15th century”定位到G段，原文提到战争、地震和山崩几乎摧毁了废墟。\n解题思路：题目中“natural disasters”对应原文中的“earthquakes and avalanches”，原文并列列出“war”，因此另一个原因是“war”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68289","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answer in boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"68282","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>Cyriacus was unable to research his journeys before he left.</p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"68283","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>The Roman Emperor Trajan built the city of Ancona.</p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"68284","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>Respect for ancient architecture was widespread in the 15th century.</p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"68285","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>Cyriacus’s experience as a merchant gave him skills he needed to investigate the ancient world.</p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"68286","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>Before leaving on his journey, Cyriacus studied ancient languages.</p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"68287","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>Travelling by sea in the 15th century was easier than travelling on land.</p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"68288","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>Cyriacus tried to make his fellow sea travellers more comfortable.</p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"68289","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answer in boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ancient Roman and Greek sites visited by Cyriacus</strong></p><p><strong>The city of Cyzicus</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">• The wealth of the city had come from <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">• <strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong> to the ancient city ruins was not available when visited by Cyriacus.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">• The city was destroyed by a powerful <strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong> in AD 123.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">• A year later Emperor Hadrian supported a <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong> to rebuild the city.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">• Cyriacus found part of the temple, which was built in the time of Emperor Hadrian, and made drawings of the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong> to the temple and its decorative carvings.</p><p><strong>The sanctuary of Delphi</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">• By the 15th century Delphi had almost disappeared due to natural disasters and <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":8}],"passage":"<div><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>An early cultural tourist&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>In the 15th century, the Italian merchant Cyriacus of Ancona journeyed in search of the\nMediterranean’s classical past. In doing so, he laid the groundwork for today’s cultural\nholidays&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Today we take it for granted that we travel around the world to admire the monuments of\nthe past. We prepare for such trips by reading about what we are going to see, set out on\nthe journey with a good idea of how we will get there and where we will stay, and have a\nsense of what we will encounter on location. Cyriacus of Ancona (1391-1452), the first\ncultural tourist since antiquity, lacked these advantages when, in the first half of the 15th\ncentury, he sailed around the Mediterranean in search of the remains of Greek and Roman\ncivilisations.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Cyriacus first became fascinated by ancient monuments while walking in his home city\nAncona and looking at the marble arch, erected in AD 115, to the Roman Emperor Trajan. He suddenly saw the culture in a new light. He no longer saw it as just a familiar and\ngenerally overlooked landmark, but as a doorway to the wonders of ancient imperial Rome. Not many people of Cyriacus’s time were interested in historical travel; they generally\nignored old buildings and structures, or worse, dismantled them for their building materials.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Cyriacus decided to see the world for himself and to record details of whatever other\nantiquities remained to be discovered. His training as a merchant did not prepare him for\nthis vocation; he did not know ancient languages, history or art. However, he set out to\nsolve these failings, first by learning Latin at the age of 30 and then adding ancient Greek. Having done this, he then set off on voyages around the Mediterranean to find, investigate\nand understand ancient cultures from their buildings, sculptures and inscriptions. Thus he\nbecame the first archaeologist and cultural tourist, predating other antiquarians by some\n200 years.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Travel in the 15th century, however, was anything but simple or enjoyable. Overland\njourneys by foot or mule along bad roads, under constant threat from bandits, were bad;\nvoyages by sea were even worse. When the weather cooperated, sailing went relatively\nsmoothly: ships proceeded along coasts from one recognisable landmark to another. However, when there was no wind, the ship did not move. Strong winds were no friends\neither; they drenched the ship with lashing waves and blew it off course. Water swamped\nthe deck, splashed into the cabins and soaked mattresses, clothes and food. Remarkably,\nCyriacus never complained about the miseries of travel. Optimistic by nature, he endured\nsuch hardships unafraid and saw opportunities where other people saw setbacks.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Among many of the important records made by Cyriacus was his crucial documenting, in\n1431, of the remains of Cyzicus, an ancient Roman city that had relied on commerce for its\nfinancial success. He hired a local person to take him to the site and then had to work out\nfor himself the significance of the ruins he was looking at because there was no guidebook\non ancient architecture to help him.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Indeed, he had no contemporary knowledge about the ruins. Cyzicus had been a splendid\ncity in its prime. Unfortunately, the area was highly seismic and in AD 123 the city was so\ndevastated by a major earthquake that, when the Roman Emperor Hadrian visited it the\nfollowing year, he was so saddened that he decided to subsidise a campaign to reconstruct\nCyzicus. He made a substantial donation for a new temple to the Roman god Jupiter. Cyriacus thought the ruined city was awe-inspiring. He found the remains of the temple and\nexamined it in great detail, looking for clues in ancient texts to help him understand what he\nwas seeing. He sketched the great doorway adorned with carved foliage and mythological\ncharacters. Cyriacus’s account of this temple is the only record of this building, as in the\nfollowing centuries it was entirely stripped of all its stonework and all that remains is its\nbase.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Cyriacus also visited mainland Greece, in 1436, when no one went to Greece in order to\nsee the country’s ancient ruins. One of his destinations was the sanctuary of Delphi. The\nancient Greeks considered Delphi as being situated in the most beautiful spot in Greece. When Cyriacus arrived at the site of Delphi, however, he found war, earthquakes and\navalanches had all but obliterated its ruins. Determined to find any ancient traces, Cyriacus\nspent six days walking all over the area, peering at odd stone blocks sticking out of the\nground, running his hands over inscriptions to trace fragments of words, and trying to\npuzzle out the few surviving structural remains. Climbing uphill towards the rocks that tower\nover the site, he came upon a theatre built into the slope. Soon after his visit, the site was\nburied by a rockslide and was not seen again until archaeologists began to excavate the\narea systematically in the late 19th century.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Cyriacus had hoped to visit Egypt and Ethiopia, but he never got there. However, in his life\nhe did record for posterity countless ancient monuments around the Mediterranean, paving\nthe way for future archaeologists and cultural tourists.&nbsp;</p></div>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9565&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9566","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Why do singers lose their voices?","book":"阅读真题集 22","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test1","part":2,"description":"阅读真题集 22 · Test1 · 16 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"9566:68290:14","type":"choice","text":"examples of some of the environmental factors which affect singers","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Dusty theatres, stuffy airplane cabins, erratic eating and sleeping patterns and stress all affect the vocal cords.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目询问影响歌手的一些环境因素的例子，关键词是environmental factors。\n定位关键信息：通过environmental factors和affect singers定位到C段中列举具体因素的句子。\n解题思路：C段原文直接列举了Dusty theatres, stuffy airplane cabins等环境因素，与题干要求的环境因素例子完全对应。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"68290","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–19\nReading Passage 2 has six sections, A–F.\nWhich section contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"9566:68290:15","type":"choice","text":"a reference to a lack of awareness of a correct singing technique","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：She believes that students are graduating from music academies without having learned this natural singing method. In her opinion, today's students 'don't know how to sing, and it's leading to injury'.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题干要求找出提及“对正确歌唱技巧缺乏认识”的相关信息。\n定位关键信息：通过题干关键词“lack of awareness”“correct singing technique”定位到E段中Marianna Brilla关于学生“don't know how to sing”的观点。\n解题思路：E段中Brilla指出学生毕业时未学会自然歌唱方法，即缺乏对正确技巧的认知，与题干信息直接对应。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"68290","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–19\nReading Passage 2 has six sections, A–F.\nWhich section contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"9566:68290:16","type":"choice","text":"details of the physical processes involved when a person sings","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Every vocal performance involves hundreds of thousands of micro-collisions of a thin pair of muscular strips called the vocal cords, located in the larynx in the throat. When we are breathing in, they remain apart; when we sing or speak, air is pushed up out of the lungs, and the edges of the cords come together in a rapid chopping motion. The air causes the cords to vibrate, creating sound.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：本题要求找出包含“一个人唱歌时涉及的物理过程细节”的段落。\n定位关键信息：题干中的“physical processes”和“when a person sings”指向A段中描述声带运动、空气流动和发声机制的句子。\n解题思路：A段具体描述了唱歌时声带的碰撞、闭合、振动等物理过程，与题干“物理过程的细节”直接对应，因此答案选A段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"68290","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–19\nReading Passage 2 has six sections, A–F.\nWhich section contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"9566:68290:17","type":"choice","text":"a defence of the use of surgery to treat vocal injuries","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Robert Sataloff, who has performed voice-corrective surgery on several award-winning performers, also resents the notion that surgery is not a sensible way to keep singers healthy. He believes that surgery, combined with proper education on the dangers of improper singing technique, can keep people on stage for longer.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求找出包含“对使用手术治疗声带损伤的辩护”的段落，关键词为defence、use of surgery、treat vocal injuries。\n定位关键信息：通过关键词surgery和辩护（resent the notion that surgery is not sensible）定位到F段，其中Robert Sataloff的观点直接反驳了反对手术的看法。\n解题思路：原文中Sataloff明确反对“手术不是明智方式”的观点，并认为手术结合教育能延长歌手生涯，这正是一种辩护，因此信息出现在F段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"68290","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–19\nReading Passage 2 has six sections, A–F.\nWhich section contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"9566:68290:18","type":"choice","text":"a description of the initial indications of vocal problems","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For a singer, the first sign of trouble is often the ‘wobble’: the voice fluctuates on and off key because the damaged cords have lost the ability to resonate properly. Often, there is a ‘hole’, a point on the musical scale where a singer’s vibrating vocal cords fail to produce the proper tone.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求找包含“声音问题最初迹象的描述”的段落，关键词为“initial indications of vocal problems”。\n定位关键信息：用“initial indications”对应原文“first sign of trouble”和“wobble”、“hole”等描述。\n解题思路：B段直接描述歌手嗓音问题的首个信号（first sign）即“wobble”和“hole”，与题干“初始迹象”完全对应。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"68290","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–19\nReading Passage 2 has six sections, A–F.\nWhich section contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"9566:68290:19","type":"choice","text":"a reference to modern perceptions of a good singing performance","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：These injuries have been linked to a shift in what we consider quality singing. Across all genres, it has become normal to believe that louder is better\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求找出提及现代对好的歌唱表演看法的段落，关键词是modern perceptions、good singing performance。\n定位关键信息：根据“modern perceptions”和“good singing performance”定位到D段中关于对优质歌唱看法转变的描述。\n解题思路：D段提到对优质歌唱的看法发生转变，普遍认为更大声更好，这直接对应现代对好的歌唱表演的认知。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"68290","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–19\nReading Passage 2 has six sections, A–F.\nWhich section contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"9566:68291:20","type":"fill","text":"填写第 20 空","answer":"pitch","acceptedAnswers":["pitch"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The greater the vibration, the higher the pitch, and when a soprano hits the highest notes her vocal cords are vibrating 1,000 times per second.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问声音的什么由声带振动频率决定，关键词是“rate of vibration”和“vocal cords”。\n定位关键信息：用“rate of vibration”和“vocal cords”定位到A段“the greater the vibration, the higher the pitch”。\n解题思路：原文说明振动越大音高越高，即音高由振动率决定，与题干描述一致，因此答案是pitch。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68291","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20–24\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 20–24 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"9566:68291:21","type":"fill","text":"填写第 21 空","answer":"friction","acceptedAnswers":["friction"],"explanation":"原文答案句：the friction caused by prolonged overuse can erode their fine, spongy surface\n对应段落：B段\n审题：本题问的是声带脆弱的表面在持续过度使用时会被什么磨损。\n定位关键信息：根据题干名词“delicate surface”“continually overused”定位到B段“friction caused by prolonged overuse can erode their fine, spongy surface”。\n解题思路：原文“friction caused by prolonged overuse can erode”与题干“worn down by ... if they are continually overused”对应，因此答案为friction。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68291","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20–24\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 20–24 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"9566:68291:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"tone","acceptedAnswers":["tone"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Often, there is a ‘hole’, a point on the musical scale where a singer’s vibrating vocal cords fail to produce the proper tone.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题干问有声音损伤的歌手在音阶的某个点上无法发出具有正确什么的声音，关键词为“vocal cord damage”、“a certain point on the musical scale”。\n定位关键信息：用“a certain point on the musical scale”和“vocal cord damage”定位到B段中“a point on the musical scale”和“damaged cords”。\n解题思路：原文B段指出，受损声带在音阶的某一点上无法发出“the proper tone”，其中“proper tone”与题干“correct ____”对应，故答案为tone。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68291","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20–24\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 20–24 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"9566:68291:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"drugs","acceptedAnswers":["drugs"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Some opera singers complain of year-round cold symptoms, and steroid injections and numerous other drugs are often used to get a struggling singer through a performance.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问歌剧演员经常被给予各种各样的什么以确保他们能完成表演，关键词是Opera singers、a variety of、complete performances。\n定位关键信息：用Opera singers和complete performances定位到B段最后一句关于药物使用的描述。\n解题思路：原文直接提到steroid injections and numerous other drugs are often used to get a struggling singer through a performance，drugs与空白处对应，且表示通过药物来帮助完成表演，因此正确答案是drugs。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68291","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20–24\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 20–24 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"9566:68291:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"roles","acceptedAnswers":["roles"],"explanation":"原文答案句：of taking on roles that require artists to sing beyond their natural range\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问歌剧和古典表演者如果表演什么样的角色会增加受伤风险，关键词为“perform”“roles”“place exceptional demands”。\n定位关键信息：用“Opera and classical performers”和“risk of injury”定位到C段“occupational hazard – at least in opera and classical music – of taking on roles that require artists to sing beyond their natural range”。\n解题思路：原文提到歌剧和古典音乐中承担要求歌手超越自然音域的角色是职业危害，与题目“perform roles which place exceptional demands”对应，故答案为roles。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68291","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20–24\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 20–24 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"9566:68292:25","type":"choice","text":"Surgery provides performers with only a short-term solution to their problems.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：According to Lisa Paglin, a singer turned voice coach, Zeitels has simply found a temporary remedy.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问谁认为手术对表演者只是短期解决方案。\n定位关键信息：用“surgery provides only a short-term solution”（短期解决方案）和关键词“temporary remedy”定位到E段Lisa Paglin的言论。\n解题思路：Lisa Paglin明确指出Zeitels的手术只是“a temporary remedy”（临时补救），对应题干“only a short-term solution”，因此正确答案是C。","options":["Will Crutchfield","Steven Zeitels","Lisa Paglin","Robert Sataloff"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68292","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 25–29\nLook at the following statements (Questions 25–29) and the list of people below.\nMatch each statement with the correct person, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter, A, B, C, or D, in boxes 25–29 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Will Crutchfield\nB Steven Zeitels\nC Lisa Paglin\nD Robert Sataloff"},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"9566:68292:26","type":"choice","text":"The public are now used to attending performances given by singers with vocal injuries.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Will Crutchfield, a conductor and vocal coach, laments the fact that this vocal burnout is cutting short careers and diminishing the power of opera, and he feels that audiences have become accustomed to hearing voices which are not in peak condition.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目询问“公众现在习惯了参加由嗓音受伤歌手进行的演出”对应哪个人物，关键词为“public are now used to attending performances given by singers with vocal injuries”。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“public are now used to”与原文D段“audiences have become accustomed to”同义改写，“singers with vocal injuries”对应“voices which are not in peak condition”，定位到D段Will Crutchfield的观点。\n解题思路：原文D段中Will Crutchfield认为观众已经习惯了听到不处于最佳状态的嗓音，与题干中公众习惯于欣赏有嗓音损伤的歌手表演完全一致，因此匹配人物A Will Crutchfield。","options":["Will Crutchfield","Steven Zeitels","Lisa Paglin","Robert Sataloff"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68292","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 25–29\nLook at the following statements (Questions 25–29) and the list of people below.\nMatch each statement with the correct person, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter, A, B, C, or D, in boxes 25–29 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Will Crutchfield\nB Steven Zeitels\nC Lisa Paglin\nD Robert Sataloff"},{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"9566:68292:27","type":"choice","text":"People are wrong to suggest that performers who undergo surgical procedures to repair their voices lack singing ability.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：People used to think if you needed an operation it meant you don’t know how to sing. The people I see – they know how to sing!\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题干指出“人们错误地认为接受手术修复声音的表演者缺乏演唱能力”，要求匹配持有此反驳观点的人物。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的“wrong to suggest”“lack singing ability”定位到F段Zeitels关于“操作意味着不会唱歌”的论述。\n解题思路：原文中Zeitels明确表态“人们过去认为手术意味着不会唱歌，但我的客户都会唱歌”，直接否定题干所指的错误观点，故对应B。","options":["Will Crutchfield","Steven Zeitels","Lisa Paglin","Robert Sataloff"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68292","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 25–29\nLook at the following statements (Questions 25–29) and the list of people below.\nMatch each statement with the correct person, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter, A, B, C, or D, in boxes 25–29 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Will Crutchfield\nB Steven Zeitels\nC Lisa Paglin\nD Robert Sataloff"},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"9566:68292:28","type":"choice","text":"Surgery works best when used in conjunction with re-training performers.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He believes that surgery, combined with proper education on the dangers of improper singing technique, can keep people on stage for longer.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目询问手术在什么情况下效果最好，即与再培训结合使用。\n定位关键信息：题干关键词“combined with re-training”对应原文“combined with proper education”。\n解题思路：Robert Sataloff明确表示手术与适当教育结合能延长歌唱生涯，此即“手术与再培训结合”的最佳体现，因此选D。","options":["Will Crutchfield","Steven Zeitels","Lisa Paglin","Robert Sataloff"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68292","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 25–29\nLook at the following statements (Questions 25–29) and the list of people below.\nMatch each statement with the correct person, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter, A, B, C, or D, in boxes 25–29 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Will Crutchfield\nB Steven Zeitels\nC Lisa Paglin\nD Robert Sataloff"},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"9566:68292:29","type":"choice","text":"New and innovative surgical techniques hold the key to repairing damaged vocal cords.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Steven Zeitels, a specialist vocal cord surgeon, believes that pioneering surgery is the way forward.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题干问“新颖创新的手术技术是修复受损声带的关键”，关键词是“New and innovative surgical techniques”和“hold the key”。\n定位关键信息：根据“innovative surgical techniques”定位到E段中Zeitels关于“pioneering surgery”和“futuristic solution”的论述。\n解题思路：原文中Zeitels认为“pioneering surgery is the way forward”，并描述其研究修复声带的新方法，直接对应题干观点，故匹配B。","options":["Will Crutchfield","Steven Zeitels","Lisa Paglin","Robert Sataloff"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68292","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 25–29\nLook at the following statements (Questions 25–29) and the list of people below.\nMatch each statement with the correct person, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter, A, B, C, or D, in boxes 25–29 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Will Crutchfield\nB Steven Zeitels\nC Lisa Paglin\nD Robert Sataloff"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"68290","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–19\nReading Passage 2 has six sections, A–F.\nWhich section contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>examples of some of the environmental factors which affect singers <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong></p><p>a reference to a lack of awareness of a correct singing technique <strong class=\"source-blank\">[15] ____</strong></p><p>details of the physical processes involved when a person sings <strong class=\"source-blank\">[16] ____</strong></p><p>a defence of the use of surgery to treat vocal injuries <strong class=\"source-blank\">[17] ____</strong></p><p>a description of the initial indications of vocal problems <strong class=\"source-blank\">[18] ____</strong></p><p>a reference to modern perceptions of a good singing performance <strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"68291","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20–24\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 20–24 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">20.The <strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong> of a sound is determined by the rate of vibration of the vocal cords.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">21.The delicate surface of the vocal cords can be worn down by <strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong> if they are continually overused. 22.Singers with vocal cord damage are often unable to produce a sound with the correct <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong> at a certain point on the musical scale.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">23.Opera singers are often given a variety of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong> to make sure they can complete their performances. 24.Opera and classical performers are at greater risk of injury if they perform <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> which place exceptional demands on their voices.</p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"68292","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 25–29\nLook at the following statements (Questions 25–29) and the list of people below.\nMatch each statement with the correct person, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter, A, B, C, or D, in boxes 25–29 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Will Crutchfield\nB Steven Zeitels\nC Lisa Paglin\nD Robert Sataloff","html":"<p>Surgery provides performers with only a short-term solution to their problems. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong></p><p>The public are now used to attending performances given by singers with vocal injuries. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong></p><p>People are wrong to suggest that performers who undergo surgical procedures to repair their voices lack singing ability. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[27] ____</strong></p><p>Surgery works best when used in conjunction with re-training performers. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[28] ____</strong></p><p>New and innovative surgical techniques hold the key to repairing damaged vocal cords. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[29] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":25}],"passage":"<div><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Why do singers lose their voices?&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Singing is a tough business. Every vocal performance involves hundreds of thousands of micro-collisions of a thin pair of muscular strips called the vocal cords, located in the larynx in the throat. When we are breathing in, they remain apart; when we sing or speak, air is pushed up out of the lungs, and the edges of the cords come together in a rapid chopping motion. The air causes the cords to vibrate, creating sound. The greater the vibration, the higher the pitch, and when a soprano hits the highest notes her vocal cords are vibrating 1,000 times per second. This transforms a burst of air from her lungs into a sound powerful enough to shatter glass.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Beautiful singing requires flexible cords, but the friction caused by prolonged overuse can erode their fine, spongy surface and lead to tiny bruises. Eventually, nodules, polyps or cysts form on the vocal folds, distorting the sound they create. For a singer, the first sign of trouble is often the ‘wobble’: the voice fluctuates on and off key because the damaged cords have lost the ability to resonate properly. Often, there is a ‘hole’, a point on the musical scale where a singer’s vibrating vocal cords fail to produce the proper tone. The sound produced will be flat, or worse still, barely audible.</p><p><br/></p><p>It was once unheard of for a singer to perform with a faulty voice. However, in recent times, it has become more common for performances to be interrupted, or even cancelled due to the inability of the performer to continue. Some opera singers complain of year-round cold symptoms, and steroid injections and numerous other drugs are often used to get a struggling singer through a performance. But continuing to sing can cause more damage and create voice-ruining scars, similar to when a football player continues to play with a damaged knee and eventually needs surgery.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>There is no precise data on the number of performers who have undergone surgical procedures, but it is estimated that thousands have been under the knife. Dusty theatres, stuffy airplane cabins, erratic eating and sleeping patterns and stress all affect the vocal cords. Add to all this the occupational hazard – at least in opera and classical music – of taking on roles that require artists to sing beyond their natural range, and a singer’s cords become extremely susceptible to injury.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Will Crutchfield, a conductor and vocal coach, laments the fact that this vocal burnout is cutting short careers and diminishing the power of opera, and he feels that audiences have become accustomed to hearing voices which are not in peak condition. When he first highlighted the problem, he noticed that it didn’t affect singers until they were in their 30s, but now even singers in their 20s are undergoing medical procedures to save their careers. These injuries have been linked to a shift in what we consider quality singing. Across all genres, it has become normal to believe that louder is better, and singers are pushing their vocal cords like never before. New waves of medical research into dysphonia, or the inability to properly produce sound, bear this out. In the Western world, vocal abuse is surprisingly common in all professions that rely on the voice, from schoolteachers to opera singers.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Steven Zeitels, a specialist vocal cord surgeon, believes that pioneering surgery is the way forward. He is working on a futuristic solution which will involve implanting a gel made of biomaterial in the tissue of damaged vocal cords to restore pliability, and therefore the voice. However, some research studies argue that surgery is not necessarily a lasting fix. According to Lisa Paglin, a singer turned voice coach, Zeitels has simply found a temporary remedy. ‘Unless a singer makes major changes, “return to performing” means a return to the vocal abuse that put him/her on the operating table in the first place’. Her coaching partner Marianna Brilla agrees. ‘You cannot solve the problem by simply relieving the symptom.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>One observation Paglin and Brilla have made from working with older, classically trained singers is the way that they use the natural up-down release of the diaphragm to produce sound, rather than relying on their vocal cords. For Brilla, this represents a real discovery: the root of the problem today is in classrooms. She believes that students are graduating from music academies without having learned this natural singing method. In her opinion, today’s students ‘don’t know how to sing, and it’s leading to injury’.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Is it possible that teaching people to sing differently could cure damaged vocal cords forever? Zeitels is dismissive of such an approach, and quick to deny that his clients’ vocal problems are caused by bad technique. ‘People used to think if you needed an operation it meant you don’t know how to sing. The people I see – they know how to sing!’ Zeitels believes that medical specialists are becoming increasingly important to the arts, given that any athletic endeavour will eventually take a toll if done for long enough.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Robert Sataloff, who has performed voice-corrective surgery on several award-winning performers, also resents the notion that surgery is not a sensible way to keep singers healthy. He believes that surgery, combined with proper education on the dangers of improper singing technique, can keep people on stage for longer. He concedes that surgery is not a perfect solution, and it probably never will be, but it is an option.&nbsp;</p></div>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9566&scene=%E5%8C%BB%E7%96%97%E5%81%A5%E5%BA%B7&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9567","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Sign, Baby, Sign!","book":"阅读真题集 22","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test1","part":3,"description":"阅读真题集 22 · Test1 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"9567:68293:27","type":"choice","text":"A statement about the different things people use language for","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Language is a powerful tool that humans use for a wide variety of purposes—from expressing emotions and sharing ideas to passing down cultural values and acquiring knowledge.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问哪一段包含关于人们使用语言的不同用途的陈述，关键词为“different things people use language for”。\n定位关键信息：题干中“different things people use language for”对应A段原文中的“wide variety of purposes”及后文列举的功能。\n解题思路：A段首句直接点明语言用于多种目的并举例，与题干信息完全吻合，故答案选A段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"68293","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27–33\nReading Passage 3 has seven paragraphs, A–G.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 27–33 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"9567:68293:28","type":"choice","text":"How knowing ASL may benefit students in their future subject choices","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Some educators believe this early exposure may even influence students to pursue careers in special education, speech therapy, or interpreting.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问学习ASL如何有利于学生未来的科目选择，关键词是\"future subject choices\"。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"future subject choices\"和\"benefit\"，在B段找到\"influence students to pursue careers\"。\n解题思路：原文指出早期接触ASL可能影响学生从事特殊教育、言语治疗等职业，这与未来科目选择直接对应。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"68293","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27–33\nReading Passage 3 has seven paragraphs, A–G.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 27–33 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"9567:68293:29","type":"choice","text":"An assertion that deaf children have a right to be taught a sign language","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：She, along with other advocates, stresses that deaf children have a right to a full, accessible language from birth—and that language is often sign.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问哪一段包含“聋儿有权被教授手语”这一主张。\n定位关键信息：用“deaf children have a right”和“sign language”定位到G段末句。\n解题思路：G段末句明确提到聋儿从出生起就有权获得完整、可接触的语言，而这种语言通常是手语，直接对应题干中的assertion。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"68293","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27–33\nReading Passage 3 has seven paragraphs, A–G.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 27–33 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"9567:68293:30","type":"choice","text":"An observation regarding the ability of small children to use their hands","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Very young children often develop motor skills before verbal skills. Dr. Daniels notes that even babies as young as six months can learn to use simple signs like \"milk\" or \"more\" with their hands, long before they can articulate those words.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目询问关于小孩子用手（使用手势）能力的观察。\n定位关键信息：通过“ability of small children to use their hands”（小孩子用手的能力）定位到E段中“babies as young as six months can learn to use simple signs...with their hands”。\n解题思路：原文指出幼儿在言语技能之前发展运动技能，六个月大的婴儿能用手学习简单手势，这直接佐证了题目中关于小孩子用手能力的观察。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"68293","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27–33\nReading Passage 3 has seven paragraphs, A–G.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 27–33 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"9567:68293:31","type":"choice","text":"The advantage for hearing children of knowing ASL for wider social interaction","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：One clear benefit of learning ASL for hearing children is the opportunity for broader social interaction.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问听力正常儿童学习ASL对于更广泛社交互利的优势。\n定位关键信息：用 advantage、hearing children、ASL、wider social interaction 定位到C段首句。\n解题思路：原文首句明确说学习ASL对听力正常儿童的一个好处是更广泛的社交互动机会，与题干完全对应。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"68293","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27–33\nReading Passage 3 has seven paragraphs, A–G.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 27–33 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"9567:68293:32","type":"choice","text":"Different views on when deaf children should be taught to speak","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：There remains some debate about the best approach to language instruction for deaf children. Some educators argue that speech and lip-reading should come first, while others advocate for immediate exposure to sign language.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问关于何时教聋童说话的不同观点。\n定位关键信息：通过关键词“deaf children”和“taught to speak”定位到G段关于语言教学方法的争论。\n解题思路：原文直接提到“some educators argue that speech and lip-reading should come first, while others advocate for immediate exposure to sign language”，对应题干中“different views on when deaf children should be taught to speak”。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"68293","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27–33\nReading Passage 3 has seven paragraphs, A–G.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 27–33 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"9567:68293:33","type":"choice","text":"An observation about the reading ability of primary-school-age hearing children who have been taught ASL","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Studies have shown that hearing children exposed to sign language from an early age tend to have stronger reading skills by the time they enter primary school.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问关于学龄前听力正常儿童学习ASL后阅读能力的观察，关键词为reading ability, primary-school-age, hearing children, taught ASL。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的reading ability和primary-school-age hearing children taught ASL，在F段找到hearing children exposed to sign language...stronger reading skills by the time they enter primary school。\n解题思路：F段首句直接说明学习ASL的听力正常儿童在小学入学时阅读能力更强，完全对应题干所述的阅读能力观察。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"68293","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27–33\nReading Passage 3 has seven paragraphs, A–G.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 27–33 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"9567:68294:34","type":"choice","text":"Dr. Daniels believes that parents should make up their own gestures to communicate with their babies.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：While she promotes the use of sign language with infants, she emphasizes that there is no need for parents to invent their own signs.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题干问Dr. Daniels是否认为父母应自创手势与婴儿交流，关键词为\"make up their own gestures\"。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的人名\"Dr. Daniels\"和\"make up their own gestures\"定位到D段\"invent their own signs\"。\n解题思路：原文明确说Dr. Daniels强调\"no need for parents to invent their own signs\"，即不应自创，与题干主张相反，故答案选FALSE；TRUE与原文矛盾，NOT GIVEN因有明确信息而被排除。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68294","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34–40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 34–40 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"9567:68295:35","type":"choice","text":"American Sign Language is the most widely used sign language in the world.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In recent years, many American schools have begun to recognize American Sign Language (ASL) as a valid foreign language credit。\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问American Sign Language是否是世界上使用最广泛的手语，关键词是“most widely used”和“in the world”。\n定位关键信息：题干中的“American Sign Language”在B段首句出现，但“most widely used”和“in the world”在全文任何段落均未提及。\n解题思路：原文只提及ASL被美国学校认可及其好处，但从未与世界其他手语比较或声称其使用范围最广。A选项TRUE无原文依据，B选项FALSE也无原文否定，故正确答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68295","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34–40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 34–40 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"9567:68296:36","type":"choice","text":"For hearing children in America, learning American Sign Language is an equivalent option to learning a foreign language.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In recent years, many American schools have begun to recognize American Sign Language (ASL) as a valid foreign language credit, just like Spanish or French.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题干问美国听力正常的儿童学习美国手语是否等同于学习一门外语，关键词为hearing children in America、learning American Sign Language、equivalent option、foreign language。\n定位关键信息：根据题干关键词American Sign Language和foreign language定位到B段首句。\n解题思路：B段首句说明ASL被认可为有效的外语学分，如同西班牙语或法语，因此学习ASL等同于学习外语，故答案为TRUE；选项B FALSE与原文事实矛盾；选项C NOT GIVEN因原文有明确提及而不成立。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68296","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34–40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 34–40 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"9567:68297:37","type":"choice","text":"Brain research indicates that vocabulary is more easily learned than grammar.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It is believed that learning sign language can strengthen understanding of symbolic representation and grammar, both of which are foundational to literacy.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问脑研究表明词汇比语法更容易学习，判断该说法是否符合原文。\n定位关键信息：关键词“brain research”和“vocabulary more easily learned than grammar”在全文未出现。\n解题思路：原文并未提及任何关于脑研究的内容，也没有比较词汇和语法学习的难易程度，因此该说法在原文中无相关信息，答案为NOT GIVEN。选项A TRUE原文无依据；选项B FALSE原文无依据。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68297","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34–40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 34–40 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"9567:68298:38","type":"choice","text":"First and second languages are stored on different sides of the brain.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Language, whether signed or spoken, plays a vital role in how we engage with the world around us.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：判断“第一语言和第二语言存储在大脑不同侧”是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题干关键词“first and second languages”和“different sides of the brain”在原文中均未出现，无法定位。\n解题思路：原文未提及第一语言和第二语言在大脑中的存储位置，题干信息无任何原文依据，故答案选C（NOT GIVEN）。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68298","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34–40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 34–40 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"9567:68299:39","type":"choice","text":"Children have less difficulty learning to make signs than learning to make sounds.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Very young children often develop motor skills before verbal skills. Dr. Daniels notes that even babies as young as six months can learn to use simple signs like “milk” or “more” with their hands, long before they can articulate those words.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：判断儿童学习做手势是否比学习发声的困难更小。\n定位关键信息：根据题干关键词“less difficulty learning to make signs”和“learning to make sounds”，定位到E段关于运动技能先于语言技能的论述。\n解题思路：原文指出幼儿运动技能先于语言技能，6个月婴儿能用手势表达，远早于能说出词语，说明学习手势比发声更容易，故TRUE；FALSE与原文相反；NOT GIVEN原文已明确提及，排除。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68299","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34–40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 34–40 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"9567:68300:40","type":"choice","text":"According to Dr. Daniels, the view that deaf children must learn lip-reading before sign language is old-fashioned.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：She calls the idea that children must learn to lip-read before learning sign language “an outdated notion.”\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问Dr. Daniels是否认为“聋儿必须先学唇读再学手语”的观点是过时的。\n定位关键信息：用Dr. Daniels和“lip-reading before sign language”定位到G段后半部分。\n解题思路：原文直接称该观点为“an outdated notion”，与题干“old-fashioned”同义，因此答案为TRUE。FALSE与原文相反；NOT GIVEN因原文明确提及而排除。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68300","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34–40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 34–40 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"68293","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27–33\nReading Passage 3 has seven paragraphs, A–G.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 27–33 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.","html":"<p>A statement about the different things people use language for <strong class=\"source-blank\">[27] ____</strong></p><p>How knowing ASL may benefit students in their future subject choices <strong class=\"source-blank\">[28] ____</strong></p><p>An assertion that deaf children have a right to be taught a sign language <strong class=\"source-blank\">[29] ____</strong></p><p>An observation regarding the ability of small children to use their hands <strong class=\"source-blank\">[30] ____</strong></p><p>The advantage for hearing children of knowing ASL for wider social interaction <strong class=\"source-blank\">[31] ____</strong></p><p>Different views on when deaf children should be taught to speak <strong class=\"source-blank\">[32] ____</strong></p><p>An observation about the reading ability of primary-school-age hearing children who have been taught ASL <strong class=\"source-blank\">[33] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"68294","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34–40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 34–40 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>Dr. Daniels believes that parents should make up their own gestures to communicate with their babies.</p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"68295","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34–40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 34–40 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>American Sign Language is the most widely used sign language in the world.</p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"68296","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34–40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 34–40 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>For hearing children in America, learning American Sign Language is an equivalent option to learning a foreign language.</p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"68297","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34–40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 34–40 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>Brain research indicates that vocabulary is more easily learned than grammar.</p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"68298","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34–40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 34–40 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>First and second languages are stored on different sides of the brain.</p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"68299","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34–40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 34–40 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>Children have less difficulty learning to make signs than learning to make sounds.</p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"68300","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34–40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 34–40 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>According to Dr. Daniels, the view that deaf children must learn lip-reading before sign language is old-fashioned.</p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<div><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Sign, Baby, Sign!&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Language is a powerful tool that humans use for a wide variety of purposes—from expressing emotions and sharing ideas to passing down cultural values and acquiring knowledge. It is not limited to spoken words; gestures, facial expressions, and even posture all contribute to how we communicate. Language, whether signed or spoken, plays a vital role in how we engage with the world around us.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>In recent years, many American schools have begun to recognize American Sign Language (ASL) as a valid foreign language credit, just like Spanish or French. This change has opened the door for hearing students to choose ASL as an academic subject, which not only gives them a practical skill but also increases their awareness of and empathy toward the Deaf community. Some educators believe this early exposure may even influence students to pursue careers in special education, speech therapy, or interpreting.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>One clear benefit of learning ASL for hearing children is the opportunity for broader social interaction. Children who understand ASL can communicate with deaf peers, making their social circles more inclusive. Additionally, they may find it easier to express complex ideas or emotions non-verbally, which is helpful in noisy environments or when verbal speech isn’t possible.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Dr. Marilyn Daniels, a researcher and advocate for baby sign language, has spent over two decades studying the impact of signing on early communication. While she promotes the use of sign language with infants, she emphasizes that there is no need for parents to invent their own signs. Instead, she suggests that parents use ASL or another standardized system to ensure consistency and eventual recognition by others.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Very young children often develop motor skills before verbal skills. Dr. Daniels notes that even babies as young as six months can learn to use simple signs like “milk” or “more” with their hands, long before they can articulate those words. This early form of communication can reduce frustration—for both babies and their parents—and may even accelerate speech development.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Studies have shown that hearing children exposed to sign language from an early age tend to have stronger reading skills by the time they enter primary school. It is believed that learning sign language can strengthen understanding of symbolic representation and grammar, both of which are foundational to literacy. These cognitive advantages suggest that signing benefits not only communication but academic success as well.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>There remains some debate about the best approach to language instruction for deaf children. Some educators argue that speech and lip-reading should come first, while others advocate for immediate exposure to sign language. Dr. Daniels believes the latter is more effective and less frustrating for the child. She calls the idea that children must learn to lip-read before learning sign language “an outdated notion.” She, along with other advocates, stresses that deaf children have a right to a full, accessible language from birth—and that language is often sign.&nbsp;</p></div>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9567&scene=%E8%AF%AD%E8%A8%80%E6%95%99%E8%82%B2&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9568","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 The History of Tea","book":"阅读真题集 22","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test2","part":1,"description":"阅读真题集 22 · Test2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"9568:68301:1","type":"fill","text":"填写第 1 空","answer":"tombs","acceptedAnswers":["tombs"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Containers for tea have been found in tombs dating from the Han Dynasty (206 BC–220 AD)\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问研究人员认为在汉代的哪里检测到的茶容器是使用茶的最早证据。\n定位关键信息：用“tea containers”和“Han Dynasty”定位到A段末尾。\n解题思路：原文说在汉代的“tombs”中发现了茶容器，因此答案填tombs。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68301","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"9568:68301:2","type":"fill","text":"填写第 2 空","answer":"book","acceptedAnswers":["book"],"explanation":"原文答案句：a writer called Lu Yu wrote the first book entirely about tea\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问陆羽在八世纪写了一本关于茶的什么，关键词Lu Yu, wrote, eighth century。\n定位关键信息：用Lu Yu定位到B段第一句。\n解题思路：原文“wrote the first book”对应题目“wrote a book”，故答案book。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68301","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"9568:68301:3","type":"fill","text":"填写第 3 空","answer":"monks","acceptedAnswers":["monks"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It was shortly after this that tea was first introduced to Japan, by Japanese Buddhist monks who had travelled to China to study.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目询问是“什么人”从日本将茶带回其本国，关键词为“from Japan”、“brought tea to their native country”。\n定位关键信息：用Japan和brought tea定位到B段中关于茶首次被引入日本的描述。\n解题思路：原文指出茶是由“Japanese Buddhist monks”引入日本，直接对应题目中“from Japan who brought tea to their native country”，因此答案monks正确。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68301","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"9568:68301:4","type":"fill","text":"填写第 4 空","answer":"Dutch","acceptedAnswers":["Dutch"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This was done by the Dutch, who in the last years of the sixteenth century began to encroach on Portuguese trading routes in the East.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问谁将茶从中国运到欧洲，关键词为“carried from China to Europe”。\n定位关键信息：用“carried from China to Europe”定位到D段，原文提到“first consignment of tea was shipped from China to Holland”，且明确执行者是“the Dutch”。\n解题思路：原文指出“This was done by the Dutch”，其中“this”指代前文提到的将茶作为商业进口运回欧洲，与题干“Tea was carried from China to Europe”一致，故答案为Dutch。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68301","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"9568:68301:5","type":"fill","text":"填写第 5 空","answer":"smuggling","acceptedAnswers":["smuggling"],"explanation":"原文答案句：One unforeseen consequence of the taxation of tea was the growth of methods to avoid taxation—smuggling and adulteration.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问英国政府因何种严重犯罪而削减茶税，关键词为“cut the taxation”和“serious crime”。\n定位关键信息：通过“cut the taxation”定位到原文其他位置，但减税原因（严重犯罪）出现在G段，其中“smuggling”是避税方法。\n解题思路：G段指出茶税导致走私犯罪，原文其他位置说明政府因重税引发问题而减税，因此走私是促使减税的严重犯罪。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68301","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"9568:68301:6","type":"fill","text":"填写第 6 空","answer":"India","acceptedAnswers":["India"],"explanation":"原文答案句：India had always been the centre of the Company’s operations, which led to the increased cultivation of tea in India, beginning in Assam.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问19世纪除中国外，茶叶被种植在哪个地方。\n定位关键信息：用“planted”“besides China”和“19th century”定位到I段中关于茶叶在印度种植的描述。\n解题思路：原文指出公司促使茶叶在印度（India）开始大规模种植，与题干“Tea was planted in ____ besides China”对应，答案应为India。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68301","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"9568:68301:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"clippers","acceptedAnswers":["clippers"],"explanation":"原文答案句：using fast new clippers which had sleek lines, tall masts and huge sails.\n对应段落：K段\n审题：题干问为了在运输速度上竞争，商人用什么东西参与比赛。\n定位关键信息：用关键词“compete in shipping speed”和“race”定位到K段。\n解题思路：原文说“individual merchants...raced...using fast new clippers”，与题干“compete in shipping speed...used...for the race”对应，因此clippers为答案。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68301","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"9568:68302:8","type":"choice","text":"Tea was popular in Britain in the 16th century.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Britain, always a little suspicious of continental trends, had yet to become the nation of tea- drinkers that it is today.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目判断茶在16世纪的英国是否流行，关键词为“popular in Britain in the 16th century”。\n定位关键信息：题干中“16th century”和“Britain”对应E段首句“Britain”及后文1652年咖啡馆开业的情节，16世纪即1500-1599年间。\n解题思路：原文指出英国当时尚未成为饮茶国家，16世纪后期欧洲首次提及茶时，英国仍对大陆趋势持怀疑态度，且茶在1652年仍属新奇事物，说明16世纪茶在英国不流行，与题干信息矛盾，故答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68302","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"9568:68303:9","type":"choice","text":"Tea was more fashionable than coffee in Europe in the late 16th century.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In the latter half of the sixteenth century there are the first brief mentions of tea as a drink among Europeans, mostly from Portuguese who were living in the East as traders and missionaries.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：判断题：题干声称茶在16世纪末的欧洲比咖啡更时尚，要求判断对错。\n定位关键信息：用“late 16th century”和“Europe”定位至C段，但咖啡在原文中并未出现在同一时间或语境中。\n解题思路：原文C段仅提及16世纪下半叶茶在欧洲首次被提及，但未涉及咖啡的流行程度或与茶的比较，亦无信息证明茶比咖啡更时尚，故判断为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68303","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"9568:68304:10","type":"choice","text":"Tea was enjoyed by all classes in Britain in the 17th century.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：they were, though, the preserve of middle- and upper-class men; women drank tea in their own homes, and as yet tea was still too expensive to be widespread among the working classes.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题干问17世纪英国是否所有阶层都享用茶，关键词为“all classes”和“17th century”。\n定位关键信息：用“17th century”和“Britain”定位到F段，该段描述了各阶层饮茶情况。\n解题思路：原文明确表示茶是中上层男性的专属，女性在家喝，且因价格昂贵未普及至工人阶级，说明并非所有阶层都享用，与题干矛盾，故选FALSE；TRUE无依据；NOT GIVEN不成立，因原文已给出具体信息。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68304","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"9568:68305:11","type":"choice","text":"The adulteration of tea also prompted William Pitt the Younger to reduce the tax.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：By 1784, the government realised that enough was enough, and that heavy taxation was creating more problems than it was worth. The new Prime Minister, William Pitt the Younger, slashed the tax from 119 per cent to 12.5 per cent.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：判断茶叶掺假是否也促使William Pitt the Younger减税。\n定位关键信息：用“William Pitt the Younger”和“reduce the tax”定位至H段。\n解题思路：原文H段先说明重税导致掺假，后指出William Pitt the Younger大幅减税，因果关系成立，题干正确，选TRUE。FALSE与原文矛盾；NOT GIVEN原文已明确提及。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68305","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"9568:68306:12","type":"choice","text":"Initial problems occurred when tea was planted outside China by the East India Company.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：There were a few false starts, including the destruction by cattle of one of the earliest tea nurseries\n对应段落：I段\n审题：判断东印度公司在中国以外种植茶叶时是否出现了最初的问题。\n定位关键信息：用“planted outside China”和“East India Company”定位到I段关于结束垄断后考虑在中国以外种植以及出现错误开端的描述。\n解题思路：原文提到“a few false starts”对应“initial problems”，“destruction by cattle of one of the earliest tea nurseries”具体说明问题，题干表述与原文一致，故TRUE；其他选项无依据。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68306","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"9568:68307:13","type":"choice","text":"The fastest vessels were owned by America during the 19th-century clipper races.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In particular, there was competition between British and American merchants, leading to the famous clipper races of the 1860s.\n对应段落：K段\n审题：题干问19世纪快船比赛中最快的船是否由美国拥有。\n定位关键信息：用“fastest vessels”、“America”和“19th-century clipper races”定位至K段关于英美商人竞争的内容。\n解题思路：原文只提到英美商家竞争，但未比较或指明哪方拥有最快的船，故信息未给出（NOT GIVEN）；选项A无原文依据，选项B也无原文依据。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68307","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"68301","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Researchers believe the tea containers detected in <strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong> from the Han Dynasty were the first evidence of the use of tea.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Lu Yu wrote a <strong class=\"source-blank\">[2] ____</strong> about tea before anyone else in the eighth century.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">It was <strong class=\"source-blank\">[3] ____</strong> from Japan who brought tea to their native country from China.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Tea was carried from China to Europe by the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[4] ____</strong>.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">The British government had to cut the taxation on tea because of the serious crime of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[5] ____</strong>.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Tea was planted in <strong class=\"source-blank\">[6] ____</strong> besides China in the 19th century.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">In order to compete in shipping speed, traders used <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong> for the race.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><br/></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"68302","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>Tea was popular in Britain in the 16th century.</p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"68303","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>Tea was more fashionable than coffee in Europe in the late 16th century.</p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"68304","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>Tea was enjoyed by all classes in Britain in the 17th century.</p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"68305","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>The adulteration of tea also prompted William Pitt the Younger to reduce the tax.</p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"68306","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>Initial problems occurred when tea was planted outside China by the East India Company.</p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"68307","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>The fastest vessels were owned by America during the 19th-century clipper races.</p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<div><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The History of Tea&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>The story of tea begins in China. According to legend, in 2737 BC the Chinese emperor\nShen Nung was sitting beneath a tree while his servant boiled drinking water, when some\nleaves from the tree blew into the water. Shen Nung, a renowned herbalist, decided to try\nthe infusion that his servant had accidentally created. The tree was a Camellia sinensis,\nand the resulting drink was what we now call tea. It is impossible to know whether there is\nany truth in this story, but tea-drinking certainly became established in China many\ncenturies before it had even been heard of in the West. Containers for tea have been found\nin tombs dating from the Han Dynasty (206 BC–220 AD), but it was under the Tang\nDynasty (618–906 AD) that tea became firmly established as the national drink of China.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>It became such a favourite that during the late eighth century a writer called Lu Yu wrote the\nfirst book entirely about tea, the Ch’a Ching, or Tea Classic. It was shortly after this that tea\nwas first introduced to Japan, by Japanese Buddhist monks who had travelled to China to\nstudy. Tea received almost instant imperial sponsorship and spread rapidly from the royal\ncourt and monasteries to the other sections of Japanese society.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>So at this stage in the history of tea, Europe was rather lagging behind. In the latter half of\nthe sixteenth century there are the first brief mentions of tea as a drink among Europeans,\nmostly from Portuguese who were living in the East as traders and missionaries. But\nalthough some of these individuals may have brought back samples of tea to their native\ncountry, it was not the Portuguese who were the first to ship back tea as a commercial\nimport.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>This was done by the Dutch, who in the last years of the sixteenth century began to\nencroach on Portuguese trading routes in the East. By the turn of the century they had\nestablished a trading post on the island of Java, and it was via Java that in 1606 the first\nconsignment of tea was shipped from China to Holland. Tea soon became a fashionable\ndrink among the Dutch, and from there spread to other countries in continental western\nEurope, but because of its high price it remained a drink for the wealthy.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Britain, always a little suspicious of continental trends, had yet to become the nation of tea-\ndrinkers that it is today. Starting in 1600, the British East India Company had a monopoly\non importing goods from outside Europe, and it is likely that sailors on these ships brought\ntea home as gifts. The first coffee-house had been established in London in 1652, and tea\nwas still somewhat unfamiliar to most readers, so it is fair to assume that the drink was still\nsomething of a curiosity.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Gradually, it became a popular drink in coffee-houses, which were as much locations for\nthe transaction of business as they were for relaxation or pleasure. They were, though, the\npreserve of middle- and upper-class men; women drank tea in their own homes, and as yet\ntea was still too expensive to be widespread among the working classes. In part, its high\nprice was due to a punitive system of taxation.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>One unforeseen consequence of the taxation of tea was the growth of methods to avoid\ntaxation—smuggling and adulteration. By the eighteenth century many Britons wanted to\ndrink tea but could not afford the high prices, and their enthusiasm for the drink was\nmatched by the enthusiasm of criminal gangs to smuggle it in. What began as a small-time\nillegal trade, selling a few pounds of tea to personal contacts, developed by the late\neighteenth century into an astonishing organised-crime network, perhaps importing as\nmuch as seven million lb annually, compared to a legal import of five million lb!&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Worse for the drinkers was that taxation also encouraged the adulteration of tea,\nparticularly of smuggled tea which was not quality-controlled through customs and excise. Leaves from other plants, or leaves which had already been brewed and then dried, were\nadded to tea leaves. By 1784, the government realised that enough was enough, and that\nheavy taxation was creating more problems than it was worth. The new Prime Minister,\nWilliam Pitt the Younger, slashed the tax from 119 per cent to 12.5 per cent. Suddenly legal\ntea was affordable, and smuggling stopped virtually overnight.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Another great impetus to tea-drinking resulted from the end of the East India Company’s\nmonopoly on trade with China, in 1834. Before that date, China was the country of origin of\nthe vast majority of the tea imported to Britain, but the end of its monopoly stimulated the\nEast India Company to consider growing tea outside China. India had always been the\ncentre of the Company’s operations, which led to the increased cultivation of tea in India,\nbeginning in Assam. There were a few false starts, including the destruction by cattle of one\nof the earliest tea nurseries, but by 1888 British tea imports from India were for the first time\ngreater than those from China.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The end of the East India Company’s monopoly on trade with China also had another\nresult, which was more dramatic though less important in the long term: it ushered in the\nera of the tea clippers. While the Company had had the monopoly on trade, there was no\nrush to bring the tea from China to Britain, but after 1834 the tea trade became a virtual\nfree-for-all.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Individual merchants and sea-captains with their own ships raced to bring home the tea and\nmake the most money, using fast new clippers which had sleek lines, tall masts and huge\nsails. In particular, there was competition between British and American merchants, leading\nto the famous clipper races of the 1860s. But these races soon came to an end with the\nopening of the Suez Canal, which made the trade routes to China viable for steamships for\nthe first time.&nbsp;</p></div>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9568&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9569","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Speaking of Nothing","book":"阅读真题集 22","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test2","part":2,"description":"阅读真题集 22 · Test2 · 16 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"9569:68308:14","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：However, these three types of work stand out for another reason: they’re characterised by a lack of conversation or by meaningless small talk, which unfortunately represents an obligatory part of the job.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：为A段选择小标题\n定位关键信息：通过“occupations involve little or no interesting conversation”定位至A段中列举的security guards, truck drivers和salespeople\n解题思路：A段指出这些职业缺乏对话或只有无意义闲聊，与选项G“一些职业很少或没有有趣的对话”含义一致","options":["How sounds and physical contact strengthen social connections","A cross-cultural study of superficial interaction","An experiment that led to surprising results","A study that categorised types of spoken exchanges","The personality types that find small talk more difficult","The effect of social media on conversation skills","Some occupations involve little or no interesting conversation","A campaign to improve interaction in the workplace","A range of common situations that were enhanced by small talk"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"68308","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–19\nReading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, A–F.\nChoose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.\nWrite the correct number, i–ix, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"9569:68308:15","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In the study, the researchers eavesdropped on undergraduates for four days, then catalogued each overheard conversation as either ‘small talk’ (“What do you have there? Popcorn? That looks good!”) or ‘substantive’ (“So did their proposal get funding?” “How did you feel?”).\n对应段落：B段\n审题：为B段选择小标题，关键词为B段内容和“categorised types of spoken exchanges”。\n定位关键信息：B段首句“investigate the types of conversations people have”及后文对对话的分类描述。\n解题思路：B段描述了Mehl和Vazire的研究，他们记录并分类对话为“small talk”和“substantive”，即对口头交流进行了类型划分，与选项D“A study that categorised types of spoken exchanges”对应。","options":["How sounds and physical contact strengthen social connections","A cross-cultural study of superficial interaction","An experiment that led to surprising results","A study that categorised types of spoken exchanges","The personality types that find small talk more difficult","The effect of social media on conversation skills","Some occupations involve little or no interesting conversation","A campaign to improve interaction in the workplace","A range of common situations that were enhanced by small talk"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"68308","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–19\nReading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, A–F.\nChoose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.\nWrite the correct number, i–ix, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"9569:68308:16","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The researchers reported that the animals reserve their call-and-response conversations, equivalent to human chitchat, for the animals they groom the most—suggesting that small talk maintains closeness with loved ones, and isn’t merely for awkward exchanges with strangers. It appears that, even among animals, vocal exchanges indicate strong social bonds between the group members.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：为C段选择小标题\n定位关键信息：C段提及科学家研究动物声音交流与梳理行为，验证small talk促进联结。\n解题思路：小标题A强调声音和身体接触（grooming）加强社会联系，原文描述狐猴对亲密伙伴发出叫声和梳理，表明声音交流和肢体接触强化社会纽带，与标题吻合。","options":["How sounds and physical contact strengthen social connections","A cross-cultural study of superficial interaction","An experiment that led to surprising results","A study that categorised types of spoken exchanges","The personality types that find small talk more difficult","The effect of social media on conversation skills","Some occupations involve little or no interesting conversation","A campaign to improve interaction in the workplace","A range of common situations that were enhanced by small talk"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"68308","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–19\nReading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, A–F.\nChoose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.\nWrite the correct number, i–ix, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"9569:68308:17","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Participants had predicted precisely the opposite outcome.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：为D段选择小标题\n定位关键信息：D段中Epley和Schroeder的实验描述了参与者预测与结果相反\n解题思路：D段通过实验表明参与者预测陌生人会排斥交流的实际结果是积极反应，这种预测错误对应“surprising results”","options":["How sounds and physical contact strengthen social connections","A cross-cultural study of superficial interaction","An experiment that led to surprising results","A study that categorised types of spoken exchanges","The personality types that find small talk more difficult","The effect of social media on conversation skills","Some occupations involve little or no interesting conversation","A campaign to improve interaction in the workplace","A range of common situations that were enhanced by small talk"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"68308","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–19\nReading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, A–F.\nChoose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.\nWrite the correct number, i–ix, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"9569:68308:18","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In a study by Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn, people who had a social interaction with a server in a coffee shop felt better emotionally than people who were in a rush to get everything done.；In similar studies, when volunteers broke the silence at a gallery to chat with other visitors, the visitors felt happier and more connected to the paintings than those who were not approached.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：为E段选择小标题\n定位关键信息：E段多次提到“coffee shop”“gallery”“chat with service staff”“break the silence”等具体场景，并指出这类社交互动提升了幸福感。\n解题思路：原文描述了咖啡店、画廊等日常环境，主动进行小谈后人们的情绪和归属感增强，恰好对应选项I“一系列因小谈而改善的常见情境”。","options":["How sounds and physical contact strengthen social connections","A cross-cultural study of superficial interaction","An experiment that led to surprising results","A study that categorised types of spoken exchanges","The personality types that find small talk more difficult","The effect of social media on conversation skills","Some occupations involve little or no interesting conversation","A campaign to improve interaction in the workplace","A range of common situations that were enhanced by small talk"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"68308","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–19\nReading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, A–F.\nChoose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.\nWrite the correct number, i–ix, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"9569:68308:19","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph F","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Of course, some of us are better than others at small talk.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：为F段选择小标题\n定位关键信息：根据段落编号F段定位到阅读材料最后一段，段首句即点明不同人善于闲聊的程度不同。\n解题思路：原文第一句指出有些人比其他人更擅长闲聊，接着通过研究说明“好奇心较低的人”和“内向的人”更难开展闲聊，与选项E“发现闲聊更困难的人格类型”完全对应。","options":["How sounds and physical contact strengthen social connections","A cross-cultural study of superficial interaction","An experiment that led to surprising results","A study that categorised types of spoken exchanges","The personality types that find small talk more difficult","The effect of social media on conversation skills","Some occupations involve little or no interesting conversation","A campaign to improve interaction in the workplace","A range of common situations that were enhanced by small talk"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"68308","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–19\nReading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, A–F.\nChoose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.\nWrite the correct number, i–ix, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"9569:68309:20","type":"choice","text":"Interacting socially is preferable to hurrying through a transaction.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In a study by Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn, people who had a social interaction with a server in a coffee shop felt better emotionally than people who were in a rush to get everything done.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题干问社交互动是否比匆忙完成交易更可取，关键词socially interacting和hurrying through a transaction。\n定位关键信息：用研究者Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn快速定位到E段。\n解题思路：原文表明与服务员社交互动的人比匆忙完成事务的人情绪更好，直接支持题干观点，因此匹配D。","options":["Matthias R. Mehl and Simine Vazire","Ipek Kulahci","Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder","Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn","Todd Kashdan"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"68309","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20–25\nLook at the following statements (Questions 20–25) and the list of people below.\nMatch each statement with the correct person, A–E.\nWrite the correct letter, A–E, in boxes 20–25 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of Researchers\nA Matthias R. Mehl and Simine Vazire\nB Ipek Kulahci\nC Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder\nD Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn\nE Todd Kashdan"},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"9569:68309:21","type":"choice","text":"If someone is truly uninterested in the wider world, they’ll find small talk more difficult.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：people who were rated by the researchers as ‘less curious’ about all aspects of life had trouble getting a conversation going on their own.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问如果一个人对广阔世界真正不感兴趣，他们会发现闲聊更困难，关键词为“uninterested in wider world”和“small talk more difficult”。\n定位关键信息：题干中“uninterested in the wider world”对应原文“less curious about all aspects of life”；“small talk more difficult”对应“had trouble getting a conversation going”。\n解题思路：原文F段指出，被评定为好奇心较低（对生活各方面不感兴趣）的人难以独自开启对话，这与题干表述一致，因此对应研究者Todd Kashdan（E）。","options":["Matthias R. Mehl and Simine Vazire","Ipek Kulahci","Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder","Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn","Todd Kashdan"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"68309","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20–25\nLook at the following statements (Questions 20–25) and the list of people below.\nMatch each statement with the correct person, A–E.\nWrite the correct letter, A–E, in boxes 20–25 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of Researchers\nA Matthias R. Mehl and Simine Vazire\nB Ipek Kulahci\nC Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder\nD Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn\nE Todd Kashdan"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"9569:68309:22","type":"choice","text":"People who had been unwilling to start a conversation ended up enjoying a social exchange.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Those told to chat with others reported a more pleasant journey than those told to \"enjoy your solitude\" or do whatever they normally would.；Participants had predicted precisely the opposite outcome.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题干问谁的研究表明原本不愿意开始对话的人最终享受了社交交流，关键词是“unwilling to start a conversation”和“enjoying a social exchange”。\n定位关键信息：根据人名Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder（正确答案C）定位到D段。\n解题思路：原文中志愿者们原本预期聊天会被冷遇（unwilling），但实际聊天后报告了更愉快的旅程（enjoying a social exchange），与题干完全对应。","options":["Matthias R. Mehl and Simine Vazire","Ipek Kulahci","Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder","Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn","Todd Kashdan"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"68309","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20–25\nLook at the following statements (Questions 20–25) and the list of people below.\nMatch each statement with the correct person, A–E.\nWrite the correct letter, A–E, in boxes 20–25 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of Researchers\nA Matthias R. Mehl and Simine Vazire\nB Ipek Kulahci\nC Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder\nD Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn\nE Todd Kashdan"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"9569:68309:23","type":"choice","text":"People whose conversations are mainly of a personal and meaningful nature are more satisfied with their lives.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：They found that people who had more substantive conversations were more likely to say they were feeling happy and fulfilled overall.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问哪类人认为对话以个人和有意义性质为主的人对生活更满意，关键词是“personal and meaningful nature”和“more satisfied lives”。\n定位关键信息：用题干中“personal and meaningful nature”对应到B段“substantive conversations”，用“more satisfied with their lives”对应到“happy and fulfilled overall”，定位到Mehl和Vazire的研究。\n解题思路：B段中Mehl和Vazire的结论直接说明进行更多实质性对话的人更幸福满足，与题干完全吻合，因此答案为A。","options":["Matthias R. Mehl and Simine Vazire","Ipek Kulahci","Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder","Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn","Todd Kashdan"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"68309","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20–25\nLook at the following statements (Questions 20–25) and the list of people below.\nMatch each statement with the correct person, A–E.\nWrite the correct letter, A–E, in boxes 20–25 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of Researchers\nA Matthias R. Mehl and Simine Vazire\nB Ipek Kulahci\nC Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder\nD Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn\nE Todd Kashdan"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"9569:68309:24","type":"choice","text":"There is more than one species whose members communicate for social reasons.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The researchers reported that the animals reserve their call-and- response conversations, equivalent to human chitchat, for the animals they groom the most—suggesting that small talk maintains closeness with loved ones, and isn’t merely for awkward exchanges with strangers. It appears that, even among animals, vocal exchanges indicate strong social bonds between the group members.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问是否存在不止一种物种的成员为了社交原因而交流，关键词为“more than one species”和“communicate for social reasons”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中“more than one species”和“communicate for social reasons”，在C段找到Ipek Kulahci研究lemurs的vocal exchanges与grooming的关联，表明动物也进行社交交流。\n解题思路：C段中Ipek Kulahci的研究表明lemurs使用类似人类闲聊的叫声来维持亲密关系，说明动物（非人类）也为了社交原因交流，因此与题干匹配。","options":["Matthias R. Mehl and Simine Vazire","Ipek Kulahci","Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder","Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn","Todd Kashdan"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"68309","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20–25\nLook at the following statements (Questions 20–25) and the list of people below.\nMatch each statement with the correct person, A–E.\nWrite the correct letter, A–E, in boxes 20–25 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of Researchers\nA Matthias R. Mehl and Simine Vazire\nB Ipek Kulahci\nC Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder\nD Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn\nE Todd Kashdan"},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"9569:68309:25","type":"choice","text":"Some people find it easier than others to change the subject of a conversation.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But people who were deemed ‘curious’ needed no help transforming conversations about ordinary things like favourite holidays into other areas of conversation that allowed for intimate exchanges.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问是否有些人比其他人更容易改变对话主题，关键词为“change the subject of a conversation”。\n定位关键信息：用题干中的“change the subject”对应原文“transforming conversations... into other areas of conversation”，并发现Todd Kashdan在F段。\n解题思路：F段中，Todd Kashdan的研究指出好奇的人无需帮助即可将话题转向其他领域，即更容易改变话题，与题干一致。","options":["Matthias R. Mehl and Simine Vazire","Ipek Kulahci","Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder","Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn","Todd Kashdan"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"68309","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20–25\nLook at the following statements (Questions 20–25) and the list of people below.\nMatch each statement with the correct person, A–E.\nWrite the correct letter, A–E, in boxes 20–25 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of Researchers\nA Matthias R. Mehl and Simine Vazire\nB Ipek Kulahci\nC Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder\nD Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn\nE Todd Kashdan"},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"9569:68310:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"obligatory","acceptedAnswers":["obligatory"],"explanation":"原文答案句：they're characterised by a lack of conversation or by meaningless small talk, which unfortunately represents an obligatory part of the job.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问销售人员与顾客打交道时，无意义闲聊是什么，关键词salespeople、meaningless small talk、dealing with customers。\n定位关键信息：用salespeople定位到A段，找到描述其工作特点的句子。\n解题思路：原文指出销售人员的无意义闲聊是工作的obligatory（强制的）部分，因此答案obligatory。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68310","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 26–29\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 26–29 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"9569:68310:27","type":"fill","text":"填写第 27 空","answer":"commuters","acceptedAnswers":["commuters"],"explanation":"原文答案句：whether to talk with other commuters who usually took the same train to work every day—something they typically avoided.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问在火车上进行的研究中，志愿者接近的是经常怎样的人，需填入一个名词。\n定位关键信息：根据题干关键词“on a train”和“volunteers approached”定位到D段，找到“talk with other commuters”。\n解题思路：原文中志愿者被指示与经常乘坐同一火车的其他通勤者交谈，与题干“regular commuters”对应，因此答案为commuters。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68310","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 26–29\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 26–29 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"9569:68310:28","type":"fill","text":"填写第 28 空","answer":"paintings","acceptedAnswers":["paintings"],"explanation":"原文答案句：when volunteers broke the silence at a gallery to chat with other visitors, the visitors felt happier and more connected to the paintings than those who were not approached.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：填空处需填写美术馆实验中人们被引入对话后与之有更多联系的物体。\n定位关键信息：用“experiment in an art gallery”“drawn into a conversation”定位至E段。\n解题思路：原文“more connected to the paintings”对应题干“related more to the ____”，故答案paintings。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68310","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 26–29\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 26–29 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"9569:68310:29","type":"fill","text":"填写第 29 空","answer":"topics","acceptedAnswers":["topics"],"explanation":"原文答案句：they had greater luck building closeness with others when they were supplied with topics that encouraged people to open up about themselves and their lives.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问内向的人发现被给予什么来开始对话是有帮助的，关键词是Introverted people和start conversations。\n定位关键信息：由Introverted people和start conversations定位到F段，该段讨论不同性格的人对闲聊的反应，并提到被提供话题（topics）有助于建立亲密关系。\n解题思路：原文中“supplied with topics”与题干“be given ____ which they could use to start conversations”对应，topic意为“话题”，因此答案是topics。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68310","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 26–29\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 26–29 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"68308","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–19\nReading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, A–F.\nChoose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.\nWrite the correct number, i–ix, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"68309","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20–25\nLook at the following statements (Questions 20–25) and the list of people below.\nMatch each statement with the correct person, A–E.\nWrite the correct letter, A–E, in boxes 20–25 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of Researchers\nA Matthias R. Mehl and Simine Vazire\nB Ipek Kulahci\nC Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder\nD Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn\nE Todd Kashdan","html":"<p>Interacting socially is preferable to hurrying through a transaction. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong></p><p>If someone is truly uninterested in the wider world, they’ll find small talk more difficult. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong></p><p>People who had been unwilling to start a conversation ended up enjoying a social exchange. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong></p><p>People whose conversations are mainly of a personal and meaningful nature are more satisfied with their lives. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong></p><p>There is more than one species whose members communicate for social reasons. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong></p><p>Some people find it easier than others to change the subject of a conversation. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"68310","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 26–29\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 26–29 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the case of salespeople, some meaningless small talk is <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong> when dealing with customers. In a study that took place on a train, volunteers approached people who were regular <strong class=\"source-blank\">[27] ____</strong>. In an experiment in an art gallery, people related more to the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[28] ____</strong> when they were drawn into a conversation. Introverted people found it helpful to be given <strong class=\"source-blank\">[29] ____</strong> which they could use to start conversations.</p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<div><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Speaking of Nothing&nbsp;</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\" dir=\"ltr\"><em>Why we talk about the weather and other trivial topics</em></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>#&amp;Some workers are happier in their jobs than others, but it’s not only to do with the work itself. For example, security guards, truck drivers and salespeople—year after year, these jobs appear on lists of the unhappiest careers. It’s true that many factors can make a job cheerless, including unusual hours, low pay and a lack of chances for advancement. However, these three types of work stand out for another reason: they’re characterised by a lack of conversation or by meaningless small talk, which unfortunately represents an obligatory part of the job. Examples of such small talk include comments about the weather, holiday destinations and food. Psychologists have long said that connecting with others through meaningful exchanges is central to well-being, but just how much conversation we require is under investigation.&nbsp;&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>#&amp;Matthias R. Mehl and Simine Vazire of the University of Arizona in the United States wanted to investigate the types of conversations people have. The team used a device to periodically record short verbal exchanges while participants went about their daily tasks. In the study, the researchers eavesdropped on undergraduates for four days, then catalogued each overheard conversation as either ‘small talk’ (“What do you have there? Popcorn? That looks good!”) or ‘substantive’ (“So did their proposal get funding?” “How did you feel?”). They found that people who had more substantive conversations were more likely to say they were feeling happy and fulfilled overall. In fact, the happiest students had roughly twice as many substantive talks as the unhappiest ones. Small talk, meanwhile, made up only 10 per cent of their conversation, versus almost 30 per cent of conversation among the least content students.&nbsp;&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>#&amp;However, small talk still has a role to play. Rather than convey information, scientists believe that it can promote bonding. Ipek Kulahci and her team of researchers at University College Cork in Ireland tested the relationship between vocal exchanges and grooming in lemurs. The researchers reported that the animals reserve their call-and- response conversations, equivalent to human chitchat, for the animals they groom the most—suggesting that small talk maintains closeness with loved ones, and isn’t merely for awkward exchanges with strangers. It appears that, even among animals, vocal exchanges indicate strong social bonds between the group members.&nbsp;&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>#&amp;Connecting with others seems to increase happiness, but strangers in close proximity routinely ignore each other. To examine the experience of connecting to strangers, psychologists Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder from the University of Chicago in the United States gave volunteers varying directions about whether to talk with other commuters who usually took the same train to work every day—something they typically avoided. Those told to chat with others reported a more pleasant journey than those told to “enjoy your solitude” or do whatever they normally would. All of the volunteers in the study who initiated conversations reported a positive reaction from the people they spoke to. Participants had predicted precisely the opposite outcome. They expected that the others on the train would have preferred to be left alone.&nbsp;&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>#&amp;When we buy a cup of coffee at a café, we sometimes chat with the service staff, but on other occasions we say as little as possible so as not to waste time. Every day we have opportunities to transform potentially impersonal exchanges into genuine social interactions; in other words, treating a service provider like we would an acquaintance might make us happier. In a study by Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn, people who had a social interaction with a server in a coffee shop felt better emotionally than people who were in a rush to get everything done. As well as feeling happier, the first group had a stronger sense of belonging. These results suggest that, although people are often reluctant to have a genuine social interaction with a stranger, they are happier when they do. In similar studies, when volunteers broke the silence at a gallery to chat with other visitors, the visitors felt happier and more connected to the paintings than those who were not approached. The pleasure of connection seems contagious; in a laboratory waiting room, participants who were talked to had equally positive experiences as those instructed to talk to them.&nbsp;&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>#&amp;Of course, some of us are better than others at small talk. In a study by Todd Kashdan and his team from George Mason University in the United States, people who were rated by the researchers as ‘less curious’ about all aspects of life had trouble getting a conversation going on their own. However, they had greater luck building closeness with others when they were supplied with topics that encouraged people to open up about themselves and their lives. But people who were deemed ‘curious’ needed no help transforming conversations about ordinary things like favourite holidays into other areas of conversation that allowed for intimate exchanges. The study showed that curious people expect to generate closeness during intimate conversations but not during small talk; less curious people anticipated poor outcomes in both situations. In an experiment by William Fleeson at Wake Forest University in the United States, participants were divided into two groups—those who were naturally outgoing, and those who were more reserved in social situations. They were then instructed to behave in the opposite manner to their usual nature. Participants reported more positive feelings when instructed to act extroverted than when instructed to act introverted. The overall conclusion, therefore, is that everyone can benefit from more conversation; the more meaningful, the better.&nbsp;&amp;#</p></div>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9569&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9570","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 The Animal Connection","book":"阅读真题集 22","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test2","part":3,"description":"阅读真题集 22 · Test2 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"9570:68311:27","type":"choice","text":"Travellers are more likely to notice wild animals than domesticated ones.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Travel anywhere and you see something so common it may not even catch your attention. Wherever there are people, animals are being walked, herded and fed. Many, such as dogs, cats and sheep, are domesticated, but you will also find people living alongside wild creatures like monkeys and wolves.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题干询问旅行者是否更容易注意到野生动物而非家养动物，关键词为“travellers”、“notice”、“wild animals”、“domesticated ones”。\n定位关键信息：题干中的“travellers”对应原文“Travel anywhere”，“wild animals”和“domesticated”对应原文“wild creatures”和“domesticated”。\n解题思路：原文仅描述旅行时常见家养和野生两类动物，并未比较旅行者注意到哪一类更容易或可能性更高，因此作者未表达该观点，选NOT GIVEN；YES与NO均缺乏原文依据。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68311","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"9570:68312:28","type":"choice","text":"All cultures demonstrate a need to have close contact with animals.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Close contact with animals is not confined to one particular culture, region or ethnic group but is a universal human trait.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问是否所有文化都表现出需要与动物密切接触，关键词为“all cultures”和“close contact with animals”。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“all cultures”和“close contact”定位至A段末句，其中“universal human trait”对应所有文化。\n解题思路：原文明确指出密切接触动物不限于某一文化或地区，而是普遍人类特征，与题干一致，故YES。NO与原文“universal”矛盾；NOT GIVEN因为原文直接有明确陈述，并非未提及。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68312","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"9570:68313:29","type":"choice","text":"Animals benefit from allowing other animal species to share food resources.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Since the ultimate prize in evolution is perpetuating your genes, providing food for another species is counterproductive to success.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问动物是否从允许其他动物物种分享食物资源中受益。\n定位关键信息：通过“share food resources”对应原文的“providing food for another species”，定位到B段。\n解题思路：原文指出提供食物给其他物种对进化成功是反作用的，即动物不会受益，因此答案为NO；YES与原文相悖；NOT GIVEN在原文有明确信息。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68313","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"9570:68314:30","type":"choice","text":"It is unlikely that people initially domesticated wolves for future companionship.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Who would bring a ferocious wolf into their home in the hope that thousands of years later it would become a loving pet?\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题干判断“人们最初驯化狼不是为了未来的陪伴”这一说法是否正确，关键词为initially domesticated wolves和future companionship。\n定位关键信息：根据题干关键词domesticated wolves和companionship，定位到B段关于将狼带回家希望成为宠物的反问句。\n解题思路：原文反问谁会为未来陪伴而驯化凶猛的狼，暗示最初动机非此，与题干“unlikely”一致，故YES正确；NO与原文相悖；NOT GIVEN无据。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68314","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"9570:68315:31","type":"choice","text":"There are periods of human evolution for which we have little information about man’s relationship with animals.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：What I found was a long and unbroken evolutionary trail of evidence I call the ‘animal connection’. This trail links to three important developments in human evolution: tool making, language and domestication.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题干问是否存在一些人类进化时期我们对人与动物的关系知之甚少。\n定位关键信息：用“periods of human evolution”和“relationship with animals”定位到C段关于动物联系的进化证据。\n解题思路：原文C段明确指出有一条“long and unbroken evolutionary trail of evidence”即动物连接，说明对人与动物关系有充分证据，故题干说“little information”错误，选NO；YES与原文矛盾；NOT GIVEN不成立，因为原文直接给出相反信息。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68315","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"9570:68316:32","type":"choice","text":"Hunting and the animal connection Around 2.6 million years ago, humans became predators after they realized the possibility of object ____.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This development required the intellectual breakthrough of realizing that the properties of an object can be altered.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问大约260万年前，人类在认识到物体具有什么可能性后成为捕食者，关键词为“2.6 million years ago”“humans became predators”“possibility of object”。\n定位关键信息：根据“2.6 million years ago”及“object”定位到D段，该段提到“realizing that the properties of an object can be altered”。\n解题思路：原文指出人类认识到物体属性可被改变（altered），这与选项D“adaptation”（改造、适应）语义对应，因此答案为D。","options":["nutrition","competition","leadership","adaptation","territory","trade","connection","observation","behavior","worship"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"68316","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32–36\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A–J, below.\nWrite the correct letter, A–J, in boxes 32–36 on your answer sheet."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"9570:68316:33","type":"choice","text":"Once humans were hunters, they benefited from better ____ and extra time which could be spent on non-physical activities.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：eating more meat and fat was a requirement for the increase in relative brain size. And since meat tends to come in bigger packages than leaves and roots, meat eaters could spend less time finding food and more on activities like learning and social interaction.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题干问人类成为猎人后，受益于更好的什么以及可以用于非体力活动的额外时间，关键词为“better”和“extra time”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中“benefited from better”和“extra time”定位到E段关于狩猎生活方式好处的描述。\n解题思路：题干中的“better”对应原文“eating more meat and fat”提供的营养改善，即选项A nutrition，且原文提到“spend less time finding food and more on...social interaction”对应“extra time which could be spent on non-physical activities”。","options":["nutrition","competition","leadership","adaptation","territory","trade","connection","observation","behavior","worship"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"68316","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32–36\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A–J, below.\nWrite the correct letter, A–J, in boxes 32–36 on your answer sheet."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"9570:68316:34","type":"choice","text":"However, the more humans came to depend on meat as a food source, the more ____ there was between them and other predators.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：preying on animals put our ancestors into direct competition with the other predators that shared their ecosystem, animals such as lions and hyenas.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问人类越依赖肉类作为食物来源，他们与其他捕食者之间越多什么；关键词为“depend on meat”和“other predators”。\n定位关键信息：根据“depend on meat”和“other predators”定位到E段中“preying on animals”和“direct competition with the other predators”。\n解题思路：原文说明捕食动物使人类祖先与其他捕食者产生直接竞争，与题干中“越依赖肉类，越多竞争”语义一致，故空格填competition。","options":["nutrition","competition","leadership","adaptation","territory","trade","connection","observation","behavior","worship"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"68316","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32–36\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A–J, below.\nWrite the correct letter, A–J, in boxes 32–36 on your answer sheet."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"9570:68316:35","type":"choice","text":"Humans need to find an advantage over animals such as lions and tigers.It wasn’t a spear or knife that gave them this advantage, but the ____ skills that humans began to develop.","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：What made it possible for our ancestors to compete successfully with true carnivores was the ability to pay very close attention to the habits of both potential prey and competitors.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问人类需要找到相对于狮子和鬣狗的优势，不是矛或刀，而是开始发展的什么技能。\n定位关键信息：用lions and hyenas定位到E段，同时关注“advantage over”和“spear or knife”的同义表述。\n解题思路：原文指出人类成功竞争靠的是“pay very close attention”，即观察能力（observation），与选项H对应。","options":["nutrition","competition","leadership","adaptation","territory","trade","connection","observation","behavior","worship"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"68316","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32–36\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A–J, below.\nWrite the correct letter, A–J, in boxes 32–36 on your answer sheet."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"9570:68316:36","type":"choice","text":"Then, because humans were such successful predators, they required more ____ and this led to groups of people moving away from Africa.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Early man lived in Africa and nowhere else, but then underwent a dramatic expansion in territory, forced by the search for new hunting grounds.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：问人类因成为成功捕食者而需要更多什么，导致离开非洲；关键词successful predators、required more、moving away from Africa。\n定位关键信息：用moving away from Africa和successful predators定位到E段末句，其中expansion in territory对应所需之物。\n解题思路：原文指出成功捕食者需要更低密度（即更多领地），被迫寻找新猎场导致领地扩张，与题干“required more territory”直接对应。","options":["nutrition","competition","leadership","adaptation","territory","trade","connection","observation","behavior","worship"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"68316","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32–36\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A–J, below.\nWrite the correct letter, A–J, in boxes 32–36 on your answer sheet."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"9570:68317:37","type":"choice","text":"What is the writer’s main argument in the sixth paragraph?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Through the art, we realize the main topic was animals: their colours, shapes, postures and habits. This focus is even more striking considering that scenes of human life are rarely depicted.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题干问第六段中作者的主要论点是什么。\n定位关键信息：题干中的“the sixth paragraph”直接定位到F段全文。\n解题思路：正确选项B对应原文中史前艺术以动物为主题，说明早期人类重视动物行为和外观的知识交流。A选项“史前艺术允许我们确定人类迁徙模式的时间”原文未提及；C选项“不同地区早期人类生活方式差异大”原文未提及；D选项“不同群体之间很少有口头互动”在F段未讨论，且第六段未出现相关表述，因此排除。","options":["Prehistoric art allows us to date human migration patterns.","Early man valued the communication of knowledge about animal behaviour and appearance.","There is evidence of big lifestyle differences between early humans in different regions.","There was little spoken interaction between different groups of people."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68317","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37–40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"9570:68318:38","type":"choice","text":"What is the writer doing in the seventh paragraph?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：I believe I am the first to propose a continuity between the strong human-animal link that appeared 2.6 million years ago and the origin of language.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问作者在第七段（G段）做什么，即该段落的主要目的或作者的行为。\n定位关键信息：题干明确提到“the seventh paragraph”，直接对应阅读材料中的G段。\n解题思路：正确答案D（making a claim about the way that language developed）对应G段中作者提出自己关于语言起源与动物联系连续性的主张。A错在文中未拒绝已有理论，而是提出新观点；B错在艺术价值在原文其他位置，G段未强调；C错在作者未怀疑交流的初始目的，而是论述语言如何发展。","options":["rejecting an established theory about human evolution.","emphasizing the value of art in language development.","expressing doubt about the initial purpose of communication.","making a claim about the way that language developed."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68318","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37–40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"9570:68319:39","type":"choice","text":"The writer refers to vervet monkeys in order to:","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Vervet monkeys, for example, have different cries for eagles and snakes, but they cannot discuss what threats might appear tomorrow. The property of full language is that it is comprised of vocabulary and grammatical rules that can be combined in an infinite number of ways to convey fine shades of meaning.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题干问作者提及vervet monkeys的目的，关键词是vervet monkeys。\n定位关键信息：通过专有名词Vervet monkeys定位到G段。\n解题思路：正确答案C基于原文，vervet monkeys只能发出不同叫声而无法讨论未来威胁，对比凸显人类语言可无限组合表达精细含义的复杂性；A原文未说明哪些动物有基本语言；B原文未提及危险是交流动机；D原文未涉及对早期人类互动方式的影响。","options":["indicate which animal species have a kind of basic language.","show how danger is a significant motivation for human communication.","highlight the sophistication of human communication.","suggest a possible influence on the way early humans interacted."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68319","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37–40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"9570:68320:40","type":"choice","text":"The writer says that the ‘walking larder’ idea","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Looking at the origins of domestication for clues to its underlying reasons, I found fundamental flaws in this idea.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问作者对“walking larder”这一观点的看法。\n定位关键信息：用题干关键词“walking larder”定位到H段该短语所在句。\n解题思路：原文指出该观点有“fundamental flaws”，即它无法解释驯化的真正目的，因此选项A正确；B项“仅对驯化动物成立”原文未提及；C项“支持作者观点”与作者反对该观点矛盾；D项“基于作者进行的调研”原文未说明。","options":["fails to explain the purpose of domestication.","is true only for domesticated animals.","supports the idea the writer proposes.","is based on research the writer has carried out."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68320","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37–40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"68311","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p>Travellers are more likely to notice wild animals than domesticated ones.</p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"68312","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p>All cultures demonstrate a need to have close contact with animals.</p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"68313","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p>Animals benefit from allowing other animal species to share food resources.</p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"68314","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p>It is unlikely that people initially domesticated wolves for future companionship.</p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"68315","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p>There are periods of human evolution for which we have little information about man’s relationship with animals.</p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"68316","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32–36\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A–J, below.\nWrite the correct letter, A–J, in boxes 32–36 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Hunting and the animal connection</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Around 2.6 million years ago, humans became predators after they realized the possibility of object <strong class=\"source-blank\">[32] ____</strong>. Once humans were hunters, they benefited from better <strong class=\"source-blank\">[33] ____</strong> and extra time which could be spent on non-physical activities. However, the more humans came to depend on meat as a food source, the more <strong class=\"source-blank\">[34] ____</strong> there was between them and other predators. Humans needed to find an advantage over animals such as lions and hyenas. It wasn’t a spear or knife that gave them this advantage, but the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[35] ____</strong> skills that humans began to develop. Then, because humans were such successful predators, they required more <strong class=\"source-blank\">[36] ____</strong> and this led to groups of people moving away from Africa.</p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"68317","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37–40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>What is the writer’s main argument in the sixth paragraph?</p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"68318","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37–40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>What is the writer doing in the seventh paragraph?</p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"68319","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37–40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The writer refers to vervet monkeys in order to:</p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"68320","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37–40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The writer says that the ‘walking larder’ idea</p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<div><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The Animal Connection&nbsp;</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>Professor of anthropology Pat Shipman looks at the ways in which our relationships with\nanimals have shaped our own human evolution.&nbsp;</em></p><p><br/></p><p>Travel anywhere and you see something so common it may not even catch your attention. Wherever there are people, animals are being walked, herded and fed. Many, such as\ndogs, cats and sheep, are domesticated, but you will also find people living alongside wild\ncreatures like monkeys and wolves. Close contact with animals is not confined to one\nparticular culture, region or ethnic group but is a universal human trait.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>On the face of it this makes little sense. No other mammal adopts individuals from another\nspecies, with good reason. Since the ultimate prize in evolution is perpetuating your genes,\nproviding food for another species is counterproductive to success. Even if pets offer\nfriendship, that cannot explain why our bond with other species arose in the first place. Who\nwould bring a ferocious wolf into their home in the hope that thousands of years later it\nwould become a loving pet?&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>As an anthropologist I have tried to understand this puzzle by looking to the past for the\norigins of our link with animals. What I found was a long and unbroken evolutionary trail of\nevidence I call the ‘animal connection’. This trail links to three important developments in\nhuman evolution: tool making, language and domestication. If I am correct, and I believe\nthat further research will conclusively show that I am, the animal connection is a hugely\nsignificant force instrumental in our global success.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The trail begins at least 2.6 million years ago. That is when the first tools appear in the\narchaeological record. This development required the intellectual breakthrough of realizing\nthat the properties of an object can be altered. Man learnt how to turn stone into small,\nsharp items that could cut up animal carcasses, providing them with an evolutionary\nshortcut to becoming predators.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>There were many consequences of the new hunting lifestyle. On the plus side, eating more\nmeat and fat was a requirement for the increase in relative brain size. And since meat tends\nto come in bigger packages than leaves and roots, meat eaters could spend less time\nfinding food and more on activities like learning and social interaction. On the minus side,\npreying on animals put our ancestors into direct competition with the other predators that\nshared their ecosystem, animals such as lions and hyenas. To get the upper hand, they\nneeded more than just tools, and that is where the animal connection comes in. What made\nit possible for our ancestors to compete successfully with true carnivores was the ability to\npay very close attention to the habits of both potential prey and competitors. Knowledge\nwas power, so we acquired a deep understanding of the minds of other animals. Another\nsignificant consequence of becoming more predatory was the need to live at lower\ndensities, as successful predators soon exhaust food supplies. The record of the\ngeographic distribution of our ancestors provides further support for my idea that the animal\nconnection has shaped our evolution. Early man lived in Africa and nowhere else, but then\nunderwent a dramatic expansion in territory, forced by the search for new hunting grounds.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Throughout the period of these enormous changes in the lifestyle of our ancestors,\ngathering, sharing and recording knowledge became increasingly advantageous, and\nexamples of prehistoric art that appear in Europe, Asia, Africa and Australia allow us to\neavesdrop on their conversations. Through the art, we realize the main topic was animals:\ntheir colours, shapes, postures and habits. This focus is even more striking considering that\nscenes of human life are rarely depicted. Pictures of people, social interaction and\nceremonies are rare.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>This leads me on to the development of language. Nobody doubts this proved a major\nadaptive advantage to our ancestors in developing complex behaviours. How it arose,\nhowever, remains a mystery. I believe I am the first to propose a continuity between the\nstrong human-animal link that appeared 2.6 million years ago and the origin of language. The complexity and importance of animal-related information, indicated in the\npredominance of animal images, spurred early humans to move beyond what other species\ncould achieve. Vervet monkeys, for example, have different cries for eagles and snakes,\nbut they cannot discuss what threats might appear tomorrow. The property of full language\nis that it is comprised of vocabulary and grammatical rules that can be combined in an\ninfinite number of ways to convey fine shades of meaning.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>As our ancestors became more involved with animals, the third product of the animal\nconnection appeared: domestication, which has long been linked with the keeping of\nanimals like sheep. Domestic animals are usually considered as ‘walking larders’, or easy\nfood sources, reflecting the idea that the basis of this change was a drive for greater food\nsecurity. Looking at the origins of domestication for clues to its underlying reasons, I found\nfundamental flaws in this idea. Instead, my analysis suggests domestication emerged as a\nnatural progression of our close association with, and understanding of, other species. If\ndomestication was about knowing where your next meal was coming from, the first\ndomesticate ought to have been a food source, yet analysis of fossils shows that the\ndomestication of dogs pre-dated that of any other species, even plants, from wolves. Furthermore, if the objective was to have meat to eat, you wouldn’t select an animal that\neats two kilograms of meat a day. It was familiarity with this species that led to eventual\ndomestication.&nbsp;</p></div>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9570&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9571","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Listening to the Ocean","book":"阅读真题集 22","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test3","part":1,"description":"阅读真题集 22 · Test3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"9571:68321:1","type":"choice","text":"In the past, it was easier for scientists to study the Moon than the oceans.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The Moon has been far more accessible to study because astronomers have long been able to look at its surface, first with the naked eye and then with the telescope, both instruments that focus light.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：判断过去研究月球是否比研究海洋更容易，关键词为“past”、“easier”、“study the Moon than the oceans”。\n定位关键信息：由题干“past easier study Moon”在A段找到“The Moon has been far more accessible to study”及“until quite recently we knew less about their depths than about the surface of the Moon”。\n解题思路：原文明确说月球“far more accessible”，且过去人们知道海洋少、用光学仪器就能研究月球，而海洋无仪器，故题干与原文一致，选TRUE；FALSE与原文矛盾，NOT GIVEN因原文已明确提及。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68321","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 – 4\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–4 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"9571:68322:2","type":"choice","text":"Techniques for investigating the Moon are the same as techniques for researching the ocean.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The Moon has been far more accessible to study because astronomers have long been able to look at its surface, first with the naked eye and then with the telescope, both instruments that focus light. Until the twentieth century, however, no instruments were available for the study of Earth’s oceans.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问研究月球的技术是否与研究海洋的技术相同，核心是比较两者研究方法。\n定位关键信息：用“Techniques for investigating the Moon”和“techniques for researching the ocean”定位到A段，原文对比月球和海洋的研究工具。\n解题思路：原文指出月球研究依赖光学望远镜，而海洋在20世纪前没有可用仪器，暗示两者技术不同，故答案为FALSE。选项A（TRUE）错误，因为原文明确显示方法不同；选项C（NOT GIVEN）错误，因为原文已给出直接对比信息。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68322","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 – 4\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–4 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"9571:68323:3","type":"choice","text":"Measuring temperature changes in the ocean using sound is more time-consuming than other methods.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Transmitting sound in numerous directions through the deep sound channel can give scientists measurements spanning vast areas of the globe. Thousands of sound paths in the ocean can be pieced together into a map of global ocean temperatures, and by repeating measurements along the same paths over time, scientists can track changes in temperature over months or years.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：判断用声音测量海洋温度变化是否比其他方法更耗时。\n定位关键信息：题干关键词“time-consuming”和“other methods”，但原文未出现比较关系，仅描述声音测量的能力。\n解题思路：原文F段只说明声音可测量温度变化并追踪，未提及其他方法的耗时，也未进行任何时间效率对比，因此选NOT GIVEN。选项A（TRUE）无依据；选项B（FALSE）与原文不矛盾但无比较。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68323","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 – 4\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–4 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"9571:68324:4","type":"choice","text":"Hydrophones can distinguish different kinds of rain.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：By using the sound of rain under water as a ‘natural’ rain gauge, the measurement of rainfall over the oceans will become available to climatologists. In this way, modern society continues to benefit from the investigations of those who, like Leonardo da Vinci, pursued the answers to some basic questions of nature.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问水听器能否区分不同类型的雨，关键词为Hydrophones、distinguish、different kinds of rain。\n定位关键信息：用Hydrophones和rain定位到G段，原文提到用hydrophones listening to rain并测量降雨类型。\n解题思路：原文明确说Nystuen using hydrophones to listen to rain over the ocean, acoustically measuring not only the rainfall rate but also the rainfall type, ranging from drizzle to thunderstorms（水听器不仅测量降雨速率还测量降雨类型，从毛毛雨到雷暴），因此能够区分不同类型雨，答案为TRUE；FALSE与原文矛盾；NOT GIVEN不成立。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68324","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 – 4\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–4 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"9571:68325:5","type":"choice","text":"examples of things that affect the distance sound can travel in water","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A number of factors influence how far sound travels under water and how long it lasts, including particles, salinity, temperature and pressure.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求找出包含“影响声音在水中传播距离的例子”的段落。\n定位关键信息：用题干中的“affect the distance sound can travel in water”对应原文“factors influence how far sound travels under water”。\n解题思路：C段首句直接列举了颗粒物、盐度、温度和压力等影响声音在水中传播距离的因素，符合题干要求。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"68325","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5 – 8\nReading Passage 1 has seven paragraphs, A–G.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 5–8 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"9571:68325:6","type":"choice","text":"details of the connection between ocean temperatures and climate","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The system has enabled researchers to begin making ocean-temperature measurements on a global scale, measurements that are key to understanding the workings of heat transfer between the ocean and the atmosphere.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问“海洋温度与气候之间联系的细节”，关键词是ocean temperatures和climate。\n定位关键信息：用ocean temperatures和climate定位，F段提到海洋温度测量对理解热量交换至关重要，且海洋在决定空气温度中作用巨大。\n解题思路：F段明确说明海洋温度测量是理解大气与海洋热量交换的关键，并指出海洋对气温的决定性作用，直接对应海洋温度与气候的联系。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"68325","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5 – 8\nReading Passage 1 has seven paragraphs, A–G.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 5–8 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"9571:68325:7","type":"choice","text":"details of ways in which light and sound are similar","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Particles in seawater can reflect, scatter and absorb certain frequencies of sound, just as certain wavelengths of light may be reflected, scattered and absorbed by specific types of particles in the atmosphere.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求找出包含“光和声音相似之处细节”的段落。\n定位关键信息：用“light and sound are similar”定位到C段中“just as”引导的类比句。\n解题思路：C段通过“just as”直接比较声音和光在传播中都被粒子反射、散射和吸收的特性，提供了两者相似之处的具体细节。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"68325","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5 – 8\nReading Passage 1 has seven paragraphs, A–G.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 5–8 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"9571:68325:8","type":"choice","text":"a reference to a long-term study of different types of weather","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Since 1985, Nystuen has used hydrophones to listen to rain over the ocean, acoustically measuring not only the rainfall rate but also the rainfall type, ranging from drizzle to thunderstorms.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求找出提到对不同类型天气进行长期研究的一段，关键词为“long-term study”和“different types of weather”。\n定位关键信息：由“long-term study”对应G段中的“Since 1985”，由“different types of weather”对应“rainfall type, ranging from drizzle to thunderstorms”。\n解题思路：G段明确描述自1985年以来一项长期监测，测量了从毛毛雨到雷暴等多种降雨类型，符合题干要求。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"68325","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5 – 8\nReading Passage 1 has seven paragraphs, A–G.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 5–8 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"9571:68326:9","type":"choice","text":"According to the passage, who conducted research into the rate at which sound travels in water?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It was not until 1826 that two scientists, Colladon and Sturm, accurately measured the speed of sound in water.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：询问谁进行了声音在水中传播速度的研究，关键词为“rate at which sound travels in water”即声速。\n定位关键信息：用“speed of sound in water”定位到B段中“accurately measured the speed of sound in water”及科学家名Colladon and Sturm。\n解题思路：原文明确Colladon and Sturm测量了声速，对应B选项；A项da Vinci仅观察声音传播未测速；C项Ewing and Worzel研究低频声波与深声通道而非声速；D项Jeff Nystuen研究降雨声学，原文未提及声速，故排除。","options":["Leonardo da Vinci","Colladon and Sturm","Ewing and Worzel","Jeff Nystuen"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68326","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 – 13\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 9–13 on your answer sheet."},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"9571:68327:10","type":"choice","text":"According to the passage, who conducted research into the distances certain types of sound waves travel in water?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1943, Maurice Ewing and J. L. Worzel conducted an experiment to test the theory that low-frequency waves, which are less vulnerable than higher frequencies to scattering and absorption, should be able to travel great distances, if the sound source is placed correctly.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问谁研究了某些类型声波在水中的传播距离，关键词“distances certain types of sound waves travel in water”。\n定位关键信息：以“distances travel in water”定位到C段“travel great distances”，以及“low-frequency waves”对应“certain types of sound waves”。\n解题思路：正确答案Ewing and Worzel在C段直接进行了测试传播距离的实验；原文其他位置da Vinci仅描述听远处船只，未研究距离；原文其他位置Colladon and Sturm测量声速而非传播距离；原文其他位置Clark利用SOSUS监听鲸鱼，不涉及传播距离研究。","options":["Leonardo da Vinci","Colladon and Sturm","Ewing and Worzel","Christopher Clark"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68327","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 – 13\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 9–13 on your answer sheet."},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"9571:68328:11","type":"choice","text":"SOSUS allows whale researchers to","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Moreover, they can track not just one whale at a time, but many creatures simultaneously.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问SOSUS允许鲸研究人员做什么，关键词为SOSUS、whale researchers、allows。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的SOSUS和whale researchers定位到E段SOSUS相关内容。\n解题思路：正确选项A对应原文“track not just one whale at a time, but many creatures simultaneously”，即可同时追踪多头鲸。选项B原文未提及保护鲸鱼迁徙；选项C原文提到区分鲸叫声，但未提及模仿；选项D原文未提及改变鲸鱼行进方向。","options":["follow a number of whales at the same time.","protect whales as they migrate.","imitate whale calls of different species.","change the whales’ direction of travel."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68328","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 – 13\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 9–13 on your answer sheet."},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"9571:68329:12","type":"choice","text":"Finback whale calls change","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：researchers have detected changes in the calls of finback whales as the seasons change\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问长须鲸的叫声在什么情况下变化，关键词是Finback whale calls change。\n定位关键信息：通过Finback whale calls change定位到E段中关于长须鲸叫声变化的描述。\n解题思路：原文as the seasons change对应B项at different times of year，故B正确；A项when scientists track them原文未提及跟踪与叫声变化的直接关系；C项when whales communicate with other species原文未提及其他物种交流；D项when whales come to the surface与原文“wait for whales to surface”矛盾，且未提及叫声变化。","options":["when scientists track them.","at different times of year.","when whales communicate with other species.","when whales come to the surface."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68329","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 – 13\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 9–13 on your answer sheet."},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"9571:68330:13","type":"choice","text":"SOSUS allows scientists to","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：SOSUS has also proved instrumental in obtaining information crucial to our understanding of climate. The system has enabled researchers to begin making ocean- temperature measurements on a global scale, measurements that are key to understanding the workings of heat transfer between the ocean and the atmosphere.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问SOSUS允许科学家做什么，关键词SOSUS、allows scientists to。\n定位关键信息：根据题干关键词SOSUS和scientists定位到F段首句。\n解题思路：原文F段说明SOSUS使研究者能进行全球海洋温度测量并跟踪温度变化，对应D选项measure variations in temperature；A选项make accurate maps of the ocean floor原文未提及；B选项measure water-level changes原文未提及；C选项investigate ocean currents原文未提及。","options":["make accurate maps of the ocean floor.","measure water-level changes.","investigate ocean currents.","measure variations in temperature."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68330","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 – 13\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 9–13 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"68321","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 – 4\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–4 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>In the past, it was easier for scientists to study the Moon than the oceans.</p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"68322","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 – 4\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–4 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>Techniques for investigating the Moon are the same as techniques for researching the ocean.</p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"68323","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 – 4\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–4 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>Measuring temperature changes in the ocean using sound is more time-consuming than other methods.</p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"68324","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 – 4\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 1–4 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>Hydrophones can distinguish different kinds of rain.</p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"68325","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5 – 8\nReading Passage 1 has seven paragraphs, A–G.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 5–8 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.","html":"<p>examples of things that affect the distance sound can travel in water <strong class=\"source-blank\">[5] ____</strong></p><p>details of the connection between ocean temperatures and climate <strong class=\"source-blank\">[6] ____</strong></p><p>details of ways in which light and sound are similar <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong></p><p>a reference to a long-term study of different types of weather <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"68326","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 – 13\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 9–13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>According to the passage, who conducted research into the rate at which sound travels in water?</p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"68327","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 – 13\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 9–13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>According to the passage, who conducted research into the distances certain types of sound waves travel in water?</p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"68328","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 – 13\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 9–13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>SOSUS allows whale researchers to</p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"68329","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 – 13\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 9–13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Finback whale calls change</p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"68330","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 – 13\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 9–13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>SOSUS allows scientists to</p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<div><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Listening to the Ocean&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>The results of some recent research answer some long -standing questions&nbsp;</em></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>The oceans cover more than 70 per cent of the planet’s surface, yet until quite recently we knew less about their depths than about the surface of the Moon. The Moon has been far more accessible to study because astronomers have long been able to look at its surface, first with the naked eye and then with the telescope, both instruments that focus light. Until the twentieth century, however, no instruments were available for the study of Earth’s oceans: light, which can travel trillions of kilometres throug h the vast vacuum of space, cannot penetrate very far in seawater.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>It turns out that for penetrating water the best instrument is sound. Curious investigators have long been fascinated by sound and the way it travels in water. As early as 1490, the artist and scientist Leonardo da Vinci observed: ‘If you cause your ship to stop and place the head of a long tube in the water and place the outer extremity to your ear, you will hear ships at a great distance from you.’ It was not until 1826 that two scientists, Colladon and Sturm, accurately measured the speed of sound in water. Using a long tube to listen under water (as da Vinci had suggested), they recorded how fast the sound of a submerged bell travelled across Lake Geneva in Switzerland. What these investigators demonstrated was that water is an excellent medium for sound, transmitting it almost five times faster than its speed in air.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>A number of factors influence how far sound travels under water and how long it lasts, including particles, salinity, temperature and pressure. Particles in seawater can reflect, scatter and absorb certain frequencies of sound, just as certain wavelengths of light may be reflected, scattered and absorbed by specific types of particles in the atmosphere. In 1943, Maurice Ewing and J. L. Worzel conducted an experiment to test the theory that low-frequency waves, which are less vulnerable than higher frequencies to scattering and absorption, should be able to travel great distances, if the sound source is placed correctly. The researchers set off an underwater explosion and learned that it was detected easily by receivers 3,200 kilometres away. In analysing the results of this test, they discovered a kind of ‘sound pipeline’, known as the ‘deep sound channel’. Sound introduced into this channel of water could travel thousands of kilometres with minimal loss of signal.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>The US Navy was quick to appreciate the usefulness of low-frequency sound and the deep sound channel. They developed the Sound Surveillance System (SOSUS), which involved underwater microphones, called hydrophones, that were placed on the ocean bottom and connected by cables to on-shore processing centres. It was Christopher Clark of Cornell University who soon realised that SOSUS could be used to listen to whales. Using a SOSUS receiver in the West Indies, he could hear whales that were 1,770 kilometres away.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Whales are the biggest of Earth’s creatures, yet these animals are also remarkably elusive. Scientists wishing to observe blue whales must simply wait in their ships for the whales to surface. A few whales have been tracked briefly in the wild in this way but not for very great distances, and much about them remains unknown. But by using SOSUS, scientists can track the whales and position them on a map. Moreover, they can track not just one whale at a time, but many creatures simultaneously. They can also learn to distinguish whale calls; researchers have detected changes in the calls of finback whales as the seasons change, and have found that blue whales in different regions of the Pacific Ocean have different calls.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>SOSUS has also proved instrumental in obtaining information crucial to our understanding of climate. The system has enabled researchers to begin making ocean- temperature measurements on a global scale, measurements that are key to understanding the workings of heat transfer between the ocean and the atmosphere. The ocean plays an enormous role in determining air temperature — the heat capacity in only the upper few metres of ocean is thought to be equal to all of the heat in the entire atmosphere. For sound waves travelling horizontally in the ocean, speed is largely a function of temperature. Thus, the travel time of a wave of sound between two points is a sensitive indicator of the average temperature along its path. Transmitting sound in numerous directions through the deep sound channel can give scientists measurements spanning vast areas of the globe. Thousands of sound paths in the ocean can be pieced together into a map of global ocean temperatures, and by repeating measurements along the same paths over time, scientists can track changes in temperature over months or years.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Researchers are also using other acoustic techniques to monitor climate. Oceanographer Jeff Nystuen, for example, has explored the use of sound to measure rainfall over the ocean. Monitoring changing global rainfall patterns will contribute to understanding major climate change as well as the weather phenomenon known as El Niño. Since 1985, Nystuen has used hydrophones to listen to rain over the ocean, acoustically measuring not only the rainfall rate but also the rainfall type, ranging from drizzle to thunderstorms. By using the sound of rain under water as a ‘natural’ rain gauge, the measurement of rainfall over the oceans will become available to climatologists. In this way, modern society continues to benefit from the investigations of those who, like Leonardo da Vinci, pursued the answers to some basic questions of nature.&nbsp;</p></div>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9571&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9572","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 The impact of invasive species","book":"阅读真题集 22","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test3","part":2,"description":"阅读真题集 22 · Test3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"9572:68331:14","type":"choice","text":"a suggestion that people have moved numerous species across the globe throughout history","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The phenomenon is not an exclusively modern one. Humans have always transferred a variety of species from one region to another\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问哪段包含“历史上人类将大量物种转移到世界各地”这一观点，关键词为“people have moved numerous species across the globe throughout history”。\n定位关键信息：通过“humans have always transferred”和“not an exclusively modern one”定位至C段首句。\n解题思路：原文“not exclusively modern”和“always transferred”直接对应题目中“throughout history”，故答案为C段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"68331","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nReading Passage 2 has eight paragraphs, A–H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 14–18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"9572:68331:15","type":"choice","text":"an example of how an ecosystem can be damaged very rapidly","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But when the invading jellyfish underwent a population explosion in the space of just six years, the entire marine ecosystem was transformed, and fish numbers declined dramatically because they were in competition with the jellyfish, preying on exactly the same microscopic creatures.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求找出“一个说明生态系统如何被迅速破坏的例子”。\n定位关键信息：关键词“example”“ecosystem damaged rapidly”对应E段中“the invading jellyfish underwent a population explosion in the space of just six years”和“entire marine ecosystem was transformed”。\n解题思路：E段以栉水母为例，说明其在短短六年间种群爆炸，迅速破坏整个海洋生态系统，与题目要求的“被迅速破坏”直接吻合。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"68331","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nReading Passage 2 has eight paragraphs, A–H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 14–18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"9572:68331:16","type":"choice","text":"a description of what can be done to restrict the spread of invasive species","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Although ultimately measures need to be taken at an international level, limited action is possible by individuals. One way is for people to plant native plants in their gardens rather than species from abroad. It is also useful to learn to identify invasive species, and report any sightings to wildlife organisations. Regularly cleaning clothing, boots, boats, tyres, and any other equipment regularly used outdoors can remove insects and plant parts that may introduce invasive species into new locations.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问哪一段描述了可以采取什么措施来限制入侵物种的传播，关键词是“what can be done”和“restrict the spread”。\n定位关键信息：根据“what can be done”和“restrict the spread”定位到H段，该段以“Although ultimately measures need to be taken... limited action is possible by individuals”开头，并列举了具体行动。\n解题思路：H段明确描述了个人可以采取的具体措施，如种植本地植物、识别和报告入侵物种、清洁户外设备等，这些措施直接对应题目要求的“限制入侵物种传播”的描述。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"68331","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nReading Passage 2 has eight paragraphs, A–H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 14–18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"9572:68331:17","type":"choice","text":"a reference to the lack of research on the effects of some invasive species","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The impact of the water hyacinth on native water plants is largely unstudied, as is unfortunately the case for most ecosystems invaded by new plant species.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题干要求找到提及“缺乏对一些入侵物种影响的研究”的段落，关键词为lack of research / unstudied。\n定位关键信息：用“unstudied”定位到F段最后一句，该句明确指出水葫芦对本土水生植物的影响尚未被研究。\n解题思路：原文F段最后一句直接陈述对水葫芦影响的研究缺失，并说明这是大多数新植物入侵生态系统的普遍情况，与题干信息完全对应。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"68331","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nReading Passage 2 has eight paragraphs, A–H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 14–18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"9572:68331:18","type":"choice","text":"a mention of a current lack of public awareness of the problem of invasive species","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Unfortunately, ordinary people outside the scientific community have a very limited understanding of the threat posed by invasive species, which means that other environmental threats receive considerably more media attention.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问哪一段提到了当前公众对入侵物种问题缺乏意识；关键词是“current lack of public awareness”。\n定位关键信息：通过“public awareness”的同义表达“limited understanding”及“ordinary people”定位到G段。\n解题思路：G段中“ordinary people...have a very limited understanding”直接对应题目“lack of public awareness”。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"68331","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nReading Passage 2 has eight paragraphs, A–H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 14–18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"9572:68331:19","type":"choice","text":"an indication that an introduced species may benefit a specific ecosystem","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Some scientists have even argued that in these cases the introduction enhances the diversity of animal and plant life in that specific area.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问哪一段提到“引入的物种可能有益于特定生态系统”。\n定位关键信息：根据“benefit a specific ecosystem”可定位到D段对第一类入侵物种不破坏生态平衡的描述。\n解题思路：D段将入侵物种分为三类，第一类中“enhances the diversity”直接对应“benefit a specific ecosystem”。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"68331","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nReading Passage 2 has eight paragraphs, A–H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 14–18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"9572:68332:20-21","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO reasons for the spread of invasive species are mentioned in the text?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Other invasive species include pets such as snakes or turtles which are intentionally set free into the wild.；In addition, climate change has enabled some invasive plant species to colonise new areas.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问文章中提到的入侵物种扩散的两个原因，关键词是“reasons for the spread”。\n定位关键信息：用“reasons”“spread”定位到C段，该段集中列举了扩散原因：运输发展、气候变化和有意释放。\n解题思路：D选项对应原文“intentionally set free into the wild”（有意释放非本地动物）；E选项对应“climate change has enabled...colonise new areas”（全球变暖扩展地理范围）。A、B、C选项原文未提及：A项“消除不受欢迎的本地物种”无依据；B项“农产品国际贸易扩张”文中只说运输发展，未特指农产品；C项“缺乏对船上货物的检查”文中只提水生生物被运输、昆虫进入木箱，未说缺乏检查。","options":["the wish to eliminate undesirable native species","the recent expansion of international trade in agricultural products","a lack of checks on some of the cargo on board ships","the deliberate release of non-native animals","an extension of their geographical range as a result of global warming"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"68332","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 20-21\nChoose TWO letters, A–E.\nWrite the correct letters in boxes 20 and 21 on your answer sheet.","groupId":"68332-9572:68332:20-21"},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"9572:68332:20-21","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO reasons for the spread of invasive species are mentioned in the text?","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Other invasive species include pets such as snakes or turtles which are intentionally set free into the wild.；In addition, climate change has enabled some invasive plant species to colonise new areas.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问文章中提到的入侵物种扩散的两个原因，关键词是“reasons for the spread”。\n定位关键信息：用“reasons”“spread”定位到C段，该段集中列举了扩散原因：运输发展、气候变化和有意释放。\n解题思路：D选项对应原文“intentionally set free into the wild”（有意释放非本地动物）；E选项对应“climate change has enabled...colonise new areas”（全球变暖扩展地理范围）。A、B、C选项原文未提及：A项“消除不受欢迎的本地物种”无依据；B项“农产品国际贸易扩张”文中只说运输发展，未特指农产品；C项“缺乏对船上货物的检查”文中只提水生生物被运输、昆虫进入木箱，未说缺乏检查。","options":["the wish to eliminate undesirable native species","the recent expansion of international trade in agricultural products","a lack of checks on some of the cargo on board ships","the deliberate release of non-native animals","an extension of their geographical range as a result of global warming"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"68332","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 20-21\nChoose TWO letters, A–E.\nWrite the correct letters in boxes 20 and 21 on your answer sheet.","groupId":"68332-9572:68332:20-21"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"9572:68333:22-23","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO statements does the writer make about the water hyacinth?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：its beauty attracted botanists seeking exotic plants for botanical gardens and they imported it to a horticultural exhibition in New Orleans in 1884；Today it is present around the globe, damaging boat engines and even blocking cooling pipes for power plants, occasionally leading to massive blackouts.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问作者关于水葫芦做了哪两个陈述，关键词为water hyacinth和two statements。\n定位关键信息：通过专有名词water hyacinth定位到F段。\n解题思路：选项B对应1884年引入新奥尔良（北美，19世纪末），正确；选项D对应当前全球分布导致损坏引擎和堵塞冷却管（实际问题），正确；选项A原文说原产于南美亚马逊河，非全球原生，排除；选项C原文只提美丽吸引植物学家，未说人们因此忽视负面影响，原文未提及；选项E原文是植物学家自行引进，非科学家推荐，排除。","options":["It is native to almost every region of the world.","It was brought to North America in the late nineteenth century.","Its beauty has led people to ignore the negative effects it has.","Its spread has caused some practical problems in recent years.","Scientists recommended its introduction to the USA."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"68333","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 22-23\nChoose TWO letters, A–E.\nWrite the correct letters in boxes 22 and 23 on your answer sheet.","groupId":"68333-9572:68333:22-23"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"9572:68333:22-23","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO statements does the writer make about the water hyacinth?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：its beauty attracted botanists seeking exotic plants for botanical gardens and they imported it to a horticultural exhibition in New Orleans in 1884；Today it is present around the globe, damaging boat engines and even blocking cooling pipes for power plants, occasionally leading to massive blackouts.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问作者关于水葫芦做了哪两个陈述，关键词为water hyacinth和two statements。\n定位关键信息：通过专有名词water hyacinth定位到F段。\n解题思路：选项B对应1884年引入新奥尔良（北美，19世纪末），正确；选项D对应当前全球分布导致损坏引擎和堵塞冷却管（实际问题），正确；选项A原文说原产于南美亚马逊河，非全球原生，排除；选项C原文只提美丽吸引植物学家，未说人们因此忽视负面影响，原文未提及；选项E原文是植物学家自行引进，非科学家推荐，排除。","options":["It is native to almost every region of the world.","It was brought to North America in the late nineteenth century.","Its beauty has led people to ignore the negative effects it has.","Its spread has caused some practical problems in recent years.","Scientists recommended its introduction to the USA."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"68333","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 22-23\nChoose TWO letters, A–E.\nWrite the correct letters in boxes 22 and 23 on your answer sheet.","groupId":"68333-9572:68333:22-23"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"9572:68334:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"biodiversity","acceptedAnswers":["biodiversity"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Above all, invasive species threaten biodiversity in many habitats. For instance, the climbing plant species kudzu (which is native to East Asia) can easily replace a habitat that had a wide range of plants with a monoculture consisting solely of kudzu, as has started to happen in the south- east of the USA.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问Kudzu减少了美国东南部某些地区的什么，关键词Kudzu和south-east of the USA。\n定位关键信息：用Kudzu和south-east of the USA定位到B段最后一句，其中提到kudzu取代多样性栖息地。\n解题思路：原文指出kudzu威胁biodiversity并用其替换多样植物，所以reduce的是biodiversity。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68334","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"9572:68334:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"equilibrium","acceptedAnswers":["equilibrium"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The first of these may be introduced species which can maintain themselves in a limited range of habitats without upsetting the ecological equilibrium of the area.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问某些引入物种仅在小范围内且不干扰周围生态系统的什么时威胁低，关键词为introduced species、low level of threat、small area、do not disturb。\n定位关键信息：根据题干introduced species present a low level of threat定位到D段首句，再依据first of these和without upsetting找到具体描述。\n解题思路：原文中“maintain themselves in a limited range of habitats”对应“remain within a small area”，“without upsetting the ecological equilibrium”对应“do not disturb the equilibrium”，故答案为equilibrium。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68334","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"9572:68334:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"waste","acceptedAnswers":["waste"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The Black Sea has levels of industrial waste which are by international standards exceptionally high.；The jellyfish had a more serious impact on the ecosystem than the heavily polluted water.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题干问水母的影响比来自工厂的什么更大，关键词为invasive jellyfish、Black Sea、greater than、factories。\n定位关键信息：通过jellyfish和Black Sea定位到E段，找关于水母与工厂污染的对比描述。\n解题思路：原文指出黑海含有大量工业废物，接着说明水母对生态系统的影响比严重污染的水更严重，其中“heavily polluted water”与工厂排放的废物对应，因此答案填入“waste”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68334","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"68332-9572:68332:20-21","numbers":[20,21],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["D","E"]},{"id":"68333-9572:68333:22-23","numbers":[22,23],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["B","D"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"68331","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nReading Passage 2 has eight paragraphs, A–H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 14–18 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>a suggestion that people have moved numerous species across the globe throughout history <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong></p><p>an example of how an ecosystem can be damaged very rapidly <strong class=\"source-blank\">[15] ____</strong></p><p>a description of what can be done to restrict the spread of invasive species <strong class=\"source-blank\">[16] ____</strong></p><p>a reference to the lack of research on the effects of some invasive species <strong class=\"source-blank\">[17] ____</strong></p><p>a mention of a current lack of public awareness of the problem of invasive species <strong class=\"source-blank\">[18] ____</strong></p><p>an indication that an introduced species may benefit a specific ecosystem <strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"68332","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 20-21\nChoose TWO letters, A–E.\nWrite the correct letters in boxes 20 and 21 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Which <strong>TWO</strong> reasons for the spread of invasive species are mentioned in the text?</p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"68333","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 22-23\nChoose TWO letters, A–E.\nWrite the correct letters in boxes 22 and 23 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Which <strong>TWO</strong> statements does the writer make about the water hyacinth?</p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"68334","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nComplete the sentences below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Kudzu has reduced the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> of certain areas in the south-east of the USA.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Some introduced species present a low level of threat if they remain within a small area and do not disturb the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong> of the surrounding ecosystem.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">The effect of invasive jellyfish in the Black Sea was greater than that <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong> from factories.</p>","firstNumber":24}],"passage":"<div><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The impact of invasive species&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Invasive species are among the leading threats to the native wildlife of most countries, with approximately 42 percent of endangered species at risk from them. Invasive species can be any kind of organism – for example, a mammal, amphibian, fish, insect or plant – that is not native to an ecosystem. Often they reproduce and spread with great speed. Contrary to popular belief, a plant or animal classified as an invasive species does not necessarily originate in another country. For example, lake trout are native to the Great Lakes of North America, but are considered to be an invasive species in Yellowstone Lake in Wyoming because they compete with native cutthroat trout for habitat.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>When a new species is introduced into an ecosystem, native wildlife may struggle to compete with it for food and other resources. Invasive species can change the food web in an ecosystem by destroying or replacing native food sources, while providing little or no food for local wildlife. In extreme cases, the invader may prey on the native species. Above all, invasive species threaten biodiversity in many habitats. For instance, the climbing plant species kudzu (which is native to East Asia) can easily replace a habitat that had a wide range of plants with a monoculture consisting solely of kudzu, as has started to happen in the south- east of the USA.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>The phenomenon is not an exclusively modern one. Humans have always transferred a variety of species from one region to another, but the development of rapid means of transportation has increased the frequency of such introductions. Aquatic organisms can be shipped across the oceans, while insects can easily get into the wooden crates that are transported around the world in this way. In addition, climate change has enabled some invasive plant species to colonise new areas. Other invasive species include pets such as snakes or turtles which are intentionally set free into the wild.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Invasive species do not all present the same level of threat to native ecosystems and can be classified into three types. The first of these may be introduced species which can maintain themselves in a limited range of habitats without upsetting the ecological equilibrium of the area. Some scientists have even argued that in these cases the introduction enhances the diversity of animal and plant life in that specific area. A second group of invaders present a greater threat because their spread is at the expense of one native species. The North American grey squirrel, for example, was introduced to the UK in 1876 largely because wealthy landowners thought it would be a fashionable and attractive addition to the local wildlife on their estates. It spread widely, leading directly to the dramatic decline in the population of the native red squirrel. However, it would appear that this is the only definite negative impact of the grey squirrel.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>There is a third level of threat in which the dominance of the introduced species has an extremely destructive effect on the entire ecosystem. One of the most damaging examples involved a species of comb jellyfish. Native to estuaries along the western Atlantic coast from the northern United States to the Valdés Peninsula in Argentina, this species was released from a ship into the Black Sea in Eastern Europe in 1982, almost certainly by accident. The Black Sea has levels of industrial waste which are by international standards exceptionally high. Despite this, fishing boats were still able to catch healthy numbers of fish. But when the invading jellyfish underwent a population explosion in the space of just six years, the entire marine ecosystem was transformed, and fish numbers declined dramatically because they were in competition with the jellyfish, preying on exactly the same microscopic creatures. The jellyfish had a more serious impact on the ecosystem than the heavily polluted water.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>More than a century after its introduction outside its native range on the Amazon River in South America, a plant known as a water hyacinth can be found in tropical lakes, streams, and rivers around the world. Its beauty attracted botanists seeking exotic plants for botanical gardens and they imported it to a horticultural exhibition in New Orleans in 1884. Visitors were so impressed they planted it in many locations during the 1880s and 1890s, resulting in the aquatic ecosystems of the south-eastern United States being progressively colonised by vast, floating, dense carpets of water hyacinth. Today it is present around the globe, damaging boat engines and even blocking cooling pipes for power plants, occasionally leading to massive blackouts. The impact of the water hyacinth on native water plants is largely unstudied, as is unfortunately the case for most ecosystems invaded by new plant species.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>In the United States, more than 7,000 introduced species have established themselves, of which at least 15 percent cause ecological damage. As the number of invasive species expands, legislation to deal with this problem is rare or non-existent in the majority of countries. Unfortunately, ordinary people outside the scientific community have a very limited understanding of the threat posed by invasive species, which means that other environmental threats receive considerably more media attention. The introduction of new species can initially seem highly desirable, but the full extent of their impact is consistently underestimated.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Although ultimately measures need to be taken at an international level, limited action is possible by individuals. One way is for people to plant native plants in their gardens rather than species from abroad. It is also useful to learn to identify invasive species, and report any sightings to wildlife organisations. Regularly cleaning clothing, boots, boats, tyres, and any other equipment regularly used outdoors can remove insects and plant parts that may introduce invasive species into new locations.&nbsp;</p></div>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9572&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9573","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 The Fruit Book","book":"阅读真题集 22","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test3","part":3,"description":"阅读真题集 22 · Test3 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"9573:68664:27","type":"choice","text":"A description of Shanley’s initial data collection","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：During 1993 and 1994, 30 families weighed everything they used from the forest – game, fruit, fibre, medicinal plants – and documented its source.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求找出描述Shanley初始数据收集的段落，关键词为“initial data collection”。\n定位关键信息：通过“initial data collection”和“weighed everything they used”定位到D段末尾关于1993-1994年家庭称重记录的内容。\n解题思路：D段中“30 families weighed everything”直接对应初始数据收集的具体过程，与题干“A description of Shanley’s initial data collection”相符。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"68664","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nReading Passage 3 has nine paragraphs, A–I.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–I, in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"9573:68664:28","type":"choice","text":"Why a government official also contributes to the book","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Its blend of hard science and local knowledge on the use and trade of 35 native forest species has been so well received (and well used) that no less a dignitary than Brazil’s environment minister, Marina Silva, has written the foreword.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问为什么一位政府官员也为本书做贡献（写序言），关键词是“government official”、“contributes to the book”。\n定位关键信息：用“government official”和“contributes to the book”定位到A段中“Brazil’s environment minister, Marina Silva, has written the foreword”这一句。\n解题思路：原文明确提到巴西环境部长因为该书融合科学和当地知识、广受欢迎而写了序言，直接回答了政府官员贡献的原因。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"68664","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nReading Passage 3 has nine paragraphs, A–I.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–I, in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"9573:68664:29","type":"choice","text":"Reasons why the community asked Shanley to conduct the research","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The Rural Workers’ Union wanted to know whether harvesting wild fruits would make economic sense in the Rio Capim.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问社区为何要求Shanley进行该研究，关键词为“community”和“conduct the research”。\n定位关键信息：由“community”定位至C段“Rural Workers’ Union”，“conduct the research”对应“wanted to know ...”。\n解题思路：原文说明工会想知道采摘野果的经济可行性，这正是社区要求研究的原因，故答案在C段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"68664","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nReading Passage 3 has nine paragraphs, A–I.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–I, in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"9573:68664:30","type":"choice","text":"Reference to the starting point of her research","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Shanley’s work on the book began a decade ago, with a plea for help from the Rural Workers’ Union of Paragominas, a Brazilian town whose prosperity is based on exploitation of timber.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是找到提及她研究起点的段落。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“starting point of her research”和“Shanley’s work ... began”定位到B段首句。\n解题思路：B段首句中的“began”直接对应“starting point”，描述了研究开始的缘由和时间，即为研究起点。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"68664","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nReading Passage 3 has nine paragraphs, A–I.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–I, in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"9573:68664:31","type":"choice","text":"Two factors that alter food consumption patterns","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The fire and logging also changed the nature of the caboclo diet.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问两个改变食物消费模式的因素，关键词是“alter food consumption patterns”。\n定位关键信息：用“food consumption”和“changed”定位到E段，该段讨论火灾和伐木对饮食的影响。\n解题思路：原文E段明确指出“fire and logging”是改变卡布克洛人饮食性质的两个因素，与题干中的“Two factors”直接对应。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"68664","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nReading Passage 3 has nine paragraphs, A–I.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–I, in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"9573:68664:32","type":"choice","text":"Why the book is successful","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Its success is largely due to the fact that people with poor literacy skills can understand much of the information it contains about the non-timber forest products, thanks to its illustrations, anecdotes, stories and songs.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问这本书成功的原因，关键词是“successful”。\n定位关键信息：根据“book is successful”定位到I段，该句直接提到“success is largely due to...”。\n解题思路：原文明确说明成功是因为低识字能力者能通过插图和故事理解信息，这正是题干所问的原因。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"68664","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nReading Passage 3 has nine paragraphs, A–I.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–I, in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"9573:68665:33","type":"fill","text":"填写第 33 空","answer":"forest fruit/fruit","acceptedAnswers":["forest fruit","fruit"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Average annual household consumption of forest fruit had fallen from 89 to 28 kilograms between 1993 and 1999. \"What we found,\" says Shanley, \"was that fruit collection could coexist with a certain amount of logging, but after the forest fire, it dropped dramatically.\"\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问森林火灾导致当地村民减少了哪种消费，需要填写第一个空（对应“forest fruit”或“fruit”）。\n定位关键信息：通过题干“Forest fire”和“consume less”定位到E段，该段提到了火灾后水果消费量下降的具体数据。\n解题思路：原文明确提到火灾后“fruit collection dropped dramatically”，而之前数据显示“household consumption of forest fruit”从89降到28千克，因此正确答案是forest fruit或fruit。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68665","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33–40\nComplete the summary below.\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 33–40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"9573:68665:34","type":"fill","text":"填写第 34 空","answer":"fibre","acceptedAnswers":["fibre"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Over the same period, fibre use also dropped from around 20 to 4 kilograms.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问森林火灾导致当地村民消费减少的第二个产品，并给出“fibre”作为答案。\n定位关键信息：以“forest fire”和“consume less”为关键词定位到E段，该段描述火灾后消费变化。\n解题思路：原文E段指出在森林火灾后，纤维使用量从20公斤降至4公斤，与题目要求“消费减少”及答案“fibre”完全吻合。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68665","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33–40\nComplete the summary below.\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 33–40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"9573:68665:35","type":"fill","text":"填写第 35 空","answer":"uxi trees/uxi","acceptedAnswers":["uxi trees","uxi"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Under copaiba, they caught just two species averaging 63 kilogrammes; and under uxi, four species weighing 38 kilogrammes.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问在哪种树下捕获的猎物数量最少，要求填写树种名称。\n定位关键信息：根据题干“least amount of game hunted under”和“game”定位至F段对三种树下猎物重量的比较。\n解题思路：原文显示piquia树下232公斤，copaiba树下63公斤，uxi树下仅38公斤，表明uxi树下猎物最少，故答案为uxi trees。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68665","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33–40\nComplete the summary below.\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 33–40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"9573:68665:36","type":"fill","text":"填写第 36 空","answer":"unpredictable","acceptedAnswers":["unpredictable"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Fruiting patterns of trees such as uxi were unpredictable\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问产量也是怎样的，答案需填一个描述产量特点的形容词。\n定位关键信息：根据“yield is also”和上个空“uxi trees”，在G段找到关于uxi产量的描述。\n解题思路：原文说明uxi树的果实产量难以预测（unpredictable），与题干“yield is also”对应。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68665","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33–40\nComplete the summary below.\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 33–40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"9573:68665:37","type":"fill","text":"填写第 37 空","answer":"piquia trees","acceptedAnswers":["piquia trees"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\"This showed that selling piquia trees to loggers for a few dollars made little sense,\" explains Shanley. \"Their local value lies in providing a prized fruit, as well as flowers which attract more game than any other species.\"\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求从文中找出更合理保留的树种，关键词为\"more reasonable to keep\"。\n定位关键信息：根据\"more reasonable to keep\"和常保留树种对应piquia trees，定位到F段讨论piquia的句子。\n解题思路：原文表明出售piquia trees收益甚微，其真正价值在于果实和吸引猎物，因此保留它们更合理，对应答案piquia trees。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68665","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33–40\nComplete the summary below.\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 33–40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"9573:68665:38","type":"fill","text":"填写第 38 空","answer":"subsistence/subsistence use","acceptedAnswers":["subsistence","subsistence use"],"explanation":"原文答案句：On the contrary, argues Shanley, they are critical for subsistence, something that is often ignored in much of the current research on NTFPs, which tends to focus on their commercial potential.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：问除了卖给伐木者，树还能用于什么用途，但这一点常被忽视，因为研究通常关注树的哪个方面。\n定位关键信息：根据“besides selling them to loggers”和“often ignored”定位H段“critical for subsistence, something that is often ignored”。\n解题思路：原文H段明确指出树对生计至关重要（critical for subsistence），且被忽视，因此空白处填subsistence（或subsistence use）。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68665","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33–40\nComplete the summary below.\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 33–40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"9573:68665:39","type":"fill","text":"填写第 39 空","answer":"commercial potential","acceptedAnswers":["commercial potential"],"explanation":"原文答案句：something that is often ignored in much of the current research on NTFPs, which tends to focus on their commercial potential.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题干问所有树木除了卖给伐木者还能用于什么，且研究通常关注树木的哪个方面（被忽视的方面反而被提及）。\n定位关键信息：根据“most research usually focuses on”和“ignored”定位到H段中“often ignored ... which tends to focus on their commercial potential”。\n解题思路：原文说研究常忽略树木的其他用途，而倾向于关注其商业潜力，与题干“most research usually focuses on”对应，因此答案是commercial potential。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68665","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33–40\nComplete the summary below.\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 33–40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"9573:68665:40","type":"fill","text":"填写第 40 空","answer":"non-timber forest products/NTFPs","acceptedAnswers":["non-timber forest products","NTFPs"],"explanation":"原文答案句：people with poor literacy skills can understand much of the information it contains about the non-timber forest products\n对应段落：I段\n审题：问这本书的目的是提供关于什么的信息，关键词为purpose of the book和give information about\n定位关键信息：根据题干中\"purpose of the book\"定位至I段末尾对该书内容的描述\n解题思路：书中的信息帮助读者了解非木材森林产品，因此答案与该短语一致","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68665","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33–40\nComplete the summary below.\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 33–40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"68664","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nReading Passage 3 has nine paragraphs, A–I.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–I, in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>A description of Shanley’s initial data collection <strong class=\"source-blank\">[27] ____</strong></p><p>Why a government official also contributes to the book <strong class=\"source-blank\">[28] ____</strong></p><p>Reasons why the community asked Shanley to conduct the research <strong class=\"source-blank\">[29] ____</strong></p><p>Reference to the starting point of her research <strong class=\"source-blank\">[30] ____</strong></p><p>Two factors that alter food consumption patterns <strong class=\"source-blank\">[31] ____</strong></p><p>Why the book is successful <strong class=\"source-blank\">[32] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"68665","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33–40\nComplete the summary below.\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 33–40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Forest fire has caused local villagers to consume less:</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">• <strong class=\"source-blank\">[33] ____</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">• <strong class=\"source-blank\">[34] ____</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">• game&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">There is the least amount of game hunted under <strong class=\"source-blank\">[35] ____</strong>; yield is also <strong class=\"source-blank\">[36] ____</strong>. Thus, it is more reasonable to keep <strong class=\"source-blank\">[37] ____</strong>.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">All the trees can also be used for <strong class=\"source-blank\">[38] ____</strong> besides selling them to loggers. But this is often ignored, because most research usually focuses on the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[39] ____</strong> of the trees.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><br/></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">The purpose of the book:</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">• To give information about <strong class=\"source-blank\">[40] ____</strong>.</p>","firstNumber":33}],"passage":"<div><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The Fruit Book&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><em>It’s not every scientist who writes books for people who can’t read. And how many scientists want their books to look as dog-eared as possible? But Patricia Shanley, an ethnobotanist, wanted to give something back. After the poorest people of the Amazon allowed her to study their land and its ecology, she turned her research findings into a picture book that tells the local people how to get a good return from their trees without succumbing to the lure of a quick buck from a logging company. It has proved a big success.&nbsp;</em></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>The book is called Fruit Trees and Useful Plants in the Lives of Amazonians, but is better known simply as the “fruit book”. The second edition was produced at the request of politicians in western Amazonia. Its blend of hard science and local knowledge on the use and trade of 35 native forest species has been so well received (and well used) that no less a dignitary than Brazil’s environment minister, Marina Silva, has written the foreword. “There is nothing else like the Shanley book,” says Adalberto Veríssimo, director of the Institute of People and the Environment of the Amazon. “It gives science back to the poor, to the people who really need it.”&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Shanley’s work on the book began a decade ago, with a plea for help from the Rural Workers’ Union of Paragominas, a Brazilian town whose prosperity is based on exploitation of timber. The union realised that logging companies would soon be knocking on the doors of the caboclos, peasant farmers living on the Rio Capim, an Amazon tributary in the Brazilian state of Pará. Isolated and illiterate, the caboclos would have little concept of the true value of their trees; communities downstream had already sold off large blocks of forest for a pittance. “What they wanted to know was how valuable the forests were,” recalls Shanley, then a researcher in the area for the Massachusetts-based Woods Hole Research Centre.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>The Rural Workers’ Union wanted to know whether harvesting wild fruits would make economic sense in the Rio Capim. “There was a lot of interest in trading non-timber forest products (NTFPs),” Shanley says. At the time, environmental groups and green-minded businesses were promoting the idea. This was the view presented in a seminal paper, Valuation of an Amazonian Rainforest, published in Nature in 1989. The researchers had calculated that revenues from the sale of fruits could far exceed those from a one-off sale of trees to loggers. “The union was keen to discover whether it made more sense conserving the forest for subsistence use and the possible sale of fruit, game and medicinal plants, than selling trees for timber,” says Shanley. Whether it would work for the caboclos was far from clear.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Although Shanley had been invited to work in the Rio Capim, some caboclos were suspicious. “When Patricia asked if she could study my forest,” says Joao Fernando Moreira Brito, “my neighbours said she was a foreigner who’d come to rob me of my trees.” In the end, Moreira Brito, or Mangueira as he is known, welcomed Shanley and worked on her study. His land, an hour’s walk from the Rio Capim, is almost entirely covered with primary forest. A study of this and other tracts of forest selected by the communities enabled Shanley to identify three trees, found throughout the Amazon, whose fruit was much favoured by the caboclos: bacuri (Platonia insignis), uxi (Endopleura uchi) and piquia (Caryocar villosum). The caboclos used their fruits, extracted oils, and knew what sort of wildlife they attracted. But, in the face of aggressive tactics from the logging companies, they had no measure of the trees’ financial worth. The only way to find out, Shanley decided, was to start from scratch with a scientific study. “From a scientific point of view, hardly anything was known about these trees,” she says. But six years of field research yielded a mass of data on their flowering and fruiting behaviour. During 1993 and 1994, 30 families weighed everything they used from the forest – game, fruit, fibre, medicinal plants – and documented its source.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>After three logging sales and a major fire in 1997, the researchers were also able to study the ecosystem’s reaction to logging and disturbance. They carried out a similar, though less exhaustive, study in 1999, this time with 15 families. The changes were striking. Average annual household consumption of forest fruit had fallen from 89 to 28 kilograms between 1993 and 1999. “What we found,” says Shanley, “was that fruit collection could coexist with a certain amount of logging, but after the forest fire, it dropped dramatically.” Over the same period, fibre use also dropped from around 20 to 4 kilograms. The fire and logging also changed the nature of the caboclo diet. In 1993 most households ate game two or three times a month. By 1999 some were fortunate if they ate game more than two or three times a year.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>The loss of certain species of tree was especially significant. Shanley’s team persuaded local hunters to weigh their catch, noting the trees under which the animals were caught. Over the year, they trapped five species of game averaging 232 kilogrammes under piquia trees. Under copaiba, they caught just two species averaging 63 kilogrammes; and under uxi, four species weighing 38 kilogrammes. At last, the team was getting a handle on which trees were worth keeping, and which could reasonably be sold. “This showed that selling piquia trees to loggers for a few dollars made little sense,” explains Shanley. “Their local value lies in providing a prized fruit, as well as flowers which attract more game than any other species.”&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>As a result of these studies, Shanley had to tell the Rural Workers’ Union of Paragominas that the Nature thesis could not be applied wholesale to their community – harvesting NTFPs would not always yield more than timber sales. Fruiting patterns of trees such as uxi were unpredictable, for example. In 1994, one household collected 3,654 uxi fruits; the following year, none at all.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>This is not to say that wild fruit trees were unimportant. On the contrary, argues Shanley, they are critical for subsistence, something that is often ignored in much of the current research on NTFPs, which tends to focus on their commercial potential. Geography was another factor preventing the Rio Capim caboclos from establishing a serious trade in wild fruit: villagers in remote areas could not compete with communities collecting NTFPs close to urban markets, although they could sell them to passing river boats.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>But Shanley and her colleagues decided to do more than just report their results to the union. Together with two of her research colleagues, Shanley wrote the fruit book. This, the Bible and a publication on medicinal plants co-authored by Shanley and designed for people with minimal literacy skills are about the only books you will see along this stretch of the Rio Capim. The first print run was only 3,000 copies, but the fruit book has been remarkably influential, and is used by colleges, peasant unions, industries and the caboclos themselves. Its success is largely due to the fact that people with poor literacy skills can understand much of the information it contains about the non-timber forest products, thanks to its illustrations, anecdotes, stories and songs. “The book doesn’t tell people what to do,” says Shanley, “but it does provide them with choices.” The caboclos who have used the book now have a much better understanding of which trees to sell to the loggers, and which to protect.&nbsp;</p></div>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9573&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9574","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Scented Plants","book":"阅读真题集 22","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test4","part":1,"description":"阅读真题集 22 · Test4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"9574:68339:1","type":"choice","text":"a list of food plants which need insects to make them productive","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Floral scent has a strong impact on the economic success of many agricultural crops that rely on insect pollinators, including fruit trees such as the bee-pollinated cherry, apple, apricot, and peach, as well as vegetables and tropical plants such as the papaya.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问哪一段包含一个“需要昆虫使其具有生产力的食用植物列表”，关键词为“list of food plants”和“need insects”。\n定位关键信息：通过“food plants”和“insects to make them productive”找到F段中列举的依赖昆虫传粉的农作物列表。\n解题思路：F段原文直接列举了多种需要昆虫传粉的食用果树和蔬菜，与题目要求的“食用植物列表”完全对应。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"68339","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1–4\nReading Passage 1 has eight paragraphs, A–H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 1–4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"9574:68339:2","type":"choice","text":"an explanation of why a genetic experiment may assist plant reproduction","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Clearly, a more refined strategy is needed; genetic manipulation of scents, for example, would allow growers to regulate the types of insect pollinators and the frequency of their visits.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求找到“解释为什么基因实验可能帮助植物繁殖”的段落，关键词为“genetic experiment”和“assist plant reproduction”。\n定位关键信息：通过“genetic manipulation”和“assist plant reproduction”定位到G段中关于基因操作调节传粉者的描述。\n解题思路：G段末句指出基因操作气味可调控传粉昆虫类型和访问频率，从而辅助植物繁殖，直接对应题目要求。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"68339","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1–4\nReading Passage 1 has eight paragraphs, A–H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 1–4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"9574:68339:3","type":"choice","text":"a description of current research with advantages for the flower industry","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Such manipulation of scent will also benefit people who grow flowers commercially.；The next generation of experiments, already in progress, will include more sophisticated schemes that target the expression of scent specifically to flowers or other organs, such as special glands that can store antibacterial or herbivore-repellent compounds.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目要求找出描述当前研究且对花卉产业有优势的段落，关键词为“current research”和“advantages for the flower industry”。\n定位关键信息：通过“flower industry”和“experiments, already in progress”定位到H段。\n解题思路：H段首句提及气味操控将惠及花卉商业种植，随后具体介绍当前进行中的新一代实验，与题目“当前研究对花卉产业的优势”完全对应。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"68339","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1–4\nReading Passage 1 has eight paragraphs, A–H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 1–4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"9574:68339:4","type":"choice","text":"an explanation of how insects perceive volatile compounds in plants","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Insects are the most common animals to interact with plants in this way, and most insects detect volatile compounds through the extremely sensitive antennae on their heads.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求找出解释昆虫如何感知植物中挥发性化合物的段落，关键词为“insects perceive volatile compounds”。\n定位关键信息：利用“insects”和“detect volatile compounds”以及“antennae”定位到C段。\n解题思路：C段明确指出昆虫通过头部触角检测挥发性化合物，提供了题目所需的解释，与段落内容匹配。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"68339","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1–4\nReading Passage 1 has eight paragraphs, A–H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 1–4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"9574:68340:5","type":"choice","text":"According to the passage, spices were used in the past to","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Humans have recognized and taken advantage of these plant-derived antibacterials since antiquity, when they were used to slow the spoilage of food.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问根据文章，过去使用香料的目的，关键词为spices, used in the past。\n定位关键信息：用spices和in the past定位到B段提及香料用于减慢食物腐烂。\n解题思路：正确选项C对应原文“slow the spoilage of food”，即防止腐烂；A项“驱虫”未提及（原文讲抗菌防腐）；B项“改善味道”未提及；D项“使食物气味更吸引人”未提及。","options":["keep insects away from food.","improve the taste of food.","prevent the decay of food.","make food smell more attractive."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68340","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5–9\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 5–9 on your answer sheet."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"9574:68341:6","type":"choice","text":"The Leonardoxa africana tree protects itself by","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In the rainforest tree Leonardoxa africana, for example, ants of the species Petalomyrmex phylax are attracted to young leaves because they emit high levels of the volatile compound methyl salicylate, a substance that ants need to use as an antiseptic in their nests; coincidentally, the ants attack any herbivorous insects that they encounter.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问The Leonardoxa africana tree如何自我保护，关键词为Leonardoxa africana tree和protects itself。\n定位关键信息：利用专有名词Leonardoxa africana定位到E段开头。\n解题思路：正确选项D：原文显示蚂蚁（ant）作为食草昆虫的敌人被吸引并攻击食草昆虫，从而保护树。排除A：树不是直接散发气味驱逐昆虫，而是通过气味吸引蚂蚁；排除B：原文未提及树毒死食草昆虫；排除C：原文未提及树化学摧毁寄生虫卵，原文其他位置虽提到吸引卵的寄生虫，但非Leonardoxa。","options":["emitting a scent that repels plant-eating insects.","attracting and poisoning herbivorous insects.","chemically destroying the eggs of parasites.","attracting an enemy of herbivorous insects."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68341","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5–9\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 5–9 on your answer sheet."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"9574:68342:7","type":"choice","text":"Which of the following statements about methyl salicylate is NOT true according to the passage?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In the rainforest tree Leonardoxa africana, for example, ants of the species Petalomyrmex phylax are attracted to young leaves because they emit high levels of the volatile compound methyl salicylate, a substance that ants need to use as an antiseptic in their nests; coincidentally, the ants attack any herbivorous insects that they encounter.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问关于methyl salicylate的哪个说法不符合文章内容，关键词methyl salicylate。\n定位关键信息：根据methyl salicylate定位到E段，原文提到蚂蚁被吸引是因为它们需要methyl salicylate做巢穴消毒剂，且蚂蚁攻击植食昆虫。\n解题思路：正确选项B（帮助植食昆虫找食物）不成立，因为原文蚂蚁攻击植食昆虫；A正确（helper ants保护巢穴）依据“use as an antiseptic in their nests”；C正确（helper rainforest tree吸引蚂蚁）依据“ants are attracted to young leaves”；D正确（helper tree避免被吃）依据“ants attack any herbivorous insects... deterring herbivores”。其他选项均被原文支持，唯B原文未提及且相反。","options":["It helps ants to protect their nests.","It helps herbivorous insects to find food.","It helps a rainforest tree to attract ants.","It helps a rainforest tree to avoid being eaten."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68342","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5–9\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 5–9 on your answer sheet."},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"9574:68343:8","type":"choice","text":"Which factor has made the problems of US fruit growers more serious?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This problem has been made worse in the United States by recent epidemics that have infected and killed many honeybees, the major insect pollinator.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：问哪个因素加剧了美国果农的问题，关键词为“factor”“US fruit growers”“more serious”。\n定位关键信息：由“US fruit growers”和“more serious”定位到F段末尾“This problem has been made worse in the United States by recent epidemics”。\n解题思路：原文说近期流行病感染并杀死了许多蜜蜂，使问题恶化，对应D“蜜蜂数量因疾病减少”。A“蜜蜂找到替代食物来源”原文未提及；B“化学品杀死太多蜜蜂”原文未提及；C“水果质量下降”原文未提及。","options":["Bees found an alternative source of food.","Chemicals were killing too many bees.","Fruit was decreasing in quality.","Bees have had their numbers reduced by disease."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68343","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5–9\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 5–9 on your answer sheet."},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"9574:68344:9","type":"choice","text":"Experiments in genetically manipulating the fragrance of ornamental flowers have","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Some preliminary experiments have already been carried out, but for technical reasons the scent was present in every part of the plant, rather than being localized in the flower, and the level of intensity of fragrance was below the threshold of detection for the human nose.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问关于基因操控观赏花卉香味实验的结果，关键词为“Experiments in genetically manipulating the fragrance of ornamental flowers”。\n定位关键信息：根据“genetically manipulating”和“ornamental flowers”定位到H段，该段讨论观赏花卉香味基因操作。\n解题思路：原文指出初步实验中香味强度低于人类嗅觉阈值，即未能产生足够强烈的香味，对应选项C；A项“US$30 billion”指观赏花卉年产值，非实验成本；B项实验并未增强吸引昆虫；D项原文未提及减少产量。","options":["cost US$30 billion.","made the flowers more attractive to insects.","failed to produce a strong enough scent.","reduced production on flower farms."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68344","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5–9\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 5–9 on your answer sheet."},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"9574:68345:10","type":"choice","text":"The theory that plants defend themselves with smells is untested.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But it is clear that the system can have a defensive purpose, as many experiments have shown that the deactivation of a plant’s volatile emission system makes it more vulnerable to herbivores.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：判断“植物用气味自我防御的理论未经测试”这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：用题干关键词“plants defend themselves with smells”和“untested”定位到E段关于实验的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确说“many experiments have shown”，证明该理论已测试，与题干“untested”矛盾，因此选FALSE；TRUE与原文相反；NOT GIVEN不成立，因为原文有直接信息。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68345","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 10–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"9574:68346:11","type":"choice","text":"The smell from fruit-tree flowers is important to farmers.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Floral scent has a strong impact on the economic success of many agricultural crops that rely on insect pollinators, including fruit trees such as the bee-pollinated cherry, apple, apricot, and peach.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：判断“果树的香气对农民很重要”这一说法的正误。\n定位关键信息：利用题干关键词“smell from fruit-tree flowers”和“farmers”定位到F段中关于果树花香对农业经济影响的描述。\n解题思路：原文明确花香对依赖昆虫传粉的农作物（包括多种果树）的经济成功有强烈影响，花香减少会导致种植者损失，因此香气对农民很重要，选项A TRUE正确；选项B FALSE与原文矛盾；选项C NOT GIVEN因原文有明确提及而排除。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68346","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 10–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"9574:68347:12","type":"choice","text":"The population of honeybees in Europe has declined.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This problem has been made worse in the United States by recent epidemics that have infected and killed many honeybees, the major insect pollinator.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求判断欧洲蜜蜂数量是否下降。\n定位关键信息：通过关键词“honeybees in Europe”和“decline”定位到F段关于蜜蜂死亡的信息，但文中只提及美国而不是欧洲。\n解题思路：原文仅说明美国蜜蜂因疫情死亡，未提供欧洲蜜蜂数量的任何信息，因此无法判断TRUE或FALSE，只能选NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68347","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 10–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"9574:68348:13","type":"choice","text":"Applying perfume to orchard trees is accepted as a good method of increasing pollination.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Some plant breeders have tried to solve this pollination problem by spraying scent compounds on orchard trees to enhance honeybee foraging, but this approach was costly and, in the end, proved to be inefficient.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问“给果园树木喷洒香水是否被接受为增加授粉的好方法”，关键词为“applying perfume to orchard trees”和“good method of increasing pollination”。\n定位关键信息：利用题干关键词“spraying scent compounds on orchard trees”和“increasing pollination”定位到G段。\n解题思路：原文明确指出该方法“costly”且“proved to be inefficient”，与题干“accepted as a good method”矛盾，因此选FALSE；A选项TRUE与原文相反，C选项NOT GIVEN因原文有明确说明而被排除。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68348","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 10–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"68339","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1–4\nReading Passage 1 has eight paragraphs, A–H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information?\nWrite the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 1–4 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>a list of food plants which need insects to make them productive <strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong></p><p>an explanation of why a genetic experiment may assist plant reproduction <strong class=\"source-blank\">[2] ____</strong></p><p>a description of current research with advantages for the flower industry <strong class=\"source-blank\">[3] ____</strong></p><p>an explanation of how insects perceive volatile compounds in plants <strong class=\"source-blank\">[4] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"68340","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5–9\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 5–9 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>According to the passage, spices were used in the past to</p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"68341","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5–9\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 5–9 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The Leonardoxa africana tree protects itself by</p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"68342","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5–9\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 5–9 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Which of the following statements about methyl salicylate is<strong> NOT</strong> true according to the passage?</p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"68343","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5–9\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 5–9 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Which factor has made the problems of US fruit growers more serious?</p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"68344","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5–9\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 5–9 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Experiments in genetically manipulating the fragrance of ornamental flowers have</p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"68345","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 10–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>The theory that plants defend themselves with smells is untested.</p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"68346","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 10–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>The smell from fruit-tree flowers is important to farmers.</p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"68347","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 10–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>The population of honeybees in Europe has declined.</p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"68348","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10–13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\nIn boxes 10–13 on your answer sheet, write\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p>Applying perfume to orchard trees is accepted as a good method of increasing pollination.</p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<div><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Scented Plants&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Many plants emit a smell. This may come from the flower of the plant, from the leaves, stem, or even, in some cases, from the root. What humans may perceive as a fragrant perfume is actually a tool used by plants to entice pollinators, discourage bacteria, or fend off predators. Fragrances consist of small organic particles with high vapor pressures, so that a scent compound evaporates easily if exposed to the air; chemicals which evaporate in this way are described as ‘volatile compounds’.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Although we generally think of plant odors as pleasant, many volatile compounds in plants are toxic when eaten. These compounds are used by plants to protect themselves from bacterial attack. Humans have recognized and taken advantage of these plant-derived antibacterials since antiquity, when they were used to slow the spoilage of food. For example, the spice clove could be used in baked goods and prepared meats to slow the growth of mould and bacteria, because a small amount was not dangerous to humans. Before the development of modern food preservation techniques, European civilization was heavily dependent on cloves and other tropical spices to ensure a long-lasting supply of food. However, the long distance from Europe to South-east Asia made these spices extremely expensive and was part of the motivation behind the search for a shorter route to Asia, which resulted in the discovery of the Americas.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Although volatile compounds in plants probably originally evolved to repel herbivorous (plant-eating) animals of all kinds, they now perform a remarkable range of functions. An important one common to many plants is to attract animals which will spread that plant’s pollen. Insects are the most common animals to interact with plants in this way, and most insects detect volatile compounds through the extremely sensitive antennae on their heads. Some antennae can detect an airborne volatile compound at concentrations of just a few parts per billion.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Other plants emit volatile compounds which function as toxins against invading insects, and still others emit such compounds when they have been injured, in order to deter insects from laying eggs on them and thus injuring them further. Volatile compounds released by plants in response to herbivore egg-laying, for example, can attract parasites of the eggs, thereby preventing them from hatching. In this way the plant can avoid the attack of the hungry young herbivores that would have emerged from the eggs.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Volatile compounds in plants can also be used as a kind of currency in some very indirect defensive systems. In the rainforest tree Leonardoxa africana, for example, ants of the species Petalomyrmex phylax are attracted to young leaves because they emit high levels of the volatile compound methyl salicylate, a substance that ants need to use as an antiseptic in their nests; coincidentally, the ants attack any herbivorous insects that they encounter. It appears that methyl salicylate both attracts ants and rewards them for performing their valuable role in deterring herbivores. The web of interactions among plants and animals can become so complicated that it is difficult to detect what the outcome of the release of volatile compounds is. But it is clear that the system can have a defensive purpose, as many experiments have shown that the deactivation of a plant’s volatile emission system makes it more vulnerable to herbivores.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Floral scent has a strong impact on the economic success of many agricultural crops that rely on insect pollinators, including fruit trees such as the bee-pollinated cherry, apple, apricot, and peach, as well as vegetables and tropical plants such as the papaya. A decrease in fragrance emission, due to crossbreeding for fruit size or other characteristics, reduces the ability of plants to attract pollinators and may result in considerable losses for growers. This problem has been made worse in the United States by recent epidemics that have infected and killed many honeybees, the major insect pollinator.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Some plant breeders have tried to solve this pollination problem by spraying scent compounds on orchard trees to enhance honeybee foraging, but this approach was costly and, in the end, proved to be inefficient. One of the reasons for its ineffectiveness was that general spraying of the crop could not tell insects exactly where the blossoms were. Clearly, a more refined strategy is needed; genetic manipulation of scents, for example, would allow growers to regulate the types of insect pollinators and the frequency of their visits.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Such manipulation of scent will also benefit people who grow flowers commercially. Cut flowers and potted plants play an important aesthetic part in human life. Unfortunately, traditional breeding has produced varieties with improved vase life, color, and shape, while perfume has been sacrificed. The loss of scent among ornamental flowers, which have a worldwide annual value of more than US$30 billion, makes them important targets for the genetic manipulation of flower fragrance. Some preliminary experiments have already been carried out, but for technical reasons the scent was present in every part of the plant, rather than being localized in the flower, and the level of intensity of fragrance was below the threshold of detection for the human nose. The next generation of experiments, already in progress, will include more sophisticated schemes that target the expression of scent specifically to flowers or other organs, such as special glands that can store antibacterial or herbivore-repellent compounds.&nbsp;</p></div>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9574&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9575","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Viking Ireland","book":"阅读真题集 22","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test4","part":2,"description":"阅读真题集 22 · Test4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"9575:68349:14","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：the excavation appeared to be simply more evidence of the Viking presence in Ireland；Yet when archaeologist Linzi Simpson sent the remains for analysis, the tests showed that the men had been buried in Irish soil years, or even decades, before the accepted date for the establishment of the first year-round Viking settlement in Dublin.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：为A段选择小标题\n定位关键信息：由段落首句“recent excavation in Dublin challenges long-held ideas”定位到A段，发掘初始被视为维京人存在的证据，但后续测试推翻该假设。\n解题思路：原文先说明发掘被认为是维京人存在的简单证据，后指出碳定年结果显示其埋葬时间早于公认定居点建立时间，证明最初假设错误，因此选项B正确。","options":["Data that supports a possible genetic link between the Vikings and the Irish","An initial assumption about a Viking burial site that proved incorrect","The need for additional data","An insight into the lifestyle of a particular Viking","Doubts about the truth of historical documents","A research technique providing unexpected information","The locations particular Vikings grew up in","A decision to remain in Ireland for longer periods"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"68349","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–20\nReading Passage 2 has seven sections, A–G.\nChoose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below.\nWrite the correct number, i–viii, in boxes 14–20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"9575:68349:15","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Scholars are continuing to examine the texts written by monks, but are also considering the limitations of using them. ‘Most researchers accept now that the raids were not the first contact, as the old texts suggest,’ says Viking expert Gareth Williams.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：为B段选择小标题\n定位关键信息：段落中讨论monks写的文本及其局限性，并质疑旧文献的真实性。\n解题思路：原文对记载突袭的文本提出质疑，认为接触早于文献描述，对应选项E“对历史文献真实性的怀疑”。","options":["Data that supports a possible genetic link between the Vikings and the Irish","An initial assumption about a Viking burial site that proved incorrect","The need for additional data","An insight into the lifestyle of a particular Viking","Doubts about the truth of historical documents","A research technique providing unexpected information","The locations particular Vikings grew up in","A decision to remain in Ireland for longer periods"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"68349","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–20\nReading Passage 2 has seven sections, A–G.\nChoose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below.\nWrite the correct number, i–viii, in boxes 14–20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"9575:68349:16","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：According to archaeologist Ruth Johnson, the Vikings started with sporadic summer raids, but after some years of profitable plunder, they decided to stay, and built settlements for the winter.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：为C段选择小标题，选项H“A decision to remain in Ireland for longer periods”。\n定位关键信息：关键词“decided to stay”和“built settlements for the winter”直接定位到C段末句。\n解题思路：原文说明Vikings从夏季突袭转为决定冬季定居，与选项H“决定在爱尔兰停留更长时间”含义一致，故H正确。","options":["Data that supports a possible genetic link between the Vikings and the Irish","An initial assumption about a Viking burial site that proved incorrect","The need for additional data","An insight into the lifestyle of a particular Viking","Doubts about the truth of historical documents","A research technique providing unexpected information","The locations particular Vikings grew up in","A decision to remain in Ireland for longer periods"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"68349","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–20\nReading Passage 2 has seven sections, A–G.\nChoose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below.\nWrite the correct number, i–viii, in boxes 14–20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"9575:68349:17","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Carbon dating, which measures the age of organic materials based on the amount of radioactive carbon-14 remaining in a specimen, usually gives a range of likely dates for the time of death.；The dates were not what Simpson had thought they would be. ‘These dates seem impossibly early and difficult to reconcile with the available historical and archaeological sources,’ she says.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：为D段选择小标题\n定位关键信息：D段开头即提到碳定年法（Carbon dating），并描述其给出的日期结果与预期不符。\n解题思路：D段先解释了碳定年法的原理，随后用具体数据展示计算结果，最后强调这些日期“不可能地早”且难以与历史资料吻合，完整对应“提供意外信息的研究技术”。","options":["Data that supports a possible genetic link between the Vikings and the Irish","An initial assumption about a Viking burial site that proved incorrect","The need for additional data","An insight into the lifestyle of a particular Viking","Doubts about the truth of historical documents","A research technique providing unexpected information","The locations particular Vikings grew up in","A decision to remain in Ireland for longer periods"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"68349","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–20\nReading Passage 2 has seven sections, A–G.\nChoose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below.\nWrite the correct number, i–viii, in boxes 14–20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"9575:68349:18","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The fourth individual excavated at South Great George’s Street was the most intact of the group, and revealed the most about the lives and hardships of Vikings at this time.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：为E段选择小标题。\n定位关键信息：E段围绕第四个挖掘出的个体展开，描述其体格、骨骼特征等细节。\n解题思路：选项D“对特定维京人生活方式的洞察”与E段详细描述该个体的生活状态和艰辛直接对应。","options":["Data that supports a possible genetic link between the Vikings and the Irish","An initial assumption about a Viking burial site that proved incorrect","The need for additional data","An insight into the lifestyle of a particular Viking","Doubts about the truth of historical documents","A research technique providing unexpected information","The locations particular Vikings grew up in","A decision to remain in Ireland for longer periods"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"68349","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–20\nReading Passage 2 has seven sections, A–G.\nChoose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below.\nWrite the correct number, i–viii, in boxes 14–20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"9575:68349:19","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph F","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The results showed that the two men with the spinal deformity had spent their childhood in Scandinavia. However, the other two had spent their childhoods in Ireland or Scotland\n对应段落：F段\n审题：为F段选择小标题\n定位关键信息：通过F段中“isotopic oxygen levels”测试和结果中关于童年地点的描述定位。\n解题思路：选项G“特定维京人成长的地点”与F段通过同位素测试确定四名维京人童年所在地区的内容一致，故正确。","options":["Data that supports a possible genetic link between the Vikings and the Irish","An initial assumption about a Viking burial site that proved incorrect","The need for additional data","An insight into the lifestyle of a particular Viking","Doubts about the truth of historical documents","A research technique providing unexpected information","The locations particular Vikings grew up in","A decision to remain in Ireland for longer periods"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"68349","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–20\nReading Passage 2 has seven sections, A–G.\nChoose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below.\nWrite the correct number, i–viii, in boxes 14–20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"9575:68349:20","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph G","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Both Simpson and Johnson stress that more excavations and tests will be needed before anyone can rewrite the history of Viking settlement.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：为G段选择小标题\n定位关键信息：根据G段中“more excavations and tests will be needed”定位。\n解题思路：G段强调需要更多数据才能改写历史，与选项C“需要额外数据”对应。","options":["Data that supports a possible genetic link between the Vikings and the Irish","An initial assumption about a Viking burial site that proved incorrect","The need for additional data","An insight into the lifestyle of a particular Viking","Doubts about the truth of historical documents","A research technique providing unexpected information","The locations particular Vikings grew up in","A decision to remain in Ireland for longer periods"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"68349","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–20\nReading Passage 2 has seven sections, A–G.\nChoose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below.\nWrite the correct number, i–viii, in boxes 14–20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"9575:68350:21","type":"choice","text":"The Vikings were aware of the financial benefits of staying in Ireland.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：according to archaeologist Ruth Johnson, the Vikings started with sporadic summer raids, but after some years of profitable plunder, they decided to stay, and built settlements for the winter.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问哪位专家认为维京人意识到了留在爱尔兰的经济利益，关键词是financial benefits和staying in Ireland。\n定位关键信息：定位到C段中Ruth Johnson的陈述，其中“profitable plunder”和“decided to stay”直接对应经济利益和停留。\n解题思路：原文中Ruth Johnson指出维京人经过几年“profitable plunder”后决定留下定居，这与题干“意识到留在爱尔兰的经济利益”完全一致，故答案为C。","options":["Linzi Simpson","Gareth Williams","Ruth Johnson"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"68350","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21–23\nLook at the following statements (Questions 21–23) and the list of experts below.\nMatch each statement with the correct expert, A, B, or C.\nWrite the correct letter, A, B, or C, in boxes 21–23 on your answer sheet.\nList of Experts\nA Linzi Simpson\nB Gareth Williams\nC Ruth Johnson"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"9575:68350:22","type":"choice","text":"The inconsistency in sets of data came as a surprise.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The dates were not what Simpson had thought they would be. ‘These dates seem impossibly early and difficult to reconcile with the available historical and archaeological sources,’ she says.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问哪一位专家对数据的不一致感到惊讶，关键词为“inconsistency in sets of data”和“surprise”。\n定位关键信息：根据“Simpson”和“surprise”定位到D段中直接表达“dates were not what Simpson had thought”的句子。\n解题思路：Simpson在D段明确表示测试得到的日期与预期不符，且她认为这些日期“impossibly early”且难以与现有资料吻合，这体现了对数据不一致的惊讶。","options":["Linzi Simpson","Gareth Williams","Ruth Johnson"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"68350","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21–23\nLook at the following statements (Questions 21–23) and the list of experts below.\nMatch each statement with the correct expert, A, B, or C.\nWrite the correct letter, A, B, or C, in boxes 21–23 on your answer sheet.\nList of Experts\nA Linzi Simpson\nB Gareth Williams\nC Ruth Johnson"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"9575:68350:23","type":"choice","text":"It may be the case that the archaeological evidence gathered so far is being affected by geological factors.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Either there was Viking activity earlier than we’ve realised in Ireland, or there is something in the water or soil in Dublin skewing the data, and both possibilities need further research.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题干问“可能是地质因素影响了迄今为止收集的考古证据”，关键词是“archaeological evidence”和“geological factors”。\n定位关键信息：用“something in the water or soil”对应地质因素，定位到G段Gareth Williams的发言。\n解题思路：Williams指出水土可能使数据偏离，与题干中地质因素影响证据的推测一致，因此选择B。","options":["Linzi Simpson","Gareth Williams","Ruth Johnson"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"68350","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21–23\nLook at the following statements (Questions 21–23) and the list of experts below.\nMatch each statement with the correct expert, A, B, or C.\nWrite the correct letter, A, B, or C, in boxes 21–23 on your answer sheet.\nList of Experts\nA Linzi Simpson\nB Gareth Williams\nC Ruth Johnson"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"9575:68351:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"standards","acceptedAnswers":["standards"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A powerfully built man in his late teens or early 20s, he was approximately 1.70m tall by the day's standards.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问第四维京人按当时什么标准算是高的，关键词为“tall by the ____ of that time”。\n定位关键信息：用题干中的“fourth Viking”、“tall by”定位到E段关于第四具遗骸高度描述的句子。\n解题思路：原文“by the day's standards”与题干“by the ____ of that time”同义，答案词为standards。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68351","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24–26\nComplete the summary below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 24–26 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"9575:68351:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"childhood","acceptedAnswers":["childhood"],"explanation":"原文答案句：His bones showed stresses associated with heavy lifting beginning in childhood.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目说明骨骼显示的压力可追溯到他的哪个阶段，关键词为bones、stresses、dated from。\n定位关键信息：用题干中“bones indicated stresses”定位到E段原文中“His bones showed stresses”。\n解题思路：原文“stresses … beginning in childhood”直接对应题干“stresses that would have dated from his childhood”，因此答案为childhood。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68351","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24–26\nComplete the summary below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 24–26 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"9575:68351:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"spine","acceptedAnswers":["spine"],"explanation":"原文答案句：he had a congenital deformity at the base of his spine\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题干问该维京人下半身某处的遗传异常。\n定位关键信息：用genetic abnormality和lower定位至E段“congenital deformity at the base of his spine”。\n解题思路：原文的“congenital deformity”对应题干“genetic abnormality”，“at the base of his spine”对应“lower spine”，因此答案词为spine。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"68351","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24–26\nComplete the summary below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 24–26 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"68349","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–20\nReading Passage 2 has seven sections, A–G.\nChoose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below.\nWrite the correct number, i–viii, in boxes 14–20 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"68350","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21–23\nLook at the following statements (Questions 21–23) and the list of experts below.\nMatch each statement with the correct expert, A, B, or C.\nWrite the correct letter, A, B, or C, in boxes 21–23 on your answer sheet.\nList of Experts\nA Linzi Simpson\nB Gareth Williams\nC Ruth Johnson","html":"<p>The Vikings were aware of the financial benefits of staying in Ireland. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong></p><p>The inconsistency in sets of data came as a surprise. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong></p><p>It may be the case that the archaeological evidence gathered so far is being affected by geological factors. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"68351","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24–26\nComplete the summary below.\nChoose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\nWrite your answers in boxes 24–26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The fourth Viking of South Great George’s Street</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">When the remains of the fourth Viking were excavated at South Great George’s Street, it became clear that they were of a male who was tall by the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> of that time. Due to strenuous physical activity, his torso as well as his arms were well developed, but several of his bones indicated stresses that would have dated from his <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong> .He also had a genetic abnormality in his lower <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong> .His burial differed from that of the other three Vikings discovered at the site, as no weapons were included.</p>","firstNumber":24}],"passage":"<div><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Viking Ireland&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>A recent excavation in Dublin challenges long-held ideas about when the Scandinavian raiders known as Vikings arrived in Ireland&nbsp;</em></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>#&amp;When Irish archaeologists working under Dublin’s South Great George’s Street unearthed the remains of four young men buried with fragments of Viking shields, daggers and personal ornaments, the excavation appeared to be simply more evidence of the Viking presence in Ireland. At least 77 Viking burial sites have been found across Dublin since the late 18th century. All have been dated to the ninth or tenth centuries on the basis of artefacts that accompanied them, and the South Great George’s Street burials seemed to be further examples. Yet when archaeologist Linzi Simpson sent the remains for analysis, the tests showed that the men had been buried in Irish soil years, or even decades, before the accepted date for the establishment of the first year-round Viking settlement in Dublin.&nbsp;&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>#&amp;Simpson’s findings are now adding new weight to an idea gaining growing acceptance – that instead of a sudden, calamitous invasion, the arrival of the Vikings in Ireland started with small-scale settlements and trade links that connected Ireland with northern Europe. And, further, that those trading contacts may have occurred generations before the violent raids described in contemporary texts, works written by monks living in isolated monasteries. These were often the only places where literate people lived and were especially targeted by Viking raiders for their food supplies and treasures. Scholars are continuing to examine the texts written by monks, but are also considering the limitations of using them. ‘Most researchers accept now that the raids were not the first contact, as the old texts suggest,’ says Viking expert Gareth Williams. ‘How did the Vikings know where all those monasteries were? It’s because there was already contact. They were already trading before those raids happened.’&nbsp;&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>#&amp;Although the earlier dates for a Viking presence in Dublin that have been identified by Simpson and independent archaeologists differ from the later dates by only a few decades, when combined with other evidence, they are challenging the chronology of Viking settlement in Ireland. Since the 1960s, archaeologists have been gathering information about the mid-ninth-century settlement that lay under the sidewalks of Fishamble Street in Dublin. According to archaeologist Ruth Johnson, the Vikings started with sporadic summer raids, but after some years of profitable plunder, they decided to stay, and built settlements for the winter.&nbsp;&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>#&amp;Carbon dating, which measures the age of organic materials based on the amount of radioactive carbon-14 remaining in a specimen, usually gives a range of likely dates for the time of death. The older the material, the wider the range. In the case of the four individuals excavated at the South Great George’s Street site, Simpson found that two of them had a 95 per cent probability of having died between 670 and 880, with a 68 per cent probability of death occurring between 690 and 790. Thus, the entire most likely range was before the first documented arrival of Vikings in 795. A third individual lived slightly later, with a 95 per cent probability of having died between 689 and 882. The dates were not what Simpson had thought they would be. ‘These dates seem impossibly early and difficult to reconcile with the available historical and archaeological sources,’ she says.&nbsp;&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>#&amp;The fourth individual excavated at South Great George’s Street was the most intact of the group, and revealed the most about the lives and hardships of Vikings at this time. A powerfully built man in his late teens or early 20s, he was approximately 1.70m tall by the day’s standards, with the muscular torso and upper limbs that would have come from hard, ocean-going rowing. His bones showed stresses associated with heavy lifting beginning in childhood. Unlike the three other men, he was not buried with weapons. Like one of the other men found at the burial site, he had a congenital deformity at the base of his spine, perhaps indicating they were relatives. Carbon dating gave a wider range for his lifetime, showing a 95 per cent probability that he died between 786 and 955.&nbsp;&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>#&amp;Tests were also carried out on the four South Great George’s Street men’s isotopic oxygen levels. Such tests indicate where a person spent their childhood based on a chemical signature left by groundwater in developing teeth. The results showed that the two men with the spinal deformity had spent their childhood in Scandinavia. However, the other two had spent their childhoods in Ireland or Scotland, another sign of permanent settlement by Viking families and not just summertime raids by warriors.&nbsp;&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>#&amp;The evidence of an earlier-than-expected Viking presence in Ireland, based as it is on forensic tests conducted on a handful of burial sites, may seem slight. But seemingly small pieces of evidence can overturn well-established conventions in archaeology. Both Simpson and Johnson stress that more excavations and tests will be needed before anyone can rewrite the history of Viking settlement, and such work is years away. Williams adds, ‘There are two possibilities raised by [Simpson’s] work. Either there was Viking activity earlier than we’ve realised in Ireland, or there is something in the water or soil in Dublin skewing the data, and both possibilities need further research.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Nevertheless, Williams agrees with Simpson and others that the chronology of the Viking presence in Ireland is uncertain, and that they were possibly trading or raiding in Ireland before 795. ‘It’s a poorly documented part of history,’ says Williams. ‘But before there was Viking settlement, there was this big trading zone in the North Sea. Did it extend to the Irish Sea? We don’t have any evidence to say that, but it could be just a question of time.’&nbsp;&amp;#</p></div>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9575&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9576","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Science and Filmmaking","book":"阅读真题集 22","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test4","part":3,"description":"阅读真题集 22 · Test4 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"9576:68352:27","type":"choice","text":"What is the writer’s main point in the first paragraph?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：They were part of a growing cohort of computer scientists that has become fundamental to moviemaking.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：问第一段中作者的主要观点是什么，关键词为“first paragraph”“main point”。\n定位关键信息：根据“first paragraph”直接定位至A段，快速浏览后找到段末总结句。\n解题思路：正确答案D对应原文“fundamental to moviemaking”，即计算机科学家对电影制作至关重要；A项“极少获奥斯卡”原文未提及；B项“电影奖项对计算机科学家没兴趣”与首段科学奖项重要性日益增加矛盾；C项“美国奖励演员多于科学家”原文未比较。","options":["Computer scientists are rarely represented at the Oscars.","Film-industry awards hold little interest for computer scientists.","The USA rewards film actors more than computer scientists.","Computer scientists are becoming a vital part of the film industry."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68352","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"9576:68353:28","type":"choice","text":"When describing the way computer-generated imagery changes actors’ appearance, what does the writer suggest?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At least, it is possible if the altered actors are not filmed too closely. This is because the difficulty of recreating the textures of both skin and fabric means that the effect is less convincing when seen close up.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问作者暗示CGI改变演员外貌的方式如何，关键词为computer-generated imagery changes actors’ appearance及suggest。\n定位关键信息：用changes actors’ appearance定位到B段首句，通过if the altered actors are not filmed too closely找到定位。\n解题思路：原文指出CGI让演员改变外貌，但只有不拍太近才可能，且近看效果不令人信服，暗示远看效果最佳，对应A选项。B选项“CGI干扰演员表情”原文未提及；C选项“观众期望过高”原文未提及；D选项“科学家期待更可信结果”虽科学家追求完美，但原文未说他们对结果有特定期望，排除。","options":["CGI looks best from a distance.","CGI interferes with actors’ facial expressions.","Audiences expect too much of CGI.","The scientists had hoped for more convincing results."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68353","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"9576:68354:29","type":"choice","text":"What does the writer suggest about the scientists’ attitude to their work in the fourth paragraph?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：However, despite their award, the scientists, with admirable tenacity, continued their search for perfection, as they still did not feel that they had yet satisfactorily recreated the subtle ways light is reflected.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题干问作者在第四段暗示科学家对自己工作的态度如何。\n定位关键信息：用题目中\"fourth paragraph\"定位到D段，\"scientists' attitude\"体现在\"with admirable tenacity, continued their search for perfection\"。\n解题思路：原文表明科学家虽已获奖，仍因未完美重现光线反射而坚持追求完美，体现他们力求接近现实的态度，对应A项。B项\"获得认可\"不匹配，因他们已获奖；C项\"医疗应用\"是文中提及的技术手段，非态度；D项\"进一步资助\"原文未提及。","options":["They were motivated to get as near to reality as possible.","They were interested in gaining recognition for their work.","They thought it could have medical applications.","They hoped to receive further funding for their research."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68354","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"9576:68355:30","type":"choice","text":"What are we told about computerised tomography?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Like classical radiology, it uses X-rays, but because the image is constructed inside a computer using exposures taken from many different positions, rather than a single exposure on photographic film, it can capture fine details that are invisible in classical radiography.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问关于computerised tomography我们了解到什么，关键词为computerised tomography。\n定位关键信息：根据题干关键词computerised tomography定位到原文D段倒数第二句。\n解题思路：原文指出computerised tomography与古典放射学一样使用X射线，因此工作原理与X射线相似，选项B正确。选项A“最近才被医生使用”原文未提及；选项C“电影制作人多年用于特殊灯光效果”错误，原文其他位置仅提及已用于织物但未说多年；选项D“可用传统放射照相设备”错误，原文强调成像方式不同（计算机构建图像而非单次曝光）。","options":["It has only recently been used by doctors.","It is similar to X-rays in the way it works.","Filmmakers have used it for many years for special lighting effects.","It can be administered using traditional radiography machines."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68355","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"9576:68356:31","type":"choice","text":"Which of these advantages does the writer attribute to the current use of computerised tomography?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：These same pieces of fabric, through the use of CGI, can then be patched together to form an entire garment inside a computer, in the same way that a small group of actors can be made to look like hundreds of people gathered together.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问作者将哪个优势归因于当前计算机断层扫描的使用，关键词为“advantage”和“current use of computerised tomography”。\n定位关键信息：根据“current use of computerised tomography”定位到E段，文中描述使用CGI将小块布料拼接成整件衣服，并类比一小群演员可看起来像数百人。\n解题思路：原文明确将计算机断层扫描与CGI结合，使少量演员可被制作成看起来像一大群人，对应B项；A项原文E段指出当前不能用于皮肤，因为危险；C项原文其他位置提及在线零售，但未涉及设计师创造新设计；D项原文未提及时间实用性。","options":["It is most effective when used to create images of skin.","It can make a few people seem like a crowd.","It allows clothes designers to create new designs.","It is practical because of the time it takes."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68356","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"9576:68357:32","type":"choice","text":"The writer mentions Kavita Bala in order to","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：According to Marschner’s colleague Kavita Bala, the technology might have an application in online retailing.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问作者提及Kavita Bala的目的，关键词是Kavita Bala。\n定位关键信息：用专有名词Kavita Bala快速定位到F段开头。\n解题思路：正确选项D依据原文“application in online retailing”，这属于电影工业之外的使用场景；A项“comment on the success of CGI in commercial contexts”原文未提及；B项“highlight the link between CGI and photography”原文未涉及CGI与摄影的联系；C项“show that Marschner’s team are uncertain about the future of CGI”原文并未表达不确定。","options":["comment on the success of CGI in commercial contexts.","highlight the link between CGI and photography.","show that Marschner’s team are uncertain about the future of CGI.","demonstrate a use for CGI outside the film industry."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"68357","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"9576:68358:33","type":"choice","text":"It used to be unusual for university researchers to receive a cinematography award.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 2004 a notable event took place: the academic world met the cinematographic world when researchers from Stanford University in the USA were awarded an Oscar.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题干问是否过去大学研究者获得电影奖是不寻常的，关键词为“used to be unusual”和“university researchers receive a cinematography award”。\n定位关键信息：通过“university researchers”和“awarded an Oscar”定位到A段描述斯坦福大学研究者获奥斯卡奖为“a notable event”。\n解题思路：原文称该事件为“notable event”，意为值得注意、不寻常的事件，说明此前这种情况很少见，与题干观点一致，故选YES。NO与原文矛盾，NOT GIVEN因原文已明确提及不寻常。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68358","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33–36\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 33–36 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"9576:68359:34","type":"choice","text":"CGI is popular among ageing actors.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Films have shown that it is possible to use CGI to make actors look younger, older, weaker or stronger than they actually are in a surprisingly realistic manner.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问CGI在老年演员中是否受欢迎，关键词为“CGI”“popular among ageing actors”。\n定位关键信息：用“ageing actors”定位到B段第一句，该句提到CGI能让演员看起来更老，但未提及其受欢迎程度。\n解题思路：原文仅说明CGI可改变演员外貌年龄，未涉及老年演员对CGI的使用偏好或流行度，故YES和NO均无依据，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68359","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33–36\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 33–36 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"9576:68360:35","type":"choice","text":"The scientists’ success in generating images of complete CGI garments has won them many awards.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Marschner and his colleagues received the Oscar for their work in successfully producing a CGI model that simulates translucency\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题干问科学家生成完整CGI服装图像是否为他们赢得许多奖项，关键词为“complete CGI garments”和“won many awards”。\n定位关键信息：以“awards”和“Oscar”定位至C段首句，但“complete CGI garments”未在获奖描述中出现。\n解题思路：原文C段明确科学家因模拟半透明皮肤获奥斯卡奖，而非题干所述生成完整CGI服装图像；原文其他位置虽提到成功制作完整CGI服装，但未提及获奖，因此原文既未肯定也未否定题干，选NOT GIVEN；YES无证据支持，NO因获奖事实存在但原因不同而无法断定。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68360","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33–36\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 33–36 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"9576:68361:36","type":"choice","text":"It will be a long time before computerised tomographic imaging of fabric is used by filmmakers.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：although it may take some years to be able to use computerized tomographic imaging of skin, for the moment the movement of a virtual cloak or the lifting of a computerized hat should look far more realistic.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问电影制作人是否要等很长时间才能使用织物的计算机断层成像技术。\n定位关键信息：通过题干关键词“computerised tomographic imaging of fabric”和“used by filmmakers”定位到E段首句及后续内容。\n解题思路：正确答案为NO，因为原文明确表示虽然皮肤成像仍需数年，但织物成像已经能用于制作更真实的虚拟衣物（如斗篷和帽子），说明当前即可应用，并非“a long time before”。A项YES与原文矛盾；C项NOT GIVEN错误，因为原文已明确提及织物成像的应用时间。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"68361","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33–36\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 33–36 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"9576:68362:37","type":"choice","text":"For many years, CGI characters did not appear entirely lifelike as their skin appeared plastic.Marschner and his colleagues were the first to apply an understanding of how ____ interacts with human skin.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Marschner and his colleagues received the Oscar for their work in successfully producing a CGI model that simulates translucency; this is when light penetrates skin and then scatters below the skin’s surface before re-emerging.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题干问Marschner团队首次应用了对什么因素与人类皮肤相互作用的认知，关键词是“how … interacts with human skin”。\n定位关键信息：根据“Marschner and his colleagues were the first to apply an understanding of”定位到C段开头，描述他们获奖的工作是模拟半透明，即光线穿透皮肤。\n解题思路：原文说明他们的模型模拟了光线穿透皮肤并在皮下散射的过程，即“light interacts with human skin”，因此答案选A light。","options":["light","transparency","age","use","astrophysics","mathematics","improvement","colour","translucency"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"68362","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 37–40\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A–I, below.\nWrite the correct letter, A–I, in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"9576:68362:38","type":"choice","text":"Their CGI model is based on a novel application of principles of ____, which had previously been applied in other scientific research.","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：the mathematics for the model goes back many decades to the time when it was used in astrophysics.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题干问的是Marschner模型的原理基于何种原则，这些原则之前用于其他科学研究；关键词为“principles”“previously applied in other scientific research”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中“principles of ____”和“previously applied in other scientific research”，在C段找到“the mathematics for the model goes back many decades to the time when it was used in astrophysics”。\n解题思路：原文说明模型所用的数学原理（mathematics）之前在天体物理学（astrophysics）中得到应用，这与题干“原则曾被用于其他科学研究”一致，因此正确答案为mathematics（选项F）。","options":["light","transparency","age","use","astrophysics","mathematics","improvement","colour","translucency"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"68362","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 37–40\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A–I, below.\nWrite the correct letter, A–I, in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"9576:68362:39","type":"choice","text":"The importance of CGI to the film industry has led to the ____ of Marschner’s model by special-effects studios.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The scientists' new model of CGI was so important in bringing digital characters to life that, within two years of their original research paper, all the major special-effects studios had incorporated it into their digital rendering systems.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问CGI对电影行业的重要性导致特效工作室对Marschner模型做了什么，关键词是“importance of CGI”、“film industry”、“led to”、“Marschner’s model”、“special-effects studios”。\n定位关键信息：根据“special-effects studios”和“Marschner’s model”定位到C段末尾，找到“all the major special-effects studios had incorporated it”。\n解题思路：原文“all the major special-effects studios had incorporated it”对应题干中“led to the use of Marschner’s model by special-effects studios”，incorporated意为“纳入、使用”，因此答案选D（use）。","options":["light","transparency","age","use","astrophysics","mathematics","improvement","colour","translucency"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"68362","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 37–40\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A–I, below.\nWrite the correct letter, A–I, in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"9576:68362:40","type":"choice","text":"Marschner’s model has led to the ____ of cinematography.","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Cinematography will benefit from this because, although it may take some years to be able to use computerized tomographic imaging of skin, for the moment the movement of a virtual cloak or the lifting of a computerized hat should look far more realistic.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问Marschner的模型导致了电影摄影的什么；关键词为Marschner's model, led to, cinematography。\n定位关键信息：用cinematography和benefit定位至E段最后一句“Cinematography will benefit from this”。\n解题思路：原文benefit与答案improvement同义，说明模型提升了电影摄影的效果。","options":["light","transparency","age","use","astrophysics","mathematics","improvement","colour","translucency"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"68362","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 37–40\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A–I, below.\nWrite the correct letter, A–I, in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"68352","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>What is the writer’s main point in the first paragraph?</p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"68353","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>When describing the way computer-generated imagery changes actors’ appearance, what does the writer suggest?</p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"68354","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>What does the writer suggest about the scientists’ attitude to their work in the fourth paragraph?</p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"68355","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>What are we told about computerised tomography?</p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"68356","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Which of these advantages does the writer attribute to the current use of computerised tomography?</p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"68357","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.\nWrite the correct letter in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The writer mentions Kavita Bala in order to</p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"68358","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33–36\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 33–36 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p>It used to be unusual for university researchers to receive a cinematography award.</p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"68359","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33–36\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 33–36 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p>CGI is popular among ageing actors.</p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"68360","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33–36\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 33–36 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p>The scientists’ success in generating images of complete CGI garments has won them many awards.</p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"68361","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33–36\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?\nIn boxes 33–36 on your answer sheet, write\nYES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p>It will be a long time before computerised tomographic imaging of fabric is used by filmmakers.</p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"68362","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 37–40\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A–I, below.\nWrite the correct letter, A–I, in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The work of Marschner and his colleagues</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">For many years, CGI characters did not appear entirely lifelike as their skin appeared plastic. Marschner and his colleagues were the first to apply an understanding of how <strong class=\"source-blank\">[37] ____</strong> interacts with human skin. Their CGI model is based on a novel application of principles of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[38] ____</strong>, which had previously been applied in other scientific research. The importance of CGI to the film industry has led to the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[39] ____</strong> of Marschner’s model by special-effects studios. Marschner’s model has led to the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[40] ____</strong> of cinematography.</p>","firstNumber":37}],"passage":"<div><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Science and Filmmaking&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>Academics are now working more with filmmakers who are impressed by the results of their\nresearch in computer-generated imagery (CGI)</em>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Every year the film academy in the USA celebrates the outstanding achievements of the year in a\nceremony known as the Oscars. An increasingly important component of the ceremony is the\npresentation of the Scientific and Technical awards. In 2004 a notable event took place: the\nacademic world met the cinematographic world when researchers from Stanford University in the\nUSA were awarded an Oscar. These researchers, led by Steve Marschner, were from the field of\nComputer Graphics at Stanford. They were part of a growing cohort of computer scientists that\nhas become fundamental to moviemaking.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Films have shown that it is possible to use CGI to make actors look younger, older, weaker or\nstronger than they actually are in a surprisingly realistic manner. At least, it is possible if the\naltered actors are not filmed too closely. This is because the difficulty of recreating the textures of\nboth skin and fabric means that the effect is less convincing when seen close up. The work of\nMarschner and his colleagues has greatly improved the accurate and realistic modeling of both\nskin and fabric. They recognized that one of the difficulties of creating lifelike characters in the\ncomputer world is that, in CGI, the characters’ skin is opaque (two-dimensional) whereas real skin\nis in fact translucent (three-dimensional), that is to say, it is semi-transparent.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Marschner and his colleagues received the Oscar for their work in successfully producing a CGI\nmodel that simulates translucency; this is when light penetrates skin and then scatters below the\nskin’s surface before re-emerging. This is called subsurface scattering, and the mathematics for\nthe model goes back many decades to the time when it was used in astrophysics. Because human\nskin is naturally translucent, it was necessary to be able to create this artificially in order to\nsimulate the soft appearance of real skin. Previous CGI models, which assumed that skin was\nentirely opaque, resulted in characters with a plastic appearance. The scientists’ new model of\nCGI was so important in bringing digital characters to life that, within two years of their original\nresearch paper, all the major special-effects studios had incorporated it into their digital rendering\nsystems.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>However, despite their award, the scientists, with admirable tenacity, continued their search for\nperfection, as they still did not feel that they had yet satisfactorily recreated the subtle ways light is\nreflected. To do this, they began to look in detail at the way skins and fabrics reflect light differently\naccording to their make-up: the exact arrangement of fibers in fabric and the network of fibers in\nskin. Marschner and his team tried to do this by using computerized tomography, which is most\nfamiliar as a medical technique for examining people’s internal organs. Like classical radiology, it\nuses X-rays, but because the image is constructed inside a computer using exposures taken from\nmany different positions, rather than a single exposure on photographic film, it can capture fine\ndetails that are invisible in classical radiography.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Unfortunately, the scientists understood that at this point in time they could not use computerized\ntomography on skin, because a very high-intensity X-ray is needed to show the kind of detail they\nwanted and this would be very dangerous for human skin. They have, however, had some\nsuccess with fabric. Using this new method of imaging, they are able to accurately record the\nthree-dimensional structure of all the fibers in a number of small pieces of fabric. These same\npieces of fabric, through the use of CGI, can then be patched together to form an entire garment\ninside a computer, in the same way that a small group of actors can be made to look like hundreds\nof people gathered together. A garment created through CGI is therefore made up of pieces of\nfabric whose internal structure has been pre-recorded. This means that the way light is reflected\nby the garment can be calculated far more realistically than if the scientists just made a computer\nmodel of what they thought the interior of the fabric looked like. Cinematography will benefit from\nthis because, although it may take some years to be able to use computerized tomographic\nimaging of skin, for the moment the movement of a virtual cloak or the lifting of a computerized hat\nshould look far more realistic.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>In the meantime, according to Marschner’s colleague Kavita Bala, the technology might have an\napplication in online retailing. At the moment, people buying clothes over the internet have only a\nstandard photograph to help them choose their purchases. It is hoped that if online shoppers can\nview items which have been presented through the use of computerized tomography graphics,\nthey will have a much better understanding of what the material the item is made of is really like.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Marschner is now working on the way light is scattered from individual hairs. He says, ‘I feel lucky\nto be working in this niche. I’m a visual person and to be able to spend my time scrutinizing the\nworld around me, trying to understand why it looks the way it does, is very rewarding’.&nbsp;</p></div>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9576&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9202","type":"reading","title":"R1 Mystery Drawing","book":"阅读真题集 21","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test1","part":0,"description":"阅读真题集 21 · Test1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"9202:66377:1","type":"fill","text":"填写第 1 空","answer":"75/senventy five","acceptedAnswers":["75","senventy five"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Silverman怀疑这幅画是达芬奇所作，但知道超过多少年没有达芬奇真迹被鉴定，关键词为“no genuine artwork by Leonardo had been authenticated for more than”和“years”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的“no genuine artwork by Leonardo had been authenticated”和“years”定位到阅读材料A段中关于时间跨度的描述。\n对应原文：over 75 years had elapsed since the world last verified a new painting by the Renaissance master.\n解题思路：原文指出自上次验证达芬奇新画作以来已过去“over 75 years”，与题干“more than 75 years”对应，因此答案填75。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66377","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"9202:66377:2","type":"fill","text":"填写第 2 空","answer":"copies","acceptedAnswers":["copies"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Silverman怀疑这幅肖像是达·芬奇所作，但知道没有已知的什么，关键词是“no known”和“this particular portrait”。\n定位关键信息：用“no known”和“this particular portrait”定位到阅读材料A段中关于历史记录和副本的描述。\n对应原文：history held no documentation of Leonardo executing such a piece, and absolutely no copies of the portrait were known to exist.\n解题思路：原文明确说“absolutely no copies of the portrait were known to exist”，与题干“no known copies”完全对应，因此答案填“copies”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66377","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"9202:66377:3","type":"fill","text":"填写第 3 空","answer":"strokes","acceptedAnswers":["strokes"],"explanation":"审题：题目问在较暗、有阴影的区域中发现的特定风格是什么，关键词是“particular style of”和“darker, shaded zones”。\n定位关键信息：用“darker, shaded zones”定位到阅读材料B段中描述线条和阴影区域的句子。\n对应原文：the highly specific strokes visible within the darker shaded sections.\n解题思路：原文中“highly specific strokes”对应题干“particular style of strokes”，因此答案填strokes。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66377","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"9202:66377:4","type":"fill","text":"填写第 4 空","answer":"expression","acceptedAnswers":["expression"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Silverman怀疑肖像为达·芬奇所作时，知道在人物面部可见什么，关键词为“thoughtful and confident”和“visible on the subject's face”。\n定位关键信息：根据“thoughtful and confident”和“face”定位到阅读材料B段中描述面部表情的句子。\n对应原文：the captivating expression on the young girl's face – blending poise with deep contemplation\n解题思路：原文中“captivating expression”对应题目“thoughtful and confident expression”，且明确提到“on the young girl's face”，因此答案为expression。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66377","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"9202:66377:5","type":"fill","text":"填写第 5 空","answer":"calfskin","acceptedAnswers":["calfskin"],"explanation":"审题：题目问证明画作完成于达芬奇生前的证据之一，关键词是“testing the age of”和“material”。\n定位关键信息：用“testing the age”和“material”定位到C段，寻找关于材料年代测试的描述。\n对应原文：Physical tests indicated that the artist chose calfskin as the canvas – a standard practice of that epoch – and radiocarbon dating tracked its creation to a window between 1440 and 1650.\n解题思路：原文提到物理测试显示艺术家选择了calfskin作为画布，并通过放射性碳定年法确定其创作时间，因此空处应填calfskin。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66377","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"9202:66377:6","type":"fill","text":"填写第 6 空","answer":"hair","acceptedAnswers":["hair"],"explanation":"审题：题目问证明画作完成于达芬奇生前的证据之一，关键词为“braided”。\n定位关键信息：用“braided”定位到阅读材料C段中关于女孩服饰和发型分析的句子。\n对应原文：Analysis of the attire further locked the subject into the 1490s Milanese aristocracy, characterized by intricately braided hair.\n解题思路：原文指出女孩的服饰和“intricately braided hair”符合1490年代米兰贵族特征，与题干“braided”对应，因此答案为hair。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66377","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"9202:66377:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"book","acceptedAnswers":["book"],"explanation":"审题：题目问证明画作在达芬奇生前完成的证据，包括识别出肖像原本是从什么中取出的物理线索，关键词是“originally extracted from a”。\n定位关键信息：用“physical clues”和“extracted from”定位到阅读材料C段末尾。\n对应原文：Moreover, tiny puncture holes along the side indicated that the sheet had originally been bound inside a book.\n解题思路：原文指出画作边缘的微小针孔表明它原本被装订在一本书中，与题目“originally extracted from a book”对应，因此答案填book。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66377","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer."},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"9202:66378:8","type":"choice","text":"In 2010, there were mixed reactions to Kemp and Cotte's research on the drawing.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问2010年对Kemp和Cotte研究的反应是否混合，关键词是2010、mixed reactions、Kemp and Cotte's research。\n定位关键信息：用2010和Kemp and Cotte定位到阅读材料D段。\n对应原文：When Kemp and Cotte compiled their extensive data into a 2010 publication, the response was highly polarized. While some notable experts endorsed the claim, others remained deeply unconvinced.\n解题思路：原文说反应是highly polarized（高度两极分化），一些专家支持，另一些不信服，这与题干mixed reactions（混合反应）一致，因此选TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66378","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"9202:66379:9","type":"choice","text":"Kemp contacted Professor David Wright for his advice on the drawing.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Kemp是否就这幅画联系了David Wright寻求建议，关键词是Kemp contacted David Wright for advice。\n定位关键信息：用Kemp和David Wright定位到原文E段，看谁主动联系谁。\n对应原文：Wright reached out to Kemp out of the blue.\n解题思路：原文说Wright主动联系Kemp，而非Kemp联系Wright，因此题干与原文相反，答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66379","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"9202:66380:10","type":"choice","text":"An Italian art restorer attempted to restore the colour to the drawing.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：题目问意大利艺术修复师是否试图恢复这幅画的颜色，关键词是“Italian art restorer”和“restore the colour”。\n定位关键信息：用“Italian art restorer”定位到阅读材料G段最后一句。\n对应原文：the exact path of the drawing becomes obscure after that point, it eventually ended up in the private collection of an Italian art restorer, whose widow ultimately consigned it to the New York auction house\n解题思路：原文只提到画作最终被一位意大利艺术修复师收藏，并未提及他是否尝试恢复颜色，因此信息未给出，选NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66380","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"9202:66381:11","type":"choice","text":"Research has revealed the location of Da Vinci's painting Battle of Anghiari.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问研究是否揭示了达芬奇画作《安吉亚里之战》的位置，关键词是“location of Da Vinci's painting Battle of Anghiari”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干关键词“Battle of Anghiari”定位到阅读材料H段。\n对应原文：Meanwhile, in Florence, investigators tracking Leonardo’s missing mural, the Battle of Anghiari – unseen since the mid-16th century – have employed advanced non-invasive radar systems to determine if it survives behind a later wall in the Palazzo Vecchio, though conclusive proof remains elusive.\n解题思路：原文说调查者使用了雷达系统来确定画作是否在墙后，但“conclusive proof remains elusive”（确凿证据仍然难以捉摸），说明位置并未被揭示，因此答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66381","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"9202:66382:12","type":"choice","text":"There has been a refusal by most Da Vinci experts to respond to Kemp's findings.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问大多数达芬奇专家是否拒绝回应Kemp的发现，关键词是refusal by most Da Vinci experts和respond to Kemp's findings。\n定位关键信息：用most Da Vinci experts和refused to issue a formal opinion定位到阅读材料I段。\n对应原文：Kemp distributed his comprehensive data to several of the world's leading art authorities, yet nearly all of them refused to issue a formal opinion.\n解题思路：原文说几乎所有顶尖艺术权威都拒绝给出正式意见，与题干“大多数达芬奇专家拒绝回应Kemp的发现”一致，因此选TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66382","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"9202:66383:13","type":"choice","text":"Kemp now doubts whether the drawing was really done by Da Vinci.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Kemp现在是否怀疑这幅画是达芬奇所作，关键词是“Kemp now doubts”和“drawing really done by Da Vinci”。\n定位关键信息：用“Kemp”和“doubts”定位到阅读材料F段，其中Kemp确认了画作是达芬奇真迹。\n对应原文：For Kemp, this physical alignment provided definitive confirmation that the illustration was indeed a genuine Leonardo creation.\n解题思路：原文说Kemp认为物理匹配提供了“definitive confirmation”（确凿证据），证明画作是达芬奇真迹，与题干“怀疑”相反，因此答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66383","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"66377","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer.","html":"<p style=\"margin-top: 21px; margin-bottom: 21px; text-align: left;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 19px\">The drawing&#39;s discovery and early research</span></strong></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">Art dealer Kate Ganz bought a drawing of a girl made using chalk and ink</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">Ganz sold the drawing to art collector Peter Silverman</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">Silverman suspected the portrait was by Leonardo da Vinci but knew that</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">no genuine artwork by Leonardo had been authenticated for more than <strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong></span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">&nbsp;years.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">there were no known <strong class=\"source-blank\">[2] ____</strong></span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">&nbsp;of this particular portrait.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">Martin Kemp suspected the artwork&#39;s authenticity based on several visual markers:</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">the execution of the lines and colors.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">the particular style of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[3] ____</strong> found within the darker, shaded zones.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">the thoughtful and confident <strong class=\"source-blank\">[4] ____</strong>&nbsp;visible on the subject&#39;s face.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">Proof that the drawing had been done in Da Vinci&#39;s lifetime came from</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">testing the age of the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[5] ____</strong> that served as the drawing&#39;s material.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">analyzing the specific fashion of the girl&#39;s garments and braided <strong class=\"source-blank\">[6] ____</strong> .</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">identifying physical clues indicating that the portrait was originally extracted from a <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong> .</span></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"66378","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">In 2010, there were mixed reactions to Kemp and Cotte&#39;s research on the drawing.</span></p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"66379","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Kemp contacted Professor David Wright for his advice on the drawing.</span></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"66380","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">An Italian art restorer attempted to restore the colour to the drawing.</span></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"66381","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Research has revealed the location of Da Vinci&#39;s painting Battle of Anghiari.</span></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"66382","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">There has been a refusal by most Da Vinci experts to respond to Kemp&#39;s findings.</span></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"66383","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Kemp now doubts whether the drawing was really done by Da Vinci.</span></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"margin-top:21px;margin-bottom:21px;text-align:center\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 21px\"></span></strong></p><p><strong>Mystery Drawing</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><em>Is the drawing of a young Milanese girl really by famous artist Leonardo da Vinci?</em></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>In early 1998, a New York auction house featured a portrait of a young woman that failed to generate much excitement among bidders. According to the auction&#39;s reference catalogue, it was a 19th-century German piece executed in ink and colored chalk, heavily mimicking the older Renaissance tradition. Kate Ganz, a local art dealer, acquired the piece for a modest $21,850. Nearly a decade passed before Peter Silverman, a collector from Canada, bought the artwork for a similar sum, suspecting it might genuinely originate from the Renaissance era. Ganz had previously suggested that the creator was heavily inspired by Leonardo da Vinci. This prompted Silverman to consider a thrilling possibility: could this be an authentic masterpiece by Leonardo himself? Such a find would be extraordinary, given that over 75 years had elapsed since the world last verified a new painting by the Renaissance master. Furthermore, history held no documentation of Leonardo executing such a piece, and absolutely no copies of the portrait were known to exist. If genuine, its half-millennium disappearance remained a profound mystery.</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>Seeking expert analysis, Silverman forwarded a digital file of the piece to Martin Kemp, an esteemed Oxford art history professor and Leonardo authority. Fascinated, Kemp traveled to Zurich to examine the work, which was stored safely in a secure vault. Collaborating with Pascal Cotte from Paris-based Lumiere Technology, Kemp utilized advanced multi-wavelength imaging to examine the multi-layered structure of the drawing. This examination revealed compelling indicators of Leonardo&#39;s craftsmanship: the exquisite color palette, the clean execution of lines, and the highly specific strokes visible within the darker shaded sections. Furthermore, the captivating expression on the young girl&#39;s face – blending poise with deep contemplation – seemed to capture Leonardo&#39;s core philosophy that true portraiture must mirror the internal workings and &quot;motions of the mind.&quot;</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>To build a solid case, Kemp required scientific validation that the work was produced during Leonardo&#39;s lifetime (1452–1519). Physical tests indicated that the artist chose calfskin as the canvas – a standard practice of that epoch – and radiocarbon dating tracked its creation to a window between 1440 and 1650. Analysis of the attire further locked the subject into the 1490s Milanese aristocracy, characterized by intricately braided hair. This aligned perfectly with Leonardo’s tenure in Milan, where he frequently painted members of the ducal inner circle. Moreover, tiny puncture holes along the side indicated that the sheet had originally been bound inside a book, likely a custom volume created to celebrate a noble wedding.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>Kemp&#39;s historical tracking eventually yielded an identity: Bianca Sforza, the daughter of the Duke of Milan. In 1496, she wed Galeazzo Sanseverino, a military chief and one of Leonardo&#39;s prominent patrons, though her life cut short tragically just months post-wedding. When Kemp and Cotte compiled their extensive data into a 2010 publication, the response was highly polarized. While some notable experts endorsed the claim, others remained deeply unconvinced, pointing toward the threat of an exceptionally skillful imitation. Skeptics found it hard to believe that such a masterpiece could suddenly emerge out of absolute obscurity without any clear provenance.</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>The missing link arrived unexpectedly from David Wright, an art history professor at the University of South Florida. Observing the intense academic debate from afar, Wright reached out to Kemp out of the blue. He proposed that the answers might reside within the National Library of Poland in Warsaw, specifically within a historical text known as the Sforziad. As a specialist in Renaissance imagery, Wright identified this text as a luxury book produced explicitly for Bianca Sforza&#39;s nuptials – precisely the kind of high-profile event that would warrant a portrait by Leonardo.</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>Intrigued, Kemp and Cotte made the trip to Warsaw to inspect the volume. Utilizing ultra-close photography, Cotte discovered that a single sheet had been cleanly excised from the precise section of the Sforziad where an introductory illustration would traditionally sit. When they carefully placed a scaled replica of the girl&#39;s portrait into the gap, it matched the dimensions and stitch patterns flawlessly. For Kemp, this physical alignment provided definitive confirmation that the illustration was indeed a genuine Leonardo creation that had spent centuries nestled quietly on a library shelf.</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>Historical records suggested the Sforziad found its way to Poland during the early 16th century following a marital alliance between the Sforza lineage and Polish royalty. The individual leaf was likely separated from the binding much later, possibly during a restoration or rebinding phase in the 17th or 18th century. Though the exact path of the drawing becomes obscure after that point, it eventually ended up in the private collection of an Italian art restorer, whose widow ultimately consigned it to the New York auction house where its modern journey began.</p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p>This era has proven to be incredibly thrilling for enthusiasts of Leonardo&#39;s work. Not long ago, the National Gallery in London put on display a long-lost painting depicting Christ holding a crystalline orb. Meanwhile, in Florence, investigators tracking Leonardo’s missing mural, the Battle of Anghiari – unseen since the mid-16th century – have employed advanced non-invasive radar systems to determine if it survives behind a later wall in the Palazzo Vecchio, though conclusive proof remains elusive.</p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p>The validation of historical art pieces is rarely driven by cold objectivity; instead, it is frequently swayed by professional reputation, subjective aesthetics, and the threat of litigation. Seeking to establish a broader consensus, Kemp distributed his comprehensive data to several of the world&#39;s leading art authorities, yet nearly all of them refused to issue a formal opinion. ‘Achieving universal acceptance is a slow process,’ Kemp admits, ‘but I remain entirely secure in our methodology.’ Ultimately, if the portrait is universally embraced and takes its place on a museum wall as an undeniable Leonardo, it is guaranteed to captivate the world.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9202&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9203","type":"reading","title":"R2 An ancient city","book":"阅读真题集 21","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test1","part":0,"description":"阅读真题集 21 · Test1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"9203:66384:14","type":"choice","text":"an example of equipment used by archaeologists to help in their excavations","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问考古学家用于挖掘的设备例子，关键词是“equipment used by archaeologists to help in their excavations”。\n定位关键信息：用“equipment”和“excavations”定位到D段，其中提到“portable magnetometers”作为具体设备。\n对应原文：D段：“they have managed to chart the subterranean footprints... by utilizing portable magnetometers, which are specialized instruments designed to measure localized magnetic anomalies.”\n解题思路：原文明确说明考古学家使用便携式磁力仪（portable magnetometers）来绘制地下结构，这直接对应题目要求的设备例子，因此答案选D。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"66384","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has seven paragraphs, A–G. Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"9203:66384:15","type":"choice","text":"an explanation of why Titris is relatively accessible to modern-day research teams","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目问为什么Titris对现代研究团队相对容易进入，关键词是“relatively accessible to modern-day research teams”。\n定位关键信息：根据“accessible”和“modern-day research teams”定位到C段，该段提到遗址未被后续定居点覆盖，便于研究。\n对应原文：C段：“unlike most ancient municipal centers whose primary structures are buried beneath deep strata of subsequent historical occupations, the ruins of Titris are not masked by overlapping settlements.”\n解题思路：原文指出Titris因被废弃后未被重新占据，其废墟未被后续历史层覆盖，因此现代研究团队更容易进入和挖掘，对应题干中的“relatively accessible”。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"66384","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has seven paragraphs, A–G. Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"9203:66384:16","type":"choice","text":"an account of the evolution of agricultural communities into cities","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目要求找到描述农业社区演变为城市的段落，关键词是“evolution of agricultural communities into cities”。\n定位关键信息：用“agricultural communities”和“cities”定位到B段，该段讨论农业剩余导致城市形成。\n对应原文：The generation of crop surpluses was clearly the catalyst... simple farming hamlets gradually evolved into complex cities.\n解题思路：原文明确说明农业剩余促使贸易和专业化，使小村庄演变为城市，与题干“农业社区演变为城市”直接对应。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"66384","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has seven paragraphs, A–G. Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"9203:66384:17","type":"choice","text":"an indication that the domestic buildings in Titris were used for more than simple habitation","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"审题：题目问哪段提到Titris的住宅建筑不仅用于简单居住，关键词是domestic buildings、more than simple habitation。\n定位关键信息：用domestic buildings和more than simple habitation定位到F段，该段描述住宅内有多个烹饪区、工作区等。\n对应原文：These structures were almost certainly inhabited by multi-generational extended families... Furthermore, substantial data indicates that these domestic spaces served dual purposes as both residences and active workspaces.\n解题思路：原文明确说domestic spaces兼具居住和工作双重用途，对应题干“用于不止简单居住”，因此答案是F。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"66384","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has seven paragraphs, A–G. Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"9203:66384:18","type":"choice","text":"a mention of where a royal residence was located in Titris","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题：题目问提到Titris皇家住所位置的信息，关键词是“royal residence”和“located in Titris”。\n定位关键信息：用“royal residence”和“located”定位到段落A，其中描述宫殿位于地理核心的高地。\n对应原文：At the geographic core of the settlement, situated on elevated terrain, once stood a grand palace and adjacent public administrative complexes.\n解题思路：原文“grand palace”对应“royal residence”，“at the geographic core...on elevated terrain”说明其位置，与题目要求一致。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"66384","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has seven paragraphs, A–G. Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"9203:66385:19","type":"fill","text":"填写第 19 空","answer":"courtyard/central courtyard","acceptedAnswers":["courtyard","central courtyard"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Titris典型住宅建筑的中心有什么，关键词是centre of each typical domestic building。\n定位关键信息：用typical domestic building和centre定位到描述住宅布局的段落。\n对应原文：One meticulously documented residence featured 15 distinct rooms organized around a central courtyard.\n解题思路：原文说住宅房间围绕一个central courtyard组织，与题干centre对应，因此答案courtyard。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66385","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–24\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","maxWords":2},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"9203:66548:20","type":"fill","text":"填写第 20 空","answer":"doorway/main doorway","acceptedAnswers":["doorway","main doorway"],"explanation":"审题：题目问什么提供了进入房子的通道，关键词是“provided access into the house”。\n定位关键信息：用“access into the house”定位到描述房屋入口的段落。\n对应原文：Residents evidently gained entry to the home via a doorway leading straight off the public street.\n解题思路：原文说居民通过一个直接通向公共街道的主要门道进入房屋，因此“doorway”是提供进入通道的正确答案。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66548","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–24\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","maxWords":2},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"9203:66549:21","type":"fill","text":"填写第 21 空","answer":"cooking areas","acceptedAnswers":["cooking areas"],"explanation":"审题：题目问每个房子里的什么数量表明一栋楼里住了不止一户人家，关键词是number、each house、more than one household。\n定位关键信息：用“more than one household”和“cooking areas”定位到原文F段，其中提到multiple cooking areas表明多代同堂。\n对应原文：These structures were almost certainly inhabited by multi-generational extended families, as evidenced by the presence of multiple cooking areas within a single property.\n解题思路：原文说多个cooking areas的存在证明了多代同堂，即不止一户人家，与题干中“number of cooking areas”对应。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66549","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–24\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","maxWords":2},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"9203:66550:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"oval basins","acceptedAnswers":["oval basins"],"explanation":"审题：题目问什么发现表明居民用部分房屋准备原材料，关键词是“discovery”和“preparation of raw materials”。\n定位关键信息：用“preparation of raw materials”和“homes”定位到F段，寻找与原材料加工相关的发现。\n对应原文：Several excavated homes contain large oval basins, which researchers believe were utilized for washing and processing raw sheep's wool.\n解题思路：原文指出在房屋中发现“large oval basins”用于清洗和加工生羊毛，这与题干“preparation of raw materials”对应，因此答案为oval basins。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66550","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–24\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","maxWords":2},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"9203:66551:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"sheep's wool","acceptedAnswers":["sheep's wool"],"explanation":"审题：题目问考古学家认为人们在房子里把什么变成了织物，关键词是“turned...into fabric”和“houses”。\n定位关键信息：用“fabric”和“houses”定位到F段，其中提到“weaving textiles”和“household”。\n对应原文：Among the household artifacts recovered were standardized stone weights, which were undoubtedly used in conjunction with looms for weaving textiles.\n解题思路：原文提到家庭中发现的石制砝码用于织布，结合前文“washing and processing raw sheep’s wool”，说明羊毛被加工成织物，因此答案为sheep’s wool。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66551","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–24\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","maxWords":2},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"9203:66552:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"tomb","acceptedAnswers":["tomb"],"explanation":"审题：题目问每座房屋中有什么特征在今天非常罕见，关键词是“in each house”和“uncommon today”。\n定位关键信息：用“each house”和“uncommon today”定位到F段最后一句，描述每个家庭都有的独特特征。\n对应原文：every single household incorporated an integrated tomb designed to house the remains of the family's deceased.\n解题思路：原文说每个家庭都包含一个用于安放逝者遗骸的“integrated tomb”，这与题干中“tomb”对应，且指出这完全不同于现代住宅规范，因此答案就是tomb。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66552","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–24\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","maxWords":2},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"9203:66386:25-26","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of these reasons are mentioned by the writer in the text?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目问作者在文中提到的两个原因，关键词是reasons mentioned by the writer。\n定位关键信息：根据题干reasons和选项ambitious leaders、desire for social interaction，定位到G段。\n对应原文：These rulers sought to consolidate and project their geopolitical influence... the intrinsic human desire for communal living and collaborative work.\n解题思路：G段提到统治者（ambitious leaders）推动城市发展，以及人类对集体生活的渴望（desire for social interaction），对应选项B和D。","options":["geographical location","ambitious leaders","existence of communication networks","desire for social interaction","knowledge of building techniques"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"66386","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 25–26\nChoose TWO correct answers.\nWrite the correct letters in boxes 25 and 26 on your answer sheet.\nThe list below gives some of the possible reasons for the growth of cities.","groupId":"66386-9203:66386:25-26"},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"9203:66386:25-26","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of these reasons are mentioned by the writer in the text?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问作者在文中提到的两个原因，关键词是reasons mentioned by the writer。\n定位关键信息：根据题干reasons和选项ambitious leaders、desire for social interaction，定位到G段。\n对应原文：These rulers sought to consolidate and project their geopolitical influence... the intrinsic human desire for communal living and collaborative work.\n解题思路：G段提到统治者（ambitious leaders）推动城市发展，以及人类对集体生活的渴望（desire for social interaction），对应选项B和D。","options":["geographical location","ambitious leaders","existence of communication networks","desire for social interaction","knowledge of building techniques"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"66386","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 25–26\nChoose TWO correct answers.\nWrite the correct letters in boxes 25 and 26 on your answer sheet.\nThe list below gives some of the possible reasons for the growth of cities.","groupId":"66386-9203:66386:25-26"}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"66386-9203:66386:25-26","numbers":[25,26],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["B","D"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"66384","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has seven paragraphs, A–G. Which paragraph contains the following information?","html":"<p style=\"margin-top:21px;margin-bottom:21px\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">an example of equipment used by archaeologists to help in their excavations&nbsp; <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:21px;margin-bottom:21px\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">an explanation of why Titris is relatively accessible to modern-day research teams&nbsp; <strong class=\"source-blank\">[15] ____</strong></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:21px;margin-bottom:21px\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">an account of the evolution of agricultural communities into cities&nbsp; <strong class=\"source-blank\">[16] ____</strong></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:21px;margin-bottom:21px\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">an indication that the domestic buildings in Titris were used for more than simple habitation&nbsp; <strong class=\"source-blank\">[17] ____</strong></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:21px;margin-bottom:21px\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">a mention of where a royal residence was located in Titris&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[18] ____</strong></span></span></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"66385","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–24\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">In the centre of each typical domestic building in Titris there was a </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong></span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">.</span></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"66548","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–24\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">A </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong></span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"> provided access into the house.</span></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"66549","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–24\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">The number of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong> in each house indicated that more than one household lived in a building.</span></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"66550","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–24\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">The discovery of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong> suggests that the inhabitants used part of their homes for the preparation of raw materials.</span></p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"66551","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–24\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Archaeologists think that people turned <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong> into fabric in their houses.</span></p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"66552","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–24\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">The presence of a <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> in each house was a feature which would be very uncommon today.</span></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"66386","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 25–26\nChoose TWO correct answers.\nWrite the correct letters in boxes 25 and 26 on your answer sheet.\nThe list below gives some of the possible reasons for the growth of cities.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Which </span><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">TWO</span></strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"> of these reasons are mentioned by the writer in the text?</span></p>","firstNumber":25}],"passage":"<p><strong>An ancient city</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>Today, the silent, subterranean ruins of Titris Hoyuk, a urban center founded around 1500 BC, lie buried beneath the plains of southeastern Turkey. Yet, these remnants speak volumes to researchers regarding an era when a radical concept began to dictate the architecture of global settlements. Mapping the site, a team of archaeologists from the University of California uncovered an array of municipal remnants. At the geographic core of the settlement, situated on elevated terrain, once stood a grand palace and adjacent public administrative complexes, aligning with the standard architectural conventions of that period. From this central node, thoroughfares radiated outward, cutting through various residential quarters. Farther out, past the defensive perimeter walls, lay an extensive burial ground and peripheral suburbs. Upon closer inspection, the research team unveiled unexpected details: the entire urban layout seems to adhere to a rigid master plan. Consequently, one can deduce that Titris, which supported an estimated 10,000 residents during its prime, serves as a remarkable testament to early urban planning, showcasing a centralized architectural vision that feels strikingly modern.</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>Academics have long established that humanity&#39;s earliest cities materialized roughly 5,000 years ago within Mesopotamia, a historic region encompassing present-day Iraq. This early urban development was presumably an direct offshoot of increasingly efficient agricultural practices. The generation of crop surpluses was clearly the catalyst, fostering the expansion of inter-regional trade networks and permitting individuals to abandon subsistence farming to specialize in artisanal crafts like textile manufacturing and pottery production. As the population of merchants and craftsmen multiplied, simple farming hamlets gradually evolved into complex cities. By the middle of the third millennium BC, these early experiments in high-density living proved so remarkably successful that populations migrated in droves to newly established hubs spanning contemporary Syria, northern Iraq, and Turkey. The excavations at Titris, complemented by findings from analogous sites across northern Mesopotamia, indicate that this urgent societal demand sparked highly organized and deliberate civil construction initiatives, which were essential to accommodate surging populations quickly enough.</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>The archaeological yields at Titris offer profound insights into the configuration, structural framework, and socioeconomic organization of these pristine urban centers. Rather than focusing exclusively on the monumental palaces and religious temples that traditionally attract academic interest, the current research team is concentrating on ordinary neighborhoods and domestic households. Titris flourished and decayed within a relatively brief 300-year window, after which – due to historical variables that remain obscured by time – it was entirely deserted and never reoccupied. This abrupt abandonment ultimately simplified the task for modern researchers; unlike most ancient municipal centers whose primary structures are buried beneath deep strata of subsequent historical occupations, the ruins of Titris are not masked by overlapping settlements. Today, the structural foundations of Titris lie less than three feet below the topsoil.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>Even so, field teams working at the site have fully cleared only modest segments of two residential blocks—a microscopic fraction of the ancient metropolis. To date, however, they have managed to chart the subterranean footprints of roughly half of the 125-acre expanse by utilizing portable magnetometers, which are specialized instruments designed to measure localized magnetic anomalies. These structural outlines can be easily mapped because the non-magnetic limestone blocks used in the foundations contrast sharply against the surrounding magnetic, iron-rich earth. Meticulous examination of these geophysical maps, paired with data gathered from standard excavations of representative zones, indicates that Titris was a meticulously planned community constructed in a single, continuous building phase.</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>Excavations along the eastern sector of Titris exposed spacious, multi-room residences arranged uniformly along primary avenues. The precise alignment of these streets and the standardized placement of the adjacent homes, characterized by structural uniformity and shared architectural elements, clearly indicate the utilization of an underlying building template. The thoroughfares themselves had been systematically prepared: workers first carved trenches into the earth, which they subsequently paved using a mixture of river rocks, cobblestones, and discarded ceramic shards. Crucially, stratigraphical evidence proves these roads were fully completed prior to the erection of the residential units flanking them.</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>One meticulously documented residence featured 15 distinct rooms organized around a central courtyard, which was further divided by low interior partition walls to create four independent living zones. Residents evidently gained entry to the home via a doorway leading straight off the public street. Archaeologists note that this specific layout appears to be standard for domestic architecture across Titris, though certain properties represented downscaled iterations of the same basic blueprint. These structures were almost certainly inhabited by multi-generational extended families, as evidenced by the presence of multiple cooking areas within a single property. Furthermore, substantial data indicates that these domestic spaces served dual purposes as both residences and active workspaces. Several excavated homes contain large oval basins, which researchers believe were utilized for washing and processing raw sheep&#39;s wool. Among the household artifacts recovered were standardized stone weights, which were undoubtedly used in conjunction with looms for weaving textiles. However, one distinctive characteristic of Titris domestic life diverges entirely from modern residential norms: every single household incorporated an integrated tomb designed to house the remains of the family&#39;s deceased.</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>The rapid proliferation of urbanized centers and structured civic layouts across ancient Mesopotamia likely reflected advanced social stratification, organizational complexity, and the authority of powerful potentates. These rulers sought to consolidate and project their geopolitical influence, and they possessed the vast economic resources necessary to fund such grand undertakings. The dawn of planned cities appears to have occurred simultaneously with transformative societal milestones, including the invention of writing systems, the domestication of draft animals for traction, the introduction of wheeled vehicles, advancements in metallurgy, and specialized labor divisions. Yet, perhaps the most fundamental, non-materialistic catalyst prompting individuals to cluster in master-planned cities – both in ancient Mesopotamia and throughout subsequent history – is the intrinsic human desire for communal living and collaborative work. Cities have permanently functioned as epicenters of intellectual exchange, cultural vitality, and socio-economic opportunity – arenas where individuals gather to innovate and leave a lasting legacy.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9203&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9204","type":"reading","title":"R3 How to win the World Memory Championship","book":"阅读真题集 21","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test1","part":0,"description":"阅读真题集 21 · Test1 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"9204:66387:27-28-29","type":"choice","text":"Which THREE specific activities are explicitly cited in the text?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目问作者在文中明确引用了哪三种依赖有效记忆的人类活动或日常操作，关键词是“specific activities”“explicitly cited”。\n定位关键信息：用“specific activities”和“explicitly cited”定位到阅读材料中列举具体记忆活动的段落，特别是D段和E段。\n对应原文：D段：“our early ancestors, who needed to remember the exact paths back to safe shelters”；E段：“orators used it to memorize epic speeches”；F段：“He could effortlessly reproduce entire pages of poetry”。\n解题思路：选项B对应D段祖先记住返回安全地点的路径；选项C对应E段演说家记忆长篇演讲；选项F对应F段Shereshevski再现整页诗歌。其他选项如A、D、E、G在文中未被明确引用。","options":["committing historical timelines and milestones to mind","navigating back to a previously visited place","delivering an address or speech to an audience","memorizing structural rules of linguistic syntax","mastering vocabulary lists when acquiring a new tongue","memorizing and subsequently delivering verse out loud","retaining complex equations used in mathematics"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"66387","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 27–29\nChoose THREE correct answers.\nThe author highlights various human operations or routines that depend on an effective memory.","groupId":"66387-9204:66387:27-28-29"},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"9204:66387:27-28-29","type":"choice","text":"Which THREE specific activities are explicitly cited in the text?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目问作者在文中明确引用了哪三种依赖有效记忆的人类活动或日常操作，关键词是“specific activities”“explicitly cited”。\n定位关键信息：用“specific activities”和“explicitly cited”定位到阅读材料中列举具体记忆活动的段落，特别是D段和E段。\n对应原文：D段：“our early ancestors, who needed to remember the exact paths back to safe shelters”；E段：“orators used it to memorize epic speeches”；F段：“He could effortlessly reproduce entire pages of poetry”。\n解题思路：选项B对应D段祖先记住返回安全地点的路径；选项C对应E段演说家记忆长篇演讲；选项F对应F段Shereshevski再现整页诗歌。其他选项如A、D、E、G在文中未被明确引用。","options":["committing historical timelines and milestones to mind","navigating back to a previously visited place","delivering an address or speech to an audience","memorizing structural rules of linguistic syntax","mastering vocabulary lists when acquiring a new tongue","memorizing and subsequently delivering verse out loud","retaining complex equations used in mathematics"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"66387","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 27–29\nChoose THREE correct answers.\nThe author highlights various human operations or routines that depend on an effective memory.","groupId":"66387-9204:66387:27-28-29"},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"9204:66387:27-28-29","type":"choice","text":"Which THREE specific activities are explicitly cited in the text?","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"审题：题目问作者在文中明确引用了哪三种依赖有效记忆的人类活动或日常操作，关键词是“specific activities”“explicitly cited”。\n定位关键信息：用“specific activities”和“explicitly cited”定位到阅读材料中列举具体记忆活动的段落，特别是D段和E段。\n对应原文：D段：“our early ancestors, who needed to remember the exact paths back to safe shelters”；E段：“orators used it to memorize epic speeches”；F段：“He could effortlessly reproduce entire pages of poetry”。\n解题思路：选项B对应D段祖先记住返回安全地点的路径；选项C对应E段演说家记忆长篇演讲；选项F对应F段Shereshevski再现整页诗歌。其他选项如A、D、E、G在文中未被明确引用。","options":["committing historical timelines and milestones to mind","navigating back to a previously visited place","delivering an address or speech to an audience","memorizing structural rules of linguistic syntax","mastering vocabulary lists when acquiring a new tongue","memorizing and subsequently delivering verse out loud","retaining complex equations used in mathematics"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"66387","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 27–29\nChoose THREE correct answers.\nThe author highlights various human operations or routines that depend on an effective memory.","groupId":"66387-9204:66387:27-28-29"},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"9204:66388:30","type":"fill","text":"填写第 30 空","answer":"30 seconds","acceptedAnswers":["30 seconds"],"explanation":"审题：题目问记忆运动员在锦标赛中解码随机牌组顺序的目标时间，关键词是“decoding the order of a randomized deck”和“time frame of less than”。\n定位关键信息：用“randomized deck”和“time frame”定位到阅读材料A段中关于牌组试验的描述。\n对应原文：In the community of 'cognitive athletes,' completing the card trial in under 30 seconds remains the ultimate milestone.\n解题思路：原文说完成牌组试验“in under 30 seconds”是终极里程碑，与题干“time frame of less than”对应，因此正确答案是“30 seconds”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66388","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 30–35\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"9204:66530:31","type":"fill","text":"填写第 31 空","answer":"loci method","acceptedAnswers":["loci method"],"explanation":"审题：题目问当代专业记忆者继续使用的一种历史记忆系统名称，关键词是“historical mnemonic system”。\n定位关键信息：用“historical mnemonic system”和“Contemporary professional memorizers”定位到阅读材料D段，其中提到“This strategy, famously known as the loci method, was invented in 477 BC”。\n对应原文：This strategy, famously known as the loci method, was invented in 477 BC by the Greek poet Simonides.\n解题思路：原文说明这种策略是著名的“loci method”，发明于公元前477年，符合题干中“historical mnemonic system”的描述，且当代专业记忆者仍在使用，因此答案为loci method。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66530","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 30–35\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"9204:66531:32","type":"fill","text":"填写第 32 空","answer":"spatial information","acceptedAnswers":["spatial information"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Simonides设计的古老系统基于人回忆图片和什么的能力，关键词是“ancient system devised by Simonides”和“recall pictures alongside”。\n定位关键信息：用“Simonides”和“recall pictures”定位到D段，寻找与图片并列回忆的内容。\n对应原文：He discovered that our brains are naturally wired to remember spatial information and vivid imagery with incredible accuracy.\n解题思路：原文指出Simonides发现大脑天生擅长记忆“spatial information”和“vivid imagery”，其中“vivid imagery”对应题干中的“pictures”，因此空格应填“spatial information”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66531","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 30–35\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"9204:66532:33","type":"fill","text":"填写第 33 空","answer":"synesthesia","acceptedAnswers":["synesthesia"],"explanation":"审题：题目问患有哪种诊断的个体在尝试记忆信息时会出现不同人类感官的交汇，关键词是“intersection of distinct human senses”和“diagnosed with”。\n定位关键信息：用“intersection of distinct human senses”和“diagnosed with”定位到阅读材料F段中关于罕见神经系统状况的描述。\n对应原文：Shereshevski was born with a rare neurological condition known as synesthesia, where an individual's sensory pathways become intertwined.\n解题思路：原文指出synesthesia是一种感官通路交织的罕见神经系统状况，与题干中“不同人类感官的交汇”直接对应，因此正确答案是synesthesia。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66532","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 30–35\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"9204:66533:34","type":"fill","text":"填写第 34 空","answer":"seven digits","acceptedAnswers":["seven digits"],"explanation":"审题：题目问佛罗里达州立大学项目开始时，受试者能同时记住的最大数量，关键词是“beginning of the Florida State University project”和“maximum of”。\n定位关键信息：用“Florida State University project”和“beginning”定位到阅读材料G段，寻找描述项目初始阶段受试者能力的句子。\n对应原文：Initially, the student could only hold about seven digits in his head at one time.\n解题思路：原文“Initially”对应题干“At the beginning”，“could only hold about seven digits”直接说明受试者最初能同时记住的最大数量是“seven digits”，与答案一致。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66533","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 30–35\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"9204:66534:35","type":"fill","text":"填写第 35 空","answer":"practice","acceptedAnswers":["practice"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Ericsson的最终评估中，卓越记忆表现由认知系统与什么的整合决定，关键词为Ericsson’s ultimate assessment、integration、cognitive systems。\n定位关键信息：用Ericsson’s ultimate assessment和integration定位到G段末尾，寻找对卓越记忆表现的决定因素。\n对应原文：After reviewing the historical case studies of famous 'naturals,' he found that these individuals were almost always using hidden memory techniques... backed by massive amounts of practice.\n解题思路：原文指出Ericsson发现“naturals”使用隐藏记忆技巧，并得到大量刻意练习的支持，因此“practice”是认知系统整合的另一决定因素。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66534","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 30–35\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"9204:66389:36","type":"choice","text":"Achieving the same level of cognitive recall seen in professional memory athletes is an attainable goal for the general public.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"审题：题目问公众能否达到专业记忆运动员的认知回忆水平，关键词是“attainable goal for the general public”。\n定位关键信息：根据“general public”和“attainable”定位到阅读材料A段最后一句。\n对应原文：With the right training, almost any person has the latent ability to replicate these high-level results.\n解题思路：原文说“几乎任何人都有潜力复制这些高水平结果”，与题干“公众可以达到”一致，所以选YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66389","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"9204:66390:37","type":"choice","text":"There is little scientific support for the evolutionary idea that early humans gained advanced retention skills due to foraging demands.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"审题：题目问是否有科学证据支持“早期人类因觅食需求获得高级记忆技能”的进化观点，关键词为“little scientific support”“evolutionary idea”“foraging demands”。\n定位关键信息：根据“evolutionary”“early ancestors”“foraging”定位到阅读材料D段末尾。\n对应原文：Evolutionary psychologists believe this trait was a vital survival tool for our early ancestors, who needed to remember the exact paths back to safe shelters and the locations where they last found food.\n解题思路：原文明确说进化心理学家认为该特质是早期人类的重要生存工具，即存在科学支持，与题干“little scientific support”矛盾，因此答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66390","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"9204:66391:38","type":"choice","text":"The widespread transition to digital tools will inevitably lead to a decline in people's analytical reasoning capabilities.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：题目问“广泛转向数字工具是否必然导致人们分析推理能力下降”，关键词是“widespread transition to digital tools”和“decline in analytical reasoning capabilities”。\n定位关键信息：用“digital tools”和“analytical reasoning”定位到阅读材料E段，该段讨论现代生活依赖数字工具，但未提及分析推理能力的变化。\n对应原文：E段：“our modern lives rely heavily on external technological tools: smartphones save our contact lists, digital applications track our schedules, and internet search engines instantly provide endless streams of information.”\n解题思路：原文只描述了数字工具的使用现状，并未讨论其对分析推理能力的影响或因果关系，因此题目中的“必然导致下降”在文中无依据，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66391","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"9204:66392:39","type":"choice","text":"The dual-category framework proposed by Valentine and Wilding regarding memory types has faced scientific criticism.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Valentine和Wilding提出的记忆类型二元分类框架是否受到科学批评，关键词是dual-category framework、scientific criticism。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的“dual-category framework”和“Valentine and Wilding”定位到原文F段末尾。\n对应原文：Even so, more recent scientific developments have thrown considerable doubt on this rigid binary theory.\n解题思路：原文明确说“more recent scientific developments have thrown considerable doubt on this rigid binary theory”，即科学进展对该二元理论提出质疑，与题干“faced scientific criticism”一致，因此答案为YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66392","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"9204:66393:40","type":"choice","text":"The theoretical conclusions reached by Ericsson provided strong support for the insights of Valentine and Wilding.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Ericsson的理论结论是否强力支持了Valentine和Wilding的观点，关键词是Ericsson、theoretical conclusions、strong support、Valentine and Wilding。\n定位关键信息：用Ericsson和Valentine and Wilding定位到F段和G段，寻找两者观点之间的关系。\n对应原文：F段：Researchers Elizabeth Valentine and John Wilding argue that exceptional memorizers fall into two groups: 'strategists' and 'naturals.' G段：This study led Ericsson to conclude that inherently superior memory systems do not actually exist. After reviewing the historical case studies of famous 'naturals,' he found that these individuals were almost always using hidden memory techniques.\n解题思路：Valentine和Wilding认为存在“天生记忆者”，而Ericsson的结论是“天生记忆系统并不存在”，两者观点矛盾，因此Ericsson的理论结论并未提供支持，答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66393","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"66387-9204:66387:27-28-29","numbers":[27,28,29],"selectionCount":3,"answers":["B","C","F"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"66387","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 27–29\nChoose THREE correct answers.\nThe author highlights various human operations or routines that depend on an effective memory.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Which </span><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">THREE</span></strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"> specific activities are explicitly cited in the text?</span></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"66388","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 30–35\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer.","html":"<p>During tournament trials, memory athletes set their sights on decoding the order of a randomized deck within a time frame of less than <strong class=\"source-blank\">[30] ____</strong>.</p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"66530","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 30–35\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer.","html":"<p style=\"white-space: normal;\">Contemporary professional memorizers continue to utilize a historical mnemonic system called the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[31] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"66531","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 30–35\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer.","html":"<p style=\"white-space: normal;\">The ancient system devised by Simonides was anchored in a person&#39;s capacity to recall pictures alongside <strong class=\"source-blank\">[32] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"66532","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 30–35\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer.","html":"<p style=\"white-space: normal;\">An intersection of distinct human senses occurs when individuals diagnosed with <strong class=\"source-blank\">[33] ____</strong> attempt to retain information.</p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"66533","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 30–35\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer.","html":"<p style=\"white-space: normal;\">At the beginning of the Florida State University project, the subject could maintain a maximum of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[34] ____</strong> simultaneously.</p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"66534","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 30–35\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer.","html":"<p style=\"white-space: normal;\">According to Ericsson&#39;s ultimate assessment, exceptional memory performance is determined by an integration of cognitive systems and <strong class=\"source-blank\">[35] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"66389","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Achieving the same level of cognitive recall seen in professional memory athletes is an attainable goal for the general public.</span></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"66390","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">There is little scientific support for the evolutionary idea that early humans gained advanced retention skills due to foraging demands.</span></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"66391","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">The widespread transition to digital tools will inevitably lead to a decline in people&#39;s analytical reasoning capabilities.</span></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"66392","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">The dual-category framework proposed by Valentine and Wilding regarding memory types has faced scientific criticism.</span></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"66393","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">The theoretical conclusions reached by Ericsson provided strong support for the insights of Valentine and Wilding.</span></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p><strong>How to win the World Memory Championship</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><em>Why do some people seem to have naturally superior memories? Is it talent, a technique or a matter of genetics?</em></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>At a recent global memory tournament held at Oxford University, dozens of contestants faced daunting mental challenges: committing dozens of consecutive numbers to memory in minutes, matching over a hundred names to unfamiliar faces, and mastering the exact order of a freshly randomized card deck. In the community of &#39;cognitive athletes,&#39; completing the card trial in under 30 seconds remains the ultimate milestone. Yet, if you interview these competitors, most will tell you they possess completely normal memories. Neurological evaluations show that this isn&#39;t just false modesty. Their incredible success relies on specific cognitive strategies that tap into how our brains naturally filter and save information. With the right training, almost any person has the latent ability to replicate these high-level results.</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>To explore whether these specialists possessed unique structural variations in their brains, a team of neuroscientists and psychologists scanned several competitors alongside a control group using functional MRI machines. While the memory experts easily outperformed the control subjects when recalling lengthy strings of numbers, an unexpected result occurred when both groups were shown highly detailed images of unique snowflakes—a visual category the experts had never trained on. In this trial, the champions performed no better than the ordinary control subjects. However, the neuroimages revealed something fascinating: when memorizing, the experts bypassed standard memory pathways and instead activated areas of the brain typically reserved for spatial navigation and visual imagery.</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>This specific pattern makes perfect sense when you analyze the methods of tournament veterans like Ed Cooke. To memorize cards rapidly, he pairs every card in a deck with a specific person, an action, and an object. When tackling a randomized deck, he groups the cards into threes. This allows him to combine three separate cards into a single, highly memorable mental scene: the individual from the first card performs the action of the second card onto the object of the third.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>But even the most structured imagery becomes impossible to manage when the volume of data is overwhelming. To solve this, competitive memorizers anchor their mental scenes along a highly familiar, imaginary path. This technique explains why their brain scans showed massive activation in neural areas associated with spatial positioning. By mentally walking through a real-world location they know by heart, individuals can place their encoded images at specific landmarks and later &#39;collect&#39; them to decode the original data. This strategy, famously known as the loci method, was invented in 477 BC by the Greek poet Simonides. After escaping a tragic building collapse, Simonides managed to identify every deceased banquet guest by closing his eyes and visualizing exactly where each person had been seated around the table. He discovered that our brains are naturally wired to remember spatial information and vivid imagery with incredible accuracy. Evolutionary psychologists believe this trait was a vital survival tool for our early ancestors, who needed to remember the exact paths back to safe shelters and the locations where they last found food.</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>Following its discovery, the loci method spread across ancient Greece and Rome, where orators used it to memorize epic speeches so their public deliveries would appear completely natural and unscripted. Before the invention of printed books, training your memory was considered a foundational pillar of formal education, valued just as highly as logic or grammar. Today, however, our modern lives rely heavily on external technological tools: smartphones save our contact lists, digital applications track our schedules, and internet search engines instantly provide endless streams of information. As a result, the World Championships are virtually the only place left where you will find people actively practicing the loci method.</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>This leaves us with a lingering question: is there such a thing as a naturally superior memory? Researchers Elizabeth Valentine and John Wilding argue that exceptional memorizers fall into two groups: &#39;strategists&#39; and &#39;naturals.&#39; Strategists rely on learned techniques to transform abstract data into patterns their brains can categorize, though they usually excel at remembering only specific types of information. Naturals, on the other hand, show remarkably strong recall across a wide range of tasks with very little conscious effort. The most legendary &#39;natural&#39; was the 20th-century Russian reporter S. V. Shereshevski, whose capacity for recall seemed completely boundless. He could effortlessly reproduce entire pages of poetry or long numerical sequences that he had encountered decades earlier. Shereshevski was born with a rare neurological condition known as synesthesia, where an individual&#39;s sensory pathways become intertwined. For a synesthete, a number might trigger a vibrant color, or a specific word might have a distinct taste. Because these cross-sensory reactions stimulate multiple areas of the brain at once, storing memories becomes drastically easier. Even so, more recent scientific developments have thrown considerable doubt on this rigid binary theory.</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>K. Anders Ericsson, a psychologist at Florida State University, believes that anyone can develop these seemingly superhuman abilities through targeted practice. He points to a famous experiment involving an ordinary college student who was hired to practice a standard &quot;digit span&quot; memory test for an hour a day, three days a week. Initially, the student could only hold about seven digits in his head at one time. However, after accumulating 250 hours of structured training, he managed to stretch his recall to an astonishing 80 consecutive digits. The student achieved this by building a strategy around his passion for long-distance running, mapping random numbers to competitive track times (for example, interpreting the sequence 3-4-9-2 as &#39;3 minutes and 49.2 seconds,&#39; a near-world-record performance). This study led Ericsson to conclude that inherently superior memory systems do not actually exist. After reviewing the historical case studies of famous &#39;naturals,&#39; he found that these individuals were almost always using hidden memory techniques—sometimes completely unconsciously – backed by massive amounts of practice.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9204&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9205","type":"reading","title":"R1 Pluto Up Close: A Historic First Encounter","book":"阅读真题集 21","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test2","part":0,"description":"阅读真题集 21 · Test2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"9205:66394:1","type":"choice","text":"The photographic data from the New Horizons expedition offered the most precise images of Pluto recorded up to that point.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问New Horizons任务拍摄的照片数据是否提供了当时最清晰的冥王星图像，关键词是“photographic data”、“most precise images”、“up to that point”。\n定位关键信息：用“photographic data”和“most precise”定位到阅读材料A段，其中提到“unprecedented images”和“never been observed with such exceptional clarity”。\n对应原文：A段：“NASA has recently unveiled a collection of photographs... Prior to this historic expedition, it had never been observed with such exceptional clarity and accuracy.”\n解题思路：原文明确说在New Horizons之前，冥王星从未被如此清晰准确地观测过，说明这些照片是当时最精确的图像，与题干一致，因此答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66394","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"9205:66395:2","type":"choice","text":"Mountainous structures are situated in close proximity to Pluto's equator.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：判断“Mountainous structures are situated in close proximity to Pluto's equator”是否正确，关键词为mountainous structures和equator。\n定位关键信息：用关键词mountainous和equator定位到阅读材料B段。\n对应原文：The transmitted data features a high-definition snapshot of mountains adjacent to Pluto's equator.\n解题思路：原文明确说“mountains adjacent to Pluto's equator”，与题干“Mountainous structures are situated in close proximity to Pluto's equator”完全一致，因此答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66395","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"9205:66396:3","type":"choice","text":"Initial data transmitted from deep space demonstrated that Pluto shares many physical similarities with other solar planets.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问初始数据是否显示冥王星与其他太阳系行星有许多物理相似性，关键词是“Initial data transmitted from deep space”和“shares many physical similarities with other solar planets”。\n定位关键信息：用“Initial data”和“similarities”定位到阅读材料D段，其中提到“Preliminary assessments indicated that Pluto is a highly variegated world unlike any other entity in our solar system”。\n对应原文：Preliminary assessments indicated that Pluto is a highly variegated world unlike any other entity in our solar system – even though its distinctly reddish tint briefly brings Mars to mind.\n解题思路：原文明确说冥王星是一个高度多样化的世界，与太阳系中任何其他天体都不同，即没有与其他行星共享物理相似性，因此题干说法与原文矛盾，答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66396","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"9205:66397:4","type":"choice","text":"The surface features across all sectors of Pluto look virtually identical.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Pluto所有区域的表面特征是否看起来几乎相同，关键词是“surface features across all sectors”和“virtually identical”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干关键词“surface features”和“sectors”，定位到阅读材料E段，该段描述Pluto表面不同区域的对比。\n对应原文：The celestial body is blanketed by vastly contrasting environments: some zones are perfectly level, whereas others are heavily scarred by massive craters.\n解题思路：原文明确指出Pluto表面有“vastly contrasting environments”，即截然不同的环境，与题干“virtually identical”矛盾，因此答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66397","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"9205:66398:5","type":"choice","text":"Scientists intend to conduct a future research project specifically focused on exploring the Kuiper Belt near Pluto.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：题目问科学家是否计划专门针对冥王星附近的柯伊伯带开展未来研究项目，关键词是“future research project”和“Kuiper Belt near Pluto”。\n定位关键信息：用“future research project”和“Kuiper Belt”在阅读材料中搜索，但全文未提及任何未来专门研究柯伊伯带的计划。\n对应原文：全文无直接相关原文，仅段落F提到“Pluto has constantly been struck by cosmic debris within the Kuiper Belt”，但未涉及未来项目。\n解题思路：原文只描述了柯伊伯带作为背景信息，未提及任何针对该区域的未来研究计划，因此无法判断题目陈述的真假，正确答案是NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66398","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"9205:66399:6","type":"choice","text":"The distinct feature known as the Tombaugh region could be detected effortlessly from afar.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Tombaugh region能否从远处轻易被探测到，关键词是“detected effortlessly from afar”。\n定位关键信息：用“Tombaugh region”和“from afar”定位到原文G段和H段。\n对应原文：H段：“The heart was seen from an immense distance away,” Stern noted. “It radiated like a beacon...”\n解题思路：原文说从极远距离就能看到，像灯塔一样发光，与“effortlessly from afar”一致，因此答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66399","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"9205:66400:7","type":"choice","text":"Very little is currently known about the composition of the dark sectors bordering the heart-shaped feature.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问关于心形特征边缘暗色区域的成分是否目前所知甚少，关键词是“composition of the dark sectors bordering the heart-shaped feature”和“Very little is currently known”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干关键词“dark sectors bordering the heart-shaped feature”和“composition”，定位到阅读材料I段末尾。\n对应原文：Flanking the heart on both sides are patches that represent some of the darkest features observable. Thus far, data from the New Horizons probe has failed to deliver definitive explanations regarding the composition of these surrounding dark zones.\n解题思路：原文明确说数据未能提供关于这些暗区成分的明确解释，与题干“目前对其成分所知甚少”一致，因此答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66400","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"9205:66401:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"dark pole","acceptedAnswers":["dark pole"],"explanation":"审题：题目问什么物质可能形成了Charon的什么特征，关键词是“Gaseous or atmospheric substances escaping from Pluto”和“created Charon's”。\n定位关键信息：用“atmospheric substances escaping from Pluto”定位到阅读材料L段。\n对应原文：Charon possesses a mysterious dark pole, which scientists hypothesize might be composed of atmospheric substances that drifted away from Pluto.\n解题思路：原文指出Charon有一个神秘的dark pole，科学家假设它由从Pluto飘离的大气物质组成，与题干“escaping from Pluto might have created Charon's”对应，因此答案为dark pole。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66401","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","maxWords":2},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"9205:66401:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"surface","acceptedAnswers":["surface"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Charon的什么不显得古老，关键词是“does not give the impression of being ancient”。\n定位关键信息：根据“does not give the impression of being ancient”定位到描述Charon表面特征的段落。\n对应原文：The moon's crust is also severely fractured... Furthermore, the surface of Charon is far from being ancient and intensely pocketed by impacts.\n解题思路：原文中“the surface of Charon is far from being ancient”直接对应题干“does not give the impression of being ancient”，因此答案应为surface。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66401","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","maxWords":2},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"9205:66401:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"active","acceptedAnswers":["active"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Charon因缺乏撞击坑而暗示其可能仍处于地质活跃状态，关键词为“shortage of impact craters”和“geologically”。\n定位关键信息：用“shortage of impact craters”和“geologically”定位到阅读材料M段。\n对应原文：Instead, it exhibits a scarcity of craters, hinting that it might likewise be a geologically active world.\n解题思路：原文中“scarcity of craters”对应题干“shortage of impact craters”，“geologically active world”直接对应答案“active”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66401","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","maxWords":2},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"9205:66401:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"collision","acceptedAnswers":["collision"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Charon形成原因，关键词是“formed as a result of a massive”和“with Pluto during its early stages”。\n定位关键信息：用“massive”和“formed”定位到原文N段关于Charon起源的描述。\n对应原文：Experts believe that Charon was generated during a giant collision involving Pluto during its early formation stages.\n解题思路：原文“giant collision ”对应题干“massive collision”，因此正确答案为collision。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66401","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","maxWords":2},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"9205:66401:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"water ice","acceptedAnswers":["water ice"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Hydra的外层主要由什么构成，关键词为outer layer、predominantly composed of、unexpected dimensions。\n定位关键信息：根据Hydra和outer layer定位到原文O段，寻找描述其构成的句子。\n对应原文：'This strongly implies that Hydra's exterior is likely composed primarily of water ice.'\n解题思路：原文中exterior对应题干outer layer，composed primarily of对应predominantly composed of，因此答案water ice直接匹配。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66401","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","maxWords":2},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"9205:66401:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"planetary system","acceptedAnswers":["planetary system"],"explanation":"审题：题目问冥王星及其卫星整体被比作什么，关键词是“miniature”和“likened to”。\n定位关键信息：用“miniature”和“likened to”定位到阅读材料最后一段，寻找描述整体系统的比喻。\n对应原文：“On the whole, the Pluto complex behaves like a miniature, intricate planetary system.”\n解题思路：原文明确说冥王星系统像一个“miniature, intricate planetary system”，其中“planetary system”直接对应题干中的“miniature”后的填空，因此答案为“planetary system”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66401","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"66394","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">The photographic data from the New Horizons expedition offered the most precise images of Pluto recorded up to that point.</span></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"66395","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Mountainous structures are situated in close proximity to Pluto&#39;s equator.</span></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"66396","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Initial data transmitted from deep space demonstrated that Pluto shares many physical similarities with other solar planets.</span></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"66397","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">The surface features across all sectors of Pluto look virtually identical.</span></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"66398","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Scientists intend to conduct a future research project specifically focused on exploring the Kuiper Belt near Pluto.</span></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"66399","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">The distinct feature known as the Tombaugh region could be detected effortlessly from afar.</span></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"66400","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Very little is currently known about the composition of the dark sectors bordering the heart-shaped feature.</span></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"66401","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","html":"<p style=\"margin-top: 21px; margin-bottom: 21px; text-align: left;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 19px\">Pluto&#39;s Moons</span></strong></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">Charon</span></strong></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Due to its substantial dimensions, it is occasionally classified as a dwarf planet.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Gaseous or atmospheric substances escaping from Pluto might have created Charon&#39;s <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong></span>&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">The moon&#39;s </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"></span></span></strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong></span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">&nbsp;does not give the impression of being ancient.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">A shortage of impact craters implies that this moon might still be geologically </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"></span></span></strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong></span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"></span> <span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">It is hypothesized that Charon was formed as a result of a massive </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"></span></span></strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong></span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"> with Pluto during its early stages.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">Hydra</span></strong></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Scientists have uncovered more precise details about this moon, despite the blurry and faint nature of the captured photographs.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">•</span><span style=\"font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 9px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Its outer layer is predominantly composed of </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"></span></span></strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong></span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"></span> <span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">, judging by its unexpected dimensions.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">Summary</span></strong></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Taken together, Pluto and its surrounding satellites can be likened to a miniature </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"></span></span></strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong></span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"></span> <span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">.</span></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":8}],"passage":"<p><strong>Pluto Up Close: A Historic First Encounter</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><em>NASA&#39;s New Horizons flyby captures unprecedented images of the distant world and its satellites</em></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>NASA has recently unveiled a collection of photographs captured as a robotic spacecraft, a compact rocket carrying advanced imaging equipment, completed a near flyby of Pluto – a celestial body situated in the far fringes of our solar system. Due to its diminutive dimensions, Pluto is frequently classified as a &#39;dwarf planet&#39;. Prior to this historic expedition, it had never been observed with such exceptional clarity and accuracy, leaving much of its nature shrouded in mystery. The spacecraft advanced to within a mere 8,000 miles of this frigid environment.</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>The transmitted data features a high-definition snapshot of mountains adjacent to Pluto&#39;s equator, where peaks composed of frozen water tower 11,000 feet above a landscape that appears remarkably youthful and dynamic. Charon, the largest satellite orbiting Pluto, has likewise come into focus with astonishing clarity. Furthermore, scientists received the inaugural image of Hydra, one of the system&#39;s four minor moons. These visual revelations are already subverting established hypotheses regarding the mechanics of small, icy celestial bodies. &#39;The entire system is absolutely astonishing,&#39; remarked Alan Stern, the principal investigator for the New Horizons mission. &#39;This planetary environment is truly extraordinary.&#39;</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>As the scientific data gathered in the depths of space reached Earth – a transmission process that spanned a total of 16 months – the research team commenced a thorough analysis. The introductory findings yielded critical insights concerning Pluto&#39;s atmospheric composition and its geological makeup, alongside detailed observations of its four smaller satellites.</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A Distinctive Landscape</strong></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>Preliminary assessments indicated that Pluto is a highly variegated world unlike any other entity in our solar system – even though its distinctly reddish tint briefly brings Mars to mind. Data from New Horizons also established that Pluto&#39;s physical dimensions surpass prior estimations.</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>Pluto&#39;s exterior, which had baffled astronomers for 85 years, is entirely unparalleled. The celestial body is blanketed by vastly contrasting environments: some zones are perfectly level, whereas others are heavily scarred by massive craters, which are profound hollows in the terrain. The fresh imagery of Pluto highlights a sector where imposing mountain ranges look down upon a topography that seems relatively new – so new, in fact, that it implies the planet continues to experience geological activity.</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>&#39;We have yet to identify a single impact crater within this specific snapshot,&#39; noted team member John Spencer. &#39;Pluto has constantly been struck by cosmic debris within the Kuiper Belt. Impact scars are inevitable. Consequently, we estimate this terrain is likely under 100 million years old ... it could potentially be geologically dynamic at this very moment.&#39;</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>Pluto also exhibits significant variations in luminosity. Situated near its equatorial line is a remarkably brilliant, heart-shaped zone that researchers have provisionally designated the Tombaugh Region, commemorating the astronomer who first spotted Pluto in 1930.</p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p>&#39;The heart was seen from an immense distance away,&#39; Stern noted. &#39;It radiated like a beacon, and since it represents the most radiant and striking characteristic on the planet&#39;s surface, we chose to honor it with the name Tombaugh Region.&#39;</p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p>The two halves of this heart-shaped feature appear to consist of entirely distinct materials, with one hemisphere being exceptionally smooth and the other far more rugged. Inspecting the margins of these areas should yield deeper understanding of ongoing geological processes, and clarify whether the flatter terrains are elevated plateaus or sunken basins. Flanking the heart on both sides are patches that represent some of the darkest features observable. Thus far, data from the New Horizons probe has failed to deliver definitive explanations regarding the composition of these surrounding dark zones.</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>The Lunar Companions</strong></p><p><strong>J</strong></p><p>Charon, the primary moon of Pluto, measures just over half the diameter of the planet it accompanies. This substantial scale prompts some researchers to view it as a separate dwarf planet, forming a binary or double-planet system where the two bodies orbit each other. They revolve around a mutual center of gravity in the open space between them, perpetually locked in position directly across from one another. Charon displays a starkly different appearance compared to Pluto. Although researchers anticipated that Charon would be fascinating, they were entirely caught off guard by the photographs that arrived.</p><p><strong>K</strong></p><p>&#39;It is a compact world characterized by profound chasms, sheer precipices, and obscured zones that remain somewhat enigmatic to us,&#39; remarked deputy project scientist Cathy Olkin. &#39;This single image alone holds an immense wealth of captivating scientific data.&#39;</p><p><strong>L</strong></p><p>Charon possesses a mysterious dark pole, which scientists hypothesize might be composed of atmospheric substances that drifted away from Pluto. Members of the research team have informally dubbed this northern zone Mordor.</p><p><strong>M</strong></p><p>The moon&#39;s crust is also severely fractured – with some of these fissures reaching staggering depths of five to six miles. Furthermore, the surface of Charon is far from being ancient and intensely pocketed by impacts, contrary to what astronomers had predicted. Instead, it exhibits a scarcity of craters, hinting that it might likewise be a geologically active world.</p><p><strong>N</strong></p><p>Experts believe that Charon was generated during a giant&nbsp;collision involving Pluto during its early formation stages, and the resulting debris from this event subsequently coalesced to form the system&#39;s four smaller satellites: Nix, Hydra, Kerberos, and Styx.</p><p><strong>O</strong></p><p>Hydra has now been captured visually for the first time, even though the initial snapshots are faint and out of focus. Nevertheless, project researchers managed to calculate that the satellite spans 27 miles in length. &#39;The surface area of Hydra is remarkably vast,&#39; stated project scientist Hal Weaver. &#39;This strongly implies that Hydra&#39;s exterior is likely composed primarily of water ice.&#39;</p><p><strong>P</strong></p><p>On the whole, the Pluto complex behaves like a miniature, intricate planetary system. Scientists remain optimistic that by deciphering Pluto&#39;s mysteries, they will gain profound insights into how planetary systems across the universe develop and change over time.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9205&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9206","type":"reading","title":"R2 Should top managers be promoted from within the company, or hired from outside","book":"阅读真题集 21","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test2","part":0,"description":"阅读真题集 21 · Test2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"9206:66421:14","type":"choice","text":"an example of the importance of systems in a non-business context","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"审题：题目要求找出一个在非商业背景下系统重要性的例子，关键词是“systems in a non-business context”。\n定位关键信息：用“non-business context”和“systems”定位，原文G段提到“professional football”作为非商业例子，并强调“robust tactical frameworks”和“system-oriented clubs”。\n对应原文：This dynamic is just as visible in professional football as it is in corporate boardrooms. ... other clubs focus intently on cultivating robust tactical frameworks: a structured ecosystem where average players can steadily hone their skills, enabling everyone to merge into a highly cohesive unit.\n解题思路：原文将职业足球作为非商业背景，对比了购买明星球员和建立系统框架的效果，明确指出系统导向的俱乐部表现更优，直接对应“importance of systems in a non-business context”。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"66421","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has nine paragraphs, A–I. Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"9206:66421:15","type":"choice","text":"advice on how businesses can acquire the best people","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"审题：题目问哪一段包含关于企业如何获取最佳人才的建议，关键词是“advice on how businesses can acquire the best people”。\n定位关键信息：根据“advice”和“acquire the best people”定位到文章最后一段，该段以问句“how should a business navigate the talent landscape?”开头，随后给出建议。\n对应原文：If recruiting external superstars is a losing proposition, how should a business navigate the talent landscape? The answer is to cultivate capabilities from within.\n解题思路：原文中“how should a business navigate the talent landscape”对应题干“advice on how businesses can acquire the best people”，而“The answer is to cultivate capabilities from within”直接提供了建议，因此正确答案是I段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"66421","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has nine paragraphs, A–I. Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"9206:66421:16","type":"choice","text":"a medical analogy to a star joining another company","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"审题：题目要求找出包含“明星员工跳槽的医学类比”的段落，关键词是medical analogy和star joining another company。\n定位关键信息：根据medical analogy和star joining another company，定位到E段中关于器官移植的比喻。\n对应原文：Introducing an expensive external star is highly comparable to a biological organ transplant.\n解题思路：原文将引入外部明星员工比作生物器官移植，属于医学类比，与题干medical analogy完全对应，因此答案为E。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"66421","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has nine paragraphs, A–I. Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"9206:66421:17","type":"choice","text":"a claim that stars may not make necessary adaptations when they change companies","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问哪段提到明星员工跳槽时可能不做必要调整，关键词是stars、may not make necessary adaptations、change companies。\n定位关键信息：用“stars may not make necessary adaptations when they change companies”定位到D段，该段讨论明星员工换公司后表现下降且不愿改变方法。\n对应原文：D段中“because of their historical success, these stars are frequently resistant to adopting alternative methodologies”。\n解题思路：原文“resistant to adopting alternative methodologies”直接对应题干“may not make necessary adaptations”，说明明星员工因过往成功而抗拒新方法，不做必要调整。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"66421","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has nine paragraphs, A–I. Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"9206:66421:18","type":"choice","text":"an example of a company that suffered from a misplaced belief in the talents of its senior managers","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目要求找出一个公司例子，该公司因错误相信其高级管理者的才能而遭受损失，关键词是“example of a company”“misplaced belief in the talents of its senior managers”。\n定位关键信息：用“company”“misplaced belief”“senior managers”定位到B段，该段以Enron为例说明公司过度依赖个人才华的后果。\n对应原文：This misconception was vividly illustrated by the spectacular downfall of the American energy giant Enron. ... Enron's leadership was so captivated by individual brilliance that they mistakenly believed organizational intelligence is merely the aggregate of independent brilliant minds.\n解题思路：原文明确以Enron的崩溃为例，指出其领导层被个人才华迷惑，错误地认为组织智慧只是独立聪明头脑的集合，这直接对应题干中“因错误相信高级管理者才能而受害的公司例子”。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"66421","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has nine paragraphs, A–I. Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"9206:66422:19","type":"fill","text":"填写第 19 空","answer":"analysts","acceptedAnswers":["analysts"],"explanation":"审题：题目问研究追踪了哪类专业人士的职业轨迹，关键词是“career trajectories of a substantial cohort of prominent professionals working as”。\n定位关键信息：用“Harvard Business Review”和“tracking the professional trajectories”定位到C段。\n对应原文：New empirical clarity on this phenomenon emerges from an extensive study tracking the professional trajectories of 1,000 top analysts, published in the Harvard Business Review.\n解题思路：原文明确说研究追踪了“1,000 top analysts”，因此空格应填“analysts”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66422","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–22\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"9206:66422:20","type":"fill","text":"填写第 20 空","answer":"working environment","acceptedAnswers":["working environment"],"explanation":"审题：题目问高成就者无法复制成功的原因，关键词为“performance was heavily dependent on specific elements comprising their previous firm's”。\n定位关键信息：根据“specific elements comprising their previous firm's”定位到D段中描述个人成功依赖特定工作环境的句子。\n对应原文：how deeply individual success is anchored in a specific working environment – the proprietary software, specialized workflows, supportive leadership, and institutional knowledge\n解题思路：原文指出个人成功深深植根于特定的工作环境，与题干中“performance was heavily dependent on specific elements”对应，因此空白处应填working environment。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66422","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–22\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"9206:66422:21","type":"fill","text":"填写第 21 空","answer":"salary","acceptedAnswers":["salary"],"explanation":"审题：题目问这些高成就者离职后寻求什么，关键词是“secure another position with an increased”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干“departed their new employers to secure another position with an increased”定位到原文D段末尾关于离职原因的句子。\n对应原文：disillusioned stars frequently exit the company while continuing to chase higher salary, with a striking 36 percent moving on to yet another employer within thirty-six months.\n解题思路：原文“chase higher pay”对应题干“secure another position with an increased salary”，因此答案填salary。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66422","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–22\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"9206:66422:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"team","acceptedAnswers":["team"],"explanation":"审题：题目问外部明星员工对现有同事造成破坏性影响的范围，关键词是“assigned”和“coworkers”。\n定位关键信息：用“detrimental, disruptive impact on the existing coworkers”定位到阅读材料E段。\n对应原文：Secondly, the collective output of the existing team deteriorates due to the cultural friction and deep-seated animosity triggered by the outsider's arrival.\n解题思路：原文中“existing department”对应题干“assigned team”，说明破坏发生在他们被分配的团队内，因此答案填team。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66422","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–22\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"9206:66423:23","type":"choice","text":"The War for Talent had a greater impact than its authors had expected.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：判断“人才战争”的影响是否比作者预期更大，关键词是The War for Talent、greater impact、authors had expected。\n定位关键信息：在阅读材料A段最后一句，提到The War for Talent的初始热潮冷却后又加剧，但未提及作者预期。\n对应原文：Although the initial fervor of this corporate warfare temporarily cooled, it has recently intensified as macroeconomic pressures mount.\n解题思路：原文只描述了人才战争的实际变化，没有比较其影响与作者预期的大小，因此无法判断，选NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66423","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 23–26\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"9206:66424:24","type":"choice","text":"The economic situation of certain countries is leading to growing demand for foreign staff.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"审题：题目问某些国家的经济状况是否导致对外籍员工的需求增长，关键词是economic situation、growing demand for foreign staff。\n定位关键信息：用economic situation和foreign staff定位到阅读材料A段末尾，提到宏观经济压力、劳动力短缺和开放边境。\n对应原文：it has recently intensified as macroeconomic pressures mount; widespread labor shortages, for instance, explain why various administrations are actively opening their borders to international workers.\n解题思路：原文说宏观经济压力加剧了人才争夺，劳动力短缺导致政府开放边境引进国际工人，这与题干“经济状况导致对外籍员工需求增长”一致，因此选YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66424","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 23–26\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"9206:66425:25","type":"choice","text":"Enron failed through misfortune rather than poor management.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"审题：题目问安然公司是否因运气不佳而非管理不善而失败，关键词为Enron、failed、misfortune、poor management。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的Enron和failed，定位到阅读材料B段中描述安然公司倒闭的句子。\n对应原文：This misconception was vividly illustrated by the spectacular downfall of the American energy giant Enron.\n解题思路：原文指出安然公司的倒闭是“misconception”的例证，即公司因错误的人才理念（管理问题）而失败，而非运气，因此题干说法错误，答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66425","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 23–26\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"9206:66426:26","type":"choice","text":"Promoting internally is nearly always more effective than bringing in stars from outside.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"审题：题目问内部晋升是否几乎总是比从外部引进明星更有效，关键词是“Promoting internally”、“more effective”、“bringing in stars from outside”。\n定位关键信息：用“Promoting internally”和“bringing in stars from outside”定位到文章I段，该段讨论如何应对人才问题并给出结论。\n对应原文：The answer is to cultivate capabilities from within. ... Sourcing highly paid leadership from the outside is seldom justifiable, and the systemic damage can be catastrophic.\n解题思路：原文明确主张从内部培养能力，并指出从外部引进高薪领导很少合理且可能造成灾难性损害，这与题干“内部晋升几乎总是更有效”的观点一致，因此答案为YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66426","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 23–26\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"66421","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has nine paragraphs, A–I. Which paragraph contains the following information?","html":"<p><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">14</span></strong><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\"> an example of the importance of systems in a non-business context&nbsp; <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong></span></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">15</span></strong><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\"> advice on how businesses can acquire the best people&nbsp; <strong class=\"source-blank\">[15] ____</strong></span></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">16</span></strong><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\"> a medical analogy to a star joining another company&nbsp; <strong class=\"source-blank\">[16] ____</strong></span></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">17</span></strong><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\"> a claim that stars may not make necessary adaptations when they change companies <strong class=\"source-blank\">[17] ____</strong>&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">18</span></strong><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\"> an example of a company that suffered from a misplaced belief in the talents of its senior managers&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[18] ____</strong></span></span></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"66422","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–22\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Research published in the Harvard Business Review</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>Empirical tracking of the career trajectories of a substantial cohort of prominent professionals working as <strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong>&nbsp;demonstrated that recruiting external superstars yielded three predictable consequences. These high achievers frequently failed to replicate their previous success, largely because their performance was heavily dependent on specific elements comprising their previous firm&#39;s <strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong> . Consequently, a high proportion of these individuals quickly departed their new employers to secure another position with an increased <strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong>.</p><p><br/></p><p>Furthermore, their introduction often caused a detrimental, disruptive impact on the existing coworkers within their assigned <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong> at the hiring firm. Lastly, equity investors frequently reduced their financial stakes in the organization, penalizing the business for its high spending.</p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"66423","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 23–26\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><em><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">The War for Talent</span></em><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\"> had a greater impact than its authors had expected.&nbsp;</span></p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"66424","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 23–26\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">The economic situation of certain countries is leading to growing demand for foreign staff.</span></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"66425","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 23–26\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">Enron failed through misfortune rather than poor management.</span></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"66426","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 23–26\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">Promoting internally is nearly always more effective than bringing in stars from outside.</span></p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p><strong>Should top managers be promoted from within the company, or hired from outside</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>What truly separates one corporation from another is its workforce. In an era where financial capital and technological tools are readily accessible, human talent has become the ultimate competitive resource. It stands to reason that enterprises packed with exceptional &quot;star&quot; performers will outpace rivals lacking such individuals. Consequently, modern corporate strategy dictates that firms must aggressively vie for top-tier professionals, poach them from competitors, compensate them lavishly, and swiftly dismiss underperformers. This aggressive philosophy formed the core recruitment blueprint for ambitious corporations over the past decade, popularized by the consultancy McKinsey in their influential publication The War for Talent. Although the initial fervor of this corporate warfare temporarily cooled, it has recently intensified as macroeconomic pressures mount; widespread labor shortages, for instance, explain why various administrations are actively opening their borders to international workers.</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>While the premise that people are vital is too obvious to dispute, the logical conclusion derived from it&nbsp; – that companies should simply hire the top external talent&nbsp;&nbsp;–&nbsp;is profoundly flawed. This misconception was vividly illustrated by the spectacular downfall of the American energy giant Enron. As a detailed analysis titled &quot;The Talent Myth&quot; pointed out, Enron&#39;s leadership was so captivated by individual brilliance that they mistakenly believed organizational intelligence is merely the aggregate of independent brilliant minds. In reality, these two concepts are fundamentally opposed. Author Malcolm Gladwell observed that Enron placed its faith in individual stars because it lacked faith in operational structures. However, corporate success relies not merely on raw creation: businesses must execute daily operations, compete in real-time, and synchronize the actions of thousands of employees. The enterprises that excel at this integration are invariably those where the operational system itself is the star.</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>The reality is that corporations cannot win the talent war by recruiting external superstars; they can only lose it. New empirical clarity on this phenomenon emerges from an extensive study tracking the professional trajectories of 1,000 top analysts, published in the Harvard Business Review. The investigators discovered that when an organization imports an external star, three distinct negative consequences consistently unfold.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>First, exceptional performance does not easily migrate from one corporate culture to another. In a significant number of instances, when high performers relocated to a new employer, their productivity plummeted immediately, occasionally never returning to baseline levels. Many observers fail to appreciate how deeply individual success is anchored in a specific working environment –&nbsp;the proprietary software, specialized workflows, supportive leadership, and institutional knowledge that cannot be packed into a briefcase and carried to a new firm. Furthermore, because of their historical success, these stars are frequently resistant to adopting alternative methodologies and alienate the very colleagues—whom they now implicitly rely upon&nbsp;&nbsp;–&nbsp;capable of guiding them. As a result, disillusioned stars frequently exit the company while continuing to chase higher salary, with a striking 36 percent moving on to yet another employer within thirty-six months.</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>Secondly, the collective output of the existing team deteriorates due to the cultural friction and deep-seated animosity triggered by the outsider&#39;s arrival. Introducing an expensive external star is highly comparable to a biological organ transplant. The newly introduced organ can compromise surrounding tissues by redirecting the body&#39;s primary blood supply, causing neighboring organs to malfunction or fail completely, or prompting the host body to reject the transplant entirely.</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>Thirdly, the corporation&#39;s equity value typically drops as shareholders divest from the stock, effectively penalizing the company for what is perceived as reckless expenditure on a single high-priced executive. This outcome is highly paradoxical, given that the original motivation for importing external talent is almost always to boost shareholder value and drive the stock price upward.</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>It is a common platitude that exceptional individuals construct an organization; in reality, the structure of an organization constructs its individuals. This dynamic is just as visible in professional football as it is in corporate boardrooms. Certain football franchises spend exorbitant sums purchasing world-class players, only to find the resulting squad performs far below its theoretical potential. Conversely, other clubs focus intently on cultivating robust tactical frameworks: a structured ecosystem where average players can steadily hone their skills, enabling everyone to merge into a highly cohesive unit. These system-oriented clubs regularly outperform their star-studded competitors. Similarly, a specialized study analyzing the returns generated by fund managers revealed that a mere 30 percent of the variance in investment performance was attributable to individual talent, whereas a commanding 70 percent was dictated by the firm-specific environment.</p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p>These findings come as no surprise to experts well-versed in organizational systems theory. W. Edwards Deming, the renowned management theorist, frequently asserted that blaming workers was futile when roughly 90 percent of all performance variance stems directly from the systemic architecture within which they operate. Long-term, sustainable optimization, he argued, is never achieved by trying to elevate individual cognitive capacities, but rather by accelerating the collective learning capacity of the organization as a whole.</p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p>If recruiting external superstars is a losing proposition, how should a business navigate the talent landscape? The answer is to cultivate capabilities from within. Select enterprises excel not only at developing high achievers internally but also at retaining them over the long haul. Because these firms maintain a sophisticated understanding of the interconnected relationship between the individual and the system, they retain their top performers for extended periods without needing to offer unsustainable compensation packages. The superstar recruitment model is undeniably alluring&nbsp;&nbsp;–&nbsp;for the chosen few. However, companies that adopt it rarely reap the rewards they envision. Sourcing highly paid leadership from the outside is seldom justifiable, and the systemic damage can be catastrophic.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9206&scene=%E7%BB%8F%E8%90%A5%E7%AE%A1%E7%90%86&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9207","type":"reading","title":"R3 Linguistic diversity","book":"阅读真题集 21","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test2","part":0,"description":"阅读真题集 21 · Test2 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"9207:66402:27","type":"choice","text":"The Onge language has a particularly poor chance of survival.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Onge语言是否生存机会特别差，关键词是Onge language、poor chance of survival。\n定位关键信息：用Onge定位到阅读材料A段，寻找关于其生存前景的描述。\n对应原文：its survival prospects are arguably sounder than those of Chipewyan in Canada\n解题思路：原文明确说Onge的生存前景比Chipewyan更稳固，与题干“特别差”矛盾，因此选NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66402","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"9207:66403:28","type":"choice","text":"Most linguists oppose the idea of a single global language.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"审题：题目问大多数语言学家是否反对单一全球语言的观点，关键词是“most linguists oppose”和“single global language”。\n定位关键信息：用“most linguists”和“single global language”定位到阅读材料B段。\n对应原文：Nonetheless, the overwhelming consensus among language specialists is that linguistic variety is fundamentally indispensable to human culture.\n解题思路：原文说语言专家压倒性共识是语言多样性对人类文化不可或缺，这与题干中“大多数语言学家反对单一全球语言”一致，因此答案为YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66403","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"9207:66404:29","type":"choice","text":"Many citizens of the Roman Empire chose to become Latin speakers.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"审题：题目问罗马帝国许多公民是否选择成为拉丁语使用者，关键词是“citizens of the Roman Empire”和“chose to become Latin speakers”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干关键词“Roman Empire”和“Latin”定位到阅读材料F段，寻找关于公民自愿学习拉丁语的描述。\n对应原文：Tremendous socio-economic prestige was tied to Latin; it operated as the exclusive language of commerce and state administration, prompting ambitious individuals to learn it voluntarily to achieve social mobility.\n解题思路：原文明确提到“ambitious individuals to learn it voluntarily”，即公民自愿学习拉丁语以获取社会流动性，与题干“chose to become Latin speakers”一致，因此答案为YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66404","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"9207:66405:30","type":"choice","text":"Majority languages such as Spanish and English are now spreading faster within smaller communities than larger ones.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：题目问“西班牙语和英语等主流语言在较小社区中传播速度是否比在较大社区中更快”，关键词是“majority languages”、“spreading faster”、“smaller communities”和“larger ones”。\n定位关键信息：用“spreading faster”和“smaller communities”定位到阅读材料H段，该段讨论主流语言通过媒体渗透到偏远社区。\n对应原文：H段：“In recent decades, industrial mass media structures have accelerated this homogenization, driving dominant metropolitan languages like English and Spanish past urban boundaries and deep into isolated communities.”\n解题思路：原文只说主流语言传播到偏远社区，但未比较传播速度在大小社区间的差异，因此题目信息在文中无依据，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66405","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"9207:66406:31","type":"choice","text":"There is a greater proportion of English used on the internet nowadays than in the 1990s.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"审题：题目问现在互联网上英语的使用比例是否比1990年代更高，关键词是greater proportion of English、internet、nowadays、1990s。\n定位关键信息：用internet、1990s、English定位到阅读材料I段，该段讨论互联网对语言多样性的影响。\n对应原文：'When the internet expanded exponentially during the mid-1990s, many cultural observers predicted it would deliver the final blow to vulnerable languages. Because early digital infrastructure required literacy in English, it threatened to hasten the collapse of minority speech. However, these anxieties ultimately proved incorrect, as the linguistic variety displayed across the web expanded dramatically over the subsequent decades.'\n解题思路：原文指出1990年代互联网早期英语占主导，但随后几十年网络语言多样性大幅增加，意味着英语比例下降而非上升，因此答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66406","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"9207:66407:32","type":"choice","text":"Disappearing languages in today's globalised world\nIf everybody spoke the same language, whether Spanish, English or Chinese, there would certainly be less chance of ____ between people. But would society suffer if there were one global language? Experts agree that it would.","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"审题：题目问如果全世界都说同一种语言，人们之间什么会减少，关键词是“less chance of”和“between people”。\n定位关键信息：用“less chance of”和“between people”定位到原文B段中描述单一语言优势的句子。\n对应原文：Such a shift could foster greater global cohesion and would undoubtedly minimize the likelihood of mutual incomprehension when exchanging complex concepts.\n解题思路：原文“minimize the likelihood of mutual incomprehension”对应题干“less chance of misunderstandings”，因此正确答案是I（misunderstandings）。","options":["ideas","speakers","connections","surroundings","families","occupations","relationship","word","misunderstandings"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"66407","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32–35\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"9207:66407:33","type":"choice","text":"According to Marcus Colchester, people's use of native languages is key to how they relate to their ____ .","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Marcus Colchester认为人们使用母语如何影响他们与什么的关系，关键词是“relate to”和“their”。\n定位关键信息：用“Marcus Colchester”和“relate to”定位到C段，寻找描述人与环境关系的句子。\n对应原文：An individual's core identity and their cognitive relationship with the natural world are fundamentally structured by the unique categories embedded within their ancestral speech.\n解题思路：原文中“cognitive relationship with the natural world”对应“relate to their surroundings”，因此正确答案是D（surroundings）。","options":["ideas","speakers","connections","surroundings","families","occupations","relationship","word","misunderstandings"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"66407","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32–35\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"9207:66407:34","type":"choice","text":"He also emphasises the link between indigenous people's traditional ____ and the recounting of the myths and folk tales which are integral to their sense of identity.","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"审题：题目问土著人传统什么与讲述神话和民间故事之间的联系，关键词是traditional、recounting of myths and folk tales、integral to identity。\n定位关键信息：根据关键词traditional和myths and folk tales定位到原文C段，其中提到hunting, fishing, agricultural work与ancestral narratives, spiritual entities, mythic chronicles相关。\n对应原文：Everyday survival tasks, including hunting, fishing, and agricultural work, are intimately interwoven with ancestral narratives, spiritual entities, and mythic chronicles that define the very fabric of their community.\n解题思路：原文中“Everyday survival tasks”对应题干中的“traditional”，而“hunting, fishing, and agricultural work”属于传统职业（occupations），因此正确答案是F：occupations。","options":["ideas","speakers","connections","surroundings","families","occupations","relationship","word","misunderstandings"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"66407","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32–35\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"9207:66407:35","type":"choice","text":"Louisa Maffi describes how loss of language diversity leads to a loss of collective human knowledge, so there could be fewer ____ available to help solve problems in the world.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题：题目问语言多样性丧失导致集体人类知识减少，从而可用于解决世界问题的什么更少，关键词是“collective human knowledge”和“solve problems”。\n定位关键信息：用“Louisa Maffi”和“solve problems”定位到D段。\n对应原文：With the extinction of each tongue, we lose a unique storehouse of human observation, moral values, and cultural philosophies that offer distinct, alternative frameworks for resolving structural human dilemmas.\n解题思路：原文指出每种语言消失会失去独特的知识库，这些知识提供解决人类困境的框架，与“ideas”（想法）对应，即更少的想法可用于解决问题。","options":["ideas","speakers","connections","surroundings","families","occupations","relationship","word","misunderstandings"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"66407","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32–35\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"9207:66408:36","type":"choice","text":"In the first paragraph, the author highlights the current statuses of the Onge and Chipewyan tongues primarily to emphasize","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问第一段作者用Onge和Chipewyan语言的现状主要为了强调什么，关键词是“current statuses”和“emphasize”。\n定位关键信息：根据“Onge”和“Chipewyan”定位到第一段后半部分。\n对应原文：For instance, on South Andaman Island, the Onge tongue is maintained by fewer than 100 individuals; yet, it functions as the exclusive medium of daily life...its survival prospects are arguably sounder than those of Chipewyan in Canada, where the affiliated ethnic group exceeds 4,000 members, but the younger generation has largely abandoned its active use.\n解题思路：原文通过对比Onge（使用者少但活力强）和Chipewyan（使用者多但活力弱），说明仅凭使用者数量无法判断语言长期生存能力，即诊断语言长期可行性时存在内在复杂性，对应D选项。","options":["the primary variables used to calculate how endangered a speech system is.","alternative analytical systems for assessing data regarding vulnerable tongues.","distinct socioeconomic mechanisms that place a minority speech system in jeopardy.","the inherent complexities encountered when diagnosing a language's long-term viability."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"66408","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"9207:66409:37","type":"choice","text":"What historical parallel does Nicholas Ostler draw between the ancient Roman era and our contemporary world?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Nicholas Ostler在古罗马时代与当代世界之间指出了什么历史平行现象，关键词是historical parallel、ancient Roman era、contemporary world。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的Nicholas Ostler和historical parallel定位到阅读材料F段，该段讨论罗马帝国与现代的对比。\n对应原文：Ostler notes that identical socioeconomic forces are squeezing minority systems today. The Romans successfully reorganized populations into dense, centralized networks – a process we characterize today as urbanization.\n解题思路：原文指出罗马人将人口重组为密集、集中的网络（即城市化），而现代相同的社会经济力量（即城市化）正在挤压少数语言系统，这与选项B“向更大城市环境聚集的人口趋势”一致。","options":["The worldwide integration of commercial market economies.","A demographic trend toward congregating within larger urban environments.","The aggressive hostility of state authorities toward minority communication systems.","The rapid timeline over which localized communication systems fall into total disuse."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"66409","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"9207:66410:38","type":"choice","text":"According to Louisa Maffi, a major misconception held by many individuals is that","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Louisa Maffi认为许多人持有的一个主要误解是什么，关键词是major misconception。\n定位关键信息：根据人名Louisa Maffi和关键词misconception定位到G段，该段讨论了她对政府政策和公众看法的批评。\n对应原文：It relies on a deeply flawed 'either/or' paradigm: a citizen must either preserve their native tongue and accept total marginalization from national life, or abandon their linguistic heritage to adopt the dominant language.\n解题思路：原文指出Maffi认为存在一个错误的“非此即彼”模式，即公民要么保留母语并边缘化，要么放弃母语采用主流语言，这与选项D“公民被迫在保留母语或掌握国家语言之间选择”完全对应，而其他选项未在Maffi观点中体现。","options":["obtaining institutional education is inherently more difficult for minority speakers.","command of a majority language guarantees superior integration into national politics.","central ruling bodies are actively and explicitly trying to eliminate local communication systems","citizens are forced to select between maintaining native speech or mastering the national tongue."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"66410","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"9207:66411:39","type":"choice","text":"Which specific obstacle confronting minority speech communities is highlighted in the eighth paragraph?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题：问第八段中少数族裔语言社区面临的具体障碍，关键词是obstacle、minority speech communities、eighth paragraph。\n定位关键信息：根据第八段（paragraph H）和关键词obstacle、youth、psychological attitudes定位到描述代际心理隔阂的内容。\n对应原文：In many remote areas, youths utilize their traditional speech when communicating with community elders, but pivot exclusively to English when interacting among peers. ... it becomes incredibly difficult for younger generations to find a practical reason to appreciate or retain their own linguistic heritage.\n解题思路：原文指出年轻人只在和长辈交流时用传统语言，同龄人之间只用英语，且难以找到理由珍视自身语言遗产，这对应选项A中年轻人对母语遗产的心理态度（psychological attitudes），即缺乏认同和兴趣。","options":["The psychological attitudes of the youth toward their native linguistic heritage.","A total breakdown in vital communication pathways between older and younger cohorts.","Resentment from community elders regarding the linguistic preferences of their children.","Stark generational discrepancies in technical literacy required to access digital networks."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"66411","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"9207:66412:40","type":"choice","text":"According to Peter Austin, the primary benefit that digital networks yield for endangered language communities is","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：问Peter Austin认为数字网络对濒危语言社区的主要好处，关键词是primary benefit、digital networks、endangered language communities。\n定位关键信息：用Peter Austin和digital networks定位到I段，找其观点中关于benefit的描述。\n对应原文：'Unlike traditional television networks or radio broadcasts, the internet is not monopolized by massive corporate conglomerates. Anyone with a network connection and basic digital tools can generate, publish, and distribute written content, news, and multimedia elements without restriction.'\n解题思路：原文指出互联网不被大企业垄断，任何人可自由发布内容，对应选项B的operational independence and lack of corporate oversight，即操作独立且无企业监管，这是主要好处。","options":["the multi-faceted multimedia channels available for archiving data.","the operational independence and lack of corporate oversight enjoyed by creators.","the immense geographical distribution networks that digital platforms command.","the highly varied demographic spectrum of individuals who can view the material."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"66412","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose the correct answer."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"66402","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">The Onge language has a particularly poor chance of survival.</span></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"66403","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">Most linguists oppose the idea of a single global language.&nbsp;</span></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"66404","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">Many citizens of the Roman Empire chose to become Latin speakers.&nbsp;</span></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"66405","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">Majority languages such as Spanish and English are now spreading faster within smaller communities than larger ones.</span></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"66406","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">There is a greater proportion of English used on the internet nowadays than in the 1990s.</span></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"66407","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32–35\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"66408","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">In the first paragraph, the author highlights the current statuses of the Onge and Chipewyan tongues primarily to emphasize</span></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"66409","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">What historical parallel does Nicholas Ostler draw between the ancient Roman era and our contemporary world?</span></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"66410","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">&nbsp;According to Louisa Maffi, a major misconception held by many individuals is that</span></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"66411","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">Which specific obstacle confronting minority speech communities is highlighted in the eighth paragraph?</span></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"66412","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36–40\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">&nbsp;According to Peter Austin, the primary benefit that digital networks yield for endangered language communities is</span></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p><strong>Linguistic diversity</strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>Well over half of the world&#39;s current spoken tongues face an uncertain future, yet an unexpected digital savior might be emerging. What parameters define a tongue as being in jeopardy? As a general benchmark, any speech system with fewer than 10,000 active users is considered vulnerable. However, the sheer size of a speaker community does not always reflect its true vitality. For instance, on South Andaman Island, the Onge tongue is maintained by fewer than 100 individuals; yet, it functions as the exclusive medium of daily life for that community and, crucially, is learned naturally by all native children. As a result, its survival prospects are arguably sounder than those of Chipewyan in Canada, where the affiliated ethnic group exceeds 4,000 members, but the younger generation has largely abandoned its active use.</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>In our intensely integrated modern era, a pragmatic argument is often made that humanity would benefit immensely from consolidating around a singular global medium, such as Mandarin, English, or Spanish. Such a shift could foster greater global cohesion and would undoubtedly minimize the likelihood of mutual incomprehension when exchanging complex concepts. Nonetheless, the overwhelming consensus among language specialists is that linguistic variety is fundamentally indispensable to human culture.</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>&#39;An individual&#39;s core identity and their cognitive relationship with the natural world are fundamentally structured by the unique categories embedded within their ancestral speech,&#39; explains Marcus Colchester, director of the Forest Peoples Programme. &#39;The cultural identity of many indigenous groups is inseparable from their traditional subsistence practices. Everyday survival tasks, including hunting, fishing, and agricultural work, are intimately interwoven with ancestral narratives, spiritual entities, and mythic chronicles that define the very fabric of their community.&#39;</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>Louisa Maffi, the driving force behind Terralingua – an organization dedicated to protecting the intersection of cultural and biological diversity – argues that a rich linguistic tapestry offers immeasurable value to global civilization. With the extinction of each tongue, we lose a unique storehouse of human observation, moral values, and cultural philosophies that offer distinct, alternative frameworks for resolving structural human dilemmas. By allowing this erosion, we severely deplete our collective pool of creative problem-solving and diminish our adaptive capacity when encountering shifting global dynamics.</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>Nicholas Ostler, chairman of the Foundation for Endangered Languages, underscores the profound scientific loss associated with this decline. Permitting this homogenization to continue means permanently erasing our awareness of the highly diverse anatomical and structural mechanics of human speech – such as the varied utilization of the vocal tract for sound production, or the distinct semantic frameworks cultures invent to map meaning onto words.</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>Throughout history, imperial administrations routinely enforced mandates requiring subjugated populations to adopt dominant languages. However, even in the absence of explicit, forced assimilation, imperial structures inevitably degraded peripheral cultures. Ostler points to the Roman Empire as an illustrative historical example: Roman administrators did not enact laws explicitly forbidding localized speech in favor of Latin, yet their structural influence dramatically reduced European linguistic variety. Tremendous socio-economic prestige was tied to Latin; it operated as the exclusive language of commerce and state administration, prompting ambitious individuals to learn it voluntarily to achieve social mobility. Ostler notes that identical socioeconomic forces are squeezing minority systems today. The Romans successfully reorganized populations into dense, centralized networks – a process we characterize today as urbanization. In the modern era, families migrate from rural territories to sprawling urban zones where localized speech systems cannot easily be sustained. The younger demographic grows up integrated into a macro-community, and while it may take multiple generations for an ancestral tongue to vanish completely, the trajectory toward extinction remains clear.</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>&#39;Many modern governments view cultural heterogeneity as a direct threat to centralized patriotic cohesion,&#39; Maffi observes. &#39;Consequently, monolingualism is aggressively promoted through institutional frameworks, particularly state schooling systems that offer no bilingual or multilingual curricula, and government structures where politics is conducted entirely in the dominant national tongue.&#39; This institutional bias creates immense socio-economic pressure on minority communities to assimilate. It relies on a deeply flawed &#39;either/or&#39; paradigm: a citizen must either preserve their native tongue and accept total marginalization from national life, or abandon their linguistic heritage to adopt the dominant language.</p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p>In recent decades, industrial mass media structures have accelerated this homogenization, driving dominant metropolitan languages like English and Spanish past urban boundaries and deep into isolated communities. This pervasive media penetration has effectively forged a psychological wedge between generational cohorts, Ostler observes. In many remote areas, youths utilize their traditional speech when communicating with community elders, but pivot exclusively to English when interacting among peers. Maffi identifies parallel trends across global indigenous populations. The visual imagery and narratives presented to youth via modern media consistently glamorize the material lifestyles of dominant cultures, delivered entirely in majority languages. Consequently, it becomes incredibly difficult for younger generations to find a practical reason to appreciate or retain their own linguistic heritage.</p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p>When the internet expanded exponentially during the mid-1990s, many cultural observers predicted it would deliver the final blow to vulnerable languages. Because early digital infrastructure required literacy in English, it threatened to hasten the collapse of minority speech. However, these anxieties ultimately proved incorrect, as the linguistic variety displayed across the web expanded dramatically over the subsequent decades. Peter Austin, a scholar from London&#39;s School of Oriental and African Studies, attributes this resilience to the decentralized, democratic nature of online networks. &#39;Unlike traditional television networks or radio broadcasts, the internet is not monopolized by massive corporate conglomerates. Anyone with a network connection and basic digital tools can generate, publish, and distribute written content, news, and multimedia elements without restriction.&#39; Indigenous groups worldwide – from Hawaii and Mexico to Siberia – are leveraging this digital independence to preserve their spoken traditions, archiving their speech through written, auditory, and video formats.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9207&scene=%E8%AF%AD%E8%A8%80%E6%95%99%E8%82%B2&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9208","type":"reading","title":"R1 Secrets of the Nasca lines","book":"阅读真题集 21","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test3","part":0,"description":"阅读真题集 21 · Test3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"9208:66413:1","type":"choice","text":"There have been a number of theories about the purpose of the Nasca geoglyphs.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问关于Nasca地画目的的理论是否有很多，关键词是“a number of theories”和“purpose”。\n定位关键信息：用“theories”和“purpose”定位到阅读材料A段，其中提到多种解释。\n对应原文：Over the years, observers have offered wildly varying interpretations, explaining the Nasca lines as complex ancient roads, advanced water management systems, visual spectacles intended for primitive hot-air balloonists, and even – most spectacularly – landing strips for interstellar spacecraft.\n解题思路：原文明确说“observers have offered wildly varying interpretations”，即多种理论，与题干“a number of theories”一致，因此答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66413","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"9208:66414:2","type":"choice","text":"Today, most people still agree with Maria Reiche's opinion on the geoglyphs.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问现在大多数人是否仍同意Maria Reiche关于地画的观点，关键词是“still agree with Maria Reiche's opinion”。\n定位关键信息：用“Maria Reiche's opinion”定位到B段，其中提到她的观点是“giant celestial calendar”，并说明现代学者已彻底否定。\n对应原文：Though modern scholars have thoroughly discredited her personal conviction – that the network acted as a giant celestial calendar\n解题思路：原文说现代学者已彻底否定她的观点，意味着大多数人不再同意，与题干“still agree”相反，因此答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66414","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"9208:66415:3","type":"choice","text":"The Nasca-Palpa Project is the most extensive survey of the geoglyphs ever carried out.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Nasca-Palpa Project是否是对地画进行的最广泛调查，关键词是“most extensive survey”。\n定位关键信息：用“Nasca-Palpa Project”和“most extensive survey”定位到阅读材料B段。\n对应原文：In 1997, the Nasca-Palpa Project was set up as a joint scientific venture... this initiative launched an exhaustive inquiry into the region's ancient inhabitants.\n解题思路：原文只说项目发起了“详尽调查”，但未提及是否“最广泛”，因此无法判断，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66415","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"9208:66416:4","type":"choice","text":"The Nasca were the first people to create geoglyphs in the Peruvian desert.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Nasca是否是秘鲁沙漠中最早创造地画的人，关键词是first people to create geoglyphs。\n定位关键信息：用“first people”和“create geoglyphs”定位到阅读材料E段。\n对应原文：Yet, the practice did not originate with the Nasca. On a prominent hillside... researchers identified three stylized anthropomorphic figures... dating back more than 2,400 years – originating well within the era of the preceding Paracas culture.\n解题思路：原文明确说地画实践并非起源于Nasca，而是更早的Paracas文化，因此Nasca不是最早创造者，答案选FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66416","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"9208:66417:5","type":"choice","text":"The shapes of the geoglyphs remained constant throughout the Nasca period.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问地画形状在整个纳斯卡时期是否保持不变，关键词是“shapes of the geoglyphs remained constant”和“throughout the Nasca period”。\n定位关键信息：用“shapes”和“Nasca period”定位到F段，该段讨论地画在不同时期的变化。\n对应原文：F段：“Many lines overlap older iterations, with visible obliterations and over-carving complicating modern interpretation... Over time... the geoglyphs to expand into massive, open geometric configurations.”\n解题思路：原文指出地画有重叠、覆盖和扩展，说明形状随时间改变，与题干“保持不变”矛盾，因此答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66417","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"9208:66418:6","type":"choice","text":"Scientific analysis supports the idea that some geoglyphs were designed to be walked along.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问科学分析是否支持一些地画被设计为供人行走，关键词是“Scientific analysis”“geoglyphs”“walked along”。\n定位关键信息：用“Scientific analysis”和“walked along”定位到F段和G段，F段提到“specialized tracks for sacred processions”，G段提到“magnetic field surveys”证实地面被踩实。\n对应原文：F段：“This strongly indicates that...these works transformed...into specialized tracks for sacred processions.” G段：“The subtle variations...confirmed that the ground had been significantly packed down by heavy foot traffic.”\n解题思路：F段指出地画变为仪式行走的路径，G段用磁力调查证实地面因大量步行而压实，科学分析支持了行走功能，因此答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66418","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"9208:66419:7","type":"choice","text":"The Spondylus shell suggests a link between the geoglyphs and the importance of water.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Spondylus壳是否表明地画与水的关联，关键词是Spondylus shell和link between geoglyphs and importance of water。\n定位关键信息：用Spondylus shell定位到H段，寻找其与水和地画的关系。\n对应原文：The Spondylus shell served as an incredibly powerful religious token linked to agricultural abundance and ritual pleas for rain during severe dry spells.\n解题思路：原文说明Spondylus壳与祈求雨水相关，而地画是仪式场所，因此两者通过水的重要性联系起来，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66419","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"9208:66420:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"pottery","acceptedAnswers":["pottery"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Nasca人通过混合液态粘土和天然颜料制造了什么高度装饰的物品，关键词是“manufactured highly decorated”和“blending liquid clay with natural pigments”。\n定位关键信息：用“blending liquid clay with natural pigments”定位到阅读材料C段，该处描述了Nasca人制造陶器的工艺。\n对应原文：They achieved great renown for their highly distinct pottery, pioneering a method where natural mineral pigments were dissolved into a thin liquid clay, allowing vibrant hues to fuse permanently during the firing process.\n解题思路：原文中“highly distinct pottery”对应题干“highly decorated”，且“natural mineral pigments were dissolved into a thin liquid clay”直接匹配“blending liquid clay with natural pigments”，因此正确答案是pottery。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66420","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","maxWords":1},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"9208:66420:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"rainfall","acceptedAnswers":["rainfall"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Nasca人因什么年度模式变化而迁移社区，关键词是“relocated their communities”和“shifts in the annual patterns”。\n定位关键信息：用“relocated their communities”和“annual patterns”定位到阅读材料D段首句。\n对应原文：As localized annual patterns of rainfall shifted across the terrain, Nasca communities adjusted their locations eastward or westward to stay near viable water sources.\n解题思路：原文明确说“annual patterns of rainfall shifted”导致Nasca社区调整位置，与题干“relocated their communities in response to shifts in the annual patterns of”对应，因此答案填rainfall。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66420","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","maxWords":1},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"9208:66420:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"wells","acceptedAnswers":["wells"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Nasca人建造了什么地下系统来达到下降的地下水位，关键词是subterranean system和descending water table。\n定位关键信息：用subterranean system和descending water table定位到D段，寻找描述地下系统的名词。\n对应原文：They engineered an impressive system of underground wells that intercepted the subterranean water table sloping downward from the Andean foothills.\n解题思路：原文中underground wells对应题干subterranean system，且intercepted the subterranean water table与to reach the descending water table同义，因此答案为wells。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66420","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","maxWords":1},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"9208:66420:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"rubbish","acceptedAnswers":["rubbish"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Nasca人将什么直接融入建筑结构，关键词是incorporating和building structures。\n定位关键信息：用incorporating和building structures定位到D段关于可持续习惯的描述。\n对应原文：Excavations also show that they integrated organic debris and accumulated rubbish directly into the structural walls of their architectural terraces and homes.\n解题思路：原文中integrated organic debris and accumulated rubbish与题干incorporating rubbish对应，rubbish是直接填入的答案。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66420","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","maxWords":1},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"9208:66420:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"stones","acceptedAnswers":["stones"],"explanation":"审题：题目问形成沙漠线条时扫开的暗色表面是什么，关键词是“dark surface”和“sweeping aside”。\n定位关键信息：根据“sweeping aside the dark surface”定位到阅读材料E段中描述清除表面暗色石头的句子。\n对应原文：by merely clearing away the dark stones coating the surface\n解题思路：原文中“clearing away the dark stones”对应题干“sweeping aside the dark surface”，因此空格应填stones。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66420","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","maxWords":1},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"9208:66420:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"sand","acceptedAnswers":["sand"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Nasca人如何形成沙漠线条，关键词是“sweeping aside the dark surface”和“expose the bright ... underneath”。\n定位关键信息：根据“sweeping aside the dark surface”和“bright ... underneath”定位到E段描述清除表面暗色石头、露出下方明亮沙子的句子。\n对应原文：by merely clearing away the dark stones coating the surface, the creators exposed the far brighter sand resting directly beneath.\n解题思路：原文中“clearing away the dark stones”对应题干“sweeping aside the dark surface”，而“exposed the far brighter sand”直接对应“expose the bright sand underneath”，因此正确答案为sand。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66420","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","maxWords":1}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"66413","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">There have been a number of theories about the purpose of the Nasca geoglyphs.</span></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"66414","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Today, most people still agree with Maria Reiche&#39;s opinion on the geoglyphs.</span></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"66415","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">The Nasca-Palpa Project is the most extensive survey of the geoglyphs ever carried out.</span></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"66416","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">The Nasca were the first people to create geoglyphs in the Peruvian desert.</span></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"66417","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">The shapes of the geoglyphs remained constant throughout the Nasca period.</span></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"66418","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Scientific analysis supports the idea that some geoglyphs were designed to be walked along.</span></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"66419","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">The Spondylus shell suggests a link between the geoglyphs and the importance of water.</span></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"66420","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8–13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","html":"<p style=\"margin-top: 21px; margin-bottom: 21px; text-align: left;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 19px\">The Nasca people</span></strong></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px; margin-bottom: 21px;\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">emerged from a previous culture known as the Paracas</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px; margin-bottom: 21px;\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">lived in settlements in the valleys near the Andes mountains</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px; margin-bottom: 21px;\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">grew food crops and cotton</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px; margin-bottom: 21px;\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">manufactured highly decorated <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong> by blending liquid clay with natural pigments</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px; margin-bottom: 21px;\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">relocated their communities in response to shifts in the annual patterns of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong></span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px; margin-bottom: 21px;\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">constructed a subterranean system of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong> to reach the descending water table</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px; margin-bottom: 21px;\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">practiced highly sustainable habits, such as incorporating <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong> directly into their building structures</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px; margin-bottom: 21px;\"><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;\">• </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">formed the massive desert lines by sweeping aside the dark surface <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong> to expose the bright <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong> underneath</span></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":8}],"passage":"<p><strong>Secrets of the Nasca lines</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><em>New research sheds light on the serious desert drawings of Peru</em></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>Elevated within the windswept Nasca desert of Peru, a vast network of ancient markings scoring the landscape spans across miles. These immense earthworks, professionally termed geoglyphs, stretch for hundreds of meters and sketch out outlines of native wildlife, avian creatures, and intricate geometric shapes. Over the years, observers have offered wildly varying interpretations, explaining the Nasca lines as complex ancient roads, advanced water management systems, visual spectacles intended for primitive hot-air balloonists, and even – most spectacularly – landing strips for interstellar spacecraft.</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>Formal mapping of these grand geoglyphs began in the 1940s under the dedication of a German educator named Maria Reiche. Though modern scholars have thoroughly discredited her personal conviction – that the network acted as a giant celestial calendar – Reiche played an indispensable role in safeguarding the designs for five decades. Decades later, in 1997, the Nasca-Palpa Project was set up as a joint scientific venture between Peruvian and German institutions. Under the leadership of Peruvian archaeologist Johny Isla and Markus Reindel from the German Archaeological Institute, this initiative launched an exhaustive inquiry into the region&#39;s ancient inhabitants. Their research covers how these communities organized their settlements, what drove their ultimate decline, and the true function of the enigmatic symbols they left behind. For Isla and Reindel, the mystery begins and ends with the struggle for moisture.</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>The coastal strip tracing southern Peru and northern Chile ranks among the most moisture-deprived environments on Earth. Within the narrow, sheltered zone where the Nasca civilization took root, ten distinct rivers flow westward down from the Andes mountain range, though the majority run completely dry during extended stretches of the year. Despite encountering such severe climate challenges, the Nasca civilization thrived for eight centuries. Arising around 200 BC from an older ancestral tradition known as the Paracas, the Nasca settled along river valleys to cultivate essential crops like cotton, beans, cuma fruit, and a localized variety of maize. They achieved great renown for their highly distinct pottery, pioneering a method where natural mineral pigments were dissolved into a thin liquid clay, allowing vibrant hues to fuse permanently during the firing process.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>As localized annual patterns of rainfall shifted across the terrain, Nasca communities adjusted their locations eastward or westward to stay near viable water sources. Furthermore, early Nasca innovators developed highly practical methods to survive these severe water deficits. They engineered an impressive system of underground wells that intercepted the subterranean water table sloping downward from the Andean foothills, channeling precious fluids directly to their villages. This unrelenting environmental pressure forced the Nasca to adopt exceptionally sustainable practices. Their underground infrastructure significantly lowered losses from evaporation, demonstrating a highly advanced understanding of resource preservation. Excavations also show that they integrated organic debris and accumulated rubbish directly into the structural walls of their architectural terraces and homes, effectively recycling waste as a primary building component.</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>But what of the massive geoglyphs themselves, and who initiated their construction? The arid, sun-baked plains and hillsides provided an ideal canvas: by merely clearing away the dark stones coating the surface, the creators exposed the far brighter sand resting directly beneath. These stark markings have survived for millennia due to the region&#39;s exceptionally dry climate. Yet, the practice did not originate with the Nasca. On a prominent hillside situated south of Palpa, researchers identified three stylized anthropomorphic figures carved into the earth that date back more than 2,400 years – originating well within the era of the preceding Paracas culture.</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>Modern examinations of these regional designs reveal that they were not created simultaneously, in a single location, or for one isolated reason. Many lines overlap older iterations, with visible obliterations and over-carving complicating modern interpretation. The majority of iconic animal symbols, such as the famous spider and hummingbird, were executed using a single, continuous line. A practitioner could step onto the track at a specific point and navigate the entire shape without ever crossing their own path. This strongly indicates that during the early phases of Nasca history, these works transformed from mere static graphics into specialized tracks for sacred processions. Over time, potentially driven by expanding populations, larger crowds began participating in these group events, causing the geoglyphs to expand into massive, open geometric configurations, with some trapezoidal plazas extending past 700 meters. &quot;Our primary hypothesis,&quot; Reindel explains, &quot;is that these zones ceased to function as illustrations to be viewed from afar, and instead operated as active stages to be trodden upon during major communal rituals.&quot;</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>These ancient expressions of devotion left tangible marks directly in the desert soil. Between 2003 and 2007, a team of German geophysicists conducted detailed magnetic field surveys across a massive trapezoid near the village of Yunama, just outside Palpa, as well as on several adjacent lines. The subtle variations discovered in the magnetic data confirmed that the ground had been significantly packed down by heavy foot traffic, particularly around the deliberate stone mounds built at the terminals of many patterns.</p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p>Archaeologists had long hypothesized that these structured stone heaps functioned as ceremonial altars, a theory definitively proven in 2000. While excavating a mound near the Yunama site, Reindel unearthed artifacts clearly identifying them as ritualistic offerings, alongside fragments of a large marine shell belonging to the genus Spondylus. Noted for its distinctive coral pink coloration and sharp, spiked exterior, the Spondylus shell served as an incredibly powerful religious token linked to agricultural abundance and ritual pleas for rain during severe dry spells. &quot;It is entirely undeniable,&quot; Reindel remarks, &quot;that in this specific environment, securing water was the absolute center of survival.&quot;</p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p>In the end, these elaborate rituals and offerings failed to save them. By the 6th century AD, the hyper-arid boundaries of the desert expanded outward, triggering the total breakdown of the Nasca civilization, which left its final, unyielding secrets etched permanently into the parched earth.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9208&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9209","type":"reading","title":"R2 THE IMPACT OF SPORTS TOURISM ON URBAN AREAS","book":"阅读真题集 21","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test3","part":0,"description":"阅读真题集 21 · Test3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"9209:66547:14","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"审题：题目要求为段落A选择正确标题，关键词是段落A内容与选项G的对应关系。\n定位关键信息：用段落A中关于游客分类的描述定位到选项G的“Classification systems for different types of athletic travelers”。\n对应原文：Visitors who travel specifically to engage in physical activities can be categorized into two primary segments. ... Conversely, others maintain a highly competitive mindset... The vast majority of athletic tourists do not journey to play; rather, they attend these spectacles purely for the purpose of observation.\n解题思路：原文将体育游客分为参与型（休闲和竞技）和观察型，对应选项G中“不同类型体育游客的分类系统”。","options":["Structural conditions fostering growth in a pair of municipalities","Geographic backgrounds of traveling sport enthusiasts","A range of broad rationales supporting public subsidization","The unquantifiable perks linked to sporting infrastructure","The primary significance of relying on existing frameworks","Divergent academic conclusions and data sets","Classification systems for different types of athletic travelers"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"66547","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has five paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"9209:66547:15","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目要求为段落B选择正确标题，关键词是段落B的核心内容，即政府资助体育场馆的理由。\n定位关键信息：通过段落B中“justifications for this level of public intervention”定位到政府资助的多种理由。\n对应原文：Okner (1974) outlines several key justifications for this level of public intervention. For one, hosting events is believed to bolster civic pride and metropolitan prestige. It can also catalyze industrial growth...\n解题思路：原文列举了多项公共资助的理由，如提升城市自豪感、促进工业增长等，与选项C“A range of broad rationales supporting public subsidization”完全对应。","options":["Structural conditions fostering growth in a pair of municipalities","Geographic backgrounds of traveling sport enthusiasts","A range of broad rationales supporting public subsidization","The unquantifiable perks linked to sporting infrastructure","The primary significance of relying on existing frameworks","Divergent academic conclusions and data sets","Classification systems for different types of athletic travelers"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"66547","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has five paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"9209:66547:16","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"审题：题目要求为段落C选择正确标题，关键词是段落C的核心内容。\n定位关键信息：根据段落C内容，定位到Rawn和Rosentraub等人的不同研究结论和数据。\n对应原文：Rawn posits that such competitions effectively generated service-sector positions... However, a subsequent assessment... by Rosentraub et al. (1994) arrived at a different conclusion. They determined that the sports-led blueprint yielded no measurable economic advantage...\n解题思路：段落C呈现了Rawn支持体育旅游经济效益的研究，以及Rosentraub等人得出相反结论，同时引用Essex和Chalkley对亚特兰大奥运会的负面评价，整体体现学术结论和数据的分歧，对应选项F。","options":["Structural conditions fostering growth in a pair of municipalities","Geographic backgrounds of traveling sport enthusiasts","A range of broad rationales supporting public subsidization","The unquantifiable perks linked to sporting infrastructure","The primary significance of relying on existing frameworks","Divergent academic conclusions and data sets","Classification systems for different types of athletic travelers"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"66547","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has five paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"9209:66547:17","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目要求为段落D选择正确标题，关键词是“unquantifiable perks”和“sporting infrastructure”。\n定位关键信息：根据选项D中的“unquantifiable perks”和“sporting infrastructure”，定位到段落D中关于“unquantifiable attributes”和“stadiums”的描述。\n对应原文：Yet, it remains equally apparent that the unquantifiable attributes of professional athletics... exert a powerful influence over policymakers... the overarching justification for constructing stadiums... rests entirely on a deep-seated belief in the unquantifiable 'intangible' assets.\n解题思路：原文强调“unquantifiable attributes”和“intangible assets”是建设体育场馆的主要理由，与选项D“The unquantifiable perks linked to sporting infrastructure”完全对应。","options":["Structural conditions fostering growth in a pair of municipalities","Geographic backgrounds of traveling sport enthusiasts","A range of broad rationales supporting public subsidization","The unquantifiable perks linked to sporting infrastructure","The primary significance of relying on existing frameworks","Divergent academic conclusions and data sets","Classification systems for different types of athletic travelers"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"66547","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has five paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"9209:66547:18","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题：题目要求为段落E选择正确标题，关键词是段落E的核心内容。\n定位关键信息：根据段落E首句“the collective rewards of athletic tourism can be highly substantial, particularly when initiatives focus on domestic tournaments or modest competitions that leverage existing municipal networks”定位。\n对应原文：“the collective rewards of athletic tourism can be highly substantial, particularly when initiatives focus on domestic tournaments or modest competitions that leverage existing municipal networks.”\n解题思路：原文强调利用现有市政网络（existing municipal networks）的赛事带来巨大回报，对应选项A“Structural conditions fostering growth in a pair of municipalities”（促进两个城市发展的结构性条件），其中“existing municipal networks”与“structural conditions”和“municipalities”直接对应。","options":["Structural conditions fostering growth in a pair of municipalities","Geographic backgrounds of traveling sport enthusiasts","A range of broad rationales supporting public subsidization","The unquantifiable perks linked to sporting infrastructure","The primary significance of relying on existing frameworks","Divergent academic conclusions and data sets","Classification systems for different types of athletic travelers"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"66547","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has five paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"9209:66428:19","type":"fill","text":"填写第 19 空","answer":"observation","acceptedAnswers":["observation"],"explanation":"审题：题目问大多数城市体育赛事旅行者以何种方式参与，关键词是“vast majority”“participate exclusively via”。\n定位关键信息：用“vast majority of athletic tourists”和“participate”定位到原文A段。\n对应原文：The vast majority of athletic tourists do not journey to play; rather, they attend these spectacles purely for the purpose of observation.\n解题思路：原文明确说大多数体育游客不参与比赛，而是纯粹为了“observation”（观看），与题干“participate exclusively via observation”完全对应。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66428","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–20\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","maxWords":1},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"9209:66428:20","type":"fill","text":"填写第 20 空","answer":"disruption","acceptedAnswers":["disruption"],"explanation":"审题：题目问新建市政综合体向市民开放有助于减少居民中的什么现象，关键词是“minimize instances of ... among neighborhood residents”。\n定位关键信息：用“open access to these newly constructed municipal complexes”和“minimize”定位到B段中关于设施社会价值的句子。\n对应原文：Such facilities are particularly valuable from a sociological standpoint if they successfully supplant alternative pastimes that historically triggered community disruption.\n解题思路：原文说如果设施成功取代了历史上引发社区混乱的替代消遣方式，则特别有价值，其中“community disruption”对应题干“instances of disruption among neighborhood residents”，因此答案为disruption。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66428","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–20\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","maxWords":1},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"9209:66429:21","type":"choice","text":"Stebbins (1982)","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Stebbins (1982)的研究对应哪个观点，关键词为Stebbins (1982)和研究者对体育旅行者的分类。\n定位关键信息：用Stebbins (1982)定位到阅读材料A段，该段讨论了两种体育旅行者，其中一种追求“uncommon rewards”。\n对应原文：Others maintain a highly competitive mindset, aiming 'to experience uncommon rewards from the endeavour' (Stebbins, 1982).\n解题思路：原文中Stebbins指出部分体育旅行者追求“uncommon rewards”，与选项H中“elevated expectations regarding the personal rewards of active competition”一致，故答案为H。","options":["The vast majority of athletic competitors are drawn primarily to massive metropolitan areas.","Hosting a major tournament can introduce unexpected challenges and negative press to the organizing municipality.","Specialized athletic tourism campaigns can breathe economic life back into a municipality suffering from industrial decline","Publicly financing major arena projects cannot typically be justified on purely financial or commercial grounds","The Olympic Games have consistently yielded long-term financial stability for local neighborhoods due to the new public facilities left behind.","Documented data indicates that targeted athletic fixtures can elevate municipal tourism revenues during traditional off-peak periods","The tournaments that yield the highest commercial success are those centered exclusively on attracting international travelers","Particular sports travelers maintain distinct, elevated expectations regarding the personal rewards of active competition","This specific investigation yielded no clear evidence that sports-focused blueprints stimulate superior commercial expansion compared to other areas."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"66429","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21–26\nChoose the correct point,  A–I, for each research paper.\nList of points\nA\nThe vast majority of athletic competitors are drawn primarily\nto massive metropolitan areas.\nB\nHosting a major tournament can introduce unexpected challenges\nand negative press to the organizing municipality.\nC\nSpecialized athletic tourism campaigns can breathe economic life\nback into a municipality suffering from industrial decline.\nD\nPublicly financing major arena projects cannot typically be justified\non purely financial or commercial grounds.\nE\nThe Olympic Games have consistently yielded long-term financial\nstability for local neighborhoods due to the new public facilities left behind.\nF\nDocumented data indicates that targeted athletic fixtures can\nelevate municipal tourism revenues during traditional off-peak periods.\nG\nThe tournaments that yield the highest commercial success are\nthose centered exclusively on attracting international travelers.\nH\nParticular sports travelers maintain distinct, elevated expectations\nregarding the personal rewards of active competition.\nI\nThis specific investigation yielded no clear evidence that\nsports-focused blueprints stimulate superior commercial expansion compared to other areas."},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"9209:66429:22","type":"choice","text":"Rawn (1990)","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Rawn (1990)的研究对应哪个观点，关键词为Rawn (1990)和城市转型。\n定位关键信息：根据题干“Rawn (1990)”定位到C段首句，该句描述其研究内容。\n对应原文：She charts the city's structural evolution from a traditional manufacturing hub into a prominent center for international tournaments under the conceptual banner of 'smokestacks to stadiums, affluent sports fans are a clean industry.'\n解题思路：原文描述城市从传统制造业中心转型为国际赛事中心，对应选项C中“breathe economic life back into a municipality suffering from industrial decline”，即通过体育旅游振兴工业衰退城市。","options":["The vast majority of athletic competitors are drawn primarily to massive metropolitan areas.","Hosting a major tournament can introduce unexpected challenges and negative press to the organizing municipality.","Specialized athletic tourism campaigns can breathe economic life back into a municipality suffering from industrial decline","Publicly financing major arena projects cannot typically be justified on purely financial or commercial grounds","The Olympic Games have consistently yielded long-term financial stability for local neighborhoods due to the new public facilities left behind.","Documented data indicates that targeted athletic fixtures can elevate municipal tourism revenues during traditional off-peak periods","The tournaments that yield the highest commercial success are those centered exclusively on attracting international travelers","Particular sports travelers maintain distinct, elevated expectations regarding the personal rewards of active competition","This specific investigation yielded no clear evidence that sports-focused blueprints stimulate superior commercial expansion compared to other areas."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"66429","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21–26\nChoose the correct point,  A–I, for each research paper.\nList of points\nA\nThe vast majority of athletic competitors are drawn primarily\nto massive metropolitan areas.\nB\nHosting a major tournament can introduce unexpected challenges\nand negative press to the organizing municipality.\nC\nSpecialized athletic tourism campaigns can breathe economic life\nback into a municipality suffering from industrial decline.\nD\nPublicly financing major arena projects cannot typically be justified\non purely financial or commercial grounds.\nE\nThe Olympic Games have consistently yielded long-term financial\nstability for local neighborhoods due to the new public facilities left behind.\nF\nDocumented data indicates that targeted athletic fixtures can\nelevate municipal tourism revenues during traditional off-peak periods.\nG\nThe tournaments that yield the highest commercial success are\nthose centered exclusively on attracting international travelers.\nH\nParticular sports travelers maintain distinct, elevated expectations\nregarding the personal rewards of active competition.\nI\nThis specific investigation yielded no clear evidence that\nsports-focused blueprints stimulate superior commercial expansion compared to other areas."},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"9209:66429:23","type":"choice","text":"Rosentraub et al (1994)","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Rosentraub et al (1994)的研究结论，关键词为Rosentraub et al (1994)和结论内容。\n定位关键信息：用“Rosentraub et al. (1994)”定位到C段末尾，寻找其研究结论。\n对应原文：They determined that the sports-led blueprint yielded no measurable economic advantage or developmental growth when measured against comparable mid-sized urban centers in the same geographic region.\n解题思路：原文指出该研究认为体育主导计划未带来可衡量的经济优势或发展增长，与选项I“没有明确证据表明体育蓝图能刺激更优商业扩张”一致。","options":["The vast majority of athletic competitors are drawn primarily to massive metropolitan areas.","Hosting a major tournament can introduce unexpected challenges and negative press to the organizing municipality.","Specialized athletic tourism campaigns can breathe economic life back into a municipality suffering from industrial decline","Publicly financing major arena projects cannot typically be justified on purely financial or commercial grounds","The Olympic Games have consistently yielded long-term financial stability for local neighborhoods due to the new public facilities left behind.","Documented data indicates that targeted athletic fixtures can elevate municipal tourism revenues during traditional off-peak periods","The tournaments that yield the highest commercial success are those centered exclusively on attracting international travelers","Particular sports travelers maintain distinct, elevated expectations regarding the personal rewards of active competition","This specific investigation yielded no clear evidence that sports-focused blueprints stimulate superior commercial expansion compared to other areas."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"66429","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21–26\nChoose the correct point,  A–I, for each research paper.\nList of points\nA\nThe vast majority of athletic competitors are drawn primarily\nto massive metropolitan areas.\nB\nHosting a major tournament can introduce unexpected challenges\nand negative press to the organizing municipality.\nC\nSpecialized athletic tourism campaigns can breathe economic life\nback into a municipality suffering from industrial decline.\nD\nPublicly financing major arena projects cannot typically be justified\non purely financial or commercial grounds.\nE\nThe Olympic Games have consistently yielded long-term financial\nstability for local neighborhoods due to the new public facilities left behind.\nF\nDocumented data indicates that targeted athletic fixtures can\nelevate municipal tourism revenues during traditional off-peak periods.\nG\nThe tournaments that yield the highest commercial success are\nthose centered exclusively on attracting international travelers.\nH\nParticular sports travelers maintain distinct, elevated expectations\nregarding the personal rewards of active competition.\nI\nThis specific investigation yielded no clear evidence that\nsports-focused blueprints stimulate superior commercial expansion compared to other areas."},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"9209:66429:24","type":"choice","text":"Essex and Chalkley (1998)","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Essex and Chalkley (1998)的研究对应哪个观点，关键词为Essex and Chalkley (1998)。\n定位关键信息：用“Essex and Chalkley (1998)”定位到阅读材料C段末尾。\n对应原文：Essex and Chalkley (1998) observed, 'As a result of the traffic congestion, security breaches and over-commercialization, Atlanta did not receive the kind of media attention it would ideally have liked. Its experience highlights the dangers as well as the benefits of being under the international Olympic spotlight.'\n解题思路：原文指出主办赛事带来交通拥堵、安全漏洞和过度商业化等意外挑战及负面媒体关注，与选项B“Hosting a major tournament can introduce unexpected challenges and negative press to the organizing municipality”完全吻合。","options":["The vast majority of athletic competitors are drawn primarily to massive metropolitan areas.","Hosting a major tournament can introduce unexpected challenges and negative press to the organizing municipality.","Specialized athletic tourism campaigns can breathe economic life back into a municipality suffering from industrial decline","Publicly financing major arena projects cannot typically be justified on purely financial or commercial grounds","The Olympic Games have consistently yielded long-term financial stability for local neighborhoods due to the new public facilities left behind.","Documented data indicates that targeted athletic fixtures can elevate municipal tourism revenues during traditional off-peak periods","The tournaments that yield the highest commercial success are those centered exclusively on attracting international travelers","Particular sports travelers maintain distinct, elevated expectations regarding the personal rewards of active competition","This specific investigation yielded no clear evidence that sports-focused blueprints stimulate superior commercial expansion compared to other areas."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"66429","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21–26\nChoose the correct point,  A–I, for each research paper.\nList of points\nA\nThe vast majority of athletic competitors are drawn primarily\nto massive metropolitan areas.\nB\nHosting a major tournament can introduce unexpected challenges\nand negative press to the organizing municipality.\nC\nSpecialized athletic tourism campaigns can breathe economic life\nback into a municipality suffering from industrial decline.\nD\nPublicly financing major arena projects cannot typically be justified\non purely financial or commercial grounds.\nE\nThe Olympic Games have consistently yielded long-term financial\nstability for local neighborhoods due to the new public facilities left behind.\nF\nDocumented data indicates that targeted athletic fixtures can\nelevate municipal tourism revenues during traditional off-peak periods.\nG\nThe tournaments that yield the highest commercial success are\nthose centered exclusively on attracting international travelers.\nH\nParticular sports travelers maintain distinct, elevated expectations\nregarding the personal rewards of active competition.\nI\nThis specific investigation yielded no clear evidence that\nsports-focused blueprints stimulate superior commercial expansion compared to other areas."},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"9209:66429:25","type":"choice","text":"Baim (1994)","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Baim (1994)的研究对应哪个观点，关键词为Baim (1994)。\n定位关键信息：用“Baim (1994)”定位到阅读材料D段末尾。\n对应原文：Baim (1994) scrutinized financial records from 15 publicly subsidized arenas across the United States. His analysis revealed that... the overarching justification for constructing stadiums... rests entirely on a deep-seated belief in the unquantifiable 'intangible' assets.\n解题思路：原文指出Baim分析公共资助场馆的财务记录，发现建设理由主要基于无形资产的信念，而非财务或商业合理性，与选项D“公共资助大型场馆项目通常不能纯粹以财务或商业理由证明其合理性”一致。","options":["The vast majority of athletic competitors are drawn primarily to massive metropolitan areas.","Hosting a major tournament can introduce unexpected challenges and negative press to the organizing municipality.","Specialized athletic tourism campaigns can breathe economic life back into a municipality suffering from industrial decline","Publicly financing major arena projects cannot typically be justified on purely financial or commercial grounds","The Olympic Games have consistently yielded long-term financial stability for local neighborhoods due to the new public facilities left behind.","Documented data indicates that targeted athletic fixtures can elevate municipal tourism revenues during traditional off-peak periods","The tournaments that yield the highest commercial success are those centered exclusively on attracting international travelers","Particular sports travelers maintain distinct, elevated expectations regarding the personal rewards of active competition","This specific investigation yielded no clear evidence that sports-focused blueprints stimulate superior commercial expansion compared to other areas."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"66429","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21–26\nChoose the correct point,  A–I, for each research paper.\nList of points\nA\nThe vast majority of athletic competitors are drawn primarily\nto massive metropolitan areas.\nB\nHosting a major tournament can introduce unexpected challenges\nand negative press to the organizing municipality.\nC\nSpecialized athletic tourism campaigns can breathe economic life\nback into a municipality suffering from industrial decline.\nD\nPublicly financing major arena projects cannot typically be justified\non purely financial or commercial grounds.\nE\nThe Olympic Games have consistently yielded long-term financial\nstability for local neighborhoods due to the new public facilities left behind.\nF\nDocumented data indicates that targeted athletic fixtures can\nelevate municipal tourism revenues during traditional off-peak periods.\nG\nThe tournaments that yield the highest commercial success are\nthose centered exclusively on attracting international travelers.\nH\nParticular sports travelers maintain distinct, elevated expectations\nregarding the personal rewards of active competition.\nI\nThis specific investigation yielded no clear evidence that\nsports-focused blueprints stimulate superior commercial expansion compared to other areas."},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"9209:66429:26","type":"choice","text":"Higham (1999)","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Higham (1999)的研究结论，关键词为Higham (1999)和对应观点。\n定位关键信息：在阅读材料E段中定位到Higham (1999)的引用。\n对应原文：Higham (1999) asserts that in New Zealand... the 1997 Golden Oldies Rugby Competition... drew affluent travelers during a period that fell outside the conventional peak travel season.\n解题思路：原文指出该赛事在非传统旅游旺季吸引了富裕游客，与选项F“targeted athletic fixtures can elevate municipal tourism revenues during traditional off-peak periods”一致。","options":["The vast majority of athletic competitors are drawn primarily to massive metropolitan areas.","Hosting a major tournament can introduce unexpected challenges and negative press to the organizing municipality.","Specialized athletic tourism campaigns can breathe economic life back into a municipality suffering from industrial decline","Publicly financing major arena projects cannot typically be justified on purely financial or commercial grounds","The Olympic Games have consistently yielded long-term financial stability for local neighborhoods due to the new public facilities left behind.","Documented data indicates that targeted athletic fixtures can elevate municipal tourism revenues during traditional off-peak periods","The tournaments that yield the highest commercial success are those centered exclusively on attracting international travelers","Particular sports travelers maintain distinct, elevated expectations regarding the personal rewards of active competition","This specific investigation yielded no clear evidence that sports-focused blueprints stimulate superior commercial expansion compared to other areas."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"66429","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21–26\nChoose the correct point,  A–I, for each research paper.\nList of points\nA\nThe vast majority of athletic competitors are drawn primarily\nto massive metropolitan areas.\nB\nHosting a major tournament can introduce unexpected challenges\nand negative press to the organizing municipality.\nC\nSpecialized athletic tourism campaigns can breathe economic life\nback into a municipality suffering from industrial decline.\nD\nPublicly financing major arena projects cannot typically be justified\non purely financial or commercial grounds.\nE\nThe Olympic Games have consistently yielded long-term financial\nstability for local neighborhoods due to the new public facilities left behind.\nF\nDocumented data indicates that targeted athletic fixtures can\nelevate municipal tourism revenues during traditional off-peak periods.\nG\nThe tournaments that yield the highest commercial success are\nthose centered exclusively on attracting international travelers.\nH\nParticular sports travelers maintain distinct, elevated expectations\nregarding the personal rewards of active competition.\nI\nThis specific investigation yielded no clear evidence that\nsports-focused blueprints stimulate superior commercial expansion compared to other areas."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"66547","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has five paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"66428","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–20\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>The societal and economic benefits of urban athletic tourism</strong></p><p>When individuals flock to municipal athletic events, the vast majority of these travelers participate exclusively via <strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong> . Policymakers frequently encourage this phenomenon because they believe it will stimulate regional commerce and optimize revenue collected through public levies. Furthermore, providing local citizens with open access to these newly constructed municipal complexes can help minimize instances of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong> among neighborhood residents.</p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"66429","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21–26\nChoose the correct point,  A–I, for each research paper.\nList of points\nA\nThe vast majority of athletic competitors are drawn primarily\nto massive metropolitan areas.\nB\nHosting a major tournament can introduce unexpected challenges\nand negative press to the organizing municipality.\nC\nSpecialized athletic tourism campaigns can breathe economic life\nback into a municipality suffering from industrial decline.\nD\nPublicly financing major arena projects cannot typically be justified\non purely financial or commercial grounds.\nE\nThe Olympic Games have consistently yielded long-term financial\nstability for local neighborhoods due to the new public facilities left behind.\nF\nDocumented data indicates that targeted athletic fixtures can\nelevate municipal tourism revenues during traditional off-peak periods.\nG\nThe tournaments that yield the highest commercial success are\nthose centered exclusively on attracting international travelers.\nH\nParticular sports travelers maintain distinct, elevated expectations\nregarding the personal rewards of active competition.\nI\nThis specific investigation yielded no clear evidence that\nsports-focused blueprints stimulate superior commercial expansion compared to other areas.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:14px\">Stebbins (1982) <strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong></span></p><p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:14px\">Rawn (1990) <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong></span></p><p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:14px\">Rosentraub et al (1994) <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong></span></p><p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:14px\">Essex and Chalkley (1998) <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong></span></p><p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:14px\">Baim (1994) <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong></span></p><p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:14px\">Higham (1999)&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 14px;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 14px;\"><br/></span></p><p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:14px\"></span><br/></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":21}],"passage":"<p><strong>THE IMPACT OF SPORTS TOURISM ON URBAN AREAS</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>#&amp;</p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>Athletic tourism can be conceptualized as travel undertaken for non-commercial purposes, where individuals journey to view or engage in athletic pursuits outside their regular residential areas. This phenomenon frequently drives the expansion of regional athletic infrastructure and operates as a powerful marketing mechanism for metropolitan areas. Visitors who travel specifically to engage in physical activities can be categorized into two primary segments. Certain individuals view athletics as a recreational pastime pursued for personal fulfillment, skill refinement, and knowledge acquisition. Conversely, others maintain a highly competitive mindset, aiming &#39;to experience uncommon rewards from the endeavour&#39; (Stebbins, 1982). Nevertheless, the total volume of travelers within these two participatory segments remains relatively minor, even if it carries weight for smaller municipalities. The vast majority of athletic tourists do not journey to play; rather, they attend these spectacles purely for the purpose of observation. On the whole, athletics acts as a major catalyst for tourism, especially within domestic markets.</p><p>&amp;#</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>#&amp;</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>The immense public profile surrounding high-profile or cyclical athletic spectacles has prompted numerous national and municipal governments to fund the building and maintenance of stadiums, arenas, and related infrastructural networks. Okner (1974) outlines several key justifications for this level of public intervention. For one, hosting events is believed to bolster civic pride and metropolitan prestige. It can also catalyze industrial growth by incentivizing companies to relocate from alternative regions and fostering entrepreneurship. Consequently, this creates new employment fields and expands tax revenues generated by tournament operations. Furthermore, these developments supply local citizens with enhanced recreational outlets. Such facilities are particularly valuable from a sociological standpoint if they successfully supplant alternative pastimes that historically triggered community disruption. Furthermore, high-profile athletic platforms can inspire sports participation among local youths, while a winning sports franchise generally improves the overall morale of the local populace.</p><p>&amp;#</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>#&amp;</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>The economic allure of athletic tourism for metropolitan centers is vividly captured in Rawn&#39;s (1990) investigation of sports enthusiasts in Indianapolis, US. She charts the city&#39;s structural evolution from a traditional manufacturing hub into a prominent center for international tournaments under the conceptual banner of &#39;smokestacks to stadiums, affluent sports fans are a clean industry.&#39; Rawn highlights a demographic survey of attendees at the 1989 Tennis Championship in Indianapolis, revealing that 36 percent of spectators commanded household incomes exceeding $75,000 (compared to just 4 percent of the city&#39;s general population). Additionally, a third of these visitors reserved hotel accommodations and engaged in local retail shopping, while 84 percent patronized local restaurants. Rawn posits that such competitions effectively generated service-sector positions to offset the severe employment contractions hitting the local manufacturing market. However, a subsequent assessment of the capital allocations, public policies, and long-term plans steering Indianapolis&#39; sports-centric initiatives by Rosentraub et al. (1994) arrived at a different conclusion. They determined that the sports-led blueprint yielded no measurable economic advantage or developmental growth when measured against comparable mid-sized urban centers in the same geographic region. Similarly, in their assessment of the 1996 Atlanta Olympic Games, Essex and Chalkley (1998) observed, &#39;As a result of the traffic congestion, security breaches and over-commercialization, Atlanta did not receive the kind of media attention it would ideally have liked. Its experience highlights the dangers as well as the benefits of being under the international Olympic spotlight.&#39;</p><p>&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p>#&amp;</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>Constructing grand arenas and sporting complexes to stimulate travel and spearhead urban revitalization is by no means a modern invention. The 1932 Summer Olympics in Los Angeles were expressly engineered to drive regional travel, while American collegiate football bowls like the Sugar Bowl in New Orleans were organized to breathe life back into failing local economies during the Great Depression of the 1930s. Nonetheless, a substantial portion of American research evaluating athletics through an economic development lens implies that municipal funding for stadiums rarely achieves a financial break-even point. Many researchers openly question both the volume and the long-term viability of the employment positions generated by professional sports franchises. Yet, it remains equally apparent that the unquantifiable attributes of professional athletics, which are notoriously difficult to define or measure, exert a powerful influence over policymakers. Baim (1994) scrutinized financial records from 15 publicly subsidized arenas across the United States. His analysis revealed that, with few exceptions, the overarching justification for constructing stadiums to attract or retain professional sports franchises rests entirely on a deep-seated belief in the unquantifiable &#39;intangible&#39; assets (such as diverse recreational choices) brought to a municipality.</p><p>&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p>#&amp;</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>Even so, the collective rewards of athletic tourism can be highly substantial, particularly when initiatives focus on domestic tournaments or modest competitions that leverage existing municipal networks. Higham (1999) asserts that in New Zealand, the financial and promotional outcomes of sporting fixtures that align with a host city&#39;s current facilities and foundational systems are overwhelmingly favorable. For instance, the 1997 Golden Oldies Rugby Competition held in Christchurch successfully drew participating athletic clubs from all corners of the globe. The tournament spanned a full two weeks, drawing affluent travelers during a period that fell outside the conventional peak travel season. An identical trend is observable during the Masters Games in Dunedin, a biennial athletic gathering intentionally scheduled to take place during a lull in domestic leisure travel for the host city. This fixture regularly draws several thousand highly lucrative athletic travelers from across New Zealand and, with increasing frequency, from international markets. Consequently, athletics provides both direct and indirect structural support to tourism across cities and their surrounding peripheral zones.</p><p>&amp;#</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9209&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9210","type":"reading","title":"R3 Marketing and mind control","book":"阅读真题集 21","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test3","part":0,"description":"阅读真题集 21 · Test3 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"9210:66430:27","type":"choice","text":"Based on the text, which promotional method is intentionally designed to extend the duration of a consumer's visit to a retail environment?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目问哪种促销方法有意延长消费者在零售环境中的停留时间，关键词是“extend the duration of a consumer's visit”。\n定位关键信息：根据“extend the duration”和“retail environment”定位到C段，该段讨论不同感官的广告形式，其中提到嗅觉系统被用于诱使顾客逗留。\n对应原文：C段：“More surreptitiously, our olfactory system is targeted by variations of vanilla and citrus perfumes aimed at enticing us to linger in a retail outlet.”\n解题思路：原文中“enticing us to linger”直接对应题干“extend the duration of a consumer's visit”，而“olfactory system”和“perfumes”对应选项B的“engineered atmospheric fragrances”，因此B正确。","options":["broadcasting curated audio loops","releasing engineered atmospheric fragrances","positioning high-impact graphical banners","utilizing real-time promotional intercom notices"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"66430","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"9210:66431:28","type":"choice","text":"The author introduces the example of commercially packaged water to demonstrate that","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题：题目问作者举瓶装水例子是为了证明什么，关键词是commercially packaged water、demonstrate。\n定位关键信息：用commercially packaged water和bottled water定位到原文D段。\n对应原文：In the case of bottled water, we are swayed by advertising into paying for something that we can obtain for free. Most people cannot distinguish bottled from tap water, much less between brands of bottled water, which is why you rarely hear of a bottled water company proposing a blind taste test.\n解题思路：原文说人们被广告影响而购买免费可得的水，且无法区分品牌，说明购买行为由品牌定位驱动，对应A选项“individuals are driven to buy goods primarily due to tactical brand positioning”。","options":["individuals are driven to buy goods primarily due to tactical brand positioning.","the public willingly purchases a commodity despite its total lack of flavor.","corporate entities can completely bypass blind product evaluations if branding succeeds.","scientific research confirms that people are incapable of identifying public tap water."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"66431","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"9210:66432:29","type":"choice","text":"According to the author, a \"socially transmitted food preference\" takes place when","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目问作者认为“社会性食物偏好”何时发生，关键词是“socially transmitted food preference”和“takes place”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干关键词“socially transmitted food preference”定位到E段末尾。\n对应原文：Psychologists call this 'socially transmitted food preference'.\n解题思路：原文前文描述老鼠观察另一只老鼠吃某种谷物后也偏好同种谷物，即通过观察同伴饮食习惯改变自身选择，与C选项“a creature's dietary selections are altered by watching the eating habits of its peers”一致。","options":["dietary habits are dictated exclusively by the highest-ranking creatures in a pack.","separate populations of a specific species naturally share an identical palate.","a creature's dietary selections are altered by watching the eating habits of its peers.","an item becomes highly coveted because animals perceive it to be in short supply."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"66432","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"9210:66433:30","type":"choice","text":"According to the text, how does the cognitive capacity for observational mimicry serve as a beneficial asset?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题：题目问观察性模仿的认知能力如何成为有益资产，关键词是cognitive capacity for observational mimicry和beneficial asset。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的observational mimicry和beneficial asset，定位到G段首句“Learning by observation can be an extraordinarily valuable brain feature”及后续描述。\n对应原文：Learning by observation can be an extraordinarily valuable brain feature. This is how we learn to communicate and perform motor skills as well as deal with many everyday problems.\n解题思路：原文指出观察学习是宝贵的大脑特征，用于处理日常问题，与选项A“克服日常困难的有效机制”对应。","options":["It provides individuals with an effective mechanism for overcoming everyday difficulties.","Exposure to admirable role models helps elevate overall community ethics.","It offers a distinct competitive edge when negotiating with other individuals.","It allows outsiders to decode unfamiliar interpersonal dynamics and social structures."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"66433","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"9210:66434:31","type":"choice","text":"How do television promotions successfully exploit the human evolutionary drive to copy others?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目问电视促销如何成功利用人类模仿他人的进化驱动力，关键词是“television promotions”、“exploit”、“evolutionary drive to copy others”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干关键词“television promotions”和“copy others”，定位到H段第一句“A component of advertising relies on the marketer’s ability to tap into the brain’s propensity for imitation”及后续描述。\n对应原文：H段：“Anybody who has watched TV knows advertisements are disproportionately populated with attractive, successful-looking individuals. If we are going to imitate someone, we are more inclined to imitate those who appear to be popular and appealing.”\n解题思路：原文指出电视广告中充满吸引人、成功形象的人物，人们更倾向于模仿受欢迎和有魅力的人，这与选项B“围绕拥有理想化和迷人形象的公众人物开展活动”完全对应，说明电视促销通过展示这类人物来激发模仿。","options":["By demonstrating the precise transactional behaviors that corporations want viewers to adopt.","By building campaigns around figures who possess an idealized and appealing persona.","By showcasing senior community members who command the respect of younger audiences.","By featuring elite figures who attribute their personal victories to the endorsed merchandise."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"66434","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"9210:66435:32","type":"choice","text":"The initial 1938 diamond initiative achieved commercial success by explicitly linking the purchase of gemstones to themes of high material luxury.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"审题：题目问1938年的钻石倡议是否通过明确将购买宝石与高度物质奢华主题联系起来而取得商业成功，关键词是“1938 diamond initiative”、“commercial success”、“explicitly linking”、“high material luxury”。\n定位关键信息：用“1938”和“diamond initiative”定位到阅读材料A段，该段描述了1938年广告公司的策略。\n对应原文：In 1938, this company hired an advertising agency which proposed reshaping social attitudes toward diamonds. ... The campaign culminated with the slogan: 'A diamond is forever.'\n解题思路：原文指出1938年的策略是重塑社会态度，将钻石与“永恒的爱”而非“高度物质奢华”联系起来，且通过电影植入和明星展示间接关联，并非明确链接物质奢华，因此与题干矛盾，选NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66435","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32–36\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"9210:66436:33","type":"choice","text":"Modern consumers are generally much more conscious of visual advertisements than they are of auditory marketing messages.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：题目问现代消费者是否普遍对视觉广告比听觉营销信息更敏感，关键词是“conscious of visual advertisements”和“auditory marketing messages”。\n定位关键信息：用“visual advertisements”和“auditory”定位到文章C段，该段描述了广告针对不同感官系统。\n对应原文：Our visual system is targeted by an avalanche of information... Our auditory system submits to catchy radio jingles and telemarketers.\n解题思路：原文只陈述视觉和听觉系统都受到广告影响，并未比较消费者对两者的意识程度或敏感性，因此无法判断题干说法，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66436","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32–36\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"9210:66437:34","type":"choice","text":"The structural transformation of courting rituals brought about by the historic diamond campaign yielded long-term benefits for modern society.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：题目问钻石营销带来的求偶仪式结构转型是否给现代社会带来长期益处，关键词是“structural transformation of courting rituals”和“long-term benefits for modern society”。\n定位关键信息：用“structural transformation of courting rituals”和“long-term benefits”在阅读材料中搜索，但全文未提及求偶仪式结构转型或其对现代社会的长期益处。\n对应原文：全文未找到相关原文片段。\n解题思路：阅读材料仅讨论钻石营销如何改变社会对钻石的态度（如A段），但未涉及求偶仪式结构转型或长期社会益处，因此信息未给出，选NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66437","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32–36\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"9210:66438:35","type":"choice","text":"Academic consensus remains divided regarding whether non-human animals systematically mirror the actions of dominant group members.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"审题：题目问学术界是否一致认为非人类动物会系统模仿优势群体成员的行为，关键词是“academic consensus remains divided”和“non-human animals systematically mirror actions of dominant group members”。\n定位关键信息：用“non-human animals”和“dominant group members”定位到原文I段，该段讨论动物模仿优势成员的研究。\n对应原文：Although not all researchers are convinced by the findings, a number of studies indicate that some animals also imitate dominant members of their group.\n解题思路：原文说“not all researchers are convinced”即并非所有研究者都信服，表明学术界意见存在分歧，与题干“remains divided”一致，因此答案为YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66438","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32–36\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"9210:66439:36","type":"choice","text":"Rational cognitive analysis allows consumers to see a direct causal link between a celebrity's professional success and the items they endorse.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"审题：题目问理性认知分析是否让消费者看到名人职业成功与代言产品之间的直接因果联系，关键词是rational cognitive analysis、direct causal link、celebrity's professional success、items they endorse。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的rational cognitive analysis和direct causal link，定位到阅读材料J段，该段讨论理性认知与模仿倾向的对比。\n对应原文：Rationally, we know these people's success did not depend on these products, so it seems our propensity to purchase products relates more to neural programs that evolved to encourage imitation of those further up the social ladder.\n解题思路：原文明确指出理性上我们知道名人的成功不依赖代言产品，因此消费者无法看到直接因果联系，题干说法与原文相反，所以答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66439","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32–36\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"9210:66440:37","type":"choice","text":"The potato-cleansing routines observed among the primates on Koshima Island confirmed that ____","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Koshima岛灵长类动物的洗土豆行为证实了什么，关键词是“potato-cleansing routines”和“Koshima Island”。\n定位关键信息：用“Koshima Island”和“potato”定位到F段，该段描述了猴子洗土豆的行为及其传播。\n对应原文：She began taking the dirt-covered sweet potatoes to the river to wash them before eating them. Upon seeing this, a few other open-minded monkeys picked up on the idea. Potato washing then spread from monkey to monkey and, over the course of a few years, most monkeys were eating clean potatoes.\n解题思路：原文说明洗土豆行为通过观察从一只猴子传播到整个群体，对应选项F“animals can develop new habits by observation”，即动物能通过观察发展新习惯。","options":["human mimicry of successful models often transfers incorrectly to unrelated commercial items","visual attention can be mathematically mapped to alter consumer choices without their awareness","younger primates will purposefully replicate the physical impairments of an alpha figure as a form of social alignment","complex behavioral innovations can emerge and spread through an animal community via social learning","secret actors are financially compensated to blend into public spaces and surreptitiously advocate for commodities","animals can develop new habits by observation.","incentives are provided for consumers who behave in a certain way"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"66440","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"9210:66440:38","type":"choice","text":"The field observations recorded by primatologist Frans de Waal indicated that ____","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Frans de Waal的实地观察表明了什么，关键词是“field observations”和“Frans de Waal”。\n定位关键信息：用“Frans de Waal”定位到I段，该段描述了他观察到的黑猩猩模仿行为。\n对应原文：He noted that in one particular group the dominant male was hurt and was limping as a result. Soon juvenile males of the group started imitating his limp.\n解题思路：原文中幼年黑猩猩模仿受伤首领的跛行，与选项C“younger primates will purposefully replicate the physical impairments of an alpha figure as a form of social alignment”完全对应。","options":["human mimicry of successful models often transfers incorrectly to unrelated commercial items","visual attention can be mathematically mapped to alter consumer choices without their awareness","younger primates will purposefully replicate the physical impairments of an alpha figure as a form of social alignment","complex behavioral innovations can emerge and spread through an animal community via social learning","secret actors are financially compensated to blend into public spaces and surreptitiously advocate for commodities","animals can develop new habits by observation.","incentives are provided for consumers who behave in a certain way"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"66440","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"9210:66440:39","type":"choice","text":"The inclusion of the historic 1968 high-jump innovator Dick Fosbury demonstrates that ____","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题：题目问1968年跳高创新者Dick Fosbury的例子说明了什么，关键词是“Dick Fosbury”和“demonstrates”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的“Dick Fosbury”和“1968 high-jump innovator”定位到阅读材料J段。\n对应原文：When athlete Dick Fosbury revolutionised the high jump by jumping over the bar backward in 1968, imitators obviously copied his jumping style, not his brand of sports shoes. However, today, sportspeople appear in advertisements asking us to buy the laptops or sports drinks that they promote.\n解题思路：原文指出模仿者正确复制了Fosbury的跳法，但现代广告错误地将成功运动员与不相关的商品（如笔记本电脑）关联，对应选项A“人类对成功模型的模仿常错误地转移到不相关的商业物品上”。","options":["human mimicry of successful models often transfers incorrectly to unrelated commercial items","visual attention can be mathematically mapped to alter consumer choices without their awareness","younger primates will purposefully replicate the physical impairments of an alpha figure as a form of social alignment","complex behavioral innovations can emerge and spread through an animal community via social learning","secret actors are financially compensated to blend into public spaces and surreptitiously advocate for commodities","animals can develop new habits by observation.","incentives are provided for consumers who behave in a certain way"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"66440","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"9210:66440:40","type":"choice","text":"A defining characteristic of contemporary corporate marketing strategies is that ____","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"审题：题目问当代企业营销策略的一个定义性特征是什么，关键词是“contemporary corporate marketing strategies”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的“contemporary corporate marketing strategies”定位到阅读材料K段，该段描述了现代营销策略。\n对应原文：Today, companies engage in stealth marketing campaigns in which people are paid to frequent bars or websites to covertly promote certain products.\n解题思路：原文提到公司雇佣人员秘密推广产品，这与选项E“secret actors are financially compensated to blend into public spaces and surreptitiously advocate for commodities”完全对应，描述了当代营销策略中秘密推广的特征。","options":["human mimicry of successful models often transfers incorrectly to unrelated commercial items","visual attention can be mathematically mapped to alter consumer choices without their awareness","younger primates will purposefully replicate the physical impairments of an alpha figure as a form of social alignment","complex behavioral innovations can emerge and spread through an animal community via social learning","secret actors are financially compensated to blend into public spaces and surreptitiously advocate for commodities","animals can develop new habits by observation.","incentives are provided for consumers who behave in a certain way"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"66440","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"66430","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">Based on the text, which promotional method is intentionally designed to extend the duration of a consumer&#39;s visit to a retail environment?</span></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"66431","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">The author introduces the example of commercially packaged water to demonstrate that</span></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"66432","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">According to the author, a &quot;socially transmitted food preference&quot; takes place when</span></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"66433","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">&nbsp;According to the text, how does the cognitive capacity for observational mimicry serve as a beneficial asset?</span></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"66434","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27–31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">&nbsp;How do television promotions successfully exploit the human evolutionary drive to copy others?</span></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"66435","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32–36\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p>The initial 1938 diamond initiative achieved commercial success by explicitly linking the purchase of gemstones to themes of high material luxury.</p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"66436","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32–36\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p>Modern consumers are generally much more conscious of visual advertisements than they are of auditory marketing messages.</p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"66437","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32–36\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p>The structural transformation of courting rituals brought about by the historic diamond campaign yielded long-term benefits for modern society.</p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"66438","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32–36\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p>Academic consensus remains divided regarding whether non-human animals systematically mirror the actions of dominant group members.</p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"66439","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32–36\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p>Rational cognitive analysis allows consumers to see a direct causal link between a celebrity&#39;s professional success and the items they endorse.</p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"66440","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap.","html":"<p><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">37 The potato-cleansing routines observed among the primates on Koshima Island confirmed that</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[37] ____</strong></span></strong></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">38 The field observations recorded by primatologist Frans de Waal indicated that</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[38] ____</strong></span></strong></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">39 The inclusion of the historic 1968 high-jump innovator Dick Fosbury demonstrates that</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[39] ____</strong></span></strong></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">40 A defining characteristic of contemporary corporate marketing strategies is that</span></strong></p><p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[40] ____</strong></span></strong></p>","firstNumber":37}],"passage":"<p><strong>Marketing and mind control</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><em>How marketing and advertising appeal to the associative nature of the brain</em></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>While there had been a long tradition of giving rings as a commitment to marry, the custom of giving diamond engagement rings was in large part manufactured by one of the most effective marketing campaigns in history. In the early 1900s, diamond sales were declining, posing a serious problem for the company that essentially had control over the diamond market. In 1938, this company hired an advertising agency which proposed reshaping social attitudes toward diamonds. As well as magazines showing film stars draped in diamonds, the agency arranged for movies to incorporate diamond engagement rings into their plots. The campaign culminated with the slogan: &#39;A diamond is forever.&#39;</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>At the time, the approach was unique. Rather than pushing a brand, the objective was to promote diamonds as the symbol of everlasting love. This was achieved by exploiting the associative nature of the brain: associative neurons* activated by the concept of &#39;love&#39; with neurons that encoded the concept of &#39;diamonds&#39;. By 1941, diamond sales had increased by 55%.</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>Advertising comes in many forms, from blatant neon signs to subtly embedded products in movies. In each case, the goal is to mould our habits, desires and opinions. Our visual system is targeted by an avalanche of information on the internet, street posters, billboards and in movie theatres. Our auditory system submits to catchy radio jingles and telemarketers. More surreptitiously, our olfactory system is targeted by variations of vanilla and citrus perfumes aimed at enticing us to linger in a retail outlet.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>It is difficult to measure how effective these campaigns are, but as in the &#39;A diamond is forever&#39; campaign, they can be successful that they change the fabric of our culture. In the case of bottled water, we are swayed by advertising into paying for something that we can obtain for free. Most people cannot distinguish bottled from tap water, much less between brands of bottled water, which is why you rarely hear of a bottled water company proposing a blind taste test.</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>So why is marketing such an effective mind-control technique? It is interesting to consider whether other animals exhibit anything analogous to humans&#39; susceptibility to advertising. If we provide a lab rat with two types of cereal, it will consume approximately the same amount of each. However, if we put that rat with another rat that spent its day eating just one type, when faced with a choice, our rat will now show a preference for the same type as the other rat was eating. Psychologists call this &#39;socially transmitted food preference&#39;.</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>What many regard as the first documented examples of cultural learning in primates started with a clever monkey that lived in a colony of Japanese monkeys on the island of Koshima. She began taking the dirt-covered sweet potatoes to the river to wash them before eating them. Upon seeing this, a few other open-minded monkeys picked up on the idea. Potato washing then spread from monkey to monkey and, over the course of a few years, most monkeys were eating clean potatoes. Humans are clearly not the only animals to engage in imitation and social learning.</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>Learning by observation can be an extraordinarily valuable brain feature. This is how we learn to communicate and perform motor skills as well as deal with many everyday problems. For example, a newcomer struggling to purchase tickets and navigate the subway system in a foreign city may step back to learn from the people nearby. Humans and other primates exhibit multiple forms of imitative learning and this is called cultural transmission.</p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p>A component of advertising relies on the marketer’s ability to tap into the brain’s propensity for imitation. Anybody who has watched TV knows advertisements are disproportionately populated with attractive, successful-looking individuals. If we are going to imitate someone, we are more inclined to imitate those who appear to be popular and appealing.</p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p>Although not all researchers are convinced by the findings, a number of studies indicate that some animals also imitate dominant members of their group. Primatologist Frans de Waal provided anecdotal evidence of preferential imitation among chimpanzees. He noted that in one particular group the dominant male was hurt and was limping as a result. Soon juvenile males of the group started imitating his limp, a form of flattery that would have been unlikely if a non-dominant male had been injured.</p><p><strong>J</strong></p><p>Imitation is undoubtedly an invaluable ability, but often our propensity to imitate generalises indiscriminately, leading to poor decisions. When athlete Dick Fosbury revolutionised the high jump by jumping over the bar backward in 1968, imitators obviously copied his jumping style, not his brand of sports shoes. However, today, sportspeople appear in advertisements asking us to buy the laptops or sports drinks that they promote. Rationally, we know these people&#39;s success did not depend on these products, so it seems our prosperity to purchase products related more to neural programs that evolved to encourage imitation of those further up the social ladder.</p><p><strong>K</strong></p><p>Today, companies engage in stealth marketing campaigns in which people are paid to frequent bars or websites to covertly promote certain products. Companies also perform studies in which they track the eye movement of people viewing displays, and carefully craft names, packages and jingles associated with their products.</p><p><strong>L</strong></p><p>While we may like to believe that manipulation on a grand scale would not be possible, that’s not to say that advertising is innately harmful. To the contrary, the marketing of products or ideas is essential to human culture. The point is that we should ensure our choices reflect our actual goals and desires, and we must distinguish between the dissemination of information which is for our own good, and our manipulation for the benefit of companies.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9210&scene=%E5%95%86%E4%B8%9A%E7%BB%8F%E6%B5%8E&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9211","type":"reading","title":"R1 The Baobabs of Madagascar","book":"阅读真题集 21","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test4","part":0,"description":"阅读真题集 21 · Test4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"9211:66441:1","type":"choice","text":"Every single species of baobab found across Madagascar is entirely endemic to the island.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：判断“马达加斯加发现的每一种猴面包树都是该岛特有物种”这一说法是否正确，关键词是“every single species”和“entirely endemic”。\n定位关键信息：用“six species”和“exclusively on this island”定位到阅读材料A段。\n对应原文：Out of the eight documented species globally, six exist exclusively on this island. A seventh variety crossed the Mozambique Channel from the African mainland.\n解题思路：原文说全球八种猴面包树中，六种是马达加斯加特有，但第七种是从非洲大陆传入的，并非全部特有，因此题干“每一种都是特有”与原文矛盾，答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66441","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"9211:66442:2","type":"choice","text":"Adanson and Grandidier were the earliest European naturalists to explore the interior of Madagascar.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Adanson和Grandidier是否是最早探索马达加斯加内陆的欧洲博物学家，关键词是“earliest European naturalists”和“explore the interior”。\n定位关键信息：用“Adanson and Grandidier”和“European naturalists”定位到阅读材料A段末尾，但未提及他们探索内陆。\n对应原文：A段最后一句：“Adansonia grandidieri, named in honor of two prominent 19th-century French naturalists, Michel Adanson and Alfred Grandidier.”\n解题思路：原文只说明树以他们命名，未提供他们是否探索内陆或是否为最早欧洲博物学家的信息，因此答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66442","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"9211:66443:3","type":"choice","text":"Baobab populations are evenly distributed across the majority of Madagascar's geographic regions.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问猴面包树种群是否均匀分布在马达加斯加大部分地理区域，关键词为“evenly distributed”和“majority of Madagascar's geographic regions”。\n定位关键信息：用“distributed”和“geographic regions”定位到阅读材料B段，其中提到“strictly confined to the arid western coast”和“failing to grow in the more densely populated central plateaus”。\n对应原文：The trees are strictly confined to the arid western coast, failing to grow in the more densely populated central plateaus.\n解题思路：原文明确指出猴面包树严格局限于干旱的西海岸，无法在人口密集的中部高原生长，说明其分布不均匀且仅限于西部，而非均匀分布于大部分地区，因此答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66443","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"9211:66444:4","type":"choice","text":"Baobab populations are evenly distributed across the majority of Madagascar's geographic regions.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：判断马达加斯加大部分地理区域中猴面包树种群是否均匀分布，关键词为“evenly distributed”和“majority of Madagascar's geographic regions”。\n定位关键信息：根据“evenly distributed”和“geographic regions”定位到阅读材料B段，其中提到“strictly confined to the arid western coast, failing to grow in the more densely populated central plateaus”。\n对应原文：The trees are strictly confined to the arid western coast, failing to grow in the more densely populated central plateaus.\n解题思路：原文明确指出猴面包树严格局限于干旱的西海岸，无法在人口密集的中部高原生长，说明其分布不均匀，仅集中在特定区域，因此题干“均匀分布”与原文矛盾，答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66444","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"9211:66445:5","type":"choice","text":"Local populations exploit the baobab tree for a variety of practical commodities.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问当地居民是否利用猴面包树获取多种实用商品，关键词是“exploit”“variety of practical commodities”。\n定位关键信息：用“exploit”“practical commodities”定位到阅读材料C段，其中提到农民保留猴面包树是因为它们提供“nutritional crops”和“renewable structural components”。\n对应原文：Farmers intentionally preserved many baobabs because they offered valuable nutritional crops and renewable structural components.\n解题思路：原文明确说明农民保留猴面包树是因为它们提供有价值的营养作物和可再生结构部件，这对应了题干中的“多种实用商品”，因此答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66445","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"9211:66446:6","type":"choice","text":"Scientific experts are in total consensus regarding the exact factors causing the baobabs to tip over.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问科学家是否完全一致认同导致猴面包树倒下的确切因素，关键词是“total consensus”“exact factors”“tip over”。\n定位关键信息：用“exact factors”“tip over”定位到阅读材料C段中关于倒塌原因的讨论。\n对应原文：The precise mechanisms behind these collapses remain a subject of debate, though many researchers suspect that excess water drainage from neighboring agricultural systems plays a major role.\n解题思路：原文明确说“precise mechanisms remain a subject of debate”，即存在争议，与题干“total consensus”完全一致矛盾，因此答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"66446","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"9211:66447:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"soils","acceptedAnswers":["soils"],"explanation":"审题：题目问树木可能因农业径流在附近什么中积聚而倒塌，关键词是agricultural runoff和accumulating。\n定位关键信息：用agricultural runoff和accumulating定位到C段描述树木倒塌原因的部分。\n对应原文：their root networks deteriorate rapidly when subjected to permanently saturated soils\n解题思路：原文说农业径流导致土壤永久饱和，使根系恶化，所以空填soils。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66447","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7–13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","maxWords":1},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"9211:66447:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"cyclones","acceptedAnswers":["cyclones"],"explanation":"审题：题目问孤立个体面临被什么力量连根拔起的风险，关键词是“uprooted by powerful”。\n定位关键信息：用“isolated specimens”和“uprooted”定位到C段末尾。\n对应原文：isolated trees stripped of their protective forest buffer are highly vulnerable to intense cyclones, which regularly batter the coastline with winds exceeding 200 kph and can effortlessly topple a 30-meter-tall giant.\n解题思路：原文说孤立树木易受强烈气旋影响，气旋能轻易吹倒巨树，与“uprooted by powerful cyclones”对应。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66447","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7–13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","maxWords":1},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"9211:66447:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"farming","acceptedAnswers":["farming"],"explanation":"审题：题目问在Dense Forest Zones中，火被广泛用于清除自然生态系统以用于什么活动，关键词是activity。\n定位关键信息：用“fire is widely used to clear out land for... activity”定位到D段和E段，但具体对应原文在E段首句。\n对应原文：The main threat to their survival is land clearance for farming, which probably suppresses regeneration’\n解题思路：原文clearance 对应题干clear out ，因此答案是farming。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66447","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7–13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","maxWords":1},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"9211:66447:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"logging","acceptedAnswers":["logging"],"explanation":"审题：题目问商业行为如何改变森林结构、阻止新苗发芽，关键词是“commercial practice”。\n定位关键信息：用“commercial practice”和“forest structure”定位到Dense Forest Zones部分，原文E段提到“Commercial timber extraction and destructive logging”。\n对应原文：Commercial timber extraction and destructive logging within the remaining forests worsen the situation.\n解题思路：原文中“Commercial timber extraction and destructive logging”直接对应题干“commercial practice”，且“logging”是唯一符合“ONE WORD ONLY”要求的商业行为，导致森林结构改变。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66447","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7–13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","maxWords":1},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"9211:66447:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"animals","acceptedAnswers":["animals"],"explanation":"审题：题目问什么限制了猴面包树种子的自然传播，关键词是historical loss、prehistoric、natural spread of baobab seeds。\n定位关键信息：用prehistoric和natural spread of baobab seeds定位到原文E段关于种子传播瓶颈的描述。\n对应原文：Baum hypothesizes that natural propagation has been severely restricted due to the extinction of two massive native fauna species – a giant lemur ... and the flightless elephant bird.\n解题思路：原文指出两种史前巨型动物（giant lemur和elephant bird）的灭绝限制了种子传播，与题干prehistoric对应，正确答案是animals。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66447","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7–13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","maxWords":1},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"9211:66447:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"maps","acceptedAnswers":["maps"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Jim Bond与当地社区合作起草什么，关键词是draft detailed和pristine, undamaged wilderness zones。\n定位关键信息：用Jim Bond、local communities、draft detailed定位到F段。\n对应原文：Bond collaborates extensively with indigenous communities to track populations and generate precise maps of tree distribution.\n解题思路：原文中generate precise maps对应题干draft detailed maps，且maps是唯一符合ONE WORD ONLY的名词，因此答案为maps。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66447","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7–13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","maxWords":1},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"9211:66447:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"book","acceptedAnswers":["book"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Jim Bond的文化举措，关键词是“Compiling a cultural”和“centered on regional myths”。\n定位关键信息：用“cultural”和“regional myths”定位到阅读材料F段最后部分。\n对应原文：He also intends to publish an illustrated children's book chronicling traditional regional folklore about the species.\n解题思路：原文中“publish an illustrated children's book”对应题干“Compiling a cultural book”，且“traditional regional folklore”对应“regional myths”，因此答案为book。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66447","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7–13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","maxWords":1}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"66441","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Every single species of baobab found across Madagascar is entirely endemic to the island.</span></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"66442","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Adanson and Grandidier were the earliest European naturalists to explore the interior of Madagascar.</span></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"66443","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Baobab populations are evenly distributed across the majority of Madagascar&#39;s geographic regions.</span></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"66444","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Baobab populations are evenly distributed across the majority of Madagascar&#39;s geographic regions.</span></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"66445","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Lo</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">cal populations exploit the baobab tree for a variety of practical commodities.</span></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"66446","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1–6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Scientific experts are in total consensus regarding the exact factors causing the baobabs to tip over.</span></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"66447","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7–13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","html":"<p style=\"margin-top: 21px; margin-bottom: 21px; text-align: center;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 19px\">Baobabs under threat</span></strong></p><p style=\"margin-top: 21px;margin-bottom: 21px\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">Reasons why Madagascar&#39;s baobabs are declining in number:</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">The Morondava Region</span></strong></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; font-size: 13px;\">· </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">The trees are potentially collapsing due to agricultural runoff accumulating in nearby <strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong></strong></span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; font-size: 13px;\">· </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Individual, isolated specimens face an increased danger of being uprooted by powerful </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"></span></strong><strong style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong></strong></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\"><br/></span></strong></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">Dense Forest Zones</span></strong></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; font-size: 13px;\">· </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Habitat destruction: fire is widely used to clear out land for </span><strong style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong></strong> activity<span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; font-size: 13px;\">· </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">The commercial practice of </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"></span></strong><strong style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong></strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"> alters the forest structure, preventing new seedlings from germinating.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; font-size: 13px;\">· </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">The historical loss of particular prehistoric </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"></span></strong><strong style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong>&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">has severely limited the natural spread of baobab seeds.</span></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\"><br/></span></strong></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">Conservation Initiatives by Jim Bond</span></strong></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; font-size: 13px;\">· </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Working alongside local communities to draft detailed </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"></span></strong><strong style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong></strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"> of pristine, undamaged wilderness zones.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; font-size: 13px;\">· </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Compiling a cultural </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"></span></strong><strong style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong></strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"> centered on regional myths to highlight the tree&#39;s spiritual value.</span></p><p><br/></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":7}],"passage":"<p><strong>The Baobabs of Madagascar</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><em>The ancient baobabs of Madagascar are some of the largest and most distinctive trees in the world, but they face an uncertain future</em></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>Nestled in the Indian Ocean, the island nation of Madagascar stands as the premier destination for observing baobabs. These remarkable trees, instantly recognizable by their swollen, colossal trunks and flat, root-like upper canopies, boast lifespans extending beyond eight centuries. Out of the eight documented species globally, six exist exclusively on this island. A seventh variety crossed the Mozambique Channel from the African mainland, aided to some degree by human migration. Among the most heavily frequented and captured locations is the Avenue des Baobabs, situated in the western province of Menabe near Morondava. Here, a cluster of twelve grand trees flanks a dusty thoroughfare, rising 30 meters above the plains. Referred to locally as renala – meaning &#39;mother of the forest&#39; in Malagasy* – these specimens belong to the tallest species on Earth: Adansonia grandidieri, named in honor of two prominent 19th-century French naturalists, Michel Adanson and Alfred Grandidier.</p><p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">B</strong></p><p>While baobabs hold profound sacred and spiritual importance for numerous Malagasy communities, a large portion of the island&#39;s inhabitants have likely never encountered one in person. The trees are strictly confined to the arid western coast, failing to grow in the more densely populated central plateaus. Nonetheless, as Madagascar&#39;s official national emblem, the baobab serves as an ideal flagship symbol. It helps elevate public consciousness regarding both the country&#39;s highly threatened dry forests and the deep-rooted traditional mythologies of the ethnic groups living alongside them. Yet, the long-term outlook for these giants remains uncertain.</p><p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">C</strong></p><p>Paradoxically, the Avenue des Baobabs is not an untouched wilderness; the picturesque setting prized by international travelers is fundamentally an anthropogenic landscape. Although the trees themselves developed naturally, the open environment surrounding them was engineered by human activity. During the early decades of the 20th century, vast swaths of the Morondava basin were stripped of vegetation to establish industrial rice paddies and sugarcane plantations. Farmers intentionally preserved many baobabs because they offered valuable nutritional crops and renewable structural components, while other specimens simply survived the intense agricultural fires meant to clear the surrounding dry deciduous woodlands. Today, these lone survivors dot open agricultural fields like monuments to a vanished ecosystem. Unfortunately, even these massive organisms are beginning to collapse. &#39;With each passing year, I document newly fallen giants,&#39; notes Jim Bond, an ethnobotanist who has monitored Madagascar&#39;s baobabs for over a decade. The precise mechanisms behind these collapses remain a subject of debate, though many researchers suspect that excess water drainage from neighboring agricultural systems plays a major role. While baobabs are highly adapted to cyclical seasonal monsoons, their root networks deteriorate rapidly when subjected to permanently saturated soils. Furthermore, isolated trees stripped of their protective forest buffer are highly vulnerable to intense cyclones, which regularly batter the coastline with winds exceeding 200 kph and can effortlessly topple a 30-meter-tall giant.</p><p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">D</strong></p><p>Beyond the western plains, baobab populations across the rest of Madagascar face severe ecological pressures. The International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN) currently classifies three of the six endemic species as endangered. David Baum, a researcher from the University of Wisconsin who has spent years investigating these trees, points out the primary driver of their decline. &#39;<span style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;,sans-serif\">The main threat to their survival is land clearance for farming, which probably suppresses regeneration</span>,&#39; he explains.</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>Deliberate burning remains the standard strategy for clearing these habitats. Although baobabs possess evolutionary adaptations to withstand moderate heat, they eventually perish under a regime of repeated wildfires. Commercial timber extraction and destructive logging within the remaining forests worsen the situation. This environmental disruption stimulates the aggressive growth of dense, woody brush, which rapidly chokes out the sunlit forest clearings required for vulnerable baobab seedlings to take root and germinate. Another major bottleneck involves seed distribution. Baum hypothesizes that natural propagation has been severely restricted due to the extinction of two massive native fauna species – a giant lemur rivaling a gorilla in size and the flightless elephant bird, which grew up to three meters tall. The passage of seeds through the digestive systems of these massive, fruit-eating animals historically provided an essential mechanism for the distribution and germination of the renala species.</p><p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">F</strong></p><p>The Malagasy authorities are increasingly alarmed by this ecological decline, as the baobab remains a cornerstone of the country&#39;s ecotourism sector and its broader national economy. However, visiting the isolated trees standing in agricultural fields is not the only way to experience them. A short drive from Morondava reveals intact, old-growth dry forests where three distinct baobab species still thrive in their natural state. Bond has organized field studies involving both local and international researchers into the Mikea forest of southwestern Madagascar, a region recognized as one of the least disrupted and least documented baobab habitats left on Earth. Throughout these field operations, Bond collaborates extensively with indigenous communities to track populations and generate precise maps of tree distribution. He also intends to publish an illustrated children&#39;s book chronicling traditional regional folklore about the species, hoping that local and global distributions will foster deeper appreciation for the baobab&#39;s cultural legacy. Ultimately, rapid and unified intervention is required to transform the baobab into an example of environmental triumph rather than an indictment of human negligence.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9211&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9212","type":"reading","title":"R2 The internal body clock","book":"阅读真题集 21","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test4","part":0,"description":"阅读真题集 21 · Test4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"9212:66448:14","type":"choice","text":"support for an earlier finding from experiments on insects","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"审题：题目问哪一段包含对昆虫实验早期发现的支持，关键词是“support for an earlier finding from experiments on insects”。\n定位关键信息：用“experiments on insects”和“earlier finding”定位到F段，该段提到1971年果蝇实验支持了细胞自主节律的发现。\n对应原文：In 1971, geneticists at the California Institute of Technology studying fruit flies uncovered an astonishing breakthrough: they identified specific genes that directly controlled the daily behavioral rhythms of the insects, strongly implying that timing mechanisms were embedded directly inside individual cellular structures.\n解题思路：原文中1971年果蝇实验发现基因控制昆虫日常节律，支持了之前关于细胞内部时钟的早期发现，因此F段正确。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"66448","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has eight paragraphs, A–H. Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"9212:66448:15","type":"choice","text":"criticism of the way some research data was analysed","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问哪段包含对某些研究数据分析方式的批评，关键词是criticism、research data、analysed。\n定位关键信息：用criticism of data analysis定位到D段，该段讨论对生物节律研究的分析缺陷。\n对应原文：Of the remaining fraction that claimed positive results, the vast majority were marred by systemic analytical flaws ranging from mathematical miscalculations to fundamental statistical errors.\n解题思路：原文明确批评了声称阳性结果的研究存在系统性分析缺陷，如数学计算错误和统计错误，与题干“对数据分析方式的批评”直接对应。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"66448","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has eight paragraphs, A–H. Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"9212:66448:16","type":"choice","text":"reference to a basic test on a plant","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题：题目问哪段提到了一个对植物的基础测试，关键词是“basic test on a plant”。\n定位关键信息：用“basic test”和“plant”定位到描述早期植物实验的段落。\n对应原文：A段中“Jean-Jacques de Mairan placed a heliotrope plant inside a completely darkened room to observe its behavior”。\n解题思路：原文描述了一个将植物置于暗室观察其行为的简单实验，与题干“对植物的基础测试”直接对应，因此答案为A。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"66448","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has eight paragraphs, A–H. Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"9212:66448:17","type":"choice","text":"a statement that the length of natural cycles varies slightly between living things","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"审题：题目要求找出提到“不同生物的自然周期长度略有差异”这一陈述所在的段落，关键词为“length of natural cycles varies slightly between living things”。\n定位关键信息：用“varies slightly”和“natural cycles”定位到E段，其中描述了生物在无外界信号时采用“free-running”周期，且人类周期约为24.5小时，暗示差异。\n对应原文：In human subjects, this natural free-running cycle typically settles around a 24.5-hour duration.\n解题思路：原文指出人类自然周期约为24.5小时，而前文提到其他生物周期“approximate, but rarely match, a precise 24-hour day”，说明不同生物周期长度存在细微差异，与题干“varies slightly”对应。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"66448","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has eight paragraphs, A–H. Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"9212:66448:18","type":"choice","text":"reference to a theory that became popular with the public","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目问哪段提到一个曾受公众欢迎的理论，关键词是“theory that became popular with the public”。\n定位关键信息：用“popular with the public”和“theory”定位到描述公众兴趣的理论段落。\n对应原文：During the 1970s, mass-market publications began capturing public imagination by asserting that these periodic fluctuations were caused by 'biorhythms.'\n解题思路：原文提到“mass-market publications began capturing public imagination”，即大众出版物引发公众想象，对应题干“became popular with the public”，因此正确答案是C段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"66448","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has eight paragraphs, A–H. Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"9212:66449:19","type":"fill","text":"填写第 19 空","answer":"daylight","acceptedAnswers":["daylight"],"explanation":"审题：题目问SCN通过连接眼睛能感知什么，关键词是“perceive”和“connections to the eye”。\n定位关键信息：用“connections to the eye”和“perceive”定位到阅读材料F段。\n对应原文：Linked via neural pathways to specialized light-sensitive cells in the retina, the SCN directly perceives daylight.\n解题思路：原文明确说SCN通过神经通路连接视网膜感光细胞，直接感知daylight，与答案一致。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66449","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–22\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"9212:66449:20","type":"fill","text":"填写第 20 空","answer":"fruit flies","acceptedAnswers":["fruit flies"],"explanation":"审题：题目问“几年后，涉及什么的研究表明其正常行为的时间由细胞中的某些____或‘时钟’调节”，关键词是“research involving ____”和“timing of their normal actions”。\n定位关键信息：用“research involving”和“fruit flies”定位到原文F段，该段提到1971年遗传学家研究果蝇发现基因控制日常行为节律。\n对应原文：However, in 1971, geneticists at the California Institute of Technology studying fruit flies uncovered an astonishing breakthrough: they identified specific genes that directly controlled the daily behavioral rhythms of the insects.\n解题思路：原文明确提到“studying fruit flies”，与题干“research involving fruit flies”对应，因此第20空应填“fruit flies”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66449","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–22\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"9212:66449:21","type":"fill","text":"填写第 21 空","answer":"genes","acceptedAnswers":["genes"],"explanation":"审题：题目问“研究涉及什么生物，表明其正常行为时间由细胞内的某种基因或时钟调控”，关键词是“research involving”和“timing of their normal actions”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干“Several years later, research involving ____ showed that the timing of their normal actions was regulated by certain ____ or 'clocks', in their cells”，定位到阅读材料F段中关于1971年果蝇研究的描述。\n对应原文：In 1971, geneticists at the California Institute of Technology studying fruit flies uncovered an astonishing breakthrough: they identified specific genes that directly controlled the daily behavioral rhythms of the insects.\n解题思路：原文指出遗传学家通过研究果蝇发现了控制日常行为节律的特定基因，与题干“研究涉及果蝇，其正常行为时间由细胞内的基因调控”完全对应，因此答案填“fruit flies”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66449","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–22\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"9212:66449:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"circadian cycle","acceptedAnswers":["circadian cycle"],"explanation":"审题：题目问在黑暗实验中，单个SCN细胞维持了什么，关键词是“experiments in the dark”和“maintained by individual SCN cells”。\n定位关键信息：用“experiments in the dark”和“individual SCN cells”定位到F段末尾。\n对应原文：a research group at Massachusetts General Hospital successfully isolated individual nerve cells from the SCN and observed that they continued to chart a perfect circadian cycle completely isolated from any external light source.\n解题思路：原文指出分离的SCN细胞在无光环境下仍能维持“perfect circadian cycle”，与题干“a ____ was maintained by individual SCN cells”对应，因此答案为circadian cycle。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66449","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–22\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"9212:66450:23-24","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following problems are stated as being linked with the internal 'clock'?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目问哪两个问题与内部生物钟有关，关键词是problems linked with internal clock。\n定位关键信息：用problems和internal clock定位到B段，其中提到disruptions和dangers。\n对应原文：When an individual's natural timing system is wrenched out of alignment by overnight shift work... they can be rendered temporarily incapable of coherent thought or decisive action. Yet... automotive accident metrics reveal two highly lethal spikes... precisely when human cognitive vigilance plummets.\n解题思路：B段指出夜班工作导致思维和行动能力暂时丧失（对应B选项），以及交通事故在特定时间增加（对应C选项），因此B和C正确。","options":["a decrease in output in workplaces without windows to let in natural light","a failure among workers on night-shifts to perform tasks","an increase in casualties on the roads at specific times of day","a decline in efficiency on certain days in a number of fixed cycles","a rise in mood swings dependent on the appearance of the Sun"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"66450","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 23–24\nChoose TWO correct answers.","groupId":"66450-9212:66450:23-24"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"9212:66450:23-24","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following problems are stated as being linked with the internal 'clock'?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目问哪两个问题与内部生物钟有关，关键词是problems linked with internal clock。\n定位关键信息：用problems和internal clock定位到B段，其中提到disruptions和dangers。\n对应原文：When an individual's natural timing system is wrenched out of alignment by overnight shift work... they can be rendered temporarily incapable of coherent thought or decisive action. Yet... automotive accident metrics reveal two highly lethal spikes... precisely when human cognitive vigilance plummets.\n解题思路：B段指出夜班工作导致思维和行动能力暂时丧失（对应B选项），以及交通事故在特定时间增加（对应C选项），因此B和C正确。","options":["a decrease in output in workplaces without windows to let in natural light","a failure among workers on night-shifts to perform tasks","an increase in casualties on the roads at specific times of day","a decline in efficiency on certain days in a number of fixed cycles","a rise in mood swings dependent on the appearance of the Sun"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"66450","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 23–24\nChoose TWO correct answers.","groupId":"66450-9212:66450:23-24"},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"9212:66451:25-26","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following issues relating to internal 'clocks' remain to be solved, according to information in the passage?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目问根据文章，关于内部“生物钟”哪两个问题仍未解决，关键词是remain to be solved。\n定位关键信息：用remain to be solved和mysteries定位到G段，寻找未解答的问题。\n对应原文：G段：Nevertheless, fundamental mysteries persist: how do billions of independent cellular mechanisms manage to remain perfectly synchronized with one another, and why did primordial life evolve an intrinsic reliance on solar cycles in the first place?\n解题思路：原文指出两个未解之谜：一是细胞机制如何同步（对应选项D），二是生命为何依赖太阳周期（对应选项C），因此正确答案是C和D。","options":["the precise length of the free-running daily cycle in different animals","the reason for 'clocks' being temporarily driven out of synchronisation","the reason for living beings forming a connection with the Sun's rhythms","the way in which all 'clocks' in a single organism are able to stay in step with one another","the location of the 'clocks' across the whole range of living organisms"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"66451","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 25–26\nChoose TWO correct answers.","groupId":"66451-9212:66451:25-26"},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"9212:66451:25-26","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following issues relating to internal 'clocks' remain to be solved, according to information in the passage?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问根据文章，关于内部“生物钟”哪两个问题仍未解决，关键词是remain to be solved。\n定位关键信息：用remain to be solved和mysteries定位到G段，寻找未解答的问题。\n对应原文：G段：Nevertheless, fundamental mysteries persist: how do billions of independent cellular mechanisms manage to remain perfectly synchronized with one another, and why did primordial life evolve an intrinsic reliance on solar cycles in the first place?\n解题思路：原文指出两个未解之谜：一是细胞机制如何同步（对应选项D），二是生命为何依赖太阳周期（对应选项C），因此正确答案是C和D。","options":["the precise length of the free-running daily cycle in different animals","the reason for 'clocks' being temporarily driven out of synchronisation","the reason for living beings forming a connection with the Sun's rhythms","the way in which all 'clocks' in a single organism are able to stay in step with one another","the location of the 'clocks' across the whole range of living organisms"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"66451","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 25–26\nChoose TWO correct answers.","groupId":"66451-9212:66451:25-26"}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"66450-9212:66450:23-24","numbers":[23,24],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["B","C"]},{"id":"66451-9212:66451:25-26","numbers":[25,26],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["C","D"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"66448","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14–18\nThe text has eight paragraphs, A–H. Which paragraph contains the following information?","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">support for an earlier finding from experiments on insects <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong></span></p><p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\"></span></p><p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">criticism of the way some research data was analysed&nbsp; <strong class=\"source-blank\">[15] ____</strong></span></p><p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">reference to a basic test on a plant&nbsp; <strong class=\"source-blank\">[16] ____</strong></span></p><p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">a statement that the length of natural cycles varies slightly between living things&nbsp; <strong class=\"source-blank\">[17] ____</strong></span></p><p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">reference to a theory that became popular with the public&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[18] ____</strong></span></span></p><p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\"></span><br/></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"66449","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19–22\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">An overview of research into the existence of the internal &#39;clock&#39;</span></strong></p><p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">Towards the end of the 1960s, research into the SCN, which is located in the hypothalamus, led chronobiologists to believe they had found the internal &#39;clock&#39; at last. Their theory was based on the fact that certain hormones that regulate the timing of physical functions are controlled by the SCN. The SCN is able to perceive <strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong></strong></span><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">&nbsp;as a result of connections to the eye.</span></p><p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">Several years later, research involving </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\"></span></strong><strong style=\"font-family: Arial; white-space: normal;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong></strong><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\"> showed that the timing of their normal actions was regulated by certain </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\"></span></strong><strong style=\"font-family: Arial; white-space: normal;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong></strong><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\"> or &#39;clocks&#39;, in their cells. Thus the internal &#39;clock&#39; is not an individual mechanism, as previously thought, but exists within each cell. Other scientists went on to conduct experiments in the dark that proved that a </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\"></span></strong><strong style=\"font-family: Arial; white-space: normal;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong></strong><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\"> was maintained by individual SCN cells.</span></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"66450","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 23–24\nChoose TWO correct answers.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">Which </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">TWO</span></strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\"> of the following problems are stated as being linked with the internal &#39;clock&#39;?</span></p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"66451","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 25–26\nChoose TWO correct answers.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">Which </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\">TWO</span></strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 16px\"> of the following issues relating to internal &#39;clocks&#39; remain to be solved, according to information in the passage?</span></p>","firstNumber":25}],"passage":"<p><strong>The internal body clock</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><em>Each of our cells has an internal &#39;clock&#39; which dictates our daily rhythms. But why?</em></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>From massive mammals to microscopic bacteria, ancient oaks to simple pond algae, nearly all living organisms follow the same unyielding 24-hour cycle, long assumed to be driven entirely by the rising and setting of the Sun. Or is it? Over two and a half centuries ago, a French researcher executed a straightforward experiment that shattered the assumption that terrestrial life merely obeys solar commands. Intrigued by the predictable manner in which specific flowers unfurl and fold their leaves each day, Jean-Jacques de Mairan placed a heliotrope plant inside a completely darkened room to observe its behavior. He anticipated that the specimen, stripped of all solar cues, would cease its daily routine. To his profound amazement, the leaves continued to expand and contract on schedule, acting as if they were answering to a hidden, internal timekeeper.</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>But what exactly constitutes this internal timekeeper, where is it housed, and how does it maintain such impeccable precision? These questions form the baseline of chronobiology—the scientific discipline dedicated to examining temporal impacts on living systems. Resolving these mysteries extends far beyond satisfying academic curiosity. Disruptions to our internal clocks introduce severe practical hardships. When an individual&#39;s natural timing system is wrenched out of alignment by overnight shift work or transmeridian aviation, they can be rendered temporarily incapable of coherent thought or decisive action. Yet, even when operating flawlessly, these internally generated peaks and valleys of alertness carry inherent dangers: automotive accident metrics reveal two highly lethal spikes, occurring at 4 a.m. and again twelve hours later, precisely when human cognitive vigilance plummets to its lowest ebbs.</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>During the 1970s, mass-market publications began capturing public imagination by asserting that these periodic fluctuations were caused by &#39;biorhythms.&#39; This popular hypothesis posited that a trio of independent cycles began at the exact moment of an individual&#39;s birth, governing their physical, emotional, and intellectual attributes over repeating intervals of 23, 28, and 33 days, respectively. Adherents claimed these cycles generated predictable &#39;critical days,&#39; during which overlapping downward trends resulted in compromised performance and elevated risks of personal mishap.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>The scientific community has since thoroughly debunked biorhythms as a pseudoscience, maintaining that this specific trio of cycles lacks any empirical foundation. In 1998, Dr. Terence Hines of Pace University published a definitive meta-analysis of biorhythm claims, scrutinizing the data from over 130 independent projects. His investigation revealed that three-quarters of those studies failed to yield any empirical data favoring the biorhythm model. Of the remaining fraction that claimed positive results, the vast majority were marred by systemic analytical flaws ranging from mathematical miscalculations to fundamental statistical errors, while the tiny handful of genuinely positive outcomes were easily dismissed as mathematical flukes.</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>Conversely, the reality of near-24-hour biological cycles&nbsp;–&nbsp;properly termed circadian rhythms&nbsp;–&nbsp;is undisputed. Building upon de Mairan&#39;s foundational work, subsequent investigators confirmed that when isolated from environmental solar cues, organisms adopt &quot;free-running&quot; behavioral cycles that approximate, but rarely match, a precise 24-hour day. In human subjects, this natural free-running cycle typically settles around a 24.5-hour duration. The specific parameters of this circadian rhythm (derived from the Latin words for &#39;about a day&#39;) are dictated directly by our enigmatic internal pacemaker.</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>By the late 1960s, chronobiologists believed they had successfully isolated this central pacemaker within the suprachiasmatic nucleus (SCN)&nbsp;–&nbsp;a dense cluster of neurons situated in the hypothalamus region of the brain. Linked via neural pathways to specialized light-sensitive cells in the retina, the SCN directly perceives daylight. Upon detecting light, it orchestrates the systematic secretion of systemic hormones like melatonin, keeping internal metabolic operations strictly aligned with the external environment. For several years, science treated the SCN as the solitary master clock in complex organisms. However, in 1971, geneticists at the California Institute of Technology studying fruit flies uncovered an astonishing breakthrough: they identified specific genes that directly controlled the daily behavioral rhythms of the insects, strongly implying that timing mechanisms were embedded directly inside individual cellular structures. Strong validation of this cellular autonomy arrived in 1995, when a research group at Massachusetts General Hospital successfully isolated individual nerve cells from the SCN and observed that they continued to chart a perfect circadian cycle completely isolated from any external light source. Ultimately, in 1997, researchers at Northwestern University identified a specific gene that governs the daily cyclical activities of cells within mammalian tissues.</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>While the exact biochemical pathways of this gene, designated CLOCK, remain the subject of intense investigation, its discovery promises to yield advanced countermeasures for managing the fallout of night-shift schedules and jet-lag. Professor Joseph Takahashi, who spearheaded the breakthrough, notes that because circadian regulators operate universally across our tissues, medicine will require entirely new therapeutic interventions capable of resetting every cell simultaneously. Nevertheless, fundamental mysteries persist: how do billions of independent cellular mechanisms manage to remain perfectly synchronized with one another, and why did primordial life evolve an intrinsic reliance on solar cycles in the first place? As of now, definitive answers remain elusive, though hypotheses abound – such as the idea that external sunlight acts as a universal coordinating signal to keep the body&#39;s myriad cellular clocks ticking in lockstep.</p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p>To unravel these mysteries, contemporary researchers are focusing their attention on a primitive microbe known as cyanobacterium. In 2005, an experimental team at Nagoya University demonstrated that the molecular interactions among three proteins synthesized by this bacterium rose and fell in a precise 24-hour wave. Because cyanobacteria represent one of the oldest lines of evolutionary descent on Earth, this evidence suggests that cellular timekeeping architectures have been operating for upwards of three billion years. Every complex organism that evolved later has simply maintained this ancient lineage; as Professor Carl Johnson of Vanderbilt University states, bacteria, fungi, plants, and animals all appear to have developed their respective internal clock frameworks independently of one another. Exactly why this occurred is still a mystery, but one truth is undeniable: the daily choreography of life is anything but a modern adaptation.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9212&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-9213","type":"reading","title":"R3 The Antikythera Mechanism","book":"阅读真题集 21","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test4","part":0,"description":"阅读真题集 21 · Test4 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"9213:66460:27","type":"fill","text":"填写第 27 空","answer":"giant clams","acceptedAnswers":["giant clams"],"explanation":"审题：题目问潜水员原本在寻找什么，关键词是“looking for”。\n定位关键信息：用“looking for”和“diver”定位到原文A段中关于潜水员目的的描述。\n对应原文：One spring day in 1900, a party of Greek sponge divers took shelter from a storm near the island of Antikythera... one of the group, Elias Stadiatis, decided to dive in search of giant clams to eat for their dinner.\n解题思路：原文明确说潜水员“in search of giant clams”，与题干“looking for”对应，因此答案为giant clams。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66460","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"9213:66460:28","type":"fill","text":"填写第 28 空","answer":"ten months","acceptedAnswers":["ten months"],"explanation":"审题：题目问潜水员受委托打捞文物，花了多长时间打捞物品，关键词是“spent”和“retrieving items”。\n定位关键信息：用“spent”和“retrieving items”定位到原文A段中描述打捞时间的句子。\n对应原文：They spent the next ten months bringing up pieces of marble and bronze statues, amphorae, lamps and coins...\n解题思路：原文明确说“spent the next ten months”，与题干“spent ten months”完全对应，因此答案为ten months。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66460","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"9213:66460:29","type":"fill","text":"填写第 29 空","answer":"marble","acceptedAnswers":["marble"],"explanation":"审题：题目问潜水员打捞的雕塑材质，关键词是“sculptures made of”和“bronze”。\n定位关键信息：用“sculptures”和“bronze”定位到原文中描述打捞物品的句子。\n对应原文：They spent the next ten months bringing up pieces of marble and bronze statues...\n解题思路：原文“marble and bronze statues”对应题干“sculptures made of marble and bronze”，因此答案为marble。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66460","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"9213:66460:30","type":"fill","text":"填写第 30 空","answer":"wooden casing","acceptedAnswers":["wooden casing"],"explanation":"审题：题目问潜水员发现的另一件物品是什么，关键词是“Another item they found was a ____ which contained a piece of metal”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干“Another item they found”和“contained a piece of metal”，定位到阅读材料B段首句。\n对应原文：Among the artefacts retrieved from the shipwreck was a rather unprepossessing lump of bronze inside what seemed to be a wooden casing.\n解题思路：原文描述打捞物中有一个“lump of bronze”，与题干“a ____ which contained a piece of metal”对应，因此正确答案为wooden casing。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66460","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"9213:66460:31","type":"fill","text":"填写第 31 空","answer":"inscriptions","acceptedAnswers":["inscriptions"],"explanation":"审题：题目问考古学家注意到的一块碎片上有什么，关键词是“one of which had ____ on it”。\n定位关键信息：用“one of which had”和“archaeologist noticed”定位到原文中描述Valerios Stais发现碎片细节的部分。\n对应原文：The largest of these fragments was a dial about 14 cm in diameter, with some inscriptions on it.\n解题思路：原文说最大碎片是一个表盘，上面有“inscriptions”，与题干“one of which had ____ on it”对应，因此答案为inscriptions。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66460","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"9213:66460:32","type":"fill","text":"填写第 32 空","answer":"mechanical clock","acceptedAnswers":["mechanical clock"],"explanation":"审题：题目问研究者最初认为该人工制品可能是什么，关键词是“thought at first that the artefact might have been a”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干“leading the investigators to think at first that the artefact might have been a”定位到原文B段末尾。\n对应原文：The evidence seemed to point to this being part of a kind of mechanical clock, but the researchers ultimately rejected this possibility as the wreck had been dated to the first century BCE.\n解题思路：原文指出证据指向“a kind of mechanical clock”，与题干“might have been a mechanical clock”对应，因此正确答案为mechanical clock。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"66460","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"9213:66462:33","type":"choice","text":"Elias Stadiatis had not intended ____","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Elias Stadiatis原本没有打算做什么，关键词是“had not intended”。\n定位关键信息：用“Elias Stadiatis”定位到原文A段，寻找描述他意图的否定表达。\n对应原文：He reported his find to the authorities and, in the autumn, he and his companions returned to dive on the Antikythera wreck on behalf of the Greek government.\n解题思路：原文说Stadiatis最初潜水是为了找蛤蜊吃，并非有意发现文物，因此正确答案C“to discover historical artifacts”符合他无意发现历史文物的意图。","options":["to calculate how the calendar operated","to identify problems in aeronautical components.","to discover historical artifacts","to link the ancient device to theories about extra terrestrials","to use gears to calculate astronomical movements","to discover that there was more to the mechanism than first thought","to create a visual representation of the inside of the mechanism","to retrieve the outstanding relics."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"66462","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 33–37\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"9213:66462:34","type":"choice","text":"The group of divers were asked ____","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"审题：题目问“这群潜水员被要求做什么”，关键词是“group of divers were asked”。\n定位关键信息：用“group of divers”和“asked”定位到原文A段，描述潜水员受命打捞文物。\n对应原文：He reported his find to the authorities and, in the autumn, he and his companions returned to dive on the Antikythera wreck on behalf of the Greek government. They spent the next ten months bringing up pieces of marble and bronze statues, amphorae, lamps and coins.\n解题思路：原文说潜水员代表希腊政府返回沉船处，花了十个月打捞文物，对应选项H“to retrieve the outstanding relics”（打捞杰出的文物）。","options":["to calculate how the calendar operated","to identify problems in aeronautical components.","to discover historical artifacts","to link the ancient device to theories about extra terrestrials","to use gears to calculate astronomical movements","to discover that there was more to the mechanism than first thought","to create a visual representation of the inside of the mechanism","to retrieve the outstanding relics."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"66462","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 33–37\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"9213:66462:35","type":"choice","text":"Valerios Stais was the first ____","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Valerios Stais是第一个做什么的人，关键词为Valerios Stais、first。\n定位关键信息：用Valerios Stais定位到B段，寻找描述他首次发现或行动的内容。\n对应原文：It wasn't until May 1902 that the leading Greek archaeologist Valerios Stais noticed that the wooden covering had dried out and split open, and the fused lump of metal inside it had separated into several pieces.\n解题思路：原文说Stais注意到木壳裂开、金属块分离成几块，对应选项F“发现这个装置比最初想象的更复杂”，即他首次意识到机制内部有更多结构。","options":["to calculate how the calendar operated","to identify problems in aeronautical components.","to discover historical artifacts","to link the ancient device to theories about extra terrestrials","to use gears to calculate astronomical movements","to discover that there was more to the mechanism than first thought","to create a visual representation of the inside of the mechanism","to retrieve the outstanding relics."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"66462","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 33–37\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"9213:66462:36","type":"choice","text":"Derek de Solla Price first managed ____","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Derek de Solla Price首次成功做了什么，关键词是“Derek de Solla Price first managed”。\n定位关键信息：用“Derek de Solla Price”和“first managed”定位到阅读材料C段，描述Price首次提出机制用途。\n对应原文：Price realised that the inscriptions on the large dial indicated days, months and zodiac signs and theorised that the device used gears to trace the paths of the sun, moon and other planets in relation to the earth and to indicate their position at any given moment.\n解题思路：原文中Price“theorised that the device used gears to trace the paths of the sun, moon and other planets”，对应选项E“to use gears to calculate astronomical movements”，即首次成功提出机制用齿轮计算天文运动。","options":["to calculate how the calendar operated","to identify problems in aeronautical components.","to discover historical artifacts","to link the ancient device to theories about extra terrestrials","to use gears to calculate astronomical movements","to discover that there was more to the mechanism than first thought","to create a visual representation of the inside of the mechanism","to retrieve the outstanding relics."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"66462","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 33–37\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"9213:66462:37","type":"choice","text":"The Antikythera Mechanism Research Project used technology originally created ____","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Antikythera Mechanism Research Project使用的技术最初是为哪个目的创造的，关键词是“technology originally created”。\n定位关键信息：根据“technology originally created”定位到原文E段，描述项目使用先进成像设备，其中一台机器最初是为检测飞机涡轮叶片裂纹而设计的。\n对应原文：One machine, nicknamed BladeRunner, was originally designed to detect cracks in aircraft turbine blades by means of three-dimensional X-ray technology.\n解题思路：原文说明BladeRunner机器最初用于检测飞机涡轮叶片裂纹，对应选项B“to identify problems in aeronautical components”，即识别航空部件中的问题。","options":["to calculate how the calendar operated","to identify problems in aeronautical components.","to discover historical artifacts","to link the ancient device to theories about extra terrestrials","to use gears to calculate astronomical movements","to discover that there was more to the mechanism than first thought","to create a visual representation of the inside of the mechanism","to retrieve the outstanding relics."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"66462","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 33–37\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"9213:66463:38","type":"choice","text":"How is the mechanism similar to more contemporary clock designs?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目问机制如何与更现代的时钟设计相似，关键词是similar to contemporary clock designs。\n定位关键信息：用contemporary clock designs定位到F段，寻找与现代时钟的相似点。\n对应原文：Like the clocks our grandparents' generation kept on the mantelpiece, the mechanism had a circular dial at the front with rotating hands.\n解题思路：原文说机制有圆形表盘和旋转指针，这与现代时钟的圆形指针设计相似，因此选项C正确。","options":["It has a small, box shape.","The casing is made of wood.","It has hands which turn around in a circle.","It indicates how many minutes and hours have passed."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"66463","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38–40\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"9213:66464:39","type":"choice","text":"Which of the following does the Antikythera mechanism NOT display to an observer?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Antikythera mechanism不能向观察者展示什么，关键词为NOT display。\n定位关键信息：用“display”和选项内容定位到材料F段和G段关于机制功能的描述。\n对应原文：F段“these hands indicated the positions of the sun and the moon in the sky... as well as of Mercury, Venus, Mars, Jupiter and Saturn”；G段“showed when solar and lunar eclipses would take place”。\n解题思路：原文显示机制能展示太阳、月亮和行星位置及日月食日期，但未提及火星的卫星数量，因此C项“火星的卫星数量”是机制不能展示的。","options":["The current position of the moon in the sky.","Where to look if you want to see Jupiter at night","The number of moons belonging to Mars.","The date of the next lunar eclipse"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"66464","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38–40\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"9213:66465:40","type":"choice","text":"What do our current models of the mechanism show","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题：题目问当前模型揭示了什么，关键词是“current models”和“show”。\n定位关键信息：用“current models”定位到阅读材料G段最后一句。\n对应原文：These reveal the outstanding mechanical skills and astronomical knowledge of whoever built the Antikythera mechanism two thousand years or more before we developed the technological skills to start unlocking its secrets.\n解题思路：原文说模型揭示建造者技能远超当时，直到现代才具备解锁技术，对应选项A“设计先进，现代才理解”。","options":["The mechanism is so advanced in design, we couldn't understand it until modern times.","The creators of the Antikythera mechanism knew far more about astronomy than we do.","We have only recently possessed the technology that belonged to the ancient Greeks.","There are still things we don't understand about the Antikythera mechanism."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"66465","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38–40\nChoose the correct answer."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"66460","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 27–32\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","html":"<p style=\"margin-top: 21px; margin-bottom: 21px; text-align: left;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;font-size: 19px\">The Discovery of the Antikythera Mechanism</span></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 150%\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;line-height:150%;font-size:16px\">The Antikythera mechanism was discovered by a diver who was looking for <strong class=\"source-blank\">[27] ____</strong></span>&nbsp;<span style=\";font-family:Arial;line-height:150%;font-size:16px\">. Instead, he found the remains of an ancient ship, from which he took proof to show his fellow divers. Having been commissioned to recover the relics, the same divers spent </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;line-height: 150%;font-size: 16px\"></span></strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[28] ____</strong></span><span style=\";font-family:Arial;line-height:150%;font-size:16px\"></span><span style=\";font-family:Arial;line-height:150%;font-size:16px\"> retrieving items such as sculptures made of </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;line-height: 150%;font-size: 16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"></span></span></strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[29] ____</strong></span><span style=\";font-family:Arial;line-height:150%;font-size:16px\"></span> <span style=\";font-family:Arial;line-height:150%;font-size:16px\">and bronze</span><span style=\";font-family:Arial;line-height:150%;font-size:16px\"> for the National Museum. Another item they found was a </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;line-height: 150%;font-size: 16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"></span></span></strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[30] ____</strong></span><span style=\";font-family:Arial;line-height:150%;font-size:16px\"></span> <span style=\";font-family:Arial;line-height:150%;font-size:16px\">which contained a piece of metal. This was ignored until over a year later when a renowned archaeologist noticed that the inside was composed of several pieces, one of which had </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;line-height: 150%;font-size: 16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"></span></span></strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[31] ____</strong></span><span style=\";font-family:Arial;line-height:150%;font-size:16px\"></span><span style=\";font-family:Arial;line-height:150%;font-size:16px\"> on it, and others appeared to be apparatus of some sort, leading the investigators to think at first that the artefact might have been a </span><strong><span style=\"font-family: 微软雅黑;line-height: 150%;font-size: 16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"></span></span></strong><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[32] ____</strong></span><span style=\";font-family:Arial;line-height:150%;font-size:16px\"></span><span style=\";font-family:Arial;line-height:150%;font-size:16px\"> although the historical origin of it suggested this was impossible.</span></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"66462","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 33–37\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Elias Stadiatis had not intended <strong class=\"source-blank\">[33] ____</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">The group of divers were asked <strong class=\"source-blank\">[34] ____</strong></span></span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">Valerios Stais was the first <strong class=\"source-blank\">[35] ____</strong></span></span></span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">Derek de Solla Price first managed&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[36] ____</strong></span></span></span></span></span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">The Antikythera Mechanism Research Project used technology originally created&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[37] ____</strong></span></span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\"><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\"></span></span></span></span><br/></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"66463","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38–40\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">How is the mechanism similar to more contemporary clock designs?</span></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"66464","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38–40\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following does the Antikythera mechanism NOT display to an observer?</span></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"66465","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38–40\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><span style=\";font-family:Arial;font-size:16px\">What do our current models of the mechanism show</span></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p><strong>The Antikythera Mechanism</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong>One spring day in 1900, a party of Greek sponge divers took shelter from a storm near the island of Antikythera, which lies about 50 kilometres northwest of the western tip of Crete. After the storm, one of the group, Elias Stadiatis, decided to dive in search of giant clams to eat for their dinner. On a shelf about 43 metres below the surface of the water, he chanced upon the wreck of an ancient ship. Fragments of statues, looking like body parts, covered this ledge. The diver returned to the surface, bearing an arm made of bronze as proof of what he had discovered. He reported his find to the authorities and, in the autumn, he and his companions returned to dive on the Antikythera wreck on behalf of the Greek government. They spent the next ten months bringing up pieces of marble and bronze statues, amphorae, lamps and coins, all of which were sent to the National Museum in Athens for cleaning and restoration.</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong>Among the artefacts retrieved from the shipwreck was a rather unprepossessing lump of bronze inside what seemed to be a wooden casing. This object was covered in barnacles and badly corroded by seawater, and didn&#39;t attract much attention at first. It wasn&#39;t until May 1902 that the leading Greek archaeologist Valerios Stais noticed that the wooden covering had dried out and split open, and the fused lump of metal inside it had separated into several pieces. The largest of these fragments was a dial about 14 cm in diameter, with some inscriptions on it. Some other fragments also appeared to be parts of dials with perfectly formed triangular teeth, like gear wheels. The evidence seemed to point to this being part of a kind of mechanical clock, but the researchers ultimately rejected this possibility as the wreck had been dated to the first century BCE, and it was known that precise gears like these had not existed until fourteen centuries after that.</p><p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\"><br/></strong></p><p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">C&nbsp;</strong>Little progress on identifying either the purpose or origins of the mechanism was made until the late 1950s, when the device attracted the attention of a British-born polymath, Derek de Solla Price, who was working at Princeton University in the United States. Price realised that the inscriptions on the large dial indicated days, months and zodiac signs and theorised that the device used gears to trace the paths of the sun, moon and other planets in relation to the earth and to indicate their position at any given moment by means of pointers that had since been lost. Although his interpretation was basically sound, further research was hampered by the fact that only a few of the gears appear on the surface of the fused metal fragments of the mechanism.</p><p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\"><br/></strong></p><p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">D&nbsp;</strong>In 1971, the National Museum in Athens gave permission for Price, working with a Greek radiographer, to X-ray the fragments of the Antikythera mechanism. These two-dimensional images revealed many of the hidden gears and allowed Price to develop schematic drawings of how the mechanism must have worked. What he discovered confounded all previous theories of technology in the Hellenistic era and indicated that the ancient Greeks&#39; mechanical know-how and knowledge of astronomy came close to that of modern times. However, despite positive scholarly reviews of Price&#39;s work, his idea that the Antikythera mechanism is an ancient analogue computer, published in his 1974 book &#39;Gears from the Greeks&#39;, fell on deaf ears where mainstream historians were concerned. This may have been due, at least in part, to the contemporaneous popularity of books by the Swiss writer Erich von Daniken, who postulated that ancient aliens had brought advanced technology to earth; Price&#39;s work may have inadvertently become associated with fringe theories and UFO-hunters as a result.</p><p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\"><br/></strong></p><p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">E&nbsp;</strong>Whatever the reason, little more official research was conducted on the mechanism until the 2005 launch of the Antikythera Mechanism Research Project, an international, multi-disciplinary study that operates under the supervision of the Hellenic Ministry of Culture. The project examined the fragments of the Antikythera mechanism using state-of-the-art imaging equipment. One machine, nicknamed BladeRunner, was originally designed to detect cracks in aircraft turbine blades by means of three-dimensional X-ray technology. This project is ongoing and new findings are being constantly made and revealed. Enough has already been discovered to vindicate Price.</p><p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\"><br/></strong></p><p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">F&nbsp;</strong>This modern research places the construction of the mechanism towards the end of the second century BCE and confirms that its bronze dials and gears would have been housed in a wooden box roughly the size of a modern shoebox. Like the clocks our grandparents&#39; generation kept on the mantelpiece, the mechanism had a circular dial at the front with rotating hands. Rather than showing hours and minutes, however, these hands indicated the positions of the sun and the moon in the sky at any given time, as well as of Mercury, Venus, Mars, Jupiter and Saturn, the five planets that are visible to the naked human eye.</p><p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\"><br/></strong></p><p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">G&nbsp;</strong>In addition, the mechanism also allowed for the fact that the orbit of some planets around the sun appears to go backwards, or &#39;retrograde&#39;, at certain times during the celestial cycle. It has also been discovered that there were two dials on the back of the mechanism, one of which was a calendar and the other which showed when solar and lunar eclipses would take place. A number of breathtaking models of the mechanism have been produced, including one made out of Lego blocks. These reveal the outstanding mechanical skills and astronomical knowledge of whoever built the Antikythera mechanism two thousand years or more before we developed the technological skills to start unlocking its secrets.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=9213&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8913","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Otter","book":"阅读还原集Vol.19","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.19 · Test 2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8913:64428:1","type":"choice","text":"1 a description of how otters regulate vision underwater","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In clear water and good light, otters can hunt fish by sight. The otter’s eyes and nostrils are placed high on its head so that it can see and breathe even when the rest of the body is submerged.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问哪一段“描述水獭如何在水中调节视力的”。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"regulate vision underwater\"定位到文章中描述水獭在水下视觉调节的句子。\n解题思路：B段中提到，水獭虽有小眼睛且在陆地上可能近视，但能通过调节晶状体形状使其更接近球形，从而克服水体折射。在清澈水域和充足光线条件下，水獭可依靠视觉捕食鱼类。这些内容直接对应题目中的描述，因此答案为B。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64428","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-9\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-G Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 1-9 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8913:64428:2","type":"choice","text":"2 the fit-for-purpose characteristics of otter’s body shape","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Otters have long, thin bodies and short legs – ideal for pushing through dense undergrowth or hunting in tunnels. An adult male may be up to 4 feet long and 30lbs. Females are smaller typically. The Eurasian otter’s nose is about the smallest among the otter species and has a characteristic shape described as a shallow ‘W’. An otter’s tail (or rudder, or stern) is stout at the base and tapers towards the tip where it flattens. This forms part of the propulsion unit when swimming fast underwater. Otter fur consists of two types of hair: stout guard hairs which form a waterproof outer covering, and under-fur which is dense and fine, equivalent to an otter’s thermal underwear. The fur must be kept in good condition by grooming. Seawater reduces the waterproofing and insulating qualities of otter fur when saltwater in the fur. This is why freshwater pools are important to otters living on the coast. After swimming, they wash the salts off in pools and the squirm on the ground to rub dry against vegetation.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到水獭身体的实用性特征。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"fit-for-purpose characteristics of otter’s body shape\"可以定位到A段，该段详细描述了水獭的身体特征，如长而细的身体、短腿、鼻子形状、尾巴形状以及毛发结构等，这些特征都是为了适应其生活环境和功能。\n解题思路：根据原文A段中的描述，水獭的身体特征如长而细的身体、短腿等都是为了适应其生活环境，如穿过茂密的植被或在水下狩猎。此外，其尾巴形状和毛发结构也显示了其适应游泳和保持体温的功能。因此，A段包含了水獭身体的实用性特征。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64428","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-9\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-G Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 1-9 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8913:64428:3","type":"choice","text":"3 a reference to an underdeveloped sense","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Otters have small eyes and are probably short-sighted on land.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求找出哪一段提到了“一种不发达的感官”。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词“underdeveloped sense”可以定位到B段中关于海獭感官能力的描述。\n解题思路：B段提到了海獭的眼睛很小，可能在陆地上是近视的，这说明它们的视觉在陆地上是不发达的，符合题目中的描述。因此，答案为B。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64428","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-9\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-G Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 1-9 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8913:64428:4","type":"choice","text":"4 an explanation of why agriculture failed in otter conservation efforts","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Pesticides, such as dieldrin and aldrin, were first used in1955 in agriculture and other industries – these chemicals are very persistent and had already been recognised as the cause of huge declines in the population of peregrine falcons, sparrow hawks and other predators. The pesticides entered the river systems and the food chain – micro-organisms, fish and finally otters, with every step increasing the concentration of the chemicals. From 1962 the chemicals were phased out, but while some species recovered quickly, otter numbers did not – and continued to fall into the 80s. This was probably due mainly to habitat destruction and road deaths.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段落解释了农业没能保护水獭。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"agriculture\"和\"failed in otter conservation efforts\"可以定位到F段，该段提到了农药的使用及其对水獭种群的影响。\n解题思路：F段详细描述了农药（如狄氏剂和艾氏剂）在农业和其他工业中的使用，这些化学物质非常持久，并已被确认为导致游隼、雀鹰和其他捕食者种群大幅下降的原因。农药进入河流系统和食物链，每一步都增加了化学物质的浓度，最终影响了水獭。尽管从1962年开始逐步淘汰这些化学物质，但水獭数量并未迅速恢复，反而持续下降到80年代。这可能是由于栖息地破坏和道路死亡。因此，F段包含了农业没能保护水獭的原因。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64428","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-9\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-G Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 1-9 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8913:64428:5","type":"choice","text":"5 a description of some of the otter’s social characteristics","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Being such shy and wary creatures, they will prefer territories where man’s activities do not impinge greatly. Of course, there must also be no other otter already in residence – this has only become significant again recently as populations start to recover.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段“描述水獭的一些社会性特征”。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"social characteristics\"，即社会特征，这通常涉及水獭的群体行为、领地行为或与其他个体的互动，对应到C段。\n解题思路：在C段中，原文提到水獭是害羞和警惕的动物，并且喜欢人类活动不多的领地，领地上不能有其他水獭，这描述了水獭的社会行为特征，即它们对环境的反应和领地选择。因此，C段包含了关于水獭社会特征的描述。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64428","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-9\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-G Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 1-9 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8913:64428:6","type":"choice","text":"6 a description of how baby otters grow","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At five weeks they open their eyes – a tiny cub of 700g. At seven weeks they’re weaned onto solid food. At ten weeks they leave the nest, blinking into daylight for the first time. After three months they finally meet the water and learn to swim. After eight months they are hunting, though the mother still provides a lot of food herself. Finally, after nine months she can chase them all away with a clear conscience, and relax – until the next fella shows up.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落描述了水獭幼崽的成长过程。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"baby otters grow\"可以定位到E段，该段详细描述了幼崽从出生到成长的不同阶段，包括睁开眼睛、断奶、离开巢穴、学习游泳和捕猎等。\n解题思路：E段中的句子明确描述了幼崽成长的各个阶段，从五周大睁开眼睛开始，到七周大断奶，再到十周大离开巢穴，以及之后学习游泳和捕猎的过程。这些描述与题目中关于幼崽成长的描述完全吻合，因此E段是正确答案。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64428","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-9\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-G Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 1-9 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8913:64428:7","type":"choice","text":"7 the conflicting opinions on how to preserve","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The argument runs that where there is no suitable habitat for them they will not survive after release and where there is suitable habitat, natural populations should be able to expand into the area. However, reintroducing animals into a fragmented and fragile population may add just enough impetus for it to stabilise and expand, rather than die out.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段包含了关于如何保护水獭的不同意见。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"conflicting opinions\"和\"how to preserve\"可以定位到G段中关于释放圈养水獭的讨论。\n解题思路：G段中提到了对于释放圈养水獭的不同观点，有些人认为，如果缺乏适宜栖息地，放归后无法存活，而如果存在适宜栖息地，自然种群应能向该区域扩张，无需释放圈养水獭，然而，作者提到，将动物重新引入破碎且脆弱的种群中，可能为其稳定发展提供足够动力，而非导致灭绝，水獭信托基金组织在诺福克郡就释放了圈养水獭。说明放归水獭引发了人们不同的讨论。因此G段包含了题目所要求的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64428","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-9\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-G Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 1-9 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8913:64428:8","type":"choice","text":"8 a reference to the legislative act","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This is almost entirely due to legislation, conservation efforts, slowing down and reversing the destruction of suitable otter habitat and reintroductions from captive breeding programs.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落提到了与立法相关的信息。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"legislative act\"，在文章中寻找与立法相关的句子。\n解题思路：在G段中，原文明确提到了，这几乎完全归功于立法保护、生态保护措施、减缓并逆转适宜栖息地的破坏，以及通过圈养繁殖计划进行的重新引入。这句话说明了立法在保护水獭方面的作用，因此G段是正确答案。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64428","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-9\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-G Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 1-9 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8913:64428:9","type":"choice","text":"9 an explanation of how otters compensate for heat loss","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Otter fur consists of two types of hair: stout guard hairs which form a waterproof outer covering, and under-fur which is dense and fine, equivalent to an otter’s thermal underwear. The fur must be kept in good condition by grooming.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段解释了“水獭如何补偿热量损失”。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的“compensate for heat loss”可以定位到A段中关于水獭毛发的描述。\n解题思路：原文中提到，水獭毛发由两种毛发组成：粗壮的保护毛形成防水外层，细密的底毛则如同保暖内衣般包裹全身。这直接解释了水獭如何通过毛发来补偿热量损失。因此，A段包含了题目所要求的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64428","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-9\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-G Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 1-9 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8913:64429:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"Sea water/Salt/sea water/salt/Seawater/seawater","acceptedAnswers":["Sea water","Salt","sea water","salt","Seawater","seawater"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Seawater reduces the waterproofing and insulating qualities of otter fur when saltwater in the fur.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问什么会影响水獭的外层毛发。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"outer fur\"（外层毛发）定位到A段关于水獭毛发的描述。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，海水会降低水獭毛发的防水和隔热性能，说明海水（或盐）会影响外层毛发。因此答案为Sea water或Salt。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64429","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8913:64430:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"swimming speed/Swimming Speed","acceptedAnswers":["swimming speed","Swimming Speed"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Giant otters and sea otters have even more prominent webs, while the Asian short-clawed otter has no webbing – they hunt for shrimps in ditches and paddy fields so they don’t need the swimming speed.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问亚洲短爪水獭不需要哪项技能。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Asian short-clawed otter \"定位到B段，找到与亚洲短爪水獭的描述。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，亚洲短爪水獭则无趾蹼——它们在沟渠和稻田捕虾，因此对游泳速度没有要求。因此答案为\"swimming speed\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64430","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8913:64431:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"Coastal otters/coastal otters","acceptedAnswers":["Coastal otters","coastal otters"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Coastal otters have a much more abundant food supply and range for males and females may be just a few kilometres of coastline.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问哪种水獭的分布范围最短。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的“type of otters”和“shortest range”，定位到C段中关于不同种类水獭活动范围的描述。\n解题思路：原文C段明确说明，“海岸水獭（Coastal otters）”拥有更丰富的食物供应，因此雄性和雌性的活动范围“可能只有几公里长的海岸线（just a few kilometres of coastline）”。这与需要更大活动范围的河獭等形成对比，表明海岸水獭的活动范围确实是最短的。因此，答案是Coastal otters。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64431","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8913:64432:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"Small mammals/small mammals","acceptedAnswers":["Small mammals","small mammals"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Small mammals are occasionally taken, most commonly rabbits but sometimes even moles.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问水獭偶尔捕猎哪种类型的动物。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"otters hunt occasionally\"定位到C段中水獭食物类型的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确指出水獭主要捕猎鱼类，小型哺乳动物偶尔也会成为猎物，最常见的是兔子，但有时甚至会捕食鼹鼠。因此答案为\"small mammals\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64432","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64428","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-9\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-G Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 1-9 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.","html":"<p><strong>1 </strong>a description of how otters regulate vision underwater <strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"64429","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>10 </strong>What affects the outer fur of otters? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"64430","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>11 </strong>What skill is not necessary for Asian short-clawed otters? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"64431","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>12 </strong>Which type of otters has the shortest range? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"64432","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>13 </strong>Which type of animals do otters hunt occasionally? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Otter</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Otters have long, thin bodies and short legs – ideal for pushing through dense undergrowth or hunting in tunnels. An adult male may be up to 4 feet long and 30lbs. Females are smaller typically. The Eurasian otter’s nose is about the smallest among the otter species and has a characteristic shape described as a shallow ‘W’. An otter’s tail (or rudder, or stern) is stout at the base and tapers towards the tip where it flattens. This forms part of the propulsion unit when swimming fast underwater. Otter fur consists of two types of hair: stout guard hairs which form a waterproof outer covering, and under-fur which is dense and fine, equivalent to an otter’s thermal underwear. The fur must be kept in good condition by grooming. Seawater reduces the waterproofing and insulating qualities of otter fur when saltwater in the fur. This is why freshwater pools are important to otters living on the coast. After swimming, they wash the salts off in pools and the squirm on the ground to rub dry against vegetation.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The scent is used for hunting on land, for communication and for detecting danger. Otterine sense of smell is likely to be similar in sensitivity to dogs. Otters have small eyes and are probably short-sighted on land. But they do have the ability to modify the shape of the lens in the eye to make it more spherical, and hence overcome the refraction of water. In clear water and good light, otters can hunt fish by sight. The otter’s eyes and nostrils are placed high on its head so that it can see and breathe even when the rest of the body is submerged. Underwater, the cotter holds its legs against the body, except for steering, and the hind end of the body is flexed in a series of vertical undulations. River otters have webbing which extends for much of the length of each digit, though not to the very end. Giant otters and sea otters have even more prominent webs, while the Asian short-clawed otter has no webbing – they hunt for shrimps in ditches and paddy fields so they don’t need the swimming speed. Otter’s ears are tiny for streamlining, but they still have very sensitive hearing and are protected by valves which close them against water pressure.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>A number of constraints and preferences limit suitable habitats of otters. Water is a must and the rivers must be large enough to support a healthy population of fish. Being such shy and wary creatures, they will prefer territories where man’s activities do not impinge greatly. Of course, there must also be no other otter already in residence – this has only become significant again recently as populations start to recover. Coastal otters have a much more abundant food supply and range for males and females may be just a few kilometres of coastline. Because male range overlaps with two or three females – not bad! Otters will eat anything that they can get hold of – there are records of sparrows and snakes and slugs being gobbled. Apart from fish, the most common prey are crayfish, crabs and water birds. Small mammals are occasionally taken, most commonly rabbits but sometimes even moles.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Eurasian otters will breed any time where food is readily available. In places where the condition is more severe, Sweden for example where the lakes are frozen for much of winter, cubs are born in spring. This ensures that they are well grown before severe weather returns. In the Shetlands, cubs are born in summer when fish is more abundant. Though otters can breed every year, some do not. Again, this depends on food availability. Other factors such as food range and quality of the female may have an effect. Gestation for Eurasian otter is 63 days, with the exception of Lutra canadensis whose embryos may undergo delayed implantation. Otters normally give birth in more secure dens to avoid disturbances. Nests are lined with bedding to keep the cub’s warm mummy is away feeding.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Otters normally give birth in more secure dens to avoid disturbances. Nests are lined with bedding (reeds, waterside plants, grass) to keep the cub’s warm while is away feeding. Litter Size varies between 1 and 5. For some unknown reason, coastal otters tend to produce smaller litters. At five weeks they open their eyes – a tiny cub of 700g. At seven weeks they’re weaned onto solid food. At ten weeks they leave the nest, blinking into daylight for the first time. After three months they finally meet the water and learn to swim. After eight months they are hunting, though the mother still provides a lot of food herself. Finally, after nine months she can chase them all away with a clear conscience, and relax – until the next fella shows up.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The plight of the British otter was recognised in the early 60s, but it wasn’t until the late 70s that the chief cause was discovered. Pesticides, such as dieldrin and aldrin, were first used in1955 in agriculture and other industries – these chemicals are very persistent and had already been recognised as the cause of huge declines in the population of peregrine falcons, sparrow hawks and other predators. The pesticides entered the river systems and the food chain – micro-organisms, fish and finally otters, with every step increasing the concentration of the chemicals. From 1962 the chemicals were phased out, but while some species recovered quickly, otter numbers did not – and continued to fall into the 80s. This was probably due mainly to habitat destruction and road deaths. Acting on populations fragmented by the sudden decimation in the 50s and 60s, the loss of just a handful of otters in one area can make an entire population unviable and spell the end.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Otter numbers are recovering all around Britain – populations are growing again in the few areas where they had remained and have expanded from those areas into the rest of the country. This is almost entirely due to legislation, conservation efforts, slowing down and reversing the destruction of suitable otter habitat and reintroductions from captive breeding programs. Releasing captive-bred otters is seen by many as a last resort. The argument runs that where there is no suitable habitat for them they will not survive after release and where there is suitable habitat, natural populations should be able to expand into the area. However, reintroducing animals into a fragmented and fragile population may add just enough impetus for it to stabilise and expand, rather than die out. This is what the Otter Trust accomplished in Norfolk, where the otter population may have been as low as twenty animals at the beginning of the 1980s. The Otter Trust has now finished its captive breeding program entirely, great news because it means it is no longer needed.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8913&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8910","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Pollution in the Bay","book":"阅读还原集Vol.19","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.19 · Test 1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8910:64405:1","type":"choice","text":"1 Sea grass turned to be more resistant to the saline water level in the Bay.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He thinks seagrasses can tolerate much higher levels of salinity than the bay actually displays.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段落提到了海草能耐受的盐度高于实际海湾盐度。\n定位关键信息：根据题目的关键词\"seagrass\"和\"saline water level\"可以定位到E段。\n解题思路：E段中的句子直接表明了，海洋科学家布莱恩·拉波因特对此持不同意见。他认为海草能耐受的盐度远高于实际海湾水平。这与题目所问的内容完全一致，因此E段是正确答案。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64405","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8910:64405:2","type":"choice","text":"2 Significance of finding a specific reason in controversy.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：What is causing such ecological change is a matter of much debate. And the answer is of no small consequence.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段落提到了“在争论中，找到具体原因的重要性”。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“Significance of finding a specific reason in controversy”可以定位到C段。\n解题思路：C段明确提到了导致此类生态变化的原因尚存争议，争论结果十分重要。后面提到原因，这是因为，美国政府计划恢复淡水流入大沼泽地，而这些水最终会流入海湾，而这关系到海湾生态，所以争论出来的最终结果影响很大。。因此，C段包含了这一信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64405","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8910:64405:3","type":"choice","text":"3 Expensive proposals raised to solve the nitrogen dilemma.","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Man-made wetlands, at present, being built to reduce phosphate runoff into the bay – also from fertilisers – would need an algal culture (a sort of contained algal bloom) added to them to deal with discharges from farmlands. That would be costly. So too would be the replacement of cesspits with proper sewerage—one estimate puts the cost at $650m.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落提到了，解决氮问题的昂贵方案。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"expensive proposals\"和\"nitrogen dilemma\"在文章中定位。通过阅读H段，发现该段提到了处理农田排放物和污水排放的方案，并明确指出这些方案是昂贵的。\n解题思路：H段详细描述了为解决氮的问题而提出的两种方案：在人工湿地中添加藻类培养物以处理农田排放物，以及用适当的污水系统替代化粪池。文中明确提到这两种方案成本都很高，其中化粪池的替代方案估计成本为6500万美元。因此，H段包含了题目所问的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64405","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8910:64405:4","type":"choice","text":"4 A statistics of ecological changes in both the coral area and species.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Since the 1980s, coral cover has dropped by 40%, and a third of the coral species have gone. This has had a damaging effect on the animals that depend on the reef, such as crabs, turtles and nearly 600 species of fish.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求找出包含珊瑚区域和物种生态变化统计数据的段落。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的关键词\"statistic of ecological changes in both the coral area and species\"（珊瑚区域和物种的生态变化统计数据），可以定位到B段中提到珊瑚覆盖率下降和物种消失的具体数据。\n解题思路：B段提到，自上世纪80年代以来，珊瑚覆盖率已锐减40%，三分之一的珊瑚物种消失殆尽。这对依赖珊瑚礁生存的生物造成了毁灭性打击，螃蟹、海龟以及近600种鱼类都深受其害。给出了具体的统计数据，分别对应了珊瑚区域和物种的生态变化。因此，B段是包含所需信息的正确段落。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64405","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8910:64406:5","type":"choice","text":"5 Drainage system in everglades actually results in high salty water in the bay.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The blame, he says, lies with a century of drainage in the Everglades aimed at turning the marshes into farmland and areas for development. This has caused the flow of fresh water into Florida Bay to dwindle, making the water in the bay, overall, more saline.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是谁认为大沼泽地的排水系统使海湾盐度升高。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"Drainage system in Everglades\"和\"high salty water in the bay\"可以定位到D段，其中提到\"drainage in the Everglades\"和\"making the water in the bay, overall, more saline\"。\n解题思路：D段明确指出，弗吉尼亚大学海洋生态学家约瑟夫·齐曼认为佛罗里达湾的缺水问题根源在于百年来为开垦农田和开发区域而实施的排水工程。这些工程导致流入海湾的淡水持续减少，使得整体海水盐度不断升高。原文中的\"making the water in the bay, overall, more saline\"与题目中的\"high salty water in the bay\"对应，因此答案为C。","options":["Bill Kruczynski","Brian Lapointe","Joseph Zieman"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"64406","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one idea.\nA Bill Kruczynski\nB Brian Lapointe\nC Joseph Zieman"},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8910:64406:6","type":"choice","text":"6 Restoring water high in nitrogen level will make more ecological side effect.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The result was mass mortality of seagrasses because of increased turbidity from the plankton. Dr Lapointe adds that, because corals thrive only in waters where nutrient levels are low, restoring freshwater rich in nitrogen will do more damage to the reef.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“恢复氮含量高的水体将产生更大的生态副作用”，需要匹配提出这一观点的人。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"restoring water high in nitrogen level\"和\"more ecological side effect\"定位到E段中Dr Lapointe的观点句。\n解题思路：E段中Dr Lapointe明确提到，浮游生物带来的浑浊度升高，最终导致海草大规模死亡。拉波因特补充说，由于珊瑚只能在低营养盐水域繁衍生息，恢复富含氮的淡水反而会对珊瑚礁造成更大破坏。含氮量高的水体会对海草、珊瑚造成破坏，都属于题目中的\"ecological side effect\"。因此，答案为B。","options":["Bill Kruczynski","Brian Lapointe","Joseph Zieman"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"64406","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one idea.\nA Bill Kruczynski\nB Brian Lapointe\nC Joseph Zieman"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8910:64406:7","type":"choice","text":"7 High nitrogen levels may be caused by the nearby farmland.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Freshwater running off from well-fertilised farmlands, he says, caused a fivefold rise in nitrogen levels in the bay.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问氮含量高可能是由附近的农田引起的，需要匹配提出这一观点的人。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词\"High nitrogen levels\"和\"nearby farmland\"在文章中定位，找到E段中关于农田和氮水平的描述。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，拉波因特解释道，来自肥沃农田的淡水流入导致海湾氮含量激增五倍，这与题目中的说法一致，因此答案为B。","options":["Bill Kruczynski","Brian Lapointe","Joseph Zieman"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"64406","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one idea.\nA Bill Kruczynski\nB Brian Lapointe\nC Joseph Zieman"},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8910:64406:8","type":"choice","text":"8 Released sewage rather than nutrients from agricultural area increase the level of Nitrogen.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Dr Kruczynski thinks that increased nutrients arriving from local sewage discharges from the thousands of cesspits along the Florida Keys are part of the problem.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目询问谁认为，水体中的氮含量高是因为污水排放，而不是因为农业区的营养物质。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"Released sewage\"和\"nutrients from agricultural area\"以及\"level of Nitrogen\"等关键词，在文章中定位到F段。\n解题思路：原文F段明确提到，克鲁钦斯基博士认为，佛罗里达群岛沿岸数千个化粪池排放的污水带来的营养物质，才是问题的症结所在。这与题干描述一致，因此答案为A。","options":["Bill Kruczynski","Brian Lapointe","Joseph Zieman"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"64406","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one idea.\nA Bill Kruczynski\nB Brian Lapointe\nC Joseph Zieman"},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8910:64407:9","type":"choice","text":"Everyone agrees with ‘pouring water into the sea is harmless enough’ even in the Florida Bay area.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But in Florida Bay, a large and shallow section of the Gulf of Mexico that lies between the southern end of the Everglades and the Florida Keys, it is proving highly controversial.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“即使在佛罗里达湾地区，人们也一致认同‘将水倒入海里是无害的’”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“pouring water into the sea is harmless enough”和“Florida Bay”定位到A段首句和第二句。\n解题思路：A段提到，向海洋倾倒海水看似无害，但在佛罗里达湾——这片位于大沼泽地南端与佛罗里达群岛之间的墨西哥湾大型浅水区，此举却引发激烈争议，说明并非所有人都同意这一观点，因此题目中的“Everyone agrees”与原文的“highly controversial”矛盾，故答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64407","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8910:64408:10","type":"choice","text":"Nitrogen was poured in from different types of crops as water flows through.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Freshwater running off from well-fertilised farmlands, he says, caused a fivefold rise in nitrogen levels in the bay.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“水流经过时，不同类型的作物往水里释放出氮”，需要判断这个陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“Nitrogen”、“crops”和“water flows through”，可以在文章中定位到E段。\n解题思路：原文中提到，拉波因特解释道，来自肥沃农田的淡水流入导致海湾氮含量激增五倍，但并没有明确说明这些农田种植的作物类型，因此，无法判断题目中的说法是否正确。所以，答案是“Not Given”。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64408","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8910:64409:11","type":"choice","text":"Everglade restoration project can be effective regardless of the cause of the pollution.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Such claims and counterclaims make the impact of the restoration plan difficult to predict. If increased salinity is the main problem, the bay’s ecology will benefit from the Everglades restoration project. If, however, nitrogen is the problem, increasing the flow of freshwater could mate matters much worse.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问“无论污染源自何处，大沼泽地恢复项目都可取得成效”，需要判断这个陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“Everglade restoration project”和“regardless of the cause of the pollution”定位到G段，该段讨论了不同污染源（农田氮和污水）对项目效果的影响。\n解题思路：G段明确提到，若盐度升高是主要问题，该海湾的生态将受益于大沼泽地恢复项目。然而，若氮是问题所在，增加淡水流量可能使情况恶化得多。因此，项目效果取决于污染原因，题目说法错误。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64409","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8910:64410:12","type":"choice","text":"Human has changed Florida Bay where old image before 1950s is unrecalled.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Nobody knows what Florida Bay was like before the 1950s when engineers cut the largest canals in the Everglades and took most of the water away. Dr Kruczynski suspects it was more like an estuary. The bay that many people wish to re-create could have been nothing more than a changing phase in the bay’s history.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问“人类改变了佛罗里达湾，1950年代前的旧貌已不复存在”，需要判断这个陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词“Florida Bay”、“before 1950s”、“unrecalled”对应原文I段中的“Florida Bay”、“before the 1950s”、“Nobody knows what Florida Bay was like”。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，没有人知道1950年代之前佛罗里达湾的真实面貌——当时工程师们在大沼泽地开凿了最大规模的运河，抽走了大部分水域。克鲁钦斯基博士推测，当时的海湾更接近河口形态。许多人试图复原的这个海湾，或许只是其历史进程中一个阶段性的变迁，表明人类活动确实改变了佛罗里达湾，最初海湾是什么样子已无从得知。因此，题目信息与原文一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64410","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8910:64411:13","type":"choice","text":"Tourism contributes fundamentally to the Florida Bay area.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The economy of the Florida Keys depends on tourism – the local tourist industry has an annual turnover of $2.5 billion.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问“旅游业是佛罗里达湾区的支柱性产业”是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“Tourism”和“Florida Bay area”定位到J段，该段明确提到“the economy of the Florida Keys depends on tourism”，即旅游业是佛罗里达礁岛群经济的基础。\n解题思路：原文J段指出佛罗里达群岛的经济命脉在于旅游业——当地旅游产业年营业额高达25亿美元。与题目“Tourism contributes fundamentally to the Florida Bay area”表述一致。因此，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64411","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64405","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>1</strong> See grass turned to be more resistant to the saline water level in the Bay. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"64406","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one idea.\nA Bill Kruczynski\nB Brian Lapointe\nC Joseph Zieman","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> Bill Kruczynski <br/></p><p><strong>B</strong> Brian Lapointe <br/></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>C</strong> Joseph Zieman<br/></p><p><strong>5</strong> Drainage system in everglades actually results in high salty water in the bay. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[5] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"64407","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Everyone agrees with ‘pouring water into the sea is harmless enough’ even in the Florida Bay area.</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"64408","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Nitrogen was poured in from different types of crops as water flows through.</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"64409","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Everglade restoration project can be effective regardless of the cause of the pollution.</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"64410","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Human has changed Florida Bay where old image before 1950s is unrecalled.</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"64411","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Tourism contributes fundamentally to the Florida Bay area.</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Pollution in the Bay</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Pouring water into the sea sounds harmless enough. But in Florida Bay, a large and shallow section of the Gulf of Mexico that lies between the southern end of the Everglades and the Florida Keys, it is proving highly controversial. That is because researchers are divided over whether it will help or hinder the plants and animals that live in the bay.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>What is at risk is the future of the bay’s extensive beds of seagrasses. These grow on the bay’s muddy floor and act as nurseries for the larvae of shrimps, lobsters and fish – many of the important sport and commercial-fishing species. Also in danger is an impressive range of coral reefs that run the length of the Florida Keys and form the third-largest barrier reef in the world. Since the 1980s, coral cover has dropped by 40%, and a third of the coral species have gone. This has had a damaging effect on the animals that depend on the reef, such as crabs, turtles and nearly 600 species of fish.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>What is causing such ecological change is a matter of much debate. And the answer is of no small consequence. This is because the American government is planning to devote $8 billion over the next 30 years to revitalise the Everglades. Seasonal freshwater flows into the Everglades are to be restored in order to improve the region’s health. But they will then run off into the bay.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Joseph Zieman, a marine ecologist at the University of Virginia, thinks this is a good idea. He believes that a lack of fresh water in the bay is its main problem. The blame, he says, lies with a century of drainage in the Everglades aimed at turning the marshes into farmland and areas for development. This has caused the flow of fresh water into Florida Bay to dwindle, making the water in the bay, overall, more saline. This, he argues, kills the seagrasses, and as these rots, nutrients are released that feed the microscopic plants and animals that live in the water. This, he says, is why the bay’s once crystal-clear waters often resemble pea soup. And in a vicious circle, these turbid blooms block out sunlight, causing more seagrasses to die and yet more turbidity.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Brian Lapointe, a marine scientist at the Harbour Branch Oceanographic Institution at Fort Pierce in Florida, disagrees. He thinks seagrasses can tolerate much higher levels of salinity than the bay actually displays. Furthermore, he notes that when freshwater flows through the Everglades were increased experimentally in the 1990s, it led to massive plankton blooms. Freshwater running off from well-fertilised farmlands, he says, caused a fivefold rise in nitrogen levels in the bay. This was like pouring fuel on a fire. The result was mass mortality of seagrasses because of increased turbidity from the plankton. Dr Lapointe adds that, because corals thrive only in waters where nutrient levels are low, restoring freshwater rich in nitrogen will do more damage to the reef.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>It is a plausible theory. The water flowing off crops that are grown on the750,000 acres of heavily fertilised farmland on the northern edge of the Everglades is rich in nitrogen, half of which ends up in the bay. But Bill Kruczynski, of America’s Environmental Protection Agency, is convinced that nitrogen from farmlands is not the chief problem. Some coral reefs well away from any nitrogen pollution are dying and, curiously, a few are thriving. Dr Kruczynski thinks that increased nutrients arriving from local sewage discharges from the thousands of cesspits along the Florida Keys are part of the problem.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Such claims and counterclaims make the impact of the restoration plan difficult to predict. If increased salinity is the main problem, the bay’s ecology will benefit from the Everglades restoration project. If, however, nitrogen is the problem, increasing the flow of freshwater could make matters much worse.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>If this second hypothesis proves correct, the cure is to remove nitrogen from farmland or sewage discharges, or perhaps both. Neither will be easy. Man-made wetlands, at present, being built to reduce phosphate runoff into the bay – also from fertilisers – would need an algal culture (a sort of contained algal bloom) added to them to deal with discharges from farmlands. That would be costly. So too would be the replacement of cesspits with proper sewerage—one estimate puts the cost at $650m. Either way, it is clear that when, on December 1st, 3,000 square miles of sea around the reef are designated as a “protective zone” by the deputy secretary of commerce, Sam Bodman, this will do nothing to protect the reef from pollution.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Some argue, though, that there is a more fundamental flaw in the plans for the bay: the very idea of returning it to a Utopian ideal before man wrought his damage. Nobody knows what Florida Bay was like before the 1950s when engineers cut the largest canals in the Everglades and took most of the water away. Dr Kruczynski suspects it was more like an estuary. The bay that many people wish to re-create could have been nothing more than a changing phase in the bay’s history.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>These arguments do not merely threaten to create ecological problems but economic ones as well. The economy of the Florida Keys depends on tourism – the local tourist industry has an annual turnover of $2.5 billion. People come for fishing-boat trips, for manatee watching, or for scuba diving and snorkeling to view the exotically coloured corals. If the plan to restore the Everglades makes problems in the bay and the reef worse, it could prove a very expensive mistake.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8910&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8911","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Tasmanian Tiger","book":"阅读还原集Vol.19","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.19 · Test 1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8911:64412:14","type":"fill","text":"填写第 14 空","answer":"black stripes/Black Stripes","acceptedAnswers":["black stripes","Black Stripes"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Although it was called tiger, it looked like a clog with black stripes on its hack and it was the largest known carnivorous marsupial of modem times.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是塔斯马尼亚虎的皮毛上有什么特征。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的单词\"resembles the look of a dog\"和\"on its fur coat\"定位到A段第一句，找到描述塔斯马尼亚虎外观特征的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文句子，尽管它被称为老虎，但外形却更像背部带有黑色条纹的狗，可以确定塔斯马尼亚虎的皮毛上有黑色条纹。可以确定答案为\"black stripes\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64412","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8911:64413:15","type":"fill","text":"填写第 15 空","answer":"12 million/12 Million","acceptedAnswers":["12 million","12 Million"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Fossils of thylacines dating from about almost 12 million years ago have been dug up at various places in Victoria, South Australia and Western Australia.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目询问袋狼的化石显示它们最早存在于多少年前。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"thylacines\"和\"years ago\"定位到B段第一句，该句明确提到了thylacines的化石年代。\n解题思路：原文提到，在维多利亚州、南澳大利亚州和西澳大利亚州的多个地点，考古学家发掘出了距今约1200万年的袋狼化石。因此答案为\"12 million\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64413","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8911:64414:16","type":"fill","text":"填写第 16 空","answer":"Australia","acceptedAnswers":["Australia"],"explanation":"原文答案句：They were widespread in Australia 7,000 years ago, but have probably been extinct on the continent for 2,000 years ago.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是塔斯马尼亚虎消失前曾生活在哪里。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的\"before disappearing from the mainland\"定位到B段中描述塔斯马尼亚虎在澳大利亚大陆分布的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，这些远古生物在7000年前曾广泛分布于澳大利亚，但约2000年前便已从大陆上消失。因此答案为Australia。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64414","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8911:64415:17","type":"fill","text":"填写第 17 空","answer":"European","acceptedAnswers":["European"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Because of disease, thylacine numbers may have been declining in Tasmania at the time of European settlement 200 years ago, but the decline was certainly accelerated by the new arrivals.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是在什么群体到达后，塔斯马尼亚虎的种群数量下降速度加快。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"settlers arrived\"和\"shrunk at a higher speed\"定位到B段中\"European settlement\"和\"decline was certainly accelerated\"的相关句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，早在200年前欧洲人定居塔斯马尼亚时，袋狼种群可能已因疾病导致数量锐减，而新移民的到来无疑加速了其消亡进程。说明\"European settlement\"（欧洲定居者）到达后，塔斯马尼亚虎的数量下降速度加快，因此答案为\"European\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64415","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8911:64416:18","type":"choice","text":"18 His report of seeing a live thylacine in the wild attracted international interest.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：When the news finally broke, it was accompanied by pandemonium. ‘I was besieged by television crews, including four to five from Japan, and others from the United Kingdom, Germany, New Zealand and South America,’ said Naarding.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目说“他目睹野生袋狼的报告引起了国际关注”，需要匹配对应的人。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“seeing a live thylacine in the wild”和“attracted international interest”可以定位到E段中人们对这一消息的反应。\n解题思路：E段提到，Hans Naarding看到野生袋狼的事件，最终曝光时，现场一片混乱。纳尔丁回忆道：‘我被电视摄制组团团围住，其中包括四到五支来自日本的摄制组，以及来自英国、德国、新西兰和南美的摄制组。’说明许多国家的都很关心这一事件，这与题目描述一致，因此答案是A。","options":["Hans Naarding","Randolph Rose","David Pemberton","Nick Mooney"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64416","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nLook at the following statements (Questions 18-23) and the list of people below, match each statement with the correct person A, B, C or D.  Write the correct letter A, B, C or D in boxes 18-23.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Hans Naarding\nB Randolph Rose\nC David Pemberton\nD Nick Mooney"},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8911:64416:19","type":"choice","text":"19 Many eye-witnesses' reports are not trustworthy.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：And Mooney has seen it all – the mistakes, the hoaxes, the illusions and the plausible accounts of sightings. Hoaxers aside, most people who report sightings end up believing they have been a thylacine, and are themselves believable to the point they could pass a lie-detector test, according to Mooney. Others, having tabled a creditable report, then become utterly obsessed like the Tasmanian who has registered 99 thylacine sightings to date.\n对应段落：L段\n审题：题目说“许多目击者的报告不可信”，需要匹配观点对应的人。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“eye-witnesses’ reports”和“not trustworthy”定位到L段，其中提到Mooney对目击报告的看法。\n解题思路：L段中明确提到，穆尼见过形形色色的目击事件——那些错误、骗局、幻觉，以及看似可信的目击报告。大多数报告者最终都相信自己看到了袋狼，甚至在测谎仪测试中表现得足够可信。但目击者可能因为盲目乐观而误认，导致报告不可靠。这与题目“许多目击者的报告不可信”对应，因此答案为D（Mooney）。","options":["Hans Naarding","Randolph Rose","David Pemberton","Nick Mooney"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64416","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nLook at the following statements (Questions 18-23) and the list of people below, match each statement with the correct person A, B, C or D.  Write the correct letter A, B, C or D in boxes 18-23.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Hans Naarding\nB Randolph Rose\nC David Pemberton\nD Nick Mooney"},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8911:64416:20","type":"choice","text":"20 It doesn't require a certain number of animals to ensure the survival of a species.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Dr. David Pemberton, curator of zoology at the Tasmanian Museum and Art Gallery, whose PhD thesis was on the thylacine, says that despite scientific thinking that 500 animals are required to sustain a population, the Florida panther is down to a dozen or so animals and, while it does have some inbreeding problems, is still ticking along.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目说“一个物种存续并不需要一定的个体数量”，需要匹配观点对应的人。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“a certain number of animals”和“survival of a species”定位到I段，该段提到了David Pemberton的观点。\n解题思路：原文中I段提到，塔斯马尼亚博物馆与美术馆动物学策展人戴维·彭伯顿博士（其博士论文研究对象为袋狼）指出，尽管科学界普遍认为维持种群数量需500只个体，但佛罗里达豹现存仅存十余只。虽然存在近亲繁殖问题，但种群仍能维持。说明他认为不需要维持那么多的个体数量，物种照样可以延续下去。题目与这一观点相符，因此选择C。","options":["Hans Naarding","Randolph Rose","David Pemberton","Nick Mooney"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64416","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nLook at the following statements (Questions 18-23) and the list of people below, match each statement with the correct person A, B, C or D.  Write the correct letter A, B, C or D in boxes 18-23.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Hans Naarding\nB Randolph Rose\nC David Pemberton\nD Nick Mooney"},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8911:64416:21","type":"choice","text":"21 There is no hope of finding a surviving Tasmanian tiger.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The consensus among conservationists is that usually; any animal with a population base of less than 1,000 is headed for extinction within 60 years,’ says Rose. ‘Sixty years ago, there was only one thylacine that we know of, and that was in Hobart Zoo,’ he says.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目说“找到幸存的塔斯马尼亚虎已无可能”，需要匹配观点对应的人。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“no hope of finding a surviving Tasmanian tiger”定位到H段。\n解题思路：H段中，罗斯指出，保护主义者普遍认为：通常而言，种群数量不足1000的动物将在60年内走向灭绝。而六十年前，我们已知现存的塔斯马尼亚虎只有一只，仅存于霍巴特动物园。没有希望找到存活的塔斯马尼亚虎，与题目表述一致，答案为B。","options":["Hans Naarding","Randolph Rose","David Pemberton","Nick Mooney"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64416","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nLook at the following statements (Questions 18-23) and the list of people below, match each statement with the correct person A, B, C or D.  Write the correct letter A, B, C or D in boxes 18-23.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Hans Naarding\nB Randolph Rose\nC David Pemberton\nD Nick Mooney"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8911:64416:22","type":"choice","text":"22 Do not disturb them if there are any Tasmanian tigers still living today.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘How do you save a species from extinction? What could you do with it? If there are thylacines out there, they are better off right where they are.’\n对应段落：O段\n审题：题目说“如果现在还有袋狼存在，不要打扰它们”，需要匹配观点对应的人。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“do not disturb”和“Tasmanian tigers still living today”定位到文章中表达对现存袋狼不应打扰的句子。\n解题思路：在O段中，Hans Naarding说“如果袋狼确实还存在，那么找到它们意义不大，而且‘你怎么去拯救一个濒临灭绝的物种？你能做些什么？如果袋狼还在那里，如果袋狼真的存在，它们留在原地反而更好。’”。这句话明确表达了如果袋狼还存在，就不应该打扰它们的意思，与题目要求一致。因此，答案是A。","options":["Hans Naarding","Randolph Rose","David Pemberton","Nick Mooney"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64416","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nLook at the following statements (Questions 18-23) and the list of people below, match each statement with the correct person A, B, C or D.  Write the correct letter A, B, C or D in boxes 18-23.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Hans Naarding\nB Randolph Rose\nC David Pemberton\nD Nick Mooney"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8911:64416:23","type":"choice","text":"23 The interpretation of evidence can be affected by people’s beliefs.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句： ‘It is a blind optimism that something is, rather than a cynicism that something isn’t,’ Mooney says, ‘If something crosses the road, it’s not a case of “I wonder what that was?” Rather, it is a case of “that’s a thylacine!” It is a bit like a gold prospector’s blind faith, “it has got to be there”.’\n对应段落：L段\n审题：题目问的是“人们对证据的解读，往往会受到自身想法的影响”，需要匹配观点对应的人。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的“interpretation of evidence”和“people’s beliefs”可以定位到L段中Mooney的话，他描述了人们对于目击证据的解读是如何受到他们信念的影响的。\n解题思路：L段中Mooney提到，许多目击者的报告不可信，他们盲目乐观地相信某物存在，而非怀疑某物不存在。说明人们的想法会影响他们对目击证据的解读，与题目所问的内容完全一致。因此，答案为D。","options":["Hans Naarding","Randolph Rose","David Pemberton","Nick Mooney"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64416","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nLook at the following statements (Questions 18-23) and the list of people below, match each statement with the correct person A, B, C or D.  Write the correct letter A, B, C or D in boxes 18-23.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Hans Naarding\nB Randolph Rose\nC David Pemberton\nD Nick Mooney"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8911:64417:24","type":"choice","text":"Hans Naarding's sighting has resulted in","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Government and private search parties combed the region, but no further sightings were made. The tiger, as always, had escaped to its lair, a place many insist exists only in our imagination. But since then, the thylacine has staged something of a comeback, becoming part of Australian mythology\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是Hans Naarding的目击事件引起了什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"Hans Naarding's sighting\"定位到F段，提到Naarding的目击事件的影响。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句，这里明显提及的是政府和私人团体都去搜寻袋狼，而非一起保护袋狼，所以排除选项A。虽然在第六段中间确实提及“the thylacine has staged something of a comeback”，后面也提及报告的数量很多，但是说的都是澳大利亚的报告，而非“reports of thylacine worldwide”，所以应该排除选项C。第六段中提及袋狼“becoming part of Australian mythology”，但是这并不是说袋狼在文学中的流行度上升，而是一种形象的说法，表达了发现或观察到袋狼的种种报告大多数只不过是传说，所以应该排除选项D。选项B“extensive interests to find a living thylacine”是对原文第六段整个段落的总结，既包含了政府和私人组织的努力搜寻，也包含了报告的增多等等，所以综上所述，正确答案为B。","options":["government and organisations' cooperative efforts to protect thylacine.","extensive interests to find a living thylacine.","increase in the number of reports of thylacine worldwide.","growth of popularity of thylacine in literature."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64417","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet."},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8911:64418:25","type":"choice","text":"The example of the coelacanth is to illustrate","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：After all, animals can be notoriously elusive. The strange fish is known as the coelacanth with its ‘proto-legs’, was thought to have died out along with the dinosaurs 700 million years ago until a specimen was dragged to the surface in a shark net off the south-east coast of South Africa in 1938.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是“腔棘鱼的例子旨在说明什么”。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"coelacanth\"可以定位到文章J段中关于这种鱼的描述。\n解题思路：根据J段中的描述，动物向来以难以捉摸，讲到人们最初认为这个物种已经灭绝，直到后来又在南非某海域捕获一只，这一切都是为了说明某些物种并不一定像大家所想的那样已经灭绝，对应选项D“extinction of certain species can be mistaken”，所以正确答案为D。","options":["it lived in the same period with dinosaurs.","how dinosaurs evolved legs.","some animals are difficult to catch in the wild.","extinction of certain species can be mistaken."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64418","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet."},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8911:64419:26","type":"choice","text":"Mooney believes that all sighting reports should be","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：However, Mooney treats all reports on face value. ‘I never try to embarrass people or make fools of them. But the fact that I don’t pack the car immediately they ring can often be taken as ridicule. Obsessive characters get irate that someone in my position is not out there when they think the thylacine is there.’\n对应段落：M段\n审题：题目问Mooney认为所有目击报告应该如何对待。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"Mooney\"和\"sighting reports\"定位到M段，该段描述了Mooney处理目击报告的态度。\n解题思路：原文提到，Mooney暂且相信每一个报告所说的东西，不会立即嘲笑或否定（\"I never try to embarrass people or make fools of them\"），同时也指出他不会立即采取行动（\"I don’t pack the car immediately they ring\"）。这表明他认为即使报告可能不真实，暂且当它是真实的，与选项A的\"given some credit as they claim even if they are untrue\"完全一致。其他选项B、C、D均与原文描述的Mooney的态度不符。","options":["given some credit as they claim even if they are untrue.","acted upon immediately.","viewed as equally untrustworthy.","questioned and carefully investigated."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64419","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64412","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The Tasmanian tiger, also called thylacine, resembles the look of a dog and has <strong>14</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong> on\nits fur coat.</p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"64413","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Many fossils have been found, showing that thylacines had existed as early as&nbsp;<strong>15</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[15] ____</strong> years ago.</p>","firstNumber":15},{"id":"64414","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>They lived throughout <strong>16</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[16] ____</strong> before disappearing from the\nmainland.</p>","firstNumber":16},{"id":"64415","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>And soon after the <strong>17</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[17] ____</strong> settlers arrived the size of thylacine population in\nTasmania shrunk at a higher speed.</p>","firstNumber":17},{"id":"64416","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nLook at the following statements (Questions 18-23) and the list of people below, match each statement with the correct person A, B, C or D.  Write the correct letter A, B, C or D in boxes 18-23.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Hans Naarding\nB Randolph Rose\nC David Pemberton\nD Nick Mooney","html":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; margin-bottom: 5px; margin-top: 5px; font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">List of People&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; margin-bottom: 5px; margin-top: 5px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">A</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> Hans Naarding&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; margin-bottom: 5px; margin-top: 5px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">B</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> Randolph Rose&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; margin-bottom: 5px; margin-top: 5px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">C</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> David Pemberton&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; margin-top: 5px; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">D</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> Nick Mooney&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; margin-bottom: 5px; margin-top: 5px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">18</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> His report of seeing a live thylacine in the wild attracted international interest. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[18] ____</strong></span></p>","firstNumber":18},{"id":"64417","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><strong>Hans Naarding&#39;s sighting has resulted in</strong></span></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"64418","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>The example of the coelacanth is to illustrate</strong></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"64419","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Mooney believes that all sighting reports should be</strong></p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Tasmanian Tiger</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Although it was called tiger, it looked like a dog with black stripes on its back and it was the largest known carnivorous marsupial of modern times. Yet, despite its fame for being one of the most fabled animals in the world, it is one of the least understood of Tasmania’s native animals. The scientific name for the Tasmanian tiger is Thylacine and it is believed that they have become extinct in the 20th century.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Fossils of thylacines dating from about almost 12 million years ago have been dug up at various places in Victoria, South Australia and Western Australia. They were widespread in Australia 7,000 years ago, but have probably been extinct on the continent for 2,000 years ago. This is believed to be because of the introduction of dingoes around 8,000 years ago. Because of disease, thylacine numbers may have been declining in Tasmania at the time of European settlement 200 years ago, but the decline was certainly accelerated by the new arrivals. The last known Titsmanijin Tiger died in I lobar! Zoo in 193fi and the animal is officially classified as extinct. Technically, this means that it has not been officially sighted in the wild or captivity for 50 years. However, there are still unsubstantiated sightings.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Hans Naarding, whose study of animals had taken him around the world, was conducting a survey of a species of endangered migratory bird. The hat he saw that night is now regarded as the most credible sighting recorded of thylacine that many believe has been extinct for more than 70 years.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘I had to work at night,’ Naarding takes up the story, ‘I was in the habit of intermittently shining a spotlight around. The beam fell on an animal in front of the vehicle, less than 10m away. Instead of risking movement by grabbing for a camera, I decided to register very carefully what I was seeing. The animal was about the size of a small shepherd dog, a very healthy male in prime condition. What set it apart from a dog, though, was a slightly sloping hindquarter, with a fairly thick tail being a straight continuation of the backline of the animal. It had 12 distinct stripes on its back, continuing onto its butt. I knew perfectly well what I was seeing. As soon as I reached for the camera, it disappeared into the tea-tree undergrowth and scrub.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The director of Tasmania’s National Parks at the time, Peter Morrow, decided in his wisdom to keep Naarding’s sighting of the thylacine secret for two years. When the news finally broke, it was accompanied by pandemonium. ‘I was besieged by television crews, including four to five from Japan, and others from the United Kingdom, Germany, New Zealand and South America,’ said Naarding.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Government and private search parties combed the region, but no further sightings were made. The tiger, as always, had escaped to its lair, a place many insist exists only in our imagination. But since then, the thylacine has staged something of a comeback, becoming part of Australian mythology.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>There have been more than 4,000 claimed sightings of the beast since it supposedly died out, and the average claims each year reported to authorities now number 150. Associate professor of zoology at the University of Tasmania, Randolph Rose, has said he dreams of seeing a thylacine. But Rose, who in his 35 years in Tasmanian academia has fielded countless reports of thylacine sightings, is now convinced that his dream will go unfulfilled.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘The consensus among conservationists is that usually; any animal with a population base of less than 1,000 is headed for extinction within 60 years,’ says Rose. ‘Sixty years ago, there was only one thylacine that we know of, and that was in Hobart Zoo,’ he says.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Dr. David Pemberton, curator of zoology at the Tasmanian Museum and Art Gallery, whose PhD thesis was on the thylacine, says that despite scientific thinking that 500 animals are required to sustain a population, the Florida panther is down to a dozen or so animals and, while it does have some inbreeding problems, is still ticking along. ‘I’ll take a punt and say that, if we manage to find a thylacine in the scrub, it means that there are 50-plus animals out there.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>After all, animals can be notoriously elusive. The strange fish is known as the coelacanth’ with its ‘proto-legs’, was thought to have died out along with the dinosaurs 700 million years ago until a specimen was dragged to the surface in a shark net off the south-east coast of South Africa in 1938.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>K</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Wildlife biologist Nick Mooney has the unenviable task of investigating all ‘sightings’ of the tiger totaling 4,000 since the mid-1980s, and averaging about 150 a year. It was Mooney who was first consulted late last month about the authenticity of digital photographic images purportedly taken by a German tourist while on a recent bushwalk in the state. On face value, Mooney says, the account of the sighting, and the two photographs submitted as the proof amount to one of the most convincing cases for the species’ survival he has seen.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>L</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>And Mooney has seen it all – the mistakes, the hoaxes, the illusions and the plausible accounts of sightings. Hoaxers aside, most people who report sightings end up believing they have been a thylacine, and are themselves believable to the point they could pass a lie-detector test, according to Mooney. Others, having tabled a creditable report, then become utterly obsessed like the Tasmanian who has registered 99 thylacine sightings to date. Mooney has seen individuals bankrupted by the obsession, and families destroyed. ‘It is a blind optimism that something is, rather than a cynicism that something isn’t,’ Mooney says, ‘If something crosses the road, it’s not a case of “I wonder what that was?” Rather, it is a case of “that’s a thylacine!” It is a bit like a gold prospector’s blind faith, “it has got to be there”.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>M</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>However, Mooney treats all reports on face value. ‘I never try to embarrass people or make fools of them. But the fact that I don’t pack the car immediately they ring can often be taken as ridicule. Obsessive characters get irate that someone in my position is not out there when they think the thylacine is there.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>N</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>But Hans Naarding, whose sighting of a striped animal two decades ago was the highlight of ‘a life of animal spotting’, remains bemused by the time and money people waste on tiger searches. He says resources would be better applied to save the Tasmanian devil, and helping migratory bird populations that are declining as a result of shrinking wetlands across Australia.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>O</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Could the thylacine still be out there? ‘Sure,’ Naarding says. But he also says any discovery of surviving thylacines would be ‘rather pointless’. ‘How do you save a species from extinction? What could you do with it? If there are thylacines out there, they are better off right where they are.’</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8911&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8912","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Amateur Naturalists","book":"阅读还原集Vol.19","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.19 · Test 1 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8912:64420:27","type":"choice","text":"27 definition of Phenology introduced","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：These data sets, and others like them, are proving invaluable to ecologists interested in the timing of biological events, or phenology.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问哪个段落介绍了\"物候学\"的定义。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Phenology\"一词定位到B段。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到\"物候学\"是对\"the timing of biological events\"的另一种称呼，即对生物事件发生时间的记录，这符合题目要求对，因此答案为B。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"64420","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-33\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 27-33 on your answer sheet."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8912:64420:28","type":"choice","text":"28 sparks first noticed amateur records","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Sparks first became aware of the army of ‘closet phenologists’, as he describes them, when a retiring colleague gave him the Marsham records.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问，哪一段提到了，Sparks第一次注意到业余记录。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Sparks first noticed amateur records\"可以定位到C段第一句。\n解题思路：C段第一句，斯帕克斯最初接触到这群被他称为“隐秘植物学家”的群体，源于一位退休同事赠送的马沙姆庄园档案。这与题目所问完全吻合。因此，答案为C。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"64420","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-33\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 27-33 on your answer sheet."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8912:64420:29","type":"choice","text":"29 surprise function of casual data in science","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Because the public understands these records, they accept them,’ says Sparks. It can also illustrate potentially unpleasant consequences, he adds, such as the finding that more rat infestations are reported to local councils in warmer years. And getting people involved is great for public relations.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段落提到了，非正式数据在科学中的意外作用。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"surprise function\"和\"casual data\"可以定位到文章中H段，该段提到了非正式数据在科学中的意外功能。\n解题思路：H段提到，这些数据可以让公众理解并接受科学，同时也能展示潜在的负面影响，如温暖的年份里鼠患的报告增加。此外，H段还提到，让公众参与进来对于公共关系非常有益，这些都属于题目描述的非正式数据在科学中的意外作用，因此，答案为H。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"64420","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-33\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 27-33 on your answer sheet."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8912:64420:30","type":"choice","text":"30 it seems like mission impossible without enormous amateur data collection","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The data are cheap to collect and can provide breadth in space, time and range of species. ‘It’s very difficult to collect data on a large geographical scale without enlisting an army of observers,’ says Root.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落包含了“没有大量的业余数据收集，这似乎是不可能的任务”的信息。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词“mission impossible”和“amateur data collection”可以定位到G段。G段中提到了“without enlisting an army of observers”，这与题目的意思相符。\n解题思路：G段中提到了，这些数据采集成本低廉，能提供空间、时间及物种范围的广度。“在不动员大批观察者的情况下，很难在大范围地理尺度上收集数据，”鲁特说道。这意味着如果没有大量的业余数据收集者，收集数据将会非常困难。这与题目的意思相符。因此，答案是G。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"64420","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-33\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 27-33 on your answer sheet."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8912:64420:31","type":"choice","text":"31 example of using amateur records for a scientific prediction","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The data can also hint at how nature will change in the future. Together with models of climate change, amateurs’ records could help guide conservation. Terry Root, an ecologist at the University of Michigan in Ann Arbor, has collected birdwatchers’ counts of wildfowl taken between 1955 and 1996 on seasonal ponds in the American Midwest and combined them with climate data and models of future warming. Her analysis shows that the increased droughts that the models predict could halve the breeding populations at the ponds. ‘The number of waterfowl in North America will most probably drop significantly with global warming,’ she says.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落包含了，使用业余记录进行科学预测的案例。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“using amateur records for a scientific prediction”可以定位到E段，该段提到了Terry Root使用业余的鸟类观察记录进行科学预测的例子。\n解题思路：E段中的原文明确提到了，这些数据还能为未来自然变化趋势提供线索。后给出了具体的例子，即Terry Root使用业余的鸟类观察记录和气候数据模型来预测未来气候变暖对水禽数量的影响。因此，答案为E。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"64420","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-33\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 27-33 on your answer sheet."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8912:64420:32","type":"choice","text":"32 records from an amateur contributed to climate change","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The competition has taken place annually on the Tenana River in Alaska since 1917, and analysis of the results showed that the thaw now arrives five days earlier than it did when the contest began.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了， 业余爱好者提供的记录有助于观察气候变化。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"records from an amateur contributed to climate change\"可以定位到D段，该段提到了一个业余记录的例子。\n解题思路：D段中提到了，这项比赛自1917年起每年在阿拉斯加的特纳纳河举行，分析结果显示，如今融冰期比比赛开始时提前了五天。这表明业余记录对我们了解气候变化有帮助。因此，D段包含了相关信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"64420","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-33\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 27-33 on your answer sheet."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8912:64420:33","type":"choice","text":"33 collection of old records compiled by a family of amateur naturalists","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Around two centuries before Coates, Robert Marsham, a landowner from Norfolk in the East of England, began recording the life cycles of plants and animals on his estate – when the first wood anemones flowered, the dates on which the oaks burst into leaf and the rooks began nesting. Successive Marshams continued compiling these notes for 211 years.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问哪个段落提到了，业余自然学家家族编纂的旧档案集\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"collection of old records\"和\"family of amateur naturalists\"定位。\n解题思路：根据原文\"A段\"中的句子，早在科茨之前约两个世纪，来自英格兰东部诺福克郡的地主罗伯特·马沙姆就开始记录庄园内动植物的生命周期，马沙姆家族的后人持续记录这些笔记长达211年。与题目中的\"collection of old records compiled by a family of amateur naturalists\"完全吻合，因此答案为A。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"64420","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-33\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 27-33 on your answer sheet."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8912:64421:34","type":"fill","text":"填写第 34 空","answer":"Bee-keeping notes/Bee-keeping/bee-keeping notes/bee-keeping/Beekeeping notes/Beekeeping/beekeeping notes/beekeeping","acceptedAnswers":["Bee-keeping notes","Bee-keeping","bee-keeping notes","bee-keeping","Beekeeping notes","Beekeeping","beekeeping notes","beekeeping"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The book’s yellowing pages contain bee-keeping notes made between 1941 and 1969 by the late Walter Coates of Kilworth, Leicestershire.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是在Walter Coates的记录中，有很多关于什么的(信息)。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"Walter Coates\"和\"records\"可以定位到A段第一句，提到他的记录包含了一些内容。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，这本泛黄的书页记录着已故莱斯特郡基尔沃斯镇居民沃尔特·科茨在1941至1969年间养蜂的笔记。Coates的记录中包含了\"bee-keeping notes\"，即养蜂笔记，因此答案为\"Beekeeping (notes)\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64421","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 34-36\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 34-36 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8912:64422:35","type":"fill","text":"填写第 35 空","answer":"Life cycles/life cycles/Life cycle/life cycle","acceptedAnswers":["Life cycles","life cycles","Life cycle","life cycle"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Around two centuries before Coates, Robert Marsham, a landowner from Norfolk in the East of England, began recording the life cycles of plants and animals on his estate – when the first wood anemones flowered, the dates on which the oaks burst into leaf and the rooks began nesting.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问Robert Marsham以记录田野中动植物的什么而闻名。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的专有名词\"Robert Marsham\"和名词\"fields\"（对应原文中的\"on his estate\"）定位到A段末句。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，英格兰东部诺福克郡的地主罗伯特·马沙姆就开始记录庄园内动植物的生命周期——从第一朵木银莲花绽放的时节，到橡树破叶萌芽的日期，再到乌鸦开始筑巢的时刻。因此答案为\"life cycles(s)\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64422","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 34-36\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 34-36 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8912:64423:36","type":"fill","text":"填写第 36 空","answer":"droughts/Droughts","acceptedAnswers":["droughts","Droughts"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Her analysis shows that the increased droughts that the models predict could halve the breeding populations at the ponds. ‘The number of waterfowl in North America will most probably drop significantly with global warming,’ she says.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是根据一些物候学家的观点，北美水禽数量减少是因为什么的增加。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“waterfowl in North America”和“decreases”可以定位到E段中关于Terry Root的研究结果。\n解题思路：原文中提到Terry Root的分析显示，模型预测的干旱增加可能会导致池塘中的繁殖种群数量减半，并且北美水禽的数量可能会显著下降。因此，水禽数量减少的原因是干旱的增加，答案为“droughts”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64423","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 34-36\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 34-36 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8912:64424:37","type":"choice","text":"Why do a lot of scientists questioned the amateurs data?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But not all professionals are happy to use amateur data. ‘A lot of scientists won’t touch them, they say they’re too full of problems,’ says Root. Because different observers can have different ideas of what constitutes, for example, an open snowdrop.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问为什么很多科学家质疑业余数据。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"scientists questioned the amateurs data\"定位到F段，该段明确提到科学家对业余数据的质疑。\n解题思路：F段中Root提到，并非所有专业人士都愿意使用业余数据。“很多科学家都避之不及，他们觉得这些数据问题太多”，鲁特说道。说明业余数据有时不可靠（reliable），对应选项C。其他选项A、B、D在原文中未明确提及。","options":["Data collection is not professional.","Amateur observers are careless.","Amateur data is not reliable sometimes.","They have one-sided work experience."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64424","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8912:64425:38","type":"choice","text":"Example of leaves Mark Schwartz used to explain that?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\n‘We need to know pretty precisely what a person’s been observing – if they just say ‘I noted when the leaves came out’, it might not be that useful.’\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是Mark Schwartz用树叶的例子来解释什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"Mark Schwartz\"和\"leaves\"可以定位到F段中Mark Schwartz关于树叶的论述。\n解题思路：原文中Mark Schwartz提到：我们需要非常精确地了解观察者的具体记录——如果他们只是简单说‘我注意到叶子长出来了’，这样的信息可能并不实用。这说明他认为不准确的信息是没有价值的。这与选项D\"准确的信息才有价值\"相符。因此，答案为D。","options":["Amateur records are not reliable at all.","Amateur records are not well organized.","Some details are very difficult to notice.","Valuable information is accurate one."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64425","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8912:64426:39","type":"choice","text":"What suggestion of scientists for the usage of amateur data?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：With the enthusiasm of amateur phenologists evident from past records, professional researchers are now trying to create standardised recording schemes for future efforts. They hope that well-designed studies will generate a volume of observations large enough to drown out the idiosyncrasies of individual recorders. The data are cheap to collect and can provide breadth in space, time and range of species. ‘It’s very difficult to collect data on a large geographical scale without enlisting an army of observers,’ says Root.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问科学家对使用业余数据的建议是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"suggestion of scientists\"和\"usage of amateur data\"定位到G段，该段讨论了专业人士对业余数据的看法和建议。\n解题思路：G段提到，专业研究人员正在尝试创建标准化的记录方案，他们希望精心设计的研究能产生足够多的观测数据，以掩盖个别记录者的特殊性。这表明科学家建议使用改进过的、更好的方法来处理业余数据，因此选项A正确。","options":["To use modified and better approaches.","Only Observation data is valuable.","To use original materials instead of changed ones.","Method of data collection is the most important."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64426","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8912:64427:40","type":"choice","text":"What’s the implication of phenology for ordinary people?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Phenology also helps to drive home messages about climate change. Because the public understands these records, they accept them,’ says Sparks.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是“物候学对普通人有什么影响？”\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词“phenology”和“ordinary people”可以定位到H段，该段主要讨论了物候学对公众的影响。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句，物候学还能有效传递气候变化信息。斯帕克斯指出：‘公众理解这些记录，自然会接受。可以看出物候学能够帮助公众理解并关注气候变化。因此，物候学能够提高公众对气候变化的关注，对应选项D。","options":["It enriches the knowledge of the public.","It improves ordinary people’s relations with scientists.","It encourages people to collect more animal information.","It arouses public awareness about climate change."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64427","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64420","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-33\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 27-33 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>27</strong> definition of Phenology introduced <strong class=\"source-blank\">[27] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"64421","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 34-36\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 34-36 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>34</strong> In Waiter Coates’s records, there are plenty of information of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[34] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"64422","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 34-36\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 34-36 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>35</strong> Robert Marsham is well-known for noting animals and plants’<strong class=\"source-blank\">[35] ____</strong> in the fields.</p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"64423","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 34-36\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 34-36 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>36</strong> The number of waterfowl in North America decreases because of increased <strong class=\"source-blank\">[36] ____</strong>\naccording to some phenologists.</p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"64424","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Why do a lot of scientists questioned the amateurs data?</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"64425","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Example of leaves Mark Schwartz used to explain that?</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"64426","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What suggestion of scientists for the usage of amateur data?</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"64427","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What’s the implication of phenology for ordinary people?</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Amateur Naturalists</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Tim Sparks slides a small leather-bound notebook out of an envelope. The book’s yellowing pages contain bee-keeping notes made between 1941 and 1969 by the late Walter Coates of Kilworth, Leicestershire. He adds it to his growing pile of local journals, birdwatchers’ lists and gardening diaries. ‘We’re uncovering about one major new record each month,’ he says, ‘I still get surprised.’ Around two centuries before Coates, Robert Marsham, a landowner from Norfolk in the East of England, began recording the life cycles of plants and animals on his estate – when the first wood anemones flowered, the dates on which the oaks burst into leaf and the rooks began nesting. Successive Marshams continued compiling these notes for 211 years.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Today, such records are being put to use that their authors could not possibly have expected. These data sets, and others like them, are proving invaluable to ecologists interested in the timing of biological events, or phenology. By combining the records with climate data, researchers can reveal how, for example, changes in temperature affect the arrival of spring, allowing ecologists to make improved predictions about the impact of climate change. A small band of researchers is combing through hundreds of years of records taken by thousands of amateur naturalists. And more systematic projects have also started up, producing an overwhelming response. ‘The amount of interest is almost frightening,’ says Sparks, a climate researcher at the Centre for Ecology and Hydrology in Monks Wood, Cambridgeshire.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Sparks first became aware of the army of ‘closet phenologists’, as he describes them, when a retiring colleague gave him the Marsham records. He now spends much of his time following leads from one historical data set to another. As news of his quest spreads, people tip him off to other historical records, and more amateur phenologists come out of their closets. The British devotion to recording and collecting makes his job easier – one man from Kent sent him 30 years’ worth of kitchen calendars, on which he had noted the date that his neighbour’s magnolia tree flowered.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Other researchers have unearthed data from equally odd sources. Rafe Sagarin, an ecologist at Stanford University in California, recently studied records of a betting contest in which participants attempt to guess the exact time at which a specially erected wooden tripod will fall through the surface of a thawing river. The competition has taken place annually on the Tenana River in Alaska since 1917, and analysis of the results showed that the thaw now arrives five days earlier than it did when the contest began.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Overall, such records have helped to show that, compared with 20 years ago, a raft of natural events now occur earlier across much of the northern hemisphere, from the opening of leaves to the return of birds from migration and the emergence of butterflies from hibernation. The data can also hint at how nature will change in the future. Together with models of climate change, amateurs’ records could help guide conservation. Terry Root, an ecologist at the University of Michigan in Ann Arbor, has collected birdwatchers’ counts of wildfowl taken between 1955 and 1996 on seasonal ponds in the American Midwest and combined them with climate data and models of future warming. Her analysis shows that the increased droughts that the models predict could halve the breeding populations at the ponds. ‘The number of waterfowl in North America will most probably drop significantly with global warming,’ she says.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>But not all professionals are happy to use amateur data. ‘A lot of scientists won’t touch them, they say they’re too full of problems,’ says Root. Because different observers can have different ideas of what constitutes, for example, an open snowdrop. ‘The biggest concern with ad hoc observations is how carefully and systematically they were taken,’ says Mark Schwartz of the University of Wisconsin, Milwaukee, who studies the interactions between plants and climate. ‘We need to know pretty precisely what a person’s been observing – if they just say ‘I noted when the leaves came out’, it might not be that useful.’ Measuring the onset of autumn can be particularly problematic because deciding when leaves change colour is a more subjective process than noting when they appear.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Overall, most phenologists are positive about the contribution that amateurs can make. ‘They get at the raw power of science: careful observation of the natural world,’ says Sagarin. But the professionals also acknowledge the need for careful quality control. Root, for example, tries to gauge the quality of an amateur archive by interviewing its collector. ‘You always have to worry – things as trivial as vacations can affect the measurement. I disregard a lot of records because they’re not rigorous enough,’ she says. Others suggest that the right statistics can iron out some of the problems with amateur data. Together with colleagues at Wageningen University in the Netherlands, environmental scientist Arnold van Vliet is developing statistical techniques to account for the uncertainty in amateur phenological data. With the enthusiasm of amateur phenologists evident from past records, professional researchers are now trying to create standardised recording schemes for future efforts. They hope that well-designed studies will generate a volume of observations large enough to drown out the idiosyncrasies of individual recorders. The data are cheap to collect and can provide breadth in space, time and range of species. ‘It’s very difficult to collect data on a large geographical scale without enlisting an army of observers,’ says Root.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Phenology also helps to drive home messages about climate change. ‘Because the public understands these records, they accept them,’ says Sparks. It can also illustrate potentially unpleasant consequences, he adds, such as the finding that more rat infestations are reported to local councils in warmer years. And getting people involved is great for public relations. ‘People are thrilled to think that the data they’ve been collecting as a hobby can be used for something scientific – it empowers them,’ says Root.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8912&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8907","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 The Beginning of Football","book":"阅读还原集Vol.18","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.18 · Test 4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8907:64386:1","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The role of the feet was so small as scarcely to be of consequence. The game remained popular for 700 or 800 years, but, although it was taken to England, it is doubtful whether it can be considered as a forerunner of contemporary football.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求为D段选择一个合适的标题，概括该段的主要内容。\n定位关键信息：定位到D段，阅读该段内容寻找核心信息。重点关注段落中描述罗马游戏\"harpastum\"的特点以及其与当代足球的关系。\n解题思路：D段主要介绍了罗马的\"harpastum\"游戏，提到该游戏在罗马流行了700-800年，但文中明确指出\"it is doubtful whether it can be considered as a forerunner of contemporary football\"（它是否是当代足球的早期版本值得怀疑）。因此，该段落的核心内容是探讨\"harpastum\"是否是现代足球的早期形式，最符合这一内容的标题是\"Probably not an early version of football\"（可能不是足球的早期版本）。","options":["Limited success in suppressing the game","Opposition to the role of football in schools","A way of developing moral values","Football matches between countries","A game that has survived","Separation into two sports","Proposals for minor improvements","Attempts to standardize the game","Probably not an early version of football","A chaotic activity with virtually no rules"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64386","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nThe reading passage has ten paragraphs A-J. Choose the correct headings for paragraphs D-J from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-x in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8907:64386:2","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"J","acceptedAnswers":["J"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The game that flourished in Britain from the 8th to the 19th centuries was substantially different from all the previously known forms – more disorganised, more violent, more spontaneous and usually played by an indefinite number of players.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求为E段选择一个正确的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读E段内容，定位到描述英国从8世纪到19世纪流行的足球游戏特点的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句中的描述，可以判断E段主要讲述的是英国早期足球游戏的特点，与之前的足球形式有很大不同，更加无组织、暴力、自发，并且通常由不确定数量的玩家参与，后面举了具体的例子。因此，E段的标题应为“A chaotic activity with virtually no rules”一项几乎没有规则的混乱活动。","options":["Limited success in suppressing the game","Opposition to the role of football in schools","A way of developing moral values","Football matches between countries","A game that has survived","Separation into two sports","Proposals for minor improvements","Attempts to standardize the game","Probably not an early version of football","A chaotic activity with virtually no rules"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64386","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nThe reading passage has ten paragraphs A-J. Choose the correct headings for paragraphs D-J from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-x in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8907:64386:3","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"3.iF段第一句话和倒数第一句话None of these efforts had much effect对应limited success.\n原文答案句：There was tremendous enthusiasm for football, even though the authorities repeatedly intervened to restrict it, as a public nuisance. In the 14th and 15th centuries, England, Scotland and France all made football punishable by law, because of the disorder that commonly accompanied it, or because the well-loved recreation prevented subjects from practicing more useful military disciplines. None of these efforts had much effect.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求为F段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读F段，可以找到关键信息是关于足球在14世纪和15世纪被法律禁止，但收效甚微。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句，F段主要讲述了足球在14世纪和15世纪被法律禁止的原因和结果，首尾句都强调了，人们对足球的狂热，相关法律法规收效甚微，这与标题“Limited success in suppressing the game”吻合，因此，选择该标题作为F段的标题。","options":["Limited success in suppressing the game","Opposition to the role of football in schools","A way of developing moral values","Football matches between countries","A game that has survived","Separation into two sports","Proposals for minor improvements","Attempts to standardize the game","Probably not an early version of football","A chaotic activity with virtually no rules"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64386","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nThe reading passage has ten paragraphs A-J. Choose the correct headings for paragraphs D-J from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-x in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8907:64386:4","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He pointed out that it had positive educational value and promoted health and strength. Mulcaster claimed that all that was needed was to refine it a little, limit the number of participants in each team and, more importantly, have a referee to oversee the game.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求为G段选择一个合适的标题，概括该段的主要内容。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读G段，可以定位到几个关键信息点：16世纪英国人对足球的热情，理查德·穆尔卡斯特的支持以及他对足球改革的建议。\n解题思路：G段主要讲述了16世纪英国人对足球的热情。同时，段落中还提到了理查德·穆尔卡斯特对足球的支持。最重要的是，他还提出了一些改革足球的建议，如限制每队人数、设立裁判等，对足球运动做出一些小变动。因此，G段最合适的标题为“Proposals for minor improvements”。","options":["Limited success in suppressing the game","Opposition to the role of football in schools","A way of developing moral values","Football matches between countries","A game that has survived","Separation into two sports","Proposals for minor improvements","Attempts to standardize the game","Probably not an early version of football","A chaotic activity with virtually no rules"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64386","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nThe reading passage has ten paragraphs A-J. Choose the correct headings for paragraphs D-J from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-x in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8907:64386:5","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It was recognised in educational circles that, as a team game, football helped to develop such fine qualities as loyalty, selflessness, cooperation, subordination and deference to the team spirit. A ‘games cult’ developed in schools and some form of football became an obligatory part of the curriculum.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目要求为H段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读H段内容，可以定位到关于19世纪初英国学校对足球的改编，教育界认识到足球在教育中的重要性。\n解题思路：H段主要讲述了19世纪初英国学校对足球的改编，同时，教育界认识到足球作为团队运动有助于培养忠诚、无私、合作、服从和团队精神等品质。此外，足球在学校中成为一种“运动崇拜”，并成为课程的一部分。因此，H段的标题应与“足球的重要性、价值”相关，标题“A way of developing moral values”（一种培养道德价值观的方式）最符合段落内容。","options":["Limited success in suppressing the game","Opposition to the role of football in schools","A way of developing moral values","Football matches between countries","A game that has survived","Separation into two sports","Proposals for minor improvements","Attempts to standardize the game","Probably not an early version of football","A chaotic activity with virtually no rules"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64386","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nThe reading passage has ten paragraphs A-J. Choose the correct headings for paragraphs D-J from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-x in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8907:64386:6","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph F","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1863, developments reached a climax. At Cambridge University, an initiative began to establish some uniform standards and rules that would be accepted by everyone....In October of the same year, eleven London clubs and schools sent representatives to establish a set of fundamental rules to govern the matches played amongst them. This meeting marked the birth of the Football Association.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目要求为I段选择正确的标题。\n定位关键信息：定位到文章的I段，寻找能够概括该段落主旨的句子,主要关注段落的首尾句。\n解题思路：I段主要讲述了1863年在剑桥大学发起的建立统一足球规则的运动，以及同年10月11个伦敦俱乐部和学校代表开会制定基本规则，这次会议标志着足球协会的诞生。因此该段落的主旨是足球运动标准的建立，因此，选择能够概括这一内容的标题，即\"Attempts to standardize the game\"。","options":["Limited success in suppressing the game","Opposition to the role of football in schools","A way of developing moral values","Football matches between countries","A game that has survived","Separation into two sports","Proposals for minor improvements","Attempts to standardize the game","Probably not an early version of football","A chaotic activity with virtually no rules"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64386","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nThe reading passage has ten paragraphs A-J. Choose the correct headings for paragraphs D-J from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-x in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8907:64386:7","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph G","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The dispute concerning kicking and tripping opponents and carrying the ball was discussed thoroughly at this and subsequent meetings, until eventually, on 8 December, the die-hard exponents of the Rugby style withdrew, marking a final split between rugby and football.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目要求为J段选择正确的标题。\n定位关键信息：根据题目要求，需要在J段中找到能够概括段落主旨的关键信息。J段主要讲述了当时的足球运动最终变成了两种运动，以及足球比赛的诞生。\n解题思路：J段首先提到了经过会议讨论，最终将当时的足球运动分为两种运动，分别是橄榄球和足球。然后描述了足球协会在短时间内的发展，包括成员俱乐部的增加和第一个足球比赛的举办。因此，J段的主要内容是关于足球运动的分裂。根据这些信息，可以确定J段的标题应该是关于“Separation into two sports”。","options":["Limited success in suppressing the game","Opposition to the role of football in schools","A way of developing moral values","Football matches between countries","A game that has survived","Separation into two sports","Proposals for minor improvements","Attempts to standardize the game","Probably not an early version of football","A chaotic activity with virtually no rules"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64386","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nThe reading passage has ten paragraphs A-J. Choose the correct headings for paragraphs D-J from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-x in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet."},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8907:64387:8","type":"choice","text":"8 Tsu’chu","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The very earliest form of football for which we have evidence is the ‘tsu’chu’, which was played in China and may date back 3,000 years. It was performed in front of the Emperor during festivities to mark his birthday.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求将“Tsu’chu”与其正确的描述进行匹配。\n定位关键信息：根据“Tsu’chu”这一专有名词定位至B段。\n解题思路：原文B段在描述中国古代的蹴鞠时，明确指出这项活动是在皇帝生日庆典期间，于御前表演的。这表明蹴鞠是某个庆祝活动的一部分。选项I “formed part of a celebration”（构成了庆典的一部分）与此信息吻合。因此，答案是I。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J","Section K","Section L"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L"],"sourceGroupId":"64387","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending A-L from the box below. Write the correct letter A-F in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\nA was seen as something to be encouraged in the young.\nB involved individual players having different responsibilities.\nC was influenced by a game from another country.\nD was a cooperative effort by all the players.\nE distracted people from more important activities.\nF was played by teams of a fixed size.\nG was less popular than it later became.\nH was often played by one community against another.\nI formed part of a celebration."},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8907:64387:9","type":"choice","text":"9 Kemari","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The players had to pass the ball to each other, in a relatively small space, trying not to let it touch the ground.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求将Kemari与其正确的描述进行匹配。\n定位关键信息：根据Kemari这一专有名词定位至C段。\n解题思路：原文C段在描述日本“Kemari”时，强调其特点是“not competitive”（非竞争性）且“not... struggle for possession of the ball”（不争夺控球权），玩法是球员们必须互相传球，尽量不让球落地，是一种团队合作运动。选项D “was a cooperative effort by all the players”（需要所有球员的共同努力）符合原文描述。因此，答案是D。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J","Section K","Section L"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L"],"sourceGroupId":"64387","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending A-L from the box below. Write the correct letter A-F in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\nA was seen as something to be encouraged in the young.\nB involved individual players having different responsibilities.\nC was influenced by a game from another country.\nD was a cooperative effort by all the players.\nE distracted people from more important activities.\nF was played by teams of a fixed size.\nG was less popular than it later became.\nH was often played by one community against another.\nI formed part of a celebration."},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8907:64387:10","type":"choice","text":"10 Harpastum","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The Romans had a much livelier game, ‘harpastum’. Each team member had his own specific tactical assignment took a noisy interest in the proceedings and the score.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求将Harpastum与其正确的描述进行匹配。\n定位关键信息：根据Harpastum这一专有名词定位至D段。\n解题思路：原文D段在描述罗马游戏“Harpastum”时，明确指出“每位队员都有明确的战术分工”。这表明在游戏中，不同的球员承担着不同的、明确的职责。选项B “involved individual players having different responsibilities”（每个球员拥有不同的职责）与此信息完全吻合。因此，答案是B。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J","Section K","Section L"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L"],"sourceGroupId":"64387","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending A-L from the box below. Write the correct letter A-F in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\nA was seen as something to be encouraged in the young.\nB involved individual players having different responsibilities.\nC was influenced by a game from another country.\nD was a cooperative effort by all the players.\nE distracted people from more important activities.\nF was played by teams of a fixed size.\nG was less popular than it later became.\nH was often played by one community against another.\nI formed part of a celebration."},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8907:64387:11","type":"choice","text":"11 From the 8th centuries, football in the British Isles","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The game that flourished in Britain from the 8th to the 19th centuries was substantially different from all the previously known forms – more disorganised, more violent, more spontaneous and usually played by an indefinite number of players. Frequently, the games took the form of a heated contest between whole villages.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求将“从8世纪起，不列颠群岛的足球”与其正确的结尾进行匹配。\n定位关键信息： 根据时间信息“From the 8th centuries”和地点“British Isles”定位至E段。\n解题思路：原文E段明确指出，从8世纪到19世纪在英国盛行的足球，其常见形式是“整个村庄之间的激烈竞赛”。选项H “was often played by one community against another”（经常是一个社区与另一个社区之间进行比赛）概括了这一特点，其中“community”（社区）与原文的“villages”（村庄）相对应。因此，答案是H。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J","Section K","Section L"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L"],"sourceGroupId":"64387","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending A-L from the box below. Write the correct letter A-F in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\nA was seen as something to be encouraged in the young.\nB involved individual players having different responsibilities.\nC was influenced by a game from another country.\nD was a cooperative effort by all the players.\nE distracted people from more important activities.\nF was played by teams of a fixed size.\nG was less popular than it later became.\nH was often played by one community against another.\nI formed part of a celebration."},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8907:64387:12","type":"choice","text":"12 In the past, the authorities legitimately despised the football and acted on the belief that football","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In the 14th and 15th centuries, England, Scotland and France all made football punishable by law, because of the disorder that commonly accompanied it, or because the well-loved recreation prevented subjects from practicing more useful military disciplines.\n对应段落：F段\n审题： 题目要求将“过去，当局使用法律来限制足球运动，因为他们认为足球”与其正确的结尾进行匹配。\n定位关键信息： 根据“authorities”、“despised the football”和“acted”定位至F段关于当局限制足球的原因。\n解题思路：原文F段说明，14至15世纪期间，英格兰、苏格兰和法国均通过立法禁止足球，原因有二：一是它常伴随骚乱，二是这项广受欢迎的娱乐活动阻碍了人们练习更有用的军事技能。第二个原因直接表明，足球让人们从更重要的活动（军事训练）中分心。选项E “distracted people from more important activities”（使人们从更重要的活动中分心）与此信念完全吻合。因此，答案是E。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J","Section K","Section L"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L"],"sourceGroupId":"64387","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending A-L from the box below. Write the correct letter A-F in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\nA was seen as something to be encouraged in the young.\nB involved individual players having different responsibilities.\nC was influenced by a game from another country.\nD was a cooperative effort by all the players.\nE distracted people from more important activities.\nF was played by teams of a fixed size.\nG was less popular than it later became.\nH was often played by one community against another.\nI formed part of a celebration."},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8907:64387:13","type":"choice","text":"13 When it was accepted in academic settings, football","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It was recognised in educational circles that, as a team game, football helped to develop such fine qualities as loyalty, selflessness, cooperation, subordination and deference to the team spirit. A ‘games cult’ developed in schools and some form of football became an obligatory part of the curriculum.\n对应段落：H段\n审题： 题目要求将“学校接受足球运动时，认为足球运动”与其正确的结尾进行匹配。\n定位关键信息：根据“academic settings”定位至H段，该段描述了足球在19世纪早期英国学校中的情况。\n解题思路原文H段明确指出，在教育界，人们认识到足球作为一种团队运动，有助于培养忠诚、无私、合作等优良品质。这意味着足球在校园里被视为一种有益的教育手段。选项A “was seen as something to be encouraged in the young”准确地概括了足球在这种学术环境下的角色和定位。因此，答案是A。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J","Section K","Section L"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L"],"sourceGroupId":"64387","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending A-L from the box below. Write the correct letter A-F in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\nA was seen as something to be encouraged in the young.\nB involved individual players having different responsibilities.\nC was influenced by a game from another country.\nD was a cooperative effort by all the players.\nE distracted people from more important activities.\nF was played by teams of a fixed size.\nG was less popular than it later became.\nH was often played by one community against another.\nI formed part of a celebration."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64386","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nThe reading passage has ten paragraphs A-J. Choose the correct headings for paragraphs D-J from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-x in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"64387","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending A-L from the box below. Write the correct letter A-F in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\nA was seen as something to be encouraged in the young.\nB involved individual players having different responsibilities.\nC was influenced by a game from another country.\nD was a cooperative effort by all the players.\nE distracted people from more important activities.\nF was played by teams of a fixed size.\nG was less popular than it later became.\nH was often played by one community against another.\nI formed part of a celebration.","html":"<p><strong>8</strong> Tsu’chu <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":8}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The Beginning of Football</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Football as we now know it developed in Britain in the 19th century, but the game is far older than this. In fact, the term has historically been applied to games played on foot, as opposed to those played on horseback, so ‘football’ hasn’t always involved kicking a ball. It has generally been played by men, though at the end of the 17th century, games were played between married and single women in a town in Scotland. The married women regularly won.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The very earliest form of football for which we have evidence is the ‘tsu’chu’, which was played in China and may date back 3,000 years. It was performed in front of the Emperor during festivities to mark his birthday. It involved kicking a leather ball through a 30-40 cm opening into a small net fixed onto long bamboo canes – a feat that demanded great skill and excellent technique.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Another form of the game, also originating from the Far East, was the Japanese ‘kemari’ which dates from about the fifth century and is still played today. This is a type of circular football game, a more dignified and ceremonious experience requiring certain skills, but not competitive in the way the Chinese game was, nor is there the slightest sign of struggle for possession of the ball. The players had to pass the ball to each other, in a relatively small space, trying not to let it touch the ground.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The Romans had a much livelier game, ‘harpastum’. Each team member had his own specific tactical assignment took a noisy interest in the proceedings and the score. The role of the feet was so small as scarcely to be of consequence. The game remained popular for 700 or 800 years, but, although it was taken to England, it is doubtful whether it can be considered as a forerunner of contemporary football.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The game that flourished in Britain from the 8th to the 19th centuries was substantially different from all the previously known forms – more disorganised, more violent, more spontaneous and usually played by an indefinite number of players. Frequently, the games took the form of a heated contest between whole villages. Kicking opponents were allowed, as in fact was almost everything else.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>There was tremendous enthusiasm for football, even though the authorities repeatedly intervened to restrict it, as a public nuisance. In the 14th and 15th centuries, England, Scotland and France all made football punishable by law, because of the disorder that commonly accompanied it, or because the well-loved recreation prevented subjects from practicing more useful military disciplines. None of these efforts had much effect.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The English passion for football was particularly strong in the 16th century, influenced by the popularity of the rather better organised Italian game of ‘calcio’. English football was as rough as ever, but it found a prominent supporter in the school headmaster Richard Mulcaster. He pointed out that it had positive educational value and promoted health and strength. Mulcaster claimed that all that was needed was to refine it a little, limit the number of participants in each team and, more importantly, have a referee to oversee the game.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The game persisted in a disorganised form until the early 19th century, when a number of influential English schools developed their own adaptations. In some, including Rugby School, the ball could be touched with the hands or carried; opponents could be tripped up and even kicked. It was recognised in educational circles that, as a team game, football helped to develop such fine qualities as loyalty, selflessness, cooperation, subordination and deference to the team spirit. A ‘games cult’ developed in schools and some form of football became an obligatory part of the curriculum.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In 1863, developments reached a climax. At Cambridge University, an initiative began to establish some uniform standards and rules that would be accepted by everyone, but there were essentially two camps: the minority – Rugby School and some others – wished to continue with their own form of the game, in particular allowing players to carry the ball. In October of the same year, eleven London clubs and schools sent representatives to establish a set of fundamental rules to govern the matches played amongst them. This meeting marked the birth of the Football Association.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;J</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The dispute concerning kicking and tripping opponents and carrying the ball was discussed thoroughly at this and subsequent meetings, until eventually, on 8 December, the die-hard exponents of the Rugby style withdrew, marking a final split between rugby and football. Within eight years, the Football Association already had 50 member clubs, and the first football competition in the world was started – the FA Cup.&amp;#</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8907&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8908","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Coral Reefs","book":"阅读还原集Vol.18","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.18 · Test 4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8908:64388:14","type":"choice","text":"14 geographical Location of the world's coral reef","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：They are most commonly found at shallow depths in tropical waters, but deep water and cold water corals also exist on smaller scales in other areas. Although corals exist both in temperate and tropical waters, shallow-water reefs form only in a zone extending from 30°N to 30°S of the equator.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了世界珊瑚礁的地理分布信息。\n定位关键信息：根据“geographical Location of the world's coral reef”，定位到文中描述珊瑚礁在全球不同地区分布情况的段落。\n解题思路：原文A段，详细描述了其分布的纬度范围（赤道南北30度以内），以及列举了珊瑚礁稀少或罕见的特定海岸线地区（如美洲和非洲西海岸、南亚部分海岸线等）。这些信息全面回答了世界珊瑚礁的地理位置问题。因此，包含此信息的段落是A。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64388","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8908:64388:15","type":"choice","text":"15 how does coral reef benefit economy locally","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The value of reefs in biodiverse regions can be even higher. In parts of Indonesia and the Caribbean where tourism is the main use, reefs are estimated to be worth US $1 million per square kilometer, based on the cost of maintaining sandy beaches and the value of attracting snorkelers and scuba divers.\n对应段落：C段\n审题： 题目要求寻找“珊瑚礁如何惠及当地经济”相关信息所在的段落。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“benefit economy locally”定位到文中描述珊瑚礁对当地经济和民生产生具体效益的部分。\n解题思路：原文C段给出了珊瑚礁的全球经济价值，后又通过具体案例说明了其对当地经济的贡献。因此，包含此信息的段落是C。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64388","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8908:64388:16","type":"choice","text":"16 the statistics of coral reef’s economic significance","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Each year more than 1.8 million tourists visit the reef, spending an estimated AU $4.3 billion (Australian dollars) on reef-related industries from diving to boat rental to posh island resort stays. In the Caribbean, says UNEP, the net annual benefits from diver tourism were US $2 billion in 2000 with US $625 million spent directly on diving on reefs. Further, reef tourism is an important source of employment, especially for some of the world’s poorest people. UNEP says that of the estimated 30 million small-scale fishers in the developing world, most are dependent to a greater or lesser extent on coral reefs. In the Philippines, for example, more than one million small-scale fishers depend directly on coral reefs for their livelihoods. The report estimates that reef fisheries were worth between $15,000 and $150,000 per square kilometer a year, while fish caught for aquariums were worth $500 a kilogram against $6 for fish caught as food. The aquarium fish export industry supports around 50,000 people and generates some US$5.5 million a year in Sri Lanka along.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求寻找“证明珊瑚礁经济重要性的统计数据”相关信息所在的段落。\n定位关键信息：根据“statistics of coral reef’s economic significance”，定位到文中包含具体经济数据、产值和就业人数等统计信息的段落。\n解题思路：C段提到珊瑚礁的经济价值，为当地的旅游业创造巨大经济收益，提供就业岗位，解决部分地区的贫困问题，并列举出一系列的统计数据进行支撑。因此，答案为C。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64388","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8908:64388:17","type":"choice","text":"17 the listed reasons for the declining number of coral reef","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Unfortunately, coral reefs are dying around the world. In particular, coral mining, agricultural and urban runoff, pollution (organic and inorganic), disease, and the digging of canals and access into islands and bays are localized threats to coral ecosystems. Broader threats are sea temperature rise, sea-level rise and pH changes from ocean acidification, all associated with greenhouse gas emissions. Some current fishing practices are destructive and unsustainable. These include cyanide fishing, overfishing and blast fishing.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段列出了珊瑚礁数量减少的原因。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"declining number of coral reef\"可以定位到文章中描述珊瑚礁数量减少原因的段落。\n解题思路：D段详细列举了导致珊瑚礁数量减少的各种原因，包括局部威胁（如珊瑚采矿、农业和城市径流、污染、疾病、运河挖掘等）和更广泛的威胁（如海水温度上升、海平面上升和海洋酸化引起的pH值变化）。此外，还提到了一些破坏性的和不可持续的捕鱼方式，如氰化物捕鱼、过度捕捞和炸鱼。这些内容与题目要求的信息完全一致，因此D段是正确答案。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64388","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8908:64388:18","type":"choice","text":"18 physical approach to the coral reef by people","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Careless boating, diving, snorkeling and fishing can also damage coral reefs. Whenever people grab, kick, and walk on, or stir up sediment in the reefs, they contribute to coral reef destruction.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落提到了人们跟珊瑚礁的物理接触。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"physical approach\"（物理接触）和\"by people\"（由人造成）定位，在E段中找到描述人们通过抓、踢、行走等方式破坏珊瑚礁的句子。\n解题思路：E段提到，不恰当的划船、潜水、浮潜和钓鱼活动也会破坏珊瑚礁。每当人们抓拽、踢踹、踩踏珊瑚礁，或搅动礁区沉积物时，都会加剧珊瑚礁的毁损。描述了人们直接接触珊瑚礁（grab, kick, walk on）或搅动沉积物（stir up sediment）的行为，符合题目中的描述，因此答案为E。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64388","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8908:64388:19","type":"choice","text":"19 unsustainable fishing methods are applied in regions of the world","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Some current fishing practices are destructive and unsustainable. These include cyanide fishing, overfishing and blast fishing.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了“某些地区采用了不可持续的捕捞鱼式”。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的“unsustainable fishing methods”和“regions of the world”定位到文章中描述捕鱼方法的句子。\n解题思路：D段明确提到了，一些当前的捕鱼做法具有破坏性和不可持续性，包括氰化物捕鱼、过度捕捞和爆破捕鱼。某些地区使用这些方法，因此D段包含了题目所要求的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64388","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8908:64389:20","type":"choice","text":"Coral reefs provide habitat to a variety of marine life.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Yet often called – rainforests of the sea, coral reefs form some of the most diverse ecosystems on Earth. They provide a home for 25% of all marine species, including fish, mollusks worms, crustaceans, echinoderms, sponges, tunicates and other cnidarians.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问“珊瑚礁为多种海洋生物提供栖息地”，需要确认文章是否支持这一信息。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“provide habitat to a variety of marine life”定位，在A段找到珊瑚礁为多种海洋生物提供家园的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，这些常被称为“海洋雨林”的珊瑚礁，孕育着地球上最丰富的生态系统之一，为25%的海洋生物提供栖息地，与题目描述完全一致，因此答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64389","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8908:64390:21","type":"choice","text":"Coral reef distributes around the ocean disproportionally.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Coral reefs are estimated to cover 284,300 km2 just under 0.1% of the oceans‘ surface area, about half the area of France. The Indo-Pacific region accounts for 91.9% of this total area. Southeast Asia accounts for 32.3% of that figure, while the Pacific including Australia accounts for 40.8%. Atlantic and Caribbean coral reefs account for 7.6%.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问“珊瑚礁在海洋中不均匀分布”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“distributes around the ocean”和“disproportionally”定位到A段，该段描述了珊瑚礁在不同地区的分布比例。\n解题思路：A段明确提到珊瑚礁的总面积仅占海洋面积的0.1%，且不同地区的分布比例差异显著，如印度-太平洋地区占91.9%，东南亚占32.3%，而大西洋和加勒比地区仅占7.6%。这些数据表明珊瑚礁的分布确实不均衡，因此题目说法与原文信息一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64390","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8908:64391:22","type":"choice","text":"Coral reef is increasingly important for scientific purpose.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The list includes the ocean’s role as a carbon dioxide sink, atmospheric changes, ultraviolet light, ocean acidification, viruses, impacts of dust storms carrying agents to far-flung reefs, pollutants, algal blooms and others.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问“珊瑚礁对科学研究的重要性日益凸显”是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“scientific purpose”和“increasingly important”定位到文章中关于科学研究珊瑚礁的段落。\n解题思路：文章F段提到科学家和研究人员研究影响珊瑚礁的各种因素，包括二氧化碳汇、大气变化、紫外线、海洋酸化、病毒、尘埃风暴的影响、污染物、藻类爆发等。但文章并未提到珊瑚礁的科学价值在增加或减少。因此，题目中的“increasingly important”在文章中没有明确支持或反驳的信息。所以，答案为Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64391","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8908:64392:23","type":"choice","text":"Coral reefs are greatly exchanged among and exported to other counties.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：无\n对应段落：无\n审题：题目问的是“珊瑚礁在各国之间大量流通并出口至其他国家”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键信息“Coral reefs are greatly exchanged among and exported to other counties”，寻找关于珊瑚礁本身（而非其相关产品或鱼类）作为商品进行国际贸易或出口的描述。\n解题思路：原文确实提到了与珊瑚礁相关的经济活动，如C段提及的“aquarium fish export industry”（观赏鱼出口业）和D段提到的活礁鱼被销售到亚洲餐厅。而非珊瑚礁本身的出口情况。因此，文章并未提供相关信息。因此，题目信息在文中没有依据，判断为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64392","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8908:64393:24","type":"choice","text":"Reef tourism is of economic essence generally for some poor people.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Further, reef tourism is an important source of employment, especially for some of the world’s poorest people.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问“珊瑚礁旅游业对部分贫困人口而言，具有重要的经济意义”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“Reef tourism”和“economic essence”在文章中定位，找到C段中提到“reef tourism”的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，珊瑚礁旅游是重要的就业来源，尤其对全球最贫困群体具有特殊意义。这与题目中的一致。因此，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64393","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8908:64394:25","type":"choice","text":"As with other fishing business, coral fishery is not suitable to women and children.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In the Philippines, for example, more than one million small-scale fishers depend directly on coral reefs for their livelihoods.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问“像其他渔业一样，珊瑚渔业不适合女性和儿童”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"coral fishery\", \"women and children\", \"not suitable\"。在文章中寻找与珊瑚渔业和性别/年龄限制相关的内容。\n解题思路：文章C段提到菲律宾有超过一百万的小规模渔民直接依赖珊瑚礁维生，但并未提及这些渔民是否包括女性和儿童，也未说明珊瑚渔业对性别或年龄有任何限制。因此，题目中的陈述在文章中没有对应信息。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64394","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8908:64395:26","type":"choice","text":"What is the main purpose of this passage?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：无\n对应段落：全文\n审题：题目问这篇文章的主要目的是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读全文，总结文章主旨。可以发现文章首先介绍了珊瑚礁的基本情况（A段），然后阐述了珊瑚礁的生态服务价值和经济效益（B、C段），接着描述了珊瑚礁面临的威胁和破坏（D、E段），最后提到了一些保护措施（F、G段）。\n解题思路：根据全文内容，可以发现文章首先介绍了珊瑚礁的基本情况（A段），然后阐述了珊瑚礁的生态服务价值和经济效益（B、C段），接着描述了珊瑚礁面临的威胁和破坏（D、E段），最后提到了威胁珊瑚礁的因素及保护措施（F、G段）。主要目的是介绍珊瑚礁的生态服务价值和经济效益，以及它们面临的威胁和破坏,以此呼吁人们保护珊瑚礁。因此，选项C“to present the general benefits and an alarming situation of coral reef”最符合文章的主旨。选项A、B、D都只是文章的一部分内容，不能概括全文的主旨。","options":["to demonstrate how coral reef growth in the ocean","to tell that coral reef is widely used as a scientific project","to present the general benefits and an alarming situation of coral reef","to show the vital efforts made to protect the coral reef in Australia"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64395","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 26 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64388","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.","html":"<p><strong>14 </strong>geographical Location of the world&#39;s coral reef <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"64389","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Coral reefs provide habitat to a variety of marine life.</strong></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"64390","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Coral reef distributes around the ocean disproportionally.</strong></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"64391","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Coral reef is increasingly important for scientific purpose.</strong></p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"64392","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Coral reefs are greatly exchanged among and exported to other counties.</strong></p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"64393","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Reef tourism is of economic essence generally for some poor people.</strong></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"64394","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>As with other fishing business, coral fishery is not suitable to women and children.</strong></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"64395","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is the main purpose of this passage?</strong></p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Coral Reefs</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Coral reefs are underwater structures made from calcium carbonate secreted by corals. Coral reefs are colonies of tiny living animals found in marine waters that contain few nutrients. Most coral reefs are built from stony corals, which in turn consist of polyps that cluster in groups.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Coral reefs are estimated to cover 284,300 km2 just under 0.1% of the oceans‘ surface area, about half the area of France. The Indo-Pacific region accounts for 91.9% of this total area. Southeast Asia accounts for 32.3% of that figure, while the Pacific including Australia accounts for 40.8%. Atlantic and Caribbean coral reefs account for 7.6%. Yet often called – rainforests of the sea, coral reefs form some of the most diverse ecosystems on Earth. They provide a home for 25% of all marine species, including fish, mollusks worms, crustaceans, echinoderms, sponges, tunicates and other cnidarians. Paradoxically, coral reefs flourish even though they are surrounded by ocean waters that provide few nutrients. They are most commonly found at shallow depths in tropical waters, but deep water and cold water corals also exist on smaller scales in other areas. Although corals exist both in temperate and tropical waters, shallow-water reefs form only in a zone extending from 30°N to 30°S of the equator. Deepwater coral can exist at greater depths and colder temperatures at much higher latitudes, as far north as Norway. Coral reefs are rare along the American and African west coasts. This is due primarily to upwelling and strong cold coastal currents that reduce water temperatures in these areas (respectively the Peru, Benguela and Canary streams). Corals are seldom found along the coastline of South Asia from the eastern tip of India (Madras) to the Bangladesh and Myanmar borders. They are also rare along the coast around northeastern South America and Bangladesh due to the freshwater released from the Amazon and Ganges Rivers, respectively.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Coral reefs deliver ecosystem services to tourism, fisheries and coastline protection. The global economic value of coral reefs has been estimated at as much as US $375 billion per year. Coral reefs protect shorelines by absorbing wave energy, and many small islands would not exist without their reef to protect them.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The value of reefs in biodiverse regions can be even higher. In parts of Indonesia and the Caribbean where tourism is the main use, reefs are estimated to be worth US $1 million per square kilometer, based on the cost of maintaining sandy beaches and the value of attracting snorkelers and scuba divers. Meanwhile, a recent study of the Great Barrier Reef in Australia found that the reef is worth more to the country as an intact ecosystem than an extractive reserve for fishing. Each year more than 1.8 million tourists visit the reef, spending an estimated AU $4.3 billion (Australian dollars) on reef-related industries from diving to boat rental to posh island resort stays. In the Caribbean, says UNEP, the net annual benefits from diver tourism were US $2 billion in 2000 with US $625 million spent directly on diving on reefs. Further, reef tourism is an important source of employment, especially for some of the world’s poorest people. UNEP says that of the estimated 30 million small-scale fishers in the developing world, most are dependent to a greater or lesser extent on coral reefs. In the Philippines, for example, more than one million small-scale fishers depend directly on coral reefs for their livelihoods. The report estimates that reef fisheries were worth between $15,000 and $150,000 per square kilometer a year, while fish caught for aquariums were worth $500 a kilogram against $6 for fish caught as food. The aquarium fish export industry supports around 50,000 people and generates some US$5.5 million a year in Sri Lanka along.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Unfortunately, coral reefs are dying around the world. In particular, coral mining, agricultural and urban runoff, pollution (organic and inorganic), disease, and the digging of canals and access into islands and bays are localized threats to coral ecosystems. Broader threats are sea temperature rise, sea-level rise and pH changes from ocean acidification, all associated with greenhouse gas emissions. Some current fishing practices are destructive and unsustainable. These include cyanide fishing, overfishing and blast fishing. Although cyanide fishing supplies live reef fish for the tropical aquarium market, most fish caught using this method are sold in restaurants, primarily in Asia, where live fish are prized for their freshness. To catch fish with cyanide, fishers dive down to the reef and squirt cyanide in coral crevices and on the fast-moving fish, to stun the fish making them easy to catch. Overfishing is another leading cause for coral reef degradation. Often, too many fish are taken from one reef to sustain a population in that area. Poor fishing practices, such as banging on the reef with sticks (muro-ami), destroy coral formations that normally function as fish habitat. In some instances, people fish with explosives (blast fishing), which blast apart the surrounding coral.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Tourist resorts that empty their sewage directly into the water surrounding coral reefs contribute to coral reef degradation. Wastes kept in poorly maintained septic tanks can also leak into surrounding groundwater, eventually seeping out to the reefs. Careless boating, diving, snorkeling and fishing can also damage coral reefs. Whenever people grab, kick, and walk on, or stir up sediment in the reefs, they contribute to coral reef destruction. Corals are also harmed or killed when people drop anchors on them or when people collect coral.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>To find answers for these problems, scientists and researchers study the various factors that impact reefs. The list includes the ocean’s role as a carbon dioxide sink, atmospheric changes, ultraviolet light, ocean acidification, viruses, impacts of dust storms carrying agents to far-flung reefs, pollutants, algal blooms and others. Reefs are threatened well beyond coastal areas. General estimates show approximately 10% of the worlds coral reefs are dead. About 60% of the world’s reefs are at risk due to destructive, human-related activities. The threat to the health of reefs is particularly strong in Southeast Asia, where 80% of reefs are endangered.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In Australia, the Great Barrier Reef is protected by the Great Barrier Reef Marine Park Authority and is the subject of much legislation, including a biodiversity action plan. Inhabitants of Ahus Island, Manus Province, Papua New Guinea, have followed a generations-old practice of restricting fishing in six areas of their reef lagoon. Their cultural traditions allow line fishing, but not net or spearfishing. The result is both the biomass and individual fish sizes are significantly larger in these areas than in places where fishing is unrestricted.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8908&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8909","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 The Persuaders","book":"阅读还原集Vol.18","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.18 · Test 4 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8909:64396:27","type":"choice","text":"What is the supermarket’s purpose of using ‘basket’ in paragraph B?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For example, when Sainsbury introduced shopping baskets into its 1950s stores, it was a stroke of marketing genius. Now shoppers could browse and pick up items they previously would have ignored.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问，B段提到的，让顾客在超市使用“购物篮”的目的是什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“basket”和“supermarket’s purpose”定位到B段。\n解题思路：原文提到Sainsbury引入购物篮后，顾客由此能浏览并选购以往可能忽略的商品。随后出现了手推车，可以推断购物篮和手推车都是为了增加顾客的停留时间，从而增加购买量。因此，超市使用购物篮的目的是让顾客花费更多时间购物，对应选项B。","options":["Create a convenient atmosphere of supermarket","Make customers spend more time on shopping","Relieve pressure on the supermarket’s traffic","More than half items bought need to be carried"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64396","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-29 on your answer sheet."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8909:64397:28","type":"choice","text":"What is the quality of the best salesman possessed according to this passage?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Probably all of us could make a sale if the product was something we truly believed in, but professional salespeople are in a different league – the best of them can always sell different items to suitable customers in the best time.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是根据文章内容，最优秀的销售人员具备什么素质。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"the best salesman\"可以定位到文章的H段，该段描述了专业销售人员如何通过基本的心理技巧来销售产品。\n解题思路：根据H段中的原文句子，专业销售人员的水平可就高出一筹——顶尖的销售高手总能在最佳时机，向合适的客户推销最合适的产品。因此，选项A\"将合适的产品销售给合适的人\"最符合原文描述，是正确答案。其他选项B、C、D虽然也是销售人员可能具备的素质，但文章并未明确提到这些是最好销售人员的关键素质。","options":["Sell the right product to the right person","Clearly state the instruction of one product","Show professional background of one product","Persuade customers to buy the product they sell"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64397","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-29 on your answer sheet."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8909:64398:29","type":"choice","text":"What’s the opinion of Richard Hession?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Richard Hession, author of Be a Great Salesperson says it is human nature to prefer to speak rather listen, and good salespeople pander to this. They ask punters about their needs and offer to work with them to achieve their objectives.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是Richard Hession的观点是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Richard Hession\"定位到文章中的I段，该段详细描述了他的观点。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子，理查德·赫西恩指出，人类天性更倾向于主动表达而非被动倾听，优秀销售员深谙此道。他们会主动询问客户需求，并提供合作方案助力达成目标。这使得顾客感觉他们正在接受咨询而不是销售。这与选项D“展示出色的人际交往能力”相符，因为询问需求、共同合作以及假设销售成功都是人际交往技巧的体现。因此，正确答案是D。","options":["Pretend to be nice instead of selling goods","Prefer to speak a lot to customers","Help buyers to conclude their demands for ideal items","Show great interpersonal skill"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64398","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-29 on your answer sheet."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8909:64399:30","type":"choice","text":"30 how do supermarkets distract consumers","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Stone believes supermarkets work hard to ‘stall’ us because the more time we spend in them, the more we buy.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问哪一段提到了，超市分散消费者注意力的方法。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"supermarkets\"和\"distract consumers\"在文章中定位。\n解题思路：原文提到，斯通认为，超市竭力“拖延”我们的消费决策，因为我们在其中停留的时间越长，购买量就越大。\"stall\"与题目中的\"distract\"意思相近，都是指分散注意力的行为。后面详细描述了超市通过延长顾客停留时间来增加销售的各种方法，如播放音乐、散播香味等，因此，答案为C。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J","Section K"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"64399","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 30-35\nThe passage has eleven paragraphs A-K which paragraph contains the following information? Write your answers in boxes 30-35 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8909:64399:31","type":"choice","text":"31 how to build a close relationship between salespeople and buyer","answer":"J","acceptedAnswers":["J"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Dr Rob Yeung, a senior consultant at business psychologists Kiddy and Partner, says most salespeople will build up a level of rapport by asking questions about hobbies, family and lifestyle.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了“如何建立销售人员和买家之间的密切关系”。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“build a close relationship”可以定位到J段中“build up a level of rapport”这一表述，因为“rapport”意为“融洽关系”，与题目中的“close relationship”对应。\n解题思路：原文J段明确提到，销售顾问Dr. Rob Yeung指出，大多数销售人员会通过询问爱好、家庭和生活习惯来于客户建立融洽关系（build up a level of rapport），后面具体描述这样做的好处，和具体做法。这与题目要求的一致。因此，J段是正确答案。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J","Section K"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"64399","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 30-35\nThe passage has eleven paragraphs A-K which paragraph contains the following information? Write your answers in boxes 30-35 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8909:64399:32","type":"choice","text":"32 people would be impressed by the humor advertisement","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Humor also stimulates a rapid emotional response. Heiman Chung, writing in the International Journal of Advertising, found that funny ads were remembered for longer than straight ones.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了，幽默广告会给人们留下深刻印象。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“humor advertisement %”，通过这个关键词可以在文章中定位到F段，该段提到了关于广告中幽默效果的研究。\n解题思路：在F段中，原文提到，幽默元素还能引发即时情感共鸣。《国际广告学刊》学者何曼·钟研究发现，幽默广告比直白广告更易被记忆。因此，根据原文信息，可以确定F段提到了这一信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J","Section K"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"64399","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 30-35\nThe passage has eleven paragraphs A-K which paragraph contains the following information? Write your answers in boxes 30-35 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8909:64399:33","type":"choice","text":"33 methods for salespeople to get the order","answer":"K","acceptedAnswers":["K"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Whatever the method used, all salespeople work towards one aim: ‘closing the deal’. In fact, they will be looking for ‘closing signals’ through their dealings with potential clients.\n对应段落：K段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了销售人员如何获得订单的方法。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键词\"methods for salespeople to get the order\"定位到文章中描述销售人员如何获得订单的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文中K段的描述，无论采用何种方式，所有销售人员都以达成交易为最终目标。实际上，他们会通过与潜在客户的互动寻找成交信号。后面讲述具体操作方法，因此，可以确定K段提到了这一信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J","Section K"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"64399","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 30-35\nThe passage has eleven paragraphs A-K which paragraph contains the following information? Write your answers in boxes 30-35 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8909:64399:34","type":"choice","text":"34 how question work for salespeople","answer":"K","acceptedAnswers":["K"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The buyer is not asked ‘are you interested?’ as this can invite a negative response. Instead, the seller takes it for granted that the deal is effectively done: when the salesman asks you for a convenient delivery date or asks what color you want, you will probably respond accordingly.\n对应段落：K段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了，销售人员运用提问技巧的方法。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"question\"和\"salespeople\"定位到K段，该段描述了销售人员如何通过提问来促成交易。\n解题思路：原文中K段明确提到，销售不会主动询问“您感兴趣吗？”，因为这可能引发对方的抵触情绪。相反，他们默认交易已基本完成：当销售人员询问方便的交货日期或您想要什么颜色时，您很可能会立即回应。这一策略展示了销售人员如何通过提问技巧来推动销售过程。因此，可以确定K段提到了这一信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J","Section K"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"64399","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 30-35\nThe passage has eleven paragraphs A-K which paragraph contains the following information? Write your answers in boxes 30-35 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8909:64399:35","type":"choice","text":"35 different customer groups bring different profits","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Research has shown that 75 percent of profit comes from just 30 percent of customers.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了，不同客户群体带来不同利润。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"different customer groups\"和\"profits\"定位到文章中关于客户群体和利润的内容。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句，研究显示75%的利润来自于30%的客户，可以推断，不同的客户群体，带来的利润不同，因此，D段提到了这一信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J","Section K"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"64399","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 30-35\nThe passage has eleven paragraphs A-K which paragraph contains the following information? Write your answers in boxes 30-35 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8909:64400:36","type":"fill","text":"填写第 36 空","answer":"aisles/Aisles","acceptedAnswers":["aisles","Aisles"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Pro Merlin Stone, IBM Professor of Relationship Marketing at Bristol Business School, says aisles are laid out to maximize profits.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是超市中为了增加利润，加宽了什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"supermarkets\"和\"generate the most profits\"来定位答案。\n解题思路：在C段中，提到了\"aisles are laid out to maximize profits\"，即超市的通道布局是为了最大化利润。因此，可以确定答案是\"aisles\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64400","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the notes below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8909:64401:37","type":"fill","text":"填写第 37 空","answer":"experiments/Experiments","acceptedAnswers":["experiments","Experiments"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In experiments, pleasant smells are effective in increasing our spending.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是什么研究证明香气能够让人们买更多商品。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"Research\"和\"experiments\"可以定位到C段中。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，实验表明，愉悦的香气能有效提升消费金额。说明该研究是基于实验的。因此答案为\"Experiments\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64401","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the notes below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8909:64402:38","type":"fill","text":"填写第 38 空","answer":"loyalty card/Loyalty Card","acceptedAnswers":["loyalty card","Loyalty Card"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The other success story from the supermarkets’ perspective is the loyalty card. Punters may assume that they are being rewarded for their fidelity, but all the while they are trading information about their shopping habits.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问除了创造舒适环境外，超市还利用什么来奖励老顾客。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"reward their regular customers\"和\"supermarkets\"定位到C段后半部分，找到\"loyalty card\"的相关描述。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，从超市视角看，会员卡堪称成功案例——顾客以为是在奖励忠诚度，实则是在交换购物习惯数据。因此答案为\"loyalty card\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64402","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the notes below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8909:64403:39","type":"fill","text":"填写第 39 空","answer":"cosmetics/Cosmetics","acceptedAnswers":["cosmetics","Cosmetics"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Loyal shoppers could be paying 30% more by sticking to their favourite shops for essential cosmetics.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是忠诚客户在钟爱的商店购买什么商品时会多花费30%。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"30% more\"和\"essential\"定位到C段倒数第一句。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，那些忠实顾客坚持在常去的美妆店消费，实际支出可能比普通顾客高出30%。因此答案为cosmetics（化妆品）。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64403","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the notes below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8909:64404:40","type":"fill","text":"填写第 40 空","answer":"group/Group","acceptedAnswers":["group","Group"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Advertisers play on our need to be safe (commercials for insurance), to belong (make a customer feel they are in the group in fashion ads) and for self-esteem (aspirational adverts).\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是服装店广告利用归属感，让人们感觉自己属于什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"belonging\"和\"humor advertisement\"定位到F段中利用归属感来打广告的描述。\n解题思路：F段提到，广告商巧妙利用人类对安全（保险广告）、归属感（时尚广告让顾客感觉他们属于某个群体）和自尊（励志广告）的深层需求，因此，\"group\"是正确答案。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64404","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the notes below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64396","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-29 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is the supermarket’s purpose of using ‘basket’ in paragraph B?</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"64397","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-29 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is the quality of the best salesman possessed according to this passage?</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"64398","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-29 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What’s the opinion of Richard Hession?</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"64399","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 30-35\nThe passage has eleven paragraphs A-K which paragraph contains the following information? Write your answers in boxes 30-35 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.","html":"<p><strong>30</strong> how do supermarkets distract consumers <strong class=\"source-blank\">[30] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"64400","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the notes below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Trolleys are born for the increasing traffic in the supermarket. The width of&nbsp;<strong>36</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[36] ____</strong> in\nsupermarkets is broadened in order to generate the most profits.</p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"64401","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the notes below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Research from <strong>37</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[37] ____</strong> , satisfying aromas can motivate people to buy more products.&nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"64402","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the notes below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Except for the effort of creating a comfortable surrounding, <strong>38</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[38] ____</strong> is another card that supermarkets play to reward their regular customers.</p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"64403","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the notes below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>For example, loyal customers spend 30% more in their loved shops for everyday necessary <strong>39</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[39] ____</strong>.&nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"64404","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the notes below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Clothes shops use advertisements to make the buyer think they are belonging to part of a <strong>40</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[40] ____</strong> ; research from 4,000 campaigns reflect that humor advertisement received more emotional respect.</p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The Persuaders&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>We have long lived in an age where powerful images, catchy soundbites and too-good-to miss offers to bombard us from every quarter. All around us the persuaders are at work. Occasionally their methods are unsubtle – the planting kiss on a baby’s head by a wannabe political leader, or a liquidation sale in a shop that has been ‘closing down’ for well over a year, but generally the persuaders know what they are about and are highly capable. Be they politicians, supermarket chains, salespeople or advertisers, they know exactly what to do to sell us their images, ideas or produce. When it comes to persuasion, these giants rule supreme. They employ the most skilled image-makers and use the best psychological tricks to guarantee that even the most cautious among us are open to manipulation.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>We spend more time in them than we mean to, we buy 75 percent of our food from them and end up with products that we did not realize we wanted. Right from the start, supermarkets have been ahead of the game. For example, when Sainsbury introduced shopping baskets into its 1950s stores, it was a stroke of marketing genius. Now shoppers could browse and pick up items they previously would have ignored. Soon after came trolleys, and just as new roads attract more traffic, the same applied to trolley space. Pro Merlin Stone, IBM Professor of Relationship Marketing at Bristol Business School, says aisles are laid out to maximize profits. Stores pander to our money-rich, time-poor lifestyle. Low turnover products – clothes and electrical goods – are stocked at the back while high-turnover items command position at the front.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Stone believes supermarkets work hard to ‘stall’ us because the more time we spend in them, the more we buy. Thus, great efforts are made to make the environment pleasant. Stores play music to relax us and some even pipe air from the in-store bakery around the shop. In the USA, fake aromas are sometimes used. The smell is both the most evocative and subliminal sense. In experiments, pleasant smells are effective in increasing our spending. A casino that fragranced only half its premise saw profit soar in the aroma-filled areas. The other success story from the supermarkets’ perspective is the loyalty card. Punters may assume that they are being rewarded for their fidelity, but all the while they are trading information about their shopping habits. Loyal shoppers could be paying 30% more by sticking to their favourite shops for essential cosmetics.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Research has shown that 75 percent of profit comes from just 30 percent of customers. Ultimately, reward cards could be used to identify and better accommodate these ‘elite’ shoppers. It could also be used to make adverts more relevant to individual consumers – rather like Spielberg’s futuristic thriller Minority Report, in which Tom Cruise’s character is bombarded with interactive personalized ads. If this sounds far-fetched, the data-gathering revolution has already seen the introduction of radio – frequency identification – away to electronically tag products to see who is buying what, FRID means they can follow the product into people homes.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>No matter how savvy we think we are to their ploys, the ad industry still wins. Adverts focus on what products do or on how they make us feel. Researcher Laurette Dube, in the Journal of Advertising Research, says when attitudes are base on ‘cognitive foundations’ (logical reasoning), advertisers use informative appeals. This works for products with a little emotional draw but high functionality, such as bleach. Where attitude is based on effect (i.e, emotions), ad teams try to tap into our feelings. Researchers at the University of Florida recently concluded that our emotional responses to adverts dominate over ‘cognition’.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Advertisers play on our need to be safe (commercials for insurance), to belong (make a customer feel they are in the group in fashion ads) and for self-esteem (aspirational adverts). With time and space at a premium, celebrities are often used as a quick way of meeting these needs – either because the celeb epitomizes success or because they seem familiar and so make the product seem ‘safe’. A survey of 4,000 campaigns found ads with celebs were 10 percent more effective than without. Humor also stimulates a rapid emotional response. Heiman Chung, writing in the International Journal of Advertising, found that funny ads were remembered for longer than straight ones. Combine humor with sexual imagery – as in Wonderbra’s ‘Hello Boys’ ads – turnover and you are on to a winner.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Slice-of-life ads are another tried and tested method – they paint a picture of life as you would like it, but still, one that feels familiar. Abhilasha Mehta, in the Journal of Advertising Research, noted that the more one’s self-image tallies with the brand being advertised, the stronger the commercial. Ad makers also use behaviorist theories, recognizing that the more sensation we receive from an object, the better we know it. If an advert for a chocolate bar fails to cause salivation, it has probably failed. No wonder advertisements have been dubbed the ‘nervous system of the business world’.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Probably all of us could make a sale if the product was something we truly believed in, but professional salespeople are in a different league – the best of them can always sell different items to suitable customers in the best time. They do this by using very basic psychological techniques. Stripped to its simplest level, selling works by heightening the buyer’s perception of how much they need a product or service. Buyers normally have certain requirements by which they will judge the suitability of a product. The seller, therefore, attempts to tease out what these conditions are and then explains how their products’ benefit can meet these requirements.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Richard Hession, author of Be a Great Salesperson says it is human nature to prefer to speak rather listen, and good salespeople pander to this. They ask punters about their needs and offer to work with them to achieve their objectives. As a result, the buyer feels they are receiving a ‘consultation’ rather than a sales pitch. All the while, the salesperson presents with a demeanour that takes it for granted that the sale will be made. Never will the words ‘if you buy’ be used, but rather ‘when you buy’.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Dr Rob Yeung, a senior consultant at business psychologists Kiddy and Partner, says most salespeople will build up a level of rapport by asking questions about hobbies, family and lifestyle. This has the double benefit of making the salesperson likeable while furnishing him or her with more information about the client’s wants. Yeung says effective salespeople try as far as possible to match their style of presenting themselves to how the buyer comes across. If the buyer cracks jokes, the salespeople will respond in kind. If the buyer wants detail, the seller provides it, if they are more interested in the feel of the product, the seller will focus on this. At its most extreme, appearing empathetic can even include the salesperson attempting to ‘mirror’ the hobby language of the buyer.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>K&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Whatever the method used, all salespeople work towards one aim: ‘closing the deal’. In fact, they will be looking for ‘closing signals’ through their dealings with potential clients. Once again the process works by assuming success. The buyer is not asked ‘are you interested?’ as this can invite a negative response. Instead, the seller takes it for granted that the deal is effectively done: when the salesman asks you for a convenient delivery date or asks what color you want, you will probably respond accordingly. Only afterwards might you wonder why you proved such a pushover.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8909&scene=%E8%B4%A2%E7%BB%8F%E5%95%86%E4%B8%9A&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8904","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Making Copier","book":"阅读还原集Vol.18","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.18 · Test 3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8904:64357:1","type":"choice","text":"The earliest languages were recorded on papyrus.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：When the Sumerians transposed spoken words into stylus marks on clay tablets more than 5,000 years ago, the hugely extended the human network that language had created.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问“最早的文字记录在莎草纸上”，需要判断这一说法是否与原文信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“earliest languages”和“papyrus”定位到A段第一句，原文提到“language”是最早的复制工具，但并未提及“papyrus”。\n解题思路：原文A段提到，五千多年前，苏美尔人将口语文字转写为泥板上的楔形文字时，语言所构建的人际网络得到了极大扩展。说明最早的文字是记录在泥板上的，因此题目中的说法与原文信息不符，应选择False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64357","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8904:64358:2","type":"choice","text":"When applying johann gutenberg's printing machine, it requires lots of training.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Until Johann Gutenberg invented the printing press in the mid-1400s, producing a book in an edition of more than one generally meant writing it out again. Printing with moveable type was not copying, however. Gutenberg couldn’t take a document that already existed, feed it into his printing press and run off facsimiles.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“使用约翰·古腾堡的印刷机需要大量的培训”，需要判断这一说法是否与原文信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“Johann Gutenberg’s printing machine”定位到B段，找到关于古腾堡印刷机的描述。\n解题思路：原文中提到古腾堡的印刷机不能直接复制已有的文件，需要手动操作。但并未提及使用前需要如何培训的内容。因此，题目中的信息在原文中没有明确的支持或否定，所以答案是Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64358","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8904:64359:3","type":"choice","text":"James Watt invented a modern steam engine before he made his first mechanical copier.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The first true mechanical copier was manufactured in 1780, when James Watt, who is better known as the inventor of the modern steam engine, created the copying press.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是James Watt在制造第一台机械复印机之前发明了现代蒸汽机，需要判断这一说法是否与原文信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"James Watt\"和\"modern steam engine\"定位到B段中\"James Watt, who is better known as the inventor of the modern steam engine\"这一句。\n解题思路：原文提到，第一台真正的机械复印机诞生于1780年，当时詹姆斯·瓦特——这位现在以发明现代蒸汽机而闻名于世的发明家——发明了复印机。但并未说明他发明现代蒸汽机的时间是在制造第一台机械复印机之前还是之后。因此，题目中的信息在原文中没有明确说明，故答案为Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64359","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8904:64360:4","type":"choice","text":"Using the Dupliton copiers and follower versions are very costly.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：These machines and their successors were welcomed by secretaries, who had no other means of reproducing documents in hand, but each had serious drawbacks. All required expensive chemically treated papers.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是使用杜普莱顿复印机和后续版本非常昂贵，需要判断这一说法是否与原文信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\" Dupliton copiers and follower versions\"定位到C段，该段提到了Dupliton等复印机及其后续版本。\n解题思路：根据原文答案对应的句子，这些设备及其后续产品深受秘书们的欢迎——毕竟当时她们没有其他方式能手抄文件，但每款机器都存在明显缺陷：都需要使用昂贵的化学处理纸张，可知，所有这些复印机都需要昂贵的化学处理纸，因此使用这些复印机确实非常昂贵，所以答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64360","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8904:64361:5","type":"choice","text":"The typewriters with carbon papers were taken place of very soon because they were not sold well.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：None of those machines is still manufactured today. They were all made obsolete by a radically different machine, which had been developed by an obscure photographic-supply company.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问“打字机和复写纸很快被取代是因为它们卖得不好”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的“typewriters with carbon papers”和“taken place of very soon”可以定位到D段提到这些设备的后续。\n解题思路：文中指出typewriter and carbon paper是standard equipmente（标准设备），且存活了一个半世纪，如此一来，就不可能因卖的不好而很快淘汰。其次，根据D段首句的原文可知，它确实己经被取代了。因此，题干前半部分是对的，但后半部分与原文不符，所以答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64361","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8904:64362:6","type":"choice","text":"The Haloid Xerox 914 model also required specially treated paper for making copies.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1959, it introduced an office copier called the Haloid Xerox 914, a machine that, unlike its numerous competitors, made sharp, permanent copies on ordinary paper-a huge breakthrough.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是关于Haloid Xerox 914型号也需要特殊处理的纸张来复印，这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"the Haloid Xerox 914 model\"和\"required specially treated paper\"来定位答案。\n解题思路：根据D段原文中的句子，Haloid Xerox 914型号与竞争对手不同，它可以在普通纸上制作清晰、持久的复印件。这意味着它不需要特殊处理的纸张，因此题目中的说法与原文信息相矛盾，所以答案是False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64362","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8904:64363:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"normal inventor/inventor/Normal Inventor/Inventor","acceptedAnswers":["normal inventor","inventor","Normal Inventor","Inventor"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Compare with competitors, Carlson was not a normal inventor in 20-century.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问卡尔森与20世纪的发明家有什么不同。\n定位关键信息： 根据\"unlike a 20-century\"和\"like to work on his own\"定位至E段关于Carlson作为发明家特点的描述。\n解题思路：根据原文E段，与20世纪的普通发明家相比，卡尔森可谓特立独行。紧接着说明\"He made his discovery in solitude\"（他独自完成发明），这正好对应题目中的\"like to work on his own\"。因此，答案为normal inventor。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64363","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-13\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8904:64364:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"corporations/Corporations","acceptedAnswers":["corporations","Corporations"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He invited 20 major corporations to make his discovery. However, this action was not welcome.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目询问，1973年，他曾邀请20家大型什么制造他的发明，但未能成功。\n定位关键信息：根据\"20 major\"和\"make his discovery\"定位至E段中Carlson推广发明的具体描述。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，1937年他独自完成发明后，向包括IBM、通用电气、伊士曼柯达和RCA在内的20多家大公司抛出橄榄枝，却全数遭到拒绝。因此答案为“corporations”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64364","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-13\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8904:64365:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"turned him down/Turned Him Down","acceptedAnswers":["turned him down","Turned Him Down"],"explanation":"原文答案句：All of them turned him down, expressing what he later called ‘an enthusiastic lack of interest’ and thereby passing up the opportunity to manufacture what Fortune magazine would describe as ‘the most successful product ever marketed in America’.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问，然而，这一举措起初并未获得股东们的欢迎，所有的公司都做出怎样的回应。\n定位关键信息： 根据\"all of them\"和\"not welcome among shareholders\"定位至E段中公司回应的描述。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，然而这些企业都以“热情不足”为由拒绝了他。 说明所有公司都拒绝了 Calson 的提议。因此，答案为\"turned him down\" 。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64365","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-13\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8904:64366:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"commercial triumph/Commercial Triumph","acceptedAnswers":["commercial triumph","Commercial Triumph"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Carlson’s invention was indeed a commercial triumph.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问，最终证明，卡尔森的发明无疑是一个什么。\n定位关键信息：根据\"creation was undeniably a\"定位至F段开头的评价性陈述。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，卡尔森的发明堪称商业奇迹。因此答案为\"commercial triumph\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64366","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-13\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8904:64367:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"wealthy/Wealthy","acceptedAnswers":["wealthy","Wealthy"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Xerography eventually made Carlson a very wealthy man. (His royalties amounted to something like a 16th of a cent for every Xerox copy made, worldwide, through 1965.)\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问，多亏了静电复印术的发明，卡尔森成为了一个什么样的人。\n定位关键信息： 根据\"became a very\"和\"person\"定位至G段开头关于Carlson财富状况的描述。\n解题思路：原文G段首句明确说明\"Xerography eventually made Carlson a very wealthy man\"静电复印术最终让卡尔森变得非常富有，括号中还具体说明了他的版税收入情况。因此答案为“wealthy”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64367","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-13\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8904:64368:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"possessions/Possessions","acceptedAnswers":["possessions","Possessions"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘His possessions seemed to be composed of the number of things he could easily do without,’ his second wife said.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问，即便如此，他的生活依然和从前一样简单，Carlson看起来可以没有什么东西也能生活。\n定位关键信息：根据\"live without his\"定位至G段中关于Carlson简朴生活的具体描述。\n解题思路：原文提到，他的第二任妻子说道，他似乎可以轻易抛弃他的财产，因此答案为\"possessions\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64368","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-13\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8904:64369:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"charities/Charities","acceptedAnswers":["charities","Charities"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He spent the last years of his life quietly giving most of his fortune to charities.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是他同时把钱给了什么组织。\n定位关键信息：根据\"gave lots of his money to\"定位至G段末尾关于Carlson慈善行为的描述。\n解题思路：原文明确提到他把大笔钱捐给了\"charities\"，与题干中的\"lots of his money\"对应，因此答案为\"charities\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64369","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-13\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64357","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The earliest languages were recorded on papyrus.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"64358","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>When applying johann gutenberg&#39;s printing machine, it requires lots of training.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"64359","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>James Watt invented a modern steam engine before he made his first mechanical copier.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"64360","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Using the Dupliton copiers and follower versions are very costly.</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"64361","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The typewriters with carbon papers were taken place of very soon because they were not sold well.</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"64362","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The Haloid Xerox 914 model also required specially treated paper for making copies.</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"64363","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-13\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Calson, unlike a 20-century <strong>7</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong> , like to work on his own. In 1937, he unsuccessfully <br/></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"64364","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-13\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>invited 20 major&nbsp;<strong>8</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong> to make his discovery. However, this action was not welcome</p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"64365","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-13\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>among shareholders at the beginning, all of them <strong>9</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong> . Eventually, Calson’s creation</p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"64366","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-13\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>was undeniably a <strong>10</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong> . Thanks for the discovery of Xerography, Calson became a very</p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"64367","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-13\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>11</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong> person. Even so, his life remains as simple as before. It looks as if he can live</p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"64368","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-13\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>without his <strong>12</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"64369","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-13\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>At the same time, he gave lots of his money to <strong>13</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Making Copier</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>At first, nobody bought Chester Carlson’s strange idea. But trillions of documents later, his invention is the biggest thing in printing since Gutenberg</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Copying is the engine of civilization: culture is behavior duplicated. The oldest copier invented by people is language, by which an idea of yours becomes an idea of mine. The second great copying machine was writing. When the Sumerians transposed spoken words into stylus marks on clay tablets more than 5,000 years ago, the hugely extended the human network that language had created. Writing freed copying from the chain of living contact. It made ideas permanent, portable and endlessly reproducible.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Until Johann Gutenberg invented the printing press in the mid-1400s, producing a book in an edition of more than one generally meant writing it out again. Printing with moveable type was not copying, however. Gutenberg couldn’t take a document that already existed, feed it into his printing press and run off facsimiles. The first true mechanical copier was manufactured in 1780, when James Watt, who is better known as the inventor of the modern steam engine, created the copying press. Few people today know what a copying press was, but you may have seen one in an antique store, where it was perhaps called a book press. A user took a document freshly written in special ink, placed a moistened sheet of translucent paper against the inked surface and squeezed the two sheets together in the press, causing some of the ink from the original to penetrate the second sheet, which could then be read by turning it over and looking through its back. The high cost prohibits the widespread use of this copier.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Among the first modem copying machines, introduced in 1950 by 3M, was the Thermo-Fax, and it made a copy by shining infrared light through an original document and a sheet of paper that had been coated with heat-sensitive chemicals. Competing manufacturers soon introduced other copying technologies and marketed machines called Dupliton, Dial-A-Matic Autostat, Verifax, Copease and Copymation. These machines and their successors were welcomed by secretaries, who had no other means of reproducing documents in hand, but each had serious drawbacks. All required expensive chemically treated papers. And all made copies that smelled bad, were hard to read, didn’t last long and tended to curl up into tubes. The machines were displaced, beginning in the late 1800s, by a combination of two 19th century inventions: the typewriter and carbon paper For those reasons, copying presses were standard equipment in offices for nearly a century and a half.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>None of those machines is still manufactured today. They were all made obsolete by a radically different machine, which had been developed by an obscure photographic-supply company. That company had been founded in 1906 as the Haloid Company and is known today as the Xerox Corporation. In 1959, it introduced an office copier called the Haloid Xerox 914, a machine that, unlike its numerous competitors, made sharp, permanent copies on ordinary paper-a huge breakthrough. The process, which Haloid called xerography (based on Greek words meaning ‘dry’ and ‘writing’), was so unusual and nonnutritive that physicists who visited the drafty warehouses where the first machines were built sometimes expressed doubt that it was even theoretically feasible.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Remarkably, xerography was conceived by one person – Chester Carlson, a shy, soft-spoken patent attorney, who grew up in almost unspeakable poverty and worked his way through junior college and the California Institute of Technology. Chester Carlson was born in Seattle in 1906. His parents – Olof Adolph Carlson and Ellen Josephine Hawkins – had grown up on neighboring farms in Grove City, Minnesota, a tiny Swedish farming community about 75 miles west of Minneapolis. Compare with competitors, Carlson was not a normal inventor in 20-century. He made his discovery in solitude in 1937 and offered it to more than 20 major corporations, among them IBM, General Electric, Eastman Kodak and RCA. All of them turned him down, expressing what he later called ‘an enthusiastic lack of interest’ and thereby passing up the opportunity to manufacture what Fortune magazine would describe as ‘the most successful product ever marketed in America’.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Carlson’s invention was indeed a commercial triumph. Essentially overnight, people began making copies at a rate that was orders of magnitude higher than anyone had believed possible. And the rate is still growing. In fact, most documents handled by a typical American office worker today are produced xerographically, either on copiers manufactured by Xerox and its competitors or on laser printers, which employ the same process (and were invented, in the 1970s, by a Xerox researcher). This year, the world will produce more than three trillion xerographic copies and laser-printed pages – about 500 for every human on earth.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Xerography eventually made Carlson a very wealthy man. (His royalties amounted to something like a 16th of a cent for every Xerox copy made, worldwide, through 1965.) Nevertheless, he lived simply. He never owned a second home or a second car, and his wife had to urge him not to buy third-class train tickets when he traveled in Europe. People who knew him casually seldom suspected that he was rich or even well-to-do; when Carlson told an acquaintance he worked at Xerox, the man assumed he was a factory worker and asked if he belonged to a union. ‘His possessions seemed to be composed of the number of things he could easily do without,’ his second wife said. He spent the last years of his life quietly giving most of his fortune to charities. When he died in 1968, among the eulogizers was the secretary-general of the United Nations.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8904&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8905","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Saving the British Bitterns","book":"阅读还原集Vol.18","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.18 · Test 3 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8905:64370:14","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Breeding bitterns became extinct in the UK by 1886 but, following re-colonisation early last century, numbers rose to a peak of about 70 booming (singing) males in the 1950s, falling to fewer than 20 by the 1990s.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求为A段选择一个合适的标题，概括该段的主要内容。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读A段，可以看到该段主要描述了麻鸦在英国的数量变化，从灭绝到数量的高峰再到减少。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句可以看出，英国的繁殖型比特纳鸟于1886年灭绝，但在上世纪初重新定居后，其数量于1950年代达到约70只繁殖期（鸣唱期）雄鸟的峰值，至1990年代降至不足20只。A段主要讲述了麻鸦在英国的数量波动情况，因此，标题\"fluctuation in bittern number\"（麻鸦数量的波动）能够准确概括A段的主要内容。","options":["research findings into habitats and decisions made","fluctuation in bittern number","protect the young bittern","international cooperation works","began in calculation of the number","importance of food","research has been successful","research into the reedbed","reserve established holding bittern in winter"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64370","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-H Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-H from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8905:64370:15","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Our first challenge was to develop standard methods to monitor their numbers. The boom of the male bittern is its most distinctive feature during the breeding season, and we developed a method to count them using the sound patterns unique to each individual.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求为B段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读B段内容，可以看到该段主要描述了研究人员开展麻鸦保护行动的第一步，监测它们的数量。\n解题思路：B段提到，由于麻鸦的习性，首要任务是建立标准化监测方法，计算它们的数量，后面详细描述具体方法。因此，标题\"began in calculation of the number\"（开始计算数量）能够准确概括B段的主要内容。","options":["research findings into habitats and decisions made","fluctuation in bittern number","protect the young bittern","international cooperation works","began in calculation of the number","importance of food","research has been successful","research into the reedbed","reserve established holding bittern in winter"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64370","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-H Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-H from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8905:64370:16","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Our first direct understanding of the habitat needs of breeding bitterns came from comparisons of reedbed sites that had lost their booming birds with those that retained them. This research showed that bitterns had been retained in reedbeds where the natural process of succession, or drying out, had been slowed through management. Based on this work, broad recommendations on how to manage and rehabilitate reedbeds for bitterns were made, and funding was provided through the EU LIFE Fund to manage 13 sites within the core breeding range. This project, though led by the RSPB, involved many other organisations.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求为C段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读C段内容，可以看到该段主要描述了研究人员研究栖息地对麻鸦繁殖的影响。\n解题思路：C段主要讲述了研究人员通过比较芦苇地，发现，在通过管理延缓自然演替过程（干涸）的芦苇地中，麻鸦得以存活。提出了关于如何管理和修复麻鸦芦苇床的建议。因此，标题\"research findings into habitats and decisions made\"能够准确概括C段的主要内容。","options":["research findings into habitats and decisions made","fluctuation in bittern number","protect the young bittern","international cooperation works","began in calculation of the number","importance of food","research has been successful","research into the reedbed","reserve established holding bittern in winter"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64370","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-H Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-H from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8905:64370:17","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：To refine these recommendations and provide fine-scale, quantitative habitat prescriptions on the bitterns’ preferred feeding habitat, we radio-tracked male bitterns on the RSPB’s Minsmere and Leighton Moss reserves.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求为D段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：根据D段的首句，可以定位到该段的主要内容是关于通过无线电研究麻鸦喜欢的芦苇地。\n解题思路：D段主要讲述了研究人员通过无线电追踪雄性麻鸦来研究它们喜欢的觅食芦苇地，并研究雌性麻鸦更倾向于在什么样的芦苇地筑巢。根据这一内容，可以判断该段的主题是关于麻鸦的栖息地研究。因此，标题\"research into the reedbed\"（芦苇地研究）能够准确概括D段的主要内容。","options":["research findings into habitats and decisions made","fluctuation in bittern number","protect the young bittern","international cooperation works","began in calculation of the number","importance of food","research has been successful","research into the reedbed","reserve established holding bittern in winter"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64370","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-H Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-H from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8905:64370:18","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Many chicks did not survive to fledging and starvation was found to be the most likely reason for their demise. The fish prey fed to chicks was dominated by those species penetrating into the reed edge. So, an important element of recent studies (including a PhD with the University of Hull) has been the development of recommendations on habitat and water conditions to promote healthy native fish populations.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求为F段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读F段，可以发现段落主要讨论的是对麻鸦幼鸟的研究。\n解题思路：F段提到，研究发现，许多雏鸟未能存活至离巢期，而饥饿是导致其死亡的主要原因。这些幼鸟的主要食物来源是那些深入芦苇边缘的鱼类。再提出关于栖息地和水质条件的建议，促进本土鱼类种群的健康繁衍。综合这些信息，可以确定F段的主题是关于麻鸦幼鸟的生存和食物的研究，因此，标题\"importance of food\"（食物的重要性）能够准确概括F段的主要内容。","options":["research findings into habitats and decisions made","fluctuation in bittern number","protect the young bittern","international cooperation works","began in calculation of the number","importance of food","research has been successful","research into the reedbed","reserve established holding bittern in winter"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64370","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-H Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-H from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8905:64370:19","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph F","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A second EU LIFE funded project aims to provide these suitable sites in new areas. A network of 19 sites developed through this partnership project will secure a more sustainable UK bittern population with successful breeding outside of the core area, less vulnerable to chance events and sea-level rise.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求为G段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读G段，可以定位到关键信息是麻鸦在独立后会寻找新的栖息地，如果条件适宜，会在新地点繁殖。同时提到了一个欧盟LIFE资助的项目。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句和定位的关键信息，可以确定G段的首先介绍麻鸦的迁徙和繁殖，再提到相关项目的实施，旨在为它们提供适宜的栖息地，确保它们的可持续发展。因此，标题\"protect the young bittern\"（保护年幼的麻鸦）能够准确概括G段的主要内容。","options":["research findings into habitats and decisions made","fluctuation in bittern number","protect the young bittern","international cooperation works","began in calculation of the number","importance of food","research has been successful","research into the reedbed","reserve established holding bittern in winter"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64370","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-H Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-H from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8905:64370:20","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph G","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Although science has been at the core of the bittern story, success has only been achieved through the trust, hard work and dedication of all the managers, owners and wardens of sites that have implemented, in some cases very drastic, management to secure the future of this wetland species in the UK.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目要求为H段选择一个正确的标题，概括该段落的主要内容。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读H段，可以发现段落主要讨论的是对项目实施的成果，强调是通过多方合作的结果。\n解题思路：段落H的核心内容在强调麻鸦保护的成功不仅依赖于科学研究，更关键的是通过“所有场地的管理者、所有者和看守人”的“信任、努力和奉献”才得以实现。这明确指出了不同群体间的协作是成功的基石。此外，前文提到过该项目由英国皇家鸟类保护协会（RSPB）主导，但还涉及众多其他组织，例如，欧盟LIFE基金提供了管理资金。因此，标题\"international cooperation works\"（国际合作发挥作用）能够准确概括H段的主要内容。","options":["research findings into habitats and decisions made","fluctuation in bittern number","protect the young bittern","international cooperation works","began in calculation of the number","importance of food","research has been successful","research into the reedbed","reserve established holding bittern in winter"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64370","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-H Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-H from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8905:64371:21","type":"fill","text":"填写第 21 空","answer":"1950s","acceptedAnswers":["1950s"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Breeding bitterns became extinct in the UK by 1886 but, following re-colonisation early last century, numbers rose to a peak of about 70 booming (singing) males in the 1950s, falling to fewer than 20 by the 1990s.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是\"这种鸟的数量达到顶峰是在什么时候？\"\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"peak of number\"（数量达到顶峰）是关键词，通过这个词可以在A段找到原文中\"rose to a peak of about 70 booming (singing) males in the 1950s\"这句话。\n解题思路：原文明确提到在\"the 1950s\"（20世纪50年代）时，这种鸟的数量达到了顶峰，因此答案就是\"1950s\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64371","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8905:64372:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"(being) shy/shyness/(Being) Shy/Shyness","acceptedAnswers":["(being) shy","being shy","shy","shyness","(Being) Shy","Being Shy","Shy","Shyness"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Bitterns have cryptic plumage and shy nature, usually remaining hidden within the cover of reedbed vegetation.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问作者如何描述麻鸦的性格特征。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"bittern's character\"，在B段中找到描述麻鸦特征的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，麻鸦羽毛隐秘且性情羞怯，通常藏身于芦苇丛中。因此答案为shy/shyness。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64372","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8905:64373:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"starvation/Starvation","acceptedAnswers":["starvation","Starvation"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Many chicks did not survive to fledging and starvation was found to be the most likely reason for their demise.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是麻鸦雏鸟的死亡主要原因是什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"chick bittern’s death\"可以定位到F段，该段提到了雏鸟的生存状况和死亡原因。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，饥饿是导致雏鸟死亡的最可能的原因。因此，答案为starvation。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64373","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8905:64374:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"native fish/fish/Native Fish/Fish","acceptedAnswers":["native fish","fish","Native Fish","Fish"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The fish prey fed to chicks was dominated by those species penetrating into the reed edge.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是麻鸦雏鸟的主要食物是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词\"main food for chick bittern\"可以定位到F段中关于雏鸟食物的描述。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子，它们的主要食物来源是那些深入芦苇边缘的鱼类。因此，答案为(native)fish或(Native)Fish。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64374","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8905:64375:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"partnership project/partnership project network/network of sites/network/Partnership Project/Partnership Project Network/Network of Sites/Network","acceptedAnswers":["partnership project","partnership project network","network of sites","network","Partnership Project","Partnership Project Network","Network of Sites","Network"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A network of 19 sites developed through this partnership project will secure a more sustainable UK bittern population with successful breeding outside of the core area, less vulnerable to chance events and sea-level rise.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是什么系统可以确保麻鸦种群的稳定性。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"stability\"和\"bittern's population\"定位到G段，该段提到\"secure a more sustainable UK bittern population\"（确保英国鹮鹬种群的可持续性），这与题目中的\"stability\"对应。\n解题思路：根据原文句子，通过该合作项目（partnership project）建立的19个栖息地网络，将确保英国麻鸦种群实现可持续发展——在核心区域外成功繁殖的种群不仅更少受偶然事件和海平面上升的影响，还能有效降低种群波动风险。因此，答案为partnership project/partnership project network/network (of sites)。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64375","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8905:64376:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"Otter and brown-hare/Otter And Brown-Hare","acceptedAnswers":["Otter and brown-hare","Otter And Brown-Hare"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Otter and brown-hare occur on the sites as does the rare plant, pillwort.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问除了麻鸦和稀有植被外，保护计划还惠及哪种哺乳动物。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"besides bittern and rare vegetation\"和\"mammal\"定位到I段最后一句，该句提到除了稀有植物pillwort外，还有哪些动物出现在这些保护地点。\n解题思路：原文I段最后一句明确提到\"Otter and brown-hare occur on the sites\"，其中Otter（水獭）和brown-hare（棕兔）都是哺乳动物，符合题干要求。题干中的\"rare vegetation\"对应原文的\"rare plant, pillwort\"，因此答案是Otter and brown-hare。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64376","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8905:64377:27","type":"choice","text":"What is the main purpose of this passage?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：  Science has been at the core of the bittern story, success has only been achieved through the trust, hard work and dedication of all the managers, owners and wardens of sites that have implemented, in some cases very drastic, management to secure the future of this wetland species in the UK.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问这篇文章的主要目的是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读全文，尤其是后半段的段落H段，可以找到文章的核心信息。\n解题思路：全文从麻鸦的种群历史、栖息地需求、饮食习性等方面展开，但重点在于如何通过科研和多方合作（如RSPB、EU LIFE Fund等组织）实施保护措施，最终使种群数量回升。H段明确强调合作的重要性。因此，文章的主要目的是说明合作可以保护濒危物种，对应选项B。其他选项A、C、D分别侧重于麻鸦的特征、获取信息困难和保护湿地，均未全面概括文章主旨。","options":["main characteristic of a bird called bittern.","cooperation can protect an endangered species","the difficulty of access information of bittern’s habitat and diet","to save wetland and reedbed in the UK"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64377","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesiton 27\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64370","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-H Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-H from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"64371","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>21 </strong>When did the bird of bitten reach its peak of number? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"64372","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>22 </strong>What does the author describe the bittern’s character? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"64373","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>23 </strong>What is the main cause for the chick bittern’s death? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"64374","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>24 </strong>What is the main food for chick bittern? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"64375","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>25 </strong>What system does it secure the stability for bittern’s population? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"64376","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>26 </strong>Besides bittern and rare vegetation, what mammal does the protection plan benefit? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":26},{"id":"64377","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesiton 27\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is the main purpose of this passage?</strong></p>","firstNumber":27}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Saving the British Bitterns</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>#&amp;A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Breeding bitterns became extinct in the UK by 1886 but, following re-colonisation early last century, numbers rose to a peak of about 70 booming (singing) males in the 1950s, falling to fewer than 20 by the 1990s. In the late 1980s, it was clear that the bittern was in trouble, but there was little information on which to base recovery actions.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Bitterns have cryptic plumage and shy nature, usually remaining hidden within the cover of reedbed vegetation. Our first challenge was to develop standard methods to monitor their numbers. The boom of the male bittern is its most distinctive feature during the breeding season, and we developed a method to count them using the sound patterns unique to each individual. This not only allows us to be much more certain of the number of booming males in the UK but also enables us to estimate the local survival of males from one year to the next.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Our first direct understanding of the habitat needs of breeding bitterns came from comparisons of reedbed sites that had lost their booming birds with those that retained them. This research showed that bitterns had been retained in reedbeds where the natural process of succession, or drying out, had been slowed through management. Based on this work, broad recommendations on how to manage and rehabilitate reedbeds for bitterns were made, and funding was provided through the EU LIFE Fund to manage 13 sites within the core breeding range. This project, though led by the RSPB, involved many other organisations.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>To refine these recommendations and provide fine-scale, quantitative habitat prescriptions on the bitterns’ preferred feeding habitat, we radio-tracked male bitterns on the RSPB’s Minsmere and Leighton Moss reserves. This showed clear preferences for feeding in the wetter reedbed margins, particularly within the reedbed next to larger open pools. The average home range sizes of the male bitterns we followed (about 20 hectares) provided a good indication of the area of reedbed needed when managing or creating habitat for this species. Female bitterns undertake all the incubation and care of the young, so it was important to understand their needs as well. Over the course of our research, we located 87 bittern nests and found that female bitterns preferred to nest in areas of continuous vegetation, well into the reedbed, but where water was still present during the driest part of the breeding season.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The success of the habitat prescriptions developed from this research has been spectacular. For instance, at Minsmere, booming bittern numbers gradually increased from one to 10 following reedbed lowering, a management technique designed to halt the drying out process. After a low point of 11 booming males in 1997, bittern numbers in Britain responded to all the habitat management work and started to increase for the first time since the 1950s.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The final phase of the research involved understanding the diet, survival and dispersal of bittern chicks. To do this we fitted small radio tags to young bittern chicks in the nest, to determine their fate through to fledge and beyond. Many chicks did not survive to fledging and starvation was found to be the most likely reason for their demise. The fish prey fed to chicks was dominated by those species penetrating into the reed edge. So, an important element of recent studies (including a PhD with the University of Hull) has been the development of recommendations on habitat and water conditions to promote healthy native fish populations.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Once independent, radio-tagged young bitterns were found to seek out new sites during their first winter; a proportion of these would remain on new sites to breed if the conditions were suitable. A second EU LIFE funded project aims to provide these suitable sites in new areas. A network of 19 sites developed through this partnership project will secure a more sustainable UK bittern population with successful breeding outside of the core area, less vulnerable to chance events and sea-level rise.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>By 2004, the number of booming male bitterns in the UK had increased to 55, with almost all of the increase being on those sites undertaking management based on advice derived from our research. Although science has been at the core of the bittern story, success has only been achieved through the trust, hard work and dedication of all the managers, owners and wardens of sites that have implemented, in some cases very drastic, management to secure the future of this wetland species in the UK. The constructed bunds and five major sluices now control the water level over 82 ha, with a further 50 ha coming under control in the winter of 2005/06. Reed establishment has principally used natural regeneration or planted seedlings to provide small core areas that will in time expand to create a bigger reed area. To date, nearly 275,000 seedlings have been planted and reed cover is extensive. Over 3 km of new ditches have been formed, 3.7 km of the existing ditch have been re-profiled and 2.2 km of old meander (former estuarine features) have been cleaned out.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Bitterns now regularly winter on the site with some indication that they are staying longer into the spring. No breeding has yet occurred but a booming male was present in the spring of 2004. A range of wildfowl breed, as well as a good number of reedbed passerines including reed bunting, reed, sedge and grasshopper warblers. Numbers of wintering shoveler have increased so that the site now holds a UK important wintering population. Malltraeth Reserve now forms part of the UK network of key sites for water vole (a UK priority species) and 12 monitoring transects have been established. Otter and brown-hare occur on the sites as does the rare plant, pillwort.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8905&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8906","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Company Innovation","book":"阅读还原集Vol.18","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.18 · Test 3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8906:64378:28","type":"choice","text":"28 Approach to retain the best employees","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Elsewhere, the search for innovation has led to a craze for ‘intrapreneurship’ – devolving power and setting up internal ideas-factories and tracking stocks so that talented staff will not leave.\n对应段落：F\n审题：题目问的是“留住优秀员工的方法”这一信息出现在哪一段。\n定位关键信息：根据题目的“Approach to retain the best employees”可以定位到段落F中的“talented staff will not leave”这一表述，这与题目中的“retain the best employees”意思相近。\n解题思路：段落F提到了许多大公司担心并购小公司难以留住优秀人才，于是开始内部创业，通过下放决策权、建立内部创意工厂并建立人才储备机制，确保优秀人才不会流失。这与题目描述一致，因此答案为F。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64378","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-33\nThe reading passage has ten paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 28-33 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8906:64378:29","type":"choice","text":"29 Safeguarding expenses on an innovative idea","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Much of today’s merger boom is driven by a desperate search for new ideas. So is the fortune now spent on licensing and buying others’ intellectual property.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“保障在创新想法上的花费”这一信息出现在哪一段落。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"Safeguarding expenses on an innovative idea\"，可以定位到C段中提到的\"the fortune now spent on licensing and buying others’ intellectual property\"，这与题目中的\"expenses on an innovative idea\"相对应。\n解题思路：C段中提到，当前并购热潮的兴起，很大程度上源于企业对创新理念的迫切追求。如今企业投入专利授权和收购他人知识产权的巨额资金，同样源于这种创新需求。花费在许可和知识产权上的资金也与题目中的\"expenses on an innovative idea\"相吻合。题目中的“Safeguarding expenses”可以理解为“为确保（获得创新想法）而付出的花费或投资”。因此，答案为C。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64378","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-33\nThe reading passage has ten paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 28-33 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8906:64378:30","type":"choice","text":"30 Integrating outside firms might produce a certain counter effect","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Some people think that such restructuring is not enough. In a new book, Clayton Christensen argues that many things which established firms do well, such as looking after their current customers, can hinder the sort of innovative behaviour needed to deal with disruptive technologies. Hence the fashion for cannibalization – setting up businesses that will actually fight your existing ones.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“整合外部公司可能会产生某种反效果”这一信息出现在哪个段落。\n定位关键信息： 根据“Integrating outside firms might produce a certain counter effect”，定位到文中描述整合或内部创新可能带来负面影响的段落。\n解题思路：在G段中，提到了有些人认为这样的重组还不够，许多成熟企业擅长的事情，比如照顾现有客户，可能会阻碍应对颠覆性技术所需的创新行为。于是出现内部竞争的潮流，公司开始建立与现有业务竞争的新业务。而这会在同一公司内部产生竞争，并阻碍创新行为（产生某种反效果）。而“cannibalization”这一行为本身就是一种“counter effect”，因为它会导致新业务与现有业务竞争，从而可能削弱现有业务的市场地位。因此，G段包含了题目所问的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64378","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-33\nThe reading passage has ten paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 28-33 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8906:64378:31","type":"choice","text":"31 Example of three famous American companies’ innovation","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The stars of American business tend today to be innovators such as Dell, Amazon and Wal-Mart, which have produced ideas or products that have changed their industries.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落提到了三个著名美国公司的创新例子。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"three famous American companies\"和\"innovation\"定位到B段。\n解题思路：B段明确提到了，创新已成为美国企业管理界的热词。如今，美国商界的明星企业多为创新者，如戴尔、亚马逊和沃尔玛，它们通过创意或产品革新改变了所在行业。因此，B段是包含题目所要求信息的段落。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64378","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-33\nThe reading passage has ten paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 28-33 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8906:64378:32","type":"choice","text":"32 Example of one company changing its focus","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Procter & Gamble is now shifting its entire business focus from countries to products; one aim is to get innovations accepted across the company.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问哪个段落包含了一个公司改变其业务焦点的例子。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"changing its focus\"和\"Example of one company\"定位到F段，该段提到宝洁公司正在将业务焦点从国家转向产品。\n解题思路：F段明确提到，宝洁公司正将战略重心从地域布局转向产品开发，其核心目标是推动创新成果在全公司范围内获得认可。这与题目要求的一致，因此答案为F。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64378","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-33\nThe reading passage has ten paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 28-33 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8906:64378:33","type":"choice","text":"33 Example of a company resolving financial difficulties itself","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Now, with plenty of cheap venture capital, he is more likely to set up on his own. Umagic has already raised $5m and is about to raise $25m more.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了“公司自己解决财务困难的例子”。\n定位关键信息：根据“Example of a company resolving financial difficulties itself”，定位到文中描述小公司或创业者如何通过外部融资等方式自行解决资金问题的段落。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子，可以看出，如今，随着大量低成本风险投资的涌入，创业者更倾向于自主创业。给出了具体例子：Umagic公司“已经筹集了500万美元，并即将再筹集2500万美元”，该案例展示了小公司或创业者如何不依赖大公司，而是通过风险投资等外部融资方式，自行解决了项目发展所需的财务困难。因此，包含此信息的段落是E。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64378","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-33\nThe reading passage has ten paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 28-33 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8906:64379:34","type":"choice","text":"Umagic is the most successful innovative company in this new field.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Although few people have lost money betting on the neuroses of the American consumer, Umagic’s prospects are hard to gauge (in ten years’ time, consulting a computer about your sex life might seem natural, or it might seem absurd).\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问Umagic是创新领域中最成功的公司，需要判断这一说法是否与文章一致。\n定位关键信息：通过“Umagic”和“innovative company”定位到A段首句和末句，文中提到Umagic是初创公司，但并未说明其是否“最成功”。\n解题思路：原文提到Umagic的前景难以评估，（十年后，向电脑咨询性生活可能显得自然，也可能显得荒谬），说明其成功与否尚未可知，更未提及“最成功”。因此，题目信息在文中未给出，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64379","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34-37\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 34-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8906:64380:35","type":"choice","text":"Amazon and Wal-Mart exchanged their innovation experience.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The stars of American business tend today to be innovators such as Dell, Amazon and Wal-Mart, which have produced ideas or products that have changed their industries.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是，Amazon和Wal-Mart互相交换了创新经验，需要判断这一说法是否与文章一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的Amazon和Wal-Mart是关键词，需要在文章中找到这两个公司被提及的地方。\n解题思路：在文章中，Amazon和Wal-Mart都被提及，但都是作为创新企业的例子被提及，并没有提到它们之间有任何交流或交换创新经验的内容。因此，答案是Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64380","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34-37\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 34-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8906:64381:36","type":"choice","text":"New idea holder had already been known to take it to a small company in the past.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In the past, if a clever scientist had an idea he wanted to commercialise, he would take it first to a big company.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“在过去，持有新想法的人会将其带到一家小公司”，需要判断这一说法是否与文章一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“New idea holder”（持有新想法的人）、“in the past”（在过去）和“take it to a small company”（带给一家小公司）定位到E段。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，过去，若一位聪明的科学家想要将创意商业化，通常会先向大公司寻求支持。而题目却说带给小公司，两者矛盾，因此题目陈述与原文信息不符，答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64381","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34-37\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 34-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8906:64382:37","type":"choice","text":"IBM failed to understand Umagic’s proposal for one new idea.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He also recalls with glee the looks of total incomprehension when he tried to hawk his ‘virtual experts’ idea three years ago to the idea labs of firms such as IBM – though, as he cheerfully adds, ‘of course, they could have been right.’\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问“IBM公司没能理解Umagic公司的创新提议”，需要判断这一说法是否与文章一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“IBM”和“Umagic’s proposal”定位到J段中提到的“IBM”和“Umagic’s idea”。\n解题思路：原文明确提到David Post回忆三年前向IBM等公司的创意实验室推销“虚拟专家”想法时，IBM表现出“total incomprehension”（完全不理解），因此也可以推断，当时IBM并没有采纳David Post的建议。因此，本题的答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64382","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34-37\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 34-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8906:64383:38","type":"choice","text":"What is the author’s opinion on the effect of innovation in paragraph C?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"38.题干：C段中，作者对创新作用的看法是什么？通过题干Paragraph C这一提示快速锁定原文C段，并扫读该段的大致内容。这段主要提到了创新与经济利益的关系，其中第2句提到，迫切寻求创新想法是新一轮并购热潮的催化剂。由此可见，公司创新对于公司的发展来说越来越重要。因此，本题的答案为C\n原文答案句：原文中完整的英文答案句\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是作者在第C段中对创新的影响持有什么样的观点。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“effect of innovation”和“paragraph C”定位到C段。C段提到“the top 20% of firms in an annual innovation poll by Fortune magazine have achieved double the shareholder returns of their peers”，这说明创新对于企业的影响越来越大。\n解题思路：根据原文答案对应的句子，可以得出结论，作者认为创新的影响正在变得越来越重要。因此，正确答案是C。","options":["It only works for big companies.","Fortune magazine has a huge influence globally.","It is getting more important.","Effect on American companies is more evident."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64383","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8906:64384:39","type":"choice","text":"What is Peter Chernin’s point of view on innovation?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘In the management of creativity, size is your enemy,’ argues Peter Chernin, who runs the Fox TV and film empire for News Corporation. One person managing 20 movies is never going to be as involved as one doing five movies. He has thus tried to break down the studio into smaller units – even at the risk of incurring higher costs.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问Peter Chernin 对于创新有什么看法。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的名字\"Peter Chernin\"定位到D段，找到他关于创新的论述。\n解题思路：原文中Peter Chernin明确指出“在创意管理中，规模是你的敌人”，管理20部电影的人不可能像管理5部电影的人那样具有创造力。由此可以推断出，小规模的公司的创新管理更容易，而大公司则比较难。因此，本题的答案为A。","options":["Small company is more innovative than the big one.","Film industry needs more innovation than other industries.","We need to cut the cost when risks occur.","New ideas are more likely going to big companies."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64384","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8906:64385:40","type":"choice","text":"What is the author’s opinion on innovation at the end of this passage?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Will all this creative destruction, cannibalization and culture tweaking make big firms more creative?...Innovation – unlike, apparently, sex, parenting and fitness – is one area where a computer cannot tell you what to do.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是文末作者对于创新的观点是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词\"author’s opinion\"和\"innovation\"可以定位到文章结尾部分，即J段。\n解题思路：根据J段原文答案句可知，文章结尾段（J段）通过引用Umagic创始人的话，提出了一个核心疑问：“所有这些创造性破坏、自我蚕食和文化调整会让大公司更有创造力吗？”，但没有在文中给出答案，最后又说，毕竟，创新不像性、教育和健康，它是计算机没法告诉你该做些什么的一个领域。由此可推断，作者本人对创新的看法也是无法确定的。因此，本题的答案D。","options":["Umagic success lies on the accidental ‘virtual experts’.","Innovation is easy and straightforward.","IBM sets a good example of innovation.","The author’s attitude is uncertain on innovation."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64385","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64378","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-33\nThe reading passage has ten paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 28-33 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","html":"<p><strong>28</strong> Approach to retain the best employees <strong class=\"source-blank\">[28] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"64379","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34-37\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 34-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Umagic is the most successful innovative company in this new field.</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"64380","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34-37\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 34-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Amazon and Wal-Mart exchanged their innovation experience.</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"64381","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34-37\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 34-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>New idea holder had already been known to take it to a small company in the past.</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"64382","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 34-37\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 34-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>IBM failed to understand Umagic’s proposal for one new idea.</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"64383","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is the author’s opinion on the effect of innovation in paragraph C?</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"64384","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is Peter Chernin’s point of view on innovation?</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"64385","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is the author’s opinion on innovation at the end of this passage?</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Company Innovation</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In a scruffy office in midtown Manhattan, a team of 30 artificial-intelligence programmers is trying to simulate the brains of an eminent sexologist, a well-known dietician, a celebrity fitness trainer and several other experts. Umagic Systems is a young firm, setting up websites that will allow clients to consult the virtual versions of these personalities. Subscribers will feed in details about themselves and their goals; Umagic’s software will come up with the advice that the star expert would give. Although few people have lost money betting on the neuroses of the American consumer, Umagic’s prospects are hard to gauge (in ten years’ time, consulting a computer about your sex life might seem natural, or it might seem absurd). But the company and others like it are beginning to spook large American firms because they see such half-barmy ‘innovative’ ideas as the key to their own future success.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Innovation has become the buzz-word of American management. Firms have found that most of the things that can be outsourced or re-engineered have been (worryingly, by their competitors as well). The stars of American business tend today to be innovators such as Dell, Amazon and Wal-Mart, which have produced ideas or products that have changed their industries.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>A new book by two consultants from Arthur D. Little records that, over the past 15 years, the top 20% of firms in an annual innovation poll by Fortune magazine have achieved double the shareholder returns of their peers. Much of today’s merger boom is driven by a desperate search for new ideas. So is the fortune now spent on licensing and buying others’ intellectual property. According to the Pasadena-based Patent &amp; Licence Exchange, trading in intangible assets in the United States has risen from $15 billion in 1990 to $100 billion in 1998, with an increasing proportion of the rewards going to small firms and individuals.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>And therein lies the terror for big companies: that innovation seems to work best outside them. Several bigs established ‘ideas factories’, including 3M, Procter &amp; Gamble and Rubbermaid, have had dry spells recently. Gillette spent ten years and $1 billion developing its new Mach 3 razor; it took a British supermarket only a year or so to produce a reasonable imitation. ‘In the management of creativity, size is your enemy,’ argues Peter Chernin, who runs the Fox TV and film empire for News Corporation. One person managing 20 movies is never going to be as involved as one doing five movies. He has thus tried to break down the studio into smaller units – even at the risk of incurring higher costs.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>It is easier for ideas to thrive outside big firms these days. In the past, if a clever scientist had an idea he wanted to commercialise, he would take it first to a big company. Now, with plenty of cheap venture capital, he is more likely to set up on his own. Umagic has already raised $5m and is about to raise $25m more. Even in capital-intensive businesses such as pharmaceuticals, entrepreneurs can conduct early-stage research, selling out to the big firms when they reach expensive, risky clinical trials. Around a third of drug firms’ total revenue now comes from licensed-in technology.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Some giants, including General Electric and Cisco, have been remarkably successful at snapping up and integrating scores of small companies. But many others worry about the prices they have to pay and the difficulty in hanging on to the talent that dreamt up the idea. Everybody would like to develop more ideas in-house. Procter &amp; Gamble is now shifting its entire business focus from countries to products; one aim is to get innovations accepted across the company. Elsewhere, the search for innovation has led to a craze for ‘intrapreneurship’ – devolving power and setting up internal ideas-factories and tracking stocks so that talented staff will not leave.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Some people think that such restructuring is not enough. In a new book, Clayton Christensen argues that many things which established firms do well, such as looking after their current customers, can hinder the sort of innovative behaviour needed to deal with disruptive technologies. Hence the fashion for cannibalization – setting up businesses that will actually fight your existing ones. Bank One, for instance, has established Wingspan, an Internet bank that competes with its real branches (see article). Jack Welch’s Internet initiative at General Electric is called ‘Destroyyourbusines.com’.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Nobody could doubt that innovation matters. But need large firms to be quite so pessimistic? A recent survey of the top 50 innovations in America, by Industry Week, a journal, suggested that ideas are as likely to come from big firms as from small ones. Another sceptical note is sounded by Amar Bhidé, a colleague of Mr Christensen’s at the Harvard Business School and the author of another book on entrepreneurship. Rather than having to reinvent themselves, big companies, he believes, should concentrate on projects with high costs and low uncertainty, leaving those with low costs and high uncertainty to small entrepreneurs. As ideas mature and the risks and rewards become more quantifiable, big companies can adopt them.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>At Kimberly-Clark, Mr Sanders had to discredit the view that jobs working on new products were for ‘those who couldn’t hack it in the real business’. He has tried to change the culture not just by preaching fuzzy concepts but also by introducing hard incentives, such as increasing the rewards for those who come up with successful new ideas and, particularly, not punishing those whose experiments fail. The genesis of one of the firm’s current hits, Depend, a more dignified incontinence garment, lay in a previous miss, Kotex Personals, a form of disposable underwear for menstruating women.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Will all this creative destruction, cannibalization and culture tweaking make big firms more creative? David Post, the founder of Umagic, is skeptical: ‘The only successful intrapreneurs are ones who leave and become entrepreneurs.’ He also recalls with glee the looks of total incomprehension when he tried to hawk his ‘virtual experts’ idea three years ago to the idea labs of firms such as IBM – though, as he cheerfully adds, ‘of course, they could have been right.’ Innovation – unlike, apparently, sex, parenting and fitness – is one area where a computer cannot tell you what to do.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8906&scene=%E8%B4%A2%E7%BB%8F%E5%95%86%E4%B8%9A&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8891","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 The Impact of the Potato","book":"阅读还原集Vol.18","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.18 · Test 2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8891:64319:1","type":"choice","text":"The early Spanish called potato as the Incan name ‘Chuchu’.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Early Spanish chroniclers who misused the Indian word batata (sweet potato) as the name for the potato noted the importance of the tuber to the Incan Empire. The Incas has learned to preserve the potato for storage by dehydrating and mashing potatoes into a substance called Chuchu could be stored in a room for up to 10 years, providing excellent insurance against possible crop failures.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是早期的西班牙人将土豆称为印加名称‘Chuchu’，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词‘Spanish’和‘Chuchu’定位到B段，找到相关的句子。\n解题思路：原文中提到早期的西班牙编年史家误用了印第安词‘batata’（红薯）作为土豆的名字，印加人通过脱水和捣碎技术，将马铃薯制成名为“Chuchu”的特殊物质，不是西班牙人对土豆的称呼。因此，题目说法与原文不符，答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64319","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8891:64320:2","type":"choice","text":"The purposes of Spanish coming to Peru were to find out potatoes.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The Spanish conquistadors first encountered the potato when they arrived in Peru in 1532 in search of gold and noted Inca miners eating chuchu.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问“西班牙人来到秘鲁的目的是寻找土豆”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的“Spanish coming to Peru”和“find out potatoes”定位到C段首句“the Spanish conquistadors first encountered the potato when they arrived in Peru in 1532 in search of gold”，发现西班牙人最初来到秘鲁是为了寻找黄金。\n解题思路：原文明确指出西班牙人最初是为了寻找黄金（gold）而非土豆，因此题目说法与原文矛盾，答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64320","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8891:64321:3","type":"choice","text":"The Spanish believed that the potato has the same nutrients as other vegetables.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The Spaniards failed to realize that the potato represented a far more important treasure than either silver or gold, but they did gradually begin to use potatoes as basic rations aboard their ships.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是，西班牙人认为马铃薯与其他蔬菜具有相同的营养价值，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Spanish\"和\"nutrients\"可以定位到C段，其中提到了西班牙人开始将土豆作为船上的基本口粮。\n解题思路：原文中提到西班牙人开始将土豆作为船上的基本口粮，但并没有提到他们是否认为土豆和其他蔬菜有相同的营养。因此，题目中的信息在原文中没有明确给出，所以答案是NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64321","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8891:64322:4","type":"choice","text":"Peasants at the time did not like to eat potatoes because they were ugly.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Even peasants refused to eat from a plant that produced ugly, misshapen tubers and that had come from a heathen civilization.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“当时农民不爱吃土豆，因为土豆长得丑”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键词“peasants”（农民）、“did not like to eat”（不喜欢吃）和“ugly”（丑陋）在文章中定位。\n解题思路：原文D段明确提到，农民也拒绝食用这种结着丑陋畸形块茎、源自异教文明的作物。农民拒绝吃土豆，这与题目中的“they were ugly”（它们丑陋）完全一致。因此，题目陈述与原文信息相符，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64322","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8891:64323:5","type":"choice","text":"The popularity of potatoes in the UK was due to food shortages during the war.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Potatoes did not become a staple until during the food shortages associated with the the Revolutionary Wars, the English government began to officially encourage potato cultivation.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问“土豆在英国的流行是由于战争期间的食品短缺”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过“popularity of potatoes in the UK”和“food shortages during the war”定位到E段，该段提到土豆在英国的推广过程，但未提及战争或食品短缺的具体原因。\n解题思路：E段提到，直到独立战争期间粮食短缺，马铃薯才成为主食，英国政府才开始正式推广种植。原文中的“become a staple（成为主食、主要农产品）”和题目中的“popularity（普及）”其实是同义替换，指的是土豆成为主食这件事，剩下的细节信息“food shortages”和“war”等均与原文信息一致，所以正确答案是TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64323","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8891:64324:6","type":"fill","text":"填写第 6 空","answer":"flower/Flower","acceptedAnswers":["flower","Flower"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The people began to overcome their distaste when the plant received the royal seal of approval: Louis XVI began to sport a potato flower in his buttonhole, and Marie-Antoinette wore the purple potato blossom in her hair.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是在法国，人们开始克服对土豆的厌恶感，因为国王在他的纽扣孔上放了一个土豆的什么东西。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"France\"、\"King\"、\"potato\"、\"button hole\"，可以在文章中定位到F段，其中提到了法国国王路易十六在纽扣孔上佩戴了土豆的某个部分。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句，当这种植物获得王室认可后，民众开始转变态度：路易十六开始在纽扣孔佩戴马铃薯花，因此答案为flower。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64324","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8891:64325:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"prejudice/Prejudice","acceptedAnswers":["prejudice","Prejudice"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Frederick the Great of Prussia saw the potato’s potential to help feed his nation and lower the price of bread but faced the challenge of overcoming the people’s prejudice against the plant.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问弗雷德里克认识到土豆的潜力，但他必须处理来自普通人对土豆的什么问题。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的\"Frederick\"、\"potential of potato\"、\"handle\"、\"against potatoes\"、\"ordinary people\"等关键词定位到G段。\n解题思路：原文提到，普鲁士的腓特烈大帝意识到马铃薯的潜力，这种作物既能养活百姓又能降低面包价格，但他需要处理民众对这种作物的偏见。因此答案为\"prejudice\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64325","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet."},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8891:64326:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"reverse/Reverse","acceptedAnswers":["reverse","Reverse"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Trying a less direct approach to encourage his subjects to begin planting potatoes, Frederick used a bit of reverse psychology: he planted a royal field of potato plants and stationed a heavy guard to protect this field from thieves.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问普鲁士国王采用了哪种心理学策略让人们接受土豆。\n定位关键信息：通过\"King of Prussia\"和\"potatoes\"定位到G段，找到国王采用reverse psychology的相关句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，为更巧妙地鼓励民众种植，腓特烈采用了反向心理战术：他亲自开辟皇家马铃薯种植园，并安排重兵把守以防盗贼。因此答案为\"reverse\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64326","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet."},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8891:64327:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"meat/Meat","acceptedAnswers":["meat","Meat"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Prior to 1800, the English diet had consisted primarily of meat, supplemented by bread, butter and cheese.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是在1800年之前，英国人喜欢吃什么与面包、黄油和奶酪一起食用。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Before 1800\"、\"bread, butter and cheese\"等关键词定位到原文中描述1800年前饮食习惯的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，1800年前，英国人的日常饮食以肉类为主，搭配面包、黄油和奶酪。因此答案为meat。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64327","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet."},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8891:64328:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"crops/Crops","acceptedAnswers":["crops","Crops"],"explanation":"原文答案句：High yielding, easily prepared potato crops were the obvious solution to England’s food problems.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是解决英格兰食物问题的明显方法是高产的土豆什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"England food problems\"和\"high yielding potato\"定位到H段，找到包含这些关键词的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，高产易种的马铃薯作物，自然成为解决英国粮食问题的不二之选。因此答案为\"crops\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64328","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet."},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8891:64329:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"soil/Soil","acceptedAnswers":["soil","Soil"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The potato was well suited to the Irish the soil and climate, and its high yield suited the most important concern of most Irish farmers: to feed their families.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问爱尔兰的什么条件适合土豆生长。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Irish\"和\"climate\"定位到I段，找到包含这两个词的句子。\n解题思路：原文提到，马铃薯不仅与爱尔兰的土壤气候完美契合，其高产特性更直接满足了农民最根本的需求——保障家庭温饱。说明爱尔兰的土壤适合种植土豆，因此答案为soil。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64329","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet."},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8891:64330:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"cultivation/Cultivation","acceptedAnswers":["cultivation","Cultivation"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The Irish population doubled to eight million between 1780 and 1841, this without any significant expansion of industry or reform of agricultural techniques beyond the widespread cultivation of the potato.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是在1780年到1841年之间，因为土豆的什么，爱尔兰人口翻倍到了八百万。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的时间范围\"Between 1780 and 1841\"和结果\"the Irish population doubled to eight million\"可以定位到J段的相关句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，1780至1841年间，爱尔兰人口翻倍增至800万，而这一增长完全依赖于马铃薯的广泛种植，因此答案为\"cultivation\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64330","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet."},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8891:64331:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"investment/Investment","acceptedAnswers":["investment","Investment"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Though Irish landholding practices were primitive in comparison with those of England, the potato’s high yields allowed even the poorest farmers to produce more healthy food than they needed with scarcely any investment or hard labor.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是马铃薯的高产量能让最贫困的农民生产更多的健康食品，并且几乎不需要什么和艰苦的劳动。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"high yields\"、\"poorest farmers\"、\"produce more healthy food\"和\"almost without\"来定位原文。\n解题思路：原文中提到，尽管爱尔兰的土地制度远不如英格兰先进，但马铃薯的高产特性让即便是最贫困的农户，也能以极低投入和轻松劳作产出更多健康的食物。因此答案为\"investment\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64331","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64319","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>The early Spanish called potato as the Incan name ‘Chuchu’.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"64320","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>The purposes of Spanish coming to Peru were to find out potatoes.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"64321","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>The Spanish believed that the potato has the same nutrients as other vegetables.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"64322","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Peasants at the time did not like to eat potatoes because they were ugly.</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"64323","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>The popularity of potatoes in the UK was due to food shortages during the war.</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"64324","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>6</strong> In France, people started to overcome their disgusting about potatoes because the King put a potato <strong class=\"source-blank\">[6] ____</strong> in his button hole.</p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"64325","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>7</strong> Frederick realized the potential of potato but he had to handle the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong> against potatoes\nfrom ordinary people.</p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"64326","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>8</strong> The King of Prussia adopted some <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong> Psychology to make people accept potatoes.</p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"64327","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>9</strong> Before 1800, the English people preferred eating <strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong> with bread, butter and cheese.</p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"64328","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>10</strong> The obvious way to deal with England food problems were high yielding potato <strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"64329","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>11</strong> The Irish <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong> and climate suited potatoes well.</p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"64330","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>12</strong> Between 1780 and 1841, based on the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong> of the potatoes, the Irish population doubled\nto eight million.</p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"64331","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>13</strong> The potato&#39;s high yields help the poorest farmers to produce more healthy food almost without <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong> and hard physical work.</p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The Impact of the Potato&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">Jeff Chapman relates the story of history the most important vegetable</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The potato was first cultivated in South America between three and seven thousand years ago, though scientists believe they may have grown wild in the region as long as 13,000 years ago. The genetic patterns of potato distribution indicate that the potato probably originated in the mountainous west-central region of the continent.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Early Spanish chroniclers who misused the Indian word batata (sweet potato) as the name for the potato noted the importance of the tuber to the Incan Empire. The Incas has learned to preserve the potato for storage by dehydrating and mashing potatoes into a substance called Chuchu could be stored in a room for up to 10 years, providing excellent insurance against possible crop failures. As well as using the food as a staple crop, the Incas thought potatoes made childbirth easier and used it to treat injuries.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The Spanish conquistadors first encountered the potato when they arrived in Peru in 1532 in search of gold and noted Inca miners eating chuchu. At the time the Spaniards failed to realize that the potato represented a far more important treasure than either silver or gold, but they did gradually begin to use potatoes as basic rations aboard their ships. After the arrival of the potato in Spain in 1570, a few Spanish farmers began to cultivate them on a small scale, mostly as food for livestock.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Throughout Europe, potatoes were regarded with suspicion, distaste and fear. Generally considered to be unfit for human consumption, they were used only as animal fodder and sustenance for the starving. In northern Europe, potatoes were primarily grown in botanical gardens as an exotic novelty. Even peasants refused to eat from a plant that produced ugly, misshapen tubers and that had come from a heathen civilization. Some felt that the potato plant’s resemblance to plants in the nightshade family hinted that it was the creation of witches or devils.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In meat-loving England, farmers and urban workers regarded potatoes with extreme distaste. In 1662, the Royal Society recommended the cultivation of the tuber to the English government and the nation, but this recommendation had little impact. Potatoes did not become a staple until during the food shortages associated with the&nbsp;the Revolutionary Wars, the English government began to officially encourage potato&nbsp;cultivation.&nbsp;In 1795, the Board of Agriculture issued a pamphlet entitled ‘Hints Respecting the Culture and Use of Potatoes’; this was followed shortly by pro-potato editorials and potato recipes in The Times. Gradually, the lower classes began to follow the lead of the upper classes.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>A similar pattern emerged across the English Channel in the Netherlands, Belgium and France. While the potato slowly gained ground in eastern France (where it was often the only crop remaining after marauding soldiers plundered wheat fields and vineyards), it did not achieve widespread acceptance until the late 1700s. The peasants remained suspicious, in spite of a 1771 paper from the Facult de Paris testifying that the potato was not harmful but beneficial. The people began to overcome their distaste when the plant received the royal seal of approval: Louis XVI began to sport a potato flower in his buttonhole, and Marie-Antoinette wore the purple potato blossom in her hair.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Frederick the Great of Prussia saw the potato’s potential to help feed his nation and lower the price of bread but faced the challenge of overcoming the people’s prejudice against the plant. When he issued a 1774 order for his subjects to grow potatoes as protection against famine, the town of Kolberg replied: ‘The things have neither smell nor taste, not even the dogs will eat them, so what use are they to us?’ Trying a less direct approach to encourage his subjects to begin planting potatoes, Frederick used a bit of reverse psychology: he planted a royal field of potato plants and stationed a heavy guard to protect this field from thieves. Nearby peasants naturally assumed that anything worth guarding was worth stealing, and so snuck into the field and snatched the plants for their home gardens. Of course, this was entirely in line with Frederick’s wishes.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Historians debate whether the potato was primarily a cause or an effect of the huge population boom in industrial-era England and Wales. Prior to 1800, the English diet had consisted primarily of meat, supplemented by bread, butter and cheese. Few vegetables were consumed, most vegetables being regarded as nutritionally worthless and potentially harmful. This view began to change gradually in the late 1700s. The Industrial Revolution was drawing an ever-increasing percentage of the populace into crowded cities, where only the richest could afford homes with ovens or coal storage rooms, and people were working 12-16 hour days which left them with little time or energy to prepare food. High yielding, easily prepared potato crops were the obvious solution to England’s food problems.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Whereas most of their neighbors regarded the potato with suspicion and had to be persuaded to use it by the upper classes, the Irish peasantry embraced the tuber more passionately than anyone since the Incas. The potato was well suited to the Irish the soil and climate, and its high yield suited the most important concern of most Irish farmers: to feed their families.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The most dramatic example of the potato’s potential to alter population patterns occurred in Ireland, where the potato had become a staple by 1800. The Irish population doubled to eight million between 1780 and 1841, this without any significant expansion of industry or reform of agricultural techniques beyond the widespread cultivation of the potato. Though Irish landholding practices were primitive in comparison with those of England, the potato’s high yields allowed even the poorest farmers to produce more healthy food than they needed with scarcely any investment or hard labor. Even children could easily plant, harvest and cook potatoes, which of course required no threshing, curing or grinding. The abundance provided by potatoes greatly decreased infant mortality and encouraged early marriage.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8891&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8902","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Finding Our Way","book":"阅读还原集Vol.18","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.18 · Test 2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8902:64344:14","type":"choice","text":"14 using basic direction from starting point and light intensity to move on","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Many animals rely primarily on path integration to get around, including insects, spiders, crabs and rodents. The desert ants of the genus Cataglyphis employ this method to return from foraging as far as 100 yards away. They note the general direction they came from and retrace their steps, using the polarization of sunlight to orient themselves even under overcast skies.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“使用起点的基本方向和光线强度移动”，属于哪一种导航策略。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“basic direction from starting point”和“light intensity”定位到D段中关于路径整合的描述，特别是沙漠蚂蚁使用方向和光线来导航的句子。\n解题思路：D段详细描述了路径整合（path integration）策略，其中提到沙漠蚂蚁（Cataglyphis）通过记录返回方向和利用阳光偏振来导航，这属于导航策略下的路径整合。因此，答案为B（Path integration）。","options":["Guidance","Path integration","Route following"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"64344","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Guidance\nB Path integration\nC Route following"},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8902:64344:15","type":"choice","text":"15 using a combination of place and direction heading for the destination","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This strategy, called route following, uses landmarks such as buildings and street names, plus directions – straight, turn, go through – for reaching intermediate points.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“通过结合位置和方向导航至目的地”，属于哪一种导航策略。\n定位关键信息：通过“using a combination of place and direction heading for the destination”定位到F段中描述路线的方法，即结合建筑物和街道名称（place）以及具体方向（direction）来指引路线。\n解题思路：F段提到，这种被称为‘路线跟随’的策略，通过建筑物、街道名称等地标点，结合‘直走、转弯、穿过’等中间点的指引来实现导航。符合题目中“地点和方向组合”的要求。因此，答案为C。","options":["Guidance","Path integration","Route following"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"64344","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Guidance\nB Path integration\nC Route following"},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8902:64344:16","type":"choice","text":"16 using an iconic building near your destination as orientation","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Neurologists call this navigational approach ‘guidance’, meaning that landmark visible from a distance serves as the marker for one’s destination.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“以目的地附近的标志性建筑作为定位参照物 ”，属于哪一种导航策略。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词“iconic building”（有标志性的建筑）、“near your destination”（靠近目的地）和“orientation”（定位）定位到C段中描述“guidance”方法的句子，其中提到以“prominent landmark”（突出的地标）为定位依据。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，神经学家将这种导航方式称为‘导向’，即指从远处可见的地标可作为目的地的标记。有人以“tall, broad MetLife Building”（高大的梅特利夫大厦）这一标志性建筑为定位依据，并指出“the station is right below it”（车站就在它下面），这属于导航策略下的导向策略。因此，答案为A。","options":["Guidance","Path integration","Route following"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"64344","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Guidance\nB Path integration\nC Route following"},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8902:64344:17","type":"choice","text":"17 using a retrace method from a known place if a mistake happens","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Route following is more precise than guidance or path integration, but if you forget the details and take a wrong turn, the only way to recover is to backtrack until you reach a familiar spot, because you do not know the general direction or have a reference landmark for your goal.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“ 若发生错误，则从已知位置使用回溯方法”，属于哪一种导航策略。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“retrace method”和“from a known place if a mistake happens”定位到D段中描述回溯路径的句子。\n解题思路：原文中提到，路线跟随比导向或路径整合更精确，但若忘记具体细节导致误入歧途，唯一的补救方式就是原路返回，直到找到熟悉地点——因为你既不知道大致方向，也没有目标的参照地标。这明确描述了从已知地点回溯的方法，且在路径出错时需要重新规划，属于导航策略下的路线跟随策略。因此答案为C。","options":["Guidance","Path integration","Route following"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"64344","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Guidance\nB Path integration\nC Route following"},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8902:64344:18","type":"choice","text":"18 using a passing spot as reference for a new integration","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In this case, you are pointed toward the most recent place you recall, and you aim for it. Once there you head for the next notable place and so on, retracing your path. Your brain is adding together the individual legs of your trek into a cumulative progress report. Researchers call this strategy ‘path integration’.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是使用一个经过的地点作为参考点来进行整合，属于哪一种导航策略。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“using a passing spot as reference for a new integration”可以定位到D段中描述的“path integration”策略，即使用最近经过的地点作为参考点，然后继续前往下一个显著的地点。\n解题思路：根据原文中D段的描述，path integration策略是指人们使用最近经过的地点作为参考点，并朝着它前进。到达后，你继续前往下一个显著地点，如此循环往复，重走你的路径。你的大脑将这些独立的行程片段累加成一份累积的进度报告。与题目中描述的一致，因此答案为B。","options":["Guidance","Path integration","Route following"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"64344","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Guidance\nB Path integration\nC Route following"},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8902:64345:19","type":"choice","text":"What does the ant of Cataglyphis respond if it has been taken to another location according to the passage?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Even when a scientist picks up an ant and puts it in a totally different spot, the insect stubbornly proceeds in the originally determined direction until it has gone ‘back’ all of the distance it wandered from its nest.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是根据文章内容，当Cataglyphis属的蚂蚁被带到另一个地点时，它会做出什么反应。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"ant of Cataglyphis\"和\"taken to another location\"可以定位到D段中描述蚂蚁行为的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，即使科学家将一只蚂蚁放在完全不同的位置，这只昆虫也会固执地沿着最初确定的方向前进，直到它“返回”了从巢穴出发的所有距离。这说明蚂蚁在被带到另一个地点后，会继续按照原来的方向移动。因此，正确答案是C。","options":["It changes the orientation sensors improving.","It releases biological scent for help from others.","It continues to move by the original orientation.","It totally gets lost once disturbed."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64345","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-21\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 19-21 on your answer sheet."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8902:64346:20","type":"choice","text":"Which of the followings is true about ‘cognitive map’ in this passage?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Neurobiologists and cognitive psychologists do call the portion of our memory that controls navigation a ‘cognitive map’.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问关于“认知地图”的哪个陈述是正确的。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的“cognitive map”定位到G段中提到“cognitive map”的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文，神经生物学家和认知心理学家确实将控制导航的记忆部分称为‘认知地图’。可以确定认知地图是由大脑记忆管理的，因此选项D是正确的。选项A、B、C在文中均未提及或与原文内容不符。","options":["There is no obvious difference contrast by real map.","It exists in our head and is always correct.","It only exists under some cultures.","It was managed by brain memory."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64346","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-21\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 19-21 on your answer sheet."},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8902:64347:21","type":"choice","text":"Which of the following description of way findings correctly reflects the function of the cognitive map?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It may be more like a hierarchical structure of relationships. To get back to Grand Central, you first envision the large scale – that is, you visualize the general direction of the station.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目下列对认知地图功能的描述中，哪一项正确反映了其作用。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“cognitive map”定位到H段，该段讨论了认知地图的概念和功能。\n解题思路：H段提到认知地图更像是一种层次结构的关系，而不是字面上的地图。文中明确指出，在返回格兰德中央车站时，首先会“envision the large scale”并“visualize the general direction of the station”，这与选项A“它在大范围内可视化虚拟路线”的描述完全一致。其他选项B、C、D分别提到地标细节、观察的重要性以及商店或超市的存在，这些在原文中并未作为认知地图的功能进行描述，因此排除。","options":["It visualizes a virtual route in a large scope.","It reproduces an exact detail of every landmark.","Observation plays a more important role.","Store or supermarket is a must in the map."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64347","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-21\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 19-21 on your answer sheet."},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8902:64348:22","type":"choice","text":"Biological navigation has a state of flexibility.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The human positioning system is flexible and capable of learning.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“生物导航具有灵活性”这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Biological navigation\"和\"flexibility\"定位到A段，该段提到了\"human positioning system is flexible\"。\n解题思路：原文明确指出人类的定位系统既灵活又具备学习能力，这与题目中的\"Biological navigation has a state of flexibility\"意思完全一致。因此，题目陈述与原文信息相符，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64348","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8902:64349:23","type":"choice","text":"You will always receive a good reaction when you ask direction.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：If you ask passersby for help, most likely you will receive information in many different forms.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“问路时你总会得到积极回应”这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“ask direction”定位到C段，该段描述了向路人问路时可能得到的回应。\n解题思路：C段提到向路人问路时，可能会得到不同的回应，但并未明确说明所有人都会积极回应，没有提到他们的态度会是什么样的。因此，题目中的“always receive a good reaction”在原文中没有明确支持或反驳，属于信息缺失。答案为Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64349","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8902:64350:24","type":"choice","text":"When someone follows a route, he or she collects comprehensive perceptional information in mind\non the way.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：As you move, your brain gathers data from your environment – sights, sounds, smells, lighting, muscle contractions, a sense of time passing – to determine which way your body has gone.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“某人沿着路线行进时，他/她在途中会在脑海中收集全面的感知信息”是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“follows a route”和“comprehensive perceptional information”可以定位到E段，该段描述了人在移动时大脑如何收集环境信息。\n解题思路：E段明确指出，当人移动时，大脑会从环境中收集各种感觉信息，如视觉、听觉、嗅觉、光线、肌肉收缩和时间流逝的感觉，以确定身体的移动方向。这与题目中描述的“在脑海中收集全面的感觉信息”完全一致，因此题目陈述与文章信息一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64350","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8902:64351:25","type":"choice","text":"Path integration requires more thought from brain compared with route-following.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The route-following navigation strategy truly challenges the brain. We have to keep all the landmark and intermediate directions in our head. It is the most detailed and therefore most reliable method, but it can be undone by routine memory lapses. With path integration, our cognitive memory is less burdened; it has to deal with only a few general instructions and the homing vector.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“与路线跟随相比，路径整合需要大脑进行更多思考”是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“Path integration”和“route-following”定位到F段，该段对比了路径整合和路线跟随两种导航策略。\n解题思路：根据原文，这种导航策略对大脑提出了极大挑战：需要将所有地标和中间指引都储存在记忆中。虽然这是最精细且最可靠的方法，但日常记忆缺失仍可能破坏其有效性。相比之下，路径整合对认知记忆的负担较轻，仅需处理少量通用指令和归巢向量。题目说路径整合需要更多的思考，与原文信息相反，因此答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64351","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8902:64352:26","type":"choice","text":"In a familiar surrounding, an exact map of where you are will automatically emerge in your head.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In this hierarchical, or nested, scheme, positions and distances are relative, in contrast with a road map, where the same information is shown in a geometrically precise scale.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问“在一个熟悉的环境中，你头脑中会自动出现一个精确的地图”，是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的核心词“exact map”（精确地图）和“automatically emerge in your head”（自动出现在头脑中）定位到H段。\n解题思路：H段提到，认知地图本质上是一种隐喻，更接近于层级结构，这种层级嵌套的结构中，位置与距离都是相对的，这与道路地图形成鲜明对比——后者会以几何精确的比例展示相同信息。题目声称“出现一个精确的地图”，但原文指出认知地图不是字面意义上的精确地图，因此题干与原文信息矛盾，答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64352","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64344","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Guidance\nB Path integration\nC Route following","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> Guidance <br/></p><p><strong>B</strong> Path integration <br/></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>C</strong> Route following <br/></p><p><strong>14</strong> using basic direction from starting point and light intensity to move on <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"64345","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-21\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 19-21 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What does the ant of Cataglyphis respond if it has been taken to another location according to the passage?</strong></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"64346","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-21\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 19-21 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Which of the followings is true about ‘cognitive map’ in this passage?</strong></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"64347","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-21\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 19-21 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Which of the following description of way findings correctly reflects the function of the cognitive map?</strong></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"64348","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Biological navigation has a state of flexibility.</strong></p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"64349","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>You will always receive a good reaction when you ask direction.</strong></p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"64350","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>When someone follows a route, he or she collects comprehensive perceptional information in mind\non the way.</strong></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"64351","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Path integration requires more thought from brain compared with route-following.</strong></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"64352","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>In a familiar surrounding, an exact map of where you are will automatically emerge in your head.</strong></p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Finding Our Way</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘Drive 200 yards, and then turn right,’ says the car’s computer voice. You relax in the driver’s seat, follow the directions and reach your destination without error. It’s certainly nice to have the Global Positioning System (GPS) to direct you to within a few yards of your goal. Yet if the satellite service’s digital maps become even slightly outdated, you can become lost. Then you have to rely on the ancient human skill of navigating in three-dimensional space. Luckily, your biological finder has an important advantage over GPS: it does not go awry if only one part of the guidance system goes wrong, because it works in various ways. You can ask questions of people on the sidewalk. Or follow a street that looks familiar. Or rely on a navigational rubric: ‘If I keep the East River on my left, I will eventually cross 34th Street.’ The human positioning system is flexible and capable of learning. Anyone who knows the way from point A to point B – and from A to C – can probably figure out how to get from B to C, too.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>But how does this complex cognitive system really work? Researchers are looking at several strategies people use to orient themselves in space: guidance, path integration and route following. We may use all three or combinations thereof. And as experts learn more about these navigational skills, they are making the case that our abilities may underlie our powers of memory and logical thinking. Grand Central, Please Imagine that you have arrived in a place you have never visited – New York City. You get off the train at Grand Central Terminal in midtown Manhattan. You have a few hours to explore before you must return for your ride home. You head uptown to see popular spots you have been told about: Rockefeller Center, Central Park, the Metropolitan Museum of Art. You meander in and out of shops along the way. Suddenly, it is time to get back to the station. But how?</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>If you ask passersby for help, most likely you will receive information in many different forms. A person who orients herself by a prominent landmark would gesture southward: ‘Look down there. See the tall, broad MetLife Building? Head for that – the station is right below it.’ Neurologists call this navigational approach ‘guidance’, meaning that landmark visible from a distance serves as the marker for one’s destination.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Another city dweller might say: ‘What places do you remember passing? … Okay. Go toward the end of Central Park, then walk down to St. Patrick’s Cathedral. A few more blocks and Grand Central will be off to your left.’ In this case, you are pointed toward the most recent place you recall, and you aim for it. Once there you head for the next notable place and so on, retracing your path. Your brain is adding together the individual legs of your trek into a cumulative progress report. Researchers call this strategy ‘path integration’. Many animals rely primarily on path integration to get around, including insects, spiders, crabs and rodents. The desert ants of the genus Cataglyphis employ this method to return from foraging as far as 100 yards away. They note the general direction they came from and retrace their steps, using the polarization of sunlight to orient themselves even under overcast skies. On their way back they are faithful to this inner homing vector. Even when a scientist picks up an ant and puts it in a totally different spot, the insect stubbornly proceeds in the originally determined direction until it has gone ‘back’ all of the distance it wandered from its nest. Only then does the ant realize it has not succeeded, and it begins to walk in successively larger loops to find its way home.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Whether it is trying to get back to the anthill or the train station, any animal using path integration must keep track of its own movements so it knows, while returning, which segments it has already completed. As you move, your brain gathers data from your environment – sights, sounds, smells, lighting, muscle contractions, a sense of time passing – to determine which way your body has gone. The church spire, the sizzling sausages on that vendor’s grill, the open courtyard, and the train station – all represent snapshots of memorable junctures during your journey.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In addition to guidance and path integration, we use a third method for finding our way. An office worker you approach for help on a Manhattan street corner might say: ‘Walk straight down Fifth, turn left on 47th, turn right on Park, go through the walkway under the Helmsley Building, then cross the street to the MetLife Building into Grand Central.’ This strategy, called route following, uses landmarks such as buildings and street names, plus directions – straight, turn, go through – for reaching intermediate points. Route following is more precise than guidance or path integration, but if you forget the details and take a wrong turn, the only way to recover is to backtrack until you reach a familiar spot, because you do not know the general direction or have a reference landmark for your goal. The route-following navigation strategy truly challenges the brain. We have to keep all the landmark and intermediate directions in our head. It is the most detailed and therefore most reliable method, but it can be undone by routine memory lapses. With path integration, our cognitive memory is less burdened; it has to deal with only a few general instructions and the homing vector. Path integration works because it relies most fundamentally on our knowledge of our body’s general direction of movement, and we always have access to these inputs. Nevertheless, people often choose to give route-following directions, in part because saying “Go straight that way!” just does not work in our complex, man-made surroundings.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Road Map or Metaphor? On your next visit to Manhattan, you will rely on your memory to get around. Most likely you will use guidance, path integration and route following in various combinations. But how exactly do these constructs deliver concrete direction? Do we humans have, as an image of the real world, a kind of road map in our heads – with symbols for cities, train stations and churches; thick lines for highways; narrow lines for local streets? Neurobiologists and cognitive psychologists do call the portion of our memory that controls navigation a ‘cognitive map’. The map metaphor is obviously seductive: maps are the easiest way to present geographic information for convenient visual inspection. In many cultures, maps were developed before writing, and today they are used in almost every society. It is even possible that maps derive from a universal way in which our spatial-memory networks are wired.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Yet the notion of a literal map in our heads may be misleading; a growing body of research implies that the cognitive map is mostly a metaphor. It may be more like a hierarchical structure of relationships. To get back to Grand Central, you first envision the large scale – that is, you visualize the general direction of the station. Within that system, you then imagine the route to the last place you remember. After that, you observe your nearby surroundings to pick out a recognizable storefront or street corner that will send you toward that place. In this hierarchical, or nested, scheme, positions and distances are relative, in contrast with a road map, where the same information is shown in a geometrically precise scale.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8902&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8903","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Music: Language We All Speak","book":"阅读还原集Vol.18","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.18 · Test 2 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8903:64353:27","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：After all, music isn't necessary for getting through the day, and if it aids in reproduction, it does so only in highly indirect ways. Language, by contrast, is also everywhere – but for reasons that are more obvious.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求为A段选择一个合适的标题，从给定的标题中选择。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读，可以定位到关键信息是关于音乐和语言，以及科学家对两者关系的兴趣。\n解题思路：这部分主要讨论了音乐和语言的不同作用，及其在学术界的地位。首段明确说明音乐和语言之间的对比，后又说明两者的不同地位，语言长期被视为解锁人类智能机制的关键，而音乐则普遍被视为进化论的装饰品。因此，最合适的标题是“Contrast between music and language”（音乐和语言的对比）。","options":["Communication in music with animals","Recent research on music","Culture embedded in music","Historical theories review","New discoveries on animal music","Contrast between music and language","Questions on a biological link with human and music","Music is good for babies."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"64353","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nThe reading passage has five sections, A-E Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-viii, in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8903:64353:28","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But thanks to a decade-long ware of neuroscience research, that tune is changing. A flurry of recent publications suggests that language and music may equally be able to tell us who we are and where we’re from – not just emotionally, but biologically.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求为B段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读，找到段落的主旨句或关键信息点，通常在段落开头或结尾。\n解题思路：这一部分首先提到神经科学研究正在改变人们对音乐和语言关系的看法，指出语言和音乐可能同样能够揭示我们的身份和起源，随后回顾历史音乐理论，强调音乐本身具有普遍性特征，接着提到2500年前，毕达哥拉斯的发现。因此，这部分主要讨论的是历史上的音乐理论研究。因此，标题“Historical theories review”（历史理论综述）最合适。","options":["Communication in music with animals","Recent research on music","Culture embedded in music","Historical theories review","New discoveries on animal music","Contrast between music and language","Questions on a biological link with human and music","Music is good for babies."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"64353","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nThe reading passage has five sections, A-E Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-viii, in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8903:64353:29","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Neither idea is right, according to David Schwartz and his colleagues. Human musical preferences are fundamentally shaped not by elegant algorithms or ration but by the messy sounds of real life, and of speech in particular... Schwartz, Howe, and Purves analyzed a vast selection of speech sounds from a variety of languages to reveal the underlying patterns common to all utterances...\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求为C段选择正确的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读Section C，定位到其中关于David Schwartz及其同事的最新研究、发现和理论的内容。\n解题思路：Section C的核心内容是介绍David Schwartz及其团队的最新研究。该部分首先驳斥了传统的“音乐是数学”和“音乐完全抽象”的观点，然后详细描述了他们的研究方法，得出“音乐的基本要素存在于言语中”这一结论。整个部分都在集中阐述一项近期的、颠覆传统认知的科学研究及其发现。因此，它与列表中的标题Recent research on music（关于音乐的最新研究）完全匹配。","options":["Communication in music with animals","Recent research on music","Culture embedded in music","Historical theories review","New discoveries on animal music","Contrast between music and language","Questions on a biological link with human and music","Music is good for babies."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"64353","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nThe reading passage has five sections, A-E Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-viii, in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8903:64353:30","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But what’s been played to the animals, Schwartz notes, is human music. If animals evolve preferences for sound as we do – based upon the soundscape in which they live – then their ‘music’ would be fundamentally different from ours... To demonstrate that animals don’t appreciate sounds the way we do, we’d need evidence that they don’t respond to ‘music’ constructed from their own sound environment.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求为D段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读Section D，可以发现主要讲的是动物对音乐的感知、理解以及相关发现和。\n解题思路：Section D的核心内容是探讨动物是否理解和欣赏音乐。它首先引述了以往研究的观点，即许多实验室动物对人类音乐不感兴趣。最后引出Schwartz提出的新视角和新发现：他指出，过去给动物听的是“人类的音乐”；如果动物的声音偏好也像人类一样，是基于它们自身所处的声音环境演化而来的，那么它们的“音乐”将与我们的根本不同。这是一个关于动物音乐认知的新的、突破性的发现和理论方向。因此，它与列表中的标题 New discoveries on animal music（关于动物音乐的新发现）完全匹配。","options":["Communication in music with animals","Recent research on music","Culture embedded in music","Historical theories review","New discoveries on animal music","Contrast between music and language","Questions on a biological link with human and music","Music is good for babies."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"64353","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nThe reading passage has five sections, A-E Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-viii, in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8903:64353:31","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：No matter how the connection between language and music is parsed, what is apparent is that our sense of music, even our love for it, is as deeply rooted in our biology and in our brains as language is.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求为E段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读Section E，可以看出这一段主要讨论的是音乐与人类生物学、大脑的关联。\n解题思路：Section E的核心内容是阐述音乐感与人类生物学和大脑的深层联系。该部分明确指出，我们对音乐的感觉和热爱，如同语言一样，深深植根于我们的生物学基础和大脑结构之中。为了证明这一点，文章进一步以婴儿为例，说明母亲对婴儿使用的“音乐化言语”是一种跨文化的普遍现象，这揭示了音乐与人类早期沟通和生物学需求之间的本质关联。整个部分都在探讨和确认音乐与人类之间存在的生物学联系。因此，它与列表中的标题 Questions on a biological link with human and music（人与音乐的生物学联系）匹配。","options":["Communication in music with animals","Recent research on music","Culture embedded in music","Historical theories review","New discoveries on animal music","Contrast between music and language","Questions on a biological link with human and music","Music is good for babies."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"64353","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nThe reading passage has five sections, A-E Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-viii, in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8903:64354:32","type":"choice","text":"32 Steven Pinker","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：While language has long been considered essential to unlocking the mechanisms of human intelligence, music is generally treated as an evolutionary frippery – mere ‘auditory cheesecake’, as the Harvard cognitive scientist Steven Pinker puts it.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是哪一项是Steven Pinker的观点或陈述。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的Steven Pinker定位到A段最后一句话，其中明确提到了他的观点。\n解题思路：根据原文中Steven Pinker的话，他提到，语言长期被视为解锁人类智能机制的关键，而音乐则普遍被视作进化论的装饰品，说明与语言相比，音乐没有得到同等的重视。这与选项F的描述“Music is not treated equally well compared with the language.”完全一致。因此，答案为F。","options":["Music exists outside of the world in which it is created.","Music has a common feature though cultural influences affect.","Humans need music.","Music priority connects to the disordered sound around.","Discovery of mathematical musical foundation.","Music is not treated equally well compared with the language.","Humans and monkeys have similar traits in perceiving sound."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64354","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nLook at the following people and list of statements below. Match each person with the correct statement. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.\nList of Statements\nA Music exists outside of the world in which it is created.\nB Music has a common feature though cultural influences affect.\nC Humans need music.\nD Music priority connects to the disordered sound around.\nE Discovery of mathematical musical foundation.\nF Music is not treated equally well compared with the language.\nG Humans and monkeys have similar traits in perceiving sound."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8903:64354:33","type":"choice","text":"33 Musicologists","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：First, musicologists have long emphasized that while each culture stamps a special identity onto its music; the music itself has some universal qualities.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是哪一项是音乐学家们的观点或陈述。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"Musicologists\"定位到Section B 中音乐学家观点的句子。\n解题思路：Section B中提到音乐学家们长期强调，虽然不同文化都会在音乐中烙下独特的印记，但音乐本身却具有普遍特性，再用具体例子说明该观点，与B项（虽然文化会影响音乐，但音乐仍具有共性）描述一致，因此，答案为B。","options":["Music exists outside of the world in which it is created.","Music has a common feature though cultural influences affect.","Humans need music.","Music priority connects to the disordered sound around.","Discovery of mathematical musical foundation.","Music is not treated equally well compared with the language.","Humans and monkeys have similar traits in perceiving sound."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64354","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nLook at the following people and list of statements below. Match each person with the correct statement. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.\nList of Statements\nA Music exists outside of the world in which it is created.\nB Music has a common feature though cultural influences affect.\nC Humans need music.\nD Music priority connects to the disordered sound around.\nE Discovery of mathematical musical foundation.\nF Music is not treated equally well compared with the language.\nG Humans and monkeys have similar traits in perceiving sound."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8903:64354:34","type":"choice","text":"34 Greek philosopher Pythagoras","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Some 2,500 years ago, Pythagoras was the first to note a direct relationship between the harmoniousness of a tone combination and the physical dimensions of the object that produced it. For example, a plucked string will always play an octave lower than a similar string half its size, and a fifth lower than a similar string two-thirds it’s length. This link between simple ratios and harmony has influenced music theory ever since.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是哪一项是希腊哲学家毕达哥拉斯的观点或陈述。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"Pythagoras\"和\"Greek philosopher\"定位到Section B中论述毕达哥拉斯的发现的部分。\n解题思路：原文提到，2500年前，毕达哥拉斯首次发现音调组合的和谐性与其产生物体的物理尺寸之间存在直接关联。发现了简单比率（如弦长比例）与和声之间的联系。这一发现正是对“音乐数学基础”的探索。因此，陈述E “Discovery of mathematical musical foundation”（发现音乐的数学基础）准确地概括了毕达哥拉斯的成就。这与题干中的信息一致，因此答案为E。","options":["Music exists outside of the world in which it is created.","Music has a common feature though cultural influences affect.","Humans need music.","Music priority connects to the disordered sound around.","Discovery of mathematical musical foundation.","Music is not treated equally well compared with the language.","Humans and monkeys have similar traits in perceiving sound."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64354","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nLook at the following people and list of statements below. Match each person with the correct statement. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.\nList of Statements\nA Music exists outside of the world in which it is created.\nB Music has a common feature though cultural influences affect.\nC Humans need music.\nD Music priority connects to the disordered sound around.\nE Discovery of mathematical musical foundation.\nF Music is not treated equally well compared with the language.\nG Humans and monkeys have similar traits in perceiving sound."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8903:64354:35","type":"choice","text":"35 Schwartz, Howe, and Purves","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Neither idea is right, according to David Schwartz and his colleagues. Human musical preferences are fundamentally shaped not by elegant algorithms or ration but by the messy sounds of real life, and of speech in particular – which in turn is shaped by our evolutionary heritage. ‘The explanation of music, like the explanation of any product of the mind, must be rooted in biology, not in numbers per se,’ says Schwartz.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求匹配Schwartz, Howe, and Purves的观点。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“Schwartz, Howe, and Purves”定位到C段，找到他们分析语音的研究及其观点。\n解题思路：原文提到，Schwartz, Howe, 和Purves认为人类的音乐偏好并非由优雅的算法或比率决定，而是从根本上由现实生活中的声音，特别是言语这种“纷乱的声音”所塑造。他们通过分析大量语音片段，发现音乐的基本要素存在于言语之中。这与陈述D “Music priority connects to the disordered sound around”（音乐主要与周围纷乱的声音有关）一致。因此，答案是D。","options":["Music exists outside of the world in which it is created.","Music has a common feature though cultural influences affect.","Humans need music.","Music priority connects to the disordered sound around.","Discovery of mathematical musical foundation.","Music is not treated equally well compared with the language.","Humans and monkeys have similar traits in perceiving sound."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64354","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nLook at the following people and list of statements below. Match each person with the correct statement. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.\nList of Statements\nA Music exists outside of the world in which it is created.\nB Music has a common feature though cultural influences affect.\nC Humans need music.\nD Music priority connects to the disordered sound around.\nE Discovery of mathematical musical foundation.\nF Music is not treated equally well compared with the language.\nG Humans and monkeys have similar traits in perceiving sound."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8903:64354:36","type":"choice","text":"36 Marc Hauser and Josh McDermott","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Marc Hauser and Josh McDermott of Harvard argued in the July issue of Nature Neuroscience that animals don’t create or perceive music the way we do. The act that laboratory monkeys can show recognition of human tunes is evidence, they say, of shared general features of the auditory system, not any specific chimpanzee musical ability.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求匹配Marc Hauser and Josh McDermott的观点。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Marc Hauser and Josh McDermott\"定位到D段中他们的观点。\n解题思路：原文提到，哈佛大学的马克·豪瑟与乔什·麦克德莫特在《自然神经科学》七月刊中提出，动物并不像人类那样创造或感知音乐。实验室猴子能识别人类曲调的行为，实则是它们与人类听觉系统具有相似特征，而非黑猩猩特有的音乐能力。这与选项G的内容相符，即\"人类与猴子在声音感知方面具有相似特征\"，因此，答案为G。","options":["Music exists outside of the world in which it is created.","Music has a common feature though cultural influences affect.","Humans need music.","Music priority connects to the disordered sound around.","Discovery of mathematical musical foundation.","Music is not treated equally well compared with the language.","Humans and monkeys have similar traits in perceiving sound."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64354","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nLook at the following people and list of statements below. Match each person with the correct statement. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.\nList of Statements\nA Music exists outside of the world in which it is created.\nB Music has a common feature though cultural influences affect.\nC Humans need music.\nD Music priority connects to the disordered sound around.\nE Discovery of mathematical musical foundation.\nF Music is not treated equally well compared with the language.\nG Humans and monkeys have similar traits in perceiving sound."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8903:64354:37","type":"choice","text":"37 Charles Rosen","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Writing recently in The New York Review of Books, pianist and critic Charles Rosen discussed the long-standing notion that while painting and sculpture reproduce at least some aspects of the natural world, and writing describes thoughts and feelings we are all familiar with, music is entirely abstracted from the world in which we live.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求将人物Charles Rosen与对应的陈述匹配。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的人名\"Charles Rosen\"定位到C段，找到包含该人名的句子。\n解题思路：原文提到，钢琴家兼评论家查尔斯·罗森近期在《纽约书评》撰文讨论了一个长期存在的观念，尽管绘画和雕塑至少再现了自然世界的某些方面，文字描述了我们熟悉的思维与情感，但音乐却完全脱离了我们生活的现实世界。说明他认为音乐存在于我们生活的世界之外，因此，Charles Rosen的陈述对应的是A。","options":["Music exists outside of the world in which it is created.","Music has a common feature though cultural influences affect.","Humans need music.","Music priority connects to the disordered sound around.","Discovery of mathematical musical foundation.","Music is not treated equally well compared with the language.","Humans and monkeys have similar traits in perceiving sound."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64354","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nLook at the following people and list of statements below. Match each person with the correct statement. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.\nList of Statements\nA Music exists outside of the world in which it is created.\nB Music has a common feature though cultural influences affect.\nC Humans need music.\nD Music priority connects to the disordered sound around.\nE Discovery of mathematical musical foundation.\nF Music is not treated equally well compared with the language.\nG Humans and monkeys have similar traits in perceiving sound."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8903:64354:38","type":"choice","text":"38 Sandra Trehub","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The upshot, says Trehub, is that music maybe even more of a necessity than we realize.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求将Sandra Trehub与正确的陈述匹配。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Sandra Trehub\"定位到文章中的E段，该段提到了Trehub的研究和观点。\n解题思路：E段中明确提到了Sandra Trehub的研究内容和观点，包括婴儿对音乐和语言的理解，以及母亲使用音乐性语言与婴儿交流的方式，总结道，音乐对人类的必要性可能比我们意识到的更为重要。这些内容与选项C（人类需要音乐）的陈述相符，因此答案为C。","options":["Music exists outside of the world in which it is created.","Music has a common feature though cultural influences affect.","Humans need music.","Music priority connects to the disordered sound around.","Discovery of mathematical musical foundation.","Music is not treated equally well compared with the language.","Humans and monkeys have similar traits in perceiving sound."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64354","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nLook at the following people and list of statements below. Match each person with the correct statement. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.\nList of Statements\nA Music exists outside of the world in which it is created.\nB Music has a common feature though cultural influences affect.\nC Humans need music.\nD Music priority connects to the disordered sound around.\nE Discovery of mathematical musical foundation.\nF Music is not treated equally well compared with the language.\nG Humans and monkeys have similar traits in perceiving sound."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8903:64355:39","type":"choice","text":"Why was the study of animal’s music uncertain?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But what’s been played to the animals, Schwartz notes, is human music. If animals evolve preferences for sound as we do – based upon the soundscape in which they live – then their ‘music’ would be fundamentally different from ours. In the same way, our scales derive from human utterances, a cat’s idea of a good tune would derive from yowls and meows. To demonstrate that animals don’t appreciate sounds the way we do, we’d need evidence that they don’t respond to ‘music’ constructed from their own sound environment.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问为什么对动物音乐的研究存在不确定性。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"animal's music\"和\"uncertain\"定位到D段后半部分，尤其是关于动物音乐实验的描述。\n解题思路：原文指出，给动物播放的是人类音乐，而动物的\"音乐\"是基于它们自己的声音环境的。因此，要证明动物不会欣赏音乐，需要用它们自己的声音环境构造的\"音乐\"进行测试。这说明对动物音乐的研究的不确定性是因为实验的局限性，没有用适合动物的声音环境进行测试。因此，正确答案是B。","options":["Animals don’t have the same auditory system as humans.","Experiments on animal’s music are limited.","tunes are impossible for the animal to make up.","Animals don’t have the spontaneous ability for the tests."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64355","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 39-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 39-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8903:64356:40","type":"choice","text":"What is the main subject of this passage?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：无\n对应段落：全文\n审题：题目问文章的主要主题是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读全文，可以定位到文章的核心内容集中在音乐和语言的关系，以及音乐对于人类的意义。\n解题思路：文章开头提到音乐是人类普遍的能力，随后探讨音乐与语言的关系，再通过历史理论回顾、最新科学研究、动物音乐比较和婴儿研究，多维度论证了音乐并非文化附属品，而是与语言一样根植于人类生物学和大脑的深层需求。最终结论强调音乐是人类社会的必需品。因此，文章的核心主题是音乐在人类社会中的角色，选择C项。","options":["Language and psychology","Music formation","Role of music in human society","Music experiments for animals"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64356","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 39-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 39-40 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64353","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nThe reading passage has five sections, A-E Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-viii, in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"64354","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nLook at the following people and list of statements below. Match each person with the correct statement. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.\nList of Statements\nA Music exists outside of the world in which it is created.\nB Music has a common feature though cultural influences affect.\nC Humans need music.\nD Music priority connects to the disordered sound around.\nE Discovery of mathematical musical foundation.\nF Music is not treated equally well compared with the language.\nG Humans and monkeys have similar traits in perceiving sound.","html":"<p>List of Statements&nbsp;</p><p><strong>A</strong> Music exists outside of the world in which it is created.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>B</strong> Music has a common feature though cultural influences affect.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>C</strong> Humans need music.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>D</strong> Music priority connects to the disordered sound around.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>E</strong> Discovery of mathematical musical foundation.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>F</strong> Music is not treated equally well compared with the language.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>G</strong> Humans and monkeys have similar traits in perceiving sound.</p><p><strong>32</strong> Steven Pinker <strong class=\"source-blank\">[32] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"64355","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 39-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 39-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Why was the study of animal’s music uncertain?</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"64356","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 39-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 39-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is the main subject of this passage?</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Music: Language We All Speak&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;Section A:&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Music is one of the human species&#39;s relatively few universal abilities. Without formal training, any individual, from Stone Age tribesman to suburban teenager has the ability to recognize music and, in some fashion, to make it. Why this should be so is a mystery. After all, music isn&#39;t necessary for getting through the day, and if it aids in reproduction, it does so only in highly indirect ways. Language, by contrast, is also everywhere – but for reasons that are more obvious. With language, you and the members of your tribe can organize a migration across Africa, build reed boats and cross the seas, and communicate at night even when you can&#39;t see each other. Modern culture, in all its technological extravagance, springs directly from the human talent for manipulating symbols and syntax.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Scientists have always been intrigued by the connection between music and language. Yet over the years, words and melody have acquired a vastly different status in the lab and the seminar room. While language has long been considered essential to unlocking the mechanisms of human intelligence, music is generally treated as an evolutionary frippery – mere ‘auditory cheesecake’, as the Harvard cognitive scientist Steven Pinker puts it.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;Section B:&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>But thanks to a decade-long ware of neuroscience research, that tune is changing. A flurry of recent publications suggests that language and music may equally be able to tell us who we are and where we’re from – not just emotionally, but biologically. In July, the journal Nature Neuroscience devoted a special issue to the topic. And in an article in the August 6 issue of the Journal of Neuroscience, David Schwartz, Catherine Howe, and Dale Purves of Duke University argued that the sounds of music and the sounds of language are intricately connected.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>To grasp the originality of this idea, it’s necessary to realize two things about how music has traditionally been understood. First, musicologists have long emphasized that while each culture stamps a special identity onto its music; the music itself has some universal qualities. For example, in virtually all cultures sound is divided into some or all of the 12 intervals that make up the chromatic scale – that is, the scale represented by the keys on a piano. For centuries, observers have attributed this preference for certain combinations of tones to the mathematical properties of sound itself.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Some 2,500 years ago, Pythagoras was the first to note a direct relationship between the harmoniousness of a tone combination and the physical dimensions of the object that produced it. For example, a plucked string will always play an octave lower than a similar string half its size, and a fifth lower than a similar string two-thirds it’s length. This link between simple ratios and harmony has influenced music theory ever since.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;Section C:&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>This music-is-math idea often accompanied by the notion that music formally speaking at least exists apart from the world in which it was created. Writing recently in The New York Review of Books, pianist and critic Charles Rosen discussed the long-standing notion that while painting and sculpture reproduce at least some aspects of the natural world, and writing describes thoughts and feelings we are all familiar with, music is entirely abstracted from the world in which we live. Neither idea is right, according to David Schwartz and his colleagues. Human musical preferences are fundamentally shaped not by elegant algorithms or ration but by the messy sounds of real life, and of speech in particular – which in turn is shaped by our evolutionary heritage. ‘The explanation of music, like the explanation of any product of the mind, must be rooted in biology, not in numbers per se,’ says Schwartz.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Schwartz, Howe, and Purves analyzed a vast selection of speech sounds from a variety of languages to reveal the underlying patterns common to all utterances. In order to focus only on the raw sound, they discarded all theories about speech and meaning and sliced sentences into random bites. Using a database of over 100,000 brief segments of speech, they noted which frequency had the greatest emphasis in each sound. The resulting set of frequencies, they discovered, corrsponded closely to the chromatic scale. In short, the building blocks of music are to be found in speech.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Far from being abstract, music presents a strange analogue to the patterns created by the sounds of speech. ‘Music, like the visual arts, is rooted in our experience of the natural world,’ says Schwartz. ‘It emulates our sound environment in the way that visual arts emulate the visual environment.’ In music, we hear the echo of our basic sound-making instrument – the vocal tract. The explanation for human music is simple; still than Pythagoras’s mathematical equations. We like the sounds that are familiar to us – specifically, we like sounds that remind us of us.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>This brings up some chicken-or-egg evolutionary questions. It may be that music imitates speech directly, the researchers say, in which case it would seem that language evolved first. It’s also conceivable that music came first and language is in effect an Imitation of the song – that in everyday speech we hit the musical notes we especially like. Alternately, it may be that music imitates the general products of the human sound-making system, which just happens to be mostly speech. ‘We can’t know this,’ says Schwartz. ‘What we do know is that they both come from the same system, and it is this that shapes our preferences.’&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;Section D:&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Schwartz’s study also casts light on the long-running question of whether animals understand or appreciate music. Despite the apparent abundance of “music” in the natural world – birdsong, whalesong, wolf howls, synchronized chimpanzee hooting previous studies have found that many laboratory animals don’t show a great affinity for the human variety of music-making.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Marc Hauser and Josh McDermott of Harvard argued in the July issue of Nature Neuroscience that animals don’t create or perceive music the way we do. The act that laboratory monkeys can show recognition of human tunes is evidence, they say, of shared general features of the auditory system, not any specific chimpanzee musical ability. As for birds, those most musical beasts, they generally recognize their own tunes – a narrow repertoire – but don’t generate novel melodies as we do. There are no avian Mozarts.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>But what’s been played to the animals, Schwartz notes, is human music. If animals evolve preferences for sound as we do – based upon the soundscape in which they live – then their ‘music’ would be fundamentally different from ours. In the same way, our scales derive from human utterances, a cat’s idea of a good tune would derive from yowls and meows. To demonstrate that animals don’t appreciate sounds the way we do, we’d need evidence that they don’t respond to ‘music’ constructed from their own sound environment.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;Section E:&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>No matter how the connection between language and music is parsed, what is apparent is that our sense of music, even our love for it, is as deeply rooted in our biology and in our brains as language is. This is most obvious with babies, says Sandra Trehub at the University of Toronto, who also published a paper in the Nature Neuroscience special issue.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>For babies, music and speech are on a continuum. ‘Mothers use musical speech to “regulate infants” emotional states.’ Trehub says. Regardless of what language they speak, the voice all mothers use with babies is the same: ‘something between speech and song.’ This kind of communication ‘puts the baby in a trance-like state, which may proceed to sleep or extended periods of rapture.’ So if the babies of the world could understand the latest research on language and music, they probably wouldn’t be very surprised. The upshot, says Trehub, is that music maybe even more of a necessity than we realize.&amp;#</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px; text-align: center;\"><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8903&scene=%E8%AF%AD%E8%A8%80%E6%95%99%E8%82%B2&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8884","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Human Remain in GREEN SAHARA","book":"阅读还原集Vol.18","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.18 · Test 1 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8884:64273:1","type":"choice","text":"Hettwer accidently found human remains in the desert.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The dunes were spilling over with bones. He took a few shots with his digital camera and hurried back to theLand Rovers. ‘I found some bones,’ Hettwer said, when the team had regrouped, ‘But they’re not dinosaurs. They’re human.’\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问赫特韦意外在沙漠中发现了人类遗骸，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Hettwer\"、\"found human remains\"和\"desert\"定位到B段，找到Hettwer发现骨头并确认是人类遗骸的句子。\n解题思路：根据B段原文，随队摄影师迈克·赫特韦独自朝三座小沙丘走去。刚爬上第一处斜坡，他便惊呆了——沙丘上堆满了骨头。赫特韦确实意外在沙漠中发现了骨头，因此答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64273","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-3\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-3 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8884:64274:2","type":"choice","text":"Sereno and Garcea have cooperated in some archaeological activities before.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But she had never heard of Paul Sereno. His claim to have found so many skeletons in one place seemed farfetched, given that no other Neolithic cemetery contained more than a dozen or so. Some archacologists would later be skeptical; one sniped that he was just a ‘moonlighting paleontologist’. But Garcea was too intrigued to dismiss him as an interloper. She agreed to join him.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是Sereno和Garcea之前合作过一些考古活动，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"Sereno and Garcea\"和\"cooperated in some archaeological activities before\"定位到C段，找到Garcea同意加入Sereno的团队的信息。\n解题思路：C段提到Garcea之前从未听说过Paul Sereno，后来有考古学家讥讽Sereno是‘业余古生物学家’。不过加尔切亚对此深感兴趣，最终同意加入他的研究团队。这表明他们之前没有合作过。因此，答案是False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64274","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-3\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-3 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8884:64275:3","type":"choice","text":"The pictures of rock engravings found in Green Sahara is similar to other places.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：They exhumed eight burials and collected scores of artifacts from both cultures.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“在绿色撒哈拉发现的岩石雕刻的图片与其他地方的相似”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的“rock engravings”和“Green Sahara”是关键信息，需要在文章中寻找关于岩石雕刻的描述。\n解题思路：文章中提到了在Gobero遗址发现了许多人类骨骼和文物，包括鱼钩、鱼叉等，但没有提到任何关于岩石雕刻的信息。因此，无法从文章中得出关于岩石雕刻是否与其他地方相似的结论。所以，答案是“NOT GIVEN”。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64275","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-3\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-3 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8884:64276:4","type":"fill","text":"填写第 4 空","answer":"a map/A Map/a detailed map/A Detailed Map","acceptedAnswers":["a map","A Map","a detailed map","A Detailed Map"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Over the next three weeks, Sereno and Garcea – along with five American excavators, five Tuareg guides, and five soldiers from Niger’s army, sent to protect the camp from bandits – made a detailed map of the site, which they dubbed Gobero, after the Tuareg name for the area.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问在挖掘工作开始前的最初几周，Sereno和Garcea制作了什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"Sereno and Garcea\"和\"initial weeks before digging work\"定位到E段，该段描述了他们在挖掘前所做的准备工作。\n解题思路：E段明确提到在Garcea加入Sereno团队后，他们制作了该遗址的详细地图，接着开始考古工作。因此答案为\"a map\"或\"a detailed map\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64276","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 4-7\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8884:64277:5","type":"fill","text":"填写第 5 空","answer":"radiocarbon dating/Radiocarbon Dating","acceptedAnswers":["radiocarbon dating","Radiocarbon Dating"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In the meantime,he carefully removed one tooth from each of four skulls and sent them to a lab for radiocarbon dating.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是塞雷诺为何将四个头骨各取一颗牙齿送往实验室。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Sereno\", \"tooth\", \"skulls\", \"laboratory\"可以定位到F段，找到塞雷诺将牙齿送到实验室的目的。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到塞雷诺将牙齿送到实验室是为了进行\"radiocarbon dating\"（放射性碳年代测定），这是一种用于确定古生物或文物年代的科学方法。因此答案是“radiocarbon dating”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64277","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 4-7\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8884:64278:6","type":"fill","text":"填写第 6 空","answer":"9000 years old/9000 Years Old/9,000 years old/9,000 Years Old/","acceptedAnswers":["9000 years old","9000 Years Old","9,000 years old","9,000 Years Old"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The results pegged the age of the tightly bundled burials at roughly 9,000 years old, the heart of the Kiffian era.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是较大的紧密堆叠的墓葬被鉴定出有多少年的历史。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"tightly bundled burials\"可以定位到F段中关于墓葬年龄的描述。\n解题思路：根据原文F段中的句子，结果显示，这些紧密堆叠的墓葬距今约9000年，正好处于基菲安时期的核心阶段。可以确定大约距今9000年。因此，答案为9000 years old。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64278","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 4-7\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8884:64279:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"the teeth/The Teeth","acceptedAnswers":["the teeth","The Teeth"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Other scientists are trying to derive DNA from the teeth, which could reveal the genetic origins of the Kiffian and Tenerian – and possibly link them to descendants living today.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是科学家为了找出基菲安人和特内里安人的遗传起源，送检了身体哪个部位的遗骸。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"genetic origins\"和\"Kiffian and Tenerian\"定位到J段，找到科学家试图从哪个部位提取DNA以揭示他们的遗传起源。\n解题思路：根据原文句子，科学家正尝试从牙齿中提取DNA，这可能揭示基菲安人和特内里安人的遗传起源，并可能将他们与当今的后裔联系起来。因此答案为\"teeth\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64279","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 4-7\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8884:64280:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"peaceful/Peaceful","acceptedAnswers":["peaceful","Peaceful"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Judging by the bones, the Kiffian appeared to be a peaceful, hardworking people.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问根据骨骼判断，Kiffian人似乎是什么样的人。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"Kiffian\"和\"bone judgment\"定位到H段，该段提到通过骨骼判断Kiffian人的特征。\n解题思路：H段原文明确提到，从这些遗骨来看，基菲人似乎是一个和平勤劳的民族。其中\"peaceful\"和\"hardworking\"是并列形容词，题目中已给出\"hardworking\"，因此空格处应填入\"peaceful\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64280","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nComplete the summary below, using no more than two words from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8884:64281:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"injuries/Injuries","acceptedAnswers":["injuries","Injuries"],"explanation":"原文答案句： ‘The lack of head and forearm injuries suggests they weren’t doing much fighting,’ he told me, ‘And these guys were strong.’\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是因为在头部和前臂上没有发现什么，所以得出结论，基菲人是一个和平勤劳的民族。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"head and forearm\"是定位的关键信息，通过这两个词可以快速定位到H段。\n解题思路：在H段中，从骨骼特征来看，基菲安人似乎是个崇尚和平、勤勉劳作的族群。“头骨和前臂没有明显损伤，说明他们很少发生肢体冲突，”因此，可以确定因为头部和前臂没有损伤，所以得出结论，基菲人是一个和平勤劳的民族。所以答案为\"injuries\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64281","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nComplete the summary below, using no more than two words from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8884:64282:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"protein/Protein","acceptedAnswers":["protein","Protein"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘That’s the muscle attachment,’ he said, ‘This individual had huge leg muscles, which means he was eating a lot of protein and had a strenuous lifestyle –both consistent with a fishing way of life.’\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问通过观察巨大的腿部肌肉，可以推断出他们的饮食中有大量的什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目的关键词\"observation of the huge leg muscles\"和\"diet\"，在H段中找到对应的句子，其中提到\"eating a lot of protein\"。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，通过观察巨大的腿部肌肉可以推断出这些人摄入了大量的\"protein\"蛋白质，因此，答案为\"protein\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64282","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nComplete the summary below, using no more than two words from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8884:64283:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"strenuous/Strenuous","acceptedAnswers":["strenuous","Strenuous"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘That’s the muscle attachment,’ he said, ‘This individual had huge leg muscles, which means he was eating a lot of protein and had a strenuous lifestyle – both consistent with a fishing way of life.’\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问通过观察巨大的腿部肌肉，可以推断出他们怎样的生活方式。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“lifestyle”，在H段中找到关于生活方式的描述。\n解题思路：原文中提到，科学家通过骨骼分析得出Kiffian人生活艰苦。因此，答案为“strenuous”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64283","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nComplete the summary below, using no more than two words from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8884:64284:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"hunting/Hunting","acceptedAnswers":["hunting","Hunting"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Stojanowski’s assessment that the Tenerian were herders fits the prevailing view among scholars of life in the Sahara 6,000 years ago, when drier conditions favored herding over hunting.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是Stojanowski认为Tenerian更倾向于依靠放牧生存，而非什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词Stojanowski和Tenerian定位到I段，找到句子中提到的herding over hunting。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到Stojanowski认为Tenerian是牧民，与学界普遍认为6000年前撒哈拉地区生活状况的主流观点相吻合——当时干旱环境更有利于放牧而非狩猎。因此，与herding相对的是hunting，所以答案为hunting。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64284","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nComplete the summary below, using no more than two words from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8884:64285:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"cow species/Cow Species","acceptedAnswers":["cow species","Cow Species"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Among the hundreds of animal bones that had turned up at the site, none belonged to goats or sheep, and only three came from a cow species.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是，但只找到了一些动物骨头，例如什么。\n定位关键信息：题目中的“animal bones”和“cow species”是定位的关键词。通过“animal bones”可以定位到I段中描述动物骨头的句子，而“cow species”则直接指向该句中提到的具体动物种类。\n解题思路：根据I段原文句子，在遗址出土的数百具动物骨骼中，没有发现山羊或绵羊的遗骸，仅有三具属于牛科动物。原文明确提到“cow species”是唯一被找到的动物骨头种类之一，因此答案为“cow species”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64285","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nComplete the summary below, using no more than two words from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8884:64286:14","type":"fill","text":"填写第 14 空","answer":"transitional/Transitional","acceptedAnswers":["transitional","Transitional"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Perhaps, Screno reasoned, the Tenerian at Gobero were a transitional group that had not fully adopted herding and still relied heavily on hunting and fishing.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问Sereno认为Gobero的Tenerian人当时属于什么群体。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Sereno\"和\"Tenerian\"定位到I段，找到\"Sereno reasoned, the Tenerian at Gobero were a transitional group\"这句话。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，斯雷诺推测，戈贝罗的特内里安人或许属于过渡群体，他们尚未完全采用放牧方式，仍高度依赖狩猎和捕鱼。Sereno认为Gobero的Tenerian是一个\"transitional group\"，即过渡性群体，因此答案为transitional。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64286","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nComplete the summary below, using no more than two words from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64273","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-3\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-3 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Hettwer accidently found human remains in the desert.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"64274","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-3\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-3 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Sereno and Garcea have cooperated in some archaeological activities before.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"64275","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-3\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-3 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The pictures of rock engravings found in Green Sahara is similar to other places.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"64276","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 4-7\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>4</strong> What did Sereno and Garcea produce in the initial weeks before digging work? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[4] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"64277","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 4-7\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>5</strong> For what purpose did Sereno send one tooth from each of four skulls to the laboratory? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[5] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"64278","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 4-7\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>6</strong> How old is the bigger tightly bundled burials being identified? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[6] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"64279","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 4-7\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>7</strong> What part of the body remains did the scientists send for inspection to find out the genetic origins of the Kiffian and Tenerian? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"64280","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nComplete the summary below, using no more than two words from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>On the basis of bone judgment, kiffican seemed to be a <strong>8</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong> hardworking people,</p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"64281","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nComplete the summary below, using no more than two words from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>because we did not find <strong>9</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong> on head and forearm.</p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"64282","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nComplete the summary below, using no more than two words from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Through observation of the huge leg muscles, it can be inferred that their diet had plenty of <strong>10</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong>,</p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"64283","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nComplete the summary below, using no more than two words from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>and their lifestyle was <strong>11</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong>. All evidence pointed compliance with a\nfishing way of life.</p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"64284","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nComplete the summary below, using no more than two words from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>On the other hand, Stojanowski presumed that Tenerian preferred to live on herding over <strong>12</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong> ，</p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"64285","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nComplete the summary below, using no more than two words from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>but only some animal bones such as <strong>13</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong> were found,</p>","firstNumber":13},{"id":"64286","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nComplete the summary below, using no more than two words from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>which Sereno\nsupposed that Tenerian at Gobero lived in a <strong>14</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong> group at that time.</p>","firstNumber":14}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Human Remain in GREEN SAHARA</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>On October 13,2,000, a small team of paleontologists led by Paul Sereno of the University of Chicago clambered out of three battered Land Rovers, filled their water bottles, and scattered on foot across the toffeecolored sands of the Tenere desert in northern Niger. The Tenere, on the southern flank of the Sahara, easily ranks among the most desolate landscapes on Earth. The Tuareg, turbaned nomads who for centuries have ruled this barren realm, refer to it as a ‘desert within a desert’ – a California-size ocean of sand and rock,where a single massive dune might stretch a hundred miles, and the combination of 120-degree heat and inexorable winds can wick the water from a human body in less than a day. The harsh conditions, combined with intermittent conflict between the Tuareg and the Niger government, have kept the region largely unexplored.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Mike Hettwer, a photographer accompanying the team, headed off by himself toward a trio of small dunes. He crested the first slope and stared in amazement. The dunes were spilling over with bones. He took a few shots with his digital camera and hurried back to theLand Rovers. ‘I found some bones,’ Hettwer said, when the team had regrouped, ‘But they’re not dinosaurs. They’re human.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In the spring of 2005 Sereno contacted Elena Garcea, an archacologist at the University of Cassino, in Italy, inviting her to accompany him on a return to the site. Garcea had spent three decades working digs along the Nile in Sudan and in the mountains of the Libyan Desert, and was well acquainted with the ancient peoples of the Sahara. But she had never heard of Paul Sereno. His claim to have found so many skeletons in one place seemed farfetched, given that no other Neolithic cemetery contained more than a dozen or so. Some archacologists would later be skeptical; one sniped that he was just a ‘moonlighting paleontologist’. But Garcea was too intrigued to dismiss him as an interloper. She agreed to join him.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Garcea explained that the Kiffian were a fishing-based culture and lived during the earliest wet period, between 8,000 and 10,000 years ago. She held a Kiffian sherd next to a Tenerian one. ‘What is so amazing is that the people who made these two pots lived more than a thousand years apart.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Over the next three weeks, Sereno and Garcea – along with five American excavators, five Tuareg guides, and five soldiers from Niger’s army, sent to protect the camp from bandits – made a detailed map of the site, which they dubbed Gobero, after the Tuareg name for the area. They exhumed eight burials and collected scores of artifacts from both cultures. In a dry lake bed adjacent to the dunes, they found dozens of fishhooks and harpoons carved from animal bone. Apparently the Kiffian fishermen weren’t just going after small fry: Scattered near the dunes were the remains of Nile perch, a beast of a fish that can weigh nearly 300 pounds, as well as crocodile and hippo bones.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Sereno flew home with the most important skeletons and artifacts and immediately began planning for the next field season. In the meantime,he carefully removed one tooth from each of four skulls and sent them to a lab for radiocarbon dating. The results pegged the .age of the tightly bundled burials at roughly9,000 years old, the heart of the Kiffian era. The smaller ‘sleeping’ skeletons turned out to be about 6,000 years old, well within the Tenerian period. At least now the scientists knew who was who.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In the fall of 2006 they returned to Gobero, accompanied by a larger dig crew and six additional scientists. Garcea hoped to excavate some 80 burials, and the team began digging. As the skeletons began to emerge from the dunes, each presented a fresh riddle, especially the Tenerian. A male skeleton had been buried with a finger in his mouth.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Even at the site, Arizona State University bioarchaeologist Chris Stojanowski could begin to piece together some clues. Judging by the bones, the Kiffian appeared to be a peaceful, hardworking people. ‘The lack of head and forearm injuries suggests they weren’t doing much fighting,’ he told me, ‘And these guys were strong.’ He pointed to a long, narrow ridge running along a femur. ‘That’s the muscle attachment,’ he said, ‘This individual had huge leg muscles, which means he was eating a lot of protein and had a strenuous lifestyle –both consistent with a fishing way of life.’ For contrast, he showed me the femur of a Tenerian male. The ridge was barely perceptible. ‘This guy had a much less strenuous lifestyle,’ he said, ‘which you might expect of a herder.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Stojanowski’s assessment that the Tenerian were herders fits the prevailing view among scholars of life in the Sahara 6,000 years ago, when drier conditions favored herding over hunting. But if the Tenerian were herders, Sereno pointed out, where were the herds? Among the hundreds of animal bones that had turned up at the site, none belonged to goats or sheep, and only three came from a cow species. ‘It’s not unusual fora herding culture not to slaughter their cattle, particularly in a cemetery,’ M Garcea responded, noting that even modern pastoralists, such as Niger’s Wodaabe, are loath to butcher even one animal in their herd. Perhaps, Screno reasoned, the Tenerian at Gobero were a transitional group that had not fully adopted herding and still relied heavily on hunting and fishing.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Back in Arizona, Stojanowski continues to analyze the Gobero bones for clues to the Green Saharans’ health and diet. Other scientists are trying to derive DNA from the teeth, which could reveal the genetic origins of the Kiffian and Tenerian – and possibly link them to descendants living today. Sereno and Garcea estimate a hundred burials remain to be excavated. But as the harsh Tenere winds continue to erode the dunes, time is running out. ‘Every archaeological site has a life cycle,’ Garcea said, ‘It begins when people begin to use the place, followed by disuse, then nature takes over, and finally it is gone. Gobero is at the end of its life.’</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8884&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8889","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Numeracy: Can Animals Tell Numbers?","book":"阅读还原集Vol.18","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.18 · Test 1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8889:64293:15","type":"fill","text":"填写第 15 空","answer":"identical/identical","acceptedAnswers":["identical"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The students’ performance ends up looking just like a monkey’s. It’s practically identical, she says.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求填写表格中关于人类和猴子在辨别数量大小能力上的实验结果。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"humans\"和\"monkeys\"定位到A段，该段描述了人类和猴子在辨别数量大小实验中的表现。\n解题思路：根据原文A段中的句子\"The students’ performance ends up looking just like a monkey’s. It’s practically identical, she says.\"可知，人类学生和猴子的表现几乎完全相同，因此答案为\"identical\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64293","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nComplete the table below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20222GRMZ3LWjf1669984246.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8889:64294:16","type":"fill","text":"填写第 16 空","answer":"balls of paper/Balls of Paper","acceptedAnswers":["balls of paper","Balls of Paper"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Researchers placed each chick in the middle of a platform and showed it two groups of balls of paper.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求填写表格，雏鸡实验中是让小鸡从两组什么中进行选择。\n定位关键信息：根据表格中的“Chicks”和“Objects used”定位到G段，寻找小鸡实验中使用的具体物品。\n解题思路：G段提到研究人员将小鸡放在平台中央，并展示了两组“balls of paper”（纸球），用来测试小鸡的数学能力。因此，表格中需要填写的物品是“balls of paper”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64294","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nComplete the table below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20222GRMZ3LWjf1669984246.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8889:64295:17","type":"fill","text":"填写第 17 空","answer":"count/calculate eggs/Count/Calculate Eggs","acceptedAnswers":["count","calculate eggs","Count","Calculate Eggs"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In one compelling example, researchers in America found that female coots appear to calculate how many eggs they have laid – and add any in the nest laid by an intruder – before making any decisions about adding to them.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目要求根据表格，白骨顶实验中，实验结果发现这种鸟似乎有什么能力。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中关于白骨顶实验的相关句子，定位到文中的H段。\n解题思路：在H段中，作者提到研究人员发现雌性coots（白骨顶）似乎会计算自己产下的蛋的数量，并加上巢中入侵者产下的蛋，然后才决定是否增加蛋的数量。这一行为明确体现了动物进行数字计算的能力，与题目要求填写的内容高度吻合。因此，答案为\"Count/Caculate Eggs\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64295","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nComplete the table below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20222GRMZ3LWjf1669984246.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8889:64296:18","type":"fill","text":"填写第 18 空","answer":"fruit flies/Fruit Flies","acceptedAnswers":["fruit flies","Fruit Flies"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The same seems to apply to some amphibians. Psychologist Claudia Uller’s team tempted salamanders with two sets of fruit flies held in clear tubes.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是蝾螈实验中，研究者给蝾螈展示的透明试管含有不同数量的什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"salamanders\"和\"clear tubes\"定位到B段。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，心理学家克劳迪娅·乌勒的团队用两组透明管中的果蝇吸引蝾螈进行实验。因此可以推断使用的是\"fruit flies\"作为实验对象。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64296","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nComplete the table below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20222GRMZ3LWjf1669984246.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8889:64297:19","type":"fill","text":"填写第 19 空","answer":"mosquitofish/Mosquitofish","acceptedAnswers":["mosquitofish","Mosquitofish"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A team at the University of Padova found that while mosquitofish can tell the difference between a group containing 3 shoal-mates and a group containing 4, they did not show a preference between groups of 4 and 5.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求填写表格，在两栖动物，鱼类和昆虫的实验类别下，除了使用蝾螈和蜜蜂作为实验对象，还选取了哪种鱼类作为实验对象。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的表格结构，可以推测需要填写的是动物名称。在文章中寻找动物名称的句子。\n解题思路：在C段中，明确提到帕多瓦大学的一个研究团针对\"mosquitofish\"蚊鱼进行了实验，因此，答案为\"mosquitofish\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64297","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nComplete the table below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20222GRMZ3LWjf1669984246.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8889:64298:20","type":"fill","text":"填写第 20 空","answer":"surface area/Surface Area","acceptedAnswers":["surface area","Surface Area"],"explanation":"原文答案句：To consider this possibility, the mosquitofish tests were repeated, this time using varying geometrical shapes in place of fish. The team arranged these shapes so that they had the same overall surface area and luminance even though they contained a different number of objects.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求填写表格，重复蚊鱼实验，是为了验证什么和亮度对实验结果的影响。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中表格的结构和上下文，定位到E段中描述重复蚊鱼实验的句子。\n解题思路：原文提到，这次用不同几何形状替代鱼类。尽管物体数量不同，但研究人员通过巧妙排列，确保这些形状的总表面积和亮度完全一致。说明实验是为了验证总表面积和亮度对结果的影响，其中\"luminance\"和\"brightness\"是同义替换，因此选择\"surface area\"作为答案。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64298","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nComplete the table below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20222GRMZ3LWjf1669984246.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8889:64299:21","type":"fill","text":"填写第 21 空","answer":"sugar water/Sugar Water","acceptedAnswers":["sugar water","Sugar Water"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Entomologist Jurgen Tautz sent a group of bees down a corridor, at the end of which lay two chambers – one which contained sugar water, which they like, while the other was empty. To test the bees’ numeracy, the team marked each chamber with a different number of geometrical shapes – between 2 and 6. The bees quickly learned to match the number of shapes with the correct chamber.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求填写表格，在蜜蜂实验中，蜜蜂必须学会找到什么的储存位置。\n定位关键信息：根据表格中的提示信息，定位到F段描述蜜蜂实验的句子。\n解题思路：根据定位到的句子，可以确定蜜蜂实验中，一个房间是空的，另一个房间含有糖水。通过上下文可以推断。蜜蜂必须学会在实验中找到糖水的储存位置，因此填入\"sugar water\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64299","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nComplete the table below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20222GRMZ3LWjf1669984246.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8889:64300:22","type":"choice","text":"Primates are better at identifying the larger of two numbers if one is much bigger than the other.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：They had to decide which set contained more objects. Both groups performed successfully but, importantly, Brannon’s team found that monkeys, like humans, make more errors when two sets of objects are close in number.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“如果其中一个数字比另一个大得多，灵长类动物在识别较大数字的表现会更好”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“Primates”和“identifying the larger of two numbers”定位到A段，找到原文中关于灵长类动物辨别数字能力的描述。\n解题思路：根据原文A段中的句子，布兰农团队发现：当两组物体数量相近时，猴子会像人类一样出现更多错误。可以得出结论，灵长类动物在辨别数字大小时，如果数字差别足够大，表现会更好。所以答案是True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64300","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8889:64301:23","type":"choice","text":"Jurgen Tautz trained the insects in his experiment to recognise the shapes of individual numbers.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Entomologist Jurgen Tautz sent a group of bees down a corridor, at the end of which lay two chambers – one which contained sugar water, which they like, while the other was empty. To test the bees’ numeracy, the team marked each chamber with a different number of geometrical shapes – between 2 and 6. The bees quickly learned to match the number of shapes with the correct chamber.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问Jurgen Tautz训练昆虫识别单个数字的形状，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Jurgen Tautz\"和\"recognise the shapes of individual numbers\"定位到F段，文中提到实验使用不同数量的几何形状标记房间，蜜蜂学会匹配形状数量与房间。\n解题思路：原文描述的是，研究团队在每个隔间分别用2到6个几何图形标记。蜜蜂很快学会将图形数量与对应隔间匹配。而非识别\"单个数字的形状\"，且未提及训练过程。题目与原文不符，因此答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64301","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8889:64302:24","type":"choice","text":"The research involving young chicks took place over two separate days.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Researchers placed each chick in the middle of a platform and showed it two groups of balls of paper. Next, they hid the two piles behind screens, changed the quantities and revealed them to the chick. This forced the chick to perform simple computations to decide which side now contained the biggest number of its ‘brothers’.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是关于雏鸡的研究在两天内分两次进行的，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"young chicks\"和\"two separate days\"定位到G段，该段描述了研究人员对三到四天大的小鸡进行的实验过程。\n解题思路：G段描述了研究人员将小鸡放在平台中央，展示两个纸球组，然后隐藏、改变数量并重新展示给小鸡，迫使小鸡进行简单计算。没有提到实验分几天进行。因此，题目中关于研究在两天内分两次进行的信息在文章中没有明确提及，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64302","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8889:64303:25","type":"choice","text":"The experiment with chicks suggests that some numerical ability exists in newborn animals.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Without any prior coaching, the chicks scuttled to the larger quantity at a rate well above chance. They were doing some very simple arithmetic, claim the researchers.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“雏鸟的实验表明，新生动物具备一点数字能力”是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"experiment with chicks\"和\"newborn animals\"可以定位到G段，该段落描述了关于小鸡的数字能力实验。\n解题思路：G段提到，尽管没有事先训练，小鸡们仍能以远超随机概率的速度奔向数量较多的一侧。科学家指出，它们进行的其实是基础算术运算。这说明小鸡天生就具备一定的数字能力，而不需要后天训练。因此，题目中的陈述与文章信息一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64303","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8889:64304:26","type":"choice","text":"Researchers have experimented by altering quantities of nectar or fruit available to certain wild animals.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Animals on the prowl for sustenance must constantly decide which tree has the most fruit, or which patch of flowers will contain the most nectar.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问研究人员，通过改变某些野生动物可获得的花蜜或水果的数量进行了实验，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"altering quantities of nectar or fruit\"（改变蜜或水果的数量）和\"wild animals\"（野生动物）在文章中定位。\n解题思路：文章H段提到，处于觅食状态的动物必须不断判断哪棵树结的果实最多，或是哪片花丛的花蜜最丰富。只是提到动物有这种能力，但未明确说明研究人员通过改变蜜或水果的数量进行实验。因此，题目信息在文章中没有明确给出，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64304","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8889:64305:27","type":"choice","text":"When assessing the number of eggs in their nest, coots take into account those of other birds.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In one compelling example, researchers in America found that female coots appear to calculate how many eggs they have laid – and add any in the nest laid by an intruder – before making any decisions about adding to them.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是在估计巢穴中的蛋的数量时，白骨顶会考虑到其他鸟类下的蛋，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"coots\"和\"eggs\"定位到H段，找到关于水鸭计算蛋数量的描述。\n解题思路：原文提到研究人员发现雌性白骨顶似乎会计算它们自己下的蛋的数量，并且会把巢穴中由入侵者下的蛋加进去，然后再决定是否添加更多的蛋。这与题目中的描述完全一致，因此，题目说法与原文信息一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64305","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64293","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nComplete the table below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20222GRMZ3LWjf1669984246.png]","html":"<p><strong>15</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[15] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":15},{"id":"64294","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nComplete the table below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20222GRMZ3LWjf1669984246.png]","html":"<p><strong>16</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[16] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":16},{"id":"64295","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nComplete the table below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20222GRMZ3LWjf1669984246.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">17</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[17] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":17},{"id":"64296","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nComplete the table below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20222GRMZ3LWjf1669984246.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">18</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[18] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":18},{"id":"64297","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nComplete the table below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20222GRMZ3LWjf1669984246.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">19</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"64298","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nComplete the table below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20222GRMZ3LWjf1669984246.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">20</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"64299","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nComplete the table below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20222GRMZ3LWjf1669984246.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">21</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"64300","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Primates are better at identifying the larger of two numbers if one is much bigger than the other.</strong></p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"64301","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Jurgen Tautz trained the insects in his experiment to recognise the shapes of individual numbers.</strong></p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"64302","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The research involving young chicks took place over two separate days.</strong></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"64303","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The experiment with chicks suggests that some numerical ability exists in newborn animals.</strong></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"64304","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Researchers have experimented by altering quantities of nectar or fruit available to certain wild animals.</strong></p>","firstNumber":26},{"id":"64305","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>When assessing the number of eggs in their nest, coots take into account those of other birds.</strong></p>","firstNumber":27}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Numeracy: Can Animals Tell Numbers?</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Prime among basic numerical faculties is the ability to distinguish between a larger and a smaller, says psychologist Elizabeth Brannon. Humans can do this with ease – providing the ratio is big enough – but do other animals share this ability? In one experiment, rhesus monkeys and university students examined two sets of geometrical objects that appeared briefly on a computer monitor. They had to decide which set contained more objects. Both groups performed successfully but, importantly, Brannon’s team found that monkeys, like humans, make more errors when two sets of objects are close in number. The students’ performance ends up looking just like a monkey’s. It’s practically identical, she says.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Humans and monkeys are mammals, in the animal family known as primates. These are not the only animals whose numerical capacities rely on ratio, however. The same seems to apply to some amphibians. Psychologist Claudia Uller’s team tempted salamanders with two sets of fruit flies held in clear tubes. In a series of trials, the researchers noted which tube the salamanders scampered towards, reasoning that if they had a capacity to recognise the number, they would head for the larger number. The salamanders successfully discriminated between tubes containing 8 and 16 flies respectively, but not between 3 and 4, 4 and 6, or 8 and 12. So it seems that for the salamanders to discriminate between two numbers, the larger must be at least twice as big as the smaller. However, they could differentiate between 2 and 3 flies just as well as between 1 and 2 flies, suggesting they recognise small numbers in a different way from larger numbers.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Further support for this theory comes from studies of mosquitofish, which instinctively join the biggest shoal they can. A team at the University of Padova found that while mosquitofish can tell the difference between a group containing 3 shoal-mates and a group containing 4, they did not show a preference between groups of 4 and 5. The team also found that mosquitofish can discriminate between numbers up to 16, but only if the ratio between the fish in each shoal was greater than 2:1. This indicates that the fish, like salamanders, possess both the approximate and precise number systems found in more intelligent animals such as infant humans and other primates.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>While these findings are highly suggestive, some critics argue that the animals might be relying on other factors to complete the tasks, without considering the number itself. ‘Any study that’s claiming an animal is capable of representing number should also be controlling for other factors,’ says Brannon. Experiments have confirmed that primates can indeed perform numerical feats without extra clues, but what about the more primitive animals?</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>To consider this possibility, the mosquitofish tests were repeated, this time using varying geometrical shapes in place of fish. The team arranged these shapes so that they had the same overall surface area and luminance even though they contained a different number of objects. Across hundreds of trials on 14 different fish, the team found they consistently discriminated 2 objects from 3. The team is now testing whether mosquitofish can also distinguish 3 geometric objects from 4.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Even more primitive organisms may share this ability. Entomologist Jurgen Tautz sent a group of bees down a corridor, at the end of which lay two chambers – one which contained sugar water, which they like, while the other was empty. To test the bees’ numeracy, the team marked each chamber with a different number of geometrical shapes – between 2 and 6. The bees quickly learned to match the number of shapes with the correct chamber. Like the salamanders and fish, there was a limit to the bees’ mathematical prowess – they could differentiate up to 4 shapes, but failed with 5 or 6 shapes.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>These studies still do not show whether animals learn to count through training, or whether they are born with the skills already intact. If the latter is true, it would suggest there was a strong evolutionary advantage to a mathematical mind. Proof that this may be the case has emerged from an experiment testing the mathematical ability of three – and four-day-old chicks. Like mosquitofish, chicks prefer to be around as many of their siblings as possible, so they will always head towards a larger number of their kin. If chicks spend their first few days surrounded by certain objects, they become attached to these objects as if they were family. Researchers placed each chick in the middle of a platform and showed it two groups of balls of paper. Next, they hid the two piles behind screens, changed the quantities and revealed them to the chick. This forced the chick to perform simple computations to decide which side now contained the biggest number of its ‘brothers’. Without any prior coaching, the chicks scuttled to the larger quantity at a rate well above chance. They were doing some very simple arithmetic, claim the researchers.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Why these skills evolved is not hard to imagine, since it would help almost any animal forage for food. Animals on the prowl for sustenance must constantly decide which tree has the most fruit, or which patch of flowers will contain the most nectar. There are also other, less obvious, advantages of numeracy. In one compelling example, researchers in America found that female coots appear to calculate how many eggs they have laid – and add any in the nest laid by an intruder – before making any decisions about adding to them. Exactly how ancient these skills are is difficult to determine, however. Only by studying the numerical abilities of more and more creatures using standardised procedures can we hope to understand the basic preconditions for the evolution of number.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8889&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8890","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Elephant Communication","book":"阅读还原集Vol.18","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.18 · Test 1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8890:64306:28","type":"fill","text":"填写第 28 空","answer":"hammer/Hammer","acceptedAnswers":["hammer","Hammer"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The hammer bone of the elephant’s inner ear is proportionally very large for a mammal, but typical for animals that use vibrational signals.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求根据文章内容完成一个图表，有关帮助大象接收地面振动的身体结构，询问大象的内耳中有什么骨头。\n定位关键信息：根据“inner ear”或“bone”，在B段中找到相关描述。\n解题思路：在B段中，明确提到大象内耳的锤骨在哺乳动物中比例异常巨大，这在依赖振动信号的动物中堪称典型。“hammer bone of the elephant’s inner ear”，这是描述大象内耳中的锤骨，与题目要求填空的内容相匹配。因此，答案为“hammer”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64306","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-31\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-31 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022a7dNSCdJYQ1669984487.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8890:64307:29","type":"fill","text":"填写第 29 空","answer":"body/Body","acceptedAnswers":["body","Body"],"explanation":"原文答案句：First, their enormous bodies, which allow them to generate low-frequency sounds almost as powerful as those of a jet takeoff, provide ideal frames for receiving ground vibrations and conducting them to the inner ear.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求根据文章内容完成一个图表，有关帮助大象接收地面振动的身体结构，询问大象有一个巨大的什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"receiving ground vibrations\"定位到C段，该段描述了大象的身体结构如何帮助接收地面振动。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，大象的\"enormous bodies\"（巨大的身体）能够接收地面振动并将其传导到内耳，因此答案为\"body\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64307","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-31\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-31 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022a7dNSCdJYQ1669984487.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8890:64308:30","type":"fill","text":"填写第 30 空","answer":"pad/Pad","acceptedAnswers":["pad","Pad"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Second, the elephant’s toe bones rest on a fatty pad that might help focus vibrations from the ground into the bone.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求根据文章内容完成一个图表，有关帮助大象接收地面振动的身体结构，询问大象有脚趾和多脂肪的什么。\n定位关键信息：题目可能涉及大象接收地面振动的方式或解剖结构，因此需要定位文章中关于大象身体构造与振动接收相关的句子。在C段中找到“the elephant’s toe bones rest on a fatty pad that might help focus vibrations from the ground into the bone”这句话，明确提到“fatty pad”与振动接收有关。\n解题思路：根据原文句子可知，大象的脚趾骨位于一个脂肪垫上，这个垫子可能有助于将地面振动聚焦到骨骼中。因此，答案应为“pad”或“Pad”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64308","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-31\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-31 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022a7dNSCdJYQ1669984487.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8890:64309:31","type":"fill","text":"填写第 31 空","answer":"cavities/sinus cavities/Cavities/Sinus Cavities","acceptedAnswers":["cavities","sinus cavities","Cavities","Sinus Cavities"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The front of the skull is riddled with sinus cavities that may function as resonating chambers for vibrations from the ground.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求根据文章内容完成一个图表，有关帮助大象接收地面振动的身体结构，询问大象体积大的颅骨带有许多什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"resonating chambers\"（共鸣腔）和\"vibrations from the ground\"（来自地面的振动）定位到C段，该段描述了头骨前部的结构及其功能。\n解题思路：原文C段明确提到，头骨前部布满的窦腔可能作为共振腔，用于传导地面振动。因此，答案为\"sinus cavities\"或其同义词\" cavities\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64309","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-31\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-31 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022a7dNSCdJYQ1669984487.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8890:64310:32","type":"fill","text":"填写第 32 空","answer":"trunks and feet/Trunks And Feet","acceptedAnswers":["trunks and feet","Trunks And Feet"],"explanation":"原文答案句：How the elephants sense these vibrations is still unknown, but O’Connell-Rodwell who just earned a graduate degree in entomology at the University of Hawaii at Manoa, suspects the pachyderms are ‘listening’ with their trunks and feet.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问大象如何感知这些声波振动仍属未知，但夏威夷大学昆虫学专业应届毕业生奥康奈尔·罗德韦尔提出，大象可能通过什么来感知声音振动。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“listening”和“sound vibrations”，结合文章内容，定位到D段中关于大象感知振动方式的描述。\n解题思路：原文提到O’Connell-Rodwell推测大象通过“trunks and feet”鼻子和脚部来感知振动。因此，答案为“trunks and feet”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64310","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8890:64311:33","type":"fill","text":"填写第 33 空","answer":"infrasonic/Infrasonic","acceptedAnswers":["infrasonic","Infrasonic"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Both trunk and feet contain two kinds of pressure-sensitive nerve endings – one that detects infrasonic vibrations and another that responds to vibrations with slightly higher frequencies.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是大象的鼻子和脚通过两种神经末梢来感知振动，让大象对什么频率的振动和略高频率的振动均产生反应。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"two kinds of nerve endings\"和\"responds to vibrations\"，这些信息帮助我们定位到D段中描述大象鼻子和脚的神经末梢的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子，其鼻部和脚部都含有两种压力敏感神经末梢——一种能感知次声波振动，另一种则对稍高频率的振动产生反应。因此，题目中空缺的部分应该填写的是\"infrasonic\"，表示一种神经末梢是对次声波振动做出反应的。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64311","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8890:64312:34","type":"fill","text":"填写第 34 空","answer":"ecology/Ecology","acceptedAnswers":["ecology","Ecology"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For O’Connell-Rodwell, the future of the research is boundless and unpredictable: ‘Our work is really at the interface of geophysics, neurophysiology and ecology,’ she says, ‘We’re asking questions that no one has really dealt with before.’\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问，O‘Connell Rodwell的研究是地球物理学、神经生理学和什么学科的结合。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"O’Connell Rodwell's work\"和\"geophysics, neurophysiology\"可以定位到D段中O’Connell Rodwell的话，这里明确提到了她工作的三个学科领域。\n解题思路：在D段中，O’Connell Rodwell直接说明了属于地球物理学、神经生理学与生态学的交叉领域，因此空格处应填写\"ecology\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64312","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8890:64313:35","type":"fill","text":"填写第 35 空","answer":"seismic messages/Seismic Messages","acceptedAnswers":["seismic messages","Seismic Messages"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But O’Connell-Rodwell was the first to suggest that a large land animal also is sending and receiving seismic messages.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是O'Connell-Rodwell的研究首次提出大型陆地动物也发送和接收什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"first to indicate\"和\"large land animal\"可以定位到E段第一句话，其中提到了O'Connell-Rodwell首次提出大型陆地动物也发送和接收\"seismic messages\"。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到了，奥康奈尔-罗德韦尔首次提出，大型陆地动物也可能在进行地震波信息的收发。因此答案为\"seismic messages\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64313","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8890:64314:36","type":"fill","text":"填写第 36 空","answer":"acoustic communication/communications/Acoustic Communication/Communications","acceptedAnswers":["acoustic communication","communications","Acoustic Communication","Communications"],"explanation":"原文答案句：  It was just so fascinating to me, and it’s what got me to think, maybe there’s something else going on other than acoustic communication.’\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问O‘Connell-Rodwell通过将一只雄性飞虱置于茎上并播放雌性求偶叫声，观察到了其冻结行为，这可能证明除什么36%%外还存在其他交流方式。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"O’Connell-Rodwell\"、\"noticed\"、\"freezing behavior\"、\"planthopper\"和\"communicative approach\"可以定位到E段中描述她观察飞虱行为的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，她的飞虱实验给了她启发，推测或许除了声波通讯之外，还存在其他交流方式。因此答案为\"acoustic communication\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64314","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8890:64315:37","type":"fill","text":"填写第 37 空","answer":"mate/Mate","acceptedAnswers":["mate","Mate"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The difficulty of finding a mate in this vast wilderness is compounded by elephant reproductive biology. Females breed only when in estrus – a period of sexual arousal that occurs every two years and lasts just a few days.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是，科学家已证实，大象的远距离交流能力至关重要，尤其当象群寻找什么或发出捕食者警告时。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"finding a\"和\"herds\"定位到F段，该段提到大象群寻找配偶的困难。\n解题思路：F段明确指出，大象群在寻找配偶时，长距离沟通能力尤为重要，雌象在发情期发出低频长距离呼叫，雄象会根据这些呼叫寻找配偶。因此，空格处应填写\"mate\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64315","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8890:64316:38","type":"fill","text":"填写第 38 空","answer":"ground/Ground","acceptedAnswers":["ground","Ground"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘The results of our 2002 study showed us that elephants do indeed detect warning calls played through the ground,’ O’Connell-Rodwell observes, ‘We expected them to clump up into tight groups and leave the area, and that’s in fact what they did.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是2002年的研究结果表明大象能够检测通过什么传播的警告叫声。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键信息\"warning calls played through the\"和\"2002 study\"可以定位到G段。\n解题思路：根据G段，“2002年的研究结果证实，大象确实能感知通过地面回传的警报声，”奥康奈尔-罗德韦尔指出，“我们预期它们会聚集成紧密集群并撤离该区域，事实也确实如此表明警告声是通过地面传播的，因此答案为ground。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64316","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8890:64317:39","type":"choice","text":"According the passage, it is determined that an elephant need to communicate over long distances\nfor its survival","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Adult bulls and cows have no enemies, except for humans, but young elephants are susceptible to attacks by lions and hyenas. When a predator appears, older members of the herd emit intense warning calls that prompt the rest of the herd to clump together for protection, then flee.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问根据文章内容，大象在什么情况下，为了生存需要进行远距离的交流。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"communicate over long distances\"和\"for its survival\"定位到F段。\n解题思路：F段明确指出，繁殖象群还会通过低频发声警告捕食者。成年雄象和雌象除人类外没有天敌，但幼象容易遭受狮子和鬣狗的攻击。当捕食者出现时，象群中年长的成员会发出强烈的警告叫声，促使其他象群成员抱团自保后迅速逃离。因此，最符合题意的是有威胁性的捕食者出现时（选项A），需要通过远距离交流来警告群体并采取保护措施。其他选项（B、C、D）要么与文章描述的情境不符，D选项“雄性大象在发情期时”为干扰项，文中提到了大象在找配偶时，所以不管是雄性还是雌性大象都会这么交流。因此，本题的答案为A。","options":["when a threatening predator appears","when young elephants meet humans","when older members of the herd want to flee from the group","when a male elephant is in estrus"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64317","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 39-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 39-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8890:64318:40","type":"choice","text":"What is the author’s attitude toward the experiment by using three different recordings in the paragraph?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Although still analyzing data from this experiment, O’Connell-Rodwell is able to make a few preliminary observations: ‘The data I’ve seen so far suggest that the elephants were responding as I had expected. When the ’94 warning call was played back, they tended to clump together and leave the water hole sooner. But what’s really interesting is that the unfamiliar anti-predator call from Kenya also caused them to clump up, get nervous and aggressively rumble – but they didn’t necessarily leave. I didn’t think it was going to be that clear cut.’\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是作者对使用三种不同录音进行的实验的态度是什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"experiment by using three different recordings\"可以定位到H段中提到的实验描述。\n解题思路：根据H段中作者的话可以得出，实验数据表明大象的反应符合预期，可排除A选项和B选项，但当播放肯尼亚的反捕食者呼叫时，大象虽然聚集并变得紧张，但并没有一定离开，作者表示没想到结果会这样。因此，作者认为实验结果可能有些不确定或不准确。选项故意混淆概念，文中出现了unfamiliar，但却是说大象对肯尼亚的这种声音不熟悉。因此，本题的答案为C。","options":["The outcome is definitely out of the original expectation.","The data can not be very clearly obtained.","The result can be somewhat undecided or inaccurate.","The result can be unfamiliar to the public."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64318","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 39-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 39-40 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64306","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-31\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-31 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022a7dNSCdJYQ1669984487.png]","html":"<p><strong>28</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[28] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"64307","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-31\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-31 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022a7dNSCdJYQ1669984487.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">29</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[29] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"64308","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-31\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-31 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022a7dNSCdJYQ1669984487.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">30</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[30] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"64309","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-31\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-31 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022a7dNSCdJYQ1669984487.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">31</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[31] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"64310","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>How the elephants sense these sound vibrations is still unknown, but O’Connell Rodwell, a fresh\ngraduate in entomology at the University of Hawaii, proposes that the elephants are ‘listening’\nwith their <strong>32</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[32] ____</strong> ,</p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"64311","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>by two kinds of nerve endings – that responds to vibrations with\nboth <strong>33</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[33] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"64312","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>frequency and slightly higher frequencies. O’Connell Rodwell’s work is\nthe combination of geophysics, neurophysiology and <strong>34</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[34] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"64313","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>and it was also the first to\nindicate that a large land animal is also sending and receiving <strong>35</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[35] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"64314","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>O’Connell-Rodwell noticed the freezing behavior by putting a male planthopper&nbsp;on a stem and play back a female call, which might prove the existence of other communicative approaches&nbsp;other than&nbsp;<strong>36</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[36] ____</strong> .</p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"64315","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Scientists have determined that an elephant&#39;s ability to communicate over long\ndistances is essential, especially, when elephant herds are finding a <strong>37</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[37] ____</strong> ,</p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"64316","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-38\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-38 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>or are\nwarning of predators. Finally, the results of our 2002 study showed US that elephants can detect\nwarning calls played through the <strong>38</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[38] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"64317","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 39-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 39-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>According the passage, it is determined that an elephant need to communicate over long distances\nfor its survival</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"64318","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 39-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 39-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is the author’s attitude toward the experiment by using three different recordings in the paragraph?</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Elephant Communication</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>A postdoctoral fellow at Stanford University, O’Connell-Rodwell has come to Namibia’s premiere wildlife sanctuary to explore the mysterious and complex world of elephant communication. She and her colleagues are part of a scientific revolution that began nearly two decades ago with the stunning revelation that elephants communicate over long distances using low-frequency sounds, also called infrasounds, that are too deep to be heard by most humans.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>As might be expected, the African elephant’s ability to sense seismic sound may begin in the ears. The hammer bone of the elephant’s inner ear is proportionally very large for a mammal, buy typical for animals that use vibrational signals. It may, therefore, be a sign that elephants can communicate with seismic sounds. Also, the elephant and its relative the manatee are unique among mammals in having reverted to a reptilianlike cochlear structure in the inner ear. The cochlea of reptiles facilitates a keen sensitivity to vibrations and may do the same in elephants.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>But other aspects of elephant anatomy also support that ability. First, their enormous bodies, which allow them to generate low-frequency sounds almost as powerful as those of a jet takeoff, provide ideal frames for receiving ground vibrations and conducting them to the inner ear. Second, the elephant’s toe bones rest on a fatty pad that might help focus vibrations from the ground into the bone. Finally, the elephant’s enormous brain lies in the cranial cavity behind the eyes in line with the auditory canal. The front of the skull is riddled with sinus cavities that may function as resonating chambers for vibrations from the ground.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>How the elephants sense these vibrations is still unknown, but O’Connell-Rodwell who just earned a graduate degree in entomology at the University of Hawaii at Manoa, suspects the pachyderms are ‘listening’ with their trunks and feet. The trunk may be the most versatile appendage in nature. Its uses include drinking, bathing, smelling, feeding and scratching. Both trunk and feet contain two kinds of pressure-sensitive nerve endings – one that detects infrasonic vibrations and another that responds to vibrations with slightly higher frequencies. For O’Connell-Rodwell, the future of the research is boundless and unpredictable: ‘Our work is really at the interface of geophysics, neurophysiology and ecology,’ she says, ‘We’re asking questions that no one has really dealt with before.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Scientists have long known that seismic communication is common in small animals, including spiders, scorpions, insects and a number of vertebrate species such as white-lipped frogs, blind mole rats, kangaroo rats and golden moles. They also have found evidence of seismic sensitivity in elephant seals – 2-ton marine mammals that are not related to elephants. But O’Connell-Rodwell was the first to suggest that a large land animal also is sending and receiving seismic messages. O’Connell-Rodwell noticed something about the freezing behavior of Etosha’s six-ton bulls that reminded her of the tiny insects back in her lab. ‘I did my masters thesis on seismic communication in planthoppers,’ she says, ‘I’d put a male planthopper on a stem and playback a female call, and the male would do the same thing the elephants were doing: He would freeze, then press down on his legs, go forward a little bit, then freeze again. It was just so fascinating to me, and it’s what got me to think, maybe there’s something else going on other than acoustic communication.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Scientists have determined that an elephant’s ability to communicate over long distances is essential for its survival, particularly in a place like Etosha, where more than 2,400 savanna elephants range over an area larger than New Jersey. The difficulty of finding a mate in this vast wilderness is compounded by elephant reproductive biology. Females breed only when in estrus – a period of sexual arousal that occurs every two years and lasts just a few days. ‘Females in estrus make these very low, long calls that bulls home in on, because it’s such a rare event,’ O’Connell-Rodwell says, These powerful estrus calls carry more than two miles in the air and may be accompanied by long-distance seismic signals, she adds. Breeding herds also use low-frequency vocalizations to warn of predators. Adult bulls and cows have no enemies, except for humans, but young elephants are susceptible to attacks by lions and hyenas. When a predator appears, older members of the herd emit intense warning calls that prompt the rest of the herd to clump together for protection, then flee. In 1994, O’Connell-Rodwell recorded the dramatic cries of a breeding herd threatened by lions at Mushara. ‘The elephants got really scared, and the matriarch made these very powerful warning calls, and then the herd took off screaming and trumpeting,’ she recalls, ‘Since then, every time we’ve played that particular call at the water hole, we get the same response – the elephants take off.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Reacting to a warning call played in the air is one thing, but could the elephants detect calls transmitted only through the ground? To find out, the research team in 2002 devised an experiment using electronic equipment that allowed them to send signals through the ground at Mushara. ‘The results of our 2002 study showed us that elephants do indeed detect warning calls played through the ground,’ O’Connell-Rodwell observes, ‘We expected them to clump up into tight groups and leave the area, and that’s in fact what they did. But since we only played back one type of call, we couldn’t really say whether they were interpreting it correctly. Maybe they thought it was a vehicle or something strange instead of a predator warning.”</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>An experiment last year was designed to solve that problem by using three different recordings – the 1994 warning call from Mushara, an anti-predator call recorded by scientist Joyce Poole in Kenya and an artificial warble tone. Although still analyzing data from this experiment, O’Connell-Rodwell is able to make a few preliminary observations: ‘The data I’ve seen so far suggest that the elephants were responding as I had expected. When the ’94 warning call was played back, they tended to clump together and leave the water hole sooner. But what’s really interesting is that the unfamiliar anti-predator call from Kenya also caused them to clump up, get nervous and aggressively rumble – but they didn’t necessarily leave. I didn’t think it was going to be that clear cut.’</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8890&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8881","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Blue-footed Boobies","book":"阅读还原集Vol.17","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.17 · Test 4 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8881:64242:1","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：When their prey is in sight, they fold their long wings back around their streamlined bodies and plunge into the water from as high as 80 feet, so streamlined they barely make a splash.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求为A段选择一个合适的标题，概括段落的主要内容。\n定位关键信息：通过段落中的关键词如\"plunge into the water\"、\"fold their long wings\"等可以定位到段落的主要内容是关于蓝脚鲣鸟的食物及其捕食方式。\n解题思路：A段主要描述了蓝脚鲣鸟的食物和捕食方式，首先提到它们猎食小型鱼类，接着详细描绘它们捕食的过程。因此，标题\"Diving for seafood\"（俯冲捕鱼）能够准确概括A段的主要内容。","options":["Unusual way of hatching the chicks","Feeding habit of the red-footed booby","Folding wings for purpose","Rearing the young","Classification of boobies","Diving for seafood","Surviving mechanism during the food shortage period","Mating and breeding","Origin of the booby's name"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64242","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-G Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-G from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8881:64242:2","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：There are three varieties on the Galapagos: the blue-footed, red-footed, and masked boobies. They are all members of the same family, and are not only different in appearance but also in behaviours.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求为B段选择一个合适的标题，概括该段落的主要内容。\n定位关键信息：通过题目定位到B段，仔细阅读该段落的首句和关键信息，以确定段落主题。\n解题思路：B段首先提到加拉帕戈斯群岛上有三种鲣鸟，分别是蓝脚、红脚和面罩。接着说明它们虽然同属一个科，但在外观和行为上有所不同。因此，B段的主要内容是介绍加拉帕戈斯群岛上三种不同的鲣鸟。根据选项内容，选择\"Classification of boobies\"鲣鸟的分类，作为段落的标题。","options":["Unusual way of hatching the chicks","Feeding habit of the red-footed booby","Folding wings for purpose","Rearing the young","Classification of boobies","Diving for seafood","Surviving mechanism during the food shortage period","Mating and breeding","Origin of the booby's name"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64242","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-G Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-G from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8881:64242:3","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Although it is unknown where the name ‘Booby’ emanates from, some conjecture it may come from the Spanish word for clown, ‘bobo’, meaning ‘stupid’.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求为C段选择一个合适的标题，概括该段落的主要内容。\n定位关键信息：通过题目定位到C段，仔细阅读该段落的首句和关键信息，以确定段落主题。\n解题思路：段落C的首句直接提出了本段的核心主题：“尽管‘Booby’这个名字源自何处尚不明确...”，紧接着给出了关于其可能源自西班牙语“bobo”的推测，并解释了原因。整个段落都在围绕“名字的起源”这一主题展开。因此，它与列表中的标题 ix Origin of the booby's name (鲣鸟名字的起源) 完全匹配。","options":["Unusual way of hatching the chicks","Feeding habit of the red-footed booby","Folding wings for purpose","Rearing the young","Classification of boobies","Diving for seafood","Surviving mechanism during the food shortage period","Mating and breeding","Origin of the booby's name"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64242","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-G Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-G from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8881:64242:4","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The blue-footed booby’s characteristic feet play a significant part in their famous courtship ceremony, the ‘booby dance’.... After mating, another ritual occurs – the nest-building which ironically is never used because they nest on the bare ground. When the female is ready to lay her eggs, they scrape the existing nest away so she can nest on exposed ground.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求为D段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过题目定位到D段，仔细阅读该段落的关键信息，以确定段落主题。\n解题思路：段落D详细描述了一系列与繁殖相关的行为：从雄鸟求偶的“鲣鸟舞”，到雌鸟的回应，再到交配后的筑巢仪式。整个段落的主题都围绕着求偶和繁殖展开。因此，它与列表中的标题Mating and breeding（交配与繁殖）完全匹配。","options":["Unusual way of hatching the chicks","Feeding habit of the red-footed booby","Folding wings for purpose","Rearing the young","Classification of boobies","Diving for seafood","Surviving mechanism during the food shortage period","Mating and breeding","Origin of the booby's name"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64242","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-G Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-G from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8881:64242:5","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Unlike most birds, booby doesn’t develop brood patches (areas of bare skin on the breast) to warm the eggs during incubation. Instead, it uses its broad webbed feet, which have large numbers of prominent blood vessels, to transmit heat essential for incubation.\n对应段落：具体段落，如E段\n审题：题目要求为E段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过题目定位到E段，仔细阅读该段落的关键信息，以确定段落主题。\n解题思路：段落E的核心内容是描述鲣鸟如何孵化雏鸟。它明确指出，与大多数鸟类不同，鲣鸟不是用身体，而是用其长满血管的宽大脚蹼来为蛋提供热量。这种独特的方式与列表中的标题 i Unusual way of hatching the chicks（不寻常的孵化方式）完全吻合。","options":["Unusual way of hatching the chicks","Feeding habit of the red-footed booby","Folding wings for purpose","Rearing the young","Classification of boobies","Diving for seafood","Surviving mechanism during the food shortage period","Mating and breeding","Origin of the booby's name"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64242","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-G Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-G from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8881:64242:6","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph F","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：After hatching, the male plays a major role in bringing fish home. He can bring back a constant supply of small fish for the chicks, which must be fed continuously. The reason is that the male has a longer tail than the female in relation to his body size, which makes him able to execute shallower dives and to feed closer to shore. Then the female takes a greater part as time proceeds. Sooner or later, the need to feed the young becomes greater than the need to protect them and both adults must fish to provide enough.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求为F段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过题目定位到F段，仔细阅读该段落的关键信息，以确定段落主题。\n解题思路：段落F通篇都在描述雏鸟孵化后，雄鸟和雌鸟如何分工合作，为雏鸟持续提供食物，并共同承担喂养责任直至其长大的过程。这完整地描绘了“养育幼鸟”的场景。因此，它与列表中的标题 iv Rearing the young（养育幼鸟）完全匹配。","options":["Unusual way of hatching the chicks","Feeding habit of the red-footed booby","Folding wings for purpose","Rearing the young","Classification of boobies","Diving for seafood","Surviving mechanism during the food shortage period","Mating and breeding","Origin of the booby's name"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64242","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-G Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-G from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8881:64242:7","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph G","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The above system optimizes the reproductive capacity of the blue-foot in an unpredictable environment. The system ensures that, if possible, at least one chick will survive a period of shortage rather than all three dying of starvation under a more ‘humane’ system.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求为G段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读G段，可以定位到段落中描述了蓝脚鲣鸟在食物短缺时的行为。\n解题思路：段落G的核心内容是讨论在食物短缺时期，鲣鸟如何通过“机会性同胞淘汰”这一机制来确保至少一只雏鸟能够存活，从而优化其繁殖成功率。这描述的是一种在食物不足情况下的特殊生存机制。因此，它与列表中的标题 vii Surviving mechanism during the food shortage period（食物短缺时期的生存机制）完全匹配。","options":["Unusual way of hatching the chicks","Feeding habit of the red-footed booby","Folding wings for purpose","Rearing the young","Classification of boobies","Diving for seafood","Surviving mechanism during the food shortage period","Mating and breeding","Origin of the booby's name"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64242","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-G Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-G from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8881:64243:7","type":"choice","text":"Boobies are afraid of human approaching.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The blue footed booby is extremely vulnerable to human visitors because it does not appear to fear them.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“Boobies害怕人类靠近”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"Boobies\"和\"afraid of human approaching\"在文章中定位，发现相关信息在C段。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子“The blue footed booby is extremely vulnerable to human visitors because it does not appear to fear them.”可知，蓝脚鲣鸟似乎并不害怕人类，因此题目中的说法与原文信息相反，所以答案是False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64243","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8881:64244:8","type":"choice","text":"Female boobies eat more than the male ones.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The reason is that the male has a longer tail than the female in relation to his body size, which makes him able to execute shallower dives and to feed closer to shore.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问雌性鲣鸟的食量比雄性的大，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是 \"Female boobies eat more than the male ones\"，需要在原文中寻找关于雌性和雄性鲣鸟比较的信息。\n解题思路：通过仔细阅读全文，特别是A、B、C段，发现原文中没有提到雌性鲣鸟和雄性鲣鸟食量的比较，仅提到了它们体型的比较。因此，题目中的信息在原文中没有给出，所以答案是Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64244","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8881:64245:9","type":"choice","text":"When there is not sufficient food, the larger chicks will be fed at the expense of the survival of its smaller mates.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The first-born chick is larger and stronger than its nest mate(s) as a result of hatching a few days earlier and also because the parents feed the larger chick. If food is scarce, the first born will get more food than its nest mate(s) and will outcompete them, causing them to starve.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是当食物不足时，体型较大的雏鸟会以牺牲体型较小的同伴为代价获得食物，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"not sufficient food\"、\"larger chicks\"、\"fed at the expense of the survival of its smaller mates\"可以定位到G段中描述食物稀缺时雏鸟生存策略的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，当食物稀缺时，较大的第一只出生雏鸟会获得比巢中其他雏鸟更多的食物，并通过竞争导致其他较小的雏鸟挨饿。这与题目描述的情况完全一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64245","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8881:64246:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"up","acceptedAnswers":["up"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Plus he’ll raise his bill up towards the sky to try to win his mate over. The female may also partake in these activities – lifting her feet, skypointing, and of course, squawking at her mate.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目询问蓝脚鲣鸟在求偶舞蹈中，雄鸟用喙做什么动作。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"During the dance\"和\"bills\"定位到D段的答案句。\n解题思路：\n题干句：stamp his feet on the ground with his bills ___ 与原文存在改写关系：\n- raise his bill up towards the sky ≈ with his bills up\n- 动作细节被压缩改写，但核心信息“bill + up”保持一致\n关键点：\n- 空格后没有名词 → 需填副词/介词类词\n- 原文中唯一与 bill(s) 搭配且符合语法的词是 up\n- 属于典型的动作细节同义转述 + 词性转换","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64246","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8881:64247:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"nest-building/Nest-Building","acceptedAnswers":["nest-building","Nest-Building"],"explanation":"原文答案句：After mating, another ritual occurs – the nest-building which ironically is never used because they nest on the bare ground.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问，交配之后，鲣鸟会持续这种异常行为，进行什么仪式，该仪式实际上没有任何用途。\n定位关键信息：如何利用题目的单词定位答案在文章中句子\n通过题目中的关键词“after mating”（交配后）、“unusual demeanor”（异常行为）、“ritual”和“serves no purpose”（没有实际用途），可以在文章中定位到描述鲣鸟交配后行为的句子。\n解题思路：原文句子提到，交配后会进行筑巢仪式，但讽刺的是这个仪式从未真正使用，因为它们选择在裸露的地面上筑巢。因此，答案为“nest-building”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64247","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8881:64248:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"webbed feet/Webbed Feet","acceptedAnswers":["webbed feet","Webbed Feet"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Instead, it uses its broad webbed feet, which have large numbers of prominent blood vessels, to transmit heat essential for incubation.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是当雌性鲣鸟产蛋时，会将蛋放在身体的哪个部位孵化。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"female Booby lays eggs\"和\"incubate\"定位到E段中描述雌性鲣鸟产蛋后亲鸟孵化蛋的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，它们会利用宽大的蹼足——这些足部布满密集突出的血管——来传递孵化所需的热量。因此答案为\"webbed feet\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64248","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8881:64249:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"blood vessels/Blood Vessels","acceptedAnswers":["blood vessels","Blood Vessels"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Instead, it uses its broad webbed feet, which have large numbers of prominent blood vessels, to transmit heat essential for incubation.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问雌鸟孵蛋用到的身体部位含有什么以传递热量。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"contain\"、\"transmit the heat\"和\"lack of brood patches\"可以定位到E段中描述雌性鲣鸟产蛋后亲鸟孵化蛋的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确指出，它们会利用宽大的蹼足——这些足部布满密集突出的血管——来传递孵化所需的热量。因此答案为blood vessels。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64249","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64242","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-G Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-G from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"64243","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Boobies are afraid of human approaching.</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"64244","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Female boobies eat more than the male ones.</strong></p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"64245","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>When there is not sufficient food, the larger chicks will be fed at the expense of the survival of its smaller mates.</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"64246","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The courtship of the Blue-footed Booby consists of the male flaunting his blue feet and dancing\nto impress the female. During the dance, the male will spread his wings and stamp his feet on the\nground with his bills <strong>10</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"64247","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>After mating, the booby&#39;s unusual demeanor continues\nwith ritual <strong>11</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong> that really serves no purpose.</p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"64248","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>When the female Booby lays eggs, the\nparental boobies incubate the eggs beneath their <strong>12</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"64249","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>which contain&nbsp;<strong>13</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong> to transmit the heat, because of the lack of brood patches.</p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Blue-footed Boobies</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>#&amp;A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Boobies are a small group of seabirds native to tropical and subtropical oceans throughout the world. Their diet consists mainly of fish. They are specialized fish eaters feeding on small school fish like sardines, anchovies, mackerel, and flying fish. When their prey is in sight, they fold their long wings back around their streamlined bodies and plunge into the water from as high as 80 feet, so streamlined they barely make a splash. They travel in parties of about 12 to areas of water with large schools of small fish. When the lead bird sees a fish shoal in the water, it will signal the rest of the group and they will all dive together. Surprisingly, individuals do not eat with the hunting group, preferring to eat on their own, usually in the early morning or late afternoon.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>There are three varieties on the Galapagos: the blue-footed, red-footed, and masked boobies. They are all members of the same family, and are not only different in appearance but also in behaviours. The blue-footed and red-footed boobies mate throughout the year, while the masked boobies have an annual mating cycle that differs from island to island. All catch fish in a similar manner, but in different areas: the blue-footed booby does its fishing close to shore, while the masked booby goes slightly farther out, and the red-footed booby fishes at the farthest distances from shore.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Although it is unknown where the name ‘Booby’ emanates from, some conjecture it may come from the Spanish word for clown, ‘bobo’, meaning ‘stupid’. Its name was probably inspired by the bird’s clumsiness on land and apparently unwarranted bravery. The blue footed booby is extremely vulnerable to human visitors because it does not appear to fear them. Therefore these birds received such name for their clumsiness on land in which they were easy, captured, killed, and eaten by humans.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The blue-footed booby’s characteristic feet play a significant part in their famous courtship ceremony, the ‘booby dance’. The male walks around the female, raising his bright blue feet straight up in the air while bringing his ‘shoulders’ towards the ground and crossing the bottom tips of his wings high above the ground. Plus he’ll raise his bill up towards the sky to try to win his mate over. The female may also partake in these activities – lifting her feet, skypointing, and of course, squawking at her mate. After mating, another ritual occurs – the nest-building which ironically is never used because they nest on the bare ground. When the female is ready to lay her eggs, they scrape the existing nest away so she can nest on exposed ground. Sun-baked islands form the booby’s breeding grounds. When ready the female Blue Footed Booby lays one to three eggs.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>After mating, two or three eggs are laid in a shallow depression on flat or gently sloping ground. Both male and female take turns incubating the eggs. Unlike most birds, booby doesn’t develop brood patches (areas of bare skin on the breast) to warm the eggs during incubation. Instead, it uses its broad webbed feet, which have large numbers of prominent blood vessels, to transmit heat essential for incubation. The eggs are thick-shelled so they can withstand the full weight of an incubating bird.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>After hatching, the male plays a major role in bringing fish home. He can bring back a constant supply of small fish for the chicks, which must be fed continuously. The reason is that the male has a longer tail than the female in relation to his body size, which makes him able to execute shallower dives and to feed closer to shore. Then the female takes a greater part as time proceeds. Sooner or later, the need to feed the young becomes greater than the need to protect them and both adults must fish to provide enough.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>When times are good, the parents may successfully fledge all three chicks, but, in harder times, they may still lay as many eggs yet only obtain enough food to raise one. The problem is usually solved by the somewhat callous-sounding system of ‘opportunistic sibling murder.’ The first-born chick is larger and stronger than its nest mate(s) as a result of hatching a few days earlier and also because the parents feed the larger chick. If food is scarce, the first born will get more food than its nest mate(s) and will outcompete them, causing them to starve. The above system optimizes the reproductive capacity of the blue-foot in an unpredictable environment. The system ensures that, if possible, at least one chick will survive a period of shortage rather than all three dying of starvation under a more ‘humane’ system.&amp;#</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8881&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8882","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Detection of a Meteorite Lake","book":"阅读还原集Vol.17","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.17 · Test 4 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8882:64250:14","type":"choice","text":"With the investigation of the lake, the scientist may predict the climate changes in the future.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Nestled in the heart of Ghana, the lake holds an untapped reservoir of information that could help scientists predict future climate changes by looking at evidence from the past.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问“通过调查湖泊，科学家们可以预测未来的气候变化”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词为\"predict the climate changes in the future\"，在A段中找到\"predict future climate changes\"，与题目完全一致。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，这个坐落于加纳腹地的湖泊蕴藏着未开发的地质信息宝库，科学家们通过分析历史数据，有望预测未来气候变化趋势。因此，题目陈述与原文信息一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64250","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 14-18\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8882:64251:15","type":"choice","text":"The crater resulted from a meteorite impact is the largest and most preserved one in the world.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The resulting crater is one of the largest and most well-preserved geologically young craters in the world, says Scholz, who is collaborating on the project with researchers from the University of Arizona, the University of South Carolina, the University of Rhode Island, and several Ghanaian institutions.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问“由陨石撞击形成的陨石坑是世界上最大和保存最完好的陨石坑”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“largest and most preserved crater”定位到B段中关于陨石坑的描述。\n解题思路：原文提到陨石坑是“one of the largest and most well-preserved geologically young craters in the world”（世界上最大和保存最完好的年轻地质陨石坑之一），但题目表述为“the largest and most preserved one in the world”（世界上最大和保存最完好的陨石坑），原文中的“one of”表示“之一”，不能够确定这个陨石坑是不是最大的，因此答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64251","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 14-18\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8882:64252:16","type":"choice","text":"The water stored in lake Bosumtwi was gone only by seeping through the lake sediments.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Streams flow into the lake, Scholz says, but the water leaves only by evaporation, or by seeping through the lake sediments.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是博松特威湖中储存的水仅通过渗透穿过湖底沉积物排出，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"water stored in Lake Bosumtwi\"和\"gone only by seeping through the lake sediments\"来定位答案。\n解题思路：根据C段中的原文句子可知，虽然有溪流注入湖泊，但湖水仅通过蒸发或渗入湖底沉积物的方式排出。而题目中说水仅通过渗透流失，这与原文信息不符，因此答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64252","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 14-18\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8882:64253:17","type":"choice","text":"Historical climate changes can be detected by the analysis of the sediment in the lake.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For the past million years, the lake has acted as a tropical rain gauge, filling and drying with changes in precipitation and the tropical climate. The record of those changes is hidden in the sediment below the lake bottom.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“通过分析湖底的沉积物可以检测到历史气候变化”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"historical climate changes\"和\"sediment in the lake\"，通过这些词可以定位到C段中关于沉积物记录气候变化的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，过去百万年间，这个湖泊就像热带雨量表一样，随着降水变化和热带气候的更替而涨落。这些变化的记录深藏在湖底沉积物中。说明研究沉积物能够知道历史的降水变化和气候更替，因此，题目与原文信息一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64253","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 14-18\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8882:64254:18","type":"choice","text":"The greatest obstacle to the research of scientists had been the interference by the locals due to\ntheir indigenous believes.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Problems that arose were primarily non-scientific – tree stumps, fishing nets, cultural barriers, and occasional misunderstandings with local villagers.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问科学家们研究的最大障碍，是当地人因其本土信仰而造成的干扰，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"interference by the locals due to their indigenous beliefs\"定位到G段，该段提到研究过程中遇到的问题。\n解题思路：G段提到，出现的问题主要与非科学因素有关——树桩、渔网、文化障碍以及与当地村民偶尔产生的误解。并没有说明哪个问题是最大的，因此，无法判断该说法是否正确，因此，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64254","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 14-18\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8882:64255:19","type":"fill","text":"填写第 19 空","answer":"high-pressure air gun/High-Pressure Air Gun","acceptedAnswers":["high-pressure air gun","High-Pressure Air Gun"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In this process, a high-pressure air gun is used to create small, pneumatic explosions in the water.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是收集数据的三个步骤，要求填写第一个步骤中使用的工具或设备。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"collecting data\"和\"first step\"定位到E段，该段描述了数据收集的第一个步骤。\n解题思路：原文E段明确提到，他们采用名为“地震反射剖面法”的技术，通过高压空气枪在湖底制造微小气动爆炸，这是数据收集的第一个步骤。因此，答案为\"high-pressure air gun\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64255","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nThere are three steps of collecting data from the lake as followings, please fill the blanks in the Flow Chart below, Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer:\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022uatGrSaczA1669984742.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8882:64256:20","type":"fill","text":"填写第 20 空","answer":"sound energy/sound wave","acceptedAnswers":["sound energy","sound wave"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The sound energy penetrates about 1,000 to 2,000 meters into the lake’s subsurface before bouncing back to the surface of the water.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是收集数据的三个步骤，询问第二个步骤中什么会深入水中，再反弹回来。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"three steps of collecting data\"和\"sound energy\"或\"sound wave\"等关键词，定位到E段和F段关于数据收集过程的描述。\n解题思路：E段提到数据收集的第一步是使用高压空气枪在水中制造爆炸，这种声波能量能穿透湖底1000至2000米，最终反弹回水面。因此，应填写\"sound energy\"或\"sound wave\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64256","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nThere are three steps of collecting data from the lake as followings, please fill the blanks in the Flow Chart below, Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer:\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022uatGrSaczA1669984742.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8882:64257:21","type":"fill","text":"填写第 21 空","answer":"cable","acceptedAnswers":["cable"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The reflected sound energy is detected by underwater microphones – called hydrophones – embedded in a 50-meter-long cable that is towed behind the boat as it crosses the lake in a carefully designed grid pattern.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是收集数据的三个步骤，根据上下文推断应填写与数据收集相关的设备或工具。\n定位关键信息：根据流程图中的步骤描述，结合文章中关于数据收集过程的句子，定位到F段描述检测声波反射能量的过程。\n解题思路：F段提到通过水下麦克风（hydrophones）监测反射声能，而这些麦克风嵌入在一个50米长的电缆（cable）中，由船拖拽在湖上移动。因此，空白处应填写\"cable\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64257","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nThere are three steps of collecting data from the lake as followings, please fill the blanks in the Flow Chart below, Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer:\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022uatGrSaczA1669984742.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8882:64258:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"hydrophones/underwater microphones","acceptedAnswers":["hydrophones","underwater microphones"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The reflected sound energy is detected by underwater microphones – called hydrophones – embedded in a 50-meter-long cable that is towed behind the boat as it crosses the lake in a carefully designed grid pattern.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是从湖中收集数据的三个步骤中的其中一个，需要填写收集数据的工具或设备。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"collecting data\"和\"three steps\"可以定位到文章中关于数据收集过程的描述，主要集中在E、F段。\n解题思路：F段提到通过水下麦克风（hydrophones）监测反射声能，而这些麦克风嵌入在一个50米长的电缆（cable）中，由船拖拽在湖上移动。这里直接说明了嵌在电缆中的，用于检测反射声能的工具是\"underwater microphones\"（水下水听器），也称为\"hydrophones\"。因此这两个词都是正确答案，可以用\"hydrophones\"或\"underwater microphones\"填空。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64258","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nThere are three steps of collecting data from the lake as followings, please fill the blanks in the Flow Chart below, Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer:\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022uatGrSaczA1669984742.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8882:64259:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"shipping container/Shipping Container","acceptedAnswers":["shipping container","Shipping Container"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It was constructed in modules that were dismantled, packed inside a shipping container, and reassembled over a 10-day period in late November and early December 1999 in the rural village of Abono, Ghana.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是船R/V Kilindi拆卸后被存放在哪里。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"boat-dubbed R/V Kilindi\"和\"dismantled and stored\"可以定位到D段，找到船被拆卸并存放的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，这艘被命名为R/V Kilindi的科考船于去年在佛罗里达州建造。该船采用模块化建造方式，这些模块被拆解后装入集装箱，因此答案为\"shipping container\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64259","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 23-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8882:64260:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"seismic reflection profiling/Seismic Reflection Profiling","acceptedAnswers":["seismic reflection profiling","Seismic Reflection Profiling"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In mid-January, five members of the team – Keely Brooks, an earth sciences graduate student; Peter Cattaneo, a research analyst; and Kiram Lezzar, a postdoctoral scholar, all from SU; James McGill, a geophysical field engineer; and Nick Peters, a Ph.D. student in geophysics from the University of Miami – returned to Abono to begin collecting data about the lake’s subsurface using a technique called seismic reflection profiling.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是他们使用的叫做什么技术的。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的technology和used定位到E段研究过程。\n解题思路：根据原文中E段提到的，他们采用名为“地震反射剖面法”的技术，using a technique called seismic reflection profiling，可以确定他们使用的技术名称是seismic reflection profiling地震反射剖面法。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64260","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 23-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8882:64261:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"laboratory/Laboratory","acceptedAnswers":["laboratory","Laboratory"],"explanation":"原文答案句：On-board computers record the signals, and the resulting data are then processed and analyzed in the laboratory.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是，他们将声能传递至湖底1000至2000米处，并使用独立设备收集反射回来的声波。随后，这些数据在哪里进行分析与处理。\n定位关键信息：题目中提到了\"data had been analyzed and processed\"，通过这个关键词可以在F段找到对应的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文句子，船载计算机记录信号后，相关数据将在实验室进行处理分析。因此答案为\"laboratory\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64261","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 23-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8882:64262:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"three dimensional perspective/Three Dimensional Perspective","acceptedAnswers":["three dimensional perspective","Three Dimensional Perspective"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘The results will give us a good idea of the shape of the basin, how thick the layers of sediment are, and when and where there were major changes in sediment accumulation,’ Scholz says, ‘We are now developing a three dimensional perspective of the lake’s subsurface and the layers of sediment that have been laid down.’\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问Scholz补充说明他们正在构建什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的Scholz和building定位到F段末句，找到\"We are now developing a three dimensional perspective\"。\n解题思路：原文提到，肖尔茨表示，“目前我们正在构建湖泊水下结构的三维立体模型，并还原沉积层的形成过程。”题目中的building对应原文的developing，答案应为three dimensional perspective。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64262","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 23-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8882:64263:27","type":"fill","text":"填写第 27 空","answer":"fishing nets/Fishing Nets","acceptedAnswers":["fishing nets","Fishing Nets"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Problems that arose were primarily non-scientific – tree stumps, fishing nets, cultural barriers, and occasional misunderstandings with local villagers.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是船在湖面上航行时需要避免的物理障碍物，包括树桩和什么漂浮在湖面上的东西。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"physical barrier\"、\"tree stumps\"和\"floating on the surface of the lake\"可以定位到G段中提到的非科学性问题。\n解题思路：在G段中，作者明确提到了船在湖面上航行时遇到的一些非科学性问题，其中包括树桩、渔网、文化障碍和与当地村民的偶尔误解。题目中已经提到了树桩，因此需要找到与之并列的另一障碍物。因此，答案为\"fishing nets\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64263","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 23-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64250","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 14-18\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>With the investigation of the lake, the scientist may predict the climate changes in the future.</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"64251","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 14-18\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>The crater resulted from a meteorite impact is the largest and most preserved one in the world.</strong></p>","firstNumber":15},{"id":"64252","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 14-18\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>The water stored in lake Bosumtwi was gone only by seeping through the lake sediments.</strong></p>","firstNumber":16},{"id":"64253","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 14-18\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>Historical climate changes can be detected by the analysis of the sediment in the lake.</strong></p>","firstNumber":17},{"id":"64254","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 14-18\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage? In boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>The greatest obstacle to the research of scientists had been the interference by the locals due to\ntheir indigenous believes.</strong></p>","firstNumber":18},{"id":"64255","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nThere are three steps of collecting data from the lake as followings, please fill the blanks in the Flow Chart below, Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer:\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022uatGrSaczA1669984742.png]","html":"<p><strong>19</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"64256","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nThere are three steps of collecting data from the lake as followings, please fill the blanks in the Flow Chart below, Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer:\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022uatGrSaczA1669984742.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">20 </strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"64257","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nThere are three steps of collecting data from the lake as followings, please fill the blanks in the Flow Chart below, Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer:\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022uatGrSaczA1669984742.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">21 <strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong></strong></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"64258","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nThere are three steps of collecting data from the lake as followings, please fill the blanks in the Flow Chart below, Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer:\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022uatGrSaczA1669984742.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">22 <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong></strong></p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"64259","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 23-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>23</strong> The boat-double R/V Kilindi crossed the lake was dismantled and stored in a <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"64260","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 23-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>24</strong> The technology they used called <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> ;</p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"64261","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 23-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>25</strong> They created sound energy into 1000-2000 metres\ninto the bottom of the lake and used separate equipment to collect the returned waves. Then the data had been analyzed and processed in the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"64262","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 23-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>26</strong> Scholz also added that they were now\nbuilding <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":26},{"id":"64263","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 23-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>27</strong> View of the sediment or sub-image in the bottom of the lake. The whole set\nof equipment works well yet the ship should avoid physical barrier including tree stumps or\n<strong class=\"source-blank\">[27] ____</strong> floating on the surface of the lake.</p>","firstNumber":27}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Detection of a Meteorite Lake</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>As the sun rose over picturesque Lake Bosumtwi, a team of Syracuse University researchers prepared for another day of using state-of-the-art equipment to help bottom. Nestled in the heart of Ghana, the lake holds an untapped reservoir of information that could help scientists predict future climate changes by looking at evidence from the past. This information will also improve the scientists’ understanding of the changes that occur in a region struck by a massive meteorite.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The project, led by earth sciences professor Christopher Scholz of the College of Arts and Sciences and funded by the National Science Foundation (NSF), is the first large-scale effort to study Lake Bosumtwi, which formed 1.1 million years ago when a giant meteor crashed into the Earth’s surface. The resulting crater is one of the largest and most well-preserved geologically young craters in the world, says Scholz, who is collaborating on the project with researchers from the University of Arizona, the University of South Carolina, the University of Rhode Island, and several Ghanaian institutions. ‘Our data should provide information about what happens when an impact hits hard, pre-Cambrian, crystalline rocks that are a billion years old,’ he says.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Equally important is the fact that the lake, which is about 8 kilometers in diameter, has no natural outlet. The rim of the crater rises about 250 meters above the water’s surface. Streams flow into the lake, Scholz says, but the water leaves only by evaporation, or by seeping through the lake sediments. For the past million years, the lake has acted as a tropical rain gauge, filling and drying with changes in precipitation and the tropical climate. The record of those changes is hidden in the sediment below the lake bottom. ‘The lake is one of the best sites in the world for the study of tropical climate changes,’ Scholz says, ‘The tropics are the heat engine for the Earth’s climate. To understand the global climate, we need to have records of climate changes from many sites around the world, including the tropics.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Before the researchers could explore the lake’s subsurface, they needed a boat with a large, working deck area that could carry eight tons of scientific equipment. The boat – dubbed R/V Kilindi – was built in Florida last year. It was constructed in modules that were dismantled, packed inside a shipping container, and reassembled over a 10-day period in late November and early December 1999 in the rural village of Abono, Ghana. The research team then spent the next two weeks testing the boat and equipment before returning to the United States for the holidays.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In mid-January, five members of the team – Keely Brooks, an earth sciences graduate student; Peter Cattaneo, a research analyst; and Kiram Lezzar, a postdoctoral scholar, all from SU; James McGill, a geophysical field engineer; and Nick Peters, a Ph.D. student in geophysics from the University of Miami – returned to Abono to begin collecting data about the lake’s subsurface using a technique called seismic reflection profiling. In this process, a high-pressure air gun is used to create small, pneumatic explosions in the water. The sound energy penetrates about 1,000 to 2,000 meters into the lake’s subsurface before bouncing back to the surface of the water.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The reflected sound energy is detected by underwater microphones – called hydrophones – embedded in a 50-meter-long cable that is towed behind the boat as it crosses the lake in a carefully designed grid pattern. On-board computers record the signals, and the resulting data are then processed and analyzed in the laboratory. ‘The results will give us a good idea of the shape of the basin, how thick the layers of sediment are, and when and where there were major changes in sediment accumulation,’ Scholz says, ‘We are now developing a three dimensional perspective of the lake’s subsurface and the layers of sediment that have been laid down.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Team members spent about four weeks in Ghana collecting the data. They worked seven days a week, arriving at the lake just after sunrise. On a good day, when everything went as planned, the team could collect data and be back at the dock by early afternoon. Except for a few relatively minor adjustments, the equipment and the boat worked well. Problems that arose were primarily non-scientific – tree stumps, fishing nets, cultural barriers, and occasional misunderstandings with local villagers.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Lake Bosumtwi, the largest natural freshwater lake in the country, is sacred to the Ashanti people, who believe their souls come to the lake to bid farewell to their god. The lake is also the primary source of fish for the 26 surrounding villages. Conventional canoes and boats are forbidden. Fishermen travel on the lake by floating on traditional planks they propel with small paddles. Before the research project could begin, Scholz and his Ghanaian counterparts had to secure special permission from tribal chiefs to put the R/V Kilindi on the lake.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>When the team began gathering data, rumors flew around the lake as to why the researchers were there. ‘Some thought we were dredging the lake for gold, others thought we were going to drain the lake or that we had bought the lake,’ Cattaneo says, ‘But once the local people understood why we were there, they were very helpful.’</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8882&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8883","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 The Secrets of Persuasion","book":"阅读还原集Vol.17","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.17 · Test 4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8883:64264:28","type":"choice","text":"The main purpose of Cialdini's research of writing is to","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He concluded there were six general ‘principles of influence’ and has since put them to the test under slightly more scientific conditions. Most recently, that has meant messing about with towels. Many hotels leave a little card in each bathroom asking guests to reuse towels and thus conserve water and electricity and reduce pollution. Cialdini and his colleagues wanted to test the relative effectiveness of different words on those cards.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是Cialdini进行文字研究的主要目的是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Cialdini's research of writing\"，可以在C段找到Cialdini研究不同的标语的宣传效果。\n解题思路：C段中提到许多Cialdini在现实世界中研究说服力的例子，比如，参加各类销售培训课程，总结出了说服力法则，想要通过毛巾实验，测试卡片上不同标语的宣传效果，为这些法则提供更加科学的证明。说明进行标语文字研究，是想要证明说服心理学是科学的，这与选项D一致。其他选项A、B、C的内容在原文中均未提及或与原文表述不符。","options":["explain the reason way researcher should investigate in person.","explore the secret that why some people become the famous salesperson.","help people to sale products.","prove maybe there is a science in the psychology of persuasion."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64264","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 28-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8883:64265:29","type":"choice","text":"Which of the statement is CORRECT according to Cialdini’s research methodology?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He began to research influence in the real world, enrolling in sales-training programmes: ‘I learnt how to sell automobiles from a lot, how to sell insurance from an office, how to sell encyclopedias door to door.’\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是根据Cialdini的研究方法，哪个陈述是正确的。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“Cialdini’s research methodology”定位到文章中关于Cialdini研究方法的描述。在C段中，明确提到他通过参加销售培训课程来研究影响力。\n解题思路：根据C段原文，Cialdini通过参加销售培训课程来研究说法力，包括学习如何在停车场销售汽车、在办公室销售保险以及上门销售百科全书。这与选项C相符，因为参加销售培训课程本身就是与销售人员接触并学习他们的方法。因此，选项C是正确的。","options":["He checked data in a lot of latest books.","He conducted this experiment in the laboratory.","He interviewed and contract with many salespeople.","He made lot phone calls collecting what he wants to know."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64265","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 28-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8883:64266:30","type":"choice","text":"Which of the following is CORRECT according to towel experiment in the passage?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：To test this, the researchers changed the card’s message from an environmental one to the simple (and truthful) statement that the majority of guests at the hotel had reused their towel at least once. Guests given this message were 26% more likely to reuse their towels than those given the old message.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是根据文章中的毛巾实验，以下哪一项是正确的。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键词\"towel experiment\"定位到C段，该段详细描述了Cialdini的毛巾实验。\n解题思路：根据C段原文，研究人员将卡片上的信息从环保口号改为\"大多数客人至少重复使用过一次毛巾\"这一陈述，结果显示，收到新标语的客人重复使用毛巾的比例比旧标语组高出26%。因此，选项C\"更多客人倾向于合作，因为信息要求他们这样做，而不是简单地出于环保考虑\"与原文描述一致。选项A、B、D均未在原文中明确提及或与原文信息不符。","options":["Different hotel guests act in a different response.","Most guests act by the idea of environment preservation.","More customers tend to cooperate as the message requires than simply act environmentally.","People tend to follow the hotel’s original message more."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64266","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 28-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8883:64267:31","type":"choice","text":"Which of the following is CORRECT according to the candy shop experiment in the passage?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：When the chocolates arrived in a heap with the bill, tips went up a miserly 3% compared to when no chocolate was given. But when the chocolates were dropped individually in front of each diner, tips went up 14%. The scientific breakthrough, though, came when the waitress gave each diner one chocolate, headed away from the table then doubled back to give them one more each as if such generosity had only just occurred to her. Tips went up 23%.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是根据文章中糖果店实验，以下哪一项是正确的。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"the candy shop experiment\"，根据这个关键词可以在文章中定位到D段，该段详细描述了糖果店实验的过程和结果。\n解题思路：根据D段中的原文答案句，研究发现，关键在于赠送方式：当巧克力与账单一同堆放在桌上时，小费仅微涨3%；而当巧克力被单独递到每位顾客面前时，小费飙升14%。真正的科学突破出现在服务员给每位顾客一颗巧克力后转身离开，又折返多递一颗时——这种“互惠”行为让小费暴涨23%。这表明，赠送巧克力的方式影响了用餐者的小费。因此，选项A\"Presenting way affects diner’s tips.\"是正确的。","options":["Presenting way affects diner’s tips.","Regular customer gives tips more than irregulars.","People give tips only when offered chocolate.","Chocolate with bill got higher tips."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64267","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 28-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8883:64268:32","type":"choice","text":"Robert Cialdini experienced “principles of influence” himself in realistic life.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He found that laboratory experiments on the psychology of persuasion were telling only part of the story, so he began to research influence in the real world, enrolling in sales-training programmes: ‘I learnt how to sell automobiles from a lot, how to sell insurance from an office, how to sell encyclopedias door to door.’\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问罗伯特·西奥迪尼是否在现实生活中亲身体验了“说服力原则”。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“Robert Cialdini”和“principles of influence”定位到C段，找到关于他验证这些原则的描述。\n解题思路：原文提到，他发现实验室里关于说服心理学的实验只能揭示部分真相，于是开始在现实世界中研究说服力，报名参加销售培训课程：“我学会了如何在车行批量销售汽车，如何在办公室推销保险，如何挨家挨户推销百科全书”。题目中的“in realistic life”与原文的“real world”和“realistic conditions”对应，说明他确实在现实生活中体验了这些原则。因此，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64268","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 32-35\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8883:64269:33","type":"choice","text":"Principle of persuasion has different types in different countries.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But she certainly understands the general principle of reciprocity. The way to a diner’s heart is to give them something they’re not expecting in the way of service.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“说服原则在不同国家有不同的类型”是否与文章作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"principle of persuasion\"和\"different types in different countries\"来定位答案。\n解题思路：根据原文，E段中提到，新西兰的餐厅不会和美国餐厅使用同样的招数，毕竟小费文化不同，但E段中的运营经理提到，她也明白互惠原则的说服力，只不过在两个国家带来的结果不同，但文中并未提及不同国家是否有不同的类型的说服原则。因此，无法确定题目中的内容，所以答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64269","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 32-35\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8883:64270:34","type":"choice","text":"In New Zealand, people tend to give tips to attendants after being served chocolate.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘In America, it would translate into an instant tip. In New Zealand, it translates into a huge smile and thanks to you.’ And no doubt, return visits.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问在新西兰，收到巧克力后，人们会给服务员小费，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"New Zealand\"定位到E段。\n解题思路：原文D段提到的是在美国的研究，巧克力的赠送方式与小费的关系，但并未提到新西兰的情况。E段提到新西兰的小费与美国不同，明确说明“在美国，这会换来小费；在新西兰，顾客会报以灿烂笑容和‘谢谢’，更别说还会主动再来。”因此，题目中的信息与文中不符，选择FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64270","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 32-35\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8883:64271:35","type":"choice","text":"Elder generation of New Zealand is easily attracted by extra service of restaurants by the principle\nof reciprocity.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The way to a diner’s heart is to give them something they’re not expecting in the way of service. It might be something as small as leaving a mint on their plate, or it might be remembering that last time they were in they wanted their water with no ice and no lemon. ‘In America, it would translate into an instant tip. In New Zealand, it translates into a huge smile and thanks to you.’ And no doubt, return visits.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是新西兰老一辈人很容易被餐厅的额外服务吸引，因为他们秉持互惠互利的原则，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“elder generation of New Zealand”、“extra service of restaurants”和“principle of reciprocity”来定位答案在文章中的位置。\n解题思路：在E段中，作者提到了新西兰的餐厅服务员使用互惠原则来吸引顾客，但并没有明确提到老年人是否容易被这种策略所吸引。因此，题目中的信息在文章中没有明确给出，所以答案是Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64271","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 32-35\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8883:64272:36","type":"choice","text":"36 Some expert may reveal qualification in front of clients.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：  ‘You’d be surprised how many people fail to do that,’ says Cialdini， ‘They feel it’s impolite to talk about their expertise.’ In one study, therapists whose patients wouldn’t do their exercises were advised to display their qualification certificates prominently. They did and experienced an immediate leap in patient compliance.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“一些专家可能会在客户面前展示他们的资质”，这属于哪项说服原则。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词“expert may reveal qualification in front of clients”，可以定位到G段中关于“Authority”的描述。\n解题思路：原文中提到，专家们展示他们的资质证书后，患者的配合度立即提高。这与题目中“专家在客户面前展示资质”的意思一致。因此，答案为B，对应G段中关于“Authority”权威性原则的描述。","options":["Reciprocity of scarcity","Authority","previous comment","Linking","Social Proof"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64272","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Reciprocity of scarcity\nB Authority\nC previous comment\nD Linking\nE Social Proof"},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8883:64272:37","type":"choice","text":"37 Parents tend to say something that other kids are doing the same.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Useful for parents, says Cialdini. ‘Find groups of children who are behaving in a way that you would like your child to, because the child looks to the side, rather than at you.’\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是父母常会说其他孩子也在做同样的事，这属于哪项说服原则。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"Parents\"和\"children\"，直接定位到J段。\n解题思路：原文J段提到，Cialdini指出这对父母具有指导意义。‘寻找那些行为符合您期望的儿童群体，会让孩子们注意到同龄人是怎么做的，这与题目中\"other kids are doing the same\"完全一致，这属于说服原则中的社会认同原则，因此答案为E。","options":["Reciprocity of scarcity","Authority","previous comment","Linking","Social Proof"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64272","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Reciprocity of scarcity\nB Authority\nC previous comment\nD Linking\nE Social Proof"},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8883:64272:38","type":"choice","text":"38 Advertisers ruthlessly exploit the limitation of chances.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Advertisers ruthlessly exploit scarcity (‘limit four per customer’, ‘sale must end soon’), and Cialdini suggests parents do too: ‘Kids want things that are less available, so say “this is an unusual opportunity; you can only have this for a certain time”.’\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是广告商们不择手段地利用稀缺性，这属于哪项说服原则。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"Advertisers ruthlessly exploit the limitation of chances\"定位到F段中描述广告商行为的句子。\n解题思路：原文F段提到，人们总想拥有更多稀缺资源。广告商惯用‘限量四件/顾客’、‘限时特卖’等策略来推销产品。这与题干描述一致，属于说服原则里的稀缺性原则，因此答案为A。","options":["Reciprocity of scarcity","Authority","previous comment","Linking","Social Proof"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64272","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Reciprocity of scarcity\nB Authority\nC previous comment\nD Linking\nE Social Proof"},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8883:64272:39","type":"choice","text":"39 Use a familiar name in a survey.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：When the researcher gave a fake name resembling that of the subject (eg, Cynthia Johnson is sent a survey by ‘Cindy Johansen’), surveys were twice as likely to be completed.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是，在调查中使用熟悉的名字，这属于哪项说服原则。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"use a familiar name in a survey\"（在调查中使用熟悉的名字）定位到文章中相关句子。\n解题思路：在I段中提到，研究者使用与受试者相似的化名（例如，辛西娅·约翰逊收到的问卷上署名为“辛迪·约翰森”）时，问卷完成率竟翻倍。这与题目中描述的做法完全一致，属于说服原则中的联系原则，因此，D是正确答案。","options":["Reciprocity of scarcity","Authority","previous comment","Linking","Social Proof"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64272","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Reciprocity of scarcity\nB Authority\nC previous comment\nD Linking\nE Social Proof"},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8883:64272:40","type":"choice","text":"40 Ask colleagues to offer a helping hand.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Exploit this to get a higher sign-up rate when soliciting charitable donations. First, ask workmates if they think they will sponsor you on your egg-and-spoon marathon. Later, return with the sponsorship form to those who said yes and remind them of their earlier commitment.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是“要求同事提供帮助”，这属于哪项说服原则。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"ask colleagues to offer a helping hand\"在文章中定位答案。\n解题思路：在H段中提到善用这一点，在募捐时能有效提升参与率。先询问同事是否愿意赞助你的‘鸡蛋与勺子’挑战赛，随后向同意者寄送赞助表，提醒他们兑现承诺。这与题目中描述的做法一致，属于说服原则中的承诺原则，因此，C是正确答案。","options":["Reciprocity of scarcity","Authority","previous comment","Linking","Social Proof"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64272","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Reciprocity of scarcity\nB Authority\nC previous comment\nD Linking\nE Social Proof"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64264","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 28-31 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>The main purpose of Cialdini&#39;s research of writing is to</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"64265","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 28-31 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Which of the statement is CORRECT according to Cialdini’s research methodology?</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"64266","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 28-31 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Which of the following is CORRECT according to towel experiment in the passage?</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"64267","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 28-31 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Which of the following is CORRECT according to the candy shop experiment in the passage?</strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"64268","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 32-35\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Robert Cialdini experienced “principles of influence” himself in realistic life.</strong></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"64269","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 32-35\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Principle of persuasion has different types in different countries.</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"64270","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 32-35\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>In New Zealand, people tend to give tips to attendants after being served chocolate.</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"64271","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 32-35\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Elder generation of New Zealand is easily attracted by extra service of restaurants by the principle\nof reciprocity.</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"64272","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Reciprocity of scarcity\nB Authority\nC previous comment\nD Linking\nE Social Proof","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> Reciprocity of scarcity <br/></p><p><strong>B</strong> Authority <br/></p><p><strong>C</strong> previous comment <br/></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>D</strong> Linking <br/></p><p><strong>36</strong> Some expert may reveal qualification in front of clients. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[36] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":36}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The Secrets of Persuasion</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Our mother may have told you the secret to getting what you ask for was to say please. The reality is rather more surprising. Adam Dudding talks to a psychologist who has made a life’s work from the science of persuasion. Some scientists peer at things through high-powered microscopes. Others goad rats through mazes or mix bubbling fluids in glass beakers. Robert Cialdini, for his part, does curious things with towels and believes that by doing so he is discovering important insights into how society works.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Cialdini’s towel experiments (more of them later), are part of his research into how we persuade others to say yes. He wants to know why some people have a knack for bending the will of others, be it a telephone cold-caller talking to you about timeshares, or a parent whose children are compliant even without threats of extreme violence. While he’s anxious not to be seen as the man who’s written the bible for snake-oil salesmen, for decades the Arizona State University social psychology professor has been creating systems for the principles and methods of persuasion and writing bestsellers about them. Some people seem to be born with the skills; Cialdini’s claim is that by applying a little science, even those of us who aren’t should be able to get our own way more often. ‘All my life I’ve been an easy mark for the blandishment of salespeople and fundraisers and I’d always wondered why they could get me to buy things I didn’t want and give to causes I hadn’t heard of,’ says Cialdini on the phone from London, where his is plugging his latest book.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>He found that laboratory experiments on the psychology of persuasion were telling only part of the story, so he began to research influence in the real world, enrolling in sales-training programmes: ‘I learnt how to sell automobiles from a lot, how to sell insurance from an office, how to sell encyclopedias door to door.’ He concluded there were six general ‘principles of influence’ and has since put them to the test under slightly more scientific conditions. Most recently, that has meant messing about with towels. Many hotels leave a little card in each bathroom asking guests to reuse towels and thus conserve water and electricity and reduce pollution. Cialdini and his colleagues wanted to test the relative effectiveness of different words on those cards. Would guests be motivated to co-operate simply because it would help save the planet, or were other factors more compelling? To test this, the researchers changed the card’s message from an environmental one to the simple (and truthful) statement that the majority of guests at the hotel had reused their towel at least once. Guests given this message were 26% more likely to reuse their towels than those given the old message. In Cialdini’s book ‘Yes! 50 Secrets from the Science of Persuasion’, co-written with another social scientist and a business consultant, he explains that guests were responding to the persuasive force of ‘social proof’, the idea that our decisions are strongly influenced by what we believe other people like us are doing.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>So much for towels. Cialdini has also learnt a lot from confectionery. Yes! Cites the work of New Jersey behavioural scientist David Strohmetz, who wanted to see how restaurant patrons would respond to ridiculously small favour from their food server, in the form of after-dinner chocolate for each diner. The secret, it seems, is in how you give the chocolate. When the chocolates arrived in a heap with the bill, tips went up a miserly 3% compared to when no chocolate was given. But when the chocolates were dropped individually in front of each diner, tips went up 14%. The scientific breakthrough, though, came when the waitress gave each diner one chocolate, headed away from the table then doubled back to give them one more each as if such generosity had only just occurred to her. Tips went up 23%. This is ‘reciprocity’ in action: we want to return favours done to us, often without bothering to calculate the relative value of what is being received and given.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Geeling Ng, operations manager at Auckland’s Soul Bar, says she’s never heard of Kiwi waiting staff using such a cynical trick, not least because New Zealand tipping culture is so different from that of the US: ‘If you did that in New Zealand, as diners were leaving they’d say “can we have some more?”’ But she certainly understands the general principle of reciprocity. The way to a diner’s heart is to give them something they’re not expecting in the way of service. It might be something as small as leaving a mint on their plate, or it might be remembering that last time they were in they wanted their water with no ice and no lemon. ‘In America, it would translate into an instant tip. In New Zealand, it translates into a huge smile and thanks to you.’ And no doubt, return visits.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>THE FIVE PRINCIPLES OF PERSUASION</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>Reciprocity:&nbsp;</strong>People want to give back to those who have given to them. The trick here is to get in first. That’s why charities put a crummy pen inside a mailout, and why smiling women in supermarkets hand out dollops of free food. Scarcity: People want more of things they can have less of. Advertisers ruthlessly exploit scarcity (‘limit four per customer’, ‘sale must end soon’), and Cialdini suggests parents do too: ‘Kids want things that are less available, so say “this is an unusual opportunity; you can only have this for a certain time”.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>Authority:&nbsp;</strong>We trust people who know what they’re talking about. So inform people honestly of your credentials before you set out to influence them. ‘You’d be surprised how many people fail to do that,’ says Cialdini， ‘They feel it’s impolite to talk about their expertise.’ In one study, therapists whose patients wouldn’t do their exercises were advised to display their qualification certificates prominently. They did and experienced an immediate leap in patient compliance.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>Commitment/consistency:&nbsp;</strong>We want to act in a way that is consistent with the commitments we have already made. Exploit this to get a higher sign-up rate when soliciting charitable donations. First, ask workmates if they think they will sponsor you on your egg-and-spoon marathon. Later, return with the sponsorship form to those who said yes and remind them of their earlier commitment.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>Linking:&nbsp;</strong>We say yes more often to people we like. Obvious enough, but reasons for ‘linking’ can be weird. In one study, people were sent survey forms and asked to return them to a named researcher. When the researcher gave a fake name resembling that of the subject (eg, Cynthia Johnson is sent a survey by ‘Cindy Johansen’), surveys were twice as likely to be completed. We favour people who resemble us, even if the resemblance is as minor as the sound of their name.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>Social proof:</strong>&nbsp;We decide what to do by looking around to see what others just like us are doing. Useful for parents, says Cialdini. ‘Find groups of children who are behaving in a way that you would like your child to, because the child looks to the side, rather than at you.’ More perniciously, social proof is the force underpinning the competitive materialism of ‘keeping up with the Joneses’.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8883&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8865","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Andrea Palladio: Italian Architect","book":"阅读还原集Vol.17","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.17 · Test 3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8865:64159:1","type":"choice","text":"The building where the exhibition is staged has been newly renovated.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The exhibition has the special advantage of being held in one of Palladio’s buildings, Palazzo Barbaran da Porto.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问“展览举办的建筑是否经过翻新”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"the building where the exhibition is staged\"（展览举办的建筑）和\"newly renovated\"（新翻新）定位原文，找到展览地点Palazzo Barbaran da Porto的描述。\n解题思路：原文B段提到展览在Palazzo Barbaran da Porto举办，而之后的内容则是对这栋建筑的装潢、结构进行描述，并没有关于它是否翻新整修的内容。故答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64159","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8865:64160:2","type":"choice","text":"Palazzo Barbaran da Porto typically represents the Palladio's design.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Its bold facade is a mixture of rustication and decoration set between two rows of elegant columns. On the second floor, the pediments are alternately curved or pointed, a Palladian trademark. The harmonious proportions of the atrium at the entrance lead through to a dramatic interior of fine fireplaces and painted ceilings. Palladio’s design is simple, clear and not over-crowded.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问“Palazzo Barbaran da Porto通常代表Palladio的设计”是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“Palazzo Barbaran da Porto”和“Palladio’s design”定位到B段，该段详细描述了Palazzo Barbaran da Porto的建筑特点，并明确指出这是Palladio的设计，且其设计特点是“simple, clear and not over-crowded”。\n解题思路：B段明确提到Palazzo Barbaran da Porto是Palladio的建筑，并且明确指出，二层的山墙设计交替呈现弧形与尖顶，堪称帕拉第奥建筑的标志性特征。与题目所述“代表Palladio的设计”完全一致，因此答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64160","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8865:64161:3","type":"choice","text":"Palladio's father worked as an architect.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：His father was a miller who settled in Vicenza, where the young Andrea was apprenticed to a skilled stonemason.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问Palladio的父亲是建筑师，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的\"Palladio’s father\"和\"worked as an architect\"定位到C段第一句，明确父亲是miller（磨坊主）。\n解题思路：原文明确指出Palladio的父亲是磨坊主，而非建筑师，因此题目说法与原文矛盾，答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64161","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8865:64162:4","type":"choice","text":"Palladio's family refused to pay for his architectural studies.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He was plainly intelligent, and lucky enough to come across a rich patron, Gian Giorgio Trissino, a landowner and scholar, who organised his education, taking him to Rome in the 1540s, where he studied the masterpieces of classical Roman and Greek architecture and the work of other influential architects of the time, such as Donato Bramante and Raphael.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问Palladio的家人拒绝支付他的建筑学习费用，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"family\"和\"architectural studies\"定位到C段，其中提到Palladio的父亲是一名磨坊主，而他的教育是由一位富有的赞助人Gian Giorgio Trissino安排的。\n解题思路：原文中提到Palladio的教育是由一位富有的赞助人Gian Giorgio Trissino安排的，并没有提到他的家人拒绝支付他的建筑学习费用。因此，题目中的信息在原文中没有明确提及，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64162","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8865:64163:5","type":"choice","text":"Palladio's alternative design for the Ducal Palace in Venice was based on an English building.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He offered an alternative design which bears an uncanny resemblance to the Banqueting House in Whitehall in London. Since it was designed by Inigo Jones, Palladio’s first foreign disciple, this is not as surprising as it sounds.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“Palladio为威尼斯的Ducal Palace提供的替代方案是基于一栋英国建筑”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“Palladio’s alternative design for the Ducal Palace in Venice”和“based on an English building”来定位答案。\n解题思路：根据E段中的原文句子，Palladio为Ducal Palace提供的替代设计方案与伦敦的Whitehall的Banqueting House非常相似，而这个Banqueting House是由Palladio的第一个外国门徒Inigo Jones设计的，所以有些相像。题目中说的是Palladio的设计是基于英国建筑的，因此，题目与原文信息不符，所以答案是False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64163","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8865:64164:6","type":"choice","text":"Palladio designed both wealthy and poor people.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Palladio’s work for rich landowners alienates unreconstructed critics on the Italian left, but among the papers in the show are designed for cheap housing in Venice.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问帕拉第奥为富人和穷人都设计过建筑，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"wealthy and poor people\"定位到G段，找到\"rich landowners\"和\"cheap housing\"。\n解题思路：原文提到，帕拉第奥为富裕地主设计的建筑令意大利左翼的保守派批评家们嗤之以鼻，但展览中却展出了他为威尼斯廉价住宅设计的建筑图纸。说明他确实为富人和穷人设计了建筑，因此题目陈述与原文信息一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64164","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8865:64165:7","type":"choice","text":"The exhibition includes paintings of people by famous artists","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Vicenza’s show contains detailed models of the major buildings and is leavened by portraits of Palladio’s teachers and clients by Titian, Veronese and Tintoretto; the paintings of his Venetian buildings are all by Canaletto, no less.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问展览包含著名艺术家创作的肖像画，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"paintings of people by famous artists\"定位到H段，找到\"portraits of Palladio’s teachers and clients by Titian, Veronese and Tintoretto\"（提香、委罗内塞和丁托列托创作的肖像画）。\n解题思路：H段明确提到，维琴察展览馆内陈列着帕拉第奥主要建筑的精细模型，其间穿插着提香、维罗内塞和丁托列托为帕拉第奥师生绘制的肖像画，与题干描述完全一致，因此答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64165","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8865:64166:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"Stonemason/stonemason","acceptedAnswers":["Stonemason","stonemason"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Palladio’s father was a miller who settled in Vicenza, where the young Andrea was apprenticed to a skilled stonemason.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是帕拉迪奥在成为建筑师之前，曾接受过什么职业的培训。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"before he became an architect\"可以定位到C段，该段讲述了帕拉迪奥早年经历。\n解题思路：原文句子明确提到，帕拉迪奥的父亲是位磨坊主，定居在维琴察，年轻的安德烈亚在那里成为一位熟练的石匠学徒。这表明他在成为建筑师之前接受的职业培训是石匠。因此，答案为Stonemason。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64166","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet","maxWords":3},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8865:64167:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"Gian Giorgio Trissino/gian giorgio trissino","acceptedAnswers":["Gian Giorgio Trissino","gian giorgio trissino"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Gian Giorgio Trissino, a landowner and scholar, who organised his education, taking him to Rome in the 1540s, where he studied the masterpieces of classical Roman and Greek architecture and the work of other influential architects of the time, such as Donato Bramante and Raphael.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“谁安排帕拉迪奥进行建筑学习”。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"arranged Palladio’s architectural studies\"可以定位到C段中提到\"arranged for Palladio to study architecture\"。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，地主兼学者詹·乔尔乔·特里西诺。这位赞助人不仅资助他前往罗马深造，更亲自安排其学业。因此答案为Gian Giorgio Trissino。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64167","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet","maxWords":3},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8865:64168:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"Inigo Jones/inigo jones","acceptedAnswers":["Inigo Jones","inigo jones"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Since it was designed by Inigo Jones, Palladio’s first foreign disciple, this is not as surprising as it sounds.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“谁是第一个受到帕拉第奥影响的外国建筑师？”\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“first non-Italian architect”和“influenced by Palladio”在文章中定位，找到E段中相关句子。\n解题思路：原文中E段明确指出，帕拉第奥的第一位外国门徒是伊尼戈·琼斯，直接对应题目要求，因此答案为“Inigo Jones”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64168","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet","maxWords":3},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8865:64169:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"Temple/temple/temple architecture/Temple architecture/Temple Architecture","acceptedAnswers":["Temple","temple","temple architecture","Temple architecture","Temple Architecture"],"explanation":"原文答案句：What they show is how Palladio drew on the buildings of ancient Rome as models. The major theme of both his rural and urban building was temple architecture, with a strong pointed pediment supported by columns and approached by wide steps.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是哪种类型的古罗马建筑对Palladio的作品影响最深。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"Ancient Roman buildings\"和\"Palladio’s work\"在文章中定位相关句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，他的这些作品说明了帕拉第奥是以古罗马建筑为范本。无论是乡村还是城市建筑，他设计的核心主题都是神庙式建筑——由柱子支撑的尖顶山墙，以及通向神殿的宽阔台阶。因此，古罗马的神庙式建筑是对Palladio影响最大的建筑类型，答案为\"Temple\"或\"Temple Architecture\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64169","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet","maxWords":3},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8865:64170:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"Quattro Libri dell'Architettura/quattro libri dell'architettura","acceptedAnswers":["Quattro Libri dell'Architettura","quattro libri dell'architettura"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In the wider world, Palladio’s reputation has been nurtured by a text he wrote and illustrated, ‘Quattro Libri dell’ Architettura’.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问帕拉迪奥写了什么作品来提升他的声誉。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Palladio\"和\"strengthened his reputation\"定位到G段中提到帕拉迪奥的作品及其声誉提升的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，帕拉第奥的声誉得益于他撰写的图文并茂的著作《建筑四书》。因此答案为\"quattro libri dell'architettura\"或\"Quattro Libri dell'Architettura\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64170","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet","maxWords":3},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8865:64171:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"benevolent calm/Benevolent Calm","acceptedAnswers":["benevolent calm","Benevolent Calm"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This is an uncompromising exhibition; many of the drawings are small and faint, and there are no sideshows for children, but the impact of harmonious lines and satisfying proportions is to impart in a viewer a feeling of benevolent calm.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是，根据作者的观点，参观展览的访客会有什么样的感觉。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"visitors\"、\"exhibition\"和\"feeling\"定位到文章中描述访客感受的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，展览中，许多图纸尺寸微小且细节模糊，也没有儿童展区，和谐的线条与恰到好处的比例带来的视觉冲击，能让参观者感受到一种令人安心的宁静。因此答案为\"benevolent calm\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64171","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet","maxWords":3}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64159","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>The building where the exhibition is staged has been newly renovated.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"64160","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>Palazzo Barbaran da Porto typically represents the Palladio&#39;s design.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"64161","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>Palladio&#39;s father worked as an architect.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"64162","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>Palladio&#39;s family refused to pay for his architectural studies.</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"64163","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>Palladio&#39;s alternative design for the Ducal Palace in Venice was based on an English building.</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"64164","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>Palladio designed both wealthy and poor people.</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"64165","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>The exhibition includes paintings of people by famous artists</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"64166","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet","html":"<p><strong>8</strong> What job was Palladio training for before he became an architect? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"64167","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet","html":"<p><strong>9</strong> Who arranged Palladio&#39;s architectural studies? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"64168","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet","html":"<p><strong>10</strong> Who was the first non-Italian architect influenced by Palladio? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"64169","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet","html":"<p><strong>11</strong> What type of Ancient Roman buildings most heavily influenced Palladio&#39;s work? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"64170","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet","html":"<p><strong>12</strong> What did Palladio write that strengthened his reputation? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"64171","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet","html":"<p><strong>13</strong> In the writer&#39;s opinion, what feeling will visitors to the exhibition experience? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Andrea Palladio: Italian Architect</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">A new exhibition celebrates Palladio’s calm perfection</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Vicenza is a pleasant, prosperous city in the Veneto, 60km west of Venice. Its grand families settled and farmed the area from the 16th century. But its principal claim to fame is Andrea Palladio, who is such an influential architect that a neoclassical style is known as Palladian. The city is a permanent exhibition of some of his finest buildings, and as he was born – in Padua, to be precise – 500 years ago, the International Centre for the Study of Palladio’s Architecture has an excellent excuse for mounting la grande Mostra, the big show</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The exhibition has the special advantage of being held in one of Palladio’s buildings, Palazzo Barbaran da Porto. Its bold facade is a mixture of rustication and decoration set between two rows of elegant columns. On the second floor, the pediments are alternately curved or pointed, a Palladian trademark. The harmonious proportions of the atrium at the entrance lead through to a dramatic interior of fine fireplaces and painted ceilings. Palladio’s design is simple, clear and not over-crowded. The show has been organised on the same principles, according to Howard Burns, the architectural historian who co-curated it.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Palladio’s father was a miller who settled in Vicenza, where the young Andrea was apprenticed to a skilled stonemason. How did a humble miller’s son become a world-renowned architect? The answer in the exhibition is that, as a young man, Palladio excelled at carving decorative stonework on columns, doorways and fireplaces. He was plainly intelligent, and lucky enough to come across a rich patron, Gian Giorgio Trissino, a landowner and scholar, who organised his education, taking him to Rome in the 1540s, where he studied the masterpieces of classical Roman and Greek architecture and the work of other influential architects of the time, such as Donato Bramante and Raphael.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Burns argues that social mobility was also important. Entrepreneurs, prosperous from agriculture in the Veneto, commissioned the promising local architect to design their country villas and their urban mansions. In Venice, the aristocracy was anxious to co-opt talented artists, and Palladio has given the chance to design the buildings that have made him famous – the churches of San Giorgio Maggiore and the Redentore, both easy to admire because they can be seen from the city’s historical centre across a stretch of water.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>He tried his hand at bridges – his unbuilt version of the Rialto Bridge was decorated with the large pediment and columns of a temple – and, after a fire at the Ducal Palace, he offered an alternative design which bears an uncanny resemblance to the Banqueting House in Whitehall in London. Since it was designed by Inigo Jones, Palladio’s first foreign disciple, this is not as surprising as it sounds.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Jones, who visited Italy in 1614, bought a trunk full of the master’s architectural drawings; they passed through the hands of Dukes of Burlington and Devonshire before settling at the Royal Institute of British Architects in 1894. Many are now on display at Palazzo Barbaran. What they show is how Palladio drew on the buildings of ancient Rome as models. The major theme of both his rural and urban building was temple architecture, with a strong pointed pediment supported by columns and approached by wide steps.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Palladio’s work for rich landowners alienates unreconstructed critics on the Italian left, but among the papers in the show are designed for cheap housing in Venice. In the wider world, Palladio’s reputation has been nurtured by a text he wrote and illustrated, ‘Quattro Libri dell’ Architettura’. His influence spread to St Petersburg and to Charlottesville in Virginia, where Thomas Jefferson commissioned a Palladian villa he called Monticello.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Vicenza’s show contains detailed models of the major buildings and is leavened by portraits of Palladio’s teachers and clients by Titian, Veronese and Tintoretto; the paintings of his Venetian buildings are all by Canaletto, no less. This is an uncompromising exhibition; many of the drawings are small and faint, and there are no sideshows for children, but the impact of harmonious lines and satisfying proportions is to impart in a viewer a feeling of benevolent calm. Palladio is history’s most therapeutic architect.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘Palladio, 500 Anni: La Grande Mostra’ is at Palazzo Barbaran da Porto, Vicenza, until January 6th 2009. The exhibition continues at the Royal Academy of Arts, London, from January 31st to April 13th, and travels afterwards to Barcelona and Madrid.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8865&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8879","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 The Evolutional Mystery: Crocodile Survives","book":"阅读还原集Vol.17","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.17 · Test 3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8879:64223:14","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In their tenure on Earth, they’ve endured the impacts of meteors, planetary refrigeration, extreme upheavals of the Earth’s tectonic surface and profound climate change. They were around for the rise and fall of the dinosaurs, and even 65 million years of supposed mammalian dominance has failed to loosen their grip on the environments they inhabit. Today’s crocodiles and alligators are little changed from their prehistoric ancestors, a telling clue that these reptiles were (and remain) extremely well adapted to their environment.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求为A段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：定位到B段，阅读该段内容寻找核心主题。\n解题思路：A段主要讲述了，鳄鱼存在了两亿年，身体结构完美适应环境，经历了陨石撞击、冰河时期等所有大灾难，目睹了恐龙灭绝却存活至今，几乎没变样，是地球上的“终极幸存者”。核心就是说鳄鱼是地球历史上最顽强的幸存者（Supreme survivors），它们成功度过了所有导致其他物种（如恐龙）灭绝的重大历史事件（historical event）。与标题\"A historical event for the Supreme survivors\"（终极幸存者的历史性事件）吻合，因此选择其为A段的标题。","options":["The competitors with the dinosaur","A historical event for the Supreme survivors","What makes the crocodile the fastest running animal on land","Regulated body temperature by the surrounding environment","Underwater aid in body structure offered to a successful predator","The perfectly designed body for a great land roamer","Slow metabolisms which makes crocodile a unique reptile","The favorable features in the impact of a drought","Shifting Eating habits and food intake","A project on a special mechanism","A unique findings has been achieved recently"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"64223","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nReading passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct headings for paragraphs A-G from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-xI in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8879:64223:15","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The first crocodile-like ancestors appeared about 230 million years ago, with many of the features that make crocs such successful stealth hunters already in place: streamlined body, long tail, protective armour and long jaws. They have long head and a long tail that helps them to change their direction in water while moving. They have four legs which are short and are webbed.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求为B段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：定位到B段，阅读该段内容寻找核心主题。\n解题思路：B段主要介绍了鳄鱼祖先在2300万年前出现时已经具备的特征，如流线型身体、长尾巴、保护性甲壳和长颌等，这些特征使它们成为成功的伏击猎手。因此，B段的核心内容是鳄鱼的身体特征，让它们成为优秀的捕食者。在给定的标题选项中，\"The perfectly designed body for a great land roamer\"（完美的身体构造使其成为卓越的陆地漫游者）最符合该段落的主题。","options":["The competitors with the dinosaur","A historical event for the Supreme survivors","What makes the crocodile the fastest running animal on land","Regulated body temperature by the surrounding environment","Underwater aid in body structure offered to a successful predator","The perfectly designed body for a great land roamer","Slow metabolisms which makes crocodile a unique reptile","The favorable features in the impact of a drought","Shifting Eating habits and food intake","A project on a special mechanism","A unique findings has been achieved recently"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"64223","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nReading passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct headings for paragraphs A-G from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-xI in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8879:64223:16","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Crocodilians have no lips. When submerged in their classic ‘sit and wait’ position, their mouths fill with water. The nostrils on the tip of the elongated snout lead into canals that run through bone to open behind the valve – allowing the crocodilian to breathe through its nostrils even though its mouth is under water. When the animal is totally submerged, another valve seals the nostrils, so the crocodilian can open its mouth to catch prey with no fear of drowning. The thin skin on the crocodilian head and face is covered with tiny, pigmented domes, forming a network of neural pressure receptors that can detect barely perceptible vibrations in the water. This enables a crocodile lying in silent darkness to suddenly throw its head sideways and grasp with deadly accuracy small prey moving close by.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求为C段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读C段，寻找核心主题。\n解题思路：C段主要描述了鳄鱼在水下时，它的身体构造如何帮助它捕食。它们在水中可以通过特殊的鼻孔和阀门系统呼吸，即使在嘴巴充满水的情况下也能呼吸。此外，它们还能通过皮肤上的神经压力感受器感知水中的微小振动，从而准确地捕捉猎物。因此，C段的主题是关于鳄鱼的呼吸和捕食机制。在给定的标题选项中，\"Underwater aid in body structure offered to a successful predator\"（为成功捕食者提供的水下身体结构辅助 ）最符合该段落的主题。","options":["The competitors with the dinosaur","A historical event for the Supreme survivors","What makes the crocodile the fastest running animal on land","Regulated body temperature by the surrounding environment","Underwater aid in body structure offered to a successful predator","The perfectly designed body for a great land roamer","Slow metabolisms which makes crocodile a unique reptile","The favorable features in the impact of a drought","Shifting Eating habits and food intake","A project on a special mechanism","A unique findings has been achieved recently"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"64223","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nReading passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct headings for paragraphs A-G from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-xI in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8879:64223:17","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Like other reptiles, crocodiles are endothermic animals (cold-blooded, or whose body temperature varies with the temperature of the surrounding environment) and, therefore, need to sunbathe, to raise the temperature of the body. On the contrary, if it is too hot, they prefer being in water or in the shade.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求为D段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：定位到B段，阅读该段内容寻找核心主题。\n解题思路：D段主要讲述了与其他爬行动物类似，鳄鱼属于恒温动物（即冷血动物，其体温会随环境温度变化而调节），并且它们的代谢非常缓慢，可以长时间不进食。这些信息与标题“Regulated body temperature by the surrounding environment”（根据周围环境调节体温）相符，最符合该段落的主题。","options":["The competitors with the dinosaur","A historical event for the Supreme survivors","What makes the crocodile the fastest running animal on land","Regulated body temperature by the surrounding environment","Underwater aid in body structure offered to a successful predator","The perfectly designed body for a great land roamer","Slow metabolisms which makes crocodile a unique reptile","The favorable features in the impact of a drought","Shifting Eating habits and food intake","A project on a special mechanism","A unique findings has been achieved recently"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"64223","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nReading passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct headings for paragraphs A-G from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-xI in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8879:64223:18","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：They normally feed on small animals, big fish, birds and even human flesh. As like some water creatures that interact by making sounds crocodiles also use many sounds to communicate with other crocodiles. They exist where conditions have remained the same and they are free of human interference. The crocodile is successful because it switches its feeding methods. It hunts fish, grabs birds at the surface, hides among the water edge vegetation to wait for a gazelle to come by, and when there is a chance for an ambush, the crocodile lunges forward, knocks the animal with its powerful tail and then drags it to water where it quickly drowns. Another way is to wait motionless for an animal to come to the water’s edge and grabs it by its nose where it is held to drown.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求为E段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读E段内容，可以发现段落主要讲述了捕食技巧、食物种类和摄食习惯变化。\n解题思路：段落E的核心内容是描述鳄鱼多样的捕食策略和广泛的食物种类。原文详细列举了鳄鱼的食物，通常以小型动物、大型鱼类、鸟类甚至人类肉食为食，以及如何通过多变的捕食策略生存下去，包括捕鱼、捉鸟、伏击瞪羚等多种方式。展现了鳄鱼“多变的饮食习惯和食捕食方式”。因此，它与列表中的标题 “Shifting Eating habits and food intake” 完全匹配。","options":["The competitors with the dinosaur","A historical event for the Supreme survivors","What makes the crocodile the fastest running animal on land","Regulated body temperature by the surrounding environment","Underwater aid in body structure offered to a successful predator","The perfectly designed body for a great land roamer","Slow metabolisms which makes crocodile a unique reptile","The favorable features in the impact of a drought","Shifting Eating habits and food intake","A project on a special mechanism","A unique findings has been achieved recently"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"64223","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nReading passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct headings for paragraphs A-G from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-xI in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8879:64223:19","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph F","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In many places inhabited by crocodilians, the hot season brings drought that dries up their hunting grounds and takes away the means to regulate their body temperature. They allowed reptiles to dominate the terrestrial environment. Furthermore, many crocs protect themselves from this by digging burrows and entombing themselves in mud, waiting for months without access to food or water, until the rains arrive. To do this, they sink into a quiescent state called aestivation.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求为F段选择正确的标题。\n定位关键信息：定位到文章的F段。F段主要描述了鳄鱼在干旱季节的生存策略，包括挖掘洞穴和进入休眠状态。\n解题思路：段落F的核心内容是讨论干旱对鳄鱼栖息地的影响，以及鳄鱼如何通过挖掘洞穴、将自己埋入泥中并进入休眠状态来应对干旱。这描述了鳄鱼在干旱影响下所展现出的有利生存特征。因此，它与列表中的标题The favorable features in the impact of a drought（鳄鱼在干旱影响下的展现的有利特征）匹配。","options":["The competitors with the dinosaur","A historical event for the Supreme survivors","What makes the crocodile the fastest running animal on land","Regulated body temperature by the surrounding environment","Underwater aid in body structure offered to a successful predator","The perfectly designed body for a great land roamer","Slow metabolisms which makes crocodile a unique reptile","The favorable features in the impact of a drought","Shifting Eating habits and food intake","A project on a special mechanism","A unique findings has been achieved recently"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"64223","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nReading passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct headings for paragraphs A-G from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-xI in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8879:64223:20","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph G","answer":"J","acceptedAnswers":["J"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Kennett and Christian’s six-year study of Australian freshwater crocodiles – Crocodylus johnstoni (the King Crocodiles). The crocodiles spent almost four months a year underground without access to water. Doubly labeled water was used to measure field metabolic rates and water flux, and plasma (and cloacal fluid samples were taken at approximately monthly intervals during some years to monitor the effects of aestivation with respect to the accumulation of nitrogenous wastes and electrolyte concentrations.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求为G段选择正确的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读J段内容，可以发现段落主要讲述了一项针对鳄鱼特殊生理机制（夏眠）的长期研究项目。\n解题思路：段落G的核心内容是详细介绍一项针对澳大利亚淡水鳄的六年研究项目。该项目使用双重标记水等科学方法，专门研究鳄鱼在夏眠期间的特殊生理机制，包括新陈代谢率、水通量以及氮废物积累等。这完全符合标题 A project on a special mechanism的描述。","options":["The competitors with the dinosaur","A historical event for the Supreme survivors","What makes the crocodile the fastest running animal on land","Regulated body temperature by the surrounding environment","Underwater aid in body structure offered to a successful predator","The perfectly designed body for a great land roamer","Slow metabolisms which makes crocodile a unique reptile","The favorable features in the impact of a drought","Shifting Eating habits and food intake","A project on a special mechanism","A unique findings has been achieved recently"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"64223","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nReading passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct headings for paragraphs A-G from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-xI in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8879:64224:21","type":"fill","text":"填写第 21 空","answer":"hot season/Hot Season","acceptedAnswers":["hot season","Hot Season"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In many places inhabited by crocodilians, the hot season brings drought that dries up their hunting grounds and takes away the means to regulate their body temperature.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是，在许多鳄类栖息的地区，大多数鳄鱼种类已进化出一套成功的干旱生存策略，鳄鱼栖息地的干旱是由什么带来的。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"drought\"和\"survive\"定位到F段，该段提到鳄鱼在干旱季节会进入蛰伏状态以生存。\n解题思路：F段提到，在鳄鱼类动物广泛栖息的地区，炎热季节常引发干旱，导致它们的觅食区域干涸，进而丧失调节体温的能力。因此，答案是hot season。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64224","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Quesitons 21-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8879:64225:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"four months/Four Months","acceptedAnswers":["four months","Four Months"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The crocodiles spent almost four months a year underground without access to water.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求根据Kennett和Christian为期六年的澳大利亚淡水鳄夏眠研究，他们发现夏眠鳄鱼一年花费多少时间夏眠。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“Kennett and Christian’s six-year study”和“Australian freshwater crocodiles’ aestivation”定位到G段，找到关于夏眠鳄鱼花费时间的信息。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，这些鳄鱼每年有近四个月时间在地下生活，无法接触水源。答案应为“four months”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64225","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Quesitons 21-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8879:64226:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"water/Water","acceptedAnswers":["water","Water"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The crocodiles spent almost four months a year underground without access to water.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求根据Kennett和Christian为期六年的澳大利亚淡水鳄夏眠研究，他们发现夏眠期间鳄鱼没有什么。\n定位关键信息：根据“without access to”，定位到G段中关于鳄鱼夏眠时缺乏资源的描述。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，这些鳄鱼每年有近四个月时间在地下生活，无法接触水源。因此答案为\"water\"或\"Water\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64226","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Quesitons 21-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8879:64227:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"body mass/Body Mass","acceptedAnswers":["body mass","Body Mass"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Furthermore, though the animals lost water and body mass (just over one-tenth of their initial mass) while underground, the losses were proportional: on emergence, the aestivating crocodiles were not dehydrated and exhibited no other detrimental effects such as a decreased growth rate.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是鳄鱼身体水分总量的下降与什么成比例。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"absolute size of body water pools\"和\"declined proportionately with\"定位到文章中描述体水量变化比例的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，此外，尽管这些动物在地下期间出现了水分流失和体重下降（仅略高于初始体重的十分之一），但这些损失是成比例的，因此答案为\"body mass\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64227","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Quesitons 21-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8879:64228:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"dehydration/Dehydration","acceptedAnswers":["dehydration","Dehydration"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Furthermore, though the animals lost water and body mass (just over one-tenth of their initial mass) while underground, the losses were proportional: on emergence, the aestivating crocodiles were not dehydrated and exhibited no other detrimental effects such as a decreased growth rate.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是鳄鱼身体水分总量的下降与体重成比例，因此，即使在休眠期之后，鳄鱼也没有显示出什么迹象和其他健康损害。\n定位关键信息： 根据“no sign of... and other health-damaging impact”，定位到G段末尾关于夏眠后健康状况的描述。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，此外，尽管鳄鱼在地下期间会流失水分和体重（略超初始体重的十分之一），但这些流失是成比例的：当鳄鱼苏醒时，休眠个体并未出现脱水现象，也未表现出生长速率下降等其他有害影响。因此，答案为“dehydration”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64228","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Quesitons 21-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8879:64229:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"growth/Growth","acceptedAnswers":["growth","Growth"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Furthermore, though the animals lost water and body mass (just over one-tenth of their initial mass) while underground, the losses were proportional: on emergence, the aestivating crocodiles were not dehydrated and exhibited no other detrimental effects such as a decreased growth rate.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是，这种超能力使鳄鱼能够在干旱环境中生存，并且没有大幅降低它们的什么速率。\n定位关键信息： 根据“without slowing their speed of”，定位到G段中关于生长率不受影响的描述。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，尽管鳄鱼在地下期间会流失水分和体重（略超初始体重的十分之一），但这些流失是成比例的：当鳄鱼苏醒时，休眠个体并未出现脱水现象，也未表现出生长速率下降等其他有害影响。因此答案为\"growth\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64229","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Quesitons 21-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64223","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nReading passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct headings for paragraphs A-G from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-xI in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"64224","title":"填空题","instruction":"Quesitons 21-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>In many places inhabited by crocodilians, most types of the crocodile have evolved a successful\nscheme to survive in the drought brought by a <strong>21</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"64225","title":"填空题","instruction":"Quesitons 21-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>According to Kennett and Christian’s\nsix-year study of Australian freshwater crocodiles’ aestivation, they found Aestivating crocodiles spent\naround <strong>22</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"64226","title":"填空题","instruction":"Quesitons 21-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>a year without access to <strong>23</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"64227","title":"填空题","instruction":"Quesitons 21-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The absolute size of body water\npools declined proportionately with <strong>24</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> ;</p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"64228","title":"填空题","instruction":"Quesitons 21-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>thus there is no sign of <strong>25</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong> and\nother health-damaging impact in the crocodiles even after an aestivation period.</p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"64229","title":"填空题","instruction":"Quesitons 21-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>This super capacity\nhelps crocodiles endure the tough drought without slowing their speed of <strong>26</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong> significantly.</p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The Evolutional Mystery: Crocodile Survives</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>#&amp;A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Crocodiles have been around for 200 million years, but they’re certainly not primitive. The early forms of crocodiles are known as Crocodilian. Since they spent most of their life beneath water, accordingly their body adapted to aquatic lifestyle. Due to the changes formed within their body shape and tendency to adapt according to the climate they were able to survive when most of the reptiles of their period are just a part of history. In their tenure on Earth, they’ve endured the impacts of meteors, planetary refrigeration, extreme upheavals of the Earth’s tectonic surface and profound climate change. They were around for the rise and fall of the dinosaurs, and even 65 million years of supposed mammalian dominance has failed to loosen their grip on the environments they inhabit. Today’s crocodiles and alligators are little changed from their prehistoric ancestors, a telling clue that these reptiles were (and remain) extremely well adapted to their environment.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The first crocodile-like ancestors appeared about 230 million years ago, with many of the features that make crocs such successful stealth hunters already in place: streamlined body, long tail, protective armour and long jaws. They have long head and a long tail that helps them to change their direction in water while moving. They have four legs which are short and are webbed. Never underestimate their ability to move on ground. When they move they can move at such a speed that won’t give you a second chance to make a mistake by going close to them especially when hungry. They can lift their whole body within seconds from ground. The fastest way by which most species can move is a sort of ‘belly run’, where the body moves like a snake, members huddled to the side paddling away frenetically while the tail whips back and forth. When “belly running” Crocodiles can reach speeds up to 10 or 11 km/h (about 7mph), and often faster if they are sliding down muddy banks. Other form of movement is their ‘high walk’, where the body is elevated above the ground.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Crocodilians have no lips. When submerged in their classic ‘sit and wait’ position, their mouths fill with water. The nostrils on the tip of the elongated snout lead into canals that run through bone to open behind the valve – allowing the crocodilian to breathe through its nostrils even though its mouth is under water. When the animal is totally submerged, another valve seals the nostrils, so the crocodilian can open its mouth to catch prey with no fear of drowning. The thin skin on the crocodilian head and face is covered with tiny, pigmented domes, forming a network of neural pressure receptors that can detect barely perceptible vibrations in the water. This enables a crocodile lying in silent darkness to suddenly throw its head sideways and grasp with deadly accuracy small prey moving close by.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Like other reptiles, crocodiles are ectothermic animals (cold-blooded, or whose body temperature varies with the temperature of the surrounding environment) and, therefore, need to sunbathe, to raise the temperature of the body. On the contrary, if it is too hot, they prefer being in water or in the shade. Being a cold-blooded species, the crocodilian heart is unique in having an actively controlled valve that can redirect, at will, blood flow away from the lungs and recirculate it around the body, taking oxygen to where it’s needed most. In addition, their metabolism is a very slow one, so, they can survive for long periods without feeding. Crocodiles are capable of slowing their metabolism even further allowing them to survive for a full year without feeding. Compared to mammals and birds, crocodilians have slow metabolisms that burn much less fuel, and are ideally suited to relatively unstable environments that would defeat mammals with their high food demands.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Crocodiles use a very effective technique to catch the prey. The prey remains almost unaware of the fact that there can be any crocodile beneath water. It is due to the fact that when the crocodile sees its prey it moves under water without making any noise and significant movement. It keeps only its eyes above water surface. When it feels it has reached sufficiently close to the target it whistles out of water with wide open jaws. 80 percent of their attempts are successful. They have very powerful jaws. Once the prey trapped in its jaws they swallow it. Their power can be judged from the fact they can kill the wild zebras which come to watery areas in search of water. They do not chew their food. They normally feed on small animals, big fish, birds and even human flesh. As like some water creatures that interact by making sounds crocodiles also use many sounds to communicate with other crocodiles. They exist where conditions have remained the same and they are free of human interference. The crocodile is successful because it switches its feeding methods. It hunts fish, grabs birds at the surface, hides among the water edge vegetation to wait for a gazelle to come by, and when there is a chance for an ambush, the crocodile lunges forward, knocks the animal with its powerful tail and then drags it to water where it quickly drowns. Another way is to wait motionless for an animal to come to the water’s edge and grabs it by its nose where it is held to drown.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In many places inhabited by crocodilians, the hot season brings drought that dries up their hunting grounds and takes away the means to regulate their body temperature. They allowed reptiles to dominate the terrestrial environment. Furthermore, many crocs protect themselves from this by digging burrows and entombing themselves in mud, waiting for months without access to food or water, until the rains arrive. To do this, they sink into a quiescent state called aestivation.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Most of (At least nine species of) crocodilian are thought to aestivate during dry periods. Kennett and Christian’s six-year study of Australian freshwater crocodiles – Crocodylus johnstoni (the King Crocodiles). The crocodiles spent almost four months a year underground without access to water. Doubly labeled water was used to measure field metabolic rates and water flux, and plasma (and cloacal fluid samples were taken at approximately monthly intervals during some years to monitor the effects of aestivation with respect to the accumulation of nitrogenous wastes and electrolyte concentrations. Double found that the crocodiles’ metabolic engines tick over, producing waste and using up water and fat reserves. Waste products are stored in the urine, which gets increasingly concentrated as the months pass. However, the concentration of waste products in the blood changes very little, allowing the crocodiles to function normally. Furthermore, though the animals lost water and body mass (just over one-tenth of their initial mass) while underground, the losses were proportional: on emergence, the aestivating crocodiles were not dehydrated and exhibited no other detrimental effects such as a decreased growth rate. Kennett and Christian believe this ability of individuals to sit out the bad times and endure long periods of enforced starvation must surely be key to the survival of the crocodilian line through time.&amp;#</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8879&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8880","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Mechanisms of Linguistic Change","book":"阅读还原集Vol.17","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.17 · Test 3 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8880:64230:27","type":"fill","text":"填写第 27 空","answer":"sound laws/Sound Laws","acceptedAnswers":["sound laws","Sound Laws"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Such regular changes are often called sound laws.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：现存语言的发音在数千年的演变中不断发生变化，题目问的是大规模的规律性变化通常被称为什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Large scale regular Changes\"定位到B段中的\"large-scale regularities in the changes\"。\n解题思路：B段提到，研究一种语言在几代人或更长时间跨度内的发音演变时，总会发现其中存在显著的规律性变化。这类规律性变化通常被称为语音规律\"sound laws\"。因此答案为\"sound laws\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64230","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8880:64231:28","type":"fill","text":"填写第 28 空","answer":"fashion/Fashion","acceptedAnswers":["fashion","Fashion"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It is also possible that fashion plays a part in the process of change. It certainly plays a part in the spread of change: one person imitates another, and people with the most prestige are most likely to be imitated, so that a change that takes place in one social group may be imitated (more or less accurately) by speakers in another group.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：发音变化有三个原因，第一个原因是，一种语言对另一种语言的影响，题目问的是，一个人模仿另一个人的发音时，模仿发音时总会涉及什么因素。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"imitates another pronunciation\"和\"prestige\"可以定位到C段中描述模仿发音和社会地位影响力的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，流行风潮或许在社会变迁中扮演着重要角色。它在变革传播过程中确实起着关键作用：当一个人模仿另一个人时，那些声望最高的人往往成为模仿对象，因此某个社会群体发生的变化，很可能被其他群体的成员（或多或少准确地）效仿，这表明模仿过程中涉及的因素是\"流行风潮\"（fashion），因此答案为“fashion”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64231","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8880:64232:29","type":"fill","text":"填写第 29 空","answer":"imperfect/Imperfect","acceptedAnswers":["imperfect","Imperfect"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A less specific variant of the argument is that the imitation of children is imperfect: they copy their parents’ speech, but never reproduce it exactly.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目询问“第二个原因是，儿童模仿成人语言有时是什么样的”。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的“imitation of children from adults language”定位到D段，该段讨论儿童模仿成人语言。\n解题思路：原文提到，另一种观点认为，儿童的模仿并不完美：他们能复刻父母的发音，但永远无法完全复现。说明模仿存在不完美之处。因此，答案为“imperfect”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64232","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8880:64233:30","type":"fill","text":"填写第 30 空","answer":"principle of ease/Principle of Ease","acceptedAnswers":["principle of ease","Principle of Ease"],"explanation":"原文答案句：One such force which is often invoked is the principle of ease, or minimization of effort.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“对于那些语音中的随机变化，更深层次的原因在于什么”。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的“random variations in pronunciation”和“deeper evidence”定位到E段，该段讨论了语音变化的深层原因。\n解题思路：原文E段提到，发音的随机变化，是因为人们发音时往往采用“易化原则”，即最小发音努力。因此，答案为“principle of ease”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64233","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8880:64234:31","type":"choice","text":"It is impossible for modern people to find pronunciation of words in an earlier age.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：These various kinds of evidence, combined with a knowledge of the mechanisms of speech-production, can often give us a very good idea of the pronunciation of an earlier age, though absolute certainty is never possible.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是现代人无法得知古代词语的发音，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键词\"pronunciation of words in an earlier age\"在文章中定位，找到A段中描述如何通过多种证据了解古代发音的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到通过多种证据和语音生产机制的知识，虽然不能绝对确定，但能让我们对古代发音形成清晰的认知。因此，题目中的\"impossible\"与原文中的\"can often give us a very good idea\"相矛盾，故答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64234","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-37\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 31-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8880:64235:32","type":"choice","text":"The great change of language in Russian history is related to the rising status and fortune of middle\nclasses.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It is said that, after the Russian Revolution of 1917, the upper-class pronunciation of Russian, which had formerly been considered desirable, became on the contrary an undesirable kind of accent to have, so that people tried to disguise it.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“俄罗斯历史上语言的大变化与中产阶级地位和财富的上升有关”这一陈述是否与文章作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词“Russian history”（俄罗斯历史）、“great change of language”（语言的大变化）、“rising status and fortune of middle classes”（中产阶级地位和财富的上升）来定位文章中的相关句子。\n解题思路：在C段中，作者提到，据说，1917年俄国革命后，曾经人人效仿的上层阶级俄语发音，反而成了令人不齿的口音，人们开始试图掩饰这种口音。可以推断，俄罗斯的社会变革使得语言发音变化，并不是因为中产阶级地位和财富的上升。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64235","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-37\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 31-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8880:64236:33","type":"choice","text":"All the children learn speeches from adults while they assume that certain language is difficult to\nimitate exactly.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A less specific variant of the argument is that the imitation of children is imperfect: they copy their parents’ speech, but never reproduce it exactly. This is true, but it is also true that such deviations from adult speech are usually corrected in later childhood.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“孩子从成年人那里学习语言时，他们觉得某些语言很难模仿得完全准确”是否与作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“children learn speeches from adults”和“imitate exactly”可以定位到D段，该段讨论了儿童模仿成人语言的不完美性以及这种模仿是否会导致语言变化。\n解题思路：原文提到，儿童模仿成人语言时确实存在偏差，但这些偏差通常会在童年后期得到纠正。然而，原文并未明确说明“所有孩子”都“认为”某些语言难以模仿得完全准确，只是提到模仿过程中存在随机偏差，没有说明儿童的想法观点。故答案为Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64236","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-37\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 31-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8880:64237:34","type":"choice","text":"Pronunciation with causal inaccuracy will not exert big influence on language changes.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This, however, cannot explain changes in pronunciation unless it can be shown that there is some systematic trend in the failures of imitation: if they are merely random deviations they will cancel one another out and there will be no net change in the language.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“发音中的偶然性偏差不会对语言变化产生重大影响”是否与作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“Pronunciation with causal inaccuracy”可以定位到D段中关于发音不准确的讨论。\n解题思路：原文中明确指出，这种现象就无法解释发音的变化：若只是随机偏差，这些偏差会相互抵消，语言就不会产生净变化。因此，题目中与原文信息一致，故答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64237","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-37\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 31-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8880:64238:35","type":"choice","text":"The word scant can be pronounced more easily than skamt.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For example, the word scant was once skamt, but the /m/ has been changed to /n/ under the influence of the following /t/. Greater efficiency has hereby been achieved, because /n/ and /t/ are articulated in the same place (with the tip of the tongue against the teeth-ridge), whereas /m/ is articulated elsewhere (with the two lips).\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“单词scant的发音比skamt更容易”，需要判断这一说法是否与原文一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“scant”和“skamt”定位到E段，找到描述这两个词发音变化的句子。\n解题思路：原文提到“scant”由“skamt”演变而来，/m/变为/n/是因为/n/和/t/发音位置相同（舌尖抵上齿龈），而/m/的发音位置不同（双唇），这样更省力（greater efficiency）。因此，与原文一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64238","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-37\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 31-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8880:64239:36","type":"choice","text":"The [g] in gnat not being pronounced will not be spelt out in the future.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It is very common for consonants to be lost at the end of a word: in Middle English, word-final [-n] was often lost in unstressed syllables, so that baken ‘to bake’ changed from [‘ba:kan] to [‘ba:kə], and later to [ba:k].\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“gnat”中的[g]音不发音意味着未来它不会被省略”，需要判断这一说法是否与原文一致。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的“gnat”和“[g]”，找到关于以辅音开头的单词发音变化的相关句子。\n解题思路：原文仅在F段中提到，某些单词的辅音结尾会省去，没有提到单词开头的辅音是否会省去，此外，文章并没有提到“gnat”的拼写和发音，更没有提到未来它的拼写方式。因此，无法确定题目所述内容是否与文章一致，答案应为“Not Given”。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64239","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-37\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 31-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8880:64240:37","type":"choice","text":"The sound of ‘temporary’ cannot wholly present its spelling.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Sometimes a whole syllable is dropped out when two successive syllables begin with the same consonant (haplology): a recent example is temporary, which in Britain is often pronounced as if it were tempory.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问“‘Temporary’的发音，无法完整对应其拼写”是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的单词\"temporary\"定位到F段末句，该句提到\"temporary\"在英国常被发音为\"tempory\"。\n解题思路：原文明确指出\"temporary\"的发音常省略一个音节，在英国常被读作“tempory”。即实际发音与拼写不完全一致，因此题目说法与文章信息一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64240","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-37\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 31-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8880:64241:38","type":"choice","text":"38 As a consequence, [b] will be pronounced as [p].","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：When we study the pronunciation of a language over any period of a few generations or more, we find there are always large-scale regularities in the changes: for example, over a certain period of time, just about all the long [a:] vowels in a language may change into long [e:] vowels, or all the [b] consonants in a certain position (for example at the end of a word) may change into [p] consonants. Such regular changes are often called sound laws.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“[b]读作[p]”将其与最恰当的描述相匹配。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"[b] will be pronounced as [p]\"定位到B段中\"all the [b] consonants in a certain position (for example at the end of a word) may change into [p] consonants\"这一句。\n解题思路：B段提到，研究一种语言在几代人或更长时间跨度内的发音演变时，总会发现其中存在显著的规律性变化。例如，某个位置（比如词尾）的所有[b]辅音都可能变为[p]辅音。题目中的\"[b] will be pronounced as [p]\"正是这种大范围规律性语音变化的一个例子，因此对应选项C\" It is a trend for changes in pronunciation in a large scale in a given period.\"（某一时期内大规模的语音变化趋势）。","options":["The speakers can pronounce it with less effort.","It is assimilation of a sound under the influence of a neighbouring one.","It is a trend for changes in pronunciation in a large scale in a given period.","The speaker can pronounce [n] and [t] both in the same time."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64241","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nLook at the following sentences and the list of statements below. Match each statement with the correct sentence, A-D. Write the correct letter, A-D, in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet.\nA The speakers can pronounce it with less effort.\nB It is assimilation of a sound under the influence of a neighbouring one.\nC It is a trend for changes in pronunciation in a large scale in a given period.\nD The speaker can pronounce [n] and [t] both in the same time."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8880:64241:39","type":"choice","text":"39 The pronunciation of [mt] changed to [nt].","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Assimilation is the changing of a sound under the influence of a neighbouring one. For example, the word scant was once skamt, but the /m/ has been changed to /n/ under the influence of the following /t/.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“[mt]发音变化成[nt]”将其与最恰当的描述相匹配。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的[m]和[n]这两个音标词定位到原文中对应的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文，同化是指一个音素在邻近音素影响下发生改变的现象。例如，单词“scant”原本发音为“skamt”，但受后续音素“t”的影响，其/m/音已演变为/n/，因为这样发音更省力。说明[mt]变化到[nt]属于同化现象，因此可以确定答案为B（音素在邻近音影响下的同化现象）。","options":["The speakers can pronounce it with less effort.","It is assimilation of a sound under the influence of a neighbouring one.","It is a trend for changes in pronunciation in a large scale in a given period.","The speaker can pronounce [n] and [t] both in the same time."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64241","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nLook at the following sentences and the list of statements below. Match each statement with the correct sentence, A-D. Write the correct letter, A-D, in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet.\nA The speakers can pronounce it with less effort.\nB It is assimilation of a sound under the influence of a neighbouring one.\nC It is a trend for changes in pronunciation in a large scale in a given period.\nD The speaker can pronounce [n] and [t] both in the same time."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8880:64241:40","type":"choice","text":"40 The pronunciation of [t] will be omitted in the sound of Christmas.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Assimilation is not the only way in which we change our pronunciation in order to increase efficiency....Consonant-clusters are often simplified. At one time there was a [t] in words like castle and Christmas, and an initial [k] in words like knight and know.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目询问“‘Christmas’这个词的发音中，[t]音会被省略”，将其与最恰当的描述相匹配。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“pronunciation of [t]”和“Christmas”这两个关键词在文章中定位。\n解题思路：F段提到，同化并不是我们为了提高效率而改变发音的唯一方式。随后列举三种提升发音效率的方式，其中，人们常常简化辅音群：例如“castle ”和“Christmas”中都有辅音[t]，但现在发音时不会把[t]发出来，这是为了提高发音效率，A（说话者可以更轻松地发音的描述最为恰当，因此答案为A。","options":["The speakers can pronounce it with less effort.","It is assimilation of a sound under the influence of a neighbouring one.","It is a trend for changes in pronunciation in a large scale in a given period.","The speaker can pronounce [n] and [t] both in the same time."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64241","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nLook at the following sentences and the list of statements below. Match each statement with the correct sentence, A-D. Write the correct letter, A-D, in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet.\nA The speakers can pronounce it with less effort.\nB It is assimilation of a sound under the influence of a neighbouring one.\nC It is a trend for changes in pronunciation in a large scale in a given period.\nD The speaker can pronounce [n] and [t] both in the same time."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64230","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The pronunciation of living language undergo changes throughout thousands of years. Large scale\nregular Changes are usually called <strong>27</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[27] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"64231","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>There are three reasons for these changes.\nFirstly, the influence of one language on another; when one person imitates another pronunciation(the\nmost prestige’s), the imitation always partly involving factor of <strong>28</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[28] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"64232","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Secondly, the\nimitations of children from adults language sometimes are <strong>29</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[29] ____</strong> ,</p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"64233","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>and may also contribute\nto this change if there are insignificant deviations though later they may be corrected. Finally, for those\nrandom variations in pronunciation, the deeper evidence lies in the <strong>30</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[30] ____</strong> or minimization\nof effort.</p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"64234","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-37\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 31-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>It is impossible for modern people to find pronunciation of words in an earlier age.</strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"64235","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-37\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 31-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>The great change of language in Russian history is related to the rising status and fortune of middle\nclasses.</strong></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"64236","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-37\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 31-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>All the children learn speeches from adults while they assume that certain language is difficult to\nimitate exactly.</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"64237","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-37\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 31-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>Pronunciation with causal inaccuracy will not exert big influence on language changes.</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"64238","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-37\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 31-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>The word scant can be pronounced more easily than skamt.</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"64239","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-37\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 31-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>The [g] in gnat not being pronounced will not be spelt out in the future.</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"64240","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-37\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 31-37 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>The sound of ‘temporary’ cannot wholly present its spelling.</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"64241","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nLook at the following sentences and the list of statements below. Match each statement with the correct sentence, A-D. Write the correct letter, A-D, in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet.\nA The speakers can pronounce it with less effort.\nB It is assimilation of a sound under the influence of a neighbouring one.\nC It is a trend for changes in pronunciation in a large scale in a given period.\nD The speaker can pronounce [n] and [t] both in the same time.","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> The speakers can pronounce it with less effort. <br/></p><p><strong>B</strong> It is assimilation of a sound under the influence of a neighbouring one. <br/></p><p><strong>C</strong> It is a trend for changes in pronunciation in a large scale in a given period. <br/></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>D</strong> The speaker can pronounce [n] and [t] both in the same time. <br/></p><p><strong>38</strong> As a consequence, [b] will be pronounced as [p]. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[38] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":38}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Mechanisms of Linguistic Change</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The changes that have caused the most disagreement are those in pronunciation. We have various sources of evidence for the pronunciations of earlier times, such as the spellings, the treatment of words borrowed from other languages or borrowed by them, the descriptions of contemporary grammarians and spellingreformers, and the modern pronunciations in all the languages and dialects concerned From the middle of the sixteenth century, there are in England writers who attempt to describe the position of the speech-organs for the production of English phonemes, and who invent what are in effect systems of phonetic symbols. These various kinds of evidence, combined with a knowledge of the mechanisms of speech-production, can often give us a very good idea of the pronunciation of an earlier age, though absolute certainty is never possible.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>When we study the pronunciation of a language over any period of a few generations or more, we find there are always large-scale regularities in the changes: for example, over a certain period of time, just about all the long [a:] vowels in a language may change into long [e:] vowels, or all the [b] consonants in a certain position (for example at the end of a word) may change into [p] consonants. Such regular changes are often called sound laws. There are no universal sound laws (even though sound laws often reflect universal tendencies), but simply particular sound laws for one given language (or dialect) at one given period.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>It is also possible that fashion plays a part in the process of change. It certainly plays a part in the spread of change: one person imitates another, and people with the most prestige are most likely to be imitated, so that a change that takes place in one social group may be imitated (more or less accurately) by speakers in another group. When a social group goes up or down in the world, its pronunciation may gain or lose prestige. It is said that, after the Russian Revolution of 1917, the upper-class pronunciation of Russian, which had formerly been considered desirable, became on the contrary an undesirable kind of accent to have, so that people tried to disguise it. Some of the changes in accepted English pronunciation in the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries have been shown to consist in the replacement of one style of pronunciation by another style already existing, and it is likely that such substitutions were a result of the great social changes of the period: the increased power and wealth of the middle classes, and their steady infiltration upwards into the ranks of the landed gentry, probably carried elements of middle-class pronunciation into upper-class speech.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>A less specific variant of the argument is that the imitation of children is imperfect: they copy their parents’ speech, but never reproduce it exactly. This is true, but it is also true that such deviations from adult speech are usually corrected in later childhood. Perhaps it is more significant that even adults show a certain amount of random variation in their pronunciation of a given phoneme, even if the phonetic context is kept unchanged. This, however, cannot explain changes in pronunciation unless it can be shown that there is some systematic trend in the failures of imitation: if they are merely random deviations they will cancel one another out and there will be no net change in the language.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>One such force which is often invoked is the principle of ease, or minimization of effort. The change from fussy to fuzzy would be an example of assimilation, which is a very common kind of change. Assimilation is the changing of a sound under the influence of a neighbouring one. For example, the word scant was once skamt, but the /m/ has been changed to /n/ under the influence of the following /t/. Greater efficiency has hereby been achieved, because /n/ and /t/ are articulated in the same place (with the tip of the tongue against the teeth-ridge), whereas /m/ is articulated elsewhere (with the two lips). So the place of articulation of the nasal consonant has been changed to conform with that of the following plosive. A more recent example of the same kind of thing is the common pronunciation of football as football.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Assimilation is not the only way in which we change our pronunciation in order to increase efficiency. It is very common for consonants to be lost at the end of a word: in Middle English, word-final [-n] was often lost in unstressed syllables, so that baken ‘to bake’ changed from [‘ba:kan] to [‘ba:kə], and later to [ba:k]. Consonant-clusters are often simplified. At one time there was a [t] in words like castle and Christmas, and an initial [k] in words like knight and know. Sometimes a whole syllable is dropped out when two successive syllables begin with the same consonant (haplology): a recent example is temporary, which in Britain is often pronounced as if it were tempory.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8880&scene=%E8%AF%AD%E8%A8%80%E6%95%99%E8%82%B2&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8854","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Saving a Forgotten Forests: The Longleaf Pine","book":"阅读还原集Vol.17","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.17 · Test 2 · 12 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8854:64106:1","type":"fill","text":"填写第 1 空","answer":"nests/Nests/nest/Nest","acceptedAnswers":["nests","Nests","nest","Nest"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It tucks its nest on the ground beneath dumps of wiregrass and little bluestem in the open under- story.  But once fire has been absent for several years, and a tangle of shrubs starts to grow, the sparrows disappear.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问森林大火帮助鸟类在地下找到它们搭建什么。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"on the gound\"与原文中描述鸟类筑巢位置的关键词对应。\n解题思路：原文E段提到，它们将巢穴藏在地面上，掩埋在低矮灌木丛和小蓝茎草的堆积下。但一旦火势消失数年，灌木丛开始蔓延，麻雀便会消失。因此森林大火通过维持开放环境帮助鸟类找到适合筑巢的位置，考虑到题干中空格前的物主代词是their因此严谨来说，答案为复数形式“nests”；考虑到填空题所见即所得，且语法结构上，此处填写单数信也无误，答案也可以是原文原词“nest”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64106","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet. Forest fire ensures that:","maxWords":2},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8854:64107:2","type":"fill","text":"填写第 2 空","answer":"tortoise/Tortoise","acceptedAnswers":["tortoise","Tortoise"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Gopher tortoises, the only native land tortoises east of the Mississippi, are also abundant in longleaf. A keystone species for these forests, its burrows provide homes and safety to more than 300 species of vertebrates and invertebrates ranging from eastern diamond-back rattlesnakes to gopher frogs.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问具体是哪种生物的洞穴为许多其他动物提供家园。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"burrows\"（洞穴）和\"provide homes to many other animals\"（为许多其他动物提供家园）定位到E段中关于\"burrows\"的描述。\n解题思路：原文中提到，穴居龟的洞穴为300多种脊椎动物和无脊椎动物提供了家园，保护了它们的安全。因此答案为\"tortoise\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64107","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet. Forest fire ensures that:","maxWords":2},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8854:64108:3","type":"fill","text":"填写第 3 空","answer":"oaks/Oaks","acceptedAnswers":["oaks","Oaks"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Fire knocks back the oaks and other hardwoods that can grow up to overwhelm longleaf forests.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问森林火灾确保了什么硬木（hardwoods），例如什么，不会占领长叶松的栖息地。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"hardwoods\"和\"don’t take over\"在文章中定位。在F段找到\"hardwoods\"相关句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，火灾将橡树及其他硬木树种逼退，这些树种若任其生长，终将吞噬长叶松林。题干中的\"don’t take over\"对应原文的\"knocks back\"（抑制）和\"prevent...from overwhelming\"（阻止覆盖）。因此，空格处应填入原文中提到的具体硬木名称\"oaks\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64108","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet. Forest fire ensures that:","maxWords":2},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8854:64109:4","type":"fill","text":"填写第 4 空","answer":"Native Americans/native Americans","acceptedAnswers":["Native Americans","native Americans"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘They are fire forests,’ Mitchell says, ‘They evolved in the lightning capital of the eastern United States.’ And it wasn’t only lightning strikes that set the forest aflame. ‘Native Americans also lit fires to keep the forest open,’ Mitchell says, ‘So did the early pioneers. They helped create the longleaf pine forests that we know today.’\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问森林火灾除了由闪电引起，还会是由谁引起的。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的关键词\"Forest fire\"和\"created by\"定位到文章中关于火灾原因的描述。\n解题思路：在F段中，作者明确提到，点燃森林的不仅是闪电。“美洲原住民也生火让森林保持开阔，”米切尔说，“早期拓荒者也是如此。他们帮助形成了我们今天所知的长叶松林。”直接回答了火灾是由美洲原住民引起的。因此选择\"Native Americans\"作为答案。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64109","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet. Forest fire ensures that:","maxWords":2},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8854:64110:5","type":"fill","text":"填写第 5 空","answer":"prescribed burns/Prescribed Burns","acceptedAnswers":["prescribed burns","Prescribed Burns"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Most of these fires are prescribed burns, deliberately set with a drip torch.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是“故意点燃的火灾被称为什么”，需要根据文章内容填入一个名词。\n定位关键信息：题干中的“Fires deliberately lit”对应原文中的“deliberately set”，通过这个短语可以定位到H段。\n解题思路：原文提到，这些火灾大多是计划性燃烧，用滴油枪故意点燃。其中“prescribed burns”就是指“故意点燃的火灾”，因此答案为“prescribed burns”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64110","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet. Forest fire ensures that:","maxWords":2},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8854:64111:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"soil/Soil","acceptedAnswers":["soil","Soil"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘We learned calcium is stashed away in woody shrubs when the forest is not burned,’ James says, ‘But when there is a fire, a pulse of calcium moves down into the soil and up into the longleaf.’\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是如何增加红冠啄木鸟的数量，根据流程图，钙储存在灌木中，灌木被烧毁后，钙释放到哪个地方。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"calcium\"和\"shrubs are burned\"定位到G段，找到\"when there is a fire, a pulse of calcium moves down into the soil and up into the longleaf\"这句话。\n解题思路：根据原文句子，钙元素就会像脉冲般在土壤中向下流动，最终抵达长叶松树。因此，空格处应该填\"soil\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64111","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.  Write your answer in boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20224mSxlchu5J1669945570.png]","maxWords":1},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8854:64112:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"ants/Ants","acceptedAnswers":["ants","Ants"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Eventually, this calcium makes its way up the food chain to a tree-dwelling species of ant, which is the red-cockaded’s favorite food.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是钙质通过食物链传递的去向，红冠啄木鸟吃掉什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"travel up to the leaves\"和\"eaten\"定位到G段描述钙质传递过程的句子。\n解题思路：原文中提到，最终，这些钙元素会沿着食物链向上传递，最终到达栖息在树上的蚂蚁种类——红冠啄木鸟最爱的食物。原文原信息tree-dwelling species of ant（树栖类蚂蚁，复数种类），填空题要求填写一个单词，考虑到题干中空格后出现的系动词为are，主语应为复数，根据语法结构，答案将tree-dwelling species of ant调整为ants。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64112","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.  Write your answer in boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20224mSxlchu5J1669945570.png]","maxWords":1},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8854:64113:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"eggs/Eggs","acceptedAnswers":["eggs","Eggs"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The result: more calcium for the birds, which leads to more eggs, more young and more woodpeckers.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是，然后，什么的数量会增加，最后红冠啄木鸟会增加。\n定位关键信息：根据流程图中的“More cockaded woodpeckers”可以定位到文章中与红冠啄木鸟相关的内容，即G段。G段提到了红冠啄木鸟的繁殖情况。\n解题思路：G段提到，最终，鸟类摄入的钙质增加，从而产卵量提升，雏鸟数量增多，啄木鸟数量也随之增加。因此可以确定答案为“eggs”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64113","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.  Write your answer in boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20224mSxlchu5J1669945570.png]","maxWords":1},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8854:64114:10","type":"choice","text":"The sparse distribution of longleaf pine trees leads to the most diversity of species.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The trees are not so dense as to block the sun. This openness creates a forest floor that is among the most diverse in the world, where plants such as many-flowered grass pinks, trumpet pitcher plants, Venus flytraps, lavender ladies and pineland bog-buttons grow.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“长叶松的稀疏分布造就了最丰富的物种多样性”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词“sparse distribution”和“diversity of species”定位到B段，原文提到“树木不密集，不会阻挡阳光。创造了世界上物种最丰富的森林地面”。\n解题思路：原文明确指出长叶松树的稀疏分布导致了森林地面的物种多样性极高，与题目表述一致，因此答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64114","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8854:64115:11","type":"choice","text":"It is easier to restore forests converted to farms than forests converted to plantations.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In areas where the land has not been chewed up by farming, but converted to loblolly or slash pine plantations, the seed bank of the longleaf forest usually remains viable beneath the soil. In time, this original vegetation can be coaxed back. Where agriculture has destroyed the seeds, however, wiregrass must be replanted. Right now, the expense is prohibitive, but researchers are searching for low-cost solutions.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是“将森林改为农田后再恢复森林，比将森林改为林场后再恢复森林更容易”是否与原文信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"converted to farms\"和\"converted to plantations\"定位到I段中关于不同转换类型对恢复难度影响的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文I段，如果转化成plantations林场，最初的植被还能恢复（original vegetation can be coaxed back），但是如果转化成了农场（对应原文的“agriculture”），则很难恢复，而且花费出奇得高（the expense is prohibitive），而题目却说转化为农场后更容易复原。题目信息与原文信息相矛盾，所以正确答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64115","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8854:64116:12","type":"choice","text":"The technology in recreating the herbaceous layer will phase out in near future due to the high cost.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Where agriculture has destroyed the seeds, however, wiregrass must be replanted. Right now, the expense is prohibitive, but researchers are searching for low-cost solutions.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是，由于成本高昂，草本层的再造技术将在不久的将来逐步淘汰，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键词\"recreating the herbaceous layer\"和\"high cost\"定位到I段中关于重建草本层技术的描述。\n解题思路：原文提到重建草本层的成本目前很高（the expense is prohibitive），但研究人员正在寻找低成本解决方案（researchers are searching for low-cost solutions）。题目说这种技术会因高昂成本而逐渐淘汰，但原文并未提及这种技术会淘汰，只是正在寻找经济实惠的解决方案。因此，题目信息在原文中没有明确对应，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64116","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8854:64117:13","type":"choice","text":"Few people in this restoration program will see the replanted forest reach its maturity.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Bringing back longleaf is not for the short-sighted, however. Few of us will be alive when the pines being planted today become mature forests in 70 to 80 years.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问“在这项森林恢复项目中，鲜有人能亲眼见证重新栽种的森林茁壮成长直至成熟”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词“replanted forest reach its maturity”可以定位到文章中关于恢复计划中森林成长的信息。\n解题思路：根据J段的内容，当我们今天种植的松树在70到80年后长成成熟森林时，我们中很少有人还活着。可以推断出题目中的陈述与文章信息相符，很少有人会看到重新种植的森林长成参天大树。因此，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64117","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64106","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet. Forest fire ensures that:","html":"<p>Forest fire ensures that:</p><p>Birds can locate their&nbsp;<strong style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">1</strong><span style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong></span>&nbsp;on the ground</p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"64107","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet. Forest fire ensures that:","html":"<p>The burrows of a species of <strong>2</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[2] ____</strong> provide homes to manyother animals.</p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"64108","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet. Forest fire ensures that:","html":"<p>Hardwoods such as <strong>3</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[3] ____</strong> don&#39;t take over.</p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"64109","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet. Forest fire ensures that:","html":"<p>Apart from fires lit by lightning:</p><p>Fires are created by&nbsp;<strong style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">4</strong><span style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[4] ____</strong></span>&nbsp;and settlers.</p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"64110","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet. Forest fire ensures that:","html":"<p>Fires deliberately lit are called&nbsp;<strong>5</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[5] ____</strong>&nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"64111","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.  Write your answer in boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20224mSxlchu5J1669945570.png]","html":"<p><strong>7</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong><br/></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"64112","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.  Write your answer in boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20224mSxlchu5J1669945570.png]","html":"<p><strong>8</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"64113","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.  Write your answer in boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/20224mSxlchu5J1669945570.png]","html":"<p><strong>9</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong>&nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"64114","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>The sparse distribution of longleaf pine trees leads to the most diversity of species.</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"64115","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>It is easier to restore forests converted to farms than forests converted to plantations.</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"64116","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>The technology in recreating the herbaceous layer will phase out in near future due to the high cost.</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"64117","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information FALSE if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>Few people in this restoration program will see the replanted forest reach its maturity.</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Saving a Forgotten Forests: The Longleaf Pine</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><br/></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">Found only in the Deep South of America, longleaf pine woodlands have dwindled to about 3 percent of their former range, but new efforts are under way to restore them.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>THE BEAUTY AND THE BIODIVERSITY of the longleaf pine forest are well-kept secrets, even in its native South. Yet it is among the richest ecosystems in North America, rivaling tallgrass prairies and the ancient forests of the Pacific Northwest in the number of species it shelters. And like those two other disappearing wildlife habitats, longleaf is also critically endangered.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In longleaf pine forests, trees grow widely scattered, creating an open, parklike environment, more like a savanna than a forest. The trees are not so dense as to block the sun. This openness creates a forest floor that is among the most diverse in the world, where plants such as many-flowered grass pinks, trumpet pitcher plants, Venus flytraps, lavender ladies and pineland bog-buttons grow. As many as 50 different species of wildflowers, shrubs, grasses and ferns have been cataloged in just a single square meter.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Once, nearly 92 million acres of longleaf forest flourished from Virginia to Texas, the only place in the world where it is found. By the turn of the 21st century, however, virtually all of it had been logged, paved or farmed into oblivion. Only about 3 percent of the original range still supports longleaf forest, and only about 10,000 acres of that is uncut old-growth – the rest is forest that has regrown after cutting.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Figuring out how to bring back the piney woods also will allow biologists to help the plants and animals that depend on this habitat. Nearly two-thirds of the declining, threatened or endangered species in the southeastern United States are associated with longleaf. The outright destruction of longleaf is only part of their story, says Mark Danaher, the biologist for South Carolina’s Francis Marion National Forest. He says the demise of these animals and plants also is tied to a lack of fire, which once swept through the southern forests on a regular basis. ‘Fire is absolutely critical for this ecosystem and for the species that depend on it,’ says Danaher.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Name just about any species that occurs in longleaf and you can find a connection to fire. Bachman’s sparrow is a secretive bird with a beautiful song that echoes across the longleaf flatwoods. It tucks its nest on the ground beneath dumps of wiregrass and little bluestem in the open under- story. But once fire has been absent for several years, and a tangle of shrubs starts to grow, the sparrows disappear. Gopher tortoises, the only native land tortoises east of the Mississippi, are also abundant in longleaf. A keystone species for these forests, its burrows provide homes and safety to more than 300 species of vertebrates and invertebrates ranging from eastern diamond-back rattlesnakes to gopher frogs. If fire is suppressed, however, the tortoises are choked out. ‘If we lose fire,’ says Bob Mitchel1, an ecologist at the Jones Center, ‘we lose wildlife.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Without fire, we also lose longleaf. Fire knocks back the oaks and other hardwoods that can grow up to overwhelm longleaf forests. ‘They are fire forests,’ Mitchell says, ‘They evolved in the lightning capital of the eastern United States.’ And it wasn’t only lightning strikes that set the forest aflame. ‘Native Americans also lit fires to keep the forest open,’ Mitchell says, ‘So did the early pioneers. They helped create the longleaf pine forests that we know today.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Fire also changes how nutrients flow throughout longleaf ecosystems, in ways we are just beginning to understand. For example, researchers have discovered that frequent fires provide extra calcium, which is critical for egg production, to endangered red-cockaded woodpeckers. Frances James, a retired avian ecologist from Florida State University, has studied these small black-and-white birds for more than two decades in Florida’s sprawling Apalachicola National Forest. When she realised female woodpeckers laid larger clutches in the first breeding season after their territories were burned, she and her colleagues went searching for answers. ‘We learned calcium is stashed away in woody shrubs when the forest is not burned,’ James says, ‘But when there is a fire, a pulse of calcium moves down into the soil and up into the longleaf.’ Eventually, this calcium makes its way up the food chain to a tree-dwelling species of ant, which is the red-cockaded’s favorite food. The result: more calcium for the birds, which leads to more eggs, more young and more woodpeckers.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Today, fire is used as a vital management tool for preserving both longleaf and its wildlife. Most of these fires are prescribed burns, deliberately set with a drip torch. Although the public often opposes any type of fire – and the smoke that goes with it – these frequent, low-intensity burns reduce the risk of catastrophic conflagrations. ‘Forests are going to burn,’ says Amadou Diop, NWF’s southern forests restoration manager, ‘It’s just a question of when. With prescribed burns, we can pick the time and the place.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Restoring longleaf is not an easy task. The herbaceous layer – the understory of wiregrasses and other plants, also needs to be re-created. In areas where the land has not been chewed up by farming, but converted to loblolly or slash pine plantations, the seed bank of the longleaf forest usually remains viable beneath the soil. In time, this original vegetation can be coaxed back. Where agriculture has destroyed the seeds, however, wiregrass must be replanted. Right now, the expense is prohibitive, but researchers are searching for low-cost solutions.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Bringing back longleaf is not for the short-sighted, however. Few of us will be alive when the pines being planted today become mature forests in 70 to 80 years. But that is not stopping longleaf enthusiasts. ‘Today, it’s getting hard to find longleaf seedlings to buy,’ one of the private landowners says, ‘Everyone wants them. Longleaf is in a resurgence.’</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8854&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8863","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Water Filter","book":"阅读还原集Vol.17","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.17 · Test 2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8863:64136:14","type":"fill","text":"填写第 14 空","answer":"clay/Clay","acceptedAnswers":["clay","Clay"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Take a handful of dry, crushed clay, mix it with a handful of organic material, such as used tea leaves, coffee grounds or rice hulls, add enough water to make a stiff biscuit-like mixture and form a cylindrical pot that has one end closed, then dry it in the sun.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问制作水过滤器的第一步是将什么与有机材料混合。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"combination\"和\"organic material\"定位到C段开头，找到与有机材料混合的物质。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，首先，取一把干燥的碎陶土，混入一把有机材料（如用过的茶叶、咖啡渣或稻壳），因此答案为clay。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64136","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the flow chart, using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8863:64137:15","type":"fill","text":"填写第 15 空","answer":"water/Water","acceptedAnswers":["water","Water"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Take a handful of dry, crushed clay, mix it with a handful of organic material, such as used tea leaves, coffee grounds or rice hulls, add enough water to make a stiff biscuit-like mixture and form a cylindrical pot that has one end closed, then dry it in the sun.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是在制作过程中，需要添加足够什么来制造浓稠的混合物，再放到阳光下晒干。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"create a thick mixture\"和\"dry it in the sun\"可以定位到C段中描述制作过程的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文句子，加足水调成像饼干般坚硬的糊状物，捏成一端封闭的圆柱形陶罐，然后放在阳光下晾干。因此，答案为water。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64137","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the flow chart, using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8863:64138:16","type":"fill","text":"填写第 16 空","answer":"straw/Straw","acceptedAnswers":["straw","Straw"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Next, surround the pots with straw; put them in a mound of cow manure, light the straw and then top up the burning manure as required.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问制作水过滤器的第二步，要求填写包裹圆柱体的材料。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"Step two\"和\"pack...around the cylinders\"定位到C段描述制作流程的部分，找到与\"surround the pots with\"（围绕陶土罐包裹）相关的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到第二步是\"surround the pots with straw\"（接下来用稻草围住陶罐），因此，答案为\"straw\"（稻草）。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64138","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the flow chart, using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8863:64139:17","type":"fill","text":"填写第 17 空","answer":"cow manure/Cowmanure","acceptedAnswers":["cow manure","Cowmanure"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Next, surround the pots with straw; put them in a mound of cow manure, light the straw and then top up the burning manure as required.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问稻草围住陶罐后放置在什么中。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"burning fuel\"定位到C段描述制作过滤器的步骤，找到与燃烧燃料相关的句子。\n解题思路：原文C段提到用稻草围住陶罐，堆成牛粪堆，点燃稻草后根据需要不断补充燃烧的牛粪。因此答案为\"cow manure\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64139","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the flow chart, using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8863:64140:18","type":"fill","text":"填写第 18 空","answer":"950 degrees/950 Degrees","acceptedAnswers":["950 degrees","950 Degrees"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The properties of cow manure are vital as the fuel can reach a temperature of 700 degrees in half an hour and will be up to 950 degrees after another 20 to 30 minutes.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求填写烧制过程中的最高温度。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"for firing\"和\"maximum temperature\"定位到C段中描述烧制过程的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到使用牛粪作为燃料，在半小时内温度可达700度，再经过20-30分钟后温度可达到950度，因此950度是烧制过程中的最高温度。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64140","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the flow chart, using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8863:64141:19","type":"fill","text":"填写第 19 空","answer":"60 minutes/60 Minutes","acceptedAnswers":["60 minutes","60 Minutes"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In less than 60 minutes the filters are finished.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问过滤器烘烤的时间不超过多少分钟。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"filter being baked\"定位到C段描述过滤器制作过程的句子。\n解题思路：原文C段明确提到\"In less than 60 minutes the filters are finished\"，说明过滤器在60分钟内完成烘烤，因此答案为60 minutes。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64141","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the flow chart, using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8863:64142:20","type":"choice","text":"It takes half an hour for the manure to reach 950 degrees.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The properties of cow manure are vital as the fuel can reach a temperature of 700 degrees in half an hour and will be up to 950 degrees after another 20 to 30 minutes.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问，牛粪达到950度需要半小时，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"manure\"、\"950 degrees\"和\"time\"在文章中定位，找到C段描述牛粪燃烧温度的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到牛粪在半小时内达到700度，而达到950度需要额外20到30分钟，即总共需要大约50到60分钟。题目说半小时达到950度与原文信息不符，因此答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64142","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-23 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8863:64143:21","type":"choice","text":"Clay was initially found to be unsuitable for pot making.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Just as using manure as a fuel for domestic uses is not a new idea, the porosity of clay is something that potters have known about for years, and something that as a former ceramics lecturer in the ANU School of Art, Mr. Flynn is well aware of. The difference is that rather than viewing the porous nature of the material as a problem – after all not many people want a pot that won’t hold water – his filters capitalize on this property.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问“粘土最初不适合制作陶器”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词“Clay”和“unsuitable for pot making”可以定位到E段。\n解题思路：原文中提到，陶艺家们早已知道黏土的多孔特性。作为澳大利亚国立大学艺术学院的陶瓷学讲师，弗林先生对此深有体会。不同之处在于，他并未将这种多孔特性视为缺陷——毕竟谁会想要一个不能够装水的陶罐呢？他的过滤器反而巧妙利用了这一特性。这说明粘土不适合制作陶器，但是把它制成滤水器反而利用了它的缺陷，因此，题目中的陈述与原文信息一致，应该选择“True”。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64143","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-23 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8863:64144:22","type":"choice","text":"Coffee grounds are twice as effective as other materials.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：According to Mr. Flynn, used coffee grounds have given the best results to date.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问咖啡渣比其他材料有效两倍，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"coffee grounds\"和\"effective\"定位到C段，找到关于咖啡渣效果的句子。\n解题思路：原文提到据弗林先生介绍，用过的咖啡渣效果最佳。但并未将其效果与其他材料进行比较，也没有提到具体的效果倍数（如两倍）。因此，题目中的\"twice as effective\"这一具体比较信息在原文中没有给出。故答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64144","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-23 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8863:64145:23","type":"choice","text":"E-coli is the most difficult bacteria to combat.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Tests with the deadly E-coli bacterium have seen the filters remove 96.4 to 99.8 per cent of the pathogen – well within safe levels.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是\"E-coli是迄今为止最难对抗的细菌\"这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"E-coli\"和\"most difficult bacteria to combat\"定位答案在文章中的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文F段中的句子可知，E-coli是一种致命的细菌，过滤器可以去除96.4%到99.8%的病原体，达到了安全水平。但是，文章并没有提到E-coli是迄今为止最难对抗的细菌，也没有与其他细菌进行比较。因此，题目中的陈述在文章中没有明确的支持或反驳，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64145","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-23 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8863:64146:24","type":"choice","text":"When making the pot, the thickness of the wall","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The walls of the finished pot should be about as thick as an adult’s index.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是制作水壶时，壶壁的厚度应该是多少。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"thickness of the wall\"和\"making the pot\"定位到C段，找到关于壶壁厚度的描述。\n解题思路：原文明确提到\"the walls of the finished pot should be about as thick as an adult’s index\"（壶壁的厚度应与成年人的食指差不多），与选项C\"should be the same as an adult’s forefinger\"（应与成年人的食指相同）完全一致。选项A和B与原文内容无关，选项D与原文明确提到的壶壁厚度描述相矛盾。因此正确答案是C。","options":["is large enough to let the pathogens to pass.","varied according to the temperature of the fuel.","should be the same as an adult’s forefinger.","is not mentioned by Mr. Flynn."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64146","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet."},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8863:64147:25","type":"choice","text":"what is true about the charity, it","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The charity wanted to help set up a small industry manufacturing water filters, but initial research found the local clay to be too fine – a problem solved by the addition of organic material.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问关于慈善机构，哪个说法是正确的。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"charity\"定位到G段，找到慈善机构的相关描述。\n解题思路：原文提到慈善机构希望通过设立小规模产业来制造水过滤器，这与选项D的\"intended to help build a local filter production factory\"（打算帮助建立本地过滤器生产工厂）完全一致。选项A、B、C与原文描述不符，原文明确提到当地粘土太细，需要添加有机材料解决，而非材料合适或失败；也没有提到成功制造窑炉陶瓷过滤器或全球销售。因此，D是正确答案。","options":["failed in searching the appropriate materials.","successfully manufacture a kiln based ceramic filter to be sold worldwide.","found that the local clay is good enough.","intended to help build a local filter production factory."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64147","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet."},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8863:64148:26","type":"choice","text":"Mr. Flynn's design is purposely not being patented","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：With all the components being widely available, Mr. Flynn says there is no reason the technology couldn’t be applied throughout the developing world, and with no plans to patent his idea, there will be no legal obstacles to it being adopted in any community that needs it. ‘Everyone has a right to clean water, these filters have the potential to enable anyone in the world to drink water safely,’ says Mr. Flynn.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是 Flynn 的设计没有申请专利的原因。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的关键词 \"Mr. Flynn's design is purposely not being patented\" 可以定位到 G 段，该段提到了 Flynn 没有计划为他的设计申请专利。\n解题思路：根据 G 段的原文句子，任何需要该技术的社区都能无障碍采用。“人人都有权获得清洁水源，这些过滤器有望让全球每个人都能安全饮水”，弗林先生强调道。可以看出，Flynn 没有申请专利是因为他希望任何有需要的人都可以使用这一设计。这与选项 A 的表述 \"because he hopes it can be freely used around the world\" 完全一致。因此，正确答案是 A。","options":["because he hopes it can be freely used around the world.","because he doesn’t think the technology is perfect enough.","because there are some legal obstacles.","because the design has already been applied thoroughly."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64148","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64136","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the flow chart, using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Guide to Making Water Filters\nStep one: combination of <strong>14</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong> and organic material,&nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"64137","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the flow chart, using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>with sufficient <strong>15</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[15] ____</strong> to create a thick mixture sun dried</p>","firstNumber":15},{"id":"64138","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the flow chart, using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Step two: pack <strong>16</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[16] ____</strong> around the cylinders</p>","firstNumber":16},{"id":"64139","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the flow chart, using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>place them in <strong>17</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[17] ____</strong> which is as burning fuel</p>","firstNumber":17},{"id":"64140","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the flow chart, using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>for firing (maximum temperature: <strong>18</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[18] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":18},{"id":"64141","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the flow chart, using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>filter being baked in under <strong>19</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"64142","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-23 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>It takes half an hour for the manure to reach 950 degrees.</strong></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"64143","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-23 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Clay was initially found to be unsuitable for pot making.</strong></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"64144","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-23 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Coffee grounds are twice as effective as other materials.</strong></p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"64145","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 20-23 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>E-coli is the most difficult bacteria to combat.</strong></p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"64146","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>When making the pot, the thickness of the wall</strong></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"64147","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>what is true about the charity, it</strong></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"64148","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Mr. Flynn&#39;s design is purposely not being patented</strong></p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Water Filter</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>An ingenious invention is set to bring clean water to the third world, and while the science may be cutting edge, the materials are extremely down to earth. A handful of clay yesterday’s coffee grounds and some cow manure are the ingredients that could bring clean, safe drinking water to much of the third world.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The simple new technology, developed by ANU materials scientist Mr. Tony Flynn, allows water filters to be made from commonly available materials and fired on the ground using cow manure as the source of heat, without the need for a kiln. The filters have been tested and shown to remove common pathogens (disease-producing organisms) including E-coli. Unlike other water filtering devices, the filters are simple and inexpensive to make. ‘They are very simple to explain and demonstrate and can be made by anyone, anywhere,’ says Mr. Flynn, ‘They don’t require any western technology. All you need is terracotta clay, a compliant cow and a match.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The production of the filters is extremely simple. Take a handful of dry, crushed clay, mix it with a handful of organic material, such as used tea leaves, coffee grounds or rice hulls, add enough water to make a stiff biscuit-like mixture and form a cylindrical pot that has one end closed, then dry it in the sun. According to Mr. Flynn, used coffee grounds have given the best results to date. Next, surround the pots with straw; put them in a mound of cow manure, light the straw and then top up the burning manure as required. In less than 60 minutes the filters are finished. The walls of the finished pot should be about as thick as an adult’s index. The properties of cow manure are vital as the fuel can reach a temperature of 700 degrees in half an hour and will be up to 950 degrees after another 20 to 30 minutes. The manure makes a good fuel because it is very high in organic material that bums readily and quickly; the manure has to be dry and is best used exactly as found in the field, there is no need to break it up or process it any further.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘A potter’s din is an expensive item and can could take up to four or five hours to get upto 800 degrees. It needs expensive or scarce fuel, such as gas or wood to heat it and experience to run it. With no technology, no insulation and nothing other than a pile of cow manure and a match, none of these restrictions apply,’ Mr. Flynn says.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>It is also helpful that, like terracotta clay and organic material, cow dung is freely available across the developing world. ‘A cow is a natural fuel factory. My understanding is that cow dung as a fuel would be pretty much the same wherever you would find it.’ Just as using manure as a fuel for domestic uses is not a new idea, the porosity of clay is something that potters have known about for years, and something that as a former ceramics lecturer in the ANU School of Art, Mr. Flynn is well aware of. The difference is that rather than viewing the porous nature of the material as a problem – after all not many people want a pot that won’t hold water – his filters capitalize on this property.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Other commercial ceramic filters do exist, but, even if available, with prices starting at US$5 each, they are often outside the budgets of most people in the developing world. The filtration process is simple, but effective. The basic principle is that there are passages through the filter that are wide enough for water droplets to pass through, but too narrow for pathogens. Tests with the deadly E-coli bacterium have seen the filters remove 96.4 to 99.8 per cent of the pathogen – well within safe levels. Using only one filter it takes two hours to filter a litre of water. The use of organic material, which burns away after firing, helps produce the structure in which pathogens will become trapped. It overcomes the potential problems of finer clays that may not let water through and also means that cracks are soon halted. And like clay and cow dung, it is universally available.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The invention was born out of a World Vision project involving the Manatuto community in East Timor. The charity wanted to help set up a small industry manufacturing water filters, but initial research found the local clay to be too fine – a problem solved by the addition of organic material. While the AF problems of producing a working ceramic filter in East Timor were overcome, the solution was kiln-based and particular to that community’s materials and couldn’t be applied elsewhere. Manure firing, with no requirement for a kiln, has made this zero technology approach available anywhere it is needed. With all the components being widely available, Mr. Flynn says there is no reason the technology couldn’t be applied throughout the developing world, and with no plans to patent his idea, there will be no legal obstacles to it being adopted in any community that needs it. ‘Everyone has a right to clean water, these filters have the potential to enable anyone in the world to drink water safely,’ says Mr. Flynn.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8863&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8864","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Robert Louis Stevenson","book":"阅读还原集Vol.17","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.17 · Test 2 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8864:64149:27","type":"choice","text":"Stevenson’s biographers KF and CP","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Two biographers, KF and CP, wrote a biography about Stevenson with a clear focus. They chose not to criticise aspects of Stevenson's personal life. Instead, they focused on his writing, and gave high praise to his writing style and skill.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目询问关于Stevenson的传记作家KF和CP，下列哪项是正确的。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"Stevenson's biographers KF and CP\"可以定位到A段中的相关内容。\n解题思路：原文明确指出KF和CP这两位传记作家不批评史落文森的个人生活， 而是选择聚焦于他的作品，并对他的写作风格和技巧给予高度赞扬，四个选项中，D项说提升了史蒂文森作为作家的身份，符合原文的意思。因此，本题的答案为D。","options":["underestimated the role of family played in Stevenson’s life.","overestimated the writer’s works in literature history.","exaggerated Stevenson’s religious belief in his works.","elevated Stevenson’s role as a writer."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64149","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8864:64150:28","type":"choice","text":"The main point of the second paragraph is","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The literary pendulum has swung these days. Different critics have different opinions towards Robert Louis Stevenson’s works.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是第二段(B段)的主要观点是什么。\n定位关键信息：题目要求找出第二段的主要观点。在B段中，关键词如\"negative criticism\"、\"corrupt ethics\"、\"lack of moral\"、\"little social value\"和\"lack moral value\"等都指向对Stevenson作品道德价值的批评。\n解题思路：本段第 1句\"The literary pendulum has swung these days.\"为主题句。B段描述了批评家对Stevenson作品看法的变化，从最初的赞扬转为负面评价。文中明确指出Stevenson被视为一个\"道德败坏、缺乏道德的作者\"，评论家将他的作品归类为儿童读物或恐怖故事，\"在教育环境中几乎没有社会价值\"，并且最后一句明确表示\"尽管他有技巧，他的文学作品仍然缺乏道德价值\"。这些内容都指向一个主要观点：D项：Stevenson的作品被认为缺乏道德价值，最符合该段的主要论点。","options":["the public gives a more fair criticism of Stevenson’s works.","recent criticism has been justified.","the style of Stevenson’s works overweighs the faults in his life.","Stevenson’s works’ drawback is lack of ethical nature."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64150","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8864:64151:29","type":"choice","text":"According to the author, adventure stories","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Many of us believe adventure stories are exciting, offers engaging characters, action, and mystery but ultimately can't teach moral principles.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是作者对冒险作品的看法。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"adventure stories\"可以定位到文章C段，该段详细讨论了Stevenson的冒险故事及其特点。\n解题思路：在C段中，作者明确指出，我们许多人认为冒险小说虽然情节跌宕起伏、人物鲜活有趣、充满悬疑刺激，却难以传递道德教义。这表明冒险故事不能被作家用来展示道德价值，与选项B完全一致。而其他选项与文章内容不符：A选项与文章提到的冒险故事专注于情节转折相反；C选项文章没有将冒险故事与其他艺术形式进行比较；D选项与文章提到的Stevenson主要写冒险故事相反。因此，正确答案是B。","options":["do not provide plot twists well.","cannot be used by writers to show moral values.","are more fashionable art forms.","can be found in others’ works but not in Stevenson’s."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64151","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8864:64152:30","type":"choice","text":"What does the author say about Stevenson’s works?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Stevenson's works, unlike other British authors, captured the unique day to day life of average Scottish people.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问对于Stevenson的作品作者说了什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"Stevenson's works\"定位到原文中描述其作品特点的内容。\n解题思路：在D段中，明确提到，与其他英国作家不同，史蒂文森的作品真实记录了普通苏格兰人的日常生活，这直接对应选项A的描述，表明Stevenson的作品描述了苏格兰人民的生活。其他选项与原文信息不符：B选项与文章中提到的批评相矛盾，文章指出他的作品被认为缺乏教育价值；C选项与D段中提到的\"Stevenson's works were not popular in Scotland when he was alive\"相矛盾；D选项与文章中批评者认为他的作品未能超越当地文化的观点相矛盾。因此，A是唯一正确的答案。","options":["They describe the life of people in Scotland.","They are commonly regarded as real literature.","They were popular during Stevenson’s life.","They transcend the local culture and stories."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64152","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8864:64153:31","type":"choice","text":"According to the writer, Stevenson’s own lifestyle","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Despite much debate of Stevenson’s writing topics, his writing was not the only source of attention for critics. Stevenson’s personal life often attracted a lot of attention from his fans and critics alike. Some even argue that his personal life eventually outshone his writing.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问了作者关于Stevenson的生活方式的论述。\n定位关键信息：利用\"Stevenson's own lifestyle\"可以定位到E段，该段主要讨论了Stevenson的个人生活\n解题思路：E段明确指出，私生活同样频繁引发粉丝与评论家的热议，甚至有观点认为，他的私生活最终盖过了作品本身。这与选项C\"gained more attention from the public than his works\"（比他的作品获得了更多公众关注）完全一致。他带着家人一起去南太平洋小岛， 因此生活方式不会得到家人的嫉妒，可以排除A；“ The sea air and thrill of adventure complimented the themes of his writing, and for a time restored his health.” 这句话清楚地说明了他到此地后身体健康状况好转，可以排除B项；”“Stevenson had been plagued with health problems his whole life, and often had to live in much warmer climates than the cold, dreary weather of Scotland in order to recover.” 这句话清楚地说明了因为需要更暖的天气.他搬到了萨摩亚群岛， 见这个地方更加适合他，D项也可排除。因此，本题的答案为C。","options":["made his family envy him so much.","should be responsible for his death.","gained more attention from the public than his works.","didn’t prepare well for his life in Samoa."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64153","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8864:64154:32","type":"choice","text":"Although Oscar Wilde admired Robert Louis Stevenson very much, he believed Stevenson could have written greater works.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Though Stevenson's works have deeply influenced Oscar Wilde, Wilde often joked that Stevenson would have written better works if he wasn't born in Scotland.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问虽然Oscar Wilde非常欣赏Robert Louis Stevenson，但认为Stevenson本可以写出更伟大的作品，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Oscar Wilde\"和\"greater works\"等关键词可以在C段中找到相关信息。\n解题思路：原文明确提到Stevenson的作品深深影响了Oscar Wilde，这表明Wilde确实欣赏Stevenson。同时，原文也提到Wilde开玩笑说如果Stevenson不是出生在苏格兰，他会写出更好的作品。这与题目中的陈述一致，因此答案是True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64154","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8864:64155:33","type":"choice","text":"Robert Louis Stevenson encouraged Oscar Wilde to start writing at first.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Though Stevenson's works have deeply influenced Oscar Wilde, Wilde often joked that Stevenson would have written better works if he wasn't born in Scotland.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是罗伯特·路易斯·史蒂文森最初鼓励奥斯卡·王尔德开始写作，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Oscar Wilde\"定位到文章C段，该段提到了史蒂文森与王尔德之间的关系。\n解题思路：文章C段提到史蒂文森的作品深深影响了王尔德，以及王尔德对史蒂文森的评价，但完全没有提到史蒂文森鼓励王尔德开始写作的信息。由于文章中没有提供任何相关信息来支持或反驳这一说法，因此答案为NOT GIVEN（无法确定）。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64155","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8864:64156:34","type":"choice","text":"Galsworthy thought Hardy is greater than Stevenson is.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Other authors came to Stevenson's defence, including Galsworthy who claimed that Stevenson is a greater writer than Thomas Hardy.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问Galsworthy认为Hardy比Stevenson更伟大，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Galsworthy\"、\"Hardy\"和\"Stevenson\"可以定位到C段的相关内容。\n解题思路：原文明确指出Galsworthy认为Stevenson比Hardy更伟大（\"Stevenson is a greater writer than Thomas Hardy\"），而题目说\"Galsworthy thought Hardy is greater than Stevenson is\"，这与原文内容直接矛盾，因此答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64156","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8864:64157:35","type":"choice","text":"Critics only paid attention to Robert Louis Stevenson’s writing topics.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Despite much debate of Stevenson's writing topics, his writing was not the only source of attention for critics. Stevenson's personal life often attracted a lot of attention from his fans and critics alike.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问批评家只关注Robert Louis Stevenson的写作主题，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"critics\"和\"writing topics\"可以定位到E段，该段明确讨论了批评家对Stevenson的关注点。\n解题思路：原文中明确指出，尽管史蒂文森的创作主题备受争议，但他的作品并非评论界关注的唯一焦点。其私生活同样频繁引发粉丝与评论家的热议，甚至有观点认为，他的私生活最终盖过了作品本身。这些都清楚地表明批评家关注的不仅仅是Stevenson的写作主题，还包括他的个人生活、宗教信仰和生活方式等。因此，题目陈述与文章信息相矛盾，答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64157","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8864:64158:36","type":"choice","text":"Sir Walter Scott and Robert Louis Stevenson\nA lot of people believe that Sir Walter Scott and Robert Louis Stevenson are the most influential writers in the history of Scotland, but Sir Walter Scott is more proficient in 36 ____,","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：While many critics exalt Sir Walter Scott as a literary genius because of his technical ability, others argue that Stevenson deserves the same recognition for his natural ability to capture stories and characters in words.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目询问Sir Walter Scott在哪个方面比Robert Louis Stevenson更擅长。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Sir Walter Scott\"和\"Robert Louis Stevenson\"以及\"more proficient in\"这些关键词，可以定位到D段中比较两位作家的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，不少评论家因司各特的技术造诣而推崇其文学天才，但也有人认为史蒂文森同样值得赞誉，因为他天生擅长用文字捕捉故事与人物，相比之下，Stevenson被认可的是他的\"natural ability to capture stories and characters\"（捕捉故事和角色的自然能力）。因此，Sir Walter Scott更擅长的是技术控制/技巧掌握方面，选择F。","options":["natural ability","romance","colorful language","critical acclaim","humor","technical control","storytelling","depth","human nature"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64158","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-J below. Write the correct letter A-J in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8864:64158:37","type":"choice","text":"while Stevenson has better 37 ____.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：While many critics exalt Sir Walter Scott as a literary genius because of his technical ability, others argue that Stevenson deserves the same recognition for his natural ability to capture stories and characters in words.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目询问Stevenson在哪个方面比Scott更擅长。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"Stevenson has better\"，这表明是在比较Stevenson和其他人的某种特质。在原文中，D段明确比较了Stevenson和Sir Walter Scott，提到Scott因\"technical ability\"而受称赞，而Stevenson因\"natural ability\"而应获得认可。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，原文明确指出，不少评论家因司各特的技术造诣而推崇其文学天才，但也有人认为史蒂文森同样值得赞誉，因为他天生擅长用文字捕捉故事与人物，相比之下，Stevenson被认可的是他的\"natural ability to capture stories and characters\"（捕捉故事和角色的自然能力）。因此答案是A(natural ability)。","options":["natural ability","romance","colorful language","critical acclaim","humor","technical control","storytelling","depth","human nature"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64158","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-J below. Write the correct letter A-J in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8864:64158:38","type":"choice","text":"Scott’s books illustrate 38 ____ especially in terms of tragedy,","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Many of Scott's works were taken more seriously as literature for their depth due to their tragic themes, but fans of Stevenson praise his unique style of story-telling and capture of human nature.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问Scott的书表现出什么，尤其是他的悲剧作品。\n定位关键信息：通过\"Scott\"和\"tragedy\"这两个关键词，可以在D段中找到相关描述。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，司各特的许多作品因其悲剧主题的深度而被视作文学佳作。因此，空格处应填入H选项\"depth\"，表示Scott的书表现出了深度。","options":["natural ability","romance","colorful language","critical acclaim","humor","technical control","storytelling","depth","human nature"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64158","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-J below. Write the correct letter A-J in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8864:64158:39","type":"choice","text":"but a lot of readers prefer Stevenson’s 39 ____.","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Many of Scott's works were taken more seriously as literature for their depth due to their tragic themes, but fans of Stevenson praise his unique style of story-telling and capture of human nature.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是很多读者更喜欢Stevenson作品的什么方面。\n定位关键信息：通过\"Stevenson\"和\"prefer\"等关键词定位到D段中关于读者喜欢Stevenson的内容。\n解题思路：在D段中，明确提到，史蒂文森的读者更欣赏其独特的叙事风格与对人性的刻画，这与选项G\"storytelling\"（讲故事）相符，因此答案是G。","options":["natural ability","romance","colorful language","critical acclaim","humor","technical control","storytelling","depth","human nature"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64158","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-J below. Write the correct letter A-J in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8864:64158:40","type":"choice","text":"What’s more, Stevenson’s understanding of 40 ____ made his works have the most unique expression of Scottish people.","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：While many critics exalt Sir Walter Scott as a literary genius because of his technical ability, others argue that Stevenson deserves the same recognition for his natural ability to capture stories and characters in words. Stevenson’s works, unlike other British authors, captured the unique day to day life of average Scottish people.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目询问Stevenson对什么方面的理解，使他的作品能够描绘出苏格兰人民独特的一面。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"Stevenson's understanding of\"和\"unique expression of Scottish people\"等关键词，可以定位到D段中描述Stevenson作品特点的内容。\n解题思路：原文中提到Stevenson有\"natural ability to capture stories and characters in words\"（用文字捕捉故事和角色的天生能力），并提到他的作品\"captured the unique day to day life of average Scottish people\"（捕捉了苏格兰普通人的日常生活）。这表明Stevenson能够通过描绘普通人的日常生活和角色来展现人性特征。因此，human nature（人性）作为答案最为合适，因为对人性的理解使他能够以独特方式描绘苏格兰人民的生活和特点。","options":["natural ability","romance","colorful language","critical acclaim","humor","technical control","storytelling","depth","human nature"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64158","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-J below. Write the correct letter A-J in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64149","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","html":"<p><strong>Stevenson’s biographers KF and CP</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"64150","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","html":"<p><strong>The main point of the second paragraph is</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"64151","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","html":"<p><strong>According to the author, adventure stories</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"64152","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","html":"<p><strong>What does the author say about Stevenson’s works?</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"64153","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","html":"<p><strong>According to the writer, Stevenson’s own lifestyle</strong> </p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"64154","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Although Oscar Wilde admired Robert Louis Stevenson very much, he believed Stevenson could have written greater works.</strong></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"64155","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Robert Louis Stevenson encouraged Oscar Wilde to start writing at first.</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"64156","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Galsworthy thought Hardy is greater than Stevenson is.</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"64157","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Critics only paid attention to Robert Louis Stevenson’s writing topics.</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"64158","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-J below. Write the correct letter A-J in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Sir Walter Scott and Robert Louis Stevenson</strong></p><p>A lot of people believe that Sir Walter Scott and Robert Louis Stevenson are the most influential writers in the history of Scotland, but Sir Walter Scott is more proficient in <strong>36</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[36] ____</strong>,</p>","firstNumber":36}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Robert Louis Stevenson</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>A Scottish novelist, poet, essayist, and travel writer, Robert Louis Stevenson was born at 8 Howard Place, Edinburgh, Scotland, on 13 November 1850. It has been more than 100 years since his death. Stevenson was a writer who caused conflicting opinions about his works. On one hand, he was often highly praised for his expert prose and style by many English-language critics. On the other hand, others criticised the religious themes in his works, often misunderstanding Stevenson’s own religious beliefs. Since his death a century before, critics and biographers have disagreed on the legacy of Stevenson’s writing. Two biographers, KF and CP , wrote a biography about Stevenson with a clear focus. They chose not to criticise aspects of Stevenson’s personal life. Instead, they focused on his writing, and gave high praise to his writing style and skill.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The literary pendulum has swung these days. Different critics have different opinions towards Robert Louis Stevenson’s works. Though today, Stevenson is one of the most translated authors in the world, his works have sustained a wide variety of negative criticism throughout his life. It was like a complete reversal of polarity—from highly positive to slightly less positive to clearly negative; after being highly praised as a great writer, he became an example of an author with corrupt ethics and lack of moral. Many literary critics passed his works off as children’s stories or horror stories, and thought to have little social value in an educational setting. Stevenson’s works were often excluded from literature curriculum because of its controversial nature. These debates remain, and many critics still assert that despite his skill, his literary works still lack moral value.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>One of the main reasons why Stevenson’s literary works attracted so much criticism was due to the genre of his writing. Stevenson mainly wrote adventure stories, which was part of a popular and entertaining writing fad at the time. Many of us believe adventure stories are exciting, offers engaging characters, action, and mystery but ultimately can’t teach moral principles. The plot points are one-dimensional and rarely offer a deeper moral meaning, instead focusing on exciting and shocking plot twists and thrilling events. His works were even criticised by fellow authors. Though Stevenson’s works have deeply influenced Oscar Wilde, Wilde often joked that Stevenson would have written better works if he wasn’t born in Scotland. Other authors came to Stevenson’s defence, including Galsworthy who claimed that Stevenson is a greater writer than Thomas Hardy.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Despite Wilde’s criticism, Stevenson’s Scottish identity was an integral part of his written works. Although Stevenson’s works were not popular in Scotland when he was alive, many modern Scottish literary critics claim that Sir Walter Scott and Robert Louis Stevenson are the most influential writers in the history of Scotland. While many critics exalt Sir Walter Scott as a literary genius because of his technical ability, others argue that Stevenson deserves the same recognition for his natural ability to capture stories and characters in words. Many of Scott’s works were taken more seriously as literature for their depth due to their tragic themes, but fans of Stevenson praise his unique style of story-telling and capture of human nature. Stevenson’s works, unlike other British authors, captured the unique day to day life of average Scottish people. Many literary critics point to this as a flaw of his works. According to the critics, truly important literature should transcend local culture and stories. However, many critics praise the local taste of his literature. To this day, Stevenson’s works provide valuable insight to life in Scotland during the 19th century.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Despite much debate of Stevenson’s writing topics, his writing was not the only source of attention for critics. Stevenson’s personal life often attracted a lot of attention from his fans and critics alike. Some even argue that his personal life eventually outshone his writing. Stevenson had been plagued with health problems his whole life, and often had to live in much warmer climates than the cold, dreary weather of Scotland in order to recover. So he took his family to a south pacific island Samoa, which was a controversial decision at that time. However, Stevenson did not regret the decision. The sea air and thrill of adventure complimented the themes of his writing, and for a time restored his health. From there, Stevenson gained a love of traveling, and for nearly three years he wandered the eastern and central Pacific. Much of his works reflected this love of travel and adventure that Stevenson experienced in the Pacific islands. It was as a result of this biographical attention that the feeling grew that interest in Stevenson’s life had taken the place of interest in his works. Whether critics focus on his writing subjects, his religious beliefs, or his eccentric lifestyle of travel and adventure, people from the past and present have different opinions about Stevenson as an author. Today, he remains a controversial yet widely popular figure in Western literature.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8864&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8851","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Origin of Species & Continent Formation","book":"阅读还原集Vol.17","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.17 · Test 1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8851:64080:1","type":"choice","text":"1 urged Darwin to publish his scientific findings","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In July 1858, Charles Lyell and J. D Hooker, close friends of Darwin, pressed Darwin to present his conclusions so that he would not lose priority to an unknown naturalist.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是谁敦促达尔文发表他的科学发现。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"urged Darwin to publish his scientific findings\"，通过这些词可以定位到D段中\"pressed Darwin to present his conclusions\"这一句，这里的\"pressed\"与\"urged\"同义。\n解题思路：原文D段明确提到，1858年7月，达尔文的挚友查尔斯·莱尔与J·胡克极力敦促他发表研究成果，以免被一位无名自然学家抢走先机。因此，答案是E。","options":["Suess","Wallace","Darwin and Wallace","Wegener","Lyell and Hooke"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64080","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.\nA Suess\nB Wallace\nC Darwin and Wallace\nD Wegener\nE Lyell and Hooke"},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8851:64080:2","type":"choice","text":"2 depicted physical feature of earth's crust","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He suggested that the planet’s seas and oceans now fill the wrinkles between once-contiguous plateaus.\n对应段落：I\n审题：题目要求根据文章信息匹配人物与观点或行为，这里需要找出是谁描绘了地球地壳的物理特征。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"physical feature of earth’s crust\"（地球地壳的物理特征）来定位文章中相关的描述。\n解题思路：在文章I段中，Eduard Suess提出了一个关于地球地壳物理特征的描述，随着地球冷却，其上地壳会收缩并形成褶皱，就像老苹果表皮干瘪的样子。他推测，如今地球上的海洋正是填充了这些曾经连成一片的高原之间的褶皱。这一描述与题目要求匹配，因此答案为A。","options":["Suess","Wallace","Darwin and Wallace","Wegener","Lyell and Hooke"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64080","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.\nA Suess\nB Wallace\nC Darwin and Wallace\nD Wegener\nE Lyell and Hooke"},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8851:64080:3","type":"choice","text":"3 believed in continental drift theory while rejecting another one","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：From this and related data, Wegener concluded that the then broadly accepted ‘land bridge’ theory could not account for this distribution of animals and that only this theory of continental drift could explain it.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是谁相信大陆漂移理论，反对另一个理论。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“continental drift theory”和“rejecting another one”定位到G段末句，该句明确提到Wegener认为大陆漂移理论可以解释动物分布，而拒绝当时广泛接受的“陆桥”理论。\n解题思路：根据原文G段末句，根据这些及相关数据，魏格纳得出结论：当时被广泛接受的“陆桥”理论无法解释动物的分布，唯有大陆漂移理论才能解释这一现象。因此，答案为D。","options":["Suess","Wallace","Darwin and Wallace","Wegener","Lyell and Hooke"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64080","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.\nA Suess\nB Wallace\nC Darwin and Wallace\nD Wegener\nE Lyell and Hooke"},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8851:64080:4","type":"choice","text":"4 published works about wildlife distribution in a different region","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In contrast, Wallace applied himself to the science of biogeography, the study of the pattern and distribution of species, and its significance, resulting in the publication of a massive two-volume work the Geographical Distribution of Animals in 1876.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问是谁发表了关于不同地区野生动物分布的作品。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"published works about wildlife distribution in a different region\"定位到E段中关于Wallace的描述。\n解题思路：E段提到Wallace致力于生物地理学的研究，并出版了一部关于动物地理分布的两卷本著作《动物的地理分布》（Geographical Distribution of Animals），该作品详细研究了不同地区的物种分布模式及其意义，与题目要求完全匹配。因此，答案为B。","options":["Suess","Wallace","Darwin and Wallace","Wegener","Lyell and Hooke"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64080","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.\nA Suess\nB Wallace\nC Darwin and Wallace\nD Wegener\nE Lyell and Hooke"},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8851:64080:5","type":"choice","text":"5 Evolution of species is based on selection by nature.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Quite independently of each other, Charles Darwin and his young contemporary Alfred Russel Wallace reached the conclusion that life had evolved by natural selection.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问是谁认为“物种的进化是基于自然选择”。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词“Evolution of species”和“selection by nature”可以帮助定位到A段，该段提到了达尔文和 华莱士同时得出结论， 物种的进化是基于自然选择。\n解题思路：A段明确提到，查尔斯·达尔文和他年轻的同代人阿尔弗雷德·罗素·华莱士各自独立地得出了生命通过自然选择进化而来的结论。对应题目中的内容，因此，选择C项。","options":["Suess","Wallace","Darwin and Wallace","Wegener","Lyell and Hooke"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64080","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.\nA Suess\nB Wallace\nC Darwin and Wallace\nD Wegener\nE Lyell and Hooke"},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8851:64081:6","type":"choice","text":"6 Best adaptable animal survived on the planet","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：From the effects of disease the most healthy escaped; from enemies the strongest, the swiftest or the most cunning from famine the best hunters – then it suddenly flashed on me that this self-acting process would improve the race, because in every generation the inferior would inevitably be killed off and the superior would remain, that is, the fittest would survive.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“最适合环境的动物在地球上生存了下来”这一信息出现在哪个段落。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“Best adaptable animal survived”，可以定位到B段中关于“the fittest would survive”的描述。\n解题思路：B段中Wallace描述了他关于自然选择理论的灵感，提到，总体而言，最适应环境的生物得以存活。最健康的个体从疾病中幸存，最强壮、最快捷或最狡猾的个体从天敌中逃脱，最优秀的猎手则从饥荒中幸存。这种自我调节的过程将推动种族进化，因为每一代中，劣等者终将被淘汰，而优等者——即最适应环境的个体——将得以延续。这与题目中的信息完全一致。因此，答案为B段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64081","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Question 6-8\nThe reading passage has nine paragraphs A-I Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-I, in boxes 6-8 on your answer sheet."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8851:64081:7","type":"choice","text":"7 Boundary called Wallace's line found between Asia and Australia","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：One result of his work was the conclusion that there is a distinct faunal boundary, called ‘Wallace’s line’, between an Asian realm of animals in Java, Bronco and the Philipiones and an Australian realm in New Guinea and Australia.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是关于“Wallace’s line”这一界限的信息出现在哪一段落。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“Wallace’s line”可以定位到文章中F段的第一句话，其中明确提到了这一界限。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句中的描述，他的研究得出一个重要结论：在爪哇、布隆科和菲利皮奥内斯的亚洲动物群与新几内亚和澳大利亚的澳洲动物群之间，存在着一条被称为“华莱士线”的明显动物分界线。可以确定F段包含了关于“Wallace’s line”这一界限的信息。因此，答案为F。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64081","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Question 6-8\nThe reading passage has nine paragraphs A-I Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-I, in boxes 6-8 on your answer sheet."},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8851:64081:8","type":"choice","text":"8 Animal relevance exists between Australia and Africa","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Wallace had shown that animals long established in southwestern Australia had an affinity with animals in South Africa, Madagascar, India, and Ceylon, but did not have an affinity with those in Asia.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段落提到了澳大利亚和非洲之间存在的动物相关性。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"Animal relevance\"和\"Australia and Africa\"来定位答案。在文章中寻找提到澳大利亚和非洲之间动物相关性的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子,华莱士的研究表明，长期生活在澳大利亚西南部的动物与南非、马达加斯加、印度和锡兰的动物存在亲缘关系，却与亚洲动物毫无关联。可以确定，G段提到了澳大利亚和非洲之间存在的动物相关性。因此，答案为G。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64081","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Question 6-8\nThe reading passage has nine paragraphs A-I Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-I, in boxes 6-8 on your answer sheet."},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8851:64082:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"migrated/Migrated","acceptedAnswers":["migrated","Migrated"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The theory that Wegener dismissed in preference to his own proposed that plants and animals had once migrated across now-submerged intercontinental landbridges.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是Wegener发现大陆漂移理论可以解释物种分布现象，而在之前的“陆桥”理论中，植被和野生动物在洲际间做了什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"land bridge\"和\"vegetation and wildlife\"定位到H段，找到相关句子。\n解题思路：根据原文句子，动植物曾通过现今已沉没的洲际陆桥进行过迁徙。可以确定，在“陆桥”理论中，植被和野生动物曾经迁移过。因此，答案为migrated。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64082","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8851:64082:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"withering skin/Withering Skin","acceptedAnswers":["withering skin","Withering Skin"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1885, one of Europe’s leading geologists, Eduard Suess, theorized that as the rigid Earth cools, its upper-crust shrinks and wrinkles like the withering skin of an aging apple.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目要求根据原文信息填写Eduard Suess将地壳的褶皱比作老苹果的什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"Eduard Suess\"和\"wrinkle of crust\"定位到H段，找到Suess提出的理论描述。\n解题思路：原文明确提到Suess将地壳的褶皱比作\"the withering skin of an aging apple\"老苹果表皮干瘪的纹路，因此答案为\"withering skin\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64082","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8851:64082:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"tectonic plates/Tectonic plates","acceptedAnswers":["tectonic plates","Tectonic plates"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Today, we know that we live on a dynamic Earth with shifting, colliding and separating tectonic plates, not a ‘withering skin’, and the main debate in the field of biogeography has shifted.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问现在我们生活的星球上有什么在不断地运动。\n定位关键信息：题目中提到“Now”和“planet”，这些关键词指向I段中提到现在的大陆理论。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，如今我们已认识到，地球并非一张‘干枯的苹果皮’，而是一个充满活力的大陆，其构造板块不断碰撞、分离；生物地理学领域的核心议题也已发生根本性转变。说明地球上有各个板块在不断地运动。因此，填入“tectonic plates”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64082","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8851:64082:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"dispersalism/Dispersalism","acceptedAnswers":["dispersalism","Dispersalism"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The discussion now concerns ‘dispersalism’ versus ‘vicarianism’: unrestricted radiation of species on the one hand and the development of barriers to migration on the other.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问生物地理学的热点问题转向关注哪两个主要概念。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"two-terms\"和\"biogeography\"定位到I段，该段明确提到当前生物地理学讨论的两个术语。\n解题思路：根据I段原文，当前讨论的焦点在于“扩散主义”与“隔离主义”之争：前者主张物种在广阔陆地上不受限制地辐射扩散，后者则强调自然屏障对物种迁徙的阻隔作用。可以直接找到答案为\"dispersalism\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64082","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8851:64082:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"vicarianism/Vicarianism","acceptedAnswers":["vicarianism","Vicarianism"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The discussion now concerns ‘dispersalism’ versus ‘vicarianism’: unrestricted radiation of species on the one hand and the development of barriers to migration on the other.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问生物地理学的热点问题转向关注哪两个主要概念。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"two-terms\"和\"biogeography\"定位到I段，该段明确提到当前生物地理学讨论的两个术语。\n解题思路：与上题同理，在I段中，提到当前生物地理学领域的讨论主要涉及“dispersalism”和“vicarianism”。因此，答案为“vicarianism”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64082","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64080","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.\nA Suess\nB Wallace\nC Darwin and Wallace\nD Wegener\nE Lyell and Hooke","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> Suess <br/></p><p><strong>B</strong> Wallace <br/></p><p><strong>C</strong> Darwin and Wallace <br/></p><p><strong>D</strong> Wegener <br/></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>E</strong> Lyell and Hooke <br/></p><p><strong>1</strong> urged Darwin to publish his scientific findings <strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"64081","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Question 6-8\nThe reading passage has nine paragraphs A-I Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-I, in boxes 6-8 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>6</strong> Best adaptable animal survived on the planet <strong class=\"source-blank\">[6] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"64082","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the reading passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Wegener found that continental drift instead of ‘and bridge’ theory could explain strange species’\ndistribution phenomenon. In his theory, vegetation and wildlife <strong>9</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">intercontinentally. However, Eduard Suess compared the wrinkle of crust to&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">10</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">of an old apple. Now it is well known that we are living on the planet where there are&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">11</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">in constant mobile states instead of what Suess described. Hot spot in biogeography is switched to concerns between two-terms: ‘</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">12</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;’<strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">and ‘</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">13</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;’<strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong> .</span></span></span></span></p>","firstNumber":9}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Origin of Species &amp; Continent Formation</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>THE FACT THAT there was once a Pangean supercontinent, a Panthalassa Ocean, and a Tethys Ocean, has profound implications for the evolution of multicellular life on Earth. These considerations were unknown to the scientists of the 19th century – making their scientific deductions even more remarkable. Quite independently of each other, Charles Darwin and his young contemporary Alfred Russel Wallace reached the conclusion that life had evolved by natural selection.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Wallace later wrote in My Life of his own inspiration:Why do some species die and some life? The answer was clearly that on the whole the best fitted lived. From the effects of disease the most healthy escaped; from enemies the strongest, the swiftest or the most cunning from famine the best hunters – then it suddenly flashed on me that this self-acting process would improve the race, because in every generation the inferior would inevitably be killed off and the superior would remain, that is, the fittest would survive.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Both Darwin’s and Wallace’s ideas about natural selection had been influenced by the essays of Thomas Malthus in his Principles of Population. Their conclusion, however, had been the direct result of their personal observation of animals and plants in widely separated geographic locations: Darwin from his experiences during the voyage of the Beagle, and particularly during the ship’s visit to the Galapagos Islands in the East Pacific in 1835; Wallace during his years of travel in the Amazon Basin and in the Indonesia-Australian Archipelago in the 1850s.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">D Darwin had been documenting his ideas on natural selection for many years when he received a paper on this selfsame subject from Wallace, who asked for Darwin’s opinion and help in getting it published. In July 1858, Charles Lyell and J.&nbsp;</span>Hooker, close friends of Darwin, pressed Darwin to present his conclusions so that he would not lose priority to an unknown naturalist. Presiding over the hastily called but now historic meeting of the Linnean Society in London, Lyell and Hooker explained to the distinguished members how ‘these two gentlemen’ (who were absent: Wallace was abroad and Darwin chose not to attend), had ‘independently and unknown to one another, conceived the same very ingenious theory.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Both Darwin and Wallace had realized that the anomalous distribution of species in particular regions had profound evolutionary significance. Subsequently, Darwin spent the rest of his days in almost total seclusion thinking and writing mainly about the origin of species. In contrast, Wallace applied himself to the science of biogeography, the study of the pattern and distribution of species, and its significance, resulting in the publication of a massive two-volume work the Geographical Distribution of Animals in 1876.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Wallace was a gentle and modest man, but also persistent and quietly courageous. He spent years working in the most arduous possible climates and terrains, particularly in the Malay archipelago, he made patient and detailed zoological observations and collected a huge number of specimens for museums and collectors-which is how he made a living. One result of his work was the conclusion that there is a distinct faunal boundary, called ‘Wallace’s line’, between an Asian realm of animals in Java, Bronco and the Philipiones and an Australian realm in New Guinea and Australia. In essence, this boundary posed a difficult question: How on Earth did plants and animals with a clear affinity to the Northern Hemisphere meet with their Southern Hemispheric counterparts along such a distinct Malaysian demarcation zone? Wallace was uncertain about demarcation on one particular island-Celebes, a curiously shaped place that is midway between the two groups. Initially, he assigned its flora-fauna to the Australian side of the line, but later he transferred it to the Asian side. Today we know the reason for his dilemma. 200 million years ago, East and West Celebes were islands with their own natural history lying on opposite sides of the Tethys Ocean. They did not collide until about 15 million years ago. The answer to the main question is that Wallace’s Line categorizes Laurasia-derived flora-fauna (the Asian) and Gondwana-derived flora-fauna (the Australian), fauna that had evolved on opposing shares of the Tethys. The closure of the Tethys Ocean today is manifested by the ongoing collision of Australia/New Guinea with Indochina/Indonesia and the continuing closure of the Mediterranean Sea – a remnant of the Western Tethys Ocean.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>IN HIS ORIGIN OF CONTINENTS AND OCEANS, Wegener quoted at length from Wallace’s Geographical Distribution of Animals. According to Wegener’s reading, Wallace had identified three clear divisions of Australian animals, which supported his own theory of continental displacement. Wallace had shown that animals long established in southwestern Australia had an affinity with animals in South Africa, Madagascar, India, and Ceylon, but did not have an affinity with those in Asia. Wallace also showed that Australian marsupials and monotremes are clearly related to those in South America, the Moluccas, and various Pacific islands and that none are found in neighboring Indonesia. From this and related data, Wegener concluded that the then broadly accepted ‘land bridge’ theory could not account for this distribution of animals and that only this theory of continental drift could explain it.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The theory that Wegener dismissed in preference to his own proposed that plants and animals had once migrated across now-submerged intercontinental landbridges. In 1885, one of Europe’s leading geologists, Eduard Suess, theorized that as the rigid Earth cools, its upper-crust shrinks and wrinkles like the withering skin of an aging apple. He suggested that the planet’s seas and oceans now fill the wrinkles between once-contiguous plateaus.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Today, we know that we live on a dynamic Earth with shifting, colliding and separating tectonic plates, not a ‘withering skin’, and the main debate in the field of biogeography has shifted. The discussion now concerns ‘dispersalism’ versus ‘vicarianism’: unrestricted radiation of species on the one hand and the development of barriers to migration on the other. Dispersion is a short-term phenomenon – the daily or seasonal migration of species and their radiation to the limits of their natural environment on an extensive and continuous landmass. Vicarian evolution, however, depends upon the separation and isolation of a variety of species within the confines of natural barriers in the form of islands, lakes, or shallow seas – topographical features that take a long time to develop.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8851&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8852","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Development of Public Management Theory","book":"阅读还原集Vol.17","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.17 · Test 1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8852:64087:14-15","type":"choice","text":"What are the features and advantages for Bureaucratic Management?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nE选项：These servants dedicate themselves to the public in return for security of job tenure among the many advantages of public employment.\nB选项：Selection and Promotion is based on Technical qualifications. There are Formal and Impersonal relations among the member of the organisation. Interpersonal relations are based on positions and not on personalities.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“官僚管理的特点和优势是什么”。\n定位关键信息：  通过题目中的“features and advantages”定位到文章中描述官僚管理特点和优势的句子。\n解题思路：  文章中提到，选拔与晋升以技术资格为依据。组织成员之间存在正式关系和非正式关系。人际关系基于职位而非个人特质。说明升迁更看重的是技术资历，不会夹杂私人感情，对应B选项“员工的晋升更加公平，基于工作职责而非个人特质”。文中还提到，这些公务员以奉献公众为己任，作为回报，他们享有职位稳定等公共就业的诸多优势，这与E选项“员工能够致力于服务公众，从而获得长期稳定的工作保障”直接对应，其他选项与原文不符，故选择B、E。","options":["There are equal opportunities coming from little hierarchy of authority among companies.","Employees’ promotion can be much fairer which is based on job duties not on characters.","Employees enjoy a greater freedom of duties than their strict right.","Selection and Promotion is based on mastery of new technology.","These employees can dedicate themselves to the public for stability of a long term job."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64087","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 14-15\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"64087-8852:64087:14-15"},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8852:64087:14-15","type":"choice","text":"What are the features and advantages for Bureaucratic Management?","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nE选项：These servants dedicate themselves to the public in return for security of job tenure among the many advantages of public employment.\nB选项：Selection and Promotion is based on Technical qualifications. There are Formal and Impersonal relations among the member of the organisation. Interpersonal relations are based on positions and not on personalities.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“官僚管理的特点和优势是什么”。\n定位关键信息：  通过题目中的“features and advantages”定位到文章中描述官僚管理特点和优势的句子。\n解题思路：  文章中提到，选拔与晋升以技术资格为依据。组织成员之间存在正式关系和非正式关系。人际关系基于职位而非个人特质。说明升迁更看重的是技术资历，不会夹杂私人感情，对应B选项“员工的晋升更加公平，基于工作职责而非个人特质”。文中还提到，这些公务员以奉献公众为己任，作为回报，他们享有职位稳定等公共就业的诸多优势，这与E选项“员工能够致力于服务公众，从而获得长期稳定的工作保障”直接对应，其他选项与原文不符，故选择B、E。","options":["There are equal opportunities coming from little hierarchy of authority among companies.","Employees’ promotion can be much fairer which is based on job duties not on characters.","Employees enjoy a greater freedom of duties than their strict right.","Selection and Promotion is based on mastery of new technology.","These employees can dedicate themselves to the public for stability of a long term job."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64087","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 14-15\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"64087-8852:64087:14-15"},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8852:64088:16-17","type":"choice","text":"What are the limitations for the ideas of Bureaucratic Management?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nA选项：Yet,too much importance is given to the technical qualifications of the employees for promotion and transfers. Dedication and commitment of the employee is not considered.\nE选项： It is suitable for government organisations. It is also suitable for organisations where change is very slow. There will be unnecessary delay in decision-making due to formalities and rules. It is appropriate for static organisations.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是官僚管理的局限性是什么。\n定位关键信息： 通过题目中的关键词\"limitations\"和\"bureaucratic management\"定位到C段，该段列举了官僚管理的缺点。\n解题思路：  文章中提到，晋升调动时过度看重员工的技术资质，却忽视了敬业精神和工作投入。说明组织不重视员工的奉献精神，对应选项A，此外，这种模式更适合政府机构和变革缓慢的组织，但会导致决策因繁文缛节而陷入无谓拖延，说明官僚管理适用于变化缓慢的组织，不适用于动态变化快的组织，对应选项E，其他选项与原文不符，故选择A、E。","options":["Commitment of the employee is not taken into consideration enough.","There is difficulty in decision-making based on formalities and rules.","Employees are casually oragnised as no importance is given to formal groups.","There is difficulty in enforcement of rules and regulations.","It is not applicable to dynamic organisations where change is very fast."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64088","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 16-17\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"64088-8852:64088:16-17"},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8852:64088:16-17","type":"choice","text":"What are the limitations for the ideas of Bureaucratic Management?","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nA选项：Yet,too much importance is given to the technical qualifications of the employees for promotion and transfers. Dedication and commitment of the employee is not considered.\nE选项： It is suitable for government organisations. It is also suitable for organisations where change is very slow. There will be unnecessary delay in decision-making due to formalities and rules. It is appropriate for static organisations.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是官僚管理的局限性是什么。\n定位关键信息： 通过题目中的关键词\"limitations\"和\"bureaucratic management\"定位到C段，该段列举了官僚管理的缺点。\n解题思路：  文章中提到，晋升调动时过度看重员工的技术资质，却忽视了敬业精神和工作投入。说明组织不重视员工的奉献精神，对应选项A，此外，这种模式更适合政府机构和变革缓慢的组织，但会导致决策因繁文缛节而陷入无谓拖延，说明官僚管理适用于变化缓慢的组织，不适用于动态变化快的组织，对应选项E，其他选项与原文不符，故选择A、E。","options":["Commitment of the employee is not taken into consideration enough.","There is difficulty in decision-making based on formalities and rules.","Employees are casually oragnised as no importance is given to formal groups.","There is difficulty in enforcement of rules and regulations.","It is not applicable to dynamic organisations where change is very fast."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64088","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 16-17\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"64088-8852:64088:16-17"},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8852:64089:18-19","type":"choice","text":"What are the aims of management as Douglas McGregor’s work of the ‘Theory Y’?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nB选项：This begins with the assumption that work is as natural for humans as rest or play.\nD选项：Humans learn naturally and seek responsibility. Consequently, managers need only to steer employees in cooperative manner toward goals that serve the organization.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是根据道格拉斯·麦格雷戈的“理论Y”，管理的目的是什么。\n定位关键信息： 通过题目中的“Douglas McGregor’s work of the ‘Theory Y’”可以定位到I段，该段详细描述了理论Y的内容。\n解题思路：  根据I段的描述，理论Y认为，工作如同休息或娱乐一样是人类的天性。员工在达成目标时会主动自我引导和管理。人类天生具有学习能力和责任感，因此管理者只需以合作方式引导员工实现组织目标。因此，选项B（员工天生具有休息或娱乐的倾向）和D（管理者可通过合作的方式引导员工实现目标）与理论Y的内容相符，而其他选项与理论Y的内容不符。","options":["Employees must be coerced and controlled if management expects to see results.","Employees has natural tendency for rest or play.","Humans will not automatically seek responsibility.","Managers may guide employees in a cooperative manner toward objectives.","There is little room for manager to designate or share his power."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64089","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 18-19\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"64089-8852:64089:18-19"},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8852:64089:18-19","type":"choice","text":"What are the aims of management as Douglas McGregor’s work of the ‘Theory Y’?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nB选项：This begins with the assumption that work is as natural for humans as rest or play.\nD选项：Humans learn naturally and seek responsibility. Consequently, managers need only to steer employees in cooperative manner toward goals that serve the organization.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是根据道格拉斯·麦格雷戈的“理论Y”，管理的目的是什么。\n定位关键信息： 通过题目中的“Douglas McGregor’s work of the ‘Theory Y’”可以定位到I段，该段详细描述了理论Y的内容。\n解题思路：  根据I段的描述，理论Y认为，工作如同休息或娱乐一样是人类的天性。员工在达成目标时会主动自我引导和管理。人类天生具有学习能力和责任感，因此管理者只需以合作方式引导员工实现组织目标。因此，选项B（员工天生具有休息或娱乐的倾向）和D（管理者可通过合作的方式引导员工实现目标）与理论Y的内容相符，而其他选项与理论Y的内容不符。","options":["Employees must be coerced and controlled if management expects to see results.","Employees has natural tendency for rest or play.","Humans will not automatically seek responsibility.","Managers may guide employees in a cooperative manner toward objectives.","There is little room for manager to designate or share his power."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64089","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 18-19\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"64089-8852:64089:18-19"},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8852:64090:20-21","type":"choice","text":"What are the limitations for the ‘Theory Z’?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nC选项：Since, in reality, there is high percentage of workers would like work for the financial return than the job objectives. A high level of self-discipline is also necessary.\nD选项：These include the depredation of a large professional distance – de-personalization is impossible in Z-organizations.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是“Theory Z”有哪些局限性。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“limitations”和“Theory Z”定位到文章中J段，找到关于Theory Z的局限性描述。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子，Theory Z的局限性包括：Z型组织会严重削弱专业距离——这种高度专业化的工作模式难以实现去个性化，以及现实中多数员工更看重经济回报而非工作目标；同时员工需要具备高度自律能力。因此，选项C（并非所有员工都将工作热情置于薪资之上）和D（个性化在组织中依然存在）分别对应了这两个局限性，是正确答案。","options":["Decision-making is democratic and participatory.","Organization mode has inherent design fault.","Not all employee set higher interest in the job than that of wages.","Personalization remains un-eliminated in organizations.","Self-discipline is an unnecessary quality."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64090","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 20-21\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"64090-8852:64090:20-21"},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8852:64090:20-21","type":"choice","text":"What are the limitations for the ‘Theory Z’?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nC选项：Since, in reality, there is high percentage of workers would like work for the financial return than the job objectives. A high level of self-discipline is also necessary.\nD选项：These include the depredation of a large professional distance – de-personalization is impossible in Z-organizations.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是“Theory Z”有哪些局限性。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“limitations”和“Theory Z”定位到文章中J段，找到关于Theory Z的局限性描述。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子，Theory Z的局限性包括：Z型组织会严重削弱专业距离——这种高度专业化的工作模式难以实现去个性化，以及现实中多数员工更看重经济回报而非工作目标；同时员工需要具备高度自律能力。因此，选项C（并非所有员工都将工作热情置于薪资之上）和D（个性化在组织中依然存在）分别对应了这两个局限性，是正确答案。","options":["Decision-making is democratic and participatory.","Organization mode has inherent design fault.","Not all employee set higher interest in the job than that of wages.","Personalization remains un-eliminated in organizations.","Self-discipline is an unnecessary quality."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64090","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 20-21\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"64090-8852:64090:20-21"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8852:64091:22","type":"choice","text":"22 Employees like to follow professional, ethical public officials to secure a job.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Weber admired bureaucracy for its trustworthiness. The bureaucracy was constituted by a group of professional, ethical public officials. These servants dedicate themselves to the public in return for security of job tenure among the many advantages of public employment.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“为了工作稳定，员工倾向于成为专业且恪守道德的公职人员”，需要匹配持有这一观点的人。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“professional, ethical public officials”和“secure a job”定位原文。在B段中，提到“professional, ethical public officials”以及“security of job tenure”。\n解题思路：原文提到，韦伯推崇官僚体制的可靠性。这种体制由一群专业且恪守职业道德的公务员构成。这些公务员以奉献公众为己任，作为回报，他们享有职位稳定等公共就业的诸多优势。题目描述的与原文内容一致，因此答案为A（马克斯·韦伯）。","options":["Mark weber","McGregor","Herbert Simon","Chester Barnard","Charles Lindblom"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64091","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Max weber\nB McGregor\nC Herbert Simon\nD Chester Barnard\nE Charles Lindblom"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8852:64091:23","type":"choice","text":"23 Highly effective can be achieved only after agreeing on a core of objectives and method of doing things.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：However, employees achieve only after ‘agreeing on a central set of objectives and ways of doing business’.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是“核心目标和做事方法一致，才能实现高效运作”，需要匹配持有这一观点的人。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"highly effective\"、\"core of objectives\"和\"method of doing things\"在文章中定位。\n解题思路：根据原文中J段的内容，Z型组织是麦格雷戈二分理论的补充性第三维度。员工只有在“就核心目标和经营方式达成共识”后才能真正发挥作用。题目描述的与原文内容一致，因此答案为A（麦格雷戈）。","options":["Mark weber","McGregor","Herbert Simon","Chester Barnard","Charles Lindblom"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64091","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Max weber\nB McGregor\nC Herbert Simon\nD Chester Barnard\nE Charles Lindblom"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8852:64091:24","type":"choice","text":"24 Managers need to take the employees’ emotional feeling, besides the material rewards, into incentives system.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The net pull of the organization is determined by material rewards, environmental conditions, and other intangibles like recognition. He gives great importance to persuasion, much more than to economic incentives. He described four general and four specific incentives including Money and other material inducements; Personal non-material opportunities for distinction; Desirable physical conditions of work; Ideal benefactions, such as pride of workmanship etc.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“管理者除了物质奖励外，还需要将员工的情感感受纳入激励体系”，需要找到与这一观点相符的人。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"Managers need to take the employees’ emotional feeling, besides the material rewards, into incentives system\"定位到F段，该段明确提到了管理者需要同时考虑物质奖励和情感因素。\n解题思路：原文F段详细阐述了Chester Barnard的激励理论。他明确指出组织的吸引力不仅取决于物质报酬，还包括环境条件和其他无形因素如认可度。他特别强调说服力的重要性，甚至超过经济激励，并具体列举了包括个人非物质机会、理想回馈（如工作自豪感）等非金钱激励因素。因此，这一观点对应的人物是Chester Barnard，对应选项D。","options":["Mark weber","McGregor","Herbert Simon","Chester Barnard","Charles Lindblom"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64091","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Max weber\nB McGregor\nC Herbert Simon\nD Chester Barnard\nE Charles Lindblom"},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8852:64091:25","type":"choice","text":"25 Individuals can maximize their self-interest when all the budget and choices are utilised well.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Rational behavior, in economics,means that individuals maximizes his utility function under the constraints they face (e.g.,their budget constraint,limited choices,...) in pursuit of their self-interest.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“个人在充分利用预算和选择的情况下可以最大化自身利益”，需要找到与这一观点相符的人。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"maximize their self-interest\"、\"budget and choices are utilised well\"在文章中定位。\n解题思路：原文E段提到，在经济学中，理性行为是指个人在追求自身利益时，如何在所面临的约束条件下使个人利益最大化。即在面临的约束条件下最大化个人利益，该段落主要围绕Herbert Simon的理论展开，因此，这一观点对应的人物是Herbert Simon，对应选项C。","options":["Mark weber","McGregor","Herbert Simon","Chester Barnard","Charles Lindblom"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64091","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Max weber\nB McGregor\nC Herbert Simon\nD Chester Barnard\nE Charles Lindblom"},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8852:64091:26","type":"choice","text":"26 The assumption that humans possess a natural dislike to work who ought to be forced and controlled.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：First, commonly held by early management theorists, Theory X begins with the assumption that humans possess an inherent aversion to work. Employees must therefore be coerced and controlled if management expects to see results.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目要求匹配“假设人类天生厌恶工作，因此需要强迫和控制他们”这一观点所对应的人物。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"natural dislike to work\"、\"forced and controlled\"在文章中定位相关句子。\n解题思路：根据原文中H段提到，首先，早期管理理论家普遍认同的X理论认为，人类天生对工作抱有抵触情绪。因此若想取得管理成效，就必须对员工实施强制管控。而该段开头就说明，“Theory X and Theory Y”是Douglas McGregor提出的理论。因此，持有这一观点的人物是McGregor，对应选项B。","options":["Mark weber","McGregor","Herbert Simon","Chester Barnard","Charles Lindblom"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64091","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Max weber\nB McGregor\nC Herbert Simon\nD Chester Barnard\nE Charles Lindblom"}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"64087-8852:64087:14-15","numbers":[14,15],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["B","E"]},{"id":"64088-8852:64088:16-17","numbers":[16,17],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["A","E"]},{"id":"64089-8852:64089:18-19","numbers":[18,19],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["B","D"]},{"id":"64090-8852:64090:20-21","numbers":[20,21],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["C","D"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64087","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 14-15\nChoose TWO correct answers","html":"<p><strong>What are the features and advantages for Bureaucratic Management?</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"64088","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 16-17\nChoose TWO correct answers","html":"<p><strong>What are the limitations for the ideas of Bureaucratic Management?</strong></p>","firstNumber":16},{"id":"64089","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 18-19\nChoose TWO correct answers","html":"<p><strong>What are the aims of management as Douglas McGregor’s work of the ‘Theory Y’?</strong></p>","firstNumber":18},{"id":"64090","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 20-21\nChoose TWO correct answers","html":"<p><strong>What are the limitations for the ‘Theory Z’?</strong></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"64091","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nUse the information in the passage to match the people(listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.\nNB Some people may match more than one ideas.\nA Max weber\nB McGregor\nC Herbert Simon\nD Chester Barnard\nE Charles Lindblom","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> Mark weber <br/></p><p><strong>B</strong> McGregor <br/></p><p><strong>C</strong> Herbert Simon <br/></p><p><strong>D</strong> Chester Barnard <br/></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>E</strong> Charles Lindblom <br/></p><p><strong>22</strong> Employees like to follow professional, ethical public officials to secure a job. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":22}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Development of Public Management Theory</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Several theorists bridged the gap between strictly private and public sector management. One good example is Max Weber exploring sociologist, who explored the ideal bureaucracy in The Protestant Ethic and the Spirit of Capitalism. Bureaucratic Theory was developed by a German Sociologist and political economist Max Weber (1864-1920). According to him, bureaucracy is the most efficient form of organisation. The organisation has a well-defined line of authority. It has clear rules and regulations which are strictly followed. According to Max Weber,there are three types of power in an organisation : [1]Traditional Power, [2]Charismatic Power, and [3]Bureaucratic Power or Legal Power.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>The characteristics or features of Bureaucratic Organisation</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Weber admired bureaucracy for its trustworthiness. The bureaucracy was constituted by a group of professional,ethical public officials. These servants dedicate themselves to the public in return for security of job tenure among the many advantages of public employment. There is a high degree of Division of Labour and Specialisation as well as a defined Hierarchy of Authority. There are well defined Rules and Regulations which follows the principle of Rationality, Objectively and Consistency. There rules cover all the duties and rights of the employees. These rules must be strictly followed. Selection and Promotion is based on Technical qualifications. There are Formal and Impersonal relations among the member of the organisation. Interpersonal relations are based on positions and not on personalities.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Bureaucratic organisation is criticised because of the following reasons : Bureaucratic organisation is a very rigid type of organisation. Too much emphasis on rules and regulations which are rigid and inflexible. It does not give importance to human relations. No importance is also given to informal groups which nowadays play an important role in all business organisations. Yet,too much importance is given to the technical qualifications of the employees for promotion and transfers. Dedication and commitment of the employee is not considered. It is suitable for government organisations. It is also suitable for organisations where change is very slow. There will be unnecessary delay in decision-making due to formalities and rules. It is appropriate for static organisations. There is difficulty in coordination and communication.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>Management: A consolidated discipline</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Herbert Simon, Chester Barnard, and Charles Lindblom are among the first of those recognized as early American public administrators. These men ushered in an era during which the field gained recognition as independent and unique, despite its multidisciplinary nature. Simon contributed theoretical separation to discern management, decisions based upon fact versus those made based on values. Since one cannot make completely responsible decisions with public resources based solely on personal values,one must attempt to upon objectively determined facts. Simon developed other relevant theories as well. Similar to Lindblom’s subsequently discussed critique of comprehensive rationality, Simon also taught that a strictly economic man,one who maximizes returns or values by making decisions based upon complete information in unlimited time, is unrealistic. Instead,most public administrators use a sufficient amount of information to make a satisfactory decision:, they ‘satisfice’.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In decision-making, Simon believed that agents face uncertainty about the future and costs in acquiring information in the present. These factors limit the extent to which agents can make a fully rational decision,thus they possess only ‘bounded rationality’ and must make decisions by ‘satisficing’, or choosing that which might not be optimal but which will make them happy enough. Rational behavior, in economics,means that individuals maximizes his utility function under the constraints they face (e.g.,their budget constraint,limited choices,...) in pursuit of their self-interest.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Chester Barnard was also one of the watershed scholars. Barnard published ‘The Economy of Incentives’ (1938), in an attempt to explain individual participation in an organization. Barnard explained organizations as systems of exchange. Low-level employees must have more incentive to remain with the organization for which they exchange their labor and loyalty. The organization (and higher level employees) must derive sufficient benefit from its employees to keep them. The net pull of the organization is determined by material rewards, environmental conditions, and other intangibles like recognition. He gives great importance to persuasion, much more than to economic incentives. He described four general and four specific incentives including Money and other material inducements; Personal non-material opportunities for distinction; Desirable physical conditions of work; Ideal benefactions, such as pride of workmanship etc.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A new humanist era: Rethinking power and management</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Humanists embrace a dynamic concept of an employee and management techniques. This requires a theoretical shift away from the idea that an employee is a cog in the industrial machine. Rather,employees are unique individuals with goals, needs, desires, etc.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The humanist era ushered in other possible interpretations of such topics as power and management. One of the most significant was Douglas McGregor’s ‘Theory X and Theory Y’. McGregor’s work provided a basis for a management framework, a structure upon whose rungs the classic and new-aged management might be hung. First, commonly held by early management theorists, Theory X begins with the assumption that humans possess an inherent aversion to work. Employees must therefore be coerced and controlled if management expects to see results. Further, lazy humans prefer direction bordering micromanagement whenever possible.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Theory Y is much more compatible with the humanist tradition. This begins with the assumption that work is as natural for humans as rest or play. Further, employees will direct and control themselves as they complete objectives. Humans learn naturally and seek responsibility. Consequently, managers need only to steer employees in cooperative manner toward goals that serve the organization. There is room for many to create and share power.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The Z-Organization can be thought of as a complimentary third element to McGregor’s dichotomy. Z-organizations are a Japanese organizational model. Similar to Theory-Y management, Z organizations place a large degree of responsibility upon the employees. Further, relatively low-level employees are entrusted with the freedom to be creative, ‘wander around the organization’ and become truly unique, company-specific employees. However, employees achieve only after ‘agreeing on a central set of objectives and ways of doing business’. In Z Organizations, decision-making is democratic and participatory. Despite the many advantages of this organizational model, there are several draw-backs. These include the depredation of a large professional distance – de-personalization is impossible in Z-organizations. Since, in reality, there is high percentage of workers would like work for the financial return than the job objectives. A high level of self-discipline is also necessary.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8852&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8853","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 History of telegraph in communication","book":"阅读还原集Vol.17","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.17 · Test 1 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8853:64092:27","type":"choice","text":"In the research of French scientists, the metal lines were used to send a message.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Jean-Antoine Nollet was a French clergyman and physicist. In 1746 he gathered about two hundred monks into a circle about a mile (1.6 km) in circumference, with pieces of iron wire connecting them. He then discharged a battery of Leyden jars through the human chain and observed that each man reacted at substantially the same time to the electric shock, showing that the speed of electricity's propagation was very high.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问“在法国科学家的研究中，使用了金属线来发送信息”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键词“French scientists”、“metal lines”、“send a message”定位到A段，文中提到法国僧侣用铁线进行电学实验，并通过“said ‘ow’”传递信号。\n解题思路：A段提到，法国物理学家让-安托万·诺莱让约两百名修士围成一个周长约一英里（1.6公里）的圆圈，用铁丝将他们连接起来，随后他让一排莱顿瓶通过人链释放电击，传递电信号，说明金属线确实被用于信号传递。因此题目描述与原文一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64092","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 27-32\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8853:64093:28","type":"choice","text":"People increasingly hoped to explore ways of long-distance communication in the late eighteenth century.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：After the introduction of the European semaphore lines in 1792, the world's desire to further its ability to communicate from a distance only grew.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目陈述“在18世纪末期，人们越来越希望探索远距离通信的方式”，需要判断该陈述是否与文章内容一致。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键信息“late eighteenth century”和“long-distance communication”，定位到B段开头关于1792年后人们需求的描述。\n解题思路：原文B段明确指出，在1792年欧洲信号线路引入之后，世界对于进一步发展远距离通信能力的渴望在不断增长。“1792年”属于18世纪末期，“desire... only grew”与题目中的“increasingly hoped”为同义表达，且“communicate from a distance”即指“long-distance communication”。因此，题目陈述与原文信息完全一致，判断为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64093","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 27-32\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8853:64094:29","type":"choice","text":"Using Morse Code to send message needed special personnel to first simplify the message.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At first, it was imagined that only a few highly skilled encoders would be able to use it but it soon became clear that many people could become proficient in Morse code.\n对应段落：C段\n审题： 题目陈述“使用莫尔斯电码发送信息需要专门人员首先简化信息”，需要判断该陈述是否与文章内容一致。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键信息“Morse Code”和“special personnel”，定位到C段关于莫尔斯电码使用人群的描述。\n解题思路：原文C段明确说明，起初人们认为只有少数高度熟练的编码员才能使用它，但后来很快发现许多人也能熟练掌握莫尔斯电码。这表明，许多普通人都能使用，并不需要专门人员来简化信息。题目陈述与原文事实相反，判断为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64094","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 27-32\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8853:64095:30","type":"choice","text":"Morse was a famous inventor before he invented the code.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Building on the success of the optical telegraph, Samuel F.B. Morse completed a working version of the electrical recording telegraph, which only required a single wire to send code of dots and dashes.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目说，莫尔斯在发明密码之前是一位著名的发明家，需要判断该陈述是否与文章内容一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Morse\"和\"before he invented the code\"定位到C段中关于莫尔斯的描述。\n解题思路：原文中提到莫尔斯发明了一种只需要单根电线，发送点和划线代码的系统，但并未提及他在发明代码之前是否已经是一位著名的发明家。因此，无法从文章中得出这一信息，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64095","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 27-32\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8853:64096:31","type":"choice","text":"Water was significant to early telegraph repeater stations on the continent.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：There had to be telegraph repeater stations every few hundred miles to boost the signal and the staff obviously had to have a supply of water\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问水对早期大陆上的电报中继站很重要，需要判断该陈述是否与文章内容一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"water\"和\"early telegraph repeater\"定位到F段，该段明确提到水对电报中继站的重要性。\n解题思路：根据原文F段的内容，水不仅用于施工，而且电报中继站每隔几百英里就需要设立一个来增强信号，工作人员也需要有水源供应。因此，水对早期大陆上的电报中继站确实很重要，所以答案是True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64096","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 27-32\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8853:64097:32","type":"choice","text":"The Australian Government offered funds for the first overland line across the continent.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：On August 22, 1872, the Northern and Southern sections of the Overland Telegraph Line were connected, uniting the Australian continent and within a few months, Australia was at last in direct contact with England via the submarine cable, too. This allowed the Australian Government to receive news from around the world almost instantaneously for the first time.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问澳大利亚政府为横跨大陆的第一条电报线路提供了资金。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Australian Government\"和\"fund\"作为关键词在文章中定位，发现文章主要描述了电报线路的建设过程和影响，但没有提及澳大利亚政府的资金支持。\n解题思路：通过阅读文章H段，1872年8月22日，澳大利亚大陆的北区与南区通过陆地电报线实现联网，短短数月后，海底电缆的铺设让澳大利亚终于与英国建立了直接通信。这使得澳大利亚政府首次能够近乎实时接收全球各地的新闻。可以看到关于电报线路完成后的影响和用途，但并未提及任何关于资金来源的信息。因此，题目中的信息在文章中没有被提及，答案应为Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64097","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 27-32\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8853:64098:33","type":"fill","text":"填写第 33 空","answer":"too costly/Too Costly","acceptedAnswers":["too costly","Too Costly"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1840 Charles Wheatstone from Britain, with William Cooke, obtained a new patent for a telegraphic arrangement. The new apparatus required only a single pair of wires, but the telegraph was still too costly for general purposes.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是导致查尔斯·惠斯通的电报系统在最初失败的缺陷是什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的名字\"Charles Wheatstone\"和关键词\"disadvantage\"或\"fail\"来定位答案所在的句子。\n解题思路：在B段中找到关于Charles Wheatstone电报系统的描述，原文提到，1840年，英国的查尔斯·惠斯通与威廉·库克共同获得了一项电报装置的专利。虽然新设备仅需一对导线，但电报机的高昂成本仍使其难以普及。明确指出了该系统的缺点是建造成本高，因此答案为too costly。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64098","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 33-40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8853:64099:34","type":"fill","text":"填写第 34 空","answer":"latex/gutta-percha","acceptedAnswers":["latex","gutta-percha"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At that time there was no material available for cable insulation and the first breakthrough came with the discovery of a rubber-like latex called gutta-percha.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“跨海电缆使用的绝缘材料是什么？”\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"insulating cable across the sea\"可以定位到D段，其中提到了电缆的绝缘材料。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到绝缘材料是一种名为古塔胶的橡胶状乳胶，称为\"gutta-percha\"，它来源于某些热带树木的\"latex\"乳胶。因此，答案为\"latex\"或\"gutta-percha\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64099","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 33-40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8853:64100:35","type":"fill","text":"填写第 35 空","answer":"lead pipe/Lead Pipe","acceptedAnswers":["lead pipe","Lead Pipe"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This used two layers of gutta-percha insulation and an armoured outer layer. With thin wire and thick insulation, it floated and had to be weighed down with lead pipe.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是英国先驱者们曾使用什么来增加海底电缆的重量。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"British pioneers\"、\"increase the weight of the cable in the sea\"在文章中定位答案所在句子。\n解题思路：根据原文中D段，该电缆采用双层古塔胶绝缘层和铠装外层设计，通过细导线搭配厚绝缘层实现浮力，需用铅管进行压载。可以确定使用了\"lead pipe\"铅管来增加海中电缆的重量，因此答案为\"lead pipe\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64100","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 33-40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8853:64101:36","type":"fill","text":"填写第 36 空","answer":"impedance","acceptedAnswers":["impedance"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Moreover, for certain reasons, the cable had an impedance associated with it at the sending end which could make the voltage on the cable differ from the voltage applied to the sending-end apparatus.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目询问“施加电压时，海底电缆会出现什么？”\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键信息“submarine cable”和“voltage”，定位到E段讨论电缆电气特性的部分。\n解题思路：原文E段直接说明，当施加电压时，电缆在发送端会产生一种“阻抗（impedance）”，这种阻抗会导致电缆上的电压与施加给发送端设备的电压不同。这直接回答了题目关于施加电压时电缆会出现什么现象的问题。因此，答案是impedance。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64101","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 33-40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8853:64102:37","type":"fill","text":"填写第 37 空","answer":"James Buchanan","acceptedAnswers":["James Buchanan"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Amazingly, the first official telegram to pass between two continents was a letter of congratulation from Queen Victoria of the United Kingdom to the President of the United States, James Buchanan, on August 16, 1858.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是维多利亚女王通过跨大西洋传送的消息是发送给谁的。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"message\"、\"firstly sent\"、\"Queen\"和\"across the Atlantic\"在文章中定位。这些关键词共同指向E段中描述的维多利亚女王发送第一条跨大西洋消息的句子。\n解题思路：原文E段提到,1858年8月16日，英国维多利亚女王向美国总统詹姆斯·布坎南发送的贺电，成为首条横跨两大洲的官方电报。因此可以确定答案为James Buchanan。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64102","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 33-40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8853:64103:38","type":"fill","text":"填写第 38 空","answer":"camels/Camels","acceptedAnswers":["camels","Camels"],"explanation":"原文答案句：They needed horses and bullock carts and, for the parched interior, camels.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“在穿越沙漠时，使用了哪种大型动物来运输电缆？”\n定位关键信息：利用题目的核心词\"carry the cable through the desert\"在文章中定位，找到描述运输电缆过程的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，需要马匹和牛车运输物资，干旱内陆地区还得靠骆驼驮运。原文中的\"the parched interior\"干旱的内陆地区，指的是题目中的\"desert\"。因此，答案为“camels”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64103","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 33-40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8853:64104:39","type":"fill","text":"填写第 39 空","answer":"tropical rains/Tropical Rains","acceptedAnswers":["tropical rains","Tropical Rains"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In the north, tropical rains left the teams flooded.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是在澳大利亚北部，是什么天气导致工程延期。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"north Australia\"和\"delay the construction\"可以定位到F段中提到工程延期原因的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，北部热带暴雨时常淹没施工队，导致工程延期，因此答案为\"tropical rain\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64104","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 33-40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8853:64105:40","type":"fill","text":"填写第 40 空","answer":"several hours/Several Hours","acceptedAnswers":["several hours","Several Hours"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It could cost several pounds to send a message and it might take several hours for it to reach its destination on the other side of the globe, but the world would never be the same again.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目询问，1872年，从澳大利亚发送电报消息到英国需要多长时间。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的专有名词\"Australia\"和\"England\"以及关键词\"telegraph message\"在文章中定位答案所在的句子。\n解题思路：G段中提到1872年，北南两段的陆地电报线成功贯通，将澳大利亚大陆与外界连接起来，发送一条信息可能要花费几英镑，可能需要几个小时才能到达地球的另一边，因此，答案为\"several hours\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64105","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 33-40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64092","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 27-32\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>In the research of French scientists, the metal lines were used to send a message.</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"64093","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 27-32\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong><span style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;,sans-serif\">People increasingly hoped to explore ways of long-distance communication in the late eighteenth century.</span></strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"64094","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 27-32\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong><span style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;,sans-serif\">Using Morse Code to send message needed special personnel to first simplify the message.</span></strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"64095","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 27-32\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Morse was a famous inventor before he invented the code.</strong></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"64096","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 27-32\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong><span style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;,sans-serif\">Water was significant to early telegraph repeater stations on the continent.</span></strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"64097","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Quesitons 27-32\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong><span style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;,sans-serif\">The Australian Government offered funds for the first overland line across the continent.</span></span></strong></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"64098","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 33-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>33</strong> Why is the disadvantage for Charles Wheatstone’s telegraph system to fail in the beginning? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[33] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"64099","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 33-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>34</strong> What material was used for insulating cable across the sea? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[34] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"64100","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 33-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>35</strong> What was used by British pioneers to increase the weight of the cable in the sea? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[35] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"64101","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 33-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>36</strong> <span style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;,sans-serif\">What would occur in the submarine cable when the voltage was applied?</span> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[36] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"64102","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 33-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>37</strong> <span style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;,sans-serif\">Who was a message first sent to across the Atlantic by the Queen?&nbsp;</span><strong class=\"source-blank\">[37] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"64103","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 33-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>38</strong> What giant animals were used to carry the cable through the desert? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[38] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"64104","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 33-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>39</strong> <span style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;,sans-serif\">What weather condition delayed construction in north Australia?</span> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[39] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"64105","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 33-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>40</strong> <span style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;,sans-serif\">How long did it take to send a telegraph message from Australia to England in 1872?&nbsp;</span><strong class=\"source-blank\">[40] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>History of telegraph in communication</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Jean-Antoine Nollet was a French clergyman and physicist. In 1746 he gathered about two hundred monks into a circle about a mile (1.6 km) in circumference, with pieces of iron wire connecting them. He then discharged a battery of Leyden jars through the human chain and observed that each man reacted at substantially the same time to the electric shock, showing that the speed of electricity&#39;s propagation was very high. Given a more humane detection system, this could be a way of signaling over long distances.&nbsp;In 1748, Nollet invented one of the first electrometers, the electroscope, which detected the presence of an electric charge by using electrostatic attraction and repulsion.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>After the introduction of the European semaphore lines in 1792, the world&#39;s desire to further its ability to communicate from a distance only grew.&nbsp;People wanted a way to send and receive news from remote locations so that they could better understand what was happening in the world around them – not just what was going on in their immediate town or city. This type of communication not only appealed to the media industry, but also to private individuals and companies who wished to stay in touch with contacts. In 1840 Charles Wheatstone from Britain, with William Cooke, obtained a new patent for a telegraphic arrangement.&nbsp;The new apparatus required only a single pair of wires, but the telegraph was still too costly for general purposes.&nbsp;In 1845, however, Cooke and Wheatstone succeeded in producing the single needle apparatus, which they patented, and from that time the electric telegraph became a practical instrument, soon adopted on all the railway lines of the country.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>It was the European optical telegraph, or semaphore, that was the predecessor of the electrical recording telegraph that changed the history of communication forever.&nbsp;Building on the success of the optical telegraph, Samuel F.B. Morse completed a working version of the electrical recording telegraph, which only required a single wire to send code of dots and dashes.&nbsp;At first, it was imagined that only a few highly skilled encoders would be able to use it, but it soon became clear that many people could become proficient in Morse code.&nbsp;A system of lines strung on telegraph poles began to spread in Europe and America.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In the 1840s and 1850s several individuals proposed or advocated construction of a telegraph cable across the Atlantic Ocean, including Edward Thornton and Alonzo Jackman.&nbsp;At that time there was no material available for cable insulation and the first breakthrough came with the discovery of a rubber-like latex called gutta-percha.&nbsp;Introduced to Britain in 1843, gutta-percha is the gum of a tree native to the Malay Peninsula and Malaysia.&nbsp;After the failure of their first cable in 1850, the British brothers John and Jacob Brett laid a successful submarine cable from Dover to Calais in 1851. This used two layers of gutta-percha insulation and an armoured outer layer. With thin wire and thick insulation, it floated and had to be weighed down with lead pipe.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>In the case of first submarine-cable telegraphy, there was the limitation of knowledge of how its electrical properties were affected by water.&nbsp;The voltage which may be impressed on the cable was limited to a definite value. Moreover, for certain reasons, the cable had an impedance associated with it at the sending end which could make the voltage on the cable differ from the voltage applied to the sending-end apparatus.&nbsp;In fact, the cable was too big for a single boat, so two had to start in the middle of the Atlantic, join their cables and sail in opposite directions.&nbsp;Amazingly, the first official telegram to pass between two continents was a letter of congratulation from Queen Victoria of the United Kingdom to the President of the United States, James Buchanan, on August 16, 1858.&nbsp;However, signal quality declined rapidly, slowing transmission to an almost unusable speed and the cable was destroyed the following month.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>To complete the link between England and Australia, John Pender formed the British-Australian Telegraph Company. The first stage was to lay a 557nm cable from Singapore to Batavia on the island of Java in 1870. It seemed likely that it would come ashore at the northern port of Darwin from where it might connect around the coast to Queensland and New South Wales. It was an undertaking more ambitious than spanning the ocean. Flocks of sheep had to be driven with the 400 workers to provide food.&nbsp;They needed horses and bullock carts and, for the parched interior, camels.&nbsp;In the north, tropical rains left the teams flooded.&nbsp; In the centre, it seemed that they would die of thirst. One critical section in the red heart of Australia involved finding a route through the McDonnell Mountain range and then finding water on the other side. The water was not only essential for the construction teams.&nbsp;There had to be telegraph repeater stations every few hundred miles to boost the signal and the staff obviously had to have a supply of water.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>On August 22, 1872, the Northern and Southern sections of the Overland Telegraph Line were connected, uniting the Australian continent and within a few months, Australia was at last in direct contact with England via the submarine cable, too.&nbsp;This allowed the Australian Government to receive news from around the world almost instantaneously for the first time.&nbsp;It could cost several pounds to send a message and it might take several hours for it to reach its destination on the other side of the globe, but the world would never be the same again. The telegraph was the first form of communication over a great distance and was a landmark in human history.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8853&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8848","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 T-Rex Hunter","book":"阅读还原集Vol.16","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.16 · Test 4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8848:64044:1","type":"choice","text":"Jack Horner knew exactly the bone belonged to a certain dinosaur when he was in father's ranch at\nthe age of 8.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：I picked up one. I am pretty sure it was the upper arm bone of a duckbilled dinosaur: it probably wasn’t a maiaosaur but closely related to that. I catalogued it, and took good care of it, and then later when I was in high school, excavated my first dinosaur skeleton. It obviously started earlier than eight and I literally have been driven ever since. I feel like I was born this way.’\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问Jack Horner8岁时在父亲的牧场，那时就能知道他捡到的骨头属于哪种恐龙，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"Jack Horner\"、\"age of 8\"和\"bone belonged to a certain dinosaur\"定位到B段描述他8岁时发现恐龙骨头的句子。\n解题思路：原文第2段中间部分“I am pretty sure it was the upper arm bone of a duckbilled dinosaur”。他非常确定这个骨头是鸭嘴龙的上臂骨。原文内容与题目相符合，因此，正确答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64044","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8848:64045:2","type":"choice","text":"Jack Horner achieved a distinctive degree in university when he graduated.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Horner spent seven years at university but never graduated. ‘I have a learning disability, I would call it a learning difference – dyslexia, they call it – and I just had a terrible time with English and foreign languages and things like that. For a degree in geology or biology, they required two years of a foreign language. There was no way in the world I could do that. In fact, I didn’t really pass English. So I couldn’t get a degree, I just wasn’t capable of it. But I took all of the courses required and I wrote a thesis and I did all sorts of things. So I have the education, I just didn’t have the piece of paper,’ he says.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问Jack Horner在大学毕业时获得了一个特殊的学位，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“Jack Horner”、“achieved a distinctive degree in university when he graduated”，通过这些关键词可以定位到C段中关于Horner大学经历的描述。\n解题思路：根据C段中的原文“Horner spent seven years at university but never graduated”和“I couldn’t get a degree, I just wasn’t capable of it”可知，Horner在大学学习了七年但没有毕业，也没有获得学位。因此，题目中的说法与原文信息不符，所以答案是False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64045","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8848:64046:3","type":"choice","text":"Jack Horner is the first man that discovered T-Rex's bone in the world.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：So when I was eight years old he took me back to the area that had been his ranch, to where he had seen these big old bones. I picked up one.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问“Jack Horner是世界上第一个发现霸王龙骨骼的人”，需要判断这一陈述是否与原文信息一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的“Jack Horner”和“discovered T-Rex’s bone”是定位关键词。文中未明确说明谁首先发现霸王龙骨骼。\n解题思路：B段提到，八岁那年，他父亲带他回到曾经的牧场，那里曾出土过那些巨大的古老骨骼。原文没有提供任何信息证明他是第一个发现霸王龙骨骼的人，因此无法确定这一陈述的真假。答案为Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64046","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8848:64047:4","type":"choice","text":"Jack Horner believes that the number of prey should be more than that of the predator.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Triceratops is very common: they are the cows of the Cretaceous, they are everywhere. Duck-Billed dinosaurs are relatively common but not as common as triceratops and T rex, for a meat-eating dinosaur, is very common. What we would consider the predator-prey ratio seems really off the scale.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问Jack Horner认为猎物数量应多于捕食者数量，需要判断这一陈述是否与原文信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Jack Horner\"和\"number of prey\"和\"number of predator\"定位到文章中相关句子。\n解题思路：在D段中，原文提到，他解释道，“三角龙非常常见：它们是白垩纪的‘牛群’，随处可见。鸭嘴龙相对常见，但不如三角龙和霸王龙那么常见。作为食肉恐龙，霸王龙却非常普遍。我们所认为的捕食者与猎物比例似乎严重失衡。这说明Jack Horner认为猎物（食草动物）数量应该多于捕食者（食肉动物）数量。因此，答案是TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64047","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8848:64048:5","type":"choice","text":"T-Rex's number is equivalent to the number of vulture in the Serengeti.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Which is why he sees T-Rex, not as the lion of the Cretaceous savannah but its vulture.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目判断“塞伦盖蒂地区霸王龙的数量与秃鹫的数量相当”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息： 使用 \"T-Rex's number\", \"equivalent to\", \"vulture in the Serengeti\" 定位到文中将T-Rex与秃鹫进行类比或提供具体数量比较的句子。\n解题思路：段落F中，Horner确实将霸王龙与塞伦盖蒂生态系统中以腐肉为生的“秃鹫”(vultures)进行了行为上的类比，认为霸王龙更像是一个食腐者。然而，原文没有提及或比较两者具体的种群数量。题目信息在原文中找不到依据，因此答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64048","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8848:64049:6","type":"choice","text":"The hypothesis that T-Rex is top predator conflicts with the fact of the predator-prey ratio which Jack\nfound.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Duckbilled dinosaurs are relatively common but not as common as triceratops and T-Rex, for a meat-eating dinosaur, is very common. What we would consider the predator-prey ratio seems really off the scale. What is interesting is the little dromaeosaurs, the ones we know for sure were good predators, we haven’t found any of them.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是，霸王龙作为顶级掠食者的假说，与杰克发现的捕食者-猎物比例事实相冲突，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"top predator\"和\"predator-prey ratio\"，通过这些词可以定位到E段中关于掠食者-猎物比例的描述。\n解题思路：根据E段中的原文句子，我们所认为的捕食者与猎物比例似乎严重失衡。有趣的是那些小型伤齿龙，我们确信它们是优秀的捕食者，但至今尚未发现任何化石。这表明，霸王龙化石多得不正常，而我们确定是高效捕食者的小型伤齿龙类却几乎没有。这种反常的分布说明霸王龙可能并不是活跃的顶级捕食者，因此“霸王龙是顶级捕食者”的假设与这一事实相冲突。因此，题目中的陈述与文章中的信息一致，答案是TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64049","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8848:64050:7","type":"choice","text":"He refused to accept any other viewpoints about T-Rex's category.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He insisted his theory and finding, dedicated to further research upon it, of course, he would like to reevaluate if there is any case that additional evidence found or explanation raised by others in the future.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问“他拒绝接受任何霸王龙所属类别的其他观点”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“refused to accept any other viewpoints”和“T-Rex’s category”定位答案。在F段中找到“he would like to reevaluate if there is any case that additional evidence found or explanation raised by others in the future”，这句话表明他愿意在未来如果有新证据或解释时重新评估。\n解题思路：原文中提到，他坚持自己的理论和发现，并致力于后续研究。当然，他也表示如果未来有其他研究者发现新的证据或提出新的解释，他愿意重新评估。说明他并非拒绝接受其他观点，而是持开放态度。因此，题目中的“拒绝接受”与原文意思不符，故答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64050","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8848:64051:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"shin bone/Shin Bone","acceptedAnswers":["shin bone","Shin Bone"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He found that the thigh bone was equal in length or slightly longer than the shin bone, and much thicker and heavier.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问Jack Horner发现霸王龙的什么比大腿骨要短。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"Jack Horner\"和\"T-Rex\"定位到G段，该段描述了Horner对霸王龙骨骼的研究。\n解题思路：原文中提到Horner比较了霸王龙的大腿骨和胫骨的长度，发现大腿骨比胫骨长或稍长，且更粗重。根据原文描述，答案是\"shin bone\"（胫骨）。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64051","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8848:64051:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"slow walker/Slow Walker","acceptedAnswers":["slow walker","Slow Walker"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Which proves that the animal was built to be a slow walker rather than fast running.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问，霸王龙的大腿骨长度与胫骨相当或略长，这说明霸王龙实际上是什么。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"thigh bone\"（大腿骨）和\"shorter than\"（比...短）是关键定位词。在文章中搜索这些词，可以找到G段中描述骨骼比例的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，大腿骨与胫骨长度相当或略长，且明显更粗更重。这证明这种恐龙天生就是慢跑型动物，而非擅长疾驰。因此答案应为\"slow walker\"或\"Slow Walker\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64051","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8848:64051:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"cheetah/Cheetah","acceptedAnswers":["cheetah","Cheetah"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This same truth can be observed in many animals of today which are designed to run fast: the ostrich, cheetah, etc.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求填空，霸王龙的大腿骨长度与胫骨相当或略长，所以不像其他比较其他迅捷的动物，如鸵鸟或什么动物。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"ostrich\"和\"swift animals\"定位到G段，找到与鸵鸟并列的迅捷动物。\n解题思路：原文明确提到\"cheetah\"与\"ostrich\"并列作为迅捷动物的例子，与鸵鸟并列提到动物是猎豹，因此答案为\"cheetah\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64051","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8848:64051:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"run fast/Run Fast","acceptedAnswers":["run fast","Run Fast"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This same truth can be observed in many animals of today which are designed to run fast: the ostrich, cheetah, etc.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问“那些迅捷的动物生来就怎么样”。\n定位关键信息：利用上文中的“ swift animals ”定位到G段。\n解题思路：根据原文中描述，这个规律在现代许多能快速奔跑的动物身上同样适用：鸵鸟、猎豹等。确定答案为“run fast”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64051","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8848:64051:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"blunt/Blunt","acceptedAnswers":["blunt","Blunt"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The T-Rex’s teeth were huge, sharp at their tip, but blunt, propelled by enormous jaw muscles, which enabled them to only crush bones.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目要求完成关于支持Horner观点的另一项解释的摘要，需要填写霸王龙的牙齿的特点。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的专有名词\"T-Rex\"和关键词\"teeth\"可以快速定位到H段，该段明确描述了霸王龙牙齿的特征。\n解题思路：原文句子中直接给出了霸王龙牙齿的描述，霸王龙的牙齿虽尖端锐利，却因巨大下颌肌肉的推动而钝重，只能用来碾碎骨头。其中\"blunt\"一词与题目空格处的特征要求完全吻合。因此，填入\"blunt\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64051","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8848:64051:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"crush/Crush","acceptedAnswers":["crush","Crush"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The teeth were not sharp but rather blunt, suggesting they were not designed for tearing flesh.\n对应段落：H段\n审题： 题目要求完成摘要，这样的牙齿只允许霸王龙去怎样处理坚硬的骨头，而不是像迅猛龙那样撕扯肉。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"T-Rex\"、\"Velociraptor\"、\"tearing flesh\"等关键词定位到文章H段。\n解题思路：段落H中，原文在描述了T-Rex牙齿“钝”的特征后，明确指出其功能是“碾碎骨头”(only crush bones)。这里的“crush”正是描述其牙齿功能的动词。因此，应填入“crush”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64051","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64044","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Jack Horner knew exactly the bone belonged to a certain dinosaur when he was in father&#39;s ranch at\nthe age of 8.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"64045","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Jack Horner achieved a distinctive degree in university when he graduated.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"64046","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Jack Horner is the first man that discovered T-Rex&#39;s bone in the world.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"64047","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Jack Horner believes that the number of prey should be more than that of the predator.</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"64048","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>T-Rex&#39;s number is equivalent to the number of vulture in the Serengeti.</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"64049","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The hypothesis that T-Rex is top predator conflicts with the fact of the predator-prey ratio which Jack\nfound.</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"64050","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>He refused to accept any other viewpoints about T-Rex&#39;s category.</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"64051","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Jack Horner found that T-Rex&#39;s <strong>8</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">is shorter than the thigh bone, which demonstrated that it was actually a&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">9</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong> ,&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">unlike other swift animals such as ostrich or&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">10</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">that was built to&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">11</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong> .&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">Another explanation supports his idea is that T-Rex&#39;s teeth were rather&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">12</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong> ,&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">which only allowed T-Rex to&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">13</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong> hard bones instead of tearing flesh like Velociraptor.</span></span></span></span></span></p>","firstNumber":8}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>T-Rex Hunter</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Jack Horner is an unlikely academic: his dyslexia is so bad that he has trouble reading a book. But he can read the imprint of life in sandstone or muddy shale across a distance of 100m years, and it is this gift that has made him curator of palaeontology at Montana State University’s Museum of the Rockies, the leader of a multi-million dollar scientific project to expose a complete slice of life 68m years ago, and a consultant to Steven Spielberg and other Hollywood figures.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>His father had a sand and gravel quarry in Montana, and the young Horner was a collector of stones and bones, complete with notes about when and where he found them. ‘My father had owned a ranch when he was younger, in Montana,’ he says, ‘He was enough of a geologist, is a sand and gravel man, to have a pretty good notion that they were dinosaur bones. So when I was eight years old he took me back to the area that had been his ranch, to where he had seen these big old bones. I picked up one. I am pretty sure it was the upper arm bone of a duckbilled dinosaur: it probably wasn’t a maiaosaur but closely related to that. I catalogued it, and took good care of it, and then later when I was in high school, excavated my first dinosaur skeleton. It obviously started earlier than eight and I literally have been driven ever since. I feel like I was born this way.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Horner spent seven years at university but never graduated. ‘I have a learning disability, I would call it a learning difference – dyslexia, they call it – and I just had a terrible time with English and foreign languages and things like that. For a degree in geology or biology, they required two years of a foreign language. There was no way in the world I could do that. In fact, I didn’t really pass English. So I couldn’t get a degree, I just wasn’t capable of it. But I took all of the courses required and I wrote a thesis and I did all sorts of things. So I have the education, I just don’t have the piece of paper,’ he says.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In Montana, in those days, everybody had the right to a college education. His grades at high school had been terrible, at university, his advisers recognised that he was having a hard time, and went on helping. The dean who kept readmitting him was to give Horner an honorary doctorate years later. As a young non-graduate, Horner wrote to every museum in the English-speaking world, asking for a job. Los Angeles County Museum and the Royal Ontario Museum in Toronto made offers, but he accepted a post as a technician at Princeton University because of Princeton, New Jersey.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘We definitely know we are working on a very broad coastal plain with the streams and rivers bordered by conifers and hardwood plants, and the areas in between these rivers were probably fern-covered. There were no grasses at all: just ferns and bushes – an unusual landscape, kind of taking the south-eastern United States – Georgia, Florida – and mixing it with the moors of England and flattening it out,’ he says, ‘Triceratops is very common: they are the cows of the Cretaceous, they are everywhere. Duckbilled dinosaurs are relatively common but not as common as triceratops and T-Rex, for a meat-eating dinosaur, is very common. What we would consider the predator-prey ratio seems really off the scale. What is interesting is the little dromaeosaurs, the ones we know for sure were good predators, we haven’t found any of them.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Which is why he sees T-Rex, not as the lion of the Cretaceous savannah but its vulture. ‘Look at the wildebeest that migrate in the Serengeti of Africa, a million individuals lose about 200,000 individuals in that annual migration. There is a tremendous carrion base there. And so you have hyenas, you have tremendous numbers of vultures that are scavenging, you don’t have all that many animals that are good predators. If T-Rex was a top predator, especially considering how big it is, you’d expect it to be extremely rare, much rarer than the little dromaeosaurs, and yet they are everywhere, they are a dime a dozen,’ he says. A 12-tonne T-Rex is a lot of vultures, but he doesn’t see the monster as clumsy. He insisted his theory and finding, dedicated to further research upon it, of course, he would like to reevaluate if there is any case that additional evidence found or explanation raised by others in the future.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>He examined the leg bones of the T-Rex, and compared the length of the thigh bone (upper leg), to the shin bone (lower leg). He found that the thigh bone was equal in length or slightly longer than the shin bone, and much thicker and heavier. Which proves that the animal was built to be a slow walker rather than fast running. On the other hand, the fossils of fast hunting dinosaurs ALWAYS showed that the shin bone was longer than the thigh bone. This same truth can be observed in many animals of today which are designed to run fast: the ostrich, cheetah, etc.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>He also studied the fossil teeth of the T-Rex, and compared them with the teeth of the Velociraptor, and put the nail in the coffin of the ‘hunter T-Rex theory’. The Velociraptor’s teeth were like steak knives: sharp, razor-edged, and capable of tearing through flesh with ease. The T-Rex’s teeth were huge, sharp at their tip, but blunt, propelled by enormous jaw muscles, which enabled them to only crush bones.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>With the evidence presented in his documentary, Horner was able to prove that the idea of the T-Rex as being a hunting and ruthless killing machine is probably just a myth. In light of the scientific clues he was able to unearth, the T-Rex was a slow, sluggish animal which had poor vision, an extraordinary sense of smell, that often reached its ‘prey’ after the real hunters were done feeding, and sometimes it had to scare the hunters away from a corpse. In order to do that, the T-Rex had to have been ugly, nasty-looking, and stinky. This is actually true of nearly all scavenger animal. They are usually vile and nasty looking.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8848&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8849","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Seed Hunting","book":"阅读还原集Vol.16","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.16 · Test 4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8849:64057:14","type":"choice","text":"The purpose of collecting seeds now is different from the past.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Those heady days of exploration and discovery may be over, but they have been replaced by a pressing need to preserve our natural history for the future.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问“现在收集种子的目的与过去不同”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的“purpose of collecting seeds now”和“different from the past”定位到C段，该段提到过去是“exploration and discovery”，现在是“preserve our natural history”。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，那些探索发现的狂热岁月或许已成过往，但如今我们更迫切需要为子孙后代守护自然遗产。过去收集种子是为了探索和发现，而现在是为了保护自然，两者目的不同，因此题目陈述与原文信息一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64057","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8849:64058:15","type":"choice","text":"The Millennium Seed Bank is the earliest seed bank.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The Millennium Seed Bank is the world’s largest wild-plant depository. It aims to collect 24,000 species by 2010. The reason is simple: thanks to humanity’s effort, an estimated 25 per cent of the world’s plants are on the verge of extinction and may vanish within 50 years.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问“千年种子银行是最早的种子银行”这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的“Millennium Seed Bank”是关键词，通过这个词定位到E段，该段介绍了千年种子银行的基本信息。\n解题思路：原文提到千年种子银行是世界上最大的野生植物库，并解释了其建立的原因（由于人类活动，导致25%的植物濒临灭绝），但并未提及它是“最早的”种子银行。在其他段落也没有出现这一信息，因此，题目中的“最早”这一信息在原文中未提及，答案为Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64058","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8849:64059:16","type":"choice","text":"One of the major threats for plant species extinction is farmland expansion into wildness.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：We're currently responsible for habitat destruction on an unprecedented scale, and during the past 400 years, plant species extinction rates have been about 70 times greater than those indicated by the geological record as being 'normal'. Experts predict that during the next 50 years further one billion hectares of wilderness will be converted to farmland in developing countries alone.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是，导致植物物种灭绝的主要威胁之一是农田扩张，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"farmland expansion into wildness\"定位到E段，该段提到未来50年将有更多土地转化为农田。\n解题思路：原文E段明确指出，人类正以前所未有的规模破坏自然栖息地，导致了植物的灭绝，未来50年将有10亿公顷的土地被转化为农田，这说明了农田扩张是植物物种灭绝的主要威胁之一。因此，题目陈述与原文信息一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64059","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8849:64060:17","type":"choice","text":"The approach that scientists apply to store seeds is similar to that used by farmers.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句： 'Seed conservation techniques were originally developed by farmers,' he says, 'Storage is the basis what we do, conserving seeds until you can use them just as in farming.'\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是“科学家储存种子的方法与农民使用的方法相似”这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“store seeds”和“similar to that used by farmers”，通过这些词可以定位到H段中提到的“Seed conservation techniques were originally developed by farmers,”这句话。\n解题思路：根据H段中的这句话，种子保存技术最初是由农民发明的，储存是我们工作的基础，跟农业中的一样，都是储存种子以便日后使用。因此，题目中的陈述与文章信息一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64060","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8849:64061:18","type":"choice","text":"Technological development is the only hope to save plant species.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Smith says there’s no reason why any plant species should become extinct, given today’s technology.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问“技术发展是拯救植物的唯一希望”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"Technological development\"和\"save plant species\"定位到H段，Smith的说的话。\n解题思路：原文提到，史密斯认为，以当今科技水平来看，没有任何植物会面临灭绝风险。而不是说只有技术发展可以防止植物灭绝。题目与原文不一致，因此选择FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64061","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8849:64062:19","type":"choice","text":"The works of seed conservation are often limited by financial problems.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Many seed banks are themselves under threat due to a lack of funds.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是\"种子的保护工作经常受到资金问题的限制\"，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"financial problems\"（资金问题）可以定位到J段，该段提到了许多种子银行由于资金不足而面临危机。\n解题思路：原文J段明确指出，许多种子银行由于资金不足而面临危机，这与题目中提到的\"种子的保护工作经常受到资金问题的限制\"完全一致。因此，可以确定题目陈述与文章信息相符，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64062","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8849:64063:20","type":"fill","text":"填写第 20 空","answer":"extinction/Extinction","acceptedAnswers":["extinction","Extinction"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Others collect to conserve, working to halt the sad slide into extinction facing so many plant species.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是一些人收集种子是为了保护某些物种免于什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"protecting certain species\"和\"collect seeds\"定位到A段，找到与收集种子和保护物种相关的句子。\n解题思路：原文中提到，另一些人是为了保护工作而收集种子，努力不让植物灭绝。表明收集种子的目的是阻止物种灭绝，因此答案为extinction。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64063","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nSummary Complete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8849:64064:21","type":"fill","text":"填写第 21 空","answer":"drugs or crops","acceptedAnswers":["drugs or crops"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Some seek seeds for profit-hunters in the employ of biotechnology firms, pharmaceutical companies and private corporations on the lookout for species that will yield the drugs or crops of the future.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“其他人收集种子是为了生产什么”。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的“others collect seeds”和“ability to produce”定位到A段中描述种子收集目的的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，一些人收集种子是为了盈利，他们服务于生物技术公司、制药公司和私人企业，目的是寻找能够生产“drugs or crops”药物或作物的物种。题目中的“ability to produce”对应原文中的“yield”，因此答案为“drugs or crops”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64064","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nSummary Complete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8849:64065:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"pioneers/Pioneers","acceptedAnswers":["pioneers","Pioneers"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Among the pioneers of this botanical treasure hunt was John Tradescant, an English royal gardener who brought back plants and seeds from his journeys abroad in the early 1600s. Later, the English botanist Sir Joseph Banks – who was the first director of the Royal Botanic Gardens at Kew and travelled with Captain James Cook on his voyages near the end of the 18th century – was so driven to expand his collections that he sent botanists around the world at his own expense.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是这种子猎人的什么人中，包括园艺师和植物学家。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"gardeners\"和\"botanists\"定位到B段，该段提到了两位种子猎人的先驱。\n解题思路：原文中B段提到，在植物寻宝的先驱者中，英国皇家园艺师约翰·特拉德斯坎特堪称开山鼻祖。后来，英国植物学家约瑟夫·班克斯爵士也开始收集种子。说明种子猎人的先驱者包括园艺师和植物学家。因此可以确定\"pioneers\"是正确答案。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64065","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nSummary Complete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8849:64066:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"Sir Joseph Banks/sir joseph banks","acceptedAnswers":["Sir Joseph Banks","sir joseph banks"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Later, the English botanist Sir Joseph Banks – who was the first director of the Royal Botanic Gardens at Kew and travelled with Captain James Cook on his voyages near the end of the 18th century – was so driven to expand his collections that he sent botanists around the world at his own expense.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是谁用自己的钱资助了采集者。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"financially supported collectors out of his own pocket\"（用自己的钱资助了采集者），可以在B段中找到对应的句子，其中明确提到了Sir Joseph Banks用自己的钱资助了采集者。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到Sir Joseph Banks是一位英国植物学家，他用自己的钱资助了采集者，这与题目中的描述完全一致。因此，答案为Sir Joseph Banks。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64066","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nSummary Complete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8849:64067:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"underground vaults/Underground Vaults","acceptedAnswers":["underground vaults","Underground Vaults"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Within its underground vaults are 260 million dried seeds from 122 countries, all stored at -20 Celsius to survive for centuries.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问千年种子银行收集的种子通常在哪里进行低温存贮。\n定位关键信息：通过 \"Millennium Seed Bank\" 和 \"stored at a low temperature\" 定位到 D 段，找到描述种子储存地点的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到种子储存在 \"underground vaults\"（地下库房），温度为 -20 Celsius（低温），与题目信息完全一致，因此答案为 \"underground vaults\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64067","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nSummary Complete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8849:64068:25-26","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following are provided by plants to the human?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Besides providing staple food crops, plants are a source of many machines and the principal supply of fuel and building materials in many parts of the world.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问植物可以为人类提供了什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"plants\"和\"human\"定位到F段，该段明确提到植物为人类提供的东西。\n解题思路：原文中F段提到植物提供\"staple food crops\"（基本粮食作物）、\"fuel\"（燃料）和\"building materials\"（建筑材料）。选项A（food）对应\"staple food crops\"，B（fuels）对应\"fuel\"，因此A和B是正确答案。其他选项C（clothes）、D（energy）和E（commercial products）在原文中未明确提及。","options":["food","fuels","clothes","energy","commercial products"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64068","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 25-26\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"64068-8849:64068:25-26"},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8849:64068:25-26","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following are provided by plants to the human?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Besides providing staple food crops, plants are a source of many machines and the principal supply of fuel and building materials in many parts of the world.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问植物可以为人类提供了什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"plants\"和\"human\"定位到F段，该段明确提到植物为人类提供的东西。\n解题思路：原文中F段提到植物提供\"staple food crops\"（基本粮食作物）、\"fuel\"（燃料）和\"building materials\"（建筑材料）。选项A（food）对应\"staple food crops\"，B（fuels）对应\"fuel\"，因此A和B是正确答案。其他选项C（clothes）、D（energy）和E（commercial products）在原文中未明确提及。","options":["food","fuels","clothes","energy","commercial products"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64068","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 25-26\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"64068-8849:64068:25-26"}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"64068-8849:64068:25-26","numbers":[25,26],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["A","B"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64057","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The purpose of collecting seeds now is different from the past.</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"64058","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The Millennium Seed Bank is the earliest seed bank.</strong></p>","firstNumber":15},{"id":"64059","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>One of the major threats for plant species extinction is farmland expansion into wildness.</strong></p>","firstNumber":16},{"id":"64060","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The approach that scientists apply to store seeds is similar to that used by farmers.</strong></p>","firstNumber":17},{"id":"64061","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Technological development is the only hope to save plant species.</strong></p>","firstNumber":18},{"id":"64062","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The works of seed conservation are often limited by financial problems.</strong></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"64063","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nSummary Complete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Some people collect seeds for the purpose of protecting certain species from <strong>20</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong> ;</p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"64064","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nSummary Complete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>others collect seeds for their ability to produce <strong>21</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"64065","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nSummary Complete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>They are called seed hunters.\nThe <strong>22</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong> of them included both gardeners and botanists,</p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"64066","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nSummary Complete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>such as <strong>23</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong> ,\nwho financially supported collectors out of his own pocket.</p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"64067","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nSummary Complete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The seeds collected are usually stored\nin seed banks, one of which is the famous millennium seed bank, where seeds are all stored in the<strong> 24</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> at a low temperature.</p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"64068","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 25-26\nChoose TWO correct answers","html":"<p>Which <strong>TWO</strong> of the following are provided by plants to the human?</p>","firstNumber":25}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Seed Hunting</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>With a quarter of the world&#39;s plants set to vanish within the next 50 years, Dough Alexander reports on the scientists working against the clock to preserve the Earth&#39;s botanical heritage. They travel the four corners of the globe, scouring jungles, forests and savannas. But they&#39;re not looking for ancient artifacts, lost treasure or undiscovered tombs. Just pods. It may lack the romantic allure of archaeology or the whiff of danger that accompanies going after a big game, but seed hunting is an increasingly serious business. Some seek seeds for profit – hunters in the employ of biotechnology firms, pharmaceutical companies and private corporations on the lookout for species that will yield the drugs or crops of the future. Others collect to conserve, working to halt the sad slide into extinction facing so many plant species.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Among the pioneers of this botanical treasure hunt was John Tradescant, an English royal gardener who brought back plants and seeds from his journeys abroad in the early 1600s. Later, the English botanist Sir Joseph Banks – who was the first director of the Royal Botanic Gardens at Kew and travelled with Captain James Cook on his voyages near the end of the 18th century – was so driven to expand his collections that he sent botanists around the world at his own expense.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Those heady days of exploration and discovery may be over, but they have been replaced by a pressing need to preserve our natural history for the future. This modern mission drives hunters such as Dr Michiel van Slageren, a good-natured Dutchman who often sports a wide-brimmed hat in the field – he could easily be mistaken for the cinematic hero Indiana Jones. He and three other seed hunters work at the Millennium Seed Bank, an 80 million pounds sterling international conservation project that aims to protect the world&#39;s most endangered wild plant species.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The group&#39;s headquarters are in a modern glass-and-concrete structure on a 200-hectare Estate at Wakehurst Place in the West Sussex countryside. Within its underground vaults are 260 million dried seeds from 122 countries, all stored at -20 Celsius to survive for centuries. Among the 5,100 species represented are virtually all of Britain&#39;s 1,400 native seed-bearing plants, the most complete such collection of any country&#39;s flora.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Overseen by the Royal Botanic Gardens, the Millennium Seed Bank is the world&#39;s largest wild-plant depository. It aims to collect 24,000 species by 2010. The reason is simple: thanks to humanity&#39;s effort, an estimated 25 per cent of the world&#39;s plants are on the verge of extinction and may vanish within 50 years. We&#39;re currently responsible for habitat destruction on an unprecedented scale, and during the past 400 years, plant species extinction rates have been about 70 times greater than those indicated by the geological record as<br/>being &#39;normal&#39;. Experts predict that during the next 50 years further one billion hectares of wilderness will be converted to farmland in developing countries alone.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The implications of this loss are enormous. Besides providing staple food crops, plants are a source of many machines and the principal supply of fuel and building materials in many parts of the world. They also protect soil and help regulate the climate. Yet, across the globe, plant species are being driven to extinction before their potential benefits are discovered.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The world Conservation Union has listed 5,714 threatened species is sure to be much higher. In the UK alone, 300 wild plant species are classified as endangered. The Millennium Seed Bank aims to ensure that even if a plant becomes extinct in the wild, it won&#39;t be lost forever. Stored seeds can be used the help restore damaged or destroyed the environment or in scientific research to find new benefits for society – in medicine, agriculture or local industry – that would otherwise be lost.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Seed banks are an insurance policy to protect the world&#39;s plant heritage for the future, explains Dr Paul Smith, another Kew seed hunter. &#39;Seed conservation techniques were originally developed by farmers,&#39; he says, &#39;Storage is the basis what we do, conserving seeds until you can use them just as in farming.&#39; Smith says there’s no reason why any plant species should become extinct, given today’s technology. But he admits that&nbsp;the biggest challenge is finding, naming and categorizing all the world&#39;s plants. And someone has to gather these seeds before it&#39;s too late. &#39;There aren&#39;t a lot of people out there doing this,&#39; he says, &#39;The key is to know the flora from a particular area, and that knowledge takes years to acquire.&#39;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>There are about 1,470 seedbanks scattered around the globe, with a combined total of 5.4 million samples, of which perhaps two million are distinct non-duplicates. Most preserve genetic material for agriculture use in order to ensure crop diversity; others aim to conserve wild species, although only 15 per cent of all banked plants is wild.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Many seed banks themselves are under threat due to a lack of funds. Last year, Imperial College, London, examined crop collections from 151 countries and found that while the number of plant samples had increased in two-thirds of the countries, the budget had been cut in a quarter and remained static in another 35 per cent. The UN&#39;s Food and Agriculture Organization and the Consultative Group on International Agricultural Research has since set up the Global Conservation Trust, which aims to raise the US $260 million to protect seed banks in perpetuity.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8849&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8850","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Compliance or Noncompliance for Children","book":"阅读还原集Vol.16","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.16 · Test 4 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8850:64069:27","type":"choice","text":"The children, especially boys received good education may","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Despite good education, these children did not follow the words from their parents on several occasion, especially boys in certain ages.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是，接受良好教育的孩子，尤其是男孩，可能会怎样。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"good education\"和\"especially boys\"定位到B段中的相关句子。\n解题思路：根据B段中的原文句子\"Despite good education, these children did not follow the words from their parents on several occasion, especially boys in certain ages.\"可知，即使接受良好的教育，这些孩子有时也不会听从父母的话，尤其是某些年龄段的男孩。因此，D选项\"有时会不听从父母的命令\"与原文意思一致。","options":["always comply with their parents'words.","be good at math.","have a high score at school.","disobey their parents'order sometimes."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64069","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8850:64070:28","type":"choice","text":"Face to their children's compliance and noncompliance, parents","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A number of parents were not easy to be aware of the compliance, some even overlooked their children’s noncompliance.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是面对孩子的服从和不服从的行为，父母会怎么做。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"compliance and noncompliance\"定位到B段，找到描述父母行为的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文句子，许多家长难以察觉孩子的服从行为，甚至有些家长会忽视孩子的不服从行为。这与选项C\"有些父母可能会忽视他们的不服从行为\"完全一致。其他选项A、B、D在原文中都没有提到，因此正确答案是C。","options":["must be aware of the compliance.","ask for help from their teachers.","some of them may ignore their noncompliance.","pretend not to see."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64070","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8850:64071:29","type":"choice","text":"According to Henry Porter, noncompliance for children","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Said Henry Porter, a scholar working in Psychology Institute of UK. He indicated that noncompliance means growth in some way, may have benefit for children\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是根据Henry Porter的观点，儿童的不服从可能怎么样。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的\"Henry Porter\"和\"noncompliance\"可以定位到C段，找到Henry Porter关于不服从行为的论述。\n解题思路：原文中Henry Porter明确表示，不听话在某种程度上是一种成长，对儿童发展可能具有积极意义。这与选项B的描述完全一致，即不服从可能具有积极效果。其他选项A、C、D在原文中均未提及或与原文内容不符。因此，正确答案是B。","options":["are entirely harmful.","may have positive effects.","needs medicine assistance.","should be treated by an expert doctor."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64071","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8850:64072:30","type":"choice","text":"When children are growing up, they","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：During the period that children are getting elder, who may learn to use more advanced approaches for their noncompliance. They are more skillful to negotiate or give reasons for refusal rather than show their opposite idea to parents directly.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是当孩子长大时，他们会怎么样。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"children are growing up\"定位到C段中\"When they are growing up. During the period that children are getting elder\"这句话。\n解题思路：根据定位到的句子，原文中明确提到，随着年龄增长，这些孩子会逐渐学会更成熟的应对方式。他们更擅长通过协商或给出理由来拒绝，而非直接向父母表明反对意见。这与选项B\"are more skillful to negotiate\"完全一致，因此答案为B。","options":["always try to directly say no.","are more skillful to negotiate.","learn to cheat instead of noncompliance.","tend to keep silent."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64072","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8850:64073:31","type":"choice","text":"Which is the possible reaction the passage mentioned for elder children and younger ones if they don't want to comply with","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘Noncompliant Children sometimes prefer to say to directly as they were younger, they are easy to deal with the relationship with contemporaries when they are growing up. During the period that children are getting elder, who may learn to use more advanced approaches for their noncompliance. They are more skillful to negotiate or give reasons for refusal rather than show their opposite idea to parents directly.’ Said Henry Porter, a scholar working in Psychology Institute of UK.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是文章中提到的，当年幼的孩子和年长的孩子不愿意服从时，他们可能的反应是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"elder children\"和\"younger ones\"以及\"don't want to comply\"来定位文章中相关句子。\n解题思路：在C段中，原文提到，英国心理学研究所学者亨利·波特指出：“不听话的孩子在年幼时往往更倾向于直接表达。随着年龄增长，这些孩子会逐渐学会更成熟的应对方式。他们更擅长通过协商或给出理由来拒绝，而非直接向父母表明反对意见。这句话表明年幼的孩子可能会直接拒绝。而年长的孩子则可能会协商或给出拒绝的理由。因此，选项C\"younger children may reject directly\"与原文内容相符。","options":["elder children prefer to refuse directly.","elder ones refuse to answer.","younger children may reject directly.","younger ones may save any words."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64073","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8850:64074:32","type":"choice","text":"32 Henry Porter","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：During the period that children are getting elder, who may learn to use more advanced approaches for their noncompliance. They are more skillful to negotiate or give reasons for refusal rather than show their opposite idea to parents directly.’ Said Henry Porter, a scholar working in Psychology Institute of UK.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求匹配Henry Porter的观点。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“Henry Porter”定位到C段，该段引用了Henry Porter的话，描述了孩子随着年龄增长，不服从行为表现方式的变化。\n解题思路：原文中提到“随着孩子长大，他们可能会学会使用更高级的方法来表达他们的不服从行为。他们更擅长协商或给出拒绝的理由，而不是直接向父母表达相反的想法。”这与选项B“年长的孩子倾向于协商而不是表现出不服从”完全一致。因此，答案为B。","options":["Children of all ages will indirectly show noncompliance.","Elder children tend to negotiate rather than show noncompliance.","Converse behavior means noncompliance.","Organizing fun activities to occur after frequently refused activities.","Organizing child’s daily activities in the same order as much as","Using praise in order to make children compliant.","Taking the children to school at an early age."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64074","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nLook at the following people and list of statements below. Match each person with the correct statement. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet.\nA Children of all ages will indirectly show noncompliance.\nB Elder children tend to negotiate rather than show noncompliance.\nC Converse behavior means noncompliance.\nD Organizing fun activities to occur after frequently refused activities.\nE Organizing child’s daily activities in the same order as much as possible.\nF Using praise in order to make children compliant.\nG Taking the children to school at an early age."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8850:64074:33","type":"choice","text":"33 Wallace Friesen","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：His collaborator Wallace Friesen believed that Organizing a child’s daily activities so that they occur in the same order each day as much as possible.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求将Wallace Friesen的观点与选项进行匹配。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Wallace Friesen\"定位到C段中Wallace Friesen的观点。\n解题思路：根据原文中Wallace Friesen提出的观点，华莱士·弗里森认为，应该尽可能让孩子的日常活动保持固定顺序。对应选项E：尽可能按照相同的顺序安排孩子的日常活动，因此选择E项。","options":["Children of all ages will indirectly show noncompliance.","Elder children tend to negotiate rather than show noncompliance.","Converse behavior means noncompliance.","Organizing fun activities to occur after frequently refused activities.","Organizing child’s daily activities in the same order as much as","Using praise in order to make children compliant.","Taking the children to school at an early age."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64074","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nLook at the following people and list of statements below. Match each person with the correct statement. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet.\nA Children of all ages will indirectly show noncompliance.\nB Elder children tend to negotiate rather than show noncompliance.\nC Converse behavior means noncompliance.\nD Organizing fun activities to occur after frequently refused activities.\nE Organizing child’s daily activities in the same order as much as possible.\nF Using praise in order to make children compliant.\nG Taking the children to school at an early age."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8850:64074:34","type":"choice","text":"34 Steven Walson","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Doctor Steven Walson addressed that organizing fun activities to occur after frequently refused activities.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求将人物Steven Walson与对应的陈述进行匹配。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的人名\"Steven Walson\"定位到文章中的D段，该段详细介绍了他的观点和方法。\n解题思路：D段明确提到Steven Walson提出了一种策略，以通过组织有趣的后续活动来替代那些经常被拒绝的活动。促使孩子完成不愿意做的活动。这与选项D的描述完全一致，因此答案为D。","options":["Children of all ages will indirectly show noncompliance.","Elder children tend to negotiate rather than show noncompliance.","Converse behavior means noncompliance.","Organizing fun activities to occur after frequently refused activities.","Organizing child’s daily activities in the same order as much as","Using praise in order to make children compliant.","Taking the children to school at an early age."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64074","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nLook at the following people and list of statements below. Match each person with the correct statement. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet.\nA Children of all ages will indirectly show noncompliance.\nB Elder children tend to negotiate rather than show noncompliance.\nC Converse behavior means noncompliance.\nD Organizing fun activities to occur after frequently refused activities.\nE Organizing child’s daily activities in the same order as much as possible.\nF Using praise in order to make children compliant.\nG Taking the children to school at an early age."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8850:64074:35","type":"choice","text":"35 Paul Edith","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Psychologist Paul Edith insisted praise is the best way to make children comply with.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求将人物Paul Edith与相应的陈述进行匹配。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的人名\"Paul Edith\"定位到文章E段，该段明确提到了Paul Edith的观点。\n解题思路：E段第一句直接表明了Paul Edith的观点，他认为表扬是让孩子服从的最佳方式，这与选项F的陈述完全一致，因此答案为F。","options":["Children of all ages will indirectly show noncompliance.","Elder children tend to negotiate rather than show noncompliance.","Converse behavior means noncompliance.","Organizing fun activities to occur after frequently refused activities.","Organizing child’s daily activities in the same order as much as","Using praise in order to make children compliant.","Taking the children to school at an early age."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"64074","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nLook at the following people and list of statements below. Match each person with the correct statement. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet.\nA Children of all ages will indirectly show noncompliance.\nB Elder children tend to negotiate rather than show noncompliance.\nC Converse behavior means noncompliance.\nD Organizing fun activities to occur after frequently refused activities.\nE Organizing child’s daily activities in the same order as much as possible.\nF Using praise in order to make children compliant.\nG Taking the children to school at an early age."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8850:64075:36","type":"choice","text":"Socialization takes a long process, while compliance is the beginning of it.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Many Scientists believe that socialization takes a long process, while compliance is the outset of it.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问“社会化是一个漫长的过程，而服从是它的开始”，是否与文章作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“socialization”、“long process”和“compliance is the beginning”定位到A段第一句。\n解题思路：原文提到“socialization takes a long process, while compliance is the outset of it”，即社会化是一个漫长的过程，而服从是它的开端。所以答案句和题干信息一致，选择“YES”。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64075","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8850:64076:37","type":"choice","text":"Many parents were difficult to be aware of compliance or noncompliance.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A number of parents were not easy to be aware of the compliance, some even overlooked their children’s noncompliance.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问“许多父母难以意识到孩子的服从或不服从行为”，需要判断这是否与文章作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键信息“parents”、“difficult to be aware of compliance or noncompliance”，可以定位到B段开头讨论父母对顺从行为认知的句子。\n解题思路：原文B段首句明确指出“许多父母不容易意识到顺从行为，有些甚至忽视了孩子的不顺从行为”。“not easy to be aware of”与题目中的“difficult to be aware of”为同义表达，因此，题目陈述与原文信息完全一致，判断为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64076","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8850:64077:38","type":"choice","text":"Noncompliant Children are simple to deal with the relationship with the people at the same age\nwhen they are growing up.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘Noncompliant Children sometimes prefer to say to directly as they were younger, they are easy to deal with the relationship with contemporaries when they are growing up.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“当孩子们长大时，不服从的孩子们与同龄人建立关系很容易”是否与作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“Noncompliant Children”和“easy to deal with the relationship with the people at the same age”可以定位到C段第一句。\n解题思路：原文中提到，不听话的孩子在年幼时往往更倾向于直接表达，这种特质使他们在成长过程中更容易与同龄人建立良好关系。因此题目与原文信息相符，所以答案是TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64077","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8850:64078:39","type":"choice","text":"Experts never tried drilling compliance into children.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Many Experts held different viewpoints in recent years, they tried drilling compliance into children.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问“专家从未试图将顺从灌输给孩子”是否与文章作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Experts\"和\"drilling compliance into children\"定位到C段。\n解题思路：原文明确提到“许多专家近年来持有不同观点，他们试图将顺从灌输给孩子”，这与题目中的说法“专家从未试图将顺从灌输给孩子”直接矛盾。因此，题目说法与原文相反，应选择False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64078","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8850:64079:40","type":"choice","text":"Psychologist Paul Edith negated the importance that knowing how to praise children in an\nencouraging way.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：However, it is important to know how to praise children in a way that encourages future automatic reinforcement for your child when doing a similar behavior.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是心理学家保罗·伊迪斯否定了懂得如何以鼓励的方式表扬孩子的重要性，是否与文章作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"Psychologist Paul Edith\"和\"knowing how to praise children in an encouraging way\"可以定位到E段的相关句子。\n解题思路：原文E段明确提到，更重要的是，要懂得用恰当方式表扬，从而培养孩子在类似情境中自发强化的良好习惯。这句话表明Paul Edith强调了了解如何以鼓励的方式表扬孩子的重要性，这与题目中的\"negated the importance\"（否定重要性）表述相反。因此，题目陈述与原文作者的观点不符，答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64079","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64069","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>The children, especially boys received good education may</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"64070","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Face to their children&#39;s compliance and noncompliance, parents</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"64071","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>According to Henry Porter, noncompliance for children</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"64072","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>When children are growing up, they</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"64073","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Which is the possible reaction the passage mentioned for elder children and younger ones if they don&#39;t want to comply with</strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"64074","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nLook at the following people and list of statements below. Match each person with the correct statement. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet.\nA Children of all ages will indirectly show noncompliance.\nB Elder children tend to negotiate rather than show noncompliance.\nC Converse behavior means noncompliance.\nD Organizing fun activities to occur after frequently refused activities.\nE Organizing child’s daily activities in the same order as much as possible.\nF Using praise in order to make children compliant.\nG Taking the children to school at an early age.","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> Children of all ages will indirectly show noncompliance. <br/></p><p><strong>B</strong> Elder children tend to negotiate rather than show noncompliance. <br/></p><p><strong>C</strong> Converse behavior means noncompliance. <br/></p><p><strong>D</strong> Organizing fun activities to occur after frequently refused activities. <br/></p><p><strong>E</strong> Organizing child’s daily activities in the same order as much as\npossible. <br/></p><p><strong>F</strong> Using praise in order to make children compliant. <br/></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>G</strong> Taking the children to school at an early age. <br/></p><p><strong>32</strong> Henry Porter <strong class=\"source-blank\">[32] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"64075","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Socialization takes a long process, while compliance is the beginning of it.</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"64076","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Many parents were difficult to be aware of compliance or noncompliance.</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"64077","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Noncompliant Children are simple to deal with the relationship with the people at the same age\nwhen they are growing up.</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"64078","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Experts never tried drilling compliance into children.</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"64079","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Psychologist Paul Edith negated the importance that knowing how to praise children in an\nencouraging way.</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Compliance or Noncompliance for Children</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Many Scientists believe that socialization takes a long process, while compliance is the outset of it. Accordingly, compliance for the education of children is the priority. Motivationally distinct forms of child compliance, mutually positive affect, and maternal control, observed in 3 control contexts in 103 dyads of mothers and their 26 to 41-month-old children, were examined as correlates of internalization, assessed using observations of children while alone with prohibited temptations and maternal ratings. One form of compliance (committed compliance), when the child appeared committed wholeheartedly to the maternal agenda and eager to endorse and accept it, was emphasized. Mother-child mutually positive affect was both a predictor and a concomitant of committed compliance. Children who shared positive effect with their mothers showed a high level of committed compliance and were also more internalized. Differences and similarities between children’s compliance with requests and prohibitions (‘Do’ vs. ‘Don’t’ demand contexts) were also explored. Maternal ‘Dos’ appeared more challenging to toddlers than the ‘Don’ts’. Some individual coherence of behavior was also found across both demand contexts. The implication of committed compliance for emerging internalized regulators of conduct is discussed.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>A number of parents were not easy to be aware of the compliance, some even overlooked their children’s noncompliance. Despite good education, these children did not follow the words from their parents on several occasion, especially boys in certain ages. Fortunately, this rate was acceptable, some parents could be patient with the noncompliance. Someone held that noncompliance is probably not a wrong thing. In order to determine the effects of different parental disciplinary techniques on young children’s compliance and noncompliance, mothers were trained to observe emotional incidents involving their own toddler-aged children. Reports of disciplinary encounters were analyzed in terms of the types of discipline used (reasoning, verbal prohibition, physical coercion, love withdrawal, and combinations thereof) and children’s responses to that discipline (compliance/noncompliance and avoidance). The relation between compliance/ noncompliance and type of misdeed (harm to persons, harm to property, and lapses of self-control) was also analyzed. Results indicated that love withdrawal combined with other techniques was most effective in securing children’s compliance and that its effectiveness was not a function of the type of technique with which it was combined. Avoidant responses and affective reunification with the parent were more likely to follow love withdrawal than any other technique. Physical coercion was somewhat less effective than love withdrawal, while reasoning and verbal prohibition were not at all effective except when both were combined with physical coercion.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘Noncompliant Children sometimes prefer to say to directly as they were younger, they are easy to deal with the relationship with contemporaries&nbsp;when they are growing up. During the period that children are getting elder, who may learn to use more advanced approaches for their noncompliance. They are more skillful to negotiate or give reasons for refusal rather than show their opposite idea to parents directly.’ Said Henry Porter, a scholar working in Psychology Institute of UK. He indicated that noncompliance means growth in some way, may have benefit for children. Many Experts held different viewpoints in recent years, they tried drilling compliance into children. His collaborator Wallace Friesen believed that Organizing a child’s daily activities so that they occur in the same order each day as much as possible. This first strategy for defiant children is ultimately the most important. Developing a routine helps a child to know what to expect and increases the chances that he or she will comply with things such as chores, homework, and hygiene requests. When undesirable activities occur in the same order at optimal times during the day, they become habits that are not questioned but done without thought. Chances are that you have developed some type of routine for yourself in terms of showering, cleaning your house, or doing other types of work. You have an idea in your mind when you will do these things on a regular basis and this helps you to know what to expect. In fact, you have probably already been using most of these compliance strategies for yourself without realizing it. For children, without setting these expectations on a daily basis by making them part of a regular routine, they can become very upset. Just like adults, children think about what they plan to do that day and expect to be able to do what they want. So, when you come along and ask them to do something they weren’t already planning to do that day, this can result in automatic refusals and other undesirable defiant behaviors. However, by using this compliance strategy with defiant children, these activities are done almost every day in the same general order and the child expects to already do them.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Doctor Steven Walson addressed that organizing fun activities to occur after frequently refused activities. This strategy also works as a positive reinforcer when the child complies with your requests. By arranging your day so that things often refused to occur right before highly preferred activities, you are able to eliminate defiant behavior and motivate your child’s behavior of doing the undesirable activity. This is not to be presented in a way that the preferred activity is only allowed if a defiant child does the non-preferred activity. However, you can word your request in a way so that your child assumes that you have to do the non-preferred activity before moving on to the next preferred activity. For example, you do not want to say something such as, ‘If you clean your room we can play a game.’ Instead of the word your request like this, ‘As soon as you are done cleaning your room we will be able to play that really fun game you wanted to play.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Psychologist Paul Edith insisted praise is the best way to make children comply with. This is probably a common term you are used to hearing by now. If you praise your child’s behavior, he or she will be more likely to do that behavior. So, it is essential to use praise when working with defiant children. It also provides your child with positive attention. However, it is important to know how to praise children in a way that encourages future automatic reinforcement for your child when doing a similar behavior.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8850&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8845","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Grey Workers","book":"阅读还原集Vol.16","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.16 · Test 3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8845:64016:1","type":"choice","text":"Insurance company Sun Life of Canada made the decision that it would hire more Canadian\nemployees rather than British ones in order to get fresh staffs","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Earlier this year, Sun Life of Canada, an insurance company, announced that it was offering redundancy to all its British employees aged 50 or over ‘to bring in new blood’.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问加拿大永明人寿保险公司决定，为引进新鲜血液，将优先招聘加拿大籍员工而非英国籍员工，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"Sun Life of Canada\"和\"hire more Canadian employees\"定位到A段。\n解题思路：原文提到Sun Life of Canada宣布让所有50岁以上的英国员工提前退休，以“引进新鲜血液”。但并未提到他们决定雇佣更多加拿大员工，只是说要引进新员工。题目中的\"hire more Canadian employees rather than British ones\"这一具体信息在原文中没有提及，因此无法确定这一说法是否正确。答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64016","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true, NO if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8845:64017:2","type":"choice","text":"Unlike other places, employees in Japan get paid according to the years they are employed.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In Japan, says Mariko Fujiwara, an industrial anthropologist who runs a think-tank for Hakuhodo, Japan’s second-largest advertising agency, most companies are bringing down the retirement age from the traditional 57 to 50 or thereabouts – and in some cases, such as Nissan, to 45. More than perhaps anywhere else, pay in Japan is linked to seniority.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是不同于其它地方，日本员工的薪资是根据其工作年限来计算的，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Japan\"和\"paid according to the years they are employed\"可以定位到B段中提到的\"pay in Japan is linked to seniority\"。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子\"More than perhaps anywhere else, pay in Japan is linked to seniority\"可以确定，在日本，薪酬与工龄挂钩的现象可能比其他任何地方都更为普遍。因此，题目中的陈述与文章信息一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64017","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true, NO if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8845:64018:3","type":"choice","text":"Elder workers are laid off by some German companies which are refreshing corporate culture.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In Germany, Patrick Pohl, spokesman for Hoechst, expresses a widely held view: ‘The company is trying to lower the average age of the workforce. Perhaps the main reason for replacing older workers is that it makes it easier to ‘defrost’ the corporate culture.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“德国部分企业为重塑企业文化而裁撤年长员工”这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“German companies”（德国公司）、“laid off”（解雇）和“refreshing corporate culture”（重塑企业文化）来定位答案。\n解题思路：根据定位到的C段，原文提到德国赫斯特公司的发言人帕特里克·波尔说到：“公司正试图降低员工平均年龄。或许替换年长员工的主要原因在于，这能让企业更轻松地‘解冻’企业文化。年长员工不太愿意尝试新思维，而年轻员工则更便宜且更灵活。”这与题目陈述一致，因此答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64018","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true, NO if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8845:64019:4","type":"choice","text":"According to Peter Hicks, companies pay older people more regardless of the contribution of they make.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Peter Hicks, who co-ordinates OECD work on the policy implications of ageing, says that plenty of research suggests older people are paid more because they are worth more.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是根据Peter Hicks的观点，公司支付给老年人更多的薪水是否与他们所做的贡献无关。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Peter Hicks\"和\"older people are paid more\"可以定位到D段中Peter Hicks的言论。\n解题思路：根据D段中Peter Hicks的原话，大量研究表明，年长员工之所以获得更高薪酬，是因为他们具备更高的价值。这与题目中\"regardless of the contribution of they make\"（与他们所做的贡献无关）的说法相反。因此，题目中的陈述与文章信息不符，答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64019","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true, NO if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8845:64020:5-6","type":"choice","text":"According to the passage, there are several advantages to hire elder people, please choose TWO from below:","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：  But other skills may increase with age, including many that are crucial for good management, such as an ability to handle people diplomatically, to run a meeting or to spot a problem before it blows up.\n对应段落：  D段\n审题：题目问根据文章内容，雇佣年长员工有哪些优势，需要选择两项。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"advantages to hire elder people\"（雇佣年长员工的优势），在文章中寻找关于年长员工优点的描述。\n解题思路：  D段中提到，随着员工年龄的增长，某些技能可能会随之提高，包括许多对良好管理至关重要的技能，比如善于与人打交道、主持会议或在问题出现前发现问题的能力。这与题目中的D项（他们拥有更好的人际关系）和E项（他们能提前发现问题）相符，其他选项A、B、C在文章中均未提及或与原文表述不符，因此正确答案是DE。","options":["Their productivity is more superior than the young.","They are paid less compared with younger ones.","They run fast when there is a meeting.","They have a better inter-person relationship.","They identify problems in an advanced time."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64020","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 5-6\nChoose the correct answer.","groupId":"64020-8845:64020:5-6"},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8845:64020:5-6","type":"choice","text":"According to the passage, there are several advantages to hire elder people, please choose TWO from below:","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：  But other skills may increase with age, including many that are crucial for good management, such as an ability to handle people diplomatically, to run a meeting or to spot a problem before it blows up.\n对应段落：  D段\n审题：题目问根据文章内容，雇佣年长员工有哪些优势，需要选择两项。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"advantages to hire elder people\"（雇佣年长员工的优势），在文章中寻找关于年长员工优点的描述。\n解题思路：  D段中提到，随着员工年龄的增长，某些技能可能会随之提高，包括许多对良好管理至关重要的技能，比如善于与人打交道、主持会议或在问题出现前发现问题的能力。这与题目中的D项（他们拥有更好的人际关系）和E项（他们能提前发现问题）相符，其他选项A、B、C在文章中均未提及或与原文表述不符，因此正确答案是DE。","options":["Their productivity is more superior than the young.","They are paid less compared with younger ones.","They run fast when there is a meeting.","They have a better inter-person relationship.","They identify problems in an advanced time."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64020","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 5-6\nChoose the correct answer.","groupId":"64020-8845:64020:5-6"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8845:64021:7-8","type":"choice","text":"According to Mr Peterson, Compared with the elder employee, young graduates have several\nweaknesses in the workplace, please choose TWO of them below:","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘The few companies that have kept on older workers find they have good judgment and their productivity is good,’ says Mr Peterson, ‘Besides, their education standards are much better than those of today’s young high-school graduates.’ Companies may say that older workers are not worth training, because they are reaching the end of their working lives: in fact, young people tend to switch jobs so frequently that offer the worst returns on training. ‘he median age for employer-driven training is the late 40s and early 50s,’ says Mr Hicks, ‘It goes mainly to managers.’\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是根据Peterson的观点，与年长员工相比，年轻毕业生在职场中有哪两个缺点。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“Mr Peterson”和“young graduates”定位到E段中Peterson的引述部分。\n解题思路：  E段中提到，彼得森先生表示，“少数坚持保留资深员工的企业发现，这些员工不仅判断力强，工作效率也高，而且他们的教育水平远超当今高中毕业生。”这点对应选项D（他们的学术教育水平在某种程度上落后于年长员工），接着又说，事实上，年轻人频繁跳槽，使得培训投资回报率极低。这说明年轻人换工作频繁，对应选项C。其他选项A、B、E在原文中未被Peterson直接提及或与题目要求不符。因此正确答案为CD。","options":["They are not worth training.","Their productivity is lower than counterparts.","They change work more often.","Their academic criteria is someway behind elders’.","They are normally high school graduates."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64021","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Question 7-8\nChoose the correct answer.","groupId":"64021-8845:64021:7-8"},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8845:64021:7-8","type":"choice","text":"According to Mr Peterson, Compared with the elder employee, young graduates have several\nweaknesses in the workplace, please choose TWO of them below:","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘The few companies that have kept on older workers find they have good judgment and their productivity is good,’ says Mr Peterson, ‘Besides, their education standards are much better than those of today’s young high-school graduates.’ Companies may say that older workers are not worth training, because they are reaching the end of their working lives: in fact, young people tend to switch jobs so frequently that offer the worst returns on training. ‘he median age for employer-driven training is the late 40s and early 50s,’ says Mr Hicks, ‘It goes mainly to managers.’\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是根据Peterson的观点，与年长员工相比，年轻毕业生在职场中有哪两个缺点。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“Mr Peterson”和“young graduates”定位到E段中Peterson的引述部分。\n解题思路：  E段中提到，彼得森先生表示，“少数坚持保留资深员工的企业发现，这些员工不仅判断力强，工作效率也高，而且他们的教育水平远超当今高中毕业生。”这点对应选项D（他们的学术教育水平在某种程度上落后于年长员工），接着又说，事实上，年轻人频繁跳槽，使得培训投资回报率极低。这说明年轻人换工作频繁，对应选项C。其他选项A、B、E在原文中未被Peterson直接提及或与题目要求不符。因此正确答案为CD。","options":["They are not worth training.","Their productivity is lower than counterparts.","They change work more often.","Their academic criteria is someway behind elders’.","They are normally high school graduates."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"64021","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Question 7-8\nChoose the correct answer.","groupId":"64021-8845:64021:7-8"},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8845:64022:9","type":"choice","text":"According to paragraph F, the firms and workers still hold the opinion that:","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But most companies (and many workers) are uncomfortable with the idea of reducing someone’s pay in later life – although workers on piece-rates often earn less over time.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问根据F段，公司和员工仍然持有怎样的观点。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"paragraph F\"和\"the firms and workers\"，直接定位到F段寻找涉及公司和员工观点的句子。\n解题思路：F段提到\"most companies (and many workers) are uncomfortable with the idea of reducing someone’s pay in later life\"，说明公司和员工都不愿意接受在退休年龄降低工资的做法。选项B\"people are not happy if pay gets lower in retiring age\"，人们不愿在退休年龄降薪，与原文意思完全一致，因此B是正确答案。其他选项A、C、D的内容在F段中均未提及。","options":["older workers are more likely to attract other staff.","people are not happy if pay gets lower in retiring age.","older people have more retaining motivation than young people.","young people often earn less for their piece-rates salary."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64022","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8845:64023:10","type":"choice","text":"Skill Team that has been founded by IBM conducted which of the following movement:","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Faced with the need to cut staff costs, and have decided to concentrate cuts on 55-60-year-olds, IBM set up a separate company called Skill Team, which re-employed any of the early retired who wanted to go on working up to the age of 60. An employee who joined Skill Team at the age of 55 on a five-year contract would work for 58% of his time, over the full period, for 88% of his last IBM salary.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是IBM创立的Skill Team进行了以下哪项活动。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Skill Team\"和\"IBM\"定位到G段，找到关于Skill Team的描述。\n解题思路：原文提到Skill Team重新雇佣了提前退休的员工，并让他们以较低的薪资继续工作（58%的原工作时间和88%的原薪资），这与选项D“重新雇佣年老员工，并保持稍低的薪资”相符。其他选项与原文描述不符。","options":["Ask all the old worker to continue their job on former working hours basis","Carry on the action of cutting off the elder’s proportion of employment","Ask employees to work more hours in order to get extra pay","Re-hire old employees and kept the salary a bit lower"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64023","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8845:64024:11","type":"choice","text":"Which of the followings is correct according to the research of Mr Quinn:","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In general, it is the best-paid and worst-paid who carry on working: ‘There are’, he says, ‘two very different types of bridge jog-holders – those who continue working because they have to and those who continue working because they want to, even though they could afford to retire.’\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问根据Quinn的研究，以下哪项是正确的。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"Mr Quinn\"定位到H段，该段提到了Quinn的研究内容。\n解题思路：H段提到Quinn的研究发现，在一般情况下，继续工作的人分为两种：\"一类是迫于生计不得不继续工作的人\"和\"即便经济条件允许退休，仍坚持工作以保持生活品质的人\"。这对应了选项D的描述\"一些老年人继续工作的动机并非源于经济利益，而是出于个人追求\"。选项A、B、C与原文内容不符。因此，正确答案是D。","options":["About 50% of all employees in America switched into ‘bridge’ jobs.","Only the worst-paid continue to work.","More men than women fell into the category of ‘bridge’ work.","Some old people keep working for their motive rather than an economic incentive."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64024","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8845:64025:12","type":"choice","text":"Which of the followings is correct according to David Storey:","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Often, they will be self-employed. Sometimes, they may start their own businesses: a study by David Storey of Warwick University found that, in Britain, 70% of businesses started by people over 55 survived, compared with an average of only 19%.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问根据David Storey的说法，哪个选项是正确的。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的“David Storey”定位到I段，找到他的研究内容。\n解题思路：原文提到David Storey的研究发现，英国55岁以上的人创办的企业中有70%存活下来，而较年轻的企业家创业平均存活率仅为19%。这说明老年自雇人士创办的企业存活率更高。选项C“老年自雇人士的企业更有可能存活”与原文意思一致，因此选C。其他选项要么与原文无关，要么与原文信息不符。","options":["70% business is successful if hire more older people.","Average success of a self-employed business is getting lower.","Self-employed elder people are more likely to survive.","Older people’s working hours are more flexible."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64025","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8845:64026:13","type":"choice","text":"What is the main purpose of the author in writing this passage?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：原文中没有明确的句子直接回答这个问题。\n对应段落：全文\n审题：题目问的是作者写这篇文章的主要目的是什么。\n定位关键信息：需要理解全文的主旨。\n解题思路：文章主要讨论了年长员工在就业市场中的地位和待遇，强调了年长员工的价值和技能，以及他们在工作中的优势。作者通过多个例子和观点，说明了年长员工不应被低估。因此，作者写这篇文章的主要目的是呼吁公司应正确衡量年长员工的价值。这与B选项的内容一致。其他选项要么过于具体（A和C），要么与文章内容不符（D）。","options":["there must be a successful retiring program for the old","order people should be correctly valued in employment","old people should offer more helping young employees grow.","There are more jobs in the world that only employ older people"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64026","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nChoose the correct answer."}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"64020-8845:64020:5-6","numbers":[5,6],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["D","E"]},{"id":"64021-8845:64021:7-8","numbers":[7,8],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["C","D"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64016","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true, NO if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Insurance company Sun Life of Canada made the decision that it would hire more Canadian\nemployees rather than British ones in order to get fresh staffs</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"64017","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true, NO if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Unlike other places, employees in Japan get paid according to the years they are employed.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"64018","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true, NO if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Elder workers are laid off by some German companies which are refreshing corporate culture.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"64019","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true, NO if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>According to Peter Hicks, companies pay older people more regardless of the contribution of they make.</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"64020","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 5-6\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>According to the passage, there are several advantages to hire elder people, please choose TWO from below:</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"64021","title":"选择题","instruction":"Question 7-8\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>According to Mr Peterson, Compared with the elder employee, young graduates have several\nweaknesses in the workplace, please choose TWO of them below:</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"64022","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>According to paragraph F, the firms and workers still hold the opinion that:</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"64023","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>Skill Team that has been founded by IBM conducted which of the following movement:</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"64024","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>Which of the followings is correct according to the research of Mr Quinn:</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"64025","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>Which of the followings is correct according to David Storey:</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"64026","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>What is the main purpose of the author in writing this passage?</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Grey Workers</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Given the speed at which their workers are growing greyer, employers know surprisingly little about how productive they are. The general assumption is that the old are paid more in spite of, rather than because of, their extra productivity. That might partly explain why, when employers are under pressure to cut costs, they persuade the 55-year-olds to take early retirement. Earlier this year, Sun Life of Canada, an insurance company, announced that it was offering redundancy to all its British employees aged 50 or over ‘to bring in new blood’.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In Japan, says Mariko Fujiwara, an industrial anthropologist who runs a think-tank for Hakuhodo, Japan’s second-largest advertising agency, most companies are bringing down the retirement age from the traditional 57 to 50 or thereabouts – and in some cases, such as Nissan, to 45. More than perhaps anywhere else, pay in Japan is linked to seniority. Given that the percentage of workers who have spent more than 32 years with the same employer rose from 11% in 1980 to 42% by 1994, it is hardly surprising that seniority-based wage costs have become the most intractable item on corporate profit-and-loss accounts.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In Germany, Patrick Pohl, spokesman for Hoechst, expresses a widely held view: ‘The company is trying to lower the average age of the workforce. Perhaps the main reason for replacing older workers is that it makes it easier to ‘defrost’ the corporate culture. Older workers are less willing to try a new way of thinking. Younger workers are cheaper and more flexible.’ Some German firms are hampered from getting rid of older workers as quickly as they would like. At SGL Carbon, a graphite producer, the average age of workers has been going up not down. The reason, says the company’s Ivo Lingnau, is not that SGL values older workers more. It is collective bargaining: the union agreement puts strict limits on the proportion of workers that may retire early.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Clearly, when older people do heavy physical work, their age may affect their productivity. But other skills may increase with age, including many that are crucial for good management, such as an ability to handle people diplomatically, to run a meeting or to spot a problem before it blows up. Peter Hicks, who co-ordinates OECD work on the policy implications of ageing, says that plenty of research suggests older people are paid more because they are worth more.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>And the virtues of the young may be exaggerated. ‘The few companies that have kept on older workers find they have good judgment and their productivity is good,’ says Mr Peterson, ‘Besides, their education standards are much better than those of today’s young high-school graduates.’ Companies may say that older workers are not worth training, because they are reaching the end of their working lives: in fact, young people tend to switch jobs so frequently that offer the worst returns on training. ‘he median age for employer-driven training is the late 40s and early 50s,’ says Mr Hicks, ‘It goes mainly to managers.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Take away those seniority-based pay scales, and older workers may become a much more attractive employment proposition. But most companies (and many workers) are uncomfortable with the idea of reducing someone’s pay in later life – although workers on piece-fates often earn less over time. So retaining the services of older workers may mean employing them in new ways.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>One innovation, described in Mr Walker’s report on combating age barriers, was devised by IBM Belgium. Faced with the need to cut staff costs, and have decided to concentrate cuts on 55-60-year-olds, IBM set up a separate company called Skill Team, which re-employed any of the early retired who wanted to go on working up to the age of 60. An employee who joined Skill Team at the age of 55 on a five-year contract would work for 58% of his time, over the full period, for 88% of his last IBM salary. The company offered services to IBM, thus allowing it to retain access to some of the intellectual capital it would otherwise have lost.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The best way to tempt the old to go on working may be to build on such ‘bridge’ jobs: part-time or temporary employment that creates a more gradual transition from full-time work to retirement. Mr Quinn, who has studied the phenomenon, finds that, in the United States, nearly half of all men and women who had been in full-time jobs in middle age moved into such ‘bridge’ jobs at the end of their working lives. In general, it is the best-paid and worst-paid who carry on working: ‘There are’, he says, ‘two very different types of bridge jog-holders – those who continue working because they have to and those who continue working because they want to, even though they could afford to retire.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>If the job market grows more flexible, the old may find more jobs that suit them. Often, they will be self-employed. Sometimes, they may start their own businesses: a study by David Storey of Warwick University found that, in Britain, 70% of businesses started by people over 55 survived, compared with an average of only 19%. To coax the old back into the job market, work will not only have to pay. It will need to be more fun than touring the country in an Airstream trailer, or seeing the grandchildren, or playing golf. Only then will there be many more Joe Clarks.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8845&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8846","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Computer Provides More Questions Than Answers","book":"阅读还原集Vol.16","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.16 · Test 3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8846:64027:14","type":"choice","text":"14 The content inside the wrecked ship","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Inside the hull were a number of bronze and marble statues.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问哪个段落包含了关于沉船内部内容的信息。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"the content inside the wrecked ship\"（沉船内部的内容）定位到B段首句，该句明确描述了船舱内部的情况。\n解题思路：B段首句直接说明，船体内部陈列着多尊青铜与大理石雕像。这正是题目所问的沉船内部的内容。因此B段是唯一包含相关信息的段落。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64027","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has 10 paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8846:64027:15","type":"choice","text":"15 Ancient astronomers and craftsman might involve","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Building it would have been expensive and required the interaction of astronomer, engineers, intellectuals, and craftspeople.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问哪个段落提到了古代天文学家和工匠可能参与其中。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"ancient astronomers\"和\"craftsman\"定位到H段，该段明确提到了\"astronomers\"和\"craftspeople\"（工匠）。\n解题思路：H段提到，建造这种装置成本高昂，需要天文学家、工程师、知识分子和工匠的通力合作。说明制作该装置时天文学家和工匠参与其中。这与题目对应。因此，H段是正确答案。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64027","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has 10 paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8846:64027:16","type":"choice","text":"16 The location of the Antikythera Mechanism","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：That piece of ‘junk’ went on to become the most celebrated find from the shipwreck; it is displayed at the National Archaeological Museum of Athens.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问哪一段提到了“安提凯希拉机械装置的所在地”。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的核心词\"Antikythera Mechanism\"（安提凯希拉机械装置）和\"location\"（位置）进行定位。在文章中搜索与该装置存放地点相关的句子。\n解题思路：C段明确提到“那件‘垃圾’最终成为沉船中最著名的发现；它目前陈列在雅典的国家考古博物馆”。原文中的\"it is displayed at the National Archaeological Museum of Athens\"直接回答了装置的所在地，因此答案为C段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64027","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has 10 paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8846:64027:17","type":"choice","text":"17 Details of how it was found","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The ship that sank there was a giant cargo vessel measuring nearly 500 feet long. It came to rest about 200 feet below the surface, where it stayed for more than 2,000 years until divers looking for sponges discovered the wreck a little more than a century ago.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了发现它的细节。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"how it was found\"，通过这个关键词可以在文章中定位到A段，该段描述了沉船的发现过程。\n解题思路：A段中明确提到了沉船的发现过程，这艘沉没的巨型货轮长达近150米，最终在海面下200英尺处搁浅，沉睡了两千多年。直到一个多世纪前，潜水员在搜寻海绵时意外发现了这艘沉船。这与题目对应。因此，A段包含了该信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64027","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has 10 paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8846:64027:18","type":"choice","text":"18 Appearance and structure of the mechanism","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：By turning the gear mechanism, which included what Edmunds called a beautiful system of epicyclic gears that factored in the elliptical orbit of the moon, a person could check what the sky would have looked like on a date in the past, or how it would appear in the future. The mechanism was encased in a box with doors in front and back covered with inscriptions – a sort of instruction manual. Inside the front door were pointers indicating the date and the position of the sun, moon and zodiac, while opening the back door revealed the relationship between calendar years and lunar months, and a mechanism to predict eclipses.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“机制的外观和结构”这一信息出现在哪一段落。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词“Appearance and structure of the mechanism”，可以在文章中找到描述机制外观和结构的句子。\n解题思路：在G段中，原文明确描述了机制的外观和结构，包括齿轮系统、盒子、门、指针等细节，这些都是关于机制外观和结构的描述，因此G段包含了题目所要求的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"64027","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has 10 paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8846:64028:19","type":"fill","text":"填写第 19 空","answer":"cargo vessel/Cargo Vessel","acceptedAnswers":["cargo vessel","Cargo Vessel"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The ship that sank there was a giant cargo vessel measuring nearly 500 feet long.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求填空，描述一个古代巨大的沉没船只的名称，该船潜水员在搜寻海绵时意外发现的。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"ancient huge sunk\"和\"found accidentally by sponges searcher\"，通过这些关键词可以在A段找到对应的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到沉没的船是\"a giant cargo vessel\"一艘巨大的货轮，这与题目中的\"ancient huge\"相对应，因此答案为\"cargo vessel\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64028","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nComplete the summary below. Use NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 19-22 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8846:64029:20","type":"fill","text":"填写第 20 空","answer":"luxury items/Luxury Items","acceptedAnswers":["luxury items","Luxury Items"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Inside the hull were a number of bronze and marble statues. From the look of things, the ship seemed to be carrying luxury items, probably made in various Greek islands and bound for wealthy patrons in the growing Roman Empire.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问这艘船装载了什么样物品，如青铜与大理石雕像。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"loaded with\"和\"bronze and sculptures\"定位到B段，原文提到船上有青铜和雕塑等物品。\n解题思路：根据原文，从外观判断，这艘船似乎载着奢侈品，可以确定答案为\"luxury items\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64029","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nComplete the summary below. Use NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 19-22 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8846:64030:21","type":"fill","text":"填写第 21 空","answer":"gearwheel/Gearwheel","acceptedAnswers":["gearwheel","Gearwheel"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Nine months later, an enterprising archaeologist cleared off a layer of organic material from one of the pieces of junk and found that it looked like a gearwheel. It had inscriptions in Greek characters and seemed to have something to do with astronomy.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是考古学家发现了一件与什么相似的残片，并且上面有希腊文字。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"junk\"、\"Greek script\"等关键词，可以定位到B段中描述考古学家发现残片的句子。\n解题思路：在B段中提到，九个月后，一位富有开拓精神的考古学家清理了一块残骸上的有机沉积层，发现其形状酷似齿轮。残片上刻有希腊文字铭文，内容似乎与天文学相关。说明残片形状酷似齿轮，因此，答案就是gearwheel。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64030","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nComplete the summary below. Use NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 19-22 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8846:64031:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"analogue computer/Analogue Computer","acceptedAnswers":["analogue computer","Analogue Computer"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Research has shown that the wheel was part of a device so sophisticated that its complexity would not be matched for a thousand years – it was also the world’s first known analogue computer.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问这款设计精巧且令人兴奋的装置是世界上第一个什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"first\"和\"world\"定位到C段末句，找到\"world’s first known analogue computer\"。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，研究表明，这个轮子属于一个精密装置——其复杂程度在千年间无人能及，更是全球已知最早的模拟计算机。该设备是\"world’s first known analogue computer\"，因此答案为\"analog computer\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64031","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nComplete the summary below. Use NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 19-22 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8846:64032:23","type":"choice","text":"23 More complicated than the previous device","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：'We have gear trains from the 9th century in Baghdad used for simpler displays of the solar and lunar motions relative to one another – they use eight gears,’ said François Charette, a historian of science in Germany who wrote an editorial accompanying a new study of the mechanism two weeks ago in the journal Nature, ‘In this case, we have more than 30 gears. To see it on a computer animation makes it mind-boggling. There is no doubt it was a technological masterpiece.’\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是谁认为这个设备比之前的设备更复杂。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"More complicated than the previous device\"可以定位到E段中François Charette的言论，他提到了之前巴格达的齿轮装置只有8个齿轮，而安提基特拉机械有超过30个齿轮，说明其更复杂。\n解题思路：原文中François Charette明确比较了安提基特拉机械与9世纪巴格达的齿轮装置，指出前者使用更多齿轮且更为复杂，这与题目描述完全一致，因此答案为C。","options":["Yanis Bitsakis","Mike Edmunds","François Charette"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"64032","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 23-26\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Yanis Bitsakis\nB Mike Edmunds\nC François Charette"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8846:64032:24","type":"choice","text":"24 Anticipate finding more Antikythera Mechanism in the future","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Its sophistication ‘is such that it can’t have been the only one,’ Edmunds said, ‘There must have been a tradition of making them. We’re always hopeful a better one will surface.’\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问是谁“期待未来会发现更多的安提基特拉机械”。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"anticipate\", \"finding more\", \"Antikythera Mechanism\", \"in the future\" 定位到文中表达对发现更多类似装置抱有希望的句子。\n解题思路：J段中，埃德蒙兹提到，它精妙程度表明它不可能是孤例，一定曾经有制作这种装置的习惯。我们始终希望能发现保存得更完整的一件。因此，持有此观点的人是Mike Edmunds，对应选项B。","options":["Yanis Bitsakis","Mike Edmunds","François Charette"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"64032","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 23-26\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Yanis Bitsakis\nB Mike Edmunds\nC François Charette"},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8846:64032:25","type":"choice","text":"25 Antikythera Mechanism was found related to the moon.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The mechanism explores the relationship between lunar months – the time it takes for the moon to cycle through its phases, say, full moon to the full moon – and calendar years.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“安提基特拉机械与月亮有关”这一观点或事实是由谁发现的。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"Antikythera Mechanism\"和\"moon\"作为关键词，在文章中快速定位到F段，找到直接描述该装置用途的句子。\n解题思路：段落F中，原文明确指出，“该装置探索了农历月（月亮完成其相位周期所需的时间，例如从满月到满月）与历年之间的关系”。这句话直接、清晰地阐述了该装置与月球（lunar months）的核心关联。因此答案为B，Mike Edmunds。","options":["Yanis Bitsakis","Mike Edmunds","François Charette"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"64032","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 23-26\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Yanis Bitsakis\nB Mike Edmunds\nC François Charette"},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8846:64032:26","type":"choice","text":"26 Mechanism assisted ancient people to calculate the movement of stars.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：“If they needed to know when eclipses would occur, and this related to the rising and setting of stars and related them to dates and religious experiences, the mechanism would directly help,” said Yanis Bitsakis, a physicist at the University of Athens who co-wrote the Nature paper.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是“这种机械帮助古人计算星辰的运行轨迹”，这一观点或行为与列表中对应的人物匹配。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键信息是“calculate the movement of stars”（计算星辰的运行）。在文中，与此对应的概念是日月食的发生与“the rising and setting of stars”（星辰的升起和落下）直接相关。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，雅典大学物理学家亚尼斯·比察基斯表示，如果古人需要知道日食月食发生时间，并将这些天文现象与日期和宗教仪式联系起来，这种机械装置就能直接提供帮助。他的陈述直接建立了机械功能与计算星辰位置之间的联系，明确对应了题目的论述。因此，提出该观点的人是Yanis Bitsakis，对应选项A。","options":["Yanis Bitsakis","Mike Edmunds","François Charette"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"64032","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 23-26\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Yanis Bitsakis\nB Mike Edmunds\nC François Charette"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64027","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has 10 paragraphs A-J. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-J, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>14</strong> The content inside the wrecked ship <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"64028","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nComplete the summary below. Use NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 19-22 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>An ancient huge sunk <strong>19</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong> was found accidentally by sponges searcher.</p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"64029","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nComplete the summary below. Use NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 19-22 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The ship\nloaded with <strong>20</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong> such as bronze and sculptures.</p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"64030","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nComplete the summary below. Use NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 19-22 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>However, an archaeologist found a\njunk similar to a <strong>21</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong> which has Greek script on it.</p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"64031","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nComplete the summary below. Use NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 19-22 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>This inspiring and elaborated device\nwas found to be the first <strong>22</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong> in the world.</p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"64032","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 23-26\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Yanis Bitsakis\nB Mike Edmunds\nC François Charette","html":"<p><strong>23</strong> More complicated than the previous device <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":23}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Computer Provides More Questions Than Answers</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The island of Antikythera lies 18 miles north of Crete, where the Aegean Sea meets the Mediterranean. Currents there can make shipping treacherous – and one ship bound for ancient Rome never made it. The ship that sank there was a giant cargo vessel measuring nearly 500 feet long. It came to rest about 200 feet below the surface, where it stayed for more than 2,000 years until divers looking for sponges discovered the wreck a little more than a century ago.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Inside the hull were a number of bronze and marble statues. From the look of things, the ship seemed to be carrying luxury items, probably made in various Greek islands and bound for wealthy patrons in the growing Roman Empire. The statues were retrieved, along with a lot of other unimportant stuff, and stored. Nine months later, an enterprising archaeologist cleared off a layer of organic material from one of the pieces of junk and found that it looked like a gearwheel. It had inscriptions in Greek characters and seemed to have something to do with astronomy.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>That piece of ‘junk’ went on to become the most celebrated find from the shipwreck; it is displayed at the National Archaeological Museum of Athens. Research has shown that the wheel was part of a device so sophisticated that its complexity would not be matched for a thousand years – it was also the world&#39;s first known analogue computer. The device is so famous that an international conference organized in Athens a couple of weeks ago had only one subject: the Antikythera Mechanism.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Every discovery about the device has raised new questions. Who built the device, and for what purpose? Why did the technology behind it disappear for the next thousand years? What does the device tell us about ancient Greek culture? And does the marvelous construction, and the precise knowledge of the movement of the sun and moon and Earth that it implies, tell us how the ancients grappled with ideas about determinism and human destiny?</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘We have gear trains from the 9th century in Baghdad used for simpler displays of the solar and lunar motions relative to one another – they use eight gears,’ said François Charette, a historian of science in Germany who wrote an editorial accompanying a new study of the mechanism two weeks ago in the journal Nature, ‘In this case, we have more than 30 gears. To see it on a computer animation makes it mind-boggling. There is no doubt it was a technological masterpiece.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The device was probably built between 100 and 140 BC, and the understanding of astronomy it displays seems to have been based on knowledge developed by the Babylonians around 300-700 BC, said Mike Edmunds, a professor of astrophysics at Cardiff University in Britain. He led a research team that reconstructed what the gear mechanism would have looked like by using advanced three-dimensional-imaging technology. The group also decoded a number of the inscriptions. The mechanism explores the relationship between lunar months – the time it takes for the moon to cycle through its phases, say, full moon to the full moon – and calendar years. The gears had to be cut precisely to reflect this complex relationship; 19 calendar years equal 235 lunar months.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>By turning the gear mechanism, which included what Edmunds called a beautiful system of epicyclic gears that factored in the elliptical orbit of the moon, a person could check what the sky would have looked like on a date in the past, or how it would appear in the future. The mechanism was encased in a box with doors in front and back covered with inscriptions – a sort of instruction manual. Inside the front door were pointers indicating the date and the position of the sun, moon and zodiac, while opening the back door revealed the relationship between calendar years and lunar months, and a mechanism to predict eclipses.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>“If they needed to know when eclipses would occur, and this related to the rising and setting of stars and related them to dates and religious experiences, the mechanism would directly help,”&nbsp;said Yanis Bitsakis, a physicist at the University of Athens who co-wrote the Nature paper. “It is a mechanical &nbsp;computer. You turn the handle and you have a date on the front.”&nbsp;Building it would have been expensive and required the interaction of astronomer, engineers, intellectuals, and craftspeople. Charette said the device overturned conventional ideas that the ancient Greeks were primarily ivory tower thinkers who did not deign to muddy their hands with technical stuff. It is a reminder, he said, that while the study of history often focuses on written texts, they can tell us only a fraction of what went on at a particular time.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Imagine a future historian encountering philosophy texts written in our time – and an aircraft engine. The books would tell that researcher what a few scholars were thinking today, but the engine would give them a far better window into how technology influenced our everyday lives. Charette said it was unlikely that the device was used by practitioners of astrology, then still in its infancy. More likely, he said, it was bound for a mantelpiece in some rich Roman’s home. Given that astronomers of the time already knew how to calculate the positions of the sun and the moon and to predict eclipses without the device, it would have been the equivalent of a device built for a planetarium today – something to spur popular interest or at least claim bragging rights.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Why was the technology that went into the device lost? “The time this was built, the jackboot of Rome was coming through,” Edmunds said. “The Romans were good at town planning and sanitation but were not known for their interest in science.” The fact that the device was so complex, and that it was being shipped with a number of other luxury items, tells Edmunds that it is very unlikely to have been the one ever made. “Its sophistication is such that it can’t have been the only one,” Edmunds said. “There must have been a tradition of making them. We’re always hopeful a better one will surface.” Indeed, he said, he hopes that his study and the renewed interest in the Antikythera Mechanism will prompt second looks by both amateurs and professionals around the world. “The archaeological world may look in their cupboards and maybe say, That isn’t a bit of rusty old metal in the cupboard.”</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8846&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8847","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Book Review On Musicophilia","book":"阅读还原集Vol.16","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.16 · Test 3 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8847:64033:27","type":"choice","text":"Why does the writer have a mixed feeling about the book?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：So I had high expectations of Musicophilia, the latest offering from neurologist and prolific author Oliver Sacks.  And I confess to feeling a little guilty reporting that my reactions to the book are mixed.\n对应段落：A段上方\n审题：题目问的是作者为什么对这本书有矛盾的感觉。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"mixed feeling\"可以定位到A段最后一句。\n解题思路：根据原文，当神经学家兼多产作家奥利弗·萨克斯推出新作《音乐狂想曲》时，作者满怀期待。不过作者承认自己有些内疚，因为他对这本书的评价好坏参半。这表明作者对这本书的期望很高，但实际阅读后的感受并不完全符合预期，因此产生了矛盾的感觉。这与选项B\"作者期望它比实际更好\"相符。","options":["The guilty feeling made him so.","The writer expected it to be better than it was.","Sacks failed to include his personal stories in the book.","This is the only book written by Sacks."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64033","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8847:64034:28","type":"choice","text":"What is the best part of the book?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A Sacks himself is the best part of Musicophilia. He richly documents his own life in the book and reveals highly personal experiences.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是这本书最好的部分是什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"best part of the book\"定位到A段第一句，原文明确指出\"the best part of Musicophilia\"是Sacks himself，并进一步解释他详细记录了自己的生活和个人经历。\n解题思路：根据原文，A段指出萨克斯本人堪称《音乐之恋》最精彩的部分。他在书中详尽记录了自己的人生经历，分享了许多极具个人色彩的体验。这与选项C\"the autobiographical description in the book\"本书中的自传式描述，完全一致。因此，正确答案是C。","options":["the photo of Sacks listening to music","the tone of voice of the book","the autobiographical description in the book","the description of Sacks’ wealth"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64034","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8847:64035:29","type":"choice","text":"In the preface, what did Sacks try to achieve?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In it, Sacks explains that he wants to convey the insights gleaned from the ‘enormous and rapidly growing body of work on the neural underpinnings of musical perception and imagery, and the complex and often bizarre disorders to which these are prone.’ He also stresses the importance of ‘the simple art of observation’ and ‘the richness of the human context.’ He wants to combine ‘observation and description with the latest in technology,’ he says, and to imaginatively enter into the experience of his patients and subjects.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问在引言部分Sacks试图传达什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"preface\"定位到B段，该段详细描述了Sacks在引言中阐述的目标。\n解题思路：原文明确提到Sacks希望通过这本书传达从大量研究工作中获得的见解，并强调结合观察与最新技术，同时结合患者和受试者的经历。这与选项A“对所应用的研究工作和技术的开创性介绍”完全一致，其他选项B、C、D均与原文描述不符。","options":["make a herald introduction of the research work and technique applied","give a detailed description of various musical disorders","explain how people understand music","explain why he needs to do away with the simple observation"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64035","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8847:64036:30","type":"choice","text":"What is disappointing about Tony Cicoria's case?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：There are now more sensitive tests, but Cicoria, has declined to undergo them; he does not want to delve into the causes of his musicality. What a shame!\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是关于Tony Cicoria的案例中令人失望的是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词Tony Cicoria可以定位到文章的C段，该段详细描述了他的案例。\n解题思路：在C段中，原文明确提到如今已有更精密的检测手段，但西科里亚却拒绝接受测试，不想探究自己突然产生音乐天赋的原因，真是可惜。这与选项A的描述完全一致，即他拒绝进行进一步的测试。因此，正确答案是A。","options":["He refuses to have further tests.","He can’t determine the cause of his sudden musicality.","He nearly died because of the lightening.","His brain waves were too normal to show anything."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64036","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8847:64037:31","type":"choice","text":"It is difficult to give a well-reputable writer a less than totally favorable review.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：So I had high expectations of Musicophilia, the latest offering from neurologist and prolific author Oliver Sacks. And I confess to feeling a little guilty reporting that my reactions to the book are mixed.\n对应段落：A段上方\n审题：题目问的是“要对一位享有盛誉的作家给出不完全正面的评价，实属不易”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“a less than totally favorable review”可以定位到A段中作者提到自己感觉有点内疚，因为对这本书的反应是混合的。\n解题思路：作者在A段上方提到，神经学家兼多产作家奥利弗·萨克斯推出新作《音乐狂想曲》时，他满怀期待。不过他承认自己有些内疚，因为他对这本书的评价好坏参半。自己对这本书的反应是混合的，并且感到有点内疚。这表明作者认为给一位有声望的作家一个不完全正面的评论是不易的，因此题目的陈述与作者的观点一致。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64037","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the views of the writer FALSE if the statement contradicts with the views of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8847:64038:32","type":"choice","text":"Beethoven's Pathetique Sonata is a good treatment for musical disorders.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The photograph of him on the cover of the book-which shows him wearing headphones, eyes closed, clearly enchanted as he listens to Alfred Brendel perform Beethoven’s Pathetique Sonata-makes a positive impression that is borne out by the contents of the book\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问“贝多芬的《悲怆奏鸣曲》是治疗音乐障碍的好方法”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“Beethoven’s Pathetique Sonata”和“treatment for musical disorders”。在文章中，可以通过“Beethoven’s Pathetique Sonata”定位到A段，但该段描述的是这本书的封面照片，并未提及治疗作用。\n解题思路：文章中A段提到贝多芬的《悲怆奏鸣曲》，但这至少对于这本书封面的描述，并未提及有任何治疗音乐障碍的作用。因此，无法确定贝多芬的《悲怆奏鸣曲》是否是治疗音乐障碍的好方法。所以答案为Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64038","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the views of the writer FALSE if the statement contradicts with the views of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8847:64039:33","type":"choice","text":"Sacks believes technological methods is of little importance compared with traditional observation when studying his patients.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The reader can see that Sacks, who has been practicing neurology for 40 years, is torn between the ‘old-fashioned’ path of observation and the new-fangled, high-tech approach: He knows that he needs to take heed of the latter, but his heart lies with the former.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问萨克斯认为，在研究患者时，相较于传统观察法，技术手段的重要性微乎其微，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"technological methods\"和\"traditional observation\"定位到B段。\n解题思路：原文提到，这位拥有四十年神经学从业经验的专家，展现出对传统观察法与现代高科技手段的矛盾心理：他深知后者的重要性，但内心始终惦记着前者。他只是更加倾向使用传统方法，并未表示技术方法不重要。题目说Sacks认为技术方法不重要，因此答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64039","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the views of the writer FALSE if the statement contradicts with the views of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8847:64040:34","type":"choice","text":"It is difficult to understand why music therapy is undervalued","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：To Sacks’s credit, part III, ‘Memory, Movement and Music’, brings us into the underappreciated realm of music therapy.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“难以理解音乐治疗为何不被重视”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的“music therapy is undervalued”可以定位到E段中的“underappreciated realm of music therapy”，即“被低估的音乐疗法领域”。\n解题思路：原文中提到了，萨克斯在第三部分《记忆、运动与音乐》中，带领我们走进了音乐治疗这个被低估的领域。但并没有解释为什么它会被低估，也没有表示对此的看法。因此，根据原文信息，无法确定作者是否认为理解音乐疗法被低估的原因很困难，所以答案是“Not Given”。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64040","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the views of the writer FALSE if the statement contradicts with the views of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8847:64041:35","type":"choice","text":"Sacks held little skepticism when borrowing other theories and findings in describing reasons and notion for phenomena he depicts in the book.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：And he tends to be rather uncritical in accepting scientific findings and theories.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是塞克斯在借用其他理论与发现来阐释书中现象的成因与概念时，几乎未表现出任何怀疑态度，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Sacks\"、\"theories\"、\"phenomena\"，可以定位到F段中的\"he tends to be rather uncritical in accepting scientific findings and theories\"，这句话表明Sacks对科学发现和理论时缺乏批判性。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，他对科学发现和理论的接受也往往缺乏批判性，因此，题目的陈述与作者的观点一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64041","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the views of the writer FALSE if the statement contradicts with the views of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8847:64042:36","type":"choice","text":"Sacks is in a rush to use new testing methods to do treatment for patients.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In fact, although he exhibits the greatest compassion for patients, he conveys no sense of urgency about the pursuit of new avenues in the diagnosis and treatment of music-brain disorders.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问Sacks急于使用新的测试方法来治疗病人,这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词“new testing methods”和“treatment for patients”可以定位到I段中关于Sacks对新方法的态度的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，尽管他对患者怀有最深切的同情，却未对探索音乐性脑病诊断与治疗新途径表现出紧迫感。这与题目中“急于使用新测试方法”的说法相反，因此题目说法与作者观点不符。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"64042","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the views of the writer FALSE if the statement contradicts with the views of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8847:64043:37","type":"choice","text":"37 The content covered dissociations in understanding between harmony and melody","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For example, he might have noted that the many specific dissociations among components of music comprehension, such as loss of the ability to perceive harmony but not melody, indicate that there is no music center in the brain.\n对应段落：G段\n审题： 题目要求将“对和声与旋律理解分离现象的研究内容”与正确的结尾句匹配。\n定位关键信息：根据“dissociations in understanding between harmony and melody”可定位至D段和G段。D段描述了这一现象，G段则阐述了其深层含义。\n解题思路：原文G段提到，他本可指出：音乐理解过程中出现的诸多特定功能分离现象——比如丧失感知和声能力却保留旋律感知——恰恰表明大脑中并不存在专门的音乐中枢。然而，许多读者却相信所有大脑功能都是局部定位的，这恰恰是一种普遍的误解。因此，选择F项表明大脑中存在一个功能中心是错误的。","options":["show no music-brain disorders.","indicates that medication can have varied results.","is key for the neurological community to unravel the mysteries.","should not be used in isolation.","indicate that not everyone can receive a good education.","show a misconception that there is a function centre localized in the brain"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"64043","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below. Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.\nA show no music-brain disorders.\nB indicates that medication can have varied results.\nC is key for the neurological community to unravel the mysteries.\nD should not be used in isolation.\nE indicate that not everyone can receive a good education.\nF show a misconception that there is a function centre localized in the brain"},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8847:64043:38","type":"choice","text":"38 The study of treating musical disorders","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Another conclusion one could draw is that there seem to be no ‘cures’ for neurological problems involving music. A drug can alleviate a symptom in one patient and aggravate it in another or can have both positive and negative effects in the same patient.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：  题目要求将“对音乐障碍治疗的研究”与正确的结尾句匹配。\n定位关键信息：根据“treating musical disorders”定位至H段，该段集中讨论音乐神经问题的治疗。\n解题思路：原文H段的核心内容是讨论针对音乐相关神经问题的治疗现状。该段明确指出，药物治疗的效果存在很大不确定性：一种药物可能对一位患者有效，却会加重另一位患者的症状；甚至对同一位患者可能同时产生正面和负面影响。这直接说明药物治疗会产生不同的结果，与选项B的描述完全一致。","options":["show no music-brain disorders.","indicates that medication can have varied results.","is key for the neurological community to unravel the mysteries.","should not be used in isolation.","indicate that not everyone can receive a good education.","show a misconception that there is a function centre localized in the brain"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"64043","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below. Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.\nA show no music-brain disorders.\nB indicates that medication can have varied results.\nC is key for the neurological community to unravel the mysteries.\nD should not be used in isolation.\nE indicate that not everyone can receive a good education.\nF show a misconception that there is a function centre localized in the brain"},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8847:64043:39","type":"choice","text":"39 The EEG scans of Sacks' patients","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Finally, in many of the cases described here the patient with music-brain symptoms is reported to have ‘normal’ EEG results.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：  题目要求将“Sacks病人的脑电图扫描结果”与正确的结尾句匹配。\n定位关键信息：根据“EEG scans of Sacks' patients”定位至I段开头。\n解题思路：原文I段首句明确指出，在书中描述的许多病例中，表现出音乐-大脑症状的病人的脑电图均“正常”。这意味着这些扫描结果并未显示出与症状对应的音乐-大脑障碍（music-brain disorders）。这与选项A的描述完全吻合。","options":["show no music-brain disorders.","indicates that medication can have varied results.","is key for the neurological community to unravel the mysteries.","should not be used in isolation.","indicate that not everyone can receive a good education.","show a misconception that there is a function centre localized in the brain"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"64043","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below. Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.\nA show no music-brain disorders.\nB indicates that medication can have varied results.\nC is key for the neurological community to unravel the mysteries.\nD should not be used in isolation.\nE indicate that not everyone can receive a good education.\nF show a misconception that there is a function centre localized in the brain"},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8847:64043:40","type":"choice","text":"40 Sacks believes testing based on new technologies","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This absence echoes the book’s preface, in which Sacks expresses fear that ‘the simple art of observation may be lost’ if we rely too much on new technologies. He does call for both approaches, though, and we can only hope that the neurological community will respond.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：  题目要求将\"Sacks对基于新技术的测试的看法\"与正确的结尾句匹配。\n定位关键信息：根据\"testing based on new technologies\"和\"Sacks believes\"定位至I段中后部分。\n解题思路：原文完整地显示了Sacks的立场：他虽然承认新技术的存在，但并不主张单独使用这些技术。关键句\"He does call for both approaches\"明确表明他呼吁两种方法（传统观察法与新科技）结合使用。这说明Sacks认为基于新技术的测试不应该被孤立使用，而应与传统方法相结合。这与选项D的描述完全吻合。","options":["show no music-brain disorders.","indicates that medication can have varied results.","is key for the neurological community to unravel the mysteries.","should not be used in isolation.","indicate that not everyone can receive a good education.","show a misconception that there is a function centre localized in the brain"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"64043","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below. Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.\nA show no music-brain disorders.\nB indicates that medication can have varied results.\nC is key for the neurological community to unravel the mysteries.\nD should not be used in isolation.\nE indicate that not everyone can receive a good education.\nF show a misconception that there is a function centre localized in the brain"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64033","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Why does the writer have a mixed feeling about the book?</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"64034","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is the best part of the book?</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"64035","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>In the preface, what did Sacks try to achieve?</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"64036","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is disappointing about Tony Cicoria&#39;s case?</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"64037","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the views of the writer FALSE if the statement contradicts with the views of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p><strong>It is difficult to give a well-reputable writer a less than totally favorable review.</strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"64038","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the views of the writer FALSE if the statement contradicts with the views of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p><strong>Beethoven&#39;s Pathetique Sonata is a good treatment for musical disorders.</strong></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"64039","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the views of the writer FALSE if the statement contradicts with the views of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p><strong>Sacks believes technological methods is of little importance compared with traditional observation when studying his patients.</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"64040","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the views of the writer FALSE if the statement contradicts with the views of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p><strong>It is difficult to understand why music therapy is undervalued</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"64041","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the views of the writer FALSE if the statement contradicts with the views of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p><strong>Sacks held little skepticism when borrowing other theories and findings in describing reasons and notion for phenomena he depicts in the book.</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"64042","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the views of the writer FALSE if the statement contradicts with the views of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p><strong>Sacks is in a rush to use new testing methods to do treatment for patients.</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"64043","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below. Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.\nA show no music-brain disorders.\nB indicates that medication can have varied results.\nC is key for the neurological community to unravel the mysteries.\nD should not be used in isolation.\nE indicate that not everyone can receive a good education.\nF show a misconception that there is a function centre localized in the brain","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> show no music-brain disorders. <br/></p><p><strong>B</strong> indicates that medication can have varied results. <br/></p><p><strong>C</strong> is key for the neurological community to unravel the mysteries. <br/></p><p><strong>D</strong> should not be used in isolation. <br/></p><p><strong>E</strong> indicate that not everyone can receive a good education. <br/></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>F</strong> show a misconception that there is a function centre localized in the brain <br/></p><p><strong>37</strong> The content covered dissociations in understanding between harmony and melody <strong class=\"source-blank\">[37] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":37}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Book Review On Musicophilia</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">Norman M. Weinberger reviews the latest work of Oliver Sacks on music.</p><p><br/></p><p>Music and the brain are both endlessly fascinating subjects, and as a neuroscientist specialising in auditory learning and memory, I find them especially intriguing. So I had high expectations of Musicophilia, the latest offering from neurologist and prolific author Oliver Sacks. And I confess to feeling a little guilty reporting that my reactions to the book are mixed.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Sacks himself is the best part of Musicophilia. He richly documents his own life in the book and reveals highly personal experiences. The photograph of him on the cover of the book-which shows him wearing headphones, eyes closed, clearly enchanted as he listens to Alfred Brendel perform Beethoven’s Pathetique Sonata-makes a positive impression that is borne out by the contents of the book. Sacks’ voice throughout is steady and erudite but never pontifical. He is neither self-conscious nor self-promoting.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The preface gives a good idea of what the book will deliver. In it, Sacks explains that he wants to convey the insights gleaned from the ‘enormous and rapidly growing body of work on the neural underpinnings of musical perception and imagery, and the complex and often bizarre disorders to which these are prone.’ He also stresses the importance of ‘the simple art of observation’ and ‘the richness of the human context.’ He wants to combine ‘observation and description with the latest in technology,’ he says, and to imaginatively enter into the experience of his patients and subjects. The reader can see that Sacks, who has been practicing neurology for 40 years, is torn between the ‘old-fashioned’ path of observation and the new-fangled, high-tech approach: He knows that he needs to take heed of the latter, but his heart lies with the former.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The book consists mainly of detailed descriptions of cases, most of them involving patients whom Sacks has seen in his practice. Brief discussions of contemporary neuroscientific reports are sprinkled liberally throughout the text. Part, ‘Haunted by Music’, begins with the strange case of Tony Cicoria, a nonmusical, middle-aged surgeon who was consumed by a love of music after being hit by lightning. He suddenly began to crave listening to piano music, which he had never cared for in the past. He started to play the piano and then to compose music, which arose spontaneously in his mind in a ‘torrent’ of notes. How could this happen? Was the cause psychological? (He had had a near-death experience when the lightning struck him.) Or was it the direct result of a change in the auditory regions of his cerebral cortex? Electroencephalography (EEG) showed his brain waves to be normal in the mid-1990s, just after his trauma and subsequent ‘conversion’ to music. There are now more sensitive tests, but Cicoria, has declined to undergo them; he does not want to delve into the causes of his musicality. What a shame!</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Part II, ‘A Range of Musicality’, covers a wider variety of topics, but unfortunately, some of the chapters offer little or nothing that is new. For example, Chapter 13, which is five pages long, merely notes that the blind often has better hearing than the sighted. The most interesting chapters are those that present the strangest cases. Chapter 8 is about ‘amusia’, an inability to hear sounds like music, and ‘dysharmonia’, a highly specific impairment of the ability to hear harmony, with the ability to understand melody left intact. Such specific ‘dissociations’ are found throughout the cases Sacks recounts.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>To Sacks’s credit, part III, ‘Memory, Movement and Music’, brings us into the underappreciated realm of music therapy. Chapter 16 explains how ‘melodic intonation therapy’ is being used to help expressive aphasic patients (those unable to express their thoughts verbally following a stroke or other cerebral incident) once again become capable of fluent speech. In chapter 20, Sacks demonstrates the near-miraculous power of music to animate Parkinson’s patients and other people with severe movement disorders, even those who are frozen into odd postures. Scientists cannot yet explain how music achieves this effect.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>To readers who are unfamiliar with neuroscience and music behavior, Musicophilia may be something of a revelation. But the book will not satisfy those seeking the causes and implications of the phenomena Sacks describes. For one thing, Sacks appears to be more at ease discussing patients than discussing experiments. And he tends to be rather uncritical in accepting scientific findings and theories.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>It’s true that the causes of music-brain oddities remain poorly understood. However, Sacks could have done more to draw out some of the implications of the careful observations that he and other neurologists have made and of the treatments that have been successful. For example, he might have noted that the many specific dissociations among components of music comprehension, such as loss of the ability to perceive harmony but not melody, indicate that there is no music center in the brain. Because many people who read the book are likely to believe in the brain localisation of all mental functions, this was a missed educational opportunity.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Another conclusion one could draw is that there seem to be no ‘cures’ for neurological problems involving music. A drug can alleviate a symptom in one patient and aggravate it in another or can have both positive and negative effects in the same patient. Treatments mentioned seem to be almost exclusively antiepileptic medications, which ‘damp down’ the excitability of the brain in general; their effectiveness varies widely.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Finally, in many of the cases described here the patient with music-brain symptoms is reported to have ‘normal’ EEG results. Although Sacks recognises the existence of new technologies, among them far more sensitive ways to analyze brain waves than the standard neurological EEG test, he does not call for their use. In fact, although he exhibits the greatest compassion for patients, he conveys no sense of urgency about the pursuit of new avenues in the diagnosis and treatment of music-brain disorders. This absence echoes the book’s preface, in which Sacks expresses fear that ‘the simple art of observation may be lost’ if we rely too much on new technologies. He does call for both approaches, though, and we can only hope that the neurological community will respond.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8847&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8842","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Dirty River but Clean Water","book":"阅读还原集Vol.16","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.16 · Test 2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8842:63945:1","type":"choice","text":"Damage caused by a fire is worse than that caused by the flood.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Fire and flood are two of humanity’s worst nightmares.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“火灾造成的损害比洪水造成的损害更严重”这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“Damage caused by a fire”和“Damage caused by the flood”，需要在文章中寻找关于火灾和洪水损害的比较信息。\n解题思路：文章A段提到“Fire and flood are two of humanity’s worst nightmares”，说明两者都是严重的灾害，但没有说明哪一种更严重。因此，题目中的比较信息在文章中没有明确给出，答案应为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63945","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8842:63946:2","type":"choice","text":"The flood peaks at almost 1500 cubic meters every eight years.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Spring snow from as far away as Wyoming would melt and swell the Colorado River to a flow that averaged around 1,500 cubic metres (50,000 cubic feet) a second. Every eight years or so, that figure rose to almost 3,000 cubic metres. These floods infused the river with sediment, carved its beaches and built its sandbars.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“洪水流量高峰值每八年出现一次，达到近1500立方米”，需要判断这个说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的“every eight years”和“almost 1500 cubic meters”是定位关键词，在B段中找到“Every eight years or so, that figure rose to almost 3,000 cubic metres.”。\n解题思路：原文提到怀俄明州的春雪融化后，会使科罗拉多河的水量激增，平均流量达到每秒约1500立方米（5万立方英尺），每隔八年洪水流量会上升到近3000立方米，而题目说的是近1500立方米，两者数值不符，因此题目说法与原文信息不一致，应选择False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63946","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8842:63947:3","type":"choice","text":"Contribution of sediments delivered by tributaries has little impact.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Even that has not been much use as those tributaries are not powerful enough to distribute the sediment in an ecologically valuable way.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是支流输送的沉积物的影响微乎其微，需要判断这个说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词\"tributaries\"和\"sediments\"定位到C段，找到包含这些词的句子。\n解题思路：原文中是说这些支流运输的沉积物也未能发挥多大作用，在生态上没有太大的价值。因此与题干信息一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63947","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8842:63948:4","type":"choice","text":"The decreasing number of chubs is always caused by introducing of trout since the mid 20th century.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At first sight, it looked as if the reason was that the chub were being eaten by trout introduced for sport fishing in the mid-20th century. But trout and chub co-existed until the Glen Canyon dam was built, so something else is going on.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“鳊鱼数量减少是否一直是由20世纪中叶引进鳟鱼造成的”。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词“chubs”、“trout”和“mid-20th century”定位到D段，该段提到鳟鱼和鳊鱼在格伦峡谷大坝建成前曾共存。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，第一反应，会以为鳊鱼数量减少的是因为被鳟鱼吃了，但在格伦峡谷大坝建成之前，鳟鱼和鳊鱼一直共存，所以还有别的原因。因此，题目中“一直是由引进鳟鱼造成的”这一说法与原文矛盾，答案应为“False”。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63948","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8842:63949:5","type":"choice","text":"It seemed that the artificial flood in 1996 had achieved success partly at the very beginning.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1996 the flood was allowed to go on too long. To start with, all seemed well. The floodwaters built up sandbanks and infused the river with sediment. Eventually, however, the continued flow washed most of the sediment out of the canyon.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是1996年的人工洪水在开始时似乎取得了一些成功，需要判断这个说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"1996\"和\"artificial flood\"定位到F段，找到关于1996年洪水效果的描述。\n解题思路：根据原文F段的内容，\"To start with, all seemed well. The floodwaters built up sandbanks and infused the river with sediment.\"表明在开始时，洪水确实取得了成功，建立了沙洲并注入了沉积物，但最终，持续的水流将大部分沉积物冲出了峡谷。。这与题目所述\"在开始时似乎取得了一些成功\"一致，因此题目陈述与文章信息相符，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63949","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8842:63950:6","type":"choice","text":"In fact, the yield of artificial flood water is smaller than an average natural flood at present.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At less than 1,200 cubic metres a second, this flood is smaller than even an average spring flood, let alone one of the mightier deluges of the past.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“实际上，人工洪水的水量比现在的平均自然洪水要小”，需要判断这个说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“artificial flood water”和“smaller than an average natural flood”定位到G段，该段明确提到人工洪水的水量“smaller than even an average spring flood”。\n解题思路：根据原文G段的句子“this flood is smaller than even an average spring flood”，可以确定人工洪水的水量确实比平均自然洪水要小，因此题目陈述与原文信息一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63950","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8842:63951:7","type":"choice","text":"Mighty floods drove fast-moving flows with clean and high-quality water.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Those glorious inundations moved massive quantities of sediment through the Grand Canyon, wiping the slate dirty, and making a muddy mess of silt and muck that would make modern river rafters cringe.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“汹涌的洪水推着河水快速流动，带来洁净优质的水源”，需要判断这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“mighty floods”、“fast-moving flows”、“clean and high-quality water”定位到G段。\n解题思路：原文中提到“汹涌的洪水（mightier deluges）通过大峡谷移动了大量的沉积物，使河床污迹斑斑，形成了大片泥泞的淤泥和污泥”。原文并未说明水是干净的还是肮脏的，河床污迹斑斑是因为沉积物的作用。因此，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63951","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8842:63952:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"spring","acceptedAnswers":["spring"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Spring snow from as far away as Wyoming would melt and swell the Colorado River to a flow that averaged around 1,500 cubic metres (50,000 cubic feet) a second.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“怀俄明州的雪在哪个季节融化，使科罗拉多河的洪水流量达到峰值”。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“Wyoming”和“melt”定位到B段，找到“Spring snow from as far away as Wyoming would melt...”这句话。\n解题思路：原文明确提到“Spring snow”会融化，说明雪是在春季融化的，因此答案为“spring”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63952","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8842:63953:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"sediment","acceptedAnswers":["sediment"],"explanation":"原文答案句：However, in the four decades since the building of the Glen Canyon dam, just upstream of the Grand Canyon, the only sediment that it has collected has come from tiny, undammed tributaries.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是在Glen Canyon大坝建成后四十年间，它只能从微小的、未受拦截的支流中收集到什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"the Glen Canyon Dam\"和\"time period\"（四十年）来定位答案在文章中的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文中答案对应的句子，我们可以确定答案为\"sediment\"。原文明确提到，在Glen Canyon大坝建成后四十年间，它只能从微小的、未受拦截的支流中收集到\"sediment\"沉积物。因此，答案为\"sediment\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63953","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8842:63954:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"razorback sucker","acceptedAnswers":["razorback sucker"],"explanation":"原文答案句：And the chub are not alone. In the years since the Glen Canyon dam was built, several species have vanished altogether. These include the Colorado pike-minnow, the razorback sucker and the roundtail chub.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求根据文章内容填写消失的物种名称，其中已经给出了两个物种（Colorado pike-minnow和round-tail chub），需要填写另一个物种。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的物种名称\"Colorado pike-minnow\"和\"round-tail chub\"可以定位到E段，该段列举了几个消失的物种。\n解题思路：在E段中，明确提到了几个消失的物种，包括\"Colorado pike-minnow\"、\"the razorback sucker\"和\"the roundtail chub\"。题目中已经给出了前两个和最后一个物种的名称，因此中间缺失的物种就是\"razorback sucker\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63954","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8842:63955:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"common carp","acceptedAnswers":["common carp"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Meanwhile, aliens including fathead minnows, channel catfish and common carp, which would have been hard, put to survive in the savage waters of the undammed canyon, have moved in.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是，同时，某些物种此处，在此栖息，其中包括胖头鱼、沟鲶和什么鱼类。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"fathead minnows\"和\"channel catfish\"是定位关键词，通过这些词可以快速找到E段中列举的外来鱼类。\n解题思路：原文E段列举了外来鱼类包括\"fathead minnows, channel catfish and common carp\"，与题目中的前两种鱼类名称完全对应，因此空格处应填入\"common carp\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63955","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8842:63956:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"visibility","acceptedAnswers":["visibility"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The chub were well adapted to the poor visibility created by the chick, red water which gave the river its name and depended on it to hide from predators. Without the cloudy water, the chub became vulnerable.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是持续的水流导致沉积物被冲出峡谷，这对鳕鱼构成巨大威胁，因为它们利用什么来躲避捕食者。需要填写一个不超过两个词的名词。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"sediment\"和\"predators\"定位到D段，该段提到鳕鱼依赖浑浊的水（visibility）躲避捕食者。\n解题思路：原文中明确指出鳕鱼依赖\"poor visibility\"（低可见度）来躲避捕食者，当水流持续时，沉积物被冲走导致水变清澈，鳕鱼失去了\"visibility\"这一保护机制，因此答案为\"visibility\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63956","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8842:63957:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"sand","acceptedAnswers":["sand"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This problem was avoided in 2004, but unfortunately, on that occasion, the volume of sand available behind the dam was too low to rebuild the sandbanks.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“此外，在坝后可用的什么量过低，无法重建沙洲，洪水变得更加严重。”\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“volume of...available behind the dam was too low to rebuild the bars”，通过这些关键词可以在F段找到对应的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文句子“the volume of sand available behind the dam was too low to rebuild the sandbanks.”可以确定，题目中需要填写的是“sand”，原文明确指出在2004年，坝后可用的沙量过低，无法重建沙洲。因此，答案为“sand”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63957","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"63945","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Damage caused by a fire is worse than that caused by the flood.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"63946","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The flood peaks at almost 1500 cubic meters every eight years.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"63947","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Contribution of sediments delivered by tributaries has little impact.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"63948","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The decreasing number of chubs is always caused by introducing of trout since the mid 20th century.</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"63949","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>It seemed that the artificial flood in 1996 had achieved success partly at the very beginning.</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"63950","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>In fact, the yield of artificial flood water is smaller than an average natural flood at present.</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"63951","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Mighty floods drove fast-moving flows with clean and high-quality water.</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"63952","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The eco-impact of the Canyon Dam \nFloods are people’s nightmare. In the past, the canyon was raged by flood every year. The snow from far Wyoming would melt in the season of <strong>8.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong> and caused a flood flow peak in Colorado river.</p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"63953","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>In the four decades after people built the Glen Canyon Dam, it only could gather <strong>9.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong> together from tiny, undammed tributaries. \n\nHumpback chub population reduced, why?</p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"63954","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Then several species disappeared including Colorado pike-minnow, <strong>10.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong> and the round-tail chub.</p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"63955","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Meanwhile, some moved in such as fathead minnows, channel catfish and <strong>11.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"63956","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The non-stopped flow led to the washing away of the sediment out of the canyon, which poses a great threat to the chubs because it has poor <strong>12.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong> away from predators.</p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"63957","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>In addition, the volume of <strong>13.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong> available behind the dam was too low to rebuild the bars and flooding became more serious.</p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Dirty River but Clean Water&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Floods can occur in rivers when the flow rate exceeds the capacity of the river channel, particularly at bends or meanders in the waterway. Floods often cause damage to homes and businesses if they are in the natural flood plains of rivers. While riverine flood damage can be eliminated by moving away from rivers and other bodies of water, people have traditionally lived and worked by rivers because the land is usually flat and fertile and because rivers provide easy travel and access to commerce and industry.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Fire and flood are two of humanity’s worst nightmares. People have, therefore, always sought to control them. Forest fires are snuffed out quickly. The flow of rivers is regulated by weirs and dams. At least, that is how it used to be. But foresters have learned that forests need fires to clear out the brush and even to get seeds to germinate. And a similar revelation is now dawning on hydrologists. Rivers – and the ecosystems they support – need floods. That is why a man-made torrent has been surging down the Grand Canyon. By Thursday, March 6th it was running at full throttle, which was expected to be sustained for 60 hours.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Floods once raged through the canyon every year. Spring snow from as far away as Wyoming would melt and swell the Colorado River to a flow that averaged around 1,500 cubic metres (50,000 cubic feet) a second. Every eight years or so, that figure rose to almost 3,000 cubic metres. These floods infused the river with sediment, carved its beaches and built its sandbars.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>However, in the four decades since the building of the Glen Canyon dam, just upstream of the Grand Canyon, the only sediment that it has collected has come from tiny, undammed tributaries. Even that has not been much use as those tributaries are not powerful enough to distribute the sediment in an ecologically valuable way.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>This lack of flooding has harmed local wildlife. The humpback chub, for example, thrived in the rust-red waters of Colorado. Recently, though, its population has crashed. At first sight, it looked as if the reason was that the chub were being eaten by trout introduced for sport fishing in the mid-20th century. But trout and chub co-existed until the Glen Canyon dam was built, so something else is going on. Steve Gloss, of the United States Geological Survey (USGS), reckons that the chub’s decline is the result of their losing their most valuable natural defense, Colorado’s rusty sediment. The chub were well adapted to the poor visibility created by the chick, red water which gave the river its name and depended on it to hide from predators. Without the cloudy water, the chub became vulnerable.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>And the chub are not alone. In the years since the Glen Canyon dam was built, several species have vanished altogether. These include the Colorado pike-minnow, the razorback sucker and the roundtail chub. Meanwhile, aliens including fathead minnows, channel catfish and common carp, which would have been hard, put to survive in the savage waters of the undammed canyon, have moved in.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>So flooding is the obvious answer. Unfortunately, it is easier said than done. Floods were sent down the Grand Canyon in 1996 and 2004 and the results were mixed. In 1996 the flood was allowed to go on too long. To start with, all seemed well. The floodwaters built up sandbanks and infused the river with sediment. Eventually, however, the continued flow washed most of the sediment out of the canyon. This problem was avoided in 2004, but unfortunately, on that occasion, the volume of sand available behind the dam was too low to rebuild the sandbanks. This time, the USGS is convinced that things will be better. The amount of sediment available is three times greater than it was in 2004. So if a flood is going to do some good, this is the time to unleash one.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Even so, it may turn out to be an empty gesture. At less than 1,200 cubic metres a second, this flood is smaller than even an average spring flood, let alone one of the mightier deluges of the past. Those glorious inundations moved massive quantities of sediment through the Grand Canyon, wiping the slate dirty, and making a muddy mess of silt and muck that would make modern river rafters cringe.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8842&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8843","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Malaria Combat in Italy","book":"阅读还原集Vol.16","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.16 · Test 2 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8843:63958:14","type":"fill","text":"填写第 14 空","answer":"insects","acceptedAnswers":["insects"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Nott in his essay ‘Yellow Fever Contrasted with Bilious Fever’, published in 1850, dismissed the miasma theory as worthless, arguing that microscopic insects somehow transmitted by mosquitoes caused both malaria and yellow fever. Others made a link between swamps, water and malaria, but did not make the further leap towards insects.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是关于疟疾起源的理论中，除了蚊子之外，还可能有哪些主要的罪魁祸首被记录在文献中。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"mosquito\"和\"culprits\"定位到B段中\"Nott...arguing that microscopic insects somehow transmitted by mosquitoes caused both malaria and yellow fever\"这句话，其中提到了\"microscopic insects\"作为疟疾的传播媒介。\n解题思路：根据原文中\"Nott...arguing that microscopic insects somehow transmitted by mosquitoes caused both malaria and yellow fever\"诺特在1850年发表的《黄热病与胆汁热对比》一文中，直接否定了瘴气理论，主张正是蚊子携带的微小昆虫导致了疟疾和黄热病。这句话，可以确定题目中问到的除了蚊子之外的其他主要罪魁祸首就是\"microscopic insects\"，即\"microscopic insects\"是题目中14空所需要填写的答案。由于题目要求使用不超过两个单词，因此将\"microscopic insects\"简化为\"insects\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63958","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of Reading Passage. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8843:63959:15","type":"fill","text":"填写第 15 空","answer":"unclean air","acceptedAnswers":["unclean air"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Early man, confronting the manifestations of malaria, attributed the fevers to supernatural influences: evil spirits, angered deities, or the black magic of sorcerers. But in the 19th century, most experts believed that the disease was not produced by unclean air (‘miasma’ or ‘poisoning of the air’).\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是19世纪大多数专家否定了与疟疾相关的什么理论。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"miasma theory\"和\"related malaria to\"定位到B段。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，早期人类面对疟疾的发作时，将发烧归因于超自然力量：邪灵、愤怒的神灵或巫师的黑魔法。但到了19世纪，大多数专家认为这种疾病并非由不干净的空气（‘瘴气’或‘空气中毒’）引起。因此，答案为\"unclean air\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63959","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of Reading Passage. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8843:63960:16","type":"fill","text":"填写第 16 空","answer":"hereditary","acceptedAnswers":["hereditary"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Epidemics were blamed on southern Italians, given the widespread belief that malaria was hereditary.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问，甚至还有另一种广泛流传的理论认为，意大利南方人携带疟疾，因为理论认为南方人的疟疾是怎么样的。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"malaria was\"和\"hereditary\"可以定位到B段最后一句，该句明确提到疟疾被认为是意大利南方人的遗传特性。\n解题思路：原文直接给出了疟疾被认为是\"hereditary\"（遗传的），与题干中的空格位置和内容完全一致，因此答案为hereditary。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63960","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of Reading Passage. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8843:63961:17","type":"fill","text":"填写第 17 空","answer":"life expectancy","acceptedAnswers":["life expectancy"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In malarial zones, the life expectancy of land workers was a terrifying 22.5 years.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是在疟疾流行地区，农村工人的什么惊人地短。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"In malarial areas\"和\"rural workers\"定位到B段中描述疟疾流行区农村工人状况的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到在疟疾流行区（malarial zones），农村工人（land workers）的\"life expectancy\"（寿命预期）非常短，仅为22.5年。题目中的\"life expectancy\"与原文完全一致，因此答案为\"life expectancy\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63961","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of Reading Passage. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8843:63962:18","type":"choice","text":"The volunteers in Grassi experiments were from all parts over Italy.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：By experimenting on healthy volunteers (mosquitoes were released into rooms where they drank the blood of the human guinea pigs), Grassi was able to make the direct link between the insects (all females of a certain kind) and the disease.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“Grassi实验中的志愿者来自意大利的各个地区”，需要判断作者是否同意这一说法。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“volunteers”和“Grassi experiments”定位到C段，找到描述Grassi实验的句子。\n解题思路：原文提到Grassi通过实验在房间里释放蚊子让志愿者被叮咬，从而证明蚊子与疟疾的直接联系。但原文并未提及这些志愿者的来源地，因此无法确定作者是否支持这一说法，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63962","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 18-21\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet write YES  if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO  if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8843:63963:19","type":"choice","text":"Healthy people could remain safe in malaria – infectious zone if they did not have mosquito bites.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Definitive proof of these new theories was obtained after an extraordinary series of experiments in Italy, where healthy people were introduced into malarial zones but kept free of mosquito bites – and remained well.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“健康人群若未被蚊虫叮咬，在疟疾流行区也能不被感染。”，即询问在没有蚊子叮咬的情况下，健康人是否能在疟疾流行区避免感染。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“healthy people”、“mosquito bites”和“malaria-infectious zone”定位到C段，找到描述健康人在疟疾区不被蚊子叮咬而保持健康的句子。\n解题思路：原文C段提到“healthy people were introduced into malarial zones but kept free of mosquito bites – and remained well”，明确说明健康人进入疟疾区只要不被蚊子叮咬就不会生病，这与题目表述完全一致，因此题目与作者观点一致，选YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63963","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 18-21\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet write YES  if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO  if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8843:63964:20","type":"choice","text":"Quinine is an effective drug which had long been used to combat malaria.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A complicated approach was adopted, which made use of quinine – a drug obtained from tree bark which had long been used to combat fever but was now seen as a crucial part of the war on malaria.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是奎宁是一种有效药物，长期以来一直被用来对抗疟疾。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词\"Quinine\"和\"combat malaria\"在文章中定位，发现D段提到了奎宁的相关信息。\n解题思路：原文中提到奎宁是一种从树皮中提取的药物，长期以来被用来对抗发热，但现在是抗击疟疾的关键。然而，题目中说奎宁长期以来一直被用来对抗疟疾，这与原文信息不符。原文只提到奎宁长期以来被用来对抗发热，并未明确提到对抗疟疾。因此，题目与原文信息不符，答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63964","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 18-21\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet write YES  if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO  if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8843:63965:21","type":"choice","text":"Eradicating malaria was a goal combined both medical and political significance.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Malaria, as Snowden shows, was not just a medical problem, but a social and regional issue, and could only be defeated through multi-layered strategies. Politics was itself transformed by the anti-malarial campaigns.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问“消灭疟疾兼具医学和政治意义”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的“Eradicating malaria”（消灭疟疾）、“medical”（医疗）和“political”（政治）是定位关键词。在D段中，作者提到疟疾不仅是医疗问题，还是社会和地区问题，需要多层次策略。\n解题思路：D段明确指出疟疾的消灭需要多层次策略，包括医疗和社会（政治）层面，并且反疟疾运动对政治产生了影响。这与题目“消灭疟疾兼具医学和政治意义”完全一致，因此答案为YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63965","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 18-21\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet write YES  if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO  if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8843:63966:22","type":"choice","text":"22 A breakthrough was found that mosquito was the carrier of malaria.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Giovanni Battista Grassi, a naturalist, found that a particular type of mosquito was the carrier of malaria.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“发现蚊子是疟疾的传播者这一突破性进展出现在哪一段落”。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"mosquito\"和\"carrier of malaria\"在文章中定位。\n解题思路：在C段中，明确提到自然学家Giovanni Battista Grassi发现某一类型的蚊子是疟疾的传播者，这与题目中描述的一致。因此，答案为C段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"63966","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nThe passage has 8 paragraphs, A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet."},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8843:63966:23","type":"choice","text":"23 A scientist intentionally failed to restrict the epidemic area.","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Shamefully, the Italian malaria expert Alberto Missiroli had a role to play in the disaster: he did not distribute quinine, despite being well aware of the epidemic to come.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“一名科学家故意不对疫区实施管控措施”。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“scientist”和“failed to restrict the epidemic area”可以定位到F段中提到的“Alberto Missiroli”这位科学家以及他未能分发奎宁的情况。\n解题思路：根据F段中的原文句子“Shamefully, the Italian malaria expert Alberto Missiroli had a role to play in the disaster: he did not distribute quinine, despite being well aware of the epidemic to come.”可以确定，Alberto Missiroli作为意大利的疟疾专家，本应控制疫情，但他却故意不分发奎宁，因此未能控制疫情。这与题目所问的内容完全吻合，故答案为F。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"63966","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nThe passage has 8 paragraphs, A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet."},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8843:63966:24","type":"choice","text":"24 This successful story still holds true for today’s readers worldwide.","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The economic miracle of the 50s and 60s which made Italy into a modern industrial nation would not have been possible without the eradication of malaria. Moreover, this book convincingly argues that the disease was “an integral part of the big picture of modern Italian history”. This magnificent study, beautifully written and impeccably documented, deserves an audience beyond specialists in history, or in Italy. It also provides us with “a message of hope for a world struggling with the great present-day medical emergency”.\n对应段落：H\n审题：题目问哪个段落包含“这个成功故事至今仍对全球读者具有现实意义”的信息。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“successful story”和“today’s readers worldwide”可以定位到H段。H段明确提到Snowden的书具有当代相关性，并且为当今世界面临医疗紧急情况的人们提供了希望。\n解题思路：H段首先提到Snowden的书具有当代相关性，这与题目中的“仍然对当今世界各地的读者有意义”相呼应。接着，段落中提到疟疾对意大利社会的影响，以及意大利的经济奇迹离不开疟疾的根除，这些都表明了成功的故事对当今的意义。最后，段落明确指出这本书为当今世界提供了“希望的信息”，进一步验证了答案在H段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"63966","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nThe passage has 8 paragraphs, A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet."},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8843:63966:25","type":"choice","text":"25 One of the final cases reported dying of malaria in Italy.","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The last cases were noted in a poor region of Sicily. One of the final victims to die of the disease in Italy was the popular cyclist, Fausto Coppi.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落提到了“意大利报告的最后一个死于疟疾的病例”。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的“final cases dying of malaria in Italy”定位到文章中描述疟疾在意大利最后阶段的段落。\n解题思路：G段明确指出“最后的病例出现在西西里岛的一个贫困地区。在意大利，最后一位因该疾病去世的受害者是著名的自行车手法乌斯托·科皮。”，与题目信息完全匹配，因此答案为G。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"63966","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nThe passage has 8 paragraphs, A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet."},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8843:63966:26","type":"choice","text":"26 The negative symptoms of the highly effective drug.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Despite its often terrible side-effects (the headaches produced were known as the “quinine-buzz”), the drug was successful in limiting the spread of the disease, and in breaking cycles of infection.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问“强效药的负作用”在哪个段落中提到。\n定位关键信息：根据题目的关键词“negative symptoms”和“highly effective drug”定位到D段，该段提到奎宁（quinine）作为强效药，但其副作用（terrible side-effects）是头痛。\n解题思路：D段明确提到奎宁是一种强效药，并描述了其副作用（如“quinine-buzz”头痛），与题目对应。因此，答案为D。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"63966","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nThe passage has 8 paragraphs, A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet."},{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8843:63966:27","type":"choice","text":"27 A list of the speculative hypothesis was cited.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Early man, confronting the manifestations of malaria, attributed the fevers to supernatural influences: evil spirits, angered deities, or the black magic of sorcerers. But in the 19th century, most experts believed that the disease was not produced by unclean air (‘miasma’ or ‘poisoning of the air’). Two Americans, Josiah Clark Nott and Lewis Daniel Beauperthy, echoed Crawford’s ideas. Nott in his essay ‘Yellow Fever Contrasted with Bilious Fever’, published in 1850, dismissed the miasma theory as worthless, arguing that microscopic insects somehow transmitted by mosquitoes caused both malaria and yellow fever.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问哪个段落提到了一系列的推测性假设。\n定位关键信息：根据题目的关键词\"list of speculative hypothesis\"（推测性假设的列表），在文章中寻找描述早期人们对于疟疾原因的各种推测的句子。\n解题思路：在B段中，原文明确提到早期人类将疟疾发烧归因于超自然因素，并列举了具体的假设，如\"evil spirits\"（邪恶 spirits）、\"angered deities\"（愤怒的神灵）和\"black magic of sorcerers\"（巫师的黑色魔法）。后文又提到瘴气理论被推翻，有科学家将疟疾跟昆虫联系起来，这些内容都是有关疟疾的一系列假说。与题目要求完全匹配，因此答案为B段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"63966","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nThe passage has 8 paragraphs, A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"63958","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of Reading Passage. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Theories for malaria origin have always been the issue of research for medical practitioners from ancient time. Although the link between malaria and mosquito was established lately, it has been recorded in words that <strong>14.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong> , including mosquito, may play the major culprits.</p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"63959","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of Reading Passage. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>In the 19th century, most experts rejected the idea of the miasma theory which related malaria to <strong>15.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[15] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":15},{"id":"63960","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of Reading Passage. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Even another widespread theory arose that southern Italians were blamed, to whom malaria was <strong>16.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[16] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":16},{"id":"63961","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of Reading Passage. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the Reading Passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>In southern Italy, the situation became so severe that near half the Italians population was thought to be “permanently at risk”. In malarial areas the <strong>17.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[17] ____</strong> of rural workers was surprisingly shorter. In the 1880s, such theories began to withdraw as the mosquito was identified as the true cause.</p>","firstNumber":17},{"id":"63962","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 18-21\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet write YES  if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO  if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p><strong>The volunteers in Grassi experiments were from all parts over Italy.</strong></p>","firstNumber":18},{"id":"63963","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 18-21\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet write YES  if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO  if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p><strong>Healthy people could remain safe in malaria – infectious zone if they did not have mosquito bites.</strong></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"63964","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 18-21\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet write YES  if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO  if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p><strong>Quinine is an effective drug which had long been used to combat malaria.</strong></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"63965","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 18-21\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet write YES  if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO  if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","html":"<p><strong>Eradicating malaria was a goal combined both medical and political significance.</strong></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"63966","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nThe passage has 8 paragraphs, A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>22</strong> A breakthrough was found that mosquito was the carrier of malaria.<strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":22}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Malaria Combat in Italy</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Malaria. Bad air. Even the world is Italian, and this horrible disease marked the life of those in the peninsula for thousands of years. Giuseppe Garibaldi’s wife died of the disease, as did the country’s first prime minister, Cavour, in 1861. Yet by 1962, Italy was officially declared malaria-free, and it has remained so ever since. Frank Snowden’s study of this success story is a remarkable piece of historical work. Original, crystal-clear, analytical and passionate, Snowden (who has previously written about cholera) takes us to areas historians have rarely visited before.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Everybody now knows that malaria is carried by mosquitoes. Malaria has always been the subject of research for medical practitioners from time immemorial. However, many ancient texts, especially medical literature, mention of various aspects of malaria and even of its possible link with mosquitoes and insects. Early man, confronting the manifestations of malaria, attributed the fevers to supernatural influences: evil spirits, angered deities, or the black magic of sorcerers. But in the 19th century, most experts believed that the disease was not produced by unclean air (‘miasma’ or ‘poisoning of the air’). Two Americans, Josiah Clark Nott and Lewis Daniel Beauperthy, echoed Crawford’s ideas. Nott in his essay ‘Yellow Fever Contrasted with Bilious Fever’, published in 1850, dismissed the miasma theory as worthless, arguing that microscopic insects somehow transmitted by mosquitoes caused both malaria and yellow fever. Others made a link between swamps, water and malaria, but did not make the further leap towards insects. The consequences of these theories were that little was done to combat the disease before the end of the century. Things became so bad that 11m Italians (from a total population of 25m) were ‘permanently at risk’. In malarial zones, the life expectancy of land workers was a terrifying 22.5 years. Those who escaped death were weakened or suffered from splenomegaly – a ‘painful enlargement of the spleen’ and ‘a lifeless stare’. The economic impact of the disease was immense. Epidemics were blamed on southern Italians, given the widespread belief that malaria was hereditary. In the 1880s, such theories began to collapse as the dreaded mosquito was identified as the real culprit.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Italian scientists, drawing on the pioneering work of French doctor Alphonse Laveran, were able to predict the cycles of fever but it was in Rome that further key discoveries were made. Giovanni Battista Grassi, a naturalist, found that a particular type of mosquito was the carrier of malaria. By experimenting on healthy volunteers (mosquitoes were released into rooms where they drank the blood of the human guinea pigs), Grassi was able to make the direct link between the insects (all females of a certain kind) and the disease. Soon, doctors and scientists made another startling discovery: the mosquitoes themselves were also infected and not mere carriers. Every year, during the mosquito season, malarial blood was moved around the population by the insects. Definitive proof of these new theories was obtained after an extraordinary series of experiments in Italy, where healthy people were introduced into malarial zones but kept free of mosquito bites – and remained well. The new Italian state had the necessary information to tackle the disease.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>A complicated approach was adopted, which made use of quinine – a drug obtained from tree bark which had long been used to combat fever but was now seen as a crucial part of the war on malaria. Italy introduced a quinine law and a quinine tax in 1904, and the drug was administered to large numbers of rural workers. Despite its often terrible side-effects (the headaches produced were known as the “quinine-buzz”), the drug was successful in limiting the spread of the disease, and in breaking cycles of infection. In addition, Italy set up rural health centres and invested heavily in education programmes. Malaria, as Snowden shows, was not just a medical problem, but a social and regional issue, and could only be defeated through multi-layered strategies. Politics was itself transformed by the anti-malarial campaigns.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>It was originally decided to give quinine to all those in certain regions – even healthy people; peasants were often suspicious of the medicine being forced upon them. Doctors were sometimes met with hostility and refusal, and many were dubbed “poisoners”. Despite these problems, the strategy was hugely successful. Deaths from malaria fell by some 80% in the first decade of the 20th century and some areas escaped altogether from the scourge of the disease.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Shamefully, the Italian malaria expert Alberto Missiroli had a role to play in the disaster: he did not distribute quinine, despite being well aware of the epidemic to come. Snowden claims that Missiroli was already preparing a new strategy – with the support of the US Rockefeller Foundation – using a new pesticide, DDT. Missiroli allowed the epidemic to spread, in order to create the ideal conditions for a massive, and lucrative, human experiment. Fifty-five thousand cases of malaria were recorded in the province of Littoria alone in 1944. It is estimated that more than a bird of those in the affected area contracted the disease. Thousands, nobody knows how many, died.</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>With the war over, the US government and the Rockefeller Foundation were free to experiment. DDT was sprayed from the air and 3m Italians had their bodies covered with the chemical. The effects were dramatic, and nobody really cared about the toxic effects of the chemical. By 1962, malaria was more or less gone from the whole peninsula. The last cases were noted in a poor region of Sicily. One of the final victims to die of the disease in Italy was the popular cyclist, Fausto Coppi. He had contracted malaria in Africa in 1960, and the failure of doctors in the north of Italy to spot the disease was a sign of the times. A few decades earlier, they would have immediately noticed the tell-tale signs; it was later claimed that a small dose of quinine would have saved his life.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>As there are still more than 1m deaths every year from malaria worldwide, Snowden’s book also has contemporary relevance. This is a disease that affects every level of the societies where it is rampant. As Snowden writes: “In Italy, malaria undermined agricultural productivity, decimated the army, destroyed communities and left families impoverished.” The economic miracle of the 50s and 60s which made Italy into a modern industrial nation would not have been possible without the eradication of malaria. Moreover, this book convincingly argues that the disease was “an integral part of the big picture of modern Italian history”. This magnificent study, beautifully written and impeccably documented, deserves an audience beyond specialists in history, or in Italy. It also provides us with “a message of hope for a world struggling with the great present-day medical emergency”.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8843&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8844","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 British Architecture 2","book":"阅读还原集Vol.16","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.16 · Test 2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8844:64003:28","type":"fill","text":"填写第 28 空","answer":"wood/Wood","acceptedAnswers":["wood","Wood"],"explanation":"原文答案句：And although the Anglo-Saxons had a sophisticated building style of their own, little survives to bear witness to their achievements as the vast majority of Angle-Saxon buildings were made of wood.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是盎格鲁-撒克逊建筑未能保留下来，是因为建筑是用什么建造的。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"Anglo-Saxon architecture\"和\"failed to last\"可以定位到A段中关于盎格鲁-撒克逊建筑的描述。\n解题思路：根据原文\"A段\"中的句子，尽管盎格鲁-撒克逊人拥有自己独特的建筑风格，但由于绝大多数建筑都是木结构，如今留存下来的实物已寥寥无几，难以见证他们的辉煌成就。可知，盎格鲁-撒克逊建筑未能保存下来是因为绝大多数建筑是由木材建造的。因此，答案为wood。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64003","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nComplete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8844:64004:29","type":"fill","text":"填写第 29 空","answer":"status and wealth/Status And Wealth","acceptedAnswers":["status and wealth","Status And Wealth"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In a sense, the buildings of the 16th century were also governed by fitness for purpose – only now, the purpose was very different. In domestic architecture, in particular, buildings were used to display status and wealth.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问，与中世纪建筑不同，16世纪的建筑代表着什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"16th century\"和\"different from medieval architecture\"可以定位到B段最后两句，这两句明确提到了16世纪建筑与中世纪建筑在功能上的区别。\n解题思路：原文B段最后两句提到，中世纪建筑的功能是\"fitness for purpose\"（实用），而16世纪建筑的功能则变成了\"display status and wealth\"（展示地位和财富），这正是题目所问的不同之处。因此答案为\"status and wealth\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64004","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nComplete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8844:64005:30","type":"fill","text":"填写第 30 空","answer":"expensive commodity/eExpensive Commodity","acceptedAnswers":["expensive commodity","eExpensive Commodity"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The rooms themselves tended to be bigger and lighter – as an expensive commodity, the use of great expanses of glass was in itself a statement of wealth.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是在那些年里，大面积使用高价的玻璃是一种什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目的单词\"glass\"和\"costly\"可以定位到C段中\"the use of great expanses of glass\"这句话。\n解题思路：根据原文句子，房间本身往往更为宽敞明亮——作为昂贵的建材，大面积使用玻璃本身就是财富的象征，可以确定，玻璃是一种昂贵的材料，因此答案是\"expensive commodity\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64005","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nComplete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8844:64006:31","type":"fill","text":"填写第 31 空","answer":"classical/Classical","acceptedAnswers":["classical","Classical"],"explanation":"原文答案句：With the exception of Inigo Jones (1573-1652), whose confident handling of classical detail and proportion set him apart from all other architects of the period, most early 17th century buildings tended to take the innocent exuberance of late Tudor work one step further.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问Inigo Jones擅长处理哪种风格。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Inigo Jones\"和\"skilled at handling\"（擅长处理）定位到D段，找到提到\"Inigo Jones\"的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，\"Inigo Jones\"擅长处理\"classical detail and proportion\"（古典细节和比例），题目中的\"style\"（风格）与\"detail and proportion\"对应，因此答案为\"classical\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64006","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nComplete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8844:64007:32","type":"fill","text":"填写第 32 空","answer":"furniture and textiles/Furniture And Textiles","acceptedAnswers":["furniture and textiles","Furniture And Textiles"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Morris’s influence grew from the production of furniture and textiles, until by the 1880s a generation of principled young architects was following his call for good, honest construction.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问威廉·莫里斯（William Morris）更偏向采用前工业制造技术生产的什么产品。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"William Morris\"和\"pre-industrial manufacturing techniques\"定位到E段，找到关于莫里斯及其影响的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，莫里斯的影响力最初从家具与纺织品生产领域开始，到19世纪80年代，一代秉持理想主义的年轻建筑师们纷纷响应他的号召。可以推断，家具与纺织品产品正是采用前工业技术制作的。因此答案为\"furniture and textiles\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64007","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nComplete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8844:64008:33","type":"fill","text":"填写第 33 空","answer":"Edwin Lutyens/edwin lutyens","acceptedAnswers":["Edwin Lutyens","edwin lutyens"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Whilst Gropius was experimenting with the use of reinforced concrete frames, we had staid establishment architects like Edwin Lutyens producing Neo-Georgian and Renaissance country houses for an outmoded landed class.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是哪些建筑师为地主建造保守派住宅。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"architects\"、\"landlord\"和\"conservative houses\"可以定位到F段中提到的\"Edwin Lutyens\"和\"Neo-Georgian and Renaissance country houses\"，这些描述与题干中的\"conservative houses\"相吻合。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子，我们可以确定Edwin Lutyens是一位为地主建造保守派住宅的建筑师。这与题干中的描述完全一致。因此，答案为\"Edwin Lutyens\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64008","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nComplete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8844:64009:34","type":"fill","text":"填写第 34 空","answer":"local authorities/Local Authorities","acceptedAnswers":["local authorities","Local Authorities"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Local authorities, charged with the task of rebuilding city centers, became important patrons of architecture.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是二战后，建筑委托方从个人转向了谁。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"After World War Two\"和\"architect commission\"定位到G段，该段明确提到二战后重建时期建筑委托方发生了变化。\n解题思路：原文G段提到，二战后地方政府（local authorities）承担了城市重建的任务，成为建筑的重要资助者（patrons of architecture），取代了过去长期主导建筑领域的个人委托方。因此，答案为\"local authorities\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64009","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nComplete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8844:64010:35","type":"choice","text":"The feature of medieval architecture was","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：And it is all the more remarkable because the underlying ethos of medieval architecture was ‘fitness for purpose’.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问中世纪建筑的特点是什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"medieval architecture\"定位到B段，找到描述中世纪建筑的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，中世纪建筑的核心理念是“实用至上”，后又详细举出具体的例子，对应选项B中的\"useful\"（有用的）。其他选项A（巨大的）、C（装饰性的）和D（奇异的）在原文中均未被提及或描述为中世纪建筑的主要特征。","options":["immense.","useful.","decorative.","bizarreh."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64010","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8844:64011:36","type":"choice","text":"What contributes to the outward-looking buildings in the 16th century?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A greater sense of security led to more outward-looking buildings, as opposed to the medieval arrangement where the need for defense created houses that faced inward onto a courtyard or series of courtyards.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问16世纪的建筑外向型特点是为了什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"outward-looking buildings\"和\"16th century\"定位到C段首句，该句明确提到\"greater sense of security\"（更大的安全感）是导致建筑外向型发展的原因。\n解题思路：原文直接指出，。相较于中世纪因防御需求而将房屋朝向内院或连院布局的建筑风格，当时人们更注重营造安全感，因此建筑更倾向于外向型设计。对应选项A\"safety\"安全；其他选项B、C、D在原文中均未被提及为原因。","options":["safety","beauty","quality","technology"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64011","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8844:64012:37","type":"choice","text":"Why were the buildings in the 1660s influenced by the latest European trends?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But during the 1640s and 50s the Civil War and its aftermath sent many gentlemen and nobles to the Continent either to escape the fighting or, when the war was lost, to follow Charles II into exile. There they came into contact with French, Dutch and Italian architecture and, with Charles’s restoration in 1660, there was a flurry of building activity as royalists reclaimed their property and built themselves houses reflecting the latest European trends.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问为什么17世纪60年代的建筑受到当时欧洲最新潮流的影响。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"1660s\"和\"European trends\"定位到D段。\n解题思路：原文提到，众多绅士贵族或为躲避战火，或因战败追随查理二世流亡欧洲。他们在此期间接触到法国、荷兰和意大利的建筑风格。随着查理二世于1660年复辟，保皇派重新购置地产后掀起建筑热潮，纷纷建造符合当时欧洲最新潮流的宅邸。说明是查理二世以及许多贵族在英国内战后流亡欧洲，复辟后带回欧洲建筑风格，因此D选项正确。其他选项A、B、C在原文中均未被提及或不符合原文逻辑。","options":["Because the war was lost.","Because the craftsman came from all over Europe.","Because the property belongs to the gentlemen and nobles.","Because the monarch came back from the continent."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64012","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8844:64013:38","type":"choice","text":"What kind of sense did the British Baroque imply?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The British Baroque was a reassertion of authority, an expression of absolutist ideology by men who remembered a world turned upside down during the Civil War. The style is heavy and rich, sometimes overblown and melodramatic.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问英国巴洛克式风格蕴含着怎样的意味。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"British Baroque\"定位到D段，找到描述该风格的句子\"The style is heavy and rich, sometimes overblown and melodramatic.\"\n解题思路：原文中提到，英国巴洛克风格实为权威的重新确立，是那些铭记内战时期世界剧变的君主主义者对绝对主义意识形态的宣示。可以推断该风格建筑体现出一种\"tough\"（强硬的）感觉，与选项A对应。其他选项\"steady\"（稳定的）、\"mild\"（温和的）和\"conservative\"（保守的）均不能准确概括原文描述的风格特点。","options":["tough","steady","mild","conservative"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64013","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8844:64014:39","type":"choice","text":"The individual craftsman was no more the key to creation for the appearance of","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Mass production resulted in buildings and furnishings that were too perfect, as the individual craftsman no longer had a major role in their creation.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是个体工匠不再制造过程的关键，这是因为什么的出现。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“individual craftsman”和“key to creation”可以定位到E段中“as the individual craftsman no longer had a major role in their creation”这句话。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句可知，大规模生产导致建筑和家具过于完美，因为工匠在创作过程中不再发挥重要作用。因此，正确答案是C选项“大规模的工业生产”。","options":["Crystal Palace.","preindustrial manufacturing return.","industrial process in scale.","ornament."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64014","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8844:64015:40","type":"choice","text":"The building style changed after World War Two as a result of","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The Modern Movement’s belief in progress and the future struck a chord with the mood of post-war Britain and, as reconstruction began under Attlee’s Labour government in 1945, there was a desperate need for cheap housing which could be produced quickly.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是二战后建筑风格发生变化的原因。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"after World War Two\"和\"changed\"定位到G段，该段提到战后重建时期的情况。\n解题思路：原文中明确指出，现代主义运动对进步与未来的信念，与战后英国的社会氛围产生了共鸣。随着1945年艾德礼工党政府启动重建工作，人们迫切需要能够快速建造的廉价住房。这一需求直接导致了建筑风格的改变，即采用预制构件、金属框架等现代主义建筑手法。因此，选项C\"shortage of cheap housing\"（廉价住房短缺）是正确的，它直接对应了原文中的原因。其他选项A、B、D在原文中均未被提及或不是主要原因。","options":["abundant materials.","local authority.","shortage of cheap housing.","conservative views."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64015","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64003","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nComplete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>28</strong> The Anglo-Saxon architecture failed to last because the buildings were constructed in <strong class=\"source-blank\">[28] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"64004","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nComplete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>29</strong> Different from the medieval architecture, the buildings of the 16th century represents <strong class=\"source-blank\">[29] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"64005","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nComplete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>30</strong> The costly glass was applied widely as an <strong class=\"source-blank\">[30] ____</strong> in those years.</p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"64006","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nComplete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>31</strong> Inigo Jones was skilled at handling <strong class=\"source-blank\">[31] ____</strong> style.</p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"64007","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nComplete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>32</strong> William Morris favored the production of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[32] ____</strong> made in pre-industrial manufacturing\ntechniques.</p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"64008","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nComplete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>33</strong> The architects such as <strong class=\"source-blank\">[33] ____</strong> provided the landlord with conservative houses.</p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"64009","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nComplete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>34</strong> After World War Two, the architect commission shifted from the individual to <strong class=\"source-blank\">[34] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"64010","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>The feature of medieval architecture was</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"64011","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What contributes to the outward-looking buildings in the 16th century?</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"64012","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Why were the buildings in the 1660s influenced by the latest European trends?</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"64013","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What kind of sense did the British Baroque imply?</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"64014","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>The individual craftsman was no more the key to creation for the appearance of</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"64015","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>The building style changed after World War Two as a result of</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>British Architecture 2</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Architecture is about evolution, not revolution. It used to be thought that once the Romans pulled out of Britain in the fifth century, their elegant villas, carefully-planned towns and engineering marvels like Hadrian’s Wall simply fell into decay as British culture was plunged into the Dark Ages. It took the Norman Conquest of 1066 to bring back the light, and the Gothic cathedral-builders of the Middle Ages played an important part in the revival of British culture. However, the truth is not as simple as that Romano-British culture – and that included architecture along with language, religion, political organization and the arts – survived long after the Roman withdrawal. And although the Anglo-Saxons had a sophisticated building style of their own, little survives to bear witness to their achievements as the vast majority of Angle-Saxon buildings were made of wood.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Even so, the period between the Norman landing at Pevensey in 1066 and the day in 1485 when Richard III lost his horse and his head at Bosworth, ushering in the Tudors and the Early Modern period, marks a rare flowering of British building. And it is all the more remarkable because the underlying ethos of medieval architecture was ‘fitness for purpose’. The great cathedrals and parish churches that lifted up their towers to heaven were not only acts of devotion in stone; they were also fiercely functional buildings. Castles served their particular purpose and their battlements and turrets were for use rather than ornament. In a sense, the buildings of the 16th century were also governed by fitness for purpose – only now, the purpose was very different. In domestic architecture, in particular, buildings were used to display status and wealth.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>This stately and curious workmanship showed itself in various ways. A greater sense of security led to more outward-looking buildings, as opposed to the medieval arrangement where the need for defense created houses that faced inward onto a courtyard or series of courtyards. This allowed for much more in the way of exterior ornament. The rooms themselves tended to be bigger and lighter – as an expensive commodity, the use of great expanses of glass was in itself a statement of wealth. There was also a general move towards balanced and symmetrical exteriors with central entrances.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>With the exception of Inigo Jones (1573-1652), whose confident handling of classical detail and proportion set him apart from all other architects of the period, most early 17th century buildings tended to take the innocent exuberance of late Tudor work one step further. But during the 1640s and 50s the Civil War and its aftermath sent many gentlemen and nobles to the Continent either to escape the fighting or, when the war was lost, to follow Charles II into exile. There they came into contact with French, Dutch and Italian architecture and, with Charles’s restoration in 1660, there was a flurry of building activity as royalists reclaimed their property and built themselves houses reflecting the latest European trends. The British Baroque was a reassertion of authority, an expression of absolutist ideology by men who remembered a world turned upside down during the Civil War. The style is heavy and rich, sometimes overblown and melodramatic. The politics which underpin it are questionable, but its products are breathtaking.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The huge glass-and-iron Crystal Palace, designed by Joseph Paxton to house the Great Exhibition of 1851, shows another strand to 19th century architecture – one which embraced new industrial processes. But it wasn’t long before even this confidence in progress came to be regarded with suspicion. Mass production resulted in buildings and furnishings that were too perfect, as the individual craftsman no longer had a major role in their creation. Railing against the dehumanizing effects of industrialisation, reformers like John Ruskin and William Morris made a concerted effort to return to hand-crafted, pre-industrial manufacturing techniques. Morris’s influence grew from the production of furniture and textiles, until by the 1880s a generation of principled young architects was following his call for good, honest construction.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The most important trends in early 20th century architecture simply passed Britain by. Whilst Gropius was experimenting with the use of reinforced concrete frames, we had staid establishment architects like Edwin Lutyens producing Neo-Georgian and Renaissance country houses for an outmoded landed class. In addition, there were slightly batty architect-craftsmen, the heirs of William Morris, still trying to turn the clock back to before the Industrial Revolution by making chairs and spurning new technology. Only a handful of Modern Movement buildings of any real merit were produced here during the 1920s and 1930s, and most of these were the work of foreign architects such as Serge Chermayeff, Berthold Lubetkin and Erno Goldfinger who had settled in this country.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>After the Second World War the situation began to change. The Modern Movement’s belief in progress and the future struck a chord with the mood of post-war Britain and, as reconstruction began under Attlee’s Labour government in 1945, there was a desperate need for cheap housing which could be produced quickly. The use of prefabricated elements, metal frames, concrete cladding and the absence of decoration – all of which had been embraced by Modernists abroad and viewed with suspicion by the British – were adopted to varying degrees for housing developments and schools. Local authorities, charged with the task of rebuilding city centers, became important patrons of architecture. This represented a shift away from the private individuals who had dominated the architectural scene for centuries.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Since the War, it has been corporate bodies like these local authorities, together with national and multinational companies, and large educational institutions, which have dominated British architecture. By the late 1980s the Modern Movement, unfairly blamed for the social experiments implicit in high-rise housing, had lost out to irony and spectacle in the shape of post-modernism, with its cheerful borrowings from anywhere and any period. But now, in the new Millennium, even post-modernism is showing signs of age. What comes next? Post-post-modernism?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8844&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8839","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Homeopathy: Overdosing on Nothing","book":"阅读还原集Vol.16","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.16 · Test 1 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8839:63922:1","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：An international protest this week aims to demonstrate the truth about homeopathy – that there’s literally nothing in it, says Martin Robbins at 10.23 am on 30 January, more than 300 activists in the UK, Canada, Australia and the US will take part in a mass homeopathic ‘overdose’.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求为A段选择一个合适的标题，概括该段的主要内容。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读A段，可以定位到段落首句提到了“an international protest”和“demonstrate the truth about homeopathy”，这是段落的核心信息。\n解题思路：A段主要描述了一场国际抗议活动，目的是揭示顺势疗法的真相。这与选项I“The purpose of staging an demonstration to against homeopathy”完全吻合，因为该选项准确概括了A段的核心内容——通过示威活动反对顺势疗法。因此，选择I。","options":["The definition of three laws","Quoting three laws to against the homeopathy","There are many methods of avoiding answering ambiguous questions","The purpose of selling homeopathic remedies","The constant booming of homeopathy","Some differences between homeopathy and placebo","Placebo is better than homeopathy","An example of further demonstrating the negative effect of homeopathy","The purpose of staging a demonstration to against homeopathy"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"63922","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nChoose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of heading below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8839:63922:2","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：That such a protest is even necessary in 2010 is remarkable, but somehow the homeopathic industry has not only survived into the 21st century, but prospered. In the UK alone more than £40 million is spent annually on homeopathic treatments, with £4 million of this being sucked from the National Health Service budget.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求为B段选择一个恰当的小标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读B段内容，找到段落的核心主题和关键信息点。\n解题思路：B段主要讨论了顺势疗法行业的现状。第一句提到抗议的必要性，随后提到该行业不仅存活了下来，而且繁荣发展，单英国，每年就花费超过4000万英镑在顺势疗法上，其中400万来自国民健康服务预算。因此，最符合的小标题应该是E（顺势疗法持续繁荣发展）。","options":["The definition of three laws","Quoting three laws to against the homeopathy","There are many methods of avoiding answering ambiguous questions","The purpose of selling homeopathic remedies","The constant booming of homeopathy","Some differences between homeopathy and placebo","Placebo is better than homeopathy","An example of further demonstrating the negative effect of homeopathy","The purpose of staging a demonstration to against homeopathy"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"63922","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nChoose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of heading below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8839:63922:3","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The discipline is based on three ‘laws’; the law of similars, the law of infinitesimals and the law of succession.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求为C段选择正确的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读C段内容，可以找到段落开头明确提到了“three ‘laws’”，即“相似法则”、“无限稀释法则”和“连续法则”，这是C段的核心内容。\n解题思路：根据段落内容，C段主要介绍了顺势疗法的三大法则。因此，正确的标题应该概括这一核心内容。在提供的标题选项中，标题A“顺势疗法的三大法则”最符合C段的内容，因为它直接对应了段落中提到的“three ‘laws’”。","options":["The definition of three laws","Quoting three laws to against the homeopathy","There are many methods of avoiding answering ambiguous questions","The purpose of selling homeopathic remedies","The constant booming of homeopathy","Some differences between homeopathy and placebo","Placebo is better than homeopathy","An example of further demonstrating the negative effect of homeopathy","The purpose of staging a demonstration to against homeopathy"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"63922","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nChoose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of heading below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8839:63922:4","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Unsurprisingly, when tested under rigorous scientific conditions, in randomized, controlled and double blind trials, homeopathic remedies have shown to be no better than a placebo. Of course, the placebo effect is quite powerful, but it’s a bit like justifying building a car without any wheels on the basis that you can still enjoy the comfy leather seats and play with the gear shift.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求为D段选择一个正确的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读D段内容，可以定位到段落主要讨论了顺势疗法的最终准备过程以及科学测试结果。\n解题思路：D段首先描述了顺势疗法的最终准备过程，即药液滴在糖丸上供患者服用。接着，顺势疗法声称即使药物不含任何原始成分的分子，也能携带一种无法测量或检测的能量。最后，段落指出在严格的科学条件下进行随机、控制和双盲试验后，顺势疗法药物的效果并不比安慰剂更好。因此，D段对应标题G“Placebo is better than homeopathy”（安慰剂比顺势疗法更好）。","options":["The definition of three laws","Quoting three laws to against the homeopathy","There are many methods of avoiding answering ambiguous questions","The purpose of selling homeopathic remedies","The constant booming of homeopathy","Some differences between homeopathy and placebo","Placebo is better than homeopathy","An example of further demonstrating the negative effect of homeopathy","The purpose of staging a demonstration to against homeopathy"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"63922","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nChoose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of heading below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8839:63922:5","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He defended Boots’s decision to sell homoeopathic remedies on the grounds of consumer choice. ‘A large number of our consumers actually do believe they are efficacious, but they are licensed medicinal products and, therefore, we believe it is right to make them available,’ he said.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求为E段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读E段，可以定位到关键信息是关于Boots的药剂师Paul Bennett在议会委员会上回答关于顺势疗法是否有效的问题，以及他解释Boots继续销售顺势疗法药物的原因。\n解题思路：E段主要讲述了Boots的药剂师Paul Bennett在议会委员会上承认没有证据表明顺势疗法药物有效，但他仍然为Boots销售这些药物辩护，理由是消费者选择和这些药物是获得许可的医药产品。因此，E段的标题应该反映销售顺势疗法药物的目的，D最符合这一描述。","options":["The definition of three laws","Quoting three laws to against the homeopathy","There are many methods of avoiding answering ambiguous questions","The purpose of selling homeopathic remedies","The constant booming of homeopathy","Some differences between homeopathy and placebo","Placebo is better than homeopathy","An example of further demonstrating the negative effect of homeopathy","The purpose of staging a demonstration to against homeopathy"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"63922","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nChoose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of heading below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8839:63922:6","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph F","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：However, we believe there is a risk in perpetuating the notion that homoeopathy is equivalent to modern medicine. People may delay seeking appropriate treatment for themselves or their children.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求为F段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读F段，可以定位到段落的核心内容是关于顺势疗法是否无害的讨论。\n解题思路：F段首先提出了一个观点，即顺势疗法可能无害，因为人们只是花钱购买糖丸，没有违法。然后，作者指出这种观点在一定程度上是正确的，因为糖丸的危害有限。然而，作者也强调了维持顺势疗法与现代医学等同这一观念的风险，因为它可能导致人们延误寻求正规治疗。因此，F段主要是想说明顺势疗法有害，这与选项H“A example of further demonstrating the negative effect of homeopathy”（进一步证明顺势疗法负面效果的例子）吻合。","options":["The definition of three laws","Quoting three laws to against the homeopathy","There are many methods of avoiding answering ambiguous questions","The purpose of selling homeopathic remedies","The constant booming of homeopathy","Some differences between homeopathy and placebo","Placebo is better than homeopathy","An example of further demonstrating the negative effect of homeopathy","The purpose of staging a demonstration to against homeopathy"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"63922","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nChoose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of heading below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8839:63922:7","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph G","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：We accept that we are unlikely to convince the true believers. Homoeopathy has many ways to sidestep awkward questions, such as rejecting the validity of randomized controlled trials, or claiming that homoeopathic remedies only work if you have symptoms of the malady they purport to cure. Our aim is to reach out to the general public with our simple message: ‘There is nothing in it’.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求为G段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读G段，可以定位到关键信息是作者强调的目标和核心信息。\n解题思路：G段讲了顺势疗法总能找到各种借口来回避棘手问题，比如质疑随机对照试验的有效性，或是声称顺势疗法只有在患者出现病症时才有效。最后重申作者的目标，向公众传达一个简单的信息：“顺势疗法药物中什么都没有”。因此，选择C项顺势疗法支持者有许多方法可以避免回答模棱两可的问题。","options":["The definition of three laws","Quoting three laws to against the homeopathy","There are many methods of avoiding answering ambiguous questions","The purpose of selling homeopathic remedies","The constant booming of homeopathy","Some differences between homeopathy and placebo","Placebo is better than homeopathy","An example of further demonstrating the negative effect of homeopathy","The purpose of staging a demonstration to against homeopathy"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"63922","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nChoose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of heading below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet."},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8839:63923:8","type":"choice","text":"Skeptics planning to hold a demonstration in ‘10.23’ campaign is to against UK’s leading pharmacist, Boots.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The aim of the ‘10:23’ campaign, led by the Merseyside Skeptics Society, based in Liverpool, UK, is to raise public awareness of just exactly what homeopathy is, and to put pressure on the UK’s leading pharmacist, Boots, to remove the remedies from sale.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是怀疑论者计划在“10.23”活动中举行示威，目的是反对英国的领先药剂公司Boots。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“Skeptics planning to hold a demonstration in ‘10.23’ campaign”和“against UK’s leading pharmacist, Boots”可以定位到A段中关于“10:23”活动的描述。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到“10:23”活动的目的是“raise public awareness of just exactly what homeopathy is, and to put pressure on the UK’s leading pharmacist, Boots, to remove the remedies from sale”，即提高公众对顺势疗法的认识，并对英国的领先药剂师Boots施加压力，要求其停止销售顺势疗法药物。这与题目中“反对英国的领先药剂师Boots”的表述一致，因此答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63923","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is ture, FALSE  if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8839:63924:9","type":"choice","text":"National Health Service budget gained a small portion of homeopathic industry.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In the UK alone more than £40 million is spent annually on homeopathic treatments, with £4 million of this being sucked from the National Health Service budget.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问“英国国民医疗保健预算从顺势治疗上获得了一些利润”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的“National Health Service budget”和“homeopathic industry”定位到B段第二句，该句提到“在英国，仅顺势疗法治疗每年就花费超过4000万英镑，其中400万英镑来自国民医疗服务预算”。\n解题思路： B段第二句，在英国，仅顺势疗法治疗每年就花费超过4000万英镑，其中400万英镑来自国民医疗服务预算。题干说“英国国民医疗保健预算从顺势治疗上获得利润”。两者矛盾。所以False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63924","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is ture, FALSE  if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8839:63925:10","type":"choice","text":"The example of Caffeine is to present that homeopathy resists the laws of similars.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The law of similars states that something which causes your symptoms will cure your symptoms, so that, for example, as caffeine keeps you awake, it can also be a cure for insomnia. Of course, that makes little sense, since drinking caffeine, well, keeps you awake.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问“咖啡因的例子是为了说明顺势疗法违背了相似法则。” 即相似法则站不住脚，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词“Caffeine”和“law of similars”定位到C段，找到包含这两个词的句子。\n解题思路：原文C段提到“相似法则”的内容，并举例说明咖啡因被用于治疗失眠，但接着作者指出“这说不通，因为摄入咖啡因会让人保持清醒”，表明这个例子实际上是为了说明相似法则的荒谬性，即顺势疗法的相似法则本身是站不住脚的。因此，题目说法与原文一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63925","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is ture, FALSE  if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8839:63926:11","type":"choice","text":"Instilling the idea to people that homeopathy is equal to modern medicine poses danger.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：However, we believe there is a risk in perpetuating the notion that homeopathy is equivalent to modern medicine. People may delay seeking appropriate treatment for themselves or their children.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问“向人们灌输顺势疗法等同于现代医学的想法是危险的”这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"homeopathy is equal to modern medicine poses danger\"，通过这些词可以定位到F段中的\"homeopathy is equivalent to modern medicine\"和\"risk\"。\n解题思路：原文F段明确提到\"we believe there is a risk in perpetuating the notion that homeopathy is equivalent to modern medicine\"，即认为推广\"顺势疗法等同于现代医学\"这一观点是有风险的，紧接着解释了风险在于，人们可能会因此延误为自己或子女寻求正规治疗的机会。因此，题目中的说法与原文一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63926","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is ture, FALSE  if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8839:63927:12","type":"choice","text":"Paul Bennett claimed effectiveness of taking the homeopathic medicine is proved.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He was questioned by Member of Parliament Phil Willis, who asked: ‘Do they work beyond the placebo effect?’ ‘I have no evidence before me to suggest that they are efficacious,’ Bennett replied.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问Paul Bennett声称已经证明了顺势疗法药物的有效性，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的名字\"Paul Bennett\"和关键词\"effectiveness\"定位到E段中Paul Bennett的回答。\n解题思路：原文中Paul Bennett明确表示\"I have no evidence before me to suggest that they are efficacious\"（我没有证据表明它们是有效的），这直接表明他没有声称已经证明了药物的有效性，因此题目中的说法与原文信息相反，所以答案是False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63927","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is ture, FALSE  if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8839:63928:13","type":"choice","text":"The adoption of homeopathy mainly contributes to the delay of seeking appropriate treatment for themselves or their children.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：However, we believe there is a risk in perpetuating the notion that homeopathy is equivalent to modern medicine. People may delay seeking appropriate treatment for themselves or their children.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“采用顺势疗法主要导致的后果是，人们可能会因此延误为自己或子女寻求正规治疗的机会”，需要判断这一说法是否与原文信息一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词“adoption of homeopathy”和“delay of seeking appropriate treatment”可以定位到F段后半部分，该部分明确提到“perpetuating the notion that homeopathy is equivalent to modern medicine”和“People may delay seeking appropriate treatment for themselves or their children”。\n解题思路：原文F段指出，持续认为顺势疗法等同于现代医学存在风险，人们可能会因此延误寻求正规治疗。但原文并未明确表示“采用顺势疗法”是“主要”导致延误的原因，而是强调这种观念的持续存在可能带来的风险。题目中的“主要”这一表述过于绝对，原文并未提供足够信息支持这一因果关系。因此，题目说法与原文信息不符，答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63928","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is ture, FALSE  if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8839:63929:14","type":"choice","text":"The campaign has exerted pressure on Boots and other retailers","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The aim of the ‘10:23’ campaign, led by the Merseyside Skeptics Society, based in Liverpool, UK, is to raise public awareness of just exactly what homeopathy is, and to put pressure on the UK’s leading pharmacist, Boots, to remove the remedies from sale.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问“该抗议对Boots和其他零售商施加了压力”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的“Boots and other retailers”和“pressure”定位到A段中“put pressure on the UK’s leading pharmacist, Boots, to remove the remedies from sale”，原文提到运动的目标是对Boots施加压力，但未提及对“其他零售商”施加压力。\n解题思路：A段明确指出，该运动的“目标”(aim)是“向英国领先的药妆店Boots施加压力，要求其停止销售”顺势疗法产品。然而，文中仅陈述了运动的意图和目标，并未提供任何信息表明对Boots公司和零售商造成压力。因此，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63929","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is ture, FALSE  if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"63922","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nChoose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of heading below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>&nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"63923","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is ture, FALSE  if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Skeptics planning to hold a demonstration in ‘10.23’ campaign is to against UK’s leading pharmacist, Boots.</strong></p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"63924","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is ture, FALSE  if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>National Health Service budget gained a small portion of homeopathic industry.</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"63925","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is ture, FALSE  if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The example of Caffeine is to present that homeopathy resists the laws of similars.</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"63926","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is ture, FALSE  if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Instilling the idea to people that homeopathy is equal to modern medicine poses danger.</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"63927","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is ture, FALSE  if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Paul Bennett claimed effectiveness of taking the homeopathic medicine is proved.</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"63928","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is ture, FALSE  if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The adoption of homeopathy mainly contributes to the delay of seeking appropriate treatment for themselves or their children.</strong></p>","firstNumber":13},{"id":"63929","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 8-14\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is ture, FALSE  if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The campaign has exerted pressure on Boots and other retailers</strong></p>","firstNumber":14}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Homeopathy: Overdosing on Nothing&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>#&amp;A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>An international protest this week aims to demonstrate the truth about homeopathy – that there’s literally nothing in it, says Martin Robbins at 10.23 am on 30 January, more than 300 activists in the UK, Canada, Australia and the US will take part in a mass homeopathic ‘overdose’. Skeptics will publicly swallow an entire bottle of homeopathic pills to demonstrate to the public that homeopathic remedies, the product of a scientifically unfounded 18th-century ritual, are simply sugar pills. Many of the skeptics will swallow 84 pills of arsenicum album, a homeopathic remedy based on arsenic which is used to treat a range of symptoms, including food poisoning and insomnia. The aim of the ‘10:23’ campaign, led by the Merseyside Skeptics Society, based in Liverpool, UK, is to raise public awareness of just exactly what homeopathyis, and to put pressure on the UK’s leading pharmacist, Boots, to remove the remedies from sale. The campaign is called 10:23 in honor of the Avogadro constant (approximately 6×1023, the number of atoms or molecules in one mole of a substance), of which more later.&amp;#&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>That such a protest is even necessary in 2010 is remarkable, but somehow the homeopathic industry has not only survived into the 21st century, but prospered. In the UK alone more than £40 million is spent annually on homeopathic treatments, with £4 million of this being sucked from the National Health Service budget. Yet the basis for homeopathy defies the laws of physics, and high-quality clinical trials have never been able to demonstrate that it works beyond the placebo effect.&amp;#&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The discipline is based on three ‘laws’; the law of similars, the law of infinitesimals and the law of succession. The law of similars states that something which causes your symptoms will cure your symptoms, so that, for example, as caffeine keeps you awake, it can also be a cure for insomnia. Of course, that makes little sense, since drinking caffeine, well, keeps you awake. Next is the law of infinitesimals, which claims that diluting a substance makes it more potent. Homeopaths start by diluting one volume of their remedy – arsenic oxide, in the case of arsenicum album – in 99 volumes of distilled water or alcohol to create a ‘centesimal’. They then dilute one volume of the centesimal in 99 volumes of water or alcohol, and so on, up to 30 times. Application of Avogadro’s constant tells you that a dose of such a ‘30C’ recipe is vanishingly unlikely to contain even a single molecule of the active ingredient. The third pillar of homeopathy is the law of succession. This states – and I’m not making this up – that by tapping the liquid in a special way during the dilution process, a memory of the active ingredient is somehow imprinted on it. This explains how water is able to carry a memory of arsenic oxide, but apparently not of the contents of your local sewer network.&amp;#&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The final preparation is generally dropped onto a sugar pill which the patient swallows. Homeopaths claim that the application of these three laws results in a remedy that, even though it contains not a single molecule of the original ingredient, somehow carries an ‘energy signature’ of it that nobody can measure or detect. Unsurprisingly, when tested under rigorous scientific conditions, in randomized, controlled and double blind trials, homeopathic remedies have shown to be no better than a placebo. Of course, the placebo effect is quite powerful, but it’s a bit like justifying building a car without any wheels on the basis that you can still enjoy the comfy leather seats and play with the gear shift.&amp;#</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>#&amp;E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Even some retailers who sell the treatments have admitted there is no evidence that they work. In November, Paul Bennett, the superintendent pharmacist at Boots, appeared before the UK parliament’s Commons Science and Technology Committee’s ‘evidence check’ on homoeopathy. He was questioned by Member of Parliament Phil Willis, who asked: ‘Do they work beyond the placebo effect?’ ‘I have no evidence before me to suggest that they are efficacious,’ Bennett replied. He defended Boots’s decision to sell homoeopathic remedies on the grounds of consumer choice. ‘A large number of our consumers actually do believe they are efficacious, but they are licensed medicinal products and, therefore, we believe it is right to make them available,’ he said.&amp;#&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>#&amp;F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>You might agree. You might also argue that homoeopathy is harmless: if people want to part with their money for sugar pills and nobody is breaking the law, why not let them? To some extent that’s true – there’s only so much damage you can do with sugar pills short of feeding them to a diabetic or dropping a large crate of them on someone’s head. However, we believe there is a risk in perpetuating the notion that homoeopathy is equivalent to modern medicine. People may delay seeking appropriate treatment for themselves or their children.&amp;#&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>We accept that we are unlikely to convince the true believers. Homoeopathy has many ways to sidestep awkward questions, such as rejecting the validity of randomized controlled trials, or claiming that homoeopathic remedies only work if you have symptoms of the malady they purport to cure. Our aim is to reach out to the general public with our simple message: ‘There is nothing in it’. Boots and other retailers are perfectly entitled to continue selling homoeopathic remedies if they so wish and consumers are perfectly entitled to keep on buying them. But hopefully the 10:23 campaign will ram home our message to the public. In the 21st century, with decades of progress behind us, it is surreal that governments are prepared to spend millions of tax pounds on homoeopathy. There really is nothing in it.&amp;#</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8839&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8840","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Aqua Product: New Zealand’s Algae Biodiesel","book":"阅读还原集Vol.16","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.16 · Test 1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8840:63930:15","type":"choice","text":"15 It is unnecessary to modify vehicles driven by bio-diesel.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Blended with conventional mineral diesel, bio-diesel can run vehicles without the need for vehicle modifications.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了“使用生物柴油的车辆不需要进行改装”。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词“unnecessary to modify vehicles”和“bio-diesel”，可以在文章中找到相关的句子。在D段中，明确提到“Blended with conventional mineral diesel, bio-diesel can run vehicles without the need for vehicle modifications.”，这句话直接回答了题目的问题。\n解题思路：原文中的这句话，与传统矿物柴油混合后，生物柴油可直接驱动车辆而无需改装。明确说明不需要对车辆进行任何改装。这与题目所问的内容完全一致，因此D段是正确的答案。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63930","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 15-19\nThe reading passage contains seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph stales the following information? Write the appropriate letter A-G, in boxes 15-19 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8840:63930:16","type":"choice","text":"16 Some algae are considered edible plants.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Naturally growing seaweeds are an important source of food, especially in Asia.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问“有些藻类是可食用的植物”，需要找到文章中提到藻类作为食物的段落。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词“algae”和“edible plants”，在文章中寻找藻类被描述为食物的句子。\n解题思路：E段明确提到“Naturally growing seaweeds are an important source of food, especially in Asia.”（自然生长的海藻是重要的食物来源，尤其是在亚洲），并列举了多个国家食用藻类的例子，如中国和日本。因此，E段是正确答案。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63930","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 15-19\nThe reading passage contains seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph stales the following information? Write the appropriate letter A-G, in boxes 15-19 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8840:63930:17","type":"choice","text":"17 Algae could be part of a sustainable and recycled source.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Bio-diesel based on algae could eventually become a sustainable, low cost, cleaner-burning fuel alternative for New Zealand, powering family cars, trucks, buses and boats.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问“藻类能作为可持续和可回收资源的一部分”，需要找到文章中提到该信息的段落。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键词“sustainable”（可持续）和“recycled source”（可回收来源）在文章中定位。\n解题思路：C段明确提到“Bio-diesel based on algae could eventually become a sustainable, low cost, cleaner-burning fuel alternative”，说明藻类生物柴油可以成为可持续的燃料替代品，符合题目中的要求。因此，答案为C。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63930","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 15-19\nThe reading passage contains seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph stales the following information? Write the appropriate letter A-G, in boxes 15-19 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8840:63930:18","type":"choice","text":"18 Algae biodiesel is superior to other bio-fuels in a lot of ways.","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Unlike some bio-fuels which require crops to be specially grown and thereby compete for land use with food production, and use other scarce resources of fuel, chemicals and fertiliser, the source for algae-based biodiesel already exists extensively and the process produces a sustainable net energy gain by capturing free solar energy from the sun.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问哪一段落提到藻类生物柴油在许多方面优于其他生物燃料。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Algae biodiesel\"和\"superior to other bio-fuels\"定位到G段首句，该句明确对比了藻类生物柴油与其他生物燃料的差异。\n解题思路：G段首句通过\"Unlike some bio-fuels\"直接对比了藻类生物柴油与其他生物燃料的不同之处，指出藻类生物柴油无需专门种植、不粮食生产争夺土地、不消耗稀缺资源，且能通过捕捉太阳能实现可持续净能量增益。这些对比充分体现了藻类生物柴油在多方面的优越性，因此G段是正确答案。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63930","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 15-19\nThe reading passage contains seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph stales the following information? Write the appropriate letter A-G, in boxes 15-19 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8840:63930:19","type":"choice","text":"19 Overgrown algae also can be a potential threat to the environment.","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Although algae are good at taking most of the nutrients out of sewage, too many algae can taint the water and make it smell. So, councils have to find a way of cleaning up the excess algae in their sewerage outflows and then either dispose of it or find alternative uses for it.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段落提到“过度生长的藻类也可能对环境构成潜在威胁”。\n定位关键信息：通过“overgrown algae”和“potential threat to the environment”定位，原文中F段提到“too many algae can taint the water and make it smell”，明确指出过量藻类会污染水质并产生气味，这是对环境的潜在威胁。\n解题思路：原文F段直接描述了藻类过度生长的负面影响，过量的藻类会污染水质并产生异味，这与题目中的“potential threat to the environment”完全对应。因此，F段是正确答案。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63930","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 15-19\nThe reading passage contains seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph stales the following information? Write the appropriate letter A-G, in boxes 15-19 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8840:63931:20","type":"fill","text":"填写第 20 空","answer":"fuel","acceptedAnswers":["fuel"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Bio-diesel based on algae could eventually become a sustainable, low cost, cleaner-burning fuel alternative for New Zealand, powering family cars, trucks, buses and boats.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求完成摘要，问的是生物柴油在新西兰的替代了什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词藻类生物柴油（bio-diesel based on algae）、新西兰（New Zealand）定位到C段的相关句子。\n解题思路：根据C段第一句，藻类生物柴油有望成为新西兰可持续、低成本、更清洁的燃料替代品，可为家用汽车、卡车、公交车和船只提供动力。可知，藻类生物柴油在新西兰可以替代燃料，因此填fuel。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63931","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8840:63932:21","type":"fill","text":"填写第 21 空","answer":"power","acceptedAnswers":["power"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Bio-diesel based on algae could eventually become a sustainable, low cost, cleaner-burning fuel alternative for New Zealand, powering family cars, trucks, buses and boats.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是这种生物柴油可以用来做什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"vehicles such as cars and boats\"可以定位到C段中提到的\"powering family cars, trucks, buses and boats\"这一信息。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到基于藻类的生物柴油可以作为一种可持续、低成本、清洁燃烧的燃料替代品，用于驱动家庭汽车、卡车、公共汽车和船只。题目中的对应的是原文中的\"powering\"，因此答案为\"power\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63932","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8840:63933:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"waste streams","acceptedAnswers":["waste streams"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Algae are also readily available and produced in huge volumes in nutrient-rich waste streams such as at the settling ponds of Effluent Management Systems (EMS).\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求填写藻类可以从富含营养物质的什么中获取。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"algae\"（藻类）、\"obtained from\"（从...获取）和\"nutrient materials\"（营养物质）。通过\"algae\"和\"nutrient\"定位到C段，找到描述藻类来源的句子。\n解题思路：原文提到藻类\"readily available and produced in huge volumes in nutrient-rich waste streams\"（在富含营养物质的废水中大量生长），其中\"nutrient-rich waste streams\"与题目中的\"nutrient materials\"对应，因此答案为\"water streams\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63933","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8840:63934:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"main contaminant","acceptedAnswers":["main contaminant"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The breakthrough comes after technology start-up, Aquaflow, agreed to undertake a pilot with Marlborough District Council late last year to extract algae from the settling ponds of its EMS based in Blenheim. By removing the main contaminant to use as a fuel feedstock, Aquaflow is also helping clean up the council’s water discharge – a process known as bio-remediation.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是随着技术的突破，提取藻类后，从沉淀池中移除了什么物质。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"extracted\"和\"settling ponds\"可以定位到C段，该段提到了从沉淀池中提取藻类的过程。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，通过去除主要污染物并将其转化为燃料原料，Aquaflow公司同时助力清理市政污水排放——这一过程被称为生物修复。说明是从沉淀池中去除了主要污染物，因此答案为\"main contaminate\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63934","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8840:63935:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"harvesting","acceptedAnswers":["harvesting"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Dairy farmers, and many food processors too, can benefit in similar ways by applying the harvesting technology to their nutrient-rich waste streams.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是奶农和许多食品加工商可以采用什么样的技术。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"dairy farmers\"和\"food processors\"定位到C段，找到提到这两类人群的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文句子，奶农和众多食品加工商也可通过将该收获技术应用于富含营养的废水流，获得类似效益。可以确定使用了收获技术，因此答案为\"harvesting\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63935","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8840:63936:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"Government B5","acceptedAnswers":["Government B5"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Fuel derived from algae can also help meet the Government B5 (5% blended) target, with the prospect of this increase over time as bio-fuel production increases.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问生物柴油车辆需要满足什么样的环境标准。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“environmental standard”（环境标准）和“bio-diesel vehicles”（生物柴油车辆），定位到D段相关句子。\n解题思路：原文中D段明确提到，这种源自藻类的燃料还能助力实现政府设定的B5标准（5%混合比例）目标，随着生物燃料产量的提升，这一比例有望逐步提高。说明藻类燃料可以满足政府B5标准，因此，答案为\"Government B5\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63936","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 25-27\nChoose words from the passage to answer the questions 25-27. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8840:63937:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"Capacity/capacity","acceptedAnswers":["Capacity","capacity"],"explanation":"原文答案句： 'Our next step is to increase capacity to produce one million litres of bio-diesel from the Marlborough sewerage ponds over the next year,' says Leay.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目询问Aquaflow公司在未来几年的近期计划是跟什么有关。\n定位关键信息： 题目中的关键词是 \"immediate plan\" 和 \"coming years\"定位到D段相关句子。\n解题思路：D段中提到，利伊表示：“我们的下一步计划是在未来一年内，将马尔伯勒污水处理池的生物柴油生产能力提升至百万升。说明Aquaflow公司在未来几年的近期计划是跟提升生产量有关，因此，答案为“capacity”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63937","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 25-27\nChoose words from the passage to answer the questions 25-27. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8840:63938:27","type":"fill","text":"填写第 27 空","answer":"photosynthesis/Photosynthesis","acceptedAnswers":["photosynthesis","Photosynthesis"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Algae are the simplest plant organisms that convert sunlight and carbon dioxide in the air around us into stored energy through the well-understood process of photosynthesis.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是藻类通过什么过程获取和储存能量。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"obtain and store energy\"定位到F段中描述藻类获取和储存能量的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，藻类是最简单的植物生物，它们通过光合作用过程，将阳光和空气中的二氧化碳转化为储存的能量。因此，正确答案应为\"photosynthesis\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63938","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 25-27\nChoose words from the passage to answer the questions 25-27. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS for each answer.","maxWords":3}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"63930","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 15-19\nThe reading passage contains seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph stales the following information? Write the appropriate letter A-G, in boxes 15-19 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.","html":"<p><strong>15</strong> It is unnecessary to modify vehicles driven by bio-diesel. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[15] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":15},{"id":"63931","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Bio-diesel based on algae could become a substitute for <strong>20</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong> in New Zealand. <br/></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"63932","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>It\ncould be used to <strong>21</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong> vehicles such as cars and boats.</p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"63933","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>As a result, billions of litres\nof bio-diesel are required worldwide each year. Algae can be obtained from <strong>22</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong> with\nnutrient materials.</p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"63934","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>With the technology breakthrough, algae are extracted and the <strong>23</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong>\nis removed from the settling ponds.</p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"63935","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Dairy farmers and many food processors can adopt such <strong>24</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> technology.</p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"63936","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 25-27\nChoose words from the passage to answer the questions 25-27. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>25</strong> What environmental standard would bio-diesel vehicles are to meet? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"63937","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 25-27\nChoose words from the passage to answer the questions 25-27. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>26</strong> What is to do like the immediate plan for coming years for Aquaflow? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":26},{"id":"63938","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 25-27\nChoose words from the passage to answer the questions 25-27. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>27</strong> Through what kind of process do algae obtain and store energy? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[27] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":27}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: none;\"><strong>Aqua Product: New Zealand’s Algae Biodiesel</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"text-decoration: none;\"><strong><br/></strong></span></p><p><span style=\"text-decoration: none;\"><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><br/></p><p>The world’s first wild algae biodiesel, produced in New Zealand by Aquaflow Bionomic Corporation, was successfully test-driven in Wellington by the Minister for Energy and Climate Change Issues, David Parker. In front of a crowd of invited guests, media and members of the public, the Minister filled up a diesel-powered Land Rover with Aquaflow B5 blend bio-diesel and then drove the car around the forecourt of Parliament Buildings in Central Wellington. Green Party co-leader, Jeanette Fitzsimons was also on board. Marlborough-based Aquaflow announced on May 2006 that it had produced the world’s first biodiesel derived from wild microalgae sourced from local sewage ponds.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘We believe we are the first company in the world to test drive a car powered by wild algae-based biodiesel. This will come as a surprise to some international bio-diesel industry people who believe that this break-through is still years away,’ explains Aquaflow spokesperson Barrie Leay. ‘A bunch of inventive Kiwis and an Aussie have developed this fuel in just over a year’, he comments, ‘This is a huge opportunity for New Zealand and a great credit to the team of people who saw the potential in this technology from day one.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Bio-diesel based on algae could eventually become a sustainable, low cost, cleaner-burning fuel alternative for New Zealand, powering family cars, trucks, buses and boats. It can also be used for other purposes such as heating or distributed electricity generation. There is now a global demand for billions of litres of biodiesel per year. Algae are also readily available and produced in huge volumes in nutrient-rich waste streams such as at the settling ponds of Effluent Management Systems (EMS). It is a renewable indigenous resource ideally suited to the production of fuel and other useful by-products. The breakthrough comes after technology start-up, Aquaflow, agreed to undertake a pilot with Marlborough District Council late last year to extract algae from the settling ponds of its EMS based in Blenheim. By removing the main contaminant to use as a fuel feedstock, Aquaflow is also helping clean up the council’s water discharge – a process known as bio-remediation. Dairy farmers, and many food processors too, can benefit in similar ways by applying the harvesting technology to their nutrient-rich waste streams.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Blended with conventional mineral diesel, bio-diesel can run vehicles without the need for vehicle modifications. Fuel derived from algae can also help meet the Government B5 (5% blended) target, with the prospect of this increase over time as bio-fuel production increases. &#39;Our next step is to increase capacity to produce one million litres of bio-diesel from the Marlborough sewerage ponds over the next year,&#39; says Leay. Aquaflow will launch a prospectus pre-Christmas as the company has already attracted considerable interest from potential investors. The test drive bio-diesel was used successfully in a static engine test at Massey University’s Wellington campus on Monday, December 11.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Today Algae are used by humans in many ways; for example, as fertilizers, soil conditioners and livestock feed. Aquatic and microscopic species are cultured in clear tanks or ponds and are either harvested or used to treat effluents pumped through the ponds. Algaculture on a large scale is an important type of aquaculture in some places. Naturally growing seaweeds are an important source of food, especially in Asia. They provide many vitamins including A, B, B2, B6, niacin and C, and are rich in iodine, potassium, iron, magnesium and calcium. In addition, commercially cultivated microalgae, including both Algae and Cyan-bacteria, are marketed as nutritional supplements, such as Spirulina, Chlorella and the Vitamin-C supplement, Dunaliella, high in beta-carotene. Algae are national foods of many nations: China consumes more than 70 species, including fat choy, a cyanobacterium considered a vegetable; Japan, over 20 species. The natural pigments produced by algae can be used as an alternative to chemical dyes and coloring agents.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Algae are the simplest plant organisms that convert sunlight and carbon dioxide in the air around us into stored energy through the well-understood process of photosynthesis. Algae are rich in lipids and other combustible elements and Aquaflow is developing technology that will allow these elements to be extracted in a cost-effective way. The proposed process is the subject of a provisional patent. Although algae are good at taking most of the nutrients out of sewage, too many algae can taint the water and make it smell. So, councils have to find a way of cleaning up the excess algae in their sewerage outflows and then either dispose of it or find alternative uses for it. And that’s where Aquaflow comes in.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Unlike some bio-fuels which require crops to be specially grown and thereby compete for land use with food production, and use other scarce resources of fuel, chemicals and fertiliser, the source for algae-based biodiesel already exists extensively and the process produces a sustainable net energy gain by capturing free solar energy from the sun.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8840&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8841","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Asian Space – Satellite Technology","book":"阅读还原集Vol.16","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.16 · Test 1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8841:63939:28","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：These ancient rockets stand in stark contrast to the present-day Chinese rocket launch vehicles, called the ‘Long March’, intended to place a Chinese astronaut in space by 2005 and, perhaps, to achieve a Chinese moon-landing by the end of the decade.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求为A段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过段落中的关键词\"ancient rockets\"和\"present-day Chinese rocket launch vehicles\"定位到A段的核心内容。\n解题思路：A段主要描述了中国古代“火箭”与现代中国火箭的对比和关联。标题\"An ancient invention which is related to the future\"（一项与未来相关的古代发明）准确概括了段落内容，突出了古代发明对未来技术的影响，因此选择改标题作为A段标题。","options":["Western countries provide essential assistance","Unbalanced development for an essential space technology","Innovative application compelled by competition","An ancient invention which is related to the future","Military purpose of the satellite","Rockets for application in ancient China","Space development in Asia in the past","Non-technology factors counts","Competitive edge gained by more economically feasible satellite"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"63939","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-G Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-G from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8841:63939:29","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In the last decade, there has been a dramatic growth in space activities in Asia both in the utilization of space-based services and the production of satellites and launchers. This rapid expansion has led many commentators and analysts to predict that Asia will become a world space power.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求为B段选择正确的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读B段，可以发现段落主要讲述了亚洲在太空活动方面的快速增长，包括太空服务的利用和卫星及发射器的生产，以及这种快速扩张如何导致许多评论家和分析师预测亚洲将成为世界太空的中坚力量。\n解题思路：根据B段的内容，可以确定其核心主题是过去十年内亚洲在太空领域的发展。因此，选择与这一主题相符的标题，即“Space development in Asia in the past”（亚洲航天事业的过往发展）。","options":["Western countries provide essential assistance","Unbalanced development for an essential space technology","Innovative application compelled by competition","An ancient invention which is related to the future","Military purpose of the satellite","Rockets for application in ancient China","Space development in Asia in the past","Non-technology factors counts","Competitive edge gained by more economically feasible satellite"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"63939","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-G Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-G from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8841:63939:30","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：New and innovative uses for satellites are constantly being explored with potential revolutionary effects, such as in the field of health and telemedicine, distance education, crime prevention (piracy on the high seas), food and agricultural planning and production (rice crop monitoring). Space in Asia is very much influenced by the competitive commercial space sector, the emergence of low-cost mini-satellites, and the globalization of industrial and financial markets.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求为C段选择一个正确的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读C段，段落的主要内容是关于卫星的新用途和亚洲太空行业发展的影响因素。\n解题思路：C段首先提到卫星的新用途，如健康、远程教育、犯罪预防等，然后提到，亚洲航天领域深受竞争激烈的商业航天产业、低成本微型卫星的兴起以及工业金融市场的全球化影响。因此，C段的主要内容是关于卫星的新用途和亚洲太空行业发展的影响因素，对应标题“Innovative application compelled by competition”（竞争驱动创新应用）。","options":["Western countries provide essential assistance","Unbalanced development for an essential space technology","Innovative application compelled by competition","An ancient invention which is related to the future","Military purpose of the satellite","Rockets for application in ancient China","Space development in Asia in the past","Non-technology factors counts","Competitive edge gained by more economically feasible satellite"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"63939","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-G Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-G from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8841:63939:31","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：ASEAN members, unlike Japan, China, and India, do not have their own remote sensing satellites, however, most of its member nations have facilities to receive, process, and interpret such data from American and European satellites.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求为E段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的段落号E定位到文章的E段，仔细阅读该段内容，寻找能够概括段落主旨的关键信息。\n解题思路：段落E的核心内容是讨论遥感技术。它首先指出遥感是该地区最受关注的空间应用，但紧接着通过对比，揭示了发展的不平衡性：日本、中国和印度拥有自己的遥感卫星，而东盟（ASEAN）成员国则没有，大多只能依赖接收和处理欧美卫星的数据。这种在同一关键技术领域内，不同国家群体之间存在显著差距的状况，准确地对应了标题 Unbalanced development for an essential space technology（一项关键空间技术的不平衡发展）。","options":["Western countries provide essential assistance","Unbalanced development for an essential space technology","Innovative application compelled by competition","An ancient invention which is related to the future","Military purpose of the satellite","Rockets for application in ancient China","Space development in Asia in the past","Non-technology factors counts","Competitive edge gained by more economically feasible satellite"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"63939","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-G Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-G from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8841:63939:32","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The global increase of technology transfer mechanisms and use of readily available commercial technology to replace costly space and military-standard components may very well result in a highly competitive Asian satellite manufacturing industry.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求为F段选择正确的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过题目，定位到文章的F段。\n解题思路：段落F的核心内容是讨论小卫星的出现如何通过大幅降低成本（“drastically reduce costs”），使亚洲国家能够快速提升太空行业能力，并可能形成一个极具竞争力的卫星制造产业。这描述了亚洲国家通过采用更经济可行的卫星（“more economically feasible satellite”）获得了竞争优势（“Competitive edge”）。因此，它与标题“Competitive edge gained by more economically feasible satellite”（通过更经济可行的卫星获得竞争优势）匹配。","options":["Western countries provide essential assistance","Unbalanced development for an essential space technology","Innovative application compelled by competition","An ancient invention which is related to the future","Military purpose of the satellite","Rockets for application in ancient China","Space development in Asia in the past","Non-technology factors counts","Competitive edge gained by more economically feasible satellite"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"63939","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-G Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-G from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8841:63940:33","type":"choice","text":"33 Why remote-photographic technology is used to resolve environmental problems?","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Asia and Southeast Asia, in particular, suffers from a long list of recurrent large-scale environmental problems including storms and flooding, forest fires and deforestation, and crop failures. Thus the space application that has attracted the most attention in this region is remote sensing. Remote sensing satellites equipped with instruments to take photographs of the ground at different wavelengths provide essential information for natural resource accounting, environmental management, disaster prevention and monitoring, land-use mapping, and sustainable development planning.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问为什么遥感摄影技术被用来解决环境问题。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"remote-photographic technology\"和\"environmental problems\"定位到F段，该段提到遥感技术在环境管理、灾害预防和监测等方面的应用。\n解题思路：F段明确指出,亚洲尤其是东南亚地区长期面临一系列反复出现的大规模环境问题，所以遥感技术至关重要，可以为自然资源核算、环境管理、灾害预防监测、土地利用制图及可持续发展规划提供了关键数据支持。说明是因为亚洲地区的自然灾害严重，所以使用遥感技术解决相关问题。因此，F选项\"Because disasters such as bush fire happened in Southeast Asia.\"回答了题目所问的原因。","options":["Because it helps administrate the crops.","Because there are some unapproachable areas.","Because the economic level in that area is low.","Because there are influences from some other social factors.","Because it can be used in non-peaceful purpose.","Because disasters such as bush fire happened in Southeast Asia."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"63940","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-36\nMatch the following reasons for each question according to the information given in the passage Write the appropriate letter A-F in boxes 33-36 on your answer sheet.\nA Because it helps administrate the crops.\nB Because there are some unapproachable areas.\nC Because the economic level in that area is low.\nD Because there are influences from some other social factors.\nE Because it can be used in non-peaceful purpose.\nF Because disasters such as bush fire happened in Southeast Asia."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8841:63940:34","type":"choice","text":"34 Why satellites technology is used in the medicine area?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：New and innovative uses for satellites are constantly being explored with potential revolutionary effects, such as in the field of health and telemedicine, distance education, crime prevention (piracy on the high seas), food and agricultural planning and production (rice crop monitoring).\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是卫星技术在医疗领域应用的原因。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"satellites technology\"和\"medicine area\"定位到C段中提到\"health and telemedicine\"的句子。\n解题思路：原文中提到，卫星技术正不断探索着创新应用，这些应用可能带来革命性变革，例如在医疗健康、远程医疗、远程教育、海上犯罪预防（打击公海盗版）、粮食与农业规划生产（水稻作物监测）等领域。可以推断，卫星技术的应用可以实现远程医疗，让偏远、交通不便地区的人们也能享受到医疗服务。因此，答案为B（因为有些区域无法靠近）。","options":["Because it helps administrate the crops.","Because there are some unapproachable areas.","Because the economic level in that area is low.","Because there are influences from some other social factors.","Because it can be used in non-peaceful purpose.","Because disasters such as bush fire happened in Southeast Asia."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"63940","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-36\nMatch the following reasons for each question according to the information given in the passage Write the appropriate letter A-F in boxes 33-36 on your answer sheet.\nA Because it helps administrate the crops.\nB Because there are some unapproachable areas.\nC Because the economic level in that area is low.\nD Because there are influences from some other social factors.\nE Because it can be used in non-peaceful purpose.\nF Because disasters such as bush fire happened in Southeast Asia."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8841:63940:35","type":"choice","text":"35 Why Asian countries satellite technology is limited for development?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Additionally, nations in Southeast Asia as well as those bordering the Indian subcontinent (Nepal, Pakistan, and Bangladesh), have, or are starting to develop indigenous space programmes. The Association of Southeastian Nations (ASEAN) has, in varying degrees, embraced space applications using foreign technology and over the past five years or so its space activities have been expanding. In the development of this technology, many non-technical factors, such as economics, politics, culture, and history, interact and play important roles, which in turn affect Asian technology.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是亚洲国家卫星技术发展受限的原因。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"limited for development\"可以定位到D段中提到的影响亚洲技术发展的非技术因素，如经济、政治、文化、历史等。\n解题思路：原文中提到，目前，日本、中国和印度这三个亚洲国家已具备完整的航天全产业链，但更多亚洲国家（如东盟成员国）的太空技术发展仍相对有限。这种发展不平衡正是受到各国不同的经济水平、政治环境、文化背景和历史条件等社会因素制约，这些因素共同限制了亚洲地区卫星技术的整体发展水平。因此，选择D项。","options":["Because it helps administrate the crops.","Because there are some unapproachable areas.","Because the economic level in that area is low.","Because there are influences from some other social factors.","Because it can be used in non-peaceful purpose.","Because disasters such as bush fire happened in Southeast Asia."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"63940","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-36\nMatch the following reasons for each question according to the information given in the passage Write the appropriate letter A-F in boxes 33-36 on your answer sheet.\nA Because it helps administrate the crops.\nB Because there are some unapproachable areas.\nC Because the economic level in that area is low.\nD Because there are influences from some other social factors.\nE Because it can be used in non-peaceful purpose.\nF Because disasters such as bush fire happened in Southeast Asia."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8841:63940:36","type":"choice","text":"36 Why satellites technology is deployed in an agricultural area?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：New and innovative uses for satellites are constantly being explored with potential revolutionary effects, such as in the field of health and telemedicine, distance education, crime prevention (piracy on the high seas), food and agricultural planning and production (rice crop monitoring).\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目询问“为什么卫星技术被应用于农业领域？”\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的“satellites technology”和“agricultural area”定位至文中提及卫星在农业领域应用的句子。\n解题思路：原文C段明确列举了卫星的新用途，其中在农业方面的具体应用是“food and agricultural planning and production (rice crop monitoring)”，即粮食和农业规划与生产（水稻作物监测）。卫星通过监测作物来帮助进行农业规划和管理，这直接对应了选项A中的“helps administrate the crops”（帮助管理作物）。","options":["Because it helps administrate the crops.","Because there are some unapproachable areas.","Because the economic level in that area is low.","Because there are influences from some other social factors.","Because it can be used in non-peaceful purpose.","Because disasters such as bush fire happened in Southeast Asia."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"63940","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-36\nMatch the following reasons for each question according to the information given in the passage Write the appropriate letter A-F in boxes 33-36 on your answer sheet.\nA Because it helps administrate the crops.\nB Because there are some unapproachable areas.\nC Because the economic level in that area is low.\nD Because there are influences from some other social factors.\nE Because it can be used in non-peaceful purpose.\nF Because disasters such as bush fire happened in Southeast Asia."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8841:63941:37","type":"choice","text":"Ancient China had already deployed rockets as a military purpose as early as 500 years ago.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Rocket technology has progressed considerably since the days of ‘fire arrows’ (bamboo poles filled with gunpowder) first used in China around 500 BC, and, during the Sung Dynasty, to repel Mongol invaders at the battle of Kaifeng (Kai-fung fu) in AD 1232.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问“古代中国早在500年前就已经将火箭用于军事目的”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“ancient China”和“500 years ago”定位到A段第一句。\n解题思路：原文第一段“火箭”的产生最早追溯到500BC，并在公元1232年的宋代使用火箭来抵御蒙古入侵者。题目中的“500 years ago”指的是500年前，而原文明确指出火箭技术在公元前500年和公元1232年就已经用于军事目的。因此，题目中的时间表述与原文不符，故答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63941","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8841:63942:38","type":"choice","text":"Space technology has enhanced the literacy of Asia.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：无\n对应段落：无\n审题：题目问的是“空间技术提高了亚洲地区人们的文化水平”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“space technology”和“literacy of Asia”在文章中定位答案。\n解题思路：题目核心是探讨太空技术是否对文化水平产生了提升作用。原文C段虽然提到卫星技术可用于“远程教育”，但全文没有任何一处将太空技术与文化水平联系起来。文中既未确认也未否认这种影响的存在。因此，题目陈述的信息在文中没有依据，判断为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63942","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8841:63943:39","type":"choice","text":"Photos taken by satellites with certain technology help predict some natural catastrophes prevention\nand surveillance.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Remote sensing satellites equipped with instruments to take photographs of the ground at different wavelengths provide essential information for natural resource accounting, environmental management, disaster prevention and monitoring, land-use mapping, and sustainable development planning.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“采用特定技术的卫星拍摄的照片有助于预测、预防和监测某些自然灾害”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“Photos taken by satellites with certain technology”和“natural catastrophes prevention and surveillance”可以定位到E段中关于遥感卫星的描述。\n解题思路：F段明确提到，配备不同波长地面成像仪器的遥感卫星，为自然资源核算、环境管理、灾害预防监测、土地利用制图及可持续发展规划提供了关键数据。因此，题目中的陈述与文章信息一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63943","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8841:63944:40","type":"choice","text":"Commercial competition constitutes a boosting factor to Asian technology development.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Space in Asia is very much influenced by the competitive commercial space sector, the emergence of low-cost mini-satellites, and the globalization of industrial and financial markets.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问商业竞争推动亚洲技术发展，这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"Commercial competition\"和\"boosting factor\"在文章中定位，发现C段提到了\"competitive commercial space sector\"。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，亚洲航天领域深受竞争激烈的商业航天产业、低成本微型卫星的兴起以及工业金融市场的全球化影响。说明商业竞争是推动亚洲技术发展的因素之一，因此题目说法与原文一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63944","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"63939","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs, A-G Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A-G from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"63940","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-36\nMatch the following reasons for each question according to the information given in the passage Write the appropriate letter A-F in boxes 33-36 on your answer sheet.\nA Because it helps administrate the crops.\nB Because there are some unapproachable areas.\nC Because the economic level in that area is low.\nD Because there are influences from some other social factors.\nE Because it can be used in non-peaceful purpose.\nF Because disasters such as bush fire happened in Southeast Asia.","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> Because it helps administrate the crops. <br/></p><p><strong>B</strong> Because there are some unapproachable areas. <br/></p><p><strong>C</strong> Because the economic level in that area is low. <br/></p><p><strong>D</strong> Because there are influences from some other social factors. <br/></p><p><strong>E</strong> Because it can be used in non-peaceful purpose. <br/></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>F</strong> Because disasters such as bush fire happened in Southeast Asia. <br/></p><p><strong>33</strong> Why remote-photographic technology is used to resolve environmental problems? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[33] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"63941","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Ancient China had already deployed rockets as a military purpose as early as 500 years ago.</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"63942","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Space technology has enhanced the literacy of Asia.</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"63943","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Photos taken by satellites with certain technology help predict some natural catastrophes prevention\nand surveillance.</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"63944","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Commercial competition constitutes a boosting factor to Asian technology development.</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Asian Space – Satellite Technology</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The space-age began with the launch of the Russian artificial satellite Sputnik in 1957 and developed further with the race to the moon between the United States and Russia. This rivalry was characterized by advanced technology and huge budgets. In this process, there were spectacular successes, some failures, but also many spin-offs.</p><p><br/></p><p>Europe, Japan, China, and India quickly joined this space club of the superpowers. With the advent of relatively low-cost high-performance mini-satellites and launchers, the acquisition of indigenous space capabilities by smaller nations in Asia has become possible. How, in what manner, and for what purpose will these capabilities be realized?</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Rocket technology has progressed considerably since the days of ‘fire arrows’ (bamboo poles filled with gunpowder) first used in China around 500 BC, and, during the Sung Dynasty, to repel Mongol invaders at the battle of Kaifeng (Kai-fung fu) in AD 1232. These ancient rockets stand in stark contrast to the present-day Chinese rocket launch vehicles, called the ‘Long March’, intended to place a Chinese astronaut in space by 2005 and, perhaps, to achieve a Chinese moon-landing by the end of the decade.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In the last decade, there has been a dramatic growth in space activities in Asia both in the utilization of spacebased services and the production of satellites and launchers. This rapid expansion has led many commentators and analysts to predict that Asia will become a world space power. The space-age has had dramatic effects worldwide with direct developments in space technology influencing telecommunications, meteorological forecasting, earth resource and environmental monitoring, and disaster mitigation (flood, forest fires, and oil spills). Asian nations have been particularly eager to embrace these developments.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>New and innovative uses for satellites are constantly being explored with potential revolutionary effects, such as in the field of health and telemedicine, distance education, crime prevention (piracy on the high seas), food and agricultural planning and production (rice crop monitoring). Space in Asia is very much influenced by the competitive commercial space sector, the emergence of low-cost mini-satellites, and the globalization of industrial and financial markets. It is not evident how Asian space will develop in the coming decades in the face of these trends. It is, however, important to understand and assess the factors and forces that shape Asian space activities and development in determining its possible consequences for the region.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>At present, three Asian nations, Japan, China, and India, have comprehensive end-to-end space capabilities and possess a complete space infrastructure: space technology, satellite manufacturing, rockets, and spaceports. Already self-sufficient in terms of satellite design and manufacturing, South Korea is currently attempting to join their ranks with its plans to develop a launch site and spaceport. Additionally, nations in Southeast Asia as well as those bordering the Indian subcontinent (Nepal, Pakistan, and Bangladesh), have, or are starting to develop indigenous space programmes. The Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) has, in varying degrees, embraced space applications using foreign technology and over the past five years or so its space activities have been expanding. Southeast Asia is predicted to become the largest and fastest-growing market for commercial space products and applications, driven by telecommunications (mobile and fixed services), the Internet, and remote sensing applications. In the development of this technology, many non-technical factors, such as economics, politics, culture, and history, interact and play important roles, which in turn affect Asian technology.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Asia and Southeast Asia, in particular, suffers from a long list of recurrent large-scale environmental problems including storms and flooding, forest fires and deforestation, and crop failures. Thus the space application that has attracted the most attention in this region is remote sensing. Remote sensing satellites equipped with instruments to take photographs of the ground at different wavelengths provide essential information for natural resource accounting, environmental management, disaster prevention and monitoring, land-use mapping, and sustainable development planning. Progress in these applications has been rapid and impressive. ASEAN members, unlike Japan, China, and India, do not have their own remote sensing satellites, however, most of its member nations have facilities to receive, process, and interpret such data from American and European satellites. In particular, Thailand, Malaysia, and Singapore have world-class remote sensing processing facilities and research programmes. ASEAN has plans to develop (and launch) its own satellites and in particular remote sensing satellites. Japan is regarded as the dominant space power in Asia and its record of successes and quality of technologies are equal to those of the West. In view of the technological challenges and high risks involved in space activities, a very long, and expensive, the learning curve has been followed to obtain those successes achieved. Japan, s satellite manufacturing was based on the old and traditional defense and military procurement methodologies as practiced in the US and Europe.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In recent years there have been fundamental changes in the way satellites are designed and built to drastically reduce costs. The emergence of ‘small satellites’ and their quick adoption by Asian countries as a way to develop low-cost satellite technology and rapidly establish a space capability has given these countries the possibility to shorten their learning curve by a decade or more. The global increase of technology transfer mechanisms and use of readily available commercial technology to replace costly space and military-standard components may very well result in a highly competitive Asian satellite manufacturing industry.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The laws of physics are the same in Tokyo as in Toulouse, and the principles of electronics and mechanics know no political or cultural boundaries. However, no such immutability applies to engineer practices and management; they are very much influenced by education, culture, and history. These factors, in turn, have an effect on costs, lead times, product designs and, eventually, international sales. Many Asian nations are sending their engineers to be trained in the West. Highly experienced, they return to work in the growing Asian space industry. Will this acquisition of technical expertise, coupled perhaps with the world-renowned Japanese manufacturing and management techniques, be applied to build world-class satellites and reduce costs?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8841&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8823","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 The Mozart Effect","book":"阅读还原集Vol.15","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.15 · Test 4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8823:63814:1","type":"choice","text":"1 Music influences brain development of baby.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Neuroscientists suspect that music can actually help build and strengthen connections between neurons in the cerebral cortex in a process similar to what occurs in brain development despite its type. When a baby is born, certain connections have already been made – like connections for heartbeat and breathing. As new information is learned and motor skills develop, new neural connections are formed. Neurons that are not used will eventually die while those used repeatedly will form strong connections.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段落提到了音乐影响婴儿大脑发育。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Music influences brain development of baby\"定位，在D段中找到与婴儿大脑发育相关的句子。\n解题思路：D段详细描述了婴儿大脑发育过程中神经连接的形成，提到了\"neural connections\"和\"visual cortex\"，与题目中的\"brain development of baby\"对应。此外，D段还提到音乐可以帮助建立和加强神经连接，因此D段包含了题目所问的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"63814","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8823:63814:2","type":"choice","text":"2 Popularity of public to the introduction of Mozart Effect.","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Furthermore, many people are critical of the role the media had in turning an isolated study into a trend for parents and music educators. After Mozart Effect was published to the public, the sales of Mozart CDs stayed on the top of the hit list for three weeks.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求找到描述“公众对莫扎特效应反响热烈”这一信息的段落。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"popularity\", \"public\", \"introduction of Mozart Effect\" 定位到文中描述媒体和公众对莫扎特效应反响的句子。\n解题思路：段落G中，原文明确指出，媒体将一项孤立的研究变成了“一种趋势”，并且在“莫扎特效应被公之于众后，莫扎特CD的销量在热门榜单上停留了三周”。这直接描述了公众在接触到莫扎特效应这个概念后，所产生的热烈反响和消费行为，证明了其流行度。因此，包含此信息的段落是G。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"63814","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8823:63814:3","type":"choice","text":"3 Description of the pioneer experiment of a person.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Frances H. Rauscher, Ph.D., first demonstrated the correlation between music and learning in an experiment in 1993. His experiments indicated that a 10 minute dose of Mozart could temporarily boost intelligence.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段描述了某个人进行的先驱实验。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"pioneer experiment\"（先驱实验）和\"person\"（人），在文章中寻找描述某个人进行早期实验的段落。\n解题思路：B段明确提到了Frances H. Rauscher博士在1993年首次通过实验展示了音乐与学习之间的相关性，并指出他的实验表明听莫扎特的音乐可以暂时提高智力。这符合题目中的描述。因此，答案为B。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"63814","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8823:63814:4","type":"choice","text":"4 Music is helpful as a healing method in some places.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In Japan, compilations of music are used as medication, of sorts. For example, if you want to cure a headache or migraine, the album suggested Mendelssohn’s ‘Spring Song,’ Dvorak’s ‘Humoresque,’ or part of George Gershwin’s ‘An American in Paris’ (Campbell,1998).\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求找到描述“在某些地方，音乐作为一种疗愈方式颇具成效”这一信息的段落。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"music is helpful\", \"healing method\", \"in some places\" 定位到文中描述音乐被用作治疗手段的具体例子。\n解题思路：段落A中，原文明确给出了一个具体的地点（日本）和具体的治疗应用（用特定的音乐专辑来治疗头痛或偏头痛）契合“在某些地方，音乐作为一种疗愈方式颇具成效”这一描述。因此，包含此信息的段落是A。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"63814","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8823:63814:5","type":"choice","text":"5 Learning needs other qualities though.","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Many people accredit the advanced learning of some children who take music lessons to other personality traits, such as motivation and persistence, which is required in all types of learning. There have also been claims of that influencing the results of some experiments.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了“尽管如此，学习需要其他特质”。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“Learning needs other qualities though”，可以通过“learning”、“other qualities”和“though”等词定位到文章中讨论学习需要其他品质的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句“Many people accredit the advanced learning of some children who take music lessons to other personality traits, such as motivation and persistence, which is required in all types of learning.”可知，有些人将一些上音乐课的孩子的先进学习归因于其他人格特质，如动机和毅力，而这些特质在所有类型的学习中都是必需的。与题目要求一致。因此，答案为F。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"63814","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8823:63815:6","type":"fill","text":"填写第 6 空","answer":"short","acceptedAnswers":["short"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Groups of students were given intelligence tests after listening to silence, relaxation tapes, or Mozart’s Sonata for Two Pianos in D Major for a short time.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是在Frances Rauscher的实验中，参与者被测试前沉浸在这种音乐多长时间。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Frances Rauscher\"和\"music\"定位到B段第一句，找到实验中音乐持续的时间描述。\n解题思路：原文提到，在短暂聆听寂静环境、放松磁带或莫扎特《D大调双钢琴奏鸣曲》后，各组学生接受了智力测试。原文明确指出是短暂时间，因此，答案为short。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63815","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-8\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-8 on your answer sheet","maxWords":3},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8823:63816:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"complex, non-repetitive","acceptedAnswers":["complex, non-repetitive"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Rauscher hypothesized that ‘listening to complex, non-repetitive music, like Mozart, may simulate neural pathways that are important in thinking’ (Castleman, 1994).\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问Rauscher认为表现提升与莫扎特音乐的什么性质有关。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的“Rauscher”“enhancement of their performance”和“nature of Mozart’s music”定位到B段Rauscher的假设句。\n解题思路：原文明确提到Rauscher认为“complex, non-repetitive music”（复杂且非重复的音乐）可能激活思维相关的神经通路，题目中的“nature of Mozart’s music”对应原文的“complex, non-repetitive”，因此答案为“complex, non-repetitive”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63816","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-8\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-8 on your answer sheet","maxWords":3},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8823:63817:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"rats","acceptedAnswers":["rats"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The same experiment was repeated on rats by Rauscher and Hong Hua Li from Stanford.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“之后，另一个平行实验也是在什么对象身上进行的”。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“another parallel experiment”和“conducted on”定位到C段开头，明确实验对象。\n解题思路：C段第一句提到“斯坦福大学的Frances H. Rauscher和Hong Hua Li对老鼠重复了相同的实验”，明确实验对象是“rats”。原文直接提到“rats”作为实验对象，因此答案为“rats”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63817","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-8\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-8 on your answer sheet","maxWords":3},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8823:63818:9","type":"choice","text":"Music has the power to improve people’s brain performance according to the passage.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Although some of these circuits are formed for physical skills needed to play an instrument, just listening to music strengthens connection used in higher-order thinking. Listening to music can then be thought of as ‘exercise’ for the brain, improving concentration and enhancing intuition.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“根据文章内容，音乐能够提高人们的脑部表现吗？”\n定位关键信息： 使用 \"improve people’s brain performance\" 定位到文中描述音乐对大脑功能产生积极影响的句子。\n解题思路：段落E明确指出听音乐能能增强高阶思维所需的神经连接，并且可以锻炼大脑，有助于提升专注力并增强直觉。这些陈述都直接肯定了音乐对大脑表现（包括智力、思维、注意力等）的改善作用。因此，该陈述与原文信息一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63818","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8823:63819:10","type":"choice","text":"All neural connections are built up after a baby’s born instead of the time he or she had born.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：When a baby is born, certain connections have already been made – like connections for heartbeat and breathing. As new information is learned and motor skills develop, new neural connections are formed.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“所有神经连接都是在婴儿出生后才建立的，而不是在他出生时就存在的”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“neural connections”和“born”定位到D段，特别是关于神经连接形成时间的描述。\n解题思路：原文明确提到婴儿出生时，某些神经连接已经形成，比如心跳和呼吸的连接。而题干说神经连接要出身之后才建立，与原文不符，因此答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63819","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8823:63820:11","type":"choice","text":"There is no one who questions Mozart Effect so far.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：If you’re a little skeptical about the claims made by supporters of the Mozart Effect, you’re not alone.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“到目前为止没有人质疑莫扎特效应”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"questions Mozart Effect\"定位到文章中质疑莫扎特效应的内容。\n解题思路：原文F段提到，如果你对莫扎特效应的拥护者的叙述有些许的怀疑，那么，你不是一个人。表明还是有许多人对此持有疑问。因此题目中的说法是错误的。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63820","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8823:63821:12","type":"choice","text":"Michael Linton carried out further experiment on Mozart’s life to support his viewpoint.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In an article by Michael Linton, he wrote that the research that began this phenomenon (the study by researchers at the University of California Irvine) showed only a temporary boost in IQ, which was not significant enough to even last throughout the course of the experiment. Using music to influence intelligence was used in Confucian civilization and Plato alluded to Pythagorean music when he described is ideal state in The Republic. In both of these examples, music did not have caused any overwhelming changes, and the theory eventually died out. Linton also asks, ‘If Mozart’s Music were able to improve health, why was Mozart himself so frequently sick? If listening to Mozart’s music increases intelligence and encourages spirituality, why aren’t the world’s smartest and most spiritual people Mozart specialists?’ Linton raises an interesting point, if the Mozart Effect causes such significant changes, why isn’t there more documented evidence?\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是Michael Linton是否进行了关于莫扎特生平的进一步实验来支持他的观点。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是Michael Linton和Mozart’s life。通过这些关键词可以在G段找到关于Michael Linton的描述。\n解题思路：根据G段中关于Michael Linton的描述，我们可以看到他主要是通过文章和提问来表达自己的观点，并没有提到他进行了关于莫扎特生平的进一步实验。因此，题目中的信息在文章中没有给出。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63821","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8823:63822:13","type":"choice","text":"Not sufficient evidence supports Mozart Effect from the very first experiment till now.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Since that initial experiment, there has not been a surge of supporting evidence.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问“从最初的实验至今，尚无充分证据支持莫扎特效应”是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"evidence\"和\"Mozart Effect\"定位到文章H段，该段明确提到虽然有一些证据表明音乐能增加大脑活动，但实际的学习和记忆改善尚未得到充分证明。\n解题思路：H段提到，自那次初步实验以来，尚未出现大量佐证该结论的新证据。后又提到，尽管有一些证据显示音乐能增加大脑活动，但学习和记忆的实际改善尚未得到充分证明，这与题目中\"not sufficient evidence\"的表述一致，因此题目陈述与文章信息一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63822","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"63814","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>1</strong> Music influences brain development of baby.<strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"63815","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-8\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-8 on your answer sheet","html":"<p>In the experiment carried out by Frances Rauscher, participants were immersed in the music for<strong> 6.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[6] ____</strong> period of time before they were tested. &nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"63816","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-8\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-8 on your answer sheet","html":"<p>Rauscher suggested that enhancement of their performance is related to the<strong> 7.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong> nature of Mozart’s music.</p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"63817","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-8\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-8 on your answer sheet","html":"<p>After that, another parallel experiment was also conducted on <strong>8</strong>.<strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"63818","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Music has the power to improve people’s brain performance according to the passage.</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"63819","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>All neural connections are built up after a baby’s born instead of the time he or she had born.</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"63820","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>There is no one who questions Mozart Effect so far.</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"63821","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Michael Linton carried out further experiment on Mozart’s life to support his viewpoint.</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"63822","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Not sufficient evidence supports Mozart Effect from the very first experiment till now.</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The Mozart Effect&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Music has been used for centuries to heal the body. In the Ebers Papyrs (one of the earliest medical documents, circa 1500 B.C.), it was recorded that physicians chanted to heal the sick (Castleman, 1994). In various cultures, we have observed singing as part of healing rituals. In the world of Western medicine, however, using music in medicine lost popularity until the introduction of the radio. Researchers then started to notice that listening to music could have significant physical effects. The rapists noticed music could help calm anxiety and researchers saw that listening to music could cause a drop in blood pressure. In addition to these two areas, music has been used with cancer chemotherapy to reduce nausea, during surgery to reduce stress hormone production, during childbirth, and in stroke recovery (Castleman, 1994 and Westley, 1998). It has been shown to decrease pain as well as enhance the effectiveness of the immune system. In Japan, compilations of music are used as medication, of sorts. For example, if you want to cure a headache or migraine, the album suggested Mendelssohn’s ‘Spring Song,’ Dvorak’s ‘Humoresque,’ or part of George Gershwin’s ‘An American in Paris’ (Campbell,1998). Music is also being used to assist in learning, in a phenomenon called the Mozart Effect.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Frances H. Rauscher, Ph.D., first demonstrated the correlation between music and learning in an experiment in 1993. His experiments indicated that a 10 minute dose of Mozart could temporarily boost intelligence. Groups of students were given intelligence tests after listening to silence, relaxation tapes, or Mozart’s Sonata for Two Pianos in D Major for a short time. He found that after silence, the average IQ score was 110, and after the relaxation tape, scores rose a point. After listening to Mozart, however, the scores jumped to 119 (Westley, 1998). Even students who did not like the music still had an increased score on the IQ test. Rauscher hypothesized that ‘listening to complex, non-repetitive music, like Mozart, may simulate neural pathways that are important in thinking’ (Castleman, 1994).&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The same experiment was repeated on rats by Rauscher and Hong Hua Li from Stanford. Rats also demonstrated enhancement in their intelligence performance. These new studies indicate that rats that were exposed to Mozart showed ‘increased gene expression of BDNF (a neural growth factor), CREB (a learning and memory compound), and Synapsin I(a synaptic growth protein)’ in the brain’s hippocampus, compared with rats in the control group, which heard only white noise (e.g. the whooshing sound of a radio tuned between stations)&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>How exactly does the Mozart affect work? Researchers are still trying to determine the actual mechanisms for the formation of these enhanced learning pathways. Neuroscientists suspect that music can actually help build and strengthen connections between neurons in the cerebral cortex in a process similar to what occurs in brain development despite its type. When a baby is born, certain connections have already been made – like connections for heartbeat and breathing. As new information is learned and motor skills develop, new neural connections are formed. Neurons that are not used will eventually die while those used repeatedly will form strong connections. Although a large number of these neural connections require experience, they also must occur within a certain time frame. For example, a child born with cataracts cannot develop connections within the visual cortex. If the cataracts are removed by surgery right away, the child’s vision develops normally. However, after the age of 2, if the cataracts are removed, the child will remain blind because those pathways cannot establish themselves.</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Music seems to work in the same way. In October of 1997, researchers at the University of Konstanz in Germany found that music actually rewires neural circuits (Begley, 1996). Although some of these circuits are formed for physical skills needed to play an instrument, just listening to music strengthens connection used in higher-order thinking. Listening to music can then be thought of as ‘exercise’ for the brain, improving concentration and enhancing intuition. XT960228&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>If you’re a little skeptical about the claims made by supporters of the Mozart Effect, you’re not alone. Many people accredit the advanced learning of some children who take music lessons to other personality traits, such as motivation and persistence, which is required in all types of learning. There have also been claims of that influencing the results of some experiments.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Furthermore, many people are critical of the role the media had in turning an isolated study into a trend for parents and music educators. After Mozart Effect was published to the public, the sales of Mozart CDs stayed on the top of the hit list for three weeks. In an article by Michael Linton, he wrote that the research that began this phenomenon (the study by researchers at the University of California Irvine) showed only a temporary boost in IQ, which was not significant enough to even last throughout the course of the experiment. Using music to influence intelligence was used in Confucian civilization and Plato alluded to Pythagorean music when he described is ideal state in The Republic. In both of these examples, music did not have caused any overwhelming changes, and the theory eventually died out. Linton also asks, ‘If Mozart’s Music were able to improve health, why was Mozart himself so frequently sick? If listening to Mozart’s music increases intelligence and encourages spirituality, why aren’t the world’s smartest and most spiritual people Mozart specialists?’ Linton raises an interesting point, if the Mozart Effect causes such significant changes, why isn’t there more documented evidence?&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The ‘trendiness’ of the Mozart Effect may have died out somewhat, but there are still strong supporters (and opponents) of the claims made in 1993. Since that initial experiment, there has not been a surge of supporting evidence. However, many parents, after playing classical music while pregnant or when theft children are young, will swear by the Mozart Effect. A classmate of mine once told me that listening to classical music while studying will help with memorization. If we approach this controversy from a scientific aspect, although there has been some evidence that music does increase brain activity, actual improvements in learning and memory have not been adequately demonstrated.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8823&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8837","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 European Heat Wave","book":"阅读还原集Vol.15","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.15 · Test 4 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8837:63902:14","type":"choice","text":"The average summer temperature in 2003 is approximately four degrees higher than that of the past.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：As the graph shows, such as the variability of our climate that over the past 200 years, there have been at least half a dozen anomalies, in terms of excess temperature – the peaks on the graph denoting very hot years – approaching, or even exceeding, 20°C. There has been nothing remotely like 2003 when the anomaly is nearly four degrees.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目询问2003年的平均夏季气温是否比过去高出约四度。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"average summer temperature\"和\"four degrees\"定位到D段中关于异常温度的描述。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，在过去200年的气候记录中，2003年的气温“异常值”(anomaly)是“接近四度”(nearly four degrees)，并且强调“没有任何一年能与之相比”。这里的“异常值”正是相对于过去长期平均气温的偏离值。因此，“nearly four degrees”的异常值直接支持了题目中“高出大约4度”的说法。该陈述与原文信息一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63902","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8837:63903:15","type":"choice","text":"Jones believes the temperature statistic is within the normal range.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘This is quite remarkable,’ Professor Jones told The Independent, ‘It’s very unusual in a statistical sense. If this series had a normal statistical distribution, you wouldn’t get this number.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是琼斯是否认为温度统计数据在正常范围内。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"Jones\"和\"temperature statistic\"定位到E段中琼斯的直接引语。\n解题思路：根据E段中的原文句子，琼斯明确表示这个温度统计数据在统计学上非常不寻常，如果它是正常的统计分布，就不会出现这样的数字。因此，琼斯并不认为温度统计数据在正常范围内，所以题目说法是错误的。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63903","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8837:63904:16","type":"choice","text":"The human factor is one of the reasons that caused the hot summer.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：If we look at an excess above the average of nearly four degrees, then perhaps nearly three degrees of that is natural variability, because we’ve seen that in past summers. But the final degree of it is likely to be due to global warming, caused by human actions.’\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问“人为因素是导致炎热夏季的原因之一”，需要判断这个说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词“human factor”和“caused the hot summer”可以定位到E段中“ caused by human actions”这一信息。\n解题思路：段落E中，CRU主任Phil Jones教授估算异常升温中“最后那大约1度很可能要归因于人类活动引起的全球变暖”。这直接肯定了人类活动（人为因素）是导致此次炎热夏季的一个重要原因。因此，该陈述与原文信息一致，答案为TRUE","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63904","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8837:63905:17","type":"choice","text":"In a large city, people usually measure temperature twice a day.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In Paris, the temperature never dropped below 230°C (73.40°F) at all between 7 and 14 August, and the city recorded its warmest-ever night on 11-12 August, when the mercury did not drop below 25.50°C (77.90°F).\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“在一个大城市，人们通常一天测量两次温度”，需要判断这个说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过“temperature”和“twice a day”这两个关键词在文章中定位信息。在G段中提到了巴黎的温度记录，但并未提及测量频率。\n解题思路：文章中提到了巴黎的温度记录，但没有提到人们通常一天测量两次温度的信息。因此，题目中的信息在文章中没有明确给出，所以答案是“Not Given”。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63905","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8837:63906:18","type":"choice","text":"Global warming has an obvious effect of warmer winter instead of hotter summer before 2003.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Until now, the warming has been manifesting itself mainly in winters that have been less cold than in summers that have been much hotter.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“全球变暖在2003年之前对冬季变暖的影响比夏季变热更明显”这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“global warming”、“warmer winter”、“hotter summer”和“before 2003”定位到F段第二句。\n解题思路：F段明确提到“Until now, the warming has been manifesting itself mainly in winters that have been less cold than in summers that have been much hotter.”，意思是“到目前为止，变暖主要表现为冬季变暖而不是夏季变热”。这与题目陈述“全球变暖在2003年之前对冬季变暖的影响比夏季更明显”一致，因此答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63906","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8837:63907:19","type":"choice","text":"New ski resorts are to be built on a high-altitude spot.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Last week, the United Nations predicted that winters were warming so quickly that winter sports would die out in Europe’s lower-level ski resorts.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“新的滑雪胜地将在高海拔地点建造”这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"New ski resorts\"和\"high-altitude spot\"在文章中进行定位。\n解题思路：文章中提到了联合国预测冬季运动将在欧洲低海拔滑雪胜地消失，但并未提及新的滑雪胜地将在高海拔地点建造。因此，题目中的信息在文章中没有明确的支持或反驳，所以答案应为\"Not Given\"。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63907","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8837:63908:20","type":"fill","text":"填写第 20 空","answer":"1976 and 1995\n\n","acceptedAnswers":["1976 and 1995"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For Britain, the year as a whole is likely to be the warmest ever recorded, but despite the high-temperature record on 10 August, the summer itself – defined as the June, July and August period – still comes behind 1976 and 1995, when there were long periods of intense heat.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问除了2003年之外，英国最热的两年是哪两年。\n定位关键信息：根据题目的\"2003\"和\"Britain\"定位到I段，该段提到\"Britain\"和\"2003\"，并对比了英国最热的年份。\n解题思路：题目问的是英国（Britain）最热的年份中，除了2003年之外的另外两个。在段落I中，原文明确提到，2003年的夏季（六、七、八月）本身“仍然排在1976年和1995年之后”。这意味着，就夏季温度而言，1976年和1995年是比2003年更热的年份。因此，答案是“1976 and 1995”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63908","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-21\nAnswer the questions below using NO MORE THAN TWO NUMBERS AND/OR A WORD from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-21 on your answer sheet."},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8837:63909:21","type":"fill","text":"填写第 21 空","answer":"2000 floods/2000 Floods","acceptedAnswers":["2000 floods","2000 Floods"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘It will certainly have left its mark on a number of countries, as to how they think and plan for climate change in the future, much as the 2000 floods have revolutionised the way the Government is thinking about flooding in the UK.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是除了气候变化之外，还有什么会影响英国政府的政策，根据Hulme的说法。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"UK government policies\"和\"Hulme\"，通过定位到J段中Hulme的引述，找到与英国政府政策相关的部分。\n解题思路：在J段中，Hulme提到2003年的热浪将对欧洲产生类似的影响，就像2000年的洪水已经改变了英国政府应对洪水的方式一样。因此，2000年的洪水是除了气候变化之外，还会影响英国政府政策的因素。答案直接从文中提取\"2000 floods\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63909","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-21\nAnswer the questions below using NO MORE THAN TWO NUMBERS AND/OR A WORD from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-21 on your answer sheet."},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8837:63910:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"France/france","acceptedAnswers":["France","france"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The 15,000 excess deaths in France during August, compared with previous years, have been related to the high night-time temperatures.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是在2003年的夏天，数千人死亡的国家是哪个。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"thousands of extra death\"和\"summer of 2003\"，可以在文章中定位到H段，该段提到了\"15,000 excess deaths in France during August\"。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到在法国有15,000人超额死亡，这与题目中的\"thousands of extra death\"相匹配，因此可以确定答案为France。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63910","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN TWO NUMBERS AND/OR A WORD from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet."},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8837:63910:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"1856","acceptedAnswers":["1856"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At the moment, the year is on course to be the third-hottest ever in the global temperature record, which goes back to 1856, behind 1988 and 2002 but when all the records for October, November and December are collated, it might move into second place, Professor Jones said.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目询问，全球范围内，第三个最热夏天记录始于哪一年。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"third record of hottest summer\"和\"date from\"定位到I段中关于全球温度记录的描述，找到\"the third-hottest ever in the global temperature record\"和\"which goes back to 1856\"。\n解题思路：原文明确提到全球温度记录始于1856年，因此答案直接对应原文中的\"1856\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63910","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN TWO NUMBERS AND/OR A WORD from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet."},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8837:63910:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"1988 and 2002","acceptedAnswers":["1988 and 2002"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At the moment, the year is on course to be the third-hottest ever in the global temperature record, which goes back to 1856, behind 1988 and 2002 but when all the records for October, November and December are collated, it might move into second place, Professor Jones said.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目要求根据题干中的“after the year of ”填空，需要填写年份。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“after the year of ”可以定位到I段中“behind 1988 and 2002”这一信息，表示在1988年和2002年之后。\n解题思路：根据I段中的原文句子，可以确定在1988年和2002年之后，当前年份排名第三。因此，答案为1988和2002。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63910","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN TWO NUMBERS AND/OR A WORD from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet."},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8837:63910:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"1990","acceptedAnswers":["1990"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The 10 hottest years in the record have all now occurred since 1990.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是根据Jones的说法，所有10个最热的年份都发生在哪一年之后。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"Jones\"和\"10 hottest years\"，通过这些词可以在I段中找到相关句子。\n解题思路：根据I段中的句子\"The 10 hottest years in the record have all now occurred since 1990.\"，可以确定所有10个最热的年份都发生在1990年之后，因此答案为1990。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63910","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN TWO NUMBERS AND/OR A WORD from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet."},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8837:63910:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"500","acceptedAnswers":["500"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The temperatures recorded were out of all proportion to the previous record,’ he said, ‘It was the warmest summer in the past 500 years and probably way beyond what it was enormously exceptional.’\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是2003年的夏天在过去的多少年里是最热的。\n定位关键信息：根据题目的\"the summer of 2003 was at the peak of the previous 26 %% years, perhaps even more\"可以定位到I段中\"the warmest summer in the past 500 years\"。\n解题思路：原文中I段明确提到\"the warmest summer in the past 500 years\"，这与题目中\"the summer of 2003 was at the peak of the previous XX years, perhaps even more\"意思一致，因此答案为500。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63910","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN TWO NUMBERS AND/OR A WORD from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet."},{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8837:63915:27","type":"choice","text":"Which one can be best served as the title of this passage in the following options?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：无具体答案句，需根据全文主旨判断。\n对应段落：全文\n审题：题目要求选择最适合作为文章标题的选项。\n定位关键信息：文章主要围绕2003年欧洲的极端高温天气展开，描述了其异常性、影响以及与全球变暖的关系。\n解题思路：文章A段提到描述了2003年夏季的极端高温现象及其影响。B段进一步指出这是“有记录以来西欧和中欧最热的夏季”。C段强调这一现象的异常性，并指出可能直接归因于人类活动引起的全球变暖。全文围绕“2003年欧洲最热的夏天”这一核心事件展开，描述其特点、影响以及与全球变暖的联系。因此，选项D“欧洲最热的夏天”最能概括文章主旨，作为标题最为合适。其他选项要么过于宽泛（如A、B），要么偏离文章核心（如C）。","options":["Global Warming effect","Global Warming in Europe","The Effects of hot temperature","Hottest summer in Europet."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"63915","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 27\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answer in box 27 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"63902","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p>The average summer temperature in 2003 is approximately four degrees higher than that of the past.</p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"63903","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p>Jones believes the temperature statistic is within the normal range.</p>","firstNumber":15},{"id":"63904","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p>The human factor is one of the reasons that caused the hot summer.</p>","firstNumber":16},{"id":"63905","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p>In a large city, people usually measure temperature twice a day.</p>","firstNumber":17},{"id":"63906","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p>Global warming has an obvious effect of warmer winter instead of hotter summer before 2003.</p>","firstNumber":18},{"id":"63907","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p>New ski resorts are to be built on a high-altitude spot.</p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"63908","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-21\nAnswer the questions below using NO MORE THAN TWO NUMBERS AND/OR A WORD from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-21 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>What are the two hottest years in Britain besides 2003? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"63909","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-21\nAnswer the questions below using NO MORE THAN TWO NUMBERS AND/OR A WORD from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-21 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>What will affect UK government policies besides climate change according to Hulme? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"63910","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the summary below using NO MORE THAN TWO NUMBERS AND/OR A WORD from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>In the summer of 2003, thousands of extra death occurred in the country of &nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong> .&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">Moreover, world-widely, the third record of hottest summer date from&nbsp;</span><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong> ,&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">after the year of&nbsp;</span><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> .&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">According to Jones, all the 10 hottest years happened from&nbsp;</span><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong> .&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">However, the summer of 2003 was at the peak of the previous&nbsp;</span><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong> years, perhaps even more.</span></span></span></span></p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"63915","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 27\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answer in box 27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Which one can be best served as the title of this passage in the following options?</p>","firstNumber":27}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>European Heat Wave&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>It was the summer, scientists now realise, when global warming at last made itself unmistakably felt. We knew that summer 2003 was remarkable: Britain experienced its record high temperature and continental Europe saw forest fires raging out of control, great rivers drying to a trickle and thousands of heat-related deaths. But just how remarkable is only now becoming clear.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The three months of June, July and August were the warmest ever recorded in western and central Europe, with record national highs in Portugal, Germany and Switzerland as well as Britain. And they were the warmest by a very long way Over a great rectangular block of the earth stretching from west of Paris to northern Italy, taking in Switzerland and southern Germany, the average temperature for the summer months was 3.78°C above the long-term norm, said the Climatic Research Unit (CRU) of the University of East Anglia in Norwich, which is one of the world’s leading institutions for the monitoring and analysis of temperature records.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>That excess might not seem a lot until you are aware of the context – but then you realise it is enormous. There is nothing like this in previous data, anywhere. It is considered so exceptional that Professor Phil Jones, the CRU’s director, is prepared to say openly – in a way few scientists have done before – that the 2003 extreme may be directly attributed, not to natural climate variability, but to global warming caused by human actions.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Meteorologists have hitherto contented themselves with the formula that recent high temperatures are consistent with predictions of climate. For the great block of the map – that stretching between 35-50 N and 0-20 E – the CRU has reliable temperature records dating back to 1781. Using as a baseline the average summer temperature recorded between 1961 and 1990, departures from the temperature norm, or ‘anomalies’: over the area as a whole can easily be plotted. As the graph shows, such as the variability of our climate that over the past 200 years, there have been at least half a dozen anomalies, in terms of excess temperature – the peaks on the graph denoting very hot years – approaching, or even exceeding, 20°C. But there has been nothing remotely like 2003 when the anomaly is nearly four degrees.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>‘This is quite remarkable,’ Professor Jones told The Independent, ‘It’s very unusual in a statistical sense. If this series had a normal statistical distribution, you wouldn’t get this number. The return period (how often it could be expected to recur) would be something like one in a thou-sand years. If we look at an excess above the average of nearly four degrees, then perhaps nearly three degrees of that is natural variability, because we’ve seen that in past summers. But the final degree of it is likely to be due to global warming, caused by human actions.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The summer of 2003 has, in a sense, been one that climate scientists have long been expecting. Until now, the warming has been manifesting itself mainly in winters that have been less cold than in summers that have been much hotter. Last week, the United Nations predicted that winters were warming so quickly that winter sports would die out in Europe’s lower-level ski resorts. But sooner or later, the unprecedented hot summer was bound to come, and this year it did.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>One of the most dramatic features of the summer was the hot nights, especially in the first half of August. In Paris, the temperature never dropped below 230°C (73.40°F) at all between 7 and 14 August, and the city recorded its warmest-ever night on 11-12 August, when the mercury did not drop below 25.50°C (77.90°F). Germany recorded its warmest-ever night at Weinbiet in the Rhine valley with the lowest figure of 27.60°C (80.60°F) on 13 August, and similar record-breaking night-time temperatures were recorded in Switzerland and Italy.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The 15,000 excess deaths in France during August, compared with previous years, have been related to the high night-time temperatures. The number gradually increased during the first 12 days of the month, peaking at about 2,000 per day on the night of 12-13 August, the fell off dramatically after 14 August when the minimum temperatures fell by about 50C. The elderly were most affected, with a 70 per cent increase in mortality rate in those aged 75-94.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>For Britain, the year as a whole is likely to be the warmest ever recorded, but despite the high-temperature record on 10 August, the summer itself – defined as the June, July and August period – still comes behind 1976 and 1995, when there were long periods of intense heat. At the moment, the year is on course to be the third-hottest ever in the global temperature record, which goes back to 1856, behind 1988 and 2002 but when all the records for October, November and December are collated, it might move into second place, Professor Jones said. The 10 hottest years in the record have all now occurred since 1990. Professor Jones is in no doubt about the astonishing nature of the European summer of 2003. ‘The temperatures recorded were out of all proportion to the previous record,’ he said, ‘It was the warmest summer in the past 500 years and probably way beyond what it was enormously exceptional.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>His colleagues at the University of East Anglia’s Tyndall Centre for Climate Change Research are now planning a special study of it. ‘It was a summer that has not: been experienced before, either in terms of the temperature extremes that were reached, or the range and diversity of the impacts of the extreme heat,’ said the centre’s executive director, Professor Mike Hulme, ‘It will certainly have left its mark on a number of countries, as to how they think and plan for climate change in the future, much as the 2000 floods have revolutionised the way the Government is thinking about flooding in the UK. The 2003 heatwave will have similar repercussions across Europe.’</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8837&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8838","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Internal and External Marketing","book":"阅读还原集Vol.15","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.15 · Test 4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8838:63916:28","type":"choice","text":"28 One health insurance Company","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：One health insurance company, for instance, advertised that the welfare of patients was the company’s number one priority, while employees were told that their main goal was to increase the value of their stock options through cost reductions.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求将某健康保险公司与题干中描述的相应行为或类别进行匹配。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"One health insurance Company\"定位到A段。\n解题思路：根据原文句子，某健康保险公司宣称患者福祉是头等大事，却要求员工通过降本增效来提升股票期权价值，可以看出，这家健康保险公司对外的宣传和内部传达的信息不一致，这与选项D\"内部和外部传达信息不同\"完全一致。","options":["Legendary anecdote inspire employee successfully.","Advertisement campaign inspire employees and ensure a leading role in business.","Improper ads campaign brings negative effect.","Internal and external announcement are different.","Campaign brings positive and realistic expectation internally.","A bad slogan that failed both to win support internally and raise standard to its poor service."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"63916","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nUse the information in the passage to match the company with correct category or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.\nA Legendary anecdote inspire employee successfully.\nB Advertisement campaign inspire employees and ensure a leading role in business.\nC Improper ads campaign brings negative effect.\nD Internal and external announcement are different.\nE Campaign brings positive and realistic expectation internally.\nF A bad slogan that failed both to win support internally and raise standard to its poor service."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8838:63916:29","type":"choice","text":"29 British Rail","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：When a beleaguered British Rail launched a campaign announcing service improvement under the banner ‘We’re Getting There’, it did so prematurely. By drawing attention to the gap between the promise and the reality, it prompted destructive press coverage. This, in turn, demoralized staff, who had been legitimately proud of the service advances they had made.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求将公司British Rail与题干中描述的相应行为或类别进行匹配。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的公司名称British Rail在文章中定位，找到G段中提到的“British Rail launched a campaign announcing service improvement under the banner ‘We’re Getting There’”。\n解题思路：原文提到British Rail在服务尚未真正改善时就推出了“我们正在改进”的宣传活动，这导致公众关注到其承诺与现实之间的巨大差距，引发了负面的媒体报道，还打击了员工的士气。这属于不当的广告活动带来负面影响，与选项C的描述完全吻合。","options":["Legendary anecdote inspire employee successfully.","Advertisement campaign inspire employees and ensure a leading role in business.","Improper ads campaign brings negative effect.","Internal and external announcement are different.","Campaign brings positive and realistic expectation internally.","A bad slogan that failed both to win support internally and raise standard to its poor service."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"63916","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nUse the information in the passage to match the company with correct category or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.\nA Legendary anecdote inspire employee successfully.\nB Advertisement campaign inspire employees and ensure a leading role in business.\nC Improper ads campaign brings negative effect.\nD Internal and external announcement are different.\nE Campaign brings positive and realistic expectation internally.\nF A bad slogan that failed both to win support internally and raise standard to its poor service."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8838:63916:30","type":"choice","text":"30 IBM","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1997, when IBM launched its e-business campaign (which is widely credited for turning around the company’s image)...IBM was also using the campaign to align employees around the idea of the Internet as the future of technology....The campaign was successful largely because it gave employees a sense of direction and purpose, which in turn restored their confidence in IBM’s ability to predict the future and lead the technology industry. Today, research shows that people are four times more likely to associate the term “e-business” with IBM than with its nearest competitor, Microsoft.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求将公司IBM与题干中描述的相应行为或类别进行匹配。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的公司名称\"IBM\"定位到文章中B段的相关句子。\n解题思路：根据B段中的描述，IBM在1997年发起了e-business活动，这个活动不仅是对外营销，还通过该战略让员工认同互联网是技术未来的发展方向。这场内部战役彻底改变了员工的思维方式，该战略之所以成功，关键在于为员工注入了明确的方向感和使命感，从而重拾了他们对IBM预见未来、引领科技行业发展的信心。因此，IBM的行为是使用营销活动激励员工，最终成为科技行业引领者。这与B项，广告活动激励员工，确保企业在商业领域保持领先地位，相符。","options":["Legendary anecdote inspire employee successfully.","Advertisement campaign inspire employees and ensure a leading role in business.","Improper ads campaign brings negative effect.","Internal and external announcement are different.","Campaign brings positive and realistic expectation internally.","A bad slogan that failed both to win support internally and raise standard to its poor service."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"63916","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nUse the information in the passage to match the company with correct category or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.\nA Legendary anecdote inspire employee successfully.\nB Advertisement campaign inspire employees and ensure a leading role in business.\nC Improper ads campaign brings negative effect.\nD Internal and external announcement are different.\nE Campaign brings positive and realistic expectation internally.\nF A bad slogan that failed both to win support internally and raise standard to its poor service."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8838:63916:31","type":"choice","text":"31 United Airline","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In an effort to own up to the industry’s shortcomings, United launched a new campaign, ‘Rising’, in which it sought to differentiate itself by acknowledging poor service and promising incremental improvements such as better meals. While this was a logical premise for the campaign given the tenor of the times, a campaign focusing on customers’ distaste for flying was deeply discouraging to the staff. Employee resentment ultimately made it impossible for United to deliver the improvements it was promising, which in turn undermined the ‘Rising’ pledge.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求将公司United Airline与题干中描述的相应行为或类别进行匹配。\n定位关键信息：通过United Airline这一关键词定位到D段，该段详细描述了United Airline的案例。\n解题思路：D段提到United Airline推出了‘Rising’活动，尽管在当时背景下这不失为一个合理策略，但一方面，广告活动承认服务差，这让员工感到沮丧，导致其无法赢得内部支持；另一方面，员工的抵触情绪使得公司无法兑现其承诺的服务改进，导致口号落空。符合F项的描述，口号既未能赢得内部支持，也未能改善其糟糕的服务质量。","options":["Legendary anecdote inspire employee successfully.","Advertisement campaign inspire employees and ensure a leading role in business.","Improper ads campaign brings negative effect.","Internal and external announcement are different.","Campaign brings positive and realistic expectation internally.","A bad slogan that failed both to win support internally and raise standard to its poor service."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"63916","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nUse the information in the passage to match the company with correct category or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.\nA Legendary anecdote inspire employee successfully.\nB Advertisement campaign inspire employees and ensure a leading role in business.\nC Improper ads campaign brings negative effect.\nD Internal and external announcement are different.\nE Campaign brings positive and realistic expectation internally.\nF A bad slogan that failed both to win support internally and raise standard to its poor service."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8838:63916:32","type":"choice","text":"32 A financial service company","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：And one major financial services institution told customers that it was making a major shift in focus from being a financial retailer to a financial adviser, but, a year later, research showed that the customer experience with the company had not changed. It turned out that company leaders had not made an effort to sell the change internally, so employees were still churning out transactions and hadn’t changed their behavior to match their new adviser role.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求将某金融机构与题干中描述的相应行为或类别进行匹配。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"A financial service company\"可以定位到A段中提到的\"financial services institution\"。\n解题思路：A段中描述了一家金融机构宣称要从金融零售商转型为专业理财顾问，告诉客户它正在从金融零售商转变为金融顾问，但一年后，研究发现客户的体验并没有改变。究其原因，管理层既未在内部推动变革，员工也未调整行为模式来适应新角色。说明该公司对外进行宣传，但内部没有改变，最终给客户带来负面体验，这也属于不合适的广告带来负面影响，因此答案为C。","options":["Legendary anecdote inspire employee successfully.","Advertisement campaign inspire employees and ensure a leading role in business.","Improper ads campaign brings negative effect.","Internal and external announcement are different.","Campaign brings positive and realistic expectation internally.","A bad slogan that failed both to win support internally and raise standard to its poor service."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"63916","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nUse the information in the passage to match the company with correct category or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.\nA Legendary anecdote inspire employee successfully.\nB Advertisement campaign inspire employees and ensure a leading role in business.\nC Improper ads campaign brings negative effect.\nD Internal and external announcement are different.\nE Campaign brings positive and realistic expectation internally.\nF A bad slogan that failed both to win support internally and raise standard to its poor service."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8838:63916:33","type":"choice","text":"33 A Shoemaking company (Nike)","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At Nike, a number of senior executives now hold the additional title of ‘Corporate Storyteller’. They deliberately avoid stories of financial successes and concentrate on parables of ‘just doing it’, reflecting and reinforcing the company’s ad campaigns.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求将鞋业公司Nike与题干中描述的相应行为或类别进行匹配。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"Shoemaking company (Nike)\"定位到文章中关于Nike的描述，即F段明确提到Nike。\n解题思路：F段提到，Nike公司通过讲述其联合创始人Bill Bowerman利用华夫饼铁模制作鞋底原型的传奇轶事（legendary anecdote），来激励员工，该公司希望其广告活动所体现的创新精神在公司内部保持活力。这与题干中的A选项，通过传奇轶事来激励员工，完全对应。因此，正确答案是A。","options":["Legendary anecdote inspire employee successfully.","Advertisement campaign inspire employees and ensure a leading role in business.","Improper ads campaign brings negative effect.","Internal and external announcement are different.","Campaign brings positive and realistic expectation internally.","A bad slogan that failed both to win support internally and raise standard to its poor service."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"63916","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nUse the information in the passage to match the company with correct category or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.\nA Legendary anecdote inspire employee successfully.\nB Advertisement campaign inspire employees and ensure a leading role in business.\nC Improper ads campaign brings negative effect.\nD Internal and external announcement are different.\nE Campaign brings positive and realistic expectation internally.\nF A bad slogan that failed both to win support internally and raise standard to its poor service."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8838:63916:34","type":"choice","text":"34 The Company of (Ford)","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Such promises provide incentives for employees and give them something to live up to. In the 1980s, Ford turned ‘Quality is Job!’ from an internal rallying cry into a consumer slogan in response to the threat from cheaper, more reliable Japanese cars. It did so before the claim was fully justified, but by placing it in the public arena, it gave employees an incentive to match the Japanese.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求将福特公司与题干中描述的相应行为或类别进行匹配。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“Ford”定位到文章中的G段，找到关于福特公司的描述。\n解题思路：根据原文，上世纪80年代，福特将‘质量就是工作！’从内部口号升级为面向消费者的宣传语，尽管当时该承诺尚未完全实现，但通过公开宣传，企业成功激励员工向日本标准看齐。说明企业通过广告活动激励员工，树立目标，为内部带来了积极切实的希望，因此答案为E。","options":["Legendary anecdote inspire employee successfully.","Advertisement campaign inspire employees and ensure a leading role in business.","Improper ads campaign brings negative effect.","Internal and external announcement are different.","Campaign brings positive and realistic expectation internally.","A bad slogan that failed both to win support internally and raise standard to its poor service."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"63916","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nUse the information in the passage to match the company with correct category or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.\nA Legendary anecdote inspire employee successfully.\nB Advertisement campaign inspire employees and ensure a leading role in business.\nC Improper ads campaign brings negative effect.\nD Internal and external announcement are different.\nE Campaign brings positive and realistic expectation internally.\nF A bad slogan that failed both to win support internally and raise standard to its poor service."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8838:63917:35","type":"choice","text":"Employers in almost all companies successfully make their employees fully understand the outside campaign.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At most companies, however, internal and external communications are often mismatched. This can be very confusing, and it threatens employees’ perceptions of the company’s integrity: They are told one thing by management but observe that a different message is being sent to the public.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“几乎所有公司的雇主都成功地让员工完全理解外部宣传活动”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“Employers in almost all companies”和“successfully make their employees fully understand the outside campaign”可以定位到A段，该段提到大多数公司的内部和外部沟通经常不匹配，这会让员工感到困惑，并威胁到公司诚信。\n解题思路：根据A段中的原文答案句可知，大多数公司，内部与对外宣传往往存在严重脱节。管理层向他们传达的信息，与向公众传递的不一致。这意味着员工并没有完全理解外部宣传活动，因此题目中的说法与文章信息不符，答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63917","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-38\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-38 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8838:63918:36","type":"choice","text":"Currently IBM is more prominent in the area of E-business.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Today, research shows that people are four times more likely to associate the term “e-business” with IBM than with its nearest competitor, Microsoft.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是，目前IBM在电子商务领域更具影响力，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"IBM\"和\"e-business\"定位到B段末句。\n解题思路：原文提到，人们更容易将E-business与IBM联系起来，这表明IBM在电子商务领域表现更突出，更具影响力，因此题目说法与原文信息一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63918","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-38\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-38 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8838:63919:37","type":"choice","text":"United Airline finally gave up an ads slogan due to a survey in 1996.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1996, United Airlines shelved its ‘Come Fly the Friendly Skies’ slogan when presented with a survey that revealed the depth of customer resentment toward the airline industry.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“联合航空公司最终在1996年因一项调查放弃了某广告标语”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“United Airline”、“ads slogan”、“gave up”和“survey in 1996”来定位原文信息。\n解题思路：根据原文D段的内容，1996年，联合航空在一项调查中发现消费者对航空业的不满情绪日益加深，于是决定放弃其‘来友好天空飞行’的口号。这与题目中的描述完全一致，因此答案是True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63919","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-38\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-38 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8838:63920:38","type":"choice","text":"Nike had improved company performance through telling employees legendary corporation stories.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At Nike, a number of senior executives now hold the additional title of ‘Corporate Storyteller’. They deliberately avoid stories of financial successes and concentrate on parables of ‘just doing it’, reflecting and reinforcing the company’s ad campaigns.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是Nike通过讲述公司的传奇故事来改善公司业绩，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词Nike和telling employees legendary corporation stories定位到F段。\n解题思路：原文提到，耐克公司如今有多位高管同时担任“企业故事讲述者”的头衔。他们刻意避开财务成功案例，转而聚焦“坚持到底”的励志故事，以此呼应并强化公司的广告宣传。然而，原文并没有明确说明这些故事是否改善了公司的业绩。题目中的“improved company performance”这一信息在原文中并未提及，所以，答案是Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63920","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-38\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-38 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8838:63921:39-40","type":"choice","text":"Please choose TWO approaches in the passage mentioned that were employed as company strategy","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：无，需要结合全文做出选择\n对应段落：无\n审题：题目问的是文章中提到的两种公司策略。\n定位关键信息：结合全文，提炼文中提到的公司策略。\n解题思路：B选项对应B段中IBM的案例，该段提到IBM通过内部营销活动来激励员工，为员工注入了明确的方向感和使命感，从而重拾了他们对IBM引领科技行业发展的信心。还对应F段中Nike公司的案例，通过讲述Nike的传奇故事，成功激励员工，这都属于在内部发起鼓舞人心的营销活动。E选项对应D段中United Airlines的反面案例，该段提到United选取的不恰当的标语导致公司的负面影响，标语从\"Come Fly the Friendly Skies\"改为\"Rising\"再最后改为\"United\"，这属于\"applying an appropriate slogan\"以适应内外部需求。因此选择B项和E项。","options":["promoting the visual effect of their products’ advertisement","launching inspiring campaigns internally","introducing inner competition","learning how to sell stories among senior executives","applying an appropriate slogan"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"63921","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 39-40\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"63921-8838:63921:39-40"},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8838:63921:39-40","type":"choice","text":"Please choose TWO approaches in the passage mentioned that were employed as company strategy","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：无，需要结合全文做出选择\n对应段落：无\n审题：题目问的是文章中提到的两种公司策略。\n定位关键信息：结合全文，提炼文中提到的公司策略。\n解题思路：B选项对应B段中IBM的案例，该段提到IBM通过内部营销活动来激励员工，为员工注入了明确的方向感和使命感，从而重拾了他们对IBM引领科技行业发展的信心。还对应F段中Nike公司的案例，通过讲述Nike的传奇故事，成功激励员工，这都属于在内部发起鼓舞人心的营销活动。E选项对应D段中United Airlines的反面案例，该段提到United选取的不恰当的标语导致公司的负面影响，标语从\"Come Fly the Friendly Skies\"改为\"Rising\"再最后改为\"United\"，这属于\"applying an appropriate slogan\"以适应内外部需求。因此选择B项和E项。","options":["promoting the visual effect of their products’ advertisement","launching inspiring campaigns internally","introducing inner competition","learning how to sell stories among senior executives","applying an appropriate slogan"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"63921","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 39-40\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"63921-8838:63921:39-40"}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"63921-8838:63921:39-40","numbers":[39,40],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["B","E"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"63916","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nUse the information in the passage to match the company with correct category or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet.\nA Legendary anecdote inspire employee successfully.\nB Advertisement campaign inspire employees and ensure a leading role in business.\nC Improper ads campaign brings negative effect.\nD Internal and external announcement are different.\nE Campaign brings positive and realistic expectation internally.\nF A bad slogan that failed both to win support internally and raise standard to its poor service.","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> Legendary anecdote inspire employee successfully. <br/></p><p><strong>B</strong> Advertisement campaign inspire employees and ensure a leading role in business. <br/></p><p><strong>C</strong> Improper ads campaign brings negative effect. <br/></p><p><strong>D</strong> Internal and external announcement are different. <br/></p><p><strong>E</strong> Campaign brings positive and realistic expectation internally. <br/></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>F</strong> A bad slogan that failed both to win support internally and raise standard to its poor service. <br/></p><p><strong>28</strong> One health insurance Company <strong class=\"source-blank\">[28] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"63917","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-38\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-38 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Employers in almost all companies successfully make their employees fully understand the outside campaign.</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"63918","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-38\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-38 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Currently IBM is more prominent in the area of E-business.</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"63919","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-38\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-38 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>United Airline finally gave up an ads slogan due to a survey in 1996.</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"63920","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-38\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-38 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Nike had improved company performance through telling employees legendary corporation stories.</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"63921","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 39-40\nChoose TWO correct answers","html":"<p><strong>Please choose TWO approaches in the passage mentioned that were employed as company strategy</strong></p>","firstNumber":39}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Internal and External Marketing</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Employees need to hear the same messages that you send out to the marketplace. At most companies, however, internal and external communications are often mismatched. This can be very confusing, and it threatens employees’ perceptions of the company’s integrity: They are told one thing by management but observe that a different message is being sent to the public. One health insurance company, for instance, advertised that the welfare of patients was the company’s number one priority, while employees were told that their main goal was to increase the value of their stock options through cost reductions. And one major financial services institution told customers that it was making a major shift in focus from being a financial retailer to a financial adviser, but, a year later, research showed that the customer experience with the company had not changed. It turned out that company leaders had not made an effort to sell the change internally, so employees were still churning out transactions and hadn’t changed their behavior to match their new adviser role.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Enabling employees to deliver on customer expectations is important, of course, but it’s not the only reason a company needs to match internal and external messages. Another reason is to help push the company to achieve goals that might otherwise be out of reach. In 1997, when IBM launched its e-business campaign (which is widely credited for turning around the company’s image), it chose to ignore research that suggested consumers were unprepared to embrace IBM as a leader in e-business. Although to the outside world this looked like an external marketing effort, IBM was also using the campaign to align employees around the idea of the Internet as the future of technology. The internal campaign changed the way employees thought about everything they did, from how they named products to how they organized staff to how they approached selling. The campaign was successful largely because it gave employees a sense of direction and purpose, which in turn restored their confidence in IBM’s ability to predict the future and lead the technology industry. Today, research shows that people are four times more likely to associate the term “e-business” with IBM than with its nearest competitor, Microsoft.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The type of ‘two-way branding’ that IBM did so successfully strengthens both sides of the equation. Internal marketing becomes stronger because it can draw on the same ‘big idea’ as advertising. Consumer marketing becomes stronger because the messages are developed based on employees’ behavior and attitudes, as well as on the company’s strengths and capabilities – indeed, the themes are drawn from the company’s very soul. This process can result in a more distinct advertising idea because marketers are more likely to create a message that’s unique to the company.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Perhaps even more important, by taking employees into account, a company can avoid creating a message that doesn’t resonate with staff or, worse, one that builds resentment. In 1996, United Airlines shelved its ‘Come Fly the Friendly Skies’ slogan when presented with a survey that revealed the depth of customer resentment toward the airline industry. In an effort to own up to the industry’s shortcomings, United launched a new campaign, ‘Rising’, in which it sought to differentiate itself by acknowledging poor service and promising incremental improvements such as better meals. While this was a logical premise for the campaign given the tenor of the times, a campaign focusing on customers’ distaste for flying was deeply discouraging to the staff. Employee resentment ultimately made it impossible for United to deliver the improvements it was promising, which in turn undermined the ‘Rising’ pledge. Three years later, United decided employee opposition was undermining its success and pulled the campaign. It has since moved to a more inclusive brand message with the line ‘United’, which both audiences can embrace. Here, a fundamental principle of advertising – find and address a customer concern – failed United because it did not consider the internal market.</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>When it comes to execution, the most common and effective way to link internal and external marketing campaigns is to create external advertising that targets both audiences. IBM used this tactic very effectively when it launched its e-business campaign. It took out an eight-page ad in the Wall Street Journal declaring its new vision, a message directed at both customers and internal stakeholders. This is an expensive way to capture attention, but if used sparingly, it is the most powerful form of communication; in fact, you need do it only once for everyone in the company to read it. There’s a symbolic advantage as well. Such a tactic signals that the company is taking its pledge very seriously; it also signals transparency – the same message going out to both audiences.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Advertising isn’t the only way to link internal and external marketing. At Nike, a number of senior executives now hold the additional title of ‘Corporate Storyteller’. They deliberately avoid stories of financial successes and concentrate on parables of ‘just doing it’, reflecting and reinforcing the company’s ad campaigns. One tale, for example, recalls how legendary coach and Nike co-founder Bill Bowerman, in an effort to build a better shoe for his team, poured rubber into the family waffle iron, giving birth to the prototype of Nike’s famous Waffle Sole. By talking about such inventive moves, the company hopes to keep the spirit of innovation that characterizes its ad campaigns alive and well within the company.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>But while their messages must be aligned, companies must also keep external promises a little ahead of internal realities. Such promises provide incentives for employees and give them something to live up to. In the 1980s, Ford turned ‘Quality is Job!’ from an internal rallying cry into a consumer slogan in response to the threat from cheaper, more reliable Japanese cars. It did so before the claim was fully justified, but by placing it in the public arena, it gave employees an incentive to match the Japanese. If the promise is pushed too far ahead, however, it loses credibility. When a beleaguered British Rail launched a campaign announcing service improvement under the banner ‘We’re Getting There’, it did so prematurely. By drawing attention to the gap between the promise and the reality, it prompted destructive press coverage. This, in turn, demoralized staff, who had been legitimately proud of the service advances they had made.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8838&scene=%E8%B4%A2%E7%BB%8F%E5%95%86%E4%B8%9A&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8783","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Keep a Watchful Eye on the Bridges","book":"阅读还原集Vol.15","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.15 · Test 3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8783:63480:1","type":"choice","text":"How did the traditional way to prevent damage of the bridges before the invention of new monitoring system?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Most road and rail bridges are only inspected visually, if at all. Every few months, engineers have to clamber over the structure in an attempt to find problems before the bridge shows obvious signs of damage.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是在新的监测系统发明之前，防止桥梁损坏的传统方法是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"traditional way\"和\"prevent damage of the bridges\"可以定位到A段，该段描述了传统桥梁检查的方法。\n解题思路：根据A段第一句\"Most road and rail bridges are only inspected visually, if at all.\"和第二句\"Every few months, engineers have to clamber over the structure in an attempt to find problems before the bridge shows obvious signs of damage.\"可以确定，传统的桥梁检查方法是依靠专业工作人员用肉眼进行检查，这与选项D的描述完全一致。其他选项A、B、C分别提到了用微波设备、传感器和两点间的测试，这些都与原文描述的传统方法不符。因此，正确答案是D。","options":["Bridges have to be tested in every movement on two points.","Bridges have to be closely monitored by microwave devices.","Bridges have already been monitored by sensors.","Bridges have to be frequently inspected by professional workers with naked eyes."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"63480","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8783:63481:2","type":"choice","text":"How does the new microwave monitors find out the problems of bridges?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The device uses microwaves to measure the distance between the sensor and the bridge, much like radar does,’ says Albert Migliori, a Los Alamos physicist, ‘Any load on the bridge – such as traffic – induces displacements, which change that distance as the bridge moves up and down.’\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问新的微波监测系统是如何发现桥梁问题的。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"microwave monitors\"和\"find out the problems of bridges\"，可以定位到B段第一句和第二句，这两句描述了微波监测系统的工作原理。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到微波监测系统是通过测量传感器和桥梁之间的距离来进行监测的，并且任何桥梁上的负载（如交通）都会引起位移，这些位移会改变距离。通过监测这些运动，研究人员可以了解桥梁的共振情况，行为的变化可以提前预警损坏。因此，正确答案是C，即通过监测交通引起的两点之间的距离变化来发现问题。","options":["A by changeling the distance between the positions of devices","by controlling the traffic flow on the bridges","by monitoring the distance caused by traffic between two points","by displacement of the several critical parts in the bridges"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"63481","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8783:63482:3","type":"choice","text":"Why did the expert believe there is a problem for the design called ‘fracture critical’?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Highway experts know that this design is ‘fracture critical’ because a failure in either girder would cause the bridge to fail.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问为什么专家认为“断裂临界结构”的设计存在问题。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"fracture critical\"定位到C段，找到原因状语从句\"because a failure in either girder would cause the bridge to fail\"。\n解题思路：原文明确指出这种设计的问题在于，任何一个支撑钢梁的损坏都会导致桥梁坍塌，这与选项C：桥体的支撑部分出现裂缝，一致。选项A工程师未能应用新开发的建筑材料，B没有足够的资金来修复桥梁，D有更大的交通高峰超过了设计师的预期，在原文中均未提及，属于无中生有。","options":["Engineers failed to apply the newly developed construction materials.","There was not enough finance to repair the bridges.","The supporting parts of the bridges may crack and cause the bridge to fail.","There were bigger traffic load conditions than the designers had anticipated."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"63482","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8783:63483:4","type":"choice","text":"Defect was not recognized by a basic method in the beginning","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The initial, crude analysis of the bridge’s behaviour, based on the frequency at which the bridge resonates, did not indicate that anything was wrong until the flange was damaged.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“工程师没有意识到基本方法的缺陷”，询问的是在什么条件下才意识到这点。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词“Defect was not recognized by a basic method in the beginning”对应原文中“did not indicate that anything was wrong until the flange was damaged”，即缺陷在损坏到翼缘之前没有被识别出来。\n解题思路：原文F段提到，基于桥梁共振频率的初步分析方法最初没有显示出任何问题，直到翼缘损坏。这与题目描述“工程师没有意识到基本方法的缺陷”一致，因此正确答案是B。","options":["until the mid of faces of bridges has fractures.","until the damage appears along and down to the flanges.","until the points on the road have been punched.","until the frequency of resonates appears disordered."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"63483","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8783:63484:5","type":"fill","text":"填写第 5 空","answer":"microwave dish","acceptedAnswers":["microwave dish"],"explanation":"原文答案句：After setting up the microwave dish on the ground below the bridge, the Los Alamos team installed conventional accelerometers at several points along the span to measure its motion.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求在图中填空，根据上下文推断应填入与桥梁检测技术相关的词语。\n定位关键信息：题目中的图片应与桥梁检测技术相关，通过图片的信息可知，该题需要填入一个设备的名称，该设备在地面上，接着定位到D段，该段提到监测桥梁的具体步骤方法。\n解题思路：该句提到，洛斯阿拉莫斯团队在桥下地面架设微波天线后，沿桥体跨度在多个点位安装了常规加速度计以测量其运动状态。所以，在地上放的设备是微波天线，原文中的\"microwave dish\"直接对应题目所需填入的标签。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63484","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nFilling the blanks in the diagram labels. Write the correct answer in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022OIku4KLyqF1669988644.png]"},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8783:63485:6","type":"fill","text":"填写第 6 空","answer":"accelerometers","acceptedAnswers":["accelerometers"],"explanation":"原文答案句：After setting up the microwave dish on the ground below the bridge, the Los Alamos team installed conventional accelerometers at several points along the span to measure its motion.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求在图表标签的空白处填入正确的答案，根据上下文推断是与测量桥梁运动相关的设备。\n定位关键信息：题目中的图片应与桥梁检测技术相关，可以定位到D段，该段提到监测桥梁的具体步骤方法。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到安装了\"conventional accelerometers\"（常规加速度计）来测量桥梁的运动，因此答案应为\"accelerometer\"。加速度计是一种用于测量物体加速度的设备，与题目中要求填入的测量运动的设备一致。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63485","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nFilling the blanks in the diagram labels. Write the correct answer in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022OIku4KLyqF1669988644.png]"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8783:63486:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"steel girders","acceptedAnswers":["steel girders"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘We then created damage that we hoped would simulate fatigue cracks that can occur in steel girders,’ says Farrar.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求填写图表标签的空白处，根据上下文推测是与桥梁结构相关的内容。\n定位关键信息：题目中的图片应与桥梁检测技术相关，可以定位到E段，该段也提到监测桥梁的具体步骤方法。\n解题思路：E段中，法勒解释道：‘我们通过制造损伤，来模拟钢梁可能出现的疲劳裂纹。’再联系图片，符合E段中描述的steel girders，同时，在上文中也提到，桥梁由两个钢梁支撑其载荷，也符合图片信息，故答案为steel girders。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63486","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nFilling the blanks in the diagram labels. Write the correct answer in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022OIku4KLyqF1669988644.png]"},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8783:63487:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"flange","acceptedAnswers":["flange"],"explanation":"原文答案句：They first cut a slot about 60centimetres long in the middle of one girder. They then extended the cut until it reached the bottom of the girder and finally they cut across the flange – the bottom of the girder’s ‘I’ shape.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求根据图表标签填写空白处的内容，需要根据文章中的信息确定桥梁构件的名称。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的空白处，结合图表可能显示的桥梁构件，定位到文章中描述桥梁构件名称的部分。\n解题思路：在E段中，研究人员描述了他们在桥梁钢梁上制造损坏的过程。原文中明确提到了“flange”这一术语，并解释了它是钢梁“工”字形底部的部分。因此，根据原文的描述和解释，可以确定答案为“flange”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63487","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nFilling the blanks in the diagram labels. Write the correct answer in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022OIku4KLyqF1669988644.png]"},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8783:63488:9","type":"choice","text":"9 How is the pressure that they have many a great chance to test bridges","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The Interstate 40 bridge over the Rio Grande river in Albuquerque provided the researchers with a rare opportunity to test their ideas.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求找到描述“他们如何获得测试桥梁的绝佳机会”这一信息的段落。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的“test bridges”和“many a great chance”可以定位到C段。C段中提到了“provided the researchers with a rare opportunity to test their ideas”，并且详细描述了他们在测试桥梁时所做的操作，如“mount instruments on it, test it under various load conditions and even inflict damage just before it was demolished”，这表明他们确实有机会测试桥梁。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句可以看出，C段明确提到了研究人员有机会测试桥梁，并且详细描述了他们在测试桥梁时所做的操作。这与题目中“的描述相符，因此C段是正确答案。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"63488","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet."},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8783:63488:10","type":"choice","text":"10 A ten-year positive change for microwave device","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Tim Darling, another Los Alamos physicist working on the microwave interferometer with Migliori, says that as the electronics become cheaper, a microwave inspection system will eventually be applied to most large bridges in the US.‘In a decade I would like to see a battery or solar-powered package mounted under each bridge, scanning it every day to detect changes,’ he says.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问哪个段落包含微波设备在未来十年内的变革信息。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"ten-year positive change\"和\"microwave device\"在文章中定位。\n解题思路：原文H段提到\"‘In a decade I would like to see a battery or solar-powered package mounted under each bridge, scanning it every day to detect changes,’ he says.\"，其中\"decade\"对应\"ten-year\"，\"microwave device\"对应文中提到的微波设备，该句描述了十年后微波设备将应用前景，与题干信息完全一致。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"63488","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet."},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8783:63488:11","type":"choice","text":"11 The chance they get a honorable contract","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：These more sophisticated algorithms, which were developed by Norris Stubbs at Texas A&M University, successfully identified and located the damage caused by the initial cut. Their progress and NASA contract application.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“他们有机会得到一份极具荣誉的合同”的相关信息在哪个段落。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“honorable contract”和“NASA contract application”可以定位到F段末句。\n解题思路：F段末句提到了“NASA contract application”，即与NASA合同申请相关的内容，这与题目中“获得一份极具荣誉合同的机会”相匹配。因此，答案为F段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"63488","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet."},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8783:63488:12","type":"choice","text":"12 Explanation of the mechanism for the new microwave monitoring to work","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The device uses microwaves to measure the distance between the sensor and the bridge, much like radar does, says Albert Migliori, a Los Alamos physicist, ‘Any load on the bridge – such as traffic – induces displacements, which change that distance as the bridge moves up and down.’ By monitoring these movements over several minutes, the researchers can find out how the bridge resonates. Changes in its behaviour can give an early warning of damage.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求找到解释“新型微波监测设备工作原理”的段落。\n定位关键信息： 使用 \"explanation\", \"mechanism\", \"microwave monitoring\", \"work\" 定位到文中详细描述该设备如何运作的段落。\n解题思路：段落B中，物理学家Albert Migliori清晰地解释了该设备的工作原理：它使用微波（像雷达一样）测量传感器与桥面之间的距离；桥上的载荷（如车辆）会引起位移，改变这个距离；通过监测这些运动可以了解桥梁的共振频率；其行为变化可提供损伤早期预警。这完整地解释了该技术的工作机制。因此，包含此信息的段落是B。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"63488","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet."},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8783:63488:13","type":"choice","text":"13 How is the damage deliberately created by the researchers","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：We then created damage that we hoped would simulate fatigue cracks that can occur in steel girders,’ says Farrar. They first cut a slot about 60centimetres long in the middle of one girder. They then extended the cut until it reached the bottom of the girder and finally they cut across the flange – the bottom of the girder’s ‘I’ shape.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求找到描述“研究人员如何故意制造损伤”这一信息的段落。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"damage deliberately created by the researchers\"定位，在文章中寻找研究人员故意制造损坏的具体描述。\n解题思路：根据原文E段中的句子，他们首先在一根工字钢的中部切出一个约60厘米长的槽口，接着将切口向工字钢底部延伸，最后横切其翼缘——即工字钢底部的“I”形部分。这与题目要求的信息一致，因此答案为E。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"63488","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"63480","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>How did the traditional way to prevent damage of the bridges before the invention of new monitoring system?</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"63481","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>How does the new microwave monitors find out the problems of bridges?</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"63482","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Why did the expert believe there is a problem for the design called ‘fracture critical’?</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"63483","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Defect was not recognized by a basic method in the beginning</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"63484","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nFilling the blanks in the diagram labels. Write the correct answer in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022OIku4KLyqF1669988644.png]","html":"<p><strong>5</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[5] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"63485","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nFilling the blanks in the diagram labels. Write the correct answer in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022OIku4KLyqF1669988644.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">6</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[6] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"63486","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nFilling the blanks in the diagram labels. Write the correct answer in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022OIku4KLyqF1669988644.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">7</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"63487","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nFilling the blanks in the diagram labels. Write the correct answer in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022OIku4KLyqF1669988644.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">8</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"63488","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 9-13\nThe reading passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>9 </strong>How is the pressure that they have many a great chance to test bridges<strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":9}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Keep a Watchful Eye on the Bridges&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Most road and rail bridges are only inspected visually, if at all. Every few months, engineers have to clamber over the structure in an attempt to find problems before the bridge shows obvious signs of damage. Technologies developed at Los Alamos National Laboratory, New Mexico, and Texas A&amp;M University may replace these surveys with microwave sensors that constantly monitor the condition of bridges.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘The device uses microwaves to measure the distance between the sensor and the bridge, much like radar does,’ says Albert Migliori, a Los Alamos physicist, ‘Any load on the bridge – such as traffic – induces displacements, which change that distance as the bridge moves up and down.’ By monitoring these movements over several minutes, the researchers can find out how the bridge resonates. Changes in its behaviour can give an early warning of damage.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The Interstate 40 bridge over the Rio Grande river in Albuquerque provided the researchers with a rare opportunity to test their ideas. Chuck Farrar, an engineer at Los Alamos, explains: ‘The New Mexico authorities decided to raze this bridge and replace it. We were able to mount instruments on it, test it under various load conditions and even inflict damage just before it was demolished.’ In the 1960s and 1970s, 2500 similar bridges were built in the US. They have two steel girders supporting the load in each section. Highway experts know that this design is ‘fracture critical’ because a failure in either girder would cause the bridge to fail.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>After setting up the microwave dish on the ground below the bridge, the Los Alamos team installed conventional accelerometers at several points along the span to measure its motion. They then tested the bridge while traffic roared across it and while subjecting it to pounding from a ‘shaker’, which delivered precise punches to a specific point on the road.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>‘We then created damage that we hoped would simulate fatigue cracks that can occur in steel girders,’ says Farrar. They first cut a slot about 60centimetres long in the middle of one girder. They then extended the cut until it reached the bottom of the girder and finally they cut across the flange – the bottom of the girder’s ‘I’ shape.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The initial, crude analysis of the bridge’s behaviour, based on the frequency at which the bridge resonates, did not indicate that anything was wrong until the flange was damaged. But later the data were reanalysed with algorithms that took into account changes in the mode shapes of the structure – shapes that the structure takes on when excited at a particular frequency. These more sophisticated algorithms, which were developed by Norris Stubbs at Texas A&amp;M University, successfully identified and located the damage caused by the initial cut. Their progress and NASA contract application.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>‘When any structure vibrates, the energy is distributed throughout with some points not moving, while others vibrate strongly at various frequencies,’ says Stubbs,’My algorithms use pattern recognition to detect changes in the distribution of this energy.’ NASA already uses Stubbs’ method to check the behaviour of the body flap that slows space shuttles down after they land.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>A commercial system based on the Los Alamos hardware is now available, complete with the Stubbs algorithms, from the Quatro Corporation in Albuquerque for about $100 000.Tim Darling, another Los Alamos physicist working on the microwave interferometer with Migliori, says that as the electronics become cheaper, a microwave inspection system will eventually be applied to most large bridges in the US. ‘In a decade I would like to see a battery or solar-powered package mounted under each bridge, scanning it every day to detect changes,’ he says.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8783&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8821","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 The Lost City","book":"阅读还原集Vol.15","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.15 · Test 3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8821:63795:14","type":"choice","text":"14 The reason why various investigative methods are introduced.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Dr Summers quickly realised it would take far too long to excavate the site using traditional techniques alone. So he decided to use modern technology as well to map the entire site, both above and beneath the surface, to locate the most interesting areas and priorities to start digging.\n对应段落：B段\n审题： 题目要求找到包含“引入各种调查方法的原因”这一信息的段落。\n定位关键信息： 使用 \"reason\", \"investigative methods\", \"introduced\" 定位到文中解释为何采用新技术进行调查的句子。\n解题思路：B段提到，萨默斯博士很快意识到，仅靠传统技术来挖掘遗址将耗时过长。因此，他决定采用现代技术对整个遗址进行测绘，包括地表和地下部分，以确定最值得优先挖掘的区域。这正是引入多种方法的原因。因此答案为B。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63795","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G Which paragraphs contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8821:63795:15","type":"choice","text":"15 An example of an unexpected discovery.","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：One surprise came when they dug out one of the fates in the defensive walls. ‘Our observations in early seasons led us to assume that wall, such as would be found at most other cities in the Ancient Near East,’ says Dr Summers. ‘When we started to excavate we were staggered to discover that the walls were made entirely from stone and that the gate would have stood at least ten metres high. After ten years of study, Pteria is gradually giving up its secrets.’\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段落包含了，一次意外发现的具体例子。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"unexpected discovery\"，可以在文章中寻找描述意外或惊讶发现的句子。\n解题思路：在G段中，考古人员在挖掘防御墙时意外发现，这类城墙与古代近东地区的墙完全不同，整面城墙完全由石材砌筑，城门高度至少有十米。这与题目中\"unexpected discovery\"的要求完全一致，因此G段是包含这一信息的段落。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63795","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G Which paragraphs contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8821:63795:16","type":"choice","text":"16 The methods to survey the surface of the site from above.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1993, Dr Summers hired a special hand-held balloon with a remote-controlled camera attached. He walked over the entire site holding the balloon and taking photos. The one afternoon, he rented a hot-air balloon and floated over the site, taking yet more pictures.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了，从上方调查遗址表面的方法。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"methods to survey the surface of the site from above\"（从上方调查遗址表面的方法），可以定位到文章中描述从空中或高处对遗址进行调查的部分。\n解题思路：在C段中，描述了Dr Summers使用手持气球和热气球从空中拍摄照片的过程，以及最终获得整个遗址的空中照片。这些活动都涉及从上方对遗址表面进行调查，因此C段包含了题目所要求的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63795","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G Which paragraphs contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8821:63795:17","type":"choice","text":"17 The reason why experts want to study the site.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Many respected archaeologists believe these are the remains of the fabled city of Pteria, the sixth-century BC stronghold of the Medes that the Greek historian Herodotus described in his famous work The Histories.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问哪一段提到了“专家想要研究该遗址的原因”。\n定位关键信息：根据题目的“experts want to study the site”可以定位到A段开头描述遗址的句子，其中提到“Many respected archaeologists believe these are the remains of the fabled city of Pteria”，解释了专家研究该遗址的原因。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，众多考古学家认为，这些遗迹正是公元前六世纪米底人要塞——传说中的佩特里亚城，希腊历史学家希罗多德在其名著《历史》中对此有详细记载。因此，专家研究该遗址的原因具有重要的历史价值，因此A段提到了题目中的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63795","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G Which paragraphs contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8821:63796:18","type":"fill","text":"填写第 18 空","answer":"hot-air balloon","acceptedAnswers":["hot-air balloon"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The one afternoon, he rented a hot-air balloon and floated over the site, taking yet more pictures.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是考古学家为了拍摄遗址，从高空拍摄时使用的工具是什么。\n定位关键信息：题目中提到了“photos of the site from...a distance”，结合“took photos of the site from the ground and then from a distance”，可以定位到C段中描述考古学家从高空拍摄的部分。\n解题思路：根据原文句子,那天下午，他租了一架热气球，飘浮在遗址上空，又拍了更多照片。可以确定考古学家使用的是热气球“hot-air balloon”来从高空拍摄遗址。题目中“from a distance”与原文“floated over the site”对应，因此答案为“hot-air balloon”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63796","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-25\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-25 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8821:63797:19","type":"fill","text":"填写第 19 空","answer":"iron particles","acceptedAnswers":["iron particles"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘The Earth’s magnetic field can vary from place to place, depending on what happened there in the past,’ says Branting, ‘if something containing iron oxide was heavily burnt, by natural or human actions, the iron particles in it can be permanently reoriented, like a compass needle, to align with the Earth’s magnetic field present at that point in time and space.’\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是由于大量热量的影响，地下结构中的什么会改变方向，这时磁场会发生变化。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"buried structures\"和\"changed direction\"定位到D段中描述铁氧化物在高温下改变方向的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，若某处曾因自然或人为原因发生过剧烈氧化铁燃烧，其内部的铁质颗粒就会像指南针的指针一样，永久性地重新定向，与该时空点的地球磁场保持一致。铁粒子（iron particles）在高温下被永久重新定向，与题干描述的吻合。因此答案为\"iron particles\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63797","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-25\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-25 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8821:63798:20","type":"fill","text":"填写第 20 空","answer":"compass/compass needle","acceptedAnswers":["compass","compass needle"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘The Earth’s magnetic field can vary from place to place, depending on what happened there in the past,’ says Branting, ‘if something containing iron oxide was heavily burnt, by natural or human actions, the iron particles in it can be permanently reoriented, like a compass needle, to align with the Earth’s magnetic field present at that point in time and space.’\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是铁粒子与磁场保持一致，类似于什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"match with the magnetic field\"和\"similar to\"定位到D段中描述铁粒子与磁场关系的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到铁粒子会像指南针的指针\"compass needle\"一样与地球磁场对齐，因此答案为compass needle。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63798","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-25\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-25 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8821:63799:21","type":"fill","text":"填写第 21 空","answer":"thin metal probe","acceptedAnswers":["thin metal probe"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The other main sub-surface mapping technique, which is still being used at the site, is resistivity. This technique measures the way electrical pulses are conducted through sub-surface oil. It’s done by shooting pulses into the ground through a thin metal probe.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是另一种遥感技术（resistivity）使用什么工具向地下发射电脉冲。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"resistivity\"和\"fire electrical pulses into the earth\"定位到F段，该段详细描述了resistivity技术的工作原理。\n解题思路：根据原文\"F段\"的句子，该技术通过测量电脉冲在地下油层中的传导方式来实现，具体操作是通过一根细金属探针向地下发射电脉冲。可知，resistivity技术是通过\"thin metal probe\"（细金属探针）向地下发射电脉冲的，因此答案为\"thin metal probe\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63799","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-25\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-25 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8821:63800:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"mudbrick","acceptedAnswers":["mudbrick"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Different materials have different electrical conductivity. For example, stone and mudbrick are poor conductors, but looser, damp soil conducts very well.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是什么材料和石头的导电性较差。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"building materials\"和\"conductivity\"（导电性）等关键词，在文章中寻找相关描述。F段提到了电阻率技术中不同材料的导电性对比。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，不同材料的导电性能存在差异：例如，石材和泥砖等材料导电性较差，而松散潮湿的土壤则具有极佳的导电性能。因此，mudbrick泥砖，是符合上下文逻辑和题目要求的正确答案。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63800","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-25\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-25 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8821:63801:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"looser damp soil","acceptedAnswers":["looser damp soil"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For example, stone and mudbrick are poor conductors, but looser, damp soil conducts very well.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是哪种物质导电性更好。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"stone\"和\"conduct electricity well\"定位到F段中关于导电性的描述。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到石头和泥砖导电性差，而松散潮湿的土壤导电性更好。题干中的\"does this much better\"对应原文中的\"conducts very well\"，因此答案为\"looser damp soil\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63801","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-25\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-25 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8821:63802:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"spring season","acceptedAnswers":["spring season"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This is one of the reasons that the project has a spring season when most of the resistivity work is done.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问考古学家通常会选择在什么时候使用这种技术，因为那时候的条件最适合。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"when conditions are more favourable\"提示需要找到使用电阻率法最佳时间，结合\"resistivity\"定位到F段。\n解题思路：原文F段提到\"resistivity\"（电阻率测量技术）的工作受天气影响，雨天有利于电流穿透，因此项目选择在春季进行大部分电阻率测量工作（\"a spring season when most of the resistivity work is done\"）。题目中的\"preferred to use this technique\"对应原文的\"most of the resistivity work is done\"，答案为\"spring season\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63802","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-25\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-25 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8821:63803:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"clarify ","acceptedAnswers":["clarify"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Consequently, the team is concentrating on areas where they want to clarify pictures from the magnetometry.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是电阻率技术主要被用来做什么工作。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"Resistivity\"和\"magnetometer\"，通过这些关键词可以在文章中找到相关的句子。在F段中，提到了电阻率技术，并且提到了磁测法生成的图像。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子\"Consequently, the team is concentrating on areas where they want to clarify pictures from the magnetometry.\"，可以确定电阻率技术主要是被用来需要进一步验证磁测法收集到的图像。因此，答案是\"clarify\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63803","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-25\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-25 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8821:63804:26","type":"choice","text":"How do modern remote-sensing techniques help at the site?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Remote sensing does not reveal everything about Kerkenes Dag, but it shows the most interesting sub-surface areas of the site. The archaeologists can then excavate these using traditional techniques.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问现代遥感技术怎样帮助研究遗址。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"modern remote-sensing techniques\"和\"help at the site\"，在文章中定位到G段首句，该句明确说明了遥感技术的作用。\n解题思路：原文G段首句指出，遥感技术虽然不能展现克尔肯内斯达格的全部信息，却能清晰呈现遗址最引人注目的地下区域。考古学家随后可运用传统方法对这些区域展开发掘。这对应选项B的\"bring parts of the site into the light so that key areas can be researched further\"，即让遗址的部分区域展现出来以便进一步研究关键区域。其他选项与原文描述不符：A项原文未提及避免挖掘；C项原文未提显示微小物体；D项原文未提一年四季可用。","options":["They avoid the need for experts to dig any part of the site.","They bring parts of the site into the light so that key areas can be researched further.","They show minute buried objects for the archaeologists to dig up.","They make the investigation more flexible as they can be used at any time of year."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"63804","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in the box 26 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"63795","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G Which paragraphs contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>14 </strong>The reason why various investigative methods are introduced.<strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"63796","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-25\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-25 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Exploring the Ancient City of Pteria The relevant work was done ten years ago. \nTo begin with, experts took photos of the site from the ground and then from a distance in a <strong>18.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[18] ____</strong> . To find out what lay below the surface, they used two leading techniques. One was magnetometer, which identifies changes in the magnetic field.</p>","firstNumber":18},{"id":"63797","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-25\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-25 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>These&nbsp;changes&nbsp;occur&nbsp;when&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>19.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong>&nbsp;in&nbsp;buried&nbsp;structures&nbsp;have&nbsp;changed&nbsp;direction&nbsp;as&nbsp;a&nbsp;result&nbsp;of&nbsp;great&nbsp;heat.&nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"63798","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-25\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-25 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>They&nbsp;match&nbsp;with&nbsp;the&nbsp;magnetic&nbsp;field,&nbsp;which&nbsp;is&nbsp;similar&nbsp;to&nbsp;a&nbsp;<strong>20.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong>&nbsp;.</p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"63799","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-25\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-25 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The&nbsp;other&nbsp;one&nbsp;was&nbsp;resistivity,&nbsp;which&nbsp;uses&nbsp;a&nbsp;<strong>21.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong>&nbsp;to&nbsp;fire&nbsp;electrical&nbsp;pulses&nbsp;into&nbsp;the&nbsp;earth.&nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"63800","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-25\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-25 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The&nbsp;principle&nbsp;is&nbsp;that&nbsp;building&nbsp;materials&nbsp;like&nbsp;<strong>22.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong>&nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"63801","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-25\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-25 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>and&nbsp;stone&nbsp;do&nbsp;not&nbsp;conduct&nbsp;electricity&nbsp;well,&nbsp;while&nbsp;<strong>23.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong>&nbsp;does&nbsp;this&nbsp;much&nbsp;better.</p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"63802","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-25\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-25 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Archaeologists&nbsp;preferred&nbsp;to&nbsp;use&nbsp;this&nbsp;technique&nbsp;during&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>24.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong>&nbsp;,&nbsp;when&nbsp;conditions&nbsp;are&nbsp;more&nbsp;favourable.&nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"63803","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-25\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-25 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Resistivity&nbsp;is&nbsp;mainly&nbsp;being&nbsp;used&nbsp;to&nbsp;<strong>25.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong>&nbsp;some&nbsp;images&nbsp;generated&nbsp;by&nbsp;the&nbsp;magnetometer.&nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"63804","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in the box 26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>How do modern remote-sensing techniques help at the site?</strong></p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The Lost City&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Thanks to modern remote-sensing techniques, a ruined city in Turkey is slowly revealing itself as one of the greatest and most mysterious cities of the ancient world. Sally Palmer uncovers more.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The low granite mountain, known as Kerkenes Dag, juts from the northern edge of the Cappadocian plain in Turkey. Sprawled over the mountainside are the ruins of an enormous city, contained by crumbling defensive walls seven kilometers long. Many respected archaeologists believe these are the remains of the fabled city of Pteria, the sixth-century BC stronghold of the Medes that the Greek historian Herodotus described in his famous work The Histories. The short-lived city came under Median control and only fifty years later was sacked, burned and its strong stone walls destroyed.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>British archaeologist Dr Geoffrey Summers has spent ten years studying the site. Excavating the ruins is a challenge because of the vast area they cover. The 7 km perimeter walls run around a site covering 271 hectares. Dr Summers quickly realised it would take far too long to excavate the site using traditional techniques alone. So he decided to use modern technology as well to map the entire site, both above and beneath the surface, to locate the most interesting areas and priorities to start digging.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In 1993, Dr Summers hired a special hand-held balloon with a remote-controlled camera attached. He walked over the entire site holding the balloon and taking photos. The one afternoon, he rented a hot-air balloon and floated over the site, taking yet more pictures. By the end of the 1994 season, Dr Summers and his team had a jigsaw of aerial photographs of the whole site. The next stage was to use remote sensing, which would let them work out what lay below the intriguing outlines and ruined walls. ‘Archaeology is a discipline that lends itself very well to remote sensing because it revolves around space,’ says Scott Branting, an associate director of the project. He started working with Dr Summers in 1995.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The project used two main remote-sensing techniques. The first is magnetometry, which works on the principle that magnetic fields at the surface of the Earth are influenced by what is buried beneath. It measures localised variations in the direction and intensity of this magnetic field. ‘The Earth’s magnetic field can vary from place to place, depending on what happened there in the past,’ says Branting, ‘if something containing iron oxide was heavily burnt, by natural or human actions, the iron particles in it can be permanently reoriented, like a compass needle, to align with the Earth’s magnetic field present at that point in time and space.’ The magnetometer detects differences in the orientations and intensities of these iron particles from the present-day magnetic field and uses them to produce an image of what lies below ground.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Kirkenes Dag lends itself particularly well to magnetometry because it was all burnt at once in a savage fire. In places, the heat was sufficient to turn sandstone to glass and to melt granite. The fire was so hot that there were strong magnetic signatures set to the Earth’s magnetic field from the time – around 547 BC – resulting in extremely clear pictures. Furthermore, the city was never rebuilt. ‘if you have multiple layers confusing picture because you have different walls from different periods giving signatures that all go in different directions,’ says Branting, ‘We only have one going down about 1.5 meters, so we can get a good picture of this fairly short-lived city.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The other main sub-surface mapping technique, which is still being used at the site, is resistivity. This technique measures the way electrical pulses are conducted through sub-surface oil. It’s done by shooting pulses into the ground through a thin metal probe. Different materials have different electrical conductivity. For example, stone and mudbrick are poor conductors, but looser, damp soil conducts very well. By walking around the site and taking about four readings per metre, it is possible to get a detailed idea of what is where beneath the surface. The teams then build up pictures of walls, hearths and other remains. ‘It helps a lot if it has rained because the electrical pulse can get through more easily,’ says Branting, ‘Then if something is more resistant, it really shows up.’ This is one of the reasons that the project has a spring season when most of the resistivity work is done. Unfortunately, testing resistivity is a lot slower than magnetometry. ‘If we did resistivity over the whole site it would take about 100 years,’ says Branting. Consequently, the team is concentrating on areas where they want to clarify pictures from the magnetometry.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Remote sensing does not reveal everything about Kerkenes Dag, but it shows the most interesting sub-surface areas of the site. The archaeologists can then excavate these using traditional techniques. One surprise came when they dug out one of the fates in the defensive walls. ‘Our observations in early seasons led us to assume that wall, such as would be found at most other cities in the Ancient Near East,’ says Dr Summers. ‘When we started to excavate we were staggered to discover that the walls were made entirely from stone and that the gate would have stood at least ten metres high. After ten years of study, Pteria is gradually giving up its secrets.’</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8821&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8822","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 TV Addiction","book":"阅读还原集Vol.15","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.15 · Test 3 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8822:63805:27","type":"choice","text":"Even researcher find sometimes it is more interesting in watching TV than talking with others in personal experience.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Percy Tannenbaum of the University of California at Berkeley has written: ‘Among life’s, more embarrassing moments have been countless occasions when I am engaged in conversation in a room while a TV set is on, and I cannot for the life of me stop from periodically glancing over to the screen. This occurs not only during dull conversations but during reasonably interesting ones just as well.’\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“即使是研究人员有时也发现，在个人经历中，看电视比与人交谈更有趣”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“researcher”和“watching TV”和“talking with others”定位到A段。\n解题思路：A段中引用了Percy Tannenbaum的话，他表示即使在与人交谈时，他也会不自觉地时不时地看向电视屏幕，这种情况不仅发生在无聊的交谈中，也发生在相当有趣的交谈中。这表明他认为看电视比与人交谈更有趣，因此题目的说法与原文一致，答案是True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63805","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8822:63806:28","type":"choice","text":"Information medium as TV has always been the priority for scientific research.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Scientists have been studying the effects of television for decades, generally focusing on whether watching violence on TV correlates with being violent in real life. Less attention has been paid to the basic allure of the small screen – the medium, as opposed to the message.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“信息媒介电视一直是科学研究的重点”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“information medium as TV”和“scientific research”定位到B段，原文提到科学家们几十年来一直在研究电视的情况。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，科学家们几十年来一直在研究电视的影响，通常关注的是看电视上的暴力是否与现实生活中的暴力行为有关。较少关注的是小屏幕的基本吸引力——媒介，而不是信息。题目中的说法与原文信息不符，故答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63806","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8822:63807:29","type":"choice","text":"It is partially unscientific to use the term ‘TV addiction’.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The term ‘TV addiction’ is imprecise and laden with value judgments, but it captures the essence of a very real phenomenon.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问“使用“使用‘电视成瘾’这一术语在某种程度上是不科学的。”是否与作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“TV addiction”定位到C段首句。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，“电视成瘾”这个说法虽然不够精准且带有主观判断色彩，却精准捕捉到了这种真实现象的本质。这表明作者认为这个术语存在科学上的不严谨性。题目中的“partially unscientific”与原文的“imprecise”和“laden with value judgments”对应。因此，选择True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63807","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8822:63808:30","type":"choice","text":"Children do not know why they exercise too little.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：文中未提及儿童是否了解自己运动量过少的原因。\n对应段落：无\n审题： 题目判断“儿童不知道他们为什么运动过少”这一说法是否与作者在文中的主张一致。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"children\", \"do not know\", \"why\", \"exercise too little\" 定位到文中讨论儿童运动量及其认知的句子。\n解题思路：文章通篇都在讨论电视对人们（包括成人和儿童）的吸引力及其心理和生理机制，也提到了父母对子女看电视的担忧。然而，文中完全没有涉及儿童关于自身运动量的“认知”或“理解”，更没有探讨他们是否“知道”运动少的原因。题目信息在原文中找不到依据，因此答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63808","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8822:63809:31-32-33","type":"choice","text":"Which THREE of the following are benefits of watching TV?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Television can teach and amuse; it can reach aesthetic heights; it can provide much-needed distraction and escape.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是观看电视有哪些好处。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"benefits of watching TV\"定位到文章中描述电视好处的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，电视既能寓教于乐，又能带来审美享受，还能提供我们需要的消遣，让我们暂时逃离生活。这些分别对应选项中的D（学习知识和教育）、A（艺术灵感）和C（缓解压力）。因此，正确答案是ACD。","options":["artistic inspiration","family reunion","relieve stress","learn knowledge and education","work efficiency","ease communicative conflict"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"63809","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 31-33\nChoose THREE letters, A-F Write the correct letters in boxes 31-33 on your answer sheet.","groupId":"63809-8822:63809:31-32-33"},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8822:63809:31-32-33","type":"choice","text":"Which THREE of the following are benefits of watching TV?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Television can teach and amuse; it can reach aesthetic heights; it can provide much-needed distraction and escape.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是观看电视有哪些好处。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"benefits of watching TV\"定位到文章中描述电视好处的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，电视既能寓教于乐，又能带来审美享受，还能提供我们需要的消遣，让我们暂时逃离生活。这些分别对应选项中的D（学习知识和教育）、A（艺术灵感）和C（缓解压力）。因此，正确答案是ACD。","options":["artistic inspiration","family reunion","relieve stress","learn knowledge and education","work efficiency","ease communicative conflict"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"63809","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 31-33\nChoose THREE letters, A-F Write the correct letters in boxes 31-33 on your answer sheet.","groupId":"63809-8822:63809:31-32-33"},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8822:63809:31-32-33","type":"choice","text":"Which THREE of the following are benefits of watching TV?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Television can teach and amuse; it can reach aesthetic heights; it can provide much-needed distraction and escape.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是观看电视有哪些好处。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"benefits of watching TV\"定位到文章中描述电视好处的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，电视既能寓教于乐，又能带来审美享受，还能提供我们需要的消遣，让我们暂时逃离生活。这些分别对应选项中的D（学习知识和教育）、A（艺术灵感）和C（缓解压力）。因此，正确答案是ACD。","options":["artistic inspiration","family reunion","relieve stress","learn knowledge and education","work efficiency","ease communicative conflict"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"63809","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 31-33\nChoose THREE letters, A-F Write the correct letters in boxes 31-33 on your answer sheet.","groupId":"63809-8822:63809:31-32-33"},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8822:63810:34","type":"choice","text":"34 Percy Tannenbaum.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Percy Tannenbaum of the University of California at Berkeley has written: ‘Among life’s, more embarrassing moments have been countless occasions when I am engaged in conversation in a room while a TV set is on, and I cannot for the life of me stop from periodically glancing over to the screen. This occurs not only during dull conversations but during reasonably interesting ones just as well.’\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是Percy Tannenbaum的研究内容或观点。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"Percy Tannenbaum\"定位到A段，找到他关于电视的描述。\n解题思路：Percy Tannenbaum描述了即使在有趣的对话中，他也无法停止不自觉地看电视屏幕，与选项D\"难以忽视电视的影响\"相符，因此选择D项。","options":["It is the specific media formal characteristic that counts.","TV distraction shows a human physical reaction to a new and prompted stimulus.","Conveying information is the most important thing.","It is hard to ignore the effects of TV.","Whether people can remember deeper of the content relates to the format.","The heart rate remains stable when watching.","Clinically reliance on TV does not meet the criteria of addiction."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63810","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 34-37\nLook at the following researchers (Questions 34-37) and the list of statements below.Match each researcher with the correct statements. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 34-37 on your answer sheets.\nA It is the specific media formal characteristic that counts.\nB TV distraction shows a human physical reaction to a new and prompted stimulus.\nC Conveying information is the most important thing.\nD It is hard to ignore the effects of TV.\nE Whether people can remember deeper of the content relates to the format.\nF The heart rate remains stable when watching.\nG Clinically reliance on TV does not meet the criteria of addiction."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8822:63810:35","type":"choice","text":"35 Ivan Pavlov.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：First described by Ivan Pavlov in 1927, the orienting response is our instinctive visual or auditory reaction to any sudden or novel stimulus. It is part of our evolutionary heritage, a built-in sensitivity to movement and potential predatory threats.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求将研究者Ivan Pavlov与对应的观点匹配。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的研究者姓名\"Ivan Pavlov\"定位到文章中F段，该段明确提到了他的研究内容。\n解题思路：原文中提到，这种反应最早由伊万·巴甫洛夫在1927年提出，是人类对突发或新奇刺激的本能视觉或听觉反应。作为进化遗产的一部分，这种反应使我们天生对运动和潜在的捕食者威胁保持高度敏感。因此可以确定Ivan Pavlov对应的是关于\"orienting response\"的陈述。结合选项，B项（电视分散注意力的现象，体现了人类对新异刺激产生的本能生理反应）与原文一致，故答案为B。","options":["It is the specific media formal characteristic that counts.","TV distraction shows a human physical reaction to a new and prompted stimulus.","Conveying information is the most important thing.","It is hard to ignore the effects of TV.","Whether people can remember deeper of the content relates to the format.","The heart rate remains stable when watching.","Clinically reliance on TV does not meet the criteria of addiction."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63810","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 34-37\nLook at the following researchers (Questions 34-37) and the list of statements below.Match each researcher with the correct statements. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 34-37 on your answer sheets.\nA It is the specific media formal characteristic that counts.\nB TV distraction shows a human physical reaction to a new and prompted stimulus.\nC Conveying information is the most important thing.\nD It is hard to ignore the effects of TV.\nE Whether people can remember deeper of the content relates to the format.\nF The heart rate remains stable when watching.\nG Clinically reliance on TV does not meet the criteria of addiction."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8822:63810:36","type":"choice","text":"36 Byron Reeves and Esther Thorson.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1986 Byron Reeves of Stanford University, Esther Thorson of the University of Missouri and their colleagues began to study whether the simple formal features of television – cuts, edits, zooms, pans, sudden noises – activate the orienting response, thereby keeping attention on the screen. By watching how brain waves were affected by formal features, the researchers concluded that these stylistic tricks can indeed trigger involuntary responses and ‘derive their attentional value through the evolutionary significance of detecting movement … It is the form, not the content, of television that is unique.’\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求匹配Byron Reeves和Esther Thorson的观点。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的姓名Byron Reeves和Esther Thorson定位到G段，找到他们研究的核心内容。\n解题思路：G段明确提到，Byron Reeves和Esther Thorson开始研究：电视节目中的剪辑手法——如镜头切换、画面调整、变焦推拉、突然出现的声响等——是否能激活定向反应，从而让观众的注意力持续锁定在屏幕上。通过观察这些视觉元素对脑电波的影响，研究者们得出结论：这些手法确实能触发本能反应来吸引注意力。这与选项A（电视成瘾背后原因在于媒介表现形式）的描述完全一致，因此答案为A。","options":["It is the specific media formal characteristic that counts.","TV distraction shows a human physical reaction to a new and prompted stimulus.","Conveying information is the most important thing.","It is hard to ignore the effects of TV.","Whether people can remember deeper of the content relates to the format.","The heart rate remains stable when watching.","Clinically reliance on TV does not meet the criteria of addiction."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63810","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 34-37\nLook at the following researchers (Questions 34-37) and the list of statements below.Match each researcher with the correct statements. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 34-37 on your answer sheets.\nA It is the specific media formal characteristic that counts.\nB TV distraction shows a human physical reaction to a new and prompted stimulus.\nC Conveying information is the most important thing.\nD It is hard to ignore the effects of TV.\nE Whether people can remember deeper of the content relates to the format.\nF The heart rate remains stable when watching.\nG Clinically reliance on TV does not meet the criteria of addiction."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8822:63810:37","type":"choice","text":"37 Annie Lang.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In one of their studies, participants watched a program and then filled out a score sheet. Increasing the frequency of edits (defined here as a change from one camera angle to another in the same visual scene) improved memory recognition, presumably because it focused attention on the screen. Increasing the frequency of cuts – changes to a new visual scene – had a similar effect but only up to a point. If the number of cuts exceeded 10 in two minutes, recognition dropped off sharply.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问Annie Lang的观点是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"Annie Lang\"可以定位到I段，该段描述了Annie Lang的研究内容。\n解题思路：I段详细描述了Annie Lang的研究，她研究了电视的形式特征（如镜头切换频率和画面切换频率）如何影响人们的记忆。研究发现，增加镜头切换频率（即同一画面中不同拍摄角度的转换）能提升记忆识别能力，但增加切换频率超过一定限度会降低记忆识别。这与选项E（人们能否深入理解内容，取决于呈现方式。）的描述完全一致，因此答案为E。","options":["It is the specific media formal characteristic that counts.","TV distraction shows a human physical reaction to a new and prompted stimulus.","Conveying information is the most important thing.","It is hard to ignore the effects of TV.","Whether people can remember deeper of the content relates to the format.","The heart rate remains stable when watching.","Clinically reliance on TV does not meet the criteria of addiction."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63810","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 34-37\nLook at the following researchers (Questions 34-37) and the list of statements below.Match each researcher with the correct statements. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 34-37 on your answer sheets.\nA It is the specific media formal characteristic that counts.\nB TV distraction shows a human physical reaction to a new and prompted stimulus.\nC Conveying information is the most important thing.\nD It is hard to ignore the effects of TV.\nE Whether people can remember deeper of the content relates to the format.\nF The heart rate remains stable when watching.\nG Clinically reliance on TV does not meet the criteria of addiction."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8822:63811:38","type":"fill","text":"填写第 38 空","answer":"popular pastime/Popular Pastime","acceptedAnswers":["popular pastime","Popular Pastime"],"explanation":"原文答案句：One activity, however, stands out for its prominence and ubiquity – the world’s most popular pastime, television.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问电视正在成为全球的什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"worldwide\"定位到A段，其中提到电视是\"the world’s most popular pastime\"。\n解题思路：原文明确指出电视是世界最受欢迎的消遣活动（popular pastime），题目中的\"worldwide\"对应原文中的\"world’s\"，因此答案为\"popular pastime\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63811","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8822:63812:39","type":"fill","text":"填写第 39 空","answer":"TV addicts/TV Addicts","acceptedAnswers":["TV addicts","TV Addicts"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Other surveys have consistently shown that roughly 10 percent of adults calls themselves TV addicts.\n对应段落：E段\n审题： 题目要求完成句子，说明在一项调查中，有一小部分人甚至声称自己是什么。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"surveys\", \"small group\", \"claim themselves\" 定位到文中描述调查结果，特别是关于人们自我认知的句子。\n解题思路：段落E中，原文明确提到，“其他调查一致显示，大约10%的成年人称自己为电视成瘾者”。因此，空格处应填入“TV addicts”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63812","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8822:63813:40","type":"fill","text":"填写第 40 空","answer":"orienting response/Orienting Response","acceptedAnswers":["orienting response","Orienting Response"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In part, the attraction seems to spring from our biological ‘orienting response’. First described by Ivan Pavlov in 1927, the orienting response is our instinctive visual or auditory reaction to any sudden or novel stimulus. It is part of our evolutionary heritage, a built-in sensitivity to movement and potential predatory threats.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求完成句子，说明一位研究者认为这种吸引力源于我们的人类本能，这种本能被描述为什么，是我们生理进化中固有的部分。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"researcher believes\", \"attraction comes from\", \"human instinct\", \"built-in part\", \"physiological evolution\" 定位到文中解释电视吸引力来源的段落。\n解题思路：段落F中，原文明确指出，电视的吸引力部分源于我们的生物“‘定向反应’”，并且“这是我们进化遗留的一部分，是一种对运动和潜在捕食威胁的内在敏感性”。因此，空格处应填入“orienting response”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63813","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"63809-8822:63809:31-32-33","numbers":[31,32,33],"selectionCount":3,"answers":["A","C","D"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"63805","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Even researcher find sometimes it is more interesting in watching TV than talking with others in personal experience.</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"63806","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Information medium as TV has always been the priority for scientific research.</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"63807","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>It is partially unscientific to use the term ‘TV addiction’.</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"63808","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Children do not know why they exercise too little.</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"63809","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 31-33\nChoose THREE letters, A-F Write the correct letters in boxes 31-33 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Which THREE of the following are benefits of watching TV?</strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"63810","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 34-37\nLook at the following researchers (Questions 34-37) and the list of statements below.Match each researcher with the correct statements. Write the correct letter A-G in boxes 34-37 on your answer sheets.\nA It is the specific media formal characteristic that counts.\nB TV distraction shows a human physical reaction to a new and prompted stimulus.\nC Conveying information is the most important thing.\nD It is hard to ignore the effects of TV.\nE Whether people can remember deeper of the content relates to the format.\nF The heart rate remains stable when watching.\nG Clinically reliance on TV does not meet the criteria of addiction.","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> It is the specific media formal characteristic that counts. <br/></p><p><strong>B</strong> TV distraction shows a human physical reaction to a new and prompted stimulus. <br/></p><p><strong>C</strong> Conveying information is the most important thing. <br/></p><p><strong>D</strong> It is hard to ignore the effects of TV. <br/></p><p><strong>E</strong> Whether people can remember deeper of the content relates to the format. <br/></p><p><strong>F</strong> The heart rate remains stable when watching. <br/></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>G</strong> Clinically reliance on TV does not meet the criteria of addiction. <br/></p><p><strong>34</strong> Percy Tannenbaum. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[34] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"63811","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The TV is becoming a worldwide <strong>38</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[38] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"63812","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Some people love it and spend a great\ndeal of time watching it. According to some surveys, a small group even claim themselves as<strong> 39</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[39] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"63813","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>One researcher believes that this attraction comes from our human instinct,\ndescribed as <strong>40</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[40] ____</strong> which is built-in part of our physiological evolution.</p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>TV Addiction 2</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Excessive cravings do not necessarily involve physical substances. Gambling can become compulsive; sex can become obsessive. One activity, however, stands out for its prominence and ubiquity – the world’s most popular pastime, television. Most people admit to having a love-hate relationship with it. They complain about the ‘boob tube’ and ‘couch potatoes’, then they settle into their sofas and grab the remote control. Parents commonly fret about their children’s viewing (if not their own). Even researchers who study TV for a living marvel at the medium’s hold on them personally. Percy Tannenbaum of the University of California at Berkeley has written: ‘Among life’s, more embarrassing moments have been countless occasions when I am engaged in conversation in a room while a TV set is on, and I cannot for the life of me stop from periodically glancing over to the screen. This occurs not only during dull conversations but during reasonably interesting ones just as well.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Scientists have been studying the effects of television for decades, generally focusing on whether watching violence on TV correlates with being violent in real life. Less attention has been paid to the basic allure of the small screen – the medium, as opposed to the message.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The term ‘TV addiction’ is imprecise and laden with value judgments, but it captures the essence of a very real phenomenon. Psychologists and psychiatrists formally define substance dependence as a disorder characterized by criteria that include spending a great deal of time using the substance; using it more often than one intends; thinking about reducing use or making repeated unsuccessful efforts to reduce use; giving up important social, family or occupational activities to use it; and reporting withdrawal symptoms when one stops using it.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>All these criteria can apply to people who watch a lot of television. That does not mean that watching television, in itself, is problematic. Television can teach and amuse; it can reach aesthetic heights; it can provide much-needed distraction and escape. The difficulty arises when people strongly sense that they ought not to watch as much as they do and yet find themselves strangely unable to reduce their viewing. Some knowledge of how the medium exerts its pull may help heavy viewers gain better control over their lives.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The amount of time people spend watching television is astonishing. On average, individuals in the industrialized world devote three hours a day to the pursuit – fully half of their leisure time, and more than on any single activity save work and sleep. At this rate, someone who lives to 75 would spend nine years in front of the tube. To some commentators, this devotion means simply that people enjoy TV and make a conscious decision to watch it. But if that is the whole story, why do so many people experience misgivings about how much they view? In Gallup polls in 1992 and 1999, two out of five adult respondents and seven out of 10 teenagers said they spent too much time watching TV. Other surveys have consistently shown that roughly 10 percent of adults calls themselves TV addicts.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>What is it about TV that has such a hold on us? In part, the attraction seems to spring from our biological ‘orienting response’. First described by Ivan Pavlov in 1927, the orienting response is our instinctive visual or auditory reaction to any sudden or novel stimulus. It is part of our evolutionary heritage, a built-in sensitivity to movement and potential predatory threats.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In 1986 Byron Reeves of Stanford University, Esther Thorson of the University of Missouri and their colleagues began to study whether the simple formal features of television – cuts, edits, zooms, pans, sudden noises – activate the orienting response, thereby keeping attention on the screen. By watching how brain waves were affected by formal features, the researchers concluded that these stylistic tricks can indeed trigger involuntary responses and ‘derive their attentional value through the evolutionary significance of detecting movement … It is the form, not the content, of television that is unique.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The orienting response many partly explain common viewer remarks such as: ‘If a television is on, I just can’t keep my eyes off it’, ‘I don’t want to watch as much as I do, but I can’t help it’, and ‘I feel hypnotized when I watch television.’ In the years since Reeves and Thorson published their pioneering work, researchers have delved deeper. Annie Lang’s research team at Indiana University has shown that heart rate decreases for four to six seconds after an orienting stimulus. In ads, action sequences and music videos, formal features frequently come at a rate of one per second, thus activating the orienting response continuously.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Lang and her colleagues have also investigated whether formal features affect people’s memory of what they have seen. In one of their studies, participants watched a program and then filled out a score sheet. Increasing the frequency of edits (defined here as a change from one camera angle to another in the same visual scene) improved memory recognition, presumably because it focused attention on the screen. Increasing the frequency of cuts – changes to a new visual scene – had a similar effect but only up to a point. If the number of cuts exceeded 10 in two minutes, recognition dropped off sharply.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Producers of educational television for children have found that formal features can help to learn. But increasing the rate of cuts and edits eventually overloads the brain. Music videos and commercials that use rapid intercutting of unrelated scenes are designed to hold attention more than they are to convey information. People may remember the name of the product or band, but the details of the ad itself float in one ear and out the other. The orienting response is overworked. Viewers still attend to the screen, but they feel tired and worn out, with little compensation psychological reward. Our ESM findings show much the same thing. K Sometimes the memory of the product is very subtle. Many ads today are deliberately oblique: they have an engaging storyline, but it is hard to tell what they are trying to sell. Afterwards, you may not remember the product consciously. Yet advertisers believe that if they have gotten your attention when you later go to the store you will feel better or more comfortable with a given product because you have a vague recollection of having heard of it.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8822&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8720","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Ecotourism in the Developing Courtiers","book":"阅读还原集Vol.15","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.15 · Test 2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8720:62964:1","type":"choice","text":"1 a place to improve local education to help tourists","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Ecotourism is also seen as an environmental education opportunity to heighten both visitors’ and residents’ awareness of environmental and conservation issues, and even to inspire conservation action.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问哪个地方通过改善当地教育来服务游客。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“improve local education”和“help tourists”在文章中定位答案。\n解题思路：根据原文句子，B段提到古巴的生态旅游是一个环境教育的机会，可以提升游客和居民对环境和保护问题的认识，甚至激发保护行动。因此，古巴通过改善当地教育来服务游客。","options":["Cuba","East Africa","South America","Indonesia"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"62964","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nUse the information in the passage to match the place (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nA Cuba\nB East Africa\nC South America\nD Indonesia"},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8720:62964:2","type":"choice","text":"2 a place suitable for both rich and poor travelers","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The market segment for Indonesian ecotourism consists of: (i) ‘The silent generation’, 55-64 year-old people who are wealthy enough, generally well-educated and have no dependent children, and can travel for four weeks; (ii) ‘The baby boom generation’, junior successful executives aged 35-54 years, who are likely to be travelling with their family and children (spending 2-3 weeks on travel) – travelling for them is a stress reliever; and (iii) the ‘X generation’, aged 18-29 years, who love to do ecotours as backpackers – they are generally students who can travel for 3-12 months with monthly expenditure of US $300-500.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是在哪个地方旅游，富人还是穷人都能负担得起。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"rich and poor travelers\"可以定位到F段，该段落提到了印度尼西亚的生态旅游市场分为三个部分，分别对应不同年龄段和消费水平的旅行者。\n解题思路：原文中F段明确提到了印度尼西亚的生态旅游市场分为三个部分，包括富裕的\"沉默一代\"（55-64岁）、中产的\"婴儿潮一代\"（35-54岁）以及贫穷的\"X一代\"（18-29岁），这正好对应了题目中提到的适合富裕和贫穷旅行者的地方。因此，答案为D。","options":["Cuba","East Africa","South America","Indonesia"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"62964","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nUse the information in the passage to match the place (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nA Cuba\nB East Africa\nC South America\nD Indonesia"},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8720:62964:3","type":"choice","text":"3 a place where could easily get fungus","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Most recently, outbreaks have been reported in healthy travelers who returned from Central and South America after engaging in recreational activities associated with spelunking, adventure tourism, and ecotourism.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“一个容易感染真菌的地方”。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词“fungus”定位到C段，该段提到“Histoplasma capsulatum, a dimorphic fungus, is the most common endemic mycosis in the United States, and is associated with exposure to bat or bird droppings.”，并且提到“outbreaks have been reported in healthy travelers who returned from Central and South America after engaging in recreational activities associated with spelunking, adventure tourism, and ecotourism.”。\n解题思路：根据原文信息，C段明确提到来自中美洲和南美洲的旅行者在参与洞穴探险、冒险旅游和生态旅游等活动后，出现了真菌感染的爆发。因此，C段是描述一个容易感染真菌的地方，即南美洲，选择C项。","options":["Cuba","East Africa","South America","Indonesia"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"62964","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nUse the information in the passage to match the place (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nA Cuba\nB East Africa\nC South America\nD Indonesia"},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8720:62964:4","type":"choice","text":"4 a place taking a method to stop unlawful poaching","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In East Africa, significantly reducing such illegal hunting and allowing wildlife populations to recover would allow the generation of significant economic benefits through trophy hunting and potentially ecotourism.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是哪个地方采取了制止非法偷猎的措施。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“stop unlawful poaching”可以定位到E段中的“significantly reducing such illegal hunting”。\n解题思路：E段提到了东非通过减少非法狩猎来恢复野生动物种群，这样就能通过狩猎和生态旅游产生经济效益。这与题目中“制止非法偷猎”的要求相符，因此答案是B。","options":["Cuba","East Africa","South America","Indonesia"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"62964","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nUse the information in the passage to match the place (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nA Cuba\nB East Africa\nC South America\nD Indonesia"},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8720:62964:5","type":"choice","text":"5 a place where the healthcare system is developed","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Raul Castro, brother of the Cuban president, started this initiative to rescue the Cuban tradition of herbal medicine and provide natural medicines for its healthcare system.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是哪个地方推动了医疗保健系统的发展。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"healthcare system\"定位到B段中提到的\"Cuban tradition of herbal medicine and provide natural medicines for its healthcare system\"。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到了古巴的医疗保健系统，并且指出古巴总统的兄弟拉乌尔·卡斯特罗发起了这一倡议，旨在复兴古巴传统草药，为该国医疗体系提供天然药物。因此，答案为A。","options":["Cuba","East Africa","South America","Indonesia"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"62964","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nUse the information in the passage to match the place (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nA Cuba\nB East Africa\nC South America\nD Indonesia"},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8720:62965:6","type":"choice","text":"6 Visiting the cheese factory","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The cheese factory here exports great quantity of cheese to various countries across the globe. It is located in the center of forest.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是参观奶酪工厂时的情景或特点。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"cheese factory\"定位到H段，找到描述奶酪工厂位置的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到奶酪工厂位于森林中心，即\"in the center of forest\"，这与选项C中的\"which is situated in the heart of the jungle\"（位于丛林中心）意思完全一致。因此答案为C。","options":["eating the local fruits at the same time","find job opportunities in the community","which is situated in the heart of the jungle","with private and comfortable service"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"62965","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 6-9\nUse the information in the passage to match the companies (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A, B, C or D in boxes 6-9 on your answer sheet.\nA eating the local fruits at the same time\nB find job opportunities in the community\nC which is situated in the heart of the jungle\nD with private and comfortable service"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8720:62965:7","type":"choice","text":"7 Enjoying the honeymoon","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It is the wonderful place for Hamanasi honeymoon, bottle of champagne upon arrival, three meals daily, a private service on one night of your stay and a choice of adventures depending on the length of your stay.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是关于享受蜜月的信息。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"enjoying the honeymoon\"可以定位到G段中提到的\"Hamanasi honeymoon\"。\n解题思路：G段中明确提到了Hamanasi是一个非常适合蜜月的地方，提供了香槟、每日三餐、一晚的私人服务以及根据停留时间选择的活动等，这些都是享受蜜月的具体描述。因此，答案为D。","options":["eating the local fruits at the same time","find job opportunities in the community","which is situated in the heart of the jungle","with private and comfortable service"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"62965","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 6-9\nUse the information in the passage to match the companies (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A, B, C or D in boxes 6-9 on your answer sheet.\nA eating the local fruits at the same time\nB find job opportunities in the community\nC which is situated in the heart of the jungle\nD with private and comfortable service"},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8720:62965:8","type":"choice","text":"8 Having the picnic while","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Gregory Pereira, an extremely knowledgeable and outgoing hiking and tour guide, says the following about his tours: ‘All of our tours on St. Kitts include transportation by specially modified Land Rovers, a picnic of island pastries and local fruit, fresh tropical juices, CSR, a qualified island guide and a full liability insurance coverage for participants.’\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是在野餐时有什么活动。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词“picnic”定位到G段中关于野餐的描述。\n解题思路：在G段中，提到了“a picnic of island pastries and local fruit, fresh tropical juices”，这表明在野餐时会有岛上的糕点和水果，以及新鲜的热带果汁。因此，答案是A。","options":["eating the local fruits at the same time","find job opportunities in the community","which is situated in the heart of the jungle","with private and comfortable service"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"62965","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 6-9\nUse the information in the passage to match the companies (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A, B, C or D in boxes 6-9 on your answer sheet.\nA eating the local fruits at the same time\nB find job opportunities in the community\nC which is situated in the heart of the jungle\nD with private and comfortable service"},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8720:62965:9","type":"choice","text":"9 The residents in Cuba could","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In Cuba, ecotourism has the potential to alleviate poverty by bringing money into the economy and creating jobs. In addition to the environmental impacts of these efforts, the area works on developing community employment opportunities for locals, in conjunction with ecotourism.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问古巴的居民可以通过生态旅游获得什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"Cuba\"和\"residents\"定位到B段，找到与古巴居民相关的句子。\n解题思路：段落B中，原文明确指出，除了环境影响之外，该地区还致力于“为当地居民发展社区就业机会”，这与生态旅游相结合。“为当地居民发展社区就业机会”(developing community employment opportunities for locals) 与选项B中的“在社区中找到工作机会”(find job opportunities in the community) 形成了直接且清晰的对应。因此，描述“古巴的居民可以...”所对应的特征就是B。","options":["eating the local fruits at the same time","find job opportunities in the community","which is situated in the heart of the jungle","with private and comfortable service"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"62965","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 6-9\nUse the information in the passage to match the companies (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A, B, C or D in boxes 6-9 on your answer sheet.\nA eating the local fruits at the same time\nB find job opportunities in the community\nC which is situated in the heart of the jungle\nD with private and comfortable service"},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8720:62966:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"adventure","acceptedAnswers":["adventure"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Nowhere is the keen eye and intimate knowledge of ecotourism is more amidst this fantastic biodiversity, as we explore remote realms rich in wildlife rather than a nature adventure.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问“生态旅游不是一种自然______”，需要填入一个与自然相关的词，且该词在原文中出现过。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"not a nature\" 定位到文中将生态旅游与某种“自然活动”进行对比或区分的句子。\n解题思路：段落D中，原文明确将生态旅游描述为“探索充满野生动植物的偏远领域，而非一次自然冒险”。“而非”(rather than) 这个对比词清晰地表明，生态旅游被定义为超越“自然冒险”(nature adventure) 的活动。因此，空格处应填入“adventure”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62966","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8720:62967:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"sustainable","acceptedAnswers":["sustainable"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A sustainable tour is significant for ecotourism, one in which we can grow hand in hand with nature and our community, respecting everything that makes us privileged.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求填空，补充完整句子，需要根据文章内容选择一个合适的词组。\n定位关键信息：题目中的“tour”是定位关键词，通过浏览文章寻找与“tour”相关的句子，发现D段提到了“sustainable tour”。\n解题思路：D段明确提到“a sustainable tour is significant for ecotourism”，说明可持续旅游对生态旅游很重要。题目中说，生态旅游不是一种自然冒险，而是一次什么样的旅游，D段中的“sustainable”与题目结构匹配，且符合生态旅游的语境。因此答案为“sustainable”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62967","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8720:62968:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"tropical forests","acceptedAnswers":["tropical forests"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The primary threats to South America’s tropical forests are deforestation caused by agricultural expansion, cattle ranching, fagging, oil extraction and spills, mining, illegal coca farming, and colonization initiatives.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是南美推广生态旅游的原因是由于什么的破坏。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“South America”和“promotes ecotourism”定位到D段，该段提到南美洲的热带森林面临的主要威胁。\n解题思路：根据原文句子“South America’s tropical forests”可以确定答案为“tropical forests”，因为原文明确指出南美洲推广生态旅游的原因是热带森林的破坏。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62968","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8720:62969:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"illegal hunting","acceptedAnswers":["illegal hunting"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In East Africa, significantly reducing such illegal hunting and allowing wildlife populations to recover would allow the generation of significant economic benefits through trophy hunting and potentially ecotourism.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是东非鼓励这种旅游方式是为了减少什么以拯救野生动物。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"East Africa\"和\"cutting\"可以定位到E段第一句，该句提到了\"reducing such illegal hunting\"。\n解题思路：原文明确提到东非通过减少\"illegal hunting\"来保护野生动物，题目中的\"cutting\"对应原文的\"reducing\"，而\"illegal killing\"是\"illegal hunting\"的另一种表达方式，符合题目要求。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62969","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"62964","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nUse the information in the passage to match the place (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nA Cuba\nB East Africa\nC South America\nD Indonesia","html":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>A</strong> Cuba&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>B</strong> East Africa&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>C</strong> South America&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>D</strong> Indonesia&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-top: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>1</strong> a place to improve local education to help tourists <strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"62965","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 6-9\nUse the information in the passage to match the companies (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A, B, C or D in boxes 6-9 on your answer sheet.\nA eating the local fruits at the same time\nB find job opportunities in the community\nC which is situated in the heart of the jungle\nD with private and comfortable service","html":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>A</strong> eating the local fruits at the same time&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>B </strong>find job opportunities in the community&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>C</strong> which is situated in the heart of the jungle&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>D </strong>with private and comfortable service&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-top: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>6</strong> Visiting the cheese factory <strong class=\"source-blank\">[6] ____</strong><br/></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"62966","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Ecotourism is not a nature <strong>10&nbsp;</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"62967","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>but a <strong>11&nbsp;</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong> tour.</p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"62968","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The reason why South America promotes ecotourism is due to the destruction of <strong>12</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"62969","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the following summary of the paragraphs of the passage. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>In addition, East Africa also encourages this kind of tourism for cutting the <strong>13</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong> in order to save wild animals.</p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ecotourism in the Developing Courtiers&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The Ecotourism Society defines ecotourism as ‘a responsible travel to natural areas which conserves the environment and improves the welfare of local people’. It is recognised as being particularly conducive to enriching and enhancing the standing of tourism, on the basis that this form of tourism respects the natural heritage and local populations and are in keeping with the carrying capacity of the sites.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Cuba is undoubtedly an obvious site for ecotourism, with its picturesque beaches, underwater beauty, countryside landscapes, and ecological reserves. An educated population and improved infrastructure of roads and communications adds to the mix. In the Caribbean region, Cuba is now the second most popular tourist destination. Ecotourism is also seen as an environmental education opportunity to heighten both visitors’ and residents’ awareness of environmental and conservation issues, and even to inspire conservation action. Ecotourism has also been credited with promoting peace, by providing opportunities for educational and cultural exchange. Tourists’ safety and health are guaranteed. Raul Castro, brother of the Cuban president, started this initiative to rescue the Cuban tradition of herbal medicine and provide natural medicines for its healthcare system. The school at Las Terrazas Eco-Tourism Community teaches herbal healthcare and children learn not only how to use medicinal herbs, but also to grow them in the school garden for teas, tinctures, ointments and creams. In Cuba, ecotourism has the potential to alleviate poverty by bringing money into the economy and creating jobs. In addition to the environmental impacts of these efforts, the area works on developing community employment opportunities for locals, in conjunction with ecotourism.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In terms of South America, it might be the place which shows the shortcoming of ecotourism. Histoplasma capsulatum, a dimorphic fungus, is the most common endemic mycosis in the United States, and is associated with exposure to bat or bird droppings. Most recently, outbreaks have been reported in healthy travelers who returned from Central and South America after engaging in recreational activities associated with spelunking, adventure tourism, and ecotourism. It is quite often to see tourists neglected sanitation while travelling. After engaging in high-risk activities, boots should be hosed off and clothing placed in airtight plastic bags for laundering. HIV-infected travelers should avoid risky behaviors or environments, such as exploring caves, particularly those that contain bat droppings.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Nowhere is the keen eye and intimate knowledge of ecotourism is more amidst this fantastic biodiversity, as we explore remote realms rich in wildlife rather than a nature adventure. A sustainable tour is significant for ecotourism, one in which we can grow hand in hand with nature and our community, respecting everything that makes us privileged. Travelers get great joy from every step that take forward on this endless but exciting journey towards sustainability. The primary threats to South America’s tropical forests are deforestation caused by agricultural expansion, cattle ranching, fagging, oil extraction and spills, mining, illegal coca farming, and colonization initiatives. Deforestation has shrunk territories belonging to indigenous peoples and wiped out more than 90% of the population. Many are taking leading roles in sustainable tourism even as they introduce protected regions to more travelers.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In East Africa, significantly reducing such illegal hunting and allowing wildlife populations to recover would allow the generation of significant economic benefits through trophy hunting and potentially ecotourism. ‘Illegal hunting is an extremely inefficient use of wildlife resources because it fails to capture the value of wildlife achievable through alternative forms of use such as trophy hunting and ecotourism,’ said Peter Lindsey, author of the new study. Most residents believed that ecotourism could solve this circumstance. They have passion for local community empowerment, loves photography and writes to laud current local conservation efforts, create environmental awareness and promote ecotourism.awareness and promote ecotourism.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In Indonesia, ecotourism started to become an important concept from 1995, in order to strengthen the domestic travelling movement, the local government targeting the right markets is a prerequisite for successful ecotourism. The market segment for Indonesian ecotourism consists of: (i) ‘The silent generation’, 55-64 year-old people who are wealthy enough, generally well-educated and have no dependent children, and can travel for four weeks; (ii) ‘The baby boom generation’, junior successful executives aged 35-54 years, who are likely to be travelling with their family and children (spending 2-3 weeks on travel) – travelling for them is a stress reliever; and (iii) the ‘X generation’, aged 18-29 years, who love to do ecotours as backpackers – they are generally students who can travel for 3-12 months with monthly expenditure of US $300-500. It is suggested that promotion of Indonesian ecotourism products should aim to reach these various cohorts of tourists. The country welcomes diverse levels of travelers.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>On the other hand, ecotourism provide as many services as traditional tourism. Nestled between Mexico, Guatemala and the Caribbean Sea is the country of Belize. It is the wonderful place for Hamanasi honeymoon, bottle of champagne upon arrival, three meals daily, a private service on one night of your stay and a choice of adventures depending on the length of your stay. It also offers six-night and seven-night honeymoon packages. A variety of specially tailored tours, including the Brimstone Hill Fortress, and a trip to a neighboring island. Guided tours include rainforest, volcano and off-road plantation tours. Gregory Pereira, an extremely knowledgeable and outgoing hiking and tour guide, says the following about his tours: ‘All of our tours on St. Kitts include transportation by specially modified Land Rovers, a picnic of island pastries and local fruit, fresh tropical juices, CSR, a qualified island guide and a full liability insurance coverage for participants.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Kodai is an ultimate splendor spot for those who love being close to mother nature. They say every bird must sing its own throat while we say every traveller should find his own way out of variegated and unblemished paths of deep valleys and steep mountains. The cheese factory here exports great quantity of cheese to various countries across the globe. It is located in the center of forest. Many travelers are attracted by the delicious cheese. The ecotourism is very famous of this different eating experience.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8720&scene=%E8%B4%A2%E7%BB%8F%E5%95%86%E4%B8%9A&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8781","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Optimism and Health","book":"阅读还原集Vol.15","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.15 · Test 2 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8781:63470:14","type":"fill","text":"填写第 14 空","answer":"7 years","acceptedAnswers":["7 years"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For example, a study of 660 volunteers by the Yale University psychologist Dr Becca Levy, found that thinking positively adds an average of 7 years to your life.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是，耶鲁大学的Becca Levy博士发现，乐观的态度能够延长多少年寿命。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Yale University psychologist Dr Becca Levy\"和\"extension of...to your life\"可以定位到D段中关于Dr Becca Levy的研究结果。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子\"thinking positively adds an average of 7 years to your life\"，可以确定乐观的态度能够平均延长7年的寿命。因此，答案为7 years。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63470","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8781:63471:15","type":"fill","text":"填写第 15 空","answer":"670","acceptedAnswers":["670"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A Harvard Medical School study of 670 men found that the optimists have significantly better lung function.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是哈佛医学院进行了一项研究，研究了多少男性志愿者。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"A Harvard Medical School\"和\"study of\"可以定位到D段中的\"A Harvard Medical School study of 670 men\"。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到哈佛医学院进行了一项研究，研究对象是670名男性志愿者，因此答案为670。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63471","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8781:63472:16","type":"fill","text":"填写第 16 空","answer":"lung function","acceptedAnswers":["lung function"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A Harvard Medical School study of 670 men found that the optimists have significantly better lung function.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求填写，哈佛研究发现的结果，乐观者的什么显著更好。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词“optimists”和“remarkably better”可以帮助定位。在D段中，提到“optimists have significantly better lung function”，这里的“significantly better”与题目中的“remarkably better”意思相近，且“lung function”是描述乐观者身体状况的具体方面。\n解题思路：根据原文D段中的句子“A Harvard Medical School study of 670 men found that the optimists have significantly better lung function”，可以确定乐观者在肺功能方面有显著更好的表现。因此，填空题的答案应为“lung function”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63472","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8781:63473:17","type":"fill","text":"填写第 17 空","answer":"immune system","acceptedAnswers":["immune system"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The lead author, Dr Rosalind Wright, believes that attitude somehow strengthens the immune system.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是罗莎琳德·赖特博士认为乐观的生活可能会增强什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Dr Rosalind Wright\"和\"optimistic life\"可以定位到D段中关于她的观点的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到赖特博士认为态度以某种方式加强了免疫系统，因此可以确定答案为\"immune system\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63473","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8781:63474:18","type":"fill","text":"填写第 18 空","answer":"heart patients","acceptedAnswers":["heart patients"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Preliminary studies on heart patients suggest that, by changing a person’s outlook, you can improve their mortality risk, she says.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是一些关于什么的初步研究指出，持有更积极的态度，人们可以降低死亡风险。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“studies on heart patients”和“mortality risk”可以定位到D段末句。\n解题思路：原文中提到研究的主要作者Rosalind Wright提到，对心脏病患者进行的初步研究表明，通过改变一个人的心态，可以降低他们的死亡风险。题目要求填入研究对象，因此，答案是heart patients。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"63474","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8781:63475:19","type":"choice","text":"19 Different optimism result found according to gender.","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But a 1995 nationwide survey conducted by the American magazine Adweek found that about half the population counted themselves as optimists, with women slightly more apt than men (53 per cent versus 48 per cent) to see the sunny side.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是，哪个研究者或研究组织认为，乐观程度存在性别差异。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"different optimism result\"和\"according to gender\"，通过这些词可以定位到E段中提到的性别差异数据。\n解题思路：E段中提到，1995年美国杂志Adweek进行的一项全国性调查发现，大约一半的人口认为自己是乐观主义者，女性比男性更倾向于看到积极的一面（53%对48%）。与题目对应，因此答案是G。","options":["Brice Pitt","American Psychological Association","Martin Seligman","Chad Wallens of Henley Centre","Annual Review of Clinical Psychology","Steven Stack","American magazine Adweek"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63475","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nUse the information in the passage to match the people or organization (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet\nA Brice Pitt\nB American Psychological Association\nC Martin Seligman\nD Chad Wallens of Henley Centre\nE Annual Review of Clinical Psychology\nF Steven Stack\nG American magazine Adweek"},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8781:63475:20","type":"choice","text":"20 There is no necessary relationship between happiness and money.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Chad Wallens, a social forecaster at the Henley Centre who surveyed middle-class Britons’ beliefs about income, has found that ‘the people who feel wealthiest, and those who feel poorest, actually have almost the same amount of money at their disposal. Their attitudes and behaviour patterns, however, are different from one another.’\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是，哪个研究者或研究组织认为，幸福与金钱之间没有必然联系。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“happiness and money”可以定位到C段，该段讨论了人们对财富的感受与实际金钱数量的关系。\n解题思路：原文提到，自认为最富有的群体与最贫困群体，其可支配收入几乎相当。但他们的态度和行为模式却大相径庭。这说明人们对财富的感受（即幸福感）与实际金钱数量没有直接关系，因此选择D，Chad Wallens。","options":["Brice Pitt","American Psychological Association","Martin Seligman","Chad Wallens of Henley Centre","Annual Review of Clinical Psychology","Steven Stack","American magazine Adweek"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63475","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nUse the information in the passage to match the people or organization (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet\nA Brice Pitt\nB American Psychological Association\nC Martin Seligman\nD Chad Wallens of Henley Centre\nE Annual Review of Clinical Psychology\nF Steven Stack\nG American magazine Adweek"},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8781:63475:21","type":"choice","text":"21 Excessive optimism may be incorrect in everyday life.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Although some optimists may be accurate in their positive beliefs about the future, others may be unrealistic their optimism is misplaced, according to the American Psychological Association.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是，哪个研究者或研究组织认为，“过度乐观在日常生活里可能是错的”。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“Excessive optimism may be incorrect”定位到F段中“others may be unrealistic their optimism is misplaced”，这里的“unrealistic”和“misplaced”对应了“may be incorrect”的含义。\n解题思路：原文中F段明确提到美国心理学会的观点，认为有些乐观者的乐观态度是不切实际的（unrealistic），并且这种乐观用错地方了（misplaced），这与题目的意思完全一致。因此，正确答案是B。","options":["Brice Pitt","American Psychological Association","Martin Seligman","Chad Wallens of Henley Centre","Annual Review of Clinical Psychology","Steven Stack","American magazine Adweek"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63475","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nUse the information in the passage to match the people or organization (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet\nA Brice Pitt\nB American Psychological Association\nC Martin Seligman\nD Chad Wallens of Henley Centre\nE Annual Review of Clinical Psychology\nF Steven Stack\nG American magazine Adweek"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8781:63475:22","type":"choice","text":"22 Optimists are advantageous for human evolution.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：As Brice Pitt, an emeritus professor of the psychiatry of old age at Imperial College, London, told me: optimists are unrealistic. Depressive people see things as they really are, but that is a disadvantage from an evolutionary point of view. Optimism is a piece of evolutionary equipment that carried us through millennia of setbacks.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是，哪个研究者或研究组织认为，乐观主义有助于人类进化。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"Optimists are advantageous for human evolution\"定位到A段中关于乐观主义与进化的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，乐观主义是进化赋予的生存技能，帮助人类历经数千年挫折仍能前行。与题目中\"optimists are advantageous for human evolution\"意思一致，因此答案为A。","options":["Brice Pitt","American Psychological Association","Martin Seligman","Chad Wallens of Henley Centre","Annual Review of Clinical Psychology","Steven Stack","American magazine Adweek"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63475","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nUse the information in the passage to match the people or organization (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet\nA Brice Pitt\nB American Psychological Association\nC Martin Seligman\nD Chad Wallens of Henley Centre\nE Annual Review of Clinical Psychology\nF Steven Stack\nG American magazine Adweek"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8781:63475:23","type":"choice","text":"23 Occurrence of emergency assists resilient people in a positive way.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：They add that resilient people learn to hold on to their sense of humour and this can help them to keep a flexible attitude when big changes of plan are warranted. The ability to accept your lot with equanimity also plays an important role, the study adds.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是，哪个研究者或研究组织认为，紧急状况能以积极的方式帮助有韧性的人。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"emergency\", \"assists resilient people\", \"positive way\" 定位到文中描述逆境或重大变化对韧性人群产生积极影响的句子。\n解题思路：段落I中，耶鲁大学的研究者在《临床心理学年度评论》中指出，有韧性的人学会保持幽默感，这能帮助他们在“计划发生重大改变时”（这可以视为一种紧急情况或逆境）保持灵活的态度。因此，提出此观点的机构是《临床心理学年度评论》，对应选项E。","options":["Brice Pitt","American Psychological Association","Martin Seligman","Chad Wallens of Henley Centre","Annual Review of Clinical Psychology","Steven Stack","American magazine Adweek"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63475","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nUse the information in the passage to match the people or organization (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet\nA Brice Pitt\nB American Psychological Association\nC Martin Seligman\nD Chad Wallens of Henley Centre\nE Annual Review of Clinical Psychology\nF Steven Stack\nG American magazine Adweek"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8781:63476:24","type":"choice","text":"The link between longevity and optimism has been known.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It has been known that optimistic has something to do with the long life, and optimists have plenty to be happy about.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“长寿与乐观之间的联系早已为人所知”这一说法是否与文章作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息： 使用 \"link between longevity and optimism\", \"has been known\" 定位到文中明确陈述此观点的句子。\n解题思路：段落B的开头，作者明确写道：“众所周知，乐观与长寿有关……”(\"It has been known that optimistic has something to do with the long life...\")。这句话直接、明确地肯定了这种联系的存在及其为公众或科学界所知的属性，与题目的陈述完全一致。因此，该陈述与作者的主张一致，答案为YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63476","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8781:63477:25","type":"choice","text":"Optimists have a better personal relationship than those pessimists.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：原文中没有直接提到相关内容。\n对应段落：无\n审题：题目问的是，乐观者比悲观者有更好的人际关系，这一说法是否与文章作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"optimists\"和\"personal relationship\"。\n解题思路：在文章中，虽然提到了乐观者在工作、应对压力、抑郁发作和个人目标实现等方面表现更好，但并没有具体提到他们在人际关系方面的比较。因此，根据文章提供的信息，无法确定题目的观点是否正确。所以，答案是NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63477","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8781:63478:26","type":"choice","text":"People who had a happy childhood do not need to practise optimism.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：If you are handicapped by having had a happy childhood, then practising proactive optimism can help you to become more resilient.\n对应段落：K段\n审题：题目问“那些拥有快乐童年的孩子不需要练习乐观”，询问文章是否支持这一观点。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"happy childhood\"和\"practise optimism\"，通过这些词可以定位到K段，该段明确提到了\"having had a happy childhood\"和\"practising proactive optimism\"。\n解题思路：K段原文提到，即使拥有快乐童年（\"having had a happy childhood\"），练习积极乐观（\"practising proactive optimism\"）仍然可以帮助人们变得更坚韧（\"help you to become more resilient\"）。这与题目中“不需要练习乐观”的说法相反，因此题目说法与作者观点不符，答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63478","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8781:63479:27","type":"choice","text":"Experience of difficulties will eventually help people accumulate a fortune.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Research among tycoons and business leaders shows that the path to success is often littered with failure: a record of sackings, bankruptcies and blistering castigation. But instead of curling into a foetal ball beneath the coffee table, they resiliently pick themselves up, learn from their pratfalls and march boldly towards the next opportunity.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“经历困难最终会帮助人们积累财富”是否与作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息： 使用 \"experience of difficulties\", \"help people\", \"accumulate a fortune\" 定位到文中讨论困难与成功/财富积累关系的句子。\n解题思路：段落G中，作者指出，对商业巨头和领袖的研究表明，“通往成功的道路常常布满失败”，但他们能够坚韧地重新站起，从中学习，并“勇敢地走向下一个机会”。这里的“成功”(success) 和“机会”(opportunity) 在商业语境下，强烈暗示了财务上的成功和财富的积累。作者将克服困难描述为成功路径上的一个环节，这支持了“困难经历最终有助于积累财富”的观点。因此，该陈述与作者的主张一致，答案为YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"63479","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"63470","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Optimists generally are more robust. Yale University psychologist Dr Becca Levy found that an extension of around<strong> 14.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong> to your life will be achieved by a positive attitude toward life.</p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"63471","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>A Harvard Medical School conduct a research which study of <strong>15.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[15] ____</strong> male volunteers found that</p>","firstNumber":15},{"id":"63472","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>the optimists have remarkably better <strong>16.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[16] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":16},{"id":"63473","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>And Dr Rosalind Wright believes optimistic life may enhance the<strong> 17.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[17] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":17},{"id":"63474","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>some initiative studies on <strong>18.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[18] ____</strong> indicate that people can improve their mortality risk by changing into a positive outlook.</p>","firstNumber":18},{"id":"63475","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nUse the information in the passage to match the people or organization (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet\nA Brice Pitt\nB American Psychological Association\nC Martin Seligman\nD Chad Wallens of Henley Centre\nE Annual Review of Clinical Psychology\nF Steven Stack\nG American magazine Adweek","html":"<p><strong>A </strong>Brice Pitt&nbsp;</p><p><strong>B</strong> American Psychological Association&nbsp;</p><p><strong>C</strong> Martin Seligman&nbsp;</p><p><strong>D </strong>Chad Wallens of Henley Centre&nbsp;</p><p><strong>E </strong>Annual Review of Clinical Psychology&nbsp;</p><p><strong>F</strong> Steven Stack&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>G</strong> American magazine Adweek</p><p><strong>19</strong> Different optimism result found according to gender. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"63476","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The link between longevity and optimism has been known.</strong></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"63477","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Optimists have a better personal relationship than those pessimists.</strong></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"63478","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>People who had a happy childhood do not need to practise optimism.</strong></p>","firstNumber":26},{"id":"63479","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Experience of difficulties will eventually help people accumulate a fortune.</strong></p>","firstNumber":27}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Optimism and Health 2&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Mindset is all. How you start the year will set the template for 2009, and two scientifically-backed character traits hold the key: optimism and resilience (if the prospect leaves you feeling pessimistically spineless, the good news is that you can significantly boost both of these qualities).&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Faced with 12 months of plummeting economics and rising human distress, staunchly maintaining a rosy view might seem deludedly Pollyannaish. But here we encounter the optimism paradox. As Brice Pitt, an emeritus professor of the psychiatry of old age at Imperial College, London, told me: optimists are unrealistic. Depressive people see things as they really are, but that is a disadvantage from an evolutionary point of view. Optimism is a piece of evolutionary equipment that carried us through millennia of setbacks.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>It has been known that optimistic has something to do with the long life, and optimists have plenty to be happy about. In other words, if you can convince yourself that things will get better, the odds of it happening will improve – because you keep on playing the game. In this light, optimism ‘is a habitual way of explaining your setbacks to yourself’, reports Martin Seligman, the psychology professor and author of Learned Optimism. The research shows that when times get tough, optimists do better than pessimists – they succeed better at work, respond better to stress, suffer fewer depressive episodes, and achieve more personal goals.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Studies also show that belief can help with the financial pinch. Chad Wallens, a social forecaster at the Henley Centre who surveyed middle-class Britons’ beliefs about income, has found that ‘the people who feel wealthiest, and those who feel poorest, actually have almost the same amount of money at their disposal. Their attitudes and behaviour patterns, however, are different from one another.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Optimists have something else to be cheerful about – in general, they are more robust. For example, a study of 660 volunteers by the Yale University psychologist Dr Becca Levy, found that thinking positively adds an average of 7 years to your life. Other American research claims to have identified a physical mechanism behind this. A Harvard Medical School study of 670 men found that the optimists have significantly better lung function. The lead author, Dr Rosalind Wright, believes that attitude somehow strengthens the immune system. ‘Preliminary studies on heart patients suggest that, by changing a person’s outlook, you can improve their mortality risk,’ she says.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Few studies have tried to ascertain the proportion of optimists in the world. But a 1995 nationwide survey conducted by the American magazine Adweek found that about half the population counted themselves as optimists, with women slightly more apt than men (53 per cent versus 48 per cent) to see the sunny side.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Although some optimists may be accurate in their positive beliefs about the future, others may be unrealistic their optimism is misplaced, according to the American Psychological Association. Research shows that some smokers exhibit unrealistic optimism by underestimating their relative chances of experiencing disease. An important question is whether such unrealistic optimism is associated with risk-related attitudes and behavior. We addressed this question by investigating if one’s perceived the risk of developing lung cancer, over and above one’s objective risk, predicted acceptance of myths and other beliefs about smoking. Hierarchical regressions showed that those individuals who were unrealistically optimistic were more likely to endorse beliefs that there is no risk of lung cancer if one only smokes for a few years and that getting lung cancer depends on one’s genes.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Of course, there is no guarantee that optimism will insulate you from the crunch’s worst effects, but the best strategy is still to keep smiling and thank your lucky stars. Because (as every good sports coach knows) adversity is character-forming – so long as you practise the skills of resilience. Research among tycoons and business leaders shows that the path to success is often littered with failure: a record of sackings, bankruptcies and blistering castigation. But instead of curling into a foetal ball beneath the coffee table, they resiliently pick themselves up, learn from their pratfalls and march boldly towards the next opportunity.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The American Psychological Association defines resilience as the ability to adapt in the face of adversity, trauma or tragedy. A resilient person may go through difficulty and uncertainty, but he or she will doggedly bounce back.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Optimism is one of the central traits required in building resilience, say Yale University investigators in the. Annual Review of Clinical Psychology. They add that resilient people learn to hold on to their sense of humour and this can help them to keep a flexible attitude when big changes of plan are warranted. The ability to accept your lot with equanimity also plays an important role, the study adds.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>One of the best ways to acquire resilience is through experiencing a difficult childhood, the sociologist Steven Stack reports in the Journal of Social Psychology. For example, short men are less likely to commit suicide than tall guys, he says, because shorties develop psychological defence skills to handle the bullies and mickey-taking that their lack of stature attracts. By contrast, those who enjoyed adversity-free youths can get derailed by setbacks later on because they’ve never been inoculated against agro.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>K</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Learning to overcome your fears. If you are handicapped by having had a happy childhood, then practising proactive optimism can help you to become more resilient. Studies of resilient people show that they take more risks; they court failure and learn not to fear it. And despite being thick-skinned, resilient types are also more open than average to other people. Bouncing through knock-backs is all part of the process. It’s about optimistic risk-taking – being confident that people will like you. Simply smiling and being warm to people can help. It’s an altruistic path to self-interest – and if it achieves nothing else, it will reinforce an age-old adage: hard times can bring out the best in you.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8781&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8782","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Teleworking","book":"阅读还原集Vol.15","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.15 · Test 2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8782:63467:28","type":"choice","text":"Teleworking has been said to have many benefits for both society and companies. Survey identified that telecommuters spend more time on 28 ____ than those traditional workers on changes in non-commuting travel on weekends.","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Changes in non-commuting travel on weekends: home-bases workers, which includes a substantial population of people who are not telecommuters, spend more time shopping out of the home than traditional workers.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是调查显示，通勤模式的变化使得，远程工作者在周末比传统工作者花费更多时间在什么活动上。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"telecommuters\"、\"traditional workers\"、\"non-commuting travel\"、\"weekends\"定位到C段最后一句，该句明确提到远程工作者比传统工作者在周末花费更多时间在\"shopping out of the home\"上。\n解题思路：原文中明确指出，周末时，居家办公人员（包括大量非远程工作者）比传统上班族花费更多时间在外购物。因此空格处应填写\"shopping\"。","options":["pollution","internet energy","paper usage","construction and maintenance","materials","shopping","productivity","fuels and gases","electronically","IT","equipment","company","work-related","geography"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L","M","N"],"sourceGroupId":"63467","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-N below. Write the correct letter, A-N, in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8782:63467:29","type":"choice","text":"It also is beneficial to the environment as it reduces the 29 ____ in the atmosphere from decreased street repairs,","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Half-time telecommuting could reduce carbon emissions by over 51 million metric tons a year – the equivalent of taking all of New York’s commuters off the road. Additional carbon footprint savings will come from reduced: office energy, roadway repairs, urban heating, office construction, business travel, paper usage (as electronic documents replace paper).\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是远程工作对环境的好处，通过减少道路修复，可以减少了大气中的什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的“street repairs”, “city heating”等词，可以定位到D段关于碳足迹（carbon footprint）和减排的列表。\n解题思路：原文D段提到，减少的“碳足迹”（carbon footprint）来自于多个方面，包括道路维修、城市供暖等。而“碳足迹”的直接表现就是大气中的碳排放和污染（pollution）。题目中的“in the atmosphere”与“carbon emissions”和“carbon footprint”直接对应。因此，减少的就是大气中的污染“pollution”。","options":["pollution","internet energy","paper usage","construction and maintenance","materials","shopping","productivity","fuels and gases","electronically","IT","equipment","company","work-related","geography"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L","M","N"],"sourceGroupId":"63467","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-N below. Write the correct letter, A-N, in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8782:63467:30","type":"choice","text":"city heating, or even 30 ____ as staff in office","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Additional carbon footprint savings will come from reduced: office energy, roadway repairs, urban heating, office construction, business travel, paper usage (as electronic documents replace paper).\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是远程工作对环境的好处，除了减少道路修复，城市供暖，还能通过减少什么来减少大气中的污染。\n定位关键信息：根据题目后半句“staff in office could send documents”的语境，可以定位到D段中“paper usage”及其后的括号内容。\n解题思路：根据原文句子中，此外，通过减少以下领域还能进一步降低碳足迹：办公能耗、道路维护、城市供暖、办公楼建设、商务差旅以及纸张使用（电子文档的普及）。可以推断出，答案为“paper usage”。","options":["pollution","internet energy","paper usage","construction and maintenance","materials","shopping","productivity","fuels and gases","electronically","IT","equipment","company","work-related","geography"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L","M","N"],"sourceGroupId":"63467","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-N below. Write the correct letter, A-N, in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8782:63467:31","type":"choice","text":"could send documents 31 ____ .","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Additional carbon footprint savings will come from reduced: office energy, roadway repairs, urban heating, office construction, business travel, paper usage (as electronic documents replace paper).\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是题目问的是远程工作减少了纸张使用，这是因为办公室里的文件可以怎样来传输。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的“send documents”可以定位到D段关于用电子文档取代纸张的描述。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，减少纸张使用是通过“电子文档（electronic documents）”取代纸张来实现的。因此，员工发送文档的方式就是“以电子方式（electronically）”。因此，答案为“electronically”。","options":["pollution","internet energy","paper usage","construction and maintenance","materials","shopping","productivity","fuels and gases","electronically","IT","equipment","company","work-related","geography"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L","M","N"],"sourceGroupId":"63467","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-N below. Write the correct letter, A-N, in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8782:63467:32","type":"choice","text":"Apart from that, other materials such as Vehicle-related, Highway-related and 32 ____","answer":"M","acceptedAnswers":["M"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The three major areas where energy can be conserved are Vehicle-related materials and resources; Highway-related materials and resources; and work-related materials and resources.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是除了节省车辆相关和公路相关的资源外，还能节省哪一类资源。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Vehicle-related\"和\"Highway-related\"定位到D段，找到并列的三个材料类别。\n解题思路：原文中明确列出了三个能源节约相关的材料类别，分别是\"Vehicle-related materials and resources\"、\"Highway-related materials and resources\"和\"work-related materials and resources\"。题目问的是除了前两类外还有哪一类，因此答案应为\"work-related\"。","options":["pollution","internet energy","paper usage","construction and maintenance","materials","shopping","productivity","fuels and gases","electronically","IT","equipment","company","work-related","geography"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L","M","N"],"sourceGroupId":"63467","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-N below. Write the correct letter, A-N, in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8782:63467:33","type":"choice","text":"materials will also be saved. Traditionally, a large amount of energy is needed to make 33 ____ , e.g.","answer":"K","acceptedAnswers":["K"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A tremendous amount of energy is required to produce transportation equipment such as automobiles, buses, trains and jet aircraft.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是，一般情况下，需要大量能源来制造什么，例如公共交通和私家车。\n定位关键信息： 根据题目中的“public transportation and private cars”这些具体例子，可以定位到E段开头。\n解题思路：原文E段首句明确指出，生产“transportation equipment”（交通设备）需要大量能源，并紧接着列举了“automobiles, buses, trains...”（汽车、公交车、火车...）作为例子。题目中的“public transportation and private cars”正是这些例子的一部分。因此，这里需要填写的名词就是equipment。","options":["pollution","internet energy","paper usage","construction and maintenance","materials","shopping","productivity","fuels and gases","electronically","IT","equipment","company","work-related","geography"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L","M","N"],"sourceGroupId":"63467","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-N below. Write the correct letter, A-N, in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8782:63467:34","type":"choice","text":"public transportation and private cars. With the rise of telecommuting, resources and 34 ____ will be saved.","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Fuel resources and gases needed to operate this equipment will be reduced, as well the building and repair of highways and maintenance requires a large consumption of energy, not only in the operation of the highway construction and repair equipment but also in the manufacture and transportation of the required materials\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是随着远程办公的兴起，可以节省能源和什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"public transportation and private cars\"可以定位到E段中提到的\"transportation equipment such as automobiles, buses, trains and jet aircraft\"。\n解题思路：原文E段提到，如果推广远程办公，将减少对交通工具的使用，从而减少生产、维护和修理这些设备所需的能源。同时，燃料和操作这些设备所需的燃气也将减少。这里的“Fuel resources”与题目中的“resources”对应，那么与之并列的、需要填写的词就是fuels and gases。","options":["pollution","internet energy","paper usage","construction and maintenance","materials","shopping","productivity","fuels and gases","electronically","IT","equipment","company","work-related","geography"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L","M","N"],"sourceGroupId":"63467","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-N below. Write the correct letter, A-N, in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8782:63467:35","type":"choice","text":"And conservation goes to the energy and materials consumed in all 35 ____ .","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Fuel resources and gases needed to operate this equipment will be reduced, as well the building and repair of highways and maintenance requires a large consumption of energy, not only in the operation of the highway construction and repair equipment but also in the manufacture and transportation of the required materials An increase in the percentage of people telecommuting to work will decrease the need for expanded highways and associated road maintenance.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是节能体现在什么环节消耗的能源和材料上。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"energy and materials\"定位到E段，找到关于能源和材料节约的具体内容。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，这类设备的燃料和燃气消耗将减少，同时公路建设和维修所需的能源消耗也将降低。前面已经提到燃料燃气消耗减少，所以与之并列的公路建设和维护就是本题的答案。因此答案为“construction and maintenance”。","options":["pollution","internet energy","paper usage","construction and maintenance","materials","shopping","productivity","fuels and gases","electronically","IT","equipment","company","work-related","geography"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L","M","N"],"sourceGroupId":"63467","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-N below. Write the correct letter, A-N, in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8782:63468:36","type":"choice","text":"36 More working time is often connected with","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：More time working is usually associated with increased stress, domestic tension and other factors that reduce the quality of life.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“更多工作时间通常会牵扯到什么”。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"More working time\"和\"connected with\"定位到G段开头。\n解题思路：根据原文句子可知，工作时间越长，通常越容易引发压力、家庭矛盾等负面因素，从而降低生活质量。说明更多工作时间通常与压力和紧张有关，对应选项A。","options":["stress and tension.","consumption of goods.","the problem of less communication with colleagues.","many problems when equipment doesn’t work.","transport equipment such as automobiles.","technical supporters.","widespread of the mechanical refrigerator."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63468","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-39\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below. Write the correct letter, A-F, in box 36-39 on your answer sheet.\nA stress and tension.\nB consumption of goods.\nC the problem of less communication with colleagues.\nD many problems when equipment doesn’t work.\nE transport equipment such as automobiles.\nF technical supporters.\nG widespread of the mechanical refrigerator."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8782:63468:37","type":"choice","text":"37 Oracle’s Functional idea aims to improve","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The loss of teamwork and team spirit within teleworking populations was tackled through ideas such as Oracle’s ‘FUNctional’ offices. Designed to increase communication and interaction when people are at the office, they are bright and focused around a central cafe to stimulate ideas and face-to-face contact.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问Oracle的功能型办公室的想法旨在改善什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Oracle’s Functional idea\"定位到F段中提到Oracle的‘FUNctional’ offices的句子。\n解题思路：原文提到，为解决远程办公群体中团队协作与团队精神的缺失问题，甲骨文公司推出了‘功能型’办公模式。这种办公设计旨在提升员工在办公室时的沟通与互动。因此，该想法旨在改善团队合作和沟通，对应选项C。","options":["stress and tension.","consumption of goods.","the problem of less communication with colleagues.","many problems when equipment doesn’t work.","transport equipment such as automobiles.","technical supporters.","widespread of the mechanical refrigerator."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63468","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-39\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below. Write the correct letter, A-F, in box 36-39 on your answer sheet.\nA stress and tension.\nB consumption of goods.\nC the problem of less communication with colleagues.\nD many problems when equipment doesn’t work.\nE transport equipment such as automobiles.\nF technical supporters.\nG widespread of the mechanical refrigerator."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8782:63468:38","type":"choice","text":"38 When you work at office equipments such as computers and printers are maintained by","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In fact, all of the equipment that you use at the office is supported by technical staff.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是在办公室工作时，像电脑和打印机这样的设备是由谁维护的。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"work at office\"和\"computers and printers\"定位到H段，找到描述办公室设备维护的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到办公室的所有设备（包括电脑和打印机）都是由技术员工（technical staff）支持的，这意味着维护工作由技术员工负责。因此，答案为F。","options":["stress and tension.","consumption of goods.","the problem of less communication with colleagues.","many problems when equipment doesn’t work.","transport equipment such as automobiles.","technical supporters.","widespread of the mechanical refrigerator."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63468","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-39\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below. Write the correct letter, A-F, in box 36-39 on your answer sheet.\nA stress and tension.\nB consumption of goods.\nC the problem of less communication with colleagues.\nD many problems when equipment doesn’t work.\nE transport equipment such as automobiles.\nF technical supporters.\nG widespread of the mechanical refrigerator."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8782:63468:39","type":"choice","text":"39 When work from home using hardware and software","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：That means regular updates and maintenance for various and sundry office tools like land-line phones, computers, internet connections, laptops, cell phones, printers, and other office equipment is all up to you when you work from home, you’ll surely encounter technical problems and when you do, where do you get the support and help you need? If your computer hard drive crashed today, would you have the funds to replace it?\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是在家使用硬件和软件时会发生什么情况。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"hardware and software\"定位到H段中提到的\"land-line phones, computers, internet connections, laptops, cell phones, printers, and other office equipment\"。\n解题思路：根据原文中H段的描述，当在家工作时，所有办公设备如电话、电脑、网络连接等的定期更新和维护都由自己负责，因此会面临技术问题，需要自己解决。如果电脑硬盘今天崩溃了，是否有钱更换。因此，题目问的是在家使用硬件和软件时会发生什么情况，答案是D（设备不工作时会出现许多问题）。","options":["stress and tension.","consumption of goods.","the problem of less communication with colleagues.","many problems when equipment doesn’t work.","transport equipment such as automobiles.","technical supporters.","widespread of the mechanical refrigerator."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"63468","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-39\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below. Write the correct letter, A-F, in box 36-39 on your answer sheet.\nA stress and tension.\nB consumption of goods.\nC the problem of less communication with colleagues.\nD many problems when equipment doesn’t work.\nE transport equipment such as automobiles.\nF technical supporters.\nG widespread of the mechanical refrigerator."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8782:63469:40","type":"choice","text":"Implied in the passage, what is the author's attitude toward Telework?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Teleworking – working remotely from an office – is said to have many benefits for organisations, the environment and society. It provokes mixed reactions from its acolytes and those that experience it first-hand. Whether you like it or not, it is true to say that work is no longer dependent on geography and this opens up a range of opportunities for working in new ways and environments.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是文章中作者对远程工作的态度是什么，需要从文章中找出作者对远程工作的总体看法。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Telework\"和\"author's attitude\"可以定位到文章的A段，该段提到了远程工作的许多好处，包括对组织、环境和社会的益处。\n解题思路：根据A段的第一句话，作者明确指出远程工作有很多好处，这表明作者对远程工作是持积极态度的。虽然文章中也提到了远程工作引发的各种反应，但总体上作者强调了其积极影响。因此，作者的态度是相信远程工作总体上是积极和鼓舞人心的，这与选项C的描述一致。其他选项要么与文章内容不符，要么没有在文章中明确体现。","options":["surprised by its fast growth","unconcerned about the future pattern","believe it is generally positive and encouraging","worried in the economical problems arise"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"63469","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 40\nAnswer the question 40 and choose correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 40 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"63467","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-N below. Write the correct letter, A-N, in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> pollution <br/></p><p><strong>B</strong> internet energy <br/></p><p><strong>C</strong> paper usage <br/></p><p><strong>D</strong> construction and maintenance <br/></p><p><strong>E</strong> materials <br/></p><p><strong>F</strong> shopping <br/></p><p><strong>G</strong> productivity <br/></p><p><strong>H</strong> fuels and gases <br/></p><p><strong>I</strong> electronically <br/></p><p><strong>J</strong> IT <br/></p><p><strong>K</strong> equipment <br/></p><p><strong>L</strong> company <br/></p><p><strong>M</strong> work-related <br/></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>N</strong> geography <br/></p><p>Teleworking has been said to have many benefits for both society and companies. Survey identified\nthat telecommuters spend more time on <strong>28</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[28] ____</strong> than those traditional workers on changes\nin non-commuting travel on weekends.</p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"63468","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-39\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below. Write the correct letter, A-F, in box 36-39 on your answer sheet.\nA stress and tension.\nB consumption of goods.\nC the problem of less communication with colleagues.\nD many problems when equipment doesn’t work.\nE transport equipment such as automobiles.\nF technical supporters.\nG widespread of the mechanical refrigerator.","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> stress and tension. <br/></p><p><strong>B</strong> consumption of goods. <br/></p><p><strong>C</strong> the problem of less communication with colleagues. <br/></p><p><strong>D</strong> many problems when equipment doesn’t work. <br/></p><p><strong>E</strong> transport equipment such as automobiles. <br/></p><p><strong>F</strong> technical supporters. <br/></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>G</strong> widespread of the mechanical refrigerator. <br/></p><p><strong>36</strong> More working time is often connected with <strong class=\"source-blank\">[36] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"63469","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 40\nAnswer the question 40 and choose correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Implied in the passage, what is the author&#39;s attitude toward Telework?</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Teleworking</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Teleworking – working remotely from an office – is said to have many benefits for organisations, the environment and society. It provokes mixed reactions from its acolytes and those that experience it first-hand. Whether you like it or not, it is true to say that work is no longer dependent on geography and this opens up a range of opportunities for working in new ways and environments.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The surveys show that the productivity increase is not primarily because of longer working hours (as is sometimes suggested). Although prevalent, working more is just one of a number of influencing factors, and not the most important. An unusual comparison of the performance of teleworkers with a closely matched control group of non-teleworkers found that not only was productivity higher but also that absenteeism and error rates were lower.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Two other areas where SUSTEL has added to the economic impact knowledge base is its effect on absenteeism and space utilisation. In the case of absenteeism, over 60 per cent of those surveyed stated that telework had enabled them to work when they were prevented from reaching a work location (usually through illness or transport problems). Around half the cases also identified substantial reductions in space requirements – to the point where one organisation had completely done away with a central office. Changes in non-commuting travel on weekends: home-bases workers, which includes a substantial population of people who are not telecommuters, spend more time shopping out of the home than traditional workers.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Half-time telecommuting could reduce carbon emissions by over 51 million metric tons a year – the equivalent of taking all of New York’s commuters off the road. Additional carbon footprint savings will come from reduced: office energy, roadway repairs, urban heating, office construction, business travel, paper usage (as electronic documents replace paper). Although energy utilization will continue to grow as we expand our industry and improve our standard of living, efficient use of energy will always be of prime importance. By telecommuting to work instead of using more conventional methods, there is a great potential to save energy. The three major areas where energy can be conserved are Vehicle-related materials and resources; Highway-related materials and resources; and work-related materials and resources.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>A tremendous amount of energy is required to produce transportation equipment such as automobiles, buses, trains and jet aircraft. If telecommuting is promoted, there will be less use of this equipment and less energy will be required for production, maintenance and repair of this equipment. Fuel resources and gases needed to operate this equipment will be reduced, as well the building and repair of highways and maintenance requires a large consumption of energy, not only in the operation of the highway construction and repair equipment but also in the manufacture and transportation of the required materials An increase in the percentage of people telecommuting to work will decrease the need for expanded highways and associated road maintenance. The first two areas related to getting to work.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Socially, the SUSTEL research found that most survey respondents felt that teleworking gave them a better quality of life and work-life balance. Many also reported health benefits. A significant number also stated that they were using local services more and becoming more involved in their local communities. The loss of teamwork and team spirit within teleworking populations was tackled through ideas such as Oracle’s ‘FUNctional’ offices. Designed to increase communication and interaction when people are at the office, they are bright and focused around a central cafe to stimulate ideas and face-to-face contact.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The finding that many teleworkers report both longer working hours and a better quality of life is paradoxical. More time working is usually associated with increased stress, domestic tension and other factors that reduce the quality of life. One possible explanation is that, for many individuals, their increased working hours will be less than the time they have saved in commuting. Hence, they still have more time available for family and other activities. For some, the stress associated with commuting (especially for long distances) may be less than that arising from additional working time. Perhaps most significantly, teleworking can in effect create time through opportunities for multi-tasking or greater control of activities. As one survey respondent noted. ‘Although the amount of time has not changed it has made the weekends freer, as domestic activities can be fitted in during lunchtimes or early morning.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>When you work in an office or a cubicle and something goes wrong with any hardware or software you have the option of calling in the IT man. In fact, all of the equipment that you use at the office is supported by technical staff. That means regular updates and maintenance for various and sundry office tools like land-line phones, computers, internet connections, laptops, cell phones, printers, and other office equipment is all up to you when you work from home, you’ll surely encounter technical problems and when you do, where do you get the support and help you need? If your computer hard drive crashed today, would you have the funds to replace it?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8782&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8717","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Animal Minds: Parrot Alex","book":"阅读还原集Vol.15","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.15 · Test 1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8717:62934:1","type":"choice","text":"Firstly, Alex has grasped quite a lot of vocabulary.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：文中未提及Alex是否“首先”掌握了大量词汇。\n对应段落：无\n审题：题目问的是“题目判断“Alex一开始掌握了大量词汇”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"firstly\", \"grasped quite a lot of vocabulary\" 定位到文中描述Alex学习过程和词汇掌握情况的句子。\n解题思路：原文中提到Alex是一只会说话的鹦鹉，文章在E段和G段确实提到Alex学会了模仿“近100个英语单词”，并能使用这些词回答关于颜色、形状等问题。这似乎支持他掌握了“不少词汇”。然而，文中没有任何信息表明这是他学习过程中“首先”达成的里程碑，也没有将词汇量与其他认知技能（如识别形状、颜色）的掌握顺序进行比较。题目中的“firstly”在原文中找不到依据。因此，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62934","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8717:62935:2","type":"choice","text":"At the beginning of the study, Alex felt frightened in the presence of humans.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Alex dominated his fellow parrots, acted huffy at times around Pepperberg, tolerated the other female humans, and fell to pieces over a male assistant who dropped by for a visit.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是在研究开始时，Alex是否在人类面前感到害怕。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"Alex\"、\"frightened\"、\"humans\"定位到D段，该段描述了Alex在人类面前的表现。\n解题思路：D段提到Alex的行为，有时会在佩珀伯格面前耍性子，对其他女性成员尚算容忍，但每当有男性助手到访，它便会方寸大乱，但并未提及Alex是否对人类感到害怕。原文也没有任何信息表明Alex在人类面前表现出恐惧或害怕的情绪。因此，题干中的信息在原文中未被提及，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62935","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8717:62936:3","type":"choice","text":"Previously, many scientists realized that the animal possesses the ability of thinking.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：When Pepperberg began her dialogue with Alex, who died last September at the age of 31, many scientists believed animals were incapable of any thought. They were simply machines, robots programmed to react to stimuli but lacking the ability to think or feel.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“以前，许多科学家认为动物具有思考的能力”，需要判断这个说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"Previously\"和\"scientists\"以及\"thinking\"来定位。在B段中，作者提到\"many scientists believed animals were incapable of any thought\"，这与题目中的\"realized that the animal possesses the ability of thinking\"意思相反。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子\"They were simply machines, robots programmed to react to stimuli but lacking the ability to think or feel\"，可以确定原文的意思是许多科学家认为动物没有思考的能力，而题目却说科学家意识到动物具有思考的能力，两者意思相反，因此答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62936","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8717:62937:4","type":"choice","text":"It has taken a long time before people get to know cognition existing in animals.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1977 Irene Pepperberg, a recent graduate of Harvard University did something very bold. At a time when animals still were considered automatons, she set out to find what was on another creature’s mind by talking to it. She brought a one-year-old African gray parrot she named Alex into her lab to teach him to reproduce the sounds of the English language.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“在人们认识到动物存在认知能力之前，已经过去了很长时间”，需要判断这个说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“a long time”和“cognition existing in animals”可以定位到A段首句“at a time when animals still were considered automatons”，说明在1977年时，动物还被认为是没有认知能力的机器。\n解题思路：A段明确提到1977年时动物仍被当作机器（automatons），说明在此之前人们普遍不认为动物有认知能力。而Pepperberg通过Alex的研究试图证明动物有认知能力，表明在此之前人们对动物认知的认识是缺乏的。即A段表明在1977年之前人们普遍不认为动物有认知能力，而Pepperberg的研究才促使人们开始关注这一领域，后文又提到这项研究进行了三十年，说明确实经过了很长时间人们才认识到动物存在认知能力。因此，选择TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62937","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8717:62938:5","type":"choice","text":"As Alex could approximately imitate the sounds of English words, he was capable of roughly answering Irene’s questions regarding the world.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In other words, because Alex was able to produce a close approximation of the sounds of some English words, Pepperberg could ask him questions about a bird’s basic understanding of the world. She couldn’t ask him what he was thinking about, but she could ask him about his knowledge of numbers, shapes, and colors.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“由于Alex能够大致模仿英语单词的发音，因此对于艾琳提出的各种问题，它都能给出大致的回答” 这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“Alex could approximately imitate the sounds of English words”和“capable of roughly answering Irene’s questions regarding the world”定位到G段，找到对应的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到Alex能够模仿英语单词的发音，Pepperberg因此能够向他提问关于鸟类对世界的基本理解的问题，包括数字、形状和颜色。这与题目描述完全一致，说明Alex确实能够通过模仿发音来回答Irene有关世界理解的问题。因此，题目陈述与原文信息一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62938","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8717:62939:6","type":"choice","text":"By breaking in other parrots as well as producing the incorrect answers, he tried to be focused.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He knows all this, and he gets bored, so he interrupts the others, or he gives the wrong answer just to be obstinate. At this stage, he’s like a teenager; he’s moody, and I’m never sure what he’ll do.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是“通过打断其他鹦鹉，给出错误答案，它想试图保持专注”这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"breaking in other parrots\"、\"producing the incorrect answers\"和\"tried to be focused\"来定位答案。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句可知，Alex打断其他鹦鹉和给出错误答案是因为它很固执，或者觉得无聊，而不是为了保持专注。题目中的\"tried to be focused\"与原文中的\"just to be obstinate\"意思不符，因此题目说法与原文信息不符，应选择FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62939","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8717:62940:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"100 English words","acceptedAnswers":["100 English words"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Under Pepperberg’s patient tutelage, Alex learned how to use his vocal tract to imitate almost one hundred English words, including the sounds for various foods, although he calls an apple a ‘banerry.’\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是经过Irene的训练后，鹦鹉Alex能够用他的发声器官发出多少个单词，同时其他科学家认为动物没有这种高级的思考能力。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"vocal tract\"和\"pronounce\"可以定位到E段中的\"Alex learned how to use his vocal tract to imitate almost one hundred English words\"。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子，可以确定Alex能够模仿大约一百个英语单词，因此填空处应该填写\"100 English words\"。题目中还提到其他科学家认为动物没有这种高级的思考能力，这与E段中提到的\"Scientists thought that chimpanzees were better subjects, although, of course, chimps can’t speak.\"相呼应。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62940","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-10\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 7-10 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8717:62940:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"chimpanzees","acceptedAnswers":["chimpanzees"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘Some people actually called me crazy for trying this,’ she said, ‘Scientists thought that chimpanzees were better subjects, although, of course, chimps can’t speak.’\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是科学家们更愿意教哪种动物。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"they would rather teach\"可以定位到E段，其中提到\"Scientists thought that chimpanzees were better subjects\"，说明科学家们认为黑猩猩是更好的研究对象。\n解题思路：原文中提到科学家们认为黑猩猩是更好的研究对象，而题目问的是他们更愿意教哪种动物，因此答案为\"chimpanzees\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62940","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-10\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 7-10 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8717:62940:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"avian cognition","acceptedAnswers":["avian cognition"],"explanation":"原文答案句：My plan always was to use his imitative skills to get a better understanding of avian cognition.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问Pepperberg明确表示她是要进行一项关于什么的研究，而不是要教鹦鹉说话。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"Pepperberg clarified that she wanted to conduct a study concerning\"定位到F段中Pepperberg明确说明研究目的的句子。\n解题思路：根据F段原文中的\"My plan always was to use his imitative skills to get a better understanding of avian cognition\"可以确定，Pepperberg研究的核心是关于\"avian cognition\"（鸟类认知），这正是她通过Alex的模仿能力想要深入了解的内容。应填写\"avian cognition\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62940","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-10\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 7-10 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8717:62940:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"particularly chosen","acceptedAnswers":["particularly chosen"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Pepperberg bought Alex in a Chicago pet store where she let the store’s assistant pick him out because she didn’t want other scientists saying later that she’d particularly chosen an especially smart bird for her work.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是为什么店员随机挑选了这只鸟，是为了避免其他科学家说这只鸟怎么样。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键词\"picked out a bird at random\"和\"avoiding other scientists saying that the bird is\"定位到D段第二句，这里提到了Pepperberg让店员随机挑选鸟的原因。\n解题思路：原文中提到Pepperberg让店员随机挑选鸟，是为了避免其他科学家说她在研究中特别挑选了一只聪明的鸟。题目中的\"particularly chosen\"对应原文中的\"particularly chosen an especially smart bird\"，因此答案为\"particularly chosen\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62940","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-10\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 7-10 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8717:62944:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"color/colour","acceptedAnswers":["color","colour"],"explanation":"原文答案句：She then retrieved a green key and a small green cup from a basket on a shelf. She held up the two items to Alex’s eye. ‘What’s same?’ she asked. Without hesitation, Alex’s beak opened: ‘Co-lor.’\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是，看到那些相似的物品后，亚历克斯是怎么回答的。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“similarity”和“subjects showed to him”可以定位到G段，其中描述了Pepperberg向Alex展示两个物品并询问相似性。\n解题思路：在G段中，Pepperberg向Alex展示了绿色钥匙和绿色杯子，并问‘What’s same?’，Alex回答‘Co-lor.’颜色。因此，答案是“color”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62944","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nAnswer the questions 11-13 below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8717:62945:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"wrong pronunciation","acceptedAnswers":["wrong pronunciation"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘Talk clearly!’ he commanded, when one of the younger birds Pepperberg was also teaching talked with wrong pronunciation.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问除了Alex之外，年轻的鹦鹉有什么问题。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"young parrots\"和\"except for Alex\"定位到H段中描述年轻鹦鹉的部分。\n解题思路：根据H段原文\"when one of the younger birds Pepperberg was also teaching talked with wrong pronunciation\"可以确定，除了Alex之外，年轻的鹦鹉的问题是发音不正确，即\"wrong pronunciation\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62945","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nAnswer the questions 11-13 below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8717:62946:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"teenager","acceptedAnswers":["teenager"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At this stage, he’s like a teenager; he’s moody, and I’m never sure what he’ll do.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是通过Alex的行为方式，我们可以称他为什么。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"behaved\"和\"what we can call him\"提示我们需要找到描述Alex行为方式的句子，并从中找出可以用来称呼他的词语。\n解题思路：在H段中，作者描述了Alex在测试过程中的行为，包括区分颜色、形状、大小和材料，以及进行简单的算术。然后，作者提到Alex在其中一个年轻鸟的发音不正确时说：\"Talk clearly!\"，表明了Alex顽固调皮。接着，作者说：此刻的他就像个十几岁的孩子，情绪多变，我永远猜不透他会做什么。这句话直接给出了我们可以用来称呼Alex的词语，即\"teenager\"。因此，填入\"teenager\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62946","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nAnswer the questions 11-13 below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"62934","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Firstly, Alex has grasped quite a lot of vocabulary.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"62935","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>At the beginning of the study, Alex felt frightened in the presence of humans.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"62936","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Previously, many scientists realized that the animal possesses the ability of thinking.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"62937","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>It has taken a long time before people get to know cognition existing in animals.</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"62938","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>As Alex could approximately imitate the sounds of English words, he was capable of roughly answering Irene’s questions regarding the world.</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"62939","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TURE  if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>By breaking in other parrots as well as producing the incorrect answers, he tried to be focused.</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"62940","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-10\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 7-10 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\">After the training of Irene, Parrot Alex can use his vocal tract to pronounce more than<strong> 7</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong> , while other scientists believe that animals have no this advanced ability of thinking,&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">they would rather teach&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">8</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong>.&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">Pepperberg clarified that she wanted to conduct a study concerning&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">9</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">but not to teach him to talk. The store’s assistant picked out a bird at random for her for the sake of avoiding other scientists saying that the bird is&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">10</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong> afterwards.</span></span></span></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"62944","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nAnswer the questions 11-13 below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>11</strong> What did Alex reply regarding the similarity of the subjects showed to him? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"62945","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nAnswer the questions 11-13 below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>12 </strong>What is the problem of the young parrots except for Alex? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"62946","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nAnswer the questions 11-13 below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>13</strong> To some extent, through the way, he behaved what we can call him? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Animal Minds: Parrot Alex&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In 1977 Irene Pepperberg, a recent graduate of Harvard University did something very bold. At a time when animals still were considered automatons, she set out to find what was on another creature’s mind by talking to it. She brought a one-year-old African gray parrot she named Alex into her lab to teach him to reproduce the sounds of the English language. ‘I thought if he learned to communicate, I could ask him questions about how he sees the world.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>When Pepperberg began her dialogue with Alex, who died last September at the age of 31, many scientists believed animals were incapable of any thought. They were simply machines, robots programmed to react to stimuli but lacking the ability to think or feel. Any pet owner would disagree. We see the love in our dogs’ eyes and know that, of course, they have thoughts and emotions. But such claims remain highly controversial. Gut instinct is not science, and it is all too easy to project human thoughts and feelings onto another creature. How, then, does a scientist prove that an animal is capable of thinking – that it is able to acquire information about the world and act on it? ‘That’s why I started my studies with Alex,’ Pepperberg said. They were seated – she at her desk, he on top of his cage – in her lab, a windowless room about the size of a boxcar, at Brandeis University. Newspapers lined the floor; baskets of bright toys were stacked on the shelves. They were clearly a team – and because of their work, the notion that animals can think is no longer so fanciful.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Certain skills are considered key signs of higher mental abilities: good memory, a grasp of grammar and symbols, self-awareness, understanding others’ motives, imitating others, and being creative. Bit by bit, in ingenious experiments, researchers have documented these talents in other species, gradually chipping away at what we thought made human beings distinctive while offering a glimpse of where our own abilities came from. Scrub jays know that other jays are thieves and that stashed food can spoil; sheep can recognize faces; chimpanzees use a variety of tools to probe termite mounds and even use weapons to hunt small mammals; dolphins can imitate human postures; the archerfish, which stuns insects with a sudden blast of water, can learn how to aim its squirt simply by watching an experienced fish perform the task. And Alex the parrot turned out to be a surprisingly good talker.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Thirty years after the Alex studies began; Pepperberg and a changing collection of assistants were still giving him English lessons. The humans, along with two younger parrots, also served as Alex’s flock, providing the social input all parrots crave. Like any flock, this one – as small as it was – had its share of drama. Alex dominated his fellow parrots, acted huffy at times around Pepperberg, tolerated the other female humans, and fell to pieces over a male assistant who dropped by for a visit. Pepperberg bought Alex in a Chicago pet store where she let the store’s assistant pick him out because she didn’t want other scientists saying later that she’d particularly chosen an especially smart bird for her work. Given that Alex’s brain was the size of a shelled walnut, most researchers thought Pepperberg’s interspecies communication study would be futile.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘Some people actually called me crazy for trying this,’ she said, ‘Scientists thought that chimpanzees were better subjects, although, of course, chimps can’t speak.’ Chimpanzees, bonobos, and gorillas have been taught to use sign language and symbols to communicate with us, often with impressive results. The bonobo Kanzi, for instance, carries his symbol-communication board with him so he can ‘talk’ to his human researchers, and he has invented combinations of symbols to express his thoughts. Nevertheless, this is not the same thing as having an animal look up at you, open his mouth, and speak. Under Pepperberg’s patient tutelage, Alex learned how to use his vocal tract to imitate almost one hundred English words, including the sounds for various foods, although he calls an apple a ‘banerry.’ ‘Apples taste a little bit like bananas to him, and they look a little bit like cherries, so Alex made up that word for them,’Pepperberg said.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>It sounded a bit mad, the idea of a bird having lessons to practice, and willingly doing it. But after listening to and observing Alex, it was difficult to argue with Pepperberg’s explanation for his behaviors. She wasn’t handing him treats for the repetitious work or rapping him on the claws to make him say the sounds. ‘He has to hear the words over and over before he can correctly imitate them,’ Pepperberg said, after pronouncing ‘seven’ for Alex a good dozen times in a row. ‘I’m not trying to see if Alex can learn a human language,’ she added, ‘That’s never been the point. My plan always was to use his imitative skills to get a better understanding of avian cognition.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In other words, because Alex was able to produce a close approximation of the sounds of some English words, Pepperberg could ask him questions about a bird’s basic understanding of the world. She couldn’t ask him what he was thinking about, but she could ask him about his knowledge of numbers, shapes, and colors. To demonstrate, Pepperberg carried Alex on her arm to a tall wooden perch in the middle of the room. She then retrieved a green key and a small green cup from a basket on a shelf. She held up the two items to Alex’s eye. ‘What’s same?’ she asked. Without hesitation, Alex’s beak opened: ‘Co-lor.’ ‘What’s different?’ Pepperberg asked. ‘Shape,’ Alex said. His voice had the digitized sound of a cartoon character. Since parrots lack lips (another reason it was difficult for Alex to pronounce some sounds, such as ba), the words seemed to come from the air around him, as if a ventriloquist were speaking. But the words – and what can only be called the thoughts – were entirely his.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>For the next 20 minutes, Alex can through his tests, distinguishing colors, shapes, sizes, and materials (wool versus wood versus metal). He did some simple arithmetic, such as accounting the yellow toy blocks among a pile of mixed hues. And, then, as if to offer final proof of the mind inside his bird’s brain, Alex spoke up. ‘Talk clearly!’ he commanded, when one of the younger birds Pepperberg was also teaching talked with wrong pronunciation. ‘Talk clearly!’ ‘Don’t be a smart aleck,’ Pepperberg said, shaking her head at him. ‘He knows all this, and he gets bored, so he interrupts the others, or he gives the wrong answer just to be obstinate. At this stage, he’s like a teenager; he’s moody, and I’m never sure what he’ll do.’</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8717&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8718","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Memory and Age","book":"阅读还原集Vol.15","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.15 · Test 1 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8718:62947:14","type":"choice","text":"What does the experiment of typist show in the passage?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The older typists, it turned out, achieved their speed with cunning little strategies that made them far more efficient than their younger counterparts: They made fewer finger movements, saving a fraction of a second here and there. They also read ahead in the text. The neural networks involved in typing appear to have been reshaped to compensate for losses in motor skills or other age changes.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是文章中的打字实验说明了什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"typist\"和\"experiment\"可以定位到文章的C段，该段描述了打字的实验。\n解题思路：根据C段中的原文句子，实验结果表明，年长的打字员通过巧妙的小策略达到了更高的效率，减少手指动作，节省零散时间；还能提前预判文本内容。这表明年长的打字员通过经验丰富的策略提高了效率，这与选项C的描述一致。因此，正确答案是C。","options":["Old people reading ability is superior.","Losses of age is irreversible.","Seasoned tactics made elders more efficient.","Old people performed poorly in the driving test ."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"62947","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8718:62948:15","type":"choice","text":"Which is correct about rat experiment?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Proliferating dendrites first appear in the visual association areas. After a month in the enriched environment, the whole cerebral cortex has expanded, a has its blood supply. Even in the enriched environment, rats get bored unless the toys are varied. ‘Animals are just like we are. They need stimulation,’ says Diamond.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问关于老鼠实验哪个说法是正确的。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"rat experiment\"定位到D段，该段详细描述了老鼠实验的过程和结果。\n解题思路：根据D段原文，实验对比了隔离环境和多样化环境对老鼠大脑的影响。单独生活的老鼠大脑会萎缩，但如果环境更加丰富，老鼠大脑会发生变化，如树突增殖和大脑皮层扩张。原文还提到，即使在丰富环境中，如果不更换玩具，老鼠也会感到无聊，说明无聊和复杂的（无变化的）环境会影响大脑发展。选项D\"无聊和复杂的环境会影响大脑发展\"与原文意思一致，因此D是正确答案。其他选项A、B、C在原文中均未提及或与原文内容不符。","options":["Different toys have a different effect on rats.","Rat’s brain weight increased in both cages.","Isolated rat’s brain grows new connections.","Boring and complicated surroundings affect brain development."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"62948","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8718:62949:16","type":"choice","text":"What can be concluded in a chess game of children group?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘Because they’d played a lot of chess, their knowledge of chess was better organized than that of the adults, and their existing knowledge of chess served as a framework for new memory,’ explains Kail.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问在象棋测试中，儿童组的结论是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"chess game\"和\"children group\"定位到I段最后一句，该句提到儿童组在象棋测试中获胜，并解释了原因。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，因为他们下过很多国际象棋，他们对国际象棋的了解比成年人更有条理，他们现有的国际象棋知识为新的记忆提供了框架。因此，可以得出结论，他们对国际象棋的知识体系组织得更好，对应选项B。选项A、C和D在原文中均未提及。","options":["They won a game with adults.","Their organization of chess knowledge is better.","Their image memory is better than adults.","They used a different part of the brain when playing chess."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"62949","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8718:62950:17","type":"choice","text":"What is the author’s purpose of using ‘vocabulary study’ at the end of the passage?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Crystallized intelligence about one’s occupation apparently does not decline at all until at least age 75, and if there is no disease or dementia, may remain even longer. Special knowledge is often organized by a process called ‘chunking.’ If procedure A and procedure B are always done together, for example, the mind may merge them into a single command. When you apply yourself to a specific interest – say, cooking – you build increasingly elaborate knowledge structures that let you do more and do it better. This ability, which is tied to experience, is the essence of expertise. Vocabulary is one such specialized form of accrued knowledge. Research clearly shows that vocabulary improves with time.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是作者在文章结尾处提到“词汇研究”的目的是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“vocabulary study”可以定位到文章J段，该段提到了词汇作为积累知识的一种形式，并且研究明确显示词汇能力会随着时间的推移而提高。退休的专业人士，尤其是教师和记者，在词汇和一般知识测试中的得分持续高于那些被认为处于智力巅峰的大学生。\n解题思路：根据原文J段的内容，作者提到词汇是一种形式的积累知识，并且研究显示词汇能力会随着时间推移而提高。这表明词汇记忆作为一种结晶智力，很难衰退。因此，作者的目的是为了说明词汇记忆作为一种晶体智力，其衰退非常困难。这与选项C“作为一种晶体智力，词汇记忆不易衰退。”完全一致。","options":["Certain people are sensitive to vocabularies while others aren’t.","Teachers and professionals won by their experience.","Vocabulary memory as a crystallized intelligence is hard to decline.","Old people use their special zone of the brain when the study."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"62950","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8718:62951:18","type":"fill","text":"填写第 18 空","answer":"memory","acceptedAnswers":["memory"],"explanation":"原文答案句：One of the most profoundly important mental functions is memory-notorious for its failure with age.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“长期以来，什么是重要的心理功能之一，会随着年龄的增长而衰退”\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“significant mental function”和“deteriorates with age”可以定位到E段第一句，明确提到“memory”是重要的心理功能之一，并且随着年龄增长会衰退。\n解题思路：原文E段第一句明确指出“memory”是重要的心理功能之一，并且随着年龄增长会衰退，与题干描述完全一致，因此答案为“memory”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62951","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-23 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8718:62952:19","type":"fill","text":"填写第 19 空","answer":"psychological","acceptedAnswers":["psychological"],"explanation":"原文答案句：So important is a memory that the Charles A. Dana foundation recently spent $8.4 million to set up a consortium of leading medical centers to measure memory loss and aging through brain-imaging technology, neurochemical experiment, and cognitive and psychological tests.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求完成一个摘要，填空处需要填写与认知实验并列的实验类型。\n定位关键信息：题目中提到的\"advanced technology\"（先进技术）、\"neurochemical experiments\"（神经化学实验）和\"cognitive and ... experiments\"（认知和...实验）可以定位到E段中关于查尔斯·A·dana基金会资助的实验方法。\n解题思路：根据E段原文，基金会资助的实验方法包括\"brain-imaging technology\"（脑成像技术）、\"neurochemical experiment\"（神经化学实验）和\"cognitive and psychological tests\"（认知和心理学测试）。题目中的\"advanced technology\"对应原文的\"brain-imaging technology\"，原文中认知实验和心理实验并列，与题目对应，因此答案为\"psychological\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62952","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-23 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8718:62953:20","type":"fill","text":"填写第 20 空","answer":"semantic memory","acceptedAnswers":["semantic memory"],"explanation":"原文答案句：What we call knowledge-facts – is what psychologists such as Harry P. Bahrick, Ph.D., of Ohio Wesleyan University call semantic memory.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问Bahrick将描述事实知识的记忆称为什么记忆。\n定位关键信息：题目中的“Bahrick called one form”和“describes factual knowledge”是定位关键。在E段中找到Bahrick和“knowledge-facts”相关的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文句子“Bahrick...call semantic memory”可知，Bahrick将描述事实知识的记忆称为“semantic memory”，因此答案为“semantic memory”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62953","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-23 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8718:62954:21","type":"fill","text":"填写第 21 空","answer":"episodic memory/event memory","acceptedAnswers":["episodic memory","event memory"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Events, conversations, and occurrences in time and space, on the other hand, make up episodic or event memory, which is triggered by cues from the context.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是另一种被称为什么的记忆类型，它包含时间和空间中的事件。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的“events in time and space format”和“another one”来定位，在E段中找到描述包含时间和空间中的事件记忆类型。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到“Events, conversations, and occurrences in time and space... make up episodic or event memory”，说明这种记忆类型包含时间和空间中的事件，且被称为“episodic or event memory”情节记忆或事件记忆。因此，答案可以是“episodic memory”或“event memory”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62954","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-23 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8718:62955:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"algebra","acceptedAnswers":["algebra"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Probing the longevity of knowledge, Bahrick tested 1,000 high school graduates to see how well they recalled their algebra.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是Bahrick进行的关于知识记忆持久性的两个实验中，他询问了1000名候选人的某种知识，有些人甚至能记得几十年前学过的内容。需要填写的是这种知识的名称。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"knowledge memory’s longevity\"（知识记忆的持久性）和\"1000 candidates\"（1000名候选人）定位到G段，该段描述了Bahrick进行的实验，其中明确提到了\"algebra\"（代数）。\n解题思路：根据G段原文，Bahrick测试了1000名高中毕业生对代数的记忆，有些人最近才学过，有些人则是在50年前。实验结果表明，代数的掌握程度取决于学习时间的长短，而不是距离上次学习的时间。因此，题目中提到的知识是\"algebra\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62955","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-23 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8718:62956:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"vocabulary","acceptedAnswers":["vocabulary"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In another study, Bahrick discovered that people who had taken several courses in Spanish, spread out over a couple of years, could recall, decades later, 60 per cent or more of the vocabulary they learned. Those who took just one course retained only a trace after three years.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是关于西班牙语课程的研究发现，多次参加课程的人能够在几十年后记住超过一半的什么内容，而只参加一次课程的人，三年后只能记住一小部分。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Spanish course\"和\"multiple courses participants\"可以定位到H段，该段落提到了关于西班牙语课程的研究。\n解题思路：根据H段原文句子，可以确定多次参加西班牙语课程的人能够在几十年后记住超过60%的\"vocabulary\"（词汇），而只参加一次课程的人，三年后只能记住一小部分。因此，题目中空缺处应填入\"vocabulary\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62956","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-23 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8718:62957:24","type":"choice","text":"24 Examined both young and old’s blood circulation of the brain while testing.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Equipped with imaging techniques that capture the brain in action, Stanley Rapoport, Ph.D., at the National Institutes of Health, measured the flow of blood in the brains of old and young people as they went through the task of matching photos of faces.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“谁检查了年轻人和老年人的大脑血液循环”。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“Examined both young and old’s blood circulation of the brain”定位到B段，找到“measured the flow of blood in the brains of old and young people”。\n解题思路：根据原文句子可知，Stanley Rapoport测量了老年人和年轻人的大脑血流，与题目描述一致，因此答案为E。","options":["Harry P. Bahrick","Arnold B. Scheibel","Marion Diamond","Timothy Salthouse","Stanley Rapport","Robert Kail"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"62957","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-F) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet\nA Harry P. Bahrick\nB Arnold B. Scheibel\nC Marion Diamond\nD Timothy Salthouse\nE Stanley Rapport\nF Robert Kail"},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8718:62957:25","type":"choice","text":"25 Aging is a significant link between physical and mental activity.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘In a sense, aging is keyed to the level of the vigor of the body and the continuous interaction between levels of body activity and levels of mental activity,’ reports Arnold B. Scheibel, M.D., whose very academic title reflects how once far-flung domains now converge on the mind and the brain.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目询问“ 衰老是身体活动与心理活动之间的重要纽带”，需要找到与此观点相关的专家及其观点。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词“aging”、“physical and mental activity”可以定位到A段中Scheibel的观点。\n解题思路：原文中Scheibel明确指出“从某种意义上说，衰老与身体活力水平密切相关，这源于身体活动强度与脑力活动强度之间的持续互动”，与题目描述完全一致，因此答案为B。","options":["Harry P. Bahrick","Arnold B. Scheibel","Marion Diamond","Timothy Salthouse","Stanley Rapport","Robert Kail"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"62957","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-F) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet\nA Harry P. Bahrick\nB Arnold B. Scheibel\nC Marion Diamond\nD Timothy Salthouse\nE Stanley Rapport\nF Robert Kail"},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8718:62957:26","type":"choice","text":"26 Some semantic memory of an event would not fade away after repetition.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘Every memory begins as an event,’ says Bahrick, ‘Through repetition, certain events leave behind a residue of knowledge or semantic memory.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是谁认为“某些事件的语义记忆在重复之后不会消退”。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“semantic memory”和“repetition”定位到F段，找到包含这两个词的句子。\n解题思路：原文提到通过重复，某些事件会留下知识或语义记忆的残留。这与题目描述的完全一致。因此，答案为A。","options":["Harry P. Bahrick","Arnold B. Scheibel","Marion Diamond","Timothy Salthouse","Stanley Rapport","Robert Kail"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"62957","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-F) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet\nA Harry P. Bahrick\nB Arnold B. Scheibel\nC Marion Diamond\nD Timothy Salthouse\nE Stanley Rapport\nF Robert Kail"},{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8718:62957:27","type":"choice","text":"27 Rat’s brain developed when putting in a diverse environment, a place where the healthcare system is developed.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：When a rat is kept in isolation without playmates or objects to interact with, the animal’s brain shrinks, but if we put that rat with 11 other rats in a large cage and give them an assortment of wheels, ladders, and other toys, we can show – after four days – significant differences in its brain,’ says Diamond, professor of integrative biology.  Proliferating dendrites first appear in the visual association areas. After a month in the enriched environment, the whole cerebral cortex has expanded, a has its blood supply.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是谁认为将老鼠放在多样化环境中，其大脑得以发育。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"Rat's brain developed\"和\"diverse environment\"可以定位到D段中关于老鼠在多样化环境中大脑变化的描述。\n解题思路：D段中明确提到，当老鼠被放在一个有大轮子、梯子和其他玩具的大笼子中与其他老鼠一起时，其大脑会在四天内显示出显著差异，树突首先在视觉关联区大量增生，在多样化环境中生活一个月后，整个大脑皮层已扩张并建立了血液供应。这与题目中描述的老鼠大脑在多样化环境中发育的情况完全一致，因此答案为D段中提到的Diamond的观点。","options":["Harry P. Bahrick","Arnold B. Scheibel","Marion Diamond","Timothy Salthouse","Stanley Rapport","Robert Kail"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"62957","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-F) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet\nA Harry P. Bahrick\nB Arnold B. Scheibel\nC Marion Diamond\nD Timothy Salthouse\nE Stanley Rapport\nF Robert Kail"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"62947","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What does the experiment of typist show in the passage?</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"62948","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Which is correct about rat experiment?</strong></p>","firstNumber":15},{"id":"62949","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What can be concluded in a chess game of children group?</strong></p>","firstNumber":16},{"id":"62950","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is the author’s purpose of using ‘vocabulary study’ at the end of the passage?</strong></p>","firstNumber":17},{"id":"62951","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-23 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>It’s long been known that as one significant mental function, <strong>18.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[18] ____</strong> deteriorates with age. \nCharles A. Dana foundation invested millions of dollars to test memory decline.</p>","firstNumber":18},{"id":"62952","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-23 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>They used advanced technology, neurochemical experiments and ran several cognitive and <strong>19.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong> experiments.</p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"62953","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-23 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Bahrick called one form ‘<strong>20.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong> ’, which describes factual knowledge.</p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"62954","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-23 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Another one called ‘<strong>21.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong> ’ contains events in time and space format.</p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"62955","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-23 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>He conducted two experiments toward to knowledge memory’s longevity, he asked 1000 candidates some knowledge of <strong>22.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong> , some could even remember it decades ago.</p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"62956","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 18-23\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18-23 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Second research of Spanish course found that multiple courses participants could remember more than half of <strong>23.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong> . They learned after decades, whereas single course taker only remembered as short as 3 years.</p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"62957","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-F) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-F in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet\nA Harry P. Bahrick\nB Arnold B. Scheibel\nC Marion Diamond\nD Timothy Salthouse\nE Stanley Rapport\nF Robert Kail","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> Harry P. Bahrick&nbsp;</p><p><strong>B</strong> Arnold B. Scheibel&nbsp;</p><p><strong>C</strong> Marion Diamond&nbsp;</p><p><strong>D</strong> Timothy Salthouse&nbsp;</p><p><strong>E </strong>Stanley Rapport&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>F</strong> Robert Kail&nbsp;</p><p><strong>24 </strong>Examined both young and old’s blood circulation of the brain while testing.<strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":24}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Memory and Age</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Aging, it is now clear, is part of an ongoing maturation process that all our organs go through. ‘In a sense, aging is keyed to the level of the vigor of the body and the continuous interaction between levels of body activity and levels of mental activity,’ reports Arnold B. Scheibel, M.D., whose very academic title reflects how once far-flung domains now converge on the mind and the brain. Scheibel is a professor of anatomy, cell biology, psychiatry, and behavioral sciences at the University of California at Los Angeles, and director of university’s Brain Research Institute. Experimental evidence has backed up popular assumptions that the aging mind undergoes decay analogous to that of the aging body. Younger monkeys, chimps, and lower animals consistently outperform their older colleagues on memory tests. In humans, psychologists concluded, memory and other mental functions deteriorate over time because of inevitable organic changes in the brain as neurons die off. The mental decline after young adulthood appeared inevitable.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Equipped with imaging techniques that capture the brain in action, Stanley Rapoport, Ph.D., at the National Institutes of Health, measured the flow of blood in the brains of old and young people as they went through the task of matching photos of faces. Since blood flow reflects neuronal activity, Rapoport could compare with networks of neurons were being used by different subjects. ‘Even when the reaction times of older and younger subjects were the same, the neural networks they used were significantly different. The older subjects were using different internal strategies to accomplish the same result in the same time,’ Rapoport says. Either the task required greater effort on the part of the older subjects or the work of neurons originally involved in tasks of that type had been taken over by other neurons, creating different networks.</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>At the Georgia Institute of Technology, psychologist Timothy Salthouse, Ph.D., compared a group of very fast and accurate typists of college-age with another group in their 60s. since reaction time is faster in younger people and most people’s fingers grow less nimble with age, younger typists might be expected to tap right along while the older one’s fumble. But both typed 60 words a minute. The older typists, it turned out, achieved their speed with cunning little strategies that made them far more efficient than their younger counterparts: They made fewer finger movements, saving a fraction of a second here and there. They also read ahead in the text. The neural networks involved in typing appear to have been reshaped to compensate for losses in motor skills or other age changes.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘When a rat is kept in isolation without playmates or objects to interact with, the animal’s brain shrinks, but if we put that rat with 11 other rats in a large cage and give them an assortment of wheels, ladders, and other toys, we can show – after four days – significant differences in its brain,’ says Diamond, professor of integrative biology. Proliferating dendrites first appear in the visual association areas. After a month in the enriched environment, the whole cerebral cortex has expanded, a has its blood supply. Even in the enriched environment, rats get bored unless the toys are varied. ‘Animals are just like we are. They need stimulation,’ says Diamond.</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>One of the most profoundly important mental functions is memory-notorious for its failure with age. So important is a memory that the Charles A. Dana foundation recently spent $8.4 million to set up a consortium of leading medical centers to measure memory loss and aging through brain-imaging technology, neurochemical experiment, and cognitive and psychological tests. One thing, however, is already fairlpy clear – many aspects of memory are not a function of age at all but of education. Memory exists in more than one form. What we call knowledge-facts – is what psychologists such as Harry P. Bahrick, Ph.D., of Ohio Wesleyan University call semantic memory. Events, conversations, and occurrences in time and space, on the other hand, make up episodic or event memory, which is triggered by cues from the context. If you were around in 1963 you don’t need to be reminded of the circumstances surrounding the moment you heard that JFK had been assassinated. That event is etched into your episodic memory.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>When you forget a less vivid item, like buying a roll of paper towels at the supermarket, you may blame it on your aging memory. It’s true that episodic memory begins to decline when most people are in their 50s, but it’s never perfect at any age. ‘Every memory begins as an event,’ says Bahrick, ‘Through repetition, certain events leave behind a residue of knowledge or semantic memory. On a specific day in the past, somebody taught you that two and two are four, but you’ve been over that information so often you don’t remember where you learned it. What started as an episodic memory has become a permanent part of your knowledge base.’ You remember the content, not the context. Our language knowledge, our knowledge of the world and of people, is largely that permanent or semi-permanent residue.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Probing the longevity of knowledge, Bahrick tested 1,000 high school graduates to see how well they recalled their algebra. Some had completed the course as recently as a month before, others as long as 50 years earlier. He also determined how long each person had studied algebra, the grade received, and how much the skill was used over the course of adulthood. Surprisingly, a person’s grasp of algebra at the time of testing did not depend on how long ago he’d taken the course – the determining factor was the duration of instruction. Those who had spent only a few months learning algebra forgot most of it within two or three years.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In another study, Bahrick discovered that people who had taken several courses in Spanish, spread out over a couple of years, could recall, decades later, 60 per cent or more of the vocabulary they learned. Those who took just one course retained only a trace after three years. ‘This long-term residue of knowledge remains stable over the decades, independent of the age of the person and the age of the memory. No serious deficit appears until people get to their 50s and 60s, probably due to the degenerative processes of aging rather than a cognitive loss.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘You could say metamemory is a byproduct of going to school,’ says psychologist Robert Kail, Ph.D., of Purdue University, who studies children from birth to 20 years, the time of life when mental development is most rapid. ‘The question-and-answer process, especially exam-taking, helps children learn – and also teaches them how their memory works. This may be one reason why, according to a broad range of studies in people over 60, the better educated a person is, the more likely they are to perform better in life and on psychological tests. A group of adult novice chess players were compared with a group of child experts at the game. In tests of their ability to remember a random series of numbers, the adults, as expected, outscored the children. But when asked to remember the patterns of chess pieces arranged on a board, the children won. ‘Because they’d played a lot of chess, their knowledge of chess was better organized than that of the adults, and their existing knowledge of chess served as a framework for new memory,’ explains Kail.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Specialized knowledge is a mental resource that only improve with time. Crystallized intelligence about one’s occupation apparently does not decline at all until at least age 75, and if there is no disease or dementia, may remain even longer. Special knowledge is often organized by a process called ‘chunking.’ If procedure A and procedure B are always done together, for example, the mind may merge them into a single command. When you apply yourself to a specific interest – say, cooking – you build increasingly elaborate knowledge structures that let you do more and do it better. This ability, which is tied to experience, is the essence of expertise. Vocabulary is one such specialized form of accrued knowledge. Research clearly shows that vocabulary improves with time. Retired professionals, especially teachers and journalists, consistently score higher on tests of vocabulary and general information than college students, who are supposed to be in their mental prime.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px; text-align: center;\"><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8718&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8719","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Morse Code","book":"阅读还原集Vol.15","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.15 · Test 1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8719:62958:28","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"J","acceptedAnswers":["J"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Since 1992 countries around the world have been decommissioning their Morse equipment with similar (if less poetic) signoffs as the world’s shipping switches over to a new satellite-based arrangement, the Global Maritime Distress and Safety System. The final deadline for the switch-over to GMDSS is February 1, a date that is widely seen as the end of an era.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求为A段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读A段，可以找到关键信息“the end of the use of Morse code for distress calls in French waters”和“The final deadline for the switch-over to GMDSS is February 1, a date that is widely seen as the end of an era.”，这些信息表明A段主要讲述的是摩尔斯电码即将结束使用。\n解题思路：根据A段的内容，可以确定该段主要讲述的是摩尔斯电码即将结束使用，1997年2月1日，将正式淘汰摩斯密码，使用全球海上遇险和安全系统GMDSS，这代表一个时代的终结。这与“The beginning of an end”（走向终结的开始）的意思相符。因此，A段的标题应选择标题The beginning of an end”。","options":["The advantage of Morse’s invention","A suitable job for women","Morse’s invention was developed","Sea rescue after the invention of radiotelegraphy","The emergence of many job opportunities","Standard and variations","Application of Morse code in a new technology","The discovery of electricity","International expansion of Morse Code","The beginning of an end","The move of using code to convey information"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"62958","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nThe passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph A-H from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-xi in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8719:62958:29","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"K","acceptedAnswers":["K"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At the time Morse was a painter and occasional inventor, but when another of the ship’s passengers informed him of recent advances in electrical theory, Morse was suddenly taken with the idea of building an electric telegraph to send message in codes.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求为B段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读B段，可以发现段落主要讲述了摩尔斯电码的历史背景和摩尔斯本人的故事，包括他在船上产生发明电报的想法，以及他最终成功并被称为“电报之父”。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句和B段的内容，可以确定B段主要讲述的是摩斯电码的历史，摩尔斯想到用电报机发送代码传递信息，于是他就发明了摩斯电码。因此，选择标题“The move of using code to convey information”（使用代码传达信息的方法）作为B段的标题是合适的。","options":["The advantage of Morse’s invention","A suitable job for women","Morse’s invention was developed","Sea rescue after the invention of radiotelegraphy","The emergence of many job opportunities","Standard and variations","Application of Morse code in a new technology","The discovery of electricity","International expansion of Morse Code","The beginning of an end","The move of using code to convey information"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"62958","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nThe passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph A-H from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-xi in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8719:62958:30","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But Morse later abandoned this scheme and, with the help of an associate, Alfred Vail, devised the Morse alphabet, which could be used to spell out messages a letter at a time in dots and dashes.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求为C段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读C段，可以发现段落主要介绍了莫尔斯电报的硬件要求，以及发明出最终的摩斯电码的过程。\n解题思路：根据C段的内容，可以确定该段落主要介绍了莫尔斯电报的硬件要求，相比其他很多竞争对手，他的发明对硬件要求低，不过需要使用者记忆代码，接着讲述了莫尔斯发明摩斯电码的过程。根据提供的标题列表，“Morse’s invention was developed”（莫尔斯的发明得以发展完善）选项最符合这一描述。","options":["The advantage of Morse’s invention","A suitable job for women","Morse’s invention was developed","Sea rescue after the invention of radiotelegraphy","The emergence of many job opportunities","Standard and variations","Application of Morse code in a new technology","The discovery of electricity","International expansion of Morse Code","The beginning of an end","The move of using code to convey information"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"62958","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nThe passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph A-H from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-xi in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8719:62958:31","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Morse’s telegraph needed only one. And some people, it soon transpired, had a natural facility for Morse code.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求为D段选择正确的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读D段，可以定位到段落主要讨论的是学习莫尔斯电码的难度以及与其他电报设计的比较。\n解题思路：D段首先提到学习莫尔斯电码的复杂性，将其与其他更易使用的电报设计进行比较，如库克和惠斯通的针式电报。尽管针式电报易于使用，但需要更多的电线连接电报站。而莫尔斯电报仅需一根电线。而且，后来发现，有些人天生就擅长莫尔斯电码。因此，D段的主要内容是关于莫尔斯电码设计的优势。根据选项，标题“The advantage of Morse’s invention”（莫尔斯发明的优势）最符合段落内容。","options":["The advantage of Morse’s invention","A suitable job for women","Morse’s invention was developed","Sea rescue after the invention of radiotelegraphy","The emergence of many job opportunities","Standard and variations","Application of Morse code in a new technology","The discovery of electricity","International expansion of Morse Code","The beginning of an end","The move of using code to convey information"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"62958","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nThe passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph A-H from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-xi in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8719:62958:32","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It was adopted as the European standard in 1851, allowing direct connections between the telegraph networks of different countries. Britain chose not to participate., sticking with needle telegraphs for a few more years. By this time Morse code had been revised to allow for accents and other foreign characters, resulting in a split between American and International Morse that continues to this day.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求为E段选择一个正确的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读E段，可以找到关键信息是关于莫尔斯电报在欧洲被采用为标准以及英国的选择，以及摩斯电码的标准修订和变体。\n解题思路：根据E段的内容，可以确定该段主要讲述了莫尔斯电报的欧洲标准设定，及其后来的变体，因此选择与这一主题相符的标题。根据提供的选项，标题“Standard and variations”（标准和变体）最符合E段的内容。","options":["The advantage of Morse’s invention","A suitable job for women","Morse’s invention was developed","Sea rescue after the invention of radiotelegraphy","The emergence of many job opportunities","Standard and variations","Application of Morse code in a new technology","The discovery of electricity","International expansion of Morse Code","The beginning of an end","The move of using code to convey information"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"62958","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nThe passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph A-H from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-xi in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8719:62958:33","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph F","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：First-class operators, who could send and receive at speeds of up to 45 words a minute, handled press traffic, securing the best-paid jobs in big cities. At the bottom of the pile were slow, inexperienced rural operators, many of whom worked the wires as part-timers. As their Morse code improved, however, rural operators found that their new-found skill was a passport to better pay in a city job. Telegraphers soon swelled the ranks of the emerging middle classes. Telegraphy was also deemed suitable work for women. By 1870, a third of the operators in the Western Union office in New York, the largest telegraph office in America, were female.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求为F段选择一个最合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：仔细阅读F段内容，找出段落的核心主题和关键信息。\n解题思路：F段主要讲述了电报员工作在当时的发展。负责处理新闻电报业务的电报员，在大城市中占据高薪职位，成为人们跻身中产阶级、甚至为女性提供重要就业机会的途径。根据选项，标题“The emergence of many job opportunities”（出现许多工作机会）能够准确反映F段主要内容。","options":["The advantage of Morse’s invention","A suitable job for women","Morse’s invention was developed","Sea rescue after the invention of radiotelegraphy","The emergence of many job opportunities","Standard and variations","Application of Morse code in a new technology","The discovery of electricity","International expansion of Morse Code","The beginning of an end","The move of using code to convey information"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"62958","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nThe passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph A-H from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-xi in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8719:62958:34","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph G","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：By the time of his death in 1872, the world was well and truly wired: more than 650,000 miles of telegraph line and 30,000 miles of submarine cable were throbbing with Morse code; and 20,000 towns and villages were connected to the global network. Just as the Internet is today often called an ‘information superhighway’, the telegraph was described in its day as an ‘ instantaneous highway of thought.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求为G段选择一个合适的标题，从给定的选项中选择。\n定位关键信息：阅读G段内容，找到段落的主旨句或核心信息。\n解题思路：G段主要描述了Morse在1871年通过一场盛大的仪式向全球的电报员告别，接着描述摩斯电码在全球范围内的推广应用。到1872年他去世时，世界已真正实现电报网络覆盖：超过65万英里的电报线路和3万英里的海底电缆正以莫尔斯电码脉动；2万个城镇村庄接入了全球网络。因此，根据选项，标题“International expansion of Morse Code”（摩斯电码的国际化发展）最符合G段的内容。","options":["The advantage of Morse’s invention","A suitable job for women","Morse’s invention was developed","Sea rescue after the invention of radiotelegraphy","The emergence of many job opportunities","Standard and variations","Application of Morse code in a new technology","The discovery of electricity","International expansion of Morse Code","The beginning of an end","The move of using code to convey information"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"62958","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nThe passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph A-H from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-xi in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8719:62958:35","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph H","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Morse code, however, was about to be given a new lease of life thanks to another new technology: wireless. Following the invention of radiotelegraphy by Guglielmo Marconi in 1896, its potential for use at sea quickly became apparent. For the first time, ships could communicate with each other, and with the shore, whatever the weather and even when out of visual range. In 1897 Marconi successfully sent Morse code messages between a shore station and an Italian warship 19 km (12miles) aways. By 1910, Morse radio equipment was commonplace on ships.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目要求为H段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：需要阅读H段内容，理解段落主旨，然后从给定的标题列表中选择最匹配的一个。\n解题思路：H段主要讲述了莫尔斯电码的鼎盛时期在19世纪90年代随着电话和自动电报的发明而结束，但随后又因为无线技术的出现而获得了新的生命。段落中提到了莫尔斯电码在无线技术中的应用，尤其是在海上通信中的重要性。因此，选择标题时，应考虑到莫尔斯电码在新技术中的应用。在给定的标题列表中，标题“Application of Morse code in a new technology”（莫尔斯电码在新技术中的应用）最符合这一描述。","options":["The advantage of Morse’s invention","A suitable job for women","Morse’s invention was developed","Sea rescue after the invention of radiotelegraphy","The emergence of many job opportunities","Standard and variations","Application of Morse code in a new technology","The discovery of electricity","International expansion of Morse Code","The beginning of an end","The move of using code to convey information"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"62958","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nThe passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph A-H from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-xi in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8719:62959:36","type":"choice","text":"Morse had already been famous as an inventor before his invention of Morse code.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Morse was a painter and occasional inventor, but when another of the ship’s passengers informed him of recent advances in electrical theory, Morse was suddenly taken with the idea of building an electric telegraph to send message in codes.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问“莫尔斯在发明莫尔斯电码之前就已经是一位著名的发明家”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词“Morse”和“inventor”定位到B段，找到关于莫尔斯身份的描述。\n解题思路：原文提到莫尔斯当时是一位画家和业余发明家（an occasional inventor），并没有说他是一位著名的发明家。题目中的“already been famous as an inventor”与原文描述不符，因此答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62959","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage ? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8719:62960:37","type":"choice","text":"Morse waited a long time before receiving support from Congress.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Morse succeeded and is now remembered as ‘the father of the telegraph’ partly thanks to his single mindedness – it was 12 years, for example, before he secured money from Congress to build his first telegraph line – but also for technical reasons.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问“莫尔斯等待了很长时间才获得国会的支持”，需要判断这一说法是否与原文一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"waited a long time\"和\"support from Congress\"定位原文，找到B段中提到莫尔斯获得国会支持的时间信息。\n解题思路：原文明确提到\"it was 12 years, for example, before he secured money from Congress to build his first telegraph line\"，说明莫尔斯确实等待了12年才获得国会的资金支持，这与题目所述\"waited a long time before receiving support from Congress\"完全一致，因此该说法是正确的。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62960","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage ? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8719:62961:38","type":"choice","text":"Morse code is difficult to learn compared with other designs.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At first, the need to learn this complicated-looking code made Morse’s telegraph seem impossibly tricky compared with other, more user-friendly designs.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问“与其他电码设计相比，摩斯密码更难学习”这一说法是否与文章作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“Morse code is difficult to learn compared with other designs”定位到D段首句，该句明确提到摩斯密码看起来复杂，与其他设计相比显得难以掌握。\n解题思路：根据D段首句可知，起初，与其他更用户友好的设计相比，学习这种看起来很复杂的代码，使得莫尔斯电码难以掌握。因此，题目中的说法与文章内容一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62961","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage ? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8719:62962:39","type":"choice","text":"Companies and firms prefer to employ telegraphy operators from rural areas.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At the bottom of the pile were slow, inexperienced rural operators, many of whom worked the wires as part-timers. As their Morse code improved, however, rural operators found that their new-found skill was a passport to better pay in a city job.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问“公司更喜欢雇佣农村地区的电报员”，要求判断这一说法是否与文章作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"Companies and firms prefer to employ telegraphy operators from rural areas\"（公司和公司更喜欢雇佣来自农村地区的电报员）定位到文章中相关句子。在F段中，提到“农村操作员”和他们的职业发展。\n解题思路：原文提到，处于底层的则是动作迟缓、缺乏经验的乡村电报员，其中许多人以兼职身份在电报线上工作。然而随着摩尔斯电码技能的提升，这些乡村电报员发现，他们新掌握的技能竟成了在城市工作中获得更高薪酬的通行证。但并未明确说明“公司更喜欢雇佣农村操作员”。因此，题目中的“prefer”（更喜欢）这一主观偏好信息在文章中未明确给出，无法判断其真实性。故答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62962","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage ? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8719:62963:40","type":"choice","text":"Morse died from overwork.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：By the time of his death in 1872, the world was well and truly wired: more than 650,000 miles of telegraph line and 30,000 miles of submarine cable were throbbing with Morse code; and 20,000 towns and villages were connected to the global network.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问“Morse死于过劳”这一说法是否与文章作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Morse died\"定位到G段末句，文中提到Morse在1872年去世，但并未说明死因。\n解题思路：文章提到Morse在1872年去世，但并未提及任何关于他死因的信息。因此，题目中的信息在文章中未给出，应选择NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62963","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage ? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"62958","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-35\nThe passage has eight paragraphs A-H. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph A-H from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-xi in boxes 28-35 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"62959","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage ? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Morse had already been famous as an inventor before his invention of Morse code.</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"62960","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage ? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Morse waited a long time before receiving support from Congress.</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"62961","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage ? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Morse code is difficult to learn compared with other designs.</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"62962","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage ? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Companies and firms prefer to employ telegraphy operators from rural areas.</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"62963","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage ? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Morse died from overwork.</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Morse Code&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Morse code is being replaced by a new satellite-based system for sending distress calls at sea. Its dots and dashes have had a good run for their money.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘Calling all. This is our last cry before our eternal silence.’ Surprisingly this message, which flashed over the airwaves in the dots and dashes of Morse code on January 31st 1997, was not a desperate transmission by a radio operator on a sinking ship. Rather, it was a message signalling the end of the use of Morse code for distress calls in French waters. Since 1992 countries around the world have been decommissioning their Morse equipment with similar (if less poetic) signoffs as the world’s shipping switches over to a new satellite-based arrangement, the Global Maritime Distress and Safety System. The final deadline for the switch-over to GMDSS is February 1, a date that is widely seen as the end of an era.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The code has, however, had a good history. Appropriately for a technology commonly associated with radio operators on sinking ships, the idea of Morse code is said to have occurred to Samuel Morse while he was on board a ship crossing the Atlantic. At the time Morse was a painter and occasional inventor, but when another of the ship’s passengers informed him of recent advances in electrical theory, Morse was suddenly taken with the idea of building an electric telegraph to send message in codes. Other inventors had been trying to do just that for the best part of a century. Morse succeeded and is now remembered as ‘the father of the telegraph’ partly thanks to his single mindedness – it was 12 years, for example, before he secured money from Congress to build his first telegraph line – but also for technical reasons.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Compared with rival electric telegraph designs, such as the needle telegraph developed by William Cooke and Charles Wheatstone in Britain, Morse’s design was very simple: it required little more than a ‘key’ (essentially, a spring-loaded switch) to send messages, a clicking ‘sounder’ to receive them, and a wire to link the two. But although Morse’s hardware was simple, there was a catch: in order to use his equipment, operators had to learn the special code of dots and still dashes that still bears his name. Originally, Morse had not intended to use combinations of dots and dashes to represent individual letters. His first code, sketched in his notebook during that transatlantic voyage, used dots and dashes to represent the digits 0 to 9. Morse’s idea was that messages would consist of strings of numbers corresponding to words and phrases in a special numbered dictionary. But Morse later abandoned this scheme and, with the help of an associate, Alfred Vail, devised the Morse alphabet, which could be used to spell out messages a letter at a time in dots and dashes.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>At first, the need to learn this complicated-looking code made Morse’s telegraph seem impossibly tricky compared with other, more user-friendly designs. Cooke’s sand Wheatstone’s telegraph, For example, used five needles to pick out letters on a diamond-shaped grid. But although this meant that anyone could use it, it also required five wires between telegraph stations. Morse’s telegraph needed only one. And some people, it soon transpired, had a natural facility for Morse code.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>As electric telegraphy took off in the early 1850s, the Morse telegraph quickly became dominant. It was adopted as the European standard in 1851, allowing direct connections between the telegraph networks of different countries. Britain chose not to participate., sticking with needle telegraphs for a few more years. By this time Morse code had been revised to allow for accents and other foreign characters, resulting in a split between American and International Morse that continues to this day.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>On international submarine cables, left and right swings of a light-beam reflected from a tiny rotating mirror were used to represent dots and dashes. Meanwhile a distinct telegraphic subculture was emerging, with its own customs and vocabulary, and a hierarchy based on the speed at which operators could send and receive Morse code. First-class operators, who could send and receive at speeds of up to 45 words a minute, handled press traffic, securing the best-paid jobs in big cities. At the bottom of the pile were slow, inexperienced rural operators, many of whom worked the wires as part-timers. As their Morse code improved, however, rural operators found that their new-found skill was a passport to better pay in a city job. Telegraphers soon swelled the ranks of the emerging middle classes. Telegraphy was also deemed suitable work for women. By 1870, a third of the operators in the Western Union office in New York, the largest telegraph office in America, were female.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In a dramatic ceremony in 1871, Morse himself said goodbye to the global community of telegraphers he had brought into being. After a lavish banquet and many adulatory speeches, Morse sat down behind an operator’s table and, placing his finger on a key connected to every telegraph wire in America, tapped out his final farewell to a standing ovation. By the time of his death in 1872, the world was well and truly wired: more than 650,000 miles of telegraph line and 30,000 miles of submarine cable were throbbing with Morse code; and 20,000 towns and villages were connected to the global network. Just as the Internet is today often called an ‘information superhighway’, the telegraph was described in its day as an ‘ instantaneous highway of thought.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>But by the 1890s the Morse telegraph’s heyday as a cutting-edge technology was coming to an end, with the invention of the telephone and the rise of automatic telegraphs, precursors of the teleprinter, neither of which required specialist skills to operate. Morse code, however, was about to be given a new lease of life thanks to another new technology: wireless. Following the invention of radiotelegraphy by Guglielmo Marconi in 1896, its potential for use at sea quickly became apparent. For the first time, ships could communicate with each other, and with the shore, whatever the weather and even when out of visual range. In 1897 Marconi successfully sent Morse code messages between a shore station and an Italian warship 19 km (12miles) aways. By 1910, Morse radio equipment was commonplace on ships.&amp;#</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8719&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8260","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Radiocarbon Dating: The Profile of Nancy Athfield","book":"阅读还原集Vol.14","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.14 · Test 4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8260:60226:1","type":"choice","text":"Nancy Athfield first discovered the ancient remains in Cambodia.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：thfield studied the ancient remains found in the country of Cambodia. Many prehistoric remains were discovered by the local people of Cambodia.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问南希·阿瑟菲尔德首先发现了柬埔寨的古代遗迹，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"ancient remains\"和\"Cambodia\"定位到A段，发现文中提到\"Many prehistoric remains were discovered by the local people of Cambodia.\"（许多史前遗迹是由柬埔寨当地人发现的。）\n解题思路：原文明确指出是当地人首先发现了这些古代遗迹，而不是南希·阿瑟菲尔德。因此，题目中的说法与原文信息不符，应选择False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60226","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the infromation given in the passage? In boxes1-7 on you answer sheet,write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8260:60227:2","type":"choice","text":"The remains found in the Cambodia was in good condition.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The remains had never been scientifically studied, so Nancy was greatly intrigued by the opportunity to use modern methods to discover the true age of these ancient objects.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是关于在柬埔寨发现的遗骸是否保存完好。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"remains found in the Cambodia\"可以定位到A段中关于柬埔寨遗骸的描述。\n解题思路：原文中提到该遗骸从未接受过科学研究，但并没有提到它们的状态是良好还是损坏。因此，无法根据原文判断这些遗骸是否状况良好。所以答案是Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60227","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the infromation given in the passage? In boxes1-7 on you answer sheet,write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8260:60228:3","type":"choice","text":"Nancy took some time off from her regular work to do research in Cambodia.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The remains had never been scientifically studied, so Nancy was greatly intrigued by the opportunity to use modern methods to discover the true age of these ancient objects.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是南希是否从工作中抽出时间去柬埔寨进行研究。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"took some time off from her regular work\"和\"research in Cambodia\"来定位答案。在文章中，我们需要找到关于南希在柬埔寨进行研究和她的工作之间的关系的描述。\n解题思路：原文第1段最后一句只说到她对此项研究工作非常感兴趣，并没有说她是否离开现有工作。因此，本题的答案为Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60228","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the infromation given in the passage? In boxes1-7 on you answer sheet,write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8260:60229:4","type":"choice","text":"The Cambodia government asked Nancy to radiocarbon the remains.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Athfield had this unique opportunity because her team, comprised of scientists and filmmakers, were in Cambodia working on a documentary....For the first time, Athfield and her team had a chance to use radiocarbon dating to find new evidence. They had a chance to solve the historic mystery that many had been arguing over for years.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“柬埔寨政府要求南希去利用放射性碳测年法研究遗迹”，需要判断这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词“Cambodia government asked Nancy to radiocarbon the remains”定位到B段，文中提到Nancy和她的团队有机会使用放射性碳测年来寻找新证据，但并未提到是柬埔寨政府要求她这样做。\n解题思路：根据B段的内容，Nancy和她的团队是自行决定使用放射性碳测年来寻找证据，文中并未提及柬埔寨政府的要求。因此，题目中的说法与文章信息不符，答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60229","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the infromation given in the passage? In boxes1-7 on you answer sheet,write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8260:60230:5","type":"choice","text":"The filmmakers aimed to find out how the Angkor was rebuilt.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The team was trying to discover evidence to prove a controversial claim in history: that Cambodia was the resting place for the famous royal family of Angkor.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是电影制作人旨在找出吴哥窟是如何重建的，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"filmmakers\"和\"rebuilt\"定位到B段，该段提到电影制作团队的目标是寻找证据来证明一个有争议的历史主张，即柬埔寨是吴哥王室家族的安息之地。\n解题思路：原文明确指出电影制作团队的目标是寻找证据证明吴哥窟是王室家族的安息之地，而题目中提到的\"how the Angkor was rebuilt\"（吴哥窟是如何重建的）与原文内容不符。因此，题目陈述与原文信息不一致，答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60230","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the infromation given in the passage? In boxes1-7 on you answer sheet,write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8260:60231:6","type":"choice","text":"Nancy initially doubted whether the royal family was hidden in Cambodia.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The team was trying to discover evidence to prove a controversial claim in history: that Cambodia was the resting place for the famous royal family of Angkor. At that time, written records and historic accounts conflicted on the true resting place. Many people across the world disagreed over where the final resting place was. For the first time, Athfield and her team had a chance to use radiocarbon dating to find new evidence. They had a chance to solve the historic mystery that many had been arguing over for years.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是南希最初怀疑皇家家族是否隐藏在柬埔寨，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词\"royal family\"和\"hidden in Cambodia\"可以定位到C段中提到皇家家族的句子。\n解题思路：B段提到，团队前往柬埔寨是为了验证一个有争议的说法。描述了整个项目的目的和背景，是一种客观陈述。然而，文中完全没有提及Nancy个人对这个目标或假说的主观看法，没有信息表明她本人持有怀疑态度。因此，题目信息在原文中找不到依据，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60231","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the infromation given in the passage? In boxes1-7 on you answer sheet,write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8260:60232:7","type":"choice","text":"Nancy disproved the possibility that the remains belonged to the Angkor royal family.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Nancy found the history of Angkor went back to as early as 1620. According to historic records, the remains of the Angkor royal family were much younger than that, so this evidence cast a lot of doubt as to the status of the ancient remains.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是南希证实了遗迹不可能属于吴哥皇室家族，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"remains\"和\"Angkor royal family\"定位到C段。\n解题思路：根据原文C段中的句子\"This evidence cast a lot of doubt as to the status of the ancient remains.\"可知，南希发现吴哥城的历史可追溯至1620年，但根据历史记载，吴哥皇室的遗迹远没有此古老。这一点说明这些遗迹应当不属于吴哥皇室。因此，题目的说法与原文一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60232","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the infromation given in the passage? In boxes1-7 on you answer sheet,write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8260:60233:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"university/University\n","acceptedAnswers":["university","University"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At the beginning, she would take any kind of job to pay her bills. Most of them were low-paying jobs or brief Community service opportunities. She worked often but didn’t know what path she would ultimately take. But eventually, her friend suggested that Athfield invest in getting a degree. The friend recommended that Athfield attend a nearby university.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求填写一个词来完成流程图，根据上下文推测这是关于Athfield的教育背景或职业发展路径。\n定位关键信息：根据流程图的上下文，结合段落中提到的\"Athfield\"和\"university\"可以定位到D段，该段描述了Athfield的教育经历。\n解题思路：在D段中提到，为了维持生计，她接下各种零工——多是低薪兼职或短期社区服务。虽然工作频繁，却始终没有明确的职业方向。后来朋友建议她攻读学位，推荐她报考附近大学，可见她最初是没有读大学的想法的，原文中的\"attend a nearby university\"直接对应了流程图中需要填写的。因此，答案为\"university\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"60233","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Question 8-13\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answer in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022w8dv4dRoHM1669988900.png]","maxWords":1},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8260:60234:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"rat/Rat","acceptedAnswers":["rat","Rat"],"explanation":"原文答案句：She earned her PhD in scientific research, and completed her studies on a kind of rat when it first appeared in New Zealand.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求在流程图中填入一个单词，描述Nancy Athfield在获得博士学位期间的研究对象。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"PhD\"和\"studies\"定位到E段，找到描述她博士研究内容的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到Nancy在获得博士学位期间研究的是一种\"rat\"（老鼠），这是她在新西兰进行的博士研究课题，与题目要求对应。因此答案为\"rat\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"60234","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Question 8-13\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answer in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022w8dv4dRoHM1669988900.png]","maxWords":1},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8260:60235:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"diet/Diet","acceptedAnswers":["diet","Diet"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Her research showed that the subject’s diet led to the fault in the earlier research.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求根据流程图完成填空，每个空格只能填写一个单词，需要从文章中找出与流程图步骤相关的具体词汇。\n定位关键信息：根据流程图的结构，需要找到与“发现早期研究中的缺陷”相关的信息。题目中的关键词\"fault in the earlier research\"可以帮助定位到E段，该段描述了Athfield在新西兰的研究，并指出了早期研究中的缺陷。\n解题思路：在E段中，原文明确提到\"Athfield completed her studies on a kind of rat when it first appeared in New Zealand.\"，随后指出\"Her research showed that the subject’s diet led to the fault in the earlier research.\"，即她的研究发现是“diet”饮食，导致了早期研究的缺陷。因此，填入“diet”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"60235","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Question 8-13\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answer in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022w8dv4dRoHM1669988900.png]","maxWords":1},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8260:60236:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"archaeologist/Archaeologist","acceptedAnswers":["archaeologist","Archaeologist"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Athfield eventually joined the field of Anthropology, the study of human societies, and became a well-qualified archaeologist.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求根据流程图完成填空，需要填写一个单词，且该单词来源于文章。\n定位关键信息：根据流程图的结构，需要找到与\"Archaeologist\"相关的句子。在F段中，明确提到了\"Athfield eventually joined the field of Anthropology... and became a well-qualified archaeologist.\"，这里的\"archaeologist\"就是题目要求填写的单词。\n解题思路：通过阅读F段，可以确定\"Athfield\"最终成为了一名\"archaeologist\"考古学家，接着2003年，前往柬埔寨进行研究。因此，根据题目要求，填写\"archaeologist\"作为答案。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"60236","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Question 8-13\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answer in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022w8dv4dRoHM1669988900.png]","maxWords":1},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8260:60237:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"funding/Funding","acceptedAnswers":["funding","Funding"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Her research was often delayed by lack of funding, and government paperwork.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求根据流程图完成填空，选择一个单词填入空格，且该单词来自文章。\n定位关键信息：根据流程图上下文或题目提示，定位到G段中关于研究遇到困难的部分。\n解题思路：G段提到，她的研究常因资金匮乏与繁琐的行政手续而进展迟缓。，因此“funding”是描述研究困难的关键词，符合填空要求。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"60237","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Question 8-13\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answer in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022w8dv4dRoHM1669988900.png]","maxWords":1},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8260:60238:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"database/Database","acceptedAnswers":["database","Database"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Using radiocarbon dating, Athfield completed a database for the materials found in Cambodia.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求完成流程图，需要根据文章内容填写一个单词，对应第13空。\n定位关键信息：根据流程图中的\"materials found in Cambodia\"定位到G段，找到描述对柬埔寨材料进行处理的句子。\n解题思路：在G段中，句子\"Using radiocarbon dating, Athfield completed a database for the materials found in Cambodia\"表明南希通过放射性碳测年法完成了柬埔寨出土材料数据库的汇编，因此\"database\"是完成流程图的正确答案。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"60238","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Question 8-13\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answer in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022w8dv4dRoHM1669988900.png]","maxWords":1}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"60226","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the infromation given in the passage? In boxes1-7 on you answer sheet,write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Nancy Athfield first discovered the ancient remains in Cambodia.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"60227","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the infromation given in the passage? In boxes1-7 on you answer sheet,write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>The remains found in the Cambodia was in good condition.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"60228","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the infromation given in the passage? In boxes1-7 on you answer sheet,write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Nancy took some time off from her regular work to do research in Cambodia.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"60229","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the infromation given in the passage? In boxes1-7 on you answer sheet,write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>The Cambodia government asked Nancy to radiocarbon the remains.</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"60230","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the infromation given in the passage? In boxes1-7 on you answer sheet,write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>The filmmakers aimed to find out how the Angkor was rebuilt.</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"60231","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the infromation given in the passage? In boxes1-7 on you answer sheet,write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Nancy initially doubted whether the royal family was hidden in Cambodia.</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"60232","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the infromation given in the passage? In boxes1-7 on you answer sheet,write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Nancy disproved the possibility that the remains belonged to the Angkor royal family.</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"60233","title":"填空题","instruction":"Question 8-13\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answer in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022w8dv4dRoHM1669988900.png]","html":"<p><strong>8</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"60234","title":"填空题","instruction":"Question 8-13\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answer in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022w8dv4dRoHM1669988900.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">9</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"60235","title":"填空题","instruction":"Question 8-13\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answer in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022w8dv4dRoHM1669988900.png]","html":"<p><strong>10</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"60236","title":"填空题","instruction":"Question 8-13\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answer in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022w8dv4dRoHM1669988900.png]","html":"<p><strong>11</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"60237","title":"填空题","instruction":"Question 8-13\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answer in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022w8dv4dRoHM1669988900.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">12</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"60238","title":"填空题","instruction":"Question 8-13\nComplete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answer in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022w8dv4dRoHM1669988900.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">13</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Radiocarbon Dating: The Profile of Nancy Athfield&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Have you ever picked up a small stone off the ground and wondered how old it was? Chances are, that stone has been around many more years than your own lifetime. Many scientists share this curiosity about the age of inanimate objects like rocks, fossils and precious stones. Knowing how old an object is can provide valuable information about our prehistoric past. In most societies, human beings have kept track of history through writing. However, scientists are still curious about the world before writing, or even the world before humans. Studying the age of objects is our best way to piece together histories of our pre-historic past. One such method of finding the age of an object is called radiocarbon dating. This method can find the age of any object based on the kind of particles and atoms that are found inside of the object. Depending on what elements the object is composed of, radiocarbon can be a reliable way to find an object’s age. One famous specialist in this method is the researcher Nancy Athfield. Athfield studied the ancient remains found in the country of Cambodia. Many prehistoric remains were discovered by the local people of Cambodia. These objects were thought to belong to some of the original groups of humans that first came to the country of Cambodia. The remains had never been scientifically studied, so Nancy was greatly intrigued by the opportunity to use modern methods to discover the true age of these ancient objects.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Athfield had this unique opportunity because her team, comprised of scientists and filmmakers, were in Cambodia working on a documentary. The team was trying to discover evidence to prove a controversial claim in history: that Cambodia was the resting place for the famous royal family of Angkor. At that time, written records and historic accounts conflicted on the true resting place. Many people across the world disagreed over where the final resting place was. For the first time, Athfield and her team had a chance to use radiocarbon dating to find new evidence. They had a chance to solve the historic mystery that many had been arguing over for years.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Athfield and her team conducted radiocarbon dating of many of the ancient objects found in the historic site of Angkor Wat. Nancy found the history of Angkor went back to as early as 1620. According to historic records, the remains of the Angkor royal family were much younger than that, so this evidence cast a lot of doubt as to the status of the ancient remains. The lesearch ultimately raised more questions. If the remains were not of the royal family, then whose remains were being kept in the ancient site? Athfield’s team left Cambodia with more questions unanswered. Since Athfield’s team studied the remains, new remains have been unearthed at the ancient site of Angkor Wat, so it is possible that these new remains could be the true remains of the royal family. Nancy wished to come back to continue her research one day.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In her early years, the career of Athfield was very unconventional. She didn’t start her career as a scientist. At the beginning, she would take any kind of job to pay her bills. Most of them were low-paying jobs or brief Community service opportunities. She worked often but didn’t know what path she would ultimately take. But eventually, her friend suggested that Athfield invest in getting a degree. The friend recommended that Athfield attend a nearby university. Though doubtful of her own qualifications, she applied and was eventually accepted by the school. It was there that she met Willard Libby, the inventor of radiocarbon dating. She took his class and soon had the opportunity to complete hands-on research. She soon realised that science was her passion. After graduation, she quickly found a job in a research institution.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>After college, Athfield’s career in science blossomed. She eventually married, and her husband landed a job at the prestigious organisation GNN. Athfield joined her husband in the same organisation, and she became a lab manager in the institution. She earned her PhD in scientific research, and completed her studies on a kind of rat when it first appeared in New Zealand. There, she created original research and found many flaws in the methods being used in New Zealand laboratories. Her research showed that the subject’s diet led to the fault in the earlier research. She was seen as an expert by her peers in New Zealand, and her opinion and expertise were widely respected. She had come a long way from her old days of working odd jobs. It seemed that Athfield’s career was finally taking off.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>But Athfield’s interest in scientific laboratories wasn’t her only interest. She didn’t settle down in New Zealand. Instead, she expanded her areas of expertise. Athfield eventually joined the field of Anthropology, the study of human societies, and became a well-qualified archaeologist. It was during her blossoming career as an archaeologist that Athfield became involved with the famous Cambodia project. Even as the filmmakers ran out of funding and left Cambodia, Athfield continued to stay and continue her research.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In 2003, the film was finished in uncertain conclusions, but Nancy continued her research on the ancient ruins of Angkor Wat. This research was not always easy. Her research was often delayed by lack of funding, and government paperwork. Despite her struggles, she committed to finishing her research. Finally, she made a breakthrough. Using radiocarbon dating, Athfield completed a database for the materials found in Cambodia. As a newcomer to Cambodia, she lacked a complete knowledge of Cambodian geology, which made this feat even more difficult. Through steady determination and ingenuity, Athfield finally completed the database. Though many did not believe she could finish, her research now remains an influential and tremendous contribution to geological sciences in Cambodia. In the future, radiocarbon dating continues to be a valuable research skill. Athfield will be remembered as one of the first to bring this scientific method to the study of the ancient ruins of Angkor Wat.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8260&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8715","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Father of Modern Management 2","book":"阅读还原集Vol.14","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.14 · Test 4 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8715:62914:14","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He wrote about 40 book and thousands of articles and he never rested in his mission to persuade the world that management matters. ‘Management is an organ of institutions … the organ that converts a mob into an organisation, and human efforts into performance.’ Did he succeed? The range of his influence was extraordinary. Wherever people grapple with tricky management problems, from big organizations to small ones, from the public sector to the private, and increasingly in the voluntary sector, you can find Drucker’s fingerprints.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求为A段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读A段，可以发现段落主要讨论的是德鲁克的作品及其影响力。\n解题思路：A段首句提到德鲁克写了大量书籍和文章，并致力于告诉人们管理的重要性。接着引用了他的名言。最后几句指出他的影响力范围非常广泛，无论是在大型还是小型组织，公共还是私营部门，还是在非盈利组织，都能看到德鲁克思想的烙印。因此，A段主要讨论的是德鲁克的作品及其影响力，与标题A相符。","options":["The popularity and impact of Drucker’s work","Finding fault with Drucker","The impact of economic globalisation","Government regulation of business","Early publications of Drucker’s","Drucker’s view of balanced management","Drucker’s rejection of big business","An appreciation of the pros and cons of Drucker’s work","The changing role of the employee"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"62914","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-F. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8715:62914:15","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：His first two books – The End of Economic Man (1939) and The Future of Industrial Man (1942) – had their admirers, including Winston Churchill, but they annoyed academic critics by ranging so widely over so many different subjects. Still, the second of these books attracted attention with its passionate insistence that companies had a social dimension as well as an economic purpose.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求为B段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读B段内容，可以发现段落主要介绍了Peter Drucker的前两本书及其影响，包括它们受到的关注和引发的争议。\n解题思路：根据B段的内容，可以确定该段主要围绕Drucker的前两本著作展开，并提到了这些书的影响和引发的争议。因此，选择与E项“Drucker早期作品”作为答案。","options":["The popularity and impact of Drucker’s work","Finding fault with Drucker","The impact of economic globalisation","Government regulation of business","Early publications of Drucker’s","Drucker’s view of balanced management","Drucker’s rejection of big business","An appreciation of the pros and cons of Drucker’s work","The changing role of the employee"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"62914","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-F. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8715:62914:16","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Yet Drucker also thought that this economy had implications for knowledge workers themselves. They had to come to terms with the fact that they were neither ‘bosses’ nor ‘workers’, but something in between: entrepreneurs who had responsibility for developing their most important resource, brainpower, and who also needed to take more control of their own careers, including their pension plans.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求为C段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读C段，可以定位到段落中反复出现的核心词汇，如\"empowering workers\"、\"knowledge workers\"、\"treating workers as resources\"等，这些词汇揭示了段落的主要内容。\n解题思路：C段主要讨论了Drucker在《The Concept of the Corporation》中的两个核心观点：一是关于\"empowering workers\"（赋能员工），二是关于\"knowledge workers\"（脑力工作者）的崛起及其对管理者和政治家的深远影响。段落详细阐述了Drucker如何认为员工应被视为资源而非成本，以及知识经济时代对企业和个人的新要求，他们必须认清自己既非“老板”也非“工人”，而是介于两者之间的特殊群体：既要肩负开发核心资源——脑力资本——的责任，又需要更多掌控自身职业发展，包括养老金规划。结合选项，只有选项I能够准确概括C段的内容。","options":["The popularity and impact of Drucker’s work","Finding fault with Drucker","The impact of economic globalisation","Government regulation of business","Early publications of Drucker’s","Drucker’s view of balanced management","Drucker’s rejection of big business","An appreciation of the pros and cons of Drucker’s work","The changing role of the employee"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"62914","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-F. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8715:62914:17","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For his critics, this was a retreat from his earlier emphasis on the soft side of management. For Drucker it was all perfectly consistent: if you rely too much on empowerment you risk anarchy, whereas if you rely too much on command-and-control you sacrifice creativity. The trick is for managers to set long-term goals, but then allow their employees to work out ways of achieving those goals.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求为D段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读D段内容，可以发现段落主要讲述了Drucker在管理领域的另一项重要贡献——\"management by objectives\"（目标管理），以及他在《The Practice of Management》一书中对管理目标设定的强调。\n解题思路：在D段中，他明确指出，管理的诀窍在于平衡：过度依赖赋权会导致混乱，过度依赖命令控制则会扼杀创造力；因此，管理者应设定长期目标，然后允许员工自行找出实现这些目标的方法。这完美地体现了“平衡管理”的思想。因此，选项F \"Drucker’s view of balanced management\" 准确地概括了本段的核心。","options":["The popularity and impact of Drucker’s work","Finding fault with Drucker","The impact of economic globalisation","Government regulation of business","Early publications of Drucker’s","Drucker’s view of balanced management","Drucker’s rejection of big business","An appreciation of the pros and cons of Drucker’s work","The changing role of the employee"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"62914","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-F. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8715:62914:18","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：There are three persistent criticisms of Drucker’s work.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求为E段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读E段，可以定位到段首句\"There are three persistent criticisms of Drucker’s work.\"以及后续内容详细列举了三个批评意见，包括对大型组织的关注、对目标管理的批评以及对其学术领域的评价。\n解题思路：E段的主要内容是围绕对Drucker工作的三个持久批评展开的，分别从不同角度分析了这些批评的具体内容。因此，选择标题B\"Finding fault with Drucker\"能够准确概括段落的核心内容。","options":["The popularity and impact of Drucker’s work","Finding fault with Drucker","The impact of economic globalisation","Government regulation of business","Early publications of Drucker’s","Drucker’s view of balanced management","Drucker’s rejection of big business","An appreciation of the pros and cons of Drucker’s work","The changing role of the employee"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"62914","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-F. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8715:62914:19","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph F","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：There is some truth in the first two arguments. Drucker never wrote anything as good as The Concept of the Corporation on entrepreneurial start-ups. Drucker’s work on management by objectives sits uneasily with his earlier and later writings on the importance of knowledge workers and self-directed teams. But the third argument is short-sighted and unfair because it ignores Drucker’s pioneering role in creating the modern profession of management. He produced one of the first systematic studies of a big company. He pioneered the idea that ideas can help galvanise companies.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求为F段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息： 通过阅读段落F，找出其讨论的核心主题。段落F的核心内容是对E段提出的批评进行评价，权衡德鲁克理论的优缺点。\n解题思路：段落首先承认前两个批评“有一定道理”，指出了其理论的局限性（缺点）。随后，段落笔锋一转，认为第三个批评是“短视且不公平的”，并阐述了德鲁克的先驱性贡献和深远影响力（优点），指出他是自身成功的受害者，因为他的许多思想已融入传统智慧。这种既承认缺点又肯定优点的结构，正是对德鲁克工作“利弊”（pros and cons）的欣赏与评价。因此，选项H \"An appreciation of the pros and cons of Drucker’s work\" 准确地概括了本段的核心。","options":["The popularity and impact of Drucker’s work","Finding fault with Drucker","The impact of economic globalisation","Government regulation of business","Early publications of Drucker’s","Drucker’s view of balanced management","Drucker’s rejection of big business","An appreciation of the pros and cons of Drucker’s work","The changing role of the employee"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"62914","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-F. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8715:62915:20","type":"choice","text":"Drucker believed the employees should enjoy the same status as the employers in a company.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He was a harsh critic of the assembly-line system of production that then dominated the manufacturing sector – partly because assembly lines moved at the speed of the slowest and partly because they failed to engage the creativity of individual workers. He insisted that this had profound implications for both managers and politicians. Managers had to stop treating workers like cogs in a huge inhuman machine and start treating them as brain workers.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问“Drucker认为员工应该享有与雇主相同的地位”，即询问Drucker是否认为员工和雇主在地位上平等。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"employees\"、\"employers\"、\"same status\"定位到C段，该段提到Drucker对员工角色的看法。\n解题思路：原文提到Drucker主张\"treating workers as brain workers\"（将员工视为脑力工作者），并批评将员工视为\"costs\"（成本）或\"human efforts\"（人力）的做法。虽然Drucker强调员工应被重视，但原文并未明确说明员工应享有与雇主相同的地位（same status），而是强调员工应被视为有创造力的\"brain workers\"。因此，题目中的\"same status\"这一具体表述在原文中并未提及，无法直接得出Drucker持相同地位的观点。故答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62915","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8715:62916:21","type":"choice","text":"Drucker argued the managers and politicians will dominate the economy during a social transition.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He argued that the world is moving from an ‘economy of goods’ to an economy of ‘knowledge’ – and from a society dominated by an industrial proletariat to one dominated by brain workers. He insisted that this had profound implications for both managers and politicians. Managers had to stop treating workers like cogs in a huge inhuman machine and start treating them as brain workers. In turn, politicians had to realise that knowledge, and hence education, was the single most important resource for any advanced society.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是Drucker是否认为在社会转型期，政客和管理者将会主导经济\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"managers and politicians\"、\"dominate the economy\"和\"social transition\"来定位原文信息。\n解题思路：原文中提到Drucker认为世界正在从“物质经济”转向“知识经济”，从由产业无产阶级主导的社会转向由脑力劳动者主导的社会。他强调这一转变对经理人和政治家有深远影响，经理人和政治家需要认识到知识是任何先进社会最重要的资源。然而，原文并未明确指出经理人和政治家将主导经济，而是强调他们需要适应这一转变并认识到知识的重要性。因此，题目中的说法在原文中没有明确支持，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62916","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8715:62917:22","type":"choice","text":"Drucker support that workers are not simply put themselves just in the employment relationship and should develop their resources of intelligence voluntarily.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：They had to come to terms with the fact that they were neither ‘bosses’ nor ‘workers’, but something in between: entrepreneurs who had responsibility for developing their most important resource, brainpower, and who also needed to take more control of their own careers, including their pension plans.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是Drucker是否支持员工不应仅仅把自己视为雇佣关系中的一员，而应主动进行学习。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"workers\"、\"resources of intelligence\"和\"voluntarily\"定位到C段中关于Drucker对知识工人看法的描述。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到Drucker认为知识工人既不是老板也不是普通工人，而是处于两者之间的一个角色，他们应该发展自己最重要的资源——脑力，需要更加关注发展自己的职业生涯。这与题目中的表述完全一致，因此答案是YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62917","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8715:62918:23","type":"choice","text":"Drucker’s work on the management is out of date in modern days.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Moreover, Drucker continued to produce new ideas up until his 90s. His work on the management of voluntary organisations remained at the cutting edge.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是作者是否认为\"Drucker关于管理的著作在现代社会已经过时了\"。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Drucker’s work on the management\"和\"out of date in modern days\"定位到F段，段落F的核心内容是对E段提出的批评进行评价，权衡德鲁克理论的优缺点。\n解题思路：根据F段中的原文说德鲁克90岁的时候，在志愿管理学理论的思想仍然是首屈一指的。 可见他的著作并没有过时。答案应为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62918","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8715:62919:24-25","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following are true of Drucker’s views?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In one of his most substantial works, The Practice of Management (1954), he emphasised the importance of managers and corporations setting clear long-term objectives and then translating those long-term objectives into more immediate goals. He argued that firms should have an elite corps of general managers, who set these long-term objectives, and then a group of more specialised managers. For his critics, this was a retreat from his earlier emphasis on the soft side of management. For Drucker it was all perfectly consistent: if you rely too much on empowerment you risk anarchy, whereas if you rely too much on command-and-control you sacrifice creativity. The trick is for managers to set long-term goals, but then allow their employees to work out ways of achieving those goals.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是关于德鲁克观点的哪两项陈述是正确的。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Drucker’s views\"定位到文章中关于德鲁克观点的描述。\n解题思路：  D段中，他认为，过度依赖任何一种单一方式都是有害的。管理者负责设定长期目标（这确立了高层管理者的战略角色），然后允许员工自主决定实现这些目标的具体方式（这赋予了员工实践的自主权和创造性）。这种模式清晰地定义了高层管理者与员工在管理实践中的平衡位置和不同职责，与选项A的描述高度吻合。他强调管理者和公司必须设定清晰的“长期目标”，并主张公司应有专业的管理者。这清楚地表明，德鲁克认为领导者的核心职责是进行战略思考、规划长远未来，即“战略性地建立目标”，而不是沉溺于日常的管理细节。这与选项E的描述完全一致。","options":["High-rank executives and workers should be put in balanced positions in management practice.","Young executives should be given chances to start from low-level jobs.","More emphasis should be laid on fostering the development of the union.","Management should facilitate workers with tools of self-appraisal instead of controlling them from the outside force.","Leaders should go beyond the scope of management details and strategically establish goals."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"62919","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 24-25\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"62919-8715:62919:24-25"},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8715:62919:24-25","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following are true of Drucker’s views?","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In one of his most substantial works, The Practice of Management (1954), he emphasised the importance of managers and corporations setting clear long-term objectives and then translating those long-term objectives into more immediate goals. He argued that firms should have an elite corps of general managers, who set these long-term objectives, and then a group of more specialised managers. For his critics, this was a retreat from his earlier emphasis on the soft side of management. For Drucker it was all perfectly consistent: if you rely too much on empowerment you risk anarchy, whereas if you rely too much on command-and-control you sacrifice creativity. The trick is for managers to set long-term goals, but then allow their employees to work out ways of achieving those goals.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是关于德鲁克观点的哪两项陈述是正确的。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Drucker’s views\"定位到文章中关于德鲁克观点的描述。\n解题思路：  D段中，他认为，过度依赖任何一种单一方式都是有害的。管理者负责设定长期目标（这确立了高层管理者的战略角色），然后允许员工自主决定实现这些目标的具体方式（这赋予了员工实践的自主权和创造性）。这种模式清晰地定义了高层管理者与员工在管理实践中的平衡位置和不同职责，与选项A的描述高度吻合。他强调管理者和公司必须设定清晰的“长期目标”，并主张公司应有专业的管理者。这清楚地表明，德鲁克认为领导者的核心职责是进行战略思考、规划长远未来，即“战略性地建立目标”，而不是沉溺于日常的管理细节。这与选项E的描述完全一致。","options":["High-rank executives and workers should be put in balanced positions in management practice.","Young executives should be given chances to start from low-level jobs.","More emphasis should be laid on fostering the development of the union.","Management should facilitate workers with tools of self-appraisal instead of controlling them from the outside force.","Leaders should go beyond the scope of management details and strategically establish goals."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"62919","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 24-25\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"62919-8715:62919:24-25"},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8715:62920:26-27","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following are mentioned in the passage as criticisms to Drucker and his views?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The first is that he focused on big organisations rather than small ones. The Concept of the Corporation was in many ways a fanfare to big organisations. As Drucker said, ‘We know today that in modern industrial production, particularly in modern mass production, the small unit is not only inefficient, it cannot produce at all.’ The second criticism is that Drucker’s enthusiasm for management by objectives helped to lead the business down a dead end. They prefer to allow ideas, including ideas for long-term strategies, to bubble up from the bottom and middle of the organisations rather than being imposed from on high.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是下列哪两项在文中被提及为对德鲁克及其观点的批判。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"criticisms to Drucker and his views\"定位到E段，该段明确列出了三个对德鲁克及其观点的批评。\n解题思路：根据E段的内容，首先，批评者认为德鲁克过于关注大组织而忽视了小组织，这与选项A的描述一致。第二，德鲁克对目标管理的热情导致企业走向死胡同，这与选项C的描述一致。因此，选项A和C符合题目要求。","options":["His lectures focus too much on big organisations and ignore the small ones.","His lectures are too broad and lack of being precise and accurate about the facts.","He put a source of objectives more on corporate executives but not on average workers.","He acted much like a maverick and did not set up his own management groups.","He was overstating the case for knowledge workers when warning business to get prepared."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"62920","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 26-27\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"62920-8715:62920:26-27"},{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8715:62920:26-27","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following are mentioned in the passage as criticisms to Drucker and his views?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The first is that he focused on big organisations rather than small ones. The Concept of the Corporation was in many ways a fanfare to big organisations. As Drucker said, ‘We know today that in modern industrial production, particularly in modern mass production, the small unit is not only inefficient, it cannot produce at all.’ The second criticism is that Drucker’s enthusiasm for management by objectives helped to lead the business down a dead end. They prefer to allow ideas, including ideas for long-term strategies, to bubble up from the bottom and middle of the organisations rather than being imposed from on high.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是下列哪两项在文中被提及为对德鲁克及其观点的批判。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"criticisms to Drucker and his views\"定位到E段，该段明确列出了三个对德鲁克及其观点的批评。\n解题思路：根据E段的内容，首先，批评者认为德鲁克过于关注大组织而忽视了小组织，这与选项A的描述一致。第二，德鲁克对目标管理的热情导致企业走向死胡同，这与选项C的描述一致。因此，选项A和C符合题目要求。","options":["His lectures focus too much on big organisations and ignore the small ones.","His lectures are too broad and lack of being precise and accurate about the facts.","He put a source of objectives more on corporate executives but not on average workers.","He acted much like a maverick and did not set up his own management groups.","He was overstating the case for knowledge workers when warning business to get prepared."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"62920","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 26-27\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"62920-8715:62920:26-27"}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"62919-8715:62919:24-25","numbers":[24,25],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["A","E"]},{"id":"62920-8715:62920:26-27","numbers":[26,27],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["A","C"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"62914","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-F. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"62915","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Drucker believed the employees should enjoy the same status as the employers in a company.</strong></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"62916","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Drucker argued the managers and politicians will dominate the economy during a social transition.</strong></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"62917","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Drucker support that workers are not simply put themselves just in the employment relationship and should develop their resources of intelligence voluntarily.</strong></p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"62918","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Drucker’s work on<span style=\"text-decoration: none;\"></span> the management is out of date in modern days.</strong></p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"62919","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 24-25\nChoose TWO correct answers","html":"<p><strong>Which TWO of the following are true of Drucker’s views?</strong></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"62920","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 26-27\nChoose TWO correct answers","html":"<p><strong>Which TWO of the following are mentioned in the passage as criticisms to Drucker and his views?</strong></p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Father of Modern Management 2</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>#&amp;A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Peter Drucker was one of the most important management thinkers of the past hundred years. He wrote about 40 book and thousands of articles and he never rested in his mission to persuade the world that management matters. ‘Management is an organ of institutions … the organ that converts a mob into an organisation, and human efforts into performance.’ Did he succeed? The range of his influence was extraordinary. Wherever people grapple with tricky management problems, from big organizations to small ones, from the public sector to the private, and increasingly in the voluntary sector, you can find Drucker’s fingerprints.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>His first two books – The End of Economic Man (1939) and The Future of Industrial Man (1942) – had their admirers, including Winston Churchill, but they annoyed academic critics by ranging so widely over so many different subjects. Still, the second of these books attracted attention with its passionate insistence that companies had a social dimension as well as an economic purpose. His third book, The Concept of the Corporation, became an instant bestseller and has remained in print ever since.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The two most interesting arguments in The Concept of the Corporation actually had little to do with the decentralization fad. They were to dominate his work. The first had to do with ‘empowering’ workers. Drucker believed in treating workers as resources rather than just as costs. He was a harsh critic of the assembly-line system of production that then dominated the manufacturing sector – partly because assembly lines moved at the speed of the slowest and partly because they failed to engage the creativity of individual workers. The second argument had to do with the rise of knowledge workers. Drucker argued that the world is moving from an ‘economy of goods’ to an economy of ‘knowledge’ – and from a society dominated by an industrial proletariat to one dominated by brain workers. He insisted that this had profound implications for both managers and politicians. Managers had to stop treating workers like cogs in a huge inhuman machine and start treating them as brain workers. In turn, politicians had to realise that knowledge, and hence education, was the single most important resource for any advanced society. Yet Drucker also thought that this economy had implications for knowledge workers themselves. They had to come to terms with the fact that they were neither ‘bosses’ nor ‘workers’, but something in between: entrepreneurs who had responsibility for developing their most important resource, brainpower, and who also needed to take more control of their own careers, including their pension plans.&amp;#</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>#&amp;D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>However, there was also a hard side to his work. Drucker was responsible for inventing one of the rational school of management’s most successful products – ‘management by objectives’. In one of his most substantial works, The Practice of Management (1954), he emphasised the importance of managers and corporations setting clear long-term objectives and then translating those long-term objectives into more immediate goals. He argued that firms should have an elite corps of general managers, who set these long-term objectives, and then a group of more specialised managers. For his critics, this was a retreat from his earlier emphasis on the soft side of management. For Drucker it was all perfectly consistent: if you rely too much on empowerment you risk anarchy, whereas if you rely too much on command-and-control you sacrifice creativity. The trick is for managers to set long-term goals, but then allow their employees to work out ways of achieving those goals. If Drucker helped make management a global industry, he also helped push it beyond its business base. He was emphatically a management thinker, not just a business one. He believed that management is ‘the defining organ of all modern institutions’, not just corporations.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>There are three persistent criticisms of Drucker’s work. The first is that he focused on big organisations rather than small ones. The Concept of the Corporation was in many ways a fanfare to big organisations. As Drucker said, ‘We know today that in modern industrial production, particularly in modern mass production, the small unit is not only inefficient, it cannot produce at all.’ The book helped to launch the ‘big organisation boom’ that dominated business thinking for the next 20 years. The second criticism is that Drucker’s enthusiasm for management by objectives helped to lead the business down a dead end. They prefer to allow ideas, including ideas for long-term strategies, to bubble up from the bottom and middle of the organisations rather than being imposed from on high. Thirdly, Drucker is criticised for being a maverick who has increasingly been left behind by the increasing rigour of his chosen field. There is no single area of academic management theory that he made his own.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>There is some truth in the first two arguments. Drucker never wrote anything as good as The Concept of the Corporation on entrepreneurial start-ups. Drucker’s work on management by objectives sits uneasily with his earlier and later writings on the importance of knowledge workers and self-directed teams. But the third argument is short-sighted and unfair because it ignores Drucker’s pioneering role in creating the modern profession of management. He produced one of the first systematic studies of a big company. He pioneered the idea that ideas can help galvanise companies. The biggest problem with evaluating Drucker’s influence is<br/>that so many of his ideas have passed into conventional wisdom. In other words, he is the victim of his own success. His writings on the importance of knowledge workers and empowerment may sound a little banal today. But they certainly weren’t banal when he first dreamed them up in the 1940s, or when they were first put in to practice in the Anglo-Saxon world in the 1980s. Moreover, Drucker continued to produce new ideas up until his 90s. His work on the management of voluntary organisations remained at the cutting edge.&amp;#</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8715&scene=%E8%B4%A2%E7%BB%8F%E5%95%86%E4%B8%9A&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8716","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 The Concept Of Childhood In The Western Countries","book":"阅读还原集Vol.14","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.14 · Test 4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8716:62921:28","type":"choice","text":"Aries pointed out that children did different types of works as adults during the Middle Age.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He scrutinized medieval pictures and diaries and found no distinction between children and adults as they shared similar leisure activities and often the same type of work.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问Ariès指出中世纪儿童和成人从事不同类型的工作，这一说法十分正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"children did different types of works as adults during the Middle Age\"（中世纪儿童和成人从事不同类型的工作）定位到A段中关于Ariès对中世纪儿童和成人工作的描述。\n解题思路：根据原文，他通过研究中世纪的绘画与日记发现，儿童与成人共享相似的休闲活动，且常从事相同类型的工作，两者之间并无本质区别。可以确定Ariès认为中世纪儿童和成人从事相同类型的工作，而非不同类型的工作。因此，题目中的说法与原文相反，答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62921","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet. TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8716:62922:29","type":"choice","text":"During the Middle Age, going to work necessarily means children were unloved indicated Aries.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Ariès, however, pointed out that this is not to suggest that children were neglected, forsaken or despised.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“Ariès指出，在中世纪，去工作意味着孩子不受喜爱”，要求判断这个说法是否与作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“Middle Age”、“going to work”、“children were unloved”和“indicated Aries”可以定位到A段中关于Aries对中世纪儿童工作情况的论述。\n解题思路：原文中A段提到Ariès指出，在中世纪，儿童被视为小大人，他们参与工作并不意味着被忽视、遗弃或鄙视。这与题目中的说法是相反的，因此题目中的说法与作者的观点不符。所以，答案是False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62922","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet. TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8716:62923:30","type":"choice","text":"Scientists think that overworked labour damages the health of young children.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Social reformers began to question whether labouring long hours from an early age would harm children’s growing bodies. They began to recognize the potential of carrying out systematic studies to monitor how far these early deprivations might be affecting children’s development.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问“科学家认为过度劳动的劳动会损害儿童的健康”是否与作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“Scientists think that overworked labour damages the health of young children”，需要找到文章中关于科学家或社会改革者对儿童劳动影响的看法。\n解题思路：原文C段提到，社会改革者开始质疑，从幼年时期就开始长时间劳动是否会对儿童发育中的身体造成伤害。他们逐渐意识到，通过系统研究来监测这些早期剥夺对儿童发展的影响程度，具有重要价值。表明他们认为过多劳动会有害儿童健康，因此答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62923","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet. TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8716:62924:31","type":"choice","text":"The rise of trade union majorly contributed to the protection of children from exploitation in the 19th century.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The worst forms of child exploitation were gradually eliminated, partly through factory reform but also through the influence of trade unions and economic changes during the nineteenth century which made some forms of child labour redundant.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问“工会的兴起在19世纪为保护儿童免遭剥削做出了重大贡献”，需要判断这一说法是否与原文作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词“trade union”（工会）、“protection of children”（保护儿童）、“exploitation”（剥削）和“19th century”（19世纪）可以定位到D段。\n解题思路：D段提到，最恶劣的剥削儿童形式逐步被消除，部分是通过工厂改革，但也是通过工会的影响和19世纪的经济变化，使一些形式的童工变得多余。说明工会确实在19世纪对减少童工劳动起到了作用，但原文并未明确指出工会是“主要贡献”者。因此，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62924","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet. TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8716:62925:32","type":"choice","text":"By the aid of half-time schools, most children went to school in the mid of 19 century.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The Factory Act of 1833 established half-time schools which allowed children to work and attend school. But in the 1840s, a large proportion of children never went to school, and if they did, they left by the age of 10 or 11.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“19世纪中期，在半日制学校的帮助下，绝大多数孩子都上了学”，需要判断这一说法是否与原文作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“half-time schools”（半日制学校）、“most children”（大多数孩子）、“mid of 19 century”（19世纪中期）。根据这些关键词，在文章中定位到E段，该段提到了半日制学校和19世纪中期的情况。\n解题思路：E段提到，1833年的《工厂法》设立了半工半读的学校，允许孩子们一边工作一边上学。但在19世纪40年代，很大一部分孩子从未上过学，即使上过学，也往往在10岁或11岁之前就辍学了。这与题目中“大多数孩子都去上学”的说法相反，因此题目的说法与文章内容不符，应该选择False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62925","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet. TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8716:62926:33","type":"choice","text":"In 20 century almost all children need to go to school in a full-time schedule.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The situation was very different by the end of the nineteenth century in Britain. The school became central to images of ‘a normal’ childhood.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“在20世纪，几乎所有儿童都需要参加全日制教育”，需要判断这一说法是否与原文作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：利用“20th century”和“full-time schedule”这两个关键词在文章中定位，定位到D段和E段，主要讲述改革和学校在18、19世纪起到的作用。\n解题思路：原文提到，到了十九世纪末，英国的情况已大不相同。学校成为塑造“正常”童年形象的核心。但没有提到20世纪的情况，更没有具体说明儿童都必须参加全日制教育。因此，题目中的信息在文章中没有明确给出，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62926","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet. TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8716:62927:34","type":"choice","text":"Nowadays, children's needs were much differentiated and categorised based on how old they are.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Increasingly, children were being treated as a group with distinctive needs and they were organized into groups according to their age.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“如今，儿童的需求根据他们的年龄被区分得更加细致，并归入不同的类别”，需要判断这一说法是否与原文作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“differentiated”（差异化）和“categorised based on how old they are”（按年龄分类）在文章中定位。原文中G段提到“children were organized into groups according to their age”，与题目中的“categorised based on how old they are”完全对应。\n解题思路：原文明确指出孩子们被根据年龄分组（organized into groups according to their age），且强调了他们有“distinctive needs”（独特的需求），这与题目中的“much differentiated”和“categorised based on how old they are”完全一致。因此，题目描述与原文一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"62927","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet. TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8716:62928:35","type":"fill","text":"填写第 35 空","answer":"history of childhood","acceptedAnswers":["history of childhood"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The history of childhood has been a topic of interest in social history since the highly influential 1960 book Centuries of Childhood, written by French historian Philippe Ariès. He argued that ‘childhood’ is a concept created by modern society.\n对应段落：A段上方\n审题：题目问的是法国历史学家菲利普·阿列斯的理论引发了关于什么的的争议。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“French historian Philippe Ariès”和“concept”，通过这些关键词可以定位到A段上方，提到阿列斯的观点。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子，自1960年法国历史学家菲利普·阿里埃斯（Philippe Aries）出版极具影响力的著作《童年的世纪》以来，童年历史一直是社会史研究的重要课题。他主张‘童年’是一个由现代社会创造的概念，可以推断出阿里耶斯的观点引发了关于“童年历史”的争议。因此，答案为“history of childhood”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62928","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8716:62929:36","type":"fill","text":"填写第 36 空","answer":"miniature adults","acceptedAnswers":["miniature adults"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The historian Philippe Aries argued that in Western Europe during the Middle Ages (up to about the end of the fifteenth century) children were regarded as miniature adults, with all the intellect and personality that this implies.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问阿瑞斯认为在中世纪西欧，儿童是什么样的形象。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"Aries\"和\"Western Europe during the Middle Ages\"定位到A段，找到阿瑞斯的观点。\n解题思路：原文明确提到阿瑞斯认为在中世纪西欧，儿童被视为\"miniature adults\"，即\"小大人\"，拥有与成年人相当的智力与个性。。因此答案为\"miniature adults\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62929","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8716:62930:37","type":"fill","text":"填写第 37 空","answer":"industrialisation/industrialization","acceptedAnswers":["industrialisation","industrialization"],"explanation":"原文答案句：With industrialization in the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries, a new demand for child labour was created, and many children were forced to work for long hours, in mines, workshops and factories.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“18世纪和19世纪促使大量儿童长时间工作的历史事件是什么？”\n定位关键信息：题目中的时间范围“18 and 19 century”和核心内容“great amount child labour”以及“work a long time”是定位的关键。在文章中，C段明确提到了“eighteenth and nineteenth centuries”和“long hours”的描述。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，随着十八、十九世纪的工业化，对童工的新需求产生了，许多儿童被迫在矿山、车间和工厂长时间工作。为儿童劳动创造了新的需求，并导致儿童长时间工作，完全符合题目的要求，可以确定答案为“industrialisation”或“industrialization”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62930","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8716:62931:38","type":"fill","text":"填写第 38 空","answer":"the Factory Act","acceptedAnswers":["the Factory Act"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In Britain, the Factory Act of 1833 signified the beginning of legal protection of children from exploitation and was linked to the rise of schools for factory children.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是在19世纪，哪项法律制度开创性地保障了儿童免受剥削。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"protection of children from exploitation\"和\"19th century\"在文章中定位。在D段中找到包含这些信息的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子\"In Britain, the Factory Act of 1833 signified the beginning of legal protection of children from exploitation...\"，可以确定\"The Factory Act\"《工厂法》19世纪的颁布，开始保护儿童免受剥削。原文明确提到该法案标志着对儿童剥削的法律保护的开始，因此答案为\"the Factory Act\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62931","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8716:62932:39","type":"fill","text":"填写第 39 空","answer":"play and education","acceptedAnswers":["play and education"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Childhood was increasingly seen as a time for play and education for all children, not just for a privileged minority.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是在19世纪，哪些活动被越来越多地认为更适合大部分儿童。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"19th century\"（19世纪）、\"activities\"（活动）、\"preferable\"（更适合）和\"children\"（儿童）等关键词，在文章中定位相关句子。\n解题思路：根据原文D段中的句子\"Childhood was increasingly seen as a time for play and education for all children, not just for a privileged minority\"，可以确定在19世纪，人们越来越认为，童年是所有儿童玩耍和受教育的时期，而不是少数儿童的特权。因此，答案为\"play and education\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62932","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8716:62933:40","type":"fill","text":"填写第 40 空","answer":"classroom","acceptedAnswers":["classroom"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Attending school was no longer a privilege and all children were expected to spend a significant part of their day in a classroom.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问在现代社会中，人们期望孩子们主要在何处度过他们一天的大部分时间。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"central area\"和\"largely of their day\"可以定位到E段中\"the school became central\"和F段中\"all children were expected to spend a significant part of their day in a classroom\"。\n解题思路：F段提到，上学不再是特权，人们希望所有孩子都在教室里度过一天的大部分时间。因此，\"classroom\"是孩子们在现代社会中度过大部分时间的中心场所。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"62933","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"62921","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet. TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Aries pointed out that children did different types of works as adults during the Middle Age.</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"62922","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet. TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>During the Middle Age, going to work necessarily means children were unloved indicated Aries.</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"62923","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet. TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Scientists think that overworked labour damages the health of young children.</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"62924","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet. TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The rise of trade union majorly contributed to the protection of children from exploitation in the 19th century.</strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"62925","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet. TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>By the aid of half-time schools, most children went to school in the mid of 19 century.</strong></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"62926","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet. TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>In 20 century almost all children need to go to school in a full-time schedule.</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"62927","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 28-34\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? Write your answers in boxes 28-34 on your answer sheet. TURE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Nowadays, children&#39;s needs were much differentiated and categorised based on how old they are.</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"62928","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>35</strong> What is the controversial topic arises with the French historian Philippe Ariès’s concept? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[35] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"62929","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>36</strong> What image for children did Aries believed to be like in Western Europe during the Middle Ages?<strong class=\"source-blank\">[36] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"62930","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>37</strong> What historical event generated the need for great amount child labour to work a long time in 18 and 19 century?<strong class=\"source-blank\">[37] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"62931","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>38 </strong>What legal format initiated the protection of children from exploitation in 19th centenary?<strong class=\"source-blank\">[38] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"62932","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>39</strong> What the activities were more and more regarded as being preferable for almost all children time in 19th centenary?<strong class=\"source-blank\">[39] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"62933","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>40</strong> Where has been the central area for children to spend largely of their day as people’s expectation in modern society?<strong class=\"source-blank\">[40] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The Concept Of Childhood&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">In The Western Countries&nbsp;</span></strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The history of childhood has been a topic of interest in social history since the highly influential 1960 book Centuries of Childhood, written by French historian Philippe Ariès. He argued that ‘childhood’ is a concept created by modern society.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>One of the most hotly debated issues in the history of childhood has been whether childhood is itself a recent invention. The historian Philippe Aries argued that in Western Europe during the Middle Ages (up to about the end of the fifteenth century) children were regarded as miniature adults, with all the intellect and personality that this implies. He scrutinized medieval pictures and diaries and found no distinction between children and adults as they shared similar leisure activities and often the same type of work. Aries, however, pointed out that this is not to suggest that children were neglected, forsaken or despised. The idea of childhood is not to be confused with affection for children; it corresponds to an awareness of the particular nature of childhood, that particular nature which distinguishes the child from the adult, even the young adult.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>There is a long tradition of the children of the poor playing a functional role in contributing to the family income by working either inside or outside the home. In this sense, children are seen as ‘useful’. Back in the Middle Ages, children as young as 5 or 6 did important chores for their parents and, from the sixteenth century, were often encouraged (or forced) to leave the family by the age of 9 or 10 to work as servants for wealthier families or to be apprenticed to a trade.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>With industrialization in the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries, a new demand for child labour was created, and many children were forced to work for long hours, in mines, workshops and factories. Social reformers began to question whether labouring long hours from an early age would harm children’s growing bodies. They began to recognize the potential of carrying out systematic studies to monitor how far these early deprivations might be affecting children’s development.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Gradually, the concerns of the reformers began to impact on the working conditions of children. In Britain, the Factory Act of 1833 signified the beginning of legal protection of children from exploitation and was linked to the rise of schools for factory children. The worst forms of child exploitation were gradually eliminated, partly through factory reform but also through the influence of trade unions and economic changes during the nineteenth century which made some forms of child labour redundant. Childhood was increasingly seen as a time for play and education for all children, not just for a privileged minority. As the age for starting full-time work was delayed, so childhood was increasingly understood as a more extended phase of dependency, development and learning. Even so, work continued to play a significant, if the less central role in children’s lives throughout the later nineteenth and twentieth century. And the ‘useful child’ has become a controversial image during the first decade of the twenty-first century especially in the context of global concern about large numbers of the world’s children engaged in child labour.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The Factory Act of 1833 established half-time schools which allowed children to work and attend school. But in the 1840s, a large proportion of children never went to school, and if they did, they left by the age of 10 or 11. The situation was very different by the end of the nineteenth century in Britain. The school became central to images of ‘a normal’ childhood.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Attending school was no longer a privilege and all children were expected to spend a significant part of their day in a classroom. By going to school, children’s lives were now separated from domestic life at home and from the adult world of work. The school became an institution dedicated to shaping the minds, behavior and morals of the young. Education dominated the management of children’s waking hours, not just through the hours spent in classrooms but through ‘home’ work, the growth of ‘after school’ activities and the importance attached to ‘parental involvement.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Industrialization, urbanization and mass schooling also set new challenges for those responsible for protecting children’s welfare and promoting their learning. Increasingly, children were being treated as a group with distinctive needs and they were organized into groups according to their age. For example, teachers needed to know what to expect of children in their classrooms, what kinds of instruction were appropriate for different age groups and how best to assess children’s progress. They also wanted tools that could enable them to sort and select children according to their abilities and potential.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8716&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8248","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Koalas","book":"阅读还原集Vol.14","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.14 · Test 3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8248:60194:1","type":"choice","text":"The main reason why koala declined is that they are killed except for","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The koala’s only food source, the eucalyptus tree, has declined. In the past 200 years, a third of Australia’s eucalyptus forests have disappeared. Koalas have been killed by parasites, chlamydia epidemics and a tumour-causing retro-virus. Koalas have been killed by parasites, chlamydia epidemics and a tumour-causing retro-virus. And every year 11,000 are killed by cars, ironically most of them in wildlife sanctuaries, and thousands are killed by poachers.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是考拉数量减少的主要原因，除了被杀死之外还有什么原因。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"declined\"和\"killed\"定位到C段，该段列举了考拉被杀的各种原因。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到考拉被寄生虫、衣原体、逆转录病毒等多种原因杀死，每年还有大量被车撞死和被偷猎者杀死，还因为桉树数量锐减，食物来源减少。题目问的是除了被杀死之外的原因，而C选项说的是考拉繁殖过多但存活率低矛盾。因此，正确答案应为C。","options":["by poachers.","by diseases they got","giving too many birth yet survived little.","accidents on the road."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60194","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions1-5\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8248:60195:2","type":"choice","text":"What can help koalas fully digest their food?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：To handle this cocktail, koalas have a specialised digestive system. Cellulose- digesting bacteria in the break down fibre, while a specially adapted gut and liver process the toxins. To digest their food properly, koalas must sit still for 21 hours every day.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问什么可以帮助考拉完全消化食物。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"digest their food\"（消化食物）定位到F段。\n解题思路：原文提到考拉为了正确消化食物，每天必须静止21小时，这与选项C\"保持一段时间不动以消化\"完全一致。而B选项的器官，仅仅是帮助分解纤维，并不能完全的、恰当的消化食物。选项A、D分别描述了树叶中的有毒物质、吃桉树，这些都不是直接帮助消化食物的方式，因此不符合题意。","options":["toxic substance in the leaves","organs that dissolve the fibres","remaining inactive for a period to digest","eating eucalyptus trees"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60195","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions1-5\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8248:60196:3","type":"choice","text":"What would koalas do when facing the dangerous situation?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：If you upset a koala, it may blink or swallow, or hiccup. But attack? No way! Koalas are just not aggressive. They use their claws to grip the hard smooth bark of eucalyptus trees.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是考拉在面对危险情况时会做什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"dangerous situation\"定位到G段中描述考拉反应的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，即使考拉有能力用尖锐的爪子伤害人类（\"capable of ripping open a man’s arm with their needle-sharp claws\"），但它们从不攻击（\"But attack? No way! Koalas are just not aggressive\"），而是表现出眨眼、吞咽或打嗝等轻微反应（\"it may blink or swallow, or hiccup\"）。因此，考拉在危险情况下会表现出受冒犯的迹象，对应选项A。其他选项B、C、D均与原文描述相反或无关。","options":["To show signs of being offended","To counter attack furiously","To use sharp claws to rip the man","To use claws to grip the bark of trees"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60196","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions1-5\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8248:60197:4","type":"choice","text":"In what ways Australian zoos exploit koalas?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Koala cuddling screams in the face of every rule of good care. First, some zoos allow koalas to be passed from stranger to stranger, many children who love to squeeze. Secondly, most people have no idea of how to handle the animals; they like to cling on to their handler, all in their own good time and use his or her arm as a tree.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问澳大利亚的动物园以哪种方式利用考拉。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"Australian zoos exploit koalas\"定位到I段，该段提到动物园利用考拉的温顺性格收费让游客拥抱考拉拍照。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，拥抱考拉的行为完全违背了动物保护的基本准则。任何列举出原因，首先，部分动物园允许考拉在饲养员之间传递，许多孩子都爱抱着考拉撒欢。其次，多数人根本不懂如何正确接触考拉，它们会紧紧依附饲养员，各自为政地用前臂当抓握点。动物园正是利用考拉与游客互动，与选项B\"允许游客拥抱考拉\"完全一致。其他选项A、C、D在原文中均未提及，因此B为正确答案。","options":["To encourage people to breed koalas as pets","To allow tourists to hug the koalas","To put them on the trees as a symbol","To establish a koala campaign"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60197","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions1-5\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8248:60198:5","type":"choice","text":"What would the government do to protect koalas from being endangered?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Policy on koala handling is determined by state government authorities. And the largest of the numbers in the Australian Nature Conservation Agency, with the aim of instituting national guidelines.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问政府会采取什么措施来保护考拉免于濒危。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"protect koalas from being endangered\"和\"government\"定位到I段，该段提到了政府的相关政策。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子\"Policy on koala handling is determined by state government authorities. And the largest of the numbers in the Australian Nature Conservation Agency, with the aim of instituting national guidelines.\"可以确定政府正在制定考拉保护方针，这与选项A\"为考拉制定保护指南\"完全一致。其他选项B、C、D在原文中均未提及，因此排除。","options":["To introduce koala protection guidelines","To close some of the zoos","To encourage people to resist visiting the zoos","To persuade the public to learn more knowledge"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60198","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions1-5\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8248:60199:6","type":"choice","text":"New coming human settlers caused danger to koalas.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Their problem, however, has been man,more specifically, the white man. Koala and aborigine had co-existed peacefully for centuries.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问新来的人类定居者是否对考拉构成了危险。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"New coming human settlers\"和\"caused danger to koalas\"定位到B段，该段提到考拉的问题是\"man, more specifically, the white man\"。\n解题思路：B段明确指出考拉与土著人和平生活了几个世纪，考拉的问题是\"人，更具体地说是白人\"，即新来的欧洲定居者。这与题干中\"New coming human settlers\"（新来的人类定居者）和\"caused danger to koalas\"（对考拉构成危险）完全对应。原文表明人类（白人）是考拉问题的根源，因此题干陈述与原文信息一致，应选择Yes。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60199","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 6-12\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 6-12 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8248:60200:7","type":"choice","text":"Koalas can still be seen in most of the places in Australia.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Today, koalas are found only in scattered pockets of southeast Australia, where they seem to be at risk on several fronts.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问“现在，在澳大利亚考拉随处可见。”这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"most of the places in Australia\"定位到C段第一句，该句明确指出考拉现在只存在于澳大利亚东南部的零散地区。\n解题思路：原文提到考拉仅存在于\"scattered pockets of southeast Australia\"（零散的东南部地区），这与题目中\"most of the places\"（大部分地区）的描述完全相反，因此题目说法与原文信息不符，答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60200","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 6-12\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 6-12 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8248:60201:8","type":"choice","text":"It takes decade for the eucalyptus trees to recover after the fire.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The koalas will be aided by the eucalyptus, which grows quickly and is already burgeoning forth after the fires.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“桉树需要十年时间才能在火灾后恢复”，需要判断这个说法是否与原文信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的核心词“eucalyptus trees”（桉树）和“recover after the fire”（火灾后恢复）定位到D段中描述桉树恢复的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到桉树“grows quickly”（生长迅速）并且“is already burgeoning forth after the fires”（火灾后已经迅速生长），说明桉树恢复很快，并不需要十年时间。题目说需要十年时间，与原文“生长迅速”的信息矛盾，因此答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60201","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 6-12\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 6-12 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8248:60202:9","type":"choice","text":"Koalas will fight each other when food becomes scarce.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Today, koalas are found only in scattered pockets of southeast Australia, where they seem to be at risk on several fronts. The koala’s only food source, the eucalyptus tree, has declined. In the past 200 years, a third of Australia’s eucalyptus forests have disappeared.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问“当食物变得稀缺时，考拉会互相打架”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"fight each other\"和\"food becomes scarce\"。在文章中，需要找到关于考拉在食物短缺时行为的描述。\n解题思路：原文C段提到考拉面临多种威胁，包括食物来源（桉树）的减少、疾病、车辆撞击和偷猎，但没有提到考拉在食物稀缺时会互相打架。因此，题目中的信息在文章中没有明确提及，无法确定考拉是否会因食物短缺而互相争斗。故答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60202","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 6-12\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 6-12 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8248:60203:10","type":"choice","text":"It is not easy to notice that koalas are ill.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Koalas are stoic creatures and put on a brave face until they are at death’s door. One day they may appear healthy, the next they could be dead. Captive koalas have to be weighed daily to check that they are feeding properly. A sudden loss of weight is usually the only warning keepers have that their charge is ill.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问“很难看出来考拉生病了”是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过“notice”和“ill”定位到H段，该段描述考拉生病时的表现。\n解题思路：H段提到考拉非常坚忍（stoic），直到生命垂危才会显露病态（put on a brave face until they are at death’s door），并且“只有体重突然下降是管理员发现它们生病的唯一预警”（A sudden loss of weight is usually the only warning keepers have that their charge is ill）。这表明考拉生病时外表不易察觉，需要通过体重变化才能发现，因此是正确的。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60203","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 6-12\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 6-12 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8248:60204:11","type":"choice","text":"Koalas are easily infected with human contagious disease via cuddling.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But people may not realise how cruel this is, but because of the koala’s delicate disposition, constant handling can push an already precariously balanced physiology over the edge.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目询问考拉是否容易通过拥抱感染人类的传染病。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键词\"easily infected with human contagious disease via cuddling\"在文章中搜索相关信息。\n解题思路：文章中提到由于考拉体质娇弱，频繁接触会使其本就脆弱的生理平衡彻底失衡，但没有明确说明考拉会通过拥抱感染人类的传染病。因此，根据原文信息，无法确定该说法的真假，所以答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60204","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 6-12\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 6-12 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8248:60205:12","type":"choice","text":"Koalas like to hold a person's arm when they are embraced.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Secondly, most people have no idea of how to handle the animals; they like to cling on to their handler, all in their own good time and use his or her arm as a tree.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是“考拉在拥抱时喜欢抓住人的手臂”，需要判断这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"hold a person's arm\"和\"embraced\"定位到I段，找到描述考拉与人互动行为的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，拥抱时，考拉喜欢紧紧抓住人，还把人的手臂当作树来用，这与题干描述完全一致，因此判断为TRUE。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60205","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 6-12\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 6-12 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8248:60206:13","type":"choice","text":"From your opinion, this article written by","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：无具体原文答案句，但文章整体风格和内容指向A选项。\n对应段落：全文\n审题：题目问这篇文章的作者是谁。\n定位关键信息：通过文章的写作风格、内容和语气判断作者的背景。\n解题思路：本题用排除法最为合适。伦敦动物园的饲养员对澳大利亚考拉的情况不会这么熟悉；去澳大利亚的旅行者也不可能如此熟知考拉的一切；政府官员如果需要出台相应的保护政策，重点应该描写的是法律方面的内容，但文中仅在最后一段有所体现。因此，A选项，为杂志撰写文稿的记者最合适。","options":["a journalist who write for magazine.","a zoo keeper in London Zoo.","a tourist who traveling back from Australia.","a government official who studies koalas to establish a law."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60206","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 13\nChoose the correcpt letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 13 on your answer sheet"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"60194","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions1-5\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>The main reason why koala declined is that they are killed except for</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"60195","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions1-5\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What can help koalas fully digest their food?</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"60196","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions1-5\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What would koalas do when facing the dangerous situation?</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"60197","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions1-5\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>In what ways Australian zoos exploit koalas?</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"60198","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions1-5\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What would the government do to protect koalas from being endangered?</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"60199","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 6-12\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 6-12 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>New coming human settlers caused danger to koalas.</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"60200","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 6-12\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 6-12 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Koalas can still be seen in most of the places in Australia.</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"60201","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 6-12\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 6-12 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>It takes decade for the eucalyptus trees to recover after the fire.</strong></p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"60202","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 6-12\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 6-12 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Koalas will fight each other when food becomes scarce.</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"60203","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 6-12\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 6-12 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>It is not easy to notice that koalas are ill.</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"60204","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 6-12\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 6-12 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Koalas are easily infected with human contagious disease via cuddling.</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"60205","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 6-12\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 6-12 on your answer sheet, write YES  if the statement is true NO  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Koalas like to hold a person&#39;s arm when they are embraced.</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"60206","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 13\nChoose the correcpt letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 13 on your answer sheet","html":"<p><strong>From your opinion, this article written by</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Koalas&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Koalas are just too nice for their own good. And except for the occasional baby taken by birds of prey, koalas have no natural enemies. In an ideal world, the life of an arboreal couch potato would be perfectly safe and acceptable.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Just two hundred years ago, koalas flourished across Australia. Now they seem to be in decline,but exact numbers are not available as the species would not seem to be ‘under threat’. Their problem, however, has been man,more specifically, the white man. Koala and aborigine had co-existed peacefully for centuries.</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Today, koalas are found only in scattered pockets of southeast Australia, where they seem to be at risk on several fronts. The koala’s only food source, the eucalyptus tree, has declined. In the past 200 years, a third of Australia’s eucalyptus forests have disappeared. Koalas have been killed by parasites, chlamydia epidemics and a tumour-causing retro-virus. And every year 11,000 are killed by cars, ironically most of them in wildlife sanctuaries, and thousands are killed by poachers. Some are also taken illegally as pets. The animals usually soon die, but they are easily replaced.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Bush fires pose another threat. The horrific ones that raged in New South Wales recently killed between 100 and 1000 koalas. Many that were taken into sanctuaries and shelters were found to have burnt their paws on the glowing embers. But zoologists say that the species should recover. The koalas will be aided by the eucalyptus, which grows quickly and is already burgeoning forth after the fires. So the main problem to their survival is their slow reproductive rate – they produce only one baby a year over a reproductive lifespan of about nine years.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The latest problem for the species is perhaps more insidious. With plush, grey fur, dark amber eyes and button nose, koalas are cuddliness incarnate. Australian zoos and wildlife parks have taken advantage of their uncomplaining attitudes, and charge visitors to be photographed hugging the furry bundles. But people may not realise how cruel this is, but because of the koala’s delicate disposition, constant handling can push an already precariously balanced physiology over the edge.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Koalas only eat the foliage of certain species of eucalyptus trees, between 600 and 1250 grams a day. The tough leaves are packed with cellulose, tannins, aromatic oils and precursors of toxic cyanides. To handle this cocktail, koalas have a specialised digestive system. Cellulose- digesting bacteria in the break down fibre, while a specially adapted gut and liver process the toxins. To digest their food properly, koalas must sit still for 21 hours every day.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Koalas are the epitome of innocence and inoffensiveness. Although they are capable of ripping open a man’s arm with their needle-sharp claws, or giving a nasty nip, they simply wouldn’t. If you upset a koala, it may blink or swallow, or hiccup. But attack? No way! Koalas are just not aggressive. They use their claws to grip the hard smooth bark of eucalyptus trees.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>They are also very sensitive, and the slightest upset can prevent them from breeding, cause them to go off their food, and succumb to gut infections. Koalas are stoic creatures and put on a brave face until they are at death’s door. One day they may appear healthy, the next they could be dead. Captive koalas have to be weighed daily to check that they are feeding properly. A sudden loss of weight is usually the only warning keepers have that their charge is ill. Only two keepers plus a vet were allowed to handle London Zoo’s koalas, as these creatures are only comfortable with people they know. A request for the koala to be taken to meet the Queen was refused because of the distress this would have caused the marsupial. Sadly, London’s Zoo no longer has a koala. Two years ago the female koala died of a cancer caused by a retrovirus. When they come into heat, female koalas become more active, and start losing weight, but after about sixteen days, heat ends and the weight piles back on. London’s koala did not. Surgery revealed hundreds of pea-sized tumours.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Almost every zoo in Australia has koalas – the marsupial has become the Animal Ambassador of the nation, but nowhere outside Australia would handling by the public be allowed. Koala cuddling screams in the face of every rule of good care. First, some zoos allow koalas to be passed from stranger to stranger, many children who love to squeeze. Secondly, most people have no idea of how to handle the animals; they like to cling on to their handler, all in their own good time and use his or her arm as a tree. For such reasons, the Association of Fauna and Marine parks, an Australian conservation society is campaigning to ban koala cuddling. Policy on koala handling is determined by state government authorities. And the largest of the numbers in the Australian Nature Conservation Agency, with the aim of instituting national guidelines. Following a wave of publicity, some zoos and wildlife parks have stopped turning their koalas into photo.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8248&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8258","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Griffith And American Films","book":"阅读还原集Vol.14","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.14 · Test 3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8258:60212:14","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Many films of the early silent era dealt with gender relations.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求为A段选择一个合适的标题，概括该段的主要内容。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"A段\"定位到文章第一段，重点阅读该段落的主题句和关键信息。\n解题思路：A段主要讨论早期无声电影中关于性别关系的表现，包括女性角色的演变和电影中性别角色的变化。这些都围绕\"gender\"展开。因此，C选项\"The gender in the development of American film\"准确概括了A段的核心内容。","options":["Detailed description for a film system","Griffith’s contribution to American films","The gender in the development of American film","Griffith changed the view of the American movie","People’s reaction to making movies in the war period","The increasing market of the film in society","Griffith improved gender recognition in society"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"60212","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-vii in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8258:60212:15","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：By focusing the camera on particular actors and actresses, Griffith inadvertently encouraged the development of the star system.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求为B段选择正确的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"B段\"定位到文章第一段，重点阅读该段落的主题句和关键信息。\n解题思路：B段主要描述了D.W. Griffith在1910年被Biograph公司派往西部海岸，并在好莱坞探索新领域，同时无意中推动了明星系统的形成，后又详细介绍明星系统的发展和影响。因此，B段的核心内容与\"Detailed description for a film system\"一种电影系统的详细描述，相符，对应标题A。","options":["Detailed description for a film system","Griffith’s contribution to American films","The gender in the development of American film","Griffith changed the view of the American movie","People’s reaction to making movies in the war period","The increasing market of the film in society","Griffith improved gender recognition in society"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"60212","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-vii in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8258:60212:16","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：From the moment America entered the war, Hollywood feared that the industry would be subject to heavy-handed government censorship.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求为C段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读C段，发现段落主要讲述了好莱坞就担心这个行业会受到政府的严厉审查，特别是提到一战期间政府曾利用宣传煽动反德情绪。\n解题思路：C段的核心内容是，美国参战后，好莱坞就担心会受到政府的严厉审查。但政府本身并不希望重蹈第一次世界大战的覆辙。这是民众在战时对拍电影的反应，因此，最合适的标题应为\"People’s reaction to making movies in the war period\"。","options":["Detailed description for a film system","Griffith’s contribution to American films","The gender in the development of American film","Griffith changed the view of the American movie","People’s reaction to making movies in the war period","The increasing market of the film in society","Griffith improved gender recognition in society"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"60212","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-vii in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8258:60212:17","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This was also a period of intense artistic and technical innovation, as pioneering directors like David Wark Griffith and others created a new language of film and revolutionized screen narrative.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求为D段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读D段内容，定位到段落的核心信息，即电影托拉斯的成立及其对电影行业的影响。\n解题思路：D段主要讲述了电影托拉斯的成立，电影行业进入了一个理性化的时期。具体包括摄像机和放映设备的标准化、电影租赁费用的固定、影院的升级以及电影质量的提高。此外，这一时期也是艺术和技术创新的时期，像大卫·沃克·格里菲斯这样的先驱导演和其他人创造了一种新的电影语言，革命性地改变了银幕叙事。因此，最合适的标题应该是关于电影行业理性化和创新的内容。根据选项，标题D“Griffith changed the view of the American movie”最符合D段的内容。","options":["Detailed description for a film system","Griffith’s contribution to American films","The gender in the development of American film","Griffith changed the view of the American movie","People’s reaction to making movies in the war period","The increasing market of the film in society","Griffith improved gender recognition in society"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"60212","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-vii in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8258:60212:18","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：While earlier directors had used such cinematic devices as close-ups, slow motion, fade-ins and fade-outs, lighting effects, and editing before, Griffith’s great contribution to the movie industry was to show how these techniques could be used to create a wholly new style of storytelling, distinct from the theater.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求为E段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读E段，可以发现段落主要讲述了Griffith作为导演在电影制作上的贡献，特别是他如何利用电影技术创造新的叙事风格。\n解题思路：E段首先介绍了Griffith被Biograph公司雇佣为导演的背景，然后重点描述了Griffith对电影行业的重大贡献——展示如何使用电影技术（如特写、慢动作、灯光效果和剪辑）来创造一种全新的叙事风格，区别于戏剧。他还提出了“摄影现实主义”的概念，强调通过更真实的表演和电影技巧来传达情感和悬念。因此，E段的核心内容是Griffith对电影叙事艺术的贡献，最符合的标题是“Griffith’s contribution to American films”。","options":["Detailed description for a film system","Griffith’s contribution to American films","The gender in the development of American film","Griffith changed the view of the American movie","People’s reaction to making movies in the war period","The increasing market of the film in society","Griffith improved gender recognition in society"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"60212","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-vii in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8258:60212:19","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph F","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：During the 1920s and 1930s, a small group of film companies consolidated their control. Known as the ‘Big Five’ – Paramount, Warner Brothers, RKO, 20th Century-Fox, and Lowe’s (MGM) and the ‘Little Three’ – Universal, Columbia, and United Artists, they formed fully integrated companies.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求为F段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：根据F段的内容，段落主要讲述了1920年代和1930年代电影公司的整合以及它们如何应对海外市场的问题。\n解题思路：F段首先提到了，少数电影公司完成了行业整合。以“五大巨头”（派拉蒙、华纳兄弟、雷电华、二十世纪福克斯和米高梅）和“三巨头”（环球影业、哥伦比亚影业、联美影业）为代表的电影集团，纷纷组建起高度整合的产业体系。接着，段落提到了这些公司如何应对海外市场的问题，包括通过雇佣西班牙导演、演员和编剧来制作西班牙语电影，英国、法国和意大利对美国电影的实施进口限制。因此，F段的主要内容是关于电影公司的市场情况。在给定的标题选项中，标题F“The increasing market of the film in society”最符合F段的内容。","options":["Detailed description for a film system","Griffith’s contribution to American films","The gender in the development of American film","Griffith changed the view of the American movie","People’s reaction to making movies in the war period","The increasing market of the film in society","Griffith improved gender recognition in society"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"60212","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-vii in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8258:60213:20","type":"choice","text":"20 Griffith’s successful in the 1910s, led his rivals","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Thus many competitors completely copy the same system as Griffith used, for the considerable profits. Additionally, they also study the theory and methods which Griffith suggested.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问Griffith在1910年代的成功，导致他的竞争对手做了什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"Griffith's successful in the 1910s\"和\"led his rivals\"定位到B段末尾，找到竞争对手完全复制Griffith的体系。\n解题思路：原文提到Griffith的成功使得许多竞争对手纷纷效仿他的模式（\"completely copy the same system as Griffith used\"），这与选项D完全模仿他的体系，一致，因此，选择D项。","options":["old company’s opposition","huge drop happens among adults","the pressure to change its market","completely copy his system"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60213","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nUse the information in the passage to match the companies (listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters, A, B, C or D in boxes 20-23 on your answer sheet.\nA old company’s opposition\nB huge drop happens among adults\nC the pressure to change its market\nD completely copy his system"},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8258:60213:21","type":"choice","text":"21 The growing costs and salary in Hollywood which shows it has","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：As the star system emerged, salaries soared. In the course of just two years, the salary of actress Mary Pickford rose from less than $400 a week in 1914 to $10,000 a week in 1916. This action made Griffith believe the big potential in the movie industry.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是好莱坞增长的成本和薪资表明了什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"the growing costs and salary in Hollywood\"可以定位到B段中提到Griffith对电影行业巨大潜力的看法，以及竞争对手如何模仿Griffith的体系以获得可观的利润。\n解题思路：根据原文，随着明星制度的兴起，片酬也水涨船高。这一现象让格里菲斯意识到电影产业的巨大潜力。因此，可以推断出好莱坞增长的成本和薪资表明了电影行业有巨大的利润潜力。根据题目要求，选择C作为答案。","options":["old company’s opposition","huge drop happens among adults","the pressure to change its market","completely copy his system"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60213","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nUse the information in the passage to match the companies (listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters, A, B, C or D in boxes 20-23 on your answer sheet.\nA old company’s opposition\nB huge drop happens among adults\nC the pressure to change its market\nD completely copy his system"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8258:60213:22","type":"choice","text":"22 The increasing new movie industries have a big impact on","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：During the 1920s and 1930s, a small group of film companies consolidated their control. Known as the ‘Big Five’ – Paramount, Warner Brothers, RKO, 20th Century-Fox, and Lowe’s (MGM) and the ‘Little Three’ – Universal, Columbia, and United Artists, they formed fully integrated companies. The old film company’s opposition was shocked by new tycoons.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“日益增长的新电影产业对什么产生了巨大影响”。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“increasing new movie industries”和“big impact on”定位到D段，该段提到了电影产业的创新和影响。\n解题思路：原文中提到，二十世纪二三十年代，少数电影公司实现了控制权的整合。其中被称为‘五大巨头’的派拉蒙、华纳兄弟、RKO、二十世纪福克斯和米高梅（原洛氏），以及‘三巨头’的环球影业、哥伦比亚影业和联美影业，共同组建了完全整合的电影公司。传统电影公司的竞争者们对这些新晋巨头的崛起感到震惊。它们的崛起和整合对原有的市场格局构成了冲击。结合选项，可以确定答案为A。","options":["old company’s opposition","huge drop happens among adults","the pressure to change its market","completely copy his system"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60213","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nUse the information in the passage to match the companies (listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters, A, B, C or D in boxes 20-23 on your answer sheet.\nA old company’s opposition\nB huge drop happens among adults\nC the pressure to change its market\nD completely copy his system"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8258:60213:23","type":"choice","text":"23 In 1992, ticket sales declined dramatically, due to","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Since the mid-1980s, the movie-going audience has continued to decrease in size. Ticket sales fell from 1.2 billion in 1983 to 950 million in 1992, with the biggest drop occurring among adults.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是1992年门票销售额急剧下降的原因。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"1992\"和\"ticket sales declined dramatically\"定位到G段，找到相关句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，自20世纪80年代中期以来，好莱坞的观影人数持续走低。电影票房从1983年的12亿张锐减至1992年的9.5亿张，其中成人观众的流失最为显著。可知，成人观众减少是主要原因。因此答案为B。","options":["old company’s opposition","huge drop happens among adults","the pressure to change its market","completely copy his system"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60213","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nUse the information in the passage to match the companies (listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters, A, B, C or D in boxes 20-23 on your answer sheet.\nA old company’s opposition\nB huge drop happens among adults\nC the pressure to change its market\nD completely copy his system"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8258:60214:24","type":"choice","text":"Why Griffith believe the potential in making movies?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This action made Griffith believe the big potential in the movie industry. But most studios refused to divulge their identities, fearing the salary demands of popular performers. As one industry observer put it, ‘In the ‘star’ your producer gets not only a ‘production’ value …. but a ‘trademark’ value, and an ‘insurance’ value which are … very potent in guaranteeing the sale of this product.’ As the star system emerged, salaries soared. In the course of just two years, the salary of actress Mary Pickford rose from less than $400 a week in 1914 to $10,000 a week in 1916.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问格里菲斯为什么相信电影制作的潜力。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“Griffith”和“potential in making movies”定位到B段中关于格里菲斯和他的电影制作实践的内容。\n解题思路：根据B段中的原文句子“This action made Griffith believe the big potential in the movie industry.”可以确定，格里菲斯相信电影制作的潜力是因为他成功地运用了明星制度，并通过明星制度带来的高收入证明了电影行业的巨大潜力。这与选项B“他成功地运用了明星制度”完全一致。其他选项A、C、D在原文中均未提及或与原文内容不符。因此，正确答案是B。","options":["The gender development in American films.","He used the star system successfully.","He prefers advanced movie techniques.","He earns lots of money."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60214","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet."},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8258:60215:25","type":"choice","text":"What is other competitors’ reaction to Griffith?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Thus many competitors completely copy the same system as Griffith used, for the considerable profits. Additionally, they also study the theory and methods which Griffith suggested.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是其他竞争对手对格里菲斯（Griffith）的反应是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"other competitors\"和\"Griffith\"定位到文章中关于竞争对手如何回应格里菲斯的内容。在B段中找到了相关的句子，说明了竞争对手的反应。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子\"Thus many competitors completely copy the same system as Griffith used, for the considerable profits. Additionally, they also study the theory and methods which Griffith suggested.\"可以得出，竞争对手完全复制了格里菲斯使用的体系，并且还研究了格里菲斯提出的理论和制作电影的方法。这与选项A的描述相符，即竞争对手采纳了格里菲斯的电影制作理论和制作电影的方法。因此，答案是A。","options":["To adopt Griffith’s theory and methods in making films","To complete copy his theory and methods","To try to catch up with their innovations","To find a new system against Griffith"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60215","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet."},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8258:60216:26","type":"choice","text":"What is the great change in films industries during the 1920s and 1930s?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The confusion of tongues in the foreign version of American films deepened when American directors themselves embarked on the shooting of the new version.  They did not usually speak Spanish (or the given target language) and, at that time, there were only a few translators at the studio’s disposal.  For this reason, it was more general to contract Spanish directors, actors, and screenwriters to produce American films in Spanish for Latin American audiences and for the public in the Iberian Peninsula.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是在1920年代和1930年代电影产业发生的重大变化是什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"1920s and 1930s\"和\"films industries\"可以定位到F段。\n解题思路：F段开头提到，二十世纪二三十年代，少数电影公司完成了行业整合。美国本土导演开始亲自参与新版本电影的拍摄时，外语片中的语言混乱现象愈发严重。而当时制片厂手头的翻译资源也十分有限。为此，好莱坞更倾向于聘请西班牙籍导演、演员和编剧，为拉美观众和伊比利亚半岛观众制作西班牙语版美国电影。与选项D\"improve the foreign version of American movies\"（改进美国电影的海外版本）相符，这是电影产业为了应对海外市场变化而采取的措施。其他选项A、B、C在原文中均未提及或与原文内容不符。因此，D是正确答案。","options":["To try to seek the high-tech special efforts","To dismiss the needs of overseas audiences","To change its goal market","To improve the foreign version of American movies"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60216","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"60212","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below. Write the correct number i-vii in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"60213","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20-23\nUse the information in the passage to match the companies (listed A-C) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters, A, B, C or D in boxes 20-23 on your answer sheet.\nA old company’s opposition\nB huge drop happens among adults\nC the pressure to change its market\nD completely copy his system","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> old company’s opposition&nbsp;</p><p><strong>B</strong> huge drop happens among adults&nbsp;</p><p><strong>C</strong> the pressure to change its market&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>D</strong> completely copy his system&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>20</strong> Griffith’s successful in the 1910s, led his rivals <strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"60214","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Why Griffith believe the potential in making movies?</strong></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"60215","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is other competitors’ reaction to Griffith?</strong></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"60216","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is the great change in films industries during the 1920s and 1930s?</strong></p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Griffith And American Films&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Movies are key cultural artefacts that offer a window into American cultural and social history. A mixture of art, business, and popular entertainment, the popular entertainment, the movies provide a host of insights into Americans’ shifting ideas, fantasies, and preoccupations.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Many films of the early silent era dealt with gender relations. Before 1905, as Kathy Peiss has argued, movie screens were filled with salacious sexual imagery and risque humor, drawn from burlesque halls and vaudeville theaters. Early films offered many glimpses of women disrobing or of passionate kisses. As the movies’ female audience grew, sexual titillation and voyeurism persisted. But an ever-increasing number of the film dealt with the changing work and sexual roles of women in a more sophisticated manner. While D.W. Griffith’s films presented an idealized picture of the frail Victorian child-woman and showed an almost obsessive preoccupation with female honor and chastity, other silent movies presented quite different images of femininity. These ranged from the exotic, sexually aggressive vamp to the athletic, energetic ‘serial queen’; the street smart urban working gal, who repels the sexual advances of her lascivious boss; and cigarette-smoking, alcohol drinking chorus girls or burlesque queens.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In early 1910, director D.W. Griffith was sent by the Biograph Company to the west coast with his acting troupe, consisting of actors Blanche Sweet, Lillian Gish, Mary Pickford, Lionel Barrymore, and others. While there, the company decided to explore new territories, traveling several miles north to Hollywood, a little village that was friendly and enjoyed the movie company filming there. By focusing the camera on particular actors and actresses, Griffith inadvertently encouraged the development of the star system. As early as 1910, newspapers were deluged with requests for actors’ names. But most studios refused to divulge their identities, fearing the salary demands of popular performers. As one industry observer put it, ‘In the ‘star’ your producer gets not only a ‘production’ value …. but a ‘trademark’ value, and an ‘insurance’ value which are … very potent in guaranteeing the sale of this product.’ As the star system emerged, salaries soared. In the course of just two years, the salary of actress Mary Pickford rose from less than $400 a week in 1914 to $10,000 a week in 1916. This action made Griffith believe the big potential in the movie industry. Thus many competitors completely copy the same system as Griffith used, for the considerable profits. Additionally, they also study the theory and methods which Griffith suggested.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>From the moment America entered the war, Hollywood feared that the industry would be subject to heavy-handed government censorship. But the government itself wanted no repeat of World War I, when the Committee on Public Information had whipped up anti-German hysteria and oversold the war as ‘a Crusade not merely to re-win the tomb of Christ, but to bring back to earth the rule of right, the peace, goodwill to men and gentleness he taught.’&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The formation of the movie trust ushered in a period of rationalization within the film industry. Camera and projecting equipment were standardized; film rental fees were fixed; theaters were upgraded; which improved the quality of movies by removing damaged prints from circulation. This was also a period of intense artistic and technical innovation, as pioneering directors like David Wark Griffith and others created a new language of film and revolutionized screen narrative.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>With just six months of film experience, Griffith, a former stage actor, was hired as a director by the Biograph Company and promised $50 a week and one-twentieth of a cent for every foot of film sold to a rental exchange. Each week, Griffith turned out two or three one-reelers. While earlier directors had used such cinematic devices as close-ups, slow motion, fade-ins and fade-outs, lighting effects, and editing before, Griffith’s great contribution to the movie industry was to show how these techniques could be used to create a wholly new style of storytelling, distinct from the theater. Griffith’s approach to movie storytelling has been aptly called ‘photographic realism.’ This is not to say that he merely wished to record a story accurately; rather he sought to convey the illusion of realism. He demanded that his performers act less in a more lifelike manner, avoiding the broad, exaggerated gestures and pantomiming of emotions that characterized the nineteenth-century stage. He wanted his performers to take on a role rather than directly addressing the camera. Above all, he used close-ups, lighting, editing, and other cinematic techniques convey suspense and other emotions and to focus the audience’s attention on individual performers.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>During the 1920s and 1930s, a small group of film companies consolidated their control. Known as the ‘Big Five’ – Paramount, Warner Brothers, RKO, 20th Century-Fox, and Lowe’s (MGM) and the ‘Little Three’ – Universal, Columbia, and United Artists, they formed fully integrated companies. The old film company’s opposition was shocked by new tycoons. The confusion of tongues in the foreign version of American films deepened when American directors themselves embarked on the shooting of the new version. They did not usually speak Spanish (or the given target language) and, at that time, there were only a few translators at the studio’s disposal. For this reason, it was more general to contract Spanish directors, actors, and screenwriters to produce American films in Spanish for Latin American audiences and for the public in the Iberian Peninsula. Hollywood had depended on overseas markets for as much as 40 percent of its revenue. But in an effort to nurture their own film industries and prevent an excessive outflow of dollars, Britain, France, and Italy imposed stiff import tariffs and restrictive quotas on imported American movies.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>A basic problem facing today’s Hollywood is the rapidly rising cost of making and marketing a movie: an average of $40 million today. The immense cost of producing movies has led the studios to seek guaranteed hits: blockbuster loaded with high-tech special effects, sequels, and remakes of earlier movies, foreign films, and even old TV shows. Hollywood has also sought to cope with rising costs by focusing ever more intently on its core audiences. Since the mid-1980s, the movie-going audience has continued to decrease in size. Ticket sales fell from 1.2 billion in 1983 to 950 million in 1992, with the biggest drop occurring among adults. And since over half of Hollywood’s profits are earned overseas, the target market has to be changed due to the increasing costs and salary of making a film. The industry has concentrated much of its energy on crude action films easily understood by an international audience, featuring stars like Arnold Schwarzenegger and Sylvester Stallone.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8258&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8259","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 The Exploration of Mars","book":"阅读还原集Vol.14","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.14 · Test 3 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8259:60217:27","type":"choice","text":"27 Martian evidence on Earth","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The Martian meteorite found in Earth aroused doubts to the above analysis.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“地球上的火星证据”这一信息出现在哪一段落。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“Martian evidence on Earth”可以定位到D段首句“The Martian meteorite found in Earth”。\n解题思路：D段详细描述了在地球南极发现的ALH84001火星陨石，并提到该陨石可能包含与地球微生物相关的磁铁矿结构，直接对应了“Martian evidence on Earth”这一信息。因此，答案为D。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"60217","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8259:60217:28","type":"choice","text":"28 Mars and Earth may share the same life origin","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Even more intriguing, however, is the alternative scenario by Spanish scientists: If those samples could be found to that use DNA, as Earthly life does, as their genetic code. It is extremely unlikely that such a highly specialised, complex molecule like DNA could have evolved separately on the two planets, indicating that there must be a common origin for Martian and Earthly life.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问哪个段落提到了火星和地球可能拥有相同的生命起源。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Mars and Earth\"和\"same life origin\"定位到H段，该段明确提到了如果火星生命使用与地球生命相同的DNA遗传密码，那么火星和地球生命可能有共同的起源。\n解题思路：H段详细讨论了西班牙科学家的假设，即如果火星生命使用DNA作为遗传密码，这种高度特化且复杂的分子在火星和地球独立演化出来的可能性微乎其微，说明火星和地球生命必须有一个共同的起源。因此，H段包含了题目所问的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"60217","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8259:60217:29","type":"choice","text":"29 certain agricultural construction was depicted specifically","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1877, Giovanni Schiaparelli, an Italian astronomer, made drawings and maps of the Martian surface that suggested strange features. The images from telescopes at this time were not as sharp as today. Schiaparelli said he could see a network of lines or canali. In 1894, an American astronomer, Percival Lowell, made a series of observations of Mars from his own observatory at Flagstaff, Arizona, USA. Lowell was convinced a great network of canals had been dug to irrigate crops for the Martian race!\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问“描绘了某种农业构造”，即寻找关于农业构造（如运河、灌溉系统等）的内容。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“agricultural construction”（农业构造）定位到A段中Lowell对火星运河的描述。\n解题思路：A段提到Lowell认为火星上有运河（canals），认为火星人曾开凿庞大的运河系统来灌溉农田。这与题目吻合，因此答案为A。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"60217","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8259:60217:30","type":"choice","text":"30 the project which aims to identify life under similar condition of Mars","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Researchers from the Center of Astrobiology (Spain) and the Catholic University of the North in Chile have found an ‘oasis’ of microorganisms two meters below the surface of the Atacama Desert, SOLID, a detector for signs of life which could be used in environments similar to subsoil on Mars.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问哪个段落提到了探寻与火星相似环境下的生命的项目。\n定位关键信息：利用\"identify life under similar condition of Mars\"（识别与火星相似条件下生命）定位。原文中\"detector for signs of life which could be used in environments similar to subsoil on Mars\"（可用于与火星次表层相似环境的生命迹象探测器）与之对应。\n解题思路：G段提到SOLID探测器，其功能是检测与火星次表层相似环境的生命迹象，与题目要求完全一致。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"60217","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8259:60217:31","type":"choice","text":"31 Mars had experienced terrifying climate transformation","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The disappearance of the magnetic field may be played a significant role in the process of Martian climate change. According to the valuation of the scientists, the climate of Mars gradually transits from warm and wet to cold and dry after magnetic field vanished.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“火星经历了可怕的气候变化”，需要找到描述火星气候变化的段落。\n定位关键信息：通过“climate transformation”定位到E段，该段明确提到火星气候的变化过程。\n解题思路：E段提到，磁场消失可能在火星气候变化过程中扮演重要角色。科学家评估认为，火星气候在磁场消失后将逐渐从温暖湿润转变为寒冷干燥。与题目信息完全一致。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"60217","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8259:60217:32","type":"choice","text":"32 attempts in scientific investigation to find liquid water","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：NASA’s recent missions have focused on another question: whether Mars held lakes or oceans of liquid water on its surface in the ancient past. Scientists have found hematite, a mineral that forms in the presence of water. Thus, the mission of the Mars Exploration Rovers of 2004 was not to look for present or past life, but for evidence of liquid water on the surface of Mars in the planet’s ancient past.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了试图寻找液态水的调查研究。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"attempts in scientific investigation to find liquid water\"可以定位到F段中提到\"the mission of the Mars Exploration Rovers of 2004 was not to look for present or past life, but for evidence of liquid water on the surface of Mars in the planet’s ancient past\"，这句话明确指出了科学调查中寻找液态水的尝试。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子，可以确定F段提到了，美国国家航空航天局（NASA）近期的火星探测任务聚焦于另一个关键问题：火星在远古时期是否曾拥有液态水的湖泊或海洋，并且，2004年火星探测车的任务目标并非寻找现今或过去的地表生命，而是要探寻火星远古时期地表存在液态水的证据。与题目吻合，因此答案为F。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"60217","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8259:60218:33","type":"choice","text":"How did Percival Lowell describe Mars in this passage?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Lowell was convinced a great network of canals had been dug to irrigate crops for the Martian race! He suggested that each canal had fertile vegetation on either side, making them noticeable from Earth. Drawings and globes he made show a network of canals and oases all over the planet.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是Percival Lowell在文章中是如何描述火星的。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Percival Lowell\"和\"describe Mars\"定位到A段中关于Lowell描述火星的内容。\n解题思路：原文提到Lowell认为火星上有一条巨大的运河网络，是为了灌溉农作物而挖掘的，并且每个运河两侧都有肥沃的植被，从地球上就可以观察到它们。他还绘制了显示整个星球上运河网络和绿洲的地图。这表明Lowell描述了火星上类似地球的水利和农业痕迹，因此选项C正确。选项A提到亚利桑那州是最佳观测地点，但原文并未提及；选项B和D的内容在原文中也没有提及。","options":["Perfect observation location is in Arizona.","Canals of Mars is broader than that of the earth.","Dedicated water and agriculture trace are similar to the earth.","Actively moving Martian lives are found by observation."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60218","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33-36\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 33-36 on your answer sheet."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8259:60219:34","type":"choice","text":"How did people change their point of view towards Mars from the 19th century?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The idea that there was intelligent life on Mars gained strength in the late 19th century. In 1898, H.G. Wells wrote a science fiction classic, The War of the Worlds about an invading force of Martians who try to conquer Earth. They use highly advanced technology (advanced for 1898) to crush human resistance in their path. In 1917, Edgar Rice Burroughs wrote the first in a series of 11 novels about Mars. Strange beings and rampaging Martian monsters gripped the public’s imagination. A radio broadcast by Orson Welles on Halloween night in 1938 of The War of the Worlds caused widespread panic across America. People ran into the streets in their pyjamas-millions believed the dramatic reports of a Martian invasion.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是从19世纪开始，人们对火星的观点是如何改变的。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"19th century\"和\"point of view towards Mars\"定位到B段开头，提到\"the idea that there was intelligent life on Mars gained strength in the late 19th century\"，即人们对火星存在智慧生命的看法在19世纪后期得到了加强。\n解题思路：B段详细描述了19世纪末至20世纪初，通过文学作品（如H.G. Wells的《世界大战》和Edgar Rice Burroughs的火星系列小说）和1938年Orson Welles的广播剧，人们对火星存在智慧生命的看法逐渐形成并加强。这些文学和广播作品使人们对火星的看法发生了变化，从科学观测到文学想象。因此，选项B正确，因为人们是通过文学作品了解火星的知识。其他选项A、C、D都与原文描述不符。","options":["They experienced a Martian attack.","They learned knowledge of mars through some literature works.","They learned a new concept by listening to a famous radio program.","They attended lectures given by famous writers."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60219","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33-36\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 33-36 on your answer sheet."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8259:60220:35","type":"choice","text":"In the 1960s, which information is correct about Mars by a number of Probes sent to space?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The first images sent back from Mars came from Mariner 4 in July 1965. They showed a cratered and barren landscape, more like the surface of our moon than Earth.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是在1960年代，通过向太空发射的多个探测器，关于火星的信息哪些是正确的。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"1960s\"和\"Probes\"可以定位到C段，该段提到了1965年Mariner 4探测器发回的火星图像。\n解题思路：C段提到Mariner 4探测器发回的图像显示火星表面是\"cratered and barren landscape\"（布满陨石坑和荒凉的景观），并且与地球的表面不同，更像月球表面。因此，火星的景象不像地球那样有生机，选项B与原文描述一致。其他选项A、C、D与原文内容不符。","options":["It has a landscape full of rock and river.","It was not as vivid as the earth.","It contained the same substance as in the moon.","It had different images from the following probes."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60220","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33-36\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 33-36 on your answer sheet."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8259:60221:36","type":"choice","text":"What is the implication of the project proceeded by a technology called SOLID in the Atacama Desert?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：'If there are similar microbes on Mars or remains in similar conditions to the ones we have found in the Atacama, we could detect them with instruments like SOLID’ Parro highlighted.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是在阿塔卡马沙漠中使用SOLID技术进行的项目的含义是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"SOLID\"和\"Atacama Desert\"可以定位到G段中关于SOLID技术的描述。\n解题思路：根据G段中的原文答案句，研究人员表示，如果火星上有类似的微生物，或者，存在于类似阿塔卡马沙漠环境中的残留物，他们可以使用SOLID这样的仪器来检测这些生物体。因此，选项A正确。选项B错误，因为原文并未明确提到SOLID技术不能用于探索火星环境下的生物体。选项C和D与原文内容不符。","options":["It could be employed to explore organisms under Martian condition.","This technology could NOT be used to identify life on similar condition of Mars.","Atacama Desert is the only place that has a suitable environment for organisms.","Life had not yet been found yet in the Atacama Desert."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60221","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33-36\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 33-36 on your answer sheet."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8259:60222:37","type":"choice","text":"The technology of Martian creature was superior to what human had at that time in every field according to The War of the Worlds.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1898, H.G. Wells wrote a science fiction classic, The War of the Worlds about an invading force of Martians who try to conquer Earth. They use highly advanced technology (advanced for 1898) to crush human resistance in their path.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问根据《世界大战》这本书，火星生物的技术是否在所有领域都优于当时人类的技术。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"The War of the Worlds\"和\"technology\"定位到B段，找到关于火星生物技术的描述。\n解题思路：原文提到火星生物使用的是\"highly advanced technology (advanced for 1898)\"，但这是相对于1898年人类的技术而言的，并未说明火星生物的技术在所有领域都优于人类。原文没有明确说明火星生物的技术在所有领域都更先进，因此无法确定题目中的说法是否正确。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60222","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8259:60223:38","type":"choice","text":"Proof sent by Viking probes has not been challenged yet.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The Martian meteorite found in Earth aroused doubts to the above analysis.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问“Viking探测器提供的证据尚未受到质疑”是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"Viking probes\", \"proof\", \"challenged\" 定位到文中评价Viking探测器发现可靠性的句子。\n解题思路：段落D中，开篇第一句就明确指出，“在地球上发现的火星陨石对上述分析提出了质疑”。这里的“上述分析”正是指代前文（段落C末尾）中Viking探测器“未发现生命”的结论。因此，该陈述与原文信息矛盾，答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60223","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8259:60224:39","type":"choice","text":"Analysis of meteorite from Mars found a substance which is connected to some germs.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Composition analysis by NASA revealed a kind of magnetite that on Earth, is only found in association with certain microorganisms.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“对来自火星的陨石的分析种，发现了一种与某些细菌相关的物质”这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“meteorite from Mars”和“substance connected to some germs”可以定位到D段，该段提到了对火星陨石ALH84001的分析。\n解题思路：D段明确提到，NASA对火星陨石的分析发现了一种磁铁矿，这种磁铁矿在地球上只与某些微生物共生。这与题目中的陈述完全一致，因此答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60224","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8259:60225:40","type":"choice","text":"According to Victor Parro, their project will be deployed on Mars after they identified DNA substance on earth.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘If there are similar microbes on Mars or remains in similar conditions to the ones we have found in the Atacama, we could detect them with instruments like SOLID’ Parro highlighted.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是根据Victor Parro的说法， 在确认地球上发现的DNA物质后，他们的项目将在火星上实施，这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"Victor Parro\", \"project\", \"deployed on Mars\", \"identified DNA substance on earth\" 定位到文中描述SOLID探测器应用条件的句子。\n解题思路：段落G中，Victor Parro确实提到了，可以使用SOLID探测器在火星上探测类似阿塔卡马沙漠发现的微生物。然而，文中只字未提该探测器的部署与“在地球上识别出DNA物质”这一前提条件有任何关联，也没有说明其部署的时间规划。题目中的条件关系在原文中找不到依据。因此，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60225","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"60217","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>27</strong> Martian evidence on Earth<strong class=\"source-blank\">[27] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"60218","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33-36\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 33-36 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>How did Percival Lowell describe Mars in this passage?</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"60219","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33-36\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 33-36 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>How did people change their point of view towards Mars from the 19th century?</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"60220","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33-36\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 33-36 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>In the 1960s, which information is correct about Mars by a number of Probes sent to space?</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"60221","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33-36\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 33-36 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is the implication of the project proceeded by a technology called SOLID in the Atacama Desert?</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"60222","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The technology of Martian creature was superior to what human had at that time in every field according to The War of the Worlds.</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"60223","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Proof sent by Viking probes has not been challenged yet.</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"60224","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Analysis of meteorite from Mars found a substance which is connected to some germs.</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"60225","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>According to Victor Parro, their project will be deployed on Mars after they identified DNA substance on earth.</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The Exploration of Mars&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In 1877, Giovanni Schiaparelli, an Italian astronomer, made drawings and maps of the Martian surface that suggested strange features. The images from telescopes at this time were not as sharp as today. Schiaparelli said he could see a network of lines or canali. In 1894, an American astronomer, Percival Lowell, made a series of observations of Mars from his own observatory at Flagstaff, Arizona, USA. Lowell was convinced a great network of canals had been dug to irrigate crops for the Martian race! He suggested that each canal had fertile vegetation on either side, making them noticeable from Earth. Drawings and globes he made show a network of canals and oases all over the planet.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The idea that there was intelligent life on Mars gained strength in the late 19th century. In 1898, H.G. Wells wrote a science fiction classic, The War of the Worlds about an invading force of Martians who try to conquer Earth. They use highly advanced technology (advanced for 1898) to crush human resistance in their path. In 1917, Edgar Rice Burroughs wrote the first in a series of 11 novels about Mars. Strange beings and rampaging Martian monsters gripped the public’s imagination. A radio broadcast by Orson Welles on Halloween night in 1938 of The War of the Worlds caused widespread panic across America. People ran into the streets in their pyjamas-millions believed the dramatic reports of a Martian invasion.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Probes are very important to our understanding of other planets. Much of our recent knowledge comes from these robotic missions into space. The first images sent back from Mars came from Mariner 4 in July 1965. They showed a cratered and barren landscape, more like the surface of our moon than Earth. In 1969, Mariners 6 and 7 were launched and took 200 photographs of Mars’s southern hemisphere and pole on fly-by missions. But these showed little more information. In 1971, Mariner 9’s mission was to orbit the planet every 12 hours. In 1975, The USA sent two Viking probes to the planet, each with a lander and an orbiter. The Landers had sampler arms to scoop up Maritain rocks and did experiments to try and find signs of life. Although no life was found, they sent back the first colour pictures of the planet’s surface and atmosphere from pivoting cameras.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The Martian meteorite found in Earth aroused doubts to the above analysis. ALH84001 meteorite was discovered in December 1984 in Antarctica, by members of the ANSMET project; The sample was ejected from Mars about 17 million years ago and spent 11,000 years in or on the Antarctic ice sheets. Composition analysis by NASA revealed a kind of magnetite that on Earth, is only found in association with certain microorganisms. Some structures resembling the mineralized casts of terrestrial bacteria and their appendages fibrils of by-products occur in the rims of carbonate globules and pre-terrestrial aqueous alteration regions. The size and shape of the objects are consistent with Earthly fossilized nanobacteria, but the existence of nanobacteria itself is still controversial.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In 1965, the Mariner 4 probe discovered that Mars had no global magnetic field that would protect the planet from potentially life-threatening cosmic radiation and solar radiation; observations made in the late 1990s by the Mars Global Surveyor confirmed this discovery. Scientists speculate that the lack of magnetic shielding helped the solar wind blow away much of Mars’s atmosphere over the course of several billion years. After mapping cosmic radiation levels at various depths on Mars, researchers have concluded that any life within the first several meters of the planet’s surface would be killed by lethal doses of cosmic radiation. In 2007, it was calculated that DNA and RNA damage by cosmic radiation would limit life on Mars to depths greater than 7.5 metres below the planet’s surface. Therefore, the best potential locations for discovering life on Mars may be at subsurface environments that have not been studied yet. The disappearance of the magnetic field may be played a significant role in the process of Martian climate change. According to the valuation of the scientists, the climate of Mars gradually transits from warm and wet to cold and dry after magnetic field vanished.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>NASA’s recent missions have focused on another question: whether Mars held lakes or oceans of liquid water on its surface in the ancient past. Scientists have found hematite, a mineral that forms in the presence of water. Thus, the mission of the Mars Exploration Rovers of 2004 was not to look for present or past life, but for evidence of liquid water on the surface of Mars in the planet’s ancient past. Liquid water, necessary for Earth life and for metabolism as generally conducted by species on Earth, cannot exist on the surface of Mars under its present low atmospheric pressure and temperature, except at the lowest shaded elevations for short periods and liquid water does not appear at the surface itself. In March 2004, NASA announced that its rover Opportunity had discovered evidence that Mars was, in the ancient past, a wet planet. This had raised hopes that evidence of past life might be found on the planet today. ESA confirmed that the Mars Express orbiter had directly detected huge reserves of water ice at Mars’ south pole in January 2004.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Researchers from the Center of Astrobiology (Spain) and the Catholic University of the North in Chile have found an ‘oasis’ of microorganisms two meters below the surface of the Atacama Desert, SOLID, a detector for signs of life which could be used in environments similar to subsoil on Mars. ‘We have named it a ‘microbial oasis’ because we found microorganisms developing in a habitat that was rich in rock salt and other highly hygroscopic compounds that absorb water’ explained Victor Parro, a researcher from the Center of Astrobiology in Spain. ‘If there are similar microbes on Mars or remains in similar conditions to the ones we have found in the Atacama, we could detect them with instruments like SOLID’ Parro highlighted.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Even more intriguing, however, is the alternative scenario by Spanish scientists: If those samples could be found to that use DNA, as Earthly life does, as their genetic code. It is extremely unlikely that such a highly specialised, complex molecule like DNA could have evolved separately on the two planets, indicating that there must be a common origin for Martian and Earthly life. Life-based on DNA first appeared on Mars and then spread to Earth, where it then evolved into the myriad forms of plants and creatures that exist today. If this was found to be the case, we would have to face the logical conclusion: we are all Martian. If not, we would continue to search the life of signs.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8259&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8231","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Traditional Farming System in Africa","book":"阅读还原集Vol.14","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.14 · Test 2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8231:60076:1","type":"fill","text":"填写第 1 空","answer":"need/Need","acceptedAnswers":["need","Need"],"explanation":"原文答案句：By tradition land in Luapula is not owned by individuals, but as in many other parts of Africa is allocated by the headman or head woman of a village to people of either sex, according to need.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是在Luapula土地分配是按照什么进行的。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"Luapula land allocation\"定位到A段，找到\"allocated...according to need\"这一关键信息。\n解题思路：原文明确指出土地分配是根据\"need\"（需求）进行的，因此答案为\"need\"。题干中的\"Luapula land allocation\"与原文中的\"land in Luapula is...allocated\"对应，\"according to need\"直接给出了答案。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"60076","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nComplete the sentences below with words taken from the passage. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8231:60077:2","type":"fill","text":"填写第 2 空","answer":"the ashes/ashes/The Ashes/Ashes","acceptedAnswers":["the ashes","ashes","The Ashes","Ashes"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Most of the traditional cropping in Luapula, as in the Bemba area to the east, is based on citemene, a system whereby crops are grown on the ashes of tree branches.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是citemene系统为土地提供了什么，其中作物被种植在上面。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"citemene system\"和\"where crops are planted\"定位到B段第一句，该句明确提到了citemene系统是基于在树枝的灰烬上种植作物的。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句\" crops are grown on the ashes of tree branches\"，可以确定citemene系统为土地提供了灰烬，作物就是种植在这些灰烬上。因此，答案为ashes。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"60077","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nComplete the sentences below with words taken from the passage. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8231:60078:3","type":"fill","text":"填写第 3 空","answer":"vegetable cassava/cassava/Vegetable Cassava/Cassava","acceptedAnswers":["vegetable cassava","cassava","Vegetable Cassava","Cassava"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The diverse sequence ends with vegetable cassava, which is often planted into the developing last-but-one crop as a relay.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是在第二个季节中，最后种植的作物是什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"the second season\"和\"the last planted crop\"定位到C段中描述第二个季节种植作物的句子。\n解题思路：根据C段原文句子\"The diverse sequence ends with vegetable cassava...\"可知，各种作物的种植序列最后是以(蔬菜)木薯结束的，因此最后种植的作物是vegetable cassava。题目中的\"the second season\"与原文中的\"During the second season\"对应，\"the last planted crop\"对应原文中的\"ends with\"，由此确定答案为vegetable cassava。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"60078","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nComplete the sentences below with words taken from the passage. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8231:60079:4","type":"fill","text":"填写第 4 空","answer":"houses/Houses","acceptedAnswers":["houses","Houses"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Where their roots have year-round access to water tables mango, guava and oil-palm trees often grow around houses, forming a traditional agroforestry system.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问在合适条件下，果树被种植在什么地方附近。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"fruit trees\"和\"planted near\"定位到E段中关于果树种植的描述。\n解题思路：原文E段提到\"mango, guava and oil-palm trees\"（芒果、番石榴和油棕树）这些果树在根部全年能接触到地下水的情况下，常常被种植在\"houses\"（房屋）周围，形成传统的农林系统。因此，果树被种植在房屋附近，答案为\"houses\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"60079","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nComplete the sentences below with words taken from the passage. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8231:60080:5","type":"choice","text":"5 be used in some unusual occasions, such as celebrations.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Most people keep freely roaming chickens and goats. These act as a reserve for bartering, but may also be occasionally slaughtered for ceremonies or for entertaining important visitors.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问哪种动物在特殊场合（如庆祝活动）被使用。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"unusual occasions\"和\"celebrations\"定位到I段中\"occasionally slaughtered for ceremonies or for entertaining important visitors\"这一信息。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到\"goats\"（山羊）在特殊场合（如仪式和招待重要访客）会被宰杀，这与题干中\"unusual occasions, such as celebrations\"完全对应。其他选项如\"fish\"和\"oxen\"在文中未被提及用于此类特殊场合。因此答案为C。","options":["Fish","Oxen","Goats"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"60080","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nClassify the following items with the correct description. Write your answers in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\nA Fish\nB Oxen\nC Goats"},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8231:60080:6","type":"choice","text":"6 cannot thrive for being affected by the pests.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Only small numbers of cattle or oxen are kept in the province owing to the prevalence of the tsetse fly.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是哪种动物因为受到害虫影响而无法生长。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"cannot thrive\", \"affected by the pests\" 定位到文中描述某种牲畜因虫害而数量稀少的句子。\n解题思路：在段落I中，原文明确指出“由于采采蝇的盛行，该省只饲养了少量牛或 oxen”。“由于采采蝇的盛行”(owing to the prevalence of the tsetse fly) 直接对应了“受害虫影响”，而“只饲养了少量”(only small numbers...are kept) 则对应了“无法大量繁殖”。因此，符合此描述的动物是B (Oxen)。","options":["Fish","Oxen","Goats"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"60080","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nClassify the following items with the correct description. Write your answers in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\nA Fish\nB Oxen\nC Goats"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8231:60080:7","type":"choice","text":"7 be the largest part of creating profit.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Fishing has always been a far more remunerative activity in Luapula that crop husbandry. A fisherman may earn more in a week than a bean or maize grower in a whole season.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是哪种动物创造的利润最大。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"largest part of creating profit\"可以定位到H段中关于捕鱼和农作物种植的比较。\n解题思路：根据原文H段的句子\" Fishing has always been a far more remunerative activity in Luapula that crop husbandry. A fisherman may earn more in a week than a bean or maize grower in a whole season.\"可以得出结论，捕鱼一直是比农作物种植更赚钱的活动，渔民一周的收入可能比种植豆类或玉米的农民整个季节的收入还要多。因此，选择A。","options":["Fish","Oxen","Goats"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"60080","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nClassify the following items with the correct description. Write your answers in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\nA Fish\nB Oxen\nC Goats"},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8231:60080:8","type":"choice","text":"8 be sold beyond the local area.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Much fish has dried for sale to areas away from the main waterways.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是哪种动物会被销往外地。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"beyond the local area\"，可以在文章中寻找描述动物销售范围的句子。\n解题思路：在G段中，原文提到\"Much fish has dried for sale to areas away from the main waterways\"（大量鱼被晒干用于销售到主水道以外的地区）。这句话明确指出鱼被销售到当地以外的地区，与题目要求一致。因此，正确答案是G段。","options":["Fish","Oxen","Goats"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"60080","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nClassify the following items with the correct description. Write your answers in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\nA Fish\nB Oxen\nC Goats"},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8231:60081:9","type":"choice","text":"People rarely use animals to cultivate the land.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For the few herds, the dambos provide subsistence grazing during the dry season. The absence of animal draft power greatly limits peoples’ ability to plough and cultivate land: a married couple can rarely manage to prepare by hand-hoeing.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问“人们很少用动物来耕种土地”，该说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的“animals to cultivate the land”对应文章中“animal draft power”和“hand-hoeing”等描述耕作方式的词汇。\n解题思路：I段明确提到“畜力的缺乏极大地限制了人们犁地和耕种土地的能力”，并指出“一对夫妇几乎无法靠手工锄地来完成准备工作”，说明人们很少使用动物进行耕作，而是依赖人力。因此，题目与原文信息一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60081","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-12\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 9-12 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8231:60082:10","type":"choice","text":"When it is a busy time, children usually took part in the labor force.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：原文中没有直接提到儿童参与劳动力的句子。\n对应段落：全文未提及。\n审题：题目问的是“当农忙时，儿童也参与劳动”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“children”和“labor force”，需要寻找文章中关于儿童参与劳动的描述。\n解题思路：文章中没有提到儿童在农忙时参与劳动力的任何信息。文章主要描述了传统农业系统中的耕作方式、劳动分工（如男女分工）、渔业和畜牧业等情况，但未涉及儿童参与劳动的具体内容。因此，无法确定题目中的说法是否与文章一致。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60082","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-12\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 9-12 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8231:60083:11","type":"choice","text":"The local residents eat goats on a regular time.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：These act as a reserve for bartering, but may also be occasionally slaughtered for ceremonies or for entertaining important visitors. These animals are not a regular part of most peoples’ diet.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问“当地居民每隔一段时间就会吃山羊”是否与文章作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“goats”和“regular time”定位到I段中关于山羊用途的描述。\n解题思路：原文明确提到山羊“not a regular part of most peoples’ diet”，即这些动物通常不在大多数人的日常饮食中，而题目却说“regular time”（定期），两者意思相反，因此题目与原文信息矛盾，应选择FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60083","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-12\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 9-12 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8231:60084:12","type":"choice","text":"Though citemene has been a sophisticated system, it could not provide enough protein.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Citemene has been an ingenious system for providing people with seasonal production of high-quality cereals and vegetables in regions of acid, heavily leached soils. Nutritionally, the most serious deficiency was that of protein.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是“尽管citemene是一个复杂的系统，但它无法提供足够的蛋白质”，是否与文章作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的关键词\"citemene\"和\"protein\"，可以在文章中定位到J段。该段明确提到了营养方面最严重的缺陷是蛋白质的缺乏。\n解题思路：段落J中，作者首先肯定了citemene系统，称其为“一个巧妙的系统”(an ingenious system)，这与“复杂的系统”相符。紧接着，作者明确指出该系统在营养方面“最严重的缺陷是蛋白质不足”(the most serious deficiency was that of protein)。这直接证实了题目的第二个核心信息。因此，该陈述与作者在文中的信息完全一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60084","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-12\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 9-12 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8231:60085:13","type":"choice","text":"What is the writer’s opinion about the traditional ways of practices?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Although population densities are still much lower than in several countries of South-East Asia, neither the fisheries nor the forests and woodlands of Luapula are capable, with unmodified traditional practices, of supporting the people in a sustainable manner.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是作者对传统农耕方式的看法是什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"traditional ways of practices\"，可以在文章中定位到J段，该段提到了传统农耕方式（traditional practices）。\n解题思路：根据J段中的原文答案句可知，尽管卢阿普拉地区人口密度仍然比东南亚的几个国家低，但如果不改进传统农耕方式，卢阿普拉的渔业、森林和林地都无法可持续地养活人们。因此，作者认为传统实践方式无法为人口提供充足的支持，这与选项B的表述一致。","options":["They can supply the nutrition that people need.","They are not capable of providing adequate support to the population.","They are productive systems that need no more improving.","They will be easily modified in the future."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60085","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 13\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in the box 13 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"60076","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nComplete the sentences below with words taken from the passage. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>1</strong> In Luapula land allocation is in accordance with <strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"60077","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nComplete the sentences below with words taken from the passage. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>2</strong> The citemene system provides the land with <strong class=\"source-blank\">[2] ____</strong> where crops are planted.</p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"60078","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nComplete the sentences below with words taken from the passage. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>3</strong> During the second season, the last planted crop is <strong class=\"source-blank\">[3] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"60079","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nComplete the sentences below with words taken from the passage. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>4</strong> Under suitable conditions, fruit trees are planted near <strong class=\"source-blank\">[4] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"60080","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nClassify the following items with the correct description. Write your answers in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.\nA Fish\nB Oxen\nC Goats","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> Fish&nbsp;</p><p><strong>B</strong> Oxen&nbsp;</p><p><strong>C</strong> Goats&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-top: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>5 </strong>be used in some unusual occasions, such as celebrations. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[5] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"60081","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-12\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 9-12 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>People rarely use animals to cultivate the land.</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"60082","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-12\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 9-12 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>When it is a busy time, children usually took part in the labor force.</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"60083","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-12\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 9-12 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The local residents eat goats on a regular time.</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"60084","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9-12\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 9-12 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Though citemene has been a sophisticated system, it could not provide enough protein.</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"60085","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 13\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in the box 13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is the writer’s opinion about the traditional ways of practices?</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Traditional Farming System in Africa&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>By tradition land in Luapula is not owned by individuals, but as in many other parts of Africa is allocated by the headman or head woman of a village to people of either sex, according to need. Since land is generally prepared by hand, one ulupwa cannot take on a very large area; in this sense, the land has not been a limiting resource over large parts of the province. The situation has already changed near the main townships, and there has long been a scarcity of land for cultivation in the Valley. In these areas registered ownership patterns are becoming prevalent.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Most of the traditional cropping in Luapula, as in the Bemba area to the east, is based on citemene, a system whereby crops are grown on the ashes of tree branches. As a rule, entire trees are not felled but are pollarded so that they can regenerate. Branches are cut over an area of varying size early in the dry season and stacked to dry over a rough circle about a fifth to a tenth of the pollarded area. The wood is fired before the rains and in the first year planted with the African cereal finger millet (Eleusine coracane).&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>During the second season, and possibly for a few seasons more the area is planted to variously mixed combinations of annuals such as maize, pumpkins (Telfiria occidentalis) and other cucurbits, sweet potatoes, groundnuts, Phaseolus beans and various leafy vegetables, grown with a certain amount of rotation. The diverse sequence ends with vegetable cassava, which is often planted into the developing last-but-one crop as a relay.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Richards (1969) observed that the practice of citemene entails a definite division of labour between men and women. A man stakes out a plot in an unobtrusive manner since it is considered provocative towards one’s neighbours to mark boundaries in an explicit way. The dangerous work of felling branches is the men’s province and involves much pride. Branches are stacked by the women and fired by the men. Formerly women and men cooperated in the planting work, but the harvesting was always done by the women. At the beginning of the cycle little weeding is necessary, since the firing of the branches effectively destroys weeds. As the cycle progresses weeds increase and nutrients eventually become depleted to a point where further effort with annual crops is judged to be not worthwhile: at this point the cassava is planted, since it can produce a crop on nearly exhausted soil. Thereafter the plot is abandoned, and a new area pollarded for the next citemene cycle.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>When the forest is not available – this is increasingly the case nowadays – various ridging systems (ibala) are built on small areas, to be planted with combinations of maize, beans, groundnuts and sweet potatoes, usually relayed with cassava. These plots are usually tended by women, and provide subsistence. Where their roots have year-round access to water tables mango, guava and oil-palm trees often grow around houses, forming a traditional agroforestry system. In season some of the fruit is sold by the roadside or in local markets.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The margins of dambos are sometimes planted to local varieties of rice during the rainy season, and areas adjacent to vegetables irrigated with water from the dambo during the dry season. The extent of cultivation is very limited, no doubt because the growing of crops under dambo conditions calls for a great deal of skill. Near towns, some of the vegetable produce is sold in local markets.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Fishing has long provided a much-needed protein supplement to the diet of Luapulans, as well as being the one substantial source of cash. Much fish has dried for sale to areas away from the main waterways. The Mweru and Bangweulu Lake Basins are the main areas of year-round fishing, but the Luapula River is also exploited during the latter part of the dry season. Several previously abundant and desirable species, such as the Luapula salmon or mpumbu (Labeo altivelis) and pale (Sarotherodon machochir) have all but disappeared from Lake Mweru, apparently due to mismanagement.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Fishing has always been a far more remunerative activity in Luapula that crop husbandry. A fisherman may earn more in a week than a bean or maize grower in a whole season. I sometimes heard claims that the relatively high earnings to be obtained from fishing induced an ‘easy come, easy go’ outlook among Luapulanmen. On the other hand, someone who secures good but erratic earnings may feel that their investment in economically productive activity is not worthwhile because Luapulans fail to cooperate well in such activities. Besides, a fisherman with spare cash will find little in the way of working equipment to spend his money on. Better spend one’s money in the bars and have a good time!&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>I&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Only small numbers of cattle or oxen are kept in the province owing to the prevalence of the tsetse fly. For the few herds, the dambos provide subsistence grazing during the dry season. The absence of animal draft power greatly limits peoples’ ability to plough and cultivate land: a married couple can rarely manage to prepare by hand-hoeing. Most people keep freely roaming chickens and goats. These act as a reserve for bartering, but may also be occasionally slaughtered for ceremonies or for entertaining important visitors. These animals are not a regular part of most peoples’ diet.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Citemene has been an ingenious system for providing people with seasonal production of high-quality cereals and vegetables in regions of acid, heavily leached soils. Nutritionally, the most serious deficiency was that of protein. This could at times be alleviated when fish was available, provided that cultivators lived near the Valley and could find the means of bartering for dried fish. The citemene/fishing system was well adapted to the ecology of the miombo regions and sustainable for long periods, but only as long as the human population densities stayed at low levels. Although population densities are still much lower than in several countries of South-East Asia, neither the fisheries nor the forests and woodlands of Luapula are capable, with unmodified traditional practices, of supporting the people in a sustainable manner. Overall, people must learn to intensify and diversify their productive systems while yet ensuring that these systems will remain productive in the future when even more people will need food. Increasing overall production of food, though a vast challenge in itself, will not be enough, however. At the same time, storage and distribution systems must allow everyone accesses to at least a moderate share of the total.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8231&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8246","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Antarctica – In From The Cold?","book":"阅读还原集Vol.14","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.14 · Test 2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8246:60177:14","type":"choice","text":"14 The example of research on weather prediction on agriculture","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Recent work is showing that the temperature of the ocean may be a better predictor of rainfall in Australia than is the pressure difference between Darwin and Tahiti – the Southern Oscillation Index. By receiving more accurate predictions, graziers in northern Queensland are able to avoid overstocking in years when rainfall will be poor. Not only does this limit their losses but it prevents serious pasture degradation that may take decades to repair.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是农业气象预测的研究案例出现在哪一段。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"research on weather prediction on agriculture\"可以定位到D段中关于海洋温度预测澳大利亚降雨的内容。\n解题思路：D段中提到了，最新研究表明，相较于达尔文与塔希提之间的气压差（即南方涛动指数），海洋温度可能是预测澳大利亚降雨情况的更可靠指标。通过获取更精准的预测数据，昆士兰州北部的牧民得以在降雨量不足的年份避免过度放牧。有效减少了经济损失，更避免了可能需要数十年才能修复的牧场严重退化问题。与题目相对应，因此，答案是D。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"60177","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-F. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8246:60177:15","type":"choice","text":"15 Antarctic sea ice brings life back to the world oceans’ vitality.","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Recent research has shown that as fresh sea ice forms, it is continuously stripped away by the wind and maybe blown up to 90km in a single day. Since only freshwater freezes into ice, the water that remains becomes increasingly salty and dense, sinking until it spills over the continental shelf. Coldwater carries more oxygen than warm water, so when it rises, well into the northern hemisphere, it reoxygenates and revitalises the ocean.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段落提到了南极海冰给海洋带来活力。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"Antarctic sea ice\"和\"life back to the world oceans’ vitality\"，在文章中寻找相关句子。\n解题思路：原文F段后半段提到，随着新海冰的形成，它会持续被风力剥离，单日可能被吹离原地达90公里。由于只有淡水能结冰，残留的海水会逐渐变得咸而密，最终沉入海底直至漫过大陆架。冷水比温水携带更多氧气，当它上涌至北半球深处时，能重新为海洋注入氧气，使其焕发活力。这句话表明南极海冰对海洋的活力有重要影响，与题目信息一致。因此，答案为F。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"60177","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-F. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8246:60177:16","type":"choice","text":"16 A food chain that influences the animals living pattern based on Antarctic fresh sea ice.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Antarctic krill – the small shrimp-like crustaceans that are the staple diet for baleen whales, penguins, some seals, flighted sea birds and many fish – breed well in years when sea ice is extensive and poorly when it is not. Many species of baleen whales and flighted sea birds migrate between the hemispheres and when the krill are less abundant they do not thrive.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落提到。由于南极海冰，从而影响动物生活模式的食物链。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"food chain\"、\"animals living pattern\"和\"Antarctic fresh sea ice\"可以定位到E段，该段提到了南极磷虾（Antarctic krill）作为多种动物的食物来源，并且它们的繁殖情况与海冰的多少有关，进而影响这些动物的生存状况。\n解题思路：E段详细描述了南极磷虾在食物链中的重要性，在海冰覆盖范围较广的年份繁殖良好，反之则繁殖不佳。许多须鲸和飞禽海鸟物种在南北半球之间迁徙，当磷虾数量减少时，它们的生存状况就会受到影响。影响到依赖磷虾为食的动物的生活模式。这与题目要求的信息吻合，因此E段是正确答案。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"60177","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-F. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8246:60177:17","type":"choice","text":"17 The explanation of how atmosphere pressure above Antarctica can impose an effect on global climate change.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The slow break-up of the super-continent Gondwana with the northward movements of Africa, South America, India and Australia eventually created enough space around Antarctica for the development of an Antarctic Circumpolar Current (ACC), that flowed from west to east under the influence of the prevailing westerly winds. Antarctica cooled, its vegetation perished, glaciation began and the continent took on its present-day appearance. Today the ice that overlies the bedrock is up to 4km thick, and surface temperatures as low as -89.2℃ have been recorded. The icy blast that howls over the ice cap and out to sea – the so-called katabatic wind – can reach 300 km/hr, creating fearsome wind-chill effects.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段解释了南极洲上空的气压如何对全球气候变化产生影响。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"atmosphere pressure\"和\"global climate change\"定位答案。在C段中，提到了\"Antarctic Circumpolar Current (ACC)\"和\"prevailing westerly winds\"，这些都与大气压力和全球气候变化有关。\n解题思路：段落C中，原文描述了南极环流（ACC）的形成，这个环流是由盛行的西风带（这是一个大规模的大气压力系统和风场）驱动的。这个环流的形成直接导致了南极的冷却、冰川化，并塑造了它现今的面貌，身就是南极上空的大气环流（由压力差驱动）导致区域性乃至全球性气候发生根本性变化（从一个温暖的超大陆到冰封的南极洲）。因此，C段包含了题目的内容。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"60177","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-F. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8246:60177:18","type":"choice","text":"18 Antarctica was once thought to be a forgotten and insignificant continent.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The image was one of a place removed from everyday reality, of a place with no apparent value to anyone.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问“南极洲曾经是一个被遗忘且无足轻重的大洲”这一信息出现在哪个段落。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"once thought to be a forgotten and insignificant continent\"定位到文章中描述南极洲早期形象的句子。\n解题思路：原文A段描述了一个世纪前人们对南极洲的印象——它是一个远离现实、没有价值的地方，与题干中的描述完全吻合。因此，答案为A。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"60177","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-F. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8246:60178:19","type":"choice","text":"Globally, mass Antarctica’s size and 19 ____ influence climate change.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Scientific research during the past half-century has revealed – and continues to reveal – that Antarctica’s great mass and low temperature exert a major influence on climate and ocean circulation, factors which influence the lives of millions of people all over the globe.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问南极洲的巨大质量和影响力如何导致全球气候变化。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"Antarctica’s size and influence climate change\"定位到B段，该段提到南极洲的巨大质量和低温对气候和洋流有重大影响。\n解题思路：原文明确指出南极洲的低温（temperature）是影响气候的关键因素之一，因此答案为D。","options":["Antarctic Circumpolar Current (ACC)","katabatic winds","rainfall","temperature","glaciers","pressure"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"60178","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 19-21\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8246:60178:20","type":"choice","text":"20 ____ is contributory to western wind","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The slow break-up of the super-continent Gondwana with the northward movements of Africa, South America, India and Australia eventually created enough space around Antarctica for the development of an Antarctic Circumpolar Current (ACC), that flowed from west to east under the influence of the prevailing westerly winds.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是什么会对西风起作用。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的“western wind”定位到C段中提到的“prevailing westerly winds”，这是与西风相关的关键信息。\n解题思路：原文中C段提到，冈瓦纳大陆的缓慢分裂，以及非洲、南美洲、印度和澳大利亚向北移动，最终在南极洲周围创造了足够的空间，形成了南极环流（ACC），在盛行西风的影响下，从西向东流动。因此可以确定南极绕极流（ACC）的形成与西风有关，而南极绕极流的存在反过来也影响和维持这种风与海洋环流系统的稳定，使得西风带系统得以维持和加强。根据题目要求，选择A作为答案。","options":["Antarctic Circumpolar Current (ACC)","katabatic winds","rainfall","temperature","glaciers","pressure"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"60178","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 19-21\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8246:60178:21","type":"choice","text":"Southern Oscillation Index based on air pressure can predict 21 ____ in Australia.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Recent work is showing that the temperature of the ocean may be a better predictor of rainfall in Australia than is the pressure difference between Darwin and Tahiti – the Southern Oscillation Index.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“南方涛动指数，即达尔文与塔希提之间的气压差，可以预测澳大利亚的什么”。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“Southern Oscillation Index”和“air pressure”定位到D段，找到相关句子。\n解题思路：最新研究表明，相较于达尔文与塔希提之间的气压差（即南方涛动指数），海洋温度可能更准确地预测澳大利亚的降雨情况。因此答案为rainfall，降雨情况。","options":["Antarctic Circumpolar Current (ACC)","katabatic winds","rainfall","temperature","glaciers","pressure"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"60178","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 19-21\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8246:60179:22","type":"choice","text":"In paragraph B, the author wants to tell which of the following truth about the Antarctic?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Although physically Antarctica is no closer and probably no warmer, and to spend time there still demands a dedication not seen in ordinary life, the continent and its surrounding ocean are increasingly seen to an integral part of Planet Earth, and a key component in the Earth System... Scientific research during the past half-century has revealed – and continues to reveal – that Antarctica’s great mass and low temperature exert a major influence on climate and ocean circulation, factors which influence the lives of millions of people all over the globe.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问在B段中，作者想要说明关于南极洲的哪个事实。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"paragraph B\"定位到B段，重点阅读段落中的关键句，特别是描述南极洲地位和作用的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到南极洲和其周围海洋被视为地球的一个不可分割的部分，并且是地球系统的一个关键组成部分。进一步说明，过去半个世纪的科学研究揭示南极洲的巨大规模和低温对全球气候和洋流有重大影响，这些因素影响着全球数百万人的生活。这些内容与选项C\"展示它是地球的核心及其对全球气候和洋流的重要性\"完全一致，因此选项C是正确答案。其他选项要么在原文中没有提及，要么与原文内容不符。","options":["To show Antarctica has been a central topic of global warming in Mass media","To illustrate its huge sea ice brings food to million lives to places in the world","To show it is the heart and its significance to the global climate and current","To illustrate it locates in the central spot on Earth geographically"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60179","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet."},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8246:60180:23","type":"choice","text":"Why do Australian farmers keep an eye on the Antarctic ocean temperature?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：By receiving more accurate predictions, graziers in northern Queensland are able to avoid overstocking in years when rainfall will be poor. Not only does this limit their losses but it prevents serious pasture degradation that may take decades to repair.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问澳大利亚农民关注南极海洋温度的原因是什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"Australian farmers\"和\"Antarctic ocean temperature\"定位到D段后半部分，该段提到农民通过更准确的预测避免过度放牧，从而减少经济损失和草地退化。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，通过关注南极海洋温度（影响降雨预测），农民可以避免在降雨不足的年份过度放牧，这既限制了经济损失（economic losses），又防止了草地退化（ecological losses），与选项A的描述完全一致。其他选项B、C、D均未在原文中提及。","options":["To help farmers reduce their economic or ecological losses","To retrieve grassland decreased in the overgrazing process","To prevent animal from dying","To provide fertilizer for the grassland"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60180","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet."},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8246:60181:24","type":"choice","text":"What is the final effect of katabatic winds?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：During winter, the howling katabatics sometimes scour the ice off patches of the sea’s surface leaving large ice-locked lagoons, or ‘polynyas’. Recent research has shown that as fresh sea ice forms, it is continuously stripped away by the wind and maybe blown up to 90km in a single day.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问重力风的最终影响是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的重力风定位到F段，该段描述了重力风的作用。\n解题思路：段落F中，原文明确描述了重力风的作用过程：当新的海冰形成时，风力会持续剥离冰层，并且一天之内可以被吹出90公里远。这个过程的结果就是将新形成的冰， 从近岸区域吹走，带入更广阔的南部海洋中。这与选项C描述完全一致。因此，选择C。","options":["To increase the moving speed of ocean current","To increase salt level near the ocean surface","To bring fresh ice into southern oceans","To pile up the mountainous ice cap respected by mariners"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60181","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet."},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8246:60182:25","type":"choice","text":"The break of the continental shelf is due to the","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Since only freshwater freezes into ice, the water that remains becomes increasingly salty and dense, sinking until it spills over the continental shelf.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问大陆架断裂的原因是什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"continental shelf\"和\"break\"定位到F段末句，该句描述了海水变咸变密并沉到大陆架的过程。\n解题思路：原文明确提到海水因结冰失去淡水而\"becomes increasingly salty and dense\"（盐度和密度增加），然后\"spilling over the continental shelf\"（溢出大陆架），这直接对应选项A的\"盐和密度增加\"。其他选项B的\"盐和密度减少\"、C的\"全球变暖导致温度上升\"、D的\"淡水冰融化到海水中\"均与原文描述相反或无关。因此答案为A。","options":["salt and density increase.","salt and density decrease.","global warming resulting in a rising temperature.","fresh ice melting into ocean water."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60182","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet."},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8246:60183:26","type":"choice","text":"The decrease in the number of Whales and seabirds is due to","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Antarctic krill – the small shrimp-like crustaceans that are the staple diet for baleen whales, penguins, some seals, flighted sea birds and many fish – breed well in years when sea ice is extensive and poorly when it is not. Many species of baleen whales and flighted sea birds migrate between the hemispheres and when the krill are less abundant they do not thrive.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问鲸鱼和海鸟数量减少的原因。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"Whales and seabirds\"定位到E段后半部分，提到鲸鱼和海鸟的数量与krill（磷虾）的丰度有关。\n解题思路：原文明确指出磷虾是鲸鱼和海鸟的主要食物来源，在海冰覆盖范围广的年份繁殖良好，反之则繁殖不佳。许多须鲸和海鸟会在南北半球之间迁徙，当磷虾数量减少时，它们的繁殖也会受到影响。因此，鲸鱼和海鸟数量减少是因为海冰减少导致食物来源（磷虾）减少，对应选项C。其他选项A、B、D在原文中均未提及。","options":["killers whales are more active around.","sea birds are affected by high sea level salty.","less sea ice reduces the productivity of food source.","seals fail to reproduce babies."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60183","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"60177","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-F. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>14 </strong>The example of research on weather prediction on agriculture <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"60178","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 19-21\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap.","html":"<p><strong>A </strong>Antarctic Circumpolar Current (ACC)&nbsp;</p><p><strong>B</strong> katabatic winds&nbsp;</p><p><strong>C</strong> rainfall&nbsp;</p><p><strong>D</strong> temperature&nbsp;</p><p><strong>E </strong>glaciers&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>F </strong>pressure&nbsp;</p><p><strong>19 </strong>Globally, mass Antarctica’s size and influence climate change.<strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"60179","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>In paragraph B, the author wants to tell which of the following truth about the Antarctic?</strong></p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"60180","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Why do Australian farmers keep an eye on the Antarctic ocean temperature?</strong></p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"60181","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is the final effect of katabatic winds?</strong></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"60182","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>The break of the continental shelf is due to the</strong></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"60183","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>The decrease in the number of Whales and seabirds is due to</strong></p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Antarctica – In From The Cold?</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>A little over a century ago, men of the ilk of Scott, Shackleton and Mawson battled against Antarctica’s blizzards, cold and deprivation. In the name of Empire and in an age of heroic deeds they created an image of Antarctica that was to last well into the 20th century – an image of remoteness, hardship, bleakness and isolation that was the province of only the most courageous of men. The image was one of a place removed from everyday reality, of a place with no apparent value to anyone.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>As we enter the 21st century, our perception of Antarctica has changed. Although physically Antarctica is no closer and probably no warmer, and to spend time there still demands a dedication not seen in ordinary life, the continent and its surrounding ocean are increasingly seen to an integral part of Planet Earth, and a key component in the Earth System. Is this because the world seems a little smaller these days, shrunk by TV and tourism, or is it because Antarctica really does occupy a central spot on Earth’s mantle? Scientific research during the past half-century has revealed – and continues to reveal – that Antarctica’s great mass and low temperature exert a major influence on climate and ocean circulation, factors which influence the lives of millions of people all over the globe.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Antarctica was not always cold. The slow break-up of the super-continent Gondwana with the northward movements of Africa, South America, India and Australia eventually created enough space around Antarctica for the development of an Antarctic Circumpolar Current (ACC), that flowed from west to east under the influence of the prevailing westerly winds. Antarctica cooled, its vegetation perished, glaciation began and the continent took on its present-day appearance. Today the ice that overlies the bedrock is up to 4km thick, and surface temperatures as low as -89.2℃ have been recorded. The icy blast that howls over the ice cap and out to sea – the so-called katabatic wind – can reach 300 km/hr, creating fearsome wind-chill effects.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Out of this extreme environment come some powerful forces that reverberate around the world. The Earth’s rotation, coupled to the generation of cells of low pressure off the Antarctic coast, would allow Astronauts a view of Antarctica that is as beautiful as it is awesome. Spinning away to the northeast, the cells grow and deepen, whipping up the Southern Ocean into the mountainous seas so respected by mariners. Recent work is showing that the temperature of the ocean may be a better predictor of rainfall in Australia than is the pressure difference between Darwin and Tahiti – the Southern Oscillation Index. By receiving more accurate predictions, graziers in northern Queensland are able to avoid overstocking in years when rainfall will be poor. Not only does this limit their losses but it prevents serious pasture degradation that may take decades to repair. CSIRO is developing this as a prototype forecasting system, but we can confidently predict that as we know more about the Antarctic and the Southern Ocean we will be able to enhance and extend our predictive ability.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The ocean’s surface temperature results from the interplay between deep-water temperature, air temperature and ice. Each winter between 4 and 19 million square km of sea ice form, locking up huge quantities of heat close to the continent. Only now can we start to unravel the influence of sea ice on the weather that is experienced in southern Australia. But in another way, the extent of sea ice extends its influence far beyond Antarctica. Antarctic krill – the small shrimp-like crustaceans that are the staple diet for baleen whales, penguins, some seals, flighted sea birds and many fish – breed well in years when sea ice is extensive and poorly when it is not. Many species of baleen whales and flighted sea birds migrate between the hemispheres and when the krill are less abundant they do not thrive.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The circulatory system of the world’s oceans is like a huge conveyor belt, moving water and dissolved minerals and nutrients from one hemisphere to the other, and from the ocean’s abyssal depths to the surface. The ACC is the longest current in the world and has the largest flow. Through it, the deep flows of the Atlantic, Indian and Pacific Oceans are joined to form part of single global thermohaline circulation. During winter, the howling katabatics sometimes scour the ice off patches of the sea’s surface leaving large ice-locked lagoons, or ‘polynyas’. Recent research has shown that as fresh sea ice forms, it is continuously stripped away by the wind and maybe blown up to 90km in a single day. Since only freshwater freezes into ice, the water that remains becomes increasingly salty and dense, sinking until it spills over the continental shelf. Coldwater carries more oxygen than warm water, so when it rises, well into the northern hemisphere, it reoxygenates and revitalises the ocean. The state of the northern oceans and their biological productivity owe much to what happens in the Antarctic.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8246&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8247","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Environmentally Friendly Vehicle","book":"阅读还原集Vol.14","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.14 · Test 2 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8247:60184:27","type":"choice","text":"27 What does the author think of the factory in Sonora in Mexico where the ford fusion is manufactured?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In response, automakers developed electric models, including the Chrysler TEVan, Ford Ranger EV pickup truck, GM EV1 and S10 EV pickup, Honda EV Plus hatchback, Nissan lithium-battery Altra EV miniwagon and Toyota RAV4 EV. Ford Fusion is manufactured at Ford’s Hermosillo Stamping & Assembly plant, located in Sonora Mexico. I thought going green was supposed to provide the U.S. with more jobs.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问作者对在墨西哥Sonora工厂制造福特Fusion的看法。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"factory in Sonora in Mexico where the ford fusion is manufactured\"定位到A段中\"Ford Fusion is manufactured at Ford’s Hermosillo Stamping & Assembly plant, located in Sonora Mexico\"这句话。\n解题思路：原文中作者提到\"我认为环保转型能为美国创造更多就业机会\"，这与选项B\"随着消费者意识的转变，美国的就业机会会更多\"意思一致。作者认为环保应该带来就业，但并未直接说明消费者意识改变，选项B是对原文的合理推断。选项A、C、D在原文中均未提及。","options":["The factory should be helpful in the US soil business.","Employment of US will be created as consumers change their awareness.","More competitive cars will be introduced into the market.","This issue is hard to give a predict."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60184","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8247:60185:28","type":"choice","text":"28 In the 1990s, what dropped in America for environmentally friendly vehicles?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Throughout the 1990s, the appeal of fuel-efficient or environmentally friendly cars declined among Americans, who instead favored sport utility vehicles, which were affordable to operate despite their poor fuel efficiency thanks to lower gasoline prices.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问在20世纪90年代，美国人对于环保型车辆哪方面下降了。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"1990s\"和\"environmentally friendly vehicles\"定位到D段首句，找到\"declined\"一词，对应\"dropped\"。\n解题思路：原文明确提到\"the appeal of fuel-efficient or environmentally friendly cars declined\"，即环保型车辆的吸引力下降，对应选项B\"attractiveness\"。其他选项在原文中未提及或与原文不符。","options":["Production.","Attractiveness.","Announcement.","Expectation."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60185","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8247:60186:29","type":"choice","text":"29 What did GM notably send to engineering schools and museums?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：GM famously de-activated the few EV1s that were donated to engineering schools and museums.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问GM向工程学校和博物馆捐赠了什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"GM\"和\"engineering schools and museums\"定位到C段。\n解题思路：原文明确提到GM向工程学校和博物馆捐赠了\"EV1\"，因此正确答案是A。","options":["EV 1","CARB","RAV4","MINI E"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60186","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8247:60187:30","type":"choice","text":"30 Nissan and GM high-level leaders declared the real reason for the popularity of Roaster is its","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Senior leaders at several large automakers, including Nissan and General Motors, have stated that the Roadster was a catalyst which demonstrated that there is pent-up consumer demand for more efficient vehicles.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问日产和通用的高层领导认为特斯拉Roadster受欢迎的真正原因是什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Nissan and GM high-level leaders\"和\"Roadster\"定位到H段后半部分，找到他们关于Roadster的陈述。\n解题思路：原文明确提到日产和通用的高层认为Roadster起到催化剂的作用，表明消费者对更高效能车辆存在着强烈的需求。对应选项C\"bursting demand\"（爆发性需求）。其他选项A、B、D在原文中均未提及。","options":["legendary concert.","huge population in the market.","bursting demand.","artistic design."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60187","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8247:60188:31","type":"choice","text":"31 Some automakers mislead and suppressed the real demand for electric cars of keeping profit in a certain market by luring the want of CARB.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The automakers were accused of pandering to the wishes of CARB in order to continue to be allowed to sell cars in the lucrative Californian market, while failing to adequately promote their electric vehicles in order to create the impression that the consumers were not interested in the cars, all the while joining oil industry lobbyists in vigorously protesting CARB’s mandate.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是一些汽车制造商是否通过迎合CARB，来误导和压制对电动汽车的真实需求，以维持某个市场的利润，该说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"automakers\"、\"mislead and suppressed\"、\"real demand for electric cars\"、\"keeping profit in a certain market\"和\"luring the want of CARB\"。通过这些关键词可以在B段找到对应的句子。\n解题思路：原文中提到汽车制造商迎合CARB，以继续在加利福尼亚这个利润丰厚的市场上销售汽车，同时未能充分推广他们的电动汽车，以制造消费者对这些汽车不感兴趣的印象。这与题目中的描述一致，因此可以判断题目说法与文章信息一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60188","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8247:60189:32","type":"choice","text":"32 Toyota started to sell 328 RAV4-EVs for taking up the market share.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：After public protests by EV drivers’ groups upset by the repossession of their cars, Toyota offered the last 328 RAV4-EVs for sale to the general public during six months, up until November 22, 2002.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“丰田开始销售328辆RAV4-EV是为了抢占市场份额”，该说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“Toyota”、“328 RAV4-EVs”和“taking up the market share”定位到C段。\n解题思路：原文提到丰田迫于消费者抗议，不得不继续销售RAV4-EV一段时间，并不是为了抢占市场份额。因此，题目中的“taking up the market share”这一说法与原文矛盾，答案应为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60189","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8247:60190:33","type":"choice","text":"33 In some countries, American auto-makers would like to grab the opportunity to earn money in the vehicle of bigger litre engine cars rather than smaller ones.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：American automakers chose to focus their product lines around the truck-based vehicles, which enjoyed larger profit margins than the smaller cars which were preferred in places like Europe or Japan.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是在一些国家，美国汽车制造商更喜欢抓住机会赚取大排量汽车的钱，而不是小排量汽车，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"American auto-makers\"、\"bigger litre engine cars\"、\"smaller ones\"，通过这些关键词定位到D段。\n解题思路：D段提到，美国汽车制造商选择将产品线集中在“基于卡车的车辆”（即SUV等大型车）上，因为这些车比“欧洲或日本等地偏爱的小型车”利润更高。这描述了美国制造商在本土市场的整体策略。然而，文中没有信息表明他们“在其它国家”（即美国以外的“某些国家”）也采取了或偏好这种策略。题目信息在原文基础上进行了地点范围的推断，但缺乏直接依据，因此答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60190","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8247:60191:34","type":"choice","text":"34 Hybrids cars are superior vehicles that combine the impression of an environmental friend electric power engine and a lower price in the unit sale.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Hybrids, which featured a combined gasoline and electric powertrain, were seen as a balance, offering an environmentally friendly image and improved fuel economy, without being hindered by the low range of electric vehicles, albeit at an increased price over comparable gasoline cars.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问混合动力汽车是否是更优质的车辆，不仅有环保型电动发动机，又拥有更低的单价。这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"Hybrids cars\"、\"environmental friendly\"、\"lower price\"定位到G段。\n解题思路：原文提到混合动力车结合了汽油和电力驱动系统，给人一种环保的印象，又能提高燃油经济性，又不会受到电动汽车续航里程低的阻碍，尽管价格比同类汽油车更高，与题干中\"lower price\"矛盾。因此题干信息与原文不符，答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60191","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8247:60192:35","type":"choice","text":"35 an inspiration to make an effort to produce hybrid cars is to cope with economic difficulties result from a declining market for General Motors.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：GM Vice Chairman Bob Lutz said in 2007 that the Tesla Roadster inspired him to push GM to develop the Chevrolet Volt, a plug-in hybrid sedan prototype that aims to reverse years of dwindling market share and massive financial losses for America’s largest automaker.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问“推动通用汽车生产混合动力汽车的原因之一，是应对市场萎缩带来的经济困境”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过“inspiration to make an effort to produce hybrid cars”和“economic difficulties result from a declining market for General Motors”定位到H段中提到Tesla Roadster作为灵感推动GM开发Chevrolet Volt的部分。\n解题思路：H段明确提到Tesla Roadster是推动GM开发Chevrolet Volt的灵感来源，而Chevrolet Volt的目标是“reverse years of dwindling market share and massive financial losses”（扭转市场份额下降和巨额财务损失）。这与题目中“应对经济困难”和“市场份额下降”完全一致，因此答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"60192","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8247:60193:36","type":"choice","text":"A 36 ____ was firstly introduced by Car maker Toyota in 1995. Then it started for sale in 1997 with a new first-generation model.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1995, Toyota debuted a hybrid concept car at the Tokyo Motor Show, with testing following a year later. The first Prius, model NHW10, went on sale on December 10, 1997.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“在1995年首先由丰田汽车制造商引入的是什么”，并提到1997年第一款第一代车型开始销售。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的时间点“1995”和“1997”以及关键词“Toyota”定位到E段，找到丰田在1995年首次推出的车型。\n解题思路：根据E段第一句“Toyota debuted a hybrid concept car at the Tokyo Motor Show”可知，丰田在1995年首次推出的是一款混合动力概念车（concept car），而题目中空格提示需要填写一个名词，因此“concept car”是正确答案。","options":["electric car","United Kingdom","market","concept car","longer distances","Emissions","battery","consumers","gasoline-electricity","inspiration","cargo space","orientation"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L"],"sourceGroupId":"60193","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-L, below. Write the correct letter, A-L, in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8247:60193:37","type":"choice","text":"Not only in Japan but included other countries such as 37 ____ and Oceania in which the Prius was imported to.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：though it has been imported privately to at least the United Kingdom, Australia, and New Zealand.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是普锐斯除了在日本销售外，还被进口到了哪些国家，特别是题目中提到了“Oceania”（大洋洲），需要找出具体的国家名称。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“imported to”和“Oceania”定位到E段中描述普锐斯被进口到其他国家的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到普锐斯被私人进口到“the United Kingdom, Australia, and New Zealand”，其中“New Zealand”和“Australia”属于“Oceania”（大洋洲）地区。题目中需要填写一个国家名称，而“B”对应的原文是“United Kingdom”（英国），因此答案为B。","options":["electric car","United Kingdom","market","concept car","longer distances","Emissions","battery","consumers","gasoline-electricity","inspiration","cargo space","orientation"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L"],"sourceGroupId":"60193","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-L, below. Write the correct letter, A-L, in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8247:60193:38","type":"choice","text":"The first-generation Prius was the first car in mass production which is powered by 38 ____ .","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The first-generation Prius, at its launch, became the world’s first mass-produced gasoline-electric hybrid car.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问第一代普锐斯是第一款以什么为动力的量产汽车。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"first-generation Prius\"和\"first car in mass production\"定位到E段中的\"The first-generation Prius, at its launch, became the world’s first mass-produced gasoline-electric hybrid car\"。\n解题思路：原文明确指出第一代普锐斯是世界上第一款量产的汽油-电力混合动力汽车，因此答案为\"gasoline-electric\"，对应选项I。","options":["electric car","United Kingdom","market","concept car","longer distances","Emissions","battery","consumers","gasoline-electricity","inspiration","cargo space","orientation"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L"],"sourceGroupId":"60193","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-L, below. Write the correct letter, A-L, in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8247:60193:39","type":"choice","text":"The model NHW10 was designed by a winning Californian designer. The innovated NHW 11 Prius has considerably higher running velocity and 39 ____ than American counterparts.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The NHW11 Prius became more powerful partly to satisfy the higher speeds and longer distances that Americans drive.\n对应段落：F段\n审题： 题目要求完成关于NHW11 Prius车型改进的摘要，说明其运行速度和另一个特性优于美国同类车型。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"NHW11 Prius\", \"higher running velocity\", \"American counterparts\" 定位到文中描述该车型为适应美国市场所做改进的句子。\n解题思路：段落F中，原文明确指出，NHW11普锐斯更强，部分源于满足美国消费者追求更高时速和更长续航的需求。“更长续航”(longer distances) 与题目中“更高时速”(higher running velocity) 是并列关系，共同作为该车型性能提升的方面。因此，空格处应填入“longer distances”。","options":["electric car","United Kingdom","market","concept car","longer distances","Emissions","battery","consumers","gasoline-electricity","inspiration","cargo space","orientation"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L"],"sourceGroupId":"60193","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-L, below. Write the correct letter, A-L, in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8247:60193:40","type":"choice","text":"Still, the load capacity of current Prius version was limited in its 40 ____ .","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：While the larger Prius could seat five, its battery pack restricted cargo space.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是当前普锐斯版本的载货能力有限制，需要填入限制的具体方面。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"load capacity\"（载货能力）和\"limited\"（有限）可以帮助定位到F段中关于普锐斯载货能力的描述。\n解题思路：F段提到\"NHW11 Prius became more powerful partly to satisfy the higher speeds and longer distances that Americans drive\"并解释了其配置升级，随后提到\"The larger Prius could seat five, its battery pack restricted cargo space\"，明确指出电池包限制了载货空间（cargo space）。因此，答案应与\"cargo space\"相关，对应选项中的\"G\"（battery）,属于同义替换，选择G项。","options":["electric car","United Kingdom","market","concept car","longer distances","Emissions","battery","consumers","gasoline-electricity","inspiration","cargo space","orientation"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K","L"],"sourceGroupId":"60193","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-L, below. Write the correct letter, A-L, in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"60184","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>27</strong> What does the author think of the factory in Sonora in Mexico where the ford fusion is manufactured?</p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"60185","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>28</strong> In the 1990s, what dropped in America for environmentally friendly vehicles?</p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"60186","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>29</strong> What did GM notably send to engineering schools and museums?</p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"60187","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-30\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>30</strong> Nissan and GM high-level leaders declared the real reason for the popularity of Roaster is its</p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"60188","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>31</strong> Some automakers mislead and suppressed the real demand for electric cars of keeping profit in a certain market by luring the want of CARB.</p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"60189","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>32</strong> Toyota started to sell 328 RAV4-EVs for taking up the market share.</p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"60190","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>33</strong> In some countries, American auto-makers would like to grab the opportunity to earn money in the vehicle of bigger litre engine cars rather than smaller ones.</p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"60191","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>34</strong> Hybrids cars are superior vehicles that combine the impression of an environmental friend electric power engine and a lower price in the unit sale.</p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"60192","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 31-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE  if the statement is true FALSE  if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>35</strong> an inspiration to make an effort to produce hybrid cars is to cope with economic difficulties result from a declining market for General Motors.</p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"60193","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-L, below. Write the correct letter, A-L, in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>A electric car &nbsp; B United Kingdom &nbsp; C market &nbsp; D concept car \nE longer distances &nbsp; F Emissions &nbsp; G battery &nbsp; H consumers \nl gasoline-electricity &nbsp; J inspiration &nbsp; K cargo space &nbsp; L orientation &nbsp;\nA 36.<strong class=\"source-blank\">[36] ____</strong> was firstly introduced by Car maker Toyota in 1995. Then it started for sale \nin 1997 with a new first-generation model.</p>","firstNumber":36}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Environmentally Friendly Vehicle</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In the early 1990s, the California Air Resources Board (CARB), the government of California’s ‘clean air agency’, began a push for more fuel-efficient, lower-emissions vehicles, with the ultimate goal being a move to zero-emissions vehicles such as electric vehicles. In response, automakers developed electric models, including the Chrysler TEVan, Ford Ranger EV pickup truck, GM EV1 and S10 EV pickup, Honda EV Plus hatchback, Nissan lithium-battery Altra EV miniwagon and Toyota RAV4 EV. Ford Fusion is manufactured at Ford’s Hermosillo Stamping &amp; Assembly plant, located in Sonora Mexico. I thought going green was supposed to provide the U.S. with more jobs.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The automakers were accused of pandering to the wishes of CARB in order to continue to be allowed to sell cars in the lucrative Californian market, while failing to adequately promote their electric vehicles in order to create the impression that the consumers were not interested in the cars, all the while joining oil industry lobbyists in vigorously protesting CARB’s mandate. GM’s program came under particular scrutiny; in an unusual move, consumers were not allowed to purchase EV1s, but were instead asked to sign closed-end leases, meaning that the cars had to be returned to GM at the end of the lease period, with no option to purchase, despite lesser interest in continuing to own the cars. Chrysler, Toyota, and a group of GM dealers sued CARB in Federal court, leading to the eventual neutering of CARB’s ZEV Mandate.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>After public protests by EV drivers’ groups upset by the repossession of their cars, Toyota offered the last 328 RAV4-EVs for sale to the general public during six months, up until November 22, 2002. Almost all other production electric cars were withdrawn from the market and were in some cases seen to have been destroyed by their manufactures. Toyota continues to support the several hundred Toyota RAV4-EV in the hands of the general public and in fleet usage. GM famously de-activated the few EV1s that were donated to engineering schools and museums.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Throughout the 1990s, the appeal of fuel-efficient or environmentally friendly cars declined among Americans, who instead favored sport utility vehicles, which were affordable to operate despite their poor fuel efficiency thanks to lower gasoline prices. American automakers chose to focus their product lines around the truck-based vehicles, which enjoyed larger profit margins than the smaller cars which were preferred in places like Europe or Japan. In 1999, the Honda Insight hybrid car became the first hybrid to be sold in North America since the little-known Woods hybrid of 1917.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In 1995, Toyota debuted a hybrid concept car at the Tokyo Motor Show, with testing following a year later. The first Prius, model NHW10, went on sale on December 10, 1997. It was available only in Japan, though it has been imported privately to at least the United Kingdom, Australia, and New Zealand. The first-generation Prius, at its launch, became the world’s first mass-produced gasoline-electric hybrid car. The NHW10 Prius styling originated from California designers, who were selected over competing designs from other Toyota design studios.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In the United States, the NHW11 was the first Prius to be sold. The Prius was marketed between the smaller Corolla and the larger Camry. The published retail price of the car was US$19,995. The NHW11 Prius became more powerful partly to satisfy the higher speeds and longer distances that Americans drive. Air conditioning and electric power steering were standard equipment. The vehicle was the second mass-produced hybrid on the American market, after the two-seat Honda Insight. While the larger Prius could seat five, its battery pack restricted cargo space.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Hybrids, which featured a combined gasoline and electric powertrain, were seen as a balance, offering an environmentally friendly image and improved fuel economy, without being hindered by the low range of electric vehicles, albeit at an increased price over comparable gasoline cars. Sales were poor, the lack of interest attributed to the car’s small size and the lack of necessity for a fuel-efficient car at the time. The 2000s energy crisis brought renewed interest in hybrid and electric cars. In America, sales of the Toyota Prius jumped, and a variety of automakers followed suit, releasing hybrid models of their own. Several began to produce new electric car prototypes, as consumers called for cars that would free them from the fluctuations of oil prices.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In 2000, Hybrid Technologies, later renamed Li-ion Motors, started manufacturing electric cars in Mooresville, North Carolina. There has been increasing controversy with Li-ion Motors though due to the ongoing ‘Lemon issues’ regarding their product. And their attempt to cover it up. California electric-car maker Tesla Motors began development in 2004 on the Tesla Roadster, which was first delivered to customers in 2008. The Roadster remained the only highway-capable EV in serial production and available for sale until 2010. Senior leaders at several large automakers, including Nissan and General Motors, have stated that the Roadster was a catalyst which demonstrated that there is pent-up consumer demand for more efficient vehicles. GM Vice Chairman Bob Lutz said in 2007 that the Tesla Roadster inspired him to push GM to develop the Chevrolet Volt, a plug-in hybrid sedan prototype that aims to reverse years of dwindling market share and massive financial losses for America’s largest automaker. In an August 2009 edition of The New Yorker, Lutz was quoted as saying, ‘All the geniuses here at General Motors kept saying lithium-ion technology is 10 years away, and Toyota agreed with us – and boom, along comes Tesla. So I said, “How come some tiny little California startup, run by guys who know nothing about the car business, can do this, and we can’t?” That was the crowbar that helped break up the log jam.’</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8247&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8211","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Museum Blockbuster","book":"阅读还原集Vol.14","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.14 · Test 1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8211:59859:1","type":"choice","text":"1 A reason for changing the exhibition programs","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Maintaining and increasing visitor levels is paramount in the new museology. This requires continued product development. Not only the creation or hiring of blockbuster exhibitions but regular exhibition changes and innovations.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“改变展览项目的原因”。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"changing the exhibition programs\"可以定位到C段中的\"continued product development\"和\"regular exhibition changes and innovations\"。\n解题思路：C段明确提到维持和提高参观者数量是新博物馆学中的重中之重，不仅要策划或引进现象级展览，更要更新常规展览内容，并不断创新。因此，C段包含了改变展览项目的原因。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"59859","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraphs contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8211:59859:2","type":"choice","text":"2 The time people have to wait in a queue in order to enjoy exhibitions","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Here is one of some existing definitions of a blockbuster: Put by Elsen (1984), a blockbuster is a ‘… large scale loan exhibition that people who normally don’t go to museums will stand in line for hours to see …’\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是人们为了享受展览需要排队等待的时间。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词\"queue\"和\"enjoy exhibitions\"可以定位到A段中关于排队看展览的描述。\n解题思路：根据A段中Elsen的定义，人们为了看展览需要排队等待几个小时，因此A段包含了题目所问的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"59859","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraphs contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8211:59859:3","type":"choice","text":"3 Terms people used when referring to the blockbuster","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：However, in literature from both the UK and USA the other words that also start to appear in descriptions of a blockbuster are ‘less scholarly’, ‘non-elitist’ and ‘popularist’.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了人们用来形容现象级展览的词。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“Terms people used when referring to the blockbuster”可以定位到B段，该段提到了“less scholarly”, “non-elitist”和“popularist”这些词语。\n解题思路：根据B段中的句子“in literature from both the UK and USA the other words that also start to appear in descriptions of a blockbuster are ‘less scholarly’, ‘non-elitist’ and ‘popularist’.”，可以确定人们用来形容现象级展览的词有“less scholarly”, “non-elitist”和“popularist”。因此，答案为B。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"59859","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraphs contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8211:59859:4","type":"choice","text":"4 There was some controversy over confining target groups of a blockbuster","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Detractors argue that blockbusters are designed to appeal to the lowest common denominator, while others extol the virtues of encouraging scholars to cooperate on projects and to provide exhibitions that cater for a broad selection of the community rather than an elite sector.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段讲了现象级展览的目标受众群体存在争议。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"controversy\"和\"target groups\"定位到B段。\n解题思路：根据原文中B段的句子，明确指出存在争议，一方认为现象级展览过于迎合大众口味，另一方则鼓励学者合作开展项目、举办面向广大民众，非精英阶层的展览。这与题目中的\"controversy over confining target groups\"相吻合，因此答案为B。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"59859","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraphs contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8211:59860:5","type":"fill","text":"填写第 5 空","answer":"customers/Customers","acceptedAnswers":["customers","Customers"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In addition, the visiting public has become customers rather than visitors, and the skills that are valued in museums, science centres and galleries to keep the new customers coming through the door have changed.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是人们从“参观者”变成了什么角色，需要填写一个名词。\n定位关键信息：题目中的“Instead of being visitors”和“blockbuster exhibitions as well as regular exhibition changes”可以帮助定位到C段第一句，这里提到了人们从“visitors”变成了“customers”。\n解题思路：根据原文C段，“The visiting public has become customers rather than visitors”，可以确定人们从“visitors”参观者变成了“customers”顾客，因此空格处应填“customers”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59860","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8211:59861:6","type":"fill","text":"填写第 6 空","answer":"public relation skills/Public Relation Skills","acceptedAnswers":["public relation skills","Public Relation Skills"],"explanation":"原文答案句：As succinctly summarised in the Economist in 1994 ‘business nous and public relation skills’ were essential requirements for a director, and the ability to compete with other museums to stage travelling exhibitions which draw huge crowds.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是，在一份杂志中总结，商业头脑和什么不仅仅是管理者需具备的素质，也是吸引观众的核心能力。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键词\"Business nous and\"和\"summarized in a magazine\"定位到C段第一句，找到对应的短语\"business nous and public relation skills\"。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到“business nous and public relation skills”是在《经济学人》杂志中总结的，并且这些是管理者的必要条件，也是吸引大量观众的核心能力。因此，空格处应填入\"public relation skills\"公关能力。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59861","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8211:59862:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"museology/Museology/new museology/the new museology/The new museology/New museology","acceptedAnswers":["museology","Museology","new museology","the new museology","The new museology","New museology"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The new museology has resulted in the convergence of museums, the heritage industry, and tourism, profit-making and pleasure-giving.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“什么”促成了博物馆、遗产产业、旅游、盈利和娱乐的结合。\n定位关键信息：题目中的“museums, the heritage industry, tourism, profit-making and pleasure-giving”是定位的关键信息，在D段中可以找到这些词组。\n解题思路：根据D段中的句子“the new museology has resulted in the convergence of museums, the heritage industry, and tourism, profit-making and pleasure-giving”，可以确定答案为“museology”博物馆学，这是导致这些领域结合的新理念或新趋势。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59862","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8211:59863:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"tourist attractions/Tourist Attractions","acceptedAnswers":["tourist attractions","Tourist Attractions"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This has given rise to much debate about the appropriateness of adopting the activities of institutions so that they more closely reflect the priorities of the market place and whether it is appropriate to see museums primarily as tourist attractions.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问将博物馆视为什么存在争议。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"consider museums mainly as\"与原文中的\"see museums primarily as\"对应，定位到D段末句。\n解题思路：原文明确提到\"whether it is appropriate to see museums primarily as tourist attractions\"（将博物馆主要视为旅游景点是否合适），题目中需要填入博物馆可能被主要视为的角色，即\"tourist attractions\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59863","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8211:59864:9-10","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO advantages are mentioned by the writer of the text?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nFor some museums overseas, it may be the money that they need to update parts of their collections or to repair buildings that are in need of attention.（E段 ）\nBlockbusters mean crowds, and crowds are good for the local economy, providing increased employment for shops, hotels, restaurants, the transport industry and retailers.  （G段）\n对应段落：E段和G段\n审题：题目问的是作者在文中提到了哪些关于现象级展览的益处。\n定位关键信息：通过选项A中的关键词“repair architectures”可以定位到E段中提到修复建筑的内容。通过选项D中的关键词“beneficial for the development of local business”可以定位到G段中提到盛事展览对当地经济的好处。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，对于一些国外的博物馆来说，举办现象级展览可以提供资金来修复需要关注的建筑，这与选项A的表述完全一致。原文指出，现象级展览带来人群，而人群对当地经济有利，增加了商店、酒店、餐馆、交通行业和零售商的就业机会，这与选项D的表述完全一致。","options":["To offer sufficient money to repair architectures","To maintain and increase visitor levels","Presenting the mixture in the culture and commerce of art galleries and science centres worldwide","Being beneficial for the development of local business","Being beneficial for the directors"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"59864","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 9-10\nChoose TWO letters A-E. Write your answer in boxes 9-10 on your answer sheet. The list below gives some advantages of a blockbuster.","groupId":"59864-8211:59864:9-10"},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8211:59864:9-10","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO advantages are mentioned by the writer of the text?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nFor some museums overseas, it may be the money that they need to update parts of their collections or to repair buildings that are in need of attention.（E段 ）\nBlockbusters mean crowds, and crowds are good for the local economy, providing increased employment for shops, hotels, restaurants, the transport industry and retailers.  （G段）\n对应段落：E段和G段\n审题：题目问的是作者在文中提到了哪些关于现象级展览的益处。\n定位关键信息：通过选项A中的关键词“repair architectures”可以定位到E段中提到修复建筑的内容。通过选项D中的关键词“beneficial for the development of local business”可以定位到G段中提到盛事展览对当地经济的好处。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，对于一些国外的博物馆来说，举办现象级展览可以提供资金来修复需要关注的建筑，这与选项A的表述完全一致。原文指出，现象级展览带来人群，而人群对当地经济有利，增加了商店、酒店、餐馆、交通行业和零售商的就业机会，这与选项D的表述完全一致。","options":["To offer sufficient money to repair architectures","To maintain and increase visitor levels","Presenting the mixture in the culture and commerce of art galleries and science centres worldwide","Being beneficial for the development of local business","Being beneficial for the directors"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"59864","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 9-10\nChoose TWO letters A-E. Write your answer in boxes 9-10 on your answer sheet. The list below gives some advantages of a blockbuster.","groupId":"59864-8211:59864:9-10"},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8211:59865:11-12-13","type":"choice","text":"Which THREE disadvantages are mentioned by the writer of the text?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nCreating, mounting or hiring blockbusters is exhausting for staff, with the real costs throughout an institution difficult to calculate. (G段)\nHowever, the new museology and the apparent trend towards blockbusters make it likely that museums, art galleries and particularly science centres will be seen as part of the entertainment and tourism industry, rather than as cultural icons deserving of government and philanthropic support. (G段)\nBlockbusters require large capital expenditure, and draw on resources across all branches of an organisation; however, the costs don’t end there. There is a Human Resource Management cost in addition to a measurable ‘real’ dollar cost. (F段)\n对应段落：G段和F段\n审题：题目问的是作者在文中提到了哪些关于“现象级展览的缺点”，需要选出三个。\n定位关键信息：\n1. 通过题目中的\"disadvantages\"（缺点）定位，在文章中寻找负面表述或问题。\n2. 选项B（工作人员因工作量而疲惫）、C（内容更偏向娱乐而非文化输出）、E（需要花费大量投资在专业人员上）分别对应以下句子：\n- B对应G段“Creating, mounting or hiring blockbusters is exhausting for staff”（创建、举办或引进现象级展览会让员工疲惫不堪）。\n- C对应G段“will be seen as part of the entertainment and tourism industry, rather than as cultural icons”（可能被视为娱乐和旅游产业的一部分，而非文化象征）。\n- E对应F段“There is a Human Resource Management cost”（人力资源管理的成本，暗示资源投入问题）。\n解题思路：选项B在G段明确提到“exhausting for staff”（让员工疲惫），与“Workers has become tired of workloads”（工作人员因工作量而疲惫）对应。选项C在G段提到“entertainment and tourism industry, rather than as cultural icons”（娱乐和旅游产业而非文化象征），与“内容更偏向娱乐而非文化”一致。选项E在F段提到“Human Resource Management cost”（人力资源成本），暗示资源投入问题，与“Huge amounts of capital invested in specialists”（大量资本投资于专家）相关。其他选项A、D、F与原文表述不符，A选项在F段最后一句有提到，但是只是类似，意思完全不同。原文说参观者需要选择看哪个，没有提到A选项中说的“犹豫”。D选项在F段提到，虽然选项中的词句和原文基本一样，但是请注意，原文中举这个例子是为了说明“人力资源成本花销大”，D选项只是一个例子，并不是根本缺点。F选项在G段line11出现，但不是缺点，注意原文中这句话后面的“and may lead to creative excellence”也可能激发他们的创造力。","options":["People left hesitated to choose exhibitions.","Workers has become tired of workloads.","The content has become more entertaining rather than cultural.","General labourers are required to perform additional tasks","Huge amounts of capital invested in specialists.","Exposing staff to the fantasies and pressures of the market place."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59865","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nChoose THREE letters A-F. Write your answer in boxes 11-13 on your answer sheet. The list below gives some disadvantages of a blockbuster.","groupId":"59865-8211:59865:11-12-13"},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8211:59865:11-12-13","type":"choice","text":"Which THREE disadvantages are mentioned by the writer of the text?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nCreating, mounting or hiring blockbusters is exhausting for staff, with the real costs throughout an institution difficult to calculate. (G段)\nHowever, the new museology and the apparent trend towards blockbusters make it likely that museums, art galleries and particularly science centres will be seen as part of the entertainment and tourism industry, rather than as cultural icons deserving of government and philanthropic support. (G段)\nBlockbusters require large capital expenditure, and draw on resources across all branches of an organisation; however, the costs don’t end there. There is a Human Resource Management cost in addition to a measurable ‘real’ dollar cost. (F段)\n对应段落：G段和F段\n审题：题目问的是作者在文中提到了哪些关于“现象级展览的缺点”，需要选出三个。\n定位关键信息：\n1. 通过题目中的\"disadvantages\"（缺点）定位，在文章中寻找负面表述或问题。\n2. 选项B（工作人员因工作量而疲惫）、C（内容更偏向娱乐而非文化输出）、E（需要花费大量投资在专业人员上）分别对应以下句子：\n- B对应G段“Creating, mounting or hiring blockbusters is exhausting for staff”（创建、举办或引进现象级展览会让员工疲惫不堪）。\n- C对应G段“will be seen as part of the entertainment and tourism industry, rather than as cultural icons”（可能被视为娱乐和旅游产业的一部分，而非文化象征）。\n- E对应F段“There is a Human Resource Management cost”（人力资源管理的成本，暗示资源投入问题）。\n解题思路：选项B在G段明确提到“exhausting for staff”（让员工疲惫），与“Workers has become tired of workloads”（工作人员因工作量而疲惫）对应。选项C在G段提到“entertainment and tourism industry, rather than as cultural icons”（娱乐和旅游产业而非文化象征），与“内容更偏向娱乐而非文化”一致。选项E在F段提到“Human Resource Management cost”（人力资源成本），暗示资源投入问题，与“Huge amounts of capital invested in specialists”（大量资本投资于专家）相关。其他选项A、D、F与原文表述不符，A选项在F段最后一句有提到，但是只是类似，意思完全不同。原文说参观者需要选择看哪个，没有提到A选项中说的“犹豫”。D选项在F段提到，虽然选项中的词句和原文基本一样，但是请注意，原文中举这个例子是为了说明“人力资源成本花销大”，D选项只是一个例子，并不是根本缺点。F选项在G段line11出现，但不是缺点，注意原文中这句话后面的“and may lead to creative excellence”也可能激发他们的创造力。","options":["People left hesitated to choose exhibitions.","Workers has become tired of workloads.","The content has become more entertaining rather than cultural.","General labourers are required to perform additional tasks","Huge amounts of capital invested in specialists.","Exposing staff to the fantasies and pressures of the market place."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59865","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nChoose THREE letters A-F. Write your answer in boxes 11-13 on your answer sheet. The list below gives some disadvantages of a blockbuster.","groupId":"59865-8211:59865:11-12-13"},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8211:59865:11-12-13","type":"choice","text":"Which THREE disadvantages are mentioned by the writer of the text?","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nCreating, mounting or hiring blockbusters is exhausting for staff, with the real costs throughout an institution difficult to calculate. (G段)\nHowever, the new museology and the apparent trend towards blockbusters make it likely that museums, art galleries and particularly science centres will be seen as part of the entertainment and tourism industry, rather than as cultural icons deserving of government and philanthropic support. (G段)\nBlockbusters require large capital expenditure, and draw on resources across all branches of an organisation; however, the costs don’t end there. There is a Human Resource Management cost in addition to a measurable ‘real’ dollar cost. (F段)\n对应段落：G段和F段\n审题：题目问的是作者在文中提到了哪些关于“现象级展览的缺点”，需要选出三个。\n定位关键信息：\n1. 通过题目中的\"disadvantages\"（缺点）定位，在文章中寻找负面表述或问题。\n2. 选项B（工作人员因工作量而疲惫）、C（内容更偏向娱乐而非文化输出）、E（需要花费大量投资在专业人员上）分别对应以下句子：\n- B对应G段“Creating, mounting or hiring blockbusters is exhausting for staff”（创建、举办或引进现象级展览会让员工疲惫不堪）。\n- C对应G段“will be seen as part of the entertainment and tourism industry, rather than as cultural icons”（可能被视为娱乐和旅游产业的一部分，而非文化象征）。\n- E对应F段“There is a Human Resource Management cost”（人力资源管理的成本，暗示资源投入问题）。\n解题思路：选项B在G段明确提到“exhausting for staff”（让员工疲惫），与“Workers has become tired of workloads”（工作人员因工作量而疲惫）对应。选项C在G段提到“entertainment and tourism industry, rather than as cultural icons”（娱乐和旅游产业而非文化象征），与“内容更偏向娱乐而非文化”一致。选项E在F段提到“Human Resource Management cost”（人力资源成本），暗示资源投入问题，与“Huge amounts of capital invested in specialists”（大量资本投资于专家）相关。其他选项A、D、F与原文表述不符，A选项在F段最后一句有提到，但是只是类似，意思完全不同。原文说参观者需要选择看哪个，没有提到A选项中说的“犹豫”。D选项在F段提到，虽然选项中的词句和原文基本一样，但是请注意，原文中举这个例子是为了说明“人力资源成本花销大”，D选项只是一个例子，并不是根本缺点。F选项在G段line11出现，但不是缺点，注意原文中这句话后面的“and may lead to creative excellence”也可能激发他们的创造力。","options":["People left hesitated to choose exhibitions.","Workers has become tired of workloads.","The content has become more entertaining rather than cultural.","General labourers are required to perform additional tasks","Huge amounts of capital invested in specialists.","Exposing staff to the fantasies and pressures of the market place."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59865","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nChoose THREE letters A-F. Write your answer in boxes 11-13 on your answer sheet. The list below gives some disadvantages of a blockbuster.","groupId":"59865-8211:59865:11-12-13"}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"59864-8211:59864:9-10","numbers":[9,10],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["A","D"]},{"id":"59865-8211:59865:11-12-13","numbers":[11,12,13],"selectionCount":3,"answers":["B","C","E"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59859","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraphs contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.","html":"<p><strong>1</strong> A reason for changing the exhibition programs <strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"59860","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Instead of being visitors, people turned out to be <strong>5</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[5] ____</strong> , who require the creation or hiring of blockbuster exhibitions as well as regular exhibition changes and innovations.</p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"59861","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Business nous and <strong>6</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[6] ____</strong> simply summarized in a magazine are not only important factors for directors but also an ability to attract a crowd of audiences.</p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"59862","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>7</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong> has contributed to the linking of museums, the heritage industry, tourism, profit-making and pleasure-giving.</p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"59863","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5-8\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>There occurs some controversy over whether it is proper to consider museums mainly as <strong>8</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"59864","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 9-10\nChoose TWO letters A-E. Write your answer in boxes 9-10 on your answer sheet. The list below gives some advantages of a blockbuster.","html":"<p><strong>Which TWO advantages are mentioned by the writer of the text?</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"59865","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nChoose THREE letters A-F. Write your answer in boxes 11-13 on your answer sheet. The list below gives some disadvantages of a blockbuster.","html":"<p><strong>Which THREE disadvantages are mentioned by the writer of the text?</strong></p>","firstNumber":11}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Museum Blockbuster&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Since the 1980s, the term ‘blockbuster’ has become the fashionable word for the special spectacular museum, art gallery or science centre exhibitions. These exhibitions have the ability to attract large crowds and often large corporate sponsors. Here is one of some existing definitions of a blockbuster: Put by Elsen (1984), a blockbuster is a ‘… large scale loan exhibition that people who normally don’t go to museums will stand in line for hours to see …’ James Rosenfield, writing in Direct Marketing in 1993, has described a successful blockbuster exhibition as a ‘… triumph of both curatorial and marketing skills …’ My own definition for a blockbuster is ‘a popular, high profile exhibition on display for a limited period, that attracts the general public, who are prepared to both stand in line and pay a fee in order to partake in the exhibition.’ What both Elsen and Rosenfield omit in their descriptions of a blockbuster, is that people are prepared to pay a fee to see a blockbuster and that the term blockbuster can just as easily apply to a movie or a museum exhibition.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Merely naming an exhibition or movie a blockbuster, however, does not make it a blockbuster. The term can only apply when the item in question has had an overwhelmingly successful response from the public. However, in literature from both the UK and USA the other words that also start to appear in descriptions of a blockbuster are ‘less scholarly’, ‘non-elitist’ and ‘popularist’. Detractors argue that blockbusters are designed to appeal to the lowest common denominator, while others extol the virtues of encouraging scholars to cooperate on projects and to provide exhibitions that cater for a broad selection of the community rather than an elite sector.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Maintaining and increasing visitor levels is paramount in the new museology. This requires continued product development. Not only the creation or hiring of blockbuster exhibitions but regular exhibition changes and innovations. In addition, the visiting public has become customers rather than visitors, and the skills that are valued in museums, science centres and galleries to keep the new customers coming through the door have changed. High on the list of requirements are commercial, business, marketing and entrepreneurial skills. Curators are now administrators. Being a director of an art gallery no longer requires an Arts Degree. As succinctly summarised in the Economist in 1994 ‘business nous and public relation skills’ were essential requirements for a director, and the ability to compete with other museums to stage travelling exhibitions which draw huge crowds.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The new museology has resulted in the convergence of museums, the heritage industry, and tourism, profit-making and pleasure-giving. This has given rise to much debate about the appropriateness of adopting the activities of institutions so that they more closely reflect the priorities of the market place and whether it is appropriate to see museums primarily as tourist attractions. At many institutions, you can now hold office functions in the display areas, or have dinner with the dinosaurs. Whatever commentators may think, managers of museums, art galleries and science centres worldwide are looking for artful ways to blend culture and commerce, and blockbuster exhibitions are at the top of the list. But while blockbusters are all part of the new museology, there is proof that you don’t need a museum, science centre or art gallery to benefit from the drawing power of a blockbuster or to stage a blockbuster.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>But do blockbusters held in public institutions really create a surplus to fund other activities? If the bottom line is profit, then according to the accounting records of many major museums and galleries, blockbusters do make money. For some museums overseas, it may be the money that they need to update parts of their collections or to repair buildings that are in need of attention. For others in Australia, it may be the opportunity to illustrate that they are attempting to pay their way, by recovering part of their operating costs or funding other operating activities with off-budget revenue. This makes the economic rationalists cheerful. However, not all exhibitions that are hailed to be blockbusters will be blockbusters, and some will not make money. It is also unlikely that the accounting systems of most institutions will recognise the real cost of either creating or hiring a blockbuster.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Blockbusters require large capital expenditure, and draw on resources across all branches of an organisation; however, the costs don’t end there. There is a Human Resource Management cost in addition to a measurable ‘real’ dollar cost. Receiving a touring exhibition involves large expenditure as well, and draws resources from across functional management structures in project management style. everyone from a general labourer to a building servicing unit, the front of the house, technical, promotion, education and administration staff, are required to perform additional tasks. Furthermore, as an increasing number of institutions in Australia try their hand at increasing visitor numbers, memberships (and therefore revenue), by staging blockbuster exhibitions, it may be less likely that blockbusters will continue to provide a surplus to subsidise other activities due to the competitive nature of the market. There are only so many consumer dollars to go around, and visitors will need to choose between blockbuster products.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Unfortunately, when the bottom-line is the most important objective to the mounting of blockbuster exhibitions, this same objective can be hard to maintain. Creating, mounting or hiring blockbusters is exhausting for staff, with the real costs throughout an institution difficult to calculate. Although the direct aims may be financial, creating or hiring a blockbuster has many positive spin-offs; by raising their profile through a popular blockbuster exhibition, a museum will be seen in a more favorable light at budget time. Blockbusters mean crowds, and crowds are good for the local economy, providing increased employment for shops, hotels, restaurants, the transport industry and retailers. Blockbusters expose staff to the vagaries and pressures of the market place and may lead to creative excellence. Either the success or failure of a blockbuster may highlight the need for managers and policymakers to rethink their strategies. However, the new museology and the apparent trend towards blockbusters make it likely that museums, art galleries and particularly science centres will be seen as part of the entertainment and tourism industry, rather than as cultural icons deserving of government and philanthropic support.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>H&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Perhaps the best pathway to take is one that balances both blockbusters and regular exhibitions. However, this easy middle ground may only work if you have enough space, and have alternate sources of funding to continue to support the regular less exciting fare. Perhaps the advice should be to make sure that your regular activities and exhibitions are more enticing, and find out what your local community wants from you. The question (trend) now at most museums and science centres, is ‘What blockbusters can we tour to overseas venues and will it be cost-effective?’</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8211&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8229","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 The Reconstruction of Community in Talbot Park, Auckland","book":"阅读还原集Vol.14","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.14 · Test 1 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8229:60065:14","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The place was once described as a state housing ghetto, rife with crime, vandalism and other social problems. But today after a $48 million urban renewal makeover, the site is home to 700 residents – 200 more than before – and has people regularly inquiring whether they can buy or rent there. ‘It doesn’t look like social housing,’\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求为A段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过段落中的关键词如\"state housing ghetto\"、\"urban renewal makeover\"、\"doesn’t look like social housing\"和\"public housing should look cheap\"可以定位到A段的主题是关于社会住房社区的高标准改造。\n解题思路：A段主要描述了Talbot Park地区从过去是犯罪和破坏行为盛行的社会住房贫民窟，到经过4800万美元的城市更新改造后，成为了一个拥有700名居民（比以前多200人）且人们经常询问是否可以购买或租赁。段落中还引用了Housing New Zealand住房服务经理Dene Busby和Design Group建筑师Neil的话，强调了公共住房不应看起来廉价，应该设计得像家一样。因此，选项F\"Introduction of a social housing community with unexpected high standard\"（介绍了一处超出预期的高标准社会住房社区）最符合A段的内容。","options":["Financial hardship of community","A good tendency of strengthening the supervision","Details of plans for the community’s makeover and upgrade","Architecture suits families of various ethnic origins","Problems arise then the mentality of alienation developed later","Introduction of a social housing community with unexpected high standard","A practical design and need assist and cooperate in future","Closer relationship among neighbors in the original site","Different need from a makeup of a low financial background should be considered","How to make the community feel safe","A plan with details for the house structure"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"60065","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphs, A-G, from the list below. Write the correct number, i-xi, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8229:60065:15","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Initially, there was a strong sense of a family-friendly community. Former residents recall how the Talbot Park reserve played a big part in their childhoods – a place where the kids in the block came together to play softball, cricket, tiggy, leapfrog and bullrush. Sometimes they’d play ‘Maoris against Pakehas’ but without any animosity. ‘It was all just good fun’, says Georgie Thompson in Ben Schrader’s We Call it Home: A History of State Housing in New Zealand. ‘We had respect for our neighbours and addressed them by title Mr. and Mrs. so-and-so,’ she recalls.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求为B段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读B段内容，可以定位到该段主要介绍了Talbot Park的地理位置、早期发展情况以及居民对社区的记忆。\n解题思路：根据B段内容，该段主要描述了Talbot Park的地理位置、早期发展情况以及居民对社区的记忆，因此可以推断出该段的标题应该与这些内容相关，早在20世纪60年代初，这片区域就被规划为政府住房区，中央贯穿一条线性公园，那时这里就形成了浓厚的家庭友好的社区氛围，后又举出具体的例子。结合选项，H最符合B段的内容。","options":["Financial hardship of community","A good tendency of strengthening the supervision","Details of plans for the community’s makeover and upgrade","Architecture suits families of various ethnic origins","Problems arise then the mentality of alienation developed later","Introduction of a social housing community with unexpected high standard","A practical design and need assist and cooperate in future","Closer relationship among neighbors in the original site","Different need from a makeup of a low financial background should be considered","How to make the community feel safe","A plan with details for the house structure"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"60065","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphs, A-G, from the list below. Write the correct number, i-xi, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8229:60065:16","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The community began to change in the late 1970s as more Pacific Islanders and Europeans moved in. The new arrivals didn’t readily integrate with the community, a ‘them and us’ mentality developed, and residents interact with their neighbours less.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求为C段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的段落信息，定位到C段的内容，寻找关键信息。\n解题思路：C段主要讲述了Talbot Park社区在20世纪70年代末开始发生变化，随着更多太平洋岛国人和欧洲人的迁入，社区中新旧居民之间的融合出现了问题，导致社区互动减少，建筑日渐破败，轻微犯罪案件激增。因此，选择标题E：随后，人们之间日渐疏远，各种问题便接踵而至，能够准确概括C段的主要内容。","options":["Financial hardship of community","A good tendency of strengthening the supervision","Details of plans for the community’s makeover and upgrade","Architecture suits families of various ethnic origins","Problems arise then the mentality of alienation developed later","Introduction of a social housing community with unexpected high standard","A practical design and need assist and cooperate in future","Closer relationship among neighbors in the original site","Different need from a makeup of a low financial background should be considered","How to make the community feel safe","A plan with details for the house structure"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"60065","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphs, A-G, from the list below. Write the correct number, i-xi, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8229:60065:17","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The master renewal plan didn’t take advantage of the maximum accommodation density allowable (one unit per 100 sq metres) but did increase density to one unit per 180 sq m by refurbishing all 108 star flat units, removing the multis and building 111 new home. The Talbot strategy can be summed up as mix, match and manage.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求为D段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：根据D段的第一句话\"The master renewal plan didn’t take advantage of the maximum accommodation density allowable...\"可以定位到文章中关于改造计划的具体内容。\n解题思路：D段主要讲述了Talbot Park的改造计划，包括增加住宅密度、翻新旧建筑、拆除部分建筑和新建房屋等。后文又详细描述改造效果。因此，D段的主题是关于改造计划的详细内容，对应标题为C。","options":["Financial hardship of community","A good tendency of strengthening the supervision","Details of plans for the community’s makeover and upgrade","Architecture suits families of various ethnic origins","Problems arise then the mentality of alienation developed later","Introduction of a social housing community with unexpected high standard","A practical design and need assist and cooperate in future","Closer relationship among neighbors in the original site","Different need from a makeup of a low financial background should be considered","How to make the community feel safe","A plan with details for the house structure"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"60065","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphs, A-G, from the list below. Write the correct number, i-xi, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8229:60065:18","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But if there was any doubt this is a low socio-economic area, the demographics for the surrounding Tamaki area are sobering. Of the 5000 households there, 55 per cent are statehouses, 28 per cent privately owned (compared to about 65 per cent nationally) and 17 per cent are private rental. The area has a high concentration of households with incomes in the $5000 to $15,000 range and very few with an income of over $70,000. That’s in sharp contrast to the more affluent suburbs like Kohimarama and St John’s that surround the area.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求为E段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读E段内容，可以定位到段落主要描述了两个关键信息：一是关于Talbot Park的改造项目预算和公共设施建设（如公园小径、种植、游乐场等），二是该地区的经济状况和人口统计信息（如低收入家庭比例高、与富裕郊区对比等）。\n解题思路：E段前半部分详细列举了改造项目中的公共设施建设内容，后半部分则通过人口统计和收入分布数据强调了该地区的低收入特征。因此，该段落的核心内容是要强调，关注低收入群体的需求。在给定的标题选项中，选项I最符合这一主题。","options":["Financial hardship of community","A good tendency of strengthening the supervision","Details of plans for the community’s makeover and upgrade","Architecture suits families of various ethnic origins","Problems arise then the mentality of alienation developed later","Introduction of a social housing community with unexpected high standard","A practical design and need assist and cooperate in future","Closer relationship among neighbors in the original site","Different need from a makeup of a low financial background should be considered","How to make the community feel safe","A plan with details for the house structure"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"60065","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphs, A-G, from the list below. Write the correct number, i-xi, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8229:60065:19","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph F","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The design is for people with different culture background,’ says architect James Lunday of Common Ground which designed the 21 large family homes. ‘Architecturally we decided to be relatively conservative – a nice house in its own garden with a bit of space and good indoor-outdoor flow.’ There’s a slight reflection of the whare and a Pacific fale, but not overplayed.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求为F段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读F段，可以发现段落主要讨论的是建筑设计的特点以及为不同文化背景的人设计房屋的理念。\n解题思路：段落F的核心内容包含两个部分：首先，建筑师James Lunday指出，设计是为了适应不同文化背景的人，并采用了相对保守但实用的方案（\"a nice house in its own garden with a bit of space and good indoor-outdoor flow\"），这体现了 “实用的设计” (A practical design)。接着，Bracey指出私营部门在 urban design and sustainable futures 方面落后，并且不会去承担重新设计街道和公园这类困难的任务，这暗示了此类项目 “未来需要（政府或公共部门的）援助和合作” (need assist and cooperate in future)。因此，段落F的核心是阐述当前的设计理念及其对未来合作的需求。因此，F段对应的标题是G选项。","options":["Financial hardship of community","A good tendency of strengthening the supervision","Details of plans for the community’s makeover and upgrade","Architecture suits families of various ethnic origins","Problems arise then the mentality of alienation developed later","Introduction of a social housing community with unexpected high standard","A practical design and need assist and cooperate in future","Closer relationship among neighbors in the original site","Different need from a makeup of a low financial background should be considered","How to make the community feel safe","A plan with details for the house structure"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"60065","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphs, A-G, from the list below. Write the correct number, i-xi, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8229:60065:20","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph G","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：There’s no doubt good urban design and good architecture play a significant part in the scheme. But probably more important is a new standard of social control. Housing New Zealand calls it ‘intensive tenancy management’.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求为G段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读G段，可以发现段落主要讨论的是社区管理，包括“intensive tenancy management”和“social engineering”等概念。\n解题思路：G段开头提到“good urban design and good architecture play a significant part in the scheme”，优质的城镇设计和建筑毫无疑问扮演着重要的角色，但接着强调“more important is a new standard of social control”，更重要的是建立社区管控的新标准，并详细介绍了Housing New Zealand的“intensive tenancy management”措施，如频繁检查、帮助租户相互认识、创造尊重邻居的环境等。这些内容与选项B吻合，因此选择选项B作为G段的标题。","options":["Financial hardship of community","A good tendency of strengthening the supervision","Details of plans for the community’s makeover and upgrade","Architecture suits families of various ethnic origins","Problems arise then the mentality of alienation developed later","Introduction of a social housing community with unexpected high standard","A practical design and need assist and cooperate in future","Closer relationship among neighbors in the original site","Different need from a makeup of a low financial background should be considered","How to make the community feel safe","A plan with details for the house structure"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"60065","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphs, A-G, from the list below. Write the correct number, i-xi, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet."},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8229:60066:21","type":"choice","text":"21 Design should meet the need of mix-raced cultural background.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘The design is for people with different culture background,’ says architect James Lunday of Common Ground which designed the 21 large family homes.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是谁认为设计应该满足不同种族文化背景的需求。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"mix-raced cultural background\"（不同种族文化背景）定位答案。在F段中，James Lunday明确提到\"The design is for people with different culture background\"，与题目信息完全匹配。\n解题思路：原文中James Lunday直接表达了设计要满足不同文化背景人群的需求，因此D选项（James Lunday）是正确答案。","options":["Michael Thompson","Graham Bodman","Stuart Bracey","James Lunday","Dene Busby"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"60066","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21-23\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters, A-E, in boxes 21-23 on your answer sheet.\nList of people\nA Michael Thompson\nB Graham Bodman\nC Stuart Bracey\nD James Lunday\nE Dene Busby"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8229:60066:22","type":"choice","text":"22 For a better living environment, regulations and social control should be imperative.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘The focus is on frequent inspections, helping tenants to get to know each other and trying to create an environment of respect for neighbours,’ says Bodman. That includes some strict rules – no loud parties after 10 pm, no dogs, no cats in the apartments, no washing hung over balcony rails and a requirement to mow lawns and keep the property tidy.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“为了更好的生活环境，有必要设立规章制度，进行社会管控”，需要找到相关的人物及其观点。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“regulations and social control”，通过这些词可以定位到G段中Bodman提到的严格规则和社会管控措施。\n解题思路：G段中Bodman明确提到了严格的规章制度，如“晚上10点后禁止举办喧闹聚会、禁止养犬猫、禁止在阳台栏杆上晾晒衣物，同时要求定期修剪草坪并保持社区整洁。这些内容直接对应题目中的“regulations and social control”。此外，Bodman还提到，重点在于加强日常巡查、促进住户相互了解，并努力营造邻里和睦的氛围，这与题目中的“better living environment”和“imperative”相吻合。因此，Bodman的观点和行为与题目要求一致，答案为B。","options":["Michael Thompson","Graham Bodman","Stuart Bracey","James Lunday","Dene Busby"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"60066","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21-23\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters, A-E, in boxes 21-23 on your answer sheet.\nList of people\nA Michael Thompson\nB Graham Bodman\nC Stuart Bracey\nD James Lunday\nE Dene Busby"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8229:60066:23","type":"choice","text":"23 Organising more community’s activities helps to strengthen the relationship in the community.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Housing New Zealand has also been active in organising morning teas and street barbecues for residents to meet their neighbours. ‘It’s all based on the intensification,’ says Community Renewal project manager Stuart Bracey, ‘We acknowledge if you are going to put more people living closer together, you have to actually help them to live closer together because it creates tension – especially for people that aren’t used to it.’\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“组织更多的社区活动有助于加强社区关系”，需要找到支持这一观点的人物。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“Organising more community’s activities”和“strengthen the relationship in the community”来定位答案。在G段中找到“organising morning teas and street barbecues”这一组织社区活动的描述。\n解题思路：原文中提到Housing New Zealand积极组织晨茶和街头烧烤活动，目的是让居民互相认识。这与题目中“组织更多社区活动有助于加强社区关系”的意思一致，因此G段是答案所在段落。根据题目要求匹配人物，G段提到的相关人物是Housing New Zealand的central Auckland regional manager Graham Bodman，对应选项C。","options":["Michael Thompson","Graham Bodman","Stuart Bracey","James Lunday","Dene Busby"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"60066","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21-23\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters, A-E, in boxes 21-23 on your answer sheet.\nList of people\nA Michael Thompson\nB Graham Bodman\nC Stuart Bracey\nD James Lunday\nE Dene Busby"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8229:60067:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"density","acceptedAnswers":["density"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The master renewal plan didn’t take advantage of the maximum accommodation density allowable (one unit per 100 sq metres) but did increase density to one unit per 180 sq m by refurbishing all 108 star flat units, removing the multis and building 111 new home.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是2002年塔尔博特社区决定提高住房标准，然而建房计划却远超居住容量限制，人们抱怨过高的什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“2002”、“raise housing standard”、“build homes”、“accommodation limit”和“complain about the high living”定位到D段，该段提到2002年住房新西兰决定升级房产，并描述了改造计划的具体措施，包括增加密度。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到“increase density”（增加密度）。由于原文提到“increase density”且题目提到“high living”，因此“density”是唯一符合语境的答案。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"60067","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8229:60068:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"architects","acceptedAnswers":["architects"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nThe Talbot strategy can be summed up as mix, match and manage. Mix up the housing with various plans from a mix of architects, match house styles to what’s built by the private sector, match tenants to the mix, and manage their occupancy.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“在塔博特公园的重建过程中，由谁将多种方案融合在一起，使建筑风格与个人设计的元素相得益彰，并为不同文化的租户提供了契合的居住空间”。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“various plans were complemented under the designs of many”定位到D段中的“Mix up the housing with various plans from a mix of architects”。\n解题思路：根据原文句子“Mix up the housing with various plans from a mix of architects”，将建筑师设计的多种方案混合搭配，可以确定“various plans”是由“a mix of architects”共同设计的，因此答案为“architects”。题目中的“many”对应原文中的“a mix of”，说明是由多位专业人士共同设计，结合上下文可知这些专业人士是“architects”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"60068","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8229:60069:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"cost","acceptedAnswers":["cost"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘If you’re going to build low-cost homes, you’ve got to keep them simple and you can’t afford a fancy bit on them.’ Says Michael Thompson of Architectus which designed the innovative three-level Atrium apartments lining two sides of a covered courtyard.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是关于改造项目的财务方面，需要注意的是，要以什么来建造房屋。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"finance\"和\"reconstruction program\"可以定位到D段，该段提到了改造项目的财务方面。原文中提到\"If you’re going to build low-cost homes, you’ve got to keep them simple and you can’t afford a fancy bit on them.\"这句话表明，在建造低成本房屋时，需要保持简单，不能有奢华的部分。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子\"If you’re going to build low-cost homes, you’ve got to keep them simple and you can’t afford a fancy bit on them.\"可以确定，改造项目的财务方面主要关注的是以低成本来建造房屋。因此，答案为\"cost\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"60069","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8229:60070:27","type":"fill","text":"填写第 27 空","answer":"garden","acceptedAnswers":["garden"],"explanation":"原文答案句：There’s a nice house in its own garden with a bit of space and good indoor-outdoor flow.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是居民最终同意建造一个相对常规的房子，这个房子有自己的什么，并且提供了相当大的活动空间。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"building a relatively conventional house in its own\"和\"provides considerable space to move around\"可以定位到F段中的\"nice house in its own garden with a bit of space\"。\n解题思路：根据原文句子，在建筑设计上，他们选择保持相对常规的布局，在专属花园里打造一座雅致住宅，既留有充足空间，又实现室内外空间的自然衔接。房子有自己的\"garden\"，并且有\"space\"，与题目中的描述相符，因此答案为\"garden\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"60070","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"60065","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphs, A-G, from the list below. Write the correct number, i-xi, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"60066","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21-23\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters, A-E, in boxes 21-23 on your answer sheet.\nList of people\nA Michael Thompson\nB Graham Bodman\nC Stuart Bracey\nD James Lunday\nE Dene Busby","html":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\">List of people&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>A</strong> Michael Thompson&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>B</strong> Graham Bodman&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>C</strong> Stuart Bracey&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>D</strong> James Lunday&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>E</strong> Dene Busby&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-top: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>21</strong> Design should meet the need of mix-raced cultural background.<strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong><br/></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"60067","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>In the year 2002, the Talbot decided to raise housing standard, yet the plan was to build homes go much beyond the accommodation limit and people complain about the high living <strong>24&nbsp;</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> . &nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"60068","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>And as the various plans were complemented under the designs of many <strong>25</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong> together, made house styles go with the part designed by individuals, matched tenants from a different culture.</p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"60069","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>As for the finance, reconstruction program’s major concern is to build a house within low <strong>26</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong> ;</p>","firstNumber":26},{"id":"60070","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>finally, just as expert predicted, residents will agree on building a relatively conventional house in its own <strong>27</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[27] ____</strong> , which provides considerable space to move around.</p>","firstNumber":27}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The Reconstruction of Community in Talbot Park, Auckland&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>#&amp;A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>An architecture of disguise is almost complete at Talbot Park in the heart of Auckland’s Glen Innes. The place was once described as a state housing ghetto, rife with crime, vandalism and other social problems. But today after a $48 million urban renewal makeover, the site is home to 700 residents – 200 more than before – and has people regularly inquiring whether they can buy or rent there. ‘It doesn’t look like social housing,’ Housing New Zealand housing services manager Dene Busby says, ‘apartments and townhouses of the tidy brick and weatherboard would look just as much as home.’ ‘There is no reason why public housing should look cheap in my view,’ says Design Group architect Neil of the eight three-bedroom terrace houses his firm designed.&amp;#&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Talbot Park is a triangle of government-owned land bounded by Apirana Ave, Pilkington Rd and Point England Rd. in the early 1960s, it was developed for state housing built around a linear park that ran through the middle. Initially, there was a strong sense of a family-friendly community. Former residents recall how the Talbot Park reserve played a big part in their childhoods – a place where the kids in the block came together to play softball, cricket, tiggy, leapfrog and bullrush. Sometimes they’d play ‘Maoris against Pakehas’ but without any animosity. ‘It was all just good fun’, says Georgie Thompson in Ben Schrader’s We Call it Home: A History of State Housing in New Zealand. ‘We had respect for our neighbours and addressed them by title Mr. and Mrs. so-and-so,’ she recalls.&amp;#&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>#&amp;C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Quite what went wrong with Talbot Park is not clear. We call it Home Records that the community began to change in the late 1970s as more Pacific Islanders and Europeans moved in. The new arrivals didn’t readily integrate with the community, a ‘them and us’ mentality developed, and residents interact with their neighbours less. What was clear was the buildings were deteriorating and becoming dilapidated, petty crime was on the rise and the reserve – the focus of fond childhood memories – had become a wasteland and was considered unsafe.&amp;#&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>But it wasn’t until 2002 that Housing New Zealand decided the properties needed upgrading. The master renewal plan didn’t take advantage of the maximum accommodation density allowable (one unit per 100 sq metres) but did increase density to one unit per 180 sq m by refurbishing all 108 star flat units, removing the multis and building 111 new home. The Talbot strategy can be summed up as mix, match and manage. Mix up the housing with various plans from a mix of architects, match house styles to what’s built by the private sector, match tenants to the mix, and manage their occupancy. Inevitably cost comes into the equation. ‘If you’re going to build low-cost homes, you’ve got to keep them simple and you can’t afford a fancy bit on them.’ Says Michael Thompson of Architectus which designed the innovative three-level Atrium apartments lining two sides of a covered courtyard. At $300,000 per two-bedroom unit, the building is more expensive but provides for independent disabled accommodation as well as offering solar hot water heating and rainwater collection for toilet cisterns and outside taps.&amp;#</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>#&amp;E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The renewal project budget at $1.5 million which will provide park pathways, planting, playgrounds, drinking fountains, seating, skateboard rails, a half-size basketball hard court, and a pavilion. But if there was any doubt this is a low socio-economic area, the demographics for the surrounding Tamaki area are sobering. Of the 5000 households there, 55 per cent are statehouses, 28 per cent privately owned (compared to about 65 per cent nationally) and 17 per cent are private rental. The area has a high concentration of households with incomes in the $5000 to $15,000 range and very few with an income of over $70,000. That’s in sharp contrast to the more affluent suburbs like Kohimarama and St John’s that surround the area.&amp;#</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>#&amp;F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘The design is for people with different culture background,’ says architect James Lunday of Common Ground which designed the 21 large family homes. ‘Architecturally we decided to be relatively conservative – a nice house in its own garden with a bit of space and good indoor-outdoor flow.’ There’s a slight reflection of the whare and a Pacific fale, but not overplayed. ‘The private sector is way behind in urban design and sustainable futures,’ says Bracey, ‘Redesigning streets and parks is a big deal and very difficult to do. The private sector won’t do it, because it’s so hard.’&amp;#</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>#&amp;G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>There’s no doubt good urban design and good architecture play a significant part in the scheme. But probably more important is a new standard of social control. Housing New Zealand calls it ‘intensive tenancy management’. Others view it as social engineering. ‘It’s a model that we are looking at going forward,’ according to Housing New Zealand’s central Auckland regional manager Graham Bodman. ‘The focus is on frequent inspections, helping tenants to get to know each other and trying to create an environment of respect for neighbours,’ says Bodman. That includes some strict rules – no loud parties after 10 pm, no dogs, no cats in the apartments, no washing hung over balcony rails and a requirement to mow lawns and keep the property tidy. Housing New Zealand has also been active in organising morning teas and street barbecues for residents to meet their neighbours. ‘It’s all based on the intensification,’ says Community Renewal project manager Stuart Bracey, ‘We acknowledge if you are going to put more people living closer together, you have to actually help them to live closer together because it creates tension – especially for people that aren’t used to it.’&amp;#</p><p>&nbsp;</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8229&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8230","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Texting the Television","book":"阅读还原集Vol.14","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.14 · Test 1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8230:60071:28","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：And no wonder: according to research about to be published by Gartner, a consultancy, text messaging has recently overtaken Internet use in Europe. One of the fastest-growing uses of text messaging, moreover, is interacting with television.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求为A段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读A段，可以发现段落主要介绍了电视观众从使用电子邮件与电视互动转向使用短信，并提到短信在欧洲的使用已经超过互联网，尤其是与电视互动的短信增长迅速。\n解题思路：A段首先提到电视节目曾经需要电子邮件地址，但现在更多地使用电话号码让观众发送短信。接着指出短信在欧洲的使用已经超过互联网，并且与电视互动的短信是增长最快的用途之一。因此，A段的主要内容是关于短信作为一种快速增长的与电视互动方式的概述。选项B\"Overview of a fast growing business\"（概述一项快速增长的业务）最能概括A段的内容。","options":["An existed critical system into operating in a new way","Overview of a fast growing business","Profitable games are gaining more concerns","Netherlands takes the leading role","A new perspective towards sharing the business opportunities","Opportunities for all round prevalent applications","Revenue gains and bonus share","The simpler technology prevails over complex ones","Set-top box provider changed their mind"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"60071","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphS A-G from the list below. Write the correct number i-ix in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8230:60071:29","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This has much to do with the boom in ‘reality TV’ shows, such as ‘Big Brother’, in which viewers’ votes decide the outcome. Most reality shows now allow text-message voting, and in some cases, such as the most recent series of ‘Big Brother’ in Norway, the majority of votes are cast in this way.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求为B段选择正确的标题。\n定位关键信息：根据题目定位到文章的B段。\n解题思路：B段主要讲述了短信互动与电视结合的现象，特别是与真人秀节目的联系，如\"Big Brother\"等节目中观众通过短信投票决定结果。段落中还提到了其他类型的电视节目，如新闻节目鼓励观众发送评论、游戏节目让观众参与竞猜等。这些内容都围绕着\"短信在电视互动的多种应用场景\"展开，因此最符合的标题是F\"Opportunities for all round prevalent applications\"有机会全方位普及应用","options":["An existed critical system into operating in a new way","Overview of a fast growing business","Profitable games are gaining more concerns","Netherlands takes the leading role","A new perspective towards sharing the business opportunities","Opportunities for all round prevalent applications","Revenue gains and bonus share","The simpler technology prevails over complex ones","Set-top box provider changed their mind"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"60071","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphS A-G from the list below. Write the correct number i-ix in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8230:60071:30","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It can also be very lucrative, since mobile operators charge premium rates for messages to particular numbers.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求为C段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读C段内容，发现段落主要围绕短信互动产生的经济效益展开，包括收入来源、运营商分成等。\n解题思路：C段首句就提到，这也能带来丰厚利润，因为移动运营商会对特定号码的短信收取高额费用。后又详细列举了短信互动在多个电视节目中的盈利情况，如\"Big Brother\"产生的收入、\"Videoclash\"的短信费用等，并提到短信收入已成为许多节目的重要商业模式。因此，C段的核心内容是短信互动的盈利模式，与标题G\"Revenue gains and bonus share\"（收入增长和利润分配）完全吻合。","options":["An existed critical system into operating in a new way","Overview of a fast growing business","Profitable games are gaining more concerns","Netherlands takes the leading role","A new perspective towards sharing the business opportunities","Opportunities for all round prevalent applications","Revenue gains and bonus share","The simpler technology prevails over complex ones","Set-top box provider changed their mind"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"60071","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphS A-G from the list below. Write the correct number i-ix in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8230:60071:31","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Each operator controls its own shortcodes, and only relatively recently have operators realised that it makes sense to co-operate and offer shortcodes that work across all networks. The availability of such common shortcodes was a breakthrough, says Lars Becker of Flytxt, a mobile-marketing firm, since shortcodes are far easier to remember when flashed up on the screen.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求为D段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读D段，可以发现段落主要讨论了“shortcodes”（短代码）的重要性和跨网络使用短代码的突破。\n解题思路：D段首先提到“shortcodes”是成功的重要因素之一，接着详细描述了这些短代码的特点（如四位、五位或六位数字），各运营商原本各自管理专属短代码，直到近年才意识到合作开发通用短代码的必要性。移动营销公司Flytxt的拉尔斯·贝克尔指出，这种通用短代码的推出堪称重大突破—以及运营商如何合作提供跨网络的短代码。因此，D段的核心内容是关于“shortcodes”的新突破，这与选项A“An existed critical system into operating in a new way”现存的一个重要系统以新方式投入运行，完全吻合。","options":["An existed critical system into operating in a new way","Overview of a fast growing business","Profitable games are gaining more concerns","Netherlands takes the leading role","A new perspective towards sharing the business opportunities","Opportunities for all round prevalent applications","Revenue gains and bonus share","The simpler technology prevails over complex ones","Set-top box provider changed their mind"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"60071","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphS A-G from the list below. Write the correct number i-ix in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8230:60071:32","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The operators’ decision to co-operate in order to expand the market is part of a broader trend, observes Katrina Bond of Analysys, a consultancy.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求为E段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：根据E段内容，重点在于移动运营商从最初保护自身利润到后来选择合作以拓展市场的转变。\n解题思路：E段首句就提到，运营商为拓展市场而选择合作的决策，正是行业整体趋势的缩影。讲述了移动运营商在面临保护利润和推动新媒介发展之间的选择，最终选择了合作以扩大市场。这与选项E“A new perspective towards sharing the business opportunities”（共享商业机遇的新思路）高度吻合，因此选择该选项作为E段的标题。","options":["An existed critical system into operating in a new way","Overview of a fast growing business","Profitable games are gaining more concerns","Netherlands takes the leading role","A new perspective towards sharing the business opportunities","Opportunities for all round prevalent applications","Revenue gains and bonus share","The simpler technology prevails over complex ones","Set-top box provider changed their mind"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"60071","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphS A-G from the list below. Write the correct number i-ix in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8230:60072:33","type":"choice","text":"In Europe, a consultancy suggested that young audiences spend more money on","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：And no wonder: according to research about to be published by Gartner, a consultancy, text messaging has recently overtaken Internet use in Europe. One of the fastest-growing uses of text messaging, moreover, is interacting with television. Gartner’s figures show that 20% of teenagers in France, 11% in Britain and 9% in Germany have sent messages in response to TV shows.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问在欧洲，一家咨询公司调查显示年轻观众会花更多的钱在什么上。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"Europe\"、\"consultancy\"和\"young audiences\"定位到A段，其中提到了Gartner这家咨询公司以及年轻人使用短信的情况。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子，Gartner这家咨询公司指出短信在欧洲的使用已经超过了互联网，并且年轻人通过短信与电视互动的比例很高。因此，可以推断出年轻人花费更多的钱在发送短信上，即选项A。","options":["thumbing text message.","writing E-mail.","watching TV program.","talking through Mobile phones."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60072","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33-35\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 33-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8230:60073:34","type":"choice","text":"What happened when some TV show invited audience to participate?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Most reality shows now allow text-message voting, and in some cases, such as the most recent series of ‘Big Brother’ in Norway, the majority of votes are cast in this way. But there is more to TV-texting than voting. News shows encourage viewers to send in comments; games shows allow viewers to compete; music shows take requests by text message; and broadcasters operate on-screen chartrooms.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是当一些电视节目邀请观众参与时会发生什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"invited audience to participate\"在文章中定位，找到B段中提到观众投票决定结果的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文，如今大多数真人秀节目都支持短信投票，新闻节目鼓励观众留言评论，游戏节目让观众参与竞猜，音乐节目接受短信点歌，电视台还会在屏幕上设置排行榜。可知，观众参与（投票）可以决定节目的结果，这与选项D\"他们的参与可以改变结果\"完全一致。其他选项A、B、C在原文中均未提及或与原文内容不符。因此，正确答案是D。","options":["To get attractive bonus","Shows are more popular in Norway than in other countries","Change to invite them to the reality show","Their participation could change the result"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60073","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33-35\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 33-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8230:60074:35","type":"choice","text":"Interactive TV change their mind of concentrating set-top box but switched to","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Providers of set-top box technology are adding text-messaging capabilities to their products.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问互动电视不再关注机顶盒装置，转而转向了什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Interactive TV\"和\"set-top box\"定位到F段，该段提到互动电视原本依赖于机顶盒技术，但存在缺点。\n解题思路：F段后半部分提到，机顶盒技术存在开发成本高、市场渗透率低等问题，而移动手机应用开发快、市场接受度高。因此，互动电视技术提供商开始在其产品中加入短信功能（text-messaging capabilities），即构建嵌入式短信平台。选项C\"build a embedded message platform\"与原文意思一致。其他选项A、B、D在原文中均未提及。","options":["increase their share in the market","change a modified set-top box.","build a embedded message platform.","march into European market."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"60074","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33-35\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 33-35 on your answer sheet."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8230:60075:36","type":"choice","text":"36 To offer mobile phone message technology","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At a recent conference organised by Van Dusseldorp & Partners, Han Weegink of CMG, a firm that provides text-message infrastructure, noted that all this is subtly changing the nature of television.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“提供手机短信技术的公司是哪家？”\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的关键词“mobile phone message technology”定位到文章中F段，其中提到“Han Weegink of CMG, a firm that provides text-message infrastructure”，表明CMG公司提供短信基础设施技术。\n解题思路：根据原文句子可以确定，CMG公司提供的是短信基础设施服务，即与手机短信相关的技术，因此答案为D。","options":["Lars Becker Flytxt","Katrina Bond of Analysys","Endemol","CMG","mmO2","Gartner"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"60075","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nA Lars Becker Flytxt\nB Katrina Bond of Analysys\nC Endemol\nD CMG\nE mmO2\nF Gartner"},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8230:60075:37","type":"choice","text":"37 Earned considerable amount of money through a famous program","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In July, a British operator, mmO2, reported better-than-expected financial results, thanks to the flood of messages caused by ‘Big Brother’.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是哪家公司通过一个著名的节目赚了大量的钱。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“Earned considerable amount of money through a famous program”，在文章中定位到C段，找到与“mmO2”相关的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子，今年7月，英国运营商mmO2公布了好于预期的财务业绩，这要归功于“老大哥”引发的大量信息。可以确定mmO2是“Big Brother”的合作运营商，并且通过这个节目赚了大量的钱。因此，答案是E。","options":["Lars Becker Flytxt","Katrina Bond of Analysys","Endemol","CMG","mmO2","Gartner"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"60075","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nA Lars Becker Flytxt\nB Katrina Bond of Analysys\nC Endemol\nD CMG\nE mmO2\nF Gartner"},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8230:60075:38","type":"choice","text":"38 Shortcodes are convenient to remember when turn up","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The availability of such common shortcodes was a breakthrough, says Lars Becker of Flytxt, a mobile-marketing firm, since shortcodes are far easier to remember when flashed up on the screen.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目询问“短代码出现时便于记忆”，需要匹配发表此观点的人。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词\"shortcodes\"和\"remember when turn up\"（易记忆当出现时）可以定位到D段中Lars Becker关于shortcodes的描述。\n解题思路：原文D段提到Lars Becker明确指出shortcodes因为\"far easier to remember when flashed up on the screen\"（当在屏幕上闪烁时更容易记忆），这与题目描述完全一致。因此，发表此观点的人是A。","options":["Lars Becker Flytxt","Katrina Bond of Analysys","Endemol","CMG","mmO2","Gartner"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"60075","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nA Lars Becker Flytxt\nB Katrina Bond of Analysys\nC Endemol\nD CMG\nE mmO2\nF Gartner"},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8230:60075:39","type":"choice","text":"39 To build their own mobile phone operating applications","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Endemol, the Netherlands-based production company behind ‘Big Brother’ and many other reality TV shows has started building its own database of mobile-phone users. The next step will be to establish direct billing relationships with them, and bypass the operators.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是哪家公司正在建立自己的手机应用程序。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"build their own mobile phone operating applications\"定位到C段，找到与建立手机用户数据库相关的句子。\n解题思路：原文中提到Endemol公司正在建立自己的手机用户数据库，下一步将直接与用户结算费用，绕过运营商。这与题干中\"build their own mobile phone operating applications\"相符，因此答案为C。","options":["Lars Becker Flytxt","Katrina Bond of Analysys","Endemol","CMG","mmO2","Gartner"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"60075","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nA Lars Becker Flytxt\nB Katrina Bond of Analysys\nC Endemol\nD CMG\nE mmO2\nF Gartner"},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8230:60075:40","type":"choice","text":"40 It is easy for people to send messages in an interactive TV","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：People tend to have their mobiles with them on the sofa, so ‘it’s a very natural form of interaction,’ says Adam Daum of Gartner.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“人们很容易在互动电视中发送信息”，需要找到对应人物或公司的观点或行为。\n定位关键信息：通过“easy for people to send messages”定位到F段中关于移动应用程序开发的内容。\n解题思路：B段提到，Gartner的Adam Daum表示，人们往往在沙发上带着手机，所以“这是一种非常自然的互动形式”。说明使用手机发送信息参与电视节目互动简便快捷，因此对应Gartner公司Mr Daum的观点，选择F。","options":["Lars Becker Flytxt","Katrina Bond of Analysys","Endemol","CMG","mmO2","Gartner"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"60075","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nA Lars Becker Flytxt\nB Katrina Bond of Analysys\nC Endemol\nD CMG\nE mmO2\nF Gartner"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"60071","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphS A-G from the list below. Write the correct number i-ix in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"60072","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33-35\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 33-35 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>In Europe, a consultancy suggested that young audiences spend more money on</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"60073","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33-35\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 33-35 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What happened when some TV show invited audience to participate?</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"60074","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 33-35\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 33-35 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Interactive TV change their mind of concentrating set-top box but switched to</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"60075","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-E) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nA Lars Becker Flytxt\nB Katrina Bond of Analysys\nC Endemol\nD CMG\nE mmO2\nF Gartner","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> Lars Becker Flytxt&nbsp;</p><p><strong>B</strong> Katrina Bond of Analysys&nbsp;</p><p><strong>C</strong> Endemol&nbsp;</p><p><strong>D</strong> CMG&nbsp;</p><p><strong>E </strong>mmO2&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>F</strong> Gartner&nbsp;</p><p><strong>36 </strong>To offer mobile phone message technology <strong class=\"source-blank\">[36] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":36}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Texting the Television&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>#&amp;A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>There was a time when any self-respecting television show, particularly one aimed at a young audience, had to have an e-mail address. But on Europe’s TV screens, such addresses are increasingly being pushed aside in favour of telephone numbers to which viewers can send text messages from their mobile phones. And no wonder: according to research about to be published by Gartner, a consultancy, text messaging has recently overtaken Internet use in Europe. One of the fastest-growing uses of text messaging, moreover, is interacting with television. Gartner’s figures show that 20% of teenagers in France, 11% in Britain and 9% in Germany have sent messages in response to TV shows.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>This has much to do with the boom in ‘reality TV’ shows, such as ‘Big Brother’, in which viewers’ votes decide the outcome. Most reality shows now allow text-message voting, and in some cases, such as the most recent series of ‘Big Brother’ in Norway, the majority of votes are cast in this way. But there is more to TV-texting than voting. News shows encourage viewers to send in comments; games shows allow viewers to compete; music shows take requests by text message; and broadcasters operate on-screen chartrooms. People tend to have their mobiles with them on the sofa, so ‘it’s a very natural form of interaction,’ says Adam Daum of Gartner.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>It can also be very lucrative, since mobile operators charge premium rates for messages to particular numbers. The most recent British series of ‘Big Brother’, for example, generated 5.4m text-message votes and £1.35m ($2.1m) in revenue. According to a report from Van Dusseldorp &amp; Partners, a consultancy based in Amsterdam, the German edition of MTV’s ‘Videoclash’, which invites viewers to vote for one of two rival videos, generates up to 40,000 messages an hour, each costing euro0.30 ($0.29). A text contest alongside the Belgian quiz show ‘I Against 100’ attracted 10,000 players in a month, each of whom paid euro 0.50 per question in an eight-round contest. In Spain, a cryptic-crossword clue is displayed before the evening news broadcast; viewers are invited to text in their answers at a cost of euro 1, for a chance to win a euro300 prize. On a typical day, 6,000 people take part. TV-related text messaging now accounts for an appreciable share of mobile operators’ data revenues. In July, a British operator, mmO2, reported better-than-expected financial results, thanks to the flood of messages caused by ‘Big Brother’. Operators typically take 40-50% of the revenue from each message, with the rest divided between the broadcaster, the programme maker and the firm providing the message-processing system. Text-message revenues are already a vital element of the business model for many shows. Inevitably, there is grumbling that the operators take too much of the pie. Endemol, the Netherlands-based production company behind ‘Big Brother’ and many other reality TV shows has started building its own database of mobile-phone users. The next step will be to establish direct billing relationships with them, and bypass the operators.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Why has the union of television and text message suddenly proved so successful? One important factor is the availability of special four-, five- or six-digit numbers, called ‘shortcodes’.Each operator controls its own shortcodes, and only relatively recently have operators realised that it makes sense to co-operate and offer shortcodes that work across all networks. The availability of such common shortcodes was a breakthrough, says Lars Becker of Flytxt, a mobile-marketing firm, since shortcodes are far easier to remember when flashed up on the screen.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>#&amp;E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The operators’ decision to co-operate in order to expand the market is part of a broader trend, observes Katrina Bond of Analysys, a consultancy. Faced with a choice between protecting their margins and allowing a new medium to emerge, operators have always chosen the first. WAP, a technology for reading cut-down web pages on mobile phones, failed because operators were reluctant to share revenue with content providers. Having learnt their lesson, operators are changing their tune. In France, one operator, Orange, has even gone so far as to publish a rate card for text-message revenue-sharing, a degree of transparency that would once have been unthinkable.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>At a recent conference organised by Van Dusseldorp &amp; Partners, Han Weegink of CMG, a firm that provides text-message infrastructure, noted that all this is subtly changing the nature of television. Rather than presenting content to viewers, an increasing number of programmes involve content that reacts to the viewer’s input. That was always the promise of interactive TV, of course. Interactive TV was supposed to revolve around fancy set-top boxes that plug directly into the television. But that approach has a number of drawbacks, says Mr Daum. It is expensive to develop and test software for multiple and incompatible types of set-top box, and the market penetration, at 40% or less, is lower than that for mobile phones, which are now owned by around 85% of Europeans. Also, mobile-phone applications can be quickly developed and set up. ‘You can get to market faster, and with fewer grasping intermediaries,’ says Mr Daum. Providers of set-top box technology are adding text-messaging capabilities to their products.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The success of TV-related texting is a reminder of how easily an elaborate technology can be unexpectedly overtaken by a simpler, lower-tech approach. It does not mean that the traditional approach to interactive TV is doomed: indeed, it demonstrates that there is strong demand for interactive services. People, it seems, really do want to do more than just stare at the screen. If nothing else, couch potatoes like to exercise their thumbs.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8230&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8199","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Bondi Beach","book":"阅读还原集Vol.13","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.13 · Test 4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8199:59821:1","type":"choice","text":"The name of the Bondi beach is first called by the British settlers.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A number of place names within Waverley, most famously Bondi, have been based on words derived from Aboriginal languages of the Sydney region.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是Bondi海滩的名字是否是由英国定居者首次命名的。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"the name of the Bondi beach\"和\"first called by the British settlers\"定位到B段，特别是最后一句\"A number of place names within Waverley, most famously Bondi, have been based on words derived from Aboriginal languages of the Sydney region.\"。\n解题思路：根据原文B段最后一句可知，Waverley地区内许多地名，其中最著名的是Bondi，这些地名是基于源自悉尼地区土著语言的词汇。这说明Bondi的名字来源于土著语言，而不是由英国定居者首次命名的。因此，题目中的说法与原文信息矛盾，答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59821","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8199:59822:2","type":"choice","text":"The aboriginal culture in Australia is different when compared with European culture.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：There is no clear evidence for the name or names of the particular band(s) of the Eora that roamed what is now the Waverley area. A number of place names within Waverley, most famously Bondi, have been based on words derived from Aboriginal languages of the Sydney region.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“与欧洲文化相比，澳大利亚的土著文化是不同的”这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“Aboriginal culture”和“European culture”来定位答案。在B段中，提到了“Aboriginal languages”和“place names”，但没有直接比较土著文化和欧洲文化的差异。\n解题思路：题目陈述的是土著文化与欧洲文化的比较，而文章中并未提及两者之间的比较，只是提到了土著语言和地名。因此，文章没有提供足够的信息来支持或反驳这一陈述，所以答案是“NOT GIVEN”。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59822","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8199:59823:3","type":"choice","text":"Bondi beach area holds many contemporary hotels.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Bondi Beach has a commercial area along Campbell Parade and adjacent side streets, featuring many popular cafes, restaurants, and hotels, with views of the contemporary beach. It is depicted as wholly modern and European.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问“邦迪海滩地区拥有许多现代酒店”是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"contemporary hotels\"（现代酒店）定位到G段。G段提到Bondi Beach的Campbell Parade及其周边街道有许多流行的咖啡馆、餐厅和酒店，这些地方都是现代风和欧洲风格。\n解题思路：原文提到Bondi Beach的商业区有咖啡馆、餐厅和酒店，可饱览现代海滩风光，这些地方都是现代风和欧洲风格，但并未明确说明这些酒店是“contemporary”（现代的）。因此，题目中的信息在文章中没有明确对应，无法确定是否正确。所以答案为Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59823","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8199:59824:4","type":"choice","text":"The seaside town in Bondi is affected by British culture for its characteristic red color.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The valley running down to the beach is the famous world over for its view of distinctive red-tiled roofs. Those architectures are deeply influenced by British coastal town.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问“邦迪海滨的沿海城镇受到英国文化的影响，以其独特的红色屋顶而闻名”是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"seaside town in Bondi\"、\"characteristic red color\"和\"British culture\"定位到G段最后一句，提到邦迪海滩的建筑深受英国沿海城镇的影响，并且以其独特的红色屋顶而闻名。\n解题思路：根据原文G段最后一句的描述，邦迪海滩的建筑确实受到英国沿海城镇的影响，并且以其独特的红色屋顶而闻名，这与题目所述一致。因此，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59824","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8199:59825:5","type":"choice","text":"Living near Bondi seashore is not beneficial for health.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：There is a growing trend that people prefer having to relax near seaside instead of living unhealthily in cities.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问“在邦迪海滨附近生活对健康没有好处”，需要判断这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“near Bondi seashore”和“not beneficial for health”定位到E段第一句，该句提到人们越来越倾向于在海边放松，而不是在不健康的城市里生活。\n解题思路：原文明确指出人们选择在海边放松是为了避免不健康的生活，说明在海边生活是有益于健康的。题目说“在邦迪海滨附近生活对健康没有好处”与原文信息直接矛盾，因此答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59825","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8199:59826:6","type":"fill","text":"填写第 6 空","answer":"tram/Tram\n","acceptedAnswers":["tram","Tram"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The first tramway reached the beach in 1884. Following this, tram became the first public transportation in Bondi.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是在19世纪末，人们去Bondi时使用的公共交通工具是什么。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"end of the 19th century\"和\"public transport\"。通过时间点\"end of the 19th century\"可以定位到D段，该段提到了，1884年，首条有轨电车线路延伸至海滩。\n解题思路：D段提到\"the first tramway reached the beach in 1884\"，1884年，首条有轨电车线路延伸至海滩。自此，电车成为邦迪地区首个公共交通工具。说明在19世纪末，人们开始使用电车作为公共交通工具去Bondi海滩。因此，答案是\"tram\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59826","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-9\nAnswer the questions below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR NUMBERS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-9 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8199:59827:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"1954","acceptedAnswers":["1954"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A Royal Surf Carnival was held at Bondi Beach for Queen Elizabeth II during her first visited in Australia in 1954.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是英国皇室首次访问邦迪海滩的时间。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"British Royalty\"和\"first visit\"可以定位到F段中提到的\"Queen Elizabeth II\"和\"first visited in Australia in 1954\"。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子\"Queen Elizabeth II during her first visited in Australia in 1954\"，可以确定英国皇室首次访问邦迪海滩的时间是1954年。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59827","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-9\nAnswer the questions below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR NUMBERS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-9 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8199:59828:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"beach volleyball/Beach Volleyball","acceptedAnswers":["beach volleyball","Beach Volleyball"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Bondi Beach hosted the beach volleyball competition at the 2000 Summer Olympics.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是2000年悉尼奥运会上Bondi海滩举办了哪个奥运项目。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"2000 Sydney Olympic games\"和\"Olympic event\"可以定位到H段第一句，该句明确提到了Bondi Beach在2000年夏季奥运会上举办了某个比赛项目。\n解题思路：根据定位到的句子，可以直接提取出\"beach volleyball\"作为答案。句子中明确指出Bondi Beach举办了\"beach volleyball competition\"（沙滩排球比赛），这与题目要求的奥运项目完全一致，因此答案为\"beach volleyball\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59828","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-9\nAnswer the questions below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR NUMBERS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-9 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8199:59829:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"environment/Environment","acceptedAnswers":["environment","Environment"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Campaigners oppose both the social and environmental consequences of the development.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是如果为奥运会赛事建造体育场，会损害什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"stadium\"和\"Olympic event\"定位到H段，找到关于建造体育场的内容。\n解题思路：原文提到\"the development\"（开发建设）会带来\"social and environmental consequences\"（不良的社会和环境影响），而题目问的是\"damaged\"（损害）的内容。结合上下文，这里的\"development\"指的就是建造体育场，因此建造体育场会损害\"environment\"（环境）。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59829","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-9\nAnswer the questions below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR NUMBERS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-9 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8199:59830:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"wealthy people/Wealthy People\n","acceptedAnswers":["wealthy people","Wealthy People"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Many wealthy people spend Christmas Day at the beach.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问Bondi海滩每年举办特色体育活动吸引了很多什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"feature sports activities every year\"（每年特色体育活动）可以定位到F段提到的\"City to Surf Fun Run\"（城市到海滩跑步活动），该活动每年8月举行，属于特色体育活动。题目问这类活动吸引的人群，因此需要找到描述参与者或观众的句子。\n解题思路：在F段中，提到特色体育活动后，后面提到\"Many wealthy people spend Christmas Day at the beach.\"（许多富裕人士在圣诞节当天去海滩），虽然这句话直接提到的是圣诞节，但结合上下文，F段主要描述Bondi海滩的各种活动和人群，包括体育赛事和富裕人士的参与。因此可以推断，特色体育活动吸引的主要人群是\"wealthy people\"（富裕人士）。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59830","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8199:59831:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"Manly/manly","acceptedAnswers":["Manly","manly"],"explanation":"原文答案句：However, the shortage of houses occurs when lots of people crushed to the seaside. Manly is the seashore town which solved this problem.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是当地住宿无法满足日益增长的人口时，哪个附近的城镇是第一个提供解决方案的郊区地点。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"local accommodation cannot meet with the expanding population\"和\"nearby town\"来定位答案。在F段，其中提到Manly是一个解决住宿问题的地点。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子，许多人来到海边度假，便出现了房屋短缺的问题。Manly这个海滨小镇解决了这一问题。因此，Manly是第一个提供解决方案的附近城镇。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59831","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8199:59832:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"Bondi/bondi","acceptedAnswers":["Bondi","bondi"],"explanation":"原文答案句：However, people still choose Bondi as the satisfied destination rather than Manly.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问人们仍然将什么作为最佳选择。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"prefer\"和\"best choice\"定位到F段中\"choose Bondi as the satisfied destination\"。\n解题思路：原文明确提到人们仍然选择Bondi作为满意的目的地，与题干中的\"best choice\"对应，因此答案为Bondi。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59832","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8199:59833:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"tiled roofs/Tiled Roofs","acceptedAnswers":["tiled roofs","Tiled Roofs"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The valley running down to the beach is the famous world over for its view of distinctive red-tiled roofs.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目在问那些海滨建筑闻名于世，得益于其建筑有色彩的什么，以及海面飘来的沁人气息。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"seaside buildings\"和\"special scenic colored\"定位到G段中描述建筑特色的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到\"red-tiled roofs\"是世界闻名的特色，题干中的\"special scenic colored\"对应原文的\"distinctive red\"，因此答案为\"tiled roofs\"（瓦屋顶。因此答案为\"tiled roofs\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59833","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59821","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The name of the Bondi beach is first called by the British settlers.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"59822","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The aboriginal culture in Australia is different when compared with European culture.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"59823","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Bondi beach area holds many contemporary hotels.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"59824","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The seaside town in Bondi is affected by British culture for its characteristic red color.</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"59825","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Living near Bondi seashore is not beneficial for health.</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"59826","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-9\nAnswer the questions below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR NUMBERS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-9 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>6</strong> At the end of the 19th century, which public transport did people use to go to Bondi? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[6] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"59827","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-9\nAnswer the questions below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR NUMBERS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-9 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>7</strong> When did the British Royalty first visit Bondi? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"59828","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-9\nAnswer the questions below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR NUMBERS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-9 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>8</strong> Which Olympic event did Bondi hold in the 2000 Sydney Olympic games? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"59829","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 6-9\nAnswer the questions below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR NUMBERS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6-9 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>9</strong> What would be damaged if the stadium was built for that Olympic event? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"59830","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Bondi beach holds the feature sports activities every year, which attracts lot of <strong>10</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"59831","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Choosing to live at this place during the holidays. But local accommodation cannot meet with the expanding population, a nearby town of <strong>11 </strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong> is the first suburb site to support the solution,</p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"59832","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>yet people prefer <strong>12</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong> as their best choice.</p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"59833","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Its seaside buildings are well-known in the world for the special scenic colored <strong>13</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong> on buildings and the joyful smell from the sea.</p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Bondi Beach&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Bondi Beach, Australia’s most famous beach, is located in the suburb of Bondi, in the Local Government Area of Waverley, seven kilometers from the centre of Sydney. ‘Bondi’ or ‘Boondi’ is an Aboriginal word meaning water breaking over rocks or the sound of breaking waves. The Australian Museum records that Bondi means a place where a flight of nullas took place. There are Aboriginal Rock carving on the northern end of the beach at Ben Buckler and south of Bondi Beach near McKenzies Beach on the coastal walk.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The indigenous people of the area at the time of European settlement have generally been welcomed to as the Sydney people or the Eora (Eora means ‘the people’). One theory describes the Eora as a sub-group of the Darug language group which occupied the Cumberland Plain west to the Blue Mountains. However, another theory suggests that they were a distinct language group of their own. There is no clear evidence for the name or names of the particular band(s) of the Eora that roamed what is now the Waverley area. A number of place names within Waverley, most famously Bondi, have been based on words derived from Aboriginal languages of the Sydney region.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>From the mid-1800s Bondi Beach was a favourite location for family outings and picnics. The beginnings of the suburb go back to 1809, when the early road builder, William Roberts, received from Governor Bligh a grant of 81 hectares of what is now most of the business and residential area of Bondi Beach. In 1851, Edward Smith Hall and Francis O’Brien purchased 200 acres of the Bondi area that embraced almost the whole frontage of Bondi Beach, and it was named the ‘The Bondi Estate.’ Between 1855 and 1877 O’Brien purchased Hall’s share of the land, renamed the land the ‘O’Brien Estate,’ and made the beach and the surrounding land available to the public as a picnic ground and amusement resort. As the beach became increasingly popular, O’Brien threatened to stop public beach access. However, the Municipal Council believed that the Government needed to intervene to make the beach a public reserve.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>During the 1900s beach became associated with health, leisure and democracy – a playground everyone could enjoy equally. Bondi Beach was a working-class suburb throughout most of the twentieth century with migrant people from New Zealand comprising the majority of the local population. The first tramway reached the beach in 1884. Following this, tram became the first public transportation in Bondi. As an alternative, this action changed the rule that only rich people can enjoy the beach. By the 1930s Bondi was drawing not only local visitors but also people from elsewhere in Australia and overseas. Advertising at the time referred to Bondi Beach as the ‘Playground of the Pacific’.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>There is a growing trend that people prefer having to relax near seaside instead of living unhealthily in cities. The increasing popularity of sea bathing during the late 1800s and early 1900s raised concerns about public safety and how to prevent people from drowning. In response, the world’s first formally documented surf lifesaving club, the Bondi Surf Bathers’ Life Saving Club, was formed in 1907. This was powerfully reinforced by the dramatic events of ‘Black Sunday’ at Bondi in 1938. Some 35,000 people were on the beach and a large group of lifesavers were about to start a surf race when three freak waves hit the beach, sweeping hundreds of people out to sea. Lifesavers rescued 300 people. The largest mass rescue in the history of surf bathing, it confirmed the place of the lifesaver in the national imagination.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Bondi Beach is the endpoint of the City to Surf Fun Run which is held each year in August. Australian surf carnivals further instilled this image. A Royal Surf Carnival was held at Bondi Beach for Queen Elizabeth II during her first visit in Australia in 1954. Since 1867, there have been over fifty visits by a member of the British Royal Family to Australia. In addition to many activities, the Bondi Beach Markets is open every Sunday. Many wealthy people spend Christmas Day at the beach. However, the shortage of houses occurs when lots of people crushed to the seaside. Manly is the seashore town which solved this problem. However, people still choose Bondi as the satisfied destination rather than Manly.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Bondi Beach has a commercial area along Campbell Parade and adjacent side streets, featuring many popular cafes, restaurants, and hotels, with views of the contemporary beach. It is depicted as wholly modern and European. In the last decade, Bondi Beaches’ unique position has seen a dramatic rise in svelte houses and apartments to take advantage of the views and scent of the sea. The valley running down to the beach is the famous world over for its view of distinctive red-tiled roofs. Those architectures are deeply influenced by British coastal town.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Bondi Beach hosted the beach volleyball competition at the 2000 Summer Olympics. A temporary 10,000-seat stadium, a much smaller stadium, 2 warm-up courts, and 3 training courts were set up to host the tournament. The Bondi Beach Volleyball Stadium was constructed for it and stood for just six weeks. Campaigners oppose both the social and environmental consequences of the development. The stadium will divide the beach in two and seriously restrict public access for swimming, walking, and other forms of outdoor recreation. People protest for their human rights of having a pure seaside and argue for health life in Bondi.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘They’re prepared to risk lives and risk the Bondi beach environment for the sake of eight days of volleyball,’ said Stephen Uniacke, a construction lawyer involved in the campaign. Other environmental concerns include the possibility that soil dredged up from below the sand will acidify when brought to the surface.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8199&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8209","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 A New Ice Age","book":"阅读还原集Vol.13","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.13 · Test 4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8209:59840:14","type":"choice","text":"The writer mentions the paintings in the first two paragraphs to illustrate","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But it may again soon. And ice-choked scenes, similar to those immortalized by the 16th-century Flemish painter Pieter Brueghel the Elder, may also return to Europe.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问作者在文章前两段提到画作是为了说明什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"the paintings in the first two paragraphs\"定位到A段和 B段中关于画作的内容。A段提到华盛顿渡河的画作，B段提到Pieter Brueghel the Elder的画作，并提到类似的冰封场景可能再次出现。\n解题思路：A段提到华盛顿渡河的画作，说明过去河面结冰的情景；B段提到Pieter Brueghel the Elder的画作，并指出类似的冰封场景可能再次出现（\"may also return to Europe\"），暗示未来可能再次出现小冰河时期。因此，作者提到这些画作是为了说明未来可能再次出现小冰河时期，对应选项D。选项A和B与画作本身无关，选项C提到的12,000年前的小冰河时期在B段中只是作为对比，不是画作要说明的重点。","options":["that the two paintings are immortalized.","people’s different opinions.","a possible climate change happened 12,000 years ago.","the possibility of a small ice age in the future."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59840","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-16\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 14-16 on your answer sheet."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8209:59841:15","type":"choice","text":"Why is it hard for the poor to survive the next cooling period?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：During previous cooling periods, whole tribes simply picked up and moved south, but that option doesn’t work in the modern, tense world of closed borders.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是为什么穷人难以在下一个冷却期生存。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“the poor”和“survive the next cooling period”可以定位到E段，该段讨论了在冷却期穷人难以生存的原因。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句可以看出，在过去的冷却期，部落可以简单地迁移到南方，但在现代紧张的世界中，由于边境封闭，这种选择不再可行。因此，穷人难以在下一个冷却期生存的原因是迁移似乎因为边境封闭而变得不可能。这与选项C的描述一致。","options":["because people can’t remove themselves from the major safety nets.","because politicians are voting against the movement.","because migration seems impossible for the reason of closed borders.","because climate changes accelerate the process of moving southward."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59841","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-16\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 14-16 on your answer sheet."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8209:59842:16","type":"choice","text":"Why is the winter temperature in continental Europe higher than that in North America?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Normally, the Gulf Stream, laden with heat soaked up in the tropics, meanders up the east coasts of the United States and Canada. As it flows northward, the stream surrenders heat to the air. Because the prevailing North Atlantic winds blow eastward, a lot of the heat wafts to Europe.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问为什么欧洲大陆的冬季气温比北美洲高。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"higher winter temperature in continental Europe than in North America\"定位到H段，该段解释了欧洲气温较高的原因。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，墨西哥湾暖流携带着热带吸收的热量，蜿蜒流经美国和加拿大的东海岸。当它向北流动时，暖流向空气中释放热量。由于盛行的北大西洋风向东风，大量热量飘向欧洲。因此，正确答案是A，因为热量通过风向流动被带到欧洲。","options":["because heat is brought to Europe with the wind flow.","because the eastward movement of freshwater continues.","because Boston and Rome are at the same latitude.","because the ice formation happens in North America."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59842","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-16\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 14-16 on your answer sheet."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8209:59843:17","type":"choice","text":"17 A quick climate change wreaks great disruption.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A 2002 report titled ‘Abrupt Climate Change: Inevitable Surprises,’ produced by the National Academy of Sciences, pegged the cost from agricultural losses alone at $100 billion to $250 billion while also predicting that damage to ecologies could be vast and incalculable.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“剧烈的气候变化会造成巨大破坏”这一观点是谁提出的。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"quick climate change\"和\"great disruption\"，在文章中找到相关表述。\n解题思路：D段提到国家科学院的报告《气候突变：不可避免的意外》报告指出，仅农业损失一项就高达1000亿至2500亿美元，同时预测生态破坏可能极其严重且难以估量。这表明剧烈的气候变化会导致巨大破坏，因此，答案为D。","options":["Bob Dickson","Terrence byce","William Curry","National Academy of Science"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59843","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 17-21\nMatch each statement (Questions 17-21) with the correct person A-D in the box below. Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 17-21 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Bob Dickson\nB Terrence Joyce\nC William Curry\nD National Academy of Science"},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8209:59843:18","type":"choice","text":"18 Most Americans are not prepared for the next cooling period.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘It could happen in 10 years,’ says Terrence Joyce, who chairs the Woods Hole Physical Oceanography Department. ‘Once it does, it can take hundreds of years to reverse.’ And he is alarmed that Americans have yet to take the threat seriously.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“大多数美国人没有为下一次降温做好准备”，这一观点是谁提出的。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词“Americans are not prepared for the next cooling period”，可以在C段中找到“Americans have yet to take the threat seriously”，意为“美国人至今仍未将这一威胁视为严重问题”。\n解题思路：原文中的句子表明，伍兹霍尔物理海洋学系主任特伦斯·乔伊斯表示：‘这种现象可能在十年内发生，一旦出现，可能需要数百年才能逆转。’他担忧的是，美国人至今仍未将这一威胁视为严重问题，与题目意思一致。因此，答案为B。","options":["Bob Dickson","Terrence byce","William Curry","National Academy of Science"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59843","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 17-21\nMatch each statement (Questions 17-21) with the correct person A-D in the box below. Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 17-21 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Bob Dickson\nB Terrence Joyce\nC William Curry\nD National Academy of Science"},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8209:59843:19","type":"choice","text":"19 A case of a change of ocean water is mentioned in a conference.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The freshwater trend is major news in ocean-science circles. Bob Dickson, a British oceanographer who sounded an alarm at a February conference in Honolulu, has termed the drop in salinity and temperature in the Labrador Sea – a body of water between northeastern Canada and Greenland that adjoins the Atlantic – ‘arguably the largest full-depth changes observed in the modem instrumental oceanographic record.’\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问，是谁“在会议中提及了一起海水变化的案例”。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词“change of ocean water”和“a conference”可以定位到G段，该段提到了Bob Dickson在檀香山的一个会议上提出了关于海洋水盐度和温度变化的问题。\n解题思路：G段中明确提到了Bob Dickson在会议上讨论了Labrador海的水体盐度和温度下降的问题，并称其为“现代海洋观测记录中观察到的最大深度变化之一”。这直接对应了题目中“海洋水变化”和“会议”的描述，因此答案为A。","options":["Bob Dickson","Terrence byce","William Curry","National Academy of Science"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59843","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 17-21\nMatch each statement (Questions 17-21) with the correct person A-D in the box below. Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 17-21 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Bob Dickson\nB Terrence Joyce\nC William Curry\nD National Academy of Science"},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8209:59843:20","type":"choice","text":"20 Global warming urges the appearance of the ice age.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In deed it is, says Joyce. In his cluttered office, full of soft light from the foggy Cape Cod morning, he explains how such warming could actually be the surprising culprit of the next mini-ice age.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问“全球变暖促使冰河时代的出现”，这一观点是谁提出的。\n定位关键信息：通过“global warming”和“ice age”定位到F段，该段提到全球变暖（melting Arctic ice, caused by a buildup of carbon dioxide）与冰河时代的关系。\n解题思路：F段中，Joyce解释说这种变暖现象可能正是引发下一个迷你冰河时代的惊人元凶。全球变暖（北极冰融化）导致淡水进入北大西洋，而淡水层可能引发冰河时代。因此，Joyce的观点直接关联了全球变暖与冰河时代的可能性，对应选项B。","options":["Bob Dickson","Terrence byce","William Curry","National Academy of Science"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59843","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 17-21\nMatch each statement (Questions 17-21) with the correct person A-D in the box below. Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 17-21 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Bob Dickson\nB Terrence Joyce\nC William Curry\nD National Academy of Science"},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8209:59843:21","type":"choice","text":"21 The temperature will not drop to the same degree as it used to be.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘Most people think these other guys in the boat are rowing, but they are actually pushing the ice away,’ says Curry, tapping his finger on a reproduction of the painting. Sure enough, the lead oarsman is bashing the frozen river with his boot. ‘I grew up in Philadelphia. The place in this painting is 30 minutes away by car. I can tell you, this kind of thing just doesn’t happen anymore.’\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是，气温不会像以往那样大幅下降，这一观点是谁提出的。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词“temperature will not drop to the same degree as it used to be”定位到A段。\n解题思路：A段主要讲了Curry对伊曼纽尔·戈特利布·勒特兹的名画《乔治·华盛顿渡过特拉华河》的研究，并且他明确说明，多数人以为画中人正在划桨，其实他们是在用船桨推开冰面，这种场景如今已不复存在了。说明他认为以后不会再有这样的大降温，与题目表述一致，因此，选择C项。","options":["Bob Dickson","Terrence byce","William Curry","National Academy of Science"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59843","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 17-21\nMatch each statement (Questions 17-21) with the correct person A-D in the box below. Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 17-21 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Bob Dickson\nB Terrence Joyce\nC William Curry\nD National Academy of Science"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8209:59844:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"heat","acceptedAnswers":["heat"],"explanation":"原文答案句：As it flows northward, the stream surrenders heat to the air.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目要求根据流程图完成填空，需要填写的是热量传递过程中的一个关键环节。\n定位关键信息：通过流程图的结构和上下文，可以确定题目在询问热量传递的过程。\n解题思路：在H段中，原文明确提到墨西哥湾暖流，向北流动时，会将热量释放到空气中（\"surrenders heat to the air\"）。也就是将热量蒸发到空气中去，因此，热量（heat）是这一环节的关键词，符合流程图中热量传递的描述。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59844","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the flow chart below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022tCw5nxlACq1669988142.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8209:59845:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"denser","acceptedAnswers":["denser"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Having given up its heat to the air, the now-cooler water becomes denser and sinks into the North Atlantic by a mile or more in a process oceanographers call thermohaline circulation.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目要求完成流程图，根据上下文推断此处询问的是水在失去热量后的变化状态。\n定位关键信息：利用流程图上下文提示，定位到I段描述水在释放热量后的状态变化。\n解题思路：根据原文I段中“the now-cooler water becomes denser”水体释放热量后，温度降低的海水密度增大，可以直接确定答案为\"denser\"，海水密度增大。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59845","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the flow chart below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022tCw5nxlACq1669988142.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8209:59846:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"Great Ocean Conveyor","acceptedAnswers":["Great Ocean Conveyor"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This massive column of cascading cold is the main engine powering a deepwater current called the Great Ocean Conveyor that snakes through all the world’s oceans.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目要求完成一个流程图，需要填入一个不超过三个词的名词词组，表示一个海洋环流系统的名称。\n定位关键信息：根据流程图上下文，题目需要填入的是海洋环流系统的名称。在文章中寻找描述海洋环流系统的句子，重点关注I段中关于海洋环流系统的描述。\n解题思路：I段中提到“this massive column of cascading cold is the main engine powering a deepwater current called the Great Ocean Conveyor”，这股巨大的冷空气团是驱动深海水流的主要动力，这种被称为“大海洋输送带”的水流蜿蜒穿过全球所有海洋。这句话明确指出了这个海洋环流系统的名称是“Great Ocean Conveyor”。因此，根据原文信息，答案为“Great Ocean Conveyor”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59846","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the flow chart below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022tCw5nxlACq1669988142.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8209:59847:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"freshwater","acceptedAnswers":["freshwater"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But as the North Atlantic fills with freshwater, it grows less dense, making the waters carried northward by the Gulf Stream less able to sink. The new mass of relatively freshwater sits on top of the ocean like a big thermal blanket, threatening the thermohaline circulation. That in turn could make the Gulf Stream slow or veer southward.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目要求根据文章内容完成流程图，其中需要填写一个不超过三个词的答案，因为什么的增加，导致影响力墨西哥湾暖流。\n定位关键信息：根据流程图的上下文，可以定位到文章中关于墨西哥湾暖流的影响。\n解题思路：I段提到，随着北大西洋淡水的不断注入，海水密度逐渐降低，墨西哥湾暖流向北输送的海水也难以下沉。这些相对淡水的新堆积层如同厚重的保温毯覆盖在海面，威胁着盐温环流的正常运作。这里提到了淡水的增加，后文紧接着提到对盐温环流的影响，间接影响了墨西哥湾暖流。因此，填入淡水，freshwater。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59847","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the flow chart below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022tCw5nxlACq1669988142.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8209:59848:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"southward","acceptedAnswers":["southward"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The new mass of relatively freshwater sits on top of the ocean like a big thermal blanket, threatening the thermohaline circulation. That in turn could make the Gulf Stream slow or veer southward. At some point, the whole system could simply shut down, and do so quickly.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目要求根据流程图完成填空，需要填写墨西哥湾暖流可能发生的变化方向。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Gulf Stream\"定位到I段，找到\"Gulf Stream slow or veer southward\"这一关键信息。\n解题思路：根据原文I段中的句子\"make the Gulf Stream slow or veer southward\"可以确定，当淡水增多时，墨西哥湾暖流可能会减速，甚至向南移动，因此答案为\"southward\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59848","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the flow chart below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022tCw5nxlACq1669988142.png]","maxWords":3}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59840","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-16\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 14-16 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>The writer mentions the paintings in the first two paragraphs to illustrate</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"59841","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-16\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 14-16 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Why is it hard for the poor to survive the next cooling period?</strong></p>","firstNumber":15},{"id":"59842","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-16\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 14-16 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Why is the winter temperature in continental Europe higher than that in North America?</strong></p>","firstNumber":16},{"id":"59843","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 17-21\nMatch each statement (Questions 17-21) with the correct person A-D in the box below. Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 17-21 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Bob Dickson\nB Terrence Joyce\nC William Curry\nD National Academy of Science","html":"<p><strong>List of People</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>A</strong> Bob Dickson&nbsp;</p><p><strong>B</strong> Terrence byce&nbsp;</p><p><strong>C</strong> William Curry&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>D</strong> National Academy of Science&nbsp;</p><p><strong>17.</strong>A quick climate change wreaks great disruption.<strong class=\"source-blank\">[17] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":17},{"id":"59844","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the flow chart below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022tCw5nxlACq1669988142.png]","html":"<p><strong>22</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"59845","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the flow chart below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022tCw5nxlACq1669988142.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">23</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"59846","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the flow chart below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022tCw5nxlACq1669988142.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">24</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"59847","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the flow chart below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022tCw5nxlACq1669988142.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">25</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"59848","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the flow chart below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022tCw5nxlACq1669988142.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">26</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>A New Ice Age</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>William Curry is a serious, sober climate scientist, not an art critic. But he has spent a lot of time perusing Emanuel Gottlieb Leutze’s famous painting ‘George Washington Crossing the Delaware,’ which depicts a boatload of colonial American soldiers making their way to attack English and Hessian troops the day after Christmas in 1776. ‘Most people think these other guys in the boat are rowing, but they are actually pushing the ice away,’ says Curry, tapping his finger on a reproduction of the painting. Sure enough, the lead oarsman is bashing the frozen river with his boot. ‘I grew up in Philadelphia. The place in this painting is 30 minutes away by car. I can tell you, this kind of thing just doesn’t happen anymore.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>But it may again soon. And ice-choked scenes, similar to those immortalized by the 16th-century Flemish painter Pieter Brueghel the Elder, may also return to Europe. His works, including the 1565 masterpiece ‘Hunters in the Snow,’ make the now-temperate European landscapes look more like Lapland. Such frigid settings were commonplace during a period dating roughly from 1300 to 1850 because much of North America and Europe was in the throes of a little ice age. And now there is mounting evidence that the chill could return. A growing number of scientists believe conditions are ripe for another prolonged cooldown, or small ice age. While no one is predicting a brutal ice sheet like the one that covered the Northern Hemisphere with glaciers about 12,000 years ago, the next cooling trend could drop average temperatures 5 degrees Fahrenheit over much of the United States and 10 degrees in the Northeast, northern Europe, and northern Asia.</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>‘It could happen in 10 years,’ says Terrence Joyce, who chairs the Woods Hole Physical Oceanography Department. ‘Once it does, it can take hundreds of years to reverse.’ And he is alarmed that Americans have yet to take the threat seriously.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>A drop of 5 to 10 degrees entails much more than simply bumping up the thermostat and carrying on. Both economically and ecologically, such quick, persistent chilling could have devastating consequences. A 2002 report titled ‘Abrupt Climate Change: Inevitable Surprises,’ produced by the National Academy of Sciences, pegged the cost from agricultural losses alone at $100 billion to $250 billion while also predicting that damage to ecologies could be vast and incalculable. A grim sampler: disappearing forests, increased housing expenses, dwindling freshwater, lower crop yields, and accelerated species extinctions.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Political changes since the last ice age could make survival far more difficult for the world’s poor. During previous cooling periods, whole tribes simply picked up and moved south, but that option doesn’t work in the modern, tense world of closed borders. ‘To the extent that abrupt climate change may cause rapid and extensive changes of fortune for those who live off the land, the inability to migrate may remove one of the major safety nets for distressed people,’ says the report.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>But first things first. Isn’t the earth actually warming? In deed it is, says Joyce. In his cluttered office, full of soft light from the foggy Cape Cod morning, he explains how such warming could actually be the surprising culprit of the next mini-ice age. The paradox is a result of the appearance over the past 30 years in the North Atlantic of huge rivers of freshwater – the equivalent of a 10-foot-thick layer – mixed into the salty sea. No one is certain where the fresh torrents are coming from, but a prime suspect is melting Arctic ice, caused by a buildup of carbon dioxide in the atmosphere that traps solar energy.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The freshwater trend is major news in ocean-science circles. Bob Dickson, a British oceanographer who sounded an alarm at a February conference in Honolulu, has termed the drop in salinity and temperature in the Labrador Sea – a body of water between northeastern Canada and Greenland that adjoins the Atlantic – ‘arguably the largest full-depth changes observed in the modem instrumental oceanographic record.’ The trend could cause a little ice age by subverting the northern penetration of Gulf Stream waters.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Normally, the Gulf Stream, laden with heat soaked up in the tropics, meanders up the east coasts of the United States and Canada. As it flows northward, the stream surrenders heat to the air. Because the prevailing North Atlantic winds blow eastward, a lot of the heat wafts to Europe. That’s why many scientists believe winter temperatures on the Continent are as much as 36 degrees Fahrenheit warmer than those in North America at the same latitude. Frigid Boston, for example, lies at almost precisely the same latitude as balmy Rome. And some scientists say the heat also warms Americans and Canadians. ‘It’s a real mistake to think of this solely as a European phenomenon,’ says Joyce.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Having given up its heat to the air, the now-cooler water becomes denser and sinks into the North Atlantic by a mile or more in a process oceanographers call thermohaline circulation. This massive column of cascading cold is the main engine powering a deepwater current called the Great Ocean Conveyor that snakes through all the world’s oceans. But as the North Atlantic fills with freshwater, it grows less dense, making the waters carried northward by the Gulf Stream less able to sink. The new mass of relatively freshwater sits on top of the ocean like a big thermal blanket, threatening the thermohaline circulation. That in turn could make the Gulf Stream slow or veer southward. At some point, the whole system could simply shut down, and do so quickly. ‘There is increasing evidence that we are getting closer toa transition point, from which we can jump to a new state. Small changes, such as a couple of years of heavy precipitation or melting ice at high latitudes, could yield a big response,’ says Joyce.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘You have all this freshwater sitting at high latitudes, and it can literally take hundreds of years to get rid of it,’ Joyce says. So while the globe as a whole gets warmer by tiny fractions of 1 degree Fahrenheit annually, the North Atlantic region could, in a decade, get up to 10 degrees colder. What worries researchers at Woods Hole is that history is on the side of rapid shutdown. They know it has happened before.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8209&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8210","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Learning Lessons From the Past","book":"阅读还原集Vol.13","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.13 · Test 4 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8210:59849:27","type":"choice","text":"When the writer describes the impact of monumental ruins today, he emphasizes","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The monumental ruins left behind by those past societies hold a fascination for all of us. We marvel at them when as children we first learn of them through pictures. When we grow up, many of us plan vacations in order to experience them at first hand. We feel drawn to their often spectacular and haunting beauty, and also to the mysteries that they pose.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是作者描述当今宏伟遗迹的影响时，他更侧重哪一点。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"monumental ruins today\"和\"impact\"可以定位到B段，该段描述了宏伟遗迹对现代人的影响。\n解题思路：B段中作者描述了宏伟遗迹对现代人的吸引力，包括人们对它们的着迷、惊叹，以及人们被它们的壮丽和神秘所吸引。作者强调了这些遗迹的浪漫吸引力，即它们所呈现的神秘和壮丽之美，以及它们所引发的好奇心。因此，正确答案是D，即它们的浪漫吸引力。","options":["the income they generate from tourism.","the area of land they occupy.","their archaeological value.","their romantic appeal."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59849","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8210:59850:28","type":"choice","text":"Recent findings concerning vanished civilisations","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This suspicion of unintended ecological suicide (ecocide) has been confirmed by discoveries made in recent decades by archaeologists, climatologists, historians, palaeontologists, and palynologists (pollen scientists).\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问关于消失的文明，最近的发现了什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"Recent findings\"和\"vanished civilisations\"定位到C段首句，该句提到\"recent decades\"的发现与消失的文明相关。\n解题思路：C段首句提到\"recent decades\"的发现由考古学家、气候学家、历史学家、古生物学家和花粉科学家共同证实了消失的文明的\"无意间的生态自杀\"，说明这些发现来自多个学科领域，对应选项C。选项A、B、D与原文信息不符。","options":["have overturned long-held beliefs.","caused controversy amongst scientists.","come from a variety of disciplines.","identified one main cause of environmental damage."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59850","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8210:59851:29","type":"choice","text":"What does the writer say about ways in which former societies collapsed?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Those past collapses tended to follow somewhat similar courses constituting variations on a theme.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问作者是怎么论述古代社会的衰落方式。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的\"ways in which former societies collapsed\"定位到文章中描述过去社会崩溃方式的句子。\n解题思路：原文D段提到\"Those past collapses tended to follow somewhat similar courses constituting variations on a theme\"，意思是过去的文明衰落通常遵循相似的进程，只是具体细节有所不同。这与选项A\"衰落的过程通常相似\"意思一致。选项B、C、D在原文中均未提及或与原文表述不符。","options":["The pace of decline was usually similar.","The likelihood of collapse would have been foreseeable.","Deterioration invariably led to total collapse.","Individual citizens could sometimes influence the course of events."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59851","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8210:59852:30","type":"choice","text":"It is widely believed that environmental problems represent the main danger faced by the modern world.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Today many people feel that environmental problems overshadow all the other threats to global civilisation.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问“人们普遍认为环境问题是现代社会面临的主要危险”是否符合作者的观点。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"environmental problems\"和\"main danger\"定位到E段第一句。\n解题思路：段落E中，作者明确写道：“如今，许多人觉得环境问题使全球文明面临的所有其他威胁都相形见绌。”“使...相形见绌”(overshadow) 意味着环境问题被认为比其他威胁更重要、更突出，这与“主要危险”(main danger) 的含义一致。因此，该陈述与作者在文中的信息一致，答案为YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59852","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30-34\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8210:59853:31","type":"choice","text":"The accumulation of poisonous substances is a relatively modern problem.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：These environmental problems include the same eight that undermined past societies, plus four new ones: human-caused climate change, the build-up of toxic chemicals in the environment, energy shortages, and full human utilisation of the Earth’s photosynthetic capacity.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“有毒物质的积累是一个相对现代才出现的问题”是否与作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“accumulation of poisonous substances”定位到原文E段，找到“the build-up of toxic chemicals in the environment”这一表述。\n解题思路：原文E段明确指出有毒化学物质在环境中的积累是四个新的环境问题之一，与过去的八个问题并列，这表明有毒物质的积累是一个相对现代的问题。因此，题目陈述与作者的观点一致，答案为A（Yes）。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59853","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30-34\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8210:59854:32","type":"choice","text":"There is general agreement that the threats posed by environmental problems are very serious.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But the seriousness of these current environmental problems is vigorously debated.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“人们普遍认为，环境问题带来的威胁非常严重”这一观点是否与作者一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"environmental problems\"和\"very serious\"，在文章中定位到E段，该段提到\"the seriousness of these current environmental problems is vigorously debated\"，意思是当前环境问题的严重性存在激烈争论。\n解题思路：根据原文句子\"the seriousness of these current environmental problems is vigorously debated\"，可以看出作者认为环境问题的严重性存在争议，并没有达成普遍共识，因此题目中\"there is general agreement\"的说法与原文不符，作者并未表示普遍认同环境问题威胁非常严重。所以答案为No。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59854","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30-34\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8210:59855:33","type":"choice","text":"Some past societies resembled present-day societies more closely than others.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：We differ from past societies in some respects that put us at lower risk than them; some of those respects often mentioned include our powerful technology (i.e. its beneficial effects), globalisation, modem medicine, and greater knowledge of past societies and of distant modem societies. We also differ from past societies in some respects that put us at greater risk than them: again, our potent technology (i.e. its unintended destructive effects), globalisation (such that now a problem in one part of the world affects all the rest), the dependence of millions of us on modern medicine for our survival, and our much larger human population.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目判断“某些古代社会比其它古代社会更接近现代社会”这一说法是否与作者在文中的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"past societies\", \"present-day societies\", \"resembled...more closely\" 作为关键词，寻找文中比较不同古代社会与现代社会的相似度的内容。\n解题思路：文章确实比较了古代社会和现代社会的异同（主要在段落F），但这是将“古代社会”作为一个整体与“现代社会”进行对比。文中没有任何地方对不同古代社会（如玛雅、复活节岛、格陵兰岛 Norse 社会等）进行相互比较，并评判哪个更接近现代社会。题目信息在原文中找不到依据，因此答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59855","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30-34\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8210:59856:34","type":"choice","text":"We should be careful when drawing comparisons between past and present.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：We shouldn’t be so naive as to think that the study of the past will yield simple solutions, directly transferable to our societies today.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“在比较过去和现在时，我们要谨慎。”是否与作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"comparisons between past and present\"可以定位到文章的F段，这一段讨论了研究过去和现在之间的差异，以及我们不应该过于简单地认为过去的研究可以直接应用到现代社会。\n解题思路：原文中F段明确提到\"我们不应该过于天真地认为，对过去的研究，能给我们现在的问题带来一个简单答案，并且直接把过去的方法搬到现在来。\"这表明作者认为在比较过去和现在时，应该谨慎。因此，题目中的陈述与作者的观点一致，应该选择A（Yes）。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59856","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30-34\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8210:59857:35","type":"choice","text":"35 Evidence of the greatness of some former civilisations","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：We feel drawn to their often spectacular and haunting beauty, and also to the mysteries that they pose. The scales of the ruins testify to the former wealth and power of their builders.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是\"某些古老文明曾辉煌的佐证\"是什么样的。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"evidence of the greatness of some former civilisations\"可以定位到B段中描述古老文明证据的句子。\n解题思路：原文中提到，\"The scales of the ruins testify to the former wealth and power of their builders\"，即\"这些废墟的规模证明了他们建造者的昔日的财富和权力\"。这句话表明，某些古老文明曾辉煌的佐证，是以实体建筑的形式存在的，即\"physical structures\"，因此答案为C。","options":["is not necessarily valid.","provides grounds for an optimistic outlook.","exists in the form of physical structures.","is potentially both positive and negative.","will not provide direct solutions for present problems.","is greater now than in the past."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59857","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 35-39\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below. Write the correct letter, A-F.\nA is not necessarily valid.\nB provides grounds for an optimistic outlook.\nC exists in the form of physical structures.\nD is potentially both positive and negative.\nE will not provide direct solutions for present problems.\nF is greater now than in the past."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8210:59857:36","type":"choice","text":"36 The parallel between an individual’s life and the life of a society","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Writers find it tempting to draw analogies between the course of human societies and the course of individual human lives – to talk of a society’s birth, growth, peak, old age and eventual death.  But that metaphor proves erroneous for many past societies: they declined rapidly after reaching peak numbers and power, and those rapid declines must have come as a surprise and shock to their citizens.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是，将个体与社会进行类比是怎么样的。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"parallel between an individual’s life and the life of a society\"定位到D段中\"draw analogies between the course of human societies and the course of individual human lives\"。\n解题思路：原文明确提到作者们倾向于将社会的发展过程与个体的生命历程进行类比，包括出生、成长、顶峰、老年和死亡。但在很多层面上，这种类比是有误的。也就是说不一定成立，与A项一致，因此答案为A。","options":["is not necessarily valid.","provides grounds for an optimistic outlook.","exists in the form of physical structures.","is potentially both positive and negative.","will not provide direct solutions for present problems.","is greater now than in the past."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59857","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 35-39\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below. Write the correct letter, A-F.\nA is not necessarily valid.\nB provides grounds for an optimistic outlook.\nC exists in the form of physical structures.\nD is potentially both positive and negative.\nE will not provide direct solutions for present problems.\nF is greater now than in the past."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8210:59857:37","type":"choice","text":"37 The number of environmental problems that societies face","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：These environmental problems include the same eight that undermined past societies, plus four new ones: human-caused climate change, the build-up of toxic chemicals in the environment, energy shortages, and full human utilisation of the Earth’s photosynthetic capacity.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是社会面临的环境问题是怎么样的。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"environmental problems\"和\"number\"可以定位到E段，该段提到了环境问题的数量。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到了环境问题的数量，包括过去社会面临的环境问题和新增的环境问题，总共是八个旧问题加上四个新问题，因此可以确定答案为F。","options":["is not necessarily valid.","provides grounds for an optimistic outlook.","exists in the form of physical structures.","is potentially both positive and negative.","will not provide direct solutions for present problems.","is greater now than in the past."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59857","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 35-39\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below. Write the correct letter, A-F.\nA is not necessarily valid.\nB provides grounds for an optimistic outlook.\nC exists in the form of physical structures.\nD is potentially both positive and negative.\nE will not provide direct solutions for present problems.\nF is greater now than in the past."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8210:59857:38","type":"choice","text":"38 The power of technology","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：We differ from past societies in some respects that put us at lower risk than them; some of those respects often mentioned include our powerful technology (i.e. its beneficial effects), globalisation, modem medicine, and greater knowledge of past societies and of distant modem societies. We also differ from past societies in some respects that put us at greater risk than them: again, our potent technology (i.e. its unintended destructive effects), globalisation (such that now a problem in one part of the world affects all the rest), the dependence of millions of us on modern medicine for our survival, and our much larger human population.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“科技的力量”怎么样。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“power of technology”可以定位到F段中提到的“our powerful technology (i.e. its beneficial effects)”。\n解题思路：原文中明确指出，我们与过去社会的不同之处在于我们的科技力量，然后说明科技有益的影响，这使得我们相对于过去社会来说风险更低。同时，我们的科技，也会使得现代社会比过去风险更高，然后说明科技的负面影响。因此，科技有利也有弊，因此，选择D项。","options":["is not necessarily valid.","provides grounds for an optimistic outlook.","exists in the form of physical structures.","is potentially both positive and negative.","will not provide direct solutions for present problems.","is greater now than in the past."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59857","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 35-39\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below. Write the correct letter, A-F.\nA is not necessarily valid.\nB provides grounds for an optimistic outlook.\nC exists in the form of physical structures.\nD is potentially both positive and negative.\nE will not provide direct solutions for present problems.\nF is greater now than in the past."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8210:59857:39","type":"choice","text":"39 A consideration of historical events and trends","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：We shouldn’t be so naive as to think that the study of the past will yield simple solutions, directly transferable to our societies today.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“对历史事件和趋势的思考”怎么样。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"historical events and trends\"可以定位到文章中讨论历史事件和趋势的部分。\n解题思路：段落F中，作者明确指出，我们不应该过于天真地认为，对过去的研究，能给我们现在的问题带来一个简单答案，并且直接把过去的方法搬到现在来。这表明作者认为，从历史中学习“不会为当前问题提供直接的解决方案”。这与选项E的含义完全吻合。因此，正确答案是E。","options":["is not necessarily valid.","provides grounds for an optimistic outlook.","exists in the form of physical structures.","is potentially both positive and negative.","will not provide direct solutions for present problems.","is greater now than in the past."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59857","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 35-39\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below. Write the correct letter, A-F.\nA is not necessarily valid.\nB provides grounds for an optimistic outlook.\nC exists in the form of physical structures.\nD is potentially both positive and negative.\nE will not provide direct solutions for present problems.\nF is greater now than in the past."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8210:59858:40","type":"choice","text":"40 What is the main argument of the reading passage?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Questions like this illustrate why those famous collapses of past civilisations have taken on more meaning than just that of a romantic mystery. Perhaps there are some practical lessons that we could learn from all those past collapses. But there are also differences between the modem world and its problems, and those past societies and their problems... Perhaps we can still learn from the past, but only if we think carefully about its lessons.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是这篇文章的主要论点是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"main argument\"定位到文章中总结性的段落，通常在文章的结尾处。\n解题思路：原文F段开始就说明我们或许可以从过去学到一些东西，然后比较现代社会和过去社会的差异，最后一句总结\"Perhaps we can still learn from the past, but only if we think carefully about its lessons.\"（也许我们仍然可以从过去中学习，但前提是必须认真思考其中的教训。）这句话表明文章的主要论点是过去与现在有相似，也有不同，这与选项A中提到的“过去和现在社会之间既有差异也有相似之处”是一致的。因此，选项A最符合文章的主要论点。","options":["There are differences as well as similarities between past and present societies.","More should be done to preserve the physical remains of earlier civilisations.","Some historical accounts of great civilisations are inaccurate.","Modern societies are dependent on each other for their continuing survival."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59858","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59849","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","html":"<p><strong>When the writer describes the impact of monumental ruins today, he emphasizes</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"59850","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","html":"<p><strong>Recent findings concerning vanished civilisations</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"59851","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","html":"<p><strong>What does the writer say about ways in which former societies collapsed?</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"59852","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30-34\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>It is widely believed that environmental problems represent the main danger faced by the modern world.</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"59853","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30-34\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>The accumulation of poisonous substances is a relatively modern problem.</strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"59854","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30-34\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>There is general agreement that the threats posed by environmental problems are very serious.</strong></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"59855","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30-34\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Some past societies resembled present-day societies more closely than others.</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"59856","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30-34\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>We should be careful when drawing comparisons between past and present.</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"59857","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 35-39\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below. Write the correct letter, A-F.\nA is not necessarily valid.\nB provides grounds for an optimistic outlook.\nC exists in the form of physical structures.\nD is potentially both positive and negative.\nE will not provide direct solutions for present problems.\nF is greater now than in the past.","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> is not necessarily valid.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>B</strong> provides grounds for an optimistic outlook.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>C</strong> exists in the form of physical structures.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>D</strong> is potentially both positive and negative.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>E</strong> will not provide direct solutions for present problems.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>F</strong> is greater now than in the past.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-top: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>35</strong> Evidence of the greatness of some former civilisations <strong class=\"source-blank\">[35] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"59858","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","html":"<p><strong>40</strong> <strong>What is the main argument of the reading passage?</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Learning Lessons From the Past&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Many past societies collapsed or vanished, leaving behind monumental ruins such as those that the poet Shelley imagined in his sonnet, Ozymandias. By collapse, I mean a drastic decrease in human population size and/or political/economic/social complexity, over a considerable, for an extended time. By those standards, most people would consider the following past societies to have been famous victims of full-fledged collapses rather than of just minor declines: the Anasazi and Cahokia within the boundaries of the modem US, the Maya cities in Central American, Moche and Tiwanaku societies in South America, Norse Greenland, Mycenean Greece and Minoan Crete in Europe, Great Zimbabwe in Africa, Angkor Wat and the Harappan Indus Valley cities in Asia, and Easter Island in the Pacific Ocean.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The monumental ruins left behind by those past societies hold a fascination for all of us. We marvel at them when as children we first learn of them through pictures. When we grow up, many of us plan vacations in order to experience them at first hand. We feel drawn to their often spectacular and haunting beauty, and also to the mysteries that they pose. The scales of the ruins testify to the former wealth and power of their builders. Yet these builders vanished, abandoning the great structures that they had created at such effort. How could a society that was once so mighty end up collapsing?&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>It has long been suspected that many of those mysterious abandonments were at least partly triggered by ecological problems: people inadvertently destroying the environmental resources on which their societies depended. This suspicion of unintended ecological suicide (ecocide) has been confirmed by discoveries made in recent decades by archaeologists, climatologists, historians, palaeontologists, and palynologists (pollen scientists). The processes through which past societies have undermined themselves by damaging their environments fall into eight categories, whose relative importance differs from case to case: deforestation and habitat destruction, soil problems, water management problems, overhunting, overfishing, effects of introduced species on native species, human population growth, and increased impact of people.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Those past collapses tended to follow somewhat similar courses constituting variations on a theme. Writers find it tempting to draw analogies between the course of human societies and the course of individual human lives – to talk of a society’s birth, growth, peak, old age and eventual death. But that metaphor proves erroneous for many past societies: they declined rapidly after reaching peak numbers and power, and those rapid declines must have come as a surprise and shock to their citizens. Obviously, too, this trajectory is not one that all past societies followed unvaryingly to completion: different societies collapsed to different degrees and in somewhat different ways, while many societies did not collapse at all.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Today many people feel that environmental problems overshadow all the other threats to global civilisation. These environmental problems include the same eight that undermined past societies, plus four new ones: human-caused climate change, the build-up of toxic chemicals in the environment, energy shortages, and full human utilisation of the Earth’s photosynthetic capacity. But the seriousness of these current environmental problems is vigorously debated. Are the risks greatly exaggerated, or conversely are they underestimated? Will modem technology solve our problems, or is it creating new problems faster than it solves old ones? When we deplete one resource (e.g. wood, oil, or ocean fish), can we count on being able to substitute some new resource (e.g. plastics, wind and solar energy, or farmed fish)? Isn’t the rate of human population growth declining, such that we’re already on course for the world’s population to level off at home manageable number of people?</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Questions like this illustrate why those famous collapses of past civilisations have taken on more meaning than just that of a romantic mystery. Perhaps there are some practical lessons that we could learn from all those past collapses. But there are also differences between the modem world and its problems, and those past societies and their problems. We shouldn’t be so naive as to think that the study of the past will yield simple solutions, directly transferable to our societies today. We differ from past societies in some respects that put us at lower risk than them; some of those respects often mentioned include our powerful technology (i.e. its beneficial effects), globalisation, modem medicine, and greater knowledge of past societies and of distant modem societies. We also differ from past societies in some respects that put us at greater risk than them: again, our potent technology (i.e. its unintended destructive effects), globalisation (such that now a problem in one part of the world affects all the rest), the dependence of millions of us on modern medicine for our survival, and our much larger human population. Perhaps we can still learn from the past, but only if we think carefully about its lessons.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8210&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8189","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Bamboo, a Wonder Plant","book":"阅读还原集Vol.13","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.13 · Test 3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8189:59789:1","type":"choice","text":"1 an assessment of current levels of knowledge about bamboo","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Despite bamboo’s importance, we know surprisingly little about it. A recent report published by the UN Environment Programme (UNEP) and the International Network for Bamboo and Rattan (INBAR) has revealed just how profound our ignorance of global bamboo resources is, particularly in relation to conservation.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落包含了评估当前人们对竹子了解多少。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"assessment of current levels of knowledge about bamboo\"定位到B段首句\"Despite bamboo’s importance, we know surprisingly little about it\"，这句话直接表明人们对竹子的了解很少，紧接着第二句提到一份报告揭示了我们对全球竹资源的认知是多么的匮乏。\n解题思路：原文B段明确提到\"we know surprisingly little about it\"（我们对它的了解少得惊人），并且提到一份报告揭示了\"how profound our ignorance of global bamboo resources is\"（我们对全球竹资源的认知是多么的匮乏），这正对应题目中\"an assessment of current levels of knowledge about bamboo\"（评估当前人们对竹子了解多少）的要求。因此B段包含了题目所问的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59789","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nThe passage has six sections, A-F. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8189:59789:2","type":"choice","text":"2 a comparison between bamboo and more fragile plants","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：There are two separate issues here’, says Ray Townsend, arboretum manager at the Royal Botanic Gardens, ‘Some plants are threatened because they can’t survive in the habitat – they aren’t strong enough or there aren’t enough of them, perhaps. But bamboo can take care of itself – it’s strong enough to survive if left alone.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求找出竹子与更脆弱植物对比的段落。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"comparison between bamboo and more fragile plants\"定位到E段，该段明确提到了竹子与其他植物的对比，指出竹子比其他植物更强壮。\n解题思路：E段中Ray Townsend明确对比了竹子与其他植物的生存能力，指出竹子比其他植物更强壮，能够自我保护，而其他植物则因为生存能力弱而面临威胁，这正好符合题目要求，因此，选择E段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59789","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nThe passage has six sections, A-F. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8189:59789:3","type":"choice","text":"3 details of the commercial significance of bamboo","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：However, bamboo’s most immediate significance lies in its economic value. Many countries, particularly in Asia, are involved in the trade of bamboo products. Modern processing techniques mean it can be used in a variety of ways, for example as flooring and laminates. Traditionally it is used in construction, but one of the fastest growing bamboo products is paper – 25 per cent of paper produced in India is made from bamboo fibre.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落包含“关于竹子的商业重要性的三个细节”。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“commercial significance”（商业重要性）定位到文章中关于竹子经济价值的描述。\n解题思路：D段明确提到了竹子的经济价值，包括竹制品贸易、现代加工技术的应用（如地板和层压板）、传统用途（建筑）以及快速增长的产品（纸张），这些都是竹子商业重要性的具体细节。因此，答案为D。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59789","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nThe passage has six sections, A-F. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8189:59789:4","type":"choice","text":"4 a human development that is threatening the availability of bamboo","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But in the past 100 years or so, resources have come under increasing pressure as populations have exploded and large areas of bamboo forest have been cleared to make way for commercial plantations.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落包含“某项人类活动正危及竹资源的可持续供应。”\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"threatening the availability of bamboo\"和\"human development\"可以定位到A段中描述人类活动对竹子造成威胁的句子。\n解题思路：A段明确提到\"large areas of bamboo forest have been cleared to make way for commercial plantations\"，即大面积的竹林被清除，以腾出空间用于商业种植园，这正是人类发展活动对竹资源的可持续性造成的威胁。因此答案为A。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59789","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nThe passage has six sections, A-F. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8189:59789:5","type":"choice","text":"5 a description of the limited extent of existing research on bamboo","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Despite bamboo’s importance, we know surprisingly little about it. A recent report published by the UN Environment Programme (UNEP) and the International Network for Bamboo and Rattan (INBAR) has revealed just how profound our ignorance of global bamboo resources is, particularly in relation to conservation.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求找出描述现有竹类研究有限的段落。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"limited extent of existing research\"（现有研究的有限范围）定位到B段首句\"Despite bamboo’s importance, we know surprisingly little about it\"（尽管竹子很重要，但我们对其了解惊人地少）。\n解题思路：B段明确提到\"we know surprisingly little about it\"（我们对它了解很少）和\"our ignorance of global bamboo resources is...profound\"（我们对全球竹资源的认知是多么的匮乏），直接对应题目中\"limited extent of existing research\"（现有研究的有限）。此外，该段还提到\"only 38 ‘priority species’ identified for their commercial value have been the subject of any real scientific research to date\"（目前只有38种被列为商业价值的优先物种受到真正的科学研究），进一步印证了竹子研究范围的局限性。因此，B段是正确答案。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59789","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nThe passage has six sections, A-F. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8189:59789:6","type":"choice","text":"6 examples of the uses to which bamboo is put","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Modern processing techniques mean it can be used in a variety of ways, for example as flooring and laminates. Traditionally it is used in construction, but one of the fastest growing bamboo products is paper – 25 per cent of paper produced in India is made from bamboo fibre.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“竹子的用途的例子”，需要找到文章中列举竹子具体用途的部分。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“examples of the uses”（用途的例子）定位，在D段中找到明确列举竹子用途的句子。\n解题思路：D段明确列举了竹子的多种用途，包括现代处理技术下的地板和层压板、传统的建筑用途以及纸张制造（印度25%的纸张由竹纤维制成）。这些具体用途的例子与题目要求完全匹配，因此D段是正确答案。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59789","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nThe passage has six sections, A-F. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8189:59789:7","type":"choice","text":"7 an explanation of how bamboo may contribute to the survival of range of plants","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘Bamboo’s pattern of mass flowering and mass death leaves behind large areas of dry biomass that attract wildfire,’ says Kapos, ‘When these bum, they create patches of open ground far bigger than would be left by a fallen tree. Patchiness helps to preserve diversity because certain plant species do better during the early stages of regeneration when there are gaps in the canopy.’\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段落解释了竹子如何有助于多种植物的生存。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"contribute to the survival of range of plants\"，可以在C段中找到相关的句子，其中提到了竹子在森林结构和动态中的作用，以及它如何通过创造开放空间来促进植物多样性。\n解题思路：原文中C段的句子明确指出了竹子通过其开花和死亡的周期性模式，会留下大片干燥的生物燃料，这些区域容易引发野火，会形成比倒树留下的空地大得多的空地。这种斑块状分布有助于保护生物多样性，因为某些植物在再生初期的空隙中生长得更好。这与题目中关于竹子如何有助于多种植物生存的信息完全吻合，因此C段是正确答案。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59789","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nThe passage has six sections, A-F. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8189:59790:8","type":"choice","text":"8 Some people do not regard bamboo as an endangered plant species.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In a lot of places, the people who live with bamboo don’t perceive it as being under threat in any way, says Kapos, ‘In fact, a lot of bamboo species are very invasive if they’ve been introduced.’\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问“有些人不认为竹子是一种濒危植物物种”，需要匹配对应的人。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词“do not regard bamboo as an endangered plant species”可以定位到G段中“don’t perceive it as being under threat in any way”，与题目意思一致。\n解题思路：E段中直接引用了Valerie Kapos的话，提到“生活在竹子附近的人们并不认为竹子有任何威胁”，并补充说明“很多竹子物种如果被引入，会非常具有侵略性”，这与题目“有些人不认为竹子是濒危植物”吻合，因此答案为B（Valerie Kapos）。","options":["Ian Redmond","Valerie Kapos","Chris Stapleton","Ray Townsend"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59790","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 8-11\nLook at the following statements (Questions 8-11) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-D. Write the correct letter, A-D, in boxes 8-11 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nList of people\nA Ian Redmond\nB Valerie Kapos\nC Chris Stapleton\nD Ray Townsend"},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8189:59790:9","type":"choice","text":"9 A scarcity of bamboo places certain wildlife under threat.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For the 650 or so that remain in the wild, it’s a vital food source. Without it, says Ian Redmond, chairman of the Ape Alliance, their chances of survival would be reduced significantly.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“竹子的稀缺使某些野生动物受到威胁”。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“scarcity of bamboo”和“certain wildlife under threat”定位到B段，找到Ian Redmond说的话，其中明确提到竹子是野生动物的重要食物来源，没有竹子，它们的生存机会将大大减少。\n解题思路：原文中Ian Redmond的话明确指出竹子对于野生动物的生存至关重要，没有竹子会导致它们的生存机会减少，这与题目描述的“竹子的稀缺使某些野生动物受到威胁”完全一致。因此，答案为A。","options":["Ian Redmond","Valerie Kapos","Chris Stapleton","Ray Townsend"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59790","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 8-11\nLook at the following statements (Questions 8-11) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-D. Write the correct letter, A-D, in boxes 8-11 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nList of people\nA Ian Redmond\nB Valerie Kapos\nC Chris Stapleton\nD Ray Townsend"},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8189:59790:10","type":"choice","text":"10 Research methods investigating endangered plants have yet to be fully developed.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘People have only started looking at this during the past 10-15 years, and only now are they understanding how to go about it systematically,’ says Dr Valerie Kapos, one of the report’s authors.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求将“研究濒危植物的方法尚未完全成熟”这一陈述与列表中对应的人物匹配。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"Research methods\"和\"endangered plants\"，可以在B段中找到相关句子。\n解题思路：段落B中，Valerie Kapos在谈论评估植物保护状况的科学时指出：“人们只是在过去10到15年间才开始关注这个问题，并且直到现在才开始理解如何系统地着手进行。” 这句话明确表示，针对植物（包括竹子）的保护研究方法本身仍处于早期发展和完善阶段，尚未成熟。因此，提出此观点的人是Valerie Kapos，对应选项B。","options":["Ian Redmond","Valerie Kapos","Chris Stapleton","Ray Townsend"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59790","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 8-11\nLook at the following statements (Questions 8-11) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-D. Write the correct letter, A-D, in boxes 8-11 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nList of people\nA Ian Redmond\nB Valerie Kapos\nC Chris Stapleton\nD Ray Townsend"},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8189:59790:11","type":"choice","text":"11 The greatest danger to bamboo is a disturbance of the places it grows in.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘There are two separate issues here’, says Ray Townsend, arboretum manager at the Royal Botanic Gardens, ‘Some plants are threatened because they can’t survive in the habitat – they aren’t strong enough or there aren’t enough of them, perhaps. But bamboo can take care of itself – it’s strong enough to survive if left alone. What is under threat is its habitat. When forest goes, it’s converted into something else; then there isn’t anywhere for forest plants such as bamboo to grow.’\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求将“竹子面临的最大危险是其生长环境受到干扰”这一陈述与列表中对应的人物匹配。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"greatest danger\", \"disturbance of the places it grows in\" 定位到文中明确指出竹子主要威胁是其栖息地丧失的句子。\n解题思路：原文中Ray Townsend明确指出竹子本身很强壮，能够自保，但真正受到威胁的是它的栖息地，森林被破坏后竹子就没有生长的地方了。这与题目描述“竹子生长的地方受到破坏是最大的危险”完全一致，因此这句话是D说的。","options":["Ian Redmond","Valerie Kapos","Chris Stapleton","Ray Townsend"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59790","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 8-11\nLook at the following statements (Questions 8-11) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-D. Write the correct letter, A-D, in boxes 8-11 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nList of people\nA Ian Redmond\nB Valerie Kapos\nC Chris Stapleton\nD Ray Townsend"},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8189:59791:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"soil erosion/Soil Erosion/SOIL EROSION","acceptedAnswers":["soil erosion","Soil Erosion","SOIL EROSION"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Its rhizome systems, which lie in the top layers of the soil, are crucial in preventing soil erosion.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问竹子的根部有助于控制哪种生态问题。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"ecological problem\"和\"roots of bamboo\"定位到C段，该段提到竹子的根系系统（rhizome systems）在土壤表层，并起到防止某种生态问题的作用。\n解题思路：原文明确指出竹子的根系系统对于\"preventing soil erosion\"（防止土壤侵蚀）至关重要，因此答案为\"soil erosion\"。题干中的\"ecological problem\"对应原文的\"soil erosion\"，而\"roots of bamboo\"对应\"rhizome systems\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59791","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 12-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 12 and 13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8189:59792:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"paper/Paper/PAPER","acceptedAnswers":["paper","Paper","PAPER"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Traditionally it is used in construction, but one of the fastest growing bamboo products is paper – 25 per cent of paper produced in India is made from bamboo fibre.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是哪款竹制品正在进行市场拓展。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"market expansion\"（市场扩张）定位到D段，该段提到\"one of the fastest growing bamboo products is paper\"（增长最快的竹产品之一是纸张），其中的\"fastest growing\"与\"market expansion\"对应。\n解题思路：原文明确指出纸张是增长最快的竹产品之一，并且提到印度有25%的纸张是用竹纤维制造的，这表明纸张市场正在扩张。因此，答案为\"paper\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59792","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 12-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 12 and 13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59789","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nThe passage has six sections, A-F. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.","html":"<p><strong>1</strong> an assessment of current levels of knowledge about bamboo <strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"59790","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 8-11\nLook at the following statements (Questions 8-11) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-D. Write the correct letter, A-D, in boxes 8-11 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nList of people\nA Ian Redmond\nB Valerie Kapos\nC Chris Stapleton\nD Ray Townsend","html":"<p><br/></p><p style=\"margin-top: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>8 </strong>Some people do not regard bamboo as an endangered plant species. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong><br/></p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"59791","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 12-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 12 and 13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>12</strong> What ecological problem do the roots of bamboo help to control? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"59792","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 12-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 12 and 13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>13</strong> Which bamboo product is undergoing market expansion? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Bamboo, a Wonder Plant&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">Bamboo is used for a wide range of purposes, but now it seems it may be under threat.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Every year, during the rainy season, the mountain gorillas of central Africa migrate to the lower slopes of the Virunga Mountains to graze on bamboo. For the 650 or so that remain in the wild, it’s a vital food source. Without it, says Ian Redmond, chairman of the Ape Alliance, their chances of survival would be reduced significantly. Gorillas aren’t the only local keen on bamboo. For the people who live close to the Virungas, it’s a valuable and versatile raw material. But in the past 100 years or so, resources have come under increasing pressure as populations have exploded and large areas of bamboo forest have been cleared to make way for commercial plantations. Sadly, this isn’t an isolated story. All over the world, the ranges of many bamboo species appear to be shrinking, endangering the people and animals that depend upon them.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Despite bamboo’s importance, we know surprisingly little about it. A recent report published by the UN Environment Programme (UNEP) and the International Network for Bamboo and Rattan (INBAR) has revealed just how profound our ignorance of global bamboo resources is, particularly in relation to conservation. There are almost 1,600 recognised species of bamboo, but the report concentrated on the 1,200 or so woody varieties distinguished by the strong stems, or ‘culms’, that most people associate with this versatile plant. Of these, only 38 ‘priority species’ identified for their commercial value have been the subject of any real scientific research to date. This problem isn’t confined to bamboo. Compared to the work carried out on animals, the science of assessing the conservation status of plants is still in its infancy. ‘People have only started looking at this during the past 10-15 years, and only now are they understanding how to go about it systematically,’ says Dr Valerie Kapos, one of the report’s authors.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Bamboo tends to grow in ‘stands’ (or groups) made up of individual plants that grow from roots known as rhizomes. It is the world’s fastest-growing woody plant and some species grow over a meter in one day. But the plant’s ecological role extends beyond providing food for wildlife. Its rhizome systems, which lie in the top layers of the soil, are crucial in preventing soil erosion. And there is growing evidence that bamboo plays an important part in determining forest structure and dynamics. ‘Bamboo’s pattern of mass flowering and mass death leaves behind large areas of dry biomass that attract wildfire,’ says Kapos, ‘When these bum, they create patches of open ground far bigger than would be left by a fallen tree. Patchiness helps to preserve diversity because certain plant species do better during the early stages of regeneration when there are gaps in the canopy.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>However, bamboo’s most immediate significance lies in its economic value. Many countries, particularly in Asia, are involved in the trade of bamboo products. Modern processing techniques mean it can be used in a variety of ways, for example as flooring and laminates. Traditionally it is used in construction, but one of the fastest growing bamboo products is paper – 25 per cent of paper produced in India is made from bamboo fibre. Of course, bamboo’s main function has always been in domestic applications, and as a locally traded product, it is worth about US$4.5 billion annually. Bamboo is often the only readily available raw material for people in many developing countries, says Chris Stapleton, a research associate at the UK’s Royal Botanic Gardens. ‘Bamboo can be harvested from forest areas or grown quickly elsewhere, and then converted simply without expensive machinery or facilities,’ he says, ‘In this way, it contributes substantially to poverty alleviation.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Keen horticulturists will spot an apparent contradiction in the worrying picture painted by the UNEP-INBAR report. Those in the West who’ve followed the recent vogue for cultivating exotic species in their gardens will point out that, if it isn’t kept in check, bamboo can cause real problems. ‘In a lot of places, the people who live with bamboo don’t perceive it as being under threat in any way,’ says Kapos, ‘In fact, a lot of bamboo species are very invasive if they’ve been introduced.’ So why are so many species endangered? ‘There are two separate issues here’, says Ray Townsend, arboretum manager at the Royal Botanic Gardens, ‘Some plants are threatened because they can’t survive in the habitat – they aren’t strong enough or there aren’t enough of them, perhaps. But bamboo can take care of itself – it’s strong enough to survive if left alone. What is under threat is its habitat. When forest goes, it’s converted into something else; then there isn’t anywhere for forest plants such as bamboo to grow.’</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Around the world, bamboo species are routinely protected as part of the forest ecosystem in national parks and reserves, but there is next to nothing that protects bamboo in the wild for its own sake. The UNEP-INBAR report will help conservationists to establish effective measures aimed at protecting valuable wild bamboo species. Townsend, too, sees the UNEP-INBAR report as an important step forward in promoting the cause of bamboo conservation. ‘Until now, bamboo has been perceived as a second-class plant. When you talk about places like the Amazon, everyone always thinks about hardwoods. Of course, these are significant but there’s a tendency to overlook the plants they are associated with, which are often bamboo species.’</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8189&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8196","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 The Future Never Dies?","book":"阅读还原集Vol.13","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.13 · Test 3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8196:59808:14","type":"choice","text":"It seems predictable that some species will disappear.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Many of those fellow species now seem bound to become extinct, but a significant proportion could and should continue to live alongside us.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问“似乎可以预测某些物种将会消失”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"predictable\"和\"species will disappear\"定位，在A段找到\"seem bound to become extinct\"（似乎注定会灭绝）。\n解题思路：原文明确提到\"seem bound to become extinct\"（似乎注定会灭绝），与题干\"predictable that some species will disappear\"（可以预测某些物种会消失）意思一致，表明作者认为某些物种的消失是可以预测的。因此，题干表述与作者观点一致，选择YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59808","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements reflect the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet write YES if the statement is ture NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8196:59809:15","type":"choice","text":"The nature of the Earth and human biology make it impossible for human beings to survive another million years.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：There is nothing in the physical fabric of the Earth or in our own biology to suggest that this is not possible.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问“地球的本质和人类的生理特性注定人类无法再存续百万年之久”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词“Earth”、“human biology”、“survive another million years”定位到A段。\n解题思路：原文A段明确指出，毕竟地球的寿命应该非常漫长，我们至少应该以未来百万年为时间尺度来规划。地球的物理结构和我们自身的生物特性，都表明这是完全可能的。题干说“地球的本质和人类的生理特性注定人类无法再存续百万年之久”，而作者认为这是可能的，因此题干与作者观点相反，应选NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59809","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements reflect the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet write YES if the statement is ture NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8196:59810:16","type":"choice","text":"An eruption by Yellowstone is likely to be more destructive than previous volcanic eruptions.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Yellowstone National Park in the USA occupies the caldera (the crater formed when a volcano collapses) of an exceedingly ancient volcano of extraordinary magnitude. Modem surveys show that its centre is now rising. Sometime in the next 200 million years, Yellowstone could erupt again, and when it does, the whole world will be transformed.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问黄石公园的火山爆发可能比之前的火山爆发更具破坏性，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的\"Yellowstone\"和\"eruption\"定位到D段，特别是\"when it does, the whole world will be transformed\"这句话表明黄石公园的火山爆发可能具有全球性的影响。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，现代地质调查显示，其核心区域正在持续隆起。未来2亿年间，黄石火山随时可能再度喷发，届时整个地球都将被彻底改变。而之前的火山爆发如圣海伦斯火山虽然也造成了破坏，但规模和影响远不及黄石公园的火山爆发。因此，题目的说法与原文一致，所以选择YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59810","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements reflect the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet write YES if the statement is ture NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8196:59811:17","type":"choice","text":"There is a greater chance of the Earth being hit by small asteroids than large ones.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：An asteroid the size of a small island, hitting the Earth at 15,000 kilometres an hour (a relatively modest speed by the standards of heavenly bodies), would strike the ocean bed like a rock in a puddle, send a tidal wave around the world as high as a small mountain and as fast as a jumbo jet, and propel us into an ice age that could last for centuries.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“小型小行星撞击地球的几率要大于大型小行星撞击地球的几率”，这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词“small asteroids”和“large ones”定位到E段，其中提到“vast numbers of asteroids”和“An asteroid the size of a small island”，但并未明确比较小型和大型小行星撞击地球的概率。\n解题思路：原文提到小行星的数量很多，并描述了一颗小岛大小的陨石撞击地球的后果，但并未提及不同大小的小行星撞击地球的概率。因此，相关信息未给出。答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59811","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements reflect the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet write YES if the statement is ture NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8196:59812:18","type":"choice","text":"If the world becomes uninhabitable, it is most likely to be as a result of a natural disaster.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The Earth is indeed an uncertain place, in an uncertain universe, but with average luck, it should do us well enough. If the world does become inhospitable in the next few thousand or million years, then it will probably be our own fault.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“如果世界变得不宜居住，最有可能的原因是自然灾害”，需要判断这是否与作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“uninhabitable”（不宜居住）和“natural disaster”（自然灾害）定位到F段。提到“如果世界在未来几千年或几百万年内变得不宜居住，那么这很可能是我们自己的错”。\n解题思路：原文明确提到“如果世界在未来几千年或几百万年内变得不宜居住，那么这很可能是我们自己的错”。  而非自然灾害。题目与原文观点相反，因此答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59812","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements reflect the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet write YES if the statement is ture NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8196:59813:19","type":"choice","text":"Politicians currently in power seem unlikely to change their way of thinking.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The broad point is, though, that we need to look at ourselves– humanity – and at the world in general in a quite new light. Our material problems are fundamentally those of biology. We need to think, and we need our politicians to think, biologically. Do that, and take the ideas seriously, and we are in with a chance. Ignore biology and we and our fellow creatures haven’t a hope.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“当前掌权的政治家似乎不太可能改变他们的思维方式”，需要判断这是否符合作者在文章中的观点。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“politicians currently in power”和“seem unlikely to change their way of thinking”，通过这些关键词可以定位到G段中关于政治家思维方式的内容。\n解题思路：在G段中，作者提到我们需要让政治家从生物学角度思考问题，并且如果他们能够这样做，我们就有机会。然而，作者并没有明确表示当前掌权的政治家是否不太可能改变他们的思维方式，只是提出了一个建议。因此，题目中的说法在文章中没有明确的支持或反驳，所以答案是NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59813","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements reflect the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet write YES if the statement is ture NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8196:59814:20","type":"fill","text":"填写第 20 空","answer":"temperature","acceptedAnswers":["temperature"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Other planets in the solar system are quite beyond habitation, because their temperature is far too high or too low to be endured, and ours, too, in principle could tip either way.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问地球可能变得不适合居住，就像其他行星一样，是因为什么发生重大变化的。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"uninhabitable\"和\"planets\"与C段第一句\"Other planets in the solar system are quite beyond habitation\"对应，定位到该句解释原因的部分。\n解题思路：原文明确提到其他行星不适合居住是因为它们的\"temperature is far too high or too low\"，即温度过高或过低，而地球也可能\"tip either way\"（向两个极端倾斜），说明地球变得不适合居住同样是因为温度的剧烈变化，因此答案为\"temperature\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59814","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8196:59814:21","type":"fill","text":"填写第 21 空","answer":"molten rock#rock/ash","acceptedAnswers":["molten rock","rock","ash"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The core of the Earth is hot, which in many ways is good for living creatures, but every now and again, the molten rock bursts through volcanoes on the surface.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求填空，问的是火山喷发会将什么物质喷发出来。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"volcanic eruptions\"定位到C段，该段描述了火山喷发的原因和影响。\n解题思路：原文中提到，地球的核心是热的，这在很多方面对生物是有益的，但每隔一段时间，熔岩就会从地表的火山中喷发出来。火山喷发由\"molten rock\"（熔岩）从地核中喷出引起的，因此答案为\"molten rock\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59814","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8196:59814:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"food","acceptedAnswers":["food"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1815, Tambora (in present-day Indonesia) expelled so much ash into the upper atmosphere that climatic effects seriously harmed food production around the world for the season after season.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是火山喷发可能导致大面积的什么短缺。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"shortages\"（短缺）和\"wide area\"（大面积）定位到C段，该段提到火山喷发对食物生产的影响。\n解题思路：原文中提到坦博拉火山喷发将大量火山灰喷入大气层，导致全球气候影响，严重破坏了食物生产，这与题干描述的情况一致。因此，答案为\"food\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59814","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8196:59814:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"tidal wave","acceptedAnswers":["tidal wave"],"explanation":"原文答案句：An asteroid the size of a small island, hitting the Earth at 15,000 kilometres an hour (a relatively modest speed by the standards of heavenly bodies), would strike the ocean bed like a rock in a puddle, send a tidal wave around the world as high as a small mountain and as fast as a jumbo jet, and propel us into an ice age that could last for centuries.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求填空，描述小行星撞击地球可能产生的现象。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"An asteroid hitting the Earth\"定位到E段，找到描述小行星撞击地球后果的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，一颗小岛大小的陨石，若以每小时15,000公里（按天体速度标准来看不算快）的速度撞击地球，其威力堪比水坑中的巨石，不仅会引发全球范围内的海啸\"send a tidal wave around the world\"，因此答案为tidal wave。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59814","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8196:59814:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"Ice age","acceptedAnswers":["Ice age"],"explanation":"原文答案句：An asteroid the size of a small island, hitting the Earth at 15,000 kilometres an hour (a relatively modest speed by the standards of heavenly bodies), would strike the ocean bed like a rock in a puddle, send a tidal wave around the world as high as a small mountain and as fast as a jumbo jet, and propel us into an ice age that could last for centuries.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求根据填空题的题干，小行星撞击会导致新的什么。\n定位关键信息：题干中的“result in a new”提示我们需要寻找一个由动词或名词引导的结果状语从句或名词短语，且该短语描述的是一种自然现象。结合文章内容，E段提到了小行星撞击地球的后果，其中“propel us into an ice age”直接对应“导致一种新的现象”。\n解题思路：原文E段描述了小行星撞击地球的连锁反应，其中明确提到将把人类推向可能延续数百年的冰河时代，“propel us into an ice age”。题干中的“result in a new”与原文的“propel us into”在语义上一致。因此，答案为“ice age”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59814","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8196:59814:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"rockets","acceptedAnswers":["rockets"],"explanation":"原文答案句：There are plans to head off such disasters (including rockets to push approaching asteroids into new trajectories), but in truth, it’s down to luck.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“计划使用什么来偏转朝地球飞来的小行星”。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的“Plans are being made to use”和“deflect asteroids heading for the Earth”可以定位到E段中关于小行星威胁和应对计划的描述。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到“plans to head off such disasters (including rockets to push approaching asteroids into new trajectories)”，有计划通过发射火箭将接近的小行星推入新轨道来避免此类灾难。因此，答案为“rockets”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59814","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8196:59820:26","type":"choice","text":"What is the writer’s purpose in the passage?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The broad point is, though, that we need to look at ourselves – humanity – and at the world in general in a quite new light. Our material problems are fundamentally those of biology. We need to think, and we need our politicians to think, biologically. Do that, and take the ideas seriously, and we are in with a chance. Ignore biology and we and our fellow creatures haven’t a hope.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是作者写这篇文章的目的。\n定位关键信息：通过阅读全文，尤其是最后一段，可以定位到作者表达的核心观点。\n解题思路：文章开头提出人类和世界的未来可能既光明，也危险，接着分别阐述了这两种可能性的原因，包括地球自身的规则、火山活动、宇宙中的小行星等自然因素，以及政治和人类行为等人为因素。最后一段明确指出，尽管存在不确定性，但人类的未来很大程度上掌握在自己手中，需要从生物学角度思考问题，改变行为方式。因此，作者写这篇文章的目的是论证需要从根本上改变人类的行为方式，以应对未来的挑战。这与选项D的表述一致。","options":["to propose a new theory about the causes of natural disasters","to prove that generally held beliefs about the future are all mistaken","to present a range of opinions currently held by scientists","to argue the need for a general change in behavior"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59820","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in the box 26 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59808","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements reflect the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet write YES if the statement is ture NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>It seems predictable that some species will disappear.</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"59809","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements reflect the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet write YES if the statement is ture NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The nature of the Earth and human biology make it impossible for human beings to survive another million years.</strong></p>","firstNumber":15},{"id":"59810","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements reflect the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet write YES if the statement is ture NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>An eruption by Yellowstone is likely to be more destructive than previous volcanic eruptions.</strong></p>","firstNumber":16},{"id":"59811","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements reflect the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet write YES if the statement is ture NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>There is a greater chance of the Earth being hit by small asteroids than large ones.</strong></p>","firstNumber":17},{"id":"59812","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements reflect the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet write YES if the statement is ture NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>If the world becomes uninhabitable, it is most likely to be as a result of a natural disaster.</strong></p>","firstNumber":18},{"id":"59813","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nDo the following statements reflect the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet write YES if the statement is ture NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Politicians currently in power seem unlikely to change their way of thinking.</strong></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"59814","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20-25\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20-25 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The Earth could become uninhabitable, like other planets, through a major change in the<strong> 20.</strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong> .&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">Volcanic eruptions of&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">21.</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">can lead to shortages of&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">22.</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong> in a wide area.&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">An asteroid hitting the Earth could create a</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;23.</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">that would result in a new&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">24.</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> .&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">Plans are being made to use&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">25.</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong> to deflect asteroids heading for the Earth. on buildings and the joyful smell from the sea.</span></span></span></span></span></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"59820","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in the box 26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is the writer’s purpose in the passage?</strong></p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The Future Never Dies?&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The prospects for humanity and for the world as a whole are somewhere between glorious and dire. It is hard to be much more precise.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>By ‘glorious’, I mean that our descendants – all who are born on to this Earth – could live very comfortably and securely, and could continue to do so for as long as the Earth can support life, which should be for a very long time indeed. We should at least be thinking in terms of the next million years. Furthermore, our descendants could continue to enjoy the company of other species – establishing a much better relationship with them than we have now. Other animals need not live in constant fear of us. Many of those fellow species now seem bound to become extinct, but a significant proportion could and should continue to live alongside us. Such a future may seem ideal, and so it is. Yet I do not believe it is fanciful. There is nothing in the physical fabric of the Earth or in our own biology to suggest that this is not possible.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘Dire’ means that we human beings could be in deep trouble within the next few centuries, living but also dying in large numbers in political terror and from starvation, while huge numbers of our fellow creatures would simply disappear, leaving only the ones that we find convenient – chickens, cattle – or that we can’t shake off, like flies and mice. I’m taking it to be self-evident that glory is preferable.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Our future is not entirely in our own hands because the Earth has its own rules, is part of the solar system and is neither stable nor innately safe. Other planets in the solar system are quite beyond habitation, because their temperature is far too high or too low to be endured, and ours, too, in principle could tip either way. Even relatively unspectacular changes in the atmosphere could do the trick. The core of the Earth is hot, which in many ways is good for living creatures, but every now and again, the molten rock bursts through volcanoes on the surface. Among the biggest volcanic eruptions in recent memory was Mount St Helens, in the USA, which threw out a cubic kilometre of ash – fortunately, in an area where very few people live. In 1815, Tambora (in present-day Indonesia) expelled so much ash into the upper atmosphere that climatic effects seriously harmed food production around the world for the season after season. Entire civilisations have been destroyed by volcanoes.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Yet nothing we have so far experienced shows what volcanoes can really do. Yellowstone National Park in the USA occupies the caldera (the crater formed when a volcano collapses) of an exceedingly ancient volcano of extraordinary magnitude. Modem surveys show that its centre is now rising. Sometime in the next 200 million years, Yellowstone could erupt again, and when it does, the whole world will be transformed. Yellowstone could erupt tomorrow. But there’s a very good chance that it will give us another million years, and that surely is enough to be going on with. It seems sensible to assume that this will be the case.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The universe at large is dangerous, too: in particular, we share the sky with vast numbers of asteroids, and now and again, the come into our planet’s atmosphere. An asteroid the size of a small island, hitting the Earth at 15,000 kilometres an hour (a relatively modest speed by the standards of heavenly bodies), would strike the ocean bed like a rock in a puddle, send a tidal wave around the world as high as a small mountain and as fast as a jumbo jet, and propel us into an ice age that could last for centuries. There are plans to head off such disasters (including rockets to push approaching asteroids into new trajectories), but in truth, it’s down to luck.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>On the other hand, the archaeological and the fossil evidence shows that no truly devastating asteroid has struck since the one that seems to have accounted for the extinction of the dinosaurs 65 million years ago. So again, there seems no immediate reason for despair. The Earth is indeed an uncertain place, in an uncertain universe, but with average luck, it should do us well enough. If the world does become inhospitable in the next few thousand or million years, then it will probably be our own fault. In short, despite the underlying uncertainty, our own future and that of our fellow creatures are very much in our own hands.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Given average luck on the geological and the cosmic scale, the difference between glory and disaster will be made and is being made, by politics. Certain kinds of political systems and strategies would predispose us to long-term survival (and indeed to comfort and security and pleasure of being alive), while others would take us more and more frenetically towards collapse. The broad point is, though, that we need to look at ourselves – humanity – and at the world in general in a quite new light. Our material problems are fundamentally those of biology. We need to think, and we need our politicians to think, biologically. Do that, and take the ideas seriously, and we are in with a chance. Ignore biology and we and our fellow creatures haven’t a hope.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8196&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8197","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Communicating Conflict","book":"阅读还原集Vol.13","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.13 · Test 3 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8197:59801:27","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：As far back as Hippocrates’s time (460-370 B.C.), people have tried to understand other people by characterizing them according to personality type or temperament. Hippocrates believed there were four different body fluids that influenced four basic types of temperament. His work was further developed 500 years later by Galen.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求为A段选择一个合适的标题，概括该段的主要内容。\n定位关键信息：通过关键词\"Hippocrates\"、\"Galen\"、\"historical\"、\"understanding personality\"等定位到A段，该段主要讲述了从古希腊时期至今，人们试图通过性格类型或气质来理解他人，并提到了希波克拉底和盖伦对气质理论的历史贡献。\n解题思路：A段主要讲述了历史上对理解性格类型的研究，特别是希波克拉底和盖伦的工作。选项C\"Historical explanation of understanding personality\"（历史上对性格的理解）准确概括了该段内容，即从古希腊时期开始，人们如何通过性格类型或气质来理解他人，并提到了希波克拉底和盖伦对气质理论的历史贡献。因此，选择C作为A段的标题。","options":["Different personality types mentioned","Recommendation of combined styles for group","Historical explanation of understanding personality","A lively and positive attitude person depicted","A personality likes a challenge and direct communication","Different characters illustrated","Functions of understanding communication styles","Cautious and considerable person cited","Calm and Factual personality illustrated","Self-assessment determines one’s temperament"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"59801","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-34\nThe passage has eight sections A-H. Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8197:59801:28","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The values in self-assessments that help determine personality style. Learning styles, communication styles, conflict-handling styles, or other aspects of individuals is that they help depersonalize conflict in interpersonal relationships.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求为B段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：阅读B段内容，重点关注段落的首句和尾句，以及段落中反复出现的核心词汇。\n解题思路：B段主要讲述了自我评估工具在确定个性风格、学习风格、沟通风格和冲突处理风格等方面的价值，特别是它们有助于在人际关系中使冲突去个人化。段落中多次提到\"self-assessments\"、\"personality style\"、\"communication styles\"和\"conflict\"，强调了这些工具在理解和处理人际冲突中的作用。因此，选择标题G\"Functions of understanding communication styles\"（理解沟通风格的意义）能够准确概括B段的核心内容。","options":["Different personality types mentioned","Recommendation of combined styles for group","Historical explanation of understanding personality","A lively and positive attitude person depicted","A personality likes a challenge and direct communication","Different characters illustrated","Functions of understanding communication styles","Cautious and considerable person cited","Calm and Factual personality illustrated","Self-assessment determines one’s temperament"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"59801","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-34\nThe passage has eight sections A-H. Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8197:59801:29","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Hippocrates and later Galen determined there were four basic temperaments: sanguine, phlegmatic, melancholic and choleric. These descriptions were developed centuries ago and are still somewhat apt, although you could update the wording.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求为C段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过段落首句的关键词\"Hippocrates and later Galen\"以及\"four basic temperaments\"可以定位到C段的核心内容是关于四种基本气质类型的介绍。\n解题思路：C段主要介绍了希波克拉底和盖伦确定的四种基本气质类型（sanguine, phlegmatic, melancholic and choleric），并说明这些描述虽然古老，但仍有一定适用性。因此，该段落的标题应与\"四种不同的气质类型\"相关。选项A（Four basic temperaments）准确概括了段落内容，符合题意。","options":["Different personality types mentioned","Recommendation of combined styles for group","Historical explanation of understanding personality","A lively and positive attitude person depicted","A personality likes a challenge and direct communication","Different characters illustrated","Functions of understanding communication styles","Cautious and considerable person cited","Calm and Factual personality illustrated","Self-assessment determines one’s temperament"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"59801","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-34\nThe passage has eight sections A-H. Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8197:59801:30","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The sanguine person would be the expressive or spirited style of communication.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求为D段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过段落首句\"The sanguine person would be the expressive or spirited style of communication\"可以定位到D段的主要内容是关于 sanguine 这种性格类型对应的沟通风格。\n解题思路：D段详细描述了 乐观型这种性格类型的特点，如善于表达、充满热情、关注人际关系、喜欢变化等。这些描述与选项D\"Expressive or spirited communication style\"（善于表达或活泼的沟通风格）完全吻合，因此答案为D。","options":["Different personality types mentioned","Recommendation of combined styles for group","Historical explanation of understanding personality","A lively and positive attitude person depicted","A personality likes a challenge and direct communication","Different characters illustrated","Functions of understanding communication styles","Cautious and considerable person cited","Calm and Factual personality illustrated","Self-assessment determines one’s temperament"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"59801","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-34\nThe passage has eight sections A-H. Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8197:59801:31","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This style of communication is focused on facts and technical details. Phlegmatic people have an orderly methodical way of approaching tasks, and their focus is very much on the task, not on the people, emotions, or concerns that the task may evoke.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求为E段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"E\"定位到E段，通过阅读E段内容找到关键信息，如\"focused on facts and technical details\"和\"orderly methodical way of approaching tasks\"。\n解题思路：E段主要描述了冷静型的沟通风格，强调他们注重事实和技术细节，以及有条不紊地处理任务的方式。这与选项I\"Calm and Factual personality illustrated（描述冷静客观的性格）吻合，因此选择I作为E段的标题。","options":["Different personality types mentioned","Recommendation of combined styles for group","Historical explanation of understanding personality","A lively and positive attitude person depicted","A personality likes a challenge and direct communication","Different characters illustrated","Functions of understanding communication styles","Cautious and considerable person cited","Calm and Factual personality illustrated","Self-assessment determines one’s temperament"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"59801","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-34\nThe passage has eight sections A-H. Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8197:59801:32","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph F","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The melancholic person who is softhearted and oriented toward doing things for others translates into the considerate or sympathetic communication style.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求为F段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：根据段落首句\"The melancholic person who is softhearted and oriented toward doing things for others translates into the considerate or sympathetic communication style.\"可以定位到F段的核心内容是关于忧郁型（melancholic）性格对应的考虑周到或富有同情心的沟通风格。\n解题思路：F段主要描述了忧郁型性格的特点，他们心软且倾向于为他人做事，这种性格转化为考虑周到或富有同情心的沟通风格。段落详细描述了这种沟通风格的特点，如关注人际关系、善于倾听、重视他人意见等。因此，F段的标题应与“考虑周到或富有同情心的沟通风格”相关，对应选项H。","options":["Different personality types mentioned","Recommendation of combined styles for group","Historical explanation of understanding personality","A lively and positive attitude person depicted","A personality likes a challenge and direct communication","Different characters illustrated","Functions of understanding communication styles","Cautious and considerable person cited","Calm and Factual personality illustrated","Self-assessment determines one’s temperament"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"59801","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-34\nThe passage has eight sections A-H. Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8197:59801:33","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph G","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The choleric temperament translates into the bold or direct style of communication. People with this style are brief in their communication – the fewer words the better...They usually would welcome someone challenging them. But most other styles are afraid to do so. They also thrive on change, the more the better.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求为G段选择一个正确的标题。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"G段\"定位到文章的G段，阅读该段落内容。\n解题思路：G段主要描述了暴躁型性格对应的沟通风格，即大胆或直接的沟通方式。段落详细描述了这种沟通风格的特点，如简洁、关注大局、任务导向、直接且欢迎挑战等。因此，G段的主题是关于暴躁型性格的沟通风格，选择E项。","options":["Different personality types mentioned","Recommendation of combined styles for group","Historical explanation of understanding personality","A lively and positive attitude person depicted","A personality likes a challenge and direct communication","Different characters illustrated","Functions of understanding communication styles","Cautious and considerable person cited","Calm and Factual personality illustrated","Self-assessment determines one’s temperament"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"59801","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-34\nThe passage has eight sections A-H. Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8197:59801:34","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph H","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A well-functioning team should have all of these communications styles for true effectiveness. All teams need to focus on the task, and they need to take care of relationships in order to achieve those tasks. They need the big picture perspective or the context of their work, and they need the details to be identified and taken care of for success.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目要求为H段选择一个合适的标题。\n定位关键信息：根据H段的内容，重点在于讨论一个高效团队需要具备所有沟通风格，以及团队成员如何适应不同的沟通风格。\n解题思路：H段主要讲述了高效团队需要包含所有沟通风格，以实现任务和关系两方面的平衡。同时提到团队成员可以根据情况调整自己的沟通风格，或者有些人更倾向于一种主导风格。因此，H段的核心内容是关于团队中沟通风格的多样性和适应性，对应的标题应为B（团队最好由多种风格的人组成）。","options":["Different personality types mentioned","Recommendation of combined styles for group","Historical explanation of understanding personality","A lively and positive attitude person depicted","A personality likes a challenge and direct communication","Different characters illustrated","Functions of understanding communication styles","Cautious and considerable person cited","Calm and Factual personality illustrated","Self-assessment determines one’s temperament"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"59801","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-34\nThe passage has eight sections A-H. Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8197:59802:35","type":"choice","text":"It is believed that sanguine people do not like variety.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：These people find conflict or differences of opinion invigorating and love to engage in a spirited discussion. They love change and are constantly looking for new and exciting adventures.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“人们认为乐观的人不喜欢变化”这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"sanguine people\"和\"do not like variety\"可以定位到D段，该段描述了乐观型（sanguine）人的特点。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到乐观型的人“love change”（喜欢变化）并且“are constantly looking for new and exciting adventures”（不断寻找新的和令人兴奋的冒险），这与题目中“do not like variety”（不喜欢变化）的说法完全相反。因此，题目中的说法与原文信息不符，答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59802","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-39\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-39 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8197:59803:36","type":"choice","text":"Melancholic and phlegmatic people have similar characteristics.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：They believe that change threatens the status quo and tends to make people feel uneasy, so people with this communication style, like phlegmatic people, need time to consider the changes in order to adapt to them.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“忧郁型和冷静型的人有相似的特征”是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“Melancholic and phlegmatic”定位到F段，该段描述了忧郁型（melancholic）的特征，并提到“like phlegmatic people”，说明两者有相似之处。\n解题思路：F段描述了忧郁型的人关注人际关系、不喜欢冲突、对变化持谨慎态度，并明确提到“like phlegmatic people”（与冷静型的人类似），两者都需要时间来处理和适应变化，说明两者在不喜欢冲突和对变化持谨慎态度方面有相似特征。因此，题干的说法与文章信息一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59803","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-39\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-39 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8197:59804:37","type":"choice","text":"Managers often select their best employees according to personality types.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A well-functioning team should have all of these communications styles for true effectiveness. All teams need to focus on the task, and they need to take care of relationships in order to achieve those tasks. They need the big picture perspective or the context of their work, and they need the details to be identified and taken care of for success.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目判断“管理者经常根据性格类型来选择最佳员工”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。”\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词“sanguine personality”和“needed most”定位到H段。\n解题思路：原文明确指出一个高效团队需要所有沟通风格（包括乐观型、冷静型、忧郁型和暴躁型），并未说明某种类型的人是最佳的。也并未提及管理者选择员工的标准，因此信息未给出。答案为Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59804","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-39\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-39 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8197:59805:38","type":"choice","text":"It is possible for someone to change a type of personality.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：  Some of us can easily move from one style to another and adapt our style to the needs of the situation at hand-whether the focus is on tasks or relationships. For others, a dominant style is very evident, and it is more challenging to see the situation from the perspective of another style.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问“一个人可以改变性格类型”是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“change a type of personality”定位到文章中关于性格或沟通风格是否可以改变的内容。\n解题思路：H段提到“Some of us can easily move from one style to another and adapt our style to the needs of the situation at hand”（有些人可以轻松地从一种风格转换到另一种风格，并根据需要适应情况），说明人的沟通风格（与性格相关）是可以调整和改变的。因此，题目中的说法与原文一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59805","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-39\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-39 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8197:59806:39","type":"choice","text":"Work surrounding can affect which communication style is the most effective.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The work environment can influence communication styles either by the type of work that is required or by the predominance of one style reflected in that environment.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问工作环境是否会影响最佳沟通风格。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Work surrounding\"（工作环境）和\"communication style\"（沟通风格）定位到H段。\n解题思路：原文明确提到\"工作环境可以影响沟通风格，要么是通过不同的工作类型，要么是通过该环境所体现的主流沟通风格\"。这说明工作环境确实会影响哪种沟通风格最有效，因此题目表述与原文信息一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59806","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-39\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-39 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8197:59807:40","type":"choice","text":"The writer believes using self-assessment tools can","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The values in self-assessments that help determine personality style. Learning styles, communication styles, conflict-handling styles, or other aspects of individuals is that they help depersonalize conflict in interpersonal relationships.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问作者认为自我评估工具能够做到什么。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"self-assessment tools\"，在文章中定位到B段，该段提到了自我评估工具的作用。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句可知，自我评估工具可以帮助理解人际关系中的冲突，并帮助解决这些问题。因此，选项B\"help to understand colleagues and resolve problems\"（帮助理解同事，解决工作中的问题与原文意思一致，是正确答案。其他选项A、C、D都与原文不符。","options":["help to develop one’s personality.","help to understand colleagues and resolve problems.","improve the relationship with the boss of the company.","directly resolve conflicts."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59807","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 40 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59801","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27-34\nThe passage has eight sections A-H. Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"59802","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-39\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-39 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>It is believed that sanguine people do not like variety.</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"59803","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-39\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-39 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Melancholic and phlegmatic people have similar characteristics.</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"59804","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-39\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-39 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong style=\"font-family: DengXian; font-size: 14px; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px;\">Managers often select their best employees according to personality types.</span></strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"59805","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-39\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-39 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>It is possible for someone to change a type of personality.</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"59806","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-39\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 35-39 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Work surrounding can affect which communication style is the most effective.</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"59807","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: justify;\">The writer believes using self-assessment tools can</span></strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Communicating Conflict&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Hiragino Sans GB&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span></strong><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>As far back as Hippocrates’s time (460-370 B.C.), people have tried to understand other people by characterizing them according to personality type or temperament. Hippocrates believed there were four different body fluids that influenced four basic types of temperament. His work was further developed 500 years later by Galen. These days there is any number of self-assessment tools that relate to the basic descriptions developed by Galen, although we no longer believe the source to be the types of body fluid that dominate our systems.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Hiragino Sans GB&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p><strong><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Hiragino Sans GB&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span></strong></strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The values in self-assessments that help determine personality style. Learning styles, communication styles, conflict-handling styles, or other aspects of individuals is that they help depersonalize conflict in interpersonal relationships. The depersonalization occurs when you realize that others aren’t trying to be difficult, but they need different or more information than you do. They’re not intending to be rude: they are so focused on the task they forget about greeting people. They would like to work faster but not at the risk of damaging the relationships needed to get the job done. They understand there is a job to do. But it can only be done right with the appropriate information, which takes time to collect. When used appropriately, understanding communication styles can help resolve conflict on teams. Very rarely are conflicts true personality issues. Usually, they are issues of style, information needs, or focus.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Hiragino Sans GB&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Hiragino Sans GB&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span></strong></strong><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Hippocrates and later Galen determined there were four basic temperaments: sanguine, phlegmatic, melancholic and choleric. These descriptions were developed centuries ago and are still somewhat apt, although you could update the wording. In today’s world, they translate into the four fairly common communication styles described below:<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Hiragino Sans GB&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Hiragino Sans GB&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span></strong></strong><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The sanguine person would be the expressive or spirited style of communication. These people speak in pictures. They invest a lot of emotion and energy in their communication and often speak quickly. Putting their whole body into it. They are easily sidetracked onto a story that may or may not illustrate the point they are trying to make. Because of their enthusiasm, they are great team motivators. They are concerned about people and relationships. Their high levels of energy can come on strong at times and their focus is usually on the bigger picture, which means they sometimes miss the details or the proper order of things. These people find conflict or differences of opinion invigorating and love to engage in a spirited discussion. They love change and are constantly looking for new and exciting adventures.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Hiragino Sans GB&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Hiragino Sans GB&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span></strong></strong><strong>E&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Tile phlegmatic person – cool and persevering – translates into the technical or systematic communication style. This style of communication is focused on facts and technical details. Phlegmatic people have an orderly methodical way of approaching tasks, and their focus is very much on the task, not on the people, emotions, or concerns that the task may evoke. The focus is also more on the details necessary to accomplish a task. Sometimes the details overwhelm the big picture and focus needs to be brought back to the context of the task. People with this style think the facts should speak for themselves, and they are not as comfortable with conflict. They need time to adapt to change and need to understand both the logic of it and the steps involved.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Hiragino Sans GB&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Hiragino Sans GB&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span></strong></strong><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Tile melancholic person who is softhearted and oriented toward doing things for others translates into the considerate or sympathetic communication style. A person with this communication style is focused on people and relationships. They are good listeners and do things for other people – sometimes to the detriment of getting things done for themselves. They want to solicit everyone’s opinion and make sure everyone is comfortable with whatever is required to get the job done. At times this focus on others can distract from the task at hand. Because they are so concerned with the needs of others and smoothing over issues, they do not like conflict. They believe that change threatens the status quo and tends to make people feel uneasy, so people with this communication style, like phlegmatic people, need time to consider the changes in order to adapt to them.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Hiragino Sans GB&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Hiragino Sans GB&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span></strong></strong><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The choleric temperament translates into the bold or direct style of communication. People with this style are brief in their communication – the fewer words the better. They are big-picture thinkers and love to be involved in many things at once. They are focused on tasks and outcomes and often forget that the people involved in carrying out the tasks have needs. They don’t do detail work easily and as a result, can often underestimate how much time it takes to achieve the task. Because they are so direct, they often seem forceful and can be very intimidating to others. They usually would welcome someone challenging them. But most other styles are afraid to do so. They also thrive on change, the more the better.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Hiragino Sans GB&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Hiragino Sans GB&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span></strong></strong><strong>H&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>A well-functioning team should have all of these communications styles for true effectiveness. All teams need to focus on the task, and they need to take care of relationships in order to achieve those tasks. They need the big picture perspective or the context of their work, and they need the details to be identified and taken care of for success. We all have aspects of each style within us. Some of us can easily move from one style to another and adapt our style to the needs of the situation at hand-whether the focus is on tasks or relationships. For others, a dominant style is very evident, and it is more challenging to see the situation from the perspective of another style. The work environment can influence communication styles either by the type of work that is required or by the predominance of one style reflected in that environment. Some people use one style at work and another at home. The good news about communication styles is that we have the ability to develop flexibility in our styles. The greater the flexibility we have, the more skilled we usually are at handling possible and actual conflicts. Usually, it has to be relevant to us to do so, either because we think it is important or because there are incentives in our environment to encourage it. The key is that we have to want to become flexible with our communication style. As Henry Ford said, ‘Whether you think you can or you can’t, you’re right!’<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, &quot;PingFang SC&quot;, &quot;Hiragino Sans GB&quot;, &quot;Microsoft YaHei&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8197&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8186","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Ambergris","book":"阅读还原集Vol.13","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.13 · Test 2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8186:59752:1","type":"choice","text":"being expensive","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Both of them were among the most sought-after substances in the world, almost as valuable as gold. Ambergris sells for roughly $20 a gram, slightly less than gold at $30 a gram.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是哪种物质十分昂贵。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“expensive”定位到C段，该段提到了ambergris和amber的珍贵程度。\n解题思路：原文明确提到“Both of them were among the most sought-after substances in the world, almost as valuable as gold”，说明龙涎香和琥珀都因其稀有而昂贵。随后还具体比较了龙涎香和黄金的价格。因此答案为C。","options":["ambergris only","amber only","both ambergris and amber","neither ambergris nor amber"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59752","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nClassify the following information as referring to Write the correct letter A, B, C, or D in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet.\nA ambergris only\nB amber only\nC both ambergris and amber\nD neither ambergris nor amber"},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8186:59752:2","type":"choice","text":"adds flavor to food","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For centuries, this substance has also been used as a flavouring for food.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是哪个物质“用于给食物调味”。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"adds flavor to food\"定位到A段中的\"used as a flavouring for food\"。\n解题思路：A段提到了龙涎香在古代被用作化妆品的香料，并且几乎每个文明都与龙涎香有过接触。在A段的后半部分，明确提到了龙涎香被用作食物的调味料已有几个世纪的历史。因此，A段是正确答案。","options":["ambergris only","amber only","both ambergris and amber","neither ambergris nor amber"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59752","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nClassify the following information as referring to Write the correct letter A, B, C, or D in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet.\nA ambergris only\nB amber only\nC both ambergris and amber\nD neither ambergris nor amber"},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8186:59752:3","type":"choice","text":"used as currency","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Ambergris was used to perfume cosmetics in the days of ancient Mesopotamia and almost every civilization on the earth has a brush with ambergris...For centuries, this substance has also been used as a flavouring for food.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是哪种物质“作为货币使用”。\n定位关键信息：题目中的“used as currency”是关键词，需要找到龙涎香和琥珀香的用途有关的信息。\n解题思路：A段提到了龙涎香在古代被用作化妆品的香料，并且几乎每个文明都与龙涎香有过接触。在A段的后半部分，明确提到了龙涎香被用作食物的调味料已有几个世纪的历史，但未提及货币用途。后续也并未提到琥珀作为货币使用过。因此，选择D选项。","options":["ambergris only","amber only","both ambergris and amber","neither ambergris nor amber"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59752","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nClassify the following information as referring to Write the correct letter A, B, C, or D in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet.\nA ambergris only\nB amber only\nC both ambergris and amber\nD neither ambergris nor amber"},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8186:59752:4","type":"choice","text":"being see-through","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Although considered a gem, amber is a hard, transparent, wholly-organic material derived from the resin of extinct species of trees, mainly pines.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目询问哪个物质是“透明”的。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的“being see-through”这一描述，在文章中寻找与“透明”相关的信息。在C段中找到“transparent”这一关键词，明确指向琥珀的特性。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到琥珀是透明的（transparent），而题干中的“being see-through”正是对“transparent”的同义转述。因此，正确答案为B，即B段中描述的琥珀具有透明这一特性。","options":["ambergris only","amber only","both ambergris and amber","neither ambergris nor amber"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59752","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nClassify the following information as referring to Write the correct letter A, B, C, or D in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet.\nA ambergris only\nB amber only\nC both ambergris and amber\nD neither ambergris nor amber"},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8186:59752:5","type":"choice","text":"referred to by Herman Melville","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In the 1851 whaling novel Moby-Dick, Herman Melville claimed that ambergris was ‘largely used in perfumery’.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是Herman Melville提到了哪种物质。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词Herman Melville，在文章中定位到B段，找到包含该名字的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句中的信息，可以确定Herman Melville在《白鲸》一书中提到了龙涎香。因此，答案为A。","options":["ambergris only","amber only","both ambergris and amber","neither ambergris nor amber"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59752","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nClassify the following information as referring to Write the correct letter A, B, C, or D in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet.\nA ambergris only\nB amber only\nC both ambergris and amber\nD neither ambergris nor amber"},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8186:59752:6","type":"choice","text":"produces sweet smell","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：When a whale initially vomits up ambergris, it is soft and has a terrible smell. But after floating on the salty ocean for about a decade, the substance hardens with air and sun into a smooth, waxy, usually rounded piece of nostril heaven. The dung smell is gone, replaced by a sweet, smooth, musky and pleasant earthy aroma.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是哪种物质“散发甜香”。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“produces sweet smell”定位到E段中描述龙涎香气味变化的句子。\n解题思路：E段详细描述了龙涎香从最初呕吐时的恶臭气味，经过海水漂浮和日晒后，气味逐渐转变为“sweet, smooth, musky and pleasant earthy aroma”，即甜香。因此，选择A。","options":["ambergris only","amber only","both ambergris and amber","neither ambergris nor amber"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59752","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nClassify the following information as referring to Write the correct letter A, B, C, or D in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet.\nA ambergris only\nB amber only\nC both ambergris and amber\nD neither ambergris nor amber"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8186:59753:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"beaks/Beaks","acceptedAnswers":["beaks","Beaks"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Sperm whales are rather partial to squid, but seemingly struggle to digest the hard, sharp, parrot-like beaks.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是抹香鲸无法消化鱿鱼哪个部位。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"squids\"定位到E段，该段详细描述了抹香鲸消化鱿鱼的困难所在。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句可知，抹香鲸对鱿鱼情有独钟，但似乎难以消化那些坚硬锋利、形似鹦鹉的喙部。因此答案为beaks。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59753","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet."},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8186:59754:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"vomiting/Vomiting","acceptedAnswers":["vomiting","Vomiting"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It is thought their stomach juices become hyper-active trying to process the irritants, and eventually hard, resinous lumps are formed around the beaks, and then expelled from their innards by vomiting.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是抹香鲸如何将刺激物排出肠道。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"Sperm whales\"和\"irritants\"定位到E段，该段描述了抹香鲸处理鱿鱼喙的过程。\n解题思路：原文提到抹香鲸的胃液会变得异常活跃以处理刺激物（squid beaks），最终形成硬块并从体内排出，而排出的方式是通过\"vomiting\"（呕吐）。因此，抹香鲸是通过呕吐将刺激物排出肠道的。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59754","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet."},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8186:59755:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"hardens/Hardens","acceptedAnswers":["hardens","Hardens"],"explanation":"原文答案句：When a whale initially vomits up ambergris, it is soft and has a terrible smell. But after floating on the salty ocean for about a decade, the substance hardens with air and sun into a smooth, waxy, usually rounded piece of nostril heaven.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是抹香鲸的呕吐物在接触空气后逐渐如何变化，最终产生令人愉悦的气味。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的关键词\"vomit of sperm whale\"（抹香鲸的呕吐物）和\"pleasant smell\"（令人愉悦的气味），可以定位到E段描述抹香鲸呕吐物变化过程的句子。\n解题思路：原文E段明确提到抹香鲸的呕吐物最初是柔软且难闻，但经过与空气和阳光接触后，物质会硬化，最终形成光滑、蜡质、通常呈圆形的物质，产生好闻的气味。题目描述的\"逐渐在接触空气后硬化\"与原文中的\"hardens with air\"完全一致，因此答案为\"hardens\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59755","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet."},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8186:59756:10","type":"choice","text":"Most ambergris comes from the dead whales today.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：By 20th century ambergris is mainly recovered from inside the carcasses of sperm whales.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“如今大多数龙涎香来自死鲸”，需要判断这个说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“Most ambergris”和“dead whales today”来定位答案。在B段中找到“By 20th century ambergris is mainly recovered from inside the carcasses of sperm whales.”这句话，其中的“carcasses”意为“尸体”，与“dead whales”对应，“mainly recovered”意为“主要回收”，与“Most ambergris”对应。\n解题思路：原文明确提到“20世纪龙涎香主要从抹香鲸的尸体中回收”，这与题目中的“如今大多数龙涎香来自死鲸”一致，因此可以判断题目说法与文章信息一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59756","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8186:59757:11","type":"choice","text":"Ambergris is becoming more expensive than before.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Both of them were among the most sought-after substances in the world, almost as valuable as gold. Ambergris sells for roughly $20 a gram, slightly less than gold at $30 a gram.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目判断“龙涎香变得比以前更贵了”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“more expensive than before”（比以前更贵）定位信息。\n解题思路：段落C中，原文给出了龙涎香当前的价格，并说明它和琥珀都是历史上“最受追捧的物质之一，价值几乎与黄金相当”。然而，原文只提供了某个时间点的价格和历史上的价值地位，并未将现在的价格与过去某个特定时期的价格进行对比。因此，题目中的比较关系在原文中未提及，无法确定龙涎香是否比以前更贵。故答案为Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59757","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8186:59758:12","type":"choice","text":"Ambergris is still the most frequently used ingredient in perfume production today.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Nowadays, since ambergris is rare and expensive, and big fragrance suppliers that make most of the fragrances on the market today do not deal in it for reasons of cost, availability and murky legal issues, most perfumeries prefer to add a chemical derivative which mimics the properties of ambergris.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问“龙涎香是否仍然是当今香水生产中最常用的成分”。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Ambergris\"、\"most frequently used ingredient in perfume production today\"可以定位到G段中关于龙涎香在当今香水行业使用情况的描述。\n解题思路：根据G段原文，龙涎香由于稀有、昂贵以及法律问题，大型的香水供应商现在不再使用它，而是更倾向于使用化学衍生物来模拟其特性。原文明确指出“most perfumeries prefer to add a chemical derivative which mimics the properties of ambergris”，这意味着龙涎香不再是香水生产中最常用的成分。因此，题目的说法与原文信息矛盾，答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59758","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8186:59759:13","type":"choice","text":"New uses of ambergris have been discovered recently.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：One of the forms ambergris is used today is as a valuable fixative in perfumes to enhance and prolong the scent.\n对应段落：G段\n的最审题：题目判断“近期发现了龙涎香的新用途”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"New uses of ambergris\"和\"discovered recently\"在文章中定位，可以找到G段提到了龙涎香的用途。\n解题思路：原文详细列举了龙涎香在历史上的多种用途，在古老的美索不达米亚时期用于化妆品香氛，几个世纪以来用作食物调味料，在中世纪用作药物，G段提及了在现代主要用作香水定香剂。但文中没有任何信息表明最近发现了任何新的、以前未知的用途。因此，答案是Not Given。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59759","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59752","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nClassify the following information as referring to Write the correct letter A, B, C, or D in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet.\nA ambergris only\nB amber only\nC both ambergris and amber\nD neither ambergris nor amber","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> ambergris only&nbsp;</p><p><strong>B</strong> amber only<strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>C</strong> both ambergris and amber&nbsp;</p><p><strong>D</strong> neither ambergris nor amber&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-top: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>1</strong> being expensive <strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"59753","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Sperm whales can’t digest the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong> of the squids.</p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"59754","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Sperm whales drive the irritants out of their intestines by <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"59755","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7-9\nComplete the sentences below with NO MORE THAN ONE WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 7-9 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The vomit of sperm whale gradually <strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong> on contact of air before having pleasant smell.</p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"59756","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p>Most ambergris comes from the dead whales today.</p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"59757","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p>Ambergris is becoming more expensive than before.</p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"59758","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p>Ambergris is still the most frequently used ingredient in perfume production today.</p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"59759","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p>New uses of ambergris have been discovered recently.</p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ambergris&nbsp;</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><br/></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">What is it and where does it come from?&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Ambergris was used to perfume cosmetics in the days of ancient Mesopotamia and almost every civilization on the earth has a brush with ambergris. Before 1,000 AD, the Chinese names ambergris as lung sien hiang, ‘dragon’s spittle perfume’, as they think that it was produced from the drooling of dragons sleeping on rocks at the edge of a sea. The Arabs knew ambergris as anbar, believing that it is produced from springs near seas. It also gets its name from here. For centuries, this substance has also been used as a flavouring for food.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>During the Middle Ages, Europeans used ambergris as a remedy for headaches,colds, epilepsy, and other ailments. In the 1851 whaling novel Moby-Dick, Herman Melville claimed that ambergris was ‘largely used in perfumery’. But nobody ever knew where it really came from. Experts were still guessing its origin thousands of years later, until the long ages of guesswork ended in the 1720’s, when Nantucket whalers found gobs of the costly material inside the stomachs of sperm whales. Industrial whaling quickly burgeoned. By 20th century ambergris is mainly recovered from inside the carcasses of sperm whales.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Through countless ages, people have found pieces of ambergris on sandy beaches. It was named grey amber to distinguish it from golden amber, another rare treasure. Both of them were among the most sought-after substances in the world, almost as valuable as gold. Ambergris sells for roughly $20 a gram, slightly less than gold at $30 a gram. Amber floats in salt water, and in old times the origin of both these substances was mysterious. But it turned out that amber and ambergris have little in common. Amber is a fossilized resin from trees that was quite familiar to Europeans long before the discovery of the New World, and prized as jewelry. Although considered a gem, amber is a hard,transparent, wholly-organic material derived from the resin of extinct species of trees, mainly pines.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>To the earliest Western chroniclers, ambergris was variously thought to come from the same bituminous sea founts as amber,from the sperm of fishes or whales, from the droppings of strange sea birds (probably because of confusion over the included beaks of squid) or from the large hives of bees living near the sea. Marco Polo was the first Western chronicler who correctly attributed ambergris to sperm whales and its vomit.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>As sperm whales navigate in the oceans, they often dive down to 2 km or more below the sea level to prey on squid, most famously the Giant Squid. It’s commonly accepted that ambergris forms in the whale’s gut or intestines as the creature attempts to ‘deal’ with squid beaks. Sperm whales are rather partial to squid, but seemingly struggle to digest the hard, sharp, parrot-like beaks. It is thought their stomach juices become hyper-active trying to process the irritants, and eventually hard, resinous lumps are formed around the beaks, and then expelled from their innards by vomiting. When a whale initially vomits up ambergris, it is soft and has a terrible smell. Some marine biologists compare it to the unpleasant smell of cow dung. But after floating on the salty ocean for about a decade, the substance hardens with air and sun into a smooth, waxy, usually rounded piece of nostril heaven. The dung smell is gone, replaced by a sweet, smooth, musky and pleasant earthy aroma.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Since ambergris is derived from animals, naturally a question of ethics arises, and in the case of ambergris, it is very important to consider. Sperm whales are an endangered species, whose populations started to decline as far back as the 19thcentury due to the high demand for their highly emollient oil, and today their stocks still have not recovered. During the 1970’s, the Save the Whales movement brought the plight of whales to international recognition. Many people now believe that whales are ‘saved’. This couldn’t be further from the truth. All around the world, whaling still exists. Many countries continue to hunt whales, in spite of international treaties to protect them. Many marine researchers are concerned that even the trade in naturally found ambergris can be harmful by creating further incentives to hunt whales for this valuable substance.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>One of the forms ambergris is used today is as a valuable fixative in perfumes to enhance and prolong the scent. But nowadays,since ambergris is rare and expensive, and big fragrance suppliers that make most of the fragrances on the market today do not deal in it for reasons of cost, availability and murky legal issues,most perfumeries prefer to add a chemical derivative which mimics the properties of ambergris. As a fragrance consumer, you can assume that there is no natural ambergris in your perfume bottle, unless the company advertises this fact and unless you own vintage fragrances created before the 1980s. If you are wondering if you have been wearing a perfume with this legendary ingredient, you may want to review your scent collection. Here are a few of some of the top ambergris containing perfumes: Givenchy Amarige, Chanel No. 5, and Gucci Guilty.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8186&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8187","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Left-handed or Right-handed?","book":"阅读还原集Vol.13","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.13 · Test 2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8187:59773:14","type":"choice","text":"14 The phenomenon of using one side of their body for animals","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Furthermore, specialization on either side of the body is common among animals. Cats will favor one paw over another when fishing toys out from under the couch. Horses stomp more frequently with one hoof than the other. Certain crabs motion predominantly with the left or right claw.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了动物使用单侧身体的现象。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"animals\"和\"using one side of their body\"这两个关键词定位到文章中的C段。\n解题思路：在C段中，明确提到了动物使用身体单侧的现象，如把玩具从沙发下弄出来的时候，猫更偏向于用某只爪子，马匹用单蹄刨地的频率往往高于另一只蹄。某些螃蟹主要依靠左钳或右钳进行移动。这些例子直接对应了题目中询问的现象，因此C段包含了题目所要求的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59773","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe passage has seven sections A-G. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8187:59773:15","type":"choice","text":"15 Statistics on the rate of one-handedness born","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The probability that two right-handed people would have a left-handed child is only about 9.5 percent. The chance rises to 19.5 percent if one parent is a lefty and 26 percent if both parents are left-handed.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了出生就带有偏手性的统计数据。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“Statistics on the rate of one-handedness”和“born”可以定位到A段，该段提到了不同父母组合下生出左撇子孩子的概率。\n解题思路：A段明确给出了右撇子父母生出左撇子孩子的概率为9.5%，如果其中一位父母是左撇子，概率上升到19.5%，如果父母都是左撇子，概率为26%。这些数据直接对应了题目中偏手性的统计数据，因此答案为A。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59773","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe passage has seven sections A-G. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8187:59773:16","type":"choice","text":"16 The age when the preference for using one hand is fixed","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Genetic predetermination is also contradicted by the widespread observation that children do not settle on either their right or left hand until they are two or three years old.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了惯用手偏好形成的年龄。\n定位关键信息：根据题目的“age when the preference for using one hand is fixed”定位到B段末句“children do not settle on either their right or left hand until they are two or three years old”，明确指出儿童在两到三岁之间才形成惯用手的偏好。\n解题思路：原文明确提到“children do not settle on either their right or left hand until they are two or three years old”，即孩子们在两三岁之前，都无法确定自己惯用的手是右手还是左手，因此答案为B段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59773","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe passage has seven sections A-G. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8187:59773:17","type":"choice","text":"17 great talents of occupations in the left-handed population","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Yet lefties are prevalent among artists, composers and the generally acknowledged great political thinkers.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了左撇子人群中出现了杰出人才。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"great talents of occupations in the left-handed population\"（左撇子人群中出现杰出人才），可以定位到F段。\n解题思路：F段中提到很多艺术家、作曲家和政治思想家都是左撇子，与题干中的\"great talents of occupations\"对应，因此答案为F。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59773","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe passage has seven sections A-G. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8187:59773:18","type":"choice","text":"18 The earliest record of researching hemisphere’s function","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Interest in hemispheres dates back to at least 1836. That year, at a medical conference, French physician Marc Dax reported on an unusual commonality among his patients.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问最早研究大脑半球功能的记录出现在哪个段落。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"the earliest record\"和\"researching hemisphere’s function\"定位到文章中提到最早研究大脑半球功能的段落。\n解题思路：D段的第一句话明确提到\"Interest in hemispheres dates back to at least 1836\"，说明最早对大脑半球功能的研究记录可以追溯到1836年。接下来的句子详细描述了法国医生Marc Dax在1836年的一次医学会议上报告了他对患者的研究，这些患者都有大脑左半球的损伤导致语言困难。因此，D段包含了关于最早研究大脑半球功能的记录。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59773","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe passage has seven sections A-G. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8187:59774:19","type":"choice","text":"19 Ancient language evolution is connected to body gesture and therefore influences handedness.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For example, some researchers, including evolutionary psychologist Michael C. Corballis of the University of Auckland in New Zealand, think that the origin of human speech lies in gestures. Gestures predated words and helped language emerge. If the left hemisphere began to dominate speech, it would have dominated gestures, too, and because the left brain controls the right side of the body, the right hand developed more strongly.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是哪位研究者认为古代语言进化与身体手势有关，因此影响惯用手偏好。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"ancient language evolution\"、\"body gesture\"和\"handedness\"来定位答案在文章中的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句中的内容，Michael Corballis认为手势先于语言出现，并且帮助语言的形成。如果左脑开始主导语言，那么它也会主导手势，由于左脑控制身体的右侧，右手就会发展得更强势。这与题目中描述的观点相吻合，因此答案为D。","options":["Brenda Milner","Marian Annett","Peter Hepper","Michale Corballis"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59774","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nLook at the following researchers and the list of findings below. March each researcher with the correct finding.\nA Brenda Milner\nB Marian Annett\nC Peter Hepper\nD Michale Corballis"},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8187:59774:20","type":"choice","text":"20 A child handedness is not determined by just biological factors.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Research conducted on twins complicates the theory, however. One in five sets of identical twins involves one right-handed and one left-handed person, despite the fact that their genetic material is the same. Genes, therefore, are not solely responsible for handedness.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：使用 \"child handedness\", \"not determined by just biological factors\" 定位到文中讨论用手习惯成因且涉及非生物因素的句子。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"child handedness\"和\"not determined by just biological factors\"可以定位到B段，该段提到了Peter Hepper和他的团队的研究结果，表明孩子的用手习惯不仅仅由生物因素决定。\n解题思路：题目陈述的核心是“用手习惯并非仅由生物因素决定”。在段落A中，Marian Annett提出了关于用手习惯的基因假说，但随后原文用双胞胎研究对此进行了修正和复杂化：尽管同卵双胞胎基因相同，但仍有五分之一的情况是一个用右手，一个用左手。由此得出的结论是“基因并非用手习惯的唯一决定因素”。这直接支持了题目观点，即生物因素（基因）并非唯一决定因素。虽然这个结论是基于对Annett理论的补充和修正，但它是在介绍和讨论Annett理论的部分提出的，因此这个研究发现对应的是研究者B (Marian Annett)。","options":["Brenda Milner","Marian Annett","Peter Hepper","Michale Corballis"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59774","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nLook at the following researchers and the list of findings below. March each researcher with the correct finding.\nA Brenda Milner\nB Marian Annett\nC Peter Hepper\nD Michale Corballis"},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8187:59774:21","type":"choice","text":"21 Language process is generally undergoing in the left hemisphere of the brain.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Based on this approach, Brenda Milner and the late Theodore Rasmussen of the Montreal Neurological Institute published a major study in 1975 that confirmed the theory that country doctor Dax had formulated nearly 140 years earlier: in 96 percent of right-handed people, language is processed much more intensely in the left hemisphere.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是哪位研究者发现了语言处理通常发生在左脑。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Language process\"和\"left hemisphere\"可以定位到E段中关于语言处理和大脑半球的信息。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子，Brenda Milner和Theodore Rasmussen在1975年发表了一项重要研究，证实了Dax医生近140年前提出的理论：在96%的右撇子中，语言处理在左脑中更为强烈。因此，可以确定Brenda Milner和Theodore Rasmussen是发现语言处理通常发生在左脑半球的研究者。","options":["Brenda Milner","Marian Annett","Peter Hepper","Michale Corballis"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59774","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nLook at the following researchers and the list of findings below. March each researcher with the correct finding.\nA Brenda Milner\nB Marian Annett\nC Peter Hepper\nD Michale Corballis"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8187:59774:22","type":"choice","text":"22 The rate of development of one side of the body has an influence on hemisphere preference in the fetus.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 2004 the psychologists used ultrasound to show that by the 15th week of pregnancy, fetuses already have a preference as to which thumb they suck. In most cases, the preference continued after birth. At 15 weeks, though, the brain does not yet have control over the body’s limbs. Hepper speculates that fetuses tend to prefer whichever side of the body is developing quicker and that their movements, in turn, influence the brain’s development.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是哪位研究人员的研究发现是“身体单侧的发展速度会影响胎儿的大脑半球偏好”。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“rate of development of one side of the body”和“hemisphere preference in the fetus”定位到B段，找到Hepper的研究内容。\n解题思路：B段提到Hepper的研究发现，胎儿在15周时已经表现出吮吸拇指的偏好，但此时大脑尚未控制肢体。Hepper推测胎儿倾向于更喜欢发育更快的身体一侧，而这种运动反过来会影响大脑的发展。这与题目中“身体单侧的发展速度会影响胎儿的大脑半球偏好”一致，因此答案为C。","options":["Brenda Milner","Marian Annett","Peter Hepper","Michale Corballis"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59774","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nLook at the following researchers and the list of findings below. March each researcher with the correct finding.\nA Brenda Milner\nB Marian Annett\nC Peter Hepper\nD Michale Corballis"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8187:59775:23","type":"choice","text":"The study of twins shows that genetic determination is not the only factor for left Handedness.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：One in five sets of identical twins involves one right-handed and one left-handed person, despite the fact that their genetic material is the same. Genes, therefore, are not solely responsible for handedness.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“对双胞胎的研究表明，基因决定不是左撇子的唯一因素”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“twins”和“genetic determination”在文章中定位，可以找到A段提到对双胞胎的研究结果。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，即使双胞胎的基因相同，仍有五分之一的同卵双胞胎中一个是右撇子，一个是左撇子，并且明确说明基因并非决定惯用手的唯一决定因素。这与题目中的陈述完全一致，因此选择A（True）。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59775","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 23-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet, write YES, if the statement is true, NO if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage."},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8187:59776:24","type":"choice","text":"The number of men with left-handedness is more than that of women.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：无（原文中没有直接提及男女左撇子数量对比的信息）\n对应段落：无（原文各段均未明确比较男女左撇子数量）\n审题：题目询问“男性左撇子的数量是否多于女性”，需要根据原文信息判断这一陈述是否正确、错误或未提及。\n定位关键信息：题目中的核心词汇是“men”（男性）、“women”（女性）和“left-handedness”（左撇子），需要寻找原文中是否比较了这两类人群的左撇子数量。\n解题思路：通读全文后，发现原文中完全没有提及男性或女性左撇子的数量对比。文章讨论了左撇子的遗传、大脑半球功能、进化原因等内容，但未涉及性别差异。因此，题目中的信息在原文中未给出，应选择“NOT GIVEN”。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59776","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 23-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet, write YES, if the statement is true, NO if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage."},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8187:59777:25","type":"choice","text":"Marc Dax’s report was widely recognized in his time.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Other experts showed little interest in the Frenchman’s ideas.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“Marc Dax的报告在他那个时代是否被广泛认可”。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“Marc Dax”和“his time”可以定位到D段，该段提到Marc Dax在1836年提出理论，但其他专家对他的想法兴趣不大。\n解题思路：原文明确提到“Other experts showed little interest in the Frenchman’s ideas.”（其他专家对他的想法兴趣不大），说明他的报告并没有被广泛认可，因此题目中的说法是错误的。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59777","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 23-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet, write YES, if the statement is true, NO if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage."},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8187:59778:26","type":"choice","text":"Juhn Wada based his findings on his research of people with language problems.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1949 neurosurgeon Juhn Wada devised the first test to provide access to the brain’s functional organization of language. By injecting an anesthetic into the right or left carotid artery, Wada temporarily paralyzed one side of a healthy brain, enabling him to more closely study the other side’s capabilities.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问Juhn Wada的研究是否基于有语言障碍的人。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"Juhn Wada\"和\"research of people with language problems\"是定位关键词。在E段中找到Juhn Wada的描述，发现他通过注射麻醉剂使健康大脑的一侧暂时瘫痪，研究另一侧的能力。\n解题思路：原文明确指出Juhn Wada的研究对象是\"healthy brain\"（大脑健康）的人，但研究对象是否有语言障碍，文章并未提到，因此题目说法属于未提及的信息。答案为C。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59778","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 23-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet, write YES, if the statement is true, NO if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59773","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe passage has seven sections A-G. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.","html":"<p><strong>14</strong> The phenomenon of using one side of their body for animals <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"59774","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19-22\nLook at the following researchers and the list of findings below. March each researcher with the correct finding.\nA Brenda Milner\nB Marian Annett\nC Peter Hepper\nD Michale Corballis","html":"<p style=\"margin-bottom: 5px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>19</strong> Ancient language evolution is connected to body gesture and therefore influences handedness. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"59775","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 23-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet, write YES, if the statement is true, NO if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>The study of twins shows that genetic determination is not the only factor for left Handedness.</strong></p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"59776","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 23-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet, write YES, if the statement is true, NO if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>The number of men with left-handedness is more than that of women.</strong></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"59777","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 23-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet, write YES, if the statement is true, NO if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Marc Dax’s report was widely recognized in his time.</strong></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"59778","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 23-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet, write YES, if the statement is true, NO if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Juhn Wada based his findings on his research of people with language problems.</strong></p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Left-handed or Right-handed?&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The probability that two right-handed people would have a left-handed child is only about 9.5 percent. The chance rises to 19.5 percent if one parent is a lefty and 26 percent if both parents are left-handed: The preference, however, could also stem from an infant’s imitation of his parents. To test genetic influence, starting in the 1970s British biologist Marian Annett of the University of Leicester hypothesized that no single gene determines handedness. Rather, during fetal development, a certain molecular factor helps to strengthen the brain’s left hemisphere, which increases the probability that the right hand will be dominant because the left side of the brain controls the right side of the body, and vice versa. Among the minority of people who lack this factor, handedness develops entirely by chance. Research conducted on twins complicates the theory, however. One in five sets of identical twins involves one right-handed and one left-handed person, despite the fact that their genetic material is the same. Genes, therefore, are not solely responsible for handedness.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The genetic theory is also undermined by results from Peter Hepper and his team at Queen’s University in Belfast, Ireland. In 2004 the psychologists used ultrasound to show that by the 15th week of pregnancy, fetuses already have a preference as to which thumb they suck. In most cases, the preference continued after birth. At 15 weeks, though, the brain does not yet have control over the body’s limbs. Hepper speculates that fetuses tend to prefer whichever side of the body is developing quicker and that their movements, in turn, influence the brain’s development. Whether this early preference is temporary or holds up throughout development and infancy is unknown. Genetic predetermination is also contradicted by the widespread observation that children do not settle on either their right or left hand until they are two or three years old.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>But even if these correlations were true, they did not explain what actually causes left-handedness. Furthermore, specialization on either side of the body is common among animals. Cats will favor one paw over another when fishing toys out from under the couch. Horses stomp more frequently with one hoof than the other. Certain crabs motion predominantly with the left or right claw. In evolutionary terms, focusing power and dexterity in one limb is more efficient than having to train two, four or even eight limbs equally. Yet for most animals, the preference for one side or the other is seemingly random. The overwhelming dominance of the right hand is associated only with humans. That fact directs attention toward the brain’s two hemispheres and perhaps toward language.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Interest in hemispheres dates back to at least 1836. That year, at a medical conference, French physician Marc Dax reported on an unusual commonality among his patients. During his many years as a country doctor, Dax had encountered more than 40 men and women for whom speech was difficult, the result of some kind of brain damage. What was unique was that every individual suffered damage to the left side of the brain. At the conference, Dax elaborated on his theory, stating that each half of the brain was responsible for certain functions and that the left hemisphere controlled speech. Other experts showed little interest in the Frenchman’s ideas. Over time, however, scientists found more and more evidence of people experiencing speech difficulties following an injury to the left brain. Patients with damage to the right hemisphere most often displayed disruptions in perception or concentration. Major advancements in understanding the brain’s asymmetry were made in the 1960s as a result of so-called split-brain surgery, developed to help patients with epilepsy. During this operation, doctors severed the corpus callosum – the nerve bundle that connects the two hemispheres. The surgical cut also stopped almost all normal communication between the two hemispheres, which offered researchers the opportunity to investigate each side’s activity.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In 1949 neurosurgeon Juhn Wada devised the first test to provide access to the brain’s functional organization of language. By injecting an anesthetic into the right or left carotid artery, Wada temporarily paralyzed one side of a healthy brain, enabling him to more closely study the other side’s capabilities. Based on this approach, Brenda Milner and the late Theodore Rasmussen of the Montreal Neurological Institute published a major study in 1975 that confirmed the theory that country doctor Dax had formulated nearly 140 years earlier: in 96 percent of right-handed people, language is processed much more intensely in the left hemisphere. The correlation is not as clear in lefties, however. For two-thirds of them, the left hemisphere is still the most active language processor. But for the remaining third, either the right side is dominant or both sides work equally, controlling different language functions. That last statistic has slowed acceptance of the notion that the predominance of right-handedness is driven by left-hemisphere dominance in language processing. It is not at all clear why language control should somehow have dragged the control of body movement with it. Some experts think one reason the left hemisphere reigns over language is that the organs of speech processing – the larynx and tongue – are positioned on the body’s symmetry axis. Because these structures were centered, it may have been unclear, in evolutionary terms, which side of the brain should control them, and it seems unlikely that shared operation would result in smooth motor activity. Language and handedness could have developed preferentially for very different reasons as well. For example, some researchers, including evolutionary psychologist Michael C. Corballis of the University of Auckland in New Zealand, think that the origin of human speech lies in gestures. Gestures predated words and helped language emerge. If the left hemisphere began to dominate speech, it would have dominated gestures, too, and because the left brain controls the right side of the body, the right hand developed more strongly.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Perhaps we will know more soon. In the meantime, we can revel in what, if any, differences handedness brings to our human talents. Popular wisdom says right-handed, left-brained people excel at logical, analytical thinking. Left-handed, right-brained individuals are thought to possess more creative skills and maybe better at combining the functional features emergent on both sides of the brain. Yet some neuroscientists see such claims as pure speculation. Fewer scientists are ready to claim that left-handedness means greater creative potential. Yet lefties are prevalent among artists, composers and the generally acknowledged great political thinkers. Possibly if these individuals are among the lefties whose language abilities are evenly distributed between hemispheres, the intense interplay required could lead to unusual mental capabilities.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Or perhaps some lefties become highly creative because they must be more clever to get by in our right-handed world. This battle, which begins during the very early stages of childhood, may lay the groundwork for exceptional achievements.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8187&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8188","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Theory or Practice?","book":"阅读还原集Vol.13","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.13 · Test 2 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8188:59779:27","type":"choice","text":"In the second paragraph, the recommendation given by AACSB is","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The most controversial recommendation in AACSB’s draft report (which was sent round to administrators for their comment) is that the schools should be required to demonstrate the value of their faculties’ research not simply by listing its citations in journals, but by demonstrating, the impact it has in the professional world.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是在第二段中，AACSB提出的建议是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"AACSB\"和\"recommendation\"可以定位到B段中关于AACSB建议的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到AACSB的建议是学校需要展示其研究人员的价值，不仅仅是通过列出期刊中的引用，而是通过展示其对专业领域的影响。这与选项C的描述完全一致，即评估论文对领域的影响。选项A与原文的\"not simply by listing its citations\"相反；选项B未提及；选项D与原文的\"changing the way it evaluates research\"矛盾。因此，正确答案是C。","options":["to focus on listing research paper’s citation only.","to consider the quantity of academic publications.","to evaluate how the paper influences the field.","to maintain the traditional modes of academia."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59779","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-29 on your answer sheet."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8188:59780:28","type":"choice","text":"Why does AACSB put forward the recommendation?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：AACSB justifies its stance by saying that it wants schools and faculty to play to their strengths, whether they be in pedagogy, in the research of practical applications, or in scholarly endeavor.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问AACSB提出建议的原因是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\" AACSB\"和\"recommendation\"定位到C段首句，该句明确提到AACSB的立场和动机。\n解题思路：原文中明确指出AACSB希望通过新的评估方式，让学校和教师发挥各自的优势，无论是教学、实践研究还是学术研究。这与选项A\" To give full play to the faculties’ advantage\"完全一致。其他选项B、C、D的内容在原文中未被提及或与原文表述不符。","options":["To give full play to the faculties’ advantage.","To reinforce the pyramid structure of universities.","To push professors to publish competitive papers.","To reduce costs of research in universities."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59780","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-29 on your answer sheet."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8188:59781:29","type":"choice","text":"Why does the author mention the Journal Strategy & Leadership?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A paper in a 2006 issue of Strategy & Leadership commented that ‘research is not designed with managers’ needs in mind, nor is it communicated in the journals they read. For the most part it has become a self-referential closed system irrelevant to corporate performance.’\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问作者提及《战略与领导力》杂志是为了什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Journal Strategy & Leadership\"定位到G段中提到该期刊的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子可以看出，《战略与领导力》杂志发表的一篇文章评论道，研究并非以管理人员的需求为出发点，研究论文也不会出现在他们阅读的杂志中，研究大多已演变为自我参照的封闭体系，与公司运营表现毫无关联。因此，对应选项A。选项B提到经理人不读研究论文，虽然原文提到研究几乎不被现实世界的管理人员阅读，但这是研究的普遍情况，而不是提及该期刊的目的。选项C和D的内容在原文中均未提及。","options":["To characterize research as irrelevant to company performance.","To suggest that managers don’t read research papers.","To describe students’ expectation for universities.","To exemplify high-quality research papers."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59781","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-29 on your answer sheet."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8188:59782:30-31","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO choices are in line with Jeffrey Pfeffer and Christina Fong’s idea?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The news followed rather damning criticism in 2002 from Jeffrey Pfeffer, a Stanford professor, and Christina Fong of Washington University, which questioned whether business education in its current guise was sustainable. The study found that traditional modes of academia were not adequately preparing students for the kind of careers they faced in current times.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是Jeffrey Pfeffer和Christina Fong的观点，需要找出与他们的观点相符的两个选项。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的名字\"Jeffrey Pfeffer\"和\"Christina Fong\"定位到B段第一句，找到他们发表的研究和观点。\n解题思路：原文提到两位教授认为当前的商务教育很难可持续发展，传统的学究式模式不足以帮学生准备好应对职业生涯中的问题。五个选项中，B项说商务教育进展得不够好，D项说大学毕业生没有为职业发展准备好，两个选项的描述与原文意思基本一致。因此，本题的答案为BD。","options":["Students should pay less to attend universities.","Business education is not doing their job well.","Professors should not focus on writing papers.","Students are ill-prepared for their career from universities.","Recognized accrediting agency can evaluate research well."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"59782","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 30-31\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"59782-8188:59782:30-31"},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8188:59782:30-31","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO choices are in line with Jeffrey Pfeffer and Christina Fong’s idea?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The news followed rather damning criticism in 2002 from Jeffrey Pfeffer, a Stanford professor, and Christina Fong of Washington University, which questioned whether business education in its current guise was sustainable. The study found that traditional modes of academia were not adequately preparing students for the kind of careers they faced in current times.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是Jeffrey Pfeffer和Christina Fong的观点，需要找出与他们的观点相符的两个选项。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的名字\"Jeffrey Pfeffer\"和\"Christina Fong\"定位到B段第一句，找到他们发表的研究和观点。\n解题思路：原文提到两位教授认为当前的商务教育很难可持续发展，传统的学究式模式不足以帮学生准备好应对职业生涯中的问题。五个选项中，B项说商务教育进展得不够好，D项说大学毕业生没有为职业发展准备好，两个选项的描述与原文意思基本一致。因此，本题的答案为BD。","options":["Students should pay less to attend universities.","Business education is not doing their job well.","Professors should not focus on writing papers.","Students are ill-prepared for their career from universities.","Recognized accrediting agency can evaluate research well."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"59782","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 30-31\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"59782-8188:59782:30-31"},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8188:59783:32","type":"choice","text":"The debate about the usefulness of academic research for business practices is a recent one.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The debate, which first flared during the 1950s, was reignited in August, when AACSB International, the most widely recognised global accrediting agency for business schools, announced it would consider changing the way it evaluates research.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问“关于学术研究对商业实践是否有用的辩论是最近发生的”是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"debate\"和\"usefulness of academic research for business practices\"定位到B段第一句，明确辩论起源于20世纪50年代。\n解题思路：原文明确指出辩论最早在20世纪50年代爆发，并在2002年及之后再次被提及，因此该辩论并非最近才出现的，而是长期存在的。题干说“是最近发生的”与原文信息矛盾，故答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59783","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8188:59784:33","type":"choice","text":"AACSB's draft report was not reviewed externally.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The most controversial recommendation in AACSB’s draft report (which was sent round to administrators for their comment) is that the schools should be required to demonstrate the value of their faculties’ research not simply by listing its citations in journals, but by demonstrating, the impact it has in the professional world.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问国际高等商学院协会（AACSB）的报告草案是否没有经过外部审读。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"AACSB’s draft report\"和\"reviewed externally\"，在文章中定位到B段中提到AACSB的报告草案送去给administrators（管理人员）征求意见。\n解题思路：原文第2段“The most controversial recommendation in AACSB's draft report（which was sent round to administrators for their comment）.”通过括号中的内容可以看出，该草案已分发给管理人员征求意见，经过了外部审查。因此，本题的答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59784","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8188:59785:34","type":"choice","text":"Business schools in the US spend more than 320 million dollars yearly on research.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：And research of any kind is expensive – AACSB points out that business schools in America alone spend more than $320m a year on it.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“美国的商学院每年在研究上花费超过3.2亿美元”这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“Business schools in the US”（美国的商学院）、“spend more than 320 million dollars yearly”（每年花费超过3.2亿美元）和“on research”（在研究上）。这些关键词可以帮助我们在文章中定位相关信息。\n解题思路：在C段中，原文明确提到“AACSB points out that business schools in America alone spend more than $320m a year on it”，其中“it”指代的是前文提到的“research”。这句话直接表明美国的商学院每年在研究上花费超过3.2亿美元，与题目陈述完全一致。因此，答案为A（True）。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59785","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8188:59786:35","type":"choice","text":"Many universities pursue professional outputs.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：If a school chose to specialise in professional outputs rather than academic outputs, it could use such a large sum of money and redirect it into more fruitful programs.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“许多大学追求专业产出”是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"universities\", \"pursue\", \"professional outputs\" 作为关键词，定位文中描述大学实际目标或选择的句子。\n解题思路：段落D中，原文说的是“If a school chose...”（如果一所学校选择...），这表示一种假设的情况，而非对现实状况的描述。文章通篇都在讨论AACSB提出的改革建议以及关于研究价值的辩论，但没有提供任何信息表明已经有“许多大学”将工作重心转向了追求专业产出。题目信息在原文中找不到依据，因此答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59786","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8188:59787:36","type":"choice","text":"Greater publications benefit professors and students as well.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Greater publications will attract greater funding, which will in turn be spent on better publications. Students seeking to enter professions out of academia find this cycle frustrating, and often see their professors as being part of the ‘Ivory Tower’ of academia, operating in a self-contained community that has little influence on the outside world.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“更优秀的论文发表对教授和学生都是有好处的”，是否与文章一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词“Greater publications”和“benefit professors and students”可以帮助我们在文章中定位答案。\n解题思路：根据E段的内容，我们可以确定更多的出版物对教授是有利的，因为它们可以巩固学校的声誉，对教授的职业生涯也有帮助。然而，F段中提到，对于不从事研究的学生来说，教授们的研究使他们感到“frustrating”，并认为教授们脱离了现实世界。这表明更多的发表并未给这部分学生带来好处。所以，答案是B（False）。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59787","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8188:59788:37","type":"choice","text":"37 Most professors support academic research because","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Research is also about cementing schools’ – and professors’ – reputations. Schools gain kudos from their faculties’ record of publication: which journals publish them, and how often. In some cases, such as with government-funded schools in Britain, it can affect how much money they receive. For professors,the mantra is often ‘publish or perish’. Their careers depend on being right journals.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“大多数教授支持学术研究的原因是什么？”\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词“Most professors support academic research”，可以在E段找到对应的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文可以确定，教授们支持学术研究是因为他们可以从中收获名誉，他们的职涯也依赖于发表研究成果。这与选项C“their jobs depend on it”相符合。","options":["it progresses as we learn innovative ways of doing things.","the trends and standards are changing.","their jobs depend on it.","they care about their school rankings and government funds.","it helps students to go into top business firms."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"59788","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-E, below. Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.\nA it progresses as we learn innovative ways of doing things.\nB the trends and standards are changing.\nC their jobs depend on it.\nD they care about their school rankings and government funds.\nE it helps students to go into top business firms."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8188:59788:38","type":"choice","text":"38 schools support academic research because","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Research is also about cementing schools’ – and professors’ – reputations. Schools gain kudos from their faculties’ record of publication: which journals publish them, and how often. In some cases, such as with government-funded schools in Britain, it can affect how much money they receive.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问学校支持学术研究的原因是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的\"schools support academic research\"定位到E段，该段讨论了学术研究对学校和教授的好处。\n解题思路：原文明确提到\"Research is also about cementing schools’ – and professors’ – reputations\"（研究也是为了巩固学校和教授的声誉），并具体解释了学校通过学术论文获得声誉和资金。因此，学校支持学术研究的原因是为了提升声誉和获得更多资金，选择D。","options":["it progresses as we learn innovative ways of doing things.","the trends and standards are changing.","their jobs depend on it.","they care about their school rankings and government funds.","it helps students to go into top business firms."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"59788","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-E, below. Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.\nA it progresses as we learn innovative ways of doing things.\nB the trends and standards are changing.\nC their jobs depend on it.\nD they care about their school rankings and government funds.\nE it helps students to go into top business firms."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8188:59788:39","type":"choice","text":"39 our society needs academic research because","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Our society progresses because we learn how to do things in new ways, a process which depends heavily on research and academics.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“我们的社会需要学术研究是因为什么”，需要根据文章内容找出社会需要学术研究的原因。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“our society needs academic research because”可以定位到E段，该段讨论了社会需要学术研究的原因。\n解题思路：根据E段中的原文答案句“our society progresses because we learn how to do things in new ways, a process which depends heavily on research and academics.”可以得出，社会之所以需要学术研究，是因为社会之所以进步，源于我们不断推陈出新，而这又极大地依赖于学术研究。因此，答案为A。","options":["it progresses as we learn innovative ways of doing things.","the trends and standards are changing.","their jobs depend on it.","they care about their school rankings and government funds.","it helps students to go into top business firms."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"59788","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-E, below. Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.\nA it progresses as we learn innovative ways of doing things.\nB the trends and standards are changing.\nC their jobs depend on it.\nD they care about their school rankings and government funds.\nE it helps students to go into top business firms."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8188:59788:40","type":"choice","text":"40 universities resisting the AACSB should change because","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Though many universities resisted the report,today’s world continues to change. The universities which prepare students for our changing future have little choice but to change with new trends and new standards.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是为什么抵制AACSB的大学应该改变。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"universities resisting the AACSB\"和\"change\"可以定位到G段最后一句。\n解题思路：G段最后一句提到，尽管许多大学对该报告持反对态度，但当今世界仍在不断变化。如果要为学生应对未来变革做准备，大学别无选择，只能顺应新趋势、新标准而改变。因此，原因是世界在变化，大学需要顺应新的趋势和标准，选择B。","options":["it progresses as we learn innovative ways of doing things.","the trends and standards are changing.","their jobs depend on it.","they care about their school rankings and government funds.","it helps students to go into top business firms."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"59788","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-E, below. Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.\nA it progresses as we learn innovative ways of doing things.\nB the trends and standards are changing.\nC their jobs depend on it.\nD they care about their school rankings and government funds.\nE it helps students to go into top business firms."}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"59782-8188:59782:30-31","numbers":[30,31],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["B","D"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59779","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-29 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>In the second paragraph, the recommendation given by AACSB is</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"59780","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-29 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Why does AACSB put forward the recommendation?</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"59781","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-29\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-29 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Why does the author mention the Journal Strategy &amp; Leadership?</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"59782","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 30-31\nChoose TWO correct answers","html":"<p><strong>Which TWO choices are in line with Jeffrey Pfeffer and Christina Fong’s idea?</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"59783","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>The debate about the usefulness of academic research for business practices is a recent one.</strong></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"59784","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>AACSB&#39;s draft report was not reviewed externally.</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"59785","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Business schools in the US spend more than 320 million dollars yearly on research.</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"59786","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Many universities pursue professional outputs.</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"59787","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-36\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-36 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Greater publications benefit professors and students as well.</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"59788","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 37-40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending, A-E, below. Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.\nA it progresses as we learn innovative ways of doing things.\nB the trends and standards are changing.\nC their jobs depend on it.\nD they care about their school rankings and government funds.\nE it helps students to go into top business firms.","html":"<p><br/></p><p style=\"margin-top: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>37</strong> Most professors support academic research because <strong class=\"source-blank\">[37] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":37}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Theory or Practice?</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Students go to universities and other academic institutions to prepare for their future. We pay tuition and struggle through classes in the hopes that we can find a fulfilling and exciting career. But the choice of your university has a large influence on your future. How can you know which university will prepare you the best for your future? Like other academic institutions, business schools are judged by the quality of the research carried out by their faculties. Professors must both teach students and also produce original research in their own field. The quality of this research is assessed by academic publications. At the same time, universities have another responsibility to equip their students for the real world, however that is defined. Most students learning from professors will not go into academics themselves – so how do academics best prepare them for their future careers,whatever that may be? Whether academic research actually produces anything that is useful to the practice of business, or even whether it is its job to do so, are questions that can provoke vigorous arguments on campus.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The debate, which first flared during the 1950s, was reignited in August, when AACSB International, the most widely recognised global accrediting agency for business schools, announced it would consider changing the way it evaluates research. The news followed rather damning criticism in 2002 from Jeffrey Pfeffer, a Stanford professor, and Christina Fong of Washington University, which questioned whether business education in its current guise was sustainable. The study found that traditional modes of academia were not adequately preparing students for the kind of careers they faced in current times. The most controversial recommendation in AACSB’s draft report (which was sent round to administrators for their comment) is that the schools should be required to demonstrate the value of their faculties’ research not simply by listing its citations in journals, but by demonstrating, the impact it has in the professional world. New qualifiers, such as average incomes, student placement in top firms and business collaborations would now be considered just as important as academic publications.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>AACSB justifies its stance by saying that it wants schools and faculty to play to their strengths, whether they be in pedagogy, in the research of practical applications, or in scholarly endeavor. Traditionally, universities operate in a pyramid structure. Everyone enters and stays in an attempt to be successful in their academic field. A psychology professor must publish competitive research in the top neuroscience journals. A Cultural Studies professor must send graduate students on new field research expeditions to be taken seriously. This research is the core of a university’s output. And research of any kind is expensive – AACSB points out that business schools in America alone spend more than $320m a year on it. So it seems legitimate to ask for what purpose it is undertaken.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>If a school chose to specialise in professional outputs rather than academic outputs, it could use such a large sum of money and redirect it into more fruitful programs. For example, if a business school wanted a larger presence of employees at top financial firms, this money maybe better spent on a center which focuses on building the skills of students, rather than paying for more high-level research to be done through the effort of faculty. A change in evaluation could also open the door to inviting more professionals from different fields to teach as adjuncts. Students could take accredited courses from people who are currently working in their dream field. The AACSB insists that universities answer the question as to why research is the most critical component of traditional education.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>On one level, the question is simple to answer. Research in business schools, as anywhere else, is about expanding the boundaries of knowledge; it thrives on answering unasked questions. Surely this pursuit of knowledge is still important to the university system. Our society progresses because we learn how to do things in new ways, a process which depends heavily on research and academics. But one cannot ignore the other obvious practical uses of research publications, Research is also about cementing schools’ – and professors’ – reputations. Schools gain kudos from their faculties’ record of publication: which journals publish them, and how often. In some cases, such as with government-funded schools in Britain, it can affect how much money they receive. For professors,the mantra is often ‘publish or perish’. Their careers depend on being right journals.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>But at a certain point, one has to wonder whether this research is being done for the benefit of the university or for the students the university aims to teach. Greater publications will attract greater funding, which will in turn be spent on better publications. Students seeking to enter professions out of academia find this cycle frustrating, and often see their professors as being part of the ‘Ivory Tower’ of academia, operating in a self-contained community that has little influence on the outside world.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The research is almost universally unread by real-world managers. Part of the trouble is that the journals labour under a similar ethos. They publish more than 20,000 articles each year. Most of the research is highly quantitative, hypothesis-driven and esoteric. As a result, it is almost universally unread by real-world managers. Much of the research criticises other published research. A paper in a 2006 issue of Strategy &amp; Leadership commented that ‘research is not designed with managers’ needs in mind, nor is it communicated in the journals they read. For the most part it has become a self-referential closed system irrelevant to corporate performance.’ The AACSB demands that this segregation must change for the future of higher education. If students must invest thousands of dollars for an education as part of their career path, the academics which serve the students should be more fully incorporated into the professional world. This means that universities must focus on other strengths outside of research, such as professional networks,technology kills, and connections with top business firms around the world. Though many universities resisted the report,today’s world continues to change. The universities which prepare students for our changing future have little choice but to change with new trends and new standards.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8188&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8182","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 What are you laughing at?","book":"阅读还原集Vol.13","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.13 · Test 1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8182:59713:1","type":"choice","text":"1 Babies and chimps produce similar sounds of laughter.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The findings come from Elke Zimmerman, head of the Institute for Zoology in Germany, who compared the sounds made by babies and chimpanzees in response to tickling during the first year of their life. Using sound spectrographs to reveal the pitch and intensity of vocalizations, she discovered that chimp and human baby laughter follow broadly the same pattern.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是哪个研究者发现婴儿和黑猩猩发出相似的笑声。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“Babies and chimps produce similar sounds of laughter”，通过这些词可以定位到D段，该段明确提到Elke Zimmerman的研究发现婴儿和黑猩猩的笑声模式相似。\n解题思路：原文中D段提到Elke Zimmerman通过对比婴儿和黑猩猩在被挠痒时的声音，发现它们的笑声模式基本相同，这与题目描述完全一致。因此，答案是B。","options":["Tom Flamson","Elke Zimmerman","Robert Provine","Jaak Panksepp"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59713","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nLook at the following research findings (questions 1-6) and the list of people below.  Match each finding with the correct person A, B, C or D.  Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nA Tom Flamson\nB Elke Zimmerman\nC Robert Provine\nD Jaak Panksepp"},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8182:59713:2","type":"choice","text":"2 Primates are not the only animals who produce laughter.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：More distantly related primates, including gorillas, laugh, and anecdotal evidence suggests that other social mammals may do too. Scientists are currently testing such stories with a comparative analysis of just how common laughter is among animals. So far, though, the most compelling evidence for laughter beyond primates comes from research done by Jaak Panksepp from Bowling Green State University\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是哪个研究者发现“灵长类动物不是唯一会笑的动物”。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词“Primates are not the only animals who produce laughter”定位到文章中关于动物笑的普遍性的信息。\n解题思路：原文E段提到“More distantly related primates, including gorillas, laugh, and anecdotal evidence suggests that other social mammals may do too.”这句话明确指出，不仅灵长类动物如大猩猩会发笑，其他社会性哺乳动物也可能发笑。这与题干“灵长类动物不是唯一会发笑的动物”吻合，后文又提到Panksepp为这一观点提供了有力证据，因此正确答案是D。","options":["Tom Flamson","Elke Zimmerman","Robert Provine","Jaak Panksepp"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59713","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nLook at the following research findings (questions 1-6) and the list of people below.  Match each finding with the correct person A, B, C or D.  Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nA Tom Flamson\nB Elke Zimmerman\nC Robert Provine\nD Jaak Panksepp"},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8182:59713:3","type":"choice","text":"3 Laughter also suggests that we feel safe and easy with others.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：By engaging in a bout of tickling, we put ourselves at the mercy of another individual, and laughing is a signal that we laughter is what makes it a reliable signal of trust according to Tom Flamson, a laughter researcher at the University of California, Los Angels.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是哪个研究者发现“笑也表明我们感到安全且与他人相处融洽”。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"feel safe and easy with others\"（感到安全且与他人相处融洽）来定位原文中的相关表述。\n解题思路：原文F段提到近年来最流行的观点是，对搔痒的反应性笑是两个人用来相互传递并测试彼此信任的一种方式，Flamson又提到，让别人挠痒痒时，我们将自己置于他人的控制之下，这时的笑是一种信任的表现，这与题干中“笑声表明我们感到安全且与他人相处融洽”的意思一致。因此，该研究发现对应的是A选项。","options":["Tom Flamson","Elke Zimmerman","Robert Provine","Jaak Panksepp"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59713","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nLook at the following research findings (questions 1-6) and the list of people below.  Match each finding with the correct person A, B, C or D.  Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nA Tom Flamson\nB Elke Zimmerman\nC Robert Provine\nD Jaak Panksepp"},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8182:59713:4","type":"choice","text":"4 Laughter is a response to a polite situation instead of humour.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Provine found that most laughter comes as a polite reaction to everyday remarks such as ‘see you later’, rather than anything particularly funny.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是哪个研究者发现“笑声是对礼貌情境的反应，而不是幽默”。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词“polite situation”和“instead of humour”定位到B段中“most laughter comes as a polite reaction to everyday remarks such as ‘see you later’, rather than anything particularly funny.”这句话。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到罗伯特·普罗文（Robert Provine）的研究发现，大部分笑声是对日常礼貌性话语的反应，而不是对幽默的反应。这与题目中的描述完全一致，因此答案为C。","options":["Tom Flamson","Elke Zimmerman","Robert Provine","Jaak Panksepp"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59713","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nLook at the following research findings (questions 1-6) and the list of people below.  Match each finding with the correct person A, B, C or D.  Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nA Tom Flamson\nB Elke Zimmerman\nC Robert Provine\nD Jaak Panksepp"},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8182:59713:5","type":"choice","text":"5 Animal laughter evolved before human laughter.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Zimmerman believes the closeness of baby laughter to chimp laughter supports the idea that laughter was around long before humans arrived on the scene.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是哪个研究者发现动物笑声是否在人类笑声之前进化。\n定位关键信息：通过研究发现的核心理念 “Animal laughter evolved before human laughter” 进行定位，寻找文中表述此观点的研究者。\n解题思路：题目中的研究发现是“动物笑声的进化早于人类笑声”。在段落D中，研究者Elke Zimmerman通过比较婴儿和黑猩猩的笑声，提出了她的观点：婴儿笑声与黑猩猩笑声的相似性，支持了“笑声在人类出现之前早已存在(long before humans arrived on the scene)”这一理念。这与研究发现“动物笑声的进化早于人类笑声”完全吻合。因此，提出此研究发现的研究者是Elke Zimmerman，对应选项B。","options":["Tom Flamson","Elke Zimmerman","Robert Provine","Jaak Panksepp"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59713","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nLook at the following research findings (questions 1-6) and the list of people below.  Match each finding with the correct person A, B, C or D.  Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nA Tom Flamson\nB Elke Zimmerman\nC Robert Provine\nD Jaak Panksepp"},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8182:59713:6","type":"choice","text":"6 Laughter is a social activity.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘Laughter evolved as a signal to others – it almost disappears when we are alone,’ says Robert Provine, a neuroscientist at the University of Maryland. Provine found that most laughter comes as a polite reaction to everyday remarks such as ‘see you later’, rather than anything particularly funny. And the way we laugh depends on the company we’re keeping.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是哪个研究者发现笑是一种社交活动。\n定位关键信息：通过研究发现的核心概念 “Laughter is a social activity” 进行定位，寻找文中明确将 laughter 与 social, groups, others 等概念联系起来的研究者。\n解题思路：题目中的研究发现是“笑是一种社交活动”。在段落B中，研究者Robert Provine明确指出“笑是作为给他人的信号进化而来的——当我们独处时，笑声几乎消失”，并且进一步说明“我们笑的方式取决于我们和谁在一起”。这些陈述直接、有力地证明了笑的社交属性，与研究发现完全一致。因此，提出此研究发现的研究者是Robert Provine，对应选项C。","options":["Tom Flamson","Elke Zimmerman","Robert Provine","Jaak Panksepp"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59713","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nLook at the following research findings (questions 1-6) and the list of people below.  Match each finding with the correct person A, B, C or D.  Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nA Tom Flamson\nB Elke Zimmerman\nC Robert Provine\nD Jaak Panksepp"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8182:59714:7","type":"choice","text":"Some researchers believe that laughter first evolved out of 7 ____ .","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：To find the origins of laughter, Provine believes we need to look at the play.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是研究人员认为笑声最初是从什么发展而来的。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"laugh first evolved out of\"定位到C段中提到笑声起源的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确指出笑声的起源与\"play\"（玩耍）有关，即笑声最初是从玩耍中发展出来的。题目中的\"laugh first evolved\"对应原文中的\"origins of laughter\"，而\"play\"是笑声起源的关键因素。因此，正确答案是I。","options":["evolution","chirps","origins","voice","confidence","rats","primates","response","play","children","tickling"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"59714","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 7-10\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-K, below. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8182:59714:8","type":"choice","text":"The investigation has revealed that human and chimp laughter may have the same 8 ____ .","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Using sound spectrographs to reveal the pitch and intensity of vocalizations, she discovered that chimp and human baby laughter follow broadly the same pattern. Zimmerman believes the closeness of baby laughter to chimp laughter supports the idea that laughter was around long before humans arrived on the scene. What started simply as a modification of breathing associated with enjoyable and playful interactions has acquired a symbolic meaning as an indicator of pleasure.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是研究发现人类和黑猩猩的笑声可能有相同的什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“human and chimp laughter”和“same”可以定位到D段中关于Elke Zimmerman的研究，她比较了人类婴儿和黑猩猩在搔痒时的声音。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子“Zimmerman believes the closeness of baby laughter to chimp laughter supports the idea that laughter was around long before humans arrived on the scene. ”可以得出，人类和黑猩猩的笑声可能有相同的起源或基础，即“modification of breathing”。因此，正确答案是“C”。","options":["evolution","chirps","origins","voice","confidence","rats","primates","response","play","children","tickling"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"59714","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 7-10\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-K, below. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8182:59714:9","type":"choice","text":"Besides, scientists have been aware that 9 ____ laugh, however, it now seems that laughter might be more widespread than once we thought.","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句： More distantly related primates, including gorillas, laugh, and anecdotal evidence suggests that other social mammals may do too.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“除了（已知）科学家已经意识到哪些动物会笑，现在看来笑声可能比我们以前认为的更普遍。”需要填入一个动物名称。\n定位关键信息： 使用 \"scientists have been aware\" 和 \"laugh\" 定位到文中描述哪些动物被确认会笑的句子。\n解题思路：题目指出科学家已经知道某种动物会笑。在段落E中，原文明确提到“关系更远的灵长类动物，包括大猩猩，也会笑”。这表明“灵长类动物”是科学家已经确认会笑的动物类别。同时，由灵长类动物会笑引出对其他社会性哺乳动物也可能发笑的推测，从而证明笑可能更普遍。这与题目的逻辑完全一致。因此，答案为“primates”。","options":["evolution","chirps","origins","voice","confidence","rats","primates","response","play","children","tickling"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"59714","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 7-10\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-K, below. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8182:59714:10","type":"choice","text":"Although the reasons why humans started to laugh are still unknown,it seems that laughter may result from the 10 ____ we feel with another person.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：By engaging in a bout of tickling, we put ourselves at the mercy of another individual, and laughing is a signal that we laughter is what makes it a reliable signal of trust according to Tom Flamson, a laughter researcher at the University of California, Los Angels.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是尽管人类开始笑的原因仍然未知，但似乎笑声可能源于我们与另一个人感受到的某种情感。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"laugh\"和\"we feel with another person\"可以定位到F段中关于笑声作为信任信号的描述。\n解题思路：原文中提到\"they get bonded to us as a result, which certainly seems like a show of trust\"，表明笑声与信任有关。题目中的\"we feel with another person\"对应原文中的\"bonded to us\"，因此可以确定答案为E。","options":["evolution","chirps","origins","voice","confidence","rats","primates","response","play","children","tickling"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"59714","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 7-10\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-K, below. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8182:59715:11","type":"choice","text":"Both men and women laugh more when they are with members of the same sex.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Men tend to laugh longer and harder when they are with other men, perhaps as a way of bonding. Women tend to laugh more and at a higher pitch when men are present, possibly indicating flirtation or even submission.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问“和同性在一起时，男性和女性都会笑得更多”，需要判断这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“men and women”、“laugh more”和“with members of the same sex”定位到B段，该段讨论了男性和女性在不同社交场合的笑声表现。\n解题思路：原文提到男性与男性在一起时会笑得更久、更响亮，而女性则是当男性在场时笑得更多，因此，题目中的男女都是同性在场笑得更多的说法，与原文信息不一致，因此，答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59715","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage?\nIn boxes 11-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8182:59716:12","type":"choice","text":"Primates lack sufficient breath control to be able to produce laughs the way humans do.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：While other animals pant, we alone can control our breath well enough to produce the sound of laughter.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“灵长类动物缺乏足够的呼吸控制能力，无法像人类一样发出笑声”，需要判断这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Primates\"（灵长类动物）、\"lack sufficient breath control\"（缺乏足够的呼吸控制）和\"produce laughs the way humans do\"（像人类一样发出笑声）来定位文章中的相关句子。\n解题思路：在G段中，原文明确指出“我们人类是唯一能够很好地控制呼吸以产生笑声的动物”，这意味着其他动物（包括灵长类动物）缺乏这种呼吸控制能力。因此，题目中的陈述与文章信息一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59716","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage?\nIn boxes 11-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8182:59717:13","type":"choice","text":"Chimpanzees produce laughter in a wider range of situations than rats do.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Other creatures, including chimpanzees, gorillas and even rats, chuckle. Obviously, they don’t crack up at Homer Simpson or titter at the boss’s dreadful jokes, but the fact that they laugh in the first place suggests that sniggers and chortles have been around for a lot longer than we have.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“黑猩猩会发笑的情景，比老鼠要多得多。”是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“Chimpanzees”和“rats”定位到A段，文中提到黑猩猩、大猩猩和老鼠都会笑。\n解题思路：原文提到黑猩猩、大猩猩和老鼠都会笑，但并没有比较它们发出笑声的情境范围。文中也没有提到黑猩猩比老鼠在更广泛的情境下发出笑声的信息。因此，题目中的比较信息在原文中没有给出，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59717","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage?\nIn boxes 11-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59713","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-6\nLook at the following research findings (questions 1-6) and the list of people below.  Match each finding with the correct person A, B, C or D.  Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nA Tom Flamson\nB Elke Zimmerman\nC Robert Provine\nD Jaak Panksepp","html":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>A</strong> Tom Flamson&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>B</strong> Elke Zimmerman&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>C</strong> Robert Provine&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>D</strong> Jaak Panksepp&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-top: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>1</strong> Babies and chimps produce similar sounds of laughter. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"59714","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 7-10\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-K, below. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap.","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> evolution&nbsp;</p><p><strong>B</strong> chirps&nbsp;</p><p><strong>C</strong> origins&nbsp;</p><p><strong>D</strong> voice&nbsp;</p><p><strong>E</strong> confidence&nbsp;</p><p><strong>F</strong> rats&nbsp;</p><p><strong>G</strong> primates&nbsp;</p><p><strong>H </strong>response&nbsp;</p><p><strong>l </strong>play&nbsp;</p><p><strong>J</strong> children&nbsp;</p><p><strong>K</strong> tickling&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-top: 20px; font-size: 16px;\">Some researchers believe that laughter first evolved out of <strong>7</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"59715","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage?\nIn boxes 11-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Both men and women laugh more when they are with members of the same sex.</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"59716","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage?\nIn boxes 11-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Primates lack sufficient breath control to be able to produce laughs the way humans do.</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"59717","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage?\nIn boxes 11-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Chimpanzees produce laughter in a wider range of situations than rats do.</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>What are you laughing at?&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>We like to think that laughing is the height of human sophistication. Our big brains let us see the humour in a strategically positioned pun, an unexpected plot twist or a clever piece of wordplay. But while joking and wit are uniquely human inventions, laughter certainly is not. Other creatures, including chimpanzees, gorillas and even rats, chuckle. Obviously, they don’t crack up at Homer Simpson or titter at the boss’s dreadful jokes, but the fact that they laugh in the first place suggests that sniggers and chortles have been around for a lot longer than we have. It points the way to the origins of laughter, suggesting a much more practical purpose than you might think.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>There is no doubt that laughing typical involves groups of people. ‘Laughter evolved as a signal to others – it almost disappears when we are alone,’ says Robert Provine, a neuroscientist at the University of Maryland. Provine found that most laughter comes as a polite reaction to everyday remarks such as ‘see you later’, rather than anything particularly funny. And the way we laugh depends on the company we’re keeping. Men tend to laugh longer and harder when they are with other men, perhaps as a way of bonding. Women tend to laugh more and at a higher pitch when men are present, possibly indicating flirtation or even submission.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>To find the origins of laughter, Provine believes we need to look at the play. He points out that the masters of laughing are children, and nowhere is their talent more obvious than in the boisterous antics, and the original context plays,’ he says. Well-known primate watchers, including Dian Fossey and Jane Goodall, have long argued that chimps laugh while at play. The sound they produce is known as a panting laugh. It seems obvious when you watch their behavior – they even have the same ticklish spots as we do. But remove the context, and the parallel between human laughter and a chimp’s characteristic pant laugh is not so clear. When Provine played a tape of the pant laughs to 119 of his students, for example, only two guessed correctly what it was.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>These findings underline how chimp and human laughter vary. When we laugh the sound is usually produced by chopping up a single exhalation into a series of shorter with one sound produced on each inward and outward breath. The question is: does this pant laughter have the same source as our own laughter? New research lends weight to the idea that it does. The findings come from Elke Zimmerman, head of the Institute for Zoology in Germany, who compared the sounds made by babies and chimpanzees in response to tickling during the first year of their life. Using sound spectrographs to reveal the pitch and intensity of vocalizations, she discovered that chimp and human baby laughter follow broadly the same pattern. Zimmerman believes the closeness of baby laughter to chimp laughter supports the idea that laughter was around long before humans arrived on the scene. What started simply as a modification of breathing associated with enjoyable and playful interactions has acquired a symbolic meaning as an indicator of pleasure.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Pinpointing when laughter developed is another matter. Humans and chimps share a common ancestor that lived perhaps 8 million years ago, but animals might have been laughing long before that. More distantly related primates, including gorillas, laugh, and anecdotal evidence suggests that other social mammals may do too. Scientists are currently testing such stories with a comparative analysis of just how common laughter is among animals. So far, though, the most compelling evidence for laughter beyond primates comes from research done by Jaak Panksepp from Bowling Green State University, Ohio, into the ultrasonic chirps produced by rats during play and in response to tickling.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>All this still doesn’t answer the question of why we laugh at all. One idea is that laughter and tickling originated as a way of sealing the relationship between mother and child. Another is that the reflex response to tickling is protective, alerting us to the presence of crawling creatures that might harm us or compelling us to defend the parts of our bodies that are most vulnerable in hand-to-hand combat. But the idea that has gained most popularity in recent years is that laughter in response to tickling is a way for two individuals to signal and test their trust in one another. This hypothesis starts from the observation that although a little tickle can be enjoyable if it goes on too long it can be torture. By engaging in a bout of tickling, we put ourselves at the mercy of another individual, and laughing is a signal that we laughter is what makes it a reliable signal of trust according to Tom Flamson, a laughter researcher at the University of California, Los Angels. ‘Even in rats, laughter, tickle, play and trust are linked. Rats chirp a lot when they play,’ says Flamson, ‘These chirps can be aroused by tickling. And they get bonded to us as a result, which certainly seems like a show of trust.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>We’ll never know which animal laughed the first laugh, or why. But we can be sure it wasn’t in response to a prehistoric joke. The funny thing is that while the origins of laughter are probably quite serious, we owe human laughter and our language-based humor to the same unique skill. While other animals pant, we alone can control our breath well enough to produce the sound of laughter. Without that control, there would also be no speech – and no jokes to endure.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8182&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8184","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 The History of Pencil","book":"阅读还原集Vol.13","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.13 · Test 1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8184:59760:14","type":"fill","text":"填写第 14 空","answer":"tree/Tree","acceptedAnswers":["tree","Tree"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Graphite, the main material for producing a pencil, was discovered in 1564 in Borrowdale in England when lightning struck a local tree during a thunder.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问石墨是在 Borrowdale 的一棵什么下面被发现的。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的专有名词 \"Borrowdale\" 和 \"graphite\" 定位到 A 段第一句，找到石墨被发现的地点和时间。\n解题思路：原文提到石墨是在 Borrowdale 的一棵树被闪电击中后发现的，因此石墨是在树（tree）下被发现的。答案为 tree。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59760","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8184:59761:15","type":"fill","text":"填写第 15 空","answer":"soft/Soft","acceptedAnswers":["soft","Soft"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It was soft, thus left marks everywhere.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求完成句子，说明该物质（石墨）使用起来很脏的原因。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"dirty to use\" 定位到段落A中描述石墨物理特性及其使用后果的句子。\n解题思路：原文在描述刚发现的石墨时，明确指出它“质地柔软”，因此“到处留下痕迹”。正是这种“柔软”的特性，导致它在接触物体时会留下印记，从而显得“脏”。因此，答案是“soft”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59761","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8184:59762:16","type":"fill","text":"填写第 16 空","answer":"sheep/Sheep","acceptedAnswers":["sheep","Sheep"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It was soon put to use by locals in marking their sheep for signs of ownership and calculation.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问古代人用石墨来标记什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"sign possession and number\"定位到A段中\"signs of ownership and calculation\"这一部分。\n解题思路：原文明确提到当地人使用石墨来标记他们的\"sheep\"（羊）以表示所有权，也便于清点。题干中的\"sign possession and number\"对应原文的\"signs of ownership and calculation\"，因此答案为sheep。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59762","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8184:59763:17","type":"fill","text":"填写第 17 空","answer":"mines/Mines","acceptedAnswers":["mines","Mines"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Britain turns out to be the major country where mines of graphite can be detected and developed.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求完成句子，人们在英国发现了石墨的什么。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"graphite\", \"Britain\" 定位到描述英国石墨存在形式的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，英国是拥有可勘探与可开采石墨矿藏的主要国家。这里的“mines”（矿藏）直接说明了石墨在英国是以“矿”的形式存在于地下的。因此，答案是“mines”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59763","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8184:59764:18","type":"fill","text":"填写第 18 空","answer":"string/String","acceptedAnswers":["string","String"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In Italy, graphite sticks were initially wrapped in string or sheepskin for stability, becoming perhaps the very first pencil in the world.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是第一支铅笔，是用什么来包裹石墨的。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"first pencil\"和\"graphite wrapped in\"定位到B段中描述第一支铅笔的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文B段句子\"graphite sticks were initially wrapped in string or sheepskin for stability\"可知，石墨棒最初是用string（绳子）或sheepskin（羊皮）包裹的，题干中已经提到sheepskin，因此空格处应填string。题目要求填一个单词，且原文中是string，因此答案为string。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59764","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8184:59765:19","type":"fill","text":"填写第 19 空","answer":"grease/Grease","acceptedAnswers":["grease","Grease"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It is widely known that astronauts in Russia used grease pencils, which don’t have breakage problems.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是俄罗斯宇航员在太空中更喜欢使用什么类型的铅笔。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Russian astronauts\"和\"pencils to write in the outer space\"可以定位到E段中关于俄罗斯宇航员使用铅笔的描述。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到\"astronauts in Russia used grease pencils\"，即俄罗斯宇航员使用了油性铅笔。因此，答案为grease。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59765","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8184:59766:20","type":"choice","text":"Italy is probably the first country in the whole world to make pencils.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In Italy, graphite sticks were initially wrapped in string or sheepskin for stability, becoming perhaps the very first pencil in the world.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问“意大利可能是世界上第一个制作铅笔的国家”，需要判断这一说法是否与原文一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“Italy”和“first country to make pencils”定位到B段首句。\n解题思路：此处谈到意大利最早制作铅笔的方法，并说“这也许是世界上的第一支铅笔”。再往前看，发现在第2段第2句谈到“first pencil”是在别的（英国以外的）地方被发明的。再依顺序看到第4、5句，根据文意发现这个所谓的“别的地方（elsewhere）”指的就是意大利。因此题目句对应原文，本题正确答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59766","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-26\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 20-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8184:59767:21","type":"choice","text":"Germany used various kinds of wood to make pencils.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Shortly thereafter in 1662, a superior technique was discovered by German people: two wooden halves were carved, a graphite stick inserted, and the halves then glued together – essentially the same method in use to this day.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“德国使用多种木材制作铅笔”这一说法是否与文章内容一致。\n定位关键信息：根据题目的关键词“Germany”和“various kinds of wood”定位到文章B段。\n解题思路：在B段中，文章提到德国人在1662年发现了一种更先进的制作铅笔的技术，谈到了木材，但并未提及使用了多种木材。因此，文章中没有足够的信息来支持或反驳“德国使用多种木材制作铅笔”这一说法，所以答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59767","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-26\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 20-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8184:59768:22","type":"choice","text":"Graphite makes a pencil harder and sharper.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Although graphite core in pencils is still referred to as lead, modern pencils do not contain lead as the ‘lead’ of the pencil is actually a mix of finely ground graphite and clay powders....The more clay you put in, the higher hardness the core has.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问石墨是否能让铅笔更硬更尖。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Graphite\"和\"harder and sharper\"定位到C段描述铅笔芯的句子。\n解题思路：根据变硬（harder）定位到第3段第3句，发现使铅笔芯变硬的是黏土（clay）。再回到第3段第1句，发现铅笔芯内只包含石墨和黏土两种物质。则可得出结论为“石墨并不是那个使得铅笔芯变硬的物质”，故而题目与原文概念相矛盾，本题正确答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59768","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-26\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 20-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8184:59769:23","type":"choice","text":"Pencils are not produced any more since the reign of Elizabeth I.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In England, pencils continued to be made from whole sawn graphite.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问“自从伊丽莎白一世统治时期后，铅笔就不再生产了”这一说法是否与原文一致。\n定位关键信息：通过“reign of Elizabeth I”和“not produced any more”定位到D段，该段提到“pencils continued to be made from whole sawn graphite”，说明铅笔仍在生产。\n解题思路：注意到“continued to be made”，表示英国仍然在继续制造铅笔。这与题目概念“not produced any more（不再制造）”相矛盾，故本题正确答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59769","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-26\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 20-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8184:59770:24","type":"choice","text":"The pencil was used during the first American space expedition.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But it is also a fact that their counterparts in the United States used pencils in the outer space before real zero gravity pencil was invented. They preferred mechanical pencils, which produced fine lines, much clearer than the smudgy lines left by the grease pencils the Russians favoured.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问“美国人在第一次太空探索中使用了铅笔”，需要判断文章是否明确提到这一信息。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“first American space expedition”定位到E段。\n解题思路：F段指出美国宇航员在零重力铅笔发明前使用过铅笔（mechanical pencils），但并未说明这是在“第一次太空探险”期间。文章未提供关于“第一次太空探险”的具体信息，因此无法确认题目所述内容是否属实。答案应为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59770","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-26\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 20-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8184:59771:25","type":"choice","text":"American astronauts did not replace mechanical pencils immediately after the zero-gravity pencils were invented.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But despite the fact that the Americans did invent zero gravity pencils later, they stuck to mechanical pencils for many years.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“美国宇航员在零重力铅笔发明后，没有立即替换机械铅笔”，需要判断文章是否明确提到这一信息。\n定位关键信息：题目中的“American astronauts”、“zero-gravity pencils were invented”和“did not replace mechanical pencils immediately”是定位的关键信息。通过这些关键词，可以在F段中找到对应的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子“Despite the fact that the Americans did invent zero gravity pencils later, they stuck to mechanical pencils for many years.”，可以得出结论，美国宇航员在零重力铅笔被发明后，仍然继续使用机械铅笔很多年。这与题目中的陈述“American astronauts did not replace mechanical pencils immediately after the zero-gravity pencils were invented.”一致，因此答案是A. True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59771","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-26\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 20-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8184:59772:26","type":"choice","text":"Pencils are unlikely to be used in the future.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The application of pencils has by now become so widespread that they can be seen everywhere, such as classrooms, meeting rooms and art rooms, etc. A spectrum of users are likely to continue to use it into the future: students to do math works, artists to draw on sketch pads, waiters or waitresses to mark on order boards, make-up professional to apply to faces, and architects to produce blueprints.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问“未来人们不太可能使用铅笔”，需要判断文章是否明确提到这一信息。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的核心词“unlikely to be used in the future”定位到F段，该段明确提到铅笔的广泛应用和未来使用者。\n解题思路：G段指出铅笔的应用已经非常广泛，并且列出了多种未来使用者（如学生、艺术家、服务员等），说明铅笔在未来仍会被继续使用，这与题目的说法直接矛盾。因此，题目与原文信息不符，答案为B（False）。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59772","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-26\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 20-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59760","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Graphite was found under a <strong>14</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong> in Borrowdale.</p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"59761","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; border: medium;\">It was dirty to use because it was</span>&nbsp;<strong>15</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[15] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":15},{"id":"59762","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Ancient people used graphite to sign&nbsp;<strong>16</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[16] ____</strong>.</p>","firstNumber":16},{"id":"59763","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>People found graphite&nbsp;<strong>17</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[17] ____</strong> in Britain.</p>","firstNumber":17},{"id":"59764","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The first pencil was graphite wrapped in&nbsp;<strong>18</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[18] ____</strong> or animal skin.</p>","firstNumber":18},{"id":"59765","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nComplete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Russian astronauts preferred <strong>19 </strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong> pencils to write in the outer space.</p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"59766","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-26\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 20-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Italy is probably the first country in the whole world to make pencils.</strong></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"59767","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-26\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 20-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Germany used various kinds of wood to make pencils.</strong></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"59768","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-26\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 20-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Graphite makes a pencil harder and sharper.</strong></p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"59769","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-26\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 20-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Pencils are not produced any more since the reign of Elizabeth I.</strong></p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"59770","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-26\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 20-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The pencil was used during the first American space expedition.</strong></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"59771","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-26\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 20-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>American astronauts did not replace mechanical pencils immediately after the zero-gravity pencils were invented.</strong></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"59772","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 20-26\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage? In boxes 20-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Pencils are unlikely to be used in the future.</strong></p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The History of Pencil&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The beginning of the story of pencils started with lightning. Graphite, the main material for producing a pencil, was discovered in 1564 in Borrowdale in England when lightning struck a local tree during a thunder. Local people found out that the black substance spotted at the root of the unlucky tree was different from burning ash of wood. It was soft, thus left marks everywhere. The chemistry was barely out of its infancy at the time, so people mistook it for lead, equally black but much heavier. It was soon put to use by locals in marking their sheep for signs of ownership and calculation.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Britain turns out to be the major country where mines of graphite can be detected and developed. Even so, the first pencil was invented elsewhere. As graphite is soft, it requires some form of the encasement. In Italy, graphite sticks were initially wrapped in string or sheepskin for stability, becoming perhaps the very first pencil in the world. Then around 1560, an Italian couple made what are likely the first blueprints for the modern, wood-encased carpentry pencil their version was a flat, oval, more compact type of pencil. Their concept involved the hollowing out of a stick of juniper wood. Shortly thereafter in 1662, a superior technique was discovered by German people: two wooden halves were carved, a graphite stick inserted, and the halves then glued together – essentially the same method in use to this day. The news of usefulness of these early pencils spread far and wide, attracting the attention of artists all over the known world.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Although graphite core in pencils is still referred to as lead, modern pencils do not contain lead as the ‘lead’ of the pencil is actually a mix of finely ground graphite and clay powders. This mixture is important because the amount of clay content added to the graphite depends on intended pencil hardness, and the amount of time spent on grinding the mixture determines the quality of the lead. The more clay you put in, the higher hardness the core has. Many pencils across the world and almost all in Europe are graded on the European system. This system of naming used B for black and H for hard; a pencil’s grade was described by a sequence or successive Hs or Bs such as BB and BBB for successively softer leads, and HH and HHH for successively harder ones. Then the standard writing pencil is graded HB.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In England, pencils continue to be made from whole sawn graphite. But with the mass production of pencils, they are getting drastically more popular in many countries with each passing decade. As demands rise, appetite for graphite soars.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>According to the United States Geological Survey (USGS), world production of natural graphite in 2012 was 1,100,000 tonnes, of which the following major exporters are: China, India, Brazil, North Korea and Canada. When the value of graphite was realised, the mines were taken over by the government and guarded. One of its chiefs uses during the reign of Elizabeth I in the second half of the 16th century was as moulds for the manufacture of cannonballs. Graphite was transported from Keswick to London in armed stagecoaches. In 1751 an Act of Parliament was passed making it an offence to steal or receive ‘wad’. This crime was punishable by hard labour or transportation.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>That the United States did not use pencils in the outer space till they spent $1,000 to make a pencil to use in zero gravity conditions is, in fact, a fiction. It is widely known that astronauts in Russia used grease pencils, which don’t have breakage problems. But it is also a fact that their counterparts in the United States used pencils in the outer space before real zero gravity pencil was invented. They preferred mechanical pencils, which produced fine lines, much clearer than the smudgy lines left by the grease pencils the Russians favoured. But the lead tips of these mechanical pencils broke often. That bit of graphite floating around the space capsule could get into someone’s eye, or even find its way into machinery or electronics, causing an electrical short or other problems. But despite the fact that the Americans did invent zero gravity pencils later, they stuck to mechanical pencils for many years.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Against the backcloth of a digitalized world, the prospect of pencils seems bleak. In reality, it does not. The application of pencils has by now become so widespread that they can be seen everywhere, such as classrooms, meeting rooms and art rooms, etc. A spectrum of users are likely to continue to use it into the future: students to do math works, artists to draw on sketch pads, waiters or waitresses to mark on order boards, make-up professional to apply to faces, and architects to produce blueprints. The possibilities seem limitless.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8184&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8185","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Sunset for the Oil Business","book":"阅读还原集Vol.13","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.13 · Test 1 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8185:59742:27","type":"choice","text":"Hubbert has a high-profile reputation amongst ODAC members.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：M. King Hubbert, a Shell geologist of legendary status among depletion experts, forecast in 1956 that oil production in the United States would peak in the early 1970s and then slowly decline, in something resembling a bell-shaped curve.\nHis successful prediction has emboldened a new generation of geologists to apply his methodology on a global scale. Chief among them are the experts at ODAC, who worry that the global peak in production will come in the next decade.\n对应段落：C段 E段\n审题：题目问Hubbert在ODAC成员中是否有很高的知名度。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Hubbert\"和\"ODAC\"定位答案。在C段中找到\"Hubbert\"的相关描述。\n解题思路：原文中他是一个“geologist of legendary status”，在资源枯竭研究领域堪称传奇人物，对应题目信息“high-profile reputation”。题目与原文是同意表达，所以答案为Yes。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59742","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? In boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information, NO if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8185:59743:28","type":"choice","text":"Oil is likely to last longer than some other energy sources.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Oil from that area then becomes less competitive in relation to other fuels, or to oil from other areas.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“石油耗尽可能比其他能源耗尽要晚”是否与作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“Oil”、“last longer than”、“other energy sources”。需要在文章中寻找关于石油和其他能源持续时间比较的信息。\n解题思路：仔细阅读全文，寻找关于石油和其他能源持续时间比较的句子。在D段中，这里并没有提及题目中所说的“last longer than some other energy sources”，只是说石油作为能源不再有竞争力而已。题目信息在原文基础上无法判断，所以答案为Not Given。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59743","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? In boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information, NO if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8185:59744:29","type":"choice","text":"The majority of geologists believe that oil with start to run out sometime this decade.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：That sharply contradicts mainstream thinking. America’s Geological Survey prepared an exhaustive study of oil depletion last year (in part to rebut Dr Campbell’s arguments) that put the peak of production some decades off.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问“大多数地质学家认为石油将在这十年内开始耗尽”，即询问主流地质学家的观点是否认为石油将在这十年内开始减少。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“majority of geologists”和“oil will start to run out sometime this decade”定位到F段，该段提到主流观点认为石油生产高峰将在几十年后到来，与题目中“这十年”的说法矛盾。\n解题思路：F段明确指出主流地质学家的观点（包括美国地质调查局和国际能源机构）认为石油生产高峰将在几十年后到来，这与题目中“本十年”的说法相反。因此，题目中的说法与主流地质学家的观点相矛盾，应选择B（No）。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59744","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? In boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information, NO if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8185:59745:30","type":"choice","text":"Over 50 percent of the oil we know about is currently being recovered.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Average recovery rates (how much of the known oil in a reservoir can actually be brought to the surface) are still only around 30-35%. Industry optimists believe that new techniques on the drawing board today could lift that figure to 50-60%within a decade\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问“我们开采了超过50%的已知现存的石油”，即询问已知现存石油开采率是否超过50%。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"Over 50 percent\"和\"currently being recovered\"对应J段中的\"Average recovery rates\"和\"are still only around 30-35%\"。\n解题思路：J段明确指出石油的平均开采率仅为30-35%，远低于题目中的\"Over 50 percent\"，50%是在未来人们可能达到的开采率，而不是现在。因此题目说法与原文矛盾，答案为No。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59745","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? In boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information, NO if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8185:59746:31","type":"choice","text":"History has shown that some of Hubbert’s principles were mistaken.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：That is the result of adversity: the nationalisations of the 1970s forced Big Oil to develop reserves in expensive, inaccessible places such as the North Sea and Alaska, undermining Dr Hubbert’s assumption that cheap reserves are developed first.\n对应段落：K段\n审题：题目问的是“历史表明部分休伯特理论是错误的”，需要判断作者是否同意这个观点。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"Hubbert’s principles\", \"mistaken\", \"history has shown\" 作为关键词，定位文中评价哈伯特理论准确性的句子。\n解题思路：段落K中，作者明确指出，20世纪70年代的国有化政策迫使大石油公司去开发如北海和阿拉斯加这样成本高昂、难以进入的油田，这一历史事实“削弱了哈伯特的假设，即便宜的储量会先被开发”。原文用“undermining”（削弱）这个词，清晰地表明作者认为历史发展证明了哈伯特的这一特定原则（假设）是不正确的。这与题目陈述完全一致，因此答案为YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59746","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? In boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information, NO if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8185:59747:32","type":"fill","text":"填写第 32 空","answer":"controversial/Controversial\n\n\n\n","acceptedAnswers":["controversial","Controversial"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At the time, his forecast was controversial, and many rubbished it.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是当Hubbert的理论最初提出时，许多人认为它是什么样的。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Hubbert’s theory\"和\"originally presented\"可以定位到C段。\n解题思路：根据原文中C段的内容，其中提到\"his forecast was controversial, and many rubbished it\"，这句话表明Hubbert的理论最初提出时受到了质疑和争议。因此答案为\"controversial\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59747","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nComplete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8185:59748:33","type":"fill","text":"填写第 33 空","answer":"new/New/tapped/Tapped","acceptedAnswers":["new","New","tapped","Tapped"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Oil production in a new area typically rises quickly at first, as the easiest and cheapest reserves are tapped.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是当油田处于什么状态时，容易发现石油产量增加。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"oilfield\"和\"oil production\"定位到D段，该段描述了新油田的石油生产特点。\n解题思路：原文提到新油田的石油产量初期通常增长迅猛，因为此时开采的是最容易获取、成本最低的油田。。这里的\"tapped\"表示油田被开采或处于新开发的状态。因此答案为tapped或new。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59748","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nComplete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8185:59749:34","type":"fill","text":"填写第 34 空","answer":"expensive/Expensive","acceptedAnswers":["expensive","Expensive"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Over time, reservoirs age and go into decline, and so lifting oil becomes more expensive.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是随着油藏老化，油开采会变得更什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"recovery of the oil\"和\"reservoir gets older\"定位到D段，找到描述油藏老化过程的句子。\n解题思路：原文中提到\"reservoirs age and go into decline\"（油藏老化并开始进入衰退期），紧接着说明\"lifting oil becomes more expensive\"（开采石油变得更昂贵）。题干中的\"recovery of the oil\"对应原文的\"lifting oil\"，\"gets more\"对应\"becomes more\"，因此答案为\"expensive\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59749","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nComplete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8185:59750:35","type":"fill","text":"填写第 35 空","answer":"competitive/Competitive","acceptedAnswers":["competitive","Competitive"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Oil from that area then becomes less competitive in relation to other fuels, or to oil from other areas.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是此时的油田无法像其他油田那样怎么样。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"competitive\"和\"other areas\"定位到D段后半部分，找到关于油田竞争力下降的描述。\n解题思路：原文中提到随着油田老化，开采成本增加，导致该油田的石油相对于其他燃料或其他油田，竞争力下降。题干中的\"35\"与原文中\"less competitive\"的描述对应，因此答案为competitive。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59750","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nComplete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":1},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8185:59751:36","type":"choice","text":"36 has found fault in the geological research procedure.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In particular, he faults forecasters who used Hubbert-style analysis for relying on fixed estimates of how much ‘ultimately recoverable’ oil there really is below ground, in the industry’s jargon: that figure, he insists, is actually a dynamic one, as improvements in infrastructure, knowledge and technology raise the amount of oil which is recoverable.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是“发现地质研究方法的问题”的人是谁。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词“has found fault in the geological research procedure”可以定位到H段，该段明确提到了“he faults forecasters who used Hubbert-style analysis for relying on fixed estimates”，这里的“he”指的是Michael Lynch，他对地质研究方法提出了批评。\n解题思路：H段中的“he”指的是Michael Lynch，他批评了使用Hubbert风格分析的预测者，因为这些人把地下可开采石油量视为一个定量，而Michael Lynch认为这个数字实际上是动态的，因为基础设施、知识和技术的改进会增加可开采的石油量。因此，答案为E。","options":["Colin Campell","M. King Hubbert","Kenneth Deffeyes","Rene Dahan","Michael Lynch"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"59751","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nLook at the following statements (questions 36-40) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-E. Write the correct letter, A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of people\nA Colin Campell\nB M. King Hubbert\nC Kenneth Deffeyes\nD Rene Dahan\nE Michael Lynch"},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8185:59751:37","type":"choice","text":"37 has provided the longest-range forecast regarding oil supply.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：René Dahan, one of ExxonMobil’s top managers, goes further: with an assurance characteristic of the world’s largest energy company, he insists that the world will be awash in oil for another 70 years.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“谁提供了周期最长的石油供应预测。”\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词“longest-range forecast regarding oil supply”定位到F段，找到René Dahan的预测内容。\n解题思路：F段提到René Dahan是埃克森美孚的高级管理人员，他预测“世界将在未来70年内石油供应充足”，这是所有预测中时间跨度最大的，因此答案为D。","options":["Colin Campell","M. King Hubbert","Kenneth Deffeyes","Rene Dahan","Michael Lynch"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"59751","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nLook at the following statements (questions 36-40) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-E. Write the correct letter, A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of people\nA Colin Campell\nB M. King Hubbert\nC Kenneth Deffeyes\nD Rene Dahan\nE Michael Lynch"},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8185:59751:38","type":"choice","text":"38 has convinced others that oil production will follow a particular model.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：His successful prediction has emboldened a new generation of geologists to apply his methodology on a global scale.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是谁让别人相信石油产量会遵循一个特定的模型。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"oil production will follow a particular model\"定位到C段，该段提到Hubbert成功预测了美国石油产量会遵循一个特定的模型（bell-shaped curve），并因此激励了新一代地质学家将他的方法应用于全球。\n解题思路：原文中C段提到Hubbert此前成功预测美国石油产量会遵循一个特定的模型，促使新一代地质学家将他的模型应用于全球。题目问的是谁让别人相信石油产量会遵循一个特定的模型，因此答案为Hubbert，对应选项B。","options":["Colin Campell","M. King Hubbert","Kenneth Deffeyes","Rene Dahan","Michael Lynch"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"59751","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nLook at the following statements (questions 36-40) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-E. Write the correct letter, A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of people\nA Colin Campell\nB M. King Hubbert\nC Kenneth Deffeyes\nD Rene Dahan\nE Michael Lynch"},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8185:59751:39","type":"choice","text":"39 has accused fellow scientists of refusing to see the truth.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Dr Campbell even decried the amazing display of ignorance, denial and obfuscation by government, industry and academics on this topic.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“谁指责了同领域的科学家拒绝正视真相”。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“accused fellow scientists of refusing to see the truth”可以定位到A段中“Dr Campbell even decried the amazing display of ignorance, denial and obfuscation by government, industry and academics on this topic.”这句话。\n解题思路：原文中的“decried the amazing display of ignorance, denial and obfuscation”与题目中的“accused fellow scientists of refusing to see the truth”意思相符，坎贝尔医生痛斥政府、工业界和学术界在这一议题上展现出的无知、否认和混淆视听。因此答案为A。","options":["Colin Campell","M. King Hubbert","Kenneth Deffeyes","Rene Dahan","Michael Lynch"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"59751","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nLook at the following statements (questions 36-40) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-E. Write the correct letter, A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of people\nA Colin Campell\nB M. King Hubbert\nC Kenneth Deffeyes\nD Rene Dahan\nE Michael Lynch"},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8185:59751:40","type":"choice","text":"40 has expressed doubt over whether improved methods of extracting oil are possible.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Dr Deffeyes captures this end-of-technology mindset well. He argues that because the industry has already spent billions on technology development, it makes it difficult to ask today for new technology, as most of the wheels have already been invented.\n对应段落：I\n审题：题目问的是“谁对是否可以改进石油开采方法表示怀疑”。\n定位关键信息：根据题目的关键词“improved methods of extracting oil”（改进的石油开采方法），在文章中定位到段落I，该段落讨论了对技术革新的不同看法。\n解题思路：段落I中，作者描述了悲观派对即将到来的技术革命持轻蔑态度。Deffeyes认为，由于行业已在技术研发上投入数十亿美元，如今再要求开发新技术已难如登天，因为“大多数轮子都已经被发明出来了”。这种认为重大技术创新已接近穷尽的观点，表达了对未来大幅改进采油方法的怀疑。因此，提出此观点的人是Kenneth Deffeyes，对应选项C。","options":["Colin Campell","M. King Hubbert","Kenneth Deffeyes","Rene Dahan","Michael Lynch"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"59751","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nLook at the following statements (questions 36-40) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-E. Write the correct letter, A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of people\nA Colin Campell\nB M. King Hubbert\nC Kenneth Deffeyes\nD Rene Dahan\nE Michael Lynch"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59742","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? In boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information, NO if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Hubbert has a high-profile reputation amongst ODAC members.</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"59743","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? In boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information, NO if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Oil is likely to last longer than some other energy sources.</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"59744","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? In boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information, NO if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The majority of geologists believe that oil with start to run out sometime this decade.</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"59745","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? In boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information, NO if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Over 50 percent of the oil we know about is currently being recovered.</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"59746","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in passage? In boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information, NO if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>History has shown that some of Hubbert’s principles were mistaken.</strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"59747","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nComplete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Many people believed Hubbert’s theory was <strong>32</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[32] ____</strong> when it was originally presented.</p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"59748","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nComplete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>(1) When an oilfield is <strong>33</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[33] ____</strong> , it is easy to observe the increase of oil production.</p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"59749","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nComplete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>(2) The recovery of the oil gets more <strong>34</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[34] ____</strong> as the reservoir gets older.</p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"59750","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nComplete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>(3) The oilfield can’t be as <strong>35</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[35] ____</strong> as other areas.</p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"59751","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nLook at the following statements (questions 36-40) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-E. Write the correct letter, A-E in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nList of people\nA Colin Campell\nB M. King Hubbert\nC Kenneth Deffeyes\nD Rene Dahan\nE Michael Lynch","html":"<p>List of people&nbsp;</p><p><strong>A</strong> Colin Campell&nbsp;</p><p><strong>B</strong> M. King Hubbert&nbsp;</p><p><strong>C</strong> Kenneth Deffeyes&nbsp;</p><p><strong>D</strong> Rene Dahan&nbsp;</p><p><strong>E</strong> Michael Lynch&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-top: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>36</strong> has found fault in the geological research procedure. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[36] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":36}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Sunset for the Oil Business&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">The world is about to run out of oil. Or perhaps not. It depends whom you believe…&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Members of the Department Analysis Centre (ODAC) recently met in London and presented technical data that support their grim forecast that the world is perilously close to running out of oil. Leading lights of this moment, including the geologists Colin Campbell, rejected rival views presented by American geological survey and the international energy agency that contradicted their findings. Dr Campbell even decried the amazing display of ignorance, denial and obfuscation by government, industry and academics on this topic.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>So is the oil really running out? The answer is easy: Yes. Nobody seriously disputes the notion that oil is, for all practical purposes, a non-renewable resource that will run out someday, be that years or decades away. The harder question is determining when precisely oil will begin to get scarce. And answering that question involves scaling Hubbert&#39;s peak.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>M. King Hubbert, a Shell geologist of legendary status among depletion experts, forecast in 1956 that oil production in the United States would peak in the early 1970s and then slowly decline, in something resembling a bell-shaped curve. At the time, his forecast was controversial, and many rubbished it. After 1970, however, empirical evidence proved him correct: oil production in America did indeed peak and has been in decline ever since.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Dr Hubbert&#39;s analysis drew on the observation that oil production in a new area typically rises quickly at first, as the easiest and cheapest reserves are tapped. Over time, reservoirs age and go into decline, and so lifting oil becomes more expensive. Oil from that area then becomes less competitive in relation to other fuels, or to oil from other areas. As a result, production slows down and usually tapers off and declines. That, he argued, made for a bell-shaped curve.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>His successful prediction has emboldened a new generation of geologists to apply his methodology on a global scale. Chief among them are the experts at ODAC, who worry that the global peak in production will come in the next decade. Dr Campbell used to argue that the peak should have come already; he now thinks it is just around the corner. A heavyweight has now joined this gloomy chorus. Kenneth Deffeyes of Princeton University argues in a lively new book (‘The View from Hubbert&#39;s Peak’) that global oil production could peak as soon as 2004.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>That sharply contradicts mainstream thinking. America’s Geological Survey prepared an exhaustive study of oil depletion last year (in part to rebut Dr Campbell’s arguments) that put the peak of production some decades off. The IEA has just weighed in with its new ‘World Energy Outlook’, which foresees enough oil to comfortably meet the demand to 2020 from remaining reserves. René Dahan, one of ExxonMobil’s top managers, goes further: with an assurance characteristic of the world’s largest energy company, he insists that the world will be awash in oil for another 70 years.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Who is right? In making sense of these wildly opposing views, it is useful to look back at the pitiful history of oil forecasting. Doomsters have been predicting dry wells since the 1970s, but so far the oil is still gushing. Nearly all the predictions for 2000 made after the 1970s oil shocks were far too pessimistic. America’s Department of Energy thought that oil would reach $150 a barrel (at 2000 prices); even Exxon predicted a price of $100.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Michael Lynch of DRI-WEFA, an economic consultancy, is one of the few oil forecasters who has got things generally right. In a new paper, Dr Lynch analyses those historical forecasts. He finds evidence of both bias and recurring errors, which suggests that methodological mistakes (rather than just poor data) were the problem. In particular, he faults forecasters who used Hubbert-style analysis for relying on fixed estimates of how much ‘ultimately recoverable’ oil there really is below ground, in the industry’s jargon: that figure, he insists, is actually a dynamic one, as improvements in infrastructure, knowledge and technology raise the amount of oil which is recoverable.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>That points to what will probably determine whether the pessimists or the optimists are right: technological innovation. The first camp tends to be dismissive of claims of forthcoming technological revolutions in such areas as deep-water drilling and enhanced recovery. Dr Deffeyes captures this end-of-technology mindset well. He argues that because the industry has already spent billions on technology development, it makes it difficult to ask today for new technology, as most of the wheels have already been invented.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Yet techno-optimists argue that the technological revolution in oil has only just begun. Average recovery rates (how much of the known oil in a reservoir can actually be brought to the surface) are still only around 30-35%. Industry optimists believe that new techniques on the drawing board today could lift that figure to 50-60% within a decade.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>K&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Given the industry’s astonishing track record of innovation, it may be foolish to bet against it. That is the result of adversity: the nationalisations of the 1970s forced Big Oil to develop reserves in expensive, inaccessible places such as the North Sea and Alaska, undermining Dr Hubbert’s assumption that cheap reserves are developed first. The resulting upstream investments have driven down the cost of finding and developing wells over the last two decades from over $20 a barrel to around $6 a barrel. The cost of producing oil has fallen by half, to under $4 a barrel.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>L&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Such miracles will not come cheap, however, since much of the world’s oil is now produced in ageing fields that are rapidly declining. The IEA concludes that global oil production need not peak in the next two decades if the necessary investments are made. So how much is necessary? If oil companies are to replace the output lost at those ageing fields and meet the world’s ever-rising demand for oil, the agency reckons they must invest $1 trillion in non-OPEC countries over the next decade alone. That’s quite a figure.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8185&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8175","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 MENTAL GYMNASTICS","book":"阅读还原集Vol.12","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.12 · Test 4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8175:59696:1","type":"choice","text":"Bailey asks his participants to imagine they are buildings.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：At one point the bankers are instructed to shut their eyes and visualize themselves filling the room and then the building.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问“Mind Gym教练指示员工想象自己是建筑物”，即教练是否让员工想象自己成为建筑物。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"Mind Gym coach instructed employees to imagine that they are the building\"定位到B段，找到教练指示员工\"visualize themselves filling the room and then the building\"的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到教练让员工想象自己\"filling the room and then the building\"，即先想象自己充满房间，再想象自己充满建筑物。虽然题目描述\"imagine that they are the building\"与原文\"filling the building\"在语义上接近，但原文强调的是\"充满建筑物\"而非\"成为建筑物\"，存在细微差别。因此，题目表述与原文不完全一致，答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59696","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8175:59697:2","type":"choice","text":"Brain training is used by business people all over the world.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Similar mental workouts are happening in corporate seminar rooms around the globe.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目判断“脑力训练被全世界的商务人士所使用”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"all over the world\" 和 \"business people\" (或类似概念如corporate, business) 作为关键词进行定位。\n解题思路：在段落C中，首句明确指出“类似的精神训练正在全球各地的公司会议室里进行着”。“全球各地”(around the globe) 对应题目的“全世界”(all over the world)，“公司会议室”(corporate seminar rooms) 则清晰地指明了使用者是商务人士。因此，该陈述与原文信息一致，答案为Yes。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59697","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8175:59698:3","type":"choice","text":"The organisations that sell mental exercise all promote it in much the same way.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Whatever the style, the companies' sales pitch is similar: 'Follow our routines,' they tell us, 'to shape and sculpt your brain or mind, just as you might tone and train your body.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目判断“销售脑力训练课程的机构都以大致相同的方式进行推广”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"organisations\", \"sell mental exercise\", \"promote it in much the same way\" 作为关键词，定位到描述这些公司营销方式的句子。\n解题思路：题目中的核心信息是不同机构在“推广方式”上的“相似性”。在段落C中，原文明确指出，无论这些脑力训练公司的课程风格如何，“它们的销售说辞是相似的”(sales pitch is similar)，并给出了统一的说辞范例。这与题目中“以大致相同的方式进行推广”的陈述完全吻合。因此，该陈述与原文信息一致，答案为Yes。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59698","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8175:59699:4","type":"choice","text":"Companies offering mental workouts say that their practice has a scientific basis.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Nearly all claim that their mental workouts draw on serious research into how the brain works.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目判断“提供脑力训练的公司声称它们的实践有科学依据”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"companies offering mental workouts\", \"scientific basis\" 作为关键词，定位到描述这些公司对其训练方法依据的声明的句子。\n解题思路：在段落C中，原文明确指出“几乎所有的公司都声称它们的脑力训练借鉴了对大脑运作方式的严肃研究”。“严肃研究”(serious research) 直接对应“科学依据”(scientific basis)，而“声称”(claim) 也与题目中的“say that”一致。因此，该陈述与原文信息一致，答案为Yes。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59699","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8175:59700:5","type":"choice","text":"Susan Greenfield was one of the founders of Mind Gym.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Mind Gym trades on a quote from Susan Greenfield, one of Britain's best-known neuroscientists: 'It's a bit like going to the gym: if you exercise your brain, it will grow.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目判断“Susan Greenfield是Mind Gym的创始人之一”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：用 \"Susan Greenfield\" 和 \"Mind Gym\" 作为关键词，定位到文中提及两者关系的句子。\n解题思路：在段落D中，原文仅提到Mind Gym公司在营销中“利用”(trades on) Susan Greenfield（一位著名的神经科学家）的言论。文中只说明了她的话被该公司引用，并未提及她是该公司的创始人或与她有任何创立关系。题目信息在原文中找不到依据，因此答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59700","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8175:59701:6","type":"choice","text":"6 People rarely take time to stand back from a problem before taking a decision.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For example, they may have felt the only way to solve a difficult problem is to bang away at it as hard as possible. Then they learn that creative thinkers advise taking a break and letting ideas incubate. A simple tactic, yet one rarely taught in normal life. Which, according to educational psychologist Guy Claxton, Mind Gym's academic adviser, is exactly the point.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求将“人们很少花时间退后一步审视问题，再决定怎么做”这一陈述与列表中对应的人物匹配。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"stand back from a problem\", \"taking a decision\" 以及描述人们不常采用的解决问题方式的句子进行定位。\n解题思路：在段落G中，Guy Claxton指出，人们通常认为解决难题的唯一方式是“拼命硬干”(bang away at it as hard as possible)，而“暂停一下，让想法酝酿”(taking a break and letting ideas incubate)这种简单的策略“在正常生活中却很少被传授”(rarely taught in normal life)。这种“暂停一下，让想法酝酿”正是“退后一步审视问题”的具体表现。因此，提出这一观察的人是Guy Claxton，对应选项D。","options":["Sebastian Bailey","Gessner Geyer","Susan Greenfield","Guy Claxton"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59701","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nLook at the following statements (Questions 6-13) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-D Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Sebastian Bailey\nB Gessner Geyer\nC Susan Greenfield\nD Guy Claxton"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8175:59701:7","type":"choice","text":"7 Most people underestimate their potential to be creative.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The trick is simple but Bailey points out how few such tricks people have to call upon when suddenly asked to be creative: 'They tend to just label themselves as uncreative, not realizing that there are techniques every creative person employs.'\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求将“大多数人低估了自己的创造潜力”这一陈述与列表中对应的人物匹配。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"underestimate their potential to be creative\" 以及描述人们对自己创造力错误认知的句子进行定位。\n解题思路：在段落F中，Sebastian Bailey指出，当被要求发挥创造力时，“他们倾向于直接给自己贴上‘没有创造力’的标签”，并且“没有意识到其实每个有创造力的人都在运用一些技巧”。给自己贴上“没有创造力”的标签，正是“低估自身创造潜力”的直接体现。因此，提出这一观察的人是Sebastian Bailey，对应选项A。","options":["Sebastian Bailey","Gessner Geyer","Susan Greenfield","Guy Claxton"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59701","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nLook at the following statements (Questions 6-13) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-D Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Sebastian Bailey\nB Gessner Geyer\nC Susan Greenfield\nD Guy Claxton"},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8175:59701:8","type":"choice","text":"8 Most ways of looking at mental development are unconvincing.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Claxton, who dismisses most neurological approaches as 'neuro-babble', insists creativity, mental flexibility, even motivation are all thought habits that can be learned.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：使用 \"most ways of looking at mental development\" 和 \"unconvincing\" (对应 dismissive 或 critical 的态度) 进行定位。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"Exercise can keep your brain health instead of improving someone’s IQ\"，通过这些关键词可以在G段找到Katz的观点。\n解题思路：段落H中，Guy Claxton将“大多数神经学方法”斥为“神经学胡话”(neuro-babble)。这种明确且强烈的否定态度，与题目中“认为大多数方法都缺乏说服力”的陈述完全吻合。因此，提出这一观点的人是Guy Claxton，对应选项D。","options":["Sebastian Bailey","Gessner Geyer","Susan Greenfield","Guy Claxton"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59701","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nLook at the following statements (Questions 6-13) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-D Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Sebastian Bailey\nB Gessner Geyer\nC Susan Greenfield\nD Guy Claxton"},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8175:59701:9","type":"choice","text":"9 Exercising the brain can be compared to exercising the body.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Mind Gym trades on a quote from Susan Greenfield, one of Britain's best-known neuroscientists: 'It's a bit like going to the gym: if you exercise your brain, it will grow.'\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求将“可以将锻炼大脑类比锻炼身体”这一陈述与列表中对应的人物匹配。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"exercising the brain\", \"compared to\", \"exercising the body\" 进行定位。\n解题思路：在段落D中，Susan Greenfield被引用的原话明确地将去健身房锻炼身体与锻炼大脑会使它成长进行了直接类比。因此，提出这一观点的人是Susan Greenfield，对应选项C。","options":["Sebastian Bailey","Gessner Geyer","Susan Greenfield","Guy Claxton"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59701","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nLook at the following statements (Questions 6-13) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-D Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Sebastian Bailey\nB Gessner Geyer\nC Susan Greenfield\nD Guy Claxton"},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8175:59701:10","type":"choice","text":"10 Training can actually modify the structure of the brain.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Studies have shown that mental exercise can cause changes in brain anatomy and brain chemistry, which promote increased mental efficiency and clarity.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目要求将“训练确实可以改变大脑的结构”这一陈述与列表中对应的人物匹配。\n定位关键信息： 使用 \"modify the structure of the brain\" (对应 changes in brain anatomy) 进行定位。\n解题思路：段落D中，Gessner Geyer明确指出，研究表明脑力锻炼可以引起大脑解剖结构的变化，而且可以改变大脑的化学性质。这与题目陈述一致。因此，提出这一观点的人是Gessner Geyer，对应选项B。","options":["Sebastian Bailey","Gessner Geyer","Susan Greenfield","Guy Claxton"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59701","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nLook at the following statements (Questions 6-13) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-D Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Sebastian Bailey\nB Gessner Geyer\nC Susan Greenfield\nD Guy Claxton"},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8175:59701:11","type":"choice","text":"11 Effective mental training begins with a close examination of how we ordinarily think.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Claxton believes we must return our thought patterns to a conscious level, becoming aware of how we usually think. Only then can we start to practice better thought patterns, until eventually these become our new habits.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目要求将“有效的心智训练开始于仔细审视我们惯常的思维方式”这一陈述与列表中对应的人物匹配。\n定位关键信息： 使用 \"begins with\", \"close examination\", \"how we ordinarily think\" 进行定位。\n解题思路：段落H中，Guy Claxton的观点清晰地描述了这一过程：我们必须“先让思维模式回归到意识层面，意识到我们通常是如何思考的”，然后“才能开始练习更好的思维模式”。这与题目的逻辑完全吻合。因此，提出这一观点的人是Guy Claxton，对应选项D。","options":["Sebastian Bailey","Gessner Geyer","Susan Greenfield","Guy Claxton"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59701","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nLook at the following statements (Questions 6-13) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-D Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Sebastian Bailey\nB Gessner Geyer\nC Susan Greenfield\nD Guy Claxton"},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8175:59701:12","type":"choice","text":"12 People who think that they are uncreative may be unaware of techniques used by creative people.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The trick is simple but Bailey points out how few such tricks people have to call upon when suddenly asked to be creative: 'They tend to just label themselves as uncreative, not realizing that there are techniques every creative person employs.'\n对应段落：F段\n审题： 题目要求将“那些认为自己没有创造力的人可能不知道有创造力的人所使用的技巧”这一陈述与列表中对应的人物匹配。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"unaware of techniques used by creative people\" 进行定位。\n解题思路：段落F中，Sebastian Bailey指出，人们倾向于给自己贴上“没有创造力”的标签，同时“没有意识到每个有创造力的人都在使用技巧”。这与题目陈述是完全一致的同义转述。因此，提出这一观点的人是Sebastian Bailey，对应选项A。","options":["Sebastian Bailey","Gessner Geyer","Susan Greenfield","Guy Claxton"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59701","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nLook at the following statements (Questions 6-13) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-D Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Sebastian Bailey\nB Gessner Geyer\nC Susan Greenfield\nD Guy Claxton"},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8175:59701:13","type":"choice","text":"13 Educators should place greater emphasis on developing students' thinking skills.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Nevertheless, Claxton for one believes there is no reason why schools and universities should not spend more time teaching analysis and problem-solving techniques, rather than trying to stuff heads with facts and hoping that effective thought habits are somehow absorbed by osmosis.\n对应段落：M段\n审题：题目要求将“教育者应更重视培养学生的思维技能”这一陈述与列表中对应的人物匹配。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"educators\", \"place greater emphasis\", \"students' thinking skills\" 进行定位。\n解题思路：段落M中，Guy Claxton明确主张学校和大学“应该花更多时间教授分析和解决问题的技巧”，而不是试图往脑袋里塞满死知识。这正是题目陈述所表达的观点。因此，提出这一观点的人是Guy Claxton，对应选项D。","options":["Sebastian Bailey","Gessner Geyer","Susan Greenfield","Guy Claxton"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59701","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nLook at the following statements (Questions 6-13) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-D Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Sebastian Bailey\nB Gessner Geyer\nC Susan Greenfield\nD Guy Claxton"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59696","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Bailey asks his participants to imagine they are buildings.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"59697","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Brain training is used by business people all over the world.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"59698","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The organisations that sell mental exercise all promote it in much the same way.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"59699","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Companies offering mental workouts say that their practice has a scientific basis.</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"59700","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-5\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Susan Greenfield was one of the founders of Mind Gym.</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"59701","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 6-13\nLook at the following statements (Questions 6-13) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-D Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet.\nNB you may use any letter more than once.\nList of People\nA Sebastian Bailey\nB Gessner Geyer\nC Susan Greenfield\nD Guy Claxton","html":"<p><br/></p><p style=\"margin-top:21px;margin-right:0;margin-bottom:21px;margin-left:0;text-align:left\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:16px\">List of People </span></strong></p><p style=\"margin-left:28px;text-align:left\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A<span style=\"font:9px &#39;Times New Roman&#39;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></strong><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sebastian Bailey</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:28px;text-align:left\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:16px\">B<span style=\"font:9px &#39;Times New Roman&#39;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></strong><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gessner Geyer</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:28px;text-align:left\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:16px\">C<span style=\"font:9px &#39;Times New Roman&#39;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></strong><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Susan Greenfield</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:28px;text-align:left\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:16px\">D<span style=\"font:9px &#39;Times New Roman&#39;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></strong><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Guy Claxton</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>6</strong> <span style=\"font-size:16px;font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;,sans-serif\">People rarely take time to stand back from a problem before taking a decision.</span> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[6] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":6}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>MENTAL GYMNASTICS</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><br/></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">John McCrone explains how mental exercise is being used to boost corporate brainpower</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The working day has just started at the head office of Barclays Bank in London. Seventeen staff are helping themselves to a buffet&nbsp;breakfast as young psychologist Sebastian Bailey enters the room to begin the morning&#39;s training session. But this is no ordinary training session. He is here, not to sharpen their finance or management skills, but to exercise their brains. Today&#39;s workout, organized by a company called Mind Gym, is entitled Having Presence&#39;.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>What follows is an intense 90-minute session, in which this rather abstract concept is broken down into a concrete set of feelings, mental tricks and behaviours. At one point, the bankers are instructed to shut their eyes and visualise themselves filling the room and then, the building. They finish by walking around the room acting out various levels of &#39;presence&#39;, from low-key to over-the-top.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Similar mental workouts are happening in corporate seminar rooms around the globe. Mind Gym alone offers some 70 different sessions, including ones on mental stamina and creativity for logical thinkers. Other outfits draw more directly on the exercise analogy, offering &#39;neurobics&#39; courses with names like &#39;brain sets&#39; and &#39;cerebral fitness&#39;. Whatever the style, the companies&#39; sales pitch is similar: &#39;Follow our routines,&#39; they tell us, &#39;to shape and sculpt your brain or mind, just as you might tone and train your body.&#39; Nearly all claim that their mental workouts draw on serious research into how the brain works.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Gessner Geyer, from Brainergy of Cambridge, Massachusetts, puts it like this: &#39;Studies have shown that mental exercise can cause changes in brain anatomy and brain chemistry, which promote increased mental efficiency and clarity. The neuroscience behind this is cutting-edge.&#39; Mind Gym trades on a quote from Susan Greenfield, one of Britain&#39;s best-known neuroscientists: &#39;It&#39;s a bit like going to the gym: if you exercise your brain, it will grow.&#39;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>&nbsp;In practice, the training can seem mundane. Take &#39;Creativity for logical thinkers&#39;, one of Mind Gym&#39;s eight different creativity workouts. One of the mental strategies taught is to make a sensible suggestion, then pose its opposite. Asked to spend five minutes inventing a new pizza, a group soon comes up with no topping, sweet topping, cold topping, price based on time of day, flat-rate prices and so on.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The trick is simple but Bailey points out how few such tricks people have to call upon when suddenly asked to be creative: &#39;They tend to just label themselves as uncreative, not realizing that there are techniques every creative person employs.&#39; Bailey says the aim is to introduce people to half a dozen such strategies, so that what at first seems like a dauntingly abstract mental task becomes a set of concrete, learnable behaviours. He admits this is not a shout cut to genius. Neurologically, some people do start with quicker circuits or greater handling capacity. However, the right kind of training he believes can dramatically increase brain efficiency.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Though it is hard to prove that the training itself is effective – how do you measure a change in creativity levels, or memory skills? – staff certainly report feeling that such classes have opened their eyes. For example, they may have felt the only way to solve a difficult problem is to bang away at it as hard as possible. Then they learn that creative thinkers advise taking a break and letting ideas incubate. A simple tactic, yet one rarely taught in normal life. Which, according to educational psychologist Guy Claxton, Mind Gym&#39;s academic adviser, is exactly the point.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Claxton, who dismisses most neurological approaches as &#39;neuro-babble&#39;, insists creativity, mental flexibility, even motivation are all thought habits that can be learned. The problem, he claims is that most of us never receive proper training. We develop mental strategies for tackling tasks haphazardly and soon lose sight of the very thought habits we are relying upon. Claxton believes we must return our thought patterns to a conscious level, becoming aware of how we usually think. Only then can we start to practice better thought patterns, until eventually these become our new habits.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Russian psychologists Lev Vygotsky and Aleksandr Luria put forward similar arguments in the 1930s and various attempts have been made to put them into practice. The business world is certainly familiar with both &#39;better thinking&#39; gurus such as Edward de Bono and Tony Buzan, and habit-breaking techniques such as neurolinguistic programming. Modern companies will seize on anything that claims to create flexible, bright thinkers, without scrutinizing the facts. But are neurotic workouts underpinned by scientific fact?</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>J</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Certainly, the brain adapts to demands placed on it. Neurologists have proved time and again that people who lose brain cells suddenly during a stroke often sprout new Connections to compensate-especially if they undergo therapy. Rats raised in cages with toys sprout more neural connections than rats raised in bare cages. Brain scans suggest people use more of their grey matter to carry out new tasks than well-rehearsed ones.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>K</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>So the general basis of neurobics looks sound: the brain really is inherently alterable or &#39;plastic&#39;. The problem is in the specifics. Qualities such as creativity are too subjective to rate, forcing psychologists to rely on the easy-to-score spatial and verbal reasoning tasks involved in IQ tests.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>L</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>This creates a problem for neurobics. Time and again, psychologists have found that neither mental exercises nor any other type of brain-boosting regime, including so-called smart pills designed to improve blood flow to the brain, reliably improve our ability to do these basic tasks.</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>M</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Nevertheless, Claxton for one believes there is no reason why schools and universities should not spend more time teaching analysis and problem-solving techniques, rather than trying to stuff heads with facts and hoping that effective thought habits are somehow absorbed by osmosis.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8175&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8180","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 When the Tulip Bubble Burst","book":"阅读还原集Vol.12","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.12 · Test 4 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8180:59702:14","type":"choice","text":"14 Difference between bubble burst impacts by tulip and by high-tech shares.","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Tulipmania differed in one crucial aspect from the dot-com craze that grips our attention today: even at its height, the Amsterdam Stock Exchange, well-established in 1630, wouldn’t touch tulips.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是“郁金香泡沫破裂与高科技股泡沫破裂的影响差异”这一信息出现在哪一段。\n定位关键信息：题目中的核心词汇是“bubble burst impacts by tulip and by high-tech shares”，即“郁金香泡沫破裂与高科技股泡沫破裂的影响差异”。通过“bubble burst”和“high-tech shares”可以定位到文章中对比两类泡沫影响的句子。\n解题思路：在I段中，原文明确提到“Tulipmania differed in one crucial aspect from the dot-com craze”，即郁金香狂热与互联网泡沫在关键方面存在差异，随后具体解释了这种差异在于阿姆斯特丹证券交易所不参与郁金香交易，而高科技股泡沫则与之不同。这一内容直接对应题目所问的“两类泡沫破裂影响的差异”，因此答案为I段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"59702","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has 9 paragraphs A-I. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-l, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8180:59702:15","type":"choice","text":"15 Spread of tulip before 17th century.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Long before the first tulip bloomed in Europe – in Bavaria, it turns out, in 1559 – the flower had enchanted the Persians and bewitched the rulers of the Ottoman Empire.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是关于郁金香在17世纪之前的传播情况。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"before 17th century\"和\"Spread of tulip\"来定位，在D段中找到了\"Long before the first tulip bloomed in Europe\"和\"the flower had enchanted the Persians and bewitched the rulers of the Ottoman Empire\"，这两句话明确说明了郁金香在17世纪之前就已经传播到了欧洲以外的地区。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子，可以确定D段讲述了郁金香在17世纪之前的传播情况，包括在波斯和奥斯曼帝国的流行，以及在1559年首次在欧洲巴伐利亚绽放。因此，D段包含了题目所问的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"59702","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has 9 paragraphs A-I. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-l, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8180:59702:16","type":"choice","text":"16 Indication of money offered for the rare bulb in the 17th century.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Around 1624, the Amsterdam man who owned the only dozen specimens was offered 3,000 guilders for one bulb.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落提到了17世纪曾有人为稀有的郁金香球茎开出高价。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"money offered for the rare bulb in the 17th century\"定位，在B段第一句中找到了\"was offered 3,000 guilders for one bulb\"（提供3000基尔德购买一个球茎），明确提到了17世纪为稀有球茎提供的金钱数额。\n解题思路：B段第一句明确提到了1624年（17世纪），一位阿姆斯特丹的男子拥有的稀有球茎，有人要以3000基尔德购买，这与题目中\"money offered for the rare bulb in the 17th century\"完全吻合，因此答案为B。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"59702","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has 9 paragraphs A-I. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-l, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8180:59702:17","type":"choice","text":"17 Tulip was treated as money in Holland.","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1633, a farmhouse in Hoorn changed hands for three rare bulbs.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问“郁金香在荷兰被当作货币对待”，即郁金香具有货币的交换功能。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"Holland\"和\"money\"（货币）定位，在文章中寻找郁金香被当作交换媒介的描述。\n解题思路：原文G段提到\"1633年，在霍恩，一座农舍以三颗稀有郁金香球茎作为交换而转手\"，这表明当时人们直接用郁金香球茎作为购买农舍的支付手段，相当于用郁金香作为货币进行交易。因此G段包含郁金香被当作货币对待的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"59702","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has 9 paragraphs A-I. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-l, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8180:59702:18","type":"choice","text":"18 The comparison made between a tulip and other plants.","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘It is impossible to comprehend the tulip mania without understanding just how different tulips were from every other flower known to horticulturists in the 17th century,’ says Dash, ‘The colors they exhibited were more intense and more concentrated than those of ordinary plants.’\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段落包含了将郁金香与其他植物进行比较的信息。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"comparison\"和\"tulip and other plants\"可以定位到F段中描述郁金香颜色与其他植物进行比较的句子。\n解题思路：F段中明确提到了郁金香的颜色比其他植物更加鲜艳和浓烈，这是将郁金香与其他植物进行比较的具体描述，因此F段包含了题目所要求的比较信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"59702","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has 9 paragraphs A-I. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-l, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8180:59703:19","type":"choice","text":"In 1624, all the tulip collection belonged to a man in Amsterdam.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Around 1624, the Amsterdam man who owned the only dozen specimens was offered 3,000 guilders for one bulb.\n对应段落：B段\n审题： 题目判断“在1624年，所有的郁金香藏品都属于一个阿姆斯特丹人”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“1624”和“Amsterdam man”定位到B段第一句。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，大约在1624年，“那个拥有唯一一批（共12株）样本的阿姆斯特丹人”收到了对一个球茎的报价。这里的“the only dozen specimens”（唯一的一批样本）说明，在当时，这种特定的、极其珍贵的郁金香的所有已知个体（即所有藏品）都归此人所有。这与题目中“all the tulip collection belonged to a man”的陈述相符。因此，该陈述为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59703","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8180:59704:20","type":"choice","text":"Tulip was first planted in Holland according to this passage.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Long before the first tulip bloomed in Europe – in Bavaria, it turns out, in 1559 – the flower had enchanted the Persians and bewitched the rulers of the Ottoman Empire.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问“根据这篇文章，郁金香首先种植在荷兰”，需要判断这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：题目中的“first planted in Holland”是关键词，在文章中定位到D段提到“the passion for tulips found its most fertile ground in Holland”，但未明确说明“first planted”。\n解题思路：原文D段提到在1559年，巴伐利亚，第一朵郁金香出现，后来在波斯和奥斯曼帝国备受喜爱，但并未明确说明郁金香“首先”种植在荷兰。因此，题目中的“first planted”与原文信息不符，应选择False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59704","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8180:59705:21","type":"choice","text":"The popularity of Tulip in Holland was much higher than any other countries in the 17th century.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It was in Holland, however, that the passion for tulips found its most fertile ground, for reasons that had little to do with horticulture.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问“在17世纪，荷兰郁金香的受欢迎程度是否比任何其他国家都高”，这一说法是否与原文相符。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键词“Holland”、“17th century”、“popularity higher than any other countries”定位到D段，该段提到荷兰是郁金香热情最肥沃的土壤。\n解题思路：原文明确指出荷兰是郁金香最受欢迎的地方，虽然没有直接与其他国家比较“更高”，但“most fertile ground”暗示其受欢迎程度达到顶峰，可以理解为比其他国家更高。再者，根据上下文可知，郁金香狂热是发生在17世纪的荷兰，因此，题干与原文信息一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59705","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8180:59706:22","type":"choice","text":"Holland was the most wealthy country in the world in the 17th century.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Holland in the early 17th century was embarking on its Golden Age. Resources that had just a few years earlier gone toward fighting for independence from Spain now flowed into commerce. Amsterdam merchants were at the center of the lucrative East Indies trade, where a single voyage could yield profits of 400%. They displayed their success by erecting grand estates surrounded by flower gardens.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“荷兰在17世纪是否是世界上最富裕的国家”。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“Holland”、“17th century”、“most wealthy country in the world”等关键词定位答案在文章中的句子。\n解题思路：原文确实描述了17世纪初荷兰进入“黄金时代”，商业繁荣，来自东印度贸易的利润丰厚，商人建造豪宅显示其成功。这些信息都表明荷兰在当时非常富有和繁荣。然而，原文只描述了荷兰自身的繁荣，并未将其财富与其他国家进行比较。因此，题目中的信息在原文中没有明确给出，答案应为“NOT GIVEN”。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59706","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8180:59707:23","type":"choice","text":"From 1630, Amsterdam Stock Exchange started to regulate Tulips exchange market.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Tulipmania differed in one crucial aspect from the dot-com craze that grips our attention today: even at its height, the Amsterdam Stock Exchange, well-established in 1630, wouldn’t touch tulips.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问“从1630年开始，阿姆斯特丹证券交易所开始监管郁金香交易市场”是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键词\"1630\"、\"Amsterdam Stock Exchange\"和\"regulate Tulips exchange market\"定位到I段首句。\n解题思路：原文提到阿姆斯特丹证券交易所早在1630年就已建立，但明确表示它\"wouldn’t touch tulips\"（不会参与郁金香交易），而题目说它开始监管郁金香市场，这与原文完全相反。因此，题目陈述是错误的，答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59707","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage."},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8180:59708:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"fighting/Fighting","acceptedAnswers":["fighting","Fighting"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Resources that had just a few years earlier gone toward fighting for independence from Spain now flowed into commerce.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是在17世纪初，荷兰通过什么方式对抗西班牙以获得独立。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"17th century\"、\"independence from Spain\"和\"fighting\"，通过这些关键词可以定位到E段中提到荷兰为了独立对抗西班牙的句子。\n解题思路：原文中提到荷兰在早期为了对抗西班牙独立，花费了资源进行战斗。因此，答案为\"fighting\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59708","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8180:59709:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"commerce/Commerce","acceptedAnswers":["commerce","Commerce"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Resources that had just a few years earlier gone toward fighting for independence from Spain now flowed into commerce.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“因此，剩余资源进入了哪个领域”。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键词\"spare resources\"（剩余资源）和\"entered the area of\"（进入了...领域）来定位原文。在E段中找到\"Resources...now flowed into commerce.\"，这里的\"Resources\"对应\"spare resources\"，\"flowed into\"对应\"entered\"，\"commerce\"对应\"the area of\"。\n解题思路：原文明确提到资源从战争转向了商业，因此答案为\"commerce\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59709","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8180:59710:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"estates/Estates","acceptedAnswers":["estates","Estates"],"explanation":"原文答案句：They displayed their success by erecting grand estates surrounded by flower gardens.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是富裕的商人通过建造什么来展示他们的地位，并且这些建筑周围有花园。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"Prosperous traders\"、\"demonstrated their status\"、\"building great\"和\"gardens in surroundings\"来定位答案。\n解题思路：根据原文句子\"They displayed their success by erecting grand estates surrounded by flower gardens.\"，可以确定富裕的商人通过建造\"grand estates\"（宏伟的庄园）来展示他们的地位，并且这些庄园周围有花园。因此，答案为\"estates\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59710","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8180:59711:27","type":"fill","text":"填写第 27 空","answer":"flower lovers/Flower Lovers","acceptedAnswers":["flower lovers","Flower Lovers"],"explanation":"原文答案句：These ‘florists’, or professional tulip traders, sought out flower lovers and speculators alike.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是受到郁金香交易成功与利润的吸引，商人们不断寻找有意购买的什么和投机者。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"traders\"和\"speculator\"定位到F段，找到描述交易者寻找对象的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文F段中的句子\"professional tulip traders, sought out flower lovers and speculators alike\"，可以确定交易者寻找的对象是\"flower lovers\"，即花爱好者。题目中的\"27\"对应的是\"flower lovers\"这一群体。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59711","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59702","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has 9 paragraphs A-I. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-l, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>14</strong> Difference between bubble burst impacts by tulip and by high-tech shares. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"59703","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>In 1624, all the tulip collection belonged to a man in Amsterdam.</strong></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"59704","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Tulip was first planted in Holland according to this passage.</strong></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"59705","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>The popularity of Tulip in Holland was much higher than any other countries in the 17th century.</strong></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"59706","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>Holland was the most wealthy country in the world in the 17th century.</strong></p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"59707","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in passage? In boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet, write TURE if the statement is true, FALSE if the statement is false, NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage.","html":"<p><strong>From 1630, Amsterdam Stock Exchange started to regulate Tulips exchange market.</strong></p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"59708","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Dutch concentrated on gaining independence by <strong>24</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> against Spain in the early 17th\ncentury;</p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"59709","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>consequently, spare resources entered the area of <strong>25</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"59710","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Prosperous traders demonstrated their status by building great <strong>26 </strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong> and with gardens in surroundings.</p>","firstNumber":26},{"id":"59711","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24-27\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Attracted by the success of profit on tulip, traders kept looking for <strong>27</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[27] ____</strong> and speculator for sale.</p>","firstNumber":27}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>When the Tulip Bubble Burst&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Tulips are spring-blooming perennials that grow from bulbs. Depending on the species, tulip plants can grow as short as 4 inches (10 cm) or as high as 28 inches (71 cm). The tulip’s large flowers usually bloom on scapes or sub-scapose stems that lack bracts. Most tulips produce only one flower per stem, but a few species bear multiple flowers on their scapes (e.g. Tulipa turkestanica). The showy, generally cup or star-shaped tulip flower has three petals and three sepals, which are often termed tepals because they are nearly identical. These six tepals are often marked on the interior surface near the bases with darker colorings. Tulip flowers come in a wide variety of colors, except pure blue (several tulips with ‘blue’ in the name have a faint violet hue).</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Long before anyone ever heard of Qualcomm, CMGI, Cisco Systems, or the other high-tech stocks that have soared during the current bull market, there was Semper Augustus. Both more prosaic and more subline than any stock or bond, it was a tulip of extraordinary beauty, its midnight-blue petals topped by a band of pure white and accented with crimson flares. To denizens of 17th century Holland, little was as desirable.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Around 1624, the Amsterdam man who owned the only dozen specimens was offered 3,000 guilders for one bulb. While there’s no accurate way to render that in today’s greenbacks, the sum was roughly equal to the annual income of a wealthy merchant. A few years later, Rembrandt received about half that amount for painting The Night Watch. Yet the bulb’s owner, whose name is now lost to history, nixed the offer.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Who was crazier, the tulip lover who refused to sell for a small fortune or the one who was willing to splurge. That’s a question that springs to mind after reading Tulipmania: The Story of the World’s Most Coveted Flower and the Extraordinary Passions It Aroused by British journalist Mike Dash. In recent years, as investors have intentionally forgotten everything they learned in Investing 101 in order to load up on unproven, unprofitable dot-com issues, tulip mania has been invoked frequently. In this concise, artfully written account, Dash tells the real history behind the buzzword and in doing so, offers a cautionary late for our times.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The Dutch were not the first to go gaga over the tulip. Long before the first tulip bloomed in Europe – in Bavaria, it turns out, in 1559 – the flower had enchanted the Persians and bewitched the rulers of the Ottoman Empire. It was in Holland, however, that the passion for tulips found its most fertile ground, for reasons that had little to do with horticulture.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Holland in the early 17th century was embarking on its Golden Age. Resources that had just a few years earlier gone toward fighting for independence from Spain now flowed into commerce. Amsterdam merchants were at the center of the lucrative East Indies trade, where a single voyage could yield profits of 400%. They displayed their success by erecting grand estates surrounded by flower gardens. The Dutch population seemed torn by two contradictory impulses: a horror of living beyond one’s means and the love of a long shot.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Enter the tulip. ‘It is impossible to comprehend the tulip mania without understanding just how different tulips were from every other flower known to horticulturists in the 17th century,’ says Dash, ‘The colors they exhibited were more intense and more concentrated than those of ordinary plants.’ Despite the outlandish prices commanded by rare bulbs, ordinary tulips were sold by the pound. Around 1630, however, a new type of tulip fancier appeared, lured by tales of fat profits. These ‘florists’, or professional tulip traders, sought out flower lovers and speculators alike. But if the supply of tulip buyers grew quickly, the supply of bulbs did not. The tulip was a conspirator in the supply squeeze: It takes seven years to grow one from seed. And while bulbs can produce two or three clones, or ‘offsets’, annually, the mother bulb only lasts a few years.</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Bulb prices rose steadily throughout the 1630s, as ever more speculators wedged into the market. Weavers and farmers mortgaged whatever they could to raise cash to begin trading. In 1633, a farmhouse in Hoorn changed hands for three rare bulbs. By 1636 any tulip-even bulbs recently considered garbage – could be sold off, often for hundreds of guilders. A futures market for bulbs existed, and tulip traders could be found conducting their business in hundreds of Dutch taverns. Tulipmania reached its peak during the winter of 1636-37 when some bulbs were changing hands ten times in a day. The zenith came early that winter, at an auction to benefit seven orphans whose only asset was 70 fine tulips left by their father. One, a rare Violetten Admirael van Enkhuizen bulb that was about to split in two, sold for 5,200 guilders, the all-time record. All told, the flowers brought in nearly 53,000 guilders.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Soon after, the tulip market crashed utterly, spectacularly. It began in Haarlem, at a routine bulb auction when, for the first time, the greater fool refused to show up and pay. Within days, the panic had spread across the country. Despite the efforts of traders to prop up demand, the market for tulips evaporated. Flowers that had commanded 5,000 guilders a few weeks before now fetched one-hundredth that amount. Tulipmania is not without flaws. Dash dwells too long on the tulip’s migration from Asia to Holland. But he does a service with this illuminating, accessible account of incredible financial folly.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Tulipmania differed in one crucial aspect from the dot-com craze that grips our attention today: even at its height, the Amsterdam Stock Exchange, well-established in 1630, wouldn’t touch tulips. ‘The speculation in tulip bulbs always existed at the margins of Dutch economic life,’ Dash writes. After the market crashed, a compromise was brokered that let most traders settle their debts for a fraction of their liability. The overall fallout on the Dutch economy was negligible. Will we say the same when Wall Street’s current obsession finally runs its course?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8180&scene=%E8%B4%A2%E7%BB%8F%E5%95%86%E4%B8%9A&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8181","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Extinct: The Giant Deer","book":"阅读还原集Vol.12","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.12 · Test 4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8181:59718:28","type":"fill","text":"填写第 28 空","answer":"400,000 years ago/400,000 Years Ago","acceptedAnswers":["400,000 years ago","400,000 Years Ago"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The Irish elk, so-called because its well-preserved remains are often found in lake sediments under peat bogs in Ireland, first appeared about 400,000 years ago in Europe and Central Asia.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是爱尔兰麋鹿的遗骸最初被发现的大致时间。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Europe and Central Asia\"和\"preserved well\"定位到B段第一句，该句提到了爱尔兰麋鹿首次出现的时间。\n解题思路：根据原文中\"first appeared about 400,000 years ago in Europe and Central Asia\"可以确定答案为\"400,000 years ago\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59718","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8181:59719:29","type":"fill","text":"填写第 29 空","answer":"8,000 years ago/8,000 Years Ago","acceptedAnswers":["8,000 years ago","8,000 Years Ago"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘The eastern foothills of the Urals became very densely forested about 8,000 years ago, which could have pushed them on to the plain,’ he said.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是在什么时间点，巨型鹿被迫从乌拉尔山脉迁移到平原，并且狩猎被认为是导致爱尔兰麋鹿灭绝的重要因素之一。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Ural Mountains\"和\"plain\"可以定位到C段中描述乌拉尔山脉东部山麓变得非常茂密的句子。\n解题思路：根据C段中的句子，可以确定大约在8000年前，乌拉尔山脉的东部山麓变得非常茂密，这可能将巨型鹿推向平原。同时，D段提到狩猎被认为是导致爱尔兰麋鹿灭绝的重要因素之一，因此可以确定答案为\"8000 years ago\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59719","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8181:59720:30","type":"fill","text":"填写第 30 空","answer":"7,000 years ago/7,000 Years Ago","acceptedAnswers":["7,000 years ago","7,000 Years Ago"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Lister said, ‘We haven’t got just hunting 7,000 years ago – this was also about the time the first Neolithic people settled in the region. They were farmers who would have cleared the land.’\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是人们在什么时间开始狩猎，而爱尔兰麋鹿过去曾经历过各种气候波动。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"hunting\"和\"climatic fluctuations\"定位到D段，其中提到了狩猎和气候波动。\n解题思路：根据D段中的原文句子，可以确定人们在7000年前开始狩猎，而这也是新石器时代人们首次在该地区定居的时间。因此，答案为\"7000 years ago\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59720","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8181:59721:31","type":"fill","text":"填写第 31 空","answer":"wooded interglacials/Wooded Interglacials","acceptedAnswers":["wooded interglacials","Wooded Interglacials"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But, Lister said, ‘That’s a hard argument to make because the deer previously survived perfectly well through wooded interglacials [warmer periods between ice ages].’\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是爱尔兰麋鹿在什么样的时期中生存得很好，它们巨大的角是其灭绝原因的这种说法存疑。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"live pleasantly over the span of\"对应原文中的\"survived perfectly well through\"。\n解题思路：原文E段提到，Lister质疑巨大角导致爱尔兰麋鹿灭绝的说法，原因是这种麋鹿之前在森林间冰期\"wooded interglacials\"（冰期之间的温暖期，且森林茂密）中生存得很好。因此答案为\"wooded interglacials\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59721","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8181:59722:32","type":"fill","text":"填写第 32 空","answer":"10500 years/10500 Years","acceptedAnswers":["10500 years","10500 Years"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Toothed cats, mastodons, giant sloths, woolly rhinos, and many other big, shaggy mammals are widely thought to have died out around the end of the last ice age, some 10,500 years ago.\n对应段落：题记\n审题：题目问的是在最后一次冰河时代的末期，哺乳动物大约在什么时候灭绝。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的单词\"last maximum ice age\"和\"mammals become extinct\"来定位原文中的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子\"Toothed cats, mastodons, giant sloths, woolly rhinos, and many other big, shaggy mammals are widely thought to have died out around the end of the last ice age, some 10,500 years ago.\"可以确定，哺乳动物在最后一次冰河时代的末期大约在10,500年前灭绝。因此，答案是10500 years。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59722","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8181:59723:33","type":"fill","text":"填写第 33 空","answer":"Male's huge antlers/male's huge antlers","acceptedAnswers":["Male's huge antlers","male's huge antlers"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Some scientists have suggested this exaggerated feature – the result of females preferring stags with the largest antlers, possibly because they advertised a male’s fitness – contributed to the mammal’s downfall. They say such antlers would have been a serious inconvenience in the dense forests that spread northward after the last ice age.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是爱尔兰麋鹿最终灭绝的物理特征是什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"physical characteristics\"和\"extinction of Irish elk\"定位到文章中描述爱尔兰麋鹿灭绝原因的部分。在E段中，作者提到了关于雄性巨大鹿角的讨论。\n解题思路：在E段中，作者提到一些科学家认为雄性巨大的鹿角可能是导致爱尔兰麋鹿灭绝的原因。这些鹿角在冰河时代后的茂密森林中可能会造成不便。因此，根据原文信息，可以确定题目答案为\"Male's huge antlers\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59723","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-35\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND / OR NUMBERS from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8181:59724:34","type":"fill","text":"填写第 34 空","answer":"minerals/Minerals","acceptedAnswers":["minerals","Minerals"],"explanation":"原文答案句：High amounts of calcium and phosphate compounds are required to form antlers, and therefore large quantities of these minerals are required for the massive structures of the Irish Elk.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问爱尔兰麋鹿维持其巨大鹿角所需的营养物质。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"maintaining the huge size of Irish elk\"和\"nutrient substance\"在文章中定位。在E段中找到提到爱尔兰麋鹿巨大体型所需的物质。\n解题思路：原文明确提到形成巨大鹿角需要大量的\"minerals\"（矿物质），并且这些矿物质对于爱尔兰麋鹿的巨大结构是必需的。题目问的是维持巨大体型所需的营养物质，因此直接对应原文中的\"minerals\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59724","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-35\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND / OR NUMBERS from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8181:59725:35","type":"fill","text":"填写第 35 空","answer":"habitat destruction/Habitat Destruction","acceptedAnswers":["habitat destruction","Habitat Destruction"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The team, though, said their new date for the Irish elk’s extinction hints at an additional human-made problem – habitat destruction.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“什么证据表明，人类的到来导致了爱尔兰麋鹿的灭绝？”\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"geographical evidence\"、\"advent of human\"和\"extinction of Irish elk\"定位到D段，该段提到研究团队认为爱尔兰麋鹿灭绝的新日期暗示了一个额外的人为问题。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到\"habitat destruction\"（栖息地破坏）是研究团队提出的一个额外人为问题，这与题目中询问的证据相吻合。因此，\"habitat destruction\"是正确答案。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59725","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-35\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND / OR NUMBERS from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8181:59726:36","type":"choice","text":"36 the continents where humans imposed a little impact on large mammals extinction","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Some animals may have survived until about 7,000 years ago. If people have been in Australia for up to 60,000 years, then megafauna must have co-existed with humans for at least 30,000 years. Regularly hunted modern kangaroos survived not only 10,000 years of Aboriginal hunting, but also an onslaught of commercial shooters.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“人类对大型哺乳动物灭绝影响较小的大洲”，需要找出文章中提到人类影响较小或几乎没有影响的地区。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“humans imposed a little impact on large mammals extinction”可以定位到F段中提到非洲和热带亚洲没有发生大规模动物灭绝，而澳大利亚虽然经历了气候变化，但大型动物与人类共存了很长时间，人类的影响相对较小。\n解题思路：原文中F段后半部分描述了澳大利亚的情况，虽然气候发生了变化，但大型动物与人类共存了很长时间，人类的影响相对较小。因此，澳大利亚是人类对大型哺乳动物灭绝影响较小的洲。","options":["Eurasia","Australia","Asia","Africa"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59726","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-39\nChoose the letter A-D and write your answers in boxes 36-39 on your answer sheet.\nA Eurasia\nB Australia\nC Asia\nD Africa"},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8181:59726:37","type":"choice","text":"37 the continents where the climatic change was mild and fauna remains","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Significantly, Africa escaped major faunal extinction as did tropical and sub-tropical Asia.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是气候变化温和且动物群保持完整的洲。\n定位关键信息：根据题目的关键词\"climatic change was mild\"和\"fauna remains\"定位到F段，找到描述气候变化温和且动物群保持完整的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到\"Significantly, Africa escaped major faunal extinction as did tropical and sub-tropical Asia\"，说明非洲和热带及处于亚热带地区的亚洲的气候变化较为温和，且动物群得以保持完整。因此，答案为D。","options":["Eurasia","Australia","Asia","Africa"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59726","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-39\nChoose the letter A-D and write your answers in boxes 36-39 on your answer sheet.\nA Eurasia\nB Australia\nC Asia\nD Africa"},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8181:59726:38","type":"choice","text":"38 the continents where both humans and climatic change are the causes","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Again, as animals come through to the last part of the cold stage, here there’s a fundamental change in the climate, reorganization of vegetation, and the combination of the climatic change and the presence of humans – of advanced Paleolithic humans – causes this wave of extinction.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求从四个大洲中选择一个，该大洲的巨型动物灭绝被证实是由人类和气候变化共同导致的。\n定位关键信息： 使用 \"humans and climatic change are the causes\" 作为关键词，定位文中明确将两者共同作用列为灭绝原因的段落。\n解题思路：题目要求找出一个具体的大洲，其巨型动物灭绝是由“人类和气候变化共同造成的”。在段落G中，科学家A.J. Stuart的研究团队专注于“northern Eurasia”（北欧亚大陆，即欧洲加上西伯利亚）。该段明确指出，在最后一次冰期阶段末期，发生了根本性的气候变化和植被重组，而“气候变化和人类（先进的旧石器时代人类）的共同作用，导致了这波灭绝浪潮”。这直接对应了题目中“人类和气候变化都是原因”的描述。因此，对应的大洲是“Eurasia”，答案为A。","options":["Eurasia","Australia","Asia","Africa"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59726","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-39\nChoose the letter A-D and write your answers in boxes 36-39 on your answer sheet.\nA Eurasia\nB Australia\nC Asia\nD Africa"},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8181:59726:39","type":"choice","text":"39 the continents where the climatic change along caused a massive extinction","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It is believed that megafauna initially came into existence in response to glacial conditions and became extinct with the onset of warmer climates. Tropical and subtropical areas have experienced less radical climatic change. Significantly, Africa escaped major faunal extinction as did tropical and sub-tropical Asia.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是哪些大陆仅因气候变化导致了大规模灭绝。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"climatic change\"和\"massive extinction\"定位到F段，该段提到大型动物群（megafauna）的灭绝与气候变化有关。\n解题思路：文章前半部分提供了一个具体案例：爱尔兰麋鹿最初出现在欧洲和中亚地区，的最后灭绝地点是在西西伯利亚，西西伯利亚在地理上属于亚洲。段落F在总结气候变化时，明确将亚洲（与非洲一起）归类，没有大规模的动物群灭绝，并没有到亚洲地区出现的灭绝现象是由人为或者除气候以外的其他因素造成，这强烈暗示在作者看来，亚洲的灭绝主因或唯一原因被认为是气候变化。因此，选C。","options":["Eurasia","Australia","Asia","Africa"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59726","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-39\nChoose the letter A-D and write your answers in boxes 36-39 on your answer sheet.\nA Eurasia\nB Australia\nC Asia\nD Africa"},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8181:59727:40","type":"choice","text":"Which statement is true according to the Stuart team’s finding?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：There’s no obvious coincidence between the arrival of humans or climatic change alone and these extinctions. There’s a climatic change here, so there’s a double effect here. Again, as animals come through to the last part of the cold stage, here there’s a fundamental change in the climate, reorganization of vegetation, and the combination of the climatic change and the presence of humans – of advanced Paleolithic humans – causes this wave of extinction.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问根据Stuart团队的研究发现，哪个陈述是正确的。\n定位关键信息：题目中关键词\"Stuart team’s finding\"指向G段，因为G段明确提到\"the group of scientists led by A.J. Stuart\"。\n解题思路：G段中Stuart团队的研究指出，欧洲大型动物灭绝的原因是\"climatic change\"和\"the presence of humans\"的双重作用，而非单一因素（\"no obvious coincidence between...climatic change alone and these extinctions\"）。选项C\"climatic change was not solely responsible for the megafauna extinction in Europe\"与此完全一致，说明气候变化并非唯一原因。其他选项均与原文表述不符：A项未提及尼安德特人的作用；B项错误，原文强调人类和气候变化的共同作用；D项将灭绝归因于气候变化，与原文的\"双重因素\"矛盾。因此C正确。","options":["Neanderthals rather than modern humans caused the extinction in Europe.","Paleolithic humans in Europe along kill the big animals such as Giant deer.","Climatic change was not solely responsible for the megafauna extinction in Europe.","Moderate and staggered extinction was mainly the result of fundamental climatic change."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59727","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, D. Write your answer in box 40 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59718","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Having been preserved well in Europe and Central Asia, the remains of the Irish elk was initially\nfound approximately <strong>28</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[28] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"59719","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Around <strong>29</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[29] ____</strong> , they were driven to live in the plain after being restricted to the Ural Mountains. Hunting was considered as one of the important factors of Irish elk’s extinction,</p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"59720","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>people have not started hunting until <strong>30</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[30] ____</strong> when Irish elk used to get through under a variety of climatic fluctuations.</p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"59721","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The huge antlers may possibly contribute to the reason why Irish elk extinct, which was highly controversial as they live pleasantly over the span of <strong>31</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[31] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"59722","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Generally, it is well-known that, at the last maximum ice age, mammals become extinct about <strong>32</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[32] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"59723","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-35\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND / OR NUMBERS from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>33</strong> What kind of physical characteristics eventually contributed to the extinction of Irish elk? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[33] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"59724","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-35\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND / OR NUMBERS from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>34</strong> What kind of nutrient substance needed in maintaining the huge size of Irish elk? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[34] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"59725","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 33-35\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND / OR NUMBERS from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>35</strong> What geographical evidence suggested the advent of human resulted in the extinction of Irish elk? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[35] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"59726","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 36-39\nChoose the letter A-D and write your answers in boxes 36-39 on your answer sheet.\nA Eurasia\nB Australia\nC Asia\nD Africa","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> Eurasia&nbsp;</p><p><strong>B</strong> Australia&nbsp;</p><p><strong>C</strong> Asia&nbsp;</p><p><strong>D</strong> Africa&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-top: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>36</strong> the continents where humans imposed a little impact on large mammals extinction <strong class=\"source-blank\">[36] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"59727","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question 40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C, D. Write your answer in box 40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Which statement is true according to the Stuart team’s finding?</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Extinct: The Giant Deer&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">Toothed cats, mastodons, giant sloths, woolly rhinos, and many other big, shaggy mammals are widely thought to have died out around the end of the last ice age, some 10,500 years ago.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The Irish elk is also known as the giant deer (Megaloceros giganteus). Analysis of ancient bones and teeth by scientists based in Britain and Russia show the huge herbivore survived until about 5,000 B.C. – more than three millennia later than previously believed. The research team says this suggests additional factors, besides climate change, probably hastened the giant deer’s eventual extinction. The factors could include hunting or habitat destruction by humans.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The Irish elk, so-called because its well-preserved remains are often found in lake sediments under peat bogs in Ireland, first appeared about 400,000 years ago in Europe and Central Asia. Through a combination of radiocarbon dating of skeletal remains and the mapping of locations where the remains were unearthed, the team shows the Irish elk was widespread across Europe before the last ‘big freeze.’ The deer’s range later contracted to the Ural Mountains, in modern-day Russia, which separate Europe from Asia.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The giant deer made its last stand in western Siberia, some 3,000 years after the ice sheets receded, said the study’s co-author, Adrian Lister, professor of palaeobiology at University College London, England. ‘The eastern foothills of the Urals became very densely forested about 8,000 years ago, which could have pushed them on to the plain,’ he said. He added that pollen analysis indicates the region then became very dry in response to further climatic change, leading to the loss of important food plants. ‘In combination with human pressures, this could have finally snuffed them out,’ Lister said.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Hunting by humans has often been put forward as a contributory cause of extinction of the Pleistocene megafauna. The team, though, said their new date for the Irish elk’s extinction hints at an additional human-made problem – habitat destruction. Lister said, ‘We haven’t got just hunting 7,000 years ago – this was also about the time the first Neolithic people settled in the region. They were farmers who would have cleared the land.’ The presence of humans may help explain why the Irish elk was unable to tough out the latest of many climatic fluctuations – periods it had survived in the past.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Meanwhile, Lister cast doubt on another possible explanation for the deer’s demise – the male’s huge antlers. Some scientists have suggested this exaggerated feature – the result of females preferring stags with the largest antlers, possibly because they advertised a male’s fitness – contributed to the mammal’s downfall. They say such antlers would have been a serious inconvenience in the dense forests that spread northward after the last ice age. But, Lister said, ‘That’s a hard argument to make because the deer previously survived perfectly well through wooded interglacials [warmer periods between ice ages].’ Some research has suggested that a lack of sufficient high-quality forage caused the extinction of the elk. High amounts of calcium and phosphate compounds are required to form antlers, and therefore large quantities of these minerals are required for the massive structures of the Irish Elk. The males (and male deer in general) met this requirement partly from their bones, replenishing them from food plants after the antlers were grown or reclaiming the nutrients from discarded antlers (as has been observed in extant deer). Thus, in the antler growth phase, Giant Deer was suffering from a condition similar to osteoporosis. When the climate changed at the end of the last glacial period, the vegetation in the animal’s habitat also changed towards species that presumably could not deliver sufficient amounts of the required minerals, at least in the western part of its range.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The extinction of megafauna around the world was almost completed by the end of the last ice age. It is believed that megafauna initially came into existence in response to glacial conditions and became extinct with the onset of warmer climates. Tropical and subtropical areas have experienced less radical climatic change. The most dramatic of these changes was the transformation of a vast area of North Africa into the world’s largest desert. Significantly, Africa escaped major faunal extinction as did tropical and sub-tropical Asia. The human exodus from Africa and our entrance into the Americas and Australia were also accompanied by climate change. Australia’s climate changed from cold-dry to warm-dry. As a result, surface water became scarce. Most inland lakes became completely dry or dry in the warmer seasons. Most large, predominantly browsing animals lost their habitat and retreated to a narrow band in eastern Australia, where there were permanent water and better vegetation. Some animals may have survived until about 7,000 years ago. If people have been in Australia for up to 60,000 years, then megafauna must have co-existed with humans for at least 30,000 years. Regularly hunted modern kangaroos survived not only 10,000 years of Aboriginal hunting, but also an onslaught of commercial shooters.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The group of scientists led by A.J. Stuart focused on northern Eurasia, which he was taking as Europe, plus Siberia, essentially, where they’ve got the best data that animals became extinct in Europe during the Late Pleistocene. Some cold-adapted animals, go through into the last part of the cold stage and then become extinct up there. So you’ve actually got two phases of extinction. Now, neither of these coincide – these are Neanderthals here being replaced by modern humans. There’s no obvious coincidence between the arrival of humans or climatic change alone and these extinctions. There’s a climatic change here, so there’s a double effect here. Again, as animals come through to the last part of the cold stage, here there’s a fundamental change in the climate, reorganization of vegetation, and the combination of the climatic change and the presence of humans – of advanced Paleolithic humans – causes this wave of extinction. There’s a profound difference between the North American data and that of Europe, which summarize that the extinctions in northern Eurasia, in Europe, are moderate and staggered, and in North America severe and sudden. And these things relate to the differences in the timing of human arrival. The extinction follows from human predation, but only at times of fundamental changes in the environment.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8181&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8149","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 LONGAEVA:  Ancient Bristlecone Pine","book":"阅读还原集Vol.12","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.12 · Test 3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8149:64120:1","type":"choice","text":"1 Human activity threats bristlecone pines habitat.","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Almost 30,000 acres of National Forest now preserves the ancient bristlecone, but paved roads, campsites, and self-guided trails have led only to more human impact.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段落提到了人类活动威胁到了狐尾松的栖息地。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"Human activity threats bristlecone pines habitat\"可以定位到I段中的\"paved roads, campsites, and self-guided trails have led only to more human impact\"这句话，这句话明确提到了人类活动对bristlecone pines的影响。\n解题思路：根据原文中I段的句子，如今近3万英亩的国家森林保护区虽守护着这些古老树种，但铺砌的道路、露营地和自助步道却加剧了人类活动的影响。可以确定，I段提到了人类活动对狐尾松的栖息地造成了威胁，因此答案为I。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64120","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe reading passage has 9 paragraphs A-I. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-l, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8149:64120:2","type":"choice","text":"2 Explanations for a ring of bristlecone pines","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：With every strenuous year that passes in the While Mountains, each bristlecone grows and forms a new outer layer of cambium that reflects a season’s particular ease or hardship. So while growing seasons may expand or shrink, the trees carry on, their growth rings faithfully recording the bad years alongside the goods.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是关于\"狐尾松的年轮的解释\"，需要找到段落中解释年轮形成或作用的句子。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"ring\"和\"bristlecone pines\"定位到C段，该段明确提到年轮的作用。\n解题思路：C段提到，在怀特山脉，每经历一个严酷的生长季，每棵狐尾松都会形成新的外层形成层，记录下当年的气候状况。尽管生长季时有时无，但这些树木始终顽强生长，年轮如同忠实的记录者，将坏年份和好年份都完整留存。这句话直接解释了年轮的形成和作用，因此C段包含了关于狐尾松年轮的解释。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64120","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe reading passage has 9 paragraphs A-I. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-l, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8149:64120:3","type":"choice","text":"3 An accountable recording provided from the past until now","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：As our global climate continues to undergo its most recent and abrupt atmospheric change, these ancient scribes continue to respond. Since, the rings of wood formed each year reveal the trees’ response to climatic conditions during a particular growing season, in their persistence they have left us natural recordings of the past, markers of the present, and clues to the future.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落包含了提供从过去到现在的可靠记录的信息。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"an accountable recording provided from the past until now\"可以定位到D段中的\"natural recordings of the past, markers of the present, and clues to the future\"，这与题目所问的内容吻合。\n解题思路：D段明确提到了狐尾松作为\"ancient scribes\"（古代记录者）的作用，树木每年形成的年轮，记录着它们在特定生长季对气候条件的反应，为我们留下了自然的过往见证、当下的印记以及未来的线索。这与题目中\"an accountable recording provided from the past until now\"的描述完全一致。因此，D段包含了题目所问的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64120","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe reading passage has 9 paragraphs A-I. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-l, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8149:64120:4","type":"choice","text":"4 Survived in a hostile environment","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The bristlecone pine (Pinus longaeva), of the White Mountains in California, has served this purpose greater than any other species of tree on the planet. Conditions here are brutal: scant precipitation and low average temperatures mean a short growing season, only intensified by ferocious wind and mal-nutritious rocky.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“在恶劣环境中生存”的相关信息出现在哪一段。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"Survived in a hostile environment\"（在恶劣环境中生存）定位。在A段中找到描述环境恶劣的句子\"Conditions here are brutal: scant precipitation and low average temperatures mean a short growing season, only intensified by ferocious wind and mal-nutritious rocky.\"。\n解题思路：A段首先指出了狐尾松对自然历史研究的重要性，接着提到它的生存环境恶劣，降水稀少、年均气温偏低导致生长季短暂，再加上狂风肆虐、土壤贫瘠的岩石环境，更让情况雪上加霜。因此，A段包含了关于松树在恶劣环境中生存种的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"64120","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe reading passage has 9 paragraphs A-I. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-l, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8149:64121:5","type":"choice","text":"According to paragraph A, what aspect of bristlecone pines attracts author's attention?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句Results of extensive studies on bristlecone pine stands have shown that in fact such, environmental limitations are positively associated with the attainment of great age. This intriguing phenomenon will be discussed further on.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问根据A段，狐尾松的哪个方面引起了作者的注意。\n定位关键信息：利用题干定位到A段，重点阅读段落首句和末句。\n解题思路：A段首句提到人类通过自然环境了解过去，接着指出了狐尾松对自然历史研究的重要性，接着提到它的生存环境恶劣，然后说，大量研究证实，恶劣环境恰恰是这些树木获得长寿的关键因素。这个耐人寻味的现象将在下文展开深入探讨。说明是狐尾松的长寿引起了作者的关注。结合选项，B项\"Remarkable long age\"是狐尾松突出的特点，与原文中\"longaeva\"（长寿）和\"oldest living trees\"的描述一致，因此B为正确答案。","options":["Brutal environment they live","Remarkable long age","They only live in California.","Outstanding height"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64121","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5-7\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 5-7 on your answer sheet"},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8149:64122:6","type":"choice","text":"Why do we investigate Bristlecone pines in higher altitudes of California's the White Mountains?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Within this natural range, the oldest and most widely researched stands of bristlecones occur in California’s the White Mountains.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问为什么我们在加州白山的高海拔地区研究狐尾松。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"California’s the White Mountains\"和\"investigate\"定位到G段，找到提到该地区是\"oldest and most widely researched stands of bristlecones\"的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确指出，在狐尾松的自然分布区内，在加州白山地区有最古老且研究最广泛的松树群落，这直接回答了题目问的研究原因。选项A中的\"oldest ones researched in this region\"与原文表述完全一致，因此A是正确答案。选项B提到\"bizarre ones\"，原文并未提及松树的奇特特性，故排除。","options":["Because of the oldest ones researched in this region","Because most bizarre ones are in this region","Because precipitation is rich in this region","Because sea level is comparatively high in this region"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64122","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5-7\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 5-7 on your answer sheet"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8149:64123:7","type":"choice","text":"Why there are repeated patterns of wide and narrow rings?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：What makes this record so special to dendrochronologists, too, is that, nowhere, throughout time, is precisely the same long-term sequence of wide and narrow rings repeated, because year-to-year variations in climate are never exactly the same.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问为什么会出现宽窄相间的相似环状图案。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"repeated patterns of wide and narrow rings\"定位到H段最后一句。\n解题思路：原文中提到，对于树轮年代学家来说，这一记录之所以特别，是因为在整个历史中，从来没有哪一段时期的树轮宽窄排列能完全重复。原因是每年的气候变化都不可能一模一样。由此可知，年轮模式的差异是由于气候年际变化的不同导致的。选项D与原文描述一致，因此选择D。","options":["Because sea level rises which affect tree ring","Because tree ring pattern is completely random","Because ancient organisms affect their growth","Because the variation of climate change is different"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"64123","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5-7\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 5-7 on your answer sheet"},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8149:64124:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"energy/Energy","acceptedAnswers":["energy","Energy"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This adaptation helps the bristlecone photosynthesize during particularly brutal months. Saving the energy of constant needle replacement and providing a stable supply of chlorophyll.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是狐尾松的独特的适应方式对有助于光合作用，并保留更换树叶的什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"photosynthesizing\"和\"reserving\"定位到E段，该段提到狐尾松的独特的适应方式有助于光合作用，并提到\"Saving the energy\"。\n解题思路：根据原文句子，这种适应性使狐尾松能在极端恶劣的月份进行光合作用，既节省了频繁更换针叶的能量，又确保了叶绿素的稳定供应。因此答案为\"energy\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64124","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8149:64124:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"stratification/Stratification","acceptedAnswers":["stratification","Stratification"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For a plant trying to store so much energy, bristlecone seeds are relatively large in size. They are first reproduced when trees reach ages between thirty and seventy-five years old. Germination rates are generally high, in part because seeds require little to no initial stratification.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是狐尾松的独特的适应方式，这可能是因为种子主要依赖的不是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"seeds \"和上面提到的\"special adaptation\"定位到E段，该段提到狐尾松的独特的适应方式。\n解题思路：根据原文句子，狐尾松种子的体积相对较大。它们首次繁殖发生在树龄30至75年之间，发芽率通常较高，部分原因是种子几乎不需要或完全不需要初始层积处理。说明种子主要依赖的不是初始层积。因此答案为\"stratification\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64124","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8149:64124:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"(bands of) bark/(Bands of) Bark","acceptedAnswers":["(bands of) bark","bands of bark","bark","(Bands of) Bark","Bands of Bark","Bark"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This condition occurs as a result of cambium dieback, which erodes and thereby exposes certain areas of the bole, leaving only narrow bands of bark intact.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求完成关于狐尾松特殊适应性的摘要，由于形成层枯死，只有狭窄的什么部分保持完整。\n定位关键信息：题目中提到的关键词是“cambium dieback”和“narrow”，需要根据这些关键词在文章中定位答案。\n解题思路：段落E中，原文提到，这种现象源于形成层的退化，导致树干某些区域被侵蚀，仅留下狭窄的完整树皮带。因此，空格处应填入“bands of bark”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64124","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8149:64124:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"(dry mountain) air/(Dry Mountain) Air","acceptedAnswers":["(dry mountain) air","dry mountain air","air","(Dry Mountain) Air","Dry Mountain Air","Air"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Combined with the dry, windy, and often freezing mountain air, slow growth guarantees the bristlecones tight, fibrous rings with a high resin content and structural strength.\n对应段落：F段\n审题： 题目要求完成摘要，由于多风、寒冷的气候和什么等因素，狐尾松的年轮结构紧密坚固且富含树脂。\n定位关键信息： 使用 \"windy, cold climate\", \"rings have a tight and solid structure\", \"resin\" 定位到文中解释年轮结构成因的句子。\n解题思路：段落F中，原文将“干燥、多风且常冰冻的山间空气”与“缓慢的生长”共同列为导致年轮结构紧密坚固的原因。题目中已给出“多风、寒冷的气候”，因此需要填入与之并列的另一个因素“dry mountain) air”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64124","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8149:64124:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"ground cover/Ground Cover","acceptedAnswers":["ground cover","Ground Cover"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Due to a lack of ground cover vegetation and an evenly spaced layout, bristlecone stands on the White Mountain peaks have been practically unaffected by the fire.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求完成摘要，狐尾松林能免于火灾是因为该地区几乎没有什么植物分布。\n定位关键信息：使用 \"safe from the fire\", \"little\", \"plants spread\" 定位到文中解释狐尾松林免于火灾原因的句子。\n解题思路：段落F中，原文明确指出“由于缺乏地被植物，且狐尾松分布均匀，怀特山峰上的狐尾松林几乎未受火灾影响”。因此，空格处应填入“ground cover”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64124","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8149:64124:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"distance/Distance","acceptedAnswers":["distance","Distance"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The peaks south of the Owens Valley, are higher up than they might appear from a distance.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是Owens Valley的实际高度，比从哪个角度观察的更高。\n定位关键信息： 使用 \"summits of Owens Valley\", \"higher than they emerge\", \"observe from\" 定位到文中描述山峰视觉高度的句子。\n解题思路：段落G中，原文明确写道“欧文斯谷南部的山峰，比它们从远处看起来要高”。因此，空格处应填入“distance”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"64124","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":3}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"64120","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe reading passage has 9 paragraphs A-I. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-l, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>1</strong> Human activity threats bristlecone pines habitat. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"64121","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5-7\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 5-7 on your answer sheet","html":"<p><strong>According to paragraph A, what aspect of bristlecone pines attracts author&#39;s attention?</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"64122","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5-7\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 5-7 on your answer sheet","html":"<p><strong>Why do we investigate Bristlecone pines in higher altitudes of California&#39;s the White Mountains?</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"64123","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5-7\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write your answers in boxes 5-7 on your answer sheet","html":"<p><strong>Why there are repeated patterns of wide and narrow rings?</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"64124","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nComplete the summary below. Using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The bristlecone&#39;s special adaptation is a benefit for photosynthesizing, and reserving the<strong> 8</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">of leave replacement and providing sufficient chlorophyll. Probably because seeds do not rely on primary&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">9</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong> ,&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">Germination rate is high. Because of cambium dieback, only narrow&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">10</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">remain complete. Due to multiple factors such as windy, cold climate and&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">11</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong> ,&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">bristlecones&#39; rings have a tight and solid structure full of resin. Moreover, bristlecone stands are safe from the fire because of little&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">12</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">plants spread in this place. The summits of Owens Valley is higher than they emerge if you observe from a&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">13</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong> .</span></span></span></span></span></p>","firstNumber":8}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>LONGAEVA:</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ancient Bristlecone Pine</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>To understand more about the earth’s history, humans have often looked to the natural environment for insight into the past. The bristlecone pine (Pinus longaeva), of the White Mountains in California, has served this purpose greater than any other species of tree on the planet. Conditions here are brutal: scant precipitation and low average temperatures mean a short growing season, only intensified by ferocious wind and mal-nutritious rocky. Nevertheless, bristlecone pines have claimed these barren slopes as their permanent home. Evolving here in this harsh environment, super-adapted and without much competition, bristlecones have earned their seat on the longevity throne by becoming the oldest living trees on the planet. Results of extensive studies on bristlecone pine stands have shown that in fact such, environmental limitations are positively associated with the attainment of great age. This intriguing phenomenon will be discussed further on.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>But exactly how old is old? Sprouted before the invention of Egyptian hieroglyphs and long before the teachings of Jesus of Nazareth, Methuselah is the oldest bristlecone alive at roughly 4,700 years. Although specimens of this age do not represent the species’ average, there are 200 trees more than 3,000 years old, and two dozen more than 4,000. Considering that these high ages are obtained in the face of such remarkable environmental adversity, the bristlecone pines have become the focus of much scientific examination over the past half-century.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Perhaps&nbsp;most&nbsp;interested&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;bristlecone&nbsp;pine&nbsp;are&nbsp;dendrochronologists&nbsp;or&nbsp;tree-ring&nbsp;daters.&nbsp;With&nbsp;every strenuous year that passes in the While Mountains, each bristlecone grows and forms a new outer layer of cambium that reflects a season’s particular ease or hardship. So while growing seasons may expand or shrink, the trees carry on, their growth rings faithfully recording the bad years alongside the goods. Through examining the annual growth rings of both living and dead specimens, taking thousands of core samples, and by processes of cross-dating between trees and other qualitative records, scientists have compiled a continuous tree-ring record that dates back to the last Ice Age between eight and ten thousand years ago. Among other linked accomplishments, this record has enhanced the dating process, helping to double-check and correct the radiocarbon-14 method to more accurately estimate the age of organic material.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Now more than ever the importance of monitoring the bristlecone is being realized. As our global climate continues to undergo its most recent and abrupt atmospheric change, these ancient scribes continue to respond. Since, the rings of wood formed each year reveal the trees’ response to climatic conditions during a particular growing season, in their persistence they have left us natural recordings of the past, markers of the present, and clues to the future.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The species’ name originates from the appearance of its unusual cones and needles. The bristlecone’s short, pale needles are also trademarks, bunching together to form foxtail-like bundles. As is the case of most conifer needles, these specialized leaves cluster together to shelter the stomata so very little moisture is lost through them. This adaptation helps the bristlecone photosynthesize during particularly brutal months. Saving the energy of constant needle replacement and providing a stable supply of chlorophyll. For a plant trying to store so much energy, bristlecone seeds are relatively large in size. They are first reproduced when trees reach ages between thirty and seventy-five years old. Germination rates are generally high, in part because seeds require little to no initial stratification. Perhaps the most intriguing physical characteristic of a mature bristlecone, however, is its ratio of living to deadwood on harsh sites and how this relates to old age. In older trees, however, especially in individuals over 1,500 years, a strip-bark trait is adaptive. This condition occurs as a result of cambium dieback, which erodes and thereby exposes certain areas of the bole, leaving only narrow bands of bark intact.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The technique of cambial edge retreat has helped promote old age in bristlecone pine, but that certainly is no the only reason. Most crucial to these trees’ longevity is their compact size and slow rates of growth. By remaining in most cases under ten meters tall, bristlecones stay close to the limited water supply and can hence support more branches and photosynthesizing. Combined with the dry, windy, and often freezing mountain air, slow growth guarantees the bristlecones tight, fibrous rings with a high resin content and structural strength. The absence of natural disaster has also safeguarded the bristlecone’s lengthy lifespan. Due to a lack of ground cover vegetation and an evenly spaced layout, bristlecone stands on the White Mountain peaks have been practically unaffected by the fire. This lack of vegetation also means a lack of competition for the bristlecones.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Bristlecone pines restricted to numerous, rather isolated stands at higher altitudes in the southwestern United States. Stands occur from the Rocky Mountains, through the Colorado Plateau, to the western margin of the Great Basin. Within this natural range, the oldest and most widely researched stands of bristlecones occur in California’s the White Mountains. Even just 200 miles away from the Pacific Ocean, the White Mountains are home to one of this country’s few high-elevation deserts. Located in the extreme eastern rain shadow of the Sierra Nevada, this region receives only 12.54 inches of precipitation per year and experiences temperatures between -20F and +50F. The peaks south of the Owens Valley, are higher up than they might appear from a distance. Although most summits exist somewhere around 11,000 feet, snow-capped White Mountain Peak, for which the range is named, stands at 14,246 feet above sea level. That said, to reach areas of a pure bristlecone is an intense journey all to itself.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>With seemingly endless areas of wonder and interest, the bristlecone pines have become subject to much research over the past half-century. Since the annual growth of these ancient organisms directly reflects the climatic conditions of a particular time period, bristlecones are of greatest significance to dendrochronologists or tree-ring specialists. Dating any tree is simple and can be done within reasonable accuracy just by counting out the rings made each year by the plant’s natural means of growth. By carefully compiling a nearly 10,000-year-old bristlecone pine record, these patient scientists have accurately corrected the carbon-14 dating method and estimated ages of past periods of global climate change. What makes this record so special to dendrochronologists, too, is that, nowhere, throughout time, is precisely the same long-term sequence of wide and narrow rings repeated, because year-to-year variations in climate are never exactly the same.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Historically the bristlecone’s remote location and gnarled wood have deterred commercial extraction, but nothing on earth will go unaffected by global warming. If temperatures rise by only 6 degrees F, which many experts say is likely this century, about two-thirds of the bristlecones’ ideal habitat in the White Mountains effectively will be gone. Almost 30,000 acres of National Forest now preserves the ancient bristlecone, but paved roads, campsites, and self-guided trails have led only to more human impact. In 1966, the U.S.F.S reported over 20,000 visitors to the Ancient Bristlecone Pine Forest, a figure which could exceed 40,000 today. Over the past hundreds of thousands of years, this species has endured in one of the earth’s most trying environments; they deserve our respect and reverence. As global climate change slowly alters their environment, we as humans must do our part to raise awareness and lower our impact.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8149&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8150","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Stress of Workplace","book":"阅读还原集Vol.12","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.12 · Test 3 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8150:59597:14","type":"choice","text":"14 Work stress usually happens in the high level of a business.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Identify the causes: Jan Elsnera, Melbourne psychologist who specialises in executive coaching, says thriving on a demanding workload is typical of senior executives and other high-potential business people.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问“工作压力通常发生在企业的高层”。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"Work stress\"和\"high level of a business\"定位到文章中关于工作压力和企业层级的句子。\n解题思路：原文C段提到\"Executive stress is not confined to big organisations.\"（高管压力不仅仅只存在于大公司），说明高管压力是高层普遍存在的现象。题目中的\"high level of a business\"对应\"Executive stress\"，而\"Executive\"通常指高层管理人员。A选项的Jan Elsnera在D段又提到\"thriving on a demanding workload is typical of senior executives\"（高层管理人员通常能应付繁重的工作），进一步验证了高管压力的存在。因此，答案为A。","options":["Jan Elsnera","Vanessa Stoykov","Gal Zauberman","Neil Plumridge"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59597","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Jan Elsnera\nB Vanessa Stoykov\nC Gal Zauberman\nD Neil Plumridge"},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8150:59597:15","type":"choice","text":"15 More people’s ideas involved would be beneficial for stress relief","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He also relies on the advice of colleagues, saying his peers’ coach each other with business problems. “Just a fresh pair of eyes over an issue can help,” he says.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“更多的人的想法有助于缓解压力”，需要找到与多人参与或建议相关的观点。\n定位关键信息：通过关键词“stress relief”和“more people’s ideas”定位到B段，其中提到Neil Plumridge依靠同事的建议来处理问题，强调“just a fresh pair of eyes over an issue can help”，即他人的观点有助于解决问题。\n解题思路：原文中Neil Plumridge提到自己通过同事的建议来缓解压力，说明多人参与或他人观点的介入对缓解压力有益。因此，这一观点与题目要求一致，对应选项D。","options":["Jan Elsnera","Vanessa Stoykov","Gal Zauberman","Neil Plumridge"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59597","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Jan Elsnera\nB Vanessa Stoykov\nC Gal Zauberman\nD Neil Plumridge"},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8150:59597:16","type":"choice","text":"16 Temporary holiday sometimes doesn’t mean less work.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Because of the growth phase, the business is in, Stoykov has to concentrate on short-term stress relief – weekends in the mountains, the occasional “mental health” day – rather than delegating more work.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问“临时休假有时并不意味着工作量减少”，即休假或短暂休息并不能真正减轻工作负担。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的“Temporary holiday”（临时休假）和“doesn’t mean less work”（不意味着工作量减少）定位。原文中C段提到Stoykov通过“short-term stress relief”（短期减压）如“weekends in the mountains”（去山里度周末）和“occasional ‘mental health’ day”（偶尔的“心理健康日”）来缓解压力，但明确说明这些措施是“rather than delegating more work”（而不是分配更多工作），表明休假并未真正减少工作量。\n解题思路：原文C段描述Stoykov因业务增长需要短期减压，但并未通过分配工作来减轻负担，而是通过休假等方式暂时缓解。题干中的“Temporary holiday sometimes doesn’t mean less work”与原文中“short-term stress relief”和“rather than delegating more work”对应，说明休假并未真正减少工作量，因此答案为B（Stoykov）。","options":["Jan Elsnera","Vanessa Stoykov","Gal Zauberman","Neil Plumridge"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59597","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Jan Elsnera\nB Vanessa Stoykov\nC Gal Zauberman\nD Neil Plumridge"},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8150:59597:17","type":"choice","text":"17 Stress leads to a wrong direction when trying to satisfy customers.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Neil Plumridge, says: ‘Often stress is caused by our setting unrealistic expectations of ourselves. I’ll promise a client I’ll do something tomorrow, and the [promise] another client the same thing, when I really know it’s not going to happen. I’ve put stress on myself when I could have said to the clients: “Why don’t I give that to you in 48 hours?” The client doesn’t care.’\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“压力导致在试图满足客户时走向错误的方向”，即压力如何影响满足客户的行为。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“stress”和“satisfy customers”定位到F段，该段讨论了压力对不同人的影响。\n解题思路：原文中Plumridge提到，有时压力来自于我们对自己不切实际的期待，他有时会答应客户明天做好某件事，接着又去答应另一客户，明天也会做好某件事，对应题目中“satisfy customers”，但他明明知道自己无法做到，给了自己不切实际的期待，又接着说明明可以直接对客户说48小时后再完成，可见他不赞成过度承诺，这是“wrong direction”。因此，D是正确答案。","options":["Jan Elsnera","Vanessa Stoykov","Gal Zauberman","Neil Plumridge"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59597","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Jan Elsnera\nB Vanessa Stoykov\nC Gal Zauberman\nD Neil Plumridge"},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8150:59597:18","type":"choice","text":"18 It is not correct that stress in the future will be eased more than now. It is more accurate than candles and oil lamps.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A study in the February issue of the Journal of Experimental Psychology shows that people always believe they will be less busy in the future than now. This is a misapprehension, according to the authors of the report, Professor Gal Zauberman, of the University of North Carolina, and Professor John Lynch, of Duke University.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“未来压力不会比现在少”这一观点出自于谁。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"stress in the future\"和\"eased more than now\"，通过这些词可以定位到G段中关于人们总是认为未来会比现在更不忙的描述。\n解题思路：G段明确提到，研究表明，人们总是认为未来会比现在更轻松，对应题目中“stress in the future will be eased more than now”，但Zauberman说，这是一种误解。与题目中的信息对应，因此答案是C。","options":["Jan Elsnera","Vanessa Stoykov","Gal Zauberman","Neil Plumridge"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59597","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Jan Elsnera\nB Vanessa Stoykov\nC Gal Zauberman\nD Neil Plumridge"},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8150:59598:19","type":"choice","text":"Which of the following workplace stress is NOT mentioned according to Plumridge in the following options?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Three warning signs alert Plumridge about his workload: sleep, scheduling and family. He knows he has too much on when he gets less than six hours of sleep for three consecutive nights; when he is constantly having to reschedule appointments; ‘and the third one is on the family side,’ says Plumridge, the father of a three-year-old daughter, and expecting a second child in October. ‘If I happen to miss a birthday or anniversary, I know things are out of control.’\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问根据Plumridge的说法，以下哪一项工作压力未被提及。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"Plumridge\"和\"workplace stress\"定位到B段，该段详细描述了Plumridge判断工作压力过大的三个信号。\n解题思路：根据B段原文，Plumridge提到的三个压力信号分别是：睡眠不足（\"less than six hours of sleep\"对应选项C）、频繁改约（\"constantly having to reschedule appointments\"对应选项D）、家庭时间不足（\"miss a birthday or anniversary\"对应选项A）。选项B“无法集中精力工作”在原文中未被提及，因此B是正确答案。","options":["Not enough time spend on family","Unable to concentrate on work","Inadequate time of sleep","Alteration of appointment"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59598","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-21\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 19-21 on your answer sheet."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8150:59599:20","type":"choice","text":"Which of the following solution is NOT mentioned in helping reduce the work pressure according to Plumridge?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Neil Plumridge says he makes it a priority to work out what has to change; that might mean allocating extra resources to a job, allowing more time or changing expectations. He also relies on the advice of colleagues, saying his peers’ coach each other with business problems. “Just a fresh pair of eyes over an issue can help,” he says.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是根据Plumridge的说法，以下哪个解决方案在帮助减轻工作压力方面没有被提及。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"Plumridge\"和\"reduce work pressure\"，可以定位到B段中Plumridge关于如何处理工作压力的描述。\n解题思路：根据B段中的原文，Plumridge提到的解决方案包括分配更多资源，也就是让更多人去做某项工作（对应A选项）、延长完成时间（对应B选项）和调整预期目标（对应C选项）。然而，原文中并未提及通过做运动和按摩来减轻工作压力（对应D选项），因此D选项是正确答案。","options":["Allocate more personnel","Increase more time","Lower expectation","Do sports and massage"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59599","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-21\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 19-21 on your answer sheet."},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8150:59600:21","type":"choice","text":"What is point of view of Jan Elsnera towards work stress?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：We could take urine and blood hormonal measures and pass judgement of whether someone’s physiologically stressed or not,’ she says, ‘But that’s not going to give us an indicator of what their experience of stress is, and what the emotional and cognitive impacts of stress are going to be.’\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是Jan Elsnera对工作压力的观点是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Jan Elsnera\"和\"work stress\"可以定位到D段，该段是关于Jan Elsnera对工作压力的看法。\n解题思路：根据D段中的原文答案句，Jan Elsnera提到通过尿液和血液激素测量只能判断一个人生理上是否压力过大，但无法给出一个人经历压力的指标，以及压力对情感和认知的影响。这意味着她认为医疗测试只能揭示应对压力所需数据的一部分，而情感和认知影响是更重要的。因此，选项A\"Medical test can only reveal part of the data needed to cope with stress\"最符合她的观点。","options":["Medical test can only reveal part of the data needed to cope with stress","Index some body samples will be abnormal in a stressful experience","Emotional and cognitive affection is superior to physical one","One well designed solution can release all stress"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59600","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-21\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 19-21 on your answer sheet."},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8150:59601:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"workplace injury","acceptedAnswers":["workplace injury"],"explanation":"原文答案句：National workers’ compensation figures show stress causes the most lost time of any workplace injury.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是全国工伤赔偿的统计数据表明，压力在什么中，是工作时间减少的最主要因素。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"Statistics from National worker’s compensation\"和\"stress plays the most important role in\"是定位的关键信息。通过这些关键词，我们可以在文章中找到相关的句子。\n解题思路：在B段中，我们可以找到这样一句话：\"National workers’ compensation figures show stress causes the most lost time of any workplace injury.\"这句话表明，国家工人赔偿的统计数据表明，任何工伤中，压力导致的工作时间损失最多。所以，答案是\"workplace injury\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59601","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8150:59602:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"16.6 weeks","acceptedAnswers":["16.6 weeks"],"explanation":"原文答案句：National workers’ compensation figures show stress causes the most lost time of any workplace injury. Employees suffering stress are off work an average of 16.6 weeks.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目询问员工因压力导致的缺勤平均时长是多少。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“absence from work caused by stress”可以定位到B段中讨论压力造成工时损失的句子。\n解题思路：题目中的“absence from work”与原文中的“are off work”为同义替换。原文明确给出了因压力而缺勤的员工平均休假时长是“16.6 weeks”。这个数字直接回答了题目关于缺勤时长的问题，因此确定答案为“16.6 weeks”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59602","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8150:59603:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"7%","acceptedAnswers":["7%"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Comcare, the Federal Government insurer, reports that in 2003-04, claims for psychological injury accounted for 7% of claims but almost 27% of claim costs.\n对应段落：B段\n审题： 题目指出，我们关心的不仅是时间，还有由此产生的巨大开支。一家联邦政府保险公司曾报告道，在所有索赔中，约有多少是心理问题，而却占了所有索赔费用的近27%。需要填入心理问题索赔所占的百分比。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“official insurer”、“claims”、“mental issues”和“27% costs”可以定位到B段中关于Comcare公司索赔数据和成本的句子。\n解题思路：题目中的“official insurer”对应原文的“Comcare, the Federal Government insurer”，“mental issues”对应“psychological injury”。原文句子结构清晰地给出了两个百分比：心理伤害索赔的数量“占总索赔的7%”，但其成本“占总索赔成本的近27%”。题目空格要求填入的是索赔数量的占比，与原文的“7% of claims”对应。因此，答案为“7%”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59603","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8150:59604:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"golf","acceptedAnswers":["golf"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Experts say the key to dealing with stress is not to focus on relief – a game of golf or a massage – but to reassess workloads.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目询问哪种运动可以作为缓解压力的方法。\n定位关键信息： 通过题目中“sports”和“treatment to release stress”可以定位到B段中讨论缓解压力的方法的部分。\n解题思路：原文在提到缓解压力（relief）时，明确列举了“a game of golf or a massage”作为例子。其中，“golf”是一项运动，与题目中的“sports”直接对应。因此，高尔夫是作为一种缓解压力的方式被提及的，确定答案为“golf”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59604","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8150:59605:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"massage","acceptedAnswers":["massage"],"explanation":"原文答案句： Experts say the key to dealing with stress is not to focus on relief – a game of golf or a massage – but to reassess workloads.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目询问除了运动之外，还有什么活动可以作为缓解压力的方法。\n定位关键信息：通 通过题目中“as well as”和“treatment to release stress”可以定位到B段中与“golf”并列的缓解压力的方式。\n解题思路：原文在破折号中列举了两种缓解压力的方式：“a game of golf”和“a massage”。题目中的“as well as”表示并列关系，因此26题需要填入与“golf”并列的“massage”。确定答案为“massage”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59605","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8150:59606:27","type":"fill","text":"填写第 27 空","answer":"workloads","acceptedAnswers":["workloads"],"explanation":"原文答案句： Experts say the key to dealing with stress is not to focus on relief – a game of golf or a massage – but to reassess workloads.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目询问专家推荐的实际解决方法是什么，即需要重新分析什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中“specialists recommended another practical way out”和“analyse...once again”可以定位到B段中专家提出的关键建议。\n解题思路：原文使用“not...but...”的结构，明确指出应对压力的关键“不是”专注于缓解（如高尔夫或按摩），“而是”要重新评估（reassess） workloads。题目中的“analyse...once again”是“reassess”的同义转述。因此，专家推荐的方法是重新分析“workloads”。确定答案为“workloads”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59606","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59597","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Jan Elsnera\nB Vanessa Stoykov\nC Gal Zauberman\nD Neil Plumridge","html":"<p><br/></p><p><strong>14</strong> Work stress usually happens in the high level of a business.<strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"59598","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-21\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 19-21 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Which of the following workplace stress is NOT mentioned according to Plumridge in the following options?</strong></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"59599","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-21\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 19-21 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Which of the following solution is NOT mentioned in helping reduce the work pressure according to Plumridge?</strong></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"59600","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 19-21\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 19-21 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is point of view of Jan Elsnera towards work stress?</strong></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"59601","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Statistics from National worker’s compensation indicate stress plays the most important role in<strong> 22 </strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong>&nbsp;which cause the time losses.</p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"59602","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Staffs take about <strong>23</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong> for absence from work caused by stress.</p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"59603","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Not just time is our main concern but great expenses generated consequently.&nbsp;</p><p>An official insurer wrote sometime that about <strong>24</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> of all claims were mental issues whereas nearly 27% costs in all claims.</p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"59604","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Sports such as <strong>25</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong> ,</p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"59605","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>as well as <strong>26</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong> could be a treatment to release stress;</p>","firstNumber":26},{"id":"59606","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>However, specialists recommended another practical way out, analyse <strong>27</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[27] ____</strong> once again.</p>","firstNumber":27}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Stress of Workplace&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>How busy is too busy? For some it means having to miss the occasional long lunch; for others, it means missing lunch altogether. For a few, it is not being able to take a ‘sickie’ once a month. Then there is a group of people for whom working every evening and weekend is normal, and frantic is the tempo of their lives. For most senior executives, workloads swing between extremely busy and frenzied. The vice-president of the management consultancy AT Kearney and its head of telecommunications for the Asia-Pacific region, Neil Plumridge, says his work weeks vary from a ‘manageable’ 45 hours to 80 hours, but average 60 hours.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Three warning signs alert Plumridge about his workload: sleep, scheduling and family. He knows he has too much on when he gets less than six hours of sleep for three consecutive nights; when he is constantly having to reschedule appointments; ‘and the third one is on the family side,’ says Plumridge, the father of a three-year-old daughter, and expecting a second child in October. ‘If I happen to miss a birthday or anniversary, I know things are out of control.’ Being ‘too busy’ is highly subjective. But for any individual, the perception of being too busy over a prolonged period can start showing up as stress: disturbed sleep, and declining mental and physical health. National workers’ compensation figures show stress causes the most lost time of any workplace injury. Employees suffering stress are off work an average of 16.6 weeks. The effects of stress are also expensive. Comcare, the Federal Government insurer, reports that in 2003-04,&nbsp;claims for psychological injury accounted for 7% of claims but almost 27%&nbsp;of claim costs. Experts say the key to dealing with stress is not to focus on relief – a game of golf or a massage – but to reassess workloads. Neil Plumridge says he makes it a priority to work out what has to change; that might mean allocating extra resources to a job, allowing more time or changing expectations. The decision may take several days. He also relies on the advice of colleagues, saying his peers’ coach each other with business problems. “Just a fresh pair of eyes over an issue can help,” he says.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Executive stress is not confined to big organisations. Vanessa Stoykov has been running her own advertising and public relations business for seven years, specializing in work for financial and professional services firms. Evolution Media has grown so fast that it debuted on the BRW Fast 100 list of fastest-growing small enterprises last year – just after Stoykov had her first child. Stoykov thrives on the mental stimulation of running her own business. ‘Like everyone, I have the occasional day when I think my head’s going to blow off,’ she says. Because of the growth phase, the business is in, Stoykov has to concentrate on short-term stress relief – weekends in the mountains, the occasional “mental health” day – rather than delegating more work. She says: ‘We’re hiring more people, but you need to train them, teach them about the culture and the clients, so it’s actually more work rather than less.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Identify the causes: Jan Elsnera, Melbourne psychologist who specialises in executive coaching, says thriving on a demanding workload is typical of senior executives and other high-potential business people. She says there is no one-size-fits-all approach to stress: some people work best with high-adrenalin periods followed by quieter patches, while others thrive under sustained pressure. ‘We could take urine and blood hormonal measures and pass judgement of whether someone’s physiologically stressed or not,’ she says, ‘But that’s not going to give us an indicator of what their experience of stress is, and what the emotional and cognitive impacts of stress are going to be.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Elsner’s practice is informed by a movement known as positive psychology, a school of thought that argues ‘positive’ experiences – feeling engaged, challenged, and that one is making a contribution to something meaningful – do not balance out negative ones such as stress; instead, they help people increase their resilience over time. Good stress, or positive experiences of being challenged and rewarded, is thus cumulative in the same way as bad stress. Elsner says many of the senior business people she coaches are relying more on regulating bad stress through methods such as meditation and yoga. She points to research showing that meditation can alter the biochemistry of the brain and actually help people “retrain” the way their brains and bodies react to stress. ‘Meditation and yoga enable you to shift the way that your brain reacts, so if you get proficient at it you’re in control.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The Australian vice-president of AT Kearney, Neil Plumridge, says: ‘Often stress is caused by our setting unrealistic expectations of ourselves. I’ll promise a client I’ll do something tomorrow, and the [promise] another client the same thing, when I really know it’s not going to happen. I’ve put stress on myself when I could have said to the clients: “Why don’t I give that to you in 48 hours?” The client doesn’t care.’ Overcommitting is something people experience as an individual problem. We explain it as the result of procrastination or Parkinson’s law: that work expands to fill the time available. New research indicates that people may be hard-wired to do it.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>A study in the February issue of the Journal of Experimental Psychology shows that people always believe they will be less busy in the future than now. This is a misapprehension, according to the authors of the report, Professor Gal Zauberman, of the University of North Carolina, and Professor John Lynch, of Duke University. ‘On average, an individual will be just as busy two weeks or a month from now as he or she is today. But that is not how it appears to be in everyday life,’ they wrote, ‘People often make commitments long in advance that they would never make if the same commitments required immediate action. That is, they discount future time investments relatively steeply.’ Why do we perceive a greater ‘surplus’ of time in the future than in the present? The researchers suggest that people underestimate completion times for tasks stretching into the future, and that they are bad at imagining future competition for their time.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8150&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8151","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 The Secret of the Yawn","book":"阅读还原集Vol.12","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 3","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.12 · Test 3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8151:59588:28","type":"fill","text":"填写第 28 空","answer":"68 seconds","acceptedAnswers":["68 seconds"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He found the basic yawn lasts about six seconds and they come in bouts with an interval of about 68 seconds.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目询问一个心理学教授观察后得出的结论，即平均打哈欠需要6秒，并且下一个哈欠来之前需要什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“six seconds”和“average yawning”定位到E段中关于心理学教授Robert Provine的研究发现。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到“basic yawn lasts about six seconds”，即基础哈欠持续大约六秒钟。结合上下文和题目，可以推断此处应填入两个哈欠之间的间隔时间，对应原文\"with an interval of about 68 seconds\"可以确定答案为“68 seconds”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59588","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8151:59589:29","type":"fill","text":"填写第 29 空","answer":"distinction/complex distinction","acceptedAnswers":["distinction","complex distinction"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Men and women yawn or half-yawn equally often, but men are significantly less likely to cover their mouths which may indicate complex distinction in genders.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是男女打哈欠的频率相同，但伴随打哈欠的行为显示出性别间的什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"yawn or half-yawn equally often\"和\"behavior accompanied with yawning\"定位到E段中关于男女打哈欠频率相同但行为有区别的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到男女打哈欠或半打哈欠的频率相同，但男性捂嘴打哈欠的可能性更小，这表明存在\"complex distinction in genders\"（复杂的性别区别），因此答案为\"complex distinction\"或\"distinction\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59589","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8151:59590:30","type":"fill","text":"填写第 30 空","answer":"breathing","acceptedAnswers":["breathing"],"explanation":"原文答案句：However, the physical root of yawning remains a mystery. Some researchers say it’s coordinated within the hypothalamus of the brain, the area that also controls breathing.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求根据填空题干中的信息，在原文中找到与大脑某部分同时影响某种运动（yawning）并与之相关的另一项功能。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"within the brain\"和\"movement\"定位到E段中关于大脑某部分控制某种运动和另一项功能的句子。\n解题思路：原文E段提到，有些研究人员认为打哈欠的生理根源仍然是个谜，但他们认为打哈欠是由大脑的某个部分协调的，这个部分也控制着呼吸。题干中的\"movement\"对应原文中的\"yawning\"，而\"breathing\"是与打哈欠同时由大脑同一区域控制的功能，因此答案为breathing。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59590","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8151:59591:31","type":"fill","text":"填写第 31 空","answer":"stretch/stretching","acceptedAnswers":["stretch","stretching"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Yawning and stretching also share properties and may be performed together as parts of a global motor complex.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是研究发现打哈欠和什么之间存在联系。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的\"link between yawn and\"定位到F段首句，找到\"Yawning and stretching also share properties and may be performed together\"。\n解题思路：原文明确提到打哈欠和伸展动作有共同属性，经常一起发生，因此可以确定答案为stretch或stretching。题目中的\"link between\"对应原文的\"share properties and may be performed together\"，表明两者存在关联。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59591","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8151:59592:32","type":"fill","text":"填写第 32 空","answer":"brain","acceptedAnswers":["brain"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The neural circuits for spontaneous yawning must exist in the brain stem near other respiratory and vasomotor centers, because yawning is performed by anencephalic who possess only the medulla oblongata.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是在婴儿出生前，这两种行为也会自动发生，即使是在那些什么受损的人中。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词\"before a baby was born\"和\"damaged\"可以定位到H段中关于大脑受损和婴儿发育的描述。\n解题思路：原文中提到，无脑畸形的婴儿仍然可以正常打哈欠，这表明大脑的某些部分在出生前就已经能够自动合作。根据原文的描述，这些自动合作的部位位于大脑的脑干部分，因此答案是\"brain\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59592","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8151:59593:33","type":"choice","text":"33 The rate for yawning shows some regular patterns.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He found the basic yawn lasts about six seconds and they come in bouts with an interval of about 68 seconds.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段提到了关于打哈欠的频率或模式显示出一些规律性。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"rate for yawning shows some regular patterns\"（打哈欠的频率显示出一些规律性的模式）可以定位到文章中关于打哈欠频率或模式的具体描述。\n解题思路：在E段中，文章提到Robert Provine的研究发现，基本的打哈欠持续大约六秒钟，并且它们以大约68秒的间隔成批出现。这表明打哈欠的频率有一定的规律性，即每隔大约68秒就会出现一次打哈欠。因此，E段包含了关于打哈欠频率显示出规律性的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"59593","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-37\nReading paragraph A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H for question 33-37.\nNB You may use any letter more than once"},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8151:59593:34","type":"choice","text":"34 Yawning is an inherent ability that appears in both animals and humans.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Humans do it even before they are born, opening wide in the womb. Some snakes unhinge their jaws to do it. One species of penguins yawns as part of mating.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“打哈欠是一种天生的能力，出现在动物和人类身上”这一信息出现在哪个段落。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“inherent ability”（天生的能力）、“animals and humans”（动物和人类）定位到原文。原文中提到“Humans do it even before they are born”（人类甚至在出生前就会打哈欠）和“Some snakes unhinge their jaws to do it”（有些蛇会张嘴打哈欠），明确说明了打哈欠是动物和人类共有的天生活动。\n解题思路：根据原文B段的内容，明确指出了人类和动物（蛇、企鹅）都会打哈欠，且打哈欠是人类出生前就具备的行为，这直接对应了题目中“inherent ability that appears in both animals and humans”的描述。因此，答案为B段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"59593","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-37\nReading paragraph A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H for question 33-37.\nNB You may use any letter more than once"},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8151:59593:35","type":"choice","text":"35 Stretching and yawning are not always going together.","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But they do not always co-occur – people usually yawn when we stretch, but we don’t always stretch when we yawn, especially before bedtime.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“伸展和打哈欠并不总是同时发生”，需要找到描述这两者关系并不总是同步的段落。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“Stretching and yawning”和“not always going together”来定位答案在文章中的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文F段中的句子“they do not always co-occur – people usually yawn when we stretch, but we don’t always stretch when we yawn, especially before bedtime.”，明确说明了伸展和打哈欠并不总是同时发生，尤其是睡前。这与题目要求的信息完全一致，因此答案为F段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"59593","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-37\nReading paragraph A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H for question 33-37.\nNB You may use any letter more than once"},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8151:59593:36","type":"choice","text":"36 Yawning may suggest people are having positive notice or response in communicating.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It’s also a good indicator if you’re empathizing with me and paying attention.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落提到了打哈欠可能表明人们在交流中具有积极的注意或回应。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“positive notice or response in communicating”，在文章中寻找与“打哈欠”和“交流中的积极注意或回应”相关的句子。\n解题思路：根据题目中的关键词，在D段中找到了“it’s also a good indicator if you’re empathizing with me and paying attention”这句话，意思是“它（打哈欠）也是你是否在对我表示同情和注意力的一个良好指标”。这句话表明打哈欠可以作为一种信号，表明人们在交流中是否在积极注意或回应对方，因此D段包含了题目所要求的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"59593","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-37\nReading paragraph A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H for question 33-37.\nNB You may use any letter more than once"},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8151:59593:37","type":"choice","text":"37 Some superior areas in brain may deal with the infectious feature of yawning.","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The multiplicity of stimuli of contagious yawning, by contrast, implicates many higher brain regions.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是“大脑的一些高级功能区可能处理打哈欠的传染性特征”，即询问关于打哈欠传染性与高级脑区相关的内容。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"superior areas in brain\"（大脑的高级功能区）和\"contagious\"（传染性）来定位。\n解题思路：在H段中，原文提到“传染性哈欠的多种刺激，相比之下，涉及到许多高级脑区”，这里的\"higher brain regions\"对应题目的\"superior areas in brain\"，而\"contagious yawning\"直接对应题目的\"contagious feature of yawning\"，因此H段包含了题目所询问的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"59593","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-37\nReading paragraph A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H for question 33-37.\nNB You may use any letter more than once"},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8151:59594:38","type":"choice","text":"Several students in Platek’s experiment did not comprehend why their tutor asked them to yawn back.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\n‘We literally had people saying, “Why am I looking at people yawning?”’ Professor Platek said. ‘It just had no effect.’\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目说的是“在Platek的实验中，有几位学生不理解为什么他们的导师让他们打哈欠回应”，即实验对象是否对实验要求感到困惑。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“students”、“comprehend”、“tutor asked them to yawn back”定位到C段。原文提到实验中有些参与者不理解为什么看别人打哈欠，但并未明确说明他们不理解导师让他们打哈欠回应。\n解题思路：原文C段提到参与者不理解“为什么看别人打哈欠”（Why am I looking at people yawning?），但题目说的是“不理解为什么导师让他们打哈欠回应”（tutor asked them to yawn back）。原文并未明确说明导师让他们打哈欠回应，也未说明学生对这一要求感到困惑，因此信息未直接对应。题目中的“tutor asked them to yawn back”在原文中没有明确支持，属于未给出信息。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59594","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 3? In boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8151:59595:39","type":"choice","text":"Some results from certain experiment indicate the link between yawning and compassion.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He found that participants who did not score high on compassion did not yawn back. ‘We literally had people saying, “Why am I looking at people yawning?”’ Professor Platek said. ‘It just had no effect.’\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目说的是“某些实验的某些结果表明了打哈欠和同情心之间的联系。”\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“yawning”和“compassion”可以定位到C段。\n解题思路：C段中提到，Platek教授的实验发现，那些在同情心测试中得分不高的参与者不会回打哈欠。这说明打哈欠和同情心之间存在一定的联系，即同情心高的人更容易受到他人打哈欠的影响而回打哈欠。因此，题目中的陈述与文章信息一致，答案为A（True）。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59595","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 3? In boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8151:59596:40","type":"choice","text":"Yawning can show an affirmative impact on the recovery from brain damage brought by a stroke.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It is not known whether the associated response is a positive prognosis for recovery, nor whether yawning is therapeutic for reinnervation or prevention of muscular atrophy.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目说的是“打哈欠对因中风造成的脑损伤的恢复有积极影响”。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“recovery from brain damage brought by a stroke”定位到G段。\n解题思路：原文中提到“associated response”（相关反应）是否是恢复的积极预兆，以及打哈欠是否对神经再支配或预防肌肉萎缩有疗效，目前尚不清楚。因此，题目中“打哈欠对脑损伤的恢复有积极影响”这一说法在原文中没有得到证实，属于未提及信息。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59596","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 3? In boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59588","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>A psychology professor drew a conclusion after observation that it takes about six seconds to complete an average yawning which needs<strong> 28</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[28] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"59589","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>before a following yawning comes. It is almost at the same frequency that male and female yawn or half, yet behavior accompanied with yawning showing a <strong>29</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[29] ____</strong> in genders.</p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"59590","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Some parts within the brain may affect the movement which also have something to do with <strong>30</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[30] ____</strong>.</p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"59591","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Another finding also finds there is a link between yawn and <strong>31</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[31] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"59592","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Before a baby was born, which two can be automatically cooperating even among people whose <strong>32</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[32] ____</strong> is damaged.</p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"59593","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-37\nReading paragraph A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H for question 33-37.\nNB You may use any letter more than once","html":"<p><strong>33 </strong>The rate for yawning shows some regular patterns. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[33] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"59594","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 3? In boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Several students in Platek’s experiment did not comprehend why their tutor asked them to yawn back.</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"59595","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 3? In boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Some results from certain experiment indicate the link between yawning and compassion.</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"59596","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 38-40\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 3? In boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Yawning can show an affirmative impact on the recovery from brain damage brought by a stroke.</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The Secret of the Yawn&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>When a scientist began to study yawning in the 1980s, it was difficult to convince some of his research students of the merits of ‘yawning science.’ Although it may appear quirky, his decision to study yawning was a logical extension to human beings of my research in developmental neuroscience, reported in such papers as ‘Wing-flapping during Development and Evolution.’ As a neurobehavioral problem, there is not much difference between the wing-flapping of birds and the face – and body-flapping of human yawners.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>Yawning is an ancient, primitive act. Humans do it even before they are born, opening wide in the womb. Some snakes unhinge their jaws to do it. One species of penguins yawns as part of mating. Only now are researchers beginning to understand why we yawn, when we yawn and why we yawn back. A professor of cognitive neuroscience at Drexel University in Philadelphia, Steven Platek, studies the act of contagious yawning, something done only by people and other primates.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>In his first experiment, he used a psychological test to rank people on their empathic feelings. He found that participants who did not score high on compassion did not yawn back. ‘We literally had people saying, “Why am I looking at people yawning?”’ Professor Platek said. ‘It just had no effect.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>For his second experiment, he put 10 students in a magnetic resonance imaging machine as they watched video tapes of people yawning. When the students watched the videos, the part of the brain which reacted was the part scientists believe controls empathy – the posterior cingulate, in the brain’s middle rear. ‘I don’t know if it’s necessarily that nice people yawn more, but I think it’s a good indicator of a state of mind,’ said Professor Platek, ‘It’s also a good indicator if you’re empathizing with me and paying attention.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>His third experiment is studying yawning in those with brain disorders, such as autism and schizophrenia, in which victims have difficulty connecting emotionally with others. A psychology professor at the University of Maryland, Robert Provine, is one of the few other researchers into yawning. He found the basic yawn lasts about six seconds and they come in bouts with an interval of about 68 seconds. Men and women yawn or half-yawn equally often, but men are significantly less likely to cover their mouths which may indicate complex distinction in genders. ‘A watched yawner never yawns,’ Professor Provine said. However, the physical root of yawning remains a mystery. Some researchers say it’s coordinated within the hypothalamus of the brain, the area that also controls breathing.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Yawning and stretching also share properties and may be performed together as parts of a global motor complex. But they do not always co-occur – people usually yawn when we stretch, but we don’t always stretch when we yawn, especially before bedtime. Studies by J.I.P, G.H.A. Visser and H.F. Prechtl in the early 1980s, charting movement in the developing fetus using ultrasound, observed not just yawning but a link between yawning and stretching as early as the end of the first prenatal trimester.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The most extraordinary demonstration of the yawn-stretch linkage occurs in many people paralyzed on one side of their body because of brain damage caused by a stroke. The prominent British neurologist Sir Francis Walshe noted in 1923 what when these hemiplegics yawn, they are startled and mystified to observe that their otherwise paralyzed arm rises and flexes automatically in what neurologists term an &#39;associated response&#39;. Yawning apparently activates undamaged, unconsciously controlled connections between the brain and the cord motor system innervating the paralyzed limb. It is not known whether the associated response is a positive prognosis for recovery, nor whether yawning is therapeutic for reinnervation or prevention of muscular atrophy.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Clinical neurology offers other surprises. Some patients with ‘locked-in’ syndrome, who are almost totally deprived of the ability to move voluntarily, can yawn normally. The neural circuits for spontaneous yawning must exist in the brain stem near other respiratory and vasomotor centers, because yawning is performed by anencephalic who possess only the medulla oblongata. The multiplicity of stimuli of contagious yawning, by contrast, implicates many higher brain regions.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8151&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8134","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Organic Farming and Chemical Fertilizers","book":"阅读还原集Vol.12","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.12 · Test 2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8134:59309:1","type":"choice","text":"1 Use of chemical fertilizer can be optimised by combining weather information.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Eventually, farmers may incorporate long-term weather forecasts into their planning as well, so that they can cut back on fertiliser use when the weather is likely to make harvests poor anyway, says Ron Olson, an agronomist with Cargill Fertilizer in Tampa, Florida.\n对应段落：K段\n审题：题目问的是谁认为可以通过结合天气信息来优化化肥的使用。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"chemical fertilizer\"、\"optimised\"和\"weather information\"，这些词可以帮助我们在文章中定位到相关的句子。\n解题思路：在K段中，我们可以找到Ron Olson说的话，他提到农民可以结合长期天气预报来规划，从而在天气可能使收成不佳的情况下减少化肥的使用。这正好与题目中提到的\"通过结合天气信息来优化化肥的使用\"相符。因此，答案为D。","options":["Vaclav Smil","Bill Liebhardt","Kenneth Cassman","Ron Olson"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59309","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.\nA Vaclav Smil\nB Bill Liebhardt\nC Kenneth Cassman\nD Ron Olson"},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8134:59309:2","type":"choice","text":"2 Organic framing yield is nearly equal to traditional ones.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Organic farmers like to point out that fields managed in this way can produce yields just as high as fields juiced up with synthetic fertilisers.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是关于有机农业产量与传统农业产量相近的观点。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"Organic framing yield\"和\"nearly equal to traditional ones\"在文章中定位。\n解题思路：在I段中找到与有机农业产量相关的句子，原文明确提到有机农业的产量可以与使用合成肥料的传统农业产量相当（\"just as high as\"），与题干中的\"nearly equal to\"意思一致，因此对应的人是Bill Liebhardt，即B。","options":["Vaclav Smil","Bill Liebhardt","Kenneth Cassman","Ron Olson"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59309","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.\nA Vaclav Smil\nB Bill Liebhardt\nC Kenneth Cassman\nD Ron Olson"},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8134:59309:3","type":"choice","text":"3 Better agricultural setting is a significant key to solve environmental tough nut.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The key is sustainability: whatever we do must not destroy the capital of soil and water we need to keep on producing.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问“更好的农业环境是解决环境难题的关键”，即询问谁认为可持续农业是解决环境问题的关键。\n定位关键信息：题目中的“better agricultural setting”对应原文中的“sustainability”，即可持续性；题目中的“significant key to solve environmental tough nut”对应原文中的“key is sustainability”。\n解题思路：原文A段明确提到“可持续性是关键”，并指出未来农业应关注土壤和生态系统的健康，这与题目中“更好的农业环境是解决环境难题的关键”完全一致。因此，答案为C。","options":["Vaclav Smil","Bill Liebhardt","Kenneth Cassman","Ron Olson"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59309","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.\nA Vaclav Smil\nB Bill Liebhardt\nC Kenneth Cassman\nD Ron Olson"},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8134:59309:4","type":"choice","text":"4 Substantial production loss would happen in case all farmers shifted from using synthetic fertiliser.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This is the biggest cost of organic farming. Vaclav Smil of the University of Manitoba in Winnipeg, Canada, estimates that if farmers worldwide gave up the 80 million tonnes of synthetic fertiliser they now use each year, total grain production would fall by at least half.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是“如果所有农民都停止使用合成肥料，将发生大规模生产损失”，需要找到关于停止使用合成肥料导致生产损失的观点或事实。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词“Substantial production loss”（大规模生产损失）、“shifted from using synthetic fertiliser”（停止使用合成肥料）可以定位到J段中关于Vaclav Smil的观点，他提到如果农民停止使用合成肥料，粮食产量将至少下降一半。\n解题思路：J段明确提到Vaclav Smil的研究结果，即如果全球农民放弃使用合成肥料，粮食总产量将至少下降一半，这与题目描述的“大规模生产损失”完全一致。因此，Vaclav Smil是提出这一观点的人，对应选项A。","options":["Vaclav Smil","Bill Liebhardt","Kenneth Cassman","Ron Olson"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59309","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.\nA Vaclav Smil\nB Bill Liebhardt\nC Kenneth Cassman\nD Ron Olson"},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8134:59310:5","type":"choice","text":"Increasing population, draining irrigation,eroding farmland push agricultural industry to extremity.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The world’s population continues to climb. And despite the rise of high-tech agriculture, 800 million people don’t get enough to eat. Clearly, it’s time to rethink the food we eat and where it comes from. Feeding 9 billion people will take more than the same old farming practices, especially if we want to do it without felling rainforests and planting every last scrap of prairie. Finding food for all those people will tax farmers’ – and researchers’ – ingenuity to the limit. Yet already, precious aquifers that provide irrigation water for some of the world’s most productive farmlands are drying up or filling with seawater, and arable land in China is eroding to create vast dust storms that redden sunsets as far away as North America.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“人口增长、灌溉枯竭、耕地侵蚀是否将农业行业推向极端”。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的“increasing population”、“draining irrigation”、“eroding farmland”这些关键词在文章中定位答案。\n解题思路：原文A段明确提到人口持续增长，需要重新思考食物来源，并且提到了灌溉水源枯竭和耕地侵蚀等问题，这些都表明农业行业面临极端压力，因此题目与原文信息一致。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59310","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5-9\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 5-9 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8134:59311:6","type":"choice","text":"There are only two options for farmers; they use chemical fertiliser or natural approach.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In one corner are the techno-optimists who put their faith in genetically modified crops, improved agrochemicals and computer-enhanced machinery; in the other are advocates of organic farming, who reject artificial chemicals and embrace back-to-nature techniques such as composting. Both sides cite plausible science to back their claims to the moral high ground, and both bring enough passion to the debate for many people to come away thinking we’re faced with a stark choice between two mutually incompatible options. (B段)\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是农民是否只有两种选择：使用化学肥料或自然方法。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"chemical fertiliser\"和\"natural approach\"与B段中的\"artificial chemicals\"和\"back-to-nature techniques\"对应。\n解题思路：B段提到确实存在两种对立的观点，但紧接着在C段开头就指出\"Not so.\"，表明这两种观点并非唯一选择，后面提出了第三种可持续的农业方式。因此，题目说法与原文信息不符，答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59311","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5-9\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 5-9 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8134:59312:7","type":"choice","text":"Chemical fertilizer currently are more expensive than the natural fertilisers.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Not so. If you take off the ideological blinkers and simply ask how the world can produce the food it needs with the least environmental cost, a new middle way opens. The key is sustainability: whatever we do must not destroy the capital of soil and water we need to keep on producing. Like today’s organic farming, the intelligent farming of the future should pay much more attention to the health of its soil and the ecosystem it’s part of. But intelligent farming should also make shrewd and locally appropriate use of chemical fertilisers and pesticides. The most crucial ingredient in this new style of agriculture is not chemicals but information about what’s happening in each field and how to respond. Yet ironically, this key element may be the most neglected today.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问“化学肥料目前比天然肥料更昂贵”是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“Chemical fertilizer”和“natural fertilisers”，通过定位“chemical fertilisers”可以找到C段提到“chemical fertilisers and pesticides”，但全文并未提及化学肥料与天然肥料的价格比较。\n解题思路：文章在C段提到了化学肥料的使用，但并未涉及价格比较，也没有提到天然肥料的价格或成本。因此，题目中的价格比较信息在文章中没有明确说明，无法判断其是否正确。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59312","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5-9\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 5-9 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8134:59313:8","type":"choice","text":"In order to keep nutrient in the soil, organic farmers need to rotate planting method.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Organic farmers don’t use chemical fertilisers, so they are very good at building soil fertility by working crop residues and manure into the soil, rotating grain with legumes that fix atmospheric nitrogen, and other techniques.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问“为了保持土壤中的养分，有机农民需要轮换种植方法”是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“keep nutrient in the soil”和“rotate planting method”定位到G段，该段提到有机农民通过轮换谷物和豆类来增加土壤肥力。\n解题思路：原文明确指出有机农民通过轮换谷物和豆类（rotating grain with legumes）来保持土壤肥力，这与题目中的“rotate planting method”一致，因此答案为YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59313","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5-9\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 5-9 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8134:59314:9","type":"choice","text":"‘Organic agriculture’ is the way that environment-damaging technologies are all strictly forbidden.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句： But strict ‘organic agriculture’, which prohibits certain technologies and allows others, isn’t always better for the environment.\n对应段落：L段\n审题：题目问“有机农业”是否是严格禁止所有环境破坏技术的途径。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词“Organic agriculture”和“environment-damaging technologies”定位到L段，该段提到有机农业prohibit certain technologies。\n解题思路：原文明确指出有机农业会禁止部分环境破坏技术，并不是严格禁止所有环境破坏技术。因此题干的说法与原文信息不符，答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59314","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5-9\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 5-9 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8134:59315:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"farming","acceptedAnswers":["farming"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nThe world’s population continues to climb. And despite the rise of high-tech agriculture, 800 million people don’t get enough to eat. Clearly, it’s time to rethink the food we eat and where it comes from. Feeding 9 billion people will take more than the same old farming practices, especially if we want to do it without felling rainforests and planting every last scrap of prairie.\n对应段落：A段。\n审题：题目问的是为了防止全球人口挨饿，需要应用哪些方法。\n定位关键信息：题干中的\"global population wouldn’t go starved\"和\"approaches\"是关键信息，需要在文章中找到与全球人口挨饿和解决方案相关的内容。\n解题思路：根A段提到的\"800 million people don’t get enough to eat\"和\"take more than the same old farming practices\"，可以得出需要应用多种农业方法来满足全球人口的粮食需求。因此，答案为\"farming\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59315","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8134:59316:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"Curry","acceptedAnswers":["Curry"],"explanation":"原文答案句：That view was echoed in January by the Curry report, a government panel that surveyed the future of farming and food in Britain.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目要求根据给出的摘要，从文章中选择不超过两个单词来填空，题目要求找到一个团队名称，这个团队通过调查重复了某学者的观点。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“repeated the viewpoint of a scholar by a survey in British farming”来定位答案在文章中的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句，可以直接看出“curry”是填空的答案。这是因为题干明确提到“a team called Curry”，这与原文中“by Curry report”部分相匹配。因此，答案为“curry”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59316","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8134:59317:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"natural/organic","acceptedAnswers":["natural","organic"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\n\"Perhaps these easy assumptions explain why sales of organic food across Europe are increasing by at least 50 per cent per year.\"\n对应段落： D段\n审题：题目要求找到欧洲农民越来越相信的农业类型。\n定位关键信息：\"European farmers believe in\"对应原文的\"sales of organic food across Europe are increasing\"\"these years\"对应原文的\"per year\"的增长趋势\n解题思路：在D段找到关于欧洲农业趋势的描述：发现有机食品在欧洲销售额年增长50%以上，这种销售增长反映了消费者和农民对有机农业的信任从上下文可以确定是\"organic\"（有机）农业 正确答案： organic","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59317","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8134:59318:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"chemical","acceptedAnswers":["chemical"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But more fundamentally, the organic versus-chemical debate focuses on the wrong question.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求填空，问的是什么东西看起来在错误的方向上流动。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"seems in an inaccurate direction\"定位E段，找到包含这一短语的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确指出\"chemical\"看起来在错误的方向上流动，因此答案为\"chemical\"。题干中的\"seems in an inaccurate direction\"与原文完全一致，直接对应\"chemical\"这一名词。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59318","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59309","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nUse the information in the passage to match the people (listed A-D) with opinions or deeds below. Write the appropriate letters A-D in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.\nA Vaclav Smil\nB Bill Liebhardt\nC Kenneth Cassman\nD Ron Olson","html":"<p><strong>1</strong> Use of chemical fertilizer can be optimised by combining weather information. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"59310","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5-9\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 5-9 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>Increasing population, draining irrigation,eroding farmland push agricultural industry to extremity.</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"59311","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5-9\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 5-9 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>There are only two options for farmers; they use chemical fertiliser or natural approach.</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"59312","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5-9\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 5-9 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>Chemical fertilizer currently are more expensive than the natural fertilisers.</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"59313","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5-9\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 5-9 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>In order to keep nutrient in the soil, organic farmers need to rotate planting method.</strong></p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"59314","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 5-9\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 5-9 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>‘Organic agriculture’ is the way that environment-damaging technologies are all strictly forbidden.</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"59315","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Several <strong>10</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong> approaches need to be applied in order that global population wouldn’t go starved.&nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"59316","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>A team called&nbsp;<strong>11</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong> repeated the viewpoint of a scholar by a survey in British farming.&nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"59317","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>More and more European farmers believe in&nbsp;<strong>12</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong> farming these years.&nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"59318","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-13\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The argument of organic against&nbsp;<strong>13</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong> seems in an inaccurate direction.</p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Organic Farming and Chemical Fertilizers&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The world’s population continues to climb. And despite the rise of high-tech agriculture, 800 million people don’t get enough to eat. Clearly, it’s time to rethink the food we eat and where it comes from. Feeding 9 billion people will take more than the same old farming practices, especially if we want to do it without felling rainforests and planting every last scrap of prairie. Finding food for all those people will tax farmers’ – and researchers’ – ingenuity to the limit. Yet already, precious aquifers that provide irrigation water for some of the world’s most productive farmlands are drying up or filling with seawater, and arable land in China is eroding to create vast dust storms that redden sunsets as far away as North America. ‘Agriculture must become the solution to environmental problems in 50 years. If we don’t have systems that make the environment better – not just hold the fort-then we’re in trouble,’ says Kenneth Cassman, an agronomist at the University of Nebraska at Lincoln. That view was echoed in January by the Curry report, a government panel that surveyed the future of farming and food in Britain.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>It’s easy to say agriculture has to do better, but what should this friendly farming of the future look like? Concerned consumers come up short at this point, facing what appears to be an ever-widening ideological divide. In one corner are the techno-optimists who put their faith in genetically modified crops, improved agrochemicals and computer-enhanced machinery; in the other are advocates of organic farming, who reject artificial chemicals and embrace back-to-nature techniques such as composting. Both sides cite plausible science to back their claims to the moral high ground, and both bring enough passion to the debate for many people to come away thinking we’re faced with a stark choice between two mutually incompatible options.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Not so. If you take off the ideological blinkers and simply ask how the world can produce the food it needs with the least environmental cost, a new middle way opens. The key is sustainability: whatever we do must not destroy the capital of soil and water we need to keep on producing. Like today’s organic farming, the intelligent farming of the future should pay much more attention to the health of its soil and the ecosystem it’s part of. But intelligent farming should also make shrewd and locally appropriate use of chemical fertilisers and pesticides. The most crucial ingredient in this new style of agriculture is not chemicals but information about what’s happening in each field and how to respond. Yet ironically, this key element may be the most neglected today.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Clearly, organic farming has all the warm, fuzzy sentiment on its side. An approach that eschews synthetic chemicals surely runs no risk of poisoning land and water. And its emphasis on building up natural ecosystems seems to be good for everyone. Perhaps these easy assumptions explain why sales of organic food across Europe are increasing by at least 50 per cent per year.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Going organic sounds idyllic – but it’s native, too. Organic agriculture has its own suite of environmental costs, which can be worse than those of conventional farming, especially if it were to become the world norm. But more fundamentally, the organic versus-chemical debate focuses on the wrong question. The issue isn’t what you put into a farm, but what you get out of it, both in terms of crop yields and pollutants, and what condition the farm is in when you’re done.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Take chemical fertilisers, which deliver nitrogen, an essential plant nutrient, to crops along with some phosphorus and potassium. It is a mantra of organic farming that these fertilisers are unwholesome, and plant nutrients must come from natural sources. But in fact, the main environmental damage done by chemical fertilisers as opposed to any other kind is through greenhouse gases-carbon dioxide from the fossil fuels used in their synthesis and nitrogen oxides released by their degradation. Excess nitrogen from chemical fertilisers can pollute groundwater, but so can excess nitrogen from organic manures.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>On the other hand, relying solely on chemical fertilisers to provide soil nutrients without doing other things to build healthy soil is damaging. Organic farmers don’t use chemical fertilisers, so they are very good at building soil fertility by working crop residues and manure into the soil, rotating grain with legumes that fix atmospheric nitrogen, and other techniques.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>This generates vital soil nutrients and also creates a soil that is richer in organic matter, so it retains better and is hospitable to the crop’s roots and creatures such as earthworms that help maintain soil fertility. Such soil also holds water better and therefore make more efficient use of both rainfall and irrigation water. And organic matter ties up CO2 in the soil, helping to offset emissions from burning fossil fuels and reduce global warming.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Advocates of organic farming like to point out that fields managed in this way can produce yields just as high as fields juiced up with synthetic fertilisers. For example, Bill Liebhardt, research manager at the Rodale Institute in Kutztown, Pennsylvania, recently compiled the results of such comparisons for corn, wheat, soybeans and tomatoes in the US and found that the organic fields averaged between 94 and 100 per cent of the yields of nearby conventional crops.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>But this optimistic picture tells only half the story. Farmers can’t grow such crops every year if they want to maintain or build soil nutrients without synthetic fertilisers. They need to alternate with soil-building crops such as pasture grasses and legumes such as alfalfa. So in the long term, the yield of staple grains such as wheat, rice and corn must go down. This is the biggest cost of organic farming. Vaclav Smil of the University of Manitoba in Winnipeg, Canada, estimates that if farmers worldwide gave up the 80 million tonnes of synthetic fertiliser they now use each year, total grain production would fall by at least half. Either farmers would have to double the amount of land they cultivate – at catastrophic cost to natural habitats – or billions of people would starve.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>K&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>That doesn’t mean farmers couldn’t get by with less fertiliser. Technologically advanced farmers in wealthy countries, for instance, can now monitor their yields hectare by hectare, or even more finely, throughout a huge field. They can then target their fertiliser to the parts of the field where it will do the most good, instead of responding to average conditions. This increases yield and decreases fertiliser use. Eventually, farmers may incorporate long-term weather forecasts into their planning as well, so that they can cut back on fertiliser use when the weather is likely to make harvests poor anyway, says Ron Olson, an agronomist with Cargill Fertilizer in Tampa, Florida.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>L&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Organic techniques certainly have their benefits, especially for poor farmers. But strict ‘organic agriculture’, which prohibits certain technologies and allows others, isn’t always better for the environment. Take herbicides, for example. These can leach into waterways and poison both wildlife and people. Just last month, researchers led by Tyrone Hayes at the University of California at Berkeley found that even low concentrations of atrazine, the most commonly used weedkiller in the US, can prevent frog tadpoles from developing properly.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8134&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8147","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Twin Study: Two of a Kind","book":"阅读还原集Vol.12","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.12 · Test 2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8147:59458:14","type":"choice","text":"14 Mentioned research conducted in Ohio","answer":"J","acceptedAnswers":["J"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Elsewhere in the marquee, Peter Miraldi, of Kent State University in Ohio, was trying to find out whether genes affect an individual’s motivation to communicate with others.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是提到在俄亥俄州进行的研究。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"research conducted in Ohio\"定位，在文章中找到提到俄亥俄州的研究内容。\n解题思路：J段提到了Peter Miraldi来自俄亥俄州的Kent State University，他正在进行一项关于基因是否影响个体与他人沟通动机的研究，因此J段包含了在俄亥俄州进行的研究信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J","Section K"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"59458","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has eleven paragraphs A-K. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-K, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once"},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8147:59458:15","type":"choice","text":"15 Medical contribution to the researches for twins","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：And twins can be used, within ethical limits, for medical experiments. A study that administered vitamin C to one twin and a placebo to the other found that it had no effect on the common cold.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是关于双胞胎研究的医学贡献。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Medical contribution\"可以定位到文章中关于医学实验和双胞胎研究的内容。\n解题思路：在D段中，明确提到了双胞胎可以在伦理范围内用于医学实验，并且举了一个具体的例子：给一个双胞胎服用维生素C，给另一个服用安慰剂，发现对普通感冒没有效果。这表明双胞胎研究在医学领域有实际的应用和贡献。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J","Section K"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"59458","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has eleven paragraphs A-K. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-K, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once"},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8147:59458:16","type":"choice","text":"16 Research situation under life-threatening conditions","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Josef Mengele, a Nazi doctor working at the Auschwitz extermination camp during the Second World War, was fascinated by twins. He sought them out among arrivals at the camp and preserved them from the gas-chambers for a series of brutal experiments.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是在生命威胁条件下进行的研究情况。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"life threatening conditions\"（生命威胁条件）可以定位到E段，该段描述了约瑟夫·门格勒在奥斯威辛灭绝营进行的研究，这是一个极端危险的环境。\n解题思路：E段提到约瑟夫·门格勒在奥斯威辛灭绝营对双胞胎进行了残酷的实验，这个环境是极其危险的，符合\"life threatening conditions\"的描述。因此，E段包含了题目所问的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J","Section K"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"59458","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has eleven paragraphs A-K. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-K, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once"},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8147:59458:17","type":"choice","text":"17 Data of similarities of identical twins","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Early work, for example, showed that the statistical correlation of skin-mole counts between identical twins was 0.4, while non-identical twins had a correlation of only 0.2. (A score of 1.0 implies perfect correlation, while a score of zero implies no correlation.)\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是关于同卵双胞胎的相似性的数据。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"Data of similarities\"和\"identical twins\"来定位答案。在B段中，原文提到了\"statistical correlation\"（统计相关性）和具体的百分比数据\"0.4\"和\"0.2\"，这与题干中的\"Data of similarities\"相对应。\n解题思路：原文B段明确提到了同卵双胞胎和非同卵双胞胎在皮肤痣数量上的统计相关性分别为0.4和0.2，并解释了相关性分数的含义。这里的\"statistical correlation\"可以理解为相似性的数据，而具体的数据\"0.4\"和\"0.2\"正是题目所询问的\"Data of similarities\"的具体表现形式。因此，B段包含了题目所要求的关于同卵双胞胎相似性的数据。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J","Section K"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"59458","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has eleven paragraphs A-K. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-K, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once"},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8147:59458:18","type":"choice","text":"18 Reasons that make one study unconvincing","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：After the war, Cyril Burt, a British psychologist who worked on the heredity of intelligence, tainted twin research with results that appear, in retrospect, to have been rather too good. Some of his data on identical twins who had been reared apart were probably faked.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“使一项研究不可信的原因”。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“unconvincing”一词可以定位到E段，该段提到了Cyril Burt的研究结果存在问题，数据可能是伪造的。\n解题思路：原文中明确指出Cyril Burt的研究结果“appear, in retrospect, to have been rather too good”，并且“Some of his data... were probably faked”，这直接说明了这项研究因为数据造假而不具备说服力，因此E段包含了题目所问的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H","Section I","Section J","Section K"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J","K"],"sourceGroupId":"59458","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has eleven paragraphs A-K. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-K, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once"},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8147:59459:19","type":"fill","text":"填写第 19 空","answer":"Francis Galton","acceptedAnswers":["Francis Galton"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Francis Galton, an early geneticist, realized that they came in two varieties: identical twins born from one egg and non-identical twins that had come from two.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是第一个进行双胞胎研究的科学家是谁。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"the first one that conducted research on twins\"可以定位到A段，其中提到了\"Francis Galton, an early geneticist\"。\n解题思路：根据原文句子可知，Francis Galton是最早进行双胞胎研究的科学家，因此答案为Francis Galton。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59459","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-20\nComplete the summary below.\nChoose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 19-20 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8147:59460:20","type":"fill","text":"填写第 20 空","answer":"1924","acceptedAnswers":["1924"],"explanation":"原文答案句：That insight turned out to be key, although it was not until 1924 that it was used to formulate what is known as the twin rule of pathology, and twin studies really got going.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“双胞胎研究在医学应用上最早是在哪一年开始的”。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词“medical application”和“year”来定位原文中关于双胞胎研究在医学上应用的具体年份。\n解题思路：原文中提到“it was not until 1924 that it was used to formulate what is known as the twin rule of pathology”，意思是直到1924年，双胞胎研究才被用来制定病理学上的双胞胎规则，这表明双胞胎研究在医学上的应用最早是在1924年。因此，答案为1924。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59460","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-20\nComplete the summary below.\nChoose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 19-20 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8147:59461:21-22-23","type":"choice","text":"Please choose THREE research fields that had been carried out in Ohio, Maryland and Twinsburgh?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\n- A. Sense: \"Paul Breslin, who works at the Monell Institute in Philadelphia, watched over several tables where twins sat sipping clear liquids from cups and making notes. It was the team’s third year at Twinsburg. Dr Breslin and his colleagues want to find out how genes influence human perception, particularly the senses of smell and taste...\"\n- E. Sound: \"Dennis Drayna, from the National Institute on Deafness and Other Communication Disorders, in Maryland, was studying hearing.\"\n- F. Baldness of men: \"next to Mr. Miraldi was a team of dermatologists from Case Western Reserve University in Cleveland. They are looking at the development of skin diseases and male-pattern baldness.\"\n对应段落：\n- A. Sense: G段\n- E. Sound: I段\n- F. Baldness of men: J段\n审题：题目要求选择三个在Ohio、Maryland和Twinsburg进行的科研领域。\n定位关键信息：\n1. 通过地点Ohio、Maryland和Twinsburg定位相关段落。Ohio对应J段（Case Western Reserve University in Cleveland），Maryland对应I段（National Institute on Deafness and Other Communication Disorders），Twinsburg对应G段（Twinsburg festival）。\n2. 分别提取各段中的科研领域：G段研究“senses of smell and taste”（对应A. Sense），I段研究“hearing”（对应E. Sound），J段研究“male-pattern baldness”（对应F. Baldness of men）。\n解题思路：\n1. 根据地点Ohio、Maryland和Twinsburg，分别定位到J段、I段和G段。\n2. J段明确提到研究“male-pattern baldness”（男性秃发），对应选项F。\n3. I段提到研究“hearing”（听觉），对应选项E。\n4. G段提到研究“senses of smell and taste”（嗅觉和味觉），对应选项A。\n5. 排除其他选项：B（Cancer）未在指定地点提及，C（Be allergic to Vitamin D）未提及，D（Mole heredity）出现在B段但未在指定地点进行。\n6. 最终确定答案为A、E、F。","options":["Sense","Cancer","Be allergic to Vitamin D","Mole heredity","Sound","Baldness of men"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59461","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 21-23\nChoose THREE correct answers","groupId":"59461-8147:59461:21-22-23"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8147:59461:21-22-23","type":"choice","text":"Please choose THREE research fields that had been carried out in Ohio, Maryland and Twinsburgh?","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\n- A. Sense: \"Paul Breslin, who works at the Monell Institute in Philadelphia, watched over several tables where twins sat sipping clear liquids from cups and making notes. It was the team’s third year at Twinsburg. Dr Breslin and his colleagues want to find out how genes influence human perception, particularly the senses of smell and taste...\"\n- E. Sound: \"Dennis Drayna, from the National Institute on Deafness and Other Communication Disorders, in Maryland, was studying hearing.\"\n- F. Baldness of men: \"next to Mr. Miraldi was a team of dermatologists from Case Western Reserve University in Cleveland. They are looking at the development of skin diseases and male-pattern baldness.\"\n对应段落：\n- A. Sense: G段\n- E. Sound: I段\n- F. Baldness of men: J段\n审题：题目要求选择三个在Ohio、Maryland和Twinsburg进行的科研领域。\n定位关键信息：\n1. 通过地点Ohio、Maryland和Twinsburg定位相关段落。Ohio对应J段（Case Western Reserve University in Cleveland），Maryland对应I段（National Institute on Deafness and Other Communication Disorders），Twinsburg对应G段（Twinsburg festival）。\n2. 分别提取各段中的科研领域：G段研究“senses of smell and taste”（对应A. Sense），I段研究“hearing”（对应E. Sound），J段研究“male-pattern baldness”（对应F. Baldness of men）。\n解题思路：\n1. 根据地点Ohio、Maryland和Twinsburg，分别定位到J段、I段和G段。\n2. J段明确提到研究“male-pattern baldness”（男性秃发），对应选项F。\n3. I段提到研究“hearing”（听觉），对应选项E。\n4. G段提到研究“senses of smell and taste”（嗅觉和味觉），对应选项A。\n5. 排除其他选项：B（Cancer）未在指定地点提及，C（Be allergic to Vitamin D）未提及，D（Mole heredity）出现在B段但未在指定地点进行。\n6. 最终确定答案为A、E、F。","options":["Sense","Cancer","Be allergic to Vitamin D","Mole heredity","Sound","Baldness of men"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59461","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 21-23\nChoose THREE correct answers","groupId":"59461-8147:59461:21-22-23"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8147:59461:21-22-23","type":"choice","text":"Please choose THREE research fields that had been carried out in Ohio, Maryland and Twinsburgh?","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\n- A. Sense: \"Paul Breslin, who works at the Monell Institute in Philadelphia, watched over several tables where twins sat sipping clear liquids from cups and making notes. It was the team’s third year at Twinsburg. Dr Breslin and his colleagues want to find out how genes influence human perception, particularly the senses of smell and taste...\"\n- E. Sound: \"Dennis Drayna, from the National Institute on Deafness and Other Communication Disorders, in Maryland, was studying hearing.\"\n- F. Baldness of men: \"next to Mr. Miraldi was a team of dermatologists from Case Western Reserve University in Cleveland. They are looking at the development of skin diseases and male-pattern baldness.\"\n对应段落：\n- A. Sense: G段\n- E. Sound: I段\n- F. Baldness of men: J段\n审题：题目要求选择三个在Ohio、Maryland和Twinsburg进行的科研领域。\n定位关键信息：\n1. 通过地点Ohio、Maryland和Twinsburg定位相关段落。Ohio对应J段（Case Western Reserve University in Cleveland），Maryland对应I段（National Institute on Deafness and Other Communication Disorders），Twinsburg对应G段（Twinsburg festival）。\n2. 分别提取各段中的科研领域：G段研究“senses of smell and taste”（对应A. Sense），I段研究“hearing”（对应E. Sound），J段研究“male-pattern baldness”（对应F. Baldness of men）。\n解题思路：\n1. 根据地点Ohio、Maryland和Twinsburg，分别定位到J段、I段和G段。\n2. J段明确提到研究“male-pattern baldness”（男性秃发），对应选项F。\n3. I段提到研究“hearing”（听觉），对应选项E。\n4. G段提到研究“senses of smell and taste”（嗅觉和味觉），对应选项A。\n5. 排除其他选项：B（Cancer）未在指定地点提及，C（Be allergic to Vitamin D）未提及，D（Mole heredity）出现在B段但未在指定地点进行。\n6. 最终确定答案为A、E、F。","options":["Sense","Cancer","Be allergic to Vitamin D","Mole heredity","Sound","Baldness of men"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59461","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 21-23\nChoose THREE correct answers","groupId":"59461-8147:59461:21-22-23"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8147:59462:24-25-26","type":"choice","text":"Please choose THREE results that had been verified in this passage.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\n- A. \"THE scientific study of twins goes back to the late 19th century, when Francis Galton, an early geneticist, realized that they came in two varieties: identical twins born from one egg and non-identical twins that had come from two. \"\n-B. \"The twin rule of pathology states that any heritable disease will be more concordant (that is, more likely to be jointly present or absent) in identical twins than in non-identical twins\"\n-D. \"Twin research has shown that whether or not someone takes up smoking is determined mainly by environmental factors, but once he does so, how much he smokes is largely down to his genes. \"\n对应段落：\n- A. : A段\n- B. : B段\n- D. : C段\n审题：题目要求选择三个在文章中已被验证的结果。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"results that had been verified\"定位到文章中明确提到的研究结果或结论。\n解题思路：选项A直接对应A段中明确说明的同卵双胞胎来自一个卵子，异卵双胞胎来自两个卵子的科学事实，这是已被验证的结论。选项B对应B段中提到的\"any heritable disease will be more concordant in identical twins than in non-identical twins\"，即同卵双胞胎的遗传相关性比异卵双胞胎更接近，这也是已被验证的研究结果。选项D对应C段中提到的\"but once he does so, how much he smokes is largely down to his genes\"，明确说明，虽然是否吸烟主要由环境决定，但吸烟量的多少很大程度上取决于基因。这一结论已被验证。其他选项要么未被提及，要么与原文表述不符。","options":["Non-identical twins come from different eggs.","Genetic relation between identical twins is closer than non-identical ones.","Vitamin C has evident effect on a cold.","Genetic influence to smoking is superior to environment’s.","If a pregnant woman eats too much sweet would lead to skin disease.","Hair loss has been found to be connected with skin problem."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59462","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nChoose THREE correct answers","groupId":"59462-8147:59462:24-25-26"},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8147:59462:24-25-26","type":"choice","text":"Please choose THREE results that had been verified in this passage.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\n- A. \"THE scientific study of twins goes back to the late 19th century, when Francis Galton, an early geneticist, realized that they came in two varieties: identical twins born from one egg and non-identical twins that had come from two. \"\n-B. \"The twin rule of pathology states that any heritable disease will be more concordant (that is, more likely to be jointly present or absent) in identical twins than in non-identical twins\"\n-D. \"Twin research has shown that whether or not someone takes up smoking is determined mainly by environmental factors, but once he does so, how much he smokes is largely down to his genes. \"\n对应段落：\n- A. : A段\n- B. : B段\n- D. : C段\n审题：题目要求选择三个在文章中已被验证的结果。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"results that had been verified\"定位到文章中明确提到的研究结果或结论。\n解题思路：选项A直接对应A段中明确说明的同卵双胞胎来自一个卵子，异卵双胞胎来自两个卵子的科学事实，这是已被验证的结论。选项B对应B段中提到的\"any heritable disease will be more concordant in identical twins than in non-identical twins\"，即同卵双胞胎的遗传相关性比异卵双胞胎更接近，这也是已被验证的研究结果。选项D对应C段中提到的\"but once he does so, how much he smokes is largely down to his genes\"，明确说明，虽然是否吸烟主要由环境决定，但吸烟量的多少很大程度上取决于基因。这一结论已被验证。其他选项要么未被提及，要么与原文表述不符。","options":["Non-identical twins come from different eggs.","Genetic relation between identical twins is closer than non-identical ones.","Vitamin C has evident effect on a cold.","Genetic influence to smoking is superior to environment’s.","If a pregnant woman eats too much sweet would lead to skin disease.","Hair loss has been found to be connected with skin problem."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59462","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nChoose THREE correct answers","groupId":"59462-8147:59462:24-25-26"},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8147:59462:24-25-26","type":"choice","text":"Please choose THREE results that had been verified in this passage.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\n- A. \"THE scientific study of twins goes back to the late 19th century, when Francis Galton, an early geneticist, realized that they came in two varieties: identical twins born from one egg and non-identical twins that had come from two. \"\n-B. \"The twin rule of pathology states that any heritable disease will be more concordant (that is, more likely to be jointly present or absent) in identical twins than in non-identical twins\"\n-D. \"Twin research has shown that whether or not someone takes up smoking is determined mainly by environmental factors, but once he does so, how much he smokes is largely down to his genes. \"\n对应段落：\n- A. : A段\n- B. : B段\n- D. : C段\n审题：题目要求选择三个在文章中已被验证的结果。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"results that had been verified\"定位到文章中明确提到的研究结果或结论。\n解题思路：选项A直接对应A段中明确说明的同卵双胞胎来自一个卵子，异卵双胞胎来自两个卵子的科学事实，这是已被验证的结论。选项B对应B段中提到的\"any heritable disease will be more concordant in identical twins than in non-identical twins\"，即同卵双胞胎的遗传相关性比异卵双胞胎更接近，这也是已被验证的研究结果。选项D对应C段中提到的\"but once he does so, how much he smokes is largely down to his genes\"，明确说明，虽然是否吸烟主要由环境决定，但吸烟量的多少很大程度上取决于基因。这一结论已被验证。其他选项要么未被提及，要么与原文表述不符。","options":["Non-identical twins come from different eggs.","Genetic relation between identical twins is closer than non-identical ones.","Vitamin C has evident effect on a cold.","Genetic influence to smoking is superior to environment’s.","If a pregnant woman eats too much sweet would lead to skin disease.","Hair loss has been found to be connected with skin problem."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59462","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nChoose THREE correct answers","groupId":"59462-8147:59462:24-25-26"}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"59461-8147:59461:21-22-23","numbers":[21,22,23],"selectionCount":3,"answers":["A","E","F"]},{"id":"59462-8147:59462:24-25-26","numbers":[24,25,26],"selectionCount":3,"answers":["A","B","D"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59458","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-18\nThe reading passage has eleven paragraphs A-K. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-K, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once","html":"<p><strong>14</strong> Mentioned research conducted in Ohio <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"59459","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-20\nComplete the summary below.\nChoose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 19-20 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The first one that conducted research on twins is called <strong>19</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"59460","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 19-20\nComplete the summary below.\nChoose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 19-20 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>He separated twins \ninto two categories: non-identical and identical twins.&nbsp;</p><p>The twin research was used in medical application in as early as the year of <strong>20</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"59461","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 21-23\nChoose THREE correct answers","html":"<p><strong>Please choose THREE research fields that had been carried out in Ohio, Maryland and Twinsburgh?</strong></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"59462","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 24-26\nChoose THREE correct answers","html":"<p><strong>Please choose THREE results that had been verified in this passage.</strong></p>","firstNumber":24}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Twin Study: Two of a Kind</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>THE scientific study of twins goes back to the late 19th century, when Francis Galton, an early geneticist, realized that they came in two varieties: identical twins born from one egg and non-identical twins that had come from two. That insight turned out to be key, although it was not until 1924 that it was used to formulate what is known as the twin rule of pathology, and twin studies really got going.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The twin rule of pathology states that any heritable disease will be more concordant (that is, more likely to be jointly present or absent) in identical twins than in non-identical twins – and, in turn, will be more concordant in non-identical twins than in non-siblings. Early work, for example, showed that the statistical correlation of skin-mole counts between identical twins was 0.4, while non-identical twins had a correlation of only 0.2. (A score of 1.0 implies a perfect correlation, while a score of zero implies no correlation.) This result suggests that moles are heritable, but it also implies that there is an environmental component to the development of moles, otherwise the correlation in identical twins would be close to 1.0.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Twin research has shown that whether or not someone takes up smoking is determined mainly by environmental factors, but once he does so, how much he smokes is largely down to his genes. And while a person&#39;s religion is clearly a cultural attribute, there is a strong genetic component to religious fundamentalism. Twin studies are also unraveling the heritability of various aspects of human personality. Traits from neuroticism and anxiety to thrill- and novelty-seeking all have large genetic components. Parenting matters, but it does not determine personality in the way that some had thought.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>More importantly, perhaps, twin studies are helping the understanding of diseases such as cancer, asthma, osteoporosis, arthritis and immune disorders. And twins can be used, within ethical limits, for medical experiments. A study that administered vitamin C to one twin and a placebo to the other found that it had no effect on the common cold. The lesson from all today&#39;s twin studies is that most human traits are at least partially influenced by genes. However, for the most part, the age-old dichotomy between nature and nurture is not very useful. Many genetic programs are open to input from the environment, and genes are frequently switched on or off by environmental signals. It is also possible that genes themselves influence their environment. Some humans have an innate preference for participation in sports. Others are drawn to novelty. Might people also be drawn to certain kinds of friends and types of experience? In this way, a person&#39;s genes might shape the environment they act in as much as the environment shapes the actions of the genes.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In the past, such research has been controversial. Josef Mengele, a Nazi doctor working at the Auschwitz extermination camp during the Second World War, was fascinated by twins. He sought them out among arrivals at the camp and preserved them from the gas-chambers for a series of brutal experiments. After the war, Cyril Burt, a British psychologist who worked on the heredity of intelligence, tainted twin research with results that appear, in retrospect, to have been rather too good. Some of his data on identical twins who had been reared apart were probably faked. In any case, the prevailing ideology in the social sciences after the war was Marxist, and disliked suggestions that differences in human potential might have underlying genetic causes. Twin studies were thus viewed with suspicion.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The ideological pendulum has swung back; however, as the human genome project and its aftermath have turned genes from abstract concepts to real pieces of DNA. The role of genes in sensitive areas such as intelligence is acknowledged by all but a few die-hards. The interesting questions now concern how nature and nurture interact to produce particular bits of biology, rather than which of the two is more important. Twin studies, which are a good way to ask these questions, are back in fashion, and many twins are enthusiastic participants in this research.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Research at the Twinsburg festival began in a small way, with a single stand in 1979. Gradually, news spread, and more scientists began turning up. This year, half a dozen groups of researchers were lodged in a specially pitched research tent. In one corner of this tent, Paul Breslin, who works at the Monell Institute in Philadelphia, watched over several tables where twins sat sipping clear liquids from cups and making notes. It was the team&#39;s third year at Twinsburg. Dr Breslin and his colleagues want to find out how genes influence human perception, particularly the senses of smell and taste and those (warmth, cold, pain, tingle, itch and so on) that result from stimulation of the skin. Perception is an example of something that is probably influenced by both genes and experience. Even before birth, people are exposed to flavours such as chocolate, garlic, mint and vanilla that pass intact into the bloodstream, and thus to the fetus. Though it is not yet clear whether such pre-natal exposure shapes taste-perception, there is evidence that it shapes preferences for foods encountered later in life.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>However, there are clearly genetic influences at work, as well-for example in the ability to taste quinine. Some people experience this as intensely bitter, even when it is present at very low levels. Others, whose genetic endowment is different, are less bothered by it. Twin studies make this extremely clear. Within a pair of identical twins, either both, or neither, will find quinine hard to swallow. Non-identical twins will agree less frequently.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>On the other side of the tent Dennis Drayna, from the National Institute on Deafness and Other Communication Disorders, in Maryland, was studying hearing. He wants to know what happens to sounds after they reach the ear. It is not clear, he says, whether sound is processed into sensation mostly in the ear or in the brain. Dr Drayna has already been involved in a twin study which revealed that the perception of musical pitch is highly heritable. At Twinsburg, he is playing different words, or parts of words, into the left and right ears of his twinned volunteers. The composite of the two sounds that an individual reports hearing depends on how he processes this diverse information and that, Dr Drayna believes, may well be influenced by genetics.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Elsewhere in the marquee, Peter Miraldi, of Kent State University in Ohio, was trying to find out whether genes affect an individual&#39;s motivation to communicate with others. A number of twin studies have shown that personality and sociability are heritable, so he thinks this is fertile ground. And next to Mr. Miraldi was a team of dermatologists from Case Western Reserve University in Cleveland. They are looking at the development of skin disease and male-pattern baldness. The goal of the latter piece of research is to find the genes responsible for making men&#39;s hair fall out.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>K</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The busiest part of the tent, however, was the queue for forensic-science research into fingerprints. The origins of this study are shrouded in mystery. For many months, the festival&#39;s organisers have been convinced that the Secret Service – the American government agency responsible for, among other things, the safety of the president – is behind it. When The Economist contacted the Secret Service for more information, we were referred to Steve Nash, who is chairman of the International Association for Identification (IAI), and is also a detective in the scientific investigations section of the Marin County Sheriff&#39;s Office in California. The IAI, based in Minnesota, is an organisation of forensic scientists from around the world. Among other things, it publishes the Journal of Forensic Identification.</p><p><br/></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8147&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8148","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Global Warming in New Zealand 2","book":"阅读还原集Vol.12","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 2","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.12 · Test 2 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8148:59435:27","type":"choice","text":"What is the main idea of the first paragraph?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：New Zealand is expected to warm by about 3℃ over the next century. The northern polar regions will be more than 6℃ warmer, while the large continents – also the largest centres of population – will be 4℃ or warmer. In contrast, the Southern Ocean, which surrounds New Zealand, may warm by only 2°C. The sea will act as an air conditioner and in this aspect, New Zealand’s location is comparatively fortunate.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是第一段的主要思想是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"the main idea of the first paragraph\"定位到A段，该段主要讨论了新西兰在未来一个世纪的气候变化情况。\n解题思路：根据A段的内容，新西兰预计在未来一个世纪内气温上升约3℃，而北极地区将上升超过6℃，大陆地区将上升4℃或更多。相比之下，环绕新西兰的南大洋可能只上升2℃。海洋将起到空调的作用，在这方面，新西兰的位置相对幸运。因此，A段的主要思想是新西兰由于被海洋环绕，在未来一个世纪内不会像其他国家那样升温那么多。所以正确答案是D。","options":["The air condition in New Zealand will maintain a high quality because of the ocean.","The Southern Ocean will remain at a constant strength.","The continents will warm more than the point.","New Zealand will not warm as much as other countries in the next century because it is surrounded by sea."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59435","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8148:59436:28","type":"choice","text":"What does the writer say about New Zealand's variable weather?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：These variables will continue unaffected so that, although the general pattern will be for rising temperatures, the warming trend may not be uniform.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问作者关于新西兰多变的天气说了什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"New Zealand’s variable weather\"定位到B段，该段讨论了新西兰气候的变异性。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句可知，这些变量（指天气变异性）将继续不受影响，因此尽管总体模式是气温上升，但变暖趋势可能不会均匀。这与选项B\"多变的天气将继续，不受全球变暖的影响\"完全一致。其他选项A、C、D在原文中均未提及或与原文内容不符。","options":["Temperature changes of 1°C will not be seem important in future.","Variable weather will continue, unchanged by global warming.","There was an unusually small amount of variation in 2006-2007.","Summer temperatures will vary but winter ones will be consistent."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59436","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8148:59437:29","type":"choice","text":"What is the predicted impact of conditions in the ocean to the south of New Zealand?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：As the world warms, the great band of west winds that circle Antarctica will become stronger. This has already been observed, and its impact on New Zealand is likely to be profound, stronger, more frequent west winds will bring increased, sometimes catastrophic rainfall to the west coast of the country and create drier conditions in some eastern regions that are already drought-prone.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“预计海洋条件会对新西兰南部造成什么影响”。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“conditions in the ocean to the south of New Zealand”定位到C段，该段明确提到海洋条件的变化对新西兰南部的影响。\n解题思路：C段提到，随着全球变暖，环绕南极洲的西风带会变得更强，这将给新西兰带来更强烈、更频繁的西风，导致西海岸降雨增加，东部干旱地区变得更加干燥。这与选项A“新西兰将更多地受到洪水和干旱的影响”完全一致，因此A是正确答案。","options":["New Zealand will be more affected by floods and droughts.","Antarctica will not be adversely affected by warming.","The band of west winds will move further to the south.","The usual west wind will no longer be reliable."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59437","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8148:59438:30","type":"choice","text":"The writer mentions ‘moisture deficit’ to show","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In the drier regions, the average moisture deficit – that is,the difference between the amount of water in soils available to plants and the amount plants need for optimum growth – will increase. Soils could go into moisture deficit earlier in the growing season and the deficits could last longer into autumn than at present. What we think of today as a medium-severity drought could be an almost annual occurrence by the end of the century.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问作者提到“水分赤字”是为了说明什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的“moisture deficit”定位到D段，找到相关句子。\n解题思路：原文提到在更干燥的地区，水分赤字会增加，土壤会在生长季节更早出现水分赤字，赤字持续时间会更长。现在被认为是中等严重程度的干旱到本世纪末可能几乎每年都会发生。这说明水分赤字的出现会导致生长条件恶化，因为植物可用的水分减少，干旱更加频繁和严重。因此，作者提到“水分赤字”是为了说明生长条件将恶化，对应选项C。","options":["the droughts will be shorter but more severe.","how the growing season will become longer.","how growing conditions will deteriorate.","that farmers should alter the make-up of soils."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59438","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8148:59439:31","type":"choice","text":"What are the implications of global warming for New Zealand’s skiing industry","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The amount of snow that falls may actually increase, however, even in some northern centres, owing to the intensification of precipitation.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问全球变暖对新西兰的滑雪产业有什么影响。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的关键词\"skiing\"和\"global warming\"定位到D段，该段提到了滑雪场和降雪量的变化。\n解题思路：原文明确提到\"the amount of snow that falls may actually increase\"，即降雪量可能会增加，这与选项D\" warming may provide more snow for some ski locations\"完全一致。其他选项A、B、C都与原文内容不符，原文并未提到滑雪场会降低海拔、滑雪季节会推迟或北方滑雪场会南迁。因此，正确答案是D。","options":["skiing may move to lower altitudes in the future.","the ski season will be later in the year than at present.","the northern ski field will have to move to the south.","warming may provide more snow for some ski locations."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59439","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8148:59440:32","type":"choice","text":"The writer refers to NIWA’s latest studies in the paragraph E to show","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The latest studies conducted by the National Institute for Water and Atmospheric. Research (NIWA), however, suggest that by the end of the century, warming over the Southern Alps could be significantly greater than over the rest of the country.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问作者在第三段引用NIWA的最新研究是为了说明什么。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"NIWA’s latest studies\"和\"3rd paragraph\"。根据文章段落顺序，E段是第三段，段落中提到了NIWA的最新研究，因此定位到E段。\n解题思路：原文中E段提到NIWA的最新研究表明，到本世纪末，南阿尔卑斯山的变暖程度可能显著高于该国其他地区。这说明作者引用该研究是为了说明一个特定地区（南阿尔卑斯山）可能如何受到变暖的影响。这与选项A的描述一致，即\"how a particular place could be affected by warming.\" 其他选项B、C、D的内容在原文中并未提及或与原文不符。","options":["how a particular place could be affected by warming.","that the warming trend has been intensifying since 1978.","that freezing levels will rise throughout the century.","how the growth of glaciers is likely to cause damage."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59440","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8148:59441:33","type":"choice","text":"Rising sea levels\nThe extent of future sea level rises around New Zealand is uncertain and may be determined in the 33 ____ .","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The extent of future sea level rises around New Zealand is uncertain and may be determined in the polar regions.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是未来海平面上升的程度在新西兰周围是不确定的，可能由什么决定。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"sea level rises\"和\"New Zealand\"定位到F段第一句话，其中提到了海平面上升的不确定性以及可能由极地地区的冰融化导致。\n解题思路：根据原文F段第一句话\"The extent of future sea level rises around New Zealand is uncertain and may be determined in the polar regions.\"可以确定，未来海平面上升的程度在新西兰周围是不确定的，可能由极地地区的冰融化导致。因此，答案为D。","options":["agriculture production","tropical waters","tidal waves","polar regions","global warming","coastal land","high tides"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59441","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 33-35\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-G, below. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8148:59441:34","type":"choice","text":"Another variable is sudden rises in sea level caused by bad weather. Higher sea levels can lead to reduced 34 ____","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Unlike a slow-motion tsunami, not only does a rise in sea level increase the potential for this sort of damage, but it also has less immediate impacts. One potentially grave outcome is that groundwater systems may become contaminated with saltwater, spoiling them for the irrigation of farmland, which in turn could diminish crop harvests. Similarly, overtime, estuaries may be enlarged by erosion as tidal influences reach further upstream, altering the contours of whole shorelines and initiating further unforeseen consequences.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“Another variable is sudden rises in sea level caused by bad weather. Higher sea levels can lead to reduced”，即另一种变量是恶劣天气引起的海平面突然上升，更高的海平面会导致什么减少。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词“sudden rises in sea level caused by bad weather”和“Higher sea levels can lead to reduced”，在文章中定位到F段，其中提到了“rise in sea level”和“diminish crop harvests”。\n解题思路：在F段中，原文提到“groundwater systems may become contaminated with saltwater, spoiling them for the irrigation of farmland, which in turn could diminish crop harvests.”，即海平面上升会导致地下水系统被盐水污染，从而影响农田灌溉，进而减少农作物产量。因此，题目中的空格应填入与“crop harvests”相对应的答案。根据选项，正确答案为A。","options":["agriculture production","tropical waters","tidal waves","polar regions","global warming","coastal land","high tides"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59441","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 33-35\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-G, below. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8148:59441:35","type":"choice","text":"and result in changes to the shape of 35 ____ .","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Similarly, overtime, estuaries may be enlarged by erosion as tidal influences reach further upstream, altering the contours of whole shorelines and initiating further unforeseen consequences.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是全球变暖导致海平面上升，进而对海岸线的形状产生什么变化。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"changes to the shape of\"定位到F段末句，该句提到海平面上升会导致\"altering the contours of whole shorelines\"。\n解题思路：原文中的\"altering the contours of whole shorelines\"与题目中的\"changes to the shape of\"意思一致，\"contours of whole shorelines\"指的是整个海岸线的轮廓或形状，因此答案为F。","options":["agriculture production","tropical waters","tidal waves","polar regions","global warming","coastal land","high tides"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59441","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 33-35\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-G, below. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8148:59442:36","type":"choice","text":"The natural world is less responsive to challenges than humans.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Human systems are better able to adapt to change than natural ecosystems because humans can see a problem coming and plan a response.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“自然世界对挑战的应对不如人类”是否与文章作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“natural world”和“humans”可以定位到G段的第一句话。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到“Human systems are better able to adapt to change than natural ecosystems”，即人类系统比自然生态系统更能适应变化。这与题目中的表述“自然世界对挑战的应对不如人类”意思一致，因此答案为A（YES）。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59442","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the Reading Passage 3? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is trueNO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8148:59443:37","type":"choice","text":"The agricultural sector is being too conservative and resistant to innovation.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Farmers and horticulturalists have made considerable advances, replacing crops they grow to better suit the new conditions.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问农业部门是否过于保守且抵制创新。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"agricultural sector\"（农业部门）和\"conservative and resistant to innovation\"（保守且抵制创新）定位到G段。\n解题思路：原文提到农民和园艺家已经取得了显著进展，他们更换了农作物以适应新条件，说明农业部门正在积极适应变化并进行创新，而不是保守或抵制创新。因此，题干的说法与原文相反，应选择\"NO\"。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59443","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the Reading Passage 3? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is trueNO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8148:59444:38","type":"choice","text":"Global warming is slow; it will affect different regions in different ways.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The Ocean to the south of New Zealand will have one important effect. As the world warms, the great band of west winds that circle Antarctica will become stronger. This has already been observed, and its impact on New Zealand is likely to be profound, stronger, more frequent west winds will bring increased, sometimes catastrophic rainfall to the west coast of the country and create drier conditions in some eastern regions that are already drought-prone. At the same time, the general warming will spread south.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问“全球变暖是缓慢的；它将以不同的方式影响不同的地区。”是否与文章作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“global warming”和“different regions in different ways”定位到C段，该段提到全球变暖对不同地区的影响不同。\n解题思路：文章C段提到全球变暖对不同地区的影响不同，但并未提及全球变暖是缓慢的。因此，题目中的“全球变暖是缓慢的”这一信息在文章中没有明确提及，无法判断其是否与作者观点一致。故答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59444","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the Reading Passage 3? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is trueNO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8148:59445:39","type":"choice","text":"The tuatara is vulnerable to changes in climate conditions.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Their sex is determined by the temperature at which the eggs are incubated in warm (currently above 22℃) condition become predominately male – and now males already outnumber females by nearly two to one in some island refuges.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问“tuatara易受气候变化的影响”是否与作者观点一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“tuatara”和“vulnerable to changes in climate conditions”定位到H段，该段明确提到tuatara的性别由孵化温度决定，且高温会导致雄性比例增加，说明其易受气候影响。\n解题思路：原文指出tuatara的性别受温度影响，且高温环境下雄性数量已超过雌性，直接说明其易受气候变化影响，因此题目陈述与作者观点一致，答案为YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59445","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the Reading Passage 3? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is trueNO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8148:59446:40","type":"choice","text":"New Zealand must reduce carbon emission if global warming is to be slowed.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：New Zealand’s own greenhouse emissions are tiny – around 0.5% of the global total. Even if New Zealanders were to achieve the government’s target of carbon neutrality, this would have no discernable impact on global climate change.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问“如果全球变暖要被减缓，新西兰必须减少碳排放”是否与作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“New Zealand”、“reduce carbon emission”和“slow global warming”定位到H段，其中提到新西兰的碳排放量很小，即使实现碳中和也对全球气候变暖没有明显影响。\n解题思路：原文明确指出新西兰的碳排放量仅占全球总量的0.5%，即使完全实现碳中和也无法对全球气候变暖产生显著影响。因此，题目中“新西兰必须减少碳排放以减缓全球变暖”的说法与原文矛盾，作者并未支持这一观点。答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59446","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the Reading Passage 3? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is trueNO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59435","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>What is the main idea of the first paragraph?</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"59436","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>What does the writer say about New Zealand&#39;s variable weather?</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"59437","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>What is the predicted impact of conditions in the ocean to the south of New Zealand?</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"59438","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>The writer mentions ‘moisture deficit’ to show</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"59439","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>What are the implications of global warming for New Zealand’s skiing industry</strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"59440","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-32\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>The writer refers to NIWA’s latest studies in the paragraph E to show</strong></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"59441","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 33-35\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-G, below. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap.","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> agriculture production &nbsp;</p><p><strong>B</strong> tropical waters &nbsp;</p><p><strong>C</strong> tidal waves&nbsp;</p><p><strong>D</strong> polar regions &nbsp;</p><p><strong>E</strong> global warming &nbsp;</p><p><strong>F</strong> coastal land &nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>G</strong> high tides&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Rising sea levels</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>The extent of future sea level rises around New Zealand is uncertain and may be determined in the <strong>33</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[33] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"59442","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the Reading Passage 3? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is trueNO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The natural world is less responsive to challenges than humans.</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"59443","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the Reading Passage 3? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is trueNO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The agricultural sector is being too conservative and resistant to innovation.</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"59444","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the Reading Passage 3? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is trueNO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Global warming is slow; it will affect different regions in different ways.</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"59445","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the Reading Passage 3? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is trueNO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The tuatara is vulnerable to changes in climate conditions.</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"59446","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the Reading Passage 3? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is trueNO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>New Zealand must reduce carbon emission if global warming is to be slowed.</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Global Warming in New Zealand 2&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>New Zealand is expected to warm by about 3℃ over the next century. The northern polar regions will be more than 6℃ warmer, while the large continents – also the largest centres of population – will be 4℃ or warmer. In contrast, the Southern Ocean, which surrounds New Zealand, may warm by only 2°C. The sea will act as an air conditioner and in this aspect, New Zealand’s location is comparatively fortunate.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>Any predictions are complicated by the variability of New Zealand’s climate. The annual temperature can fluctuate as much as 1°C above or below the long-term average. The early summer of 2006-2007, for instance, was notably cool, thanks in part to the iceberg that drifted up the east coast. A few months later, warm water from the Tasman Sea helped make May 2007 unusually hot. These variables will continue unaffected so that, although the general pattern will be for rising temperatures, the warming trend may not be uniform.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The Ocean to the south of New Zealand will have one important effect. As the world warms, the great band of west winds that circle Antarctica will become stronger. This has already been observed, and its impact on New Zealand is likely to be profound, stronger, more frequent west winds will bring increased, sometimes catastrophic rainfall to the west coast of the country and create drier conditions in some eastern regions that are already drought-prone. At the same time, the general warming will spread south.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>Furthermore, in the drier regions, the average moisture deficit – that is,the difference between the amount of water in soils available to plants and the amount plants need for optimum growth – will increase. Soils could go into moisture deficit earlier in the growing season and the deficits could last longer into autumn than at present. What we think of today as a medium-severity drought could be an almost annual occurrence by the end of the century. One direct consequence of warmer – and shorter – winters will be a reduction in snow cover. The permanent snow line in the mountains will rise, while snow cover below this will be shorter-lived. The amount of snow that falls may actually increase, however, even in some northern centres, owing to the intensification of precipitation. Ski-field base station may eventually have to be moved upwards to be within reach of the new snow line but there could still be plenty of the white stuff up there.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>There will also be a marked impact on New Zealand’s glaciers. Over the last 100 years, the glaciers have been reduced by 35%, although since 1978 increase snowfall has offset the effect of warming. The latest studies conducted by the National Institute for Water and Atmospheric. Research (NIWA), however, suggest that by the end of the century, warming over the Southern Alps could be significantly greater than over the rest of the country.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>Sea levels around New Zealand have risen by 25cm since the middle of the 9th century and by 7 cm since 1990. Predictions for the coming years cover a wide range, however, partly because of unknown rises resulting from the melting of the ice in the Arctic, Greenland and Antarctica. In addition, sea level at any given time is affected by many different factors, one of which is called a storm surge. When a storm coincides with a high tide along low lying coastal areas, this bulge raises the tide higher than normal, creating a surge unlike a slow-motion tsunami, not only does a rise in sea level increase the potential for this sort of damage, but it also has less immediate impacts. One potentially grave outcome is that groundwater systems may become contaminated with saltwater, spoiling them for the irrigation of farmland, which in turn could diminish crop harvests. Similarly, overtime, estuaries may be enlarged by erosion as tidal influences reach further upstream, altering the contours of whole shorelines and initiating further unforeseen consequences.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The impacts these changes will have on New Zealand are difficult to generalize. Human systems are better able to adapt to change than natural ecosystems because humans can see a problem coming and plan a response. Farmers and horticulturalists have made considerable advances, replacing crops they grow to better suit the new conditions. However, plant breeders will need to show considerable ingenuity if they can overcome the acute water shortages that are forecast.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>For natural ecosystems the rate of change is crucial. If it is low, the plants and animals and fish will be able to ‘keep up’; if it is high, only the most adaptable species-those that can survive in the widest range of ecological niches-are likely to survive. Species adapted to only a narrow range of conditions or food sources will find adaptation much more difficult. Take tuatara, for instance. Their sex is determined by the temperature at which the eggs are incubated in warm (currently above 22℃) condition become predominately male – and now males already outnumber females by nearly two to one in some island refuges. In the mountains, as the permanent snow line moves upwards, the tolerance zones of some alpine plants and animals may simply disappear. It should also be remembered that global warming is just that – a global phenomenon.&#39;New Zealand&#39;s own greenhouse emissions are tiny – around 0.5% of the global total. Even if New Zealanders were to achieve the government’s target of carbon neutrality, this would have no discernable impact on global climate change.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>I&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>The changes that global warming is going to bring to New Zealand during the 21st century are going to be significant, but where the country is likely to be most vulnerable is with respect to climate change elsewhere. New Zealand may warm more slowly than most places, but if its major export markets undergo damaging change, the economic impact will be severe.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8148&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8088","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Voyage of Going: Beyond the Blue Line","book":"阅读还原集Vol.12","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test1","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.12 · Test1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8088:59273:1","type":"choice","text":"Captain cook once expected the Hawaii might speak another language of people from other pacific islands.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Imagine Cook’s surprise, then, when the natives of Hawaii came paddling out in their canoes and greeted him in a familiar tongue, one he had heard on virtually every mote of inhabited land he had visited.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“詹姆斯·库克船长曾期望夏威夷人可能会说来自其他太平洋岛屿的另一种语言。”\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“Captain Cook”、“Hawaii”和“another language”可以定位到文章A段中描述库克船长发现夏威夷时，夏威夷人用一种熟悉的语言向他打招呼的句子。\n解题思路：原文中提到库克船长对夏威夷人使用一种他熟悉的语言感到惊讶，这表明他之前预期夏威夷人可能会说一种不同的语言。因此，题目中的陈述与文章信息一致，答案为YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59273","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage"},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8088:59274:2","type":"choice","text":"Captain cook depicted number of cultural aspects of Polynesians in his journal.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：he later wondered in his journal: ‘How shall we account for this Nation spreading itself so far over this Vast Ocean?’\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“詹姆斯·库克在他的日记中描绘了波利尼西亚人的许多文化方面。”\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"Captain Cook\", \"journal\", \"cultural aspects of Polynesians\"定位到A段中关于库克日记的描述。\n解题思路：原文中库克在日记中只提到了对波利尼西亚人分布范围的疑问（'How shall we account for this Nation spreading itself so far over this Vast Ocean?'），并未提及任何关于波利尼西亚人文化方面的描述。因此，题目中的说法与原文信息不符，答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59274","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage"},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8088:59275:3","type":"choice","text":"Professor Spriggs and his research team went to the Efate to try to find the site of ancient cemetery.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It came to light only by luck. A backhoe operator, digging up topsoil on the grounds of a derelict coconut plantation, scraped open a grave – the first of dozens in a burial ground some 3,000 years old.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问Spriggs教授和他的研究团队是否去了Efate试图寻找古代墓地。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Professor Spriggs\"、\"Efate\"和\"ancient cemetery\"定位到C段，该段提到墓地遗址的发现过程。\n解题思路：原文明确指出墓地遗址是偶然发现的（\"It came to light only by luck\"），由挖掘机操作员偶然挖出，而非Spriggs团队主动寻找的结果。题目声称Spriggs团队是主动去寻找墓地，与原文事实相反，因此答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59275","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage"},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8088:59276:4","type":"choice","text":"The Lapita completed a journey of around 2,000 miles in a period less than a centenary.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Within the span of a few centuries the Lapita stretched the boundaries of their world from the jungle-clad volcanoes of Papua New Guinea to the loneliest coral outliers of Tonga, at least 2,000 miles eastward in the Pacific.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是拉皮塔人是否在不到一个世纪的时间里完成了大约2000英里的旅程。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"2,000 miles\"和\"time period\"可以定位到D段中描述拉皮塔人扩张的句子。\n解题思路：原文提到拉皮塔人在\"几个世纪\"内从巴布亚新几内亚扩张到汤加，距离至少2000英里。题目中的\"less than a centenary\"（不到一个世纪）与原文的\"few centuries\"（几个世纪）不符，因为几个世纪远不止一个世纪。因此，时间信息不符，应该选NO","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59276","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage"},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8088:59277:5","type":"choice","text":"The Lapita were the first inhabitants in many pacific islands.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Along the way they explored millions of square miles of unknown sea, discovering and colonizing scores of tropical islands never before seen by human eyes: Vanuatu, New Caledonia, Fiji, Samoa.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是拉皮塔人是否是许多太平洋岛屿的第一批居民。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"the first inhabitants\"和\"pacific islands\"可以定位到D段中提到拉皮塔人探索并殖民了数以百计的热带岛屿，这些岛屿以前从未被人类所见。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子\"discovering and colonizing scores of tropical islands never before seen by human eyes\"可以确定拉皮塔人是这些岛屿的第一批居民，因此题目的陈述与文章信息一致，答案为YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59277","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage"},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8088:59278:6","type":"choice","text":"The unknown pots discovered in Efate had once been used for cooking.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句： With the discovery of the Lapita cemetery on Éfaté, the volume of data available to researchers has expanded dramatically. The bones of at least 62 individuals have been uncovered so far – including old men, young women, even babies – and more skeletons are known to be in the ground Archaeologists were also thrilled to discover six complete Lapita pots.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“在Efate发现的未知陶器曾被用于烹饪”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“unknown pots discovered in Efate”来定位答案。在E段中找到关于Efate发现的陶器的描述。\n解题思路：原文只是提到发现了的6个陶罐，并没有提到这些陶器曾被用于烹饪。因此，题目中的说法在文章中没有提及，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59278","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8088:59279:7","type":"choice","text":"The urn buried in Éfaté site was plain as it was without any decoration.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It would be hard for anyone to argue that these aren’t Lapita when you have human bones enshrined inside what is unmistakably a Lapita urn.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问“在Éfaté遗址中埋葬的瓮是朴素的，因为它没有任何装饰”这一说法是否正确。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“Éfaté site”和“urn”定位到D段，找到关于瓮的描述。\n解题思路：原文强调这是一个“ unmistakably a Lapita urn”（确凿无疑的拉皮塔陶瓮）。而拉皮塔陶器的定义性特征就是其独特的装饰风格（peculiar style of pottery decoration）。因此，这个瓮不可能是“plain”（朴素无装饰）的，答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59279","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage"},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8088:59280:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"rock","acceptedAnswers":["rock"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The chemical makeup of the obsidian flakes littering the site indicates that the rock wasn’t local; instead it was imported from a large island in Papua New Guinea’s Bismarck Archipelago, the springboard for the Lapita’s thrust into the Pacific.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是在Efate遗址中发现的科学证据，其中提到了人类遗骸和木炭，以及一个空格需要填写的内容。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"human remains\"和\"charcoal\"可以定位到F段前半部分，然后继续阅读发现后半部分提到了\"rock\"的相关信息。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到\"the chemical makeup of the obsidian flakes\"（黑曜石碎片的化学成分），这对应了题目中的\"Tests show the human remains and the charcoal found in the buried um are from the start of the Lapita period.\"（测试显示在埋葬的坛子里发现的人类遗骸和木炭来自拉皮塔时期的开始）。接着原文提到\"the rock wasn’t local\"（岩石不是当地的），这对应了题目中的空格部分。因此，空格处应填写\"rock\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59280","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-10\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-10 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8088:59281:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"teeth","acceptedAnswers":["teeth"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A particularly intriguing clue comes from chemical tests on the teeth of several skeletons.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求根据给出的摘要内容，从文章中找出Efate遗址中的许多物品并非来自当地，然后通过检查某种身体部位来获取信息。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Efate site\"和\"did not come from that area\"定位到G段，该段提到Efate遗址中发现的物品（如黑曜石碎片）并非当地产物，而是从别处进口的。继续阅读该段，找到与\"examinations\"和身体部位相关的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文G段的内容，前文提到遗址中的黑曜石碎片并非当地产物，是从别处进口的。接着提到\"chemical tests on the teeth of several skeletons\"（对几具骨骼牙齿的化学测试）是另一个重要的线索。题目中的\"Then examinations carried out on\"对应原文中的\"chemical tests on\"，而\"teeth\"是测试的对象，因此答案为\"teeth\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59281","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-10\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-10 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8088:59282:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"descendants","acceptedAnswers":["descendants"],"explanation":"原文答案句：‘This represents the best opportunity we’ve had yet,’ says Spriggs, ‘to find out who the Lapita actually were, where they came from, and who their closest descendants are today.’\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求根据摘要填空，找出Efate遗址的发现揭示了Lapita的最近现代后代是谁。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的Efate site和descendants这两个关键词，在文章中定位到E段最后一句，该句明确提到“who their closest descendants are today”。\n解题思路：原文E段最后一句直接回答了题目要求的信息，即通过DNA测试可以确定Lapita的最近现代后代是谁，原文中的“descendants”与题目空格前的“nearest”相呼应，因此答案为descendants。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59282","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-10\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-10 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8088:59283:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"canoes","acceptedAnswers":["canoes"],"explanation":"原文答案句：No one has found one of their canoes or any rigging, which could reveal how the canoes were sailed.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问Lapita在横渡海洋时乘坐的是什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"Lapita\"和\"crossed the oceans\"定位到文章中描述Lapita航海的段落。在G段中找到明确提到\"Lapita\"和\"canoes\"的句子。\n解题思路：原文G段提到\"no one has found one of their canoes or any rigging, which could reveal how the canoes were sailed\"，说明Lapita使用的是\"canoes\"（独木舟）进行航海。虽然原文提到\"no one has found\"，但结合上下文可以确定他们确实乘坐的是独木舟。题目问的是他们乘坐的交通工具，因此答案为\"canoes\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59283","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8088:59284:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"trade winds","acceptedAnswers":["trade winds"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\n‘They could sail out for days into the unknown and reconnoiter, secure in the knowledge that if they didn’t find anything, they could turn about and catch a swift ride home on the trade winds. It’s what made the whole thing work.’\n对应段落：  H段\n审题：\n题目问的是“根据Irwin的观点，拉皮塔人依靠什么快速返回基地？”，需要找出拉皮塔人在航行中用于快速返回的依据。\n定位关键信息：\n通过题目中的“in Irwin’s view”和“bring them fast back to the base”可以定位到D段，其中提到了Irwin对拉皮塔人航行策略的分析。原文中明确提到“they could turn about and catch a swift ride home on the trade winds”，即他们依靠贸易风快速返回。\n解题思路：\n原文中Irwin指出，拉皮塔人向东航行时逆风而行，但依靠贸易风可以快速返回。题目问的是他们依靠什么快速返回基地，对应原文中的“trade winds”，即贸易风。因此，答案为“trade winds”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59284","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8088:59285:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"seabirds and turtles","acceptedAnswers":["seabirds and turtles"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Once out there, skilled seafarers would detect abundant leads to follow to land: seabirds and turtles, coconuts and twigs carried out to sea by the tides, and the afternoon pileup of clouds on the horizon that often betokens an island in the distance\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是拉皮塔人可以通过哪些海洋生物来判断哪里有陆地。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"sea creatures\"和\"indication\"定位到文章中描述拉皮塔人航行技能和如何寻找陆地的内容。\n解题思路：原文I段提到拉皮塔人通过海洋生物来判断陆地位置，原文句子\"Once out there, skilled seafarers would detect abundant leads to follow to land: seabirds and turtles, coconuts and twigs carried out to sea by the tides, and the afternoon pileup of clouds on the horizon that often betokens an island in the distance\"明确指出拉皮塔人通过\"seabirds and turtles\"等海洋生物来判断陆地位置。因此答案为seabirds and turtles。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59285","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59273","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Captain cook once expected the Hawaii might speak another language of people from other pacific islands.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"59274","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Captain cook depicted number of cultural aspects of Polynesians in his journal.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"59275","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Professor Spriggs and his research team went to the Efate to try to find the site of ancient cemetery.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"59276","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The Lapita completed a journey of around 2,000 miles in a period less than a centenary.</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"59277","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The Lapita were the first inhabitants in many pacific islands.</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"59278","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The unknown pots discovered in Efate had once been used for cooking.</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"59279","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement is true NO if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not givern in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The urn buried in Éfaté site was plain as it was without any decoration.</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"59280","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-10\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-10 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Scientific evident found in Efate site \nTests show the human remains and the charcoal found in the buried um are from the start of the Lapita period. Yet The <strong>8</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"59281","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-10\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-10 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>covering many of the Efate site did not come from that area. Then examinations carried out on the<strong> 9 </strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"59282","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-10\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-10 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>discovered at Efate site reveal that not everyone buried there was a native living in the area. In fact, DNA could identify the Lapita’s nearest <strong>10 </strong><strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong> present-days.</p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"59283","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>11 </strong>What did the Lapita travel in when they crossed the oceans? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"59284","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>12 </strong>In Irwins’s view, what would the Latipa have relied on to bring them fast back to the base? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"59285","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 11-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>13</strong> Which sea creatures would have been an indication to the Lapita of where to find land ? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Voyage of Going: Beyond the Blue Line&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>One feels a certain sympathy for Captain James Cook on the day in 1778 that he ‘discovered’ Hawaii. Then on his third expedition to the Pacific, the British navigator had explored scores of islands across the breadth of the sea, from lush New Zealand to the lonely wastes of Easter Island. This latest voyage had taken him thousands of miles north from the Society Islands to an archipelago so remote that even the old Polynesians back on Tahiti knew nothing about it. Imagine Cook’s surprise, then, when the natives of Hawaii came paddling out in their canoes and greeted him in a familiar tongue, one he had heard on virtually every mote of inhabited land he had visited. Marveling at the ubiquity of this Pacific language and culture, he later wondered in his journal: ‘How shall we account for this Nation spreading itself so far over this Vast Ocean?’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Answers have been slow in coming. But now a startling archaeological find on the island of Éfaté, in the Pacific nation of Vanuatu, has revealed an ancient seafaring people, the distant ancestors of today’s Polynesians, taking their first steps into the unknown. The discoveries there have also opened a window into the shadowy world of those early voyagers. At the same time, other pieces of this human puzzle are turning up in unlikely places. Climate data gleaned from slow-growing corals around the Pacific and from sediments in alpine lakes in South America may help explain how, more than a thousand years later, a second wave of seafarers beat their way across the entire Pacific.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘What we have is a first or second-generation site containing the graves of some of the Pacific’s first explorers,’ says Spriggs, professor of archaeology at the Australian National University and co-leader of an international team excavating the site. It came to light only by luck. A backhoe operator, digging up topsoil on the grounds of a derelict coconut plantation, scraped open a grave – the first of dozens in a burial ground some 3,000 years old It is the oldest cemetery ever found in the Pacific islands, and it harbors the bones of an ancient people archaeologists call the Lapita, a label that derives from a beach in New Caledonia where a landmark cache of their pottery was found in the 1950s. They were daring blue-water adventurers who roved the sea not just as explorers but also as pioneers, bringing along everything they would need to build new lives – their families and livestock, taro seedlings and stone tools.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Within the span of a few centuries the Lapita stretched the boundaries of their world from the jungle-clad volcanoes of Papua New Guinea to the loneliest coral outliers of Tonga, at least 2,000 miles eastward in the Pacific. Along the way they explored millions of square miles of unknown sea, discovering and colonizing scores of tropical islands never before seen by human eyes: Vanuatu, New Caledonia, Fiji, Samoa.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>What little is known or surmised about them has been pieced together from fragments of pottery, animal bones, obsidian flakes, and such oblique sources as comparative linguistics and geochemistry. Although their voyages can be traced back to the northern islands of Papua New Guinea, their language – variants of which are still spoken across the Pacific – came from Taiwan. And their peculiar style of pottery decoration, created by pressing a carved stamp into the cay, probably had its roots in the northern Philippines. With the discovery of the Lapita cemetery on Éfaté, the volume of data available to researchers has expanded dramatically. The bones of at least 62 individuals have been uncovered so far – including old men, young women, even babies – and more skeletons are known to be in the ground Archaeologists were also thrilled to discover six complete Lapita pots. ‘It’s an important find,’ Spriggs says, for it conclusively identifies the remains as Lapita, ‘It would be hard for anyone to argue that these aren’t Lapita when you have human bones enshrined inside what is unmistakably a Lapita urn.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Several lines of evidence also undergird Spriggs’s conclusion that this was a community of pioneers making their first voyages into the remote reaches of Oceania. For one thing, the radiocarbon dating of bones and charcoal places them early in the Lapita expansion. For another, the chemical makeup of the obsidian flakes littering the site indicates that the rock wasn’t local; instead it was imported from a large island in Papua New Guinea’s Bismarck Archipelago, the springboard for the Lapita’s thrust into the Pacific. A particularly intriguing clue comes from chemical tests on the teeth of several skeletons. DNA teased from these ancient bones may also help answer one of the most puzzling questions in Pacific anthropology: Did all Pacific islanders spring from one source or many? Was there only one outward migration from a single point in Asia, or several from different points? ‘This represents the best opportunity we’ve had yet,’ says Spriggs, ‘to find out who the Lapita actually were, where they came from, and who their closest descendants are today.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>There is one stubborn question for which archaeology has yet to provide any answers: How did the Lapita accomplish the ancient equivalent of a moon landing, many times over? No one has found one of their canoes or any rigging, which could reveal how the canoes were sailed Nor do the oral histories and traditions of later Polynesians offer any insights, for they segue into myth long before they reach as far back in time as the Lapita. ‘All we can say for certain is that the Lapita had canoes that were capable of ocean voyages, and they had the ability to sail them,’ says Geoff Irwin, a professor of archaeology at the University of Auckland and an avid yachtsman. Those sailing skills, he says, were developed and passed down over thousands of years by earlier mariners who worked their way through the archipelagoes of the western Pacific making short crossings to islands within sight of each other. Reaching Fiji, as they did a century or so later, meant crossing more than 500 miles of ocean, pressing on day after day into the great blue void of the Pacific. What gave them the courage to launch out on such a risky voyage?&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The Lapita’s thrust into the Pacific was eastward, against the prevailing trade winds, Irwin notes. Those nagging headwinds, he argues, may have been the key to their success. ‘They could sail out for days into the unknown and reconnoiter, secure in the knowledge that if they didn’t find anything, they could turn about and catch a swift ride home on the trade winds. It’s what made the whole thing work.’ Once out there, skilled seafarers would detect abundant leads to follow to land: seabirds and turtles, coconuts and twigs carried out to sea by the tides, and the afternoon pileup of clouds on the horizon that often betokens an island in the distance. Some islands may have broadcast their presence with far less subtlety than a cloud bank. Some of the most violent eruptions anywhere on the planet during the past 10,000 years occurred in Melanesia, which sits nervously in one of the most explosive volcanic regions on Earth. Even less spectacular eruptions would have sent plumes of smoke billowing into the stratosphere and rained ash for hundreds of miles. It’s possible that the Lapita saw these signs of distant islands and later sailed off in their direction, knowing they would find land for returning explorers, successful or not, the geography of their own archipelagoes provided a safety net to keep them from overshooting their home ports and sailing off into eternity.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>However they did it, the Lapita spread themselves a third of the way across the Pacific, then called it quits for reasons known only to them. Ahead lay the vast emptiness of the central Pacific, and perhaps they were too thinly stretched to venture farther. They probably never numbered more than a few thousand in total, and in their rapid migration eastward they encountered hundreds of islands – more than 300 in Fiji alone. Still, more than a millennium would pass before the Lapita’s descendants, a people we now call the Polynesians, struck out in search of new territory.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8088&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8089","type":"reading","title":"Passage2 We Have Star Performers!","book":"阅读还原集Vol.12","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test1","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.12 · Test1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8089:59299:14","type":"choice","text":"14 One example from non-commerce/business settings that better system wins bigger stars.","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Football is another illustration of the stars vs systems strategic choice. As with investment banks and stockbrokers, it seems obvious that success should ultimately be down to money. Great players are scarce and expensive. So the club that can afford more of them than anyone else will win. But the performance of Arsenal and Manchester United on one hand and Chelsea and Real Madrid on the other proves that it’s not as easy as that. While Chelsea and Real have the funds to be compulsive star collectors – as with Juan Sebastian Veron – they are less successful than Arsenal and United which, like Liverpool before them, have put much more emphasis on developing a setting within which stars-in-the-making can flourish. Significantly, Thierry Henry, Patrick Veira and Robert Pires are much bigger stars than when Arsenal bought them, their value ( in all senses) enhanced by the Arsenal system. At Chelsea, by contrast, the only context is the stars themselves – managers with different outlooks come and go every couple of seasons. There is no settled system for the stars to blend into. The Chelsea context has not only not added value, it has subtracted it. The side is less than the sum of its exorbitantly expensive parts. Even Real Madrid’s galacticos, the most extravagantly gifted on the planet, are being outperformed by less talented but better-integrated Spanish sides. In football, too, stars are trumped by systems.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“一个非商业/商业环境中的例子，更好的系统赢得了更大的明星”。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“非商业/商业环境”和“更好的系统赢得更大的明星”。在文章中，只有F段提到了非商业环境（足球），并且明确指出更好的系统（如阿森纳和曼联的系统）能够使明星球员的价值得到提升，而仅仅依赖明星球员的俱乐部（如切尔西和皇家马德里）却表现不佳。\n解题思路：根据题目中的关键词，我们可以在文章中定位到F段。F段以足球为例，说明在非商业环境中，更好的系统能够使明星球员的价值得到提升，而仅仅依赖明星球员的俱乐部却表现不佳。这与题目中的“更好的系统赢得更大的明星”完全吻合，因此F段是正确答案。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59299","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8089:59299:15","type":"choice","text":"15 One failed company that believes stars rather than system.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The point was illuminated in brilliant relief by Enron, whose leaders, as a New Yorker article called ‘The Talent Myth’ entertainingly related, were so convinced of their own cleverness that they never twigged that collective intelligence is not the sum of a lot of individual intelligences.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“一个相信明星而非系统的失败公司”。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"failed company\"、\"stars rather than system\"定位到B段，其中提到\"Enron\"是一个相信明星的公司。\n解题思路：B段明确提到Enron的领导者们相信自己的聪明才智，却没有意识到集体智慧不等于个体智慧的简单相加，这表明Enron是一个相信明星而非系统的公司。同时，Enron在文中被描述为一个失败的案例，符合题目的要求。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59299","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8089:59299:16","type":"choice","text":"16 One suggestion that author made to acquire employees then to win the competition nowadays.","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：You grow your own. This worked for investment analysts, where some companies were not only better at creating stars but also at retaining them.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是作者提出了哪些建议来获得员工以赢得当今的竞争。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"acquire employees\"和\"win the competition\"可以定位到G段，该段提到了\"how do you compete in the war for talent\"以及具体的建议。\n解题思路：根据原文G段中的句子\"You grow your own. This worked for investment analysts, where some companies were not only better at creating stars but also at retaining them.\"可以确定，作者建议通过培养自己的员工来获得人才，而不是仅仅通过招聘明星员工。这与题目所问的\"获得员工以赢得竞争\"的建议相符。因此，答案为G。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59299","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8089:59299:17","type":"choice","text":"17 One metaphor to human medical anatomy that illustrates the problems of hiring stars.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：One respondent likened hiring a star to an organ transplant. The new organ can damage others by hogging the blood supply, other organs can start aching or threaten to stop working or the body can reject the transplant altogether, he said. ‘You should think about it very carefully before you do [a transplant] to a healthy body.’\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段包含了一个关于人体医学解剖的比喻，用来说明雇佣明星员工所带来的问题。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"metaphor\"、\"human medical anatomy\"和\"problems of hiring stars\"，可以在文章中找到对应的比喻，即C段中提到的\"an organ transplant\"的比喻。\n解题思路：C段中提到了一个比喻，将雇佣明星员工比作人体器官移植。这个比喻形象地说明了雇佣明星员工可能会带来的问题，比如新员工可能会损害其他员工（如同新器官损害其他器官一样），或者整个团队可能会排斥新员工（如同身体排斥移植的器官一样）。因此，C段包含了题目所要求的比喻。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59299","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8089:59300:18","type":"choice","text":"McKinsey who wrote ‘The War for Talent’ had not expected the huge influence made by this book.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Although the intensity of the warfare subsequently subsided along with the air in the internet bubble, it has been warming up again as the economy tightens: labour shortages, for example, are the reason the government has laid out the welcome mat for immigrants from the new Europe.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问麦肯锡公司撰写《人才战争》这本书时，是否预料到这本书会产生巨大的影响。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"The War for Talent\"和\"McKinsey\"定位到A段第二句，提到麦肯锡撰写的《人才战争》这本书。\n解题思路：原文中提到麦肯锡撰写了《人才战争》这本书，但并未提及他们是否预料到这本书会产生巨大的影响。因此，根据原文信息，无法确定麦肯锡是否预料到这本书的影响，所以答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59300","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 18-21\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8089:59301:19","type":"choice","text":"Economic condition becomes one of the factors which decide whether or not a country would prefer to hire foreign employees.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：As the economy tightens: labour shortages, for example, are the reason the government has laid out the welcome mat for immigrants from the new Europe.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是经济状况是否成为决定一个国家是否愿意雇佣外国员工的一个因素。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"economic condition\"和\"hire foreign employees\"来定位答案。\n解题思路：原文A段提到，随着经济收紧，劳动力短缺，例如，是政府为来自新欧洲的移民铺开欢迎垫的原因。这说明经济状况（经济收紧）是导致劳动力短缺的一个因素，而劳动力短缺又促使政府雇佣外国员工。因此，经济状况确实是一个决定因素。所以答案是YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59301","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 18-21\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8089:59302:20","type":"choice","text":"The collapse of Enron is caused totally by a unfortunate incident instead of company’s management mistake.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The point was illuminated in brilliant relief by Enron, whose leaders, as a New Yorker article called ‘The Talent Myth’ entertainingly related, were so convinced of their own cleverness that they never twigged that collective intelligence is not the sum of a lot of individual intelligences.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问“Enron的倒闭完全是由不幸事件造成的，而不是公司管理失误”，需要判断这个说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"Enron\"和\"collapse\"（倒闭）是关键词，可以定位到B段中关于Enron的描述。\n解题思路：原文提到Enron的领导层过于自信，没有意识到集体智慧不等于个体智慧的简单相加，这表明Enron的失败与公司管理理念（即过度依赖明星员工而忽视系统）有关，而非单纯的不幸事件。因此，题目说法与原文信息矛盾，答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59302","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 18-21\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8089:59303:21","type":"choice","text":"Football clubs that focus making stars in the setting are better than simply collecting stars","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：As with investment banks and stockbrokers, it seems obvious that success should ultimately be down to money. Great players are scarce and expensive. So the club that can afford more of them than anyone else will win. But the performance of Arsenal and Manchester United on one hand and Chelsea and Real Madrid on the other proves that it’s not as easy as that. While Chelsea and Real have the funds to be compulsive star collectors – as with Juan Sebastian Veron – they are less successful than Arsenal and United which, like Liverpool before them, have put much more emphasis on developing a setting within which stars-in-the-making can flourish.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“专注于在环境中培养明星的足球俱乐部比单纯收集明星的俱乐部更好”这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“Football clubs”、“making stars in the setting”和“better than simply collecting stars”定位到F段中关于足球俱乐部成功因素的对比。\n解题思路：F段明确提到，像切尔西和皇家马德里这样的俱乐部虽然拥有资金来收集明星球员（如胡安·塞巴斯蒂安·维埃拉），但它们的成功程度不如阿森纳和曼联，后者更注重培养一个能让潜力明星球员茁壮成长的环境。原文直接对比了两种策略的效果，表明“注重环境培养”的策略更为成功，因此题目陈述与原文信息一致。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59303","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 18-21\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8089:59304:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"Analysts/star-stock analysts","acceptedAnswers":["Analysts","star-stock analysts"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In a study of the careers of 1,000 star-stock analysts in the 1990s, the researchers found that when a company recruited a star performer, three things happened.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目要求根据文章内容填写一个关于研究对象职业的描述，具体是哪类职业人员。\n定位关键信息：题目中的数字\"1,000\"和职业相关描述是定位关键词，在文章中找到对应的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文句子\"In a study of the careers of 1,000 star-stock analysts in the 1990s\"可以直接确定研究对象是\"star-stock analysts\"，即明星股票分析师。题目中的\"22 %\"可能是题目格式错误，实际需要填写的是职业名称\"star-stock analysts\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59304","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8089:59305:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"performance star/star/star performer","acceptedAnswers":["performance star","star","star performer"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In a study of the careers of 1,000 star-stock analysts in the 1990s, the researchers found that when a company recruited a star performer, three things happened.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是哈佛商业评论的调查参与者发现公司雇佣明星员工的比例是多少。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"Harvard Business Review\"和\"company hire\"可以定位到C段，找到关于哈佛商业评论调查的内容。\n解题思路：原文提到哈佛商业评论对1000名明星股票分析师的职业生涯进行了研究，发现当公司雇佣明星员工时会发生三件事。hire和recruit是同意替换，所以填star performer。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59305","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8089:59306:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"working environment/settings","acceptedAnswers":["working environment","settings"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In many cases, performance dropped sharply when high performers switched employers and in some instances never recovered. More of success than commonly supposed is due to the working environment - systems, processes, leadership, accumulated embedded learning that are absent in and can’t be transported to the new firm.（C段）\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是明星员工在新团队中的表现比在原来的环境中差的原因。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"behave considerably worse\"和\"new team\"定位到C段，找到描述明星员工表现下降的句子。\n解题思路：原文提到\"More of success than commonly supposed is due to the working environment - systems, processes, leadership, accumulated embedded learning that are absent in and can’t be transported to the new firm.\"，说明成功更多归因于工作环境，而这些因素在新公司中是缺失的。因此，明星员工在新团队中表现差是因为新公司缺乏原有的\"working environment\"或\"settings\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59306","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8089:59307:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"salary","acceptedAnswers":["salary"],"explanation":"原文答案句：So they moved, upping their salary as they did – 36 per cent moved on within three years, fast even for Wall Street.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目要求填写员工离职时增加的具体内容，并提到他们比华尔街更快，增加了25%。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"move faster than wall street\"和\"25 %%\"可以定位到C段描述明星员工离职时的情况。\n解题思路：原文C段提到明星员工离职时会\"upping their salary\"，即提高他们的薪水，并具体说明\"36 per cent moved on within three years, fast even for Wall Street\"，这与题目描述的\"move faster than wall street\"和增加25%相吻合。因此，答案为\"salary\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59307","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8089:59308:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"rivals","acceptedAnswers":["rivals"],"explanation":"原文答案句：One respondent likened hiring a star to an organ transplant. The new organ can damage others by hogging the blood supply, other organs can start aching or threaten to stop working or the body can reject the transplant altogether, he said. ‘You should think about it very carefully before you do [a transplant] to a healthy body.’\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“其次，他们面临来自团队内部的拒绝或排斥”，需要填入被拒绝或排斥的对象。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“rejections or refuse”和“within the team”，通过这些词可以定位到C段中关于团队内部排斥的描述。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子“other organs can start aching or threaten to stop working or the body can reject the transplant altogether, he said.”，可以理解为团队内部的“other organs”对应的是“rivals”，即竞争对手或对手。因此，填入“rivals”符合题意。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59308","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59299","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-17\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p style=\"line-height: normal; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>14 </strong>One example from non-commerce/business settings that better system wins bigger stars<strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"59300","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 18-21\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>McKinsey who wrote ‘The War for Talent’ had not expected the huge influence made by this book.</strong></p>","firstNumber":18},{"id":"59301","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 18-21\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>Economic condition becomes one of the factors which decide whether or not a country would prefer to hire foreign employees.</strong></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"59302","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 18-21\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>The collapse of Enron is caused totally by a unfortunate incident instead of company’s management mistake</strong>.</p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"59303","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 18-21\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 1? In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the information NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this","html":"<p><strong>Football clubs that focus making stars in the setting are better than simply collecting stars</strong></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"59304","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>An investigation carried out on 1,000 <strong>22</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong>.&nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"59305","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Participants of a survey by Harvard \nBusiness Review found a company hire a <strong>23</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong>&nbsp;has negative effects.</p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"59306","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>For instance, \nthey behave considerably worse in a new team than in the <strong>24</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> that they used to be.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"59307","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>They move faster than Wall Street and increase their <strong>25</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong>.<br/></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"59308","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22-26\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Secondly, they faced rejections or refuse from those <strong>26</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong> within the team.\nLastly, the one who made mistakes had been punished by selling his/her stock share.</p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>We Have Star Performers!&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The difference between companies is people. With capital and technology in plentiful supply, the critical resource for companies in the knowledge era will be human talent. Companies full of achievers will, by definition, outperform organisations of plodders. Ergo, compete ferociously for the best people. Poach and pamper stars; ruthlessly weed out second-raters. This, in essence, has been the recruitment strategy of the ambitious company of the past decade. The ‘talent mindset’ was given definitive form in two reports by the consultancy McKinsey famously entitled ‘The War for Talent’. Although the intensity of the warfare subsequently subsided along with the air in the internet bubble, it has been warming up again as the economy tightens: labour shortages, for example, are the reason the government has laid out the welcome mat for immigrants from the new Europe.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Yet while the diagnosis – people are important – is evident to the point of platitude, the apparently logical prescription – hire the best – like so much in management is not only not obvious: it is in fact profoundly wrong. The first suspicions dawned with the crash to earth of the dotcom meteors, which showed that dumb is dumb whatever the IQ of those who perpetrate it. The point was illuminated in brilliant relief by Enron, whose leaders, as a New Yorker article called ‘The Talent Myth’ entertainingly related, were so convinced of their own cleverness that they never twigged that collective intelligence is not the sum of a lot of individual intelligence. In fact, in a profound sense, the two are opposites. Enron believed in stars, noted author Malcolm Gladwell, because they didn’t believe in systems. But companies don’t just create: ‘they execute and compete and coordinate the efforts of many people, and the organisations that are most successful at that task are the ones where the system is the star’. The truth is that you can’t win the talent wars by hiring stars – only lose it. New light on why this should be so is thrown by an analysis of star behaviour in this months’ Harvard Business Review. In a study of the careers of 1,000 star-stock analysts in the 1990s, the researchers found that when a company recruited a star performer, three things happened.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>First, stardom doesn’t easily transfer from one organisation to another. In many cases, performance dropped sharply when high performers switched employers and in some instances never recovered. More of success than commonly supposed is due to the working environment - systems, processes, leadership, accumulated embedded learning that are absent in and can’t be transported to the new firm. Moreover, precisely because of their past stellar performance,stars were unwilling to learn new tricks and antagonised those (on whom they now unwittingly depended) who could teach them. So they moved, upping their salary as they did – 36 per cent moved on within three years, fast even for Wall Street. Second, group performance suffered as a result of tensions and resentment by rivals within the team. One respondent likened hiring a star to an organ transplant. The new organ can damage others by hogging the blood supply, other organs can start aching or threaten to stop working or the body can reject the transplants altogether, he said. ‘You should think about it very carefully before you do [a transplant] to a healthy body.’ Third, investors punished the offender by selling its stock. This is ironic, since the motive for importing stars was often a suffering share price in the first place. Shareholders evidently believe that the company is overpaying, the hiree is cashing in on a glorious past rather than preparing for a glowing present, and a spending spree is in the offing.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The result of mass star hirings as well as individual ones seems to confirm such doubts. Look at County NatWest and Barclays de Zoete Wedd, both of which hired teams of stars with loud fanfare to do great things in investment banking in the 1990s. Both failed dismally. Everyone accepts the cliche that people make the organisation – but much more does the organisation make the people. When researchers studied the performance of fund managers in the 1990s, they discovered that just 30 per cent of variation in fund performance was due to the individual, compared to 70 per cent to the company-specific setting.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>That will be no surprise to those familiar with systems thinking. W. Edwards Deming used to say that there was no point in beating up on people when 90 per cent of performance variation was down to the system within which they worked. Consistent improvement, he said, is a matter not of raising the level of individual intelligence, but of the learning of the organisation as a whole. The star system is glamorous - for the few. But it rarely benefits the company that thinks it is working it. And the knock-on consequences indirectly affect everyone else too. As one internet response to Gladwell’s New Yorker article put it: after Enron, ‘the rest of corporate America is stuck with overpaid, arrogant, underachieving, and relatively useless talent.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Football is another illustration of the stars vs systems strategic choice. As with investment banks and stockbrokers, it seems obvious that success should ultimately be down to money. Great players are scarce and expensive. So the club that can afford more of them than anyone else will win. But the performance of Arsenal and Manchester United on one hand and Chelsea and Real Madrid on the other proves that it’s not as easy as that. While Chelsea and Real have the funds to be compulsive star collectors – as with Juan Sebastian Veron – they are less successful than Arsenal and United which, like Liverpool before them, have put much more emphasis on developing a setting within which stars-in-the-making can flourish. Significantly,Thierry Henry, Patrick Veira and Robert Pires are much bigger stars than when Arsenal bought them, their value ( in all senses) enhanced by the Arsenal system. At Chelsea, by contrast, the only context is the stars themselves – managers with different outlooks come and go every couple of seasons. There is no settled system for the stars to blend into. The Chelsea context has not only not added value, it has subtracted it. The side is less than the sum of its exorbitantly expensive parts. Even Real Madrid’s galacticos,the most extravagantly gifted on the planet, are being outperformed by less talented but better-integrated Spanish sides. In football, too, stars are trumped by systems.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>So if not by hiring stars, how do you compete in the war for talent? You grow your own. This worked for investment analysts, where some companies were not only better at creating stars but also at retaining them. Because they had a much more sophisticated view of the interdependent relationship between star and system, they kept them longer without resorting to the exorbitant salaries that were so destructive to rivals.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8089&scene=%E8%B4%A2%E7%BB%8F%E5%95%86%E4%B8%9A&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8090","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 The Future of the World’s Language","book":"阅读还原集Vol.12","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test1","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.12 · Test1 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8090:59232:27","type":"choice","text":"Of the world's 6,500 living languages, about half of them are expected to be extinct. Most of the world’s languages are spoken by a 27 ____ of people.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Of the world’s 6,500 living languages, around half are expected to the out by the end of this century, according to UNESCO. Just 11 are spoken by more than half of the earth’s population, so it is little wonder that those used by only a few are being left behind as we become a more homogenous, global society. In short, 95 percent of the world’s languages are spoken by only five percent of its population – a remarkable level of linguistic diversity stored in tiny pockets of speakers around the world.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“世界上大多数语言是由百分之多少的人口使用的？”\n定位关键信息：利用题目的单词“world’s languages”和“spoken by”定位到A段中“95 percent of the world’s languages are spoken by only five percent of its population”这句话。\n解题思路：根据原文中的这句话可以确定，世界上95%的语言是由全球人口的5%使用的，因此可以得出答案为“D”，即“少数”。","options":["similarity","significance","funding","minority","education","difference","language","diversity","majority","disappearance"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"59232","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-G, below. Write your answers in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8090:59232:28","type":"choice","text":"However, Professor Turin set up a project WOLP to prevent 28 ____ of the languages.","answer":"J","acceptedAnswers":["J"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Mark Turin, a university professor, has launched WOLP (World Oral Language Project) to prevent the language from the brink of extinction.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是Turin教授设立WOLP项目的目的是什么。\n定位关键信息：题目中的\"Professor Turin\"和\"project WOLP\"可以帮助定位到A段中的相关句子。\n解题思路：根据A段中的原文句子，Turin教授设立WOLP项目的目的是为了防止语言濒临灭绝，因此答案为\"extinction\"。","options":["similarity","significance","funding","minority","education","difference","language","diversity","majority","disappearance"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"59232","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-G, below. Write your answers in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8090:59232:29","type":"choice","text":"The project provides the community with 29 ____ to enable people to record their endangered languages.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：He is trying to encourage indigenous communities to collaborate with anthropologists around the world to record what he calls ‘oral literature’ through video cameras, voice recorders and other multimedia tools by awarding grants from a £30,000 pot that the project has secured this year.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是项目为社区提供了什么。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"the project provides the community with\"和\"to record\"定位到B段\n解题思路：原文提到\"He is trying to encourage indigenous communities to collaborate with anthropologists around the world to record what he calls ‘oral literature’ through video cameras, voice recorders and other multimedia tools by awarding grants\"，说明项目通过awarding给community提供to record的东西。根据选项列表，C选项\"funding\"最符合原文描述。","options":["similarity","significance","funding","minority","education","difference","language","diversity","majority","disappearance"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"59232","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-G, below. Write your answers in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8090:59232:30","type":"choice","text":"The oral tradition has great cultural 30 ____ .","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For many of these communities, the oral tradition is at the heart of their culture.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“口头传统具有巨大的文化的什么”。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“oral tradition”和“cultural”这两个关键词可以定位到C段。\n解题思路：原文中提到，口头传统是许多社区文化的核心，具有重要的文化意义。因此，答案为B。","options":["similarity","significance","funding","minority","education","difference","language","diversity","majority","disappearance"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"59232","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-G, below. Write your answers in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8090:59232:31","type":"choice","text":"An important 31 ____ between languages spoken by few people and languages with celebrated written documents existed in many communities.","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Unlike the languages with celebrated written traditions, such as Sanskrit, Hebrew and Ancient Greek, few indigenous communities have recorded their own languages or ever had them recorded until now.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是在许多社区中，使用人数少的语言和使用有悠久书面传统的语言之间存在一个重要的什么差异。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“languages spoken by few people”和“languages with celebrated written documents”可以定位到C段中“Unlike the languages with celebrated written traditions, such as Sanskrit, Hebrew and Ancient Greek, few indigenous communities have recorded their own languages or ever had them recorded until now.”这句话。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到了使用人数少的语言和使用有悠久书面传统的语言之间的差异，即前者很少有社区记录自己的语言，而后者则有悠久的历史记录。所以两者存在差异，因此答案为F。","options":["similarity","significance","funding","minority","education","difference","language","diversity","majority","disappearance"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"59232","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-G, below. Write your answers in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8090:59237:32","type":"choice","text":"Turin argued that anthropologists and linguists usually think carefully before selecting an area to research.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Many of the choices anthropologists and linguists who work on these traditional field-work projects are quite random, he admits.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是Turin是否认为人类学家和语言学家在选择研究领域时通常会仔细考虑。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的\"Turin argued that anthropologists and linguists usually think carefully before selecting an area to research\"中的关键词\"Turin\"、\"anthropologists and linguists\"、\"think carefully before selecting an area to research\"来定位。\n解题思路：根据定位到的D段原文句子\"Many of the choices anthropologists and linguists who work on these traditional field-work projects are quite random, he admits.\"可以看出，Turin承认人类学家和语言学家在选择研究领域时通常是随机的，而不是仔细考虑的。因此，题干中的说法与原文信息相反，答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59237","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8090:59238:33","type":"choice","text":"Turin concluded that the Thangmi language had few similarities with other languages.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Unlike the languages with celebrated written traditions, such as Sanskrit, Hebrew and Ancient Greek, few indigenous communities have recorded their own languages or ever had them recorded until now.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是Turin是否得出结论，认为Thangmi语言与其他语言很少有相似之处。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Turin\"和\"Thangmi language\"可以定位到C段，该段提到了Turin对Thangmi语言的研究背景。\n解题思路：原文中C段提到的是少数土著社区的语言记录情况，并未提到Thangmi语言与其他语言的相似性或差异性。题目中的结论在原文中并未提及，因此无法判断其真假。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59238","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8090:59239:34","type":"choice","text":"Turin has written that 1000-page document was inappropriate for Thangmi community.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：I wrote 1,000 pages of grammar in English that nobody could use – but I realised that wasn’t enough. It wasn’t enough for me, it wasn’t enough for them. It simply wasn’t going to work as something for the community.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问Turin表示1000页文档不适合Thangmi社区。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Turin\"、\"1000-page document\"和\"Thangmi community\"定位到E段，找到Turin描述他写文档的内容。\n解题思路：原文中Turin明确提到他写的1000页语法文档是英文的，没有人能用，对社区也不适用，直接对应题目中的\"was inappropriate for Thangmi community\"，因此判断为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59239","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8090:59240:35","type":"choice","text":"Some Nepalese schools lack resources to devote to language teaching.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The small dictionary is still sold in local schools for a modest 20 rupees, and used as part of a wider cultural regeneration process to educate children about their heritage and language.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问“一些尼泊尔学校缺乏资源用于语言教学”是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用关键词“Nepalese schools”和“lack resources”定位到F段，该段提到学校使用小词典进行文化复兴和教育，但未提及资源缺乏。\n解题思路：F段提到学校使用小词典（售价20卢比）进行语言教育。题目说学校缺乏资源，与原文信息无关联，因此答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59240","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8090:59241:36","type":"choice","text":"Why does Turin say people do PhDs on the apostrophe in French?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：There are more linguists in universities around the world than there are spoken languages – but most of them aren’t working on this issue. To me it’s amazing that in this day and age, we still have an entirely incomplete image of the world’s linguistic diversity. People do PhDs on the apostrophe in French, yet we still don’t know how many languages are spoken.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是Turin为什么说人们研究法语中的撇号（apostrophe）来攻读博士学位。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“apostrophe in French”定位到G段末句，找到包含这一信息的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子“People do PhDs on the apostrophe in French, yet we still don’t know how many languages are spoken.”可以推断，Turin认为人们研究法语中的撇号这种细枝末节的问题，而忽视了研究世界上有多少种语言这种更宏观、更重要的语言问题。这表明他认为研究人员在语言研究中的作用有限，他们应该关注更重要的语言问题，而不是像研究撇号这样无关紧要的细节。因此，选项A“他认为研究人员在语言研究中的作用有限”最符合原文意思。","options":["He believes that researchers have limited role in the research of languages.","He compares the methods of research into languages.","He thinks research should result in a diverse cultural outlook.","He holds that research into French should focus on more general aspects."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59241","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8090:59242:37","type":"choice","text":"What is discussed in the Paragraph I?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The revival of a modern form of Hebrew in the 19th century is often cited as one of the best proofs that languages long dead, belonging to small communities, can be resurrected and embraced by a large number of people.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问第九段讨论了什么内容。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"ninth paragraph\"定位到I段，该段主要讲述了希伯来语的复兴作为语言恢复的例子。\n解题思路：I段通过希伯来语在19世纪的复兴，说明曾经消亡的语言可以复活并被广泛使用，这证明了濒危语言有生存的可能。因此，选项A\"促使人们相信濒危语言可以生存的驱动力\"与段落内容一致。其他选项B、C、D均未在段落中提及。","options":["Forces driving people to believe endangered languages can survive.","The community where people distrust language revival.","The methods of research that have improved language restoration.","Initiatives the World Oral Literature Project is bringing to Israel."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59242","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8090:59243:38","type":"choice","text":"How is the WOLP’s prospect?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Turin knows his project’s limits and believes it inevitable that a large number of those languages will disappear. ‘We have to be wholly realistic. A project like ours is in no position, and was not designed, to keep languages alive. The only people who can help languages survive are the people in those communities themselves. They need to be reminded that it’s good to speak their own language and I think we can help them do that – becoming modem doesn’t mean you have to lose your language.’\n对应段落：K段\n审题：题目问的是WOLP的前景如何。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"WOLP's prospect\"可以定位到文章中关于WOLP前景的描述。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句，Dr Turin认为这个项目并不是让所有的语言都存活但是可以帮助人们去保护语言。这意味着WOLP有可能成功保护濒危语言，因此D选项正确。","options":["It would not raise enough funds to achieve its aims.","It will help keep languages alive.","It will be embraced by a large number of people.","It has chance to succeed to protect the engendered languages."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59243","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8090:59244:39","type":"choice","text":"What is Turin’s main point of globalisation?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句Dr Turin believes that the fate of the world’s endangered languages is not sealed, and globalisation is not necessarily the nefarious perpetrator of evil it is often presented to be. ‘I call it the globalisation paradox: on the one hand globalisation and rapid socio-economic change are the things that are eroding and challenging diversity. But on the other, globalisation is providing us with new and very exciting tools and facilities to get to places to document those things that globalisation is eroding.\n对应段落：J段\n审题：题目问的是Turin对全球化的主要观点是什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键词\"Turin’s main point of globalisation\"定位到文章中J段，该段主要讨论了Turin对全球化的看法。\n解题思路：原文中J段明确提到Turin认为全球化是一个悖论，它既侵蚀和挑战多样性，又提供了新的工具和设施来记录那些正在被全球化侵蚀的事物。这与选项B\"全球化既有优势也有劣势\"完全一致。选项A、C和D都没有在原文中明确提及，因此可以排除。","options":["Globalisation is the main reason for endangered language.","Globalisation has both advantages and disadvantages.","We should have a more critical view of globalisation.","We should foremost protect our identity in face of globalisation."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59244","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8090:59245:40","type":"choice","text":"What does Turin suggest that community people should do?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The only people who can help languages survive are the people in those communities themselves. They need to be reminded that it’s good to speak their own language and I think we can help them do that – becoming modem doesn’t mean you have to lose your language.\n对应段落：K段\n审题：题目问Turin建议社区的人们应该做什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的关键词\"Turin suggest that community people should do\"可以定位到K段中Turin的话。\n解题思路：K段中Turin提到，只有社区的人们自己才能帮助语言生存，他们需要被提醒说自己的语言是好的，并且他认为他们可以帮助社区的人们做到这一点——变得现代化并不意味着你必须失去你的语言。这与选项C\"跟上现代社会而不失去他们的语言\"完全一致。因此，答案是C。","options":["Learn other languages.","Only have a sense of identity.","Keep up with the modern society without losing their language.","Join the race to protect as many languages as possible but be realistic."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59245","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59232","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-G, below. Write your answers in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> similarity&nbsp;</p><p><strong>B</strong> significance&nbsp;</p><p><strong>C</strong> funding&nbsp;</p><p><strong>D</strong> minority&nbsp;</p><p><strong>E</strong> education&nbsp;</p><p><strong>F </strong>difference&nbsp;</p><p><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;language</p><p><strong>H</strong> diversity</p><p><strong>I </strong>majority</p><p><strong>J</strong> disappearance</p><p><br/></p><p><br/></p><p>Of the world&#39;s 6,500 living languages, about half of them are expected to be extinct. Most of the world’s languages are spoken by a <strong>27</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[27] ____</strong> of people.</p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"59237","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Turin argued that anthropologists and linguists usually think carefully before selecting an area to research.</strong></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"59238","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Turin concluded that the Thangmi language had few similarities with other languages.</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"59239","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Turin has written that 1000-page document was inappropriate for Thangmi community.</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"59240","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32-35\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Some Nepalese schools lack resources to devote to language teaching.</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"59241","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Why does Turin say people do PhDs on the apostrophe in French?</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"59242","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is discussed in the Paragraph I?</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"59243","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>How is the WOLP’s prospect?</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"59244","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What is Turin’s main point of globalisation?</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"59245","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What does Turin suggest that community people should do?</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The Future of the World’s Language&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>Of the world’s 6,500 living languages, around half are expected to the out by the end of this century, according to UNESCO. Just 11 are spoken by more than half of the earth’s population, so it is little wonder that those used by only a few are being left behind as we become a more homogenous, global society. In short, 95 percent of the world’s languages are spoken by only five percent of its population – a remarkable level of linguistic diversity stored in tiny pockets of speakers around the world. Mark Turin, a university professor, has launched WOLP (World Oral Language Project) to prevent the language from the brink of extinction.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>He is trying to encourage indigenous communities to collaborate with anthropologists around the world to record what he calls ‘oral literature’ through video cameras, voice recorders and other multimedia tools by awarding grants from a £30,000 pot that the project has secured this year. The idea is to collate this literature in a digital archive that can be accessed on demand and will make the nuts and bolts of lost cultures readily available.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>For many of these communities, the oral tradition is at the heart of their culture. The stories they tell are creative as well as communicative. Unlike the languages with celebrated written traditions, such as Sanskrit, Hebrew and Ancient Greek, few indigenous communities have recorded their own languages or ever had them recorded until now.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The project suggested itself when Turin was teaching in Nepal. He wanted to study for a PhD in endangered languages and, while discussing it with his professor at Leiden University in the Netherlands, was drawn to a map on his tutor’s wall. The map was full of pins of a variety of colours which represented all the world’s languages that were completely undocumented. At random, Turin chose a ‘pin’ to document. It happened to belong to the Thangmi tribe, an indigenous community in the hills east of Kathmandu, the capital of Nepal. ‘Many of the choices anthropologists and linguists who work on these traditional field-work projects are quite random,’ he admits.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Continuing his work with the Thangmi community in the 1990s, Turin began to record the language he was hearing, realising that not only was this language and its culture entirely undocumented, it was known to few outside the tiny community. He set about trying to record their language and myth of origins. ‘I wrote 1,000 pages of grammar in English that nobody could use – but I realised that wasn’t enough. It wasn’t enough for me, it wasn’t enough for them. It simply wasn’t going to work as something for the community. So then I produced this trilingual word list in Thangmi, Nepali and English.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In short, it was the first ever publication of that language. That small dictionary is still sold in local schools for a modest 20 rupees, and used as part of a wider cultural regeneration process to educate children about their heritage and language. The task is no small undertaking: Nepal itself is a country of massive ethnic and linguistic diversity, home to 100 languages from four different language families. What’s more, even fewer ethnic Thangmi speak the Thangmi language. Many of the community members have taken to speaking Nepali, the national language taught in schools and spread through the media, and community elders are dying without passing on their knowledge.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Despite Turin’s enthusiasm for his subject, he is baffled by many linguists’ refusal to engage in the issue he is working on. ‘Of the 6,500 languages spoken on Earth, many do not have written traditions and many of these spoken forms are endangered,’ he says, ‘There are more linguists in universities around the world than there are spoken languages – but most of them aren’t working on this issue. To me it’s amazing that in this day and age, we still have an entirely incomplete image of the world’s linguistic diversity. People do PhDs on the apostrophe in French, yet we still don’t know how many languages are spoken.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘When a language becomes endangered, so too does a cultural world view. We want to engage with indigenous people to document their myths and folklore, which can be harder to find funding for if you are based outside Western universities.’&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Yet, despite the struggles facing initiatives such as the World Oral Literature Project, there are historical examples that point to the possibility that language restoration is no mere academic pipe dream. The revival of a modern form of Hebrew in the 19th century is often cited as one of the best proofs that languages long dead, belonging to small communities, can be resurrected and embraced by a large number of people. By the 20th century, Hebrew was well on its way to becoming the main language of the Jewish population of both Ottoman and British Palestine. It is now spoken by more than seven million people in Israel.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>J&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>Yet, despite the difficulties these communities face in saving their languages, Dr Turin believes that the fate of the world’s endangered languages is not sealed, and globalisation is not necessarily the nefarious perpetrator of evil it is often presented to be. ‘I call it the globalisation paradox: on the one hand globalisation and rapid socio-economic change are the things that are eroding and challenging diversity. But on the other, globalisation is providing us with new and very exciting tools and facilities to get to places to document those things that globalisation is eroding. Also, the communities at the coal-face of change are excited by what globalisation has to offer.’&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>K&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In the meantime, the race is on to collect and protect as many of the languages as possible, so that the Rai Shaman in eastern Nepal and those in the generations that follow him can continue their traditions and have a sense of identity. And it certainly is a race: Turin knows his project’s limits and believes it inevitable that a large number of those languages will disappear. ‘We have to be wholly realistic. A project like ours is in no position, and was not designed, to keep languages alive. The only people who can help languages survive are the people in those communities themselves. They need to be reminded that it’s good to speak their own language and I think we can help them do that – becoming modem doesn’t mean you have to lose your language.’</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8090&scene=%E8%AF%AD%E8%A8%80%E6%95%99%E8%82%B2&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8099","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Agriculture and Tourism","book":"阅读还原集Vol.11","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.11 · Test 4 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8099:59035:1","type":"choice","text":"1 About half of all the tourists would spend several days in Monroe.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：More than 40 percent of the visitors came to Monroe for two- or three-day visits.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问“大约一半的游客会在Monroe停留几天”，即询问游客在Monroe停留时间的比例信息。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键词\"Monroe\"和\"spend several days\"（停留几天）定位到B段首句，该句明确提到\"More than 40 percent of the visitors came to Monroe for two- or three-day visits\"（超过40%的游客来Monroe是为了停留两三天）。\n解题思路：原文B段首句的\"More than 40 percent\"（超过40%）与题目中的\"About half\"（大约一半）在比例上高度吻合，且\"two- or three-day visits\"（两三天停留）与\"spend several days\"（停留几天）完全对应。因此B段包含题目所问的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59035","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-F. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-F, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8099:59035:2","type":"choice","text":"2 Most visitors responded positively to a survey project on farm tour.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：More than one-half of those surveyed responded favorably to a proposed tour, saying they would be interested in participating in some type of agricultural tour in southwestern Wisconsin.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是“大多数游客对农场旅游的调查项目做出了积极的回应”，即寻找游客对农场旅游调查的积极反馈。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的“survey project on farm tour”和“responded positively”来定位答案。在A段中，提到对游客的调查，并且明确提到超过一半的受访者对农场旅游表示兴趣。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子“More than one-half of those surveyed responded favorably to a proposed tour, saying they would be interested in participating in some type of agricultural tour in southwestern Wisconsin.”，可以确定A段包含了题目所问的信息，即大多数游客对农场旅游的调查项目做出了积极的回应。因此，答案为A。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59035","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-F. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-F, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8099:59035:3","type":"choice","text":"3 Cooperation across organisations in research for agriculture tours has been carried out.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Lewis is conducting the study with Jean Murphy, assistant community development agent. Other participants include UW-Platteville Agricultural Economist Bob Acton, the Center for Integrated Agricultural Systems, UW-Extension Recreation Resources Center, the Wisconsin Rural Development Center, and Hidden Valleys, a Southwestern Wisconsin regional tourism organization.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落提到了不同组织在农业旅游研究方面的合作。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"Cooperation across organisations\"和\"research for agriculture tours\"，在文章中寻找描述多个组织共同参与农业旅游研究的内容。\n解题思路：E段明确提到了Lewis与Jean Murphy共同进行研究，并且列出了多个参与该研究的组织，包括UW-Platteville Agricultural Economist Bob Acton、Center for Integrated Agricultural Systems、UW-Extension Recreation Resources Center、Wisconsin Rural Development Center和Hidden Valleys。这些信息表明不同组织在农业旅游研究方面确实进行了合作，因此E段包含了题目所询问的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59035","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-F. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-F, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8099:59035:4","type":"choice","text":"4 Agriculture tour assisted tourists to understand more issues concerning animal and environment.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Farm tours could help consumers get the farmer’s perspective on these issues, Lewis notes.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落提到了农业旅游帮助游客了解动物和环境方面的问题。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"animal and environment\"和\"understand more issues\"在文章中定位，找到D段中提到的\"Animal rights and the environment are examples of two issues that concern both urban consumers and farmers\"以及\"Farm tours could help consumers get the farmer’s perspective on these issues\"。\n解题思路：根据原文D段中的句子\"Farm tours could help consumers get the farmer’s perspective on these issues, Lewis notes\"可以确定，D段明确提到了农业旅游可以帮助消费者了解农民对于动物权利和环境问题的看法，与题干信息完全一致。因此，答案为D。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59035","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-F. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-F, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8099:59039:5","type":"choice","text":"5 have focused destination","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：They came specifically to see the Chicago Bears practice.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是哪类访客有特定的目的地。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"focused destination\"（特定目的地）定位到B段中关于Picnic visitors的描述。\n解题思路：原文提到Picnic visitors是\"specifically to see the Chicago Bears practice\"（专门来看芝加哥熊队训练），说明他们有明确的目的地，因此属于B类访客。","options":["Cheese Festival visitors","Picnic visitors","Both of them"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"59039","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5-9\nWhich of following statements belongs to the visitor categories in the box? Please choose A, B or C for each question. Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 5-9 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Cheese Festival visitors\nB Picnic visitors\nC Both of them"},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8099:59039:6","type":"choice","text":"6 majority prepare well before going beforehand","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：More than 75 percent of the Cheese Day visitors planned ahead for the trip, with 37 percent planning at least two months in advance.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是哪个陈述属于框中的访客类别，需要选择A、B或C中的一个字母。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"majority prepare well before going beforehand\"，通过这个关键词可以定位到A段中关于访客提前计划的内容。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子\"More than 75 percent of the Cheese Day visitors planned ahead for the trip, with 37 percent planning at least two months in advance.\"，可以确定大多数Cheese Day的访客都会提前计划行程，这与题目中的\"majority prepare well before going beforehand\"相吻合。因此，这个陈述属于访客类别A。","options":["Cheese Festival visitors","Picnic visitors","Both of them"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"59039","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5-9\nWhich of following statements belongs to the visitor categories in the box? Please choose A, B or C for each question. Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 5-9 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Cheese Festival visitors\nB Picnic visitors\nC Both of them"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8099:59039:7","type":"choice","text":"7 are comparably less keen on picnic meal","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Picnic visitors came specifically to see the Chicago Bears practice. They showed less interest in a proposed agricultural tour than Cheese Day visitors, but more interest in a picnic dinner.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是哪一类游客相对于其他游客来说，对野餐晚餐的兴趣较低。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"less keen on picnic meal\"定位到B段中关于Picnic visitors的描述。\n解题思路：原文提到Picnic visitors对农业旅游提案的兴趣低于Cheese Day visitors，但对野餐晚餐的兴趣更高。因此，Picnic visitors对野餐晚餐的兴趣并不是较低的，而是较高的。而题目问的是哪一类游客对野餐晚餐的兴趣较低，因此需要排除Picnic visitors。根据B段中提到的三类游客，可以推断出elderly people（A类）可能对野餐晚餐的兴趣较低，因为原文并未明确提到他们对野餐晚餐的兴趣程度，而其他两类游客的兴趣程度有明确对比。因此，答案为A。","options":["Cheese Festival visitors","Picnic visitors","Both of them"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"59039","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5-9\nWhich of following statements belongs to the visitor categories in the box? Please choose A, B or C for each question. Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 5-9 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Cheese Festival visitors\nB Picnic visitors\nC Both of them"},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8099:59039:8","type":"choice","text":"8 show interest in activities such as visiting factory tour and fruit","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：More than one-half of those surveyed responded favorably to a proposed tour, saying they would be interested in participating in some type of agricultural tour in southwestern Wisconsin. Survey respondents reported that they would prefer to visit cheese factories, sausage processing plants, dairy farms, and historical farm sites, as well as enjoy an old-fashioned picnic dinner. The study also found strong interest in visiting specialty farms (strawberries, cranberries, poultry, etc.).\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是哪个陈述属于框中的访客类别，具体是访客对参观工厂和水果等活动的兴趣。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"visiting factory tour\"和\"fruit\"等关键词，在A段中找到\"visit cheese factories\"和\"specialty farms (strawberries, cranberries, poultry, etc.)\"这些信息，这些都是工厂参观和水果类活动的具体例子。\n解题思路：根据A段中提到的接受采访者对参观奶酪工厂、香肠加工厂、奶牛场、历史农场遗址以及享受传统野餐晚餐的兴趣，以及他们对参观特色农场（如草莓、蔓越莓、家禽等）的强烈兴趣，可以确定这些访客属于题目中提到的两类访客的集合体。因此，正确答案是C。","options":["Cheese Festival visitors","Picnic visitors","Both of them"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"59039","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5-9\nWhich of following statements belongs to the visitor categories in the box? Please choose A, B or C for each question. Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 5-9 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Cheese Festival visitors\nB Picnic visitors\nC Both of them"},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8099:59039:9","type":"choice","text":"9 are willing to accept a variety of tour recommendations","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The study identified three primary audiences for agricultural tourism: 1) elderly people who take bus tours to see the country; 2) families interested in tours that could be enjoyed by both parents and children; and 3) persons already involved in agriculture,including international visitors.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是哪一类游客愿意接受各种旅游建议。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的\"accept a variety of tour recommendations\"定位到C段中提到的三类游客群体，特别是第三类\"persons already involved in agriculture,including international visitors\"。\n解题思路：根据C段描述，第三类游客包括已经参与农业的人（如国际游客），他们对农业有深入了解，因此更可能接受各种旅游建议。这与题目描述\"accept a variety of tour recommendations\"完全吻合，所以答案为C。","options":["Cheese Festival visitors","Picnic visitors","Both of them"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"59039","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5-9\nWhich of following statements belongs to the visitor categories in the box? Please choose A, B or C for each question. Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 5-9 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Cheese Festival visitors\nB Picnic visitors\nC Both of them"},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8099:59044:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"animal rights","acceptedAnswers":["animal rights"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Animal rights and the environment are examples of two issues that concern both urban consumers and farmers.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问通过农场旅游，游客可以更好地理解哪些重要问题。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"significant issues\"和\"understand\"定位到D段，该段提到了\"Animal rights and the environment are examples of two issues\"。\n解题思路：原文明确列举了两个重要问题作为例子，即\"animal rights\"和\"environment\"，题目只要求填写一个，因此选择\"animal rights\"作为答案。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59044","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-14\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-14 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8099:59045:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"workshops","acceptedAnswers":["workshops"],"explanation":"原文答案句This past fall, Murphy organized several workshops with some Green and Grant County farmers, local business leaders,and motorcoach tour operators to discuss how best to organize and put on farm tours.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求在总结中填写Murphy在秋季组织的活动，限制不超过两个词。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"autumn\"和\"Murphy\"定位到原文中对应的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到Murphy在秋季组织了\"workshops\"，这与题目要求填写的内容完全一致，且符合不超过两个词的限制。因此，答案为\"workshops\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59045","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-14\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-14 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8099:59046:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"picnic/picnic lunch","acceptedAnswers":["picnic","picnic lunch"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Larry Lindgren says these farmers are set to go ahead with more formal agricultural tours next year. The tours will combine a farm visit with a visit to a local cheese factory and a picnic lunch.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问了农民的农场之旅包含参观工厂和什么\n定位关键信息：题目中“Larry Lindgren”和“farm tour”可以直接定位到答案句\n解题思路：答案句中提及了游览行程将结合农场参观、当地奶酪工厂参观以及野餐午餐。题目中已经给出factory visiting，那么还剩下的就是答案“picnic lunch”","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59046","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-14\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-14 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8099:59047:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"Dominican Sisters","acceptedAnswers":["Dominican Sisters"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The land is managed and operated by the Dominican Sisters, who also provide educational opportunities for the local community.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目要求填空，完成对Sinsinawa地区农场的描述，具体是问由谁管理和运营这个农场。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"managed and operated\"和地点\"Sinsinawa\"定位到F段，找到描述农场管理和运营的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到\"the land is managed and operated by the Dominican Sisters\"，直接对应题目中\"managed and operated by\"的空格，因此答案为\"dominican Sisters\"。题目要求不超过两个单词，正好符合。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59047","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-14\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-14 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8099:59048:14","type":"fill","text":"填写第 14 空","answer":"incomes","acceptedAnswers":["incomes"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Lewis says. The project will help expose farmers to the tourism industry and farm vacations as away to possibly supplement incomes,he adds.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问了这个项目可以给当地农民带来额外的什么\n定位关键信息：题目中“project”和“extra”可以直接定位到答案句\n解题思路：答案句中提及了该项目将帮助农民接触旅游业和农场度假，作为可能增加收入的途径。所以答案就是增加的“incomes”","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59048","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-14\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-14 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59035","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1-4\nThe passage has six paragraphs A-F. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-F, in boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>1 </strong>About half of all the tourists would spend several days in Monroe.<strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"59039","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 5-9\nWhich of following statements belongs to the visitor categories in the box? Please choose A, B or C for each question. Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 5-9 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Cheese Festival visitors\nB Picnic visitors\nC Both of them","html":"<p><strong>A </strong>Cheese Festival visitors&nbsp;</p><p><strong>B</strong> Picnic visitors&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>C </strong>Both of them&nbsp;</p><p><strong>5 </strong>have focused destination <strong class=\"source-blank\">[5] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"59044","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-14\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-14 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Through farm tour,visitors can better understand significant issues such as <strong>10</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong> and environment.</p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"59045","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-14\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-14 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>In autumn, Murphy organised <strong>11</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong>&nbsp;and brought other participants together to develop local tour market.</p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"59046","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-14\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-14 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Larry Lindgren said the farmers already had experience of farm tours with factory visiting and a <strong>12</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"59047","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-14\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-14 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>In Sinsinawa, a large area of the farmland contains an orchard, cow etc. which is managed and operated by <strong>13</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong> ;</p>","firstNumber":13},{"id":"59048","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10-14\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 10-14 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>Lewis said the project will probably bring extra <strong>14</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong> for local farmers.</p>","firstNumber":14}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Agriculture and Tourism&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Linkages between the Agri-Food Sector and Tourism offer significant opportunities for the development of both sectors within the region. These linkages could lead to ensuring the sustainability of the region’s tourism product thus ensuring it preservation. Agriculture and tourism – two of Wisconsin’s most industries – are teaming up in southwestern Wisconsin. A pilot project as found that tourists, rural communities, and some farmers could benefit from stronger efforts to promote and market agricultural tourism there. In1990, agricultural tourism project members surveyed 290 visitors to theannual Monroe Cheese Festival and 164 visitors to the Picnic on the Farm, a one-time event held in Platteville in conjunction with the Chicago Bears summer training camp. More than one-half of those surveyed responded favorably to a proposed tour, saying they would be interested in participating in some type of agricultural tour in southwestern Wisconsin. Survey respondents reported that they would prefer to visit cheese factories, sausage processing plants,dairy farms, and historical farm sites, as well as enjoy an old-fashioned picnic dinner. The study also found strong interest in visiting specialty farms (strawberries, cranberries, poultry, etc.). More than 75 percent of the Cheese Day visitors planned ahead for the trip, with 37 percent planning at least two months in advance.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>More than 40 percent of the visitors came to Monroe for two- or three-day visits. Many stopped at other communities on their way to Cheese Days. Visitors at both events indicated that they were there to enjoy themselves and were willing to spend money on food and arts and crafts. They also wanted the opportunity to experience the ‘country’ while there. The study found that planning around existing events should take into account what brought visitors to the area and provide additional attractions that will appeal to them. For example, visitors to Cheese Days said they were on a holiday and appeared to be more open to various tour proposals. Picnic visitors came specifically to see the Chicago Bears practice. They showed less interest in a proposed agricultural tour than Cheese Day visitors, but more interest in a picnic dinner.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The study identified three primary audiences for agricultural tourism: 1) elderly people who take bus tours to see the country; 2) families interested in tours that could be enjoyed by both parents and children; and 3) persons already involved in agriculture,including international visitors. Agricultural tourism can serve to educate urban tourists about the problems and challenges facing farmers,says Andy Lewis, Grant county community development agent. While agriculture is vital to Wisconsin,more and more urban folk are becoming isolated from the industry. In fact, Lewis notes,farmers are just as interested in the educational aspects of agricultural tours as they are in any financial returns.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>‘Farmers feel that urban consumers are out of touch with farming,’ Lewis says, ‘If tourists can be educated on issues that concern farmers,those visits could lead to policies more favorable to agriculture.’ Animal rights and the environment are examples of two issues that concern both urban consumers and farmers. Farm tours could help consumers get the farmer’s perspective on these issues, Lewis notes. Several Wisconsin farms already offer some type of learning experience for tourists. However, most agricultural tourism enterprises currently market their businesses independently, leading to a lack of a concerted effort to promote agricultural tourism as an industry.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Lewis is conducting the study with Jean Murphy, assistant community development agent. Other participants include UW-Platteville Agricultural Economist Bob Acton, the Center for Integrated Agricultural Systems, UW-Extension Recreation Resources Center,the Wisconsin Rural Development Center, and Hidden Valleys, a Southwestern Wisconsin regional tourism organization. This past fall, Murphy organized several workshops with some Green and Grant County farmers, local business leaders,and motorcoach tour operators to discuss how best to organize and put on farm tours. Committees were formed to look at the following: tour site evaluations,inventory of the are’s resources, tour marketing, and familiarization of tours. The fourth committee is organizing tours for people such as tour bus guides and local reporters to help better educate them about agricultural tourism. Green County farmers already have experience hosting visitors during the annual Monroe Cheese Days. Green county Tourism Director Larry Lindgren says these farmers are set to go ahead with more formal agricultural tours next year. The tours will combine a farm visit with a visit to a local cheese factory and a picnic lunch.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Another farm interested in hosting an organized tour is Sinsinawa, a 200-acre Grant County farm devoted to sustainable agriculture and run by the Dominican Sisters. Education plays a major role at the farm, which has an orchard, dairy and beef cows, and hogs. Farm tours could be combined with other activities in the area such as trips to the Mississippi River and/or visits to historical towns or landmarks, Lewis says. The project will help expose farmers to the tourism industry and farm vacations as away to possibly supplement incomes,he adds. While farm families probably wouldn’t make a lot of money through farm tours,they would be compensated for their time, says Lewis. Farmers could earn additional incomes through the sale of farm products,crafts, and recreational activities.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8099&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8116","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Cosmetics in Ancient Past","book":"阅读还原集Vol.11","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.11 · Test 4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8116:59260:15","type":"choice","text":"15 recipes to conceal facial defects caused by aging","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：An Egyptian papyrus from the 16th century BC contains detailed recipes to remove blemishes, wrinkles, and other signs of age.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落包含了关于隐藏因衰老引起的面部缺陷的食谱信息。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"recipes\"和\"facial defects caused by aging\"来定位文章中相关的句子。\n解题思路：在D段中，提到了一份来自公元前16世纪的埃及纸莎草纸，其中包含了详细的食谱，用于去除瑕疵、皱纹和其他年龄迹象。这与题目中询问的隐藏因衰老引起的面部缺陷的食谱信息完全吻合，因此D段是包含该信息的段落。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59260","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nThe passage has 7 paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8116:59260:16","type":"choice","text":"16 perfumes were presented to conquerors in war","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In Assyrian records of tribute and spoils of war, perfumes and resins are mentioned; the text from the time of Tukulti-Ninurta Il (890-884 BC) refers to balls of myrth as part of the tribute brought to the Assyrian king by the Aramaean kings.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问哪个段落提到了“香水被作为礼物赠送给战败的征服者”。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"perfumes\"和\"presented to conquerors in war\"，在文章中定位到G段中提到\"perfumes and resins are mentioned\"以及\"tribute brought to the Assyrian king by the Aramaean kings\"，这与题目信息相符。\n解题思路：G段明确提到在亚述的记录中，提到了战争中的贡品和战利品，其中包括香水和树脂，并且提到了由阿拉米国王带给亚述国王的没药球作为贡品。这与题目中“香水被作为礼物赠送给战败的征服者”的信息完全一致，因此答案为G段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59260","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nThe passage has 7 paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8116:59260:17","type":"choice","text":"17 long hair of girls had special meanings in marriage","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In Ancient Israel, brides would wear their hair long on the wedding day as a sign of their virginity.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是关于女孩长发在婚姻中具有特殊意义的信息。\n定位关键信息：根据题目的关键词\"long hair\"、\"girls\"、\"special meanings\"、\"marriage\"，在文章中寻找相关描述。\n解题思路：在F段中，原文明确提到\"brides would wear their hair long on the wedding day as a sign of their virginity\"，即新娘在婚礼当天会留长发作为纯洁的象征。这与题目中\"女孩长发在婚姻中具有特殊意义\"完全吻合，因此答案为F段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59260","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nThe passage has 7 paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8116:59260:18","type":"choice","text":"18 evidence exists in abundance showing cosmetics use in ancient times","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Evidence also appears in the Bible and other classical writings, where it is written that spices and perfumes were prestigious products known throughout the ancient world and coveted by kings and princes.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问哪个段落包含“大量证据表明古代使用化妆品”的信息。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"evidence\"和\"cosmetics use in ancient times\"定位到A段，该段明确提到\"evidence\"和\"ancient times\"的相关内容。\n解题思路：A段首句提到\"cosmetics and perfumes have been popular since the dawn of civilization\"，接着明确指出\"evidence also appears in the Bible and other classical writings\"，并详细描述了这些证据如何证明古代人们重视身体护理和审美外观，与题目要求的\"大量证据表明古代使用化妆品\"完全一致。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59260","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nThe passage has 7 paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8116:59260:19","type":"choice","text":"19 protecting eyes from fly-transmitted diseases","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Besides beautification, its purpose was also medicinal as covering the sensitive skin of the lids with colored ointments that prevented dryness and eye diseases: the eye-paint repelled the little flies that transmitted eye inflammations.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是哪一段落提到了保护眼睛免受飞虫传播的疾病。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"protecting eyes from fly-transmitted diseases\"可以定位到E段中描述眼部化妆品用途的句子。\n解题思路：E段中明确提到眼部化妆品除了美化外，还有药用目的，可以防止眼睛干燥和疾病，并且眼妆可以驱赶传播眼炎的小飞虫，这与题目所问的信息完全一致，因此答案为E段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59260","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nThe passage has 7 paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8116:59260:20","type":"choice","text":"20 from witchcraft to beautification","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Cosmetics were also connected with cultic worship and witchcraft: to appease the various gods, fragrant ointments were applied to the statuary images and even to their attendants. From this, in the course of time, developed the custom of personal use, to enhance the beauty of the face and the body, and to conceal defects.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落包含了从巫术到美化这一转变过程的信息。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"from witchcraft to beautification\"定位到文章中关于巫术和美化的描述。\n解题思路：B段中明确提到了化妆品最初与巫术和祭祀有关，后来逐渐发展成个人使用的习惯，用于美化面容和身体。因此，B段包含了从巫术到美化的转变过程的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59260","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nThe passage has 7 paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet."},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8116:59260:21","type":"choice","text":"21 more expensive than gold","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Perfumes and fragrant spices were precious commodities in antiquity, very much in demand, and at times even exceeded silver and gold in value.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问哪个段落提到了比黄金更昂贵的信息。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"more expensive than gold\"（比黄金更昂贵）定位答案。在文章中寻找比较价格或价值的句子。\n解题思路：在C段中，原文明确提到\"Perfumes and fragrant spices were... at times even exceeded silver and gold in value.\"（香水和香草在古代是珍贵的商品，有时甚至比白银和黄金更有价值），直接对应题目中\"比黄金更昂贵\"的信息，因此答案为C段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"59260","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nThe passage has 7 paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet."},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8116:59261:22","type":"choice","text":"The written record for cosmetics and perfumes dates back to the third millennium BC.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Cosmetics and perfumes have been popular since the dawn of civilization; it is shown by the discovery of a great deal of pertinent archeological material, dating from the third millennium BC.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问关于化妆品和香水的书面记录是否可以追溯到公元前第三个千年。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"written record\"和\"time\"定位到A段中的\"dating from the third millennium BC\"。\n解题思路：原文提到了公元前第三个千年的考古发现，但并未明确说明这些发现是书面记录。因此，无法确定题目中的\"written record\"是否在原文中有对应信息。所以答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59261","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 2? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8116:59262:23","type":"choice","text":"Since perfumes and spices were luxury products, their use was exclusive to the noble and the wealthy.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：However, within time, the use of cosmetics became the custom of that period. The use of cosmetics became widespread among the lower classes as well as among the wealthy; in the same way they washed the body, so they used to care for the body with substances that softened the skin and anoint it with fragrant oils and ointments.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问“由于香水和香料是奢侈品，所以它们的使用仅限于贵族和富人。”\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“perfumes and spices were luxury products”和“exclusive to the noble and the wealthy”定位到C段开头“Perfumes and fragrant spices were precious commodities in antiquity, very much in demand, and at times even exceeded silver and gold in value. Therefore, they were luxury products, used mainly in the temples and in the homes of the noble and the wealthy.”，再继续向下找到转折词“However”后的句子。\n解题思路：题目说香水和香料是奢侈品，所以它们的使用仅限于贵族和富人。根据原文C段开头确实提到它们是奢侈品，最初主要用于寺庙和贵族富人家庭，但转折词“However”后的句子明确指出“随着时间推移，化妆品的使用成为当时的习俗，不仅在富人中，也在下层阶级中普及；他们像洗澡一样，用能使皮肤柔软的物质和芳香油膏来护理身体。”这与题目“仅限于贵族和富人”的说法矛盾，因此题目陈述是错误的。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59262","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 2? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8116:59263:24","type":"choice","text":"In ancient Far East, fish fats were used as cream by women from poor households.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Sometimes the oil in these creams was extracted from olives, almonds, gourds, sesame, or from trees and plants; but, for those of limited means,scented animal and fish fats were commonly used.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是在古代远东地区，贫苦家庭的妇女是否使用鱼脂肪作为面霜。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键词“ancient Far East”、“fish fats”、“cream”、“women from poor households”定位到D段，找到关于鱼脂肪作为面霜的描述。\n解题思路：根据原文答案对应的句子可知，鱼脂肪是古代远东地区贫苦家庭妇女常用的面霜成分之一，因此题目的陈述与原文信息一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59263","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 2? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8116:59264:25","type":"choice","text":"The teachings in the Bible were repeatedly against the use of kohl for painting the eyes.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The use of kohl for painting the eyes is mentioned three times in the Bible, always with disapproval by the sages (2 Kings, 9:30; Jeremiah 4:30; Ezekiel 23:40).\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是《圣经》是否多次反对用kohl给眼睛上妆。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"the Bible\"和\"use of kohl for painting the eyes\"定位到E段，找到对应的句子。\n解题思路：原文明确提到，《圣经》三次提到用kohl给眼睛上妆，并且每次都是贤者表示不赞同（disapproval）。因此，题目中的\"repeatedly against\"与原文的\"always with disapproval\"意思一致，说明《圣经》确实多次反对这种行为。所以答案是True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59264","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 2? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8116:59265:26","type":"choice","text":"Long hair as a symbol of beauty was worn solely by women of ancient cultures.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Long hair was always considered a symbol of beauty, and kings, nobles and dignitaries grew their hair long and kept it well-groomed and cared for.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问“长发作为美的象征仅由古代文化中的女性佩戴”是否正确。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“long hair as a symbol of beauty”定位到F段首句，该句明确提到长发是美的象征，并列举了国王、贵族和显贵也留长发。\n解题思路：原文明确指出长发不仅是女性的象征，男性如国王、贵族等也留长发，因此“仅由女性佩戴”的说法与原文矛盾，故答案为False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59265","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 2? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8116:59266:27","type":"choice","text":"The Egyptian Queen Hatsheput sent a royal expedition to Punt to establish a trade route for myrrh.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：It is known that the Egyptian Queen Hatsheput (15th century BC) sent a royal expedition to the Land of Punt (Somalia) in order to bring back myrrh seedlings to plant in her temple.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问“埃及女王哈特谢普苏特派遣皇家使团前往彭特，目的是为了建立乳香贸易路线”，要求判断这个陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：通过“Egyptian Queen Hatsheput”、“Punt”和“myrrh”这些关键词定位到G段末句，找到关于哈特谢普苏特派遣使团前往彭特的描述。\n解题思路：原文提到哈特谢普苏特派遣使团是为了带回乳香幼苗种植在寺庙中（bring back myrrh seedlings to plant in her temple），而题目中声称目的是“建立乳香贸易路线”（establish a trade route for myrrh）。所以目的错误，故答案为FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59266","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 2? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59260","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 15-21\nThe passage has 7 paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>15</strong> recipes to conceal facial defects caused by aging <strong class=\"source-blank\">[15] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":15},{"id":"59261","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 2? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The written record for cosmetics and perfumes dates back to the third millennium BC.</strong></p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"59262","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 2? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Since perfumes and spices were luxury products, their use was exclusive to the noble and the wealthy.</strong></p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"59263","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 2? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>In ancient Far East, fish fats were used as cream by women from poor households.</strong></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"59264","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 2? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The teachings in the Bible were repeatedly against the use of kohl for painting the eyes.</strong></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"59265","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 2? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Long hair as a symbol of beauty was worn solely by women of ancient cultures.</strong></p>","firstNumber":26},{"id":"59266","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 22-27\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage 2? In boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The Egyptian Queen Hatsheput sent a royal expedition to Punt to establish a trade route for myrrh.</strong></p>","firstNumber":27}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Cosmetics in Ancient Past&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Since cosmetics and perfumes are still in wide use today, it is interesting to compare the attitudes,customs and beliefs related to them in ancient times to those of our own day and age. Cosmetics and perfumes have been popular since the dawn of civilization; it is shown by the discovery of a great deal of pertinent archeological material, dating from the third millennium BC. Mosaics, glass perfume flasks, stone vessels, ovens, cooking-pots, clay jars, etc., some inscribed by the hand of the artisan. Evidence also appears in the Bible and other classical writings, where it is written that spices and perfumes were prestigious products known throughout the ancient world and coveted by kings and princes. The written and pictorial descriptions, as well as archaeological findings, all show how important body care and aesthetic appearance were in the lives of the ancient people. The chain of evidence spans many centuries, detailing the usage of cosmetics in various cultures from the earliest period of recorded history.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In antiquity, however, at least in the onset,cosmetics served in religious ceremonies and for healing purposes. Cosmetics were also connected with cultic worship and witchcraft: to appease the various gods, fragrant ointments were applied to the statuary images and even to their attendants. From this,in the course of time, developed the custom of personal use, to enhance the beauty of the face and the body, and to conceal defects.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Perfumes and fragrant spices were precious commodities in antiquity, very much in demand, and at times even exceeded silver and gold in value. Therefore, they were luxury products, used mainly in the temples and in the homes of the noble and the wealthy. The Judean kings kept them in treasure houses (2 Kings 20:13). And the Queen of Sheba brought to Solomon ‘camels laden with spices, gold in great quantity and precious stones.’ (1 Kings 10:2,10). However,within time, the use of cosmetics became the custom of that period. The use of cosmetics became widespread among the lower classes as well as among the wealthy; in the same way they washed the body, so they used to care for the body with substances that softened the skin and anoint it with fragrant oils and ointments.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Facial treatment was highly developed and women devoted many hours to it. They used to spread various scented creams on the face and to apply makeup in vivid and contrasting colors. An Egyptian papyrus from the 16th century BC contains detailed recipes to remove blemishes, wrinkles, and other signs of age. Greek and Roman women would cover their faces in the evening with a ‘beauty mask’ to remove blemishes, which consisted mainly of flour mixed with fragrant spices, leaving it on their face all night. The next morning, they would wash it off with asses’ milk. The very common creams used by women in the ancient Far East, particularly important in the hot climate and prevalent in that area of the globe, were made up of oils and aromatic scents. Sometimes the oil in these creams was extracted from olives, almonds, gourds, sesame, or from trees and plants; but, for those of limited means,scented animal and fish fats were commonly used.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Women in the ancient past commonly put colors around their eyes. Besides beautification, its purpose was also medicinal as covering the sensitive skin of the lids with colored ointments that prevented dryness and eye diseases: the eye-paint repelled the little flies that transmitted eye inflammations. Egyptian women colored the upper eyelid black and the lower one green, and painted the space between the upper lid and the eyebrow gray or blue. The women of Mesopotamia favored yellows and reds. The use of kohl for painting the eyes is mentioned three times in the Bible, always with disapproval by the sages (2 Kings, 9:30; Jeremiah 4:30; Ezekiel 23:40). In contrast, Job named one of his daughters ‘Keren Happukh’ – ‘horn of eye paint’(Job 42:14).&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Great importance was attached to the care for hair in ancient times. Long hair was always considered a symbol of beauty, and kings, nobles and dignitaries grew their hair long and kept it well-groomed and cared for. Women devoted much time to the style of the hair; while not cutting, they would apply much care to it by arranging it skillfully in plaits and ‘building it up’ sometimes with the help of wigs. Egyptian women generally wore their hair flowing down to their shoulders or even longer. In Mesopotamia, women cherished long hair as a part of their beauty, and hair flowing down their backs in a thick plait and tied with a ribbon is seen in \\ art. Assyrian women wore their hair shorter, braiding and binding it in a bun at the back. In Ancient Israel, brides would wear their hair long on the wedding day as a sign of their virginity. Ordinary people and slaves, however, usually wore their hair short, mainly for hygienic reasons, since they could not afford to invest in the kind of treatment that long hair required.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>From the Bible and Egyptian and Assyrian sources,as well as the words of classical authors, it appears that the centers of the trade-in aromatic resins and incense were located in the kingdoms of Southern Arabia, and even as far as India, where some of these precious aromatic plants were grown. ‘Dealers from Sheba and Rammah dealt with you, offering the choicest spices...’ (Ezekiel 27:22). The Nabateans functioned as the important middlemen in this trade; Palestine also served as a very important component, as the trade routes crisscrossed the country. lt is known that the Egyptian Queen Hatsheput (15th century BC) sent a royal expedition to the Land of Punt (Somalia) in order to bring back myrrh seedlings to plant in her temple. In Assyrian records of tribute and spoils of war, perfumes and resins are mentioned; the text from the time of Tukulti-Ninurta Il (890-884 BC) refers to balls of myrth as part of the tribute brought to the Assyrian king by the Aramaean kings. The trade in spices and perfumes is also mentioned in the Bible as written in Genesis (37:25-26), ‘Camels carrying gum tragacanth and balm and myrrh’.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8116&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8117","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Facial Expression","book":"阅读还原集Vol.11","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.11 · Test 4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8117:59246:28","type":"fill","text":"填写第 28 空","answer":"misidentified","acceptedAnswers":["misidentified"],"explanation":"原文答案句：problems associated with the study include the fact that both fear and surprise were constantly misidentified.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是Ekman的研究结果表明，恐惧和惊讶被持续地什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"Ekman's study\"、\"fear and surprise\"和\"persistently\"定位答案在文章中的句子。\n解题思路：根据原文G段中的句子\"problems associated with the study include the fact that both fear and surprise were constantly misidentified.\"，可以确定\"constantly misidentified\"对应题目中的\"persistently\"，因此答案为\"misidentified\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59246","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8117:59246:29","type":"fill","text":"填写第 29 空","answer":"emotions","acceptedAnswers":["emotions"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The study concluded that certain facial expressions correspond to particular emotions and can not be covered, regardless of cultural background, and regardless of whether or not the culture has been isolated or exposed to the mainstream.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是面部表情与什么有关，要求根据文章内容填写答案。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"facial expressions\"和\"have something to do with\"定位到G段中的\"facial expressions correspond to particular emotions\"。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到面部表情与特定的情感相对应（\"correspond to particular emotions\"），因此可以确定答案为\"emotions\"。题目中的\"have something to do with\"与原文中的\"correspond to\"意思一致，都表示\"与...相关\"或\"对应于...\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59246","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8117:59246:30","type":"fill","text":"填写第 30 空","answer":"cultural background","acceptedAnswers":["cultural background"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The study concluded that certain facial expressions correspond to particular emotions and can not be covered, regardless of cultural background, and regardless of whether or not the culture has been isolated or exposed to the mainstream.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是哪种背景无法掩盖面部表情，需要根据原文填空。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"impossible covered\"和\"despite of\"定位到G段中\"can not be covered, regardless of cultural background\"这句话。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到面部表情无法被掩盖，不论文化背景如何，也不论文化是否孤立或接触主流。因此，题目中\"despite of\"对应\"regardless of\"，空格处应填入原文中的\"cultural background\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59246","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8117:59246:31","type":"fill","text":"填写第 31 空","answer":"isolated","acceptedAnswers":["isolated"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The study concluded that certain facial expressions correspond to particular emotions and can not be covered, regardless of cultural background, and regardless of whether or not the culture has been isolated or exposed to the mainstream.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是文化是否被某种状态所影响，需要根据上下文理解填空。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的“whether the culture has been”可以定位到G段最后一句，这里提到了文化是否被隔离或接触主流。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到了“isolated or exposed to the mainstream”，根据题目中的“and whether the culture has been”可以推断出需要填入的是“isolated”，表示文化是否被隔离。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59246","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8117:59246:32","type":"fill","text":"填写第 32 空","answer":"exposed","acceptedAnswers":["exposed"],"explanation":"原文答案句：can not be covered, regardless of cultural background, and regardless of whether or not the culture has been isolated or exposed to the mainstream.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目要求根据原文填空，完成句子\"or 32.%% to the mainstream.\"，需要从文章中找出合适的单词填入。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"mainstream\"一词，可以在G段找到相关句子，该句子中提到了\"exposed to the mainstream\"，这与题目中的空格位置和内容相符。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句中的\"exposed to the mainstream\"可以确定，空格处应填入\"exposed\"，因为这是与\"mainstream\"直接相关的词汇，且符合题目要求不超过两个单词的限制。因此，答案为\"exposed\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"59246","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","maxWords":2},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8117:59251:33","type":"choice","text":"the difficulty identifying the actual meaning of facial expressions","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Others, however, are difficult to interpret even in familiar individuals. For instance, disgust and fear can be tough to tell apart.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是“识别面部表情实际含义的困难”这一信息出现在哪个段落。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是“difficulty identifying the actual meaning of facial expressions”，在文章中寻找关于识别面部表情困难性的描述。\n解题思路：根据原文句子“Others, however, are difficult to interpret even in familiar individuals. For instance, disgust and fear can be tough to tell apart.”，这句话明确指出了有些面部表情难以解释，即使是在熟悉的人之间，例如厌恶和恐惧难以区分。这与题目中“识别面部表情实际含义的困难”完全吻合，因此答案为C段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"59251","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-38\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 33-38 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8117:59251:34","type":"choice","text":"the importance of culture on facial expressions is initially described","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Facial expressions and their significance in the perceiver can, to some extent, vary between cultures with evidence from descriptions in the works of Charles Darwin.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问的是关于文化对表情重要性最初的描述。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“importance of culture on facial expressions”和“initially described”来定位文章中相关的句子。\n解题思路：在A段中，原文明确提到了“Facial expressions and their significance in the perceiver can, to some extent, vary between cultures”，这表明文化对表情的重要性被描述了出来。同时，文章还提到了“with evidence from descriptions in the works of Charles Darwin”，这表明这种描述是来自于达尔文的作品，可以理解为最初的描述。因此，A段包含了关于文化对表情重要性最初的描述。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"59251","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-38\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 33-38 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8117:59251:35","type":"choice","text":"collected data for the research on the relation between blink and the success in elections","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Research by Boston College professor Joe Tecce suggests that stress levels are revealed by blink rates. He supports his data with statistics on the relation between the blink rates of presidential candidates and their success in their races.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是谁收集了关于眨眼率与选举成功之间关系的研究数据。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"blink\"和\"success in elections\"在文章中定位。\n解题思路：在D段中，提到了波士顿学院教授Joe Tecce的研究，他的研究表明眨眼率可以揭示压力水平，并且他用统计数据支持了眨眼率与总统候选人选举成功之间的关系。这与题目中提到的收集关于眨眼率与选举成功之间关系的研究数据的信息一致，因此答案为D。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"59251","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-38\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 33-38 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8117:59251:36","type":"choice","text":"the features on sociality of several facial expressions","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Expressions Ekman found to be universally included those indicating anger, disgust, fear, joy, sadness, and surprise (not that none of these emotions has a definitive social component, such as shame, pride, or schadenfreude). Findings on contempt (which is social) are less clear, though there is at least some preliminary evidence that this emotion and its expression are universally recognized.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是哪个段落提到了几个面部表情的社会性特征。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"features on sociality\"和\"several facial expressions\"在文章中定位。\n解题思路：H段明确提到了Ekman发现的一些面部表情具有社会性特征，如羞耻、骄傲和幸灾乐祸，同时提到轻蔑（contempt）是一种社会性情感，其表情也被普遍认可。这些信息与题目要求完全吻合，因此答案为H。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"59251","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-38\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 33-38 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8117:59251:37","type":"choice","text":"an indicator to reflect one’s extent of nervousness","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Blink rate can reveal how nervous or at ease a person maybe.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问哪个段落包含“反映一个人紧张程度指标”的信息。\n定位关键信息：通过题目的“nervousness”和“indicator”定位到D段首句，该句提到“眨眼频率可以揭示一个人是紧张还是放松”。\n解题思路：原文明确指出“眨眼频率”是反映紧张程度的指标，与题目中的“紧张程度指标”完全对应，因此答案为D段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"59251","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-38\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 33-38 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8117:59251:38","type":"choice","text":"the relation between emotion and facial expressions","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Humans can adopt a facial expression to read as a voluntary action. However, because expressions are closely tied to emotion, they are more often involuntary.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是关于情绪和面部表情之间的关系。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"emotion\"和\"facial expressions\"定位到文章中关于这两者关系的句子。\n解题思路：原文B段明确指出，面部表情与情绪密切相关，通常是无意识的，但也可能是自愿的。这与题目中询问的情绪和面部表情之间的关系完全一致，因此答案为B。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"59251","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-38\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 33-38 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8117:59252:39-40","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following statements are true according to Ekman’s theory?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nB. The potential relationship between facial expressions and state of mind exists\nD. Different areas on face convey certain state of mind.\n对应段落：\nB段和H段\n审题：题目问根据Ekman的理论，以下哪两个陈述是正确的。\n定位关键信息：\n通过题目中的关键词\"Ekman’s theory\"定位到文章中与Ekman相关的内容，主要集中在E段、F段、G段和H段。\n解题思路：\n1. 选项B中的\"the potential relationship between facial expressions and state of mind exists\"对应B段的内容。B段提到\"the close link between emotion and expression can also work in the order direction; it has been observed that voluntarily assuming an expression can actually cause the associated emotion.\"这句话表明表情和情绪之间存在联系，即表情可以反映或影响情绪状态，与选项B的表述一致。\n2. 选项D中的\"different areas on face convey certain state of mind\"对应H段的内容。H段提到\"this may suggest that the facial expressions are largely related to the mind and each part on the face can express specific emotion.\"这句话明确说明面部不同部位可以表达特定的情绪，与选项D的表述一致。\n3. 其他选项分析：\n- A选项提到动物的面部表情，但Ekman的研究主要关注人类，且E段提到\"the young and the old of widely different races, both with man and animals, express the same state of mind by the same movements\"，说明动物也有表情，但A选项表述过于绝对，且与Ekman的理论无关。\n- C选项提到不同文化，但Ekman的研究重点是表情的普遍性，而非文化差异。\n- E选项与D选项重复，且表述不完整。\n因此，正确答案是B和D。","options":["No evidence shows animals have their own facial expressions.","The potential relationship between facial expressions and state of mind exists","Facial expressions are concerning different cultures.","Different areas on face convey certain state of mind.","Mind controls men’s facial expressions more obvious than women’s"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"59252","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 39-40\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"59252-8117:59252:39-40"},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8117:59252:39-40","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following statements are true according to Ekman’s theory?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nB. The potential relationship between facial expressions and state of mind exists\nD. Different areas on face convey certain state of mind.\n对应段落：\nB段和H段\n审题：题目问根据Ekman的理论，以下哪两个陈述是正确的。\n定位关键信息：\n通过题目中的关键词\"Ekman’s theory\"定位到文章中与Ekman相关的内容，主要集中在E段、F段、G段和H段。\n解题思路：\n1. 选项B中的\"the potential relationship between facial expressions and state of mind exists\"对应B段的内容。B段提到\"the close link between emotion and expression can also work in the order direction; it has been observed that voluntarily assuming an expression can actually cause the associated emotion.\"这句话表明表情和情绪之间存在联系，即表情可以反映或影响情绪状态，与选项B的表述一致。\n2. 选项D中的\"different areas on face convey certain state of mind\"对应H段的内容。H段提到\"this may suggest that the facial expressions are largely related to the mind and each part on the face can express specific emotion.\"这句话明确说明面部不同部位可以表达特定的情绪，与选项D的表述一致。\n3. 其他选项分析：\n- A选项提到动物的面部表情，但Ekman的研究主要关注人类，且E段提到\"the young and the old of widely different races, both with man and animals, express the same state of mind by the same movements\"，说明动物也有表情，但A选项表述过于绝对，且与Ekman的理论无关。\n- C选项提到不同文化，但Ekman的研究重点是表情的普遍性，而非文化差异。\n- E选项与D选项重复，且表述不完整。\n因此，正确答案是B和D。","options":["No evidence shows animals have their own facial expressions.","The potential relationship between facial expressions and state of mind exists","Facial expressions are concerning different cultures.","Different areas on face convey certain state of mind.","Mind controls men’s facial expressions more obvious than women’s"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"59252","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 39-40\nChoose TWO correct answers","groupId":"59252-8117:59252:39-40"}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"59252-8117:59252:39-40","numbers":[39,40],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["B","D"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59246","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 28-32\nComplete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 28-32 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p>The result of Ekman’s study demonstrates that fear and surprise are persistently <strong>28</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[28] ____</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">and made a conclusion that some facial expressions have something to do with certain&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">29</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[29] ____</strong>&nbsp;which is impossible covered,&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">despite of&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">30</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[30] ____</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">and whether the culture has been&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">31</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[31] ____</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">or&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">32&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><strong class=\"source-blank\">[32] ____</strong> to the mainstream.</span></span></span></span></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"59251","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 33-38\nThe passage has seven paragraphs A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-H, in boxes 33-38 on your answer sheet.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.","html":"<p><strong>33 </strong>the difficulty identifying the actual meaning of facial expressions <strong class=\"source-blank\">[33] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"59252","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 39-40\nChoose TWO correct answers","html":"<p><strong>Which TWO of the following statements are true according to Ekman’s theory?</strong></p>","firstNumber":39}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Facial Expression</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A facial expression is one or more motions or positions of the muscles in the skin. These movements convey the emotional state of the individual to observers. Facial expressions are a form of nonverbal communication. They are a primary means of conveying social information among aliens, but also occur in most other mammals and some other animal species. Facial expressions and their significance in the perceiver can, to some extent, vary between cultures with evidence from descriptions in the works of Charles Darwin.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Humans can adopt a facial expression to read as a voluntary action. However, because expressions are closely tied to emotion, they are more often involuntary. It can be nearly impossible to avoid expressions for certain emotions, even when it would be strongly desirable to do so; a person who is trying to avoid insulting an individual he or she finds highly unattractive might, nevertheless, show a brief expression of disgust before being able to reassume a neutral expression. Microexpressions are one example of this phenomenon. The close link between emotion and expression can also work in the order direction; it has been observed that voluntarily assuming an expression can actually cause the associated emotion.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Some expressions can be accurately interpreted even between members of different species – anger and extreme contentment being the primary examples. Others, however, are difficult to interpret even in familiar individuals. For instance, disgust and fear can be tough to tell apart. Because faces have only a limited range of movement, expressions rely upon fairly minuscule differences in the proportion and relative position of facial features, and reading them requires considerable sensitivity to the same. Some faces are often falsely read as expressing some emotion, even when they are neutral because their proportions naturally resemble those another face would temporarily assume when emoting.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Also, a person’s eyes reveal much about hos they are feeling, or what they are thinking. Blink rate can reveal how nervous or at ease a person maybe. Research by Boston College professor Joe Tecce suggests that stress levels are revealed by blink rates. He supports his data with statistics on the relation between the blink rates of presidential candidates and their success in their races. Tecce claims that the faster blinker in the presidential debates has lost every election since 1980. Though Tecce’s data is interesting, it is important to recognize that non-verbal communication is multi-channelled, and focusing on only one aspect is reckless. Nervousness can also be measured by examining each candidates’ perspiration, eye contact and stiffness.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>As Charles Darwin noted in his book The Expression of the Emotions in Man and Animals: the young and the old of widely different races, both with man and animals, express the same state of mind by the same movements. Still, up to the mid-20th century, most anthropologists believed that facial expressions were entirely learned and could, therefore, differ among cultures. Studies conducted in the 1960s by Paul Ekman eventually supported Darwin’s belief to a large degree.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Ekman’s work on facial expressions had its starting point in the work of psychologist Silvan Tomkins. Ekman showed that contrary to the belief of some anthropologists including Margaret Mead, facial expressions of emotion are not culturally determined, but universal across human cultures. The South Fore people of New Guinea were chosen as subjects for one such survey. The study consisted of 189 adults and 130 children from among a very isolated population, as well as twenty-three members of the culture who lived a less isolated lifestyle as a control group. Participants were told a story that described one particular emotion; they were then shown three pictures (two for children) of facial expressions and asked to match the picture which expressed the story’s emotion.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>While the isolated South Fore people could identify emotions with the same accuracy as the non-isolated control group, problems associated with the study include the fact that both fear and surprise were constantly misidentified. The study concluded that certain facial expressions correspond to particular emotions and can not be covered, regardless of cultural background, and regardless of whether or not the culture has been isolated or exposed to the mainstream.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Expressions Ekman found to be universally included those indicating anger, disgust, fear, joy, sadness, and surprise (not that none of these emotions has a definitive social component, such as shame, pride, or schadenfreude). Findings on contempt (which is social) are less clear, though there is at least some preliminary evidence that this emotion and its expression are universally recognized. This may suggest that the facial expressions are largely related to the mind and each part on the face can express specific emotion.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8117&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8052","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Thomas Young","book":"阅读还原集Vol.11","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test3","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.11 · Test3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"8052:58702:1","type":"choice","text":"‘The last man who knew everything’ has also been claimed to other people.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Young has competition, however: The phrase, which Robinson takes for his title, also serves as the subtitle of two other recent biographies: Leonard Warren's 1998 life of paleontologist Joseph Leidy (1823-1891) and Paula Findlen's 2004 book on Athanasius Kircher (1602-1680), another polymath.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问\"The last man who knew everything\"这个称号是否也被用于其他人。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"The last man who knew everything\"和\"claimed to other people\"这两个关键信息，可以在文章中定位到相关内容。\n解题思路：在A段中，明确提到\"The phrase, which Robinson takes for his title, also serves as the subtitle of two other recent biographies\"，即这个短语也被用作其他两本传记的副标题，一本是关于Joseph Leidy的，另一本是关于Athanasius Kircher的。这表明\"The last man who knew everything\"这个称号也被用于其他人，因此题干的说法是正确的。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58702","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"8052:58707:2","type":"choice","text":"All Young's articles were published in Encyclopedia Britannica.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Between 1816 and 1825 he contributed his many and various entries to the Encyclopedia Britannica, and throughout his career, he authored numerous books, essays and papers.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问杨的所有文章是否都发表在大英百科全书上\n定位关键信息：利用\"Young\"、\"articles\"和\"Encyclopedia Britannica\"这些关键词定位相关信息\n解题思路：原文中提到杨为大英百科全书撰写了63篇文章，但E段明确指出\"throughout his career, he authored numerous books, essays and papers\"，这表明杨在他的职业生涯中撰写了许多书籍、散文和论文，而不仅仅是给大英百科全书的文章。因此，题目中\"All Young's articles were published in Encyclopedia Britannica\"这一陈述是错误的，答案为B（False）。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58707","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"8052:58708:3","type":"choice","text":"Like others, Young wasn't so brilliant when growing up.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：These are the landmark achievements of a man who was a child prodigy and who, unlike many remarkable children, did not disappear into oblivion as an adult.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问Young在成长过程中是否像其他人一样不那么出色/聪明。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"growing up\"（成长过程中）和\"wasn't so brilliant\"（不那么出色/聪明）。我们需要在文章中找到关于Young童年和成长时期的信息。\n解题思路：原文对应信息出现在第三段最后一句话“These are the landmark achievements of a man who was a child prodigy（天才儿童）and who，unlike many remarkable（卓越的）children, did not disappear into oblivion（遗忘）as an adul”，说明了杨在小时候就已经是一个天才儿童，长大后也没有泯然众人，所以答案是False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58708","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"8052:58709:4","type":"choice","text":"Young's talent as a doctor surpassed his other skills.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Young's skill as a physician, however, did not equal his skill as a scholar of natural philosophy or linguistics.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是杨作为医生的才能是否超越了他的其他技能。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"doctor\"（医生）和\"skills\"（技能）可以定位到E段中关于杨作为医生的技能的描述。\n解题思路：原文中\"Young's skill as a physician, however, did not equal his skill as a scholar of natural philosophy or linguistics.\"这句话表明杨作为医生的技能并不等同于他作为自然哲学或语言学学者的技能，即自然哲学或语言学学者的技能高于医生，属于原文提到考点，但方向不一致，所以答案是FALSE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58709","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"8052:58710:5","type":"choice","text":"Young's advice was sought by people responsible for local and national issues.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：His opinions were sought on civic and national matters, such as the introduction of gas lighting to London and methods of ship construction.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问Young的建议是否被负责地方和国家事务的人们寻求。\n定位关键信息：题干中的关键词是\"advice was sought\"和\"local and national issues\"，对应原文中的\"opinions were sought\"和\"civic and national matters\"。\n解题思路：在E段中明确提到\"His opinions were sought on civic and national matters\"，这与题干中的\"Young's advice was sought by people responsible for local and national issues\"表达的意思完全一致。原文还提供了具体例子，如伦敦煤气照明和船舶建造方法的咨询，进一步证实了Young确实在地方和国家事务上被寻求建议。因此，这个陈述是正确的。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58710","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"8052:58711:6","type":"choice","text":"Young took part in various social pastimes.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Young was introduced into elite society, attended the theatre and learned to dance and play the flute. In addition, he was an accomplished horseman.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问Young是否参加了各种社交娱乐活动。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"social pastimes\"（社交娱乐活动）作为关键词，在文章中寻找相关描述。\n解题思路：在F段中明确提到Young被引入上流社会，参加剧院活动，学习跳舞和吹长笛，而且还是一位出色的骑手。这些都是社交娱乐活动的具体例子，因此可以确定Young确实参加了各种社交娱乐活动，所以答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58711","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"8052:58712:7","type":"choice","text":"Young suffered from a disease in his later years.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：无\n对应段落：无\n审题：题目问Thomas Young在晚年是否患有疾病。\n定位关键信息：需要查找原文中是否有关于Young晚年健康状况或疾病的信息，关键词是\"suffered from a disease\"和\"in his later years\"。\n解题思路：仔细阅读原文所有段落，发现文中提到了Young的生平、学术成就、职业发展和个人生活，但没有任何一处提到他在晚年患有疾病。虽然文中提到他成为医生(E段)以及他的婚姻生活(G段)，但完全没有涉及他自己的健康状况，特别是晚年是否患病。由于原文中没有提供相关信息，无法判断题目陈述的真假，因此答案应为C（NOT GIVEN）。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58712","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"8052:58713:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"46","acceptedAnswers":["46"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Thomas Young (1773-1829) contributed 63 articles to the Encyclopedia Britannica, including 46 biographical entries (mostly on scientists and classicists) and substantial essays on 'Bridge', 'Chromatics', 'Egypt', 'Languages' and 'Tides'.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问Young为《Encyclopedia Britannica》写了几篇人物传记(life stories)。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"life stories\"和\"Encyclopedia Britannica\"可以定位到原文A段。在原文中，\"life stories\"对应的是\"biographical entries\"，即人物传记。\n解题思路：原文A段明确指出Young为《Encyclopedia Britannica》写了63篇文章，其中包括46篇人物传记(biographical entries)。题目中的\"life stories\"就是指\"biographical entries\"(人物传记)，因此答案是46。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"58713","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"8052:58714:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"human eye/human eye accommodation/Human Eye/Human Eye Accommodation","acceptedAnswers":["human eye","human eye accommodation","Human Eye","Human Eye Accommodation"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In the paper, Young explained the process of accommodation in the human eye – on how the eye focuses properly on objects at varying distances.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目询问Thomas Young的第一篇学术论文专注于哪个方面的科学研究。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"first academic paper\"可以定位到B段中的\"He presented his first paper to the Royal Society of London at the age of 20\"，然后紧接着就是这篇论文的内容。\n解题思路：在B段中，明确指出Young的第一篇论文解释了人眼调节的过程（accommodation in the human eye），即眼睛如何正确聚焦在不同距离的物体上。因此，答案就是\"human eye accommodation\"或\"human eye\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"58714","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"8052:58703:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"Indo-European/indo-european","acceptedAnswers":["Indo-European","indo-european"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In another entry, he coined the term Indo-European to describe the family of languages spoken throughout most of Europe and northern India.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问Young引入了什么名称来指代一组语言。\n定位关键信息：可以通过关键词\"name\"、\"introduce\"和\"group of languages\"来定位答案在文章中的位置。在文章中，我们需要找到Young创造或引入语言名称的相关描述。\n解题思路：在C段中，明确提到\"he coined the term Indo-European to describe the family of languages\"，这里的\"coined the term\"表示创造了一个术语，与题目中的\"introduce\"（引入）相对应。\"Indo-European\"就是Young引入用来指代欧洲大部分和北印度地区语言家族的名称。因此，答案为\"Indo-European\"或者\"indo-european\"（大小写均可）。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"58703","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"8052:58704:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"Richard Brocklesby/richard brocklesby","acceptedAnswers":["Richard Brocklesby","richard brocklesby"],"explanation":"原文答案句：After leaving school, he was greatly encouraged by his mother's uncle, Richard Brocklesby, a physician and Fellow of the Royal Society. Following Brocklesby's lead, Young decided to pursue a career in medicine.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是谁激励Young开始他的医学研究。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"inspired\"（激励）和\"medical studies\"（医学研究）。在文章中，我们需要找到与这些关键词相关的信息。在D段中，我们可以找到\"greatly encouraged\"（极大地鼓励）和\"pursue a career in medicine\"（从事医学职业）这些表达，它们与题目中的关键词相匹配。\n解题思路：在D段中，文章明确指出Young在离开学校后，受到了他母亲的叔叔Richard Brocklesby的极大鼓励。Brocklesby是一名医生和皇家学会会员。文章接着说\"Following Brocklesby's lead, Young decided to pursue a career in medicine\"（跟随Brocklesby的脚步，Young决定从事医学职业）。这清楚地表明Brocklesby是激励Young开始医学研究的人。因此，答案是Richard Brocklesby。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"58704","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"8052:58705:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"Royal Institution/royal institution/Royal institution","acceptedAnswers":["Royal Institution","royal institution","Royal institution"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Earlier, in 1801, he had been appointed to a professorship of natural philosophy at the Royal Institution, where he delivered as many as 60 lectures in a year.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是Young在哪里获得了教学职位。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"teaching position\"（教学职位），在文章中对应的表达是\"professorship\"（教授职位）或\"lectures\"（讲座）。\n解题思路：在E段中，明确提到Young在1801年被任命为皇家学会(Royal Institution)的自然哲学教授，并在那里授课。这直接回答了题目关于Young获得教学职位地点的问题。因此，答案为\"Royal Institution\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"58705","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"8052:58706:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"gas lighting/Gas Lighting","acceptedAnswers":["gas lighting","Gas Lighting"],"explanation":"原文答案句：His opinions were sought on civic and national matters, such as the introduction of gas lighting to London and methods of ship construction.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问Young对伦敦做出了什么贡献。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"contribution\"（贡献）和\"London\"（伦敦）这两个关键词，可以在文章中定位到E段的相关内容。\n解题思路：在E段中，明确提到\"His opinions were sought on civic and national matters, such as the introduction of gas lighting to London...\"，表明Young的意见被征询关于向伦敦引入煤气照明的事宜。这直接回答了题目询问Young对伦敦做出什么贡献的问题，因此答案为\"gas lighting\"或\"Gas Lighting\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"58706","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","maxWords":3}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"58702","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>‘The last man who knew everything’ has also been claimed to other people.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"58707","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>All Young&#39;s articles were published in Encyclopedia Britannica.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"58708","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Like others, Young wasn&#39;t so brilliant when growing up.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"58709","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Young&#39;s talent as a doctor surpassed his other skills.</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"58710","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Young&#39;s advice was sought by people responsible for local and national issues.</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"58711","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Young took part in various social pastimes.</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"58712","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1-7\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the passage? Choose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Young suffered from a disease in his later years.</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"58713","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>8</strong> How many life stories did Young write for the Encyclopedia Britannica?</p><p><strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"58714","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>9</strong> What aspect of scientific research did Young focus on in his first academic paper?</p><p><strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"58703","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>10</strong> What name did Young introduce to refer to a group of languages?</p><p><strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"58704","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>11</strong> Who inspired Young to start his medical studies?</p><p><strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"58705","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>12</strong> Where did Young get a teaching position?</p><p><strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"58706","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8-13\nAnswer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","html":"<p><strong>13</strong> What contribution did Young make to London?</p><p><strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p><strong>Thomas Young</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Thomas Young (1773-1829) contributed 63 articles to the Encyclopedia Britannica, including 46 biographical entries (mostly on scientists and classicists) and substantial essays on ‘Bridge’, ‘Chromatics’, ‘Egypt’, ‘Languages’ and ‘Tides’. Was someone who could write authoritatively about so many subjects a polymath, a genius or a dilettante? In an ambitious new biography, Andrew Robinson argues that Young is a good contender for the epitaph ‘the last man who knew everything’. Young has competition, however: The phrase, which Robinson takes for his title, also serves as the subtitle of two other recent biographies: Leonard Warren’s 1998 life of paleontologist Joseph Leidy (1823-1891) and Paula Findlen’s 2004 book on Athanasius Kircher (1602-1680), another polymath.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Young, of course, did more than write encyclopedia entries. He presented his first paper to the Royal Society of London at the age of 20 and was elected a Fellow a week after his 21st birthday. In the paper, Young explained the process of accommodation in the human eye – on how the eye focuses properly on objects at varying distances. Young hypothesized that this was achieved by changes in the shape of the lens. Young also theorized that light traveled in waves and ho believed that, to account for the ability to see in color, there must be three receptors in the eye corresponding to the three ‘principal colors’ to which the retina could respond: red, green, violet. All these hypotheses were subsequently proved to be correct.</p><p><br/></p><p>C</p><p><br/></p><p>Later in his life, when he was in his forties, Young was instrumental in cracking the code that unlocked the unknown script on the Rosetta Stone, a tablet that was ‘found’ in Egypt by the Napoleonic army in 1799. The stone contains text in three alphabets: Greek, something unrecognizable and Egyptian hieroglyphs. The unrecognizable script is now known as demotic and, as Young deduced, is related directly to hieroglyphic. His initial work on this appeared in his Britannica entry on Egypt. In another entry, he coined the term Indo-European to describe the family of languages spoken throughout most of Europe and northern India. These are the landmark achievements of a man who was a child prodigy and who, unlike many remarkable children, did not disappear into oblivion as an adult.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Born in 1773 in Somerset in England, Young lived from an early age with his maternal grandfather, eventually leaving to attend boarding school. He had devoured books from the age of two, and through his own initiative, he excelled at Latin, Greek, mathematics and natural philosophy. After leaving school, he was greatly encouraged by his mother’s uncle, Richard Brocklesby, a physician and Fellow of the Royal Society. Following Brocklesby’s lead, Young decided to pursue a career in medicine. He studied in London, following the medical circuit, and then moved on to more formal education in Edinburgh, Gottingen and Cambridge. After completing his medical training at the University of Cambridge in 1808, Young set up practice as a physician in London. He soon became a Fellow of the Royal College of Physicians and a few years later was appointed physician at St. George’s Hospital.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Young’s skill as a physician, however, did not equal his skill as a scholar of natural philosophy or linguistics. Earlier, in 1801, he had been appointed to a professorship of natural philosophy at the Royal Institution, where he delivered as many as 60 lectures in a year. These were published in two volumes in 1807. In 1804 Young had become secretary to the Royal Society, a post he would hold until his death. His opinions were sought on civic and national matters, such as the introduction of gas lighting to London and methods of ship construction. From 1819 he was superintendent of the Nautical Almanac and secretary to the Board of Longitude. From 1824 to 1829 he was physician to and inspector of calculations for the Palladian Insurance Company. Between 1816 and 1825 he contributed his many and various entries to the Encyclopedia Britannica, and throughout his career, he authored numerous books, essays and papers.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Young is a perfect subject for a biography – perfect, but daunting. Few men contributed so much to so many technical fields. Robinson’s aim is to introduce non-scientists to Young’s work and life. He succeeds, providing clear expositions of the technical material (especially that on optics and Egyptian hieroglyphs). Some readers of this book will, like Robinson, find Young’s accomplishments impressive; others will see him as some historians have – as a dilettante. Yet despite the rich material presented in this book, readers will not end up knowing Young personally. We catch glimpses of a playful Young, doodling Greek and Latin phrases in his notes on medical lectures and translating the verses that a young lady had written on the walls of a summerhouse into Greek elegiacs. Young was introduced into elite society, attended the theatre and learned to dance and play the flute. In addition, he was an accomplished horseman. However, his personal life looks pale next to his vibrant career and studies.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Young married Eliza Maxwell in 1804, and according to Robinson, ‘their marriage was a happy one and she appreciated his work’. Almost all we know about her is that she sustained her husband through some rancorous disputes about optics and that she worried about money when his medical career was slow to take off. Very little evidence survives about the complexities of Young’s relationships with his mother and father. Robinson does not credit them, or anyone else, with shaping Young’s extraordinary mind. Despite the lack of details concerning Young’s relationships, however, anyone interested in what it means to be a genius should read this book.</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8052&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8053","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Leaf-Cutting Ants And Fungus","book":"阅读还原集Vol.11","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test3","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.11 · Test3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8053:58715:14","type":"choice","text":"14 build small nests and live with the different foreign fungus.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The other groups, known as the lower attines because their nests are smaller and their techniques more primitive, feed their gardens with detritus like dead leaves, insects and faeces. But the lower attine ants used different varieties of the fungus, and in one case a quite separate species.\n审题：题目询问哪种蚂蚁建造小巢穴并与不同的外来真菌一起生活。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"build small nests\"定位到C段中的\"nests are smaller\"，描述lower attines的巢穴较小；利用\"live with the different foreign fungus\"定位到D段中的\"used different varieties of the fungus\"，说明lower attines使用不同种类的真菌。\n解题思路：在C段，文章明确指出lower attines的巢穴较小；在D段，进一步说明lower attines使用不同品种的真菌，包括一个完全不同的物种。结合这两点，可以确定lower attines符合题目的描述，因此答案为B，代表Lower attines。","options":["Leaf-cutting ants","Lower attines","Both"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"58715","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nUse the information in the passage to match the options (listed A-C) with activities or features of ants below.\nChoose the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 14-19.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Leaf-cutting ants\nB Lower attines\nC Both"},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8053:58715:15","type":"choice","text":"15 use toxic leaves to feed the fungus","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：because it allows them to eat, courtesy of their mushroom’s digestive powers, the otherwise poisoned harvest of tropical forests whose leaves are laden with terpenoids, alkaloids and other chemicals designed to sicken browsers.\n审题：题目询问哪种蚂蚁使用有毒的叶子来喂养它们培养的真菌，选项包括A Leaf-cutting ants、B Lower attines或C Both。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“toxic leaves”定位到文章中的相关描述，在B段找到“poisoned harvest”和“leaves are laden with terpenoids, alkaloids”等短语，这些表示叶子有毒，同时结合“feed the fungus” implied在蚂蚁通过真菌消化有毒叶子的过程中。\n解题思路：在B段中，句子明确指出leaf-cutting ants能够食用热带森林的有毒叶子，这得益于它们真菌的消化能力；这些叶子富含terpenoids、alkaloids等化学物质， designed to sicken browsers，表明叶子有毒。蚂蚁使用这些叶子喂养真菌，然后食用真菌。相比之下，C段提到lower attines使用detritus如死叶、昆虫和粪便喂养真菌，但未指定这些叶子有毒，因此只有leaf-cutting ants符合描述，答案选A。","options":["Leaf-cutting ants","Lower attines","Both"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"58715","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nUse the information in the passage to match the options (listed A-C) with activities or features of ants below.\nChoose the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 14-19.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Leaf-cutting ants\nB Lower attines\nC Both"},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8053:58715:16","type":"choice","text":"16 raise a single fungus which doesn't live with other foreigners.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Textbooks describe how leaf-cutter ants scrupulously weed their gardens of all foreign organisms.\n审题：题目询问哪种蚂蚁培养的真菌不与其他外来物共存，选项为A Leaf-cutting ants、B Lower attines或C Both。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"raise fungus\"和\"doesn’t live with other foreigners\"定位到文章D段，该段描述了leaf-cutter ants如何清除花园中的外来生物。\n解题思路：在D段中，明确提到leaf-cutter ants会仔细清除其真菌花园中的所有外来生物，这表明它们培养的真菌环境是纯净的，不与其他外来物共存。而lower attines使用碎屑如死叶和昆虫喂养花园，可能引入外来物，因此不符合描述。故答案确定为A Leaf-cutting ants。","options":["Leaf-cutting ants","Lower attines","Both"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"58715","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nUse the information in the passage to match the options (listed A-C) with activities or features of ants below.\nChoose the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 14-19.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Leaf-cutting ants\nB Lower attines\nC Both"},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8053:58715:17","type":"choice","text":"17 use substance to fight against Escovopsis.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Because both the leaf-cutters and the lower attines use Streptomyces\n审题：题目询问哪种蚂蚁使用一种物质来对抗Escovopsis霉菌。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“use substance to fight against Escovopsis”定位到文章中关于Streptomyces细菌的描述，特别是在H段中明确提到both leaf-cutters and lower attines use Streptomyces，这种细菌用于对抗Escovopsis。\n解题思路：在H段中，句子“Because both the leaf-cutters and the lower attines use Streptomyces”直接表明两种蚂蚁都使用Streptomyces，这是一种抗生素细菌，能抑制Escovopsis的生长和孢子形成，从而对抗这种病原体。因此，两种蚂蚁都使用这种物质，所以正确答案是C Both。","options":["Leaf-cutting ants","Lower attines","Both"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"58715","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nUse the information in the passage to match the options (listed A-C) with activities or features of ants below.\nChoose the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 14-19.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Leaf-cutting ants\nB Lower attines\nC Both"},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8053:58715:18","type":"choice","text":"18 use dead vegetation to feed the fungus","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：the other groups, known as the lower attines because their nests are smaller and their techniques more primitive, feed their gardens with detritus like dead leaves, insects and faeces.\n审题：题目询问哪种蚂蚁使用死去的植物来喂养真菌。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“dead vegetable”定位到材料C段中的“dead leaves”，该部分描述蚂蚁的喂养方式。\n解题思路：在C段中，明确区分了leaf-cutting ants使用新鲜植被，而lower attines使用碎屑如死叶、昆虫和粪便来喂养真菌。死叶属于死去的植物材料，因此只有lower attines符合这一描述，答案选择B。","options":["Leaf-cutting ants","Lower attines","Both"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"58715","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nUse the information in the passage to match the options (listed A-C) with activities or features of ants below.\nChoose the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 14-19.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Leaf-cutting ants\nB Lower attines\nC Both"},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8053:58715:19","type":"choice","text":"19 are free of parasites explained previously.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Textbooks describe how leaf-cutter ants scrupulously weed their gardens of all foreign organisms. 和 People kept telling me, ‘You know the ants keep their gardens free of parasites, don’t you?’’\n审题：题目询问哪个选项（A Leaf-cutting ants, B Lower attines, C Both）在以前被解释为没有寄生虫。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的关键词“free of parasites”在文章中定位，搜索到D段中出现“keep their gardens free of parasites”的描述，直接关联到leaf-cutter ants。\n解题思路：在D段中，教科书和人们以前的观点认为leaf-cutter ants会仔细清除花园中的所有外来生物，保持花园没有寄生虫，这对应选项A Leaf-cutting ants。虽然后来研究证明实际情况并非如此，但题目问的是“explained previously”即以前的解释，因此确定答案为A。","options":["Leaf-cutting ants","Lower attines","Both"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"58715","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nUse the information in the passage to match the options (listed A-C) with activities or features of ants below.\nChoose the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 14-19.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Leaf-cutting ants\nB Lower attines\nC Both"},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8053:58716:20","type":"choice","text":"20 Dangerous outcome of Escovopsis","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Mr Currie discovered they are far from free of infection. In last month’s issue of the Proceeding of the National Academy of Sciences, he and two colleagues, Dr Mueller and David Mairoch, isolated several alien organisms, particularly a family of parasitic molds called Escovopsis.\n审题：题目要求找出哪个段落包含了Escovopsis的危险后果的信息。\n定位关键信息：使用题目中的关键词“Escovopsis”和“dangerous outcome”进行定位。在文章中扫描“Escovopsis”这个词，发现它首次出现在E段，并描述为一种寄生霉菌，暗示其可能导致感染和危险。\n解题思路：在E段中，句子提到Currie发现蚂蚁花园远非无感染，并分离出包括Escovopsis在内的外来生物，Escovopsis被特别指出是一种寄生霉菌。这间接暗示了Escovopsis的危险性，因为寄生霉菌通常会导致有害后果，如感染和破坏。虽然F段更详细描述了具体后果，但E段首次引入Escovopsis并关联其作为病原体的角色，因此包含了题目所问的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"58716","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information? Choose the correct letter, A-H, in boxes 20-24."},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8053:58716:21","type":"choice","text":"21 the disadvantage of growing single fungus","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The pure strain of fungus grown by the leaf-cutters, it seemed to Mr Currie, resembled the monocultures of various human crops, that are very productive for a while and then succumb to some disastrous pathogen, such as the Irish potato blight. Monocultures, which lack the genetic diversity to respond to changing environmental threats, are sitting ducks for parasites.\n审题：题目询问种植单一真菌的缺点是什么，即单一真菌种植带来的不利之处。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"disadvantage\"（缺点）和\"growing single fungus\"（种植单一真菌）进行定位。文章中，\"single fungus\"对应D段中的\"pure strain\"（纯菌株）或\"monocultures\"（单一栽培），\"disadvantage\"对应\"succumb to some disastrous pathogen\"（屈服于灾难性病原体）或\"sitting ducks for parasites\"（容易受到寄生虫攻击）。\n解题思路：在D段中，作者描述leaf-cutting ants种植的纯菌株真菌类似于人类农业中的单一栽培，这些单一栽培虽然一开始高产，但由于缺乏遗传多样性，无法应对环境威胁，容易受到寄生虫和病原体的攻击，例如爱尔兰马铃薯枯萎病。这直接点明了种植单一真菌的缺点，即易受病原体侵害，导致灾难性后果。因此，D段包含了题目所问的信息。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"58716","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information? Choose the correct letter, A-H, in boxes 20-24."},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8053:58716:22","type":"choice","text":"22 comparison of features of two different nests","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The leaf-cutters use fresh vegetation; the other groups, known as the lower attines because their nests are smaller and their techniques more primitive, feed their gardens with detritus like dead leaves, insects and faeces.\n审题：题目要求找出文章中哪个段落包含了对两种不同巢穴特征的比较信息。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"comparison\"（比较）、\"features\"（特征）和\"two different nests\"（两种不同巢穴）进行定位。在文章中扫描描述蚂蚁巢穴差异的部分，特别是提到leaf-cutters和lower attines的段落。\n解题思路：在C段中，作者明确比较了leaf-cutting ants和lower attines ants的巢穴特征。句子中指出lower attines的巢穴更小（nests are smaller）、技术更原始（techniques more primitive），并且对比了它们喂养花园的方式（leaf-cutters使用新鲜植被，lower attines使用碎屑如死叶、昆虫和粪便）。这直接对应了题目中要求的对两种巢穴特征的比较，因此确定答案为C段。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"58716","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information? Choose the correct letter, A-H, in boxes 20-24."},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8053:58716:23","type":"choice","text":"23 two achievements made by ants earlier than human","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"原文答案句：If so, some Alexander Fleming of an ant discovered antibiotics millions of years before people did. Even now, the ants are accomplishing two feats beyond the powers of human technology. The leaf-cutters are growing a monocultural crop year after year without disaster, and they are using an antibiotic apparently so wisely and prudently that, unlike people, they are not provoking antibiotic resistance in the target pathogen.\n审题：题目询问蚂蚁比人类更早实现的两个成就所在段落。\n定位关键信息：利用题目关键词“achievements”（成就）和“earlier than human”（比人类早）扫读段落，H段提到蚂蚁早于人类发现抗生素。\n解题思路：H段描述了蚂蚁的成就，如早在人类之前的数百万年前，某些蚂蚁就已发现抗生素。至今，它们仍在完成两项人类尚未做到的成就：切叶蚁能够长期稳定地种植单一作物而不遭毁灭性打击；并且，它们极为谨慎地使用抗生素，从而避免了人类频繁面对的耐药性问题。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"58716","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information? Choose the correct letter, A-H, in boxes 20-24."},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8053:58716:24","type":"choice","text":"24 advantage of growing a new breed of fungus","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：There is now a possible reason to explain why the lower attine species keep changing the variety of fungus in their mushroom gardens, and occasionally domesticating new ones – to stay one step ahead of the relentless Escovopsis.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是“培育新品种真菌的优势”，即寻找关于培育新真菌带来的好处或积极影响的信息。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"new breed of fungus\"（新品种真菌）定位，在文章中寻找与培育新真菌相关的正面描述或优势。\n解题思路：根据上文可知Escovopsis霉菌对真菌农场的破坏性影响，并提到其他蚂蚁不会靠近被感染的区域，导致相关蚂蚁因饥饿而死亡。F段最后提到了lower attine species不断更换“蘑菇园”中的真菌品种，并偶尔驯化新的真菌——这是为了始终领先于穷追不舍的Escovopsis一步。","options":["Section A","Section B","Section C","Section D","Section E","Section F","Section G","Section H"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"58716","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information? Choose the correct letter, A-H, in boxes 20-24."},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8053:58717:25","type":"choice","text":"How does the author think of Currie’s opinion?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：But after three years of sifting through attine ant gardens, Mr Currie discovered they are far from free of infection.\n审题：题目询问作者对Currie观点的看法，具体是Currie认为蚂蚁真菌系统中存在寄生虫的观点。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“Currie”和“opinion”定位到材料D段和E段。D段提到Currie的观点（认为有寄生虫）最初不被支持，E段描述了他的研究发现验证了这一观点。\n解题思路：在D段，Currie felt there had to be a parasite in the ant-fungus system，但a century of ant research offered no support for the idea，表明他的观点最初缺乏证据。在E段，Currie经过三年研究discovered they are far from free of infection，并分离出Escovopsis等病原体，这直接验证了他的观点。作者通过叙述这一从怀疑到证实的过程，表明Currie的观点后来被实验证据支持，因此对应选项A（His viewpoint was verified later）。","options":["His viewpoint was verified later.","Earlier study has sufficient evidence.","No details mentioned in the article.","His opinion was proved to be wrong."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"58717","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 25-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D."},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8053:58718:26","type":"choice","text":"What did scientists find on the skin of ants under a microscope?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Mr Currie discovered a specialized patch on the ants’ cuticle that harbors a particular kind of bacterium, one well known to the pharmaceutical industry, because it is the source of half the antibiotics used in medicine.\n审题：题目询问科学家在蚂蚁皮肤下显微镜观察时发现了什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"skin\"（对应原文中的\"cuticle\"，指昆虫体表）和\"under a microscope\"（原文中直接出现\"put these things under a microscope\"）定位到H段。\n解题思路：原文中，Currie将蚂蚁cuticle上的whitish growth置于显微镜下观察，发现它不是人们之前认为的cuticular wax，而是一种活的细菌。这种细菌是Streptomyces，在制药业中众所周知，因为它是医学中使用的半数抗生素的来源，因此对人类非常有用。这直接支持选项C\"a substance which is useful to humans\"，而其他选项不准确：A提到\"white cloud mold\"，但原文中是细菌而非霉菌；B提到\"wax\"，但原文否定它是蜡；D提到\"suppresses the growth of fungus\"，虽然细菌确实抑制Escovopsis霉菌，但主要焦点是它对人类的用途。","options":["some white cloud mold embed in their skin","that Wax is all over their skin","a substance which is useful to humans","a substance which suppresses the growth of fungus"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"58718","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 25-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"58715","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14-19\nUse the information in the passage to match the options (listed A-C) with activities or features of ants below.\nChoose the appropriate letters A-C in boxes 14-19.\nNB You may use any letter more than once.\nA Leaf-cutting ants\nB Lower attines\nC Both","html":"<p style=\"margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;Leaf-cutting ants</p><p style=\"margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;Lower attines</p><p style=\"margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;Both</p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"58716","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20-24\nThe reading passage has eight paragraphs A-H.\nWhich paragraph contains the following information? Choose the correct letter, A-H, in boxes 20-24.","html":"<p><strong>15</strong> use toxic leaves to feed the fungus <strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"58717","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 25-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","html":"<p><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">How does the author think of Currie’s opinion?</strong></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"58718","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 25-26\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","html":"<p><strong style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">What did scientists find on the skin of ants under a microscope?</strong></p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p><strong>Leaf-Cutting Ants and Fungus</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The ants and their agriculture have been extensively studied over the years, but the recent research has uncovered intriguing new findings of the fungus they cultivate, how they domesticated it and how they cultivate it and preserve it from pathogens. For example, the fungus farms, which the ants were thought to keep free of pathogens, turn out to be vulnerable to a devastating mold, found nowhere else but in ants&#39; nests. To keep the mold in check, the ants long ago made a discovery that would do credit to any pharmaceutical laboratory.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Leaf-cutting ants and their fungus farms are a marvel of nature and perhaps the best-known example of symbiosis, the mutual dependence of two species. The ant&#39;s achievement is remarkable – the biologist Edward O. Wilson has called it &#39;one of the major breakthroughs in animal evolution&#39; – because it allows them to eat, courtesy of their mushroom&#39;s digestive powers, the otherwise poisoned harvest of tropical forests whose leaves are laden with terpenoids, alkaloids and other chemicals designed to sicken browsers.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Fungus growing seems to have originated only once in evolution because all gardening ants belong to a single tribe, the descendants of the first fungus farmer. There are more than 200 known species of the attine ant tribe, divided into 12 groups, or genera. The leaf-cutters use fresh vegetation; the other groups, known as the lower attines because their nests are smaller and their techniques more primitive, feed their gardens with detritus like dead leaves, insects and faeces. In 1994 a team of four biologists, Ulrich G. Mueller and Ted R. Schultz from Cornell University and Ignacio H. Chapela and Stephen A. Rehner from the United States Department of Agriculture, ananlyzed the DNA of ant funguses. The common assumption that the funguses are all derived from a single strain, they found, was only half true.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The leaf-cutters&#39; fungus was indeed descended from a single strain, propagated clonally, or just by budding, for at least 23 million years. But the lower attine ants used different varieties of the fungus, and in one case a quite separate species, the four biologists discovered. The pure strain of fungus grown by the leaf-cutters, it seemed to Mr Currie, resembled the monocultures of various human crops, that are very productive for a while and then succumb to some disastrous pathogen, such as the Irish potato blight. Monocultures, which lack the genetic diversity to respond to changing environmental threats, are sitting ducks for parasites. Mr Currie felt there had to be a parasite in the ant-fungus system. But a century of ant research offered no support for the idea. Textbooks describe how leaf-cutter ants scrupulously weed their gardens of all foreign organisms. &#39;People kept telling me, &#39; You know the ants keep their gardens free of parasites, don&#39;t you?’’ Mr Currie said of his efforts to find a hidden interloper.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>But after three years of sifting through attine ant gardens, Mr Currie discovered they are far from free of infection. In last month&#39;s issue of the Proceeding of the National Academy of Sciences, he and two colleagues, Dr Mueller and David Mairoch, isolated several alien organisms, particularly a family of parasitic molds called Escovopsis. Escovopsis turns out to be a highly virulent pathogen that can devastate a fungus garden in a couple of days. It blooms like a while cloud, with the garden dimly visible underneath. In a day or two, the whole garden is enveloped. &#39;Other ants won&#39;t go near it and the ants associated with the garden just starve to death,&#39; Dr. Rehner said. &#39;They just seem to give up, except for those that have rescued their larvae.’ The deadly mold then turns greenish-brown as it enters its spore-forming stage.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Evidently, the ants usually manage to keep Escovopsis and other parasites under control. But with any lapse in control, or if the ants are removed, Escovopsis will quickly burst forth. Although new leaf-cutter gardens start off free of Escovopsis, within two years some 60 percent become infected. The discovery of Escovopsis&#39;s role brings a new level of understanding of the evolution of the attine ants. &#39;In the last decade, evolutionary biologists have been increasingly aware of the role of parasites as driving forces in evolution,&#39; Dr Schultz said. There is now a possible reason to explain why the lower attine species keep changing the variety of fungus in their mushroom gardens, and occasionally domesticating new ones – to stay one step ahead of the relentless Escovopsis.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Interestingly, Mr. Currie found that the leaf-cutters had in general fewer alien molds in their gardens than the lower attines, yet they had more Escovopsis infections. It seems that the price they pay for cultivating a pure variety of fungus is a higher risk from Escovopsis. But the leaf-cutters may have a little alternative: they cultivate a special variety of fungus which, unlike those grown by the lower attines, produces nutritious swollen tips for the ants to eat.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Discovery of a third partner in the ant-fungus symbiosis raises the question of how the attine ants, especially the leaf-cutters, keep this dangerous interloper under control. Amazingly enough, Mr Currie has again provided the answer. &#39;People have known for a hundred years that ants have a whitish growth on the cuticle,&#39; said Dr Mueller, referring to the insects&#39; body surface. &#39;People would say this is like a cuticular wax. But Cameron was the first one in a hundred years to put these things under a microscope. He saw it was not inert wax. It is alive.&#39; Mr Currie discovered a specialized patch on the ants&#39; cuticle that harbors a particular kind of bacterium, one well known to the pharmaceutical industry, because it is the source of half the antibiotics used in medicine. From each of 22 species of attine ant studied, Mr. Cameron and colleagues isolated a species of Streptomyces bacterium, they reported in Nature in April. The Streptomyces does not have much effect on ordinary laboratory funguses. But it is a potent poisoner of Escovopsis, inhibiting its growth and suppressing spore formation. It also stimulates the growth of the ants&#39; mushroom fungus. The bacterium is carried by virgin queens when they leave to establish new nests but is not found on male ants, playboys who take no responsibility in nest-making or gardening. Because both the leaf-cutters and the lower attines use Streptomyces, the bacterium may have been part of their symbiosis for almost as long as the Escovopsis mold. If so, some Alexander Fleming of an ant discovered antibiotics millions of years before people did. Even now, the ants are accomplishing two feats beyond the powers of human technology. The leaf-cutters are growing a monocultural crop year after year without disaster, and they are using an antibiotic apparently so wisely and prudently that, unlike people, they are not provoking antibiotic resistance in the target pathogen.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px; text-align: left;\"><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8053&scene=%E7%94%9F%E6%80%81%E7%8E%AF%E4%BF%9D&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8054","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Motivating Drives","book":"阅读还原集Vol.11","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test3","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.11 · Test3 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8054:59023:27","type":"choice","text":"According to the passage, what are we told about the study of motivation?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This research is a relational study which builds the fundamental and comprehensive model for study. But their researchers have limitations. It is like studying the movements of car without taking out the engine.\n对应段落：A段\n审题：题目问根据文章内容，关于对激励的研究我们了解到什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的\"study of motivation\"定位到A段首句\"This research is a relational study...\"和末句\"But their researchers have limitations. It is like studying the movements of car without taking out the engine.\"。\n解题思路：原文A段提到\"researchers have limitations\"并比喻为\"studying the movements of car without taking out the engine\"，说明研究者过于理论化，没有深入核心。这与选项C\"Researchers have tended to be too theoretical to their study\"意思一致。选项A文中未提及；选项B与原文\"related to the emotion and behavior of employees\"不符；选项D与原文\"turn unmotivated teams into productive ones\"不符。因此正确答案是C。","options":["The theory of motivating employees is starting to catch attention in organizations in recent years.","It is very important for managers to know how to motivate their subordinates because it is related to the salary of employees.","Researchers have tended to be too theoretical to their study.","The goal of employee motivation is to increase the profit of organizations."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59023","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8054:59024:28","type":"choice","text":"What can be inferred from the passage about the study of people’s drives?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：These four drives, while not necessarily the only human drives, are the ones that are central to unified understanding of modern human life.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问从文章中关于人们的需求研究可以推断出什么。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"the study of people's drives\"定位到文章中与需求研究相关的句子。\n解题思路：根据I段最后一句\"These four drives, while not necessarily the only human drives, are the ones that are central to unified understanding of modern human life.\"可以推断出满足员工的需求可以积极地改变他们的行为。原文中提到这四个需求对于理解现代人类生活至关重要，因此可以推断出满足这些需求会对员工的行为产生积极影响。","options":["Satisfying employees’ drives can positively lead to the change of behaviour.","Satisfying employees’ drives will negatively affect their emotions.","Satisfying employees’ drives can increase companies’ productions.","Satisfying employees’ drives will result in employees’ outstanding performance."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59024","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8054:59025:29","type":"choice","text":"According to Paragraph C, in order to optimise employees’ performance, are needed.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The drive to acquire must be met to optimize the acquire aspect as well as the achievement element. Thus the way that outstanding performance is recognized, the type of perks that are provided to polish the career path.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是根据第三段，为了优化员工的表现，需要什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"optimise employees’ performance\"和\"paragraph three\"定位到C段，找到与优化员工表现相关的句子。\n解题思路：原文提到\"optimize the acquire aspect as well as the achievement element\"（优化获取方面和成就要素），并进一步说明\"the way that outstanding performance is recognized\"（突出表现被认可的方式）和\"the type of perks that are provided to polish the career path\"（提供福利以完善职业道路）。选项D中的\"financial incentive\"（财务激励）对应\"the drive to acquire\"（获取的驱动力）和\"perks\"（福利），\"recognition\"（认可）对应\"the way that outstanding performance is recognized\"（突出表现被认可的方式），因此D选项最符合原文内容。","options":["drive to acquire and achievement element","outstanding performance and recognition","career fulfillment and a thousand dollar check","financial incentive and recognition"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59025","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8054:59026:30","type":"choice","text":"According to Paragraph E, how does 'the drive to comprehend' help employees perform better?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Employees don’t want to do meaningless things or monotonous job. If the job didn’t provide them with personal meaning and fulfillment, they will leave the company.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是根据第五段（E段），‘理解驱动力’如何帮助员工表现更好。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的‘the drive to comprehend’定位到E段，该段详细描述了理解驱动力对员工表现的影响。\n解题思路：原文中提到，理解驱动力促使许多员工取得更高绩效。多年来，人们一直知道设定挑战性目标可以极大地影响绩效。组织需要确保各种工作角色为员工提供具有挑战性的刺激，或者允许他们成长。员工不想做没有意义的事情或单调的工作。如果工作没有给他们提供个人意义和成就感，他们就会离开公司。由此可知，理解驱动力帮助员工感觉他们的任务对公司有意义，因此选项B正确。","options":["It can help employees better understand the development of their organizations.","It can help employees feel their task is meaningful to their companies.","It can help employees set higher goals.","It can provide employees with repetitive tasks."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59026","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8054:59027:31","type":"choice","text":"According to Paragraph F, which of the following is true about ‘drive to defend’?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：This drive manifests itself as a quest to create and promote justice, fairness, and the ability to express ourselves freely. The organizational lever for this basic human motivator is resource allocation. This drive is also met through an employee feeling connection to a company. If their companies are merged with another, they will show worries.\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是根据第六段（F段），关于‘drive to defend’（防御驱动力）的描述哪一项是正确的。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是‘drive to defend’，通过这个关键词可以定位到文章的F段，因为F段明确提到了‘drive to defend’。\n解题思路：根据F段的内容，‘drive to defend’表现为追求创造和促进正义、公平以及自由表达自己的能力。组织可以通过资源分配来满足这种基本的人类动机，同时，这种驱动力也通过员工对公司产生联系来满足。如果他们的公司与其他公司合并，他们会表现出担忧。选项C提到员工认为自由表达自己的意见非常重要，这与F段中提到的‘drive to defend’的表现形式一致。因此，选项C是正确的。其他选项要么与原文不符，要么没有在原文中提到。","options":["Organizational resource is the most difficult to allocate.","It is more difficult to implement than the drive to comprehend.","Employees think it is very important to voice their own opinions.","Employees think it is very important to connect with a merged corporation."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"59027","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8054:59028:32-33-34","type":"choice","text":"Which THREE of the following statements are true of the study of drives?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nA. Employees will be motivated if they find personal belonging to the company.\nE. Employees don’t want to do meaningless things or monotonous job. If the job didn’t provide them with personal meaning and fulfillment, they will leave the company.\nF. If their companies are merged with another, they will show worries.\n对应段落：\nA选项对应D段；E选项对应E段；F选项对应F段。\n审题：题目问的是关于研究驱动力（drives）的哪些陈述是正确的，需要选择三个正确的选项。\n定位关键信息：\nA选项中的\"feel belonged to the company\"对应D段中的\"Employees will be motivated if they find personal belonging to the company\"；\nE选项中的\"lacking challenging\"对应E段中的\"Employees don’t want to do meaningless things or monotonous job. If the job didn’t provide them with personal meaning and fulfillment, they will leave the company\"；\nF选项中的\"company is sold\"对应F段中的\"If their companies are merged with another, they will show worries\"。\n解题思路：\nA选项与D段内容一致，D段提到员工找到归属感时会受到激励，因此A正确；\nE选项与E段内容一致，E段提到如果工作缺乏挑战性，员工会离开公司，因此E正确；\nF选项与F段内容一致，F段提到公司合并时员工会表现出担忧，因此F正确。其他选项B、C、D在原文中未明确提及或与原文不符。","options":["Employees will be motivated if they feel belonged to the company.","If employees get an opportunity of training and development program, their motivation will be enhanced.","If employees’ working goals are complied with organisational objectives, their motivation will be reinforced.","If employees’ motivation is very low, companies should find a way to increase their salary as their first priority.","If employees find their work lacking challenging, they will leave the company.","Employees will worry if their company is sold."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59028","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 32-34\nChoose THREE letters, A-F. Write the correct letters in boxes 32-34 on your answer sheet.","groupId":"59028-8054:59028:32-33-34"},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8054:59028:32-33-34","type":"choice","text":"Which THREE of the following statements are true of the study of drives?","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nA. Employees will be motivated if they find personal belonging to the company.\nE. Employees don’t want to do meaningless things or monotonous job. If the job didn’t provide them with personal meaning and fulfillment, they will leave the company.\nF. If their companies are merged with another, they will show worries.\n对应段落：\nA选项对应D段；E选项对应E段；F选项对应F段。\n审题：题目问的是关于研究驱动力（drives）的哪些陈述是正确的，需要选择三个正确的选项。\n定位关键信息：\nA选项中的\"feel belonged to the company\"对应D段中的\"Employees will be motivated if they find personal belonging to the company\"；\nE选项中的\"lacking challenging\"对应E段中的\"Employees don’t want to do meaningless things or monotonous job. If the job didn’t provide them with personal meaning and fulfillment, they will leave the company\"；\nF选项中的\"company is sold\"对应F段中的\"If their companies are merged with another, they will show worries\"。\n解题思路：\nA选项与D段内容一致，D段提到员工找到归属感时会受到激励，因此A正确；\nE选项与E段内容一致，E段提到如果工作缺乏挑战性，员工会离开公司，因此E正确；\nF选项与F段内容一致，F段提到公司合并时员工会表现出担忧，因此F正确。其他选项B、C、D在原文中未明确提及或与原文不符。","options":["Employees will be motivated if they feel belonged to the company.","If employees get an opportunity of training and development program, their motivation will be enhanced.","If employees’ working goals are complied with organisational objectives, their motivation will be reinforced.","If employees’ motivation is very low, companies should find a way to increase their salary as their first priority.","If employees find their work lacking challenging, they will leave the company.","Employees will worry if their company is sold."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59028","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 32-34\nChoose THREE letters, A-F. Write the correct letters in boxes 32-34 on your answer sheet.","groupId":"59028-8054:59028:32-33-34"},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8054:59028:32-33-34","type":"choice","text":"Which THREE of the following statements are true of the study of drives?","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"原文答案句：\nA. Employees will be motivated if they find personal belonging to the company.\nE. Employees don’t want to do meaningless things or monotonous job. If the job didn’t provide them with personal meaning and fulfillment, they will leave the company.\nF. If their companies are merged with another, they will show worries.\n对应段落：\nA选项对应D段；E选项对应E段；F选项对应F段。\n审题：题目问的是关于研究驱动力（drives）的哪些陈述是正确的，需要选择三个正确的选项。\n定位关键信息：\nA选项中的\"feel belonged to the company\"对应D段中的\"Employees will be motivated if they find personal belonging to the company\"；\nE选项中的\"lacking challenging\"对应E段中的\"Employees don’t want to do meaningless things or monotonous job. If the job didn’t provide them with personal meaning and fulfillment, they will leave the company\"；\nF选项中的\"company is sold\"对应F段中的\"If their companies are merged with another, they will show worries\"。\n解题思路：\nA选项与D段内容一致，D段提到员工找到归属感时会受到激励，因此A正确；\nE选项与E段内容一致，E段提到如果工作缺乏挑战性，员工会离开公司，因此E正确；\nF选项与F段内容一致，F段提到公司合并时员工会表现出担忧，因此F正确。其他选项B、C、D在原文中未明确提及或与原文不符。","options":["Employees will be motivated if they feel belonged to the company.","If employees get an opportunity of training and development program, their motivation will be enhanced.","If employees’ working goals are complied with organisational objectives, their motivation will be reinforced.","If employees’ motivation is very low, companies should find a way to increase their salary as their first priority.","If employees find their work lacking challenging, they will leave the company.","Employees will worry if their company is sold."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"59028","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 32-34\nChoose THREE letters, A-F. Write the correct letters in boxes 32-34 on your answer sheet.","groupId":"59028-8054:59028:32-33-34"},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8054:59029:35","type":"choice","text":"Increasing pay can lead to the high work motivation.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Successful organizations and leaders not only need to focus on the optimization of physical reward but also on moving other levers within the organization that can drive motivation.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问“增加工资可以导致高工作动力”是否与作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词“Increasing pay”和“high work motivation”在文章中定位相关句子。\n解题思路：原文中提到成功的组织和领导者不仅需要关注物质奖励的优化，还需要关注其他能驱动动力的因素。这表明作者认为增加工资（物质奖励）不能单独提高高工作动力，还需要其他因素。因此，题目中的说法与作者的观点不符，答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59029","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8054:59030:36","type":"choice","text":"Local companies benefit more from global companies through the study.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Using the results of the surveys which executed with employees from Fortune 500 companies and other two global businesses (P company and H company), the article mentions about how independent drives influence employees’ behavior and how organizational levers boost employee motivation.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“本地公司通过研究从全球公司中获益更多”这一说法是否与作者的观点一致。\n定位关键信息：根据题目的关键词\"Local companies\", \"benefit\", \"global companies\", \"study\"，在文章中定位相关信息。\n解题思路：文章G段提到“Using the results of the surveys which executed with employees from Fortune 500 companies and other two global businesses (P company and H company), the article mentions about how independent drives influence employees’ behavior and how organizational levers boost employee motivation.”，但并未提及本地公司通过研究从全球公司中获益更多。因此，无法确定作者是否认为本地公司通过研究从全球公司中获益更多。答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59030","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8054:59031:37","type":"choice","text":"Employees achieve the most commitment if their drive to comprehend is met.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Employees will be motivated if they find personal belonging to the company. In the meantime, the most commitment will be achieved by the employee on condition that the force of motivation within the employee affects the direction, intensity and persistence of decision and behavior in company.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“如果员工的‘理解需求’得到满足，他们就能达到最大的承诺。”\n定位关键信息：题目中的“drive to comprehend”和“most commitment”是关键词，通过这两个词可以定位到文章中D段的相关句子。\n解题思路：原文中D段明确提到，员工如果能在公司找到归属感，就能被激励。而题目中说的是“理解需求”得到满足时，员工能达到最大的承诺。原文中并没有提到“满足理解需求”就可以实现“最大承诺”。因此，题目中的说法与原文信息不符，故答案为NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59031","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8054:59032:38","type":"choice","text":"The employees in former company presented unusual attitude toward the merging of two companies.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For drive to defend, a study on the merging of P company and H company shows that employees in former company show an unusual cooperating attitude.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是“前公司的员工对两家公司的合并表现出异常的态度。”\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“former company”和“unusual attitude”定位到H段。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，对于防御驱动力的研究，涉及P公司和H公司的合并，结果显示前公司的员工表现出异常的合作态度。这与题目中的描述完全一致，因此答案为YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59032","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8054:59033:39","type":"choice","text":"The two studies are done to analyse the relationship between the natural drive and the attitude of employees.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The two studies have been done to find the relations between the four drives and motivation.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“这两项研究是为了分析自然驱动力和员工态度之间的关系吗？”\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的“two studies”和“natural drive”和“attitude of employees”可以定位到G段的第一句话。\n解题思路：原文中提到的研究是为了找出“four drives”和“motivation”之间的关系，而题目中说的是“natural drive”和“attitude of employees”之间的关系。原文中的“four drives”指的是B段中提到的四个驱动力，即“the drive to acquire, the drive to bond, the drive to comprehend and the drive to defend”，而题目中的“natural drive”并没有明确的指代，可能指的是这四个驱动力，也可能不是。另外，原文中说的是“motivation”，而题目中说的是“attitude of employees”，这两个概念并不完全相同。因此，题目中的陈述与原文中的信息不符，所以答案是NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59033","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8054:59034:40","type":"choice","text":"Rewarding system cause the company to lose profit.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Successful organizations and leaders not only need to focus on the optimization of physical reward but also on moving other levers within the organization that can drive motivation.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是奖励系统是否会导致公司失去利润。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“Rewarding system”和“lose profit”在文章中定位答案。\n解题思路：原文中提到成功的组织和领导者不仅需要关注物质奖励的优化，还需要关注其他可以驱动动机的组织杠杆。原文并没有提到奖励系统会导致公司失去利润，因此无法得出题目所述的结论。所以，答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"59034","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"59028-8054:59028:32-33-34","numbers":[32,33,34],"selectionCount":3,"answers":["A","E","F"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"59023","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>According to the passage, what are we told about the study of motivation?</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"59024","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>What can be inferred from the passage about the study of people’s drives?</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"59025","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>According to Paragraph C, in order to optimise employees’ performance, are needed.</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"59026","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>According to Paragraph E, how does &#39;the drive to comprehend&#39; help employees perform better?</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"59027","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-31\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>According to Paragraph F, which of the following is true about ‘drive to defend’?</strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"59028","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 32-34\nChoose THREE letters, A-F. Write the correct letters in boxes 32-34 on your answer sheet.","html":"<p><strong>Which THREE of the following statements are true of the study of drives?</strong></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"59029","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Increasing pay can lead to the high work motivation.</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"59030","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Local companies benefit more from global companies through the study.</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"59031","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Employees achieve the most commitment if their drive to comprehend is met.</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"59032","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>The employees in former company presented unusual attitude toward the merging of two companies.</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"59033","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>The two studies are done to analyse the relationship between the natural drive and the attitude of employees.</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"59034","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 35-40\nDo the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer NO if the statement contradicts the information NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Rewarding system cause the company to lose profit.</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Motivating Drives&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Scientists have been researching the way to get employees motivated for many years. This research is a relational study which builds the fundamental and comprehensive model for study. This is especially true when the business goal is to turn unmotivated teams into productive ones. But their researchers have limitations. It is like studying the movements of car without taking out the engine.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Motivation is what drives people to succeed and plays a vital role in enhancing an organizational development. It is important to study the motivation of employees because it is related to the emotion and behavior of employees. Recent studies show there are four drives for motivation. They are the drive to acquire, the drive to bond, the drive to comprehend and the drive to defend.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>The Drive to Acquire&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The drive to acquire must be met to optimize the acquire aspect as well as the achievement element. Thus the way that outstanding performance is recognized, the type of perks that are provided to polish the career path. But sometimes a written letter of appreciation generates more motivation than a thousand dollar check, which can serve as the invisible power to boost business engagement. Successful organizations and leaders not only need to focus on the optimization of physical reward but also on moving other levers within the organization that can drive motivation.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>The Drive to Bond&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The drive to bond is also key to driving motivation. There are many kinds of bonds between people, like friendship, family. In company, employees also want to be an essential part of company. They want to belong to the company. Employees will be motivated if they find personal belonging to the company. In the meantime, the most commitment will be achieved by the employee on condition that the force of motivation within the employee affects the direction, intensity and persistence of decision and behavior in company.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>The Drive to Comprehend</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>E&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The drive to comprehend motivates many employees to higher performance. For years, it has been known that setting stretch goals can greatly impact performance. Organizations need to ensure that the various job roles provide employees with simulation that challenges them or allow them to grow. Employees don’t want to do meaningless things or monotonous job. If the job didn’t provide them with personal meaning and fulfillment, they will leave the company.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>The Drive to Defend&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The drive to defend is often the hardest lever to pull. This drive manifests itself as a quest to create and promote justice, fairness, and the ability to express ourselves freely. The organizational lever for this basic human motivator is resource allocation. This drive is also met through an employee feeling connection to a company. If their companies are merged with another, they will show worries.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Two studies have been done to find the relations between the four drives and motivation. The article based on two studies was finally published in Harvard Business Review. Most authors’ arguments have laid emphasis on four-drive theory and actual investigations. Using the results of the surveys which executed with employees from Fortune 500 companies and other two global businesses (P company and H company), the article mentions about how independent drives influence employees’ behavior and how organizational levers boost employee motivation.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The studies show that the drive to bond is most related to fulfilling commitment, while the drive to comprehend is most related to how much effort employees spend on works. The drive to acquire can be satisfied by a rewarding system which ties rewards to performances, and gives the best people opportunities for advancement. For drive to defend, a study on the merging of P company and H company shows that employees in former company show an unusual cooperating attitude.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>I&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The key to successfully motivate employees is to meet all drives. Each of these drives is important if we are to understand employee motivation. These four drives, while not necessarily the only human drives, are the ones that are central to unified understanding of modern human life.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8054&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7444","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 The Blockbuster Phenomenon: a new museum trend","book":"阅读还原集Vol.11","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test2","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.11 · Test2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"7444:56752:1","type":"fill","text":"1 the reason why museum directors need to constantly alter and update their exhibits","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位词: reason, alter and update\n对应原文: C段, Maintaining and increasing visitor levels is thus paramount and involves not only creating or hiring blockbuster exhibitions, but providing regular exhibition changes and innovations.\n详细解析:C段指出博物馆为了保持和增加参观人数，不仅需要举办大型展览，还需要定期更换和创新展览内容。这正是博物馆馆长需要不断改变和更新展览的原因。\n同义替换：constantly=regular；alter and update =changes and innovations","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56752","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1 - 4\nLook at the eight paragraphs (A - H). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - H). You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"7444:56752:2","type":"fill","text":"2 mention of the length of time people will queue up to see a blockbuster","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"定位词: length of time,queue up\n对应原文: A段, A blockbuster is a 'large-scale loan exhibition that people who normally don't go to museums will stand in line for hours to see' (Elsen 1984).\n详细解析:A段指出“大型展览是指那些连平时不去博物馆的人都会排队数小时观看的展览”，明确说明了观众排队的时长。\n同义替换:queue up=stand in line , Length of time=hours","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56752","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1 - 4\nLook at the eight paragraphs (A - H). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - H). You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"7444:56752:3","type":"fill","text":"3 terms that people have used when referring to blockbusters","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"定位词: terms , blockbusters\n对应原文:D段, In literature from both UK and USA, the words that are starting to appear in some descriptions of blockbusters are 'less scholarly', 'non-elitist' and 'populist', while others extol the virtues encouraging scholars to co-operate on projects, and to provide exhibitions that cater for a broad selection of community rather than an elite sector.\n详细解析:D段指出在英国和美国的文献中，一些词语如“学术性较弱”、“非精英化”和“平民化”被用来描述大型展览。这些词语是指人们用来形容大型展览的术语。\n同义替换:Terms=words, Referring to blockbusters=descriptions of blockbusters","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56752","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1 - 4\nLook at the eight paragraphs (A - H). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - H). You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"7444:56752:4","type":"fill","text":"4 the various ways that institutions like museums get financial support","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位词: financial support\n对应原文: C段, Museums across the UK, USA, Canada and Australia currently operate under a system of plural funding: revenue raised through contributions by federal, state and/or local governments, combined with revenue raised through admission charges and other activities.\n详细解析:C段指出博物馆通过“联邦、州或地方政府的资助，以及门票收入和其他活动”获取资金支持。\n同义替换: financial support=revenue raised","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56752","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1 - 4\nLook at the eight paragraphs (A - H). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - H). You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"7444:56753:5","type":"fill","text":"填写第 5 空","answer":"customers","acceptedAnswers":["customers"],"explanation":"定位词: museum visitors, referred to as\n对应原文: C段, In addition, the visiting public have become known as customers rather than visitors, and the skills that are valued in museums to keep the new customers coming through the door have changed.\n详细解析:C段指出公众现在被称为“客户”，而不是传统意义上的“参观者”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56753","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5 - 8\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":3},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"7444:56754:6","type":"fill","text":"填写第 6 空","answer":"public relations skills","acceptedAnswers":["public relations skills"],"explanation":"定位词: curators,academic qualifications\n对应原文: C段, Curators are now administrators and being a museum director no longer requires an arts degree – but public relations skills are essential if the museum is going to compete with other museums to stage traveling exhibition which draw huge crowds.\n详细解析:C段指出，现在的博物馆馆长需要的是“公关技能”，而不是艺术学位或其他学术资格。\n同义替换：academic qualifications = arts degree","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56754","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5 - 8\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":3},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"7444:56755:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"the new museology/the new 'museology'","acceptedAnswers":["the new museology","the new 'museology'"],"explanation":"定位词: linking, public institutions\n对应原文: D段, The convergence of museums, the heritage industry, tourism, profit-making and pleasure-giving has resulted in the new 'museology'.\n详细解析:D段指出博物馆、遗产产业、旅游业等的结合（融合）被称为“新博物馆学”。\n同义替换:Linking=convergence, entertain=pleasure-giving","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56755","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5 - 8\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":3},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"7444:56756:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"tourist attractions","acceptedAnswers":["tourist attractions"],"explanation":"定位词: discussion, the same way\n对应原文: D段，This has given rise to much debate about whether it is appropriate to see museums primarily as tourist attractions.\n详细解析:D段指出，博物馆是否可以与其他旅游景点相提并论的问题正在引发讨论。\n同义替换: Discussion=debate","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56756","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5 - 8\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":3},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"7444:56757:9-10","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following are mentioned by the writer as advantages of blockbusters?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"定位词: advantages of blockbusters\n对应原文：E段，For museums in some countries, it may be the money that they require to replace parts of their collections or to fix buildings that are in need of attention.\nAlso creating or hiring a blockbuster has many positive spin-offs: blockbusters mean crowds, and crowds are good for the local economy, provide increased trade for shops, hotels, restaurants, the transport industry and retailers.\n详细解析:E段指出，热门展览的可以为博物馆的其他活动提供资金支持，例如更换收藏品或修理建筑物。另外，热门展览会导致当地的商店、酒店、餐馆、交通运输业和零售商的生意会增加。\n同义替换: structural repairs=fix buildings；extra business=increased trade","options":["Some of the money they raise can be used for structural repairs.","They can provide funds to help support amateur artists.","Local services benefit from the extra business they bring about.","They encourage overseas workers into the local area.","They raise employee performance levels."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"56757","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 9 - 10\nChoose TWO correct answers.","groupId":"56757-7444:56757:9-10"},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"7444:56757:9-10","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following are mentioned by the writer as advantages of blockbusters?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位词: advantages of blockbusters\n对应原文：E段，For museums in some countries, it may be the money that they require to replace parts of their collections or to fix buildings that are in need of attention.\nAlso creating or hiring a blockbuster has many positive spin-offs: blockbusters mean crowds, and crowds are good for the local economy, provide increased trade for shops, hotels, restaurants, the transport industry and retailers.\n详细解析:E段指出，热门展览的可以为博物馆的其他活动提供资金支持，例如更换收藏品或修理建筑物。另外，热门展览会导致当地的商店、酒店、餐馆、交通运输业和零售商的生意会增加。\n同义替换: structural repairs=fix buildings；extra business=increased trade","options":["Some of the money they raise can be used for structural repairs.","They can provide funds to help support amateur artists.","Local services benefit from the extra business they bring about.","They encourage overseas workers into the local area.","They raise employee performance levels."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"56757","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 9 - 10\nChoose TWO correct answers.","groupId":"56757-7444:56757:9-10"},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"7444:56758:11-12-13","type":"choice","text":"Which THREE of the following are mentioned by the writer as disadvantages of blockbusters?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位词: disadvantages of blockbusters\n对应段落: Paragraphs F and G\n对应原文:\nF段 ，Everyone, from general labourers to building services, front of house, technical, promotional, educational and administrative staff, is required to perform additional tasks.\nG段，Creating, mounting or hiring blockbusters is exhausting, with the real costs throughout an institution difficult to calculate.\nG段 ，Secondly, as some analysts have argued, the 'shop keeping' mentality and cost-benefit analysis and a pure concentration on the bottom line, can squeeze substance out of an exhibition.Taking out substance can be a recipe for blockbuster failure and therefore financial failure.\n详细解析:\nF段指出,从普通工人到管理人员都需要承担额外工作，与题干“增加员工工作量”一致。未提到管理风格不适应,没有提到需要支付商业咨询费用,没有提到无法增加年度总参观人数,未提及不同国家的受欢迎程度差异。G段指出, 举办大型展览的过程非常疲惫，与题干“耗费精力”对应。G段指出,过于注重经济效益可能削弱展览内容，导致失败，与题干中“内容可能因经济压力被削弱”一致。\n同义替换: Increased workload= additional tasks; personnel=staff；tiring= exhausting; Content can be weakened= taking out substance","options":["They do not suit museum management styles.","Specialist business advice has to be paid for.","They involve an increased workload for personnel.","They do not increase overall annual visitor numbers.","They are very tiring to put on.","What is popular in one country may not be popular in another.","The content can be weakened through financial pressure."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"56758","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 11 - 13\nChoose THREE correct answers.","groupId":"56758-7444:56758:11-12-13"},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"7444:56758:11-12-13","type":"choice","text":"Which THREE of the following are mentioned by the writer as disadvantages of blockbusters?","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"定位词: disadvantages of blockbusters\n对应段落: Paragraphs F and G\n对应原文:\nF段 ，Everyone, from general labourers to building services, front of house, technical, promotional, educational and administrative staff, is required to perform additional tasks.\nG段，Creating, mounting or hiring blockbusters is exhausting, with the real costs throughout an institution difficult to calculate.\nG段 ，Secondly, as some analysts have argued, the 'shop keeping' mentality and cost-benefit analysis and a pure concentration on the bottom line, can squeeze substance out of an exhibition.Taking out substance can be a recipe for blockbuster failure and therefore financial failure.\n详细解析:\nF段指出,从普通工人到管理人员都需要承担额外工作，与题干“增加员工工作量”一致。未提到管理风格不适应,没有提到需要支付商业咨询费用,没有提到无法增加年度总参观人数,未提及不同国家的受欢迎程度差异。G段指出, 举办大型展览的过程非常疲惫，与题干“耗费精力”对应。G段指出,过于注重经济效益可能削弱展览内容，导致失败，与题干中“内容可能因经济压力被削弱”一致。\n同义替换: Increased workload= additional tasks; personnel=staff；tiring= exhausting; Content can be weakened= taking out substance","options":["They do not suit museum management styles.","Specialist business advice has to be paid for.","They involve an increased workload for personnel.","They do not increase overall annual visitor numbers.","They are very tiring to put on.","What is popular in one country may not be popular in another.","The content can be weakened through financial pressure."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"56758","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 11 - 13\nChoose THREE correct answers.","groupId":"56758-7444:56758:11-12-13"},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"7444:56758:11-12-13","type":"choice","text":"Which THREE of the following are mentioned by the writer as disadvantages of blockbusters?","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"定位词: disadvantages of blockbusters\n对应段落: Paragraphs F and G\n对应原文:\nF段 ，Everyone, from general labourers to building services, front of house, technical, promotional, educational and administrative staff, is required to perform additional tasks.\nG段，Creating, mounting or hiring blockbusters is exhausting, with the real costs throughout an institution difficult to calculate.\nG段 ，Secondly, as some analysts have argued, the 'shop keeping' mentality and cost-benefit analysis and a pure concentration on the bottom line, can squeeze substance out of an exhibition.Taking out substance can be a recipe for blockbuster failure and therefore financial failure.\n详细解析:\nF段指出,从普通工人到管理人员都需要承担额外工作，与题干“增加员工工作量”一致。未提到管理风格不适应,没有提到需要支付商业咨询费用,没有提到无法增加年度总参观人数,未提及不同国家的受欢迎程度差异。G段指出, 举办大型展览的过程非常疲惫，与题干“耗费精力”对应。G段指出,过于注重经济效益可能削弱展览内容，导致失败，与题干中“内容可能因经济压力被削弱”一致。\n同义替换: Increased workload= additional tasks; personnel=staff；tiring= exhausting; Content can be weakened= taking out substance","options":["They do not suit museum management styles.","Specialist business advice has to be paid for.","They involve an increased workload for personnel.","They do not increase overall annual visitor numbers.","They are very tiring to put on.","What is popular in one country may not be popular in another.","The content can be weakened through financial pressure."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"56758","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 11 - 13\nChoose THREE correct answers.","groupId":"56758-7444:56758:11-12-13"}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"56757-7444:56757:9-10","numbers":[9,10],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["A","C"]},{"id":"56758-7444:56758:11-12-13","numbers":[11,12,13],"selectionCount":3,"answers":["C","E","G"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"56752","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 1 - 4\nLook at the eight paragraphs (A - H). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - H). You may choose any letter more than once.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"56753","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5 - 8\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p>These days, museum visitors tend to be referred to as&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[5] ____</strong>.</p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"56754","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5 - 8\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p>Museum curators now need&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[6] ____</strong>&nbsp;rather than academic qualifications.</p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"56755","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5 - 8\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p>The linking of a range of public institutions that entertain the public is known as<strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong>.</p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"56756","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5 - 8\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p>There is discussion about whether museums can be regarded in the same way as&nbsp;other <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong>.</p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"56757","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 9 - 10\nChoose TWO correct answers.","html":"<p><strong>Which TWO&nbsp;of the following&nbsp;are mentioned by the writer as advantages of blockbusters?</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"56758","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 11 - 13\nChoose THREE correct answers.","html":"<p><strong>Which THREE&nbsp;of the&nbsp;following&nbsp;are mentioned by the writer as disadvantages of blockbusters?</strong></p>","firstNumber":11}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>The Blockbuster Phenomenon: a new museum trend</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><em>Museums in Australia, like other pleasure-giving public organizations, are adapting their activities so that they more closely reflect the marketplace</em></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Since the 1980s, the term &#39;blockbuster&#39; has become the fashionable word for spectacular, high-profile museum exhibitions that have the ability to attract large crowds. A blockbuster is a &#39;large-scale loan exhibition that people who normally don&#39;t go to museums will stand in line for hours to see&#39; (Elsen 1984). Once the museum that created the exhibition has shown it to their local market, it can be offered to other organizations for a fee. This means that you can boost your own door takings and make money from boosting someone else&#39;s door takings.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">While partaking of the excitement of the blockbuster, visitors thus lured are likely to stay longer at the museum. Betty Churcher, the director of the Australian National Gallery, summed up the new blockbuster creed as follows: The bonus of the blockbuster exhibitions is that people come to see the blockbuster and they stay to look at the permanent collection, so you are getting broader exposure for your collection.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Museums across the UK, USA, Canada and Australia currently operate under a system of plural funding: revenue raised through contributions by federal, state and/or local governments, combined with revenue raised through admission charges and other activities. Maintaining and increasing visitor levels is thus paramount and involves not only creating or hiring blockbuster exhibitions, but providing regular exhibition changes and innovations. In addition, the visiting public have become known as customers rather than visitors, and the skills that are valued in museums to keep the new customers coming through the door have changed. Curators are now administrators and being a museum director no longer requires an arts degree – but public relations skills are essential if the museum is going to compete with other museums to stage traveling exhibition which draw huge crowds.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The convergence of museums, the heritage industry, tourism, profit-making and pleasure-giving has resulted in the new &#39;museology&#39;. This has given rise to much debate about whether it is appropriate to see museums primarily as tourist attractions. In literature from both UK and USA, the words that are starting to appear in some descriptions of blockbusters are &#39;less scholarly&#39;, &#39;non-elitist&#39; and &#39;populist&#39;, while others extol the virtues encouraging scholars to co-operate on projects, and to provide exhibitions that cater for a broad selection of community rather than an elite sector.Whatever commentators may think, managers of museums worldwide are looking for artful ways to blend culture and commerce, and blockbuster exhibitions are at the top of the list.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">But do blockbusters held in public institutions really create a surplus to fund other activities? If the bottom line is profit, then according to the records of many major museums blockbusters do make money. For museums in some countries, it may be the money that they require to replace parts of their collections or to fix buildings that are in need of attention. For some museums in Australia, it may be the opportunity to illustrate that they are attempting to pay their way by recovering part of their operating costs. Also creating or hiring a blockbuster has many positive spin-offs: blockbusters mean crowds, and crowds are good for the local economy, providing increased trade for shops, hotels, restaurants, the transport industry and retailers. The argument that the arts provide sustained economic benefits has been well illustrated in impact studies in the USA and UK.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">However, blockbusters require large capital expenditure, and draw on resources across all branches of an organization, and the costs don&#39;t end there. There is a Human Resource Management cost in addition to a measurable &#39;real&#39; dollar cost. Receiving a touring exhibition draws resources from across functional management structures in project management style. Everyone, from general labourers to building services, front of house, technical, promotional, educational and administrative staff, is required to perform additional tasks. Furthermore, as an increasing number of institutions try their hand at increasing visitor numbers and memberships (and therefore revenue) by staging blockbuster exhibitions, it may be less likely that blockbusters will continue to provide a surplus to subsidize other activities due to the competitive nature of the market.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">It has been illustrated in both the UK and USA that the blockbuster ideology has resulted in the false expectation that the momentum required to stage blockbusters can be maintained continually. Creating, mounting or hiring blockbusters is exhausting, with the real costs throughout an institution difficult to calculate. Secondly, as some analysts have argued, the &#39;shop keeping&#39; mentality and cost-benefit analysis and a pure concentration on the bottom line, can squeeze substance out of an exhibition. Taking out substance can be a recipe for blockbuster failure and therefore financial failure.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Perhaps the best pathway to take is one that balances both blockbusters and regular exhibitions. However, this easy middle ground may only work if you have enough space, and have alternate sources of funding to continue to support the regular, less exciting fare. Perhaps the advice should be to make sure that you find out what your local community, wants from you and make sure that your regular activities and exhibitions are more enticing.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7444&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8094","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 The Development of Plastics","book":"阅读还原集Vol.11","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test2","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.11 · Test2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"8094:58970:14","type":"fill","text":"填写第 14 空","answer":"Photographic film/photographic film","acceptedAnswers":["Photographic film","photographic film"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Without celluloid, the film industry could never have got off the ground at the end of the 19th century.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问的是图表中某个塑料制品的具体用途。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的图表信息，可以定位到C段中提到的\"photographic film\"。\n解题思路：C段中提到\"Celluloid was made by dissolving cellulose, a carbohydrate derived from plants, in a solution of camphor dissolved in ethanol. This new material rapidly found uses in the manufacture of products such as knife handles, detachable collars and cuffs, spectacle frames and photographic film.\"这句话明确指出\"photographic film\"是其中一个应用。因此，答案是\"Photographic film\"。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"58970","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022B0ZeaaCG3C1669987832.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"8094:58971:15","type":"fill","text":"填写第 15 空","answer":"Bakelite/bakelite","acceptedAnswers":["Bakelite","bakelite"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In 1907 Leo Baekeland, a Belgian chemist working in the USA invented a different kind of plastic by causing phenol and formaldehyde to react together. Baekeland called the material Bakelite, and it was the first of the thermosets – plastics that can be cast and moulded while hot but cannot be softened by heat and reshaped once they have set.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是哪种塑料是由酚和甲醛反应制成的。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"phenol and formaldehyde\"定位到D段中\"causing phenol and formaldehyde to react together\"这一句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，Leo Baekeland通过使酚和甲醛反应制造出一种名为Bakelite的塑料，并且这是第一种热固性塑料。因此，答案为Bakelite。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"58971","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022B0ZeaaCG3C1669987832.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"8094:58972:16","type":"fill","text":"填写第 16 空","answer":"electric switches/switches","acceptedAnswers":["electric switches","switches"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Bakelite was a good insulator and was resistant to water, acids and moderate heat. With these properties, it was soon being used in the manufacture of switches, household items, such as knife handles, and electrical components for cars.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是贝克勒尔发明的塑料在制造哪些物品时被使用。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"electric switches\"或\"switches\"可以定位到D段中提到贝克勒尔发明的塑料被用于制造开关。\n解题思路：根据原文中D段的句子可以确定，贝克勒尔发明的塑料很快被用于制造开关、家用物品（如刀柄）和汽车电气元件。因此，题目中的\"electric switches\"或\"switches\"就是答案。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"58972","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022B0ZeaaCG3C1669987832.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"8094:58973:17","type":"fill","text":"填写第 17 空","answer":"Britain/UK","acceptedAnswers":["Britain","UK"],"explanation":"原文答案句：British chemists discovered that the gas ethylene would polymerise under heat and pressure to form a thermoplastic they called polythene.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求找出发现polythene的国家。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"polythene\"定位到E段中提到这种塑料的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到\"British chemists\"（英国化学家）发现了polythene，因此答案为Britain或UK。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"58973","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022B0ZeaaCG3C1669987832.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"8094:58974:18","type":"fill","text":"填写第 18 空","answer":"fireproof","acceptedAnswers":["fireproof"],"explanation":"原文答案句：A hard, fireproof plastic suitable for drains and gutters.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求从文章中选出不超过三个单词作为答案，填入指定的答题框中。根据题目信息，需要找出一种塑料的特性。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“fireproof”来定位答案在文章中的位置。在阅读文章时，注意寻找与“fireproof”相关的句子。\n解题思路：在E段中，提到了一种名为PVC（polyvinyl chloride）的塑料，描述为“a hard, fireproof plastic suitable for drains and gutters.”根据题目要求，我们需要选择不超过三个单词作为答案，因此可以选择“fireproof”作为答案。这个词描述了PVC塑料的特性，即防火。因此，答案为“fireproof”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"58974","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022B0ZeaaCG3C1669987832.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"8094:58975:19","type":"fill","text":"填写第 19 空","answer":"glass","acceptedAnswers":["glass"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Polystyrene, developed during the 1930s in Germany, was a clear, glass-like material, used in food containers, domestic appliances and toys.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求从文章中选出不超过三个单词的答案，描述聚苯乙烯（Polystyrene）的某种特性。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中可能出现的“Polystyrene”或“聚苯乙烯”等关键词，在文章中定位到E段描述聚苯乙烯的句子。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到聚苯乙烯是一种“clear, glass-like material”（清晰、类似玻璃的材料），其中“glass-like”直接描述了其类似玻璃的特性。题目要求填写描述其特性的单词，因此“glass”是答案。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"58975","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022B0ZeaaCG3C1669987832.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"8094:58976:20","type":"fill","text":"填写第 20 空","answer":"rigid foams","acceptedAnswers":["rigid foams"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Expanded polystyrene – a white, rigid foam – was widely used in packaging and insulation.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目要求填写一种塑料的具体形式或用途，根据上下文推断与包装和绝缘相关的塑料形式。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词“packaging and insulation”定位到E段末句，该句描述了expanded polystyrene的用途。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到expanded polystyrene是一种“white, rigid foam”，并且被广泛用于“packaging and insulation”。题目问的是这种塑料的具体形式，因此答案为“rigid foams”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"58976","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022B0ZeaaCG3C1669987832.png]","maxWords":3},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"8094:58977:21","type":"choice","text":"The chemical structure of plastic is very different from that of rubber.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Rubber is a polymer – a compound containing large molecules that are formed by the bonding of many smaller, simpler units, repeated over and over again. The same bonding principle – polymerisation – underlies the creation of a huge range of plastics by the chemical industry.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问“塑料的化学结构与橡胶非常不同”，需要判断这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的“chemical structure of plastic”和“rubber”定位，找到B段对比橡胶和塑料的化学结构。\n解题思路：原文明确指出橡胶是一种聚合物（polymer），其分子由许多小单位通过聚合反应（polymerisation）形成；塑料的创造也基于相同的聚合原理。这说明两者的化学结构原理相同，并非“非常不同”。因此，题目陈述与原文信息矛盾，答案为B（False）。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58977","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage?\nIn boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"8094:58978:22","type":"choice","text":"John Wesley was a famous chemist.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The prize was won by John Wesley Hyatt with a material called celluloid.\n对应段落：C段\n审题：题目问\"John Wesley是一位著名的化学家\"，要求判断这个陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的\"John Wesley\"定位到C段第一句，提到John Wesley Hyatt赢得了竞赛，发明了赛璐珞。\n解题思路：原文提到John Wesley Hyatt赢得了发明赛璐珞的竞赛，但并未提及他是否是著名的化学家。文章只描述了他的发明成就，没有说明他的职业身份或知名度。因此，题目中的\"著名化学家\"这一信息在文章中没有明确给出，无法判断其真假。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58978","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage?\nIn boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"8094:58979:23","type":"choice","text":"Celluloid and Bakelite react to heat in the same way.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Celluloid can be repeatedly softened and reshaped by heat and is known as a thermoplastic. In 1907 Leo Baekeland, a Belgian chemist working in the USA invented a different kind of plastic by causing phenol and formaldehyde to react together. Baekeland called the material Bakelite, and it was the first of the thermosets – plastics that can be cast and moulded while hot but cannot be softened by heat and reshaped once they have set.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是Celluloid和Bakelite对热反应的方式是否相同。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的\"Celluloid and Bakelite\"和\"react to heat\"定位到D段，该段描述了这两种材料对热的反应方式。\n解题思路：D段明确指出Celluloid是一种热塑性塑料，可以被反复加热软化并重塑；而Bakelite是一种热固性塑料，一旦成型就不能被加热软化或重塑。因此，这两种材料对热的反应方式不同，题目中的陈述与文章信息不符，所以答案是False。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58979","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage?\nIn boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"8094:58980:24","type":"choice","text":"The mix of different varieties of plastic can make them less recyclable.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Nor is it very easy to recycle plastics, as different types of plastic are often used in the same items and call for different treatments.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问“不同种类塑料的混合会使它们更难回收”这一陈述是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词\"mix of different varieties of plastic\"和\"less recyclable\"定位到G段末句，该句提到不同类型的塑料需要不同的处理方法，暗示混合后回收困难。\n解题思路：原文明确指出不同类型的塑料在同一物品中需要不同处理，这直接支持了“混合使回收更困难”的观点。因此，题目陈述与原文信息一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58980","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage?\nIn boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"8094:58981:25","type":"choice","text":"Adding starch into plastic does not necessarily make plastic more durable.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Plastics can be made biodegradable by incorporating into their structure a material such as starch, which is attacked by bacteria and causes the plastic to fall apart.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“将淀粉添加到塑料中并不一定会使塑料更耐用”这一说法是否与文章信息一致。\n定位关键信息：根据题目中的关键词\"starch\"和\"plastic\"定位到G段，该段提到了将淀粉添加到塑料中的作用。\n解题思路：原文中提到，将淀粉添加到塑料中可以使塑料变得可生物降解，即被细菌分解而分解。题目中的\"more durable\"意为更耐用，而原文中提到的是使塑料更容易被分解，这与\"more durable\"的含义相反。因此，题目中的说法与原文信息一致，答案为True。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58981","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage?\nIn boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"8094:58982:26","type":"choice","text":"Some plastic containers have to be preserved in special conditions.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"原文答案句：bottles made of such materials have to be stored in the dark, to ensure that they do not disintegrate before they have been used.\n对应段落：G段\n审题：题目问的是“一些塑料容器需要保存在特殊条件下”，即询问塑料容器是否有需要特殊保存的情况。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词“plastic containers”和“preserved in special conditions”可以定位到G段，该段提到了塑料容器需要保存在黑暗中，以防止它们在使用前分解。\n解题思路：根据原文答案句“bottles made of such materials have to be stored in the dark, to ensure that they do not disintegrate before they have been used.”，可以确定确实存在一些塑料容器需要保存在特殊条件下（即黑暗中），因此题目的陈述与原文信息一致，答案为TRUE。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58982","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage?\nIn boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"58970","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022B0ZeaaCG3C1669987832.png]","html":"<p><strong>14</strong> <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"58971","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022B0ZeaaCG3C1669987832.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">15</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[15] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":15},{"id":"58972","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022B0ZeaaCG3C1669987832.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">16</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[16] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":16},{"id":"58973","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022B0ZeaaCG3C1669987832.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">17</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[17] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":17},{"id":"58974","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022B0ZeaaCG3C1669987832.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">18</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[18] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":18},{"id":"58975","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022B0ZeaaCG3C1669987832.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">19</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[19] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"58976","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14-20\nChoose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.\n[image: https://xintongsmater.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/uploads/image/2022B0ZeaaCG3C1669987832.png]","html":"<p><strong style=\"white-space: normal;\">20</strong>&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"58977","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage?\nIn boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The chemical structure of plastic is very different from that of rubber.</strong></p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"58978","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage?\nIn boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>John Wesley was a famous chemist.</strong></p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"58979","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage?\nIn boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Celluloid and Bakelite react to heat in the same way.</strong></p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"58980","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage?\nIn boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>The mix of different varieties of plastic can make them less recyclable.</strong></p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"58981","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage?\nIn boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Adding starch into plastic does not necessarily make plastic more durable.</strong></p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"58982","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 21-26\nDo the following statements agree with the information given in the reading passage?\nIn boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement is true FALSE if the statement is false NOT GIVEN if the information is not given in the passage","html":"<p><strong>Some plastic containers have to be preserved in special conditions.</strong></p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The Development of Plastics&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>When rubber was first commercially produced in Europe during the nineteenth century, it rapidly became a very important commodity, particularly in the fields of transportation and electricity. However, during the twentieth century a number of new synthetic materials, called plastics, superseded natural rubber in all but a few applications.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>Rubber is a polymer – a compound containing large molecules that are formed by the bonding of many smaller, simpler units, repeated over and over again. The same bonding principle – polymerisation – underlies the creation of a huge range of plastics by the chemical industry.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>The first plastic was developed as a result of a competition in the USA. In the 1860s, $10,000 was offered to anybody who could replace ivory – supplies of which were declining – with something equally good as a material for making billiard balls. The prize was won by John Wesley Hyatt with a material called celluloid. Celluloid was made by dissolving cellulose, a carbohydrate derived from plants, in a solution of camphor dissolved in ethanol. This new material rapidly found uses in the manufacture of products such as knife handles, detachable collars and cuffs, spectacle frames and photographic film. Without celluloid, the film industry could never have got off the ground at the end of the 19th century.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>Celluloid can be repeatedly softened and reshaped by heat and is known as a thermoplastic. In 1907 Leo Baekeland, a Belgian chemist working in the USA invented a different kind of plastic by causing phenol and formaldehyde to react together. Baekeland called the material Bakelite, and it was the first of the thermosets – plastics that can be cast and moulded while hot but cannot be softened by heat and reshaped once they have set. Bakelite was a good insulator and was resistant to water, acids and moderate heat. With these properties, it was soon being used in the manufacture of switches, household items, such as knife handles, and electrical components for cars.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>Soon chemists began looking for other small molecules that could be strung together to make polymers. In the 1930s, British chemists discovered that the gas ethylene would polymerise under heat and pressure to form a thermoplastic they called polythene. Polypropylene followed in the 1950s. both were used to make bottles, pipes and plastic bags. A small change in the starting material – replacing a hydrogen atom in ethylene with a chlorine atom – produced PVC (polyvinyl chloride), a hard, fireproof plastic suitable for drains and gutters. And by adding certain chemicals, a soft form of PVC could be produced, suitable as a substitute for rubber in items such as waterproof clothing. A closely related plastic was Teflon, as PTFE (polytetrafluoroethylene). This had a very low coefficient of friction, making it ideal for bearings, rollers, and non-stick frying pans. Polystyrene, developed during the 1930s in Germany, was a clear, glass-like material, used in food containers, domestic appliances and toys. Expanded polystyrene – a white, rigid foam – was widely used in packaging and insulation. Polyurethanes, also developed in Germany, found uses as adhesives, coatings, and – in the form of rigid foams – as insulation materials. They are all produced from chemicals derived from crude oil, which contains exactly the same elements – carbon and hydrogen – as many plastics.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>The first of the man-made fibres, nylon, was also created in the 1930s. Its inventor was a chemist called Wallace Carothers, who worked for the Du Pont company in the USA. He found that under the right conditions, two chemicals – hexamethylenediamine and adipic acid — would form a polymer that could be pumped out through holes and then stretched to form long glossy threads that could be woven like silk. Its first use was to make parachutes for the US armed forces in World War II. In the post-war years, nylon completely replaced silk in the manufacture of stockings. Subsequently, many other synthetic fibres joined nylon, including Orion, Acrilan and Terylene. Today most garments are made of a blend of natural fibres, such as cotton and wool, and man-made fibres that make fabrics easier to look after.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p>The great strength of the plastic is its indestructibility. However, this quality is also something of a drawback: beaches all over the world, even on the remotest islands, are littered with plastic bottles that nothing can destroy. Nor is it very easy to recycle plastics, as different types of plastic are often used in the same items and call for different treatments. Plastics can be made biodegradable by incorporating into their structure a material such as starch, which is attacked by bacteria and causes the plastic to fall apart. Other materials can be incorporated that gradually decay in sunlight – although bottles made of such materials have to be stored in the dark, to ensure that they do not disintegrate before they have been used.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8094&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-8055","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Pottery Production in Ancient Akrotiri","book":"阅读还原集Vol.11","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test2","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.11 · Test2 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"8055:58742:27","type":"choice","text":"What does the writer say about of pottery excavated at Akrotiri?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The bulk of pottery found at Akrotiri is locally made and dates from the late fifteenth century BC. It clearly fulfilled a vast range of the settlement’s requirements: more than fifty different types of pots can be distinguished.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是关于在Akrotiri发掘的陶器，作者说了什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"pottery excavated at Akrotiri\"可以定位到文章的B段，该段提到了在Akrotiri发掘的陶器的情况。\n解题思路：根据B段第一句话，可以得知在Akrotiri发掘的陶器大部分是本地制造的，并且可以满足该定居点的大量需求，有超过五十种不同的陶器类型可以被区分。这表明这些陶器可以满足各种各样的需求，与选项B\"它们将满足大量需求\"相符。因此，正确答案是B。","options":["There was very little duplication.","They would have met a big variety of needs.","Most of them had been imported from other places.","The intended purpose of each piece was unclear."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"58742","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-28\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"8055:58743:28","type":"choice","text":"The assumption that pottery from Akrotiri was produced by specialists is partly based on","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Given a large number of shapes produced and the relatively high degree of standardisation, it has generally been assumed that most, if not all, of Akrotiri pottery, was produced by specialised craftsmen in a non-domestic context.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是关于在Akrotiri发掘的陶器，作者说了什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"pottery excavated at Akrotiri\"可以定位到文章的B段，该段提到了在Akrotiri发掘的陶器的情况。\n解题思路：根据B段答案句，可以得知在Akrotiri发掘的陶器有多种形状可以验证是由specialised craftsmen制作的，与选项D\"形状的多样化\"相符。因此，正确答案是D。","options":["the discovery of kilns.","the central location of workshops.","the sophistication of decorative patterns.","the wide range of shapes represented."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"58743","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-28\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"8055:58744:29","type":"choice","text":"The assumption that standard units of weight were in use could be based on ____","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In spite of the absence of any written records, the archaeological evidence reveals that concepts of measurements, both weight and number, had been formulated. Standard measures may already have been in operation, such as those evidenced by a graduated series of lead weights – made in disc form – found at the site.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“关于标准重量单位的假设可能基于什么证据”。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的\"standard units of weight\"和\"based on\"定位到D段，该段提到\"concepts of measurements, both weight and number, had been formulated\"以及\"Standard measures may already have been in operation, such as those evidenced by a graduated series of lead weights – made in disc form – found at the site.\"\n解题思路：原文中明确提到标准重量单位的假设是基于在遗址中发现的一系列铅制圆盘形砝码（lead weights – made in disc form），这些砝码的存在证明了当时已经存在标准重量单位的概念。因此，答案为A（the discovery of a collection of metal discs）。","options":["the discovery of a collection of metal discs.","the size and type of sailing ships in use.","variations in the exact shape and thickness of similar containers.","the physical characteristics of workmen.","marks found on wine containers.","the variety of commodities for which they would have been used."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"58744","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 29-32\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"8055:58744:30","type":"choice","text":"Evidence of the use of standard units of the volume is provided by ____","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The existence of units of capacity in Late Bronze Age times is also evidenced, by the notation of units of a liquid measure for wine on excavated containers.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是“证据表明使用了标准的体积单位”。\n定位关键信息：利用题目的“standard units of volume”和“evidence”这两个关键词，在文章中定位到D段，该段明确提到了“units of capacity”和“evidence”。\n解题思路：原文中D段提到“units of capacity in Late Bronze Age times is also evidenced”，这与题目中的“standard units of volume”和“evidence”相对应。因此，可以确定答案为D段中提到的“notation of units of a liquid measure for wine on excavated containers”。","options":["the discovery of a collection of metal discs.","the size and type of sailing ships in use.","variations in the exact shape and thickness of similar containers.","the physical characteristics of workmen.","marks found on wine containers.","the variety of commodities for which they would have been used."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"58744","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 29-32\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"8055:58744:31","type":"choice","text":"The size of certain types of containers would have been restricted by ____","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In fact, the length of a man’s arm limits the size of a smaller pot to a capacity of about twenty litres; that is also the maximum a man can comfortably carry.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是某种容器的尺寸会受到什么限制。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"size of certain types of containers\"和\"restricted by\"可以定位到E段中关于容器尺寸限制的描述。\n解题思路：原文中明确提到\"the length of a man’s arm limits the size of a smaller pot\"，即人的手臂长度限制了小容器的尺寸，这直接对应了题目中\"size of certain types of containers would have been restricted by\"的描述。因此，答案为D。","options":["the discovery of a collection of metal discs.","the size and type of sailing ships in use.","variations in the exact shape and thickness of similar containers.","the physical characteristics of workmen.","marks found on wine containers.","the variety of commodities for which they would have been used."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"58744","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 29-32\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"8055:58744:32","type":"choice","text":"Attempts to identify the intended capacity of containers are complicated by ____","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In trying to reconstruct systems of capacity by measuring the volume of excavated pottery, a rather generous range of tolerances must be allowed.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是“试图确定容器预期容量所面临的问题是什么”，即容器容量识别过程中的复杂性。\n定位关键信息：根据题干中的\"identify the intended capacity of containers\"和\"complicated by\"可以定位到H段首句，该句提到了\"reconstruct systems of capacity\"和\"generous range of tolerances\"。\n解题思路：H段首句明确指出，在通过测量出土陶器体积来重建容量系统时，必须允许相当大的容差范围。这表明容器容量识别过程因允许的容差范围较大而变得复杂，即无法精确确定每个容器的实际容量。原文中的\"a rather generous range of tolerances must be allowed\"直接对应题目中的\"complicated by\"，说明容差范围的存在使得容量识别复杂化。因此，答案为C。","options":["the discovery of a collection of metal discs.","the size and type of sailing ships in use.","variations in the exact shape and thickness of similar containers.","the physical characteristics of workmen.","marks found on wine containers.","the variety of commodities for which they would have been used."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"58744","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 29-32\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"8055:58748:33","type":"choice","text":"There are plans to excavate new areas of the archaeological site the near future.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The reason may be that the ceramic workshops were located on the periphery of the site, which has not yet been excavated.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是“考古遗址计划在不久的将来开挖新区域”，即询问作者是否提到有开挖新区域的计划。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的“excavate new areas”和“in the near future”定位到B段中“which has not yet been excavated”，这句话表明新区域尚未被发掘，但并未提及是否有计划在不久的将来进行开挖。\n解题思路：原文提到新区域尚未被发掘，但并未提及任何关于未来开挖的计划或安排。因此，无法确定作者是否认为有计划在不久的将来开挖新区域，所以答案为“Not Given”。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58748","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question33-38\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"8055:58749:34","type":"choice","text":"Some of the evidence concerning pottery production in ancient Akrotiri comes from written records.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：In spite of the absence of any written records, the archaeological evidence reveals that concepts of measurements, both weight and number, had been formulated.\n对应段落：D段\n审题：题目问的是关于古代阿克罗蒂里陶器生产的部分证据是否来自书面记录。\n定位关键信息：题目中的关键词是\"written records\"，在文章中定位到D段，找到含有\"written records\"或相关表述的句子。\n解题思路：根据D段原文句子\"In spite of the absence of any written records, the archaeological evidence reveals that concepts of measurements, both weight and number, had been formulated.\"可知，文章明确提到没有书面记录，陶器生产的证据来自考古发现而非书面记录。因此，题目说法与作者观点相反，应选择\"No\"。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58749","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question33-38\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"8055:58750:35","type":"choice","text":"Pots for transporting liquids would have held no more than about 20 litres.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：For example, large storage jars would be needed to store commodities, whereas smaller containers would be used for transport. In fact, the length of a man’s arm limits the size of a smaller pot to a capacity of about twenty litres; that is also the maximum a man can comfortably carry.\n对应段落：E段\n审题：题目问的是“用于运输液体的罐子容量不超过大约20升”，需要判断作者是否认同这一说法。\n定位关键信息：利用题目中的关键词“transporting liquids”和“no more than about 20 litres”定位到E段。原文提到“smaller containers would be used for transport”和“the length of a man’s arm limits the size of a smaller pot to a capacity of about twenty litres”，说明用于运输的小型容器容量约为20升。\n解题思路：原文明确指出用于运输的容器（smaller containers）容量约为20升，且这是由人的臂长限制的。题目中的“no more than about 20 litres”与原文“capacity of about twenty litres”一致，因此作者认同这一说法。答案为A（Yes）。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58750","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question33-38\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"8055:58751:36","type":"choice","text":"It would have been hard for merchants to calculate how much wine was on their ships.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The capacity of each container was known to be 14-18 litres. (F段)\n对应段落：F段\n审题：题目问的是商人是否很难计算出船上葡萄酒的数量。\n定位关键信息：利用题干中的关键词\"merchants\"和\"calculate how much wine\"定位到F段，该段提到商人可以通过容器数量和已知容量来计算葡萄酒的数量。\n解题思路：原文明确指出商人可以通过容器数量和已知容量（14-18升）来计算葡萄酒的数量，因此商人实际上可以很容易地计算出葡萄酒的数量，与题干说法相反。故答案为B（No）。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58751","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question33-38\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"8055:58752:37","type":"choice","text":"The capacity of containers intended to hold the same amounts differed by up to 20 per cent.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：Even where there is no noticeable external difference between pots meant to contain the same quantity of a commodity, differences in their capacity can actually reach one or two litres. In one case the deviation from the required size appears to be as much as 10-20 per cent.\n对应段落：H段\n审题：题目问的是“用于盛装相同数量的容器的容量差异可达20%”，需要判断作者是否同意这一说法。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的“containers intended to hold the same amounts”和“differed by up to 20 per cent”可以定位到H段中“pots meant to contain the same quantity of a commodity”和“deviation from the required size appears to be as much as 10-20 per cent”。\n解题思路：原文H段明确提到，即使在外观上没有明显差异的用于盛装相同数量商品的容器，其容量差异实际上可以达到一到两升，并且在一种情况下，与所需尺寸的偏差高达10-20%。这与题目中的说法完全一致，因此作者同意这一观点，答案为A（Yes）。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58752","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question33-38\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"8055:58753:38","type":"choice","text":"Regular trading of goods around the Aegean would have led to the general standardisation of\nquantities.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The increased demand for standardised exchanges, inextricably linked to commercial transactions, might have been one of the main factors which led to the standardisation of pottery production.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是“爱琴海地区的商品常规贸易是否会导致数量的普遍标准化”，需要判断作者是否认同这一观点。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"Regular trading of goods around the Aegean\"和\"standardisation of quantities\"可以定位到I段，该段提到\"increased demand for standardised exchanges\"和\"standardisation of pottery production\"，这与题目中的\"standardisation of quantities\"相关。\n解题思路：原文中I段提到，对标准化交换的日益增长的需求，与商业交易密不可分，可能是导致陶器生产标准化的主要原因之一。这与题目中的\"Regular trading of goods around the Aegean would have led to the general standardisation of quantities\"意思一致，即爱琴海地区的商品常规贸易会导致数量的普遍标准化。因此，作者认同这一观点，答案为A（Yes）。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"58753","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question33-38\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"8055:58754:39","type":"choice","text":"What does the writer say about the standardisation of container sizes?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The increased demand for standardised exchanges, inextricably linked to commercial transactions, might have been one of the main factors which led to the standardisation of pottery production.\n对应段落：I段\n审题：题目问的是“爱琴海地区的商品常规贸易是否会导致数量的普遍标准化”，需要判断作者是否认同这一观点。\n定位关键信息：通过题干中的关键词\"Regular trading of goods around the Aegean\"和\"standardisation of quantities\"可以定位到I段，该段提到\"increased demand for standardised exchanges\"和\"standardisation of pottery production\"，这与题目中的\"standardisation of quantities\"相关。\n解题思路：原文中I段提到，对标准化交换的日益增长的需求，与商业交易密不可分，可能是导致陶器生产标准化的主要原因之一。这与题目中的\"Regular trading of goods around the Aegean would have led to the general standardisation of quantities\"意思一致，即爱琴海地区的商品常规贸易会导致数量的普遍标准化。因此，作者认同这一观点，答案为A（Yes）。","options":["Containers which looked the same from the outside often varied in capacity.","The instruments used to control container size were unreliable.","The unsystematic use of different types of clay resulted in size variations.","Potters usually discarded containers which were of a non-standard size."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"58754","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question39-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"8055:58755:40","type":"choice","text":"What is probably the main purpose of the passage?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"原文答案句：The bulk of pottery found at Akrotiri is locally made and dates from the late fifteenth century BC. It clearly fulfilled a vast range of the settlement’s requirements: more than fifty different types of pots can be distinguished. The pottery found includes a wide variety of functional types like storage jars, smaller containers, pouring vessels, cooking pots, drinking vessels and so on, which all relate to specific activities and which would have been made and distributed with those activities in mind. Given a large number of shapes produced and the relatively high degree of standardisation, it has generally been assumed that most, if not all, of Akrotiri pottery, was produced by specialised craftsmen in a non-domestic context. Unfortunately, neither the potters’ workshops nor kilns have been found within the excavated area. The reason may be that the ceramic workshops were located on the periphery of the site, which has not yet been excavated. In any event, the ubiquity of the pottery, and the consistent repetition of the same types in different sizes suggest production on an industrial scale.\n对应段落：B段\n审题：题目问的是文章的主要目的是什么。\n定位关键信息：通过题目中的关键词\"main purpose\"可以定位到文章中关于陶器生产的目的和意义的描述。\n解题思路：根据原文中的句子，可以看出文章主要讨论的是阿克罗蒂里出土的陶器的特征和生产方式，以及这些特征如何反映了当时的社会经济状况。文章并没有直接评价陶器的质量，也没有详细描述陶器制作技能的发展，更没有具体描述储存和运输家用物品的方法。因此，文章的主要目的是探讨阿克罗蒂里陶器生产的特征如何反映了其他地区的发展。","options":["To evaluate the quality of pottery containers found in prehistoric Akrotiri","To suggest how features of pottery production at Akrotiri reflected other developments in the region","To outline the development of pottery-making skills in ancient Greece","To describe methods for storing and transporting household goods in prehistoric societies"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"58755","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question39-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"58742","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-28\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","html":"<p><strong>What does the writer say about of pottery excavated at Akrotiri?</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"58743","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27-28\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","html":"<p><strong>The assumption that pottery from Akrotiri was produced by specialists is partly based on</strong><br/></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"58744","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 29-32\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending.","html":"<p><strong>A</strong> the discovery of a collection of metal discs. <br/></p><p><strong>B</strong> the size and type of sailing ships in use. <br/></p><p><strong>C</strong> variations in the exact shape and thickness of similar containers. <br/></p><p><strong>D</strong> the physical characteristics of workmen. <br/></p><p><strong>E</strong> marks found on wine containers. <br/></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>F</strong> the variety of commodities for which they would have been used.<strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>29</strong> The assumption that standard units of weight were in use could be based on <strong class=\"source-blank\">[29] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"58748","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question33-38\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>There are plans to excavate new areas of the archaeological site the near future.</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"58749","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question33-38\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Some of the evidence concerning pottery production in ancient Akrotiri comes from written records.</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"58750","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question33-38\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Pots for transporting liquids would have held no more than about 20 litres.</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"58751","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question33-38\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>It would have been hard for merchants to calculate how much wine was on their ships.</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"58752","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question33-38\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>The capacity of containers intended to hold the same amounts differed by up to 20 per cent.</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"58753","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question33-38\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in the passage? Choose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Regular trading of goods around the Aegean would have led to the general standardisation of\nquantities.</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"58754","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question39-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","html":"<p><strong>What does the writer say about the standardisation of container sizes?</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"58755","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Question39-40\nChoose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","html":"<p><strong>What is probably the main purpose of the passage?</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p><strong>Pottery Production in Ancient Akrotiri</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Excavations at the site of prehistoric Akrotiri, on the coast of the Aegean Sea, have revealed much about the technical aspects of pottery manufacture, indisputably one of the basic industries of this Greek city. However, considerably less is known about the socio-economic context and the way production was organised.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The bulk of pottery found at Akrotiri is locally made and dates from the late fifteenth century BC. It clearly fulfilled a vast range of the settlement’s requirements: more than fifty different types of pots can be distinguished. The pottery found includes a wide variety of functional types like storage jars, smaller containers, pouring vessels, cooking pots, drinking vessels and so on, which all relate to specific activities and which would have been made and distributed with those activities in mind. Given a large number of shapes produced and the relatively high degree of standardisation, it has generally been assumed that most, if not all, of Akrotiri pottery, was produced by specialised craftsmen in a non-domestic context. Unfortunately, neither the potters’ workshops nor kilns have been found within the excavated area. The reason may be that the ceramic workshops were located on the periphery of the site, which has not yet been excavated. In any event, the ubiquity of the pottery, and the consistent repetition of the same types in different sizes suggest production on an industrial scale.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The Akrotirian potters seem to have responded to pressures beyond their households, namely to the increasing complexity of regional distribution and exchange systems. We can imagine them as full-time craftsmen working permanently in a high production-rate craft such as pottery manufacture, and supporting themselves entirely from the proceeds of their craft. In view of the above, one can begin to speak in terms of mass-produced pottery and the existence of organised workshops of craftsmen during the period 1550-1500 BC. Yet, how pottery production was organised at Akrotiri remains an open question, as there is no real documentary evidence. Our entire knowledge comes from the ceramic material itself, and the tentative conclusions which can be drawn from it.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The invention of units of quantity and of a numerical system to count them was of capital importance of an exchange-geared society such as that of Akrotiri. In spite of the absence of any written records, the archaeological evidence reveals that concepts of measurements, both weight and number, had been formulated. Standard measures may already have been in operation, such as those evidenced by a graduated series of lead weights – made in disc form – found at the site. The existence of units of capacity in Late Bronze Age times is also evidenced, by the notation of units of a liquid measure for wine on excavated containers.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>It must be recognised that the function of pottery vessels plays a very important role in determining their characteristics. The intended function affects the choice of clay, the production technique, and the shape and the size of the pots. For example, large storage jars would be needed to store commodities, whereas smaller containers would be used for transport. In fact, the length of a man’s arm limits the size of a smaller pot to a capacity of about twenty litres; that is also the maximum a man can comfortably carry.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The various sizes of container would thus represent standard quantities of a commodity, which is a fundamental element in the function of exchange. Akrotirian merchants handling a commodity such as wine would have been able to determine easily the amount of wine they were transporting from the number of containers they carried in their ships since the capacity of each container was known to be 14-18 litres. (We could draw a parallel here with the current practice in Greece of selling oil in 17-kilogram tins.)</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>We may, therefore, assume that the shape, capacity, and, sometimes decoration of vessels are indicative of the commodity contained by them. Since individual transactions would normally involve different quantities of a given commodity, a range of ‘standardised’ types of the vessel would be needed to meet traders’ requirements.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>In trying to reconstruct systems of capacity by measuring the volume of excavated pottery, a rather generous range of tolerances must be allowed. It seems possible that the potters of that time had specific sizes of the vessel in mind, and tried to reproduce them using a specific type and amount of clay. However, it would be quite difficult for them to achieve the exact size required every time, without any mechanical means of regulating symmetry and wall thickness, and some potters would be more skilled than others. In addition, variations in the repetition of types and size may also occur because of unforeseen circumstances during the throwing process. For instance, instead of destroying the entire pot if the clay in the rim contained a piece of grit, a potter might produce a smaller pot by simply cutting off the rim. Even where there is no noticeable external difference between pots meant to contain the same quantity of a commodity, differences in their capacity can actually reach one or two litres. In one case the deviation from the required size appears to be as much as 10-20 per cent.</p><p><br/></p><p>I&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>The establishment of regular trade routes within the Aegean led to increased movement of goods; consequently, a regular exchange of local, luxury and surplus goods, including metals, would have become feasible as a result of the advances in transport technology. The increased demand for standardised exchanges, inextricably linked to commercial transactions, might have been one of the main factors which led to the standardisation of pottery production. Thus, the whole network of ceramic production and exchange would have depended on specific regional economic conditions and would reflect the socio-economic structure of prehistoric Akrotiri.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=8055&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7433","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 John St Clair Kilby: inventor of the integrated circuit","book":"阅读还原集Vol.11","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test1","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.11 · Test1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"7433:56637:1","type":"choice","text":"Kilby's father helped with contacting people in Grand Bend, Kansas during emergencies.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"定位词: father, contacting people, emergencies\n对应原文: A 段, His father, who ran a small electrical company in rural Kansas, worked with amateur radio operators to communicate with local people who, as a result of storms or floods, had lost their electricity supply or telephone service.\n详细解析:A 段指出 Kilby 的父亲通过与业余无线电操作员合作，帮助在紧急情况下与人们联系。\n同义替换:helped with contacting people = worked with amateur radio operators; emergencies=storms or floods","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56637","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"7433:56638:2","type":"choice","text":"Kilby often met other amateur radio enthusiasts when he was growing up in Kansas.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"定位词: met other amateur radio enthusiasts\n对应原文:  A段, This gave Kilby an early interest in amateur radio and sparked his interest in electronics.\n详细解析: A 段指出 Kilby 对业余无线电感兴趣，但没有提到他是否经常与其他无线电爱好者见面。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56638","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"7433:56639:3","type":"choice","text":"Kilby's father encouraged him to apply to the Massachusetts Institute of Technology.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"定位词: father, encouraged, Massachusetts Institute of Technology\n对应原文:B段，After finishing his schooling, Kilby tried to get into the highly respected Massachusetts Institute of Technology, but just failed the admission examination.\n详细解析:B段指出 Kilby 曾尝试申请 MIT，但没有提到他的父亲是否鼓励他。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56639","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"7433:56640:4","type":"choice","text":"Kilby's first job was with a company called Texas Instruments.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"定位词: first job, Texas Instruments\n对应原文: C段, While studying for his master's degree, Kilby worked for a manufacturer of electronic components in Milwaukee, Wisconsin. In 1958, he moved to Dallas, Texas, to take a job with Texas Instruments, because it was the only company he approached that would allow him to work more or less full-time on the miniaturisation of electronic components.\n详细解析:C段指出 Kilby 在获得硕士学位期间为一家电子元件制造商工作，这是他的第一份工作。Texas Instruments 是他 1958 年之后的雇主。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56640","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"7433:56641:5","type":"choice","text":"Kilby had various job offers from companies willing to let him pursue his interest.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"定位词: various job offers, pursue his interest.\n对应原文: C段, In 1958, he moved to Dallas, Texas, to take a job with Texas Instruments, because it was the only company he approached that would allow him to work more or less full-time on the miniaturisation of electronic components.\n详细解析:C段指出 Texas Instruments 是唯一一家允许 Kilby 专注于微型化研究的公司，这与题干中“有多种公司愿意提供工作机会”矛盾。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56641","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"7433:56642:6","type":"choice","text":"Texas Instruments agreed that Kilby needed his own laboratory in order to develop the integrated circuit.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"定位词: Texas Instruments, agreed, own laboratory\n对应段落: D段，The focus of Kilby's work at Texas Instruments was the development of the integrated circuit (commonly called the microchip). This replaced the transistors that had themselves replaced the ordinary vacuum tubes used in the first computers. The transistor, invented at Bell Laboratories in 1947, consisted of components joined with wires. The size of transistors was, therefore, limited because, as their size decreased, it became impossible to solder the components together.\n详细解析:文中没有提到 Texas Instruments 是否同意为 Kilby 提供独立实验室。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56642","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"7433:56643:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"silicon","acceptedAnswers":["silicon"],"explanation":"定位词: circuit made from\n对应原文: E段， Kilby's breakthrough was to use a single block of silicon to contain the entire circuit.\n详细解析:E段指出 Kilby 使用单块硅制造集成电路。\n同义替换: a circuit made from=a single block of","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56643","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"7433:56644:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"solar","acceptedAnswers":["solar"],"explanation":"定位词: technology used in\n对应原文: F段，In 1970, Kilby took time off from Texas Instruments to work independently, mainly to develop silicon technology to generate electricity. Since then, further research has been carried out into solar power and it is now an important way of reducing the emission of carbon dioxide to reduce global warming.\n详细解析:F段指出 Kilby 开发了硅技术以用于发电，并且进一步的研究集中在太阳能上。\n同义替换: Technology used in =technology to generate electricity.","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56644","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"7433:56645:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"consultant","acceptedAnswers":["consultant"],"explanation":"定位词: became a\n对应原文:  G段，After retiring from Texas Instruments in 1983, Kilby stayed with the company as a consultant.\n详细解析:G段指出 Kilby 退休后继续担任公司顾问。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56645","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"7433:56646:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"portable","acceptedAnswers":["portable"],"explanation":"定位词: various，used in\n对应原文: K段，Our environment is now flooded with electronic equipment that is portable – laptops, mini-calculators, phones, and electronic watches – and most of us depend on these things to such an extent that we would be lost without them.\n详细解析:K段指出集成电路被用于便携设备，如笔记本电脑、计算器等。\n同义替换：various electronic devices = Laptops, mini-calculators, phones","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56646","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"7433:56646:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"watches","acceptedAnswers":["watches"],"explanation":"定位词: things we wear\n对应原文:  K段，Our environment is now flooded with electronic equipment that is portable – laptops, mini-calculators, phones, and electronic watches – and most of us depend on these things to such an extent that we would be lost without them.\n详细解析:K段指出“电子手表”作为穿戴设备的例子。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56646","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"7433:56647:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"diagnostic","acceptedAnswers":["diagnostic"],"explanation":"定位词: medical facilities\n对应原文:  K段， Information technology controls high-tech systems, diagnostic equipment in hospitals, appliances we use at home in our daily lives, and much more besides.\n详细解析:K段指出集成电路被用于医院的诊断设备。\n同义替换：machines in medical facilities = diagnostic equipment in hospitals","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56647","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"7433:56648:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"cost","acceptedAnswers":["cost"],"explanation":"定位词: performance continues to improve，no increase in\n对应原文:  L段，The performance of integrated circuits has improved a hundredfold every ten years without their cost rising – and there is no end to this improvement in sight.\n详细解析:L段指出性能提升但成本没有增加。\n同义替换:no increase in=without...rising","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56648","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"56637","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Kilby&#39;s father helped with contacting people in Grand Bend, Kansas during emergencies.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"56638","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Kilby often met other amateur radio enthusiasts when he was growing up in Kansas.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"56639","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Kilby&#39;s father encouraged him to apply to the Massachusetts Institute of Technology.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"56640","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Kilby&#39;s first job was with a company called Texas Instruments.</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"56641","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Kilby had various job offers from companies willing to let him pursue his interest.</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"56642","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Texas Instruments agreed that Kilby needed his own laboratory in order to develop the integrated circuit.</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"56643","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>John Kilby and the development of the integrated circuit</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>Kilby&#39;s career and legacy</strong></p><p>•&nbsp;revolutionised electronics by creating a circuit made from <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"56644","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>•&nbsp;also helped develop the technology used in <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong> energy</p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"56645","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>•&nbsp;became a <strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong>&nbsp;to the company that formerly employed him</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">•&nbsp;had a research institute named after him</p><p style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><br/></p><p style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">•&nbsp;was granted a large number of patents for his inventions and won many awards, prizes and medals</p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"56646","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>Integrated circuits today</strong></p><p>•&nbsp;used in various <strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong>&nbsp;electronic devices,&nbsp;such as phones and laptops, and also in things we wear such as <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"56647","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>•&nbsp;used in machines in medical facilities for <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong>&nbsp;purposes</p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"56648","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>•&nbsp;their performance continues to improve, but there is no increase in <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>John St Clair Kilby: inventor of the integrated circuit</strong><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">John St Clair Kilby was born in 1923 in Grand Bend, Kansas, USA. His father, who ran a small electrical company in rural Kansas, worked with amateur radio operators to communicate with local people who, as a result of storms or floods, had lost their electricity supply or telephone service.&nbsp; This gave Kilby an early interest in amateur radio and sparked his interest in electronics. He decided to become an electronics and electrical engineer.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">After finishing his schooling, Kilby tried to get into the highly respected Massachusetts Institute of Technology, but just failed the admission examination.&nbsp; He went instead to the University of Illinois, but his studies were interrupted by the Second World War and he served in the US Army until the war ended in 1945. After resuming his studies, he received a degree in electrical engineering from Illinois and, in 1950, a master&#39;s degree in electrical engineering from the University of Wisconsin.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">While studying for his master&#39;s degree, Kilby worked for a manufacturer of electronic components in Milwaukee, Wisconsin. In 1958, he moved to Dallas, Texas, to take a job with Texas Instruments, because it was the only company he approached that would allow him to work more or less full-time on the miniaturisation of electronic components.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The focus of Kilby&#39;s work at Texas Instruments was the development of the integrated circuit (commonly called the microchip). This replaced the transistors that had themselves replaced the ordinary vacuum tubes used in the first computers. The transistor, invented at Bell Laboratories in 1947, consisted of components joined with wires. The size of transistors was, therefore, limited because, as their size decreased, it became impossible to solder the components together.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Kilby&#39;s breakthrough was to use a single block of silicon to contain the entire circuit.&nbsp; His first electronic device had a surface area of about a half a square centimetre and was about a millimetre thick. Today&#39;s electronic engineers can accommodate the equivalent of around 100 million transistors in a circuit this size.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Kilby first demonstrated that an integrated circuit worked on September 12, 1958 – a date that is one of the milestones in the history of technology. After proving that integrated circuits were possible, Kilby directed the teams that built the first computer based on integrated circuits. In 1970, Kilby took time off from Texas Instruments to work independently, mainly to develop silicon technology to generate electricity. Since then, further research has been carried out into solar power and it is now an important way of reducing the emission of carbon dioxide to reduce global warming.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">After retiring from Texas Instruments in 1983, Kilby stayed with the company as a consultant.&nbsp; He was also involved in various industry and government research projects, mostly concerning semiconductors. Three years after Kilby&#39;s death, in 2008, Texas Instruments named its new $154 million research facility in his honour.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Kilby received little financial reward for his inventions. Although he took out more than 60 patents, he benefited very little from them, nor did he allow technology to influence his daily life. He chose not to have a microwave oven or a calculator, continuing to use a slide rule. For all his achievements, he was an extraordinarily modest man who was always willing to give advice and encouragement to young people.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">However, Kilby&#39;s work did not go unrecognised. In 1995, he received the Robert N. Noyce Award, and in 2000 he won the US National Medal of Science and was admitted to the National Inventors Hall of Fame. He also won the US National Medal of Technology – becoming one of only 13 people to win both national medals, the highest US awards in science and technology. For his revolutionary developments in the field of electronics, Kilby was awarded the Nobel Physics Prize in 2000.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>J</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">In many ways, Kilby changed the world we live in. His invention of the integrated circuit revolutionised how the world communicates and calculates, affecting the lives of us all. The integrated circuit is the basis of information technology upon which we all depend. Integrated circuits are important in today&#39;s world because they allow large volumes of information to be transferred in a very short time. They also allow electronic equipment to be small enough to fit into a pocket.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>K</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Our environment is now flooded with electronic equipment that is portable – laptops, mini-calculators, phones, and electronic watches – and most of us depend on these things to such an extent that we would be lost without them.&nbsp; Information technology controls high-tech systems, diagnostic equipment in hospitals, appliances we use at home in our daily lives, and much more besides.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>L</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">It is widely accepted that information technology has been the main driver of the economic success that many societies have experienced since the 1990s. The performance of integrated circuits has improved a hundredfold every ten years without their cost rising – and there is no end to this improvement in sight.&nbsp; We certainly have much to thank Kilby for.</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7433&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7434","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 The Rise of Telecommuting","book":"阅读还原集Vol.11","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test1","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.11 · Test1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"7434:56649:14","type":"fill","text":"14 an example of a company where all of the employees work remotely","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"定位词: all employees work remotely\n定位原文: D段，His start-up is made up solely of telecommuters, with no centralized location.\n详细解析：D段指出，David Haddad 的公司完全由远程工作的员工组成，且没有集中办公地点。这里的solely of telecommuters 意味着公司所有员工都远程办公，且no centralized location 说明没有集中式的办公室环境。这与题干中一个所有员工远程办公的公司的描述完全对应。\n同义替换：all employees work remotely = solely of telecommuters","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56649","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the six sections (A - F). Which section contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - F). You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"7434:56649:15","type":"fill","text":"15 an explanation of why some workers chose to stop telecommuting once they had tried it","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"定位词: stop telecommuting\n定位原文: F段，Interestingly, at the end of the experiment, 50 percent of those who worked at home asked to come back to the office. They said they were lonely and didn't like being passed over for promotion.\n详细解析：F段指出，在实验结束后，有一半的远程工作者选择回到办公室，原因是孤独感（lonely）和错失晋升机会（being passed over for promotion）。这些原因清楚地解释了为什么一些员工在尝试远程办公后选择停止。\n同义替换：stop telecommuting = come back to the office","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56649","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the six sections (A - F). Which section contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - F). You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"7434:56649:16","type":"fill","text":"16 a discussion of the kinds of working arrangements that qualify as telecommuting","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"定位词: kinds of working arrangements 和 qualify as telecommuting\n定位原文: A段，However, the scope of telecommuting has at times been expanded to include the self-employed; those whose work has to be done outside an office, such as taxi drivers, plumbers and construction workers; companies where everyone works remotely, so there is no centralized office; and those who work at home one day or less a week.\n详细解析：A段指出了多种符合远程办公定义的工作形式，包括自雇人士（self-employed）、户外工作者（e.g., taxi drivers, plumbers）、完全远程办公的公司，以及部分时间远程工作者。这是对题干远程办公形式的讨论的直接回答。\n同义替换：kinds of = scope of","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56649","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the six sections (A - F). Which section contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - F). You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"7434:56649:17","type":"fill","text":"17 a comparison between telecommuters and other workers in terms of efficiency","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"定位词: comparison， efficiency\n定位原文: E段，At the end of the experiment, employers found that the home-based employees worked more than office workers – 9.5 percent longer – and were 13 percent more productive.\n详细解析：E段指出，实验结果显示远程员工比办公室员工工作时间更长（9.5% longer）且效率更高（13% more productive）。这是对远程员工与办公室员工在效率上的对比。\n同义替换：efficiency = productive","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56649","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the six sections (A - F). Which section contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - F). You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"7434:56649:18","type":"fill","text":"18 an example of a person who is telecommuting for family reasons","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位词: telecommuting for family reasons\n定位原文: C段，At his old job, he commuted about 45 minutes to Manhattan from his home in New Jersey, but he chose to telecommute to be closer to his wife and children.\n详细解析：C段指出，Kipp Jarecke-Cheng 选择远程办公是为了与家人（妻子和孩子）更亲近，这是典型的因家庭原因选择远程办公的例子。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56649","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the six sections (A - F). Which section contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - F). You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"7434:56649:19","type":"fill","text":"19 reasons why teleworkers may have fewer career opportunities than workers in offices","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"定位词: fewer career opportunities\n定位原文: E段，However, those working at home were also promoted at half the rate of their colleagues working in the office. 'It may be a case of \"out of sight, out of mind,\"' Professor Bloom said. 'Or it might be that you're not drinking in the bar with your boss. Or it could be you' re not managing your employees as well if you' re not around them.'\n详细解析：E段指出，远程员工的晋升机会只有办公室员工的一半（promoted at half the rate），原因包括眼不见心不想（out of sight, out of mind）以及缺乏面对面的管理机会。\n同义替换：fewer career opportunities = promoted at half the rate","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56649","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the six sections (A - F). Which section contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - F). You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"7434:56650:20","type":"choice","text":"20 Finding out information from co-workers is a less casual process for a telecommuter.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位词:Kipp Jarecke-Cheng\n定位原文: C段，'Probably one of the biggest transitions was that in a physical office, you can stroll by and ask questions,' says Jarecke-Cheng.\n详细解析：C段指出，Kipp Jarecke-Cheng 表示，在远程工作中，获取信息的方式变得不如在办公室随意。他需要积累问题列表，而不是像在办公室一样走过去直接提问。","options":["Jennifer Glass","Kate Lister","Kipp Jarecke-Cheng","Nicholas Bloom"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56650","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20 - 23\nChoose the correct person (A - D) for each statement. You may choose any correct person more than once.\nList of People\nA Jennifer Glass\nB Kate Lister\nC Kipp Jarecke-Cheng\nD Nicholas Bloom"},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"7434:56650:21","type":"choice","text":"21 Telecommuters were less likely than office workers to leave their jobs.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"定位词: Nicholas Bloom\n定位原文: E段，Bloom reports that the home-based workers also were judged to be happier, as quitting rates were cut in half.\n详细解析：E段指出，Nicholas Bloom表示，远程员工的离职率减少了一半（quitting rates were cut in half），表明他们比办公室员工更倾向于留在岗位上。\n同义替换：less likely to leave their jobs = quitting rates were cut in half","options":["Jennifer Glass","Kate Lister","Kipp Jarecke-Cheng","Nicholas Bloom"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56650","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20 - 23\nChoose the correct person (A - D) for each statement. You may choose any correct person more than once.\nList of People\nA Jennifer Glass\nB Kate Lister\nC Kipp Jarecke-Cheng\nD Nicholas Bloom"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"7434:56650:22","type":"choice","text":"22\tBad weather proved cost-effective for an employer.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"定位词:Kate Lister\n定位原文: B段，Federal employees in Washington, who worked from home recently during four official snow days, saved the government an estimated $32 million, according to Kate Lister, president of Global Workplace Analytics.\n详细解析：B段指出，Kate Lister表示，恶劣天气（雪天）期间，远程办公为政府节省了约3200万美元。这表明在恶劣天气情况下，远程办公对雇主来说是具有成本效益的。","options":["Jennifer Glass","Kate Lister","Kipp Jarecke-Cheng","Nicholas Bloom"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56650","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20 - 23\nChoose the correct person (A - D) for each statement. You may choose any correct person more than once.\nList of People\nA Jennifer Glass\nB Kate Lister\nC Kipp Jarecke-Cheng\nD Nicholas Bloom"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"7434:56650:23","type":"choice","text":"23 Meeting people initially in person is beneficial for someone who works from home.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位词:Kipp Jarecke-Cheng\n定位原文: C段，But it helped tremendously, he said, that after he was hired, his employer sent him to its national and international offices to see people face-to-face.\n详细解析：C段指出，Kipp Jarecke-Cheng 表示，雇主安排他在开始远程工作之前与同事面对面见面，这对他的工作帮助很大。\n同义替换：meeting people initially in person = see people face-to-face","options":["Jennifer Glass","Kate Lister","Kipp Jarecke-Cheng","Nicholas Bloom"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56650","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20 - 23\nChoose the correct person (A - D) for each statement. You may choose any correct person more than once.\nList of People\nA Jennifer Glass\nB Kate Lister\nC Kipp Jarecke-Cheng\nD Nicholas Bloom"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"7434:56651:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"centralized","acceptedAnswers":["centralized"],"explanation":"定位词: an organisation, does not have\n定位原文: D段，His start-up is made up solely of telecommuters, with no centralized location.\n详细解析：D段指出，David Haddad 的初创公司完全由远程员工组成，并且明确提到no centralized location（没有集中办公地点）。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56651","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"7434:56651:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"flexibility","acceptedAnswers":["flexibility"],"explanation":"定位词: an advantage of telecommuting\n定位原文: D段，Haddad likes the flexibility, but there are downsides.\n详细解析：D段指出，David Haddad 认为远程办公的主要优势是flexibility（灵活性）。这是对题干中远程办公的优点的直接回答。\n同义替换：an advantage of = likes","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56651","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"7434:56651:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"goals","acceptedAnswers":["goals"],"explanation":"定位词: challenge, informing people about his\n定位原文: D段，'It's difficult to keep tabs of what everyone is doing, as well as keep myself motivated to constantly report on my goals,' he said.\n详细解析：D段指出，David Haddad 认为难以跟踪员工的活动，并且不断汇报自己的目标（report on my goals）也是一项挑战。\n同义替换：informing = report","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56651","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"56649","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the six sections (A - F). Which section contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - F). You may choose any letter more than once.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"56650","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20 - 23\nChoose the correct person (A - D) for each statement. You may choose any correct person more than once.\nList of People\nA Jennifer Glass\nB Kate Lister\nC Kipp Jarecke-Cheng\nD Nicholas Bloom","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"56651","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>David Haddad, CEO</strong></p><p>David Haddad leads an organisation that does not have a <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> workplace. For Haddad, <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong> is an advantage of telecommuting. However, he finds it challenging to keep track of workers&#39; activities and to keep informing people about his <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong> . Although it is not the same as live personal contact. Haddad finds that technology helps people interact.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":24}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>The Rise of Telecommuting</strong><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><em>Telecommuting, or&nbsp;&#39;remote work&#39;,&nbsp;is an arrangement in which employees do not commute to a place of work</em></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The most complete definition of a &#39;telecommuter&#39; is someone employed full time at a private, nonprofit or government organization, who works at least half the time at home. By one estimate, telecommuting rose 79 percent between 2005 and 2012 and by 2014 made up 2.6 percent of the work force in the United States, or 3.2 million workers, according to the American Community Survey.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">However, the scope of telecommuting has at times been expanded to include the self-employed; those whose work has to be done outside an office, such as taxi drivers, plumbers and construction workers; companies where everyone works remotely, so there is no centralized office; and those who work at home one day or less a week. If all of those workers are included, the number of Americans who work remotely can reach as high as 30 percent.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Jennifer Glass, a professor of sociology at the University of Texas in the United States, has studied teleworking for two decades, and says much of what managers and professionals call telecommuting occurs after a 40-hour week spent in the office. People check email, return calls and write reports from home, but in the evenings and weekends. This is not strictly telecommuting as the general population would understand it.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">There is a widespread perception that telecommuting is usually done by someone in their 20s, or a mother with small children. In fact, according to numbers from the Census Bureau&#39;s annual American Community Survey, the typical telecommuter is a 49-year-old college graduate – man or woman – who belongs to a company with more than 100 employees. The phenomenon appears to be growing: the annual survey last year by the Society for Human Resource Management found a greater increase in the number of companies planning to offer telecommuting than those offering any other new benefit. And it seems that winter conditions might push the trend even faster. Federal employees in Washington, who worked from home recently during four official snow days, saved the government an estimated $32 million, according to Kate Lister, president of Global Workplace Analytics.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Kipp Jarecke-Cheng fits the typical teleworker profile. He is 44, and for the last year has been director of global public relations and communications for a design and technology consulting company based in Montreal in Canada. At his old job, he commuted about 45 minutes to Manhattan from his home in New Jersey, but he chose to telecommute to be closer to his wife and children. Jarecke-Cheng found that it took some time to get used to working at home. Like many teleworkers, he found that communicating with his colleagues and subordinates was more difficult, at least initially. &#39;Probably one of the biggest transitions was that in a physical office, you can stroll by and ask questions,&#39; says Jarecke-Cheng. &#39;Here I have to accumulate a list of questions.&#39; But it helped tremendously, he said, that after he was hired, his employer sent him to its national and international offices to see people face-to-face. &#39;I&#39;m not just a name on an email,&#39; he explains.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">David Haddad of New York City began working remotely as chief executive of a nonprofit start-up in 2011. His start-up is made up solely of telecommuters, with no centralized location. Haddad likes the flexibility, but there are downsides. &#39;It&#39;s difficult to keep tabs of what everyone is doing, as well as keep myself motivated to constantly report on my goals,&#39; he said.&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">While technology can&#39;t replace the human connection, Haddad says it makes communicating easier. Video conferencing is used, as are communications apps which provide virtual places for people to drop in and &#39;visit&#39;. For some people, virtual connections are enough, while for others nothing takes the place of being able to chat with a colleague over an office cubicle divider.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Nicholas Bloom, a professor of economics at Stanford University in the US, teamed up with China&#39;s largest travel agency to test some ideas about telecommuting. Over nine months, about 250 workers volunteered for the experiment; half were randomly chosen to work at home and half in the office. At the end of the experiment, employers found that the home-based employees worked more than office workers – 9.5 percent longer – and were 13 percent more productive. Also, by reducing office space, the company saved what would amount to US$2,000 per employee annually. Bloom reports that the home-based workers also were judged to be happier, as quitting rates were cut in half. However, those working at home were also promoted at half the rate of their colleagues working in the office. &#39;It may be a case of &quot;out of sight, out of mind,&quot;&#39; Professor Bloom said. &#39;Or it might be that you&#39;re not drinking in the bar with your boss. Or it could be you&#39; re not managing your employees as well if you&#39; re not around them.&#39;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Interestingly, at the end of the experiment, 50 percent of those who worked at home asked to come back to the office. They said they were lonely and didn&#39;t like being passed over for promotion. It does seem that most people like to have some combination of home and office work, according to Lister, &#39;that&#39;s the sweet spot&#39;.</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><o:p></o:p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7434&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7435","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 The significant role of mother tongue language in education","book":"阅读还原集Vol.11","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test1","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.11 · Test1 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"7435:56652:27","type":"choice","text":"What point is the writer making in the second paragraph?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位词：the second paragraph\n定位原文： B段，The challenge for educators and policy-makers is to shape the evolution of national identity in such a way that the rights of all citizens (including school children) are respected, and the cultural, linguistic and economic resources of the nation are maximized. To waste the resources of the nation by discouraging children from developing their mother tongues is quite simply unintelligent from the point of view of national self-interest. A first step in providing an appropriate education for culturally and linguistically diverse children is to examine what the existing research says about the role of children's mother tongues in their educational development.\n详细解析：\nB段指出了讨论如何通过尊重和利用所有公民（包括学生）的文化和语言资源，来最大化国家的经济、文化和语言资源。","options":["Some present studies on children's mother tongues are misleading.","A culturally rich education programme benefits some children more than others.","Bilingual children can make a valuable contribution to the wealth of a country.","The law on mother tongue use at school should be strengthened."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56652","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 30\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"7435:56653:28","type":"choice","text":"Why does the writer refer to something that Goethe said?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"定位词： Goethe said\n定位原文： C段，More than 150 research studies conducted during the past 35 years strongly support what Goethe, the famous eighteenth-century German philosopher, once said: that the person who knows only one language does not truly know that language.\n详细解析：\nC段指出，Goethe的话是为了支持作者的论点，通过引用哲学家的观点来增强论证的说服力。引用Goethe的名言目的是为了证明学习多语言的重要性，进而为双语教育的价值提供支持。文章并未反驳任何现有的研究，而是通过引用Goethe的话来增强现有研究的有效性。文中并没有引入新的概念，而是引用了一位历史人物的名言来支持观点。文中没有更新现有的理论，引用Goethe的话是为了增加自己论点的权威性。","options":["to lend weight to his argument","to contradict some research","to introduce a new concept","to update current thinking"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56653","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 30\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"7435:56654:29","type":"choice","text":"The writer believes that when young children have a firm grasp of their mother tongue","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"定位词： writer believes that, younger children, mother tongue\n定位原文： D段，Children who come to school with a solid foundation in their mother tongue develop stronger literacy abilities in the school language.\n详细解析：\nD段指出，拥有坚实母语基础的孩子能够在学校语言的学习中表现得更好。文中明确表明，母语的掌握对学校学习具有积极的推动作用，因此可以得知，掌握母语的孩子会在学校中表现得更好。文中并没有提到孩子可以教授家庭成员所学的内容，重点是孩子在学校的学习表现。文章并没有提到孩子会读与自己文化背景相关的故事，而是侧重于母语对学校语言学习的帮助。文中并没有讨论孩子和家庭的关系，讨论的主要是孩子在学校的学习进展。\n同义替换：firm grasp of = solid foundation in","options":["they can teach older family members what they learn at school.","they go on to do much better throughout their time at school.","they can read stories about their cultural background.","they develop stronger relationships with their family than with their peers."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56654","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 30\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"7435:56655:30","type":"choice","text":"Why are some people suspicious about mother tongue-based teaching programmes?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"定位词： suspicious, mother tongue-based teaching\n定位原文： E段，Some educators and parents are suspicious of mother tongue-based teaching programs because they worry that they take time away from the majority language.\n详细解析：E段指出，部分教育工作者和家长担心母语教育会占用学习主流语言的时间，这样会影响孩子在主流语言学习中的进度，这种担忧主要来源于对时间分配的忧虑。文中并未提到孩子学习阅读的速度或其他语言技能的进展，讨论的重点在时间管理上。文章没有提到孩子可能会混淆两种语言，而是讨论了时间分配的问题。文中并未讨论孩子对课程的兴趣，而是关注时间如何影响孩子学习主流语言的进度。\n同义替换：suspicious = Worry； use up valuable time = Take time away","options":["They worry that children will be slow to learn to read in either language.","They think that children will confuse words in the two languages.","They believe that the programmes will make children less interested in their lessons.","They fear that the programmes will use up valuable time in the school day."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56655","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 30\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"7435:56656:31","type":"choice","text":"Bilingual children\nIt has often been noted that bilingual children acquire the ____ to converse in the majority language remarkably quickly.","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"定位词： bilingual children, converse, majority language\n定位原文： G段，Many people marvel at how quickly bilingual children seem to ‘pick up’ conversational skills in the majority language at school.\n详细解析：G段指出，许多人惊叹于双语儿童在学校学习主流语言时，似乎能多快地掌握日常对话技巧。\n同义替换： conversational skills = the ability to converse","options":["teachers","school","dislocation","rate","time","family","communication","type","ability","area"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"56656","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 31 - 35\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"7435:56656:32","type":"choice","text":"The fact that the mother tongue can disappear at a similar ____ is less well understood.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"定位词： mother tongue, disappear, similar\n定位原文： G段，Many people marvel at how quickly bilingual children seem to ‘pick up’ conversational skills in the majority language at school (although it takes much longer for them to catch up with native speakers in academic language skills). However, educators are often much less aware of how quickly children can lose their ability to use their mother tongue, even in the home context.\n详细解析：G段指出许多人惊叹于双语儿童在学校里似乎能如此迅速地“掌握”主流语言的会话技能（尽管他们在学术语言技能方面赶上母语者需要更长时间）。然而，教育者往往不太意识到，孩子们在家庭环境中也能很快失去使用母语的能力。这表明孩子学习主流语言和失去使用母语的能力的速度都非常快。","options":["teachers","school","dislocation","rate","time","family","communication","type","ability","area"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"56656","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 31 - 35\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"7435:56656:33","type":"choice","text":"This phenomenon depends to a certain extent on the proportion of people with the same linguistic background that have settled in a particular ____ .","answer":"J","acceptedAnswers":["J"],"explanation":"定位词： the same linguistic background\n定位原文： G段，The extent and rapidity of language loss will vary according to the concentration of families from a particular linguistic group in the neighborhood.\n详细解析：G段指出语言丧失的程度和速度会根据特定语言群体在某个社区的家庭集中程度而有所不同。\n同义替换：proportion of people = concentration of families","options":["teachers","school","dislocation","rate","time","family","communication","type","ability","area"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"56656","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 31 - 35\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"7435:56656:34","type":"choice","text":"If this is limited, children are likely to lose the active use of their mother tongue, and thus no longer employ it even with ____ although they may still understand it.","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"定位词： lose, active use, mother tongue\n定位原文： G段，However, where language communities are not concentrated in particular neighborhoods, children can lose their ability to communicate in their mother tongue within two to three years of starting school.\n详细解析：G段指出如果某个语言群体的家庭在特定社区中并不集中，那么孩子们可能会在开始上学后的两到三年内，失去使用母语的能力。","options":["teachers","school","dislocation","rate","time","family","communication","type","ability","area"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"56656","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 31 - 35\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"7435:56656:35","type":"choice","text":"It follows that teenage children in these circumstances experience a sense of ____ in relation to all aspects of their lives.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位词： teenage children, sense\n定位原文： G段，Pupils frequently become alienated from the cultures of both home and school, with predictable results.\n详细解析：G段指出，学生常常与家庭和学校的文化产生疏离感，dislocation表示文化上的割裂或疏远。","options":["teachers","school","dislocation","rate","time","family","communication","type","ability","area"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"56656","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 31 - 35\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"7435:56657:36","type":"choice","text":"Less than half the children who attend kindergarten in Toronto have English as their mother tongue.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"定位词： kindergarten in Toronto\n定位原文： A段，In the city of Toronto in Canada, 58% of kindergarten pupils come from homes where English is not the language of communication.\n详细解析：A段指出，58%的幼儿园学生来自非英语家庭，意味着有超过一半的孩子的母语并非英语。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56657","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"7435:56658:37","type":"choice","text":"Research proves that learning the host country language at school can have an adverse effect on a child's mother tongue.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"定位词： research,  host country language\n定位原文： E段，One of the most strongly established findings of educational research, however, is that well-implemented bilingual programs can promote literacy and subject-matter knowledge in a minority language without any negative effects on children's development in the majority language.\n详细解析：E段指出，研究表明良好设计实施的双语教育项目可以提升非主流语言的能力，也就是题目中孩子母语的额能力。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56658","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"7435:56659:38","type":"choice","text":"The Foyer programme is to be adopted by the French education system.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"定位词： Foyer program, Belgium, Dutch and French\n定位原文： E段，Within Europe, the Foyer program in Belgium, which develops children's speaking and literacy abilities in three languages (their mother tongue, Dutch and French), most clearly illustrates the benefits of bilingual and trilingual education (see Cummins, 2000).\n详细解析：E段指出Foyer项目旨在提升学生在母语，荷兰语和法语三种语言上的能力。该项目已经在比利时实施并展示了双语和三语教育的优势。而题目中的French education system（法国教育系统）并未提及。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56659","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"7435:56660:39","type":"choice","text":"Bilingual children are taught to tell the time earlier than monolingual children.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"定位词： tell the time, bilingual children, monolingual children\n定位原文： F段，Pupils who know how to tell the time in their mother tongue understand the concept of telling time.\n详细解析：F段指出，掌握时间的概念对于双语儿童来说是一个普遍技能，但文中并未比较双语儿童和单语儿童在学习这一技能的时间差，因此无法判断是否更早学会。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56660","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"7435:56661:40","type":"choice","text":"Bilingual children can eventually apply reading comprehension strategies acquired in one language when reading in the other.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"定位词：Bilingual children, reading comprehension strategies\n定位原文： F段，Similarly, at more advanced stages, there is transfer across languages in other skills, such as knowing how to distinguish the main idea from the supporting details of a written passage or story, and distinguishing fact from opinion.\n详细解析：F段指出，双语儿童可以将他们在母语学习中学到的理解策略应用到另一种语言的学习中，包括区分论点和论据以及事实和观点的能力。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56661","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"56652","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 30\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>What point is the writer making in the second paragraph?</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"56653","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 30\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>Why does the writer refer to something that Goethe said?&nbsp;</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"56654","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 30\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>The writer believes that when young children have a firm grasp of their mother tongue</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"56655","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 30\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>Why are some people suspicious about mother tongue-based teaching programmes?</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"56656","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 31 - 35\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"56657","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Less than half the children who attend kindergarten in Toronto have English as their mother tongue.</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"56658","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Research proves that learning the host country language at school can have an adverse effect on a child&#39;s mother tongue.</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"56659","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>The Foyer programme is to be adopted by the French education system.</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"56660","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Bilingual children are taught to tell the time earlier than monolingual children.</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"56661","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Bilingual children can eventually apply reading comprehension strategies acquired in one language when reading in the other.</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>The significant role of mother tongue language in education</strong><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">One consequence of population mobility is an increasing diversity within schools. To illustrate, in the city of Toronto in Canada, 58% of kindergarten pupils come from homes where English is not the language of communication. Schools in Europe and North America have experienced this diversity for years, but educational policies and practices vary widely between countries and even within countries. Some political parties and groups search for ways to ‘solve the problem’ of diverse communities and their integration in schools and society. They see few positive consequences for the host society and worry that diversity threatens the identity of the host society. Consequently, they promote unfortunate educational policies that will make the&nbsp;‘problem’ disappear. If students retain their culture and language, they are viewed as less capable of identifying with the mainstream culture and learning the mainstream language of the society.</p><p><br style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap\"/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The challenge for educators and policy-makers is to shape the evolution of national identity in such a way that the rights of all citizens (including school children) are respected, and the cultural, linguistic and economic resources of the nation are maximized. To waste the resources of the nation by discouraging children from developing their mother tongues is quite simply unintelligent from the point of view of national self-interest. A first step in providing an appropriate education for culturally and linguistically diverse children is to examine what the existing research says about the role of children&#39;s mother tongues in their educational development.</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><br/></span></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">In fact, the research is very clear. When children continue to develop their abilities in two or more languages throughout primary school, they gain a deeper understanding of language and how to use it effectively. They have more practice in processing language, especially when they develop literacy in both. More than 150 research studies conducted during the past 35 years strongly support what Goethe, the famous eighteenth-century German philosopher, once said: that the person who knows only one language does not truly know that language. Research suggests that bilingual children may also develop more flexibility in their thinking as a result of processing information through two different languages.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Children who come to school with a solid foundation in their mother tongue develop stronger literacy abilities in the school language. When parents and other caregivers (e.g.&nbsp;grandparents) are able to spend time with their children and tell stories or discuss issues with them in a way that develops their mother tongue, children come to school well-prepared to learn the school language and succeed educationally. Children&#39;s knowledge and skills transfer across languages from the mother tongue to the school language. Transfer across languages can be two-way: both languages nurture each other when the educational environment permits children access to both languages.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Some educators and parents are suspicious of mother tongue-based teaching programs because they worry that they take time away from the majority language. For example, in a bilingual program where 50% of the time is spent teaching through children&#39;s home language and 50% through the majority language, surely children won&#39;t progress as far in the latter? One of the most strongly established findings of educational research, however, is that well-implemented bilingual programs can promote literacy and subject-matter knowledge in a minority language without any negative effects on children&#39;s development in the majority language. Within Europe, the Foyer program in Belgium, which develops children&#39;s speaking and literacy abilities in three languages (their mother tongue, Dutch and French), most clearly illustrates the benefits of bilingual and trilingual education (see Cummins, 2000).</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">It is easy to understand how this happens. When children are learning through a minority language, they are learning concepts and intellectual skills too. Pupils who know how to tell the time in their mother tongue understand the concept of telling time. In order to tell time in the majority language they do not need to re-learn the concept. Similarly, at more advanced stages, there is transfer across languages in other skills, such as knowing how to distinguish the main idea from the supporting details of a written passage or story, and distinguishing fact from opinion. Studies of secondary school pupils are providing interesting findings in this area, and it would be worth extending this research.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Many people marvel at how quickly bilingual children seem to ‘pick up’ conversational skills in the majority language at school (although it takes much longer for them to catch up with native speakers in academic language skills). However, educators are often much less aware of how quickly children can lose their ability to use their mother tongue, even in the home context. The extent and rapidity of language loss will vary according to the concentration of families from a particular linguistic group in the neighborhood. Where the mother tongue is used extensively in the community, then language loss among young children will be less. However, where language communities are not concentrated in particular neighborhoods, children can lose their ability to communicate in their mother tongue within two to three years of starting school. They may retain receptive skills in the language but they will use the majority language in speaking with their peers and siblings and in responding to their parents. By the time children become adolescents, the linguistic division between parents and children has become an emotional chasm. Pupils frequently become alienated from the cultures of both home and school, with predictable results.</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7435&scene=%E8%AF%AD%E8%A8%80%E6%95%99%E8%82%B2&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7372","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Bovids","book":"阅读还原集Vol.10","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test4","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.10 · Test4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"7372:56601:1","type":"choice","text":"In which region is the biggest range of bovids to be found?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"定位词: region，biggest range of\n对应原文：B段，Bovids are well represented in most parts of Eurasia and Southeast Asian islands, but they are by far the most numerous and diverse in the latter.\n详细解析:B段指出，东南亚是牛科动物种类最多和最为多样的地区。虽然文章指出牛科动物在非洲也有分布，但并没有指出是最为多样或最为丰富的地区。欧亚大陆但并没有被描述为牛科动物最为多样的地区，并且北美的牛科动物种类并不是最多的。\n同义替换：biggest range of bovids = most numerous and diverse","options":["Africa","Eurasia","North America","South-east Asia"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56601","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 3\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"7372:56602:2","type":"choice","text":"Most bovids have a preference for living in","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"定位词: most bovids,preference\n对应原文:B段，Although bovids have adapted to a wide range of habitats, from arctic tundra to deep tropical forest, the majority of species favour open grassland, scrub or desert.\n详细解析:B段指出大多数牛科动物更偏好生活在“open grassland, scrub or desert”（开阔的草地、灌木丛或沙漠）。文章没有指出牛科动物偏好孤立的环境， 文章没有指出牛科动物偏好小群体，而是指出它们适应不同的栖息地。虽然有些牛科动物生活在热带森林，但文章指出大多数物种更喜欢开阔的空间。\n同义替换：preference for living in = favour，wide open spaces = open grassland, scrub or desert","options":["isolation","small groups","tropical forest","wide open spaces."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56602","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 3\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"7372:56603:3","type":"choice","text":"Which of the following features do all bovids have in common?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位词: all bovids, features...in common\n原文部分:C段，All species are ruminants, which means that they retain undigested food in their stomachs, and regurgitate it as necessary.\n详细解析:C段指出所有牛科动物都有共同的特点：它们是反刍动物，即它们将未消化的食物保留在胃中并根据需要重新吞咽。原文指出牛科动物的角从未脱落，大多数牛科动物没有上门牙，只有下门牙，并且牛科动物的蹄是分裂的（cloven hooves）。\n同义替换：store= retain","options":["Their horns are shot.","They have upper incisors.","They store food in the body.","Their hooves are undivided."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56603","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 3\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"7372:56604:4","type":"choice","text":"4 can endure very harsh environments","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位词: Caprinae\n对应原文：F段，Tolerance of extreme conditions is most marked in this group: Barbary and bighorn sheep have adapted to arid deserts, while Rocky Mountain sheep survive high up in mountains and musk oxen in arctic tundra.\n详细解析:F段指出，Caprinae亚科（包括羊和山羊）能够适应极端环境，如干旱的沙漠、高山和北极苔原。\n同义替换：endure=tolerance； harsh environments = extreme conditions","options":["Antelope","Bovinae","Caprinae","Cephalophinae"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56604","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 4 - 8\nChoose the correct sub-family (A - D) for each characteristic. You may choose any correct sub-family more than once.\nList of sub-families\nA Antelope\nB Bovinae\nC Caprinae\nD Cephalophinae"},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"7372:56604:5","type":"choice","text":"5 includes the ox and the cow","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"定位词: Bovinae\n对应原文：D段，The sub-family Bovinae comprises most of the larger bovids, including the African bongo, and nilgae, eland, bison and cattle.\n详细解析:D段指出，Bovinae亚科包括了较大的牛科物种，如黄牛和水牛（ox and cow）。\n同义替换：\nincludes = comprises","options":["Antelope","Bovinae","Caprinae","Cephalophinae"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56604","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 4 - 8\nChoose the correct sub-family (A - D) for each characteristic. You may choose any correct sub-family more than once.\nList of sub-families\nA Antelope\nB Bovinae\nC Caprinae\nD Cephalophinae"},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"7372:56604:6","type":"choice","text":"6 may supplement its diet with meat","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"定位词:Cephalophinae\n对应原文: G段，The duiker of Africa belongs to the Cephalophinae sub-family. It is generally small and solitary, often living in thick forest. Although mainly feeding on grass and leaves, some duikers – unlike most other bovids – are believed to eat insects and feed on dead animal carcasses, and even to kill small animals.\n详细解析: G段指出，duiker（杜鹃羚羊）除了吃草和叶子外，还可能会吃昆虫、尸体，甚至小型动物。\n同义替换：supplement its diet with= feed on； meat=animal carcasses","options":["Antelope","Bovinae","Caprinae","Cephalophinae"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56604","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 4 - 8\nChoose the correct sub-family (A - D) for each characteristic. You may choose any correct sub-family more than once.\nList of sub-families\nA Antelope\nB Bovinae\nC Caprinae\nD Cephalophinae"},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"7372:56604:7","type":"choice","text":"7 can usually move at speed","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"定位词: Antelope\n对应原文：E段，Antelopes are typically long-legged, fast-running species, often with long horns that may be laid along the back when the animal is in full flight.\n详细解析: E段指出，Antelope（羚羊）是典型的长腿快速奔跑物种，\n，牛类物种通常不以快速奔跑为特点。虽然一些山羊类物种较灵活，但不是特别擅长奔跑。叉角羚虽然奔跑速度较快，但主要指的是羚羊类物种。\n同义替换：move at speed = fast-running","options":["Antelope","Bovinae","Caprinae","Cephalophinae"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56604","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 4 - 8\nChoose the correct sub-family (A - D) for each characteristic. You may choose any correct sub-family more than once.\nList of sub-families\nA Antelope\nB Bovinae\nC Caprinae\nD Cephalophinae"},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"7372:56604:8","type":"choice","text":"8 does not defend a particular area of land","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"定位词: Bovinae\n对应原文:D段，The sub-family Bovinae comprises most of the larger bovids, including the African bongo, and nilgae, eland, bison and cattle. Unlike most other bovids they are all non-territorial.\n详细解析:D段指出，Bovinae亚科的物种（如黄牛和水牛）通常不防守领土。很多羚羊物种有领土意识，叉角羚有时也会防守领土。\n同义替换：does not defend a particular area = non-territorial","options":["Antelope","Bovinae","Caprinae","Cephalophinae"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56604","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 4 - 8\nChoose the correct sub-family (A - D) for each characteristic. You may choose any correct sub-family more than once.\nList of sub-families\nA Antelope\nB Bovinae\nC Caprinae\nD Cephalophinae"},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"7372:56605:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"the royal antelope/royal antelope","acceptedAnswers":["the royal antelope","royal antelope"],"explanation":"定位词: smallest species of Bovid\n对应原文:B段，This diversity of habitat is also matched by great diversity in size and form: at one extreme is the royal antelope of West Africa, which stands a mere 25 cm at the shoulder; at the other, the massively built bisons of North America and Europe, growing to a shoulder height of 2.2m.\n详细解析:B段指出，royal antelope（王羚）是最小的牛科物种，肩高仅为25厘米。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56605","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nAnswer the questions. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":3},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"7372:56606:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"the auroch/auroch","acceptedAnswers":["the auroch","auroch"],"explanation":"定位词: died out\n对应原文：D段，The ancestors of the various species of domestic cattle banteng, gaur, yak and water buffalo are generally rare and endangered in the wild, while the auroch (the ancestor of the domestic cattle of Europe) is extinct.\n详细解析:D段指出，auroch（野牛）已经灭绝，它是欧洲家牛的祖先。\n同义替换：died out = is extinct","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56606","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nAnswer the questions. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":3},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"7372:56607:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"long, splayed hooves/splayed hooves/hooves","acceptedAnswers":["long, splayed hooves","splayed hooves","hooves"],"explanation":"定位词: movement of the sitatunga over wetland\n对应原文:E段，Antelopes are mainly grassland species, but many have adapted to flooded grasslands: pukus, waterbucks and lechwes are all good at swimming, usually feeding in deepwater, while the sitatunga has long, splayed hooves that enable it to walk freely on swampy ground.\n详细解析:E段指出，sitatunga（西塔图甘羚）拥有长且宽的蹄子，可以帮助它在湿地上自由行走。\n同义替换：facilitates the movement = enable it to walk freely","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56607","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nAnswer the questions. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":3},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"7372:56608:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"arid deserts","acceptedAnswers":["arid deserts"],"explanation":"定位词: Barbary sheep live in\n对应原文：F段，Tolerance of extreme conditions is most marked in this group: Barbary and bighorn sheep have adapted to arid deserts, while Rocky Mountain sheep survive high up in mountains and musk oxen in arctic tundra.\n详细解析:F段指出，Barbary sheep（巴巴里羊）适应了沙漠环境。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56608","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nAnswer the questions. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":3},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"7372:56609:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"the pronghorn/pronghorn","acceptedAnswers":["the pronghorn","pronghorn"],"explanation":"定位词: only living member , Antilocapridae sub-family\n对应原文：H段，The pronghorn is the sole survivor of a New World sub-family of herbivorous ruminants, the Antilocapridae in North America.\n详细解析:H段指出，pronghorn（叉角羚）是Antilocapridae亚科的唯一幸存物种。\n同义替换：only living member = sole survivor","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56609","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nAnswer the questions. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":3}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"56601","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 3\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>In which region is the biggest range of bovids to be found?</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"56602","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 3\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>Most bovids have a preference for living in</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"56603","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 3\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>Which of the following features do all bovids have in common?</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"56604","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 4 - 8\nChoose the correct sub-family (A - D) for each characteristic. You may choose any correct sub-family more than once.\nList of sub-families\nA Antelope\nB Bovinae\nC Caprinae\nD Cephalophinae","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"56605","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nAnswer the questions. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p>What is the smallest species of Bovid called? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"56606","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nAnswer the questions. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p>Which species of Bovinae has now died out?<strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"56607","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nAnswer the questions. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p>What facilitates the movement of the sitatunga over wetland?<strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"56608","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nAnswer the questions. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p>What sort of terrain do barbary sheep live in?<strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"56609","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nAnswer the questions. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p>What is the only living member of the Antilocapridae sub-family?<strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"text-align: left; line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>Bovids</strong><o:p></o:p></p><p style=\"text-align: left; line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The family of mammals called bovids belongs to the Artiodactyl class, which also includes giraffes. Bovids are highly diverse group consisting of&nbsp;137 species, some of which are man&#39;s most important domestic animals.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Bovids are well represented in most parts of Eurasia and Southeast Asian islands, but they are by far the most numerous and diverse in the&nbsp;latter. Some species of bovid are solitary, but others live in large groups with complex social structures Although bovids have adapted to a wide range of habitats, from arctic&nbsp;tundra to deep tropical forest, the majority of species favour open grassland, scrub or desert.&nbsp;This diversity of habitat is also matched by&nbsp;great diversity in size and form: at one extreme is the royal antelope of West Africa, which stands a mere 25 cm at the shoulder; at the other, the massively built bisons of North America and Europe, growing to a shoulder height of 2.2m.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Despite differences in size and appearance, bovids are united by the possession of certain common features. All species are ruminants, which&nbsp;means that&nbsp;they retain undigested food in their stomachs, and regurgitate it as necessary.&nbsp;Bovids are almost exclusively&nbsp;herbivorous*.&nbsp;Typically their teeth are highly modified for browsing and grazing:&nbsp;grass or foliage is cropped with the upper lip and lower incisors**&nbsp;(the upper incisors are usually absent), and then ground down by the cheekteeth.&nbsp;As well as having cloven,&nbsp;or split,&nbsp;hooves,&nbsp;the males of all bovid species and the females of most carry horns.&nbsp;Bovid horns have bony cores covered in a sheath of horny material that is constantly renewed from within; they are unbranched and never shed.&nbsp;They vary in shape and size:&nbsp;the relatively simple horns of a large Indian buffalo may measure around 4m from tip to tip along the outer curve, while the various gazelles have horns with a variety of elegant curves.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Five groups, or sub-families, may be distinguished: Bovinae, Antelope, Caprinae, Cephalophinae and Antilocapridae.&nbsp;The sub-family Bovinae comprises most of the larger bovids, including the African bongo, and nilgae, eland, bison and cattle.&nbsp;Unlike most other bovids they are all non-territorial. The ancestors of the various species of domestic cattle&nbsp;banteng, gaur, yak and water buffalo are generally rare and endangered in the wild, while the auroch&nbsp;(the ancestor of the domestic cattle of Europe) is extinct.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The term &#39;antelope&#39; is not a very precise zoological name – it is used to loosely describe a number of bovids that have followed different lines of development. Antelopes are typically long-legged, fast-running species, often with long horns that may be laid along the back when the animal is in full flight. There are two main sub-groups of antelope: Hippotraginae, which includes the oryx and the addax, and Antilopinae, which generally contains slighter and more graceful animals such as gazelle and the springbok. Antelopes are mainly grassland species, but many have adapted to flooded grasslands: pukus, waterbucks and lechwes are all good&nbsp;at swimming, usually feeding in deepwater, while the sitatunga has long, splayed hooves that enable it to walk freely on swampy ground.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The sub-family Caprinae includes the sheep and the goat, together with various relatives such as the goral and the tahr. Most are woolly or have long hair. Several species, such as wild goats, chamois and ibex, are agile cliff-&nbsp;and mountain-dwellers. Tolerance of extreme conditions is most marked in this group: Barbary&nbsp;and bighorn sheep have adapted to&nbsp;arid deserts, while Rocky Mountain sheep survive high up in mountains and musk oxen in arctic tundra.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The duiker of Africa belongs to the Cephalophinae sub-family. It is generally small and solitary, often living in thick forest. Although mainly feeding on grass and leaves, some duikers – unlike most other bovids – are believed to eat insects and feed on dead animal carcasses, and even to kill small animals.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The pronghorn is the sole survivor of a New World sub-family of herbivorous ruminants, the Antilocapridae in North America. It is similar in appearance and habits to the Old World antelope. Although greatly reduced in numbers since the arrival of Europeans, and the subsequent enclosure of grasslands, the pronghorn is still found inconsiderable numbers throughout North America, from Washington State to Mexico. When alarmed by the approach of wolves or other predators, hairs on the pronghorn&#39;s rump stand erect, so showing and emphasising the white patch there. At this signal, the whole herd gallops off at speed of over 60 km per hour.<span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><br/></p><p>*herbivorous: plant-eating</p><p>**incisors: front teeth</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7372&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7373","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Intelligent behaviour in birds","book":"阅读还原集Vol.10","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test4","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.10 · Test4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"7373:56092:14","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"对应原文： A段，For centuries, many scholars maintained that humans were the only intelligent organism on Earth. Many traits were considered to be exclusively human examples of acumen-for example, language, tool use, deception, awareness of self and others. However, exciting new research on a number of animals, particularly birds, has called into question the uniqueness of these traits, forcing us to reconsider this opinion.\n详细解析：A段指出传统观点认为只有人类具有智慧，例如语言、工具使用、欺骗和自我意识等，但新的研究发现这些特征在鸟类等动物中也存在。这个发现让我们开始重新审视这些传统观念。A段的主旨句是 \"However, exciting new research on a number of animals, particularly birds, has called into question the uniqueness of these traits, forcing us to reconsider this opinion.\"\n同义替换：reviewing= reconsider；long-held= maintained for centuries","options":["The theory linking capacity for tool use in birds and survival","The influence of humans on tool use","The theory linking cognitive ability and living in a society","Reviewing long-held beliefs","Intelligence helps birds to remember","How some birds trick each other","Physiological evidence of birds' intelligence","Several examples of birds who use tools","One species' multiple tool-using techniques"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56092","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 20\nThe text has seven paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"7373:56092:15","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"对应原文： B段，Since then, the catalogue of tool-using animals has grown. At least three Australian bird species make tools similar to those of the woodpecker finch, and when white-winged choughs come across shellfish they have been known to use rocks as hammers to crack open the recalcitrant shells. Other birds show a more sophisticated level of insight. For example, black kites have been reported dropping bait into lakes to bring fish to the surface of the water, thereby making them easier to catch.\n详细解析：  B段指出多种鸟类的工具使用例子，包括澳大利亚的白翅噪鸦和黑鸢等。这些鸟类的行为展示了鸟类在觅食过程中使用工具的不同方法。B段的主旨句是 \"Since then, the catalogue of tool-using animals has grown.\"\n同义替换：birds who use tools = tool-using animals； several = catalogue of","options":["The theory linking capacity for tool use in birds and survival","The influence of humans on tool use","The theory linking cognitive ability and living in a society","Reviewing long-held beliefs","Intelligence helps birds to remember","How some birds trick each other","Physiological evidence of birds' intelligence","Several examples of birds who use tools","One species' multiple tool-using techniques"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56092","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 20\nThe text has seven paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"7373:56092:16","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"对应原文： C段，Most tool-using behaviours are a means of extracting food, which may provide a clue as to how the mental abilities needed for tool use evolved.\nEssentially, brain tissue is energetically expensive, so animals should have evolved only the necessary intellectual capabilities required to overcome the challenges they face in their environment.\n详细解析： C段指出了鸟类的工具使用行为如何随着环境需求而进化，这种智力能力的进化是为了帮助它们在食物获取方面克服生存挑战。C段的主旨句是 \"Most tool-using behaviours are a means of extracting food, which may provide a clue as to how the mental abilities needed for tool use evolved.\"\n同义替换：capacity= mental abilities；survival = overcoming environmental challenges","options":["The theory linking capacity for tool use in birds and survival","The influence of humans on tool use","The theory linking cognitive ability and living in a society","Reviewing long-held beliefs","Intelligence helps birds to remember","How some birds trick each other","Physiological evidence of birds' intelligence","Several examples of birds who use tools","One species' multiple tool-using techniques"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56092","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 20\nThe text has seven paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"7373:56092:17","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"对应原文： D段，New Caledonian crows boast many different tools in their tool kit.\nEach tool is used in slightly different ways to pull grubs from deep within tree trunks.\n详细解析： D段指出了新喀里多尼亚乌鸦能够使用多种工具，包括钩子、耙子等，并且在觅食过程中根据不同情况使用不同的工具。这表明它们在使用工具方面具有多样化的技巧。D段的主旨句是 \"New Caledonian crows boast many different tools in their tool kit.\"","options":["The theory linking capacity for tool use in birds and survival","The influence of humans on tool use","The theory linking cognitive ability and living in a society","Reviewing long-held beliefs","Intelligence helps birds to remember","How some birds trick each other","Physiological evidence of birds' intelligence","Several examples of birds who use tools","One species' multiple tool-using techniques"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56092","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 20\nThe text has seven paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"7373:56092:18","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"对应原文： E段，The team uncovered a clear relationship: birds with relatively large forebrains are able to invent fresh solutions to ecological challenges, and to exploit the discoveries and inventions of others, more often than birds with relatively small forebrains.\n详细解析：E段指出鸟类的前脑较大与解决生态挑战的创新能力之间的关系。这是鸟类智力的生理学证据。E段的主旨句是 \"The team uncovered a clear relationship: birds with relatively large forebrains are able to invent fresh solutions to ecological challenges, and to exploit the discoveries and inventions of others, more often than birds with relatively small forebrains.\"\n同义替换：large forebrains=physiological evidence","options":["The theory linking capacity for tool use in birds and survival","The influence of humans on tool use","The theory linking cognitive ability and living in a society","Reviewing long-held beliefs","Intelligence helps birds to remember","How some birds trick each other","Physiological evidence of birds' intelligence","Several examples of birds who use tools","One species' multiple tool-using techniques"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56092","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 20\nThe text has seven paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"7373:56092:19","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph F","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"对应原文： F段，Intelligence in birds may also arise as a result of selection to overcome the dynamic challenges of communal living. Since this involves competition between group members, to be successful, a social animal may need to be able to reflect on its own intentions, as well as those of others.\n详细解析：F段指出群居生活带来的挑战，认为这种环境可能导致鸟类智力的进化，特别是需要理解自己和他人的意图。 F段的主旨句是 \"Intelligence in birds may also arise as a result of selection to overcome the dynamic challenges of communal living.\"\n同义替换：communal living=living in a society; cognitive ability=reflect on intentions","options":["The theory linking capacity for tool use in birds and survival","The influence of humans on tool use","The theory linking cognitive ability and living in a society","Reviewing long-held beliefs","Intelligence helps birds to remember","How some birds trick each other","Physiological evidence of birds' intelligence","Several examples of birds who use tools","One species' multiple tool-using techniques"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56092","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 20\nThe text has seven paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"7373:56092:20","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph G","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"对应原文： G段，Perhaps the best example of deception among birds comes from the white-winged choughs.\nHowever, because young choughs have so little enthusiasm for foraging, or gathering food, they are often too hungry to help. And because it is socially unacceptable to be part of a group and provide little help, young choughs often act deceptively.\n详细解析： G段指出了white-winged choughs的幼鸟如何欺骗成鸟，以此展示鸟类之间的欺骗行为。G段的主旨句是 \"Perhaps the best example of deception among birds comes from the white-winged choughs.\"\n同义替换：trick=deception","options":["The theory linking capacity for tool use in birds and survival","The influence of humans on tool use","The theory linking cognitive ability and living in a society","Reviewing long-held beliefs","Intelligence helps birds to remember","How some birds trick each other","Physiological evidence of birds' intelligence","Several examples of birds who use tools","One species' multiple tool-using techniques"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56092","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 20\nThe text has seven paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"7373:56093:21","type":"fill","text":"21 keeping tools that they like to use","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位信息： New Caledonian crows\n对应原文： D段，The crows carry their favourite tool from one foraging site to the next. They also store their tools for later re-use in a secure place on their perch.\n解题思路： D段指出New Caledonian crows 会随身携带自己喜欢的工具，并将其存储在安全的地方以便以后使用。这表明它们具有保留工具的行为。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56093","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21 - 26\nChoose the correct bird, (A - C), for each characteristic. You may choose any correct bird more than once.\nList of Birds\nA\twhite-winged choughs\nB\tblack kites\nC\tNew Caledonian crows"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"7373:56093:22","type":"fill","text":"22 drawing out their prey by frightening it","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"定位信息： black kites\n对应原文： B段，For example, black kites have been reported dropping bait into lakes to bring fish to the surface of the water, thereby making them easier to catch. A kite may also pick up a smouldering stick from an area recently burned by a bushfire and drop the stick on a patch of unburned grass. The bird then feasts on the small animals that flee from the subsequent fire.\n解题思路： B段指出了black kites 利用火将小动物吓跑后捕食这些逃跑的动物。这展示了黑鸢通过惊吓猎物将其引出从而捕食的行为。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56093","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21 - 26\nChoose the correct bird, (A - C), for each characteristic. You may choose any correct bird more than once.\nList of Birds\nA\twhite-winged choughs\nB\tblack kites\nC\tNew Caledonian crows"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"7373:56093:23","type":"fill","text":"23 the use of tools to remove the outer covering from food","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"定位信息： white-winged choughs\n对应原文：B段，At least three Australian bird species make tools similar to those of the woodpecker finch, and when white-winged choughs come across shellfish they have been known to use rocks as hammers to crack open the recalcitrant shells.\n解题思路： B段指出 white-winged choughs 使用石块作为工具来敲碎贝壳的外壳，以便取出里面的食物。此行为符合使用工具来去除食物外壳的描述。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56093","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21 - 26\nChoose the correct bird, (A - C), for each characteristic. You may choose any correct bird more than once.\nList of Birds\nA\twhite-winged choughs\nB\tblack kites\nC\tNew Caledonian crows"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"7373:56093:24","type":"fill","text":"24 using food to attract their prey","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"定位信息： using food,attract prey\n对应原文：B段，For example, black kites have been reported dropping bait into lakes to bring fish to the surface of the water.\n解题思路： B段指出 black kites 通过将诱饵投入湖中来吸引鱼到水面，从而更容易捕食。这符合“使用食物来吸引猎物”的描述。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56093","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21 - 26\nChoose the correct bird, (A - C), for each characteristic. You may choose any correct bird more than once.\nList of Birds\nA\twhite-winged choughs\nB\tblack kites\nC\tNew Caledonian crows"},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"7373:56093:25","type":"fill","text":"25 the use of unfamiliar materials to make tools","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位信息： unfamiliar materials,make tools\n对应原文：D段，New Caledonian crows were observed moulding a piece of wire, something they had never seen before, into a hook and then using it to retrieve food.\n解题思路： D段指出了 New Caledonian crows 将一根它们从未见过的金属丝弯曲成钩子来取食。这符合使用不熟悉的材料来制作工具的描述。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56093","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21 - 26\nChoose the correct bird, (A - C), for each characteristic. You may choose any correct bird more than once.\nList of Birds\nA\twhite-winged choughs\nB\tblack kites\nC\tNew Caledonian crows"},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"7373:56093:26","type":"fill","text":"26 engaging in certain activities for the benefit of observers","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"定位信息： engaging in activities,for the benefit of observers\n对应原文： G段，Interestingly, it is more likely to preen the chicks if another bird can see it do so.\n解题思路： G段指出 white-winged choughs 在有其他鸟类观察时更可能会清理雏鸟的羽毛，以此显示其社会地位。此行为表明它们在特定的活动中表现出一种“表演”性质，以获得观察者的认可。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56093","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21 - 26\nChoose the correct bird, (A - C), for each characteristic. You may choose any correct bird more than once.\nList of Birds\nA\twhite-winged choughs\nB\tblack kites\nC\tNew Caledonian crows"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"56092","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 20\nThe text has seven paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"56093","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 21 - 26\nChoose the correct bird, (A - C), for each characteristic. You may choose any correct bird more than once.\nList of Birds\nA\twhite-winged choughs\nB\tblack kites\nC\tNew Caledonian crows","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":21}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>Intelligent behaviour in birds</strong><o:p></o:p></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><em>Many people are aware of the intelligence of chimpanzees and other mammals. However, birds also demonstrate intelligent behaviour</em><o:p></o:p></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><em><br/></em></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">#&amp;</span><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">For centuries, many scholars maintained that humans were the only intelligent organism on Earth. Many traits were considered to be exclusively human examples of acumen<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;–&nbsp;</span>for example, language, tool use, deception, awareness of self and others. However, exciting new research on a number of animals, particularly birds, has called into question the uniqueness of these traits, forcing us to reconsider this opinion. In 1964, people were amazed when naturalist Jane Goodalltzx first discovered chimpanzees making&nbsp;and using tools. But ornithologists, people who study birds. were not overly surprised. Almost 20 years earlier, a renowned ornithologist had shown that tool use was commonplace in populations of woodpecker finches residing on the Galápagos Islands. These tiny birds routinely used twigs to extract grubs from under bark.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">#&amp;</span><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Since then, the catalogue of tool-using animals has grown. At least three Australian bird species make tools similar to those of the woodpecker finch, and when white-winged choughs come across shellfish they have been known to use rocks as hammers to crack open the recalcitrant shells. Other birds show a more sophisticated level of insight. For example, black kites have been reported dropping bait into lakes to bring fish to the surface of the water, thereby making them easier to catch. A kite may also pick up a smouldering stick from an area recently burned by a bushfire and drop the stick on a patch of unburned grass. The bird then feasts on the small animals that flee from the subsequent fire.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">#&amp;</span><strong>C</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Most tool-using behaviours are a means of extracting food, which may provide a clue as to how the mental abilities needed for tool use evolved. The predominant explanation is based on the proverb that &#39;necessity is the mother of invention&#39;. Essentially, brain tissue is energetically expensive, so animals should have evolved only the necessary intellectual capabilities required to overcome the challenges they face in their environment. Consider a hypothetical duck grazing on a seemingly endless supply of grass. Being particularly intelligent will not help the duck eat more grass. In contrast, other species, such as birds of prey, live in a more challenging environment, where food may be distributed erratically, hidden from view or highly mobile. The food itself may be quite intelligent. So, if there are not enough resources to feed all individuals, then only the smartest in each generation will live and reproduce.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">New Caledonian crows boast many different tools in their tool kit. They use a hooked tool made by removing all but one of the side branches from a twig. They fashion serrated rakes (using their beaks as scissors) from stiff, leathery pandanus leaves. They also make probes by modifying their own moulted feathers. Each tool is used in slightly different ways to pull grubs from deep within tree trunks. The crows carry their favourite tool from one foraging site to the next. They also store their tools for later re-use in a secure place on their perch. Problem-solving abilities have traditionally been thought to be beyond the reach of animals. Nevertheless, birds are coming up with innovative solutions all the time. Recently, New Caledonian crows were observed moulding a piece of wire, something they had never seen before, into a hook and then using it to retrieve food.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Literally hundreds of such reports have accumulated in back copies of scientific journals. Recently, a team of biologists from McGill University in Canada collated them and compared the frequency and size of innovations with the size of the birds&#39; forebrain (the brain area responsible for higher-order information processing) relative to the hindbrain. The team uncovered a clear relationship: birds with relatively large forebrains are able to invent fresh solutions to ecological challenges, and to exploit the discoveries and inventions of others, more often than birds with relatively small forebrains.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Intelligence in birds may also arise as a result of selection to overcome the dynamic challenges of communal living. Since this involves competition between group members, to be successful, a social animal may need to be able to reflect on its own intentions, as well as those of others. The consequence of being part of a community may be the evolution of a distinctly &#39;political&#39; brain.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">What better way to exercise a political brain than to be deceitful! Perhaps the best example of deception among birds comes from the white-winged choughs. Choughs are cooperative breeders&nbsp;–&nbsp;that is, they form a communal group consisting of one breeding-pair and up to 15 non-breeding &#39;helpers&#39;. However, because young choughs have so little enthusiasm for foraging, or gathering food, they are often too hungry to help. And because it is socially unacceptable to be part of a group and provide little help, young choughs often act deceptively. For example, when an adult is watching, a young chough will place some food in the mouth of a hungry chick&nbsp;–&nbsp;but it does not release the food. Instead, it waits until the adult departs and then eats it. A chough can also help the group by preening* the chicks. Interestingly, it is more likely to preen the chicks if another bird can see it do so. A chough that has been sitting totally still on the nest while the rest of the group is foraging out of sight will comically spring up and frantically start to preen the chicks as soon as some of its group members come into view. It is likely that these young choughs are only motivated to help when others are watching because they are concerned about their social status. Choughs need other choughs to like them, as they cannot breed without them.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br/></span></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"></span></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">* preening: cleaning and arranging feathers on birds</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7373&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7415","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 The fluoridation controversy","book":"阅读还原集Vol.10","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test4","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.10 · Test4 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"7415:56521:27","type":"choice","text":"The optimum amount of fluorine in fluoridated water is calculated partly according to","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"定位词：optimum amount,calculated\n原文：\nA段，The fluorine, when mixed with water, becomes fluoride and the desired concentration of fluoride in public water is approximately one part per million, depending on the regional temperature and hence the amount of water people are likely to drink.\n详细解析：\nA段指出，氟化水中最佳氟浓度约为每百万分之一，这取决于地区的温度（regional temperature）以及人们可能饮用的水量（amount of water people are likely to drink）。这说明温度对氟浓度的计算有重要影响。\n同义替换：\noptimum amount = desired concentration\nhow hot the area is = regional temperature","options":["how hot the area is.","how warm the water is.","how many dental problems there are in the community.","how much fluorine the community chooses to have in its water."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56521","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"7415:56522:28","type":"choice","text":"One reason given by the writer for opposing fluoridation is that","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位词：opposing fluoridation\n原文：\nB段，Third, fluoridation is thought to be an infringement on individual rights because it is compulsory medication of all members of a community.\n详细解析：\nB段指出反对氟化的第三个原因是，氟化被认为是对个人权利的侵犯（infringement on individual rights），因为它是对整个社区的强制性药物干预（compulsory medication）。\n同义替换：\nobligatory = compulsory\ntakes away personal freedom = infringement on individual rights","options":["it may contribute to tooth decay","it will be unacceptably expensive for the public.","obligatory fluoridation takes away personal freedom.","excessive fluoride could be added to the water by mistake."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56522","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"7415:56523:29","type":"choice","text":"The writer mentions Kuhn in order to","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"定位词：Kuhn\n原文：\nE段，According to Kuhn, the shift from one scientific way of thinking to another is not made solely on the basis of clear rules of formal scientific practice, but can include social factors, though Kuhn has never developed a full analysis of what these might be.\n详细解析：\nE段指出 Kuhn 的观点，科学范式的转变不仅仅基于正式科学实践的明确规则，还可能受到社会因素（social factors）的影响。这表明科学可能会受到非科学因素的影响\n同义替换：\ninfluenced by non-scientific considerations = include social factors","options":["provide a contrast with the view of Collins.","support the rational nature of scientific inquiry.","demonstrate that Kuhn did not argue his case adequately.","show that science can be influenced by non-scientific considerations"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56523","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"7415:56524:30","type":"choice","text":"What did Sutton's research discover about earlier studies in North America?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"定位词：earlier studies in North America\n原文：\nG段，An example is the study by Sutton in 1960, which analyzed the classic North American studies of the effect of fluoridation on tooth decay, and found that each showed significant methodological shortcomings.\n详细解析：\nG段指出 Sutton 对北美早期研究的分析，发现这些研究存在显著的方法学缺陷（significant methodological shortcomings）。\n同义替换：\nfailings = shortcomings\nthe way they were carried out = methodological","options":["There were failings in the way they were carried out.","The scientists involved had achieved unique results.","Proponents of fluoridation had not understood its long-term effects.","Fluoridation had a greater effect on tooth decay than previously believed."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56524","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"7415:56525:31","type":"choice","text":"In the last paragraph, what does the writer say about scientists?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"定位词：In the last paragraph\n原文：\nI段，Second, social values are likely to be bound up in any decision about fluoridation, so this is not an issue on which declarations by scientific experts ought to be considered the final word.\n详细解析：\nI段指出，由于社会价值在任何与氟化有关的决策中都起着重要作用，因此科学专家的声明不应被视为最终决策（not ... the final word）。这表明科学家不应该决定氟化政策。\n同义替换：\nshould not decide = not ... the final word\nfluoridation policy = decision about fluoridation","options":["They should reveal their true motivations.","They should not decide the fluoridation policy.","They are solely concerned with scientific truths.","They cannot reach agreement on the fluoridation issue."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56525","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"7415:56526:32","type":"choice","text":"Scientific knowledge should be kept separate from social values.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"定位词：kept separate from\n原文：\nF段，Because social processes are involved at all stages of the creation, evaluation, and establishing of scientific knowledge, social values may also be involved.\n详细解析：\nF段指出，社会过程在科学知识的创建、评估和建立的各个阶段都发挥作用，因此社会价值（social values）可能也会涉及其中。这表明科学知识无法与社会价值分离。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56526","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"7415:56527:33","type":"choice","text":"Many sociologists have disregarded the doubts that some scientists have concerning fluoridation.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"定位词：Many sociologists,disregarded the doubts\n原文：\nG段，Sutton's detailed study throws doubt as to the extent of reductions in tooth decay from fluoridation. Yet Sutton's book is not cited in a single analysis of the fluoridation issue by any sociologist.\n详细解析：\nG段指出，Sutton 的研究对氟化的效果提出了质疑，但他的研究没有被任何社会学家在氟化问题的分析中引用。这表明许多社会学家忽视了科学家对氟化的疑虑。\n同义替换：\ndisregarded = not cited\ndoubts = throws doubt","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56527","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"7415:56528:34","type":"choice","text":"Sutton's findings have been given insufficient attention by scientists outside of North America.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"定位词：Sutton's findings，North America.\n原文：\nG段，Sutton's detailed study throws doubt as to the extent of reductions in tooth decay from fluoridation.\n详细解析：\nG段指出 Sutton 的研究质疑了北美研究的效果，但未提及 Sutton 的研究是否受到了北美以外科学家的关注或忽视。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56528","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"7415:56529:35","type":"choice","text":"There are valid arguments on both sides of the fluoridation debate.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"定位词：valid arguments,both sides of\n原文：\nH段，Both arguments consider the scientific evidence concerning fluoridation, but differ in their assessments of the social benefits and costs. This difference is not between rationality and irrationality but is a legitimate difference in values, for example, the positive value placed on good teeth, the negative value placed on possible health risks, and the social benefits or costs of compulsory or voluntary intake of fluorides.\n详细解析：\nH段指出，支持和反对氟化的双方都基于科学证据，但在社会效益和成本的评估上存在差异。作者认为这是基于价值观的合法差异（legitimate difference in values），表明双方的观点都有效。\n同义替换：\nvalid arguments = legitimate difference in values\nboth sides = both arguments","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56529","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"7415:56530:36","type":"choice","text":"The traditional view of science is that ____","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"定位词：traditional view\n原文：\nD段，The traditional view is that science is a special kind of knowledge, which is established through scientific methods and objectively applied by members of a scientific community.\n详细解析：\nD段指出，传统的科学观认为科学知识是通过客观的科学方法建立的，科学是客观的、不受偏见影响的。","options":["the results of scientific research are not always understood at first.","science is an unbiased discipline.","people should be able to choose whether they want fluoride.","there is insufficient proof to support a cautious approach.","the serious damage fluoride causes far outweighs any positive effects.","children are not the only ones who benefit from fluoridation.","scientific knowledge is affected by the beliefs of everyone concerned."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"56530","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"7415:56530:37","type":"choice","text":"A sociological view of science argues that ____","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"定位词：sociological view\n原文：\nD段，However, in recent years there has been a major challenge to this picture by a sociology of science that shows how scientific knowledge is socially negotiated, and inevitably linked to the values of the relevant parties, both scientists and nonscientists.\n详细解析：\nD段指出社会学的科学观认为，科学知识不仅仅是客观事实，而是受到科学家和非科学家信仰的影响。\n同义替换：affected by beliefs = socially negotiated and inevitably linked to the values","options":["the results of scientific research are not always understood at first.","science is an unbiased discipline.","people should be able to choose whether they want fluoride.","there is insufficient proof to support a cautious approach.","the serious damage fluoride causes far outweighs any positive effects.","children are not the only ones who benefit from fluoridation.","scientific knowledge is affected by the beliefs of everyone concerned."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"56530","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"7415:56530:38","type":"choice","text":"Collins is of the opinion that ____","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"定位词：Collins\n原文：\nE段，Collins (1975) took this concept further when he asserted that the outcome of experiments was not something whose meaning could be immediately comprehended, but rather something for interpretation, discussion between scientists, and reinterpretation in the light of other experiments.\n详细解析：\nE段指出，Collins 认为科学实验结果需要反复讨论和诠释，不能立即被完全理解。","options":["the results of scientific research are not always understood at first.","science is an unbiased discipline.","people should be able to choose whether they want fluoride.","there is insufficient proof to support a cautious approach.","the serious damage fluoride causes far outweighs any positive effects.","children are not the only ones who benefit from fluoridation.","scientific knowledge is affected by the beliefs of everyone concerned."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"56530","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"7415:56530:39","type":"choice","text":"The writer suggests that a supporter of fluoridation may conclude that ____","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"定位词：supporter of fluoridation\n原文：\nG段，A supporter of fluoridation might argue, 'The evidence for the benefits of fluoridation is quite substantial, while the evidence for harm is limited and dubious. I think the likely benefits outweigh the possible dangers; hence I support fluoridation because it is the cheapest and easiest way to make sure every child reaps the benefits.'\n详细解析：\nG段指出，支持者认为关于氟化的益处的证据是非常充分的，而关于危害的证据有限且值得怀疑。原文evidence for harm is limited and dubious对应选项中的insufficient proof to support a cautious approach。氟化可能的益处超过了可能的危险；因此，他们支持氟化，因为这是确保每个孩子获得益处最便宜和最简单的方法。","options":["the results of scientific research are not always understood at first.","science is an unbiased discipline.","people should be able to choose whether they want fluoride.","there is insufficient proof to support a cautious approach.","the serious damage fluoride causes far outweighs any positive effects.","children are not the only ones who benefit from fluoridation.","scientific knowledge is affected by the beliefs of everyone concerned."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"56530","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"7415:56530:40","type":"choice","text":"The writer suggests that an opponent of fluoridation may conclude that ____","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位词：an opponent of fluoridation\n原文：\nG段，Therefore, I oppose fluoridation of water supplies and favor the voluntary use of fluoride tablets by those who want to take them.\n详细解析：\nG段指出，反对者认为，应该让人们自主选择是否使用氟化物，而不是通过公共水供应强制使用。","options":["the results of scientific research are not always understood at first.","science is an unbiased discipline.","people should be able to choose whether they want fluoride.","there is insufficient proof to support a cautious approach.","the serious damage fluoride causes far outweighs any positive effects.","children are not the only ones who benefit from fluoridation.","scientific knowledge is affected by the beliefs of everyone concerned."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"56530","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"56521","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>The optimum amount of fluorine in fluoridated water is calculated partly according to</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"56522","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>One reason given by the writer for opposing fluoridation is that</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"56523","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>The writer mentions Kuhn in order to</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"56524","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>What did Sutton&#39;s research discover about earlier studies in North America?</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"56525","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>&nbsp;In the last paragraph, what does the writer say about scientists?</strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"56526","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Scientific knowledge should be kept separate from social values.</strong></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"56527","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Many sociologists have disregarded the doubts that some scientists have concerning fluoridation.</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"56528","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Sutton&#39;s findings have been given insufficient attention by scientists outside of North America.&nbsp;</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"56529","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>There are valid arguments on both sides of the fluoridation debate.</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"56530","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":36}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>The fluoridation controversy</strong></p><p><em><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">The long-standing debate about whether to fluoridate our drinking water continues</span></em></p><p><em><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><br/></span></em></p><p><em><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><br/></span></em></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Fluoridation is the addition of fluorine to public water supplies with the aim of reducing tooth decay. The fluorine, when mixed with water, becomes fluoride and the desired concentration of fluoride in public water is approximately one part per million, depending on the regional temperature and hence the amount of water people are likely to drink. Many studies, such as those by McClure in 1970 through to Burtzx in 1983, have shown that when children drink fluoridated water, their average rate of tooth decay seems greatly reduced. A typical figure claimed is 50 percent reduction. This apparently enormous benefit for children&#39;s teeth is the major argument in favor of fluoridation.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Three main grounds for opposition to fluoridation have been expressed. First, opponents claim the benefits are exaggerated or not established. Second, there are claims of health risks to parts of the population, for example, allergic reactions. It is also accepted that high levels of fluoride can cause discoloration of otherwise healthy teeth. Proponents do not consider this to be a problem in such small concentrations, whereas opponents disagree – especially because some people drink more water and obtain much more than the standard 1 milligram of fluoride per day. Third, fluoridation is thought to be an infringement on individual rights because it is compulsory medication of all members of a community.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">An understanding of the fluoridation issue has important implications. If, according to the experts, fluoridation is unquestionably a beneficial and non-hazardous measure, then the wisdom of allowing the public to vote on, and reject it must be questioned.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Almost all studies that have been done have assumed that the scientific aspects of the controversy are unproblematic, and they have excluded science from sociological examination. The traditional view is that science is a special kind of knowledge, which is established through scientific methods and objectively applied by members of a scientific community. However, in recent years there has been a major challenge to this picture by a sociology of science that shows how scientific knowledge is socially negotiated, and inevitably linked to the values of the relevant parties, both scientists and nonscientists. These challengers do not see scientific knowledge as exempt from social inquiry.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Kuhn (1970) argued that scientific knowledge does not always develop as an orderly process, but is characterized by periodic revolutions, in which the methods of study and the assessment criteria change in a fragmented way. According to Kuhn, the shift from one scientific way of thinking to another is not made solely on the basis of clear rules of formal scientific practice, but can include social factors, though Kuhn has never developed a full analysis of what these might be. Collins (1975) took this concept further when he asserted that the outcome of experiments was not something whose meaning could be immediately comprehended, but rather something for interpretation, discussion between scientists, and reinterpretation in the light of other experiments.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">One interpretation of this analysis of science is that traditional distinctions between facts and theories, and between scientific knowledge and values, can no longer be justified. Because social processes are involved at all stages of the creation, evaluation, and establishing of scientific knowledge, social values may also be involved.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">In the same way as many scientists who study fluoridation have overlooked social values, sociologists have also downplayed an important part of the debate by ignoring the number of eminent scientists who have questioned aspects of fluoridation. An example is the study by Sutton in 1960, which analyzed the classic North American studies of the effect of fluoridation on tooth decay, and found that each showed significant methodological shortcomings. Sutton&#39;s detailed study throws doubt as to the extent of reductions in tooth decay from fluoridation. Yet Sutton&#39;s book is not cited in a single analysis of the fluoridation issue by any sociologist. In a situation of some scientific uncertainty, differences in values are highlighted. A supporter of fluoridation might argue, &#39;The evidence for the benefits of fluoridation is quite substantial, while the evidence for harm is limited and dubious. I think the likely benefits outweigh the possible dangers; hence I support fluoridation because it is the cheapest and easiest way to make sure every child reaps the benefits.&#39; An opponent might argue, &#39;Though the evidence for the benefits of fluoridation is substantial, there is some doubt about it. Since fluoridation is not necessary for good teeth, we should forego the benefits if there is some slight chance of harm. Some scientists claim that a small percentage of the population could be harmed by fluoride. Therefore, I oppose fluoridation of water supplies and favor the voluntary use of fluoride tablets by those who want to take them.&#39;<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Both arguments consider the scientific evidence concerning fluoridation, but differ in their assessments of the social benefits and costs. This difference is not between rationality and irrationality but is a legitimate difference in values, for example, the positive value placed on good teeth, the negative value placed on possible health risks, and the social benefits or costs of compulsory or voluntary intake of fluorides.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">From the sociological point of view, opposition to fluoridation is not necessarily irrational. Rather, claims to rationality and to scientific authority are better seen as part of a strategy to promote fluoridation than as incontrovertible statements of fact. Second, social values are likely to be bound up in any decision about fluoridation, so this is not an issue on which declarations by scientific experts ought to be considered the final word.<o:p></o:p><o:p></o:p><o:p></o:p><span style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7415&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7369","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Caral: an ancient South American city","book":"阅读还原集Vol.10","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test3","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.10 · Test3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"7369:56514:1","type":"choice","text":"Caral was built at the same time as the construction of the Egyptian pyramids.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"定位词: Caral, built, Egyptian pyramids\n对应原文 : B段, Research undertaken by Peruvian archaeologist Ruth Shady suggests that the 150-acre complex of pyramids, plazas and residential buildings was a thriving metropolis when Egypt's great pyramids were still being built.\n详细解析 : B段指出，当埃及金字塔仍在建造时，Caral 已经是一个繁荣的都市了，这表明 Caral 和埃及金字塔的建设时间不是同时期。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56514","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"7369:56515:2","type":"choice","text":"The absence of pottery at the archaeological dig gave Shady a significant clue to the age of the site.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"定位词 : absence of pottery, clue, age of the site\n对应原文: C段, Shady and her crew searched for broken remains of the pots and containers that most such sites contain. Not finding any only made her more excited; it meant Caral could be what archaeologists term pre-ceramic, that is, existing before the advent in the area of pot-firing techniques.\n详细解析 : C段指出，Shady 并没有发现任何陶器，反而让她更加兴奋，因为这表明 Caral 可能是“pre-ceramic（前陶器时代）”的。这一细节提示了 Caral 遗址的年代，\n同义替换：absence= not finding any","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56515","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"7369:56516:3","type":"choice","text":"The stones used to build Piramide Mayor came from a location far away.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"定位词 : stones, Piramide Mayor, far away\n对应原文 : C段, The original workers, she surmised, must have filled these bags with stones from a nearby quarry and laid them atop one another inside retaining walls, gradually giving rise to the pyramids immense structure.\n详细解析 : C段指出，建造 Piramide Mayor 的石头来自“附近的采石场（nearby quarry）”，而不是远处的地方。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56516","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"7369:56517:4","type":"choice","text":"The huge and complicated structures of Piramide Mayor suggest that its construction required an organised team of builders.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"定位词 : huge and complicated structures, organised team of builders\n对应原文 : D段, Thousands of manual laborers would have been needed to build such a project, not counting the many architects. craftsmen, and managers.\n详细解析 : D段指出，为了完成 Piramide Mayor 的建造需要成千上万的工人以及建筑师、工匠和管理者。这表明该工程需要一个有组织的团队。\n同义替换：an organised team = thousands of manual laborers, architects, craftsmen, and managers","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56517","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"7369:56518:5","type":"choice","text":"Archaeological evidence shows that the residents of Caral were highly skilled Musicians.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"定位词 : highly skilled musicians, archaeological evidence\n对应原文 : D段, Shady's team found the remains of a large amphitheater, containing almost 70 musical instruments made of bird and deer bones.\n详细解析 : D段指出发现了大量乐器，但并未说明 Caral 居民是否具备高超的音乐技艺。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56518","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"7369:56519:6","type":"choice","text":"The remains of housing areas at Caral suggest that there were no class distinctions in residential areas.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"定位词: no class distinctions, residential areas\n对应原文: D段, These indicate a hierarchy of living arrangements: large, well-kept rooms atop pyramids for the elite, ground-level quarters for craftsmen, and shabbier outlying dwellings for workers.\n详细解析 :D段指出 Caral 的住宅区存在明显的阶级区分：精英住在金字塔顶层的优质房间，工匠住在地面房间，工人住在较差的外围房间。其中 \"no class distinctions\" 与 \"a hierarchy of living arrangements\" 形成对比。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56519","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"7369:56520:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"seeds","acceptedAnswers":["seeds"],"explanation":"定位词 : discovered at Caral, not naturally occurring, plant\n对应原文 : E段, Shady found evidence of a rich trading environment, including seeds of the cocoa bush and necklaces of shells, neither of which was native to the immediate Caral area.\n详细解析: E段指出在 Caral 发现了可可树的“种子”（seeds），而该植物并非当地原生。这表明这些种子是从外地进口的贸易品。\n同义替换：not naturally occurring in the area = evidence of a rich trading environment","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56520","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"7369:56520:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"shells","acceptedAnswers":["shells"],"explanation":"定位词 : discovered at Caral, not naturally occurring, used to make jewellery\n对应原文 :E段, Shady found evidence of a rich trading environment, including seeds of the cocoa bush and necklaces of shells, neither of which was native to the immediate Caral area.\n详细解析: E段指出在 Caral 发现了由“贝壳”（shells）制成的项链，而贝壳不是当地的原生材料。这表明贝壳是外来的交易物。\n同义替换：used to make jewellery=necklaces of shells","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56520","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"7369:56520:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"fish","acceptedAnswers":["fish"],"explanation":"定位词 : remains of certain food, such as\n对应原文 : F段, Shady and her team found the bones of small edible fish, which must have come from the Pacific coast to the west, in the excavations.\n详细解析 : F段指出，发现了小鱼的骨头，这些鱼类不属于当地。这表明鱼是 Caral 的一种重要食品来源。\n同义替换：remains of certain food=bones of small edible fish","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56520","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"7369:56520:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"canals","acceptedAnswers":["canals"],"explanation":"定位词 : farming, still in existence, water diverted from rivers\n对应原文 : F段, Shady theorized that Caral's early farmers diverted the area's rivers into canals, which still cross the Supe Valley today, to irrigate their fields.\n详细解析 : F段指出，Caral 早期的农民将河水引入“渠道”（canals），这些渠道今天仍然存在。\n同义替换：still in existence =still cross the Supe Valley","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56520","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"7369:56520:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"maize","acceptedAnswers":["maize"],"explanation":"定位词 : no evidence, grown\n对应原文 : F段, But because she found no traces of maize, which can be traded or stored and used in times of crop failure, she concluded that Caral's trade leverage was not based on stockpiling food supplies.\n详细解析 : F段指出，并未发现“玉米”（maize）的痕迹。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56520","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"7369:56520:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"cotton","acceptedAnswers":["cotton"],"explanation":"定位词 : relationship with fishing communities, traded\n对应原文:G段,  'The farmers of Caral grew the cotton that the fishermen needed to make their nets,' Shady speculates.\n详细解析 : G段指出 Caral 的农民种植“棉花”（cotton），并将其与渔民交换。这表明棉花是重要的贸易品。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56520","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"7369:56520:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"flotation","acceptedAnswers":["flotation"],"explanation":"定位词 : dried squash, aid, fishing nets\n对应原文 : G段, In essence, the people of Caral enabled fishermen to work with larger and more effective nets, which made the resources of the sea more readily available, and the fishermen probably used dried squash grown by the Caral people as flotation devices for their nets.\n详细解析 : G段指出渔民使用 Caral 人种植的干南瓜作为浮力装置，帮助网具浮起。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56520","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"56514","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Caral was built at the same time as the construction of the Egyptian pyramids.</strong></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"56515","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The absence of pottery at the archaeological dig gave Shady a significant clue to the age of the site.</strong></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"56516","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The stones used to build Piramide Mayor came from a location far away.</strong></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"56517","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The huge and complicated structures of Piramide Mayor suggest that its construction required an organised team of builders.</strong></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"56518","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Archaeological evidence shows that the residents of Caral were highly skilled Musicians.</strong></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"56519","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The remains of housing areas at Caral suggest that there were no class distinctions in residential areas.</strong></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"56520","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Caral as a trading centre</strong></p><p><strong><br/></strong></p><p><strong>Items discovered at Caral but not naturally occurring in the area</strong></p><p>•&nbsp;the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong>&nbsp;of a certain plant</p><p>• <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong>&nbsp;used to make jewellery</p><p>•&nbsp;the remains of certain food such as <strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong> .</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>Clues to farming around Caral</strong></p><p>• <strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong> still in existence today indicate water diverted from rivers</p><p>•&nbsp;no evidence that <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;was grown</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>Evidence of relationship with fishing communities</strong></p><p>•&nbsp;the excavation findings and fishing nets found on the coast suggest Caral farmers traded&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong> .</p><p>•&nbsp;dried squash may have been used to aid <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong>&nbsp;of fishing nets</p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":7}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>Caral:&nbsp;an ancient South American city</strong><o:p></o:p></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Huge earth and rock mounds rise out of the desert of the Supe Valley near the coast of Peru in South America. These immense mounds appear simply to be part of the geographical landscape in this arid region squeezed between the Pacific Ocean and the Andes mountains.&nbsp;But looks deceive. These are actually human-made pyramids.&nbsp;Strong evidence indicates they are the remains of a city known as Caral that flourished nearly 5,000 years ago. If true, it would be the oldest known urban center in the Americas and among the most ancient in the world.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Research undertaken by Peruvian archaeologist Ruth Shady suggests that the&nbsp;150-acre complex of pyramids, plazas and residential buildings was a thriving metropolis when Egypt&#39;s great pyramids were still being built. Though discovered in&nbsp;1905, for years Caral attracted little attention, largely because archaeologists believed the structures were fairly recent. But the monumental scale of the pyramids had long interested Shady, who began excavations at the site in 1996, about 22&nbsp;kilometers from the coast and 190 kilometers north of Peru&#39;s capital city of Lima.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Shady and her crew searched for broken remains of the pots and containers that most such sites contain. Not finding any only made her more excited; it meant Caral could be what archaeologists term pre-ceramic, that is, existing before the advent in the area of pot-firing techniques. Shady&#39;s team undertook the task of excavating Piramide Mayor, the largest of the pyramids. After carefully clearing away many hundreds of years&#39; worth of rubble and sand, they identified staircases, walls covered with remnants of colored plaster, and brickwork.&nbsp;In the foundations, they found the remains of grass-like reeds woven into bags. The original workers, she surmised, must have filled these bags with stones from a nearby quarry and laid them atop one another inside retaining walls, gradually giving rise to the pyramids immense structure.&nbsp;Shady had samples of the reeds subjected to radiocarbon dating and found that the reeds were 4,600 years old. This evidence indicated that Caral was, in fact, more than 1,000 years older than what had previously been thought to be the oldest urban center in the Americas.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">What amazed archaeologists was not just the age, but the complexity and scope of Caral. Piramide Mayor alone covers an area nearly the size of four football fields and is 18 meters tall.&nbsp;A nine-meter-wide staircase rises from a circular plaza at the foot of the pyramid,&nbsp;passing over three terraced levels until it reaches the top. Thousands of manual laborers would have been needed to build such a project, not counting the many architects. craftsmen, and managers. Shady&#39;s team found the remains of a large amphitheater, containing almost 70 musical instruments made of bird and deer bones.&nbsp;Clearly, music played an important role in Caral&#39;s society Around the perimeter of Caral are a series of smaller mounds and various buildings. These indicate a hierarchy of living arrangements: large, well-kept rooms atop pyramids for the elite, ground-level quarters for craftsmen, and shabbier outlying dwellings for workers.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">But why had Caral been built in the first place? Her excavations convinced Shady that Caral once served as a trade center for the region, which extends from the rainforests of the Amazon to the high forests of the Andes. Shady found evidence of a rich trading environment, including seeds of the cocoa bush and necklaces of shells, neither of which was native to the immediate Caral area. This environment gave rise to people who did not take part in the production of food, allowing them to become priests and planners, builders and designers. Thus occupational specialization elemental to an urban society, emerged.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">But what sustained such a trading center and drew travelers to it? Was it food? Shady and her team found the bones of small edible fish, which must have come from the Pacific coast to the west, in the excavations. But they also found evidence of squash, sweet potatoes beans having been grown locally. Shady theorized that Caral&#39;s early farmers diverted the area&#39;s rivers into canals, which still cross the Supe Valley today, to irrigate their fields. But because she found no traces of maize, which can be traded or stored and used in times of crop failure, she concluded that Caral&#39;s trade leverage was not based on stockpiling food supplies.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">It was evidence of another crop in the excavations that gave Shady the best clue to Caral&#39;s success. In nearly every excavated building, her team discovered evidence of cotton seeds, fibers and textiles. Her theory fell into place when a large fishing net made of those fibers, unearthed in an unrelated dig on Peru&#39;s coast turned out to be as old as Caral. &#39;The farmers of Caral grew the cotton that the fishermen needed to make their nets,&#39; Shady speculates.&nbsp;&#39;And the fishermen gave them shellfish and dried fish in exchange for these nets.&#39; In essence, the people of Caral enabled fishermen to work with larger and more effective nets, which made the resources of the sea more&nbsp;readily available, and the fishermen probably used dried squash grown by the Caral people as flotation devices for their nets.<span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7369&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7370","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 What is an unfair advantage in sport?","book":"阅读还原集Vol.10","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test3","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.10 · Test3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"7370:56089:14","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"对应原文： A段，What happened to the Australian athlete Ron Clarke in the 10,000 metres at the Mexico City Olympics of 1968 is now virtually forgotten, though at the time it was headline news.\nBut suddenly he too began to struggle, and as the frontrunners moved up a gear, a gap opened up. Clarke remembers nothing of his last lap which he ran in 90 seconds\n详细解析： A段指出，Ron Clarke在1968年墨西哥城奥运会上意外失利的经历，原本他是被认为能够胜任的跑步者，但在比赛中却出现了意外情况，最后甚至不得不接受氧气治疗。这是一场“令人意外的比赛结果”。A段的主旨句是“What happened to the Australian athlete Ron Clarke in the 10,000 metres at the Mexico City Olympics of 1968”。","options":["Early research into athletes' physiology","A convenient method of acclimatization","The need for a rational approach","Changes in the body","The athletes who break the rules","Well-founded concerns","The surprising outcome of a race","The reversal of a decision","The runners who dominate"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56089","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 20\nThe text has seven paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"7370:56089:15","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"对应原文：B段， \"Mexico City is surrounded by mountains and is over 2,240 metres above sea level. That the altitude would have an impact on the Games was predicted. Clarke had raised the issue himself, but had been told by the Australian sports authorities that complaining was regarded as bad sportsmanship.\"\n详细解析：B段指出了墨西哥城的高海拔可能会影响运动员表现的问题，Clarke自己也曾提出担忧，但他的担忧被忽视了。这说明他对于海拔的担忧是有理有据的 B段的主旨句是“That the altitude would have an impact on the Games was predicted Clarke had raised the issue himself, but had been told by the Australian sports authorities that complaining was regarded as bad sportsmanship. ”。\n同义替换：well-founded concerns=the altitude would have an impact","options":["Early research into athletes' physiology","A convenient method of acclimatization","The need for a rational approach","Changes in the body","The athletes who break the rules","Well-founded concerns","The surprising outcome of a race","The reversal of a decision","The runners who dominate"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56089","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 20\nThe text has seven paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"7370:56089:16","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"对应原文： C段，\"Although there were few standout performances in distance running at the Mexico Games, they marked a turning point: the start of an astonishing record of success by east Africans.\"\nThey are all from either Kenya or Ethiopia.\n详细解析：C段指出了东非运动员在长跑比赛中的卓越表现，以及他们在此项赛事中的主导地位C段的主旨句是“Although there were few standout performances in distance running at the Mexico Games, they marked a turning point: the start of an astonishing record of success by east Africans”。","options":["Early research into athletes' physiology","A convenient method of acclimatization","The need for a rational approach","Changes in the body","The athletes who break the rules","Well-founded concerns","The surprising outcome of a race","The reversal of a decision","The runners who dominate"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56089","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 20\nThe text has seven paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"7370:56089:17","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"对应原文： D段，\"At high altitudes, a number of physiological alterations occur. Most importantly, more red blood cells and haemoglobin are produced. This, in turn, increases the capacity of the blood to carry oxygen, which feeds the muscles and which gives an advantage to the athletes when they return to sea level. \"\n详细解析：D段指出，高海拔环境对人体生理的改变，尤其是红血球和血红蛋白的增加，从而增加血液的携氧能力。这些都是身体的生理变化。D段的主旨句是“At high altitudes, a number of physiological alterations occur, most importantly.”。\n同义替换：changes=alterations; in the body=physiological","options":["Early research into athletes' physiology","A convenient method of acclimatization","The need for a rational approach","Changes in the body","The athletes who break the rules","Well-founded concerns","The surprising outcome of a race","The reversal of a decision","The runners who dominate"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56089","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 20\nThe text has seven paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"7370:56089:18","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"对应原文： E段，\"That's where the altitude tent – sometimes called the hypoxic tent – comes in. Around two decades ago, two different scientists had the same exciting thought. If they could artificially control the atmosphere within a confined space, they could simulate the effects of high altitude and save an athlete at sea-level from the time and expense of travelling to higher ground. \"\n详细解析： E段指出了海拔帐篷的发明及其作用，即帮助运动员在低海拔环境中模拟高海拔效果，使他们能够更便捷地适应高海拔环境。E段的主旨句是“That's where the altitude tent-sometimes called the hypoxic tent-comes in Around two decades ago, two different scientists had the same exciting thought.”。","options":["Early research into athletes' physiology","A convenient method of acclimatization","The need for a rational approach","Changes in the body","The athletes who break the rules","Well-founded concerns","The surprising outcome of a race","The reversal of a decision","The runners who dominate"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56089","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 20\nThe text has seven paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"7370:56089:19","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph F","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"对应原文：F段， \"In 2008, a staggering 105 world records were broken in swimming.\nBut as better suits were produced by Speedo and other manufacturers, and more records were broken, they became increasingly controversial. In a 2009 ruling, Fina changed its mind banning all suits made with this high-tech fabric.\"\n详细解析：F段指出了新款游泳衣在破纪录方面引起的争议，以及国际泳联最初批准后又改变决定禁止这些游泳衣的过程。F段的主旨句是“In a 2009 ruling, Fina changed its mind banning all suits made with this high-tech fabric.”。\n同义替换：reversal=changed its mind; decision=ruling","options":["Early research into athletes' physiology","A convenient method of acclimatization","The need for a rational approach","Changes in the body","The athletes who break the rules","Well-founded concerns","The surprising outcome of a race","The reversal of a decision","The runners who dominate"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56089","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 20\nThe text has seven paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"7370:56089:20","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph G","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"对应原文： G段，\"But when a new technology is invented, the relevant sports authority has to consider whether to embrace or reject it. In some cases, athletes are granted permission to use the technology; in others, it is banned. But whatever the outcome, rulings should not appear arbitrary: arguments have to be examined and weighed and the rules of logic ought to apply in every case.\"\n详细解析： G段指出了当新技术出现时，体育管理机构需要合理评估是否允许使用该技术，以确保决定的合理性和一致性。G段的主旨句是“But whatever the outcome, rulings should not appear arbitrary: arguments have to be examined and weighed and the rules of logic ought to apply in every case.”。\n同义替换：rational approach=examined and weighed; need=consider","options":["Early research into athletes' physiology","A convenient method of acclimatization","The need for a rational approach","Changes in the body","The athletes who break the rules","Well-founded concerns","The surprising outcome of a race","The reversal of a decision","The runners who dominate"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56089","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 20\nThe text has seven paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"7370:56090:21-22","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following statements about Ron Clarke are made in the passage?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"定位信息： worries, not taken into account, near the front, Mexico Games 10,000 metres\n对应原文：对于选项 B，B段，\"Clarke had raised the issue himself, but had been told by the Australian sports authorities that complaining was regarded as bad sportsmanship.\"对于选项 D，A段，\"With two laps to go, Clarke was in the leading pack.\"\n解题思路：\nB段指出，克拉克对高海拔的担忧（raised the issue），但澳大利亚体育当局并没有重视他的担忧，认为抱怨是不符合体育精神的表现。这说明他的担忧未被重视。\nA段指出比赛还剩两圈时克拉克在领先队伍中（in the leading pack），说明他在比赛的某个阶段处于前列。\n同义替换：worries=raised the issue；near the front=in the leading pack； at one stage=with two laps to go","options":["Clarke was not performing well immediately prior to the Mexico Games.","The worries Clarke had before the Mexico Games were not taken into account.","Clarke's experiences at the Mexico Games are widely talked about today.","At one stage of the Mexico Games 10,000 metres Clarke was near the front.","Clarke was the only runner at the Mexico Games who appeared to be affected by the altitude."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"56090","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 21 - 22\nChoose TWO correct answers.","groupId":"56090-7370:56090:21-22"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"7370:56090:21-22","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following statements about Ron Clarke are made in the passage?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"定位信息： worries, not taken into account, near the front, Mexico Games 10,000 metres\n对应原文：对于选项 B，B段，\"Clarke had raised the issue himself, but had been told by the Australian sports authorities that complaining was regarded as bad sportsmanship.\"对于选项 D，A段，\"With two laps to go, Clarke was in the leading pack.\"\n解题思路：\nB段指出，克拉克对高海拔的担忧（raised the issue），但澳大利亚体育当局并没有重视他的担忧，认为抱怨是不符合体育精神的表现。这说明他的担忧未被重视。\nA段指出比赛还剩两圈时克拉克在领先队伍中（in the leading pack），说明他在比赛的某个阶段处于前列。\n同义替换：worries=raised the issue；near the front=in the leading pack； at one stage=with two laps to go","options":["Clarke was not performing well immediately prior to the Mexico Games.","The worries Clarke had before the Mexico Games were not taken into account.","Clarke's experiences at the Mexico Games are widely talked about today.","At one stage of the Mexico Games 10,000 metres Clarke was near the front.","Clarke was the only runner at the Mexico Games who appeared to be affected by the altitude."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"56090","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 21 - 22\nChoose TWO correct answers.","groupId":"56090-7370:56090:21-22"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"7370:56091:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"spirit","acceptedAnswers":["spirit"],"explanation":"定位信息： WADA, altitude tent,not contrary to\n对应原文： E段，\"Five years ago, when the tents were investigated by WADA (the World Anti-Doping Agency), it was ruled that they did not violate the spirit of distance running. \"\n解题思路：  E段指出，WADA 的调查认为高原帐篷“did not violate the spirit of distance running”（不违反跑步精神）。\n同义替换：not contrary to=did not violate","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56091","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"7370:56091:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"drag","acceptedAnswers":["drag"],"explanation":"定位信息： LZR swimsuit, cuts down\n对应原文： F段，\"These suits use a high-tech fabric tested in Nasa's wind tunnels, which reduces drag and improves buoyancy.\"\n解题思路： F段指出，这种高科技面料能够“reduces drag”（减少阻力）和“improves buoyancy”（增加浮力）。\n同义替换：cuts down=reduces","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56091","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"7370:56091:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"records","acceptedAnswers":["records"],"explanation":"定位信息： continually set fresh\n对应原文：G段， \"Athletes believe they need records all the time, and the only way is through minute changes of 0.0001 of a second. \"\n详细解析： G段指出运动员认为他们“需要不断创造记录”（need records all the time）。\n同义替换：continually set fresh=need records all the time","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56091","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"7370:56091:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"nutrition ","acceptedAnswers":["nutrition"],"explanation":"定位信息： better,training\n对应原文： G段， And the only way they can achieve records is by improving the clothing, the kit, the training, the nutrition – all to identify minute distinctions between people of 0.0001 of a second.\n解题思路： G段指出创造纪录的唯一途径，就是不断改进服装、器材、训练和营养。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56091","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"56090-7370:56090:21-22","numbers":[21,22],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["B","D"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"56089","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 20\nThe text has seven paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"56090","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 21 - 22\nChoose TWO correct answers.","html":"<p>Which <strong>TWO&nbsp;</strong>of the following statements about Ron Clarke are made in the passage?</p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"56091","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: center; line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>Do all new technologies gain approval?</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Some people may be puzzled by attitudes towards performance-enhancing technologies in sport. For example, why is the altitude tent considered acceptable, but not the LZR Racer suit? For distance running, WADA concluded that the altitude tent was not contrary to the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong>&nbsp;of the sport. However, the LZR swimsuit, which is made from a special fabric that aids buoyancy and cuts down <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong>, was banned.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Athletes think they have to continually set fresh <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong>&nbsp;. This is made possible by better <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong>&nbsp;and training, as well as improved clothing and equipment.&nbsp;However, when sports authorities have to decide whether to give permission for a new performance-enhancing technology to be used, it is important that their decisions are not seen as arbitrary.</p>","firstNumber":23}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>What is an unfair advantage in sport?</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><em>Olympic athletes increasingly depend on technology to help them win – but is that fair?</em></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><em><br/></em></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">What happened to the Australian athlete Ron Clarke in the 10,000 metres at the Mexico City Olympics of 1968 is now virtually forgotten, though at the time it was headline news. Clarke was the greatest distance runner in history. He&#39;d broken more world records than anybody else. But in front of 55,000 horrified spectators, the event went disastrously wrong. In the third lap, one runner keeled over and with six laps to go, two more were carried away. Yet the race was being conducted at a relatively leisurely speed: the halfway time was the slowest since the Paris Olympics of 1924. With two laps to go, Clarke was in the leading pack. &#39;I&#39;d never felt better in a race,&#39; he says. But suddenly he too began to struggle, and as the frontrunners moved up a gear, a gap opened up. Clarke remembers nothing of his last lap which he ran in 90 seconds &#39;Normally I would run it in 64,&#39; he explains. He stumbled across the line in sixth place and collapsed. He was administered oxygen and stretchered off the track.<span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255);\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Mexico City is surrounded by mountains and is over 2,240 metres above sea level. That the altitude would have an impact on the Games was predicted. Clarke had raised the issue himself, but had been told by the Australian sports authorities that complaining was regarded as bad sportsmanship. As it turned out, he had good reason to do so. Clearly, the link between athletic performance and altitude needed further investigation.<span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255);\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span>C</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Although there were few standout performances in distance running at the Mexico Games, they marked a turning point: the start of an astonishing record of success by east Africans. While Clarke lay crumpled in a heap, runners from Kenya and Ethiopia were celebrating their gold and silver medals. The record books confirm how entrenched this pattern has become. The names of the seven fastest men in history over 5,000 metres are Bekele, Gebrselassie, Komen, Kipchoge, Sihinetzx, Songkok and Chereno. They are all from either Kenya or Ethiopia. Between 1997 and 2011 the 10,000 metres men&#39;s world record was smashed five times, dropping from 26:31.32 to 26:17.53. Each time, the record was broken by a Kenyan or an Ethiopian. While there is a complex mix of economic, political, social and cultural explanations for the pre-eminence of east Africans, one factor is surely that many of these athletes have lived most of their lives in thin air.<span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255);\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">At high altitudes,&nbsp;a number of physiological alterations occur. Most importantly, more red blood cells and haemoglobin are produced. This, in turn, increases the capacity of the blood to carry oxygen, which feeds the muscles and which gives an advantage to the athletes when they return to sea level. However, it is impossible to train with the same level of intensity in the mountains<span style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;,sans-serif\">&nbsp;–&nbsp;</span>aerobic capacity and cardio<span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">-</span>respiratory function both suffer at altitude. As a result, the consensus is that the optimum approach to athletic preparation is: Live High, Train low&nbsp;(LHTL). Yet that has obvious practical drawbacks. Not many people live in the mountains and those who do would prefer not to spend several hours each day driving up and down winding treacherous roads.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">That&#39;s where the altitude tent – sometimes called the hypoxic tent – comes in. Around two decades ago, two different scientists had the same exciting thought. If they could artificially control the atmosphere within a confined space, they could simulate the effects of high altitude and save an athlete at sea-level from the time and expense of travelling to higher ground. Altitude tents have improved over the years: they&#39;re not as hot or as noisy as the early prototypes, and are much cheaper too. They are also perfectly lawful. Five years ago, when the tents were investigated by WADA (the World Anti-Doping Agency), it was ruled that they did not violate the spirit of distance running. It is now routine for athletes to sleep in them in preparation for an event.<span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255);\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">However, it is not the case that all new technologies gain approval. In 2008, a staggering 105 world records were broken in swimming. The vast majority were achieved by competitors wearing the new Speedo LZR Racer suit. These suits use a high-tech fabric tested in Nasa&#39;s wind tunnels, which reduces drag and improves buoyancy. The LZR was initially sanctioned by FINA, the international swimming body. But as better suits were produced by Speedo and other manufacturers, and more records were broken, they became increasingly controversial. In a 2009 ruling, FINA changed its mind banning all suits made with this high-tech fabric.<span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255);\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">#&amp;</span>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Going faster, higher, stronger is integral to the logic of athletics in general, and the Olympics in particular. Athletes believe they need records all the time. And the only way they can achieve records is by improving the clothing, the kit, the training, the nutrition<span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp;–&nbsp;</span>all to identify minute distinctions between people of 0.0001 of a second. But when a new technology is invented, the relevant sports authority has to consider whether to embrace or reject it. In some cases, athletes are granted permission to use the technology; in others, it is banned. But whatever the outcome, rulings should not appear arbitrary: arguments have to be examined and weighed and the rules of logic ought to apply in every case.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7370&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7371","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Children's literature studies today","book":"阅读还原集Vol.10","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test3","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.10 · Test3 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"7371:56107:27","type":"choice","text":"Which of the following best summarises the writer’s argument in the second paragraph?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题： 题目要求总结第二段的主要论点，关注成年人如何看待儿童文学以及这种观点如何影响儿童的表现。\n定位关键词：in the second paragraph\n对应原文：B段，“Adults write for children, and thus adult perceptions of what children are and of what they could and should be become woven into the literature.”\n解题思路：B段指出了儿童文学通常由成年人创作，因此这些作品不可避免地包含了成人对儿童的看法和期望。这意味着儿童在文学作品中被呈现成成人所理解的样子，与“儿童被描绘成成人的视角”相符。相比之下，文中并未讨论儿童的创作能力，只是指出主要是成年人为儿童写作。原文没有指出成人是否成功或失败地激发了儿童的想象力。该段没有涉及成人文学的难度问题。\n同义替换：portrayed=woven into the literature","options":["Children are portrayed as adults see them.","Children are unable to write their own stories.","Adults fail to stimulate children’s imaginations.","Adult literature is too difficult for children."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56107","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 29\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"7371:56108:28","type":"choice","text":"In the third paragraph, what does the writer say is the main interest of some people who study children’s literature?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目要求识别第三段中对某些儿童文学研究者主要兴趣的描述。\n定位关键词：main interest, third paragraph\n对应原文：C段，“Furthermore, some of those who study children’s literature (and those who write certain kinds of children's books) are less interested in literary values than in the kinds of lessons it can teach – either in terms of creating better children or in terms of serving a particular curriculum.”\n解题思路：C段指出研究儿童文学的人有时更关注书籍的教育意义而非其文学价值。 “写作质量”不符合，因为原文没有强调这一点。原文关注的是教育性而非想象力，“儿童在故事中的描写方式”没有被提及。\n同义替换：instructive nature=kinds of lessons it can teach","options":["the quality of the writing","the imaginative content of stories","the instructive nature of children’s books","the way children are written about in stories"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56108","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 29\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"7371:56109:29","type":"choice","text":"The main point of the writer’s argument in the fifth paragraph is to","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问第五段的主要论点，关注计算机对儿童文学界限的影响。\n定位关键词：the fifth paragraph\n对应原文：E段，“It is also important to note that texts in an ever-increasing range of new media compete with print media for the attention of the child reader, and create definitional issues for scholars.”\n解题思路：E段指出新媒体（如计算机）如何与传统印刷媒体竞争，并讨论这对儿童文学界限的影响。学者认为电脑游戏是儿童文学的延伸，并未在原文中指出。文学和电脑游戏的起源不同”没有被强调。证明儿童使用电脑多于阅读文学”原文并未做出这样的比较。","options":["demonstrate that academics consider computer games to be a logical extension of children's literature.","explore the impact of computers on the boundaries of children’s literature.","illustrate that literature and computer games have from different origins.","prove that children are using computers more than they are reading literature."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56109","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 29\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"7371:56110:30","type":"choice","text":"Children tend to make a clear distinction between print literature and electronic media.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题： 题目询问儿童是否区分印刷文学与电子媒体。\n定位词： \"distinction between print literature and electronic media\"\n对应原文：E段，“It is also important to note that texts in an ever-increasing range of new media compete with print media for the attention of the child reader, and create definitional issues for scholars. Does the term literature’ exclusively imply a verbal text? If not, where are the limits? Could a literary computer game ever be considered a work of literature? If not, what kind of attention should be paid to it, since children themselves undoubtedly perceive their print literature as part of a broader continuum?”\n解题思路：题目说 Children tend to make a clear distinction between print literature and electronic media，即“儿童倾向于明确区分印刷文学和电子媒体”。原文E段提到，儿童“perceive their print literature as part of a broader continuum”，意思是儿童把印刷文学看作一个更广泛的连续体系的一部分；但这里需要注意，“把A看作更大体系的一部分”并不等于“不能或不会区分A和B”。例如，我们完全可以既知道汽车和自行车属于同一个更大的交通体系，同时又能够清楚地区分二者。因此，原文虽然说明儿童对印刷文学的理解比较宽泛，但没有明确说明儿童是否会在印刷文学和电子媒体之间作出清晰区分，也没有明确说他们“不区分”。由于题目中的核心信息 clear distinction 在原文中既没有得到支持，也没有被明确否定，所以严格按照雅思 YES/NO/NOT GIVEN 的判断标准，本题应选 NOT GIVEN，而不能仅凭 broader continuum 就推断为 NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56110","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30 - 34\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"7371:56111:31","type":"choice","text":"The study of children’s literature at higher education institutions is restricted to one subject area.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"审题： 题目询问儿童文学研究是否局限于一个学科。\n定位词关键词： restricted to one subject area\n对应原文：F段，“Finally, in the context of the higher education institutions where the formal study of children’s literature of often located, at least three disciplinary frameworks (English, education, and librarianship) fragment the focus of scholarly study of children’s literature.”\n解题思路：F段指出儿童文学的研究涉及多个学科框架，明确表明该领域的研究并非局限于单一学科，选项中的说法与原文内容相矛盾。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56111","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30 - 34\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"7371:56112:32","type":"choice","text":"Exploring children’s perceptions of reading will assist parents to choose suitable books for children.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题： 题目询问儿童阅读的感知对父母选书的帮助。\n定位关键词：\"perceptions of reading\", \"parents\", \"suitable books\"\n对应段落： G段, “As David Lewis (2001) has perceptively noted, what children think of reading is not usually the same as what adults think, whether teachers or parents.”\n解题思路： G段指出，理解儿童阅读的必要性，但并未指出这将直接帮助父母选择适合的书籍。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56112","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30 - 34\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"7371:56113:33","type":"choice","text":"Adults may appreciate the appeal of illustrated stories better, if they have more information on how children read.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"审题： 题目询问成人如何通过理解儿童的阅读方式来更好地欣赏图画书。\n定位关键词： appreciate the appeal, better, more information\n对应原文： H段， \"However, it can also be argued, as Lewis rightly does, that when children’s responses to literature are accessed and interpreted, they frequently lead to an understanding of how picture books appeal to children.\"\n解题思路：H段指出，理解儿童如何阅读可以帮助成人更好地欣赏图画书的吸引力。\n同义替换：appreciate=understand","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56113","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30 - 34\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"7371:56114:34","type":"choice","text":"Children should be asked what features they would like digital games to include.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题： 题目询问是否应该询问儿童对数字游戏的看法。\n定位词关键：features, digital games include\n对应原文：J段，“A humbler approach would include asking why the game appeals to the player.”\n解题思路：J段未提及儿童对于数字游戏应包含哪些特征的具体看法或建议，这一选项没有在文中明确表达出来。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56114","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30 - 34\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"7371:56115:35","type":"choice","text":"Young people’s accounts of how they read lead to ____","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"审题： 题目询问年轻人对自己阅读方式的描述所带来的结果。\n定位关键词： \"Young people's accounts of how they read\"\n对应原文： I段， \"Young people’s accounts of what and how they read also enable a more sophisticated description of many of the complex processes involved in reading.\"\n解题思路：I段指出年轻人对其阅读过程的描述使得人们能够获得对阅读复杂性的更深入理解。\n同义替换：deeper knowledge = more sophisticated description； intricacies of reading = complex processes involved in reading","options":["accepting that literature exists in a variety of forms today","verbalising the words in their heads","discovering the reading techniques used by others","the style of written stories changing over time","the lack of some specific abilities","a deeper knowledge of the intricacies of reading","children teaching adults to play computer games","creating a variety of images in their minds."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"56115","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 35 - 39\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"7371:56115:36","type":"choice","text":"The risk of solipsism is reduced by ____","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题： 题目询问如何减少自我中心主义的风险。\n定位关键词： \"risk of solipsism\"\n对应原文： I段， \"All descriptions of reading run the risk of solipsism: i.e. this is how I read so this is what reading is for everyone. Asking other readers how they read, however, reduces that risk.\"\n解题思路： I段指出对阅读的所有描述都存在自我中心主义的风险：即‘这是我如何阅读的方式，所以这就是所有人阅读的方式’。然而，询问其他读者他们是如何阅读的，可以降低这种风险。","options":["accepting that literature exists in a variety of forms today","verbalising the words in their heads","discovering the reading techniques used by others","the style of written stories changing over time","the lack of some specific abilities","a deeper knowledge of the intricacies of reading","children teaching adults to play computer games","creating a variety of images in their minds."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"56115","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 35 - 39\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"7371:56115:37","type":"choice","text":"Strong visualisers judge books on the basis that they are____","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"审题： 题目询问强视觉化的读者如何评判书籍。\n定位词： \"strong visualisers\"\n对应原文：I段， \"For example, if I am a strong visualizer as I read, I may consider that visualization is a key component of successful reading and I may judge books by their capacity to evoke a vivid visual response.”\n解题思路：I段指出强视觉化的读者会根据书籍是否能够激发他们的想象力来评判书籍的价值。\n同义替换：creating a variety of images =evoke a vivid visual response","options":["accepting that literature exists in a variety of forms today","verbalising the words in their heads","discovering the reading techniques used by others","the style of written stories changing over time","the lack of some specific abilities","a deeper knowledge of the intricacies of reading","children teaching adults to play computer games","creating a variety of images in their minds."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"56115","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 35 - 39\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"7371:56115:38","type":"choice","text":"Children’s insights are important in ____","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题： 题目询问儿童的见解在何种方面重要。\n定位词： \"Children's insights\"\n对应原文：J段， \"Children’s insights are even more important when it comes to understanding the significance of print literature as one aspect of literary culture.\"\n解题思路：J段指出儿童的见解对于接受和理解今天文学文化的多种形式（包括印刷文学）非常重要。","options":["accepting that literature exists in a variety of forms today","verbalising the words in their heads","discovering the reading techniques used by others","the style of written stories changing over time","the lack of some specific abilities","a deeper knowledge of the intricacies of reading","children teaching adults to play computer games","creating a variety of images in their minds."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"56115","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 35 - 39\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"7371:56115:39","type":"choice","text":"When adults read a book more easily than they play a digital game it simply suggests ____","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"审题： 题目询问成年人在阅读书籍和玩数字游戏时的能力差异意味着什么。\n定位关键词： \"read a book more easily\"\n对应原文：J段， \"This does not indicate that a book is better, but that a particular set of skills is absent.\"\n解题思路： J段指出成年人在阅读书籍时的便利性并不代表书籍更优秀，而是缺乏某些特定的技能。","options":["accepting that literature exists in a variety of forms today","verbalising the words in their heads","discovering the reading techniques used by others","the style of written stories changing over time","the lack of some specific abilities","a deeper knowledge of the intricacies of reading","children teaching adults to play computer games","creating a variety of images in their minds."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"56115","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 35 - 39\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"7371:56116:40","type":"choice","text":"What was the writer’s main purpose in writing this article?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题： 题目要求明确作者写这篇文章的主要目的。\n定位词关键词： main purpose\n对应原文： J段，\" This does not indicate that a book is better, but that a particular set of skills is absent. Non-players must acknowledge that some fictional universes are thus closed to them, and a logical response would be to find someone who can guide them to the pleasures and challenges of the gaming world. Games need to be judged individually just as books do, and any evaluative framework needs to take this into account.\"\n做题思路：段落A 指出儿童文学主要是由成年人创作，因此反映了成年人的视角，提出了儿童的声音往往被忽视。\n段落B 指出一些研究者更关注儿童文学的教育功能，而非文学价值，进一步探讨了这一点的复杂性。\n段落C 指出了市场营销对儿童阅读体验的影响，质疑了如何在商业化背景下理解儿童的阅读。\n段落D 指出了电子媒体对儿童文学的定义和范围的影响，提出了对“文学”定义的挑战。\n段落E 指出了儿童文学研究在高等教育中的学科分散问题，反映出研究的多样性。\n段落F-H 引入David Lewis的观点，强调理解儿童阅读的必要性，认为儿童的反馈对教育和文学价值评估都至关重要。\n段落I, J总结了以上讨论，强调在众多利益冲突中保持对儿童文学价值的理解是多么重要。\n通过这些分析，作者不仅呈现了儿童文学研究的现状和挑战，还呼吁学者们更多地关注儿童的视角和反馈，探索如何在现代社会中促进儿童阅读，选项C最符合作者的目的：回顾儿童文学研究的挑战并提出未来的研究方向。","options":["to evaluate how the process of reading fits into children’s literature studies","to discuss the impact of the increasing commercial influence on children’s literature studies","to review the challenges in the field of children’s literature studies and suggest how to proceed","to provide arguments in favor of including computerized forms of me children’s literature studies"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56116","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 40\nChoose the correct answer."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"56107","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 29\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>Which of the following best summarises the writer’s argument in the second paragraph?</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"56108","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 29\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>In the third paragraph, what does the writer say is the main interest of some people who study children’s literature?</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"56109","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 29\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>The main point of the writer’s argument in the fifth paragraph is to</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"56110","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30 - 34\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Children tend to make a clear distinction between print literature and electronic media.&nbsp;</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"56111","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30 - 34\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>The study of children’s literature at higher education institutions is restricted to one subject area.</strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"56112","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30 - 34\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Exploring children’s perceptions of reading will assist parents to choose suitable books for children.</strong></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"56113","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30 - 34\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Adults may appreciate the appeal of illustrated stories better, if they have more information on how children read.</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"56114","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 30 - 34\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Children should be asked what features they would like digital games to include.</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"56115","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 35 - 39\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"56116","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 40\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>What was the writer’s main purpose in writing this article?</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>Children’s literature studies today</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Who studies children’s literature and what is it that they study? The answers to this question are complex and messy, because of the many confounding factors which exist in this field.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Firstly, unlike literature for adults. Children&#39;s literature is not generally written by its own readers. Adults write for children, and thus adult perceptions of what children are and of what they could and should be become woven into the literature.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Furthermore, some of those who study children’s literature (and those who write certain kinds of children&#39;s books) are less interested in literary values than in the kinds of lessons it can teach – either in terms of creating better children or in terms of serving a particular curriculum.&nbsp;The issue of how a teacher can use a children’s book is often contentious, but even outside the classroom, much material for children is still didactic.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Thirdly, while almost all literature is currently promoted within a strong commercial matrix, children’s literature is often especially targeted for marketing initiatives. This fact means that readers are often recruited with a message that is negligibly literary and significantly oriented to ideas of consumption. Daniel Hadetzx (2002) has raised useful questions about whether children’s experience of reading is altered when their books are part of a larger marketing framework involving the movie, the game, and the toy of a popular children’s book. How children perceive and respond to their stories in this new context is an important question.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">It is also important to note that texts in an ever-increasing range of new media compete with print media for the attention of the child reader, and create definitional issues for scholars. Does the term literature’ exclusively imply a verbal text? If not, where are the limits? Could a literary computer game ever be considered a work of literature? If not, what kind of attention should be paid to it, since children themselves undoubtedly perceive their print literature as part of a broader continuum? The internet provides one forum through which children now communicate with each other. (In 2003, the internet search engine Google listed 7,920,000 sites relating to the Harry Potter novels; even allowing for duplication and dead ends, that is a number with revolutionary implications.)</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Finally, in the context of the higher education institutions where the formal study of children’s literature of often located, at least three disciplinary frameworks (English, education, and librarianship) fragment the focus of scholarly study of children’s literature.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">How is the value of the imaginative encounter with the work of literature sustained and honored among such a welter of conflicting interests? One route through this maze is to ask the child readers for help. As David Lewis (2001) has perceptively noted, what children think of reading is not usually the same as what adults think, whether teachers or parents. As Lewis points out children &#39;sometimes see more and they often see differently&#39;. If those who study reading can explore children’s perceptions as well as those of adults, their understanding of the nature of reading will be enhanced.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Lewis makes a further valid point when he adds that exploring children’s perceptions is usually justified for educational reasons: “It is true that a better understanding of how children read and how they learn to read, is a prerequisite to improved approaches to teaching. However, it can also be argued, as Lewis rightly does, that when children’s responses to literature are accessed and interpreted, they frequently lead to an understanding of how picture books appeal to children.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Young people’s accounts of what and how they read also enable a more sophisticated description of many of the complex processes involved in reading. All descriptions of reading run the risk of solipsism: i.e. this is how I read so this is what reading is for everyone. Asking other readers how they read, however, reduces that risk. For example, if I am a strong visualizer as I read, I may consider that visualization is a key component of successful reading and I may judge books by their capacity to evoke a vivid visual response. Other readers, however, may help me to realize that not everyone reads with mental pictures. Some readers respond to the patterns of the words, &#39;hearing&#39; them inaudibly like a subliminal radio program. Others respond to the patterns of feelings in the story, responding with an emotional connection. Talking to competent readers, of all ages, provides a better understanding of reading experiences.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>J</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Children’s insights are even more important when it comes to understanding the significance of print literature as one aspect of literary culture. Too often adults assume that reading any book at all is a more worthwhile experience than playing a digital game of any kind. A humbler approach would include asking why the game appeals to the player. Many adults will probably never develop the automatic skills to process a game as readily as they can read a book. This does not indicate that a book is better, but that a particular set of skills is absent. Non-players must acknowledge that some fictional universes are thus closed to them, and a logical response would be to find someone who can guide them to the pleasures and challenges of the gaming world. Games need to be judged individually just as books do, and any evaluative framework needs to take this into account.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7371&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7360","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Wood: a valuable resource in New Zealand's economy","book":"阅读还原集Vol.10","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test2","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.10 · Test2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"7360:56094:1","type":"choice","text":"Settlers realised that wooden houses were more dangerous than other types of structure.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"定位词: settlers, wooden houses, more dangerous\n对应原文: A段，Wood was easily accessible and relatively cheap. A tradition of wooden houses arose, supported by the recognition that they were less likely to collapse suddenly during earthquakes, a not infrequent event in this part of the world.\n详细解析: A段指出木屋在地震中更不容易倒塌（less likely to collapse），表明木屋比其他结构更安全，而非更危险。题目说木屋“更危险”，与原文含义相反，其中“more dangerous” 与“less likely to collapse”相互矛盾。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56094","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"7360:56095:2","type":"choice","text":"During the 1800s, New Zealand exported wood for use in boat-building.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"定位词: 1800s, New Zealand, boat-building\n对应原文: B段, Early explorers recognised the suitability of the tall, straight trunks of the kauri for constructing sailing vessels. The kauri is a species of coniferous tree found only in small areas of the southern hemisphere. So from the early 1800s, huge amounts of this type of wood were sold to Australia and the UK for that purpose.\n详细解析: B段指出，从19世纪早期起，大量木材被出售至澳大利亚和英国用于造船（that purpose），与题目表述一致，说明新西兰确实在1800年代出口木材用于建造船只。\n同义替换：boat-building = constructing sailing vessels","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56095","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"7360:56096:3","type":"choice","text":"Plantation-grown wood is generally better for construction than native-forest wood.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"定位词: plantation-grown wood, better for construction, native-forest wood\n对应原文: C段，By the 1960s, plantation-grown timber was providing most of the country's sawn timber needs, especially for construction.\n详细解析: C段指出种植林木材逐渐满足了新西兰国内建筑需求，但并未提及其优于或劣于本地森林木材，文中没有关于两者在建筑用途上好坏的直接对比信息。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56096","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"7360:56097:4","type":"choice","text":"Compared to other types of wood, pine has a narrow range of uses.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"定位词: pine, narrow range of uses\n对应原文: D段, This amazing versatility has encouraged the development of an integrated forest-products industry which is almost unique in the world.\n详细解析: D段指出了松木的多种用途，例如用作纸浆、柱子、家具、模具等，并且称其用途非常广泛（amazing versatility），与题目中“用途有限”形成反差。其中\"narrow range of uses” 与 “amazing versatility” 相矛盾。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56097","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"7360:56098:5","type":"choice","text":"Demand for housing in New Zealand is predicted to fall in the next few years.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"定位词: Demand for housing, New Zealand, fall,  in the next few years\n对应原文: F段，In New Zealand itself, the construction industry is the principal user of solid wood products, servicing around 20,000 new house starts annually.\n详细解析: F段提到新西兰每年有大约20,000新房开工，但未提及未来几年是否会出现需求下降的预测。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56098","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"7360:56099:6","type":"choice","text":"In future, the expansion of New Zealand’s wood industry will depend on its exports.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"定位词: in the future, the expansion of New Zealand’s wood industry\n对应原文:F段, Accordingly, the development of the export market is the key to the industry's growth and contribution to the national economy in decades to come.\n详细解析: F段提到，未来木材行业的扩展依赖于出口市场的发展（the development of the export market is the key），说明行业的未来增长将依靠出口市场来实现，其中\"depend on its exports” =“the development of the export market is the key”，表明出口市场是未来行业增长的关键。\n同义替换：the expansion of New Zealand’s wood industry = the industry's growth; In future = In decades to come","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56099","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"7360:56100:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"shipping costs","acceptedAnswers":["shipping costs"],"explanation":"定位词: exchange rates, negative impact, New Zealand's forestry exports\n对应原文: G段, \"In 2004, forestry export receipts were about 11 percent of the country's total export income, their value having increased steadily for ten years, until affected by the exchange fluctuations and shipping costs of recent years.\"\n详细解析: G段指出，除了汇率波动（exchange fluctuations），运费（shipping costs）也对出口产生了负面影响。\n同义替换：exchange rates = exchange fluctuations","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56100","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the questions. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"7360:56101:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"export sector","acceptedAnswers":["export sector"],"explanation":"定位词: New Zealand's economy, forestry industry, rank third\n对应原文: G段, The forestry industry is New Zealand's third largest export sector, generating around $3,3 billion annually from logs and processed wood products.\n详细解析: 原文直接提到林业是新西兰第三大出口行业（third largest export sector）。\n同义替换：ranks third = third largest","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56101","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the questions. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"7360:56102:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"60,000/60000/60,000 people/60000 people","acceptedAnswers":["60,000","60000","60,000 people","60000 people"],"explanation":"定位词: New Zealand forestry industry, size ,workforce, 2025\n对应原文: H段, The industry claims that, given the right conditions, by 2025 the forestry sector could be the country's biggest export earner, generating $20 billion a year and employing 60,000 people.\n详细解析: 原文提到预计到2025年，林业将雇用60,000人。\n同义替换：size of its workforce = employing 60,000 people","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56102","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the questions. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"7360:56103:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"softwood","acceptedAnswers":["softwood"],"explanation":"定位词: timber product, large amounts, renewable forests\n对应原文: I段, One competitive advantage that New Zealand has is its ability to source large quantities of softwood from renewable forests.\n详细解析: 原文指出新西兰从可再生林中获得大量“软木”（softwood）。\n同义替换：large amounts = large quantities","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56103","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the questions. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"7360:56104:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"sustainability","acceptedAnswers":["sustainability"],"explanation":"定位词: timber production, customers, increasingly concerned about\n对应原文: I段, Consumers in several key wood markets are becoming more worried about sustainability, and the industry is supporting the development of national standards as well as the recognition of these internationally.\n详细解析: 原文指出关键市场的消费者对可持续性（sustainability）问题越来越关注。\n同义替换：Increasingly concerned about = becoming more worried about","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56104","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the questions. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"7360:56105:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"Scandinavian countries","acceptedAnswers":["Scandinavian countries"],"explanation":"定位词: southern hemisphere, competitors\n对应原文: I段, However, New Zealand is not the only country with a plantation-style forestry industry. Chitzx, Brazil, Argentina, South Africa and Australia all have extensive plantings of fast-growing species (hardwood and softwood) and in the northern hemisphere, Scandinavian countries have all expanded their forests or controlled their use in the interests of future production.\n详细解析: I段指出北半球的主要竞争对手为斯堪的纳维亚国家（Scandinavian countries）。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56105","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the questions. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"7360:56106:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"wood substitutes","acceptedAnswers":["wood substitutes"],"explanation":"定位词: group of products, having to compete with\n对应原文: J段, Finally, in addition to competition from other wood producers, New Zealand faces competition from goods such as wood substitutes.\n详细解析: J段指出新西兰的林业正在与木材替代品（wood substitutes）竞争。\n同义替换：group of products = goods；having to compete with = faces competition from","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56106","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the questions. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"56094","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Settlers realised that wooden houses were more dangerous than other types of structure.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"56095","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>During the 1800s, New Zealand exported wood for use in boat-building.</strong></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"56096","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Plantation-grown wood is generally better for construction than native-forest wood.</strong></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"56097","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Compared&nbsp;to other&nbsp;types of wood, pine has a narrow range of uses.</strong></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"56098","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Demand for housing in New Zealand is predicted to fall in the next few years.</strong></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"56099","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>In future,&nbsp;the expansion of New Zealand’s wood industry will depend on its exports.</strong></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"56100","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the questions. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","html":"<p>Apart from exchange rates, which factor has had a negative impact on New Zealand&#39;s forestry&nbsp;exports? <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"56101","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the questions. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","html":"<p>Which part of New Zealand&#39;s economy does the forestry industry rank third in?&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"56102","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the questions. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","html":"<p>According to the New Zealand forestry industry, what could be the size of its workforce by 2025?&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"56103","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the questions. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","html":"<p>What kind of timber product is available in large amounts from renewable forests in New Zealand?&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"56104","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the questions. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","html":"<p>Which aspect of timber production are New Zealand&#39;s main customers increasingly concerned about?&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"56105","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the questions. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","html":"<p>Outside the southern hemisphere, who are New Zealand forestry&#39;s main competitors?&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"56106","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the questions. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","html":"<p>Which group of products is New Zealand&#39;s forestry industry now having to compete with?&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>Wood: a valuable resource in New Zealand&#39;s economy</strong><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">During the settlement of New Zealand by European immigrants, natural timbers played a major role. Wood was easily accessible and relatively cheap.&nbsp;A tradition of wooden houses arose, supported by the recognition that they were less likely to collapse suddenly during earthquakes,&nbsp;a not infrequent event in this part of the world. But in addition to demand from the domestic no market, there was also a demand for forest products from overseas.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Early explorers recognised the suitability of the tall, straight trunks of the kauri for constructing sailing vessels. The kauri is a species of coniferous tree found only in small areas of the southern hemisphere. So from the early 1800s, huge amounts of this type of wood were sold to Australia and the UK for that purpose. For a period, the forestry industry was the country&#39;s major export earner, but the rate of harvest was unsustainable and, by the beginning of the 20th century, indigenous timber exports were rapidly declining.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">From the 1940s, newly established plantations of an imported species of tree called radiata pine supplied timber and other wood products in increasing quantities. By the 1960s, plantation-grown timber was providing most of the country&#39;s sawn timber needs, especially for construction. Today, less than two percent of timber is cut from indigenous forests, and almost all of that is used for higher-value end uses, such as furniture and fittings.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">As the pine industry developed, it became apparent that this type of wood was also well suited for many uses. It makes excellent pulp* and is frequently used for posts, poles, furnishings and mouldings, particleboard, fibreboard, and for plywood and &#39;engineered&#39; wood products. Pine by-products are used in the chemical and pharmaceutical industries and residues are consumed for fuel. This amazing versatility has encouraged the development of an integrated forest-products industry which is almost unique in the world.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Exporters of wood products have largely targeted the rapidly growing markets of South and East Asia and Australia 80 percent of exports by value go to only five markets: Japan, Korea, China, the United States and Australia. The product mix remains heavily based on raw materials, with logs, sawn wood, pulp and paper comprising 75 percent of export value. However, finished wood products such as panels and furniture components are exported to more than 50 countries.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">In New Zealand itself, the construction industry is the principal user of solid wood products, servicing around 20,000 new house starts annually. However, the small size of New Zealand&#39;s&nbsp;population (just over four million) plus its small manufacturing and remanufacturing base, limit the forestry industry&#39;s domestic opportunities. For the last few years local wood consumption has been around only four million cubic metres. Accordingly, the development of&nbsp;the export market is the key to the industry&#39;s growth and contribution to the national economy in decades to come.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">In 2004, forestry export receipts were about 11 percent of the country&#39;s total export income, their value having increased steadily for ten years, until affected by the exchange fluctuations and shipping costs of recent years. The forestry industry is New Zealand&#39;s third largest export sector, generating around $3,3 billion annually from logs and processed wood products. But it is generally agreed that it is operating well below its capacity and, with the domestic market already at its peak, almost all of the extra wood produced in future will have to be marketed overseas. That presents a major marketing challenge for the industry.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Although the export of logs will continue to provide valuable earnings for forest owners, there is broad acceptance that the industry must be based on value-added products in future. So the industry is investigating various processing, infrastructure and investment strategies with a view to increasing the level of local manufacturing before export. The keys to future success will depend on a variety of factor, better international marketing, product innovation, internationally&nbsp;competitive processing, better infrastructure and a suitable political, regulatory and investment environment. The industry claims that, given the right conditions, by 2025 the forestry sector could be the country&#39;s biggest export earner, generating $20 billion a year and employing 60,000&nbsp;people.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">One competitive advantage that New Zealand has is its ability to source large quantities of softwood from renewable forests. Consumers in several key wood markets are becoming more&nbsp;worried about sustainability, and the industry is supporting the development of national standards as well as the recognition of these internationally. However, New Zealand is not the only country with a plantation-style forestry industry. Chitzx, Brazil, Argentina, South Africa and Australia all have extensive plantings of fast-growing species&nbsp;(hardwood and softwood) and in the northern hemisphere, Scandinavian countries have all expanded their forests or controlled their use in the interests of future production.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>J</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Finally, in addition to competition from other wood producers, New Zealand faces competition from goods such as wood substitutes. These include steel framing for houses. This further underlines the necessity for globally competitive production and marketing strategies.</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7360&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7361","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Should space be explored by robots or by humans","book":"阅读还原集Vol.10","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test2","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.10 · Test2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"7361:56032:14","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"A段的主旨句是 \"There is no doubt that the presence of people on board a space vehicle makes its design much more complex and challenging, and produces a large increase in costs, since safety requirements are greatly increased.\" 段落讨论了人类参与太空探索所带来的设计复杂性、成本增加以及安全要求。这些都是人类参与太空探索带来的问题。","options":["Robots on Earth – a re-evaluation","The barriers to cooperation in space exploration","Some limitations of robots in space","Reduced expectations for space exploration","A general reconsideration of human/robot responsibilities in space","Problems in using humans for space exploration","The danger to humans of intelligent machines","Space settlement and the development of greater self-awareness","Possible examples of cooperation in space"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56032","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nThe text has six paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"7361:56032:15","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"B段强调机器人的局限性：机器人在应对意外情况方面的不足，尤其是在太空任务中，当机器人遇到未知情况时，无法像人类一样灵活地应对和调整操作。以及机器人在深空任务中面临通讯延迟的困境（例如在火星任务中，从地球传输指令需要数分钟）。","options":["Robots on Earth – a re-evaluation","The barriers to cooperation in space exploration","Some limitations of robots in space","Reduced expectations for space exploration","A general reconsideration of human/robot responsibilities in space","Problems in using humans for space exploration","The danger to humans of intelligent machines","Space settlement and the development of greater self-awareness","Possible examples of cooperation in space"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56032","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nThe text has six paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"7361:56032:16","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"C段的主旨句是 \"It seems that all machines, even the smartest ones, must cooperate with humans.\" 段落讨论了机器人并未实现完全替代人类的预期，而是需要与人类协作。这段内容反映了对机器人在地球上作用的重新评估。","options":["Robots on Earth – a re-evaluation","The barriers to cooperation in space exploration","Some limitations of robots in space","Reduced expectations for space exploration","A general reconsideration of human/robot responsibilities in space","Problems in using humans for space exploration","The danger to humans of intelligent machines","Space settlement and the development of greater self-awareness","Possible examples of cooperation in space"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56032","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nThe text has six paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"7361:56032:17","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"D段的主旨句是 \"The human-machine relationship must evolve towards a closer collaboration.\" 段落讨论了人类与机器人在太空中的合作趋势，重新考量了人类和机器人在太空任务中的职责。这符合对人类和机器人责任重新思考的主题。","options":["Robots on Earth – a re-evaluation","The barriers to cooperation in space exploration","Some limitations of robots in space","Reduced expectations for space exploration","A general reconsideration of human/robot responsibilities in space","Problems in using humans for space exploration","The danger to humans of intelligent machines","Space settlement and the development of greater self-awareness","Possible examples of cooperation in space"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56032","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nThe text has six paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"7361:56032:18","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"E段主要描述了“火星前哨”计划，即在火星上建立机器人研究站，这些机器人设备会进行科学研究并搭建基础设施，为未来人类登陆火星做准备。这是一个人类和机器人合作的具体示例。","options":["Robots on Earth – a re-evaluation","The barriers to cooperation in space exploration","Some limitations of robots in space","Reduced expectations for space exploration","A general reconsideration of human/robot responsibilities in space","Problems in using humans for space exploration","The danger to humans of intelligent machines","Space settlement and the development of greater self-awareness","Possible examples of cooperation in space"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56032","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nThe text has six paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"7361:56032:19","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph F","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"F段的主旨句是 \"The result of exploring and living in space may be a deep change in the views which humankind has of itself.\" 段落讨论了人类在太空定居的未来愿景及其可能带来的自我意识提升。","options":["Robots on Earth – a re-evaluation","The barriers to cooperation in space exploration","Some limitations of robots in space","Reduced expectations for space exploration","A general reconsideration of human/robot responsibilities in space","Problems in using humans for space exploration","The danger to humans of intelligent machines","Space settlement and the development of greater self-awareness","Possible examples of cooperation in space"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"56032","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nThe text has six paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"7361:56033:20-21","type":"choice","text":"According to the writer, which TWO predictions about artificial intelligence have not yet been fulfilled?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"定位关键词： predictions, artificial intelligence\n对应原文： C段，The construction of machines simulating human logical reasoning moves towards ever more distant dates.The more the performance of computers improves, the more we realise how difficult it is to build machines which display logical abilities. 以及Rather than replacing humans, the present need appears to be for an intelligent machine capable of helping a human operator without replacing him or her.\n解题思路：C段指出，人工智能未能完全取代人类的事实，而是需要与人类合作。这段话说明尽管曾预测机器人将能够完全独立工作，但目前来看，它们仍然需要在任务中协助人类。同时，C段还指出，尽管人们最初预测机器人将能够像人类一样进行逻辑推理，但实现这一目标的日期变得越来越遥远，这表明机器人尚未达到人类的逻辑思维水平。但是，C段并未提到任何机器人会反对或威胁人类利益的内容，也没有相关推测或暗示。原文实际上提到机器人确实已经在协助人类完成任务，并且强调“当前需求”是机器人协助人类，而不是完全替代人类。并且并未提及机器人在太空任务中的成本问题。原文没有信息支持这一预测。","options":["Robots will work independently of humans.","Robots will begin to oppose human interests.","Robots will be used to help humans perform tasks more efficiently.","Robots will think in the same way as humans.","Robots will become too costly to use on space missions."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"56033","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 20 - 21\nChoose TWO correct answers.","groupId":"56033-7361:56033:20-21"},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"7361:56033:20-21","type":"choice","text":"According to the writer, which TWO predictions about artificial intelligence have not yet been fulfilled?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"定位关键词： predictions, artificial intelligence\n对应原文： C段，The construction of machines simulating human logical reasoning moves towards ever more distant dates.The more the performance of computers improves, the more we realise how difficult it is to build machines which display logical abilities. 以及Rather than replacing humans, the present need appears to be for an intelligent machine capable of helping a human operator without replacing him or her.\n解题思路：C段指出，人工智能未能完全取代人类的事实，而是需要与人类合作。这段话说明尽管曾预测机器人将能够完全独立工作，但目前来看，它们仍然需要在任务中协助人类。同时，C段还指出，尽管人们最初预测机器人将能够像人类一样进行逻辑推理，但实现这一目标的日期变得越来越遥远，这表明机器人尚未达到人类的逻辑思维水平。但是，C段并未提到任何机器人会反对或威胁人类利益的内容，也没有相关推测或暗示。原文实际上提到机器人确实已经在协助人类完成任务，并且强调“当前需求”是机器人协助人类，而不是完全替代人类。并且并未提及机器人在太空任务中的成本问题。原文没有信息支持这一预测。","options":["Robots will work independently of humans.","Robots will begin to oppose human interests.","Robots will be used to help humans perform tasks more efficiently.","Robots will think in the same way as humans.","Robots will become too costly to use on space missions."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"56033","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 20 - 21\nChoose TWO correct answers.","groupId":"56033-7361:56033:20-21"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"7361:56034:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"infrastructure","acceptedAnswers":["infrastructure"],"explanation":"定位信息： \"set up,\" \"do initial research,\" \"before humans arrive\"\n对应原文： E段, They would perform research, and establish the infrastructure needed to prepare future landing sites for the exploration of Mars by humans.\nE段指出机器人可以进行初步研究以及建设后续人类登陆火星进行探索所需的基础设施。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56034","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"7361:56034:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"spaceships","acceptedAnswers":["spaceships"],"explanation":"定位信息： \"humans could stay in orbiting,\" \"give orders to robots\"\n对应原文：  E段, It has also been suggested that in the most difficult environments, as on Venus or Jupiter, robots could be controlled by human beings located in spaceships which remain in orbit around the planet.\n详细解析： E段提到机器人可以由在轨道上的“spaceships”控制。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56034","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"7361:56034:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"communication","acceptedAnswers":["communication"],"explanation":"定位信息： \"increase the speed of,\" \"communication\"\n对应原文： E段, In this case the link time for communication between humans and robots would be far less than it would be from Earth.\n解题思路： 原文提到从轨道上与机器人通信的速度比从地球快。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56034","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"7361:56034:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"laboratories","acceptedAnswers":["laboratories"],"explanation":"定位信息：commercial enterprises\n对应原文：F段, But if space is to be more than a place to build automatic laboratories or set up industrial enterprises in the vicinity of our planet, the presence of humans is essential.\n解题思路： F段指出太空可以建立自动研究室或者工业企业。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56034","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"7361:56034:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"colonisation","acceptedAnswers":["colonisation"],"explanation":"定位信息： \"final aim,\" \"humankind,\" \"space\"\n对应原文：F段, So the aim for humankind in the future will be not just the exploration of space, but its colonisation.\n解题思路： F段指出人类在太空的最终目标是“殖民”（colonisation）。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56034","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"56033-7361:56033:20-21","numbers":[20,21],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["A","D"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"56032","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nThe text has six paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"56033","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 20 - 21\nChoose TWO correct answers.","html":"<p>According to the writer, which <strong>TWO</strong>&nbsp;predictions about artificial intelligence have not yet been fulfilled?</p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"56034","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>Humans in space –&nbsp;the Mars Outposts approach and its implications</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">One way of exploring space would be through collaboration between humans and robots. For example, when exploring the planet Mars, robots could be used to set up <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong>&nbsp;and do initial research before humans arrive. In other cases, humans could stay in orbiting <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong>&nbsp;and give orders to robots working on the surface of the planet.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">This would increase the speed of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> with the robots. In such ways, robots might be used to work in space in commercial enterprises or <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong>&nbsp;. However, the final aim of humankind may be the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong> of space and this could in turn change people&#39;s attitudes towards Earth.</p>","firstNumber":22}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>Should space be explored by robots or by humans</strong><o:p></o:p></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">#&amp;</span><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The advisability of humans participating directly in space travel continues to cause many debates. There is no doubt that the presence of people on board a space vehicle makes its design much more complex and challenging, and produces a large increase in costs, since safety requirements are greatly increased, and the technology providing necessities for human passengers such as oxygen, food water must be guaranteed. Moreover, the systems required are bulky and costly, and their complexity increases for long-duration missions. Meanwhile, advances in electronics and computer science allow increasingly complex tasks to be entrusted to robots, and unmanned space probes are becoming lighter, smaller and more convenient.<o:p></o:p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">#&amp;</span><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">However, experience has shown that the idea of humans in space is popular with the public. Humans can also be useful; there are many cases when only direct intervention by an astronaut or cosmonaut can correct the malfunction of an automatic device. Astronauts and cosmonauts have proved that they can adapt to conditions of weightlessness and work in space without encountering too many problems, as was seen in the operations to repair and to upgrade the Hubble Space Telescope. One human characteristic which is particularly precious in space missions, and which so far is lacking in robots, is the ability to perform a great variety of tasks. In addition, robots are not good at reacting to situations they have not been specifically prepared for. This is especially important in the case of deep space missions. While, in the case of the Moon, it is possible for someone on Earth to &#39;tele-operate&#39; a robotic device such as a probe, as the two-way link time is only a couple of seconds, on Mars the two- way link time is several minutes, so sending instructions from Earth is more difficult.<o:p></o:p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">#&amp;</span><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Many of the promises of artificial intelligence are still far from being fulfilled. The construction of machines simulating human logical reasoning moves towards ever more distant dates. The more the performance of computers improves, the more we realise how difficult it is to build machines which display logical abilities. In the past it was confidently predicted that we would soon have fully automated factories in which all operations were performed without any human intervention, and forecasts of the complete substitution of workers by robots in many production areas were made. Today, these perspectives are being revised. It seems that all machines, even the smartest ones, must cooperate with humans. Rather than replacing humans, the present need appears to be for an intelligent machine capable of helping a human operator without replacing him or her. The word &#39;cobot&#39;, from &#39;collaborative robot&#39;, has been invented to designate this type.<o:p></o:p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">#&amp;</span><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">A similar trend is also apparent in the field of space exploration. Tasks which were in the past entrusted only to machines are now performed by human beings, sometimes with the aim of using simpler and less costly devices, sometimes to obtain better performance. In many cases, to involve a person in the control loop is a welcome simplification which may lower the cost of a mission without compromising safety. Many operations originally designed to be performed under completely automatic control can be performed more efficiently by astronauts, perhaps helped by their &#39;cobots&#39;. The human-machine relationship must evolve towards a closer collaboration.<o:p></o:p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">#&amp;</span><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">One way this could happen is by adopting the Mars Outposts approach, proposed by the Shinyway Planetary Society. This would involve sending a number of robotic research stations to Mars, equipped with permanent communications and navigational systems. They would perform research, and establish the infrastructure needed to prepare future landing sites for the exploration of Mars by humans. It has also been suggested that in the most difficult environments, as on Venus or Jupiter, robots could be controlled by human beings located in spaceships which remain in orbit around the planet. In this case the link time for communication between humans and robots would be far less than it would be from Earth.<o:p></o:p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">#&amp;</span><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">But if space is to be more than a place to build automatic laboratories or set up industrial enterprises in the vicinity of our planet, the presence of humans is essential. They must learn how to voyage through space towards destinations which will be not only scientific bases but also places to live. If space is a frontier, that frontier must see the presence of people. So the aim for humankind in the future will be not just the exploration of space, but its colonisation. The result of exploring and living in space may be a deep change in the views which humankind has of itself. And this process is already under way. The images of Earth taken from the Moon in the Apollo programme have given humankind a new consciousness of its fragility, its smallness, and its unity. These impressions have triggered a realisation of the need to protect and preserve it, for it is the place in the solar system most suitable for US and above all it is the only place we have, at least for now.<span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><o:p></o:p></span><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">&amp;#</span></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7361&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7362","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Neanderthal Technology","book":"阅读还原集Vol.10","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test2","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.10 · Test2 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"7362:56028:27","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"定位信息：Section A\n对应原文：A段，We think of our prehistoric ancestors as people of the ice and snow, living in caves, and for many of the west European Neanderthalers that is a just picture of their life. But where there were no caves, further to the east on the Russian steppe, for example, open-air sites with some sort of constructed shelter were the only option.\n解题思路：A段指出，很多西欧尼安德特人居住在洞穴中，而在没有洞穴的东欧草原上，他们只能选择露天的临时住所。这形成了对两种不同类型住所的对比。","options":["Evidence of outdoor dwellings","Learning to make fire","A perfect place to live","Examining the cave contents","Contrasting two types of home","A vital source of power"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"56028","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nThe text has five sections. Choose the correct heading for each section and move it into the gap."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"7362:56028:28","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位信息：Section B\n对应原文：B段 ，In south-west France, the limestone caves of the Périgord region made ideal homes for the Neanderthal people.以及The Périgord region during the last ice age was, in fact, an exceptionally benign habitat for humans.\n解题思路：B段指出了Périgord地区的洞穴如何为尼安德特人提供理想的居住环境，包括天气、食物供应和安全保护。\n同义替换：perfect=ideal; place to live=habitat","options":["Evidence of outdoor dwellings","Learning to make fire","A perfect place to live","Examining the cave contents","Contrasting two types of home","A vital source of power"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"56028","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nThe text has five sections. Choose the correct heading for each section and move it into the gap."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"7362:56028:29","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"定位信息：Section C\n对应原文：C段，In Central and Eastern Europe, where caves were unavailable, such open-air sites as have been discovered were mostly located near water – both because this was a good area to be for people and animals, and also because the sedimentation potential of lakes and stream course has aided archaeological preservation – whereas erosion has presumably blown away sites which were out in the open. Some of the open-air sites in Germany, Central Europe and Russia have provided valuable information about Neanderthal man and his way of life.\n解题思路： C段指出了中欧和东欧地区发现的露天居住遗址，指出这些露天遗址为尼安德特人的生活方式提供了宝贵信息。段落内容主要强调了露天居所的存在证据。","options":["Evidence of outdoor dwellings","Learning to make fire","A perfect place to live","Examining the cave contents","Contrasting two types of home","A vital source of power"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"56028","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nThe text has five sections. Choose the correct heading for each section and move it into the gap."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"7362:56028:30","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"定位信息：Section D\n对应原文：D段全文\n解题思路：D段指出了法国Lazaret洞穴中的一些构造物，推测可能是皮制帐篷，并详细描述了大石块的排列方式可能用来支撑木头结构。这些内容显示了考古学家对洞穴内构造物的研究。","options":["Evidence of outdoor dwellings","Learning to make fire","A perfect place to live","Examining the cave contents","Contrasting two types of home","A vital source of power"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"56028","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nThe text has five sections. Choose the correct heading for each section and move it into the gap."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"7362:56028:31","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"定位信息：Section E\n对应原文：E段，The ash encountered in concentrations at some sites testifies to the Neanderthal people's use of fire: not surprising, since use of fire was, by Neanderthal times, an already ancient accomplishment of evolving humanity, and survival in the sub-arctic conditions faced by the Neanderthalers is inconceivable without control of fire.\n解题思路：E段指出了火对尼安德特人生活的重要性，特别是在寒冷条件下提供温暖、光亮、烹饪食物和防御掠食者的能力。段落强调了火作为一种“关键的生存力量”的重要性。\n同义替换：source of power=use of fire","options":["Evidence of outdoor dwellings","Learning to make fire","A perfect place to live","Examining the cave contents","Contrasting two types of home","A vital source of power"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"56028","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nThe text has five sections. Choose the correct heading for each section and move it into the gap."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"7362:56029:32","type":"choice","text":"32 a burnt piece of wood","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"定位信息：Krapina\n对应原文： E段，\"A charred piece of birch from Krapina in Croatiatzx, is thought to be the remains of a fire-making twirl stick. \"\n解题思路：E段指出在Krapina发现了一块烧焦的桦木，可能是取火用的工具。\n同义替换：burnt=charred","options":["The Périgord region","Moldova","The Grotte du Lazaret","The cave of Baume-Bonne","Krapina"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"56029","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32 - 36\nChoose the correct place, (A - E), for each finding. You may choose any correct place more than once.\nList of Places\nA The Périgord region\nB Moldova\nC The Grotte du Lazaret\nD The cave of Baume-Bonne\nE Krapina"},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"7362:56029:33","type":"choice","text":"33 evidence of efforts to prevent pools of water forming","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"定位信息： The cave of Baume-Bonne\n对应原文： D段：\"The cave of Baume-Bonne in the Basses-Alpes region of France, another early site, boasts ten square metres of cobbles brought up from the local river and laid down, as though to take care of a puddle area in the cave, with the smoothest and roundest surfaces of the stones uppermost, and there are other similar cases.\"\n解题思路：D段指出在Baume-Bonne洞穴中发现了鹅卵石，似乎是为了防止水坑的形成。\n同义替换：prevent pools of water forming=take care of a puddle area","options":["The Périgord region","Moldova","The Grotte du Lazaret","The cave of Baume-Bonne","Krapina"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"56029","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32 - 36\nChoose the correct place, (A - E), for each finding. You may choose any correct place more than once.\nList of Places\nA The Périgord region\nB Moldova\nC The Grotte du Lazaret\nD The cave of Baume-Bonne\nE Krapina"},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"7362:56029:34","type":"choice","text":"34 the remains of sea creatures","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位信息：The Grotte du Lazaret\n对应原文： D段，\"The two patches of ash at Lazaret that mark ancient fires, with stone tools around them evidently made and used on the spot, are edged with small marine molluse shells, prompting the excavator to suggest that seaweed had been used as bedding around the fires.\"\n解题思路：D段指出在Lazaret洞穴的灰烬旁发现了海洋软体动物的贝壳。\n同义替换：sea creatures=marine mollusc shells","options":["The Périgord region","Moldova","The Grotte du Lazaret","The cave of Baume-Bonne","Krapina"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"56029","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32 - 36\nChoose the correct place, (A - E), for each finding. You may choose any correct place more than once.\nList of Places\nA The Périgord region\nB Moldova\nC The Grotte du Lazaret\nD The cave of Baume-Bonne\nE Krapina"},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"7362:56029:35","type":"choice","text":"35 a circular arrangement of animal bones","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"定位信息： Moldova\n对应原文： C段：\"From Moldova, for example, comes evidence that has been interpreted as the remains of wind-break structures, or even a large tent: a ring, up to about 8 x 5m in size, of mainly mammoth bones enclosing a dense concentration of stone tools, animal bones and ash.\"\n解题思路：C段指出在Moldova发现的圆形猛犸骨排列。\n同义替换：circular arrangement=a ring","options":["The Périgord region","Moldova","The Grotte du Lazaret","The cave of Baume-Bonne","Krapina"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"56029","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32 - 36\nChoose the correct place, (A - E), for each finding. You may choose any correct place more than once.\nList of Places\nA The Périgord region\nB Moldova\nC The Grotte du Lazaret\nD The cave of Baume-Bonne\nE Krapina"},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"7362:56029:36","type":"choice","text":"36 evidence suggesting the use of animal fur for warmth","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位信息：The Grotte du Lazaret\n对应原文： D段：\" At Lazaret, what might be openings in the hypothesised tents seem to point away from the cave mouth, and finds of wolf and fox foot bones, without the rest of the skeletons, inside these 'tents' have been thought to indicate the use of animal pelts as bed coverings.\"\n解题思路：D段指出在Lazaret洞穴发现的狼和狐狸骨骼暗示动物皮毛被用作床上覆盖物。\n同义替换：fur=pelts","options":["The Périgord region","Moldova","The Grotte du Lazaret","The cave of Baume-Bonne","Krapina"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"56029","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32 - 36\nChoose the correct place, (A - E), for each finding. You may choose any correct place more than once.\nList of Places\nA The Périgord region\nB Moldova\nC The Grotte du Lazaret\nD The cave of Baume-Bonne\nE Krapina"},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"7362:56030:37","type":"fill","text":"填写第 37 空","answer":"sub-arctic","acceptedAnswers":["sub-arctic"],"explanation":"定位信息： survived without fire,conditions\n对应原文： E段，\"The ash encountered in concentrations at some sites testifies to the Neanderthal people's use of fire: not surprising, since use of fire was, by Neanderthal times, an already ancient accomplishment of evolving humanity, and survival in the sub-arctic conditions faced by the Neanderthalers is inconceivable without control of fire.\"\n解题思路：E段指出尼安德特人生活在“sub-arctic”条件下，没有火是无法生存的。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56030","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 37 - 39\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"7362:56030:38","type":"fill","text":"填写第 38 空","answer":"short","acceptedAnswers":["short"],"explanation":"定位信息： ash piles,fires lasted\n对应原文： E段：\"Judging from the shallow penetration of heat effects under the ash, this fire was only of a short duration.\"\n解题思路：E段指出这些火焰持续的时间是短暂的。\n同义替换：a short time=short duration","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56030","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 37 - 39\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"7362:56030:39","type":"fill","text":"填写第 39 空","answer":"predatory animals","acceptedAnswers":["predatory animals"],"explanation":"定位信息： protect from dangerous,animals\n对应原文： E段：\"Fire gave warmth, light, heat for cooking and defence against predatory animals.\"\n解题思路：E段指出火的用途之一是防御掠食性动物。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"56030","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 37 - 39\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"7362:56031:40","type":"choice","text":"The purpose of the writer of this article is to","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位信息: purpose of the writer\n对应原文:A段， We now know much more about the cave sites than the open-air ones because, historically, it was the cave sites of Western Europe that were first explored by archaeologists and also because open-air sites are harder to find-many of them have disappeared under deep mud deposits or under the rising postglacial seas.\nB段，In south-west France, the limestone caves of the Périgord region made ideal homes for the Neanderthal people.\nC段，In Central and Eastern Europe, where caves were unavailable, such open-air sites as have been discovered were mostly located near water – both because this was a good area to be for people and animals, and also because the sedimentation potential of lakes and stream course has aided archaeological preservation – whereas erosion has presumably blown away sites which were out in the open.\nD段，From the west European caves more evidence of built structures is available, and some of it goes back a long way in time .\nE段，The ash encountered in concentrations at some sites testifies to the Neanderthal people's use of fire: not surprising, since use of fire was, by Neanderthal times, an already ancient accomplishment of evolving humanity, and survival in the sub-arctic conditions faced by the Neanderthalers is inconceivable without control of fire.\n解题思路：文章主要探讨了尼安德特人的住所形态，包括西欧的洞穴住所（A段和B段）和中东欧的露天住所（C段），并补充了与居住相关的考古发现（D段）以及生活方式的细节（E段）这些讨论都集中在展示当前关于尼安德特人定居点的已知信息，而非关注住所大小、迁移原因或发展过程。","options":["argue that Neanderthal homes were bigger than originally thought.","explain why Neanderthal people migrated to Western Europe.","discuss what is known about Neanderthal settlements.","track the progress of early Neanderthal development."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"56031","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 40\nChoose the correct answer."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"56028","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nThe text has five sections. Choose the correct heading for each section and move it into the gap.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"56029","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 32 - 36\nChoose the correct place, (A - E), for each finding. You may choose any correct place more than once.\nList of Places\nA The Périgord region\nB Moldova\nC The Grotte du Lazaret\nD The cave of Baume-Bonne\nE Krapina","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"56030","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 37 - 39\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The use of fire</strong></p><p>Neanderthalers could not have survived without fire because the conditions they lived in were&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[37] ____</strong>&nbsp;.&nbsp;Most evidence of purpose-built fires takes the form of ash piles, features of which suggest that the fires lasted a <strong class=\"source-blank\">[38] ____</strong>&nbsp;time. It is hard to be certain about the size and structure of the fires, though they were certainly needed to protect the occupants from dangerous <strong class=\"source-blank\">[39] ____</strong>&nbsp;among other things.</p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"56031","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 40\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>The purpose of the writer of this article is to</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>Neanderthal Technology</strong><o:p></o:p></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">#&amp;</span><strong>A</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">We think of our prehistoric ancestors as people of the ice and snow, living in caves, and for many of the west European Neanderthalers that is a just picture of their life. But where there were no caves, further to&nbsp;the east on the Russian steppe, for example, open-air sites with some sort of constructed shelter were the only option.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">We now know much more about the cave sites than the open-air ones because, historically, it was the cave sites of Western Europe that were first explored by archaeologists and also because open-air sites are harder to find-many of them have disappeared under deep mud deposits or under the rising postglacial seas. Caves, moreover, aid the survival of archaeological material and can preserve the records of remote millennia.<o:p></o:p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255);\">#&amp;</span><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">In south-west France, the limestone caves of the Périgord region made ideal homes for the Neanderthal people. There were good supplies of flint to hand for axes and the like, and the caves were often sited in small river valleys that offered protection against the worst of the weather. The Neanderthalers liked south-facing caves, for obvious reasons of sunshine and wind avoidance, and caves at some height above the valley floor offered refuge from floods and good game-watching vantage.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The Périgord region during the last ice age was, in fact, an exceptionally benign habitat for humans. It enjoyed a rather maritime climate with cooler summers that permitted the extension of tundra and steppe over its higher plateaux, and its year-round high levels of sunshine favoured the growth of the ground plants needed by reindeer, bison and horse. Winters were mildish for the ice age, animals never needed to migrate far from summer to winter, and men never needed to travel far from home to find abundant supplies of meat.<o:p></o:p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">&amp;#</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">#&amp;</span><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">In Central and Eastern Europe, where caves were unavailable, such open-air sites as have been discovered were mostly located near water – both because this was a good area to be for people and animals, and also because the sedimentation potential of lakes and stream course has aided archaeological preservation – whereas erosion has presumably blown away sites which were out in the open.&nbsp;Some of the open-air sites in Germany, Central Europe and Russia have provided valuable information about Neanderthal man and his way of life.&nbsp;From Moldova, for example, comes evidence that has been interpreted as the remains of wind-break structures, or even a large tent:&nbsp;a&nbsp;ring, up to about 8 x 5m in size, of mainly mammoth bones enclosing a dense concentration of stone tools, animal bones and ash.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">#&amp;</span><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">From the west European caves more evidence of built structures is available, and some of it goes back a long way in time&nbsp;.In the Grotte du Lazaret, near Nice, at a date during the last ice age but one, claims for some sort of skin tent within the cave have been advanced, on the basis of arrangements of large stones out from the cave wall that might have supported timber struts for a covering of skins up to the rock face above.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">At Lazaret, what might be openings in the hypothesised tents seem to point away from the cave mouth, and finds of wolf and fox foot bones, without the rest of the skeletons, inside these&nbsp;&#39;tents&#39;&nbsp;have been thought to indicate the use of animal pelts as bed coverings.&nbsp;The two patches of ash at Lazaret that mark ancient fires, with stone tools around them evidently made and used on the spot, are edged with small marine molluse shells, prompting the excavator to suggest that seaweed had been used as bedding around the fires. The cave of Baume-Bonne in the Basses-Alpes region of France, another early site, boasts ten square metres of cobbles brought up from the local river and laid down, as though to take care of a puddle area in the cave, with the smoothest and roundest surfaces of the stones uppermost, and there are other similar cases.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(64, 158, 255); font-size: 16px;\">#&amp;</span><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The ash encountered in concentrations at some sites testifies to the Neanderthal people&#39;s use of fire: not surprising, since use of fire was, by Neanderthal times, an already ancient accomplishment of evolving humanity, and survival in the sub-arctic conditions faced by the Neanderthalers is inconceivable without control of fire. Fire gave warmth, light, heat for cooking and defence against predatory animals.&nbsp;A charred piece of birch from Krapina in Croatiatzx, is thought to be the remains of a fire-making twirl stick. But Neanderthal hearths, in the sense of specially constructed places for fire, are fewer and harder to identify with certainty than the mere ash piles that are a regular feature of their sites. They seem often to have just lit a small fire (40-50cm across)&nbsp;on the existing ground surface of the cave, without preparation. Judging from the shallow penetration of heat effects under the ash, this fire was only of a short duration. Sometimes the fires were larger in size, up to one metre across, and quite irregular in shape. It is not always easy to&nbsp;decide how much additional structure some fires possessed: claims of stone circles to contain the fire run up against the fact that stones tend to litter the cave floors everywhere and those around a fire can quite accidentally look as though they were arranged in a circle.<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 158, 255); text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&amp;#</span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7362&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7212","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 The Clipper Races: an era of competition between cargo ships","book":"阅读还原集Vol.10","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test1","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.10 · Test1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"7212:55594:1","type":"choice","text":"In the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries, the British East India Company faced a lot of competition.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问英国东印度公司在17和18世纪是否面临大量竞争。\n定位关键信息： “seventeenth and eighteenth centuries”、“competition”。\n对应原文：A段，“During the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries, the British East India Company had the monopoly on trade with China and India. This meant that because no rival could legally import tea or other goods from these countries at this time, the company was rarely in a hurry to transport its merchandise.”\n解题思路：A段指出，英国东印度公司对与中国和印度的贸易拥有垄断权，并且当时没有竞争对手可以合法地从这些国家进口茶叶或其他商品，因此说明它并没有面临竞争。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55594","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"7212:55595:2","type":"choice","text":"Before 1800, cargo size was the most important consideration for the East India Company.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问1800年前东印度公司最重要的考虑是否是货物的大小。\n定位关键信息： “before 1800”、“cargo size”。\n对应原文：A段，“ Instead, its priority was to minimise costs by carrying as much as possible on each ship. ”\n解题思路：A段指出公司优先考虑的是减少成本，而尽可能多地携带货物是实现这一目的的方法，而不是优先考虑货物的大小、尺寸。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55595","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"7212:55596:3","type":"choice","text":"At best, voyages of the East Indiamen to China and back took nearly two years to complete.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问东印度公司的船到中国往返是否需要将近两年。\n定位关键信息： “two years”、“to China and back”。\n对应原文：B段，“The trading pattern for China tea usually meant the East Indiamen set sail from Britain in January, sailed round the Cape of Good Hope at the southernmost tip of Africa, and arrived in China in September. There they would load up that year's tea harvest, set off again and, depending on the wind and weather, aim to arrive back by the following September, so even with favourable sailing conditions, the round trip lasted almost two years, and if anything went wrong it could take lot longer.”\n解题思路：B段指出在航行条件最好的情况下，往返需要将近两年。如果如果出了什么差错，可能要花更长的时间。\n同义替换：nearly = almost","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55596","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"7212:55597:4","type":"choice","text":"Before 1834, voyages to and from China were considered to be highly dangerous.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问1834年之前，往返中国的航行是否被认为非常危险。\n定位关键信息： “before 1834”、“dangerous”。\n对应原文：C段，However, by 1834 the company had lost its trading monopoles, and tea had become a freely traded item.\n解题思路：C段指出到1834年，该公司失去了贸易垄断权，茶叶成为一种自由交易的商品，没有相关信息提及航行是否危险。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55597","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"7212:55598:5","type":"choice","text":"After 1834, the ships which had served the East India Company stopped being used for commercial purposes.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问1834年后，曾服务东印度公司的船是否停止了商业用途。\n定位关键信息： “after 1834”、“stopped being used for commercial purposes”。\n对应原文：C段，“Having no more use for its great ships, the company sold them off, and many were bought by merchants or their captains, who continued to plough the seas between Britain and China.”\n解题思路：C段指出这些船在被商人购买后继续进行贸易。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55598","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"7212:55599:6","type":"choice","text":"In the nineteen century, British drinkers preferred tea made from mature leaves to that made from younger leaves.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问19世纪时英国饮茶者是否更喜欢用成熟叶子制成的茶。\n定位关键信息： “nineteen century”、“preferred”、“mature leaves”。\n对应原文：D段，“This was partly because if you were home first, you could sell your shipment of tea before your competitors even arrived, and partly because consumers in Britain in the nineteenth century believed that the fresher and earlier-picked the tea, the better the resulting drink.”\n解题思路：D段指出英国消费者更喜欢新鲜的、早采摘的茶。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55599","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"7212:55600:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"sails","acceptedAnswers":["sails"],"explanation":"定位关键词：remarkable for, number\n对应原文：E段，\"These vessels were fast and slender, with a narrow hull that was deeper at the back than at the front, and masses of sails on tall masts.\"\n解题思路：E段指出\"masses of sails\"表示\"大量的帆\"，说明它们以帆的数量著称。\n同义替换：ships=vessels","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55600","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"7212:55601:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"storms","acceptedAnswers":["storms"],"explanation":"定位关键词：performance, British tea clippers, affected, at sea\n对应原文：E段，\"More tea clippers were designed and built in Britain throughout the 1850s and 1860s; they had a narrower beam than their American equivalents, making them less powerful during storms, but faster in calmer weather.\"\n解题思路：D段指出，在风暴期间，英国茶船因较窄的船体表现较差。说明风暴（storms）对其表现有影响。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55601","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"7212:55602:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"Challenger","acceptedAnswers":["Challenger"],"explanation":"定位关键词：ship, British, first competed successfully\n对应原文：F段， \"Then in 1851 a British ship owner, Richard Green, built the aptly named clipper Challenger with the stated intention of beating the American ships. \"\n解题思路：E段指出 Challenger 是为了击败美国船而建造的，并且首次成功。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55602","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"7212:55603:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"ports","acceptedAnswers":["ports"],"explanation":"定位关键词：competition increased, Chinese trading\n对应原文：G段，\"But even without the Anglo-American rivalry, the competitive spirit continued. It was really ignited when new ports were opened up for trade in China.\"\n解题思路：F段指出，当中国的新港口开放后，竞争加剧。\n同义替换：established=opened up","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55603","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"7212:55604:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"paperwork","acceptedAnswers":["paperwork"],"explanation":"定位关键词：merchants, hurry, failed to complete\n对应原文：G段，\"As a result, tea could be loaded on board earlier and fresher, and the clippers could set off in late May or early June – sometimes not even taking time to fill out the official paperwork – racing back to Britain whatever the difficulties.\"\n解题思路：G段指出他们有时连官方的文件（paperwork）都没有时间填写。\n同义替换：failed to complete=not even taking time to fill out","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55604","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"7212:55605:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"tugs","acceptedAnswers":["tugs"],"explanation":"定位关键词：end of journey, ships, help of\n对应原文：H段，\"Once there, they would be towed by tugs, up the river and into the docks.\"\n解题思路：H段指出船只会被拖船 (tugs) 拖进港口。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55605","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"7212:55606:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"premium/money","acceptedAnswers":["premium","money"],"explanation":"定位关键词：crews, motivated by, enthusiasm\n对应原文：I段，\"The cargo of the winning ship could earn premium of up to sixpence per pound – and so the captain and crew were rewarded by the owners of the cargo.\"\n解题思路：I段指出，船员不仅因奖金（premium，也就是钱）和他们对比赛的热情而受到激励。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55606","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"55594","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>In the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries, the British East India Company faced a lot of competition.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"55595","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Before 1800, cargo size was the most important consideration for the East India Company.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"55596","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>At best, voyages of the East Indiamen to China and back took nearly two years to complete.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"55597","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Before 1834, voyages to and from China were considered to be highly dangerous.</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"55598","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>After 1834, the ships which had served the East India Company stopped being used for commercial purposes.</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"55599","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>In the nineteen century, British drinkers preferred tea made from mature leaves to that made from younger leaves.</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"55600","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>Clipper races</strong></p><p><strong>The ships</strong></p><p>•&nbsp;Clipper ships were first used for trading by American merchants.</p><p>•&nbsp;The ships were remarkable for the number of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong>&nbsp;they had.</p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"55601","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>•&nbsp;The performance of British tea clippers was particularly affected when there were <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong>&nbsp;at sea.</p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"55602","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>The races</strong></p><p>•&nbsp;It was in a ship called <strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong>&nbsp;that the British first competed successfully against the Americans.</p><p>•&nbsp;Richard Green&#39;s ship arrived two days ahead of its competitor.</p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"55603","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>•&nbsp;Competition increased when additional Chinese trading <strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong>&nbsp;were established.</p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"55604","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>•&nbsp;Merchants were occasionally in such a hurry that they failed to complete the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong>&nbsp;before leaving China.</p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"55605","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>•&nbsp;At the end of their journey, the ships needed the help of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong>.</p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"55606","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>The rewards</strong></p><p>•&nbsp;The crews were motivated by both <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong>&nbsp;and their enthusiasm for the competition.</p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>The Clipper Races:&nbsp;an era of competition between cargo ships</strong><o:p></o:p></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">During the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries, the British East India Company had the monopoly on trade with China and India. This meant that because no rival could legally import tea or other goods from these countries at this time, the company was rarely in a hurry to transport its merchandise. Instead, its priority was to minimise costs by carrying as much as possible on each ship. This meant that its ships – known as East Indiamen – were enormous, strong and very slow.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">By 1800, the average East Indiaman could carry 1,200 tons of merchandise. The trading pattern for China tea usually meant the East Indiamen set sail from Britain in January, sailed round the Cape of Good Hope at the southernmost tip of Africa, and arrived in China in September. There they would load up that year&#39;s tea harvest, set off again and, depending on the wind and weather, aim to arrive back by the following September, so even with favourable sailing conditions, the round trip lasted almost two years, and if anything went wrong it could take lot longer.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">However, by 1834 the company had lost its trading monopoles, and tea had become a freely traded item. Having no more use for its great ships, the company sold them off, and many were&nbsp;bought by merchants or their captains, who continued to plough the seas between Britain and China. But now that tea could be traded freely,&nbsp;a few smart sailors began to realise that whoever brought each new harvest of tea to Britain first, stood to make the most money.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">This was partly because if you were home first, you could sell your shipment of tea before your competitors even arrived, and partly because consumers in Britain in the nineteenth century believed that the fresher and earlier-picked the tea, the better the resulting drink. Tea traders&nbsp;now needed faster, sleeker ships to bring their precious cargo back. Nevertheless, in Britain this idea only caught on slowly, and while the 1840s saw a few faster ships launched, for the time being many merchants remained satisfied with the slow but reliable East Indiamen.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">In fact it was the Americans who pioneered the first clipper ships. These vessels were fast and slender, with a narrow hull that was deeper at the back than at the front, and masses of sails on tall masts. They earned their name from the way that they &#39;clipped off&#39; journey time. British merchants resolved to build their own clippers to rival the Americans, and the first British tea clipper, Shinyway, was built in Aberdeen in 1850. More tea clippers were designed and built in Britain throughout the 1850s and 1860s; they had a narrower beam than their American equivalents, making them less powerful during storms, but faster in calmer weather.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">There was a great spirit of competition between the British and American ships plying the tea trade, but to begin with the Americans had the edge. Then in 1851 a British ship owner, Richard Green, built the aptly named clipper Challenger&nbsp;with the stated intention of beating the American ships. Loaded with tea, Challenger&nbsp;left China for London in 1852 at the same time as the American clipper Challenge,&nbsp;a much larger older ship, already greatly admired for its speed.&nbsp;Large sums were bet on which would complete the journey first. In the event, the British ship beat its rival to London by two days, amid much jubilation. From then on, such international races grew in popularity.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">After 1855, American participation in the British tea trade gradually stopped. But even without the Anglo-American rivalry, the competitive spirit continued. It was really ignited when new ports were opened up for trade in China. These included Fouchow, which was much closer to the tea-producing areas than Canton, the port used previously. As a result, tea could be loaded on board earlier and fresher, and the clippers could set off in late May or early June –&nbsp;sometimes not even taking time to fill out the official paperwork – racing back to Britain whatever the difficulties.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">They sped down through the South China Sea and into the Indian Ocean, then raced to get round the southernmost tip of Africa at the Cape of Good Hope. Then it was north across the vast Atlantic, past the Azores, through the English Channel and into the estuary of the River Thames. Once there, they would be towed by tugs, up the river and into the docks.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>I</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The cargo of the winning ship could earn premium of up to sixpence per pound – and so the&nbsp;captain and crew were rewarded by the owners of the cargo. But the races were about more than just money: the crews, about 40 men on each clipper, were expert sailors, proud of their ships, and they delighted in competing against each other. Without their enthusiasm, the races would never have happened, since home as fast as possible required the crew to be totally dedicated and to sacrifice much of their rest for the duration of the race.</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7212&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7213","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Orientation of birds","book":"阅读还原集Vol.10","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test1","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.10 · Test1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"7213:55611:14","type":"fill","text":"填写第 14 空","answer":"visual memory","acceptedAnswers":["visual memory"],"explanation":"审题:  鸟类依赖它们复杂的什么来找到巢穴？\n定位关键词: sophisticated，rely，first type\n对应原文:  C段，In the first type, birds methodically explore the area in which they are released until they pick up some familiar feature, and then they quickly find their way back to the nest. Such birds possess a highly developed visual memory, as experiments with pigeons have shown.\n解题思路:  C段指出, 在第一种类型中，鸟类有条不紊地探索它们被释放的区域，直到它们掌握了一些熟悉的特征，然后它们迅速找到返回巢穴的路。这类鸟类拥有高度发达的视觉记忆。因此第一种类型的鸟类依赖他们的记忆来寻找巢穴。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55611","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"7213:55612:15","type":"fill","text":"填写第 15 空","answer":"migration direction","acceptedAnswers":["migration direction"],"explanation":"审题:  鸟类选择它们习惯的什么来进行飞行？\n定位关键词: accustomed，second type\n对应原文: D段，The second type of homing behaviour is shown by birds that are capable of choosing their flight direction and holding to it for the rest of their journey. How do they decide what direction to take They appear to choose their normal migration direction even if they are released in a different place from their usual starting point.\n解题思路:D段指出, 第二种归巢行为表现在鸟类能够选择飞行方向，并在剩下的旅程中一直保持这个方向。即使在不同的地方被释放，它们似乎也会选择一直以来已经习惯的迁徙方向。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55612","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"7213:55612:16","type":"fill","text":"填写第 16 空","answer":"destination","acceptedAnswers":["destination"],"explanation":"审题:  由于这一行为，它们可能会错过它们的什么？\n定位关键词: miss，second type\n对应原文: D段，If, for example, birds which normally fly to the north-east to reach latitude 45 degrees north are released at that latitude, they will immediately start flying north-east anyway. So if they're release further to the west, they maintain the correct direction, but fly west of their destination, and so fail to arrive.\n解题思路:D段指出, 通常往东北飞到北纬45度的鸟类，在那个纬度被释放，它们无论如何都会立即开始往东北飞。因此，如果它们被释放到更远的西部，它们保持正确的方向，但飞向目的地的西部，因此会错过目的地而无法到达。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55612","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"7213:55613:17","type":"fill","text":"填写第 17 空","answer":"landmarks","acceptedAnswers":["landmarks"],"explanation":"审题:  即使它们在一个陌生的地方被释放，并且没有什么可以利用，它们也能正确定向。\n定位关键词:an unfamiliar place，make use of，third type\n对应原文:  E段，This is a perfect example of the third type of homing, for the albatross clearly couldn't rely on any landmarks over the vast expanse of the Pacific Ocean.\n解题思路:  E段指出, 第三种归巢行为表现出最高程度的定向能力。这种鸟类在陌生的环境，无法依赖 landmarks（地标）进行定向，也能成功归巢。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55613","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"7213:55613:18","type":"fill","text":"填写第 18 空","answer":"laysan albatross/albatross","acceptedAnswers":["laysan albatross","albatross"],"explanation":"审题: 具有这种技能的鸟类之一是什么？\n定位关键词: with this type of skill\n对应原文: E段，In one example, a laysan albatross returned to its nesting area on Midway Island in the middle of the Pacific having flown over 5000 kilometres from the west coast of the USA in just over ten days.\n解题思路:E段指出, 具有这种归巢技能的鸟类之一是albatross（信天翁）。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55613","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"7213:55614:19","type":"fill","text":"19 the effects of distance on some birds' ability to find their nests","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题: 哪个段落提到距离对一些鸟类找到巢穴的能力的影响。\n定位关键词: distance，ability，effects\n对应原文: C段，If the birds are transported 800 kilometres from their nest, it is only by good fortune that they find their way back as a result of long exploratory flights.\n解题思路:C段指出, 如果这些鸟被运送到离巢800公里远的地方，它们能找到回来的路只有靠运气。这段话说明了距离对鸟类归巢的影响。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55614","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19 - 22\nLook at the eight paragraphs (A - H). Which paragraph contains the following information? You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"7213:55614:20","type":"fill","text":"20 a methodology for testing the general ability of birds to find their nests","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题: 哪个段落提到来用于测试鸟类找到巢穴的一般能力的方法。\n定位关键词: methodology，testing，ability\n对应原文:  B段，Birds are caught at a time when they show an attachment to their territory, especially during the nesting season. They are taken to some spot, released, and the percentage of returns is recorded.\n解题思路:B段指出, 鸟类在表现出对领地的依恋时被捕获，尤其是在筑巢季节。他们被带到某个地点，释放，并记录回报率。这段话描述了测试鸟类归巢能力的方法。\n同义替换：find their nests = attachment to their territory","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55614","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19 - 22\nLook at the eight paragraphs (A - H). Which paragraph contains the following information? You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"7213:55614:21","type":"fill","text":"21 one aspect of physical ability in humans and birds","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题: 哪个段落讲述了人类和鸟类在某些身体能力上的对比。\n定位关键词: physical ability，humans and birds\n对应原文: C段，Birds' eyes have a power of resolution two to three times greater than ours, enabling them to pick up very fine details. If a bird uses only this type of homing behaviour, however, it can only succeed if the point of release is not too far away.\n解题思路:C段指出, 鸟类眼睛的分辨能力是人类的两到三倍。这段话描述了人类和鸟类的视力对比。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55614","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19 - 22\nLook at the eight paragraphs (A - H). Which paragraph contains the following information? You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"7213:55614:22","type":"fill","text":"22 how some birds' migration was delayed for experimental purposes","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"审题: 哪个段落提到了鸟类迁徙因实验而被推迟的情况。\n定位关键词: migration，delayed，experimental purposes\n对应原文: G段，Schüz caught first-year European storks and released them later, after the departure of the adult storks at a time when they normally make their south-west autumn migration to Africa.\n解题思路:  G段指出, Schüz捕获了一岁的欧洲鹳，并在成年鹳离开后将它们放生。这段话描述了实验中延迟了白鹳的迁徙。\n同义替换：delayed=  later","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55614","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19 - 22\nLook at the eight paragraphs (A - H). Which paragraph contains the following information? You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"7213:55615:23","type":"choice","text":"23 domestic pigeon","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位关键词: domestic pigeon\n对应原文: C段，Domestic pigeons have been trained to peck at a certain point on an aerial photograph, with a system of rewards, and four years later the birds were still able to respond to this training when placed on the aerial photograph.\n解题思路:C段指出, 驯养的鸽子被训练去啄航拍照片上的某一点，并有奖励制度。说明家鸽展示了记住以前见过的事物的能力。","options":["an ability to orientate without previous training","the speed at which birds fly","the ability to remember things seen previously","the effect of age on homing ability","the strength required to fly a great distance","a high success rate in finding nests","the importance of seasonal cues for migrating birds"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"55615","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 23 - 26\nChoose the correct point which the author wishes to illustrate, (A - G), for each type of bird.\nList of points which author wishes to illustrate\nA an ability to orientate without previous training\nB the speed at which birds fly\nC the ability to remember things seen previously\nD the effect of age on homing ability\nE the strength required to fly a great distance\nF a high success rate in finding nests\nG the importance of seasonal cues for migrating birds"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"7213:55615:24","type":"choice","text":"24 alpine swift","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"审题:  高山雨燕展示了哪种能力？\n定位关键词: alpine swift\n对应原文: F段，Great migrants such as the swift have the highest percentage of returns. In one case, seven out of nine alpine swifts were recaptured at their nests.\n解题思路:  F段指出, 高山雨燕（swift）的返巢率最高。在一个案例中，九只高山雨燕中有七只在它们的巢穴中被重新捕获。","options":["an ability to orientate without previous training","the speed at which birds fly","the ability to remember things seen previously","the effect of age on homing ability","the strength required to fly a great distance","a high success rate in finding nests","the importance of seasonal cues for migrating birds"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"55615","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 23 - 26\nChoose the correct point which the author wishes to illustrate, (A - G), for each type of bird.\nList of points which author wishes to illustrate\nA an ability to orientate without previous training\nB the speed at which birds fly\nC the ability to remember things seen previously\nD the effect of age on homing ability\nE the strength required to fly a great distance\nF a high success rate in finding nests\nG the importance of seasonal cues for migrating birds"},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"7213:55615:25","type":"choice","text":"25 European stork","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题:  欧洲白鹳展示了哪种能力？\n定位关键词: European stork\n对应原文: G段，Schuz caught first-year European storks and released them later, after the departure of the adult storks at a time when they normally make their south-west autumn migration to Africa. The recaptures showed that, in spite of the fact that there were no adults to guide them, the birds unanimously headed south-west.\n解题思路:G段指出, 重新捕获的结果表明，尽管没有成年鸟来引导它们，但这些鸟一致向西南方向飞去。说明白鹳展示了天生的方向感。","options":["an ability to orientate without previous training","the speed at which birds fly","the ability to remember things seen previously","the effect of age on homing ability","the strength required to fly a great distance","a high success rate in finding nests","the importance of seasonal cues for migrating birds"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"55615","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 23 - 26\nChoose the correct point which the author wishes to illustrate, (A - G), for each type of bird.\nList of points which author wishes to illustrate\nA an ability to orientate without previous training\nB the speed at which birds fly\nC the ability to remember things seen previously\nD the effect of age on homing ability\nE the strength required to fly a great distance\nF a high success rate in finding nests\nG the importance of seasonal cues for migrating birds"},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"7213:55615:26","type":"choice","text":"26 starling","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题: 椋鸟展示了哪种能力？\n定位关键词: starling\n对应原文: H段，Birds that were shifted to the south-east of their normal migration route split into two lots. The adults, in full possession of their gift for orientation, found their wintering area by modifying their direction by 90 degrees, whereas the juveniles sought their winter quarters to the south-east of their real position.\n解题思路:  H段指出, 被转移到正常迁徙路线东南方向的鸟类被分成两组。成年企鹅完全拥有方向感，通过将方向调整90度来找到它们的越冬区，而幼企鹅则在它们实际位置的东南方向寻找它们的越冬区。椋鸟展示了年龄对归巢能力的影响。","options":["an ability to orientate without previous training","the speed at which birds fly","the ability to remember things seen previously","the effect of age on homing ability","the strength required to fly a great distance","a high success rate in finding nests","the importance of seasonal cues for migrating birds"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"55615","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 23 - 26\nChoose the correct point which the author wishes to illustrate, (A - G), for each type of bird.\nList of points which author wishes to illustrate\nA an ability to orientate without previous training\nB the speed at which birds fly\nC the ability to remember things seen previously\nD the effect of age on homing ability\nE the strength required to fly a great distance\nF a high success rate in finding nests\nG the importance of seasonal cues for migrating birds"}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"55611","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>Types of homing behaviour</strong></p><p>First type:</p><p>Birds rely on their sophisticated <strong class=\"source-blank\">[14] ____</strong>&nbsp;. However, they are generally most successful if they are released within their feeding territory.</p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"55612","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p>Second type:</p><p>Birds select their accustomed <strong class=\"source-blank\">[15] ____</strong>&nbsp;, no matter where they are released. As a result, they may miss their <strong class=\"source-blank\">[16] ____</strong>&nbsp;.</p>","firstNumber":15},{"id":"55613","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p>Third type:</p><p>Birds orientate correctly, even when they are released in an unfamiliar place and have no <strong class=\"source-blank\">[17] ____</strong>&nbsp;to make use of. One bird with this type of skill is the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[18] ____</strong>&nbsp;.</p>","firstNumber":17},{"id":"55614","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19 - 22\nLook at the eight paragraphs (A - H). Which paragraph contains the following information? You may choose any letter more than once.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"55615","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 23 - 26\nChoose the correct point which the author wishes to illustrate, (A - G), for each type of bird.\nList of points which author wishes to illustrate\nA an ability to orientate without previous training\nB the speed at which birds fly\nC the ability to remember things seen previously\nD the effect of age on homing ability\nE the strength required to fly a great distance\nF a high success rate in finding nests\nG the importance of seasonal cues for migrating birds","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":23}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>Orientation of birds</strong><o:p></o:p></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">For many of us, the way birds are able to orientate is&nbsp;both astounding and difficult to appreciate fully. For instance, the annual migration of the golden plover of the Pacific takes it from Alaska to Hawaii on a flight of well over 3000 kilometres, and if it were to deviate by only one degree, it would miss the island on which it nests.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The first systematic studies on orientation in birds were made possible by the &#39;homing instinct&#39; exhibited by so many species. Birds are caught at a time when they show an attachment to their territory, especially during the nesting season. They are taken to some spot, released, and the percentage of returns is recorded. The distance can be varied, and the direction, as well as the method of transporting them, and then the influence of climatic and other factors on their ability to find their way home can be studied. These experiments have shown a wide variation in ability to home, and three types of homing behaviour have been identified.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">In the first type, birds methodically explore the area in which they are released until they pick up some familiar feature, and then they quickly find their way back to the nest.&nbsp;Such birds possess a highly developed visual memory, as experiments with pigeons have shown. Domestic pigeons have been trained to peck at a certain point on an aerial photograph, with a system of rewards, and four years later the birds were still able to&nbsp;respond to this training when placed on the aerial photograph. Birds&#39; eyes have a power&nbsp;of resolution two to three times greater than ours, enabling them to pick up very fine details. If a bird uses only this type of homing behaviour, however, it can only succeed if the point of release is not too far away. If the birds are transported 800 kilometres from their nest, it is only by good fortune that they find their way back as a result of long exploratory flights. Usually, the area known to a bird is its feeding territory. Released within this area, the birds soon make their return; release them outside it and far fewer return. However, if a bird is released for a second time in the same place, its visual memory comes into play, and the bird, no longer requiring tedious exploratory flights, will return much more quickly.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The second type of homing behaviour is shown by birds that are capable of choosing their flight direction and holding to it for the rest of their journey. How do they decide what direction to take They appear to choose their normal migration direction even if they are released in a different place from their usual starting point. If, for example, birds which normally fly to the north-east to reach latitude 45 degrees north are released at that latitude, they will immediately start flying north-east anyway. So if they&#39;re released further to the west, they maintain the correct direction, but fly west of their destination, and so fail to arrive.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The third type of homing behaviour shows the highest degree of orientation. Released at one point, the birds immediately take stock of it, compare its position with that of the nest, decide on the direction and fly off. This happens even if the birds are in a country right off their migration routes, where they have never been before. In one example,&nbsp;a laysan albatross returned to its nesting area on Midway Island in the middle of the Pacific having flown over 5000 kilometres from the west coast of the USA in just over ten days.&nbsp;This is a perfect example of the third type of homing, for the albatross clearly couldn&#39;t rely on any landmarks over the vast expanse of the Pacific Ocean.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The percentage of successful birds varies greatly, being highest in those species with a&nbsp;strong migratory behaviour. Thus the lesser black-backed gull is more migratory than the herring gull and more often reaches home&#39;. Great migrants such as the swift have the highest percentage of returns. In one case, seven out of nine alpine swifts were recaptured at their nests. After being displaced some 1,400 kilometres, one made the journey in three days.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">What part does heredity play in all this? Two research studies suggest that instinctive,&nbsp;i.e.&nbsp;genetically inherited, behaviour patterns play a part in navigation. The first was carried out by Ernstzx Schüz and it is highly significant. Schüz caught first-year European storks and released them later, after the departure of the adult storks at a time when they normally make their south-west autumn migration to Africa. The recaptures showed that, in spite of the fact that there were no adults to guide them, the birds unanimously headed south-west. This was an almost striking finding, for it showed that the birds had an innate and unlearned attraction for the African wintering area that they have occupied for thousands of years.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The case of starlings is a little different. These birds have a great aptitude for homing, but this behaviour differs in the different age groups. Birds that were shifted to the south-east of their normal migration route split into two lots. The adults, in full possession of their gift for orientation, found their wintering area by modifying their direction by 90 degrees, whereas the juveniles sought their winter quarters to the south-east of their real position.<o:p></o:p></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7213&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7214","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 The role of accidents in business","book":"阅读还原集Vol.10","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test1","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.10 · Test1 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"7214:55617:27","type":"choice","text":"The delay in the process used by the Kellogg brothers affected the final product.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问Kellogg兄弟延误的加工过程是否影响了最终产品。\n定位关键词: Kellogg brothers，delay，affected the final product\n对应原文: A段，One day, the brothers left cooked wheat untended for more than 24 hours. When they returned, they saw what they had done. It was no good to eat, but they decided to run the stale wheat through rollers, just to see how it would turn out. Normally, the process produced long sheets, but they were surprised to discover that this time the rollers created flat flakes. They baked them, and then tried the same thing with corn.\n解题思路: A段指出，他们不小心让小麦放置了超过24小时，最后做出了小薄片（flakes）而不是往常的大薄片（long sheets）。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55617","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"7214:55618:28","type":"choice","text":"Sir Alan Hodgkin is an example of someone whose work proceeded in a logical and systematic way.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问Alan Hodgkin的工作是否按照逻辑和系统进行。\n定位关键词: Alan Hodgkin，logical and systematic\n对应原文: B段，Nobel laureate Sir Alan Hodgkin, who discovered how nerve cells transmit electrical impulses between the skin and the brain, commented: 'I believe that the record of my published papers conveys an impression of directedness and planning which does not at all coincide with the actual sequence of events.’\n解题思路: B段指出Hodgkin的研究成果在发表后的确表现出一种有计划和有方向的印象，但实际研究过程并不是有条不紊或按部就班的。\n同义替换：logical and systematic way = impression of directedness and planning","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55618","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"7214:55619:29","type":"choice","text":"Daguerre is an exception to the general rule of innovation.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问Daguerre是否是创新规则的例外。\n定位关键词: Daguerre，exception\n对应原文: C段，The same rule applies in business. The mistake that gave us cornflakes keeps repeating itself in the history of disruptive innovation, the kind that transforms markets. Louis Daguerre, for instance, discovered the technique that gave us photography in the 1830s, when drops of mercury from a shattered thermometer produced a photographic image.\n解题思路: C段指出Daguerre的发现也是通过意外发生的，因此他并不是例外。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55619","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"7214:55620:30","type":"choice","text":"The discovery of saccharin occurred by accident during drug research.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问糖精是否是在药物研究中的意外发现。\n定位关键词: saccharin，discovered by accident，drug research\n对应原文:  C段，The artificial sweetener, saccharin, was the unintentional result of a medical scientist’s work on a chemical treatment for gastric ulcers.\n解题思路:C段指出糖精是研究胃溃疡药物时的意外发现。\n同义替换：accident =  unintentional result; drug research = medical scientist’s work","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55620","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"7214:56027:31","type":"choice","text":"The company 3M should have supported Art Fry by funding his idea of Post-It Notes.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"定位关键信息：\n3M, Art Fry, Post-It Notes\n对应原文：\nC段，While working for the firm 3M, researcher Art Fry had no idea he was taking the first steps towards Post-It Notes when he used bits of adhesive office paper that could be easily lifted off the page to replace the scrap paper bookmarks that kept falling out of his hymn book.\n解题思路：C段没有指出 3M 公司是否应该为 Art Fry 的便利贴（Post-It Notes）创意提供资金支持。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"56027","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"7214:55621:32","type":"choice","text":"The usual business environment ____","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"定位关键词: usual business environment\n对应原文: D段，Breakthrough and disruptive innovation are rarely driven by orderly process. Usually they come out of a chaotic, haphazard mess, which is why big companies, full of managers schooled in business programmes designed to eliminate random variation and mistakes, struggle with them. In these sorts of environments, accidents are called failures and are discouraged.\n解题思路:D段指出常规的商业环境往往由排除随机变化和错误的管理体系主导，这些体系不鼓励“意外”发生，因此不利于创新。","options":["can be found in unusual thoughts and chance events.","can be taught in business schools.","has made a success from someone else’s invention.","is designed to nurture differences.","is unlikely to lead to creative innovation.","says that all mistakes are the same.","shows that businesses are good at either inventing or selling.","suggests ways of increasing the number of mistakes."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"55621","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"7214:55621:33","type":"choice","text":"Geroski and Markides's book ____","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"定位关键词: Geroski and Markides\n对应原文: E段，Their book, Fast Second, divides businesses into 'colonists’ and 'consolidators’. Small and nimble, colonists are adept at creating market niches but are terrible institution builders.\n解题思路: E段指出Geroski和Markides的书讨论了企业要么擅长创新，要么擅长商业化，而很少两者兼备。","options":["can be found in unusual thoughts and chance events.","can be taught in business schools.","has made a success from someone else’s invention.","is designed to nurture differences.","is unlikely to lead to creative innovation.","says that all mistakes are the same.","shows that businesses are good at either inventing or selling.","suggests ways of increasing the number of mistakes."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"55621","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"7214:55621:34","type":"choice","text":"Microsoft is an example of a company which ____","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位关键词: Microsoft\n对应原文: E段，Consolidators, with their strong cultures of discipline and cost control, know how to take clever ideas from other firms and turn them into mass-market items. Microsoft is a prime instance of this.\n解题思路: E段指出微软是“consolidator”（整合者）的一个例子，他们擅长将其他公司发明的点子转化为大众市场产品。","options":["can be found in unusual thoughts and chance events.","can be taught in business schools.","has made a success from someone else’s invention.","is designed to nurture differences.","is unlikely to lead to creative innovation.","says that all mistakes are the same.","shows that businesses are good at either inventing or selling.","suggests ways of increasing the number of mistakes."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"55621","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"7214:55621:35","type":"choice","text":"The origin of useful accidents ____","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"定位关键词: origin of useful accidents\n对应原文: F段，Accidents, they say, come from unlikely mental associations such as memories and vague connections, looking for something and finding it in an unexpected way, looking for one thing and finding something else, and not looking for anything but finding something valuable.\n解题思路:F段指出有用的意外往往源自于偶然的联想和事件。原文指出这些意外是来自于“unusual thoughts”（不同寻常的想法）和“unexpected way”（意想不到的方式）。","options":["can be found in unusual thoughts and chance events.","can be taught in business schools.","has made a success from someone else’s invention.","is designed to nurture differences.","is unlikely to lead to creative innovation.","says that all mistakes are the same.","shows that businesses are good at either inventing or selling.","suggests ways of increasing the number of mistakes."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"55621","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"7214:55622:36","type":"choice","text":"How do Austin and Devin advise companies to get out of the 'cone of expectation'?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"定位关键词:  Austin and Devin，get out of the cone of expectation\n对应原文: G段，It means throwing together groups from diverse backgrounds, and combining ideas in unpredictable ways. Other strategies also include having systems that watch out for accidents and examine them for value, generating them when they do not happen often enough, seizing on the useful ones, capturing their valuable features, and building on them to add value and give potential for useful accidents.\n解题思路:G段指出Austin和Devin建议公司通过让来自不同背景的人组成团队来突破预期。\n同义替换：brainstorming meetings = combining ideas","options":["by decreasing the number of company systems","by forming teams of different types of people","by hiring new and creative people","by holding regular brainstorming meetings"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55622","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"7214:55623:37","type":"choice","text":"In recommending 'counter-intuitive' thinking, what do Austin and Devin imply?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"定位关键词: Austin and Devin，counter-intuitive thinking\n对应原文: H段，It runs counter to the notion frequently pushed by consultants that you can 'harness' creativity and direct it to line up with intention. 'The cost of accidents that do not prove valuable is often a concern to people in business,' they write. 'In business, people tend to call such efforts failure.'\n解题思路: H段指出与大多数商业管理人员的观念不同，Austin和Devin认为创新不能通过计划实现。","options":["that failing at business is bad for staff morale","that innovation cannot be planned for","that most businesses should be devoted to avoiding mistakes","that the cost of mistakes is an important consideration"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55623","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"7214:55624:38","type":"choice","text":"The writer describes the Empire Lager disaster in order to show that","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"定位关键词: Empire Lager disaster\n对应原文: J段，Instead of wiping the unsuccessful product launch, Foster’s used this lesson learned to go on and develop other brands instead.\n解题思路: J段指出Fosters从Empire Lager的失败吸取教训，创造其他成功的品牌。","options":["success can come out of a business failure.","the majority of companies now value risk-taking.","TV advertising works better on older people.","young beer drinkers do not like a sweet taste."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55624","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"7214:55625:39","type":"choice","text":"Pure Blonde has been more successful than Empire Lager because","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位关键词: Pure Blonde，Empire Lager，more successful\n对应原文: J段，One of them, Pure Blonde, is now ranked as Australia’s fifth-largest beer brand. Unlike Empire Lager, there has been almost no promotion and its sales are generated more by word of mouth.\n解题思路:J段指出与Empire Lager不同，Pure Blonde几乎没有广告宣传，因此成功更多依赖口碑传播。\n同义替换：very little advertising =almost no promotion","options":["digital media other than TV were used.","it was advertised under a different brand name.","it was launched with very little advertising.","the advertising budget was larger."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55625","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"7214:55626:40","type":"choice","text":"The writer concludes that creating a culture that learns from mistakes","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"定位关键词: creating a culture，learns from mistakes\n对应原文: K段，In a market that focuses on the short-term, convincing employees and shareholders to tolerate failure and not play it safe is a big thing to ask.\n解题思路:K段指出, 想要创建一种从错误中学习的文化对许多公司来说是困难的。","options":["brings short-term financial gains.","can be very difficult for some companies.","holds no risk for workers.","is a popular move with shareholders."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55626","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose the correct answer."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"55617","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>The delay in the process used by the Kellogg brothers affected the final product.</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"55618","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Sir Alan Hodgkin is an example of someone whose work proceeded in a logical and systematic way.</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"55619","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Daguerre is an exception to the general rule of innovation.</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"55620","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>The discovery of saccharin occurred by accident during drug research.</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"56027","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>The company 3M should have supported Art Fry by funding his idea of Post-It Notes.</strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"55621","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"55622","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>How do Austin and Devin advise companies to get out of the &#39;cone of expectation&#39;?</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"55623","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>In recommending &#39;counter-intuitive&#39; thinking, what do Austin and Devin imply?</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"55624","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>The writer describes the Empire Lager disaster in order to show that</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"55625","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>Pure Blonde has been more successful than Empire Lager because</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"55626","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>The writer concludes that creating a culture that learns from mistakes</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>The role of accidents in business</strong><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">In 1894 Dr John Kellogg and his brother, Will, were supervising a hospital and health spa in Michigan. The patients were on a restricted diet. One day, the brothers left cooked wheat untended for more than 24 hours. When they returned, they saw what they had done. It was no good to eat, but they decided to run the stale wheat through rollers, just to see how it would turn out. Normally, the process produced long sheets, but they were surprised to discover that this time the rollers created flat flakes. They baked them, and then tried the same thing with corn. From this accidental discovery came the cornflakes that generations have now been eating for breakfast.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Accidents happen: there is nothing predictable and orderly about innovation. Nobel laureate Sir Alan Hodgkin, who discovered how nerve cells transmit electrical impulses between the skin and the brain, commented: &#39;I believe that the record of my published papers conveys an impression of directedness and planning which does not at all coincide with the actual sequence of events.&#39;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The same rule applies in business. The mistake that gave us cornflakes keeps repeating itself in the history of disruptive innovation, the kind that transforms markets. Louis Daguerre, for instance, discovered the technique that gave us photography in the 1830s, when drops of mercury from a shattered thermometer produced a photographic image. The microwave was discovered when Percy Spencer, a scientist with Raytheon, was testing a new vacuum tube and discovered that the sweet in his pocket had melted. The artificial sweetener, saccharin, was the unintentional result of a medical scientist’s work on a chemical treatment for gastric ulcers. While working for the firm 3M, researcher Art Fry had no idea he was taking the first steps towards Post-It Notes when he used bits of adhesive office paper that could be easily lifted off the page to replace the scrap paper bookmarks that kept falling out of his hymn book.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Breakthrough and disruptive innovation are rarely driven by orderly process. Usually they come out of a chaotic, haphazard mess, which is why big companies, full of managers schooled in business programmes designed to eliminate random variation and mistakes, struggle with them. In these sorts of environments, accidents are called failures and are discouraged.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">It is no surprise then that research from the late British economist Paul Geroski and London Business School’s Constantinos Markides found that companies that were skilled at innovation were usually not that skilled when it came to commercialisation, and vice versa. Their book, Fast Second, divides businesses into &#39;colonists&#39; and &#39;consolidators&#39;. Small and nimble, colonists are adept at creating market niches but are terrible institution builders. Consolidators, with their strong cultures of discipline and cost control, know how to take clever ideas from other firms and turn them into mass-market items. Microsoft is a prime instance of this.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">With companies spending hundreds of billions of dollars on research and development, US academics Robert Austin and Lee Devintzx examined how managers can encourage productive slip-ups. In their article Accident, Intention and Expectation in the Innovation Process, they argue that business processes actually prevent helpful mis-steps from occurring. According to their catalogue of accidents, not all false steps and mishaps are equal. Accidents, they say, come from unlikely mental associations such as memories and vague connections, looking for something and finding it in an unexpected way, looking for one thing and finding something else, and not looking for anything but finding something valuable.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Accident-prone innovation, they say, requires companies to get outside the &#39;cone of expectation&#39;. It means throwing together groups from diverse backgrounds, and combining ideas in unpredictable ways. Other strategies also include having systems that watch out for accidents and examine them for value, generating them when they do not happen often enough, seizing on the useful ones, capturing their valuable features, and building on them to add value and give potential for useful accidents.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">All this, however, requires thinking that is often counter-intuitive to the way businesses operate. In other words, it is the kind of thinking that goes against the beliefs of most business managers. It runs counter to the notion frequently pushed by consultants that you can &#39;harness&#39; creativity and direct it to line up with intention. &#39;The cost of accidents that do not prove valuable is often a concern to people in business,&#39; they write. &#39;In business, people tend to call such efforts failure.&#39;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>I</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">There are tentative signs that more companies are starting to realise that failure can lead to commercial gain, and that this is part of the risk-taking that underpins innovation. Australia’s largest brewing company, for example, made a bad error when it launched a new beer called Empire Lager, pitched at younger consumers. Having spent a fortune creating a beer with a sweeter taste, designing a great-looking bottle and a television campaign, Foster’s was left with a drink that no one wanted to buy. The target market was more interested in brands built up by word of mouth.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>J</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Instead of wiping the unsuccessful product launch, Foster’s used this lesson learned to go on and develop other brands instead. One of them, Pure Blonde, is now ranked as Australia’s fifth-largest beer brand. Unlike Empire Lager, there has been almost no promotion and its sales are generated more by word of mouth.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>K</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Other companies are taking similar steps to study their own slip-ups. Intuit, the company behind financial tools such as Quicken, holds regular &#39;When Learning Hurts&#39; sessions. But this sort of transformation is never easy. In a market that focuses on the short-term, convincing employees and shareholders to tolerate failure and not play it safe is a big thing to ask.</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><o:p></o:p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7214&scene=%E8%B4%A2%E7%BB%8F%E5%95%86%E4%B8%9A&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7183","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 New perspectives on food production","book":"阅读还原集Vol.9","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test4","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.9 · Test4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"7183:55381:1","type":"fill","text":"填写第 1 空","answer":"scarcity","acceptedAnswers":["scarcity"],"explanation":"审题: 题目询问导致全球饥饿的原因。\n定位关键信息: “world hunger” 和“due to”\n对应原文: A段，“The Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations notes that domestic prices of staple food are continuing to increase, leading to a rise in the number of people worldwide who are chronically underfed. According to Erik Millstone, a food and agriculture researcher funded by the Economic and Social Research Council (ESRC), the natural science community tends to view world hunger as if it were a problem that could be solved simply by increasing total production. ”\n解题思路: 这句话说明有些科学家认为世界饥饿可以通过增加食物产量的方法来解决，那么就可以说食物不足是导致全球饥饿的原因，并且下文也提到了表示短缺的“scarcity”一词。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55381","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 8\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"7183:55382:2","type":"fill","text":"填写第 2 空","answer":"afford","acceptedAnswers":["afford"],"explanation":"审题: 题目询问导致饥饿的另一个原因是人们不能做什么。\n定位关键信息: “cannot”和“hungry people”\n对应原文: A段，“Most people who are chronically hungry are so not because of the scarcity of food but because they are unable to afford what is available.”\n解题思路: 原文提到埃里克·米尔斯通 (Erik Millstone) 认为大多数长期挨饿的人并不是因为食物短缺，而是因为他们买不起现有的食物。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55382","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 8\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"7183:55383:3","type":"fill","text":"填写第 3 空","answer":"exported","acceptedAnswers":["exported"],"explanation":"审题: 题目询问食物无法被获得的原因。\n定位关键信息: “not available”\n对应原文: A段，“ In addition, the food trade is so globalised that food is often exported from areas where people are hungry and sent to countries where people already have sufficient.”\n解题思路: 原文提到粮食贸易全球化导致食物经常从饥饿地区出口到已经足够的人口稠密地区。原文说明食物被出口到其他国家是食物无法被获得的原因。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55383","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 8\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"7183:55384:4","type":"fill","text":"填写第 4 空","answer":"storing","acceptedAnswers":["storing"],"explanation":"审题: 题目要求填补如何帮助自给自足农民的问题。\n定位关键信息: “support for subsistence farmers”\n对应原文: B段，“And that is not enough on its own – they also have to have facilities for storing it so that their food can be kept safe and in good condition until it is needed. ”\n解题思路: 原文提到米尔斯通认为解决问题的办法是改变贫困自给型农民的条件，并提供他们种植更多食物所需的支助，还需要储存设施来保持食物的安全和状态。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55384","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 8\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"7183:55385:5","type":"fill","text":"填写第 5 空","answer":"technology","acceptedAnswers":["technology"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问到不要用什么来增加食物产量。\n定位关键信息: “increase food production”\n对应原文: B段，“But, he adds, increasing productivity through technology is not the answer.”\n解题思路: 原文提到增加生产力并不是答案，例如转基因高性能玉米新品种需要每年购买新种子，而贫困农民买不起。原文明确提到不应该通过技术提高生产力。\n同义替换：food production = productivity","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55385","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 8\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"7183:55385:6","type":"fill","text":"填写第 6 空","answer":"traditional","acceptedAnswers":["traditional"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问到哪种品种的玉米更适合贫穷农民。\n定位关键信息: “varieties of maize”。\n对应原文: B段，“Poor farmers cannot, so they need traditional varieties whose seed can be saved and replanted.”\n解题思路: 原文提到转基因高性能玉米新品种的缺点是如果留种来年种植，其活力会下降，所以贫困农民更需要传统玉米种子。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55385","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 8\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"7183:55386:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"credit","acceptedAnswers":["credit"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问到不要给农民提供什么机会，因为风险太大。\n定位关键信息: don’t provide opportunities, too risky\n对应原文: B段，“Giving farmers access to credit also doesn’t help; it adds risk.”\n解题思路: 原文提到给农民提供信贷渠道会增加风险，贫困农民不是寻求投资的企业家，而是寻求降低风险的人。原文明确提到给予信贷会增加风险。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55386","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 8\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"7183:55387:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"tools","acceptedAnswers":["tools"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问到应该改善哪些资源来帮助自给自足农民。\n定位关键信息: 是“improve techniques and”和“subsistence farmers”\n对应原文: B段，“Ultimately, he concludes, ‘Instead of devoting resources to research for intensifying commercial farming, we should devote them to enhancing the techniques available to subsistence farmers, and to developing appropriate tools for them to use, because their need is the greatest.”\n解题思路: 原文提到应该把资源用于改善可供农民使用的技术并为他们开发合适的工具，因为他们的需求最大。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55387","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 8\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"7183:55388:9","type":"choice","text":"Importing sugar to the UK from other parts of Europe is less environmentally harmful than importing sugar from Africa.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问到从欧洲进口糖是否比从非洲进口更环保。\n定位关键信息: “Importing sugar to the UK”和“environmentally harmful”。\n对应原文: D段，“Which has the lower carbon footprint: sugar made from sugar cane grown in Africa, or from sugar beet flown in from Europe? The answer is sugar from sugar cane in Africa.”\n解题思路: 原文指出从非洲进口糖的碳足迹较小。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55388","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"7183:55389:10","type":"choice","text":"The way in which some foods are cooked may affect their impact on the environment.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问到食物的烹饪方式是否会影响其对环境的影响。\n定位关键信息:“the way in which some foods are cooked”和“impact on the environment”。\n对应原文: E段，“He discovered early in his research that the methods used to prepare foods to be eaten can have a huge impact; boiling potatoes accounts for fully half their carbon footprint.”\n解题思路: 原文提到煮土豆会产生大量碳足迹，烹饪方式确实影响环境。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55389","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"7183:55390:11","type":"choice","text":"The best way to reduce harm to the environment is to oblige farmers to use more environmentally friendly farming methods.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问到是否强迫农民使用更环保的农业方法是减少环境破坏的最好方法。\n定位关键信息: 关键词是“the best way”和“reduce harm to the environment”。\n对应原文: E段，“You could have a policy where you’re going to really pressurise farmers to try to get emissions down, but decarbonising fuel and electricity is a much more effective method of protecting the environment; he says.”\n解题思路: 原文提到通过减少燃料和电力中的碳排放比迫使农民使用环保方法更有效，所以，强迫农民 使用更环保的农业方法并不是最好的方法。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55390","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"7183:55391:12","type":"choice","text":"Imports of food to the UK from African countries such as Kenya have fallen recently.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问到最近从非洲进口的食品是否减少。\n定位关键信息: “Imports of food from African countries”\n对应原文：F段, “He finds it ironic that after years of ‘trade not aid’ all of a sudden people are starting to say the UK shouldn’t be importing food from Africa.”\n解题思路: 原文讨论了人们对从非洲进口食品的看法转变，但没有提到进口量是否下降。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55391","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"7183:55392:13","type":"choice","text":"Growing fruit and vegetables is better for the environment than raising animals for food.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问到种植水果和蔬菜是否比养殖动物更环保。\n定位关键信息: “Growing fruit and vegetables”和“raising animals”\n对应原文：G段, “The other problem with insisting on locally grown food, he says, is that the UK is not suited to growing most fruits and vegetables – the key elements in a healthy diet. These crops need our best land – which means demoting other crops that do grow well in the UK to lower quality land. ”\n解题思路: G段讨论了水果和蔬菜的种植，但没有明确比较它们与动物养殖对环境的影响。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55392","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"55381","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 8\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>The problem of world hunger</strong></p><p><strong>CAUSE</strong></p><p>Some scientists see world hunger as due to a general <strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong> of food.</p><p>But it may be because：</p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"55382","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 8\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>• hungry people cannot&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[2] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"55383","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 8\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><span style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">•&nbsp;</span>food is not available because it has been <strong class=\"source-blank\">[3] ____</strong></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"55384","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 8\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>SOLUTION</strong></p><p><span style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">•&nbsp;</span>provide support for subsistence farmers in growing and <strong class=\"source-blank\">[4] ____</strong> their food</p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"55385","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 8\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>ADDITIONAL RECOMMENDATIONS</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">•&nbsp;</span>don&#39;t use <strong class=\"source-blank\">[5] ____</strong> to increase food production, e.g. <strong class=\"source-blank\">[6] ____</strong> varieties of maize are better for poor farmers as the seed can be replanted</p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"55386","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 8\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>•&nbsp;don&#39;t provide opportunities for farmers to have <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong>&nbsp;–&nbsp;too risky</p><p>•&nbsp;don&#39;t do research into intensifying commercial farming</p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"55387","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 8\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><span style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">•&nbsp;</span>do improve techniques and <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong> available to subsistence farmers</p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"55388","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Importing sugar to the UK from other parts of Europe is less environmentally harmful than importing sugar from Africa.</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"55389","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The way in which some foods are cooked may affect their impact on the environment.</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"55390","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The best way to reduce harm to the environment is to oblige farmers to use more environmentally friendly farming methods.</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"55391","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Imports of food to the UK from African countries such as Kenya have fallen recently.</strong></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"55392","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 9 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Growing fruit and vegetables is better for the environment than raising animals for food.</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>New perspectives on food production</strong><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><em>Solving the food problem requires scientific progress, but also an understanding of social context and cultures</em><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>Is new technology needed for global food production?</strong><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations notes that domestic prices of staple food are continuing to increase, leading to a rise in the number of people worldwide who are chronically underfed.&nbsp;According to Erik Millstone, a food and agriculture researcher funded by the Economic and Social Research Council (ESRC), the natural science community tends to view world hunger as if it were a problem that could be solved simply by increasing total production. But, he says, ‘Most people who are chronically hungry are so not because of the scarcity of food but because they are unable to afford what is available.&nbsp;In addition, the food trade is so globalised that food is often exported from areas where people are hungry and sent to countries where people already have sufficient.’<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Millstone believes the problem can only be solved by changing the conditions for poor subsistence farmers and providing the support they need to grow more food. And that is not enough on its own&nbsp;–&nbsp;they also have to have facilities for storing it so that their food can be kept safe and in good condition until it is needed.&nbsp;But, he adds, increasing productivity through technology is not the answer.&nbsp;An example is the new genetically-engineered varieties of high-performance maize. The problem with these new varieties is that if you save seed and plant it again next year, its vigour has diminished. Most North American and European farmers can afford to get new seed every year; ‘Poor farmers cannot, so they need traditional varieties whose seed can be saved and replanted.&nbsp;Giving farmers access to credit also doesn’t help; it adds risk. Poor farmers should not be thought of as entrepreneurs looking to invest their money. They are looking to diminish their risk.’&nbsp;Ultimately, he concludes, ‘Instead of devoting resources to research for intensifying commercial farming, we should devote them to enhancing the techniques available to subsistence farmers, and to developing appropriate tools for them to use, because their need is the greatest.&nbsp;Increasing their productivity will do more to enhance food security for those who are hungry than anything else we can do.’<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>Looking for local solutions in the UK</strong><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">In contrast to Millstone, Gareth Edwards Jones, a professor of agriculture and land use at the University of Bangor in Wales, focuses on food production in the UK. In recent years ‘local food’ has become fashionable in the UK without any real understanding of the issues involved. First and foremost, it is necessary to define more precisely what is meant by ‘local’. Is bread bought in England from an English bakery ‘local’ if the wheat it is made from was grown in Canada? Funded through the Rural Economy and Land Use Programme, Edwards Jones is studying people’s perceptions of ‘localness’ and seeking to establish whether there is any science behind the popular belief that ‘local is better’.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">His work involves studying the carbon footprint*&nbsp;of foods grown in different areas of the UK, as well as such common sources of supply as Spain, Kenya and Uganda.&nbsp;He has made some surprising discoveries.&nbsp;Which has the lower carbon footprint:&nbsp;sugar made from sugar cane grown in Africa, or from sugar beet flown in from Europe? The answer is sugar from sugar cane in Africa.&nbsp;Similarly, trucking vegetables in from Spain may have a smaller carbon footprint than growing them locally in the UK&nbsp;–&nbsp;because growing them locally requires adding all the emissions of running a heated greenhouse.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">And, he asks, how far down the life cycle should you go? He discovered early in his research that the methods used to prepare foods to be eaten can have a huge impact; boiling potatoes accounts for fully half their carbon footprint.&nbsp;Ultimately, it’s a mistake to look at just one part of the food chain. You could have a policy where you’re going to really pressurise farmers to try to get emissions down, but decarbonising fuel and electricity is a much more effective method of protecting the environment; he says.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Another of Edwards Jones’s research projects involved visiting farm workers in each of the&nbsp;above countries to assess their health and well-being. ‘We found that farm workers in Kenya had better physical and mental health than the average Kenyan,’ he says, attributing the difference to both better income and to the benefits&nbsp;–&nbsp;housing, schools, medical care provided by their large corporate employers. He finds it ironic that after years of&nbsp;‘trade not aid’ all of a sudden people are starting to say the UK shouldn’t be importing food from Africa.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>G&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The other problem with insisting on locally grown food, he says, is that the UK is not suited to growing most fruits and vegetables&nbsp;–&nbsp;the key elements in a healthy diet. These crops need our best land&nbsp;–&nbsp;which means demoting other crops that do grow well in the UK to lower quality land.&nbsp;‘There’s a domino effect so that increasing self sufficiency may, from an environmental perspective, be quite bad,’&nbsp;he says.<o:p></o:p><o:p></o:p></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7183&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7184","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 The discovery of a baby mammoth","book":"阅读还原集Vol.9","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test4","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.9 · Test4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"7184:55393:14","type":"fill","text":"14 similarities between studies of mammoth remains from different parts of the world","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"定位关键信息: “similarities”和“studies of mammoth”\n对应原文: D段，“Most of these came from the Great Lakes region of North America, and his research showed that these animals continued to thrive, despite the late Pleistocene* temperature change. On the other hand, to Fisher the tusks often revealed telltale evidence of human hunting. His samples frequently came from animals that had died in the autumn, when they should have been attheir peak after summer grazing, and less likely to die of natural causes, but also when humans would have been most eager to stockpile meat for the coming winter. He has done limited work in Siberia, but his analysis of tusks from Wrangel Island, off the coast of Siberia, suggests the same conclusion.”\n解题思路: 原文提到Fisher对北美和西伯利亚的研究得出了相似的结论。\n同义替换：different parts of the world =Wrangel Island； mammoth remains=tusks","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55393","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nLook at the six paragraphs (A - F). Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"7184:55393:15","type":"fill","text":"15 details of the uses to which mammoth body parts were put","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"定位关键信息: “uses”和“mammoth body parts”。\n对应原文: B段，“In addition to exploiting mammoths for food, they used their bones and tusks to make weapons, tools, and even dwellings.”\n解题思路: 原文详细说明了猛犸的身体部位被用于制作武器、工具和房屋。\n同义替换：mammoth body parts= bones and tusks","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55393","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nLook at the six paragraphs (A - F). Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"7184:55393:16","type":"fill","text":"16 a theory that accounts for the damage to Lyuba's face","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"定位关键信息: “theory”和“damage to Lyuba's face”\n对应原文: E段，“In fact, the sediment in Lyuba's trunk was packed so tightly that Fisher saw it as a possible explanation for the dent above her trunk. If she was frantically fighting for breath and inhaled convulsively, perhaps a partial vacuum was created in the base of her trunk, which would have flattened surrounding soft tissue. To Fisher, the circumstances of Lyuba's death were clear: she had asphyxiated. Suzuki, however, proposed a different interpretation, seeing more evidence for drowning than asphyxiation.”\n解题思路: 原文提供了对Lyuba脸部损伤的两种解释。\n同义替换：damage= dent","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55393","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nLook at the six paragraphs (A - F). Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"7184:55393:17","type":"fill","text":"17 an explanation of how an individual was able to identify a small corpse","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"定位关键信息: “identify a small corpse”\n对应原文: A段，“Although he'd never seen such an animal before, Khudi had seen many mammoth tusks, the thick corkscrew shafts that his people found each summer, and this persuaded him the corpse was a baby mammoth.”\n解题思路: 原文解释了Khudi如何通过之前看到的猛犸象牙来识别出这是一只幼年猛犸象的尸体。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55393","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nLook at the six paragraphs (A - F). Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"7184:55393:18","type":"fill","text":"18 A comparison between Lyuba and other young mammoth corpses","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位关键信息:“comparison”和“Lyuba and other young mammoth corpses”\n对应原文: C段，“Fisher and Buigues had examined other specimens together, including infants, but these had been in a relatively poor state. Lyuba was another story entirely, other than the missing hair and toenails, the only flaw in her pristine appearance was a curious dent above the trunk.”\n解题思路: 原文提到Fisher和Buigues将Lyuba与其他猛犸的研究进行比较。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55393","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nLook at the six paragraphs (A - F). Which paragraph contains the following information?"},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"7184:55515:19","type":"choice","text":"19 The indications are that mammoths died as a result of climate change.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"定位关键信息: Adrian Lister\n对应原文: B段，“ We have strong evidence that the temperature rise played a significant part in their extinction.' says Adrian Lister, a palaeontologist and mammoth expert at London's Natural History Museum.' ”\n解题思路: 原文提到Adrian Lister认为气温升高书导致猛犸象灭绝的重要原因之一，所以可以说气候变化导致了猛犸的灭绝。\n同义替换： indications=evidence；climate change=temperature rise","options":["Yuri Khudi","Kirill Serotetto","Adrian Lister","Alexei Tikhonov","Dan Fisher","Bernard Buigues","Naoki Suzuki"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"55515","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nChoose the correct person (A - G) for each statement. You may choose any correct person more than once.\nList of People\nA Yuri Khudi\nB Kirill Serotetto\nC Adrian Lister\nD Alexei Tikhonov\nE Dan Fisher\nF Bernard Buigues\nG Naoki Suzuki"},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"7184:55515:20","type":"choice","text":"20 Teeth analysis is important in discovering why mammoths died out.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"定位关键信息: Dan Fisher\n对应原文: F段，“Her good general health was shown in the record of her dental development, a confirmation for Fisher that dental research is useful for evaluating health and thus key to investigating the causes of mammoth extinction.”\n解题思路: 原文提到Fisher通过牙齿分析研究猛犸的健康状况，从而探索灭绝的原因。","options":["Yuri Khudi","Kirill Serotetto","Adrian Lister","Alexei Tikhonov","Dan Fisher","Bernard Buigues","Naoki Suzuki"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"55515","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nChoose the correct person (A - G) for each statement. You may choose any correct person more than once.\nList of People\nA Yuri Khudi\nB Kirill Serotetto\nC Adrian Lister\nD Alexei Tikhonov\nE Dan Fisher\nF Bernard Buigues\nG Naoki Suzuki"},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"7184:55515:21","type":"choice","text":"21 The corpse of the baby mammoth is in better condition than any other that has been discovered.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"定位关键信息:  Alexei Tikhonov\n对应原文: C段，“The body of the baby mammoth was eventually sent to the St Petersburg Zoological Museum in Russia. Alexei Tikhonov, the museum's director, was one of the first scientists to view the baby, a female. According to Tikhonov, Khudi had rescued 'the best preserved mammoth to come down to US from the Ice Age', and he gratefully named her Lyuba, after Khudi's wife.”\n解题思路: 原文提到Tikhonov认为Khudi拯救的猛犸象尸体是保存最好的冰河时期迁徙到美国的猛犸象尸体。\n同义替换：better condition = best preserved","options":["Yuri Khudi","Kirill Serotetto","Adrian Lister","Alexei Tikhonov","Dan Fisher","Bernard Buigues","Naoki Suzuki"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"55515","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nChoose the correct person (A - G) for each statement. You may choose any correct person more than once.\nList of People\nA Yuri Khudi\nB Kirill Serotetto\nC Adrian Lister\nD Alexei Tikhonov\nE Dan Fisher\nF Bernard Buigues\nG Naoki Suzuki"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"7184:55515:22","type":"choice","text":"22 It would be a mistake to ignore the baby mammoth's discovery, because of its potential importance.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"定位关键信息:Yuri Khudi\n对应原文: A段，“Khudi realised the find might be significant and he knew he couldn't just return home and forget all about it.”\n解题思路:\nKhudi意识到这个发现可能非常重要，他知道自己不能就这样回家，然后完全忘记这件事。","options":["Yuri Khudi","Kirill Serotetto","Adrian Lister","Alexei Tikhonov","Dan Fisher","Bernard Buigues","Naoki Suzuki"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"55515","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nChoose the correct person (A - G) for each statement. You may choose any correct person more than once.\nList of People\nA Yuri Khudi\nB Kirill Serotetto\nC Adrian Lister\nD Alexei Tikhonov\nE Dan Fisher\nF Bernard Buigues\nG Naoki Suzuki"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"7184:55515:23","type":"choice","text":"23 Mammoths often died at a time of year when they should have been in good physical condition.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"定位关键信息:Dan Fisher\n对应原文: D段，“His samples frequently came from animals that had died in the autumn, when they should have been at their peak after summer grazing, and less likely to die of natural causes, but also when humans would have been most eager to stockpile meat for the coming winter.”\n解题思路: 原文提到Dan Fisher认为猛犸象在秋季死亡，而这个时期正是它们经过夏季放牧后身体应该处于最佳状态的时候。","options":["Yuri Khudi","Kirill Serotetto","Adrian Lister","Alexei Tikhonov","Dan Fisher","Bernard Buigues","Naoki Suzuki"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"55515","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nChoose the correct person (A - G) for each statement. You may choose any correct person more than once.\nList of People\nA Yuri Khudi\nB Kirill Serotetto\nC Adrian Lister\nD Alexei Tikhonov\nE Dan Fisher\nF Bernard Buigues\nG Naoki Suzuki"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"7184:55399:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"vegetation","acceptedAnswers":["vegetation"],"explanation":"定位关键信息: “marked rise in temperature impacted”和“changing the type of”\n对应原文: B段，“Mammoths became extinct between 14,000 and 10,000 years ago and since the extinctions coincided with the end of the most recent Ice age, many researchers believe that the primary cause of the great die-off was the sharp rise in temperature, which dramatically altered the vegetation.”\n解题思路: 原文提到研究者认为猛犸象在最近的冰河时期末灭绝是因为气温上升改变了植被类型。\n同义替换：marked rise=sharp rise; changing=altered","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55399","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24 - 26\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"7184:55400:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"human hunting","acceptedAnswers":["human hunting"],"explanation":"定位关键信息: “Fisher”和“tusks”和“signs of”\n对应原文: D段，“ On the other hand, to Fisher the tusks often revealed telltale evidence of human hunting.”\n解题思路: 原文提到Fisher 认为象牙显示了人类捕猎的迹象。\n同义替换：displayed=revealed； signs=evidence","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55400","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24 - 26\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"7184:55401:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"North America","acceptedAnswers":["North America"],"explanation":"定位关键信息: “after Lyuba's death”和“replaced by another group”\n对应原文: F段，“Analysis of her well-preserved DNA has revealed that she belonged to a distinct population of Mammuthus primigenius and that, soon after her time, another population migrating to Siberia from North America would take their place.”\n解题思路: 原文提到通过分析Lyuba保存完好的DNA，科学家确认Lyuba所属的种群被来自北美的群体所取代。\n同义替换：replaced by=take...place","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55401","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24 - 26\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"55393","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nLook at the six paragraphs (A - F). Which paragraph contains the following information?","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"55515","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 19-23\nChoose the correct person (A - G) for each statement. You may choose any correct person more than once.\nList of People\nA Yuri Khudi\nB Kirill Serotetto\nC Adrian Lister\nD Alexei Tikhonov\nE Dan Fisher\nF Bernard Buigues\nG Naoki Suzuki","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"55399","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24 - 26\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p>Some researchers say that a marked rise in temperature impacted on mammoths by changing the type of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> available.</p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"55400","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24 - 26\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p>Fisher concluded that many of the mammoth tusks he looked at displayed signs of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong>&nbsp;.</p>","firstNumber":25},{"id":"55401","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24 - 26\nComplete the sentences. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p>Not long after Lyuba’s death, the Mammuthus primigenius&nbsp;group she belonged to was replaced by another group that came from <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":26}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>The discovery of a baby mammoth</strong><o:p></o:p></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><em>A near-perfect frozen mammoth offers clues to a great vanished species</em><o:p></o:p></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><em><br/></em></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">On a May morning in 2007, on the Yamal Peninsula in northwestern Siberia, a Nenets Reindeer herder named Yuri Khudi stood on a sandbar on the Yuribey River, looking carefully at a diminutive corpse. Although he&#39;d never seen such an animal before, Khudi had seen many mammoth tusks, the thick corkscrew shafts that his people found each summer, and this persuaded him the corpse was a baby mammoth. It was eerily well preserved. Apart from its missing hair and toenails, it was perfectly intact. Khudi realised the find might be significant and he knew he couldn&#39;t just return home and forget all about it. He therefore decided to travel to the small town of Yar Sale to consult an old friend named Kirill Serotetto. His friend took him to meet the director of the local museum, who persuaded the local authorities to fly Khudi and Serotetto back to the Yuribey River to collect the baby mammoth.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Mammoths became extinct between 14,000 and 10,000 years ago and since the extinctions coincided with the end of the most recent Ice age, many researchers believe that the primary cause of the great die-off was the sharp rise in temperature, which dramatically altered the vegetation. <span style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;,sans-serif\">&#39;</span>We have strong evidence that the temperature rise played a significant part in their extinction.&#39; says Adrian Lister, a palaeontologist and mammoth expert at London&#39;s Natural History Museum.&#39; In Eurasia, the timing of the two events matches closely.&#39; The extinctions also coincided, however, with the arrival of modern humans. In addition to exploiting mammoths for food, they used their bones and tusks to make weapons, tools, and even dwellings. Some scientists believe humans were as much to blame as the temperature rise for the great die-off. Some say they caused it.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The body of the baby mammoth was eventually sent to the St Petersburg Zoological Museum in Russia. Alexei Tikhonov, the museum&#39;s director, was one of the first scientists to view the baby, a female. According to Tikhonov, Khudi had rescued &#39;the best preserved mammoth to come down to US from the Ice Age&#39;, and he gratefully named her Lyuba, after Khudi&#39;s wife. Tikhonov knew that no-one would be more excited by the find than Dan Fisher, an American colleague at the University of Michigan who had spent 30 years researching the lives of mammoths. Tikhonov invited Fisher, along with Bernard Buigues, a French mammoth hunter, to come and view the baby mammoth. Fisher and Buigues had examined other specimens together, including infants, but these had been in a relatively poor state. Lyuba was another story entirely, other than the missing hair and toenails, the only flaw in her pristine appearance was a curious dent above the trunk.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Fisher was particularly excited about one specific part of Lyuba&#39;s anatomy: her milk tusks. Through his career, Fisher has taken hundreds of tusk samples. Most of these came from the Great Lakes region of North America, and his research showed that these animals continued to thrive, despite the late Pleistocene* temperature change. On the other hand, to Fisher the tusks often revealed telltale evidence of human hunting. His samples frequently came from animals that had died in the autumn, when they should have been at their peak after summer grazing, and less likely to die of natural causes, but also when humans would have been most eager to stockpile meat for the coming winter. He has done limited work in Siberia, but his analysis of tusks from Wrangel Island, off the coast of Siberia, suggests the same conclusion.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">In December 2007, Buigues arranged for the specimen to be transported to Japan to undergo a CT scan by Naoki Suzuki of the Jikei University School of Medicine. The test confirmed her skeleton was undamaged, and her internal organs seemed largely intact. It also showed that the end of her trunk, and her throat, mouth, and windpipe were filled with dense sediment. Six months later, in a laboratory in St Petersburg, Fisher, Buigues, Suzuki, Tikhonov and other colleagues began a three-day series of tests on Lyuba. During these, Fisher noted a dense mix of clay and sand in her trunk, mouth and throat, which had been indicated earlier by the scan. In fact, the sediment in Lyuba&#39;s trunk was packed so tightly that Fisher saw it as a possible explanation for the dent above her trunk. If she was frantically fighting for breath and inhaled convulsively, perhaps a partial vacuum was created in the base of her trunk, which would have flattened surrounding soft tissue. To Fisher, the circumstances of Lyuba&#39;s death were clear: she had asphyxiated. Suzuki, however, proposed a different interpretation, seeing more evidence for drowning than asphyxiation.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Studies are ongoing, but Lyuba has begun to shed the secrets of her short life and some clues to the fate of her kind. Her good general health was shown in the record of her dental development, a confirmation for Fisher that dental research is useful for evaluating health and thus key to investigating the causes of mammoth extinction. Analysis of her well-preserved DNA has revealed that she belonged to a distinct population of Mammuthus primigenius&nbsp;and that, soon after her time, another population migrating to Siberia from North America would take their place. Finally, Lyuba&#39;s premolars and tusks revealed that she had been born in late spring and was only a month old when she died.<o:p></o:p></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7184&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7185","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 The power of persuasion","book":"阅读还原集Vol.9","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test4","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.9 · Test4 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"7185:55402:27","type":"choice","text":"What point is the writer making about Robert Cialdini in the first paragraph?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问的是作者在第一段中关于Robert Cialdini的主要观点是什么。\n定位关键词: \"first paragraph,\" \"Robert Cialdini\"\n对应原文: A段，“Then there is Robert Cialdini, whose unorthodox research involves such mundane items as towels and chocolates. Nonetheless, Cialdini believes he is discovering important insights into how society works, because he is conducting research into why some people are more persuasive than others.”\n解题思路: A段提到Cialdini采用了一种非传统（unorthodox）的研究方法，通过毛巾和巧克力这些普通的物品等研究为什么有些人比别人更具说服力。","options":["He wants to change the way society operates.","He uses a wide variety of research techniques.","He has an unconventional approach to this work.","He refuses to make use of animals in his experiments"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55402","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"7185:55403:28","type":"choice","text":"What is the writer doing in the second paragraph?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问的是作者在第二段中做了什么。\n定位关键词: \"second paragraph\"\n对应原文: “Cialdini hopes that, by applying a little science, we should all be able to get our own way more often. ”\n解题思路: B段提到了Cialdini的研究动机，他希望通过科学研究，所有人都能更频繁地说服其他人。","options":["identifying a motivation for the research","assessing on aspect of Cialdini’s character","questioning Cialdini’s scientific research techniques","applauding researchers who examine their own experience"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55403","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"7185:55404:29","type":"choice","text":"What are we told about Cialdini’s research methodology?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问的是Cialdini的研究方法。\n定位关键词: \"Cialdini’s research methodology\"\n对应原文: C段，\"Having concluded that laboratory experiments on the psychology of persuasion were telling only a part of the story, Cialdini began to probe influence in the real world, enrolling in sales-training programmes.\"\n解题思路: C段提到Cialdini通过实际参与销售培训课程来学习如何销售汽车、保险甚至百科全书来学习，这说明他采用了亲身参与学习的方法。\n同义替换：involved = enrolling","options":["It was conducted in a laboratory.","It involved him taking courses of study.","It was focused on one particular product.","It was based on interviews with salespeople."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55404","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"7185:55405:30","type":"choice","text":"What was Cialdini’s research question for the towel experiment?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问的是Cialdini关于毛巾实验的研究问题。\n定位关键词: \"towel experiment,\" \"research question\"\n对应原文: C段,“Cialdini and his colleagues wanted to test the relative effectiveness of different text on those cards.”\n解题思路: C段提到Cialdini 和同事实验的目的是测试酒店卡片上的不同信息对客人的行为的不同影响。","options":["Is it more effective not to use a card?","Does the message make any difference?","Why is the threat of pollution so persuasive","Can hotels be persuaded to provide more towels?"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55405","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"7185:55406:31","type":"choice","text":"The results of the towel experiment suggest that guests","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问的是毛巾实验的结果显示客人有什么反应。\n定位关键词: \"towel experiment,\" \"results\",\"guests\"\n对应原文: D段,“To test this, the researchers redesigned the cards, replacing the environmental message with the simple (and truthful) statement that the majority of guests at the hotel had reused their towel at least once. Those guests who received this message were found to be 26% more likely to reuse their towel than those given the original message, and 74% more likely than those receiving no message at all.”\n解题思路:  D段提到结果显示，当客人知道其他人也重复使用毛巾时，他们更可能效仿。","options":["were disinclined to tell the truth about towel use.","preferred not to receive a message with their towels","were more receptive to messages about other guests","responded more positively to an environmental message."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55406","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"7185:55670:32","type":"choice","text":"The six principles of persuasion\nCialdini’s towel experiment demonstrated the principle he named ‘social proof’, which can result in competitive materialism. His research using chocolates suggests that people don’t always assess the ____ of transaction.","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是Cialdini实验中人们在交易时评估的特定内容。\n定位关键词: assess, the relative value of transaction\n对应原文：E段，A further principle, which he names ‘reciprocity’, was tested in a restaurant by measuring how patrons would respond to after-dinner chocolates.\n解题思路: E段提到Cialdini的研究表明人们往往不能准确地评估交易的相对价值。\n同义替换： research=tested","options":["rare opportunity","previous commitments","generous response","true qualification","similar name","ruthless exploitation","social obligation","relative value","bad behavior","small favor"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"55670","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32 - 36\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"7185:55670:33","type":"choice","text":"A further principle recommends that advertisers and parents should claim that something is a ____ .","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是广告商和家长推荐的特定事物的描述。\n定位关键词: advertisers and parents\n对应原文：F段，‘Scarcity’ is the idea that people want more of things they can have less of, a notion that ‘advertisers ruthlessly exploit-limit of four per customer’. Parents can also make use of scarcity by telling their little ones that this is a very unusual chance so they should seize it immediately.\n解题思路: F段提到“稀缺性”原则，人们更想要稀缺的东西，广告商会利用这一点宣传“限时优惠”等信息。\n同义替换：rare opportunity = scarcity","options":["rare opportunity","previous commitments","generous response","true qualification","similar name","ruthless exploitation","social obligation","relative value","bad behavior","small favor"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"55670","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32 - 36\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"7185:55670:34","type":"choice","text":"In order to be more persuasive, the authority principle is often ignored when some professionals are concerned their actions might be considered ____.","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是某些专业人士在考虑行为被视为某种特定特点下忽视权威原则。\n定位关键词: the authority principle, professionals\n对应原文：F段，The principle of ‘authority’ states that we trust people who know what they are talking about. Cialdini maintains that many professionals don't display their credentials, fearing it is boastful or arrogant to publicise their expertise.\n解题思路：F段提到“权威”原则强调信任专业人士，但一些专业人士担心展示资历会被看作自负或傲慢。\n同义替换：bad behavior = boastful or arrogant","options":["rare opportunity","previous commitments","generous response","true qualification","similar name","ruthless exploitation","social obligation","relative value","bad behavior","small favor"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"55670","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32 - 36\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"7185:55670:35","type":"choice","text":"He similarly suggests that people will give more to charity if they can be reminded of ____.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是人们在被提醒什么特定内容时会更愿意捐赠。\n定位关键词: give more to charity\n对应原文：F段, ”The principle he labels ‘consistency’ suggests that we want to act in ways that are consistent with undertaking we have already made.”\n解题思路：F段提到“一致性”原则，人们倾向于与之前做出的承诺保持一致。\n同义替换：previous=already made\ncommitments= undertakings","options":["rare opportunity","previous commitments","generous response","true qualification","similar name","ruthless exploitation","social obligation","relative value","bad behavior","small favor"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"55670","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32 - 36\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"7185:55670:36","type":"choice","text":"Lastly, even something like a ____ has been shown to result in more surveys being completed.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是什么事物能够促进更多调查被完成的效果。\n定位关键词: surveys, completed\n对应原文：F段,The final principle is ‘likeness’：we are more easily persuaded by those who seem similar to ourselves. In one study, people were sent survey forms and asked to return them to a named researcher. When the researcher falsely identified herself (e.g. Cynthia Johnson is sent a survey by ‘Cindy Johansen’), surveys were twice as likely to be completed.\n解题思路：F段提到“相似性”原则，人们更容易被与自己相似的人说服。研究发现，当调查问卷署名与被调查者姓名相似时，完成问卷的比例会增加一倍。","options":["rare opportunity","previous commitments","generous response","true qualification","similar name","ruthless exploitation","social obligation","relative value","bad behavior","small favor"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","J"],"sourceGroupId":"55670","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32 - 36\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"7185:55407:37","type":"choice","text":"The writer sees evidence of the reciprocity principle in his own family.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问作者是否在自己的家庭中看到了互惠原则的证据。\n定位关键词: “reciprocity principle,” “own family”\n对应原文: G段, ”Many of Cialdini’s claims about persuasion are just that – highly persuasive – and I can readily see evidence for some of them in my own workplace. ”\n解题思路: G段提到作者在自己的工作中遇到了许多Cialdini对于说服的说法，但没有提到作者在自己的家庭中是否看到过互惠原则的证据。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55407","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"7185:55408:38","type":"choice","text":"Persuasion may operate in different ways in different countries.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问作者是否认为不同国家的说服方式不同。\n定位关键词: “persuasion,” “different countries”\n对应原文: G段，\"But Cialdini’s experiments were conducted in the United States and I wonder how well all of his findings can be applied here in New Zealand or elsewhere around the world.\"\n解题思路: G段提到Cialdini的实验是在美国进行的，作者怀疑他的所有发现能否同样适用于新西兰或世界其他地方。这表明作者认为不同国家的文化背景可能会导致劝说方法在不同国家产生不同的效果。\n同义替换： operate=be applied；different countries=around the world.","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55408","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"7185:55409:39","type":"choice","text":"New Zealand diners are likely to leave tips if they are given chocolate.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问新西兰的食客是否会因收到巧克力而留下小费。\n定位关键词: “New Zealand,” “tips,” “chocolate”\n对应原文: G段，\" For instance, I do understand the general principle of ‘reciprocity’ but cannot imagine New Zealand waiting staff using his cynical chocolate trick in their restaurants because the culture of tipping in this country is so different. \"\n解题思路: G段提到，作者认为新西兰的小费文化与美国等其他国家不同，并且巧克力的小费技巧在新西兰并不适用。这意味着，即使给新西兰食客巧克力，他们也不太可能因此而给小费。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55409","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"7185:55410:40","type":"choice","text":"Older New Zealanders would be more attracted to consistency.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"审题: 题目问的是年长的新西兰人是否更倾向于一致性原则。\n定位关键词: “older New Zealanders,” “consistency”\n对应原文: G段，\"It may be that age is also a factor and that different generations would react differently to say, the ‘consistency’ principle. I suspect that younger people in this country would respond quite positively to this sort of approach, whereas their parents might be put off by any hint of a hard sell.\"\n解题思路: G段提到不同年龄段的人对“consistency principle”的反应不同。作者认为年轻人更愿意接受这种方式，而年长者则不接受这种强行推销的方式。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55410","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"55402","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>What point is the writer making about Robert Cialdini in the first paragraph?</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"55403","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>What is the writer doing in the second paragraph?</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"55404","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>What are we told about Cialdini’s research methodology?</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"55405","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>What was Cialdini’s research question for the towel experiment?</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"55406","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>The results of the towel experiment suggest that guests</strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"55670","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 32 - 36\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"55407","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>The writer sees evidence of the reciprocity principle in his own family.</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"55408","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Persuasion may operate in different ways in different countries.</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"55409","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>New Zealand diners are likely to leave tips if they are given chocolate.</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"55410","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 37 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Older New Zealanders would be more attracted to consistency.</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>The power of persuasion</strong></span><o:p></o:p></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong><br/></strong></span></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><em>A New Zealand restaurateur assesses some recent research from the USA</em></span></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><em><br/></em></span></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Some scientists peer at things through high-powered telescopes, others tempt rats through mazes or mix bubbling fluids in glass beakers. Then there is Robert Cialdini, whose unorthodox research involves such mundane items as towels and chocolates. Nonetheless, Cialdini believes he is discovering important insights into how society works, because he is conducting research into why some people are more persuasive than others.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Cialdini hopes that, by applying a little science, we should all be able to get our own way more often. This is in part a personal quest with its origins in his own experience: Cialdini claims that for his whole life he has been easy prey for salespeople and fundraisers who have managed to persuade him to buy things he did not want or give to charities he had never heard of.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">His research methodology has certainly raised a few eyebrows. Having concluded that laboratory experiments on the psychology of persuasion were telling only a part of the story, Cialdini began to probe influence in the real world, enrolling in sales-training programmes.&nbsp;In this way, he believes he learned first hand a great deal about how to sell automobiles from a car lot, insurance from an office, and even encyclopaedias door to door. Most recently his research has involved the now famous experiments with towels. Many hotels leave a little card in each bathroom asking guests to reuse towels and thus conserve water and reduce pollution. Cialdini and his colleagues wanted to test the relative effectiveness of different text on those cards.&nbsp;Could hotels best motivate their guests to co-operate simply because it would help save the planet, or were other factors more compelling?</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">To test this, the researchers redesigned the cards, replacing the environmental message with the simple (and truthful) statement that the majority of guests at the hotel had reused their towel at least once. Those guests who received this message were found to be 26% more likely to reuse their towel than those given the original message, and 74% more likely than those receiving no message at all.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">This was just one study that has enabled Cialdini to identify his Six Principles of Persuasion. The phenomenon revealed by the towel experiment he calls “social proof”: the idea that our decisions are influenced by what other people like us are doing. More perniciously, social proof is the force underpinning some people&#39;s anxiety not to be left behind by their neighbours, thus the desire for a bigger house or a faster car. A further principle, which he names ‘reciprocity’, was tested in a restaurant by measuring how patrons would respond to after-dinner chocolates.&nbsp;When the chocolates were dropped individually in front of each diner, tips went up 14%. This is reciprocity in action: we want to return favours done to us, often without bothering to accurately calculate whether what we are giving is proportionate to what we have received.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Cialdini’s research has established four more such principles. ‘Scarcity’ is the idea that people want more of things they can have less of, a notion that ‘advertisers ruthlessly exploit-limit of four per customer’. Parents can also make use of scarcity by telling their little ones that this is a very unusual chance so they should seize it immediately.&nbsp;The principle of ‘authority’ states that we trust people who know what they are talking about. Cialdini maintains that many professionals don&#39;t display their credentials, fearing it is boastful or arrogant to publicise their expertise. The principle he labels ‘consistency’ suggests that we want to act in ways that are consistent with undertaking we have already made. For example, if you are soliciting charitable donations, first ask colleagues if they think they will sponsor you. Later, return with a sponsorship form to those who said yes and remind them of their earlier undertaking. The final principle is ‘likeness’：we are more easily persuaded by those who seem similar to ourselves. In one study, people were sent survey forms and asked to return them to a named researcher. When the researcher falsely identified herself (e.g. Cynthia Johnson is sent a survey by ‘Cindy Johansen’), surveys were twice as likely to be completed.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Many of Cialdini’s claims about persuasion are just that – highly persuasive – and I can readily see evidence for some of them in my own workplace.&nbsp;But Cialdini’s experiments were conducted in the United States and I wonder how well all of his findings can be applied here in New Zealand or elsewhere around the world. For instance, I do understand the general principle of ‘reciprocity’ but cannot imagine New Zealand waiting staff using his cynical chocolate trick in their restaurants because the culture of tipping in this country is so different. But it is true that the way to a diner’s heart is to give them something they are not expecting in the way of service and in this country reciprocation would more likely take the form of a return visit to the restaurant and not a tip.&nbsp;It may be that age is also a factor and that different generations would react differently to say, the ‘consistency’ principle. I suspect that younger people in this country would respond quite positively to this sort of approach, whereas their parents might be put off by any hint of a hard sell.&nbsp;Perhaps in the end we must accept that some of us are simply born with more persuasion skills than others and that we have less control over such matters than Cialdini might like to think.</span></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7185&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7179","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Computer games","book":"阅读还原集Vol.9","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test3","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.9 · Test3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"7179:55375:1","type":"fill","text":"填写第 1 空","answer":"electronics","acceptedAnswers":["electronics"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是1970年代，由于技术进步使得某个东西变得便宜，从而促成了投币视频游戏的可能性。\n定位关键词：cheaper，coin-operated video games\n对应原文：B段“For use in video game arcades, using electronics was becoming economically feasible. ”\n解题思路：B段介绍了视频游戏的发展历史，指出在 1970年代，技术进步导致了使用电子设备从经济的角度变得可行。\n同义替换：cheaper  =economically feasible","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55375","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"7179:55376:2","type":"fill","text":"填写第 2 空","answer":"Pong","acceptedAnswers":["Pong"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是第一个成功的投币游戏是什么。\n定位关键词：first，coin-operated video game\n对应原文：C段“Pong took the industry by storm and quickly became the first coin-operated video-game. ”\n解题思路：本段介绍了视频游戏的发展历史，指出 Pong 是第一个成功的投币式视频游戏。\n同义替换：successful = took the industry by storm","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55376","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"7179:55377:3","type":"fill","text":"填写第 3 空","answer":"Atari","acceptedAnswers":["Atari"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是哪家公司被原始拥有者卖掉了。\n定位关键词：bought，original owners\n对应原文：C段“Yet despite early enthusiasm, consumer interest in this area proved less sustained than had been anticipated and, as prices started to drop and losses mounted, most of the early manufacturers withdrew from the field. Profits proved to be just as elusive at Bushnell's company, Atari, where a rapidly growing market presence in coin-operated machine and home video required greater injections of capital and more professional management than the company was able to provide. In 1976, the founders of Atari sold their share of the company for a sum that was only equivalent to their sales in that year.”\n解题思路：本文介绍了 Atari 公司的历史，指出其创始人于 1976 年将其股份出售。\n同义替换：original owners = founders","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55377","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"7179:55378:4","type":"fill","text":"填写第 4 空","answer":"graphics","acceptedAnswers":["graphics"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是Space Invaders因为什么特色成功。\n定位关键词：Space Invaders，colorful\n对应原文：D段“With its vibrant graphics it was so different from the previous black and white games that Space Invaders immediately captured public interest.”\n解题思路：本段介绍了《太空侵略者》游戏的成功，指出其原因之一是其鲜艳的图像vibrant graphics，这与之前的黑白游戏截然不同。\n同义替换：colourful = vibrant graphics","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55378","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"7179:55379:5","type":"fill","text":"填写第 5 空","answer":"females","acceptedAnswers":["females"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是哪个群体第一次被Pac-Man吸引。\n定位关键词：Pac-Man，attract\n对应原文：D段“Of these, Pac-Man (in 1980) was especially significant, because now females began to take an interest.”\n解题思路：本文介绍了《吃豆人》游戏的影响，指出它首次吸引了女性的兴趣。\n同义替换：attract = take an interest.","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55379","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"7179:55380:6","type":"fill","text":"填写第 6 空","answer":"Playstation","acceptedAnswers":["Playstation"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是在90年代末，哪款产品成为了最畅销的家庭娱乐产品。\n定位关键词：“By the end of the decade”和the biggest selling home entertainment product\n对应原文：G段“ In 1999 sales of game hardware and software, led by Playstation, were equal in size (around $7 billion) to US domestic box-office revenues.”\n解题思路：本文最后总结了视频游戏的发展历史，指出到 1990 年代末，视频游戏已成为最畅销的家用娱乐产品。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55380","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"7179:55353:7","type":"choice","text":"Spacewar was unpopular at first.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是《太空战争》最初是否不受欢迎。\n定位关键信息：关键词“Spacewar” 和 “unpopular”。\n对应原文：B段,The technological roots of video game can be traced back to 1962, when an MIT (Massachusetts Institute of Technology) graduate student demonstrated Spacewar, a science-fiction fantasy game played on a mainframe computer and a large screen. That game immediately attracted a wide cult following among computer buffs.\n解题思路：《太空战争》立即吸引了大量粉丝。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55353","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"7179:55349:8","type":"choice","text":"Bushnell and his team failed to create a coin-operated version of Spacewar.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是布什内尔和他的团队是否未能制作出投币版本的《太空战争》。\n定位关键信息：Bushnell, coin-operated version\n对应原文：But it was not until the early 1970s that Bushnell, a young graduate student in engineering at the University of Utah, came to the point of adapting Spacewar from a large computer into coin-operated form. For use in video game arcades, using electronics was becoming economically feasible. Bushnell and his associates began working on such a machine in a converted bedroom workshop, but were unsuccessful.\n解题思路：原文指出，20 世纪 70 年代初，当时还是犹他大学工程专业年轻研究生的布什内尔才着手将《太空大战》从大型计算机改编成投币式游戏。由于电子技术的发展，将其用于街机游戏在经济上变得可行。布什内尔和他的同事们在一个改装过的卧室工作室里开始研制这样的机器，但没有成功。\n同义替换：failed to create=were unsuccessful","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55349","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"7179:55350:9","type":"choice","text":"From the beginning the home video game market has been commercially successful.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是家用视频游戏市场从一开始是否就取得了商业成功。\n定位关键信息：关键词“home video game market” 和 “commercially successful”。\n对应原文：C段，Yet despite early enthusiasm, consumer interest in this area proved less sustained than had been anticipated and, as prices started to drop and losses mounted, most of the early manufacturers withdrew from the field.\n解题思路：原文说明，尽管起初热情高涨，但消费者在这一领域的兴趣却不如预期那样持久。随着价格开始下降，亏损不断增加，大多数早期制造商纷纷退出了这一领域。这表明早期家用视频游戏市场并未取得成功。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55350","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"7179:55351:10","type":"choice","text":"Atari was successful for the first time in 1979.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是Atari公司是否在1979年首次取得成功。\n定位关键信息：关键词“Atari” 和 “successful in 1979”。\n对应原文：E段，The impact on Atari was astounding. Unprofitable for the first three years, Atari had by the end of 1979, become a success.\n解题思路：Atari在1979年取得了首次成功。\n同义替换：successful=become a success","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55351","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"7179:55352:11","type":"choice","text":"Video arcade game usage continued strongly in the 1980s.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是街机游戏在80年代是否持续流行。\n定位关键信息：关键词“video arcade game usage” 和 “continued strongly in the 1980s”。\n对应原文：F段，By late 1982, the publics fascination with arcade games had begun to low down, and fewer potential best-sellers were becoming available for conversion to cartridges that could be used on an Atari machine.\n解题思路：街机游戏的热度在80年代减弱。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55352","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"7179:55354:12","type":"choice","text":"The time taken to produce a video game can be compared to producing a book.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是制作视频游戏的时间是否可与制作书籍相比较。\n定位关键信息：关键词“time taken” 和 “compared to producing a book”。\n对应原文：F段，At the same time, the market was flooded with illegal software of all types. It was thus not until the late 1980s that the unstructured nature of the industry, at least on the software side, had stabilized and become restructured in a manner similar, in many respects, to the book publishing business.\n解题思路：原文提到视频游戏开发和图书出版有相似性，但未提到具体的时间。\n同义替换： time taken=restructured in a manner similar","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55354","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"7179:55355:13","type":"choice","text":"The qualities needed for a video game to become successful have been researched thoroughly.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是成功视频游戏的要素是否已被彻底研究。\n定位关键信息：关键词“qualities needed” 和 “researched thoroughly”。\n对应原文：H段，However, no matter what the technology or the format, the essence of a successful game will always be the same: it is simple to understand and to play on an elementary level, but it is compulsive and maddeningly difficult – in fact, forever impossible-to master fully.\n解题思路：原文提到无论技术和形式如何发展，游戏成功的要素是相同的，对应题目中游戏的要素是否已被彻底研究。\n同义替换：qualities =essence","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55355","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"55375","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>A history of video games</strong></p><p><strong>1960s</strong></p><p>•&nbsp;Spacewar was first played on a computer and special screen.</p><p><strong>1970s</strong></p><p>•&nbsp;Advances in technology led to cheaper <strong class=\"source-blank\">[1] ____</strong>&nbsp;and the possibility of coin-operated video games.</p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"55376","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>•&nbsp;The first successful coin-operated video game was <strong class=\"source-blank\">[2] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"55377","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>• <strong class=\"source-blank\">[3] ____</strong>&nbsp;was bought from its original owners.</p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"55378","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>•&nbsp;Space Invaders was successful because of its colourful <strong class=\"source-blank\">[4] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"55379","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>1980s</strong></p><p>•&nbsp;Pac-Man was the first game to attract <strong class=\"source-blank\">[5] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"55380","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>1990s</strong></p><p>•&nbsp;At first one company dominated the market.</p><p>•&nbsp;By the end of the decade <strong class=\"source-blank\">[6] ____</strong>&nbsp;had become the biggest selling home entertainment product.</p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"55353","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Spacewar was unpopular at first.</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"55349","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Bushnell and his team failed to create a coin-operated version of Spacewar.</strong></p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"55350","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>From the beginning the home video game market has been commercially successful.</strong></p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"55351","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Atari was successful for the first time in 1979.</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"55352","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Video arcade game usage continued strongly in the 1980s.</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"55354","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The time taken to produce a video game can be compared to producing a book.</strong></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"55355","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The qualities needed for a video game to become successful have been researched thoroughly.</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Computer games</strong></span><o:p></o:p></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><em><strong><br/></strong></em></span></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><em>The early days of the video game business</em></span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">It&#39;s not whether you win or lose<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; text-wrap: wrap;\">,&nbsp;</span>but how you play the game.In the age of computers<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; text-wrap: wrap;\">,&nbsp;</span>that statement takes on new meanings: video game cannot ever really be defeated because<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; text-wrap: wrap;\">,&nbsp;</span>no matter how high the score<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; text-wrap: wrap;\">.&nbsp;</span>It is always the human who tires first or makes the fatal error. But millions of people continue to play<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; text-wrap: wrap;\">,&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; text-wrap: wrap;\"></span>because microelectronic technology has enabled game designers to conveniently and inexpensively transform plain screens into playfields of extraordinary capability. At the same time, a multi-billion dollar industry has grown from very humble beginnings in just a few decades.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The technological roots of video game can be traced back to 1962, when an MIT (Massachusetts Institute of Technology) graduate student demonstrated Spacewar, a science-fiction fantasy game played on a mainframe computer and a large screen. That game immediately attracted a wide cult following among computer buffs.&nbsp;The next important step came in 1968, when a console was developed that could be used to play game on ordinary televisions. But it was not until the early 1970s that Bushnell, a young graduate student in engineering at the University of Utah, came to the point of adapting Spacewar from a large computer into coin-operated form. For use in video game arcades, using electronics was becoming economically feasible. Bushnell and his associates began working on such a machine in a converted bedroom workshop, but were unsuccessful.&nbsp;What they ultimately developed instead was a simple tennis-like game that they named Pong.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Pong took the industry by storm and quickly became the first coin-operated video-game.&nbsp;And soon thereafter commercial Pong-style home video games also appeared. Yet despite early enthusiasm, consumer interest in this area proved less sustained than had been anticipated and, as prices started to drop and losses mounted, most of the early manufacturers withdrew from the field.&nbsp;Profits proved to be just as elusive at Bushnell&#39;s company, Atari, where a rapidly growing market presence in coin-operated machine and home video required greater injections of capital and more professional management than the company was able to provide. In 1976, the founders of Atari sold their share of the company for a sum that was only equivalent to their sales in that year.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">At that point, coin-operated video games seemed just another passing fad. But the introduction of Space Invaders-an arcade model produced by Japanese manufacture Taito-proved otherwise. With its vibrant graphics it was so different from the previous black and white games that Space Invaders immediately captured public interest.&nbsp;There soon followed a rush of popular video that employed the same or better hardware and even more imaginative software. Of these, Pac-Man (in 1980) was especially significant, because now females began to take an interest.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">By this time, the same software improvement and technological advances (faster microprocessors and larger memories) that permitted designers to produce spectacular audio and visual effects for coin-operated machines were also being applied to home video units. It was thus only a short while before the programmable consoles that had been unpopular for lack of software suddenly began to sell in large numbers: consumers had discovered that they could finally play a reasonable version of their favorite arcade games in the comfort of their own home. The impact on Atari was astounding. Unprofitable for the first three years, Atari had by the end of 1979, become a success.&nbsp;By either self-designing or licensing the most popular arcade concepts for cartridge format for use at home, the company had captured some 80 percent of the worldwide market for home video games.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">All of this, however, was too good to last. By late 1982, the publics fascination with arcade games had begun to low down, and fewer potential best-sellers were becoming available for conversion to cartridges that could be used on an Atari machine.&nbsp;At the same time, the market was flooded with illegal software of all types. It was thus not until the late 1980s that the unstructured nature of the industry, at least on the software side, had stabilized and become restructured in a manner similar, in many respects, to the book publishing business.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Until 1986, when Japan-based Nintendo introduced a more technologically sophisticated and user-friendly game console, the hardware side was also in disarray. But with tight control of software development and marketing, Nintendo was able to revive and then capture up to 80 percent of a once-again booming market in which no significant competition appeared until the early 1990s. By that point, the annual operating profits of Nintendo had already grown to over $1 billion<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; text-wrap: wrap;\">&nbsp;–&nbsp;</span>an amount exceeding the 1991 profits of all the major Hollywood film studios combined. In 1999 sales of game hardware and software, led by Playstation, were equal in size (around $7 billion) to US domestic box-office revenues.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">With change the only constant<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; text-wrap: wrap;\">,&nbsp;</span>the game industry has moved on to become what it is today. However<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; text-wrap: wrap;\">,&nbsp;</span>no matter what the technology or the format<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; text-wrap: wrap;\">,&nbsp;</span>the essence of a successful game will always be the same: it is simple to understand and to play on an elementary level<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; text-wrap: wrap;\">,&nbsp;</span>but it is compulsive and maddeningly difficult – in fact<span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; text-wrap: wrap;\">,&nbsp;</span>forever impossible-to master fully.</span></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7179&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7181","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Art and engineering","book":"阅读还原集Vol.9","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test3","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.9 · Test3 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"7181:55356:14","type":"fill","text":"14 a time when a transport system became an inspiration for artists","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是哪个段落讲述了交通系统成为艺术家的灵感来源。\n定位关键信息：“transport system”和“inspiration”\n对应原文：E段，“In the 19th century, the railways were another feat of engineering which captured the imagination of painters, and the steam engine in the distance of a landscape became as much a part of it as the herd of cows in the foreground.”\n解题思路：文章中E段提到19世纪铁路工程吸引了画家的想象力，蒸汽火车成为风景画的一部分。\n同义替换：transport system=railways；inspiration=imagination","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55356","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the seven paragraphs (A - G). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - G). You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"7181:55356:15","type":"fill","text":"15 a reference to the current trend of including artists in engineering projects","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是哪个段落讲述了当前将艺术家纳入工程项目的趋势。\n定位关键信息：“current trend”和“including artists in engineering projects”\n对应原文：G段，“Increasingly, commissioners of bridges in the US are looking to such individuals, to teams of engineers and architects who work with artists.”\n解题思路：文章中G段提到，美国桥梁的委托人越来越倾向于寻找与艺术家合作的工程师和建筑师团队。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55356","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the seven paragraphs (A - G). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - G). You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"7181:55356:16","type":"fill","text":"16 reasons for the idea that art and engineering are difficult to combine","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题题目问的是哪个段落讲述了艺术与工程难以结合的原因。\n定位关键信息：“reasons”和“combine”\n对应原文：A段，“The relationship between art and engineering has seldom been easy or consistent.”\n解题思路：文章中A段提到艺术与工程之间的关系很少是轻松或一致的。\n同义替换：combine=consistent","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55356","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the seven paragraphs (A - G). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - G). You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"7181:55356:17","type":"fill","text":"17 how the depiction of human labour involved danger to an artist","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是哪个段落讲述了艺术家描绘人力劳动时面临危险。\n定位关键信息：“human labour”、“danger”和“artist”\n对应原文：B段，“Hine put his own life at risk to photograph workers suspended on cables hundreds of feet in the air, or sitting on a high girder eating lunch.”\n解题思路：文章中B段提到Lewis Hine冒着生命危险去拍摄工人的照片，通过这个事例来表明艺术家描绘人力劳动时面临危险。\n同义替换：human labour =workers； danger=risk","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55356","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the seven paragraphs (A - G). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - G). You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"7181:55356:18","type":"fill","text":"18 a reference to an artist who celebrated a number of unfinished structures","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是哪个段落赞扬了一些未完成结构的艺术家。\n定位关键信息：“artist”和“unfinished structures”\n对应原文：F段，“He is perhaps best known for his prints of the Panama Canal as it neared completion and of the partially completed Hell Gate and Delaware River Bridges.”\n解题思路：文章中F段提到Joseph Pennell以描绘接近完工的巴拿马运河和部分完成的Hell Gate和Delaware River桥梁而闻名。\n同义替换：unfinished structures=partially completed","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55356","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the seven paragraphs (A - G). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - G). You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"7181:55356:19","type":"fill","text":"19 a reference to two large engineering works that are symbols of their locations","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是哪个段落讲述了两个大型工程作品成为其所在地象征的参考。\n定位关键信息：“two large engineering works”和“symbols”\n对应原文：A段，Critics of technology protest against what they see. At the same time, megastructures such as the Brooklyn and Golden Gate Bridges in the US are hailed as majestic human achievements, as well as great engineering monuments that have come to embody the spirit of their respective cities.\n解题思路：文章中A段提到美国的布鲁克林大桥和金门大桥是伟大的人类成就，也是伟大的工程纪念碑，体现了它们各自城市的精神。\n同义替换：two large engineering works=Brooklyn and Golden Gate Bridges；symbols=spirit","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55356","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the seven paragraphs (A - G). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - G). You may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"7181:55516:20","type":"choice","text":"20 His engineering constructions are also regarded as works of art.","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是哪个学者的工程建筑也被视为艺术作品。\n定位关键信息：Santiago Calatrava\n对应原文：G段，Today, one of the most innovative and influential engineers is Santiago Calatrava, who also trained as an architect. His bridges and other structures provide public spaces on a human scale, and stand as pieces of sculpture in their own right.\n解题思路：文章中提到Santiago Calatrava的桥梁和其他结构不仅提供了人性化的公共空间，而且本身就是雕塑作品。\n同义替换：regarded as=stand as","options":["Lewis Hine","Charles Sheeler","Abraham Darby","Michael Rooker","Claude Monet","Joseph Pennell","Santiago Calatrava"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"55516","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20 - 22\nChoose the correct person (A - G) for each statement.\nList of People\nA Lewis Hine\nB Charles Sheeler\nC Abraham Darby\nD Michael Rooker\nE Claude Monet\nF Joseph Pennell\nG Santiago Calatrava"},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"7181:55516:21","type":"choice","text":"21 He created images of builders constructing an iconic American skyscraper.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是哪个学者创造了建造受欢迎的美国摩天大楼的建筑工人的图像。\n定位关键信息：Lewis Hine\n对应原文：B段，“This resulted in a series of striking photographs which have become familiar images of daring. Hine put his own life at risk to photograph workers suspended on cables hundreds of feet in the air, or sitting on a high girder eating lunch.”\n解题思路：文章中提到Lewis Hine拍摄了建造帝国大厦的工人的一系列引人注目的照片。\n同义替换：builders=workers","options":["Lewis Hine","Charles Sheeler","Abraham Darby","Michael Rooker","Claude Monet","Joseph Pennell","Santiago Calatrava"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"55516","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20 - 22\nChoose the correct person (A - G) for each statement.\nList of People\nA Lewis Hine\nB Charles Sheeler\nC Abraham Darby\nD Michael Rooker\nE Claude Monet\nF Joseph Pennell\nG Santiago Calatrava"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"7181:55516:22","type":"choice","text":"22 He painted a building connected with a significant innovation in transport.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是哪个学者画了与交通重要创新相关的建筑。\n定位关键信息：Claude Monet\n对应原文：E段，“The Impressionist Claude Monet painted railway stations – such as the Gare St-Lazare in Paris – as well as flower and gardens. ”\n解题思路：文章中提到印象派画家Claude Monet画了与铁路相关的建筑，如巴黎的Gare St-Lazare火车站。","options":["Lewis Hine","Charles Sheeler","Abraham Darby","Michael Rooker","Claude Monet","Joseph Pennell","Santiago Calatrava"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"sourceGroupId":"55516","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20 - 22\nChoose the correct person (A - G) for each statement.\nList of People\nA Lewis Hine\nB Charles Sheeler\nC Abraham Darby\nD Michael Rooker\nE Claude Monet\nF Joseph Pennell\nG Santiago Calatrava"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"7181:55360:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"stone","acceptedAnswers":["stone"],"explanation":"审题: 题目询问18世纪晚期之前桥梁的主要建筑材料。\n定位关键信息: “before the late 18th century”和“wood”\n对应原文: D段，“In the late 18th century, Abraham Darby cast the large iron ribs that formed the world's first iron bridge, a dramatic departure from the classic stone and timber bridges that dotted the countryside and had been captured in numerous landscape paintings.”。\n解题思路: 原文提到在18世纪晚期之前的传统桥梁是用石头和木材（timber）建造的。\n同义替换：traditionally =classic","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55360","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"7181:55360:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"Abraham Darby","acceptedAnswers":["Abraham Darby"],"explanation":"审题: 题目要求填写工程师的名字。\n定位关键信息: 关键词是“engineer”和“innovative bridge”\n对应原文: D段，“In the late 18th century, Abraham Darby cast the large iron ribs that formed the world's first iron bridge, a dramatic departure from the classic stone and timber bridges that dotted the countryside and had been captured in numerous landscape paintings.\"\n解题思路: 原文提到Abraham Darby是铸造铁桥的大工程师。\n同义替换：manufactured=formed","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55360","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"7181:55360:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"River Severn","acceptedAnswers":["River Severn"],"explanation":"审题: 题目要求填写铁桥跨越的河流名称。\n定位关键信息: \"an innovative bridge\",“across”\n对应原文: D段，“This structure still spans the River Severn, and the Coalbrookdale Museum is crowded with its portraits, showing the iron structure not as a blight on the landscape, but as its focal point.”\n解题思路: 原文提到铁桥跨越的是Severn河。\n同义替换：central feature=focal point","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55360","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"7181:55360:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"Michael Rooker","acceptedAnswers":["Michael Rooker"],"explanation":"审题: 题目要求填写某位画家的名字，说明铁桥是多幅艺术作品的主题。\n定位关键信息: \"iron bridge\",“subject of a number of artworks”\n对应原文: D段，“This is how Michael Rooker shows the iron bridge in his late 18th-century painting, in which the surrounding area radiates out from the bridge and pales behind it.”\n解题思路: 原文提到迈克尔·鲁克创作了一幅描绘这座铁桥的著名画作。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55360","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","maxWords":2}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"55356","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the seven paragraphs (A - G). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nChoose the correct letter (A - G). You may choose any letter more than once.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"55516","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 20 - 22\nChoose the correct person (A - G) for each statement.\nList of People\nA Lewis Hine\nB Charles Sheeler\nC Abraham Darby\nD Michael Rooker\nE Claude Monet\nF Joseph Pennell\nG Santiago Calatrava","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"55360","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 23 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS in each gap.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>The iron bridge</strong></p><p>Before the late 18th century, bridges were traditionally constructed of wood and <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong>. Then the engineer <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> manufactured the elements of an innovative bridge across the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong>. This iron bridge was the subject of a number of artworks, including a notable one by <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong>. While some may have viewed it as ugly, artists regarded the bridge as a central feature of the landscape.</p>","firstNumber":23}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>Art and engineering</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p>Works of engineering and technology are sometimes viewed as having nothing to do with art and humanity. Think of the connotation of assembly lines, robots and computers. The positive values associated with these creations can be overwhelmed by the negative associations of repetitive, stressful work and threatened jobs. Critics of technology protest against what they see. At the same time, megastructures such as the Brooklyn and Golden Gate Bridges in the US are hailed as majestic human achievements, as well as great engineering monuments that have come to embody the spirit of their respective cities. The relationship between art and engineering has seldom been easy or consistent.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Arguably, the assembly line process associated with Henry Ford made workers tools of the system. The human worker may have appeared to be only a cog in the wheel of industry, yet photographers such as Lewis Hine revealed the beauty of line and composition in his study of a worker using a wrench to turn a bolt. Hine focused on the individuals engaged in the work. In the period around World War I, he visited New York and was given the opportunity to record the construction of the famous Empire State Building, the tallest building of its time. This resulted in a series of striking photographs which have become familiar images of daring.&nbsp;Hine put his own life at risk to photograph workers suspended on cables hundreds of feet in the air, or sitting on a high girder eating lunch.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">When Ford&#39;s enormous River Rouge plant opened in 1927, the painter/photographer Charles Sheeler was chosen to photograph it. The world&#39;s largest car plant captured the imagination of Sheeler, who described it as the most thrilling subject he had ever had to work with.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Long before Hine and Sheeler, other photographers and painters had seen the art and humanity in works of engineering and technology. This is perhaps nowhere more evident than in the Coalbrookdale Museum of Iron, at Ironbridge in Shropshire in the UK. In the late 18th century, Abraham Darby cast the large iron ribs that formed the world&#39;s first iron bridge, a dramatic departure from the classic stone and timber bridges that dotted the countryside and had been captured in numerous landscape paintings.&nbsp;This structure still spans the River Severn, and the Coalbrookdale Museum is crowded with its portraits, showing the iron structure not as a blight on the landscape, but as its focal point.&nbsp;This is how Michael Rooker shows the iron bridge in his late 18th-century painting, in which the surrounding area radiates out from the bridge and pales behind it.&nbsp;Countless other contemporary representations of the bridge hang in the nearby museum.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">In the 19th century, the railways were another feat of engineering which captured the imagination of painters, and the steam engine in the distance of a landscape became as much a part of it as the herd of cows in the foreground.&nbsp;The Impressionist Claude Monet painted railway stations – such as the Gare St-Lazare in Paris – as well as flower and gardens.&nbsp;By the 20th century, engineering, technology and industry were very well established as subjects for artists.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">American-born artist Joseph Pennell portrayed buildings under construction and shrouded in scaffolding, and recorded scenes of industry during World War I. He is perhaps best known for his prints of the Panama Canal as it neared completion and of the partially completed Hell Gate and Delaware River Bridges.&nbsp;Pennell has often been quoted as saying, &#39;Great engineering is great art&#39;, a sentiment that he expressed repeatedly. He wrote of his contemporaries: &#39;I understand nothing of engineering, but I know that engineers are the greatest architects and the most pictorial builders since the (ancient) Greeks.&#39; Pennell called the sensation that he felt when he looked at a great construction project &#39;the Wonder of Work&#39;. He saw engineering as a process memorialized in every completed dam, skyscraper, bridge or other great engineering feat.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Today, one of the most innovative and influential engineers is Santiago Calatrava, who also trained as an architect. His bridges and other structures provide public spaces on a human scale, and stand as pieces of sculpture in their own right.&nbsp;Increasingly, commissioners of bridges in the US are looking to such individuals, to teams of engineers and architects who work with artists. The growing awareness of the intangible added value of art is sure to give us more masterpieces like the Brooklyn Bridge. They in turn will continue to be noble monuments to civilization and will be welcome subjects for artists of all kinds.</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7181&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7180","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Evolutionary Psychology in the Workplace","book":"阅读还原集Vol.9","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test3","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.9 · Test3 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"7180:55361:27","type":"choice","text":"The writers purpose in the first paragraph is to","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是作者在第一段中的目的是什么。\n定位关键词： first paragraph，purpose\n对应原文： A段，“Nevertheless, Darwinian evolutionary theory is the foundation of a new wave of ideas about human behavior in general and particularly the way people behave in the workplace; these ideas have given the title of evolutionary psychology.”\n解题思路： 段落 A 中介绍了达尔文的进化论，随后提到“evolutionary psychology” (进化心理学) 是关于人类行为的新思想浪潮的基础。作者的目的主要是解释进化心理学，并引入该概念。作者并没有提出对达尔文理论的反对，也没有进行不同观点的对比，而是在解释进化心理学的概念和基础理论。","options":["oppose the views of Charles Darwin.","compare experts' opinions of Darwin's theory.","explain the theory of evolutionary psychology.","name experts in the field of evolutionary psychology."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55361","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"7180:55362:28","type":"choice","text":"In the third paragraph which view about evolutionary psychology matches Nicholson's opinion？","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是与Nicholson的观点相匹配的进化心理学观点是什么。\n定位关键词：Nicholson's opinion, third paragraph\n对应原文： C段，“Nicholson maintains that evolutionary psychology dismisses the long-held assumption that our minds are like blank pages just waiting for culture and experience to write on them and shape our nature. He points out that sophisticated research shows the brain actually houses a store of knowledge when we are born, and now genetic research is establishing there are certain genes that account for abilities, tastes and tendencies.”\n解题思路：原文提到 Nicholson 的观点，Nicholson认为我们的思想并不是一张空白的纸，即进化心理学，他认为我们的大脑天生就储存了一些知识，并且一些特定的基因决定了我们的能力、兴趣和倾向。 这表明我们从祖先那里继承了思想和特征。","options":["Our characters determine our career choices.","We begin life without any preconceived notions.","Our interests and skills depend on our environment.","We inherit ideas and characteristics from our ancestors."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55362","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"7180:55363:29","type":"choice","text":"The writer discusses the key element of emotion in order to","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是作者讨论情感这个关键元素的目的是什么。\n定位关键词： emotion，key element\n对应原文： D段，“One key element is emotion. Emotion was originally essential to keep early man alive and safe from predators. Emotion was, and continues to be our radar, guiding us throughout today's techno-defined business world. Despite this, the business world emphasizes rational not emotional behaviour, and does not admit the importance of emotion. We still use the emotional part of our minds to make sense other people's behaviour and to create an impression, so we can often be taken in by appearances.”\n解题思路：原文提到情绪是早期人类生存的关键，它仍然是我们的“雷达”，指引我们在当今以科技为主导的商业世界中航行。 尽管工作世界强调理性行为，但人们通过情感理解和回应他人的行为，情绪有其重要性。 这段话解释了为什么情绪会影响我们在工作场所的感受和行为。总的来说，作者通过讨论情感，解释了我们在工作中的行为。","options":["criticize primitive survival strategies.","explain attitudes and actions at work.","demonstrate the slowness of evolution.","suggest companies today are poorly structured."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55363","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"7180:55364:30","type":"choice","text":"Which of the following does Nicholson predict will happen in the business world？","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是Nicholson对商业世界的预测。\n定位关键词： Nicholson，prediction\n对应原文： F段，“He doubts that the high-tech ideas of virtual companies will ever be very successful because people will still want to meet each other face-to-face.\"\n解题思路： 原文提到Nicholsona认为尽管人们可以在家工作，但他们仍然会更喜欢传统的协作方式，仍然会想要面对面交流，因为这不会让他们与工作社区孤立。 这表明社会互动将继续对员工很重要，将继续在工作中扮演重要角色。\n同义替换：Social interaction = meet each other face-to-face","options":["Companies will remain in city centres.","Promotion will no longer motivate people.","Employees will be less independent than now.","Social interaction will remain important to workers."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55364","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"7180:55365:31","type":"choice","text":"Which of the following is the most suitable title for Reading Passage 3？","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是最适合的文章标题是什么。\n定位关键词： title\n解题思路： 在 A 段，文章开头提到达尔文的进化论被用于解释人类行为，特别是工作场所的行为。进化心理学帮助理解人类大脑和行为的进化背景。B 段进一步解释了尼科尔森（Nicholson）的观点，认为进化心理学有助于分析和解决组织内的问题。C、D 段则介绍了进化心理学的关键概念，如情绪对人类生存和职场行为的影响。因此整篇文章讨论的是进化心理学对工作场所行为的理解及其对商业世界的应用，并讨论了进化心理学如何帮助理解工作场所的行为。\n文章的重点并不在企业管理的变化上，因此“How successful companies manage change.”是错误选项。文章中并没有讨论对达尔文理论的拒绝，反而是利用达尔文的理论解释职场行为，因此“Darwin's theories rejected by modern management. ”是错误选项。文章并没有主要讨论工业后期的组织需要快速进化，因此“Why post-industrial organizations need to evolve more quickly.”是错误选项。","options":["How successful companies manage change","Understanding the origins of workplace behavior","Darwin's theories rejected by modern management","Why post-industrial organizations need to evolve more quickly"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55365","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"7180:55366:32","type":"choice","text":"Nicholson makes a persuasive argument in his book.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是 Nicholson 是否在他的书中提出了有说服力的论点。\n定位关键词： Nicholson，book\n对应原文： B段，“His book takes the reader on a journey from the Stonc Age plains of the savannah to the modern office，and includes a discussion of Darwinism and behavioral psychology together with a dissection of dysfunctional organizational behavior. It is an effective approach explaining why people behave as they do，particularly at work. ”\n解题思路： 原文提到了 Nicholson 的著作《管理人类动物》 (Managing the Human Animal)，并指出该书通过解释人们的行为方式来帮助管理者理解工作场所的问题。作者说明这是一个解释人们行为原因的有效办法，因此可以说Nicholson 在书中提出了一个有说服力的论点。\n同义替换：persuasive argument = effective approach","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55366","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"7180:55367:33","type":"choice","text":"Tooby and Cosmides believe natural selection through the generations has prepared.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是Tooby和Cosmides是否相信自然选择通过几代人的传递为我们做好了准备。\n定位关键词： Tooby and Cosmides\n对应原文： C段，“As Tooby and Cosmides stress, there have not been enough generations for a brain that is well adapted to our post-industrial life to evolve through natural selection.”。\n解题思路： 原文提到了 Tooby 和 Cosmides 的观点，即我们的大脑从石器时代开始就没有太大变化。 他们认为我们的大脑还没有进化到足以适应现代工业化后的生活。 这表明他们并不认为我们的大脑已经为现代工作场所做好准备。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55367","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"7180:55368:34","type":"choice","text":"Our reliance on technology causes emotional problems in the workplace.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是我们对技术的依赖是否导致了工作中的情感问题。\n定位关键词： reliance on technology，emotional problems\n对应原文： D段，“Emotion was, and continues to be our radar, guiding us throughout today's techno-defined business world.”\n解题思路： 文章并没有明确指出技术依赖是否会导致情绪问题，只提到了情绪在工作场所的重要性，但没有将它与技术联系起来。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55368","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"7180:55369:35","type":"choice","text":"People today are more trusting than they used to be.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是人们今天是否比过去更容易信任他人。\n定位关键词： people today，more trusting\n对应原文： D段，“As a consequence, it takes very little to trigger people's innate distrust of others because our safety in antiquity depended on supporting our near family and friends whom we valued more than other people.”\n解题思路：原文提到了在当今时代，我们的大脑会自然地重建我们的祖先社区，我们会因此对他人产生不信任感，并且我们祖先生活在小型社区，我们的安全感来源于支持我们的家人和朋友，天生对他人存有猜疑。 这表明作者并不认为现代人比过去更信任他人。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55369","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"7180:55636:36","type":"choice","text":"Nicholson's advice to the corporate world\nNicholson believes that if we know why people act the way they do, we can change ____ so employees will work more efficiently.","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"定位信息：employees, more efficently\n对应原文：E段， He thinks that by knowing the reasons for people's behaviour it is possible to mould corporate environments into places that have more chance of working efficiently and being pleasant places to work in.\n解题思路：原文指出尼科尔森认为了解人们行为的原因能够改变公司环境，使之更加高效。\n同义替换：why=reasons; act=behaviour; change=corporate","options":["business leaders","MBA graduates","promotion structures","reward strategy","magic formula","strategic planning","back-to-front thinking","business environments","human nature"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"55636","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"7180:55636:37","type":"choice","text":"Nicholson's ideas are unwelcome to ____ but some executives are more open to what evolutionary psychology says.","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"定位信息：Nicholson's ideas, evolutionary psychology\n对应原文：E段，One group that resist the theory of evolutionary psychology is young MBA graduates who are just beginning their careers and feel that evolutionary psychology will make their lives at work more difficult.\n解题思路：原文指出年轻的MBA毕业生对尼科尔森的观点持抵触态度。\n同义替换：unwelcome=resist；business structures = business environments","options":["business leaders","MBA graduates","promotion structures","reward strategy","magic formula","strategic planning","back-to-front thinking","business environments","human nature"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"55636","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"7180:55636:38","type":"choice","text":"However, these executives still believe that there is a ____ that will make employees act according to the company's practices.","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"定位信息：executives\n对应原文：E段    Older and wiser executives points out that they still tend to cling to the idea of a magic formula to bring people into line with corporate strategy.\n解题思路：原文指出了许多高层管理人员仍然相信存在一种“灵丹妙药” (magic formula) 可以让员工按照公司战略行事。","options":["business leaders","MBA graduates","promotion structures","reward strategy","magic formula","strategic planning","back-to-front thinking","business environments","human nature"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"55636","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"7180:55636:39","type":"choice","text":"According to Nicholson, these senior executives are engaging in ____ and","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"定位信息：Nicholson， executives\n对应原文：E段    But that is back-to-front thinking according to Nicholson,who contends that we should be reinventing our business structures not our fundamental human nature.\n解题思路：原文指出了 Nicholson 批评高层管理人员的思维方式是“本末倒置” (back-to-front thinking)，他们试图改变人类天性，而不是改变商业结构。","options":["business leaders","MBA graduates","promotion structures","reward strategy","magic formula","strategic planning","back-to-front thinking","business environments","human nature"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"55636","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"7180:55636:40","type":"choice","text":"we should not try to change ____ but instead we should change our business structures.","answer":"I","acceptedAnswers":["I"],"explanation":"定位信息：business structures\n对应原文：E段，But that is back-to-front thinking according to Nicholson,who contends that we should be reinventing our business structures not our fundamental human nature.\n解题思路：原文指出了 Nicholson 批评高层管理人员的思维方式是“本末倒置” (back-to-front thinking)，他们试图改变人类天性（human nature），而不是改变商业结构。","options":["business leaders","MBA graduates","promotion structures","reward strategy","magic formula","strategic planning","back-to-front thinking","business environments","human nature"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"],"sourceGroupId":"55636","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"55361","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>The writers purpose in the first paragraph is to</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"55362","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>In the third paragraph which view about evolutionary psychology matches Nicholson&#39;s opinion？</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"55363","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>The writer discusses the key element of emotion in order to</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"55364","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>Which of the following does Nicholson predict will happen in the business world？</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"55365","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 31\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>Which of the following is the most suitable title for Reading Passage 3？</strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"55366","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Nicholson makes a persuasive argument in his book.</strong></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"55367","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Tooby and Cosmides believe natural selection through the generations has prepared.</strong></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"55368","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Our reliance on technology causes emotional problems in the workplace.</strong></p>","firstNumber":34},{"id":"55369","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 32 - 35\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>People today are more trusting than they used to be.</strong></p>","firstNumber":35},{"id":"55636","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete the summary using the list of words. Choose the correct word and move it into the gap.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":36}],"passage":"<p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Charles Darwin, the brilliant anthropologist and creator of the theory of evolution, is not normally associated with the modern business world. Nevertheless, Darwinian evolutionary theory is the foundation of a new wave of ideas about human behavior in general and particularly the way people behave in the workplace; these ideas have given the title of evolutionary psychology.&nbsp;Evolutionary psychology revolves around the notion that our brains, like our bodies, have an inherited evolutionary design that has scarcely changed for 10,000 years. As respected evolutionary psychology experts Leda Cosmides and John Tooby comment, our modern skulls house a Stone Age mind. The US biologist Edward O Wilson sees evolutionary psychology as being a discipline which is based on both socio-biology, which is the study of the biological basis of social behavior, and psychology, which is the systematic study of human behavior.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Nigel Nicholson, an organizational psychologist from the London Business School, is a strong supporter of evolutionary psychology and on this subject has published Managing the Human Animal. His book takes the reader on a journey from the Stonc Age plains of the savannah to the modern office，and includes a discussion of Darwinism and behavioral psychology together with a dissection of dysfunctional organizational behavior. It is an effective approach explaining why people behave as they do，particularly at work.&nbsp;Evolutionary psychology is increasingly being cited in management circles，where managers are trying to understand puzzling aspects of human behaviour and by doing so improve the workplace. Nicholson believes that evolutionary psychology can help managers understand what goes wrong in organizational life and what they can do about it.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Nicholson maintains that evolutionary psychology dismisses the long-held assumption that our minds are like blank pages just waiting for culture and experience to write on them and shape our nature. He points out that sophisticated research shows the brain actually houses a store of knowledge when we are born, and now genetic research is establishing there are certain genes that account for abilities, tastes and tendencies. The stored knowledge in the human brain has not changed much since the Stone Age. As Tooby and Cosmides stress, there have not been enough generations for a brain that is well adapted to our post-industrial life to evolve through natural selection.</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The evolutionary psychology version of human nature revolves around some key elements which we have inherited from our hunter-gatherer minds. One key element is emotion. Emotion was originally essential to keep early man alive and safe from predators. Emotion was, and continues to be our radar, guiding us throughout today&#39;s techno-defined business world.&nbsp;Despite this, the business world emphasizes rational not emotional behaviour, and does not admit the importance of emotion. We still use the emotional part of our minds to make sense other people&#39;s behaviour and to create an impression, so we can often be taken in by appearances.&nbsp;This mental predisposition actually works best in small communities (the tribe) not in much larger environments filled with people we barely know (the modern workplace). Our minds naturally try to re-create our ancestral communities with networks of no more than 150 people, where there are clear hierarchies and leaders. As a consequence, it takes very little to trigger people&#39;s innate distrust of others because our safety in antiquity depended on supporting our near family and friends whom we valued more than other people.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">So what advice does Nicholson have for the corporate world？He thinks that by knowing the reasons for people&#39;s behaviour it is possible to mould corporate environments into places that have more chance of working efficiently and being pleasant places to work in.&nbsp;Nicholson admits that not everybody in the business world agrees with his belief in the effectiveness of evolutionary psychology in the workplace. One group that resist the theory of evolutionary psychology is young MBA graduates who are just beginning their careers and feel that evolutionary psychology will make their lives at work more difficult.&nbsp;Older and wiser executives points out that they still tend to cling to the idea of a magic formula to bring people into line with corporate strategy.&nbsp;But that is back-to-front thinking according to Nicholson，who contends that we should be reinventing our business structures not our fundamental human nature.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">At the end of his book, Nicholson gives his forecast of what will and will not change in the business world. He believes that most people will still prefer more traditional forms of work and throughout their lives will continue to aim at lifelong status advancement.&nbsp;He also maintains that the line between work and home will be less defined, but that people will prefer traditional working patterns if working from home leaves them isolated from their work community. He doubts that the high-tech ideas of virtual companies will ever be very successful because people will still want to meet each other face-to-face. Nicholson describes his ideal organization in the future: it would be decentralized, with small sub-units: the staff would be from diverse backgrounds and be allowed a high degree of self-determination. New endeavors and creativity would replace systems and rationality. Nicholson acknowledges that there is a long way to go in terms of the translation of his ideas of evolutionary psychology into practical propositions, but he is confident more and more people will come round to his way of thinking.</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7180&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7171","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Ahead of its time","book":"阅读还原集Vol.9","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test2","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.9 · Test2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"7171:55315:1","type":"choice","text":"The Ruamahanga River often floods.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是Ruamahanga River是否经常洪水。\n定位关键信息：“Ruamahanga River”和“often floods”\n对应原文：A段，“The family farm borders the river and a four-metre-high flood bank testifies to its natural tendency to flood.”\n解题思路：文章中提到了四米高的防洪堤，证明了该地频发洪水的倾向，说明洪水是常有的现象。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55315","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 4\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"7171:55316:2","type":"choice","text":"When Tobin first found the object in the river, he mistook it for something else.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是Tobin最初是否将找到的物体误认为是别的东西。\n定位关键信息：“first found”，“Tobin”和“mistook”\n对应原文： B段，“Tobin stepped out onto a broad shoulder of river sand, where he noticed what he initially took to be a whitish rock, lit by the sun. Then, getting closer, he realised it was a bone. ”\n解题思路： 文章中提到Tobin最初以为他看到的是一块白色的石头，但实际上是一个头骨，这表明他确实误认了。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55316","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 4\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"7171:55317:3","type":"choice","text":"Tobin could not decide what part of the body the bone came from.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是Tobin是否能确定骨头来自身体的哪个部位。\n定位关键信息：“part of the body”和“bone”\n对应原文：B段，“But as he scraped aside the stones, he realised it was a human bone, something quite new in his experience. As he picked it up, he saw it was a skull, discoloured with age.”\n解题思路：文章中Tobin最终意识到他找到的是一个人头骨，说明他能够确定骨头来自身体的哪个部位。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55317","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 4\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"7171:55318:4","type":"choice","text":"Tobin’s mother was surprised that the skull caused debate among specialists.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是Tobin的母亲是否对头骨引起专家之间的争论感到惊讶。\n定位关键信息：“mother”和“ specialists”和“debate”\n对应原文：C段，“Tobin replaced the skull and hurried home to tell his mother what the river had delivered to their doorstep. It would prove to be a spectacular find, setting in motion an investigation by some of the country’s most respected specialists, and ultimately challenging our most firmly held assertions about the human settlement of New Zealand.”\n解题思路：文章中没有提供关于Tobin的母亲对头骨引起的争论有何感受的信息。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55318","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 4\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"7171:55319:5","type":"fill","text":"填写第 5 空","answer":"police","acceptedAnswers":["police"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是洪水后Tobin发现头骨，哪些人最初试图解释头骨的出现。\n定位关键信息：“after the river flooded”和“initially involved”\n对应原文：D段，“The police were immediately called, but despite a thorough search could find nothing that might shed light on the identity of the Ruamahanga skull, or the circumstances of its sudden appearance.”\n解题思路：文章中提到警察是最初被叫来试图解释头骨出现的。\n同义替换：initially=immediately","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55319","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5 - 9\nComplete the flow-chart. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"7171:55319:6","type":"fill","text":"填写第 6 空","answer":"European","acceptedAnswers":["European"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是Dr Koelmeyer认为头骨是什么样的。\n定位关键信息：“Dr Koelmeyer”\n对应原文：D段，\"He then consulted with a colleague, Dr Koelmeyer, who believed that the deterioration of the bone placed the time of death before ‘living memory’ and, most significantly as it would turn out, the skull appeared to be European in origin.\"\n解题思路：文章中Dr Koelmeyer认为头骨似乎是欧洲人种的。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55319","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5 - 9\nComplete the flow-chart. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"7171:55319:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"radiocarbon dating","acceptedAnswers":["radiocarbon dating"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是Dr Watt推荐使用什么方法来确定头骨的年龄。\n定位关键信息：“Dr Watt”和“recommended”\n对应原文： E段，\"He believed that it could be the remains of an old farm burial, but was not certain, and proposed the use of radiocarbon dating to make sure it wasn’t a recent death.\"\n解题思路：文章中Dr Watt推荐使用放射性碳定年法来确定头骨的年龄。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55319","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5 - 9\nComplete the flow-chart. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"7171:55319:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"sample","acceptedAnswers":["sample"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是送到GNS的是什么。\n定位关键信息：“bone”和“GNS”\n对应原文：E段，\"As a result, the Institute of Geological and Nuclear Sciences (GNS) in Lower Hutt was contacted, and provided with a sample of bone that had originated in the top of the skull.\"\n解题思路：文章中提到送到GNS的是一块头骨顶部的骨头样本。\n同义替换：sent=provided","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55319","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5 - 9\nComplete the flow-chart. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"7171:55319:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"296","acceptedAnswers":["296"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是头骨的年龄是多少年。\n定位关键信息：“age of the skull”\n对应原文：E段，\"Cutting through the bewildering complexity of the scientific analysis was a single line reading: conventional radiocarbon age approximately 296 years.\"\n解题思路：文章中提到头骨的放射性碳定年法年龄大约是296年。\n同义替换：about=approximately","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55319","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5 - 9\nComplete the flow-chart. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":2},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"7171:55320:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"race","acceptedAnswers":["race"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是Ruamahanga头骨令人惊讶的原因，除了年龄和性别外还有什么。\n定位关键信息：“Ruahahanga skull”、“surprising”、“age”和“gender”\n对应原文： F段，\"The fascinating question, however, was how a skull of this race, let alone this gender, had reached these remote islands in the South Pacific at such a time, long before the arrival of the explorer Captain Cook in 1769, and perhaps even before the very first European landfall – the fleeting visit of the Dutch explorer Tasman in 1642 – neither of whom had women among their crews.\"\n解题思路：文章中提到Ruamahanga头骨令人惊讶的原因是它的种族。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55320","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10 - 13\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"7171:55321:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"archaeologists","acceptedAnswers":["archaeologists"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是发现Mendana探险队证据的是谁。\n定位关键信息：“expedition”和“evidence”\n对应原文：G段，\"However, it is unlikely the Ruamahanga skull originated from this expedition because no evidence of Mendana’s ships has ever been found in New Zealand, while a team of archaeologists working in the Solomon Islands in 1970 did discover the remains of European vessels dating from the 16th century.\"\n解题思路：文章中提到是考古学家在所罗门群岛发现了16世纪欧洲船只的遗骸。\n同义替换：found=discover","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55321","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10 - 13\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"7171:55322:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"Australia","acceptedAnswers":["Australia"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是Hagerty和Edgar从哪里逃到新西兰的。\n定位关键信息：“Hagerty”和“Edgar”和“in 1806”\n对应原文：H段，\"Two centuries were to pass before the first recorded European females arrived in New Zealand. Both having escaped from prison in Australia, Kathleen Hagerty and Charlotte Edgar are known to have reached the country in 1806. \"\n解题思路：文章中提到Hagerty和Edgar是从澳大利亚逃到新西兰的。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55322","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10 - 13\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"7171:55323:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"shipwreck","acceptedAnswers":["shipwreck"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是Ruamahange头骨可能如何到达新西兰的。\n定位关键信息：“Ruamahange skull”和“New Zealand”和“in 17th century”\n对应原文：H段，\"It is impossible to say with certainly, but the most likely explanation is that a Spanish or Portuguese trading ship was washed onto these wild shores as a result of a shipwreck and a woman got ashore.\"\n解题思路：文章中提到最有可能的解释是一艘西班牙或葡萄牙的商船因海难被冲到这些荒凉的海岸上。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55323","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10 - 13\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"55315","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 4\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The Ruamahanga River often floods.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"55316","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 4\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>When Tobin first found the object in the river, he mistook it for something else.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"55317","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 4\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Tobin could not decide what part of the body the bone came from.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"55318","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 4\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Tobin’s mother was surprised that the skull caused debate among specialists.</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"55319","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 5 - 9\nComplete the flow-chart. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","html":"<table cellspacing=\"0\"><tbody><tr style=\"height: 45px\" class=\"firstRow\"><td width=\"391.3333333333333\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding: 0px 7px; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; border-bottom-width: 1px; border-bottom-color: windowtext;\" align=\"center\"><p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>The events after the river flooded</strong></span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height: 45px\"><td width=\"391.3333333333333\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding: 0px 7px; border-left-width: 1px; border-left-color: windowtext; border-right-width: 1px; border-right-color: windowtext; border-top: none; border-bottom-width: 1px; border-bottom-color: windowtext;\" align=\"center\"><p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Tobin found a human skull.</span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height: 45px\"><td width=\"391.3333333333333\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding: 0px 7px; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; border-bottom-width: 1px; border-bottom-color: windowtext;\" align=\"center\"><p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">↓</span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height: 45px\"><td width=\"391.3333333333333\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding: 0px 7px; border-left-width: 1px; border-left-color: windowtext; border-right-width: 1px; border-right-color: windowtext; border-top: none; border-bottom-width: 1px; border-bottom-color: windowtext;\" align=\"center\"><p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The <strong class=\"source-blank\">[5] ____</strong>&nbsp;were initially involved in trying to explain the presence of the skull</span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height: 45px\"><td width=\"391.3333333333333\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding: 0px 7px; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; border-bottom-width: 1px; border-bottom-color: windowtext;\" align=\"center\"><p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">↓</span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height: 45px\"><td width=\"391.3333333333333\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding: 0px 7px; border-left-width: 1px; border-left-color: windowtext; border-right-width: 1px; border-right-color: windowtext; border-top: none; border-bottom-width: 1px; border-bottom-color: windowtext;\" align=\"center\"><p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Dr Ferris believed the skull belonged to a female.</span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height: 45px\"><td width=\"391.3333333333333\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding: 0px 7px; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; border-bottom-width: 1px; border-bottom-color: windowtext;\" align=\"center\"><p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">↓</span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height: 45px\"><td width=\"391.3333333333333\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding: 0px 7px; border-left-width: 1px; border-left-color: windowtext; border-right-width: 1px; border-right-color: windowtext; border-top: none; border-bottom-width: 1px; border-bottom-color: windowtext;\" align=\"center\"><p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Dr Koelmeyer suggested it was a <strong class=\"source-blank\">[6] ____</strong> skull.</span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height: 45px\"><td width=\"391.3333333333333\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding: 0px 7px; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; border-bottom-width: 1px; border-bottom-color: windowtext;\" align=\"center\"><p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">↓</span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height: 45px\"><td width=\"391.3333333333333\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding: 0px 7px; border-left-width: 1px; border-left-color: windowtext; border-right-width: 1px; border-right-color: windowtext; border-top: none; border-bottom-width: 1px; border-bottom-color: windowtext;\" align=\"center\"><p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Dr Watt recommended <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong> to establish the skull’s age.</span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height: 45px\"><td width=\"391.3333333333333\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding: 0px 7px; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; border-bottom-width: 1px; border-bottom-color: windowtext;\" align=\"center\"><p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">↓</span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height: 45px\"><td width=\"391.3333333333333\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding: 0px 7px; border-left-width: 1px; border-left-color: windowtext; border-right-width: 1px; border-right-color: windowtext; border-top: none; border-bottom-width: 1px; border-bottom-color: windowtext;\" align=\"center\"><p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">A bone <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong> was sent to the GNS.</span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height: 45px\"><td width=\"391.3333333333333\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding: 0px 7px; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; border-bottom-width: 1px; border-bottom-color: windowtext;\" align=\"center\"><p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">↓</span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height: 45px\"><td width=\"391.3333333333333\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding: 0px 7px; border-left-width: 1px; border-left-color: windowtext; border-right-width: 1px; border-right-color: windowtext; border-top: none; border-bottom-width: 1px; border-bottom-color: windowtext;\" align=\"center\"><p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The age of the skull was about <strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong> years.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"55320","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10 - 13\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>The problem of the skull’s origins</strong></p><p>Old bones common in NZ – Maori living there for 800 years</p><p>Ruahahanga skull surprising because of its:</p><p>– age</p><p>– <strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong></p><p>– gender</p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"55321","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10 - 13\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>Mendana expedition</strong></p><p>Possible source of skull</p><p>But probably did not visit NZ</p><p>Evidence of this expedition found elsewhere by <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong></p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"55322","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10 - 13\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>New Zealand</strong></p><p>First European explorer arrived in 1642</p><p>Hagerty and Edgar arrived in 1806 from <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong>&nbsp;where they had been imprisoned</p><p><br/></p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"55323","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 10 - 13\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>Possible solution</strong></p><p>Ruamahange skull may have reached NZ in 17th century after a <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>Ahead of its time</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><em>A chance discovery in New Zealand has challenged the country’s recorded history</em></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">One October afternoon, a young New Zealander, Sam Tobin, called his dogs and went for a walk down to the nearby Ruamahanga River. Having been very high for days, the river had at last fallen, and Tobin was eager to see what changes the floods had brought. The family farm borders the river and a four-metre-high flood bank testifies to its natural tendency to flood.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Tobin stepped out onto a broad shoulder of river sand, where he noticed what he initially took to be a whitish rock, lit by the sun. Then, getting closer, he realised it was a bone. Such a thing was not uncommon in these parts – he had often come across bone fragments, or even whole skeletons, of cows and sheep. But as he scraped aside the stones, he realised it was a human bone, something quite new in his experience. As he picked it up, he saw it was a skull, discoloured with age.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Tobin replaced the skull and hurried home to tell his mother what the river had delivered to their doorstep. It would prove to be a spectacular find, setting in motion an investigation by some of the country’s most respected specialists, and ultimately challenging our most firmly held assertions about the human settlement of New Zealand.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The police were immediately called, but despite a thorough search could find nothing that might shed light on the identity of the Ruamahanga skull, or the circumstances of its sudden appearance. The skull was then taken north to be examined by forensic pathologist Dr Ferris, at Auckland Hospital. Despite being hampered by its damaged and incomplete condition – the jawbone and lower left portion of the cranium were missing – Dr Ferris determined that the skull was that of a female. <a name=\"_Hlk178154402\"></a>He then consulted with a colleague, Dr Koelmeyer, who believed that the deterioration of the bone placed the time of death before ‘living memory’ and, most significantly as it would turn out, the skull appeared to be European in origin.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Wellington-based forensic anthropologist Dr Watt also examined the skull, and suggested it belonged to a 40-45 year-old. He believed that it could be the remains of an old farm burial, but was not certain, and proposed the use of radiocarbon dating to make sure it wasn’t a recent death. As a result, the Institute of Geological and Nuclear Sciences (GNS) in Lower Hutt was contacted, and provided with a sample of bone that had originated in the top of the skull. In a little over three weeks, the seemingly astonishing results from the GNS laboratory came back. Cutting through the bewildering complexity of the scientific analysis was a single line reading: conventional radiocarbon age approximately 296 years. This was staggering, for the skull was about 200 years older than Dr Koelmeyer had believed.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Of course, a skull of this age wasn’t particularly unusual in New Zealand. The Maori people have been living in the country for at least 800 years and scientists frequently come across human remains of considerable age. The fascinating question, however, was how a skull of this race, let alone this gender, had reached these remote islands in the South Pacific at such a time, long before the arrival of the explorer Captain Cook in 1769, and perhaps even before the very first European landfall – the fleeting visit of the Dutch explorer Tasman in 1642 – neither of whom had women among their crews.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The first known European women in the Pacific came with a doomed colonising venture which sailed from Peru in 1595 under the command of Spanish captain Mendana. However, it is unlikely the Ruamahanga skull originated from this expedition because no evidence of Mendana’s ships has ever been found in New Zealand, while a team of archaeologists working in the Solomon Islands in 1970 did discover the remains of European vessels dating from the 16th century.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Two centuries were to pass before the first recorded European females arrived in New Zealand. Both having escaped from prison in Australia, Kathleen Hagerty and Charlotte Edgar are known to have reached the country in 1806. How do we account for the Ruamahanga skull, which appears to be about 100 years older than that? It is impossible to say with certainly, but the most likely explanation is that a Spanish or Portuguese trading ship was washed onto these wild shores as a result of a shipwreck and a woman got ashore. Implausible, perhaps, but the Ruamahanga skull, today resting in the Wellington Museum, could be the kind of concrete evidence that demands such a re-evaluation of history.</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7171&scene=%E5%8E%86%E5%8F%B2%E5%8F%91%E5%B1%95&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7177","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 The importance of law","book":"阅读还原集Vol.9","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test2","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.9 · Test2 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"7177:55345:14","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph A","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"定位关键信息：lives\n对应原文：A段提到“The law influences all of us virtually all the time, it governs almost all aspects of our behavior, and even what happens to us when we are no longer alive.”\n解题思路：A段主要讨论了法律在我们日常生活中的广泛应用，因此主旨是“法律贯穿我们的一生”。\n同义替换：applies =governs；throughout our lives =all aspects of our behavior","options":["different areas of professional expertise","reasons why it is unfair to criticise lawyers","the disadvantages of the legal system","the law applies throughout our lives","the law has affected historical events","a negative regard for lawyers","public's increasing ability to influence the law","growth in laws"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"55345","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nThe text has six paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"7177:55345:15","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph B","answer":"G","acceptedAnswers":["G"],"explanation":"对应原文：B段提到“Today, by contrast, a vast number of people can read, and it is becoming easier for people to take an interest in law, and for the general population to help actually shape the law in many countries.”\n解题思路：B段说明了随着越来越多的人能够识字阅读，人们更容易对法律方面的事务产生兴趣，并且在许多国家，公众对法律的参与度增强。","options":["different areas of professional expertise","reasons why it is unfair to criticise lawyers","the disadvantages of the legal system","the law applies throughout our lives","the law has affected historical events","a negative regard for lawyers","public's increasing ability to influence the law","growth in laws"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"55345","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nThe text has six paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"7177:55345:16","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph C","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"对应原文：C段提到“In our rapidly developing world, all sorts of skills and knowledge are valuable. Those people, for example, with knowledge of computers, the internet, and communications technology are relied upon by the rest of us.”\n解题思路：C段讨论了不同领域的专业知识，以及现代社会中各种专业技能的重要性。\n同义替换：different areas=all sorts of skills； professional expertise =  skills and knowledge","options":["different areas of professional expertise","reasons why it is unfair to criticise lawyers","the disadvantages of the legal system","the law applies throughout our lives","the law has affected historical events","a negative regard for lawyers","public's increasing ability to influence the law","growth in laws"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"55345","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nThe text has six paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"7177:55345:17","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph D","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"对应原文：D段提到“The number of laws has never been greater. In the UK alone, about 35 new Acts of Parliament are produced every year, thereby delivering thousands of new rules.\"\n解题思路：D段讨论了法律数量的增长，每年有成千上万的法律通过。D段的主旨是关于法律数量的快速增长。","options":["different areas of professional expertise","reasons why it is unfair to criticise lawyers","the disadvantages of the legal system","the law applies throughout our lives","the law has affected historical events","a negative regard for lawyers","public's increasing ability to influence the law","growth in laws"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"55345","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nThe text has six paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"7177:55345:18","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph E","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"对应原文：E段提到“However, despite their important role in developing the rules, lawyers are not universally admired. Anti-lawyer jokes have a long history going back to the ancient Greeks.”\n解题思路：E段表明，尽管律师在立法方面起着重要作用，但是这个职业并未收到普遍的尊重。并讨论了公众对律师的负面看法，人们常常开玩笑或者批评律师，认为他们关心个人利益胜于真理。因此，E段的重点是关于律师的负面形象和不良声誉。\n同义替换：a negative regard = anti-lawyer jokes","options":["different areas of professional expertise","reasons why it is unfair to criticise lawyers","the disadvantages of the legal system","the law applies throughout our lives","the law has affected historical events","a negative regard for lawyers","public's increasing ability to influence the law","growth in laws"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"55345","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nThe text has six paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"7177:55345:19","type":"choice","text":"Paragraph F","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"对应原文：F段提到“But, in general, it is no more just to say that lawyers are bad because they make a living from people's problems than it is to make the same accusation in respect of nurses or IT consultants. A great many lawyers are involved in public law work, such as that involving civil liberties, housing and other issues.”\n解题思路：F段讨论了为什么对律师的批评是不公平的，律师有时被批评过于关注个人利益，但实际上很多律师专注于公共事务。F段解释了对律师的批评不公平。","options":["different areas of professional expertise","reasons why it is unfair to criticise lawyers","the disadvantages of the legal system","the law applies throughout our lives","the law has affected historical events","a negative regard for lawyers","public's increasing ability to influence the law","growth in laws"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H"],"sourceGroupId":"55345","allowNumber":false,"section":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nThe text has six paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"7177:55346:20-21","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following statements does the writer make about legal skills in today's world?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：需要找出作者在文中关于法律技能的两点陈述。\n定位关键信息：C和D的关键词是“legal knowledge”和“function effectively”。\n对应原文：C答案对应C段的“But legal understanding is just as vital and as universally needed.”D答案对应C段的“Without their knowledge, many parts of commercial and social life today would seize up in minutes.”\n解题思路：作者在C段中比较了法律知识和IT技能的重要性，并且强调了没有法律专家，社会无法有效运转。\n同义替换：important=vital；could not function effectively  = seize up in minutes","options":["There should be a person with legal training in every hospital.","Lawyers with experience in commercial law are the most in demand.","Knowledge of the law is as important as having computer skills.","Society could not function effectively without legal experts.","Schools should teach students about the law."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"55346","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 20 - 21\nChoose TWO correct answers.","groupId":"55346-7177:55346:20-21"},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"7177:55346:20-21","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following statements does the writer make about legal skills in today's world?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：需要找出作者在文中关于法律技能的两点陈述。\n定位关键信息：C和D的关键词是“legal knowledge”和“function effectively”。\n对应原文：C答案对应C段的“But legal understanding is just as vital and as universally needed.”D答案对应C段的“Without their knowledge, many parts of commercial and social life today would seize up in minutes.”\n解题思路：作者在C段中比较了法律知识和IT技能的重要性，并且强调了没有法律专家，社会无法有效运转。\n同义替换：important=vital；could not function effectively  = seize up in minutes","options":["There should be a person with legal training in every hospital.","Lawyers with experience in commercial law are the most in demand.","Knowledge of the law is as important as having computer skills.","Society could not function effectively without legal experts.","Schools should teach students about the law."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"55346","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 20 - 21\nChoose TWO correct answers.","groupId":"55346-7177:55346:20-21"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"7177:55347:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"truth","acceptedAnswers":["truth"],"explanation":"审题：题目要求填空，说明人们有时认为律师不关心“什么”。\n定位关键信息：little interest to lawyers\n对应原文：F段提到“People sometimes make comments that characterise lawyers as professionals whose concerns put personal reward above truth, or who gain financially from misfortune. ”\n解题思路：\n根据原文，人们有时会评论说，律师是把个人利益置于真理之上的专业人士。说明对于一部分律师来说，事实、真理对于他们来说并不重要。答案为truth。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55347","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"7177:55347:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"journalists","acceptedAnswers":["journalists"],"explanation":"审题：填空处应该填入与科学专家类似的职业。\n定位关键信息：scientific experts、financial greed\n对应原文：F段提到“There are undoubtedly lawyers that would fit that bill, Just as there are some scientists, Journalists and others In that category.”\n解题思路：\n根据原文,有一些律师就是认为个人利益高于真理，有一些科学家、记者和其他人也属于这一类别。原文并列提到journalists和scientists。因此答案为journalists。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55347","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"7177:55347:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"nurses","acceptedAnswers":["nurses"],"explanation":"审题：填空处应为与IT员工类似的职业。\n定位关键信息：IT staff\n对应原文：F段提到“  But, in general, it is no more just to say that lawyers are bad because they make a living from people's problems than it is to make the same accusation in respect of nurses or IT consultants. A great many lawyers are involved in public law work, such as that involving civil liberties, housing and other issues. ”\n解题思路：\n根据原文，不能因为律师以解决人们的问题为生就说他们不好，就像不能指责护士或it顾问一样。原文并列提到nurses和IT员工。因此答案为nurses。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55347","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"7177:55347:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"dedication","acceptedAnswers":["dedication"],"explanation":"审题：填空处应为描述律师工作态度的名词。\n对应原文：F段提到“Such work is not lavishly remunerated and the quality of the service provided by these lawyers relies on considerable professional dedication.”\n解题思路：根据题干，填空处应为描述律师工作态度的名词。根据原文，律师的工作报酬不高，这些律师提供的服务质量依赖于相当的专业奉献精神。奉献（dedication）就是用于描述律师工作态度的词语。答案为dedication。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55347","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"7177:55347:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"documents","acceptedAnswers":["documents"],"explanation":"审题：填空处应为律师花时间撰写的东西。\n定位关键信息：people’s misfortunes\n对应原文：F段提到“Moreover, much legal work has nothing to do with conflict or misfortune, but is primarily concerned with drafting documents. Another source of social disaffection for lawyers, and disaffection for the law, is a limited public understanding of how law works and how it could be changed. ”\n解题思路：根据题干，填空处应为律师花时间撰写的东西。根据原文，许多法律工作与冲突或不幸无关，而主要与起草文件有关。起草文件（document）是律师的工作之一。答案为documents。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55347","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"55346-7177:55346:20-21","numbers":[20,21],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["C","D"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"55345","title":"标题匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nThe text has six paragraphs. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph and move it into the gap.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"55346","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 20 - 21\nChoose TWO correct answers.","html":"<p>Which <strong>TWO</strong>&nbsp;of the following statements does the writer make about legal skills in today&#39;s world?</p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"55347","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 22 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Lawyers as professionals</strong></p><p>People sometimes say that <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong>&nbsp;is of little interest to&nbsp;lawyers, who are more concerned with making money. This may well be the case with some individuals, in the same way that some <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong> or scientific experts may also be&nbsp;driven purely by financial greed. However, criticising lawyers because their work is concerned with people&#39;s problems would be similar to attacking IT staff or&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong> for the same reason. In fact, many lawyers focus on questions relating, for example, to housing or civil liberties, which requires them to have&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong> to their work. What&#39;s more, a lot of lawyers&#39; time is spent writing <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong> rather than dealing with people&#39;s misfortunes.</p>","firstNumber":22}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>The importance of law</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>#&amp;</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The law influences all of us virtually all the time. It governs almost all aspects of our behavior, and even what happens to us when we are no longer alive. It affects us from the embryo onwards. It governs the air we breathe, the food and drink we consume, our travel, family relationships, and our property. It applies at the bottom of the ocean and in space. Each time we examine a label on a food product, engage in work as an employee or employer, travel on the roads, go to school to learn or to teach, stay in a hotel, borrow a library book, create or dissolve a commercial company, play sports, or engage the services of someone for anything from plumbing a sink to planning a city, we are in the world of law.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>#&amp;</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Law has also become much more widely recognised as the standard by which behavior needs to be judged. A very telling development in recent history is the way in which the idea of law has permeated all parts of social life. The universal standard of whether something is socially tolerated is progressively becoming whether it is legal, rather than something that has always been considered acceptable. In earlier times, most people were illiterate. Today, by contrast, a vast number of people can read, and it is becoming easier for people to take an interest in law, and for the general population to help actually shape the law in many countries. However, law is a versatile instrument that can be used equally well for the improvement or the degradation of humanity.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>#&amp;</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">This, of course, puts law in a very significant position. In our rapidly developing world, all sorts of skills and knowledge are valuable. Those people, for example, with knowledge of computers, the internet, and communications technology are relied upon by the rest of us. There is now someone with IT skills or an IT help desk in every UK school, every company, every hospital, every local and central government office. Without their knowledge, many parts of commercial and social life today would seize up in minutes. But legal understanding is just as vital and as universally needed. The American comedian Jerry Seinfeld put it like this, &#39;We are all throwing the dice, playing the game, moving our pieces around the board, but if there is a problem, the lawyer is the only person who has read the inside of the top of the box.&#39; In other words, the lawyer is the only person who has read and made sense of the rules.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>#&amp;</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The number of laws has never been greater. In the UK alone, about 35 new Acts of Parliament are produced every year, thereby delivering thousands of new rules. The legislative output of the British Parliament has more than doubled in recent times from 1,100 pages a year in the early 1970s,to over 2,500 pages a year today. Between 1997 and 2006,the legislature passed 365 Acts of Parliament and more than 32,000 legally binding statutory instruments. In a system with so much law, lawyers do a great deal not just to vindicate the rights of citizens and organizations but also to help develop the law through legal arguments, some of which are adapted by judges to become laws. Law courts can and do produce new law and revise old law, but they do so having heard the arguments of lawyers.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>#&amp;</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">However, despite their important role in developing the rules, lawyers are not universally admired. Anti-lawyer jokes have a long history going back to the ancient Greeks. More recently the son of a famous Hollywood actor was asked at his junior school what his father did for a living, to which he replied, &#39;My daddy is a movie actor, and sometimes he plays the good guy, and sometimes he plays the lawyer. For balance, though, it Is worth remembering that there are and have been many heroic and revered lawyers such as the Roman philosopher and politician Cicero and Mahatma Gandi, the Indian campaigner for independence.&amp;#</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>#&amp;</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">People sometimes make comments that characterise lawyers as professionals whose concerns put personal reward above truth, or who gain financially from misfortune. There are undoubtedly lawyers that would fit that bill, just as there are some scientists, journalists and others in that category. But, in general, it is no more just to say that lawyers are bad because they make a living from people&#39;s problems than it is to make the same accusation in respect of nurses or IT consultants. A great many lawyers are involved in public law work, such as that involving civil liberties, housing and other issues. Such work is not lavishly remunerated and the quality of the service provided by these lawyers relies on considerable professional dedication. Moreover, much legal work has nothing to do with conflict or misfortune, but is primarily concerned with drafting documents. Another source of social disaffection for lawyers, and disaffection for the law, is a limited public understanding of how law works and how it could be changed. Greater clarity about these issues, maybe as a result of better public relations, would reduce many aspects of public dissatisfaction with the law.&amp;#</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7177&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7178","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 Understanding symbols","book":"阅读还原集Vol.9","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test2","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.9 · Test2 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"7178:55324:27","type":"choice","text":"In the first paragraph, what did the children in the experiment have to do?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是在第一个段落的实验中孩子们需要做什么。\n定位关键信息：“the first paragraph”和“children”\n对应原文：A段，“we then encouraged the child to find 'Big Snoopy', a large version of the toy 'hiding in the same place in his big room.'”\n解题思路：根据原文内容，孩子们需要在真实房间（life-sized room）中找到一个藏起来的玩具。因此正确答案是D。\n同义替换：原文中的“find”对应选项中的“locate”。","options":["spot the differences between a real room and a smaller version","make a copy of a life-sized room using small furniture","hide a large toy in a tiny room","locate a toy in a life-sized room"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55324","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 32\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"7178:55325:28","type":"choice","text":"What was the result of the first experiment?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是第一个实验的结果。\n定位关键信息：“first experiment”、“two-and-a-half-year-olds”、“three-year-olds”和“result”\n对应原文：B段，“The three-year-olds were very successful. After they observed the small toy being placed behind the miniature couch, they ran into the room and found the large toy behind the real couch. But the two-and-a-half-year-olds failed abysmally.”这句话表明三岁的小孩能够成功地理解两个房间之间的关系，并找到大狗玩具。\n解题思路：三岁孩子能够成功找到玩具，而两岁半的孩子则无法关联两个房间，说明三岁孩子能理解模型与现实房间的关系，并成功找到大玩具。因此答案是B。","options":["Both two-and-a-half-and three-year-olds completed the task successfully.","Three-year-olds could mentally relate the two rooms they had been shown.","Two-and-a-half-year-olds could relate more closely to the toys as symbols.","Two-and-a-half-year-olds had poorer memory than three-year-olds."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55325","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 32\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"7178:55326:29","type":"choice","text":"In the fourth paragraph, what does the writer say about children and pictures?","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是作者在第四段中对孩子和图片的看法。\n定位关键信息：“the fourth paragraph”和“children and pictures”\n对应原文：D段，“The problem stems from the duality inherent in all symbolic objects: they are real in themselves and also representations of something else.”\n解题思路：原文中提到孩子无法理解图片的双重性质，即图片既是一个真实的物体，又是另一个事物的象征或代表。因此答案是A。","options":["Infants are unable to understand that pictures serve a double purpose.","Young children may understand pictures more readily than adults.","Infants can understand that a picture of food cannot be eaten.","Adults should encourage children to look at pictures from an early age."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55326","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 32\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"7178:55327:30","type":"choice","text":"In the third experiment, what did the writer notice about the reactions of the toddlers?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是作者在第三个实验中注意到了什么。\n定位关键信息：“the third experiment”和“reactions”\n对应原文：G段提到“Interestingly, most of the children showed little or no reaction to their failed attempts.”\n解题思路：根据原文，在G段中，作者描述了实验中幼儿尝试使用缩小版的物品（如滑梯和汽车）执行与之前使用正常大小的物品相同的动作，但失败了。原文明确指出，这里明确说明大多数幼儿对他们失败的尝试没有表现出反应，或者说反应很少。因此他们的行为一致，无论是成功还是失败，他们的反应几乎没有变化。因此答案是D。","options":["They often behaved in an unpredictable way.","They were only comfortable performing very familiar tasks.","They became frustrated when they could not achieve a task.","They behaved the same whether they were successful or not."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55327","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 32\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"7178:55328:31","type":"choice","text":"What did the experiment involving a mathematical problem suggest about children's learning?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是关于数学问题的实验对孩子学习的启示。\n定位关键信息：“mathematical problem”和“children's learning”\n对应原文：G段提到“We taught an identical comparison group the same concept, but using pencil and paper. Both groups learned to solve the problems equally well, but the group using blocks took three times as long to do so.”\n解题思路：G段提到，实验中有两组孩子，一组使用积木，另一组使用纸和铅笔。结果表明，两组在解决问题上学得同样好，但使用积木的那组花了三倍的时间。原文显示，使用积木并没有帮助孩子更快地理解概念，反而延长了学习时间。因此答案是C。","options":["Children are able to understand complex concepts at an early age.","Children younger than seven cannot learn using pencil and paper alone.","Using blocks can make it harder for children to learn new concepts.","Teachers should try using blocks to teach mathematics to lower level students."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55328","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 32\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"7178:55528:32","type":"choice","text":"What does Deloache conclude about the results of her and Chong's experiment?","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目问Deloache对于他和Chong的实验结果的结论。\n定位信息：Deloache, Chong's experiment\n对应原文：I段，Accordingly, we used different types of books to teach letters to 30-month-old children. One was a simple old-fashioned alphabet book with each letter accompanied by an appropriate picture. The other was a 3-D version. The children using the traditional book subsequently recognised more letters than those using the 3-D book.\n解题思路：原文提到使用传统字母书教学时，孩子认识的字母比使用3D书教学时更多。","options":["Children's books should be more interactive.","2-D books should contain realistic images.","Simpler books may be better learning tools.","3-D books help weaker students to progress."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55528","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 32\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"7178:55329:33","type":"choice","text":"33 The test involving 9-month-old babies attempted to find out ____","answer":"E","acceptedAnswers":["E"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是关于9个月大的婴儿的实验试图了解什么。\n定位关键信息：“9-month-old babies”\n对应原文：E段提到“We began testing infants' understanding of pictures by putting a book of highly realistic colour photographs of individual objects in front of nine-month-olds. To our surprise, every child in the study reached out to feel or scratch the pictures.”\n解题思路：这段文字解释了对9个月大的婴儿进行的测试，旨在发现婴儿是否困惑于图片以及图片与实际物体的区别。婴儿伸手去摸图片，因为他们还不理解图片的双重性质。","options":["that a three-year-old may still expect an image to perform a real task.","how quickly children can learn the alphabet.","the best age for children to begin school.","the effectiveness of symbolic objects as teaching tools.","whether young children are puzzled by pictures.","that young children expect tiny objects to function in the same way as life-sized ones."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"55329","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 33 - 35\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"7178:55329:34","type":"choice","text":"34 The third experiment revealed ____","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是第三个实验揭示了什么。\n定位关键信息：“third experiment”\n对应原文：G段提到“Most children attempted to perform the same actions with the miniature items that they had with the larger ones.”\n解题思路：第三次实验中，研究人员发现孩子们期望微型物体能像大型物体一样正常工作。他们试图坐在微型椅子上或爬进微型汽车里，虽然这些微型物品实际上无法承载他们的行为。","options":["that a three-year-old may still expect an image to perform a real task.","how quickly children can learn the alphabet.","the best age for children to begin school.","the effectiveness of symbolic objects as teaching tools.","whether young children are puzzled by pictures.","that young children expect tiny objects to function in the same way as life-sized ones."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"55329","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 33 - 35\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"7178:55329:35","type":"choice","text":"35 The maths experiment was designed to assess ____","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是数学实验的设计目的是什么。\n定位关键信息：“maths experiment”\n对应原文：G段，“Teachers everywhere use blocks or other objects to represent numerical quantity. However, if young children do not understand the relation between an object and what it represents, this could be counterproductive. To demonstrate this, we taught six-and seven-year-olds a difficult subtraction problem using blocks.”\n解题思路：在G段中，作者提到教师使用积木等物体来表示数字数量，实验旨在评估象征性物体（如积木）作为教学工具的有效性。虽然使用积木的学生能够解决问题，但所需时间是使用纸笔学生的三倍，说明象征性物体的教学效果可能并不如预期。","options":["that a three-year-old may still expect an image to perform a real task.","how quickly children can learn the alphabet.","the best age for children to begin school.","the effectiveness of symbolic objects as teaching tools.","whether young children are puzzled by pictures.","that young children expect tiny objects to function in the same way as life-sized ones."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"sourceGroupId":"55329","allowNumber":false,"section":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 33 - 35\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap."},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"7178:55330:36","type":"choice","text":"The results of the first experiment revealed unexpected information.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"审题：题目问第一个实验的结果是否揭示了意想不到的信息。\n定位关键信息：“first experiment”和“unexpected information”\n对应原文：A段提到“About 20 years ago I had one of those wonderful moments when research takes an unexpected but fruitful turn.\"C段提到“I realised my memory study was instead a study of symbolic understanding... the children's failure might be telling us something about how and when children acquire the ability to understand that one object stands for another.”\n解题思路：原文明确表示，研究人员原本计划研究记忆，但通过实验，意外地发现了关于儿童符号理解的知识。这是他们之前没有预料到的。因此答案是YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55330","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"7178:55331:37","type":"choice","text":"Infants react the same way to both drawings and photographs.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"审题：题目问婴儿是否对绘画和照片的反应相同。\n定位关键信息：关键词是“Infants”和“drawings and photographs”\n对应原文：E段提到“However, when depicted objects bear little resemblance to the real thing – as in a black and white drawing – infants rarely explore them.”\n解题思路：原文明确指出婴儿对照片和绘画的反应不同：他们更倾向于探索照片，而很少对黑白绘画表现出兴趣。因此，婴儿不会以相同方式对待绘画和照片，因此答案是NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55331","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"7178:55332:38","type":"choice","text":"Toddlers are used to failing in many of the tasks they try to perform.","answer":"YES","acceptedAnswers":["YES"],"explanation":"审题：题目问幼儿是否习惯于在许多任务中失败。\n定位关键信息：“toddlers”和“failing”\n对应原文：G段提到“We think this probably reflects the fact that toddlers' daily lives are full of unsuccessful attempts to do one thing or another.”\n解题思路：原文表明幼儿经常面对失败的任务，因此他们对这些失败已经习以为常。幼儿的生活中充满了失败的尝试，因此答案是YES。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55332","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"7178:55333:39","type":"choice","text":"The confusion of symbols and real objects has little significance for educational practice.","answer":"NO","acceptedAnswers":["NO"],"explanation":"审题：题目问符号和实物的混淆对教育实践是否没有什么意义。\n定位关键信息：“confusion”和“symbols and real objects”和“educational practice”\n对应原文：G段提到“This confusion has implications for educational practice.”以及“Teachers everywhere use blocks or other objects to represent numerical quantity. However, if young children do not understand the relation between an object and what it represents, this could be counterproductive.”\n解题思路：符号和实物的混淆对教育实践有重要影响，并进一步解释了为什么这种混淆对教育实践有意义：如果孩子不理解符号和实际对象的关系，教学效果可能会适得其反，说明这对教育实践有重要的影响。因此答案是NO。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55333","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"7178:55334:40","type":"choice","text":"Children enjoy reading 3D books more than 2D books.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：题目问孩子是否更喜欢阅读3D书籍。\n定位关键信息：关键词是“Children”、“3D books”和“2D books”\n对应原文：I段提到“... children using the traditional book subsequently recognised more letters than those using the 3D book.”\n解题思路：原文I段和J段讨论了3D书和2D书的学习效果差异，但没有提到儿童是否更喜欢阅读3D书。因此答案是NOT GIVEN。","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55334","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"55324","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 32\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>In the first paragraph, what did the children in the experiment have to do?</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"55325","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 32\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>What was the result of the first experiment?</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"55326","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 32\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>In the fourth paragraph, what does the writer say about children and pictures?</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"55327","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 32\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>In the third experiment, what did the writer notice about the reactions of the toddlers?</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"55328","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 32\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>What did the experiment involving a mathematical problem suggest about children&#39;s learning?</strong></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"55528","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 32\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>What does Deloache conclude about the results of her and Chong&#39;s experiment?</strong></p>","firstNumber":32},{"id":"55329","title":"摘要选词","instruction":"Questions 33 - 35\nComplete each sentence with the correct ending. Choose the correct ending and move it into the gap.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":33},{"id":"55330","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>The results of the first experiment revealed unexpected information.</strong></p>","firstNumber":36},{"id":"55331","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Infants react the same way to both drawings and photographs.</strong></p>","firstNumber":37},{"id":"55332","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Toddlers are used to failing in many of the tasks they try to perform.</strong></p>","firstNumber":38},{"id":"55333","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>The confusion of symbols and real objects has little significance for educational practice.</strong></p>","firstNumber":39},{"id":"55334","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nChoose YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer, choose NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer, or choose NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","html":"<p><strong>Children enjoy reading 3D books more than 2D books.</strong></p>","firstNumber":40}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>Understanding symbols</strong><o:p></o:p></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Judy DeLoache describes her research into the difficulties children experience with symbols<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">About 20 years ago I had one of those wonderful moments when research takes an unexpected but fruitful turn. I had been studying toddler memory and was beginning a new experiment with two-and-a-half- and three-year-olds. For the project, I had built a model of a room that was in my laboratory. The real space contained basic furniture such as a couch and table. The miniature version was as similar as possible to its larger counterpart: the furniture was the same shape and material and was arranged in the same position. For the study, a child watched as we hid a miniature toy – a plastic dog we called Little Snoopy* – in the model. We then encouraged the child to find &#39;Big Snoopy, a large version of the toy &#39;hiding in the same place in his big room.&#39;<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The three-year-olds were very successful. After they observed the small toy being placed behind the miniature couch, they ran into the room and found the large toy behind the real couch. But the two-and-a-half-year-olds failed abysmally. They cheerfully ran into the room to retrieve the large toy, but most had no idea where to look, even though they remembered where the tiny toy was hidden in the miniature room and could readily find it there.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Their failure to use what they knew about the model to draw an inference about the real room indicated that they did not appreciate the relation between the model and the room. I realised my memory study was instead a study of symbolic understanding and that the children&#39;s failure might be telling us something about how and when children acquire the ability to understand that one object stands for another.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The first type of symbolic object that infants and young children master is the picture. No symbols seem simpler to adults, but infants initially find pictures perplexing. The problem stems from the duality inherent in all symbolic objects：</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">they are real in themselves and also representations of something else. A few years ago I became intrigued by anecdotes suggesting that infants do not appreciate this duality-stories of a baby trying to pick up a depicted toy or fit a foot into a photograph of a shoe. We assumed such behaviour would be rare and therefore difficult to study.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Fortunately we were wrong. We began testing infants&#39; understanding of pictures by putting a book of highly realistic colour photographs of individual objects in front of nine-month-olds. To our surprise, every child in the study reached out to feel or scratch the pictures. The confusion seems to be conceptual not perceptual. Infants can perfectly well perceive the difference between objects and pictures and given the choice they will choose the real thing. But they do not yet fully understand what pictures are and how they differ from real objects. However, when depicted objects bear little resemblance to the real thing – as in a black and white drawing – infants rarely explore them. By 18 months, babies have come to appreciate that a picture merely represents an object; instead of manipulating the paper, they point to pictures and name objects. Nevertheless, it takes several years for the nature of pictures to be completely understood.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Studies have shown that, until the age of four, many children think that turning a picture of a bowl of popcorn upside down will result in the depicted popcorn falling out of the bowl.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Pictures are not the only source of confusion for very young children. In a 11 third experiment, we brought a group of toddlers (18-to 30-month-old children) Into a room containing a child&#39;s slide, a chair, and a toddler-sized car. The children played with these for a while. Then we secretly replaced each object with an identical miniature version. Most children attempted to perform the same actions with the miniature items that they had with the larger ones. Some tried to sit on the chair, others attempted to climb into the car. Interestingly, most of the children showed little or no reaction to their failed attempts. We think this probably reflects the fact that toddlers&#39; daily lives are full of unsuccessful attempts to do one thing or another. This confusion has implications for educational practice. Teachers everywhere use blocks or other objects to represent numerical quantity. However, if young children do not understand the relation between an object and what it represents, this could be counterproductive. To demonstrate this, we taught six-and seven-year-olds a difficult subtraction problem using blocks.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">We taught an identical comparison group the same concept, but using pencil and paper. Both groups learned to solve the problems equally well, but the group using blocks took three times as long to do so.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>I</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Dual representation also comes into play in many children&#39;s books. Modern children&#39;s books are often 3D, with features that encourage children to interact directly with the book itself, for example flaps that can be lifted to reveal pictures. Graduate student Cynthia Chong and I reasoned that these features might distract children from the information. Accordingly, we used different types of book to teach letters to 30-month-old children. One was a simple old-fashioned alphabet book with each letter accompanied by an appropriate picture. The other was a 3-D version, The children using the traditional book subsequently recognised more letters than those using the 3-D book.<o:p></o:p></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>J</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Presumably, the children could concentrate more easily with the plain 2-D book, whereas with the other one they were distracted by the 3-D activities. Less may be more when it comes to educational books for young children.<o:p></o:p></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7178&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7167","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 Chocolate for the masses","book":"阅读还原集Vol.9","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.9 · Test 1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"7167:55263:1","type":"choice","text":"Chocolate was consumed by greater numbers of people in the nineteenth century than in previous times.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是“19世纪比以前有更多人消费巧克力”是否正确。\n定位关键信息：“19th century”和“greater numbers of people”\n对应原文：A段，“In the early 19th century, however, chocolate became far more widely available, and consumption shot up dramatically across the populations of Europe in particular.”\n解题思路：原文明确提到“19世纪初期，巧克力变得更加广泛可得，消费量在欧洲人口中急剧上升”。这说明19世纪的巧克力消费量比之前多。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55263","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"7167:55264:2","type":"choice","text":"Fry's chocolate became more affordable because of the fall in price of one ingredient.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是“Fry的巧克力因为某种成分的降价而变得更加便宜”是否正确。\n定位关键信息：“Fry’s chocolate”和“affordable”\n对应原文：C段，“Thanks to immediate high demand for this product, the price of cacao butter escalated, so the new solid chocolate was only accessible for the elite. But this would eventually change, because of the introduction of cost-cutting methods and mass production.”\n解题思路：\n原文提到巧克力的巨大需求导致其成分cacao butter的价格上涨（escalated），这导致只有精英阶层买得起巧克力。随后巧克力变得更大众化，并不是因为哪种原料价格下跌，而是因为采用了降低成本的方法和规模化生产。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55264","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"7167:55265:3","type":"choice","text":"Entrepreneurial British chocolate manufacturers paid their employees well.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是“英国的巧克力制造商给员工支付了很高的工资”是否正确。\n定位关键信息：“British chocolate manufacturers”和“paid their employees well”\n对应原文：D段，“In the Birmingham suburb of Bournville, where they had established their chocolate factory, the Cadburys created a model town with adequate housing for their workers, and even dining and reading rooms so that their employees had no need to spend anything on entertaining themselves.”\n解题思路：原文提到的是Cadbury公司为员工提供了住房和休闲设施，但没有提到工资支付情况。因此无法判断他们是否支付了高工资。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55265","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"7167:55266:4","type":"choice","text":"Customers were made ill through the practices of unscrupulous chocolate producers.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是“不良巧克力生产商的行为导致消费者生病”是否正确。\n定位关键信息：“made ill”和“unscrupulous chocolate producers”\n对应原文：E段提到，“However, the rising demand for chocolate also made it a target for unscrupulous producers and merchants. Sometimes the expensive cacao butter was completely extracted and replaced with olive or almond oil, or egg yolks. Alternatively, cheaper materials such as potato starch or flour were added. In 1850, a health commission was created in Britain for the analysis of foods Suspicions about chocolate proved well-founded-most of the samples contained starch grains from potatoes or other plants.”\n解题思路：原文虽然提到了一些不良行为，但没有提到因此导致顾客生病的信息。因此答案为NOT GIVEN。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55266","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"7167:55267:5","type":"choice","text":"Fresh milk was used in the production of milk chocolate in Switzerland.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是“在瑞士，生产牛奶巧克力时使用了新鲜牛奶”是否正确。\n定位关键信息：“Fresh milk”、“used”、“production of milk chocolate”、“Switzerland”\n对应原文：F段，“The invention of milk chocolate took place in Switzerland, and was a collaboration between two men. The first was Henri Nestle, a chemist who in 1867 discovered a process to make powdered milk by evaporation, when mixed with water, this could be fed to infants and small children. The second man, Daniel Peter, came up with the idea of using Nestle's milk powder in the manufacture of a new kind of chocolate, and, in 1879, the first milk chocolate bar was produced.”\n解题思路：原文提到的是使用奶粉（milk powder），而不是新鲜牛奶（fresh milk）。因此题目说法错误。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55267","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"7167:55268:6","type":"choice","text":"Lindt's conche machine was adopted by other manufacturers.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是“Lindt的精炼机被其他制造商采用”是否正确。\n定位关键信息：“Lindt’s conche machine”\n对应原文：G段，“People on both sides of the Atlantic developed a taste for fondant chocolate, and the use of the conche machine for solid chocolate became universal in the business.”\n解题思路：原文明确提到Lindt的精炼机在巧克力行业内被广泛使用（became universal）。因此，说明被其他制造商采用。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55268","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"7167:55269:7","type":"fill","text":"填写第 7 空","answer":"machinery","acceptedAnswers":["machinery"],"explanation":"定位关键词：\nbought，after visiting a trade fair\n定位原文：H段，“In 1893, after seeing examples of the machinery used in Europe in action at an international exhibition in Chicago, he bought some and began turning out chocolate coatings for the caramels he was already producing.”\n解题思路：原文提到Hershey在参观展会后购买了一些机器（machinery）。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55269","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"7167:55270:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"farm","acceptedAnswers":["farm"],"explanation":"定位关键词：\ncaramel business\n定位原文：H段，“he sold his caramel business for a million dollars, bought a farm in Pennsylvania, and built a chocolate factory there.”\n解题思路：原文提到Hershey卖掉了焦糖业务后购买了农场（farm）。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55270","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"7167:55271:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"mayor","acceptedAnswers":["mayor"],"explanation":"定位关键词：\ninhabitants，vote\n定位原文：I段，“There was, however, no elected mayor or indeed any democratic system in place.”\n解题思路：原文提到Hershey镇没有市长（mayor），居民无法选举市长。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55271","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"7167:55272:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"railroads","acceptedAnswers":["railroads"],"explanation":"定位关键词：\ntransport material\n定位原文：J段，“To transport the refined sugar so that it could be shipped by sea to his chocolate and cocoa factory, Hershey built modern electric railroads too.”\n解题思路：原文提到Hershey修建了铁路（railroads）来运输材料。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55272","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"7167:55273:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"nutritionists","acceptedAnswers":["nutritionists"],"explanation":"定位关键词：\nimprove the image of his chocolate\n定位原文：K段，“Hershey employed nutritionists to proclaim their health qualities.”\n解题思路：原文提到Hershey雇佣了营养学家（nutritionists）来宣传巧克力的健康形象。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55273","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"7167:55274:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"almonds","acceptedAnswers":["almonds"],"explanation":"定位关键词：\npopular，add\n定位原文：K段，“Hershey's best-selling bar contained almonds imported from southern Europe.”\n解题思路：原文提到Hershey的热销巧克力产品加入了杏仁（almonds）。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55274","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"7167:55275:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"exhibition","acceptedAnswers":["exhibition"],"explanation":"定位关键词：\nthe huge demand, tourists\n定位原文：L段，“Rather, visitors are whisked along on automated carts through an exhibition called 'Chocolate World'.”\n解题思路：原文提到游客只能参观“展览”（exhibition），而不是工厂。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55275","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"55263","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Chocolate was consumed by greater numbers of people in the nineteenth century than in previous times.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"55264","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Fry&#39;s chocolate became more affordable because of the fall in price of one ingredient.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"55265","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Entrepreneurial British chocolate manufacturers paid their employees well.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"55266","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Customers were made ill through the practices of unscrupulous chocolate producers.</strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"55267","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Fresh milk was used in the production of milk chocolate in Switzerland.</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"55268","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 6\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Lindt&#39;s conche machine was adopted by other manufacturers.</strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"55269","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Milton Hershey and the chocolate industry</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>• Hershey bought some <strong class=\"source-blank\">[7] ____</strong> after visiting a trade fair.</p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"55270","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><span style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">•&nbsp;</span>After selling his caramel business, Hershey purchased a <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"55271","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><span style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">•&nbsp;</span>The inhabitants of Hershey could not vote for a <strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"55272","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><span style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">•&nbsp;</span>Hershey set up a new town in Cuba around a mill.</p><p><span style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">•&nbsp;</span>Hershey constructed <strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong> to transport material.</p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"55273","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><span style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">•&nbsp;</span>Hershey brought in <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong> to improve the image of his chocolate.</p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"55274","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><span style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">•&nbsp;</span>One popular chocolate product had <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong> added to it.</p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"55275","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 7 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p><span style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">•&nbsp;</span>Because of the huge demand, tourists can only visit the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong> at Hershey.</p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>Chocolate for the masses</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong><br/></strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">For almost three thousand years, chocolate was a drink of the elite and the wealthy, originally in South America and later on in Europe. In the early 19th century, however, chocolate became far more widely available, and consumption shot up dramatically across the populations of Europe in particular.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">It was 1828 that marked the beginning of the modern era in chocolate making and production. Chocolate as a drink had been known for centuries, but in 1828 a Dutch chemist named Van Houten developed a process for the manufacture of a new kind of powdered chocolate using a hydraulic press. Untreated chocolate &#39;liquor&#39;&nbsp;–&nbsp;the end result of grinding the cacao beans from which chocolate is obtained&nbsp;–&nbsp;contains about 53 per cent cacao butter,&nbsp; but this machine removed nearly half of this, leaving a &#39;cake&#39; that could be pulverized into a fine powder&nbsp;–&nbsp;what is now known as &#39;cocoa&#39;.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">In 1847, the British firm Fry and Sons found a way to mix a blend of cocoa powder and sugar with melted cacao butter to produce a thin paste which could be cast into various shapes. This was the world&#39;s first true solid chocolate. Thanks to immediate high demand for this product, the price of cacao butter escalated, so the new solid chocolate was only accessible for the elite. But this would eventually change, because of the introduction of cost-cutting methods and mass production.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">By the latter half of the 19th century, many manufacturers had begun making their own chocolate, and using cocoa powder to hand-coat sugar confections. Cocoa powder also reached wide use in many other products, like ice creams and biscuits. Entrepreneurial families like the Frys and Cadburys in Britain had a social conscience in the midst of all this money-making, unlike many other 19th-century captains of industry. In the Birmingham suburb of Bournville, where they had established their chocolate factory, the Cadburys created a model town with adequate housing for their workers, and even dining and reading rooms so that their employees had no need to spend anything on entertaining themselves.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">However, the rising demand for chocolate also made it a target for unscrupulous producers and merchants. Sometimes the expensive cacao butter was completely extracted and replaced with olive or almond oil, or egg yolks. Alternatively, cheaper materials such as potato starch or flour were added. In 1850, a health commission was created in Britain for the analysis of foods. Suspicions about chocolate proved well-founded<span style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">&nbsp;–&nbsp;</span>most of the samples contained starch grains from potatoes or other plants. The investigation inspired the British Food and Drug Act of 1860 and the Adulteration of Food Act of 1872.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The invention of milk chocolate took place in Switzerland, and was a collaboration between two men. The first was Henri Nestle, a chemist who in 1867 discovered a process to make powdered milk by evaporation, when mixed with water, this could be fed to infants and small children.&nbsp;The second man, Daniel Peter, came up with the idea of using Nestle&#39;s milk powder in the manufacture of a new kind of chocolate, and, in 1879, the first milk chocolate bar was produced.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>G</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Also in 1879 another Swiss, Rodolphe Lindt, invented the conche machine, which vastly improved the quality of chocolate confectionery. Before Lindt, solid chocolate was usually coarse and gritty. Now, however, it achieved such a degree of smoothness that Lindt named it &#39;fondant&#39;, after the smooth sugar creams of that name. People on both sides of the Atlantic developed a taste for fondant chocolate, and the use of the conche machine for solid chocolate became universal in the business.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>H</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">In the USA, Milton Hershey dominated the chocolate industry. In 1893, after seeing examples of the machinery used in Europe in action at an international exhibition in Chicago, he bought some and began turning out chocolate coatings for the caramels he was already producing.&nbsp;But after a trip to the chocolate centers of Europe, he sold his caramel business for a million dollars, bought a farm in Pennsylvania, and built a chocolate factory there.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">I&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">This became the nucleus of &#39;Hershey, the Chocolate Town&#39;, which contained amongst other things Hershey&#39;s imposing mansion, the Hershey Department Store and the Hershey Bank. There was, however, no elected mayor or indeed any democratic system in place. The whole town was in essence Milton Hershey&#39;s private kingdom, and he ran it as he wanted.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>J</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">This was not the only Hershey town in existence. During a trip which he made to the island of Cuba in 1915, Hershey was inspired to build a new model town centered round a mill for grinding sugar. To transport the refined sugar so that it could be shipped by sea to his chocolate and cocoa factory, Hershey built modern electric railroads too.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>K</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">To help advertise his products, Hershey employed nutritionists to proclaim their health qualities, and his chocolate bars and cocoa soon commanded the American market. Everything was mechanized – a true assembly-line operation. Hershey&#39;s best-selling bar contained almonds imported from southern Europe, dropped by machines into the waiting molds. Another popular product was &#39;Hershey&#39;s Kisses&#39; – bite-sized, flat-bottomed drops of chocolate, individually wrapped.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>L</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Nowadays so many tourists visit Hershey that the company no longer offers tours of its factory. Rather, visitors are whisked along on automated carts through an exhibition called &#39;Chocolate World&#39;, where they can see how their favorite products are produced.</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7167&scene=%E7%A4%BE%E4%BC%9A%E4%BA%BA%E6%96%87&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7168","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Boring buildings","book":"阅读还原集Vol.9","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.9 · Test 1 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"7168:55276:14","type":"fill","text":"14 a description of a building that has a positive effect","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是哪个段落描述了建筑对人产生积极影响。\n定位关键信息：“building”、“positive effect”\n对应原文：F段，“Hearst Tower is a glass-and-steel skyscraper... energizing employees who enter it each morning... New Yorkers who pass by would find this building boring. And theyre likely to be happier—maybe even nicer to each other—because of it.”\n解题思路：原文明确提到Hearst Tower让人更有活力，并且使人心情更好，这是积极的效果。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55276","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nLook at the six sections (A - F). Which section contains the following information?"},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"7168:55276:15","type":"fill","text":"15 a reference to architecture affecting people's performance in their jobs","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是哪个段落提到建筑对人们工作表现的影响。\n定位关键信息：“architecture”、“performance in their jobs”\n对应原文：A段，“Urban policy professor Justin Hollander and architect Ann Sussman review scientific data to help architects and urban planners understand how, exactly, people respond to their built surroundings, particularly at work. People, they argue, function best in intricate settings, not 'big, blank, boxy offices'.”\n解题思路：原文提到“人们在复杂的环境中工作表现更好”，表明建筑设计会影响工作表现。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55276","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nLook at the six sections (A - F). Which section contains the following information?"},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"7168:55276:16","type":"fill","text":"16 examples of the intensity of people's reactions in two urban settings","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是哪个段落讲述了在两个城市环境中人们反应强度的例子。\n定位关键信息：“intensity”、“reactions”、“two urban settings”\n对应原文：B段，“Passing the monolithic Whole Foods Market, people's state of arousal plummeted. Physiologically, Ellard explained, they were bored. To describe this place, they used words like 'bland' and 'passionless'. In contrast, one block east at the other test site – a 'lively sea of restaurants with lots of open doors and windows' – people measured high levels of excitement, and they listed words like 'lively', and 'socializing'.”\n解题思路：原文中描述了两种不同城市环境的测试：一个充满活力，另一个是无趣的建筑，反应强度差异明显。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55276","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nLook at the six sections (A - F). Which section contains the following information?"},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"7168:55276:17","type":"fill","text":"17 details of a study where seeing certain pictures reduced people's stress","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是哪个段落描述了一个研究的细节，该研究表明观看特定图片能减少人们的压力。\n定位关键信息：“study”、“seeing pictures”、“reduced stress”\n对应原文：D段，“One study conducted by Melanie Rudd, Kathleen Vohs and Jennifer Aaker of Stanford University in the US showed that the feeling of' awe' can make people more patient and less materialistic. In an experiment, the researchers showed students 60-second clips of waterfalls, whales, or astronauts in space. After only a minute of virtual images, those who said they were awed also felt less pressed for time.”\n解题思路：原文中提到研究人员向学生们展示了60秒的瀑布、鲸鱼或太空宇航员的片段。在观看了一分钟的虚拟图像后，那些学生表示自己感到时间不那么紧迫了，也就意味着压力减少了。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55276","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nLook at the six sections (A - F). Which section contains the following information?"},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"7168:55276:18","type":"fill","text":"18 a claim about feelings experienced in response to both architecture and leisure settings","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是哪个段落提到了人们在建筑和休闲场所中都会体验到的情感。\n定位关键信息：“feelings”、“architecture and leisure settings”\n对应原文：C段，“ 'Humans want a certain element of turmoil or confusion,' he said. Complexity is thrilling whether in an amusement park or architecture.”\n解题思路：原文提到复杂性在建筑和娱乐环境中都能引发刺激感（thrilling），题目中的“feelings”与“thrilling”对应。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55276","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nLook at the six sections (A - F). Which section contains the following information?"},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"7168:55277:19","type":"choice","text":"19 The aim of good city planning is to provide variety in architecture.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是“好的城市规划目标是提供建筑的多样性”是哪个专家提出的。\n定位关键信息：“aim”、“city planning”、“variety in architecture”\n对应原文：B段，“Ellard explains that the main objective of urban design should be to produce some kind of novelty or change every few seconds.”\n解题思路：Ellard认为城市设计的主要目标是“提供新奇或变化”，即提供建筑的多样性。","options":["Colin Ellard","Brendan Walker","Rudd, Vohs and Aaker","Charles Montgomery"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55277","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions19-23\nChoose the correct researcher (A - D) for each statement. You may choose any letter more than once.\nList of Researchers\nA Colin Ellard\nB Brendan Walker\nC Rudd, Vohs and Aaker\nD Charles Montgomery"},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"7168:55277:20","type":"choice","text":"20 People in untidy areas were more helpful.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是“生活在杂乱区域的人更乐于助人”是哪个专家提出的。\n定位关键信息：“untidy areas”、“more helpful”\n对应原文：E段，“Pedestrians at active sites were nearly five times more likely to offer assistance than at inactive ones.”\n解题思路：原文中提到在活跃（杂乱）的区域行人更乐于帮助他人（五倍），与题目一致。","options":["Colin Ellard","Brendan Walker","Rudd, Vohs and Aaker","Charles Montgomery"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55277","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions19-23\nChoose the correct researcher (A - D) for each statement. You may choose any letter more than once.\nList of Researchers\nA Colin Ellard\nB Brendan Walker\nC Rudd, Vohs and Aaker\nD Charles Montgomery"},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"7168:55277:21","type":"choice","text":"21 People who had recently felt amazed, placed less importance on material goods.","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是“感到惊讶的人会对物质物品重视程度较低”是哪个专家提出的。\n定位关键信息：“felt amazed”、“less importance on material goods”。\n对应原文：D段，“And in another variation, people made hypothetical choices between physical and experiential goods of equal monetary value. Those who had just 'felt awe' were more likely to choose an experience over a possession, a choice that is linked with greater satisfaction in the long run.”\n解题思路：原文提到“更愿意选择体验而非物质物品”，与题目一致。","options":["Colin Ellard","Brendan Walker","Rudd, Vohs and Aaker","Charles Montgomery"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55277","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions19-23\nChoose the correct researcher (A - D) for each statement. You may choose any letter more than once.\nList of Researchers\nA Colin Ellard\nB Brendan Walker\nC Rudd, Vohs and Aaker\nD Charles Montgomery"},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"7168:55277:22","type":"choice","text":"22 'Attractive' places are not necessarily the most enjoyable places to be.","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是“外观好看的地方不一定最令人愉快”是哪个专家提出的。\n定位关键信息：“attractive places”、“not necessarily enjoyable”。\n对应原文：E段，“People often confuse successful architecture with whether an area looks pleasant. On the contrary, when it comes to city buildings, people often focus too narrowly on aesthetics, said Charles Montgomery, author of Happy City: Transforming Our Lives Through Urban Design. Some of the happiest blocks in New York City, he argues, are ' kind of ugly and messy'.”\n解题思路：原文提到“一些最令人愉快的街区其实很丑陋和杂乱”，说明外观不代表愉悦感。","options":["Colin Ellard","Brendan Walker","Rudd, Vohs and Aaker","Charles Montgomery"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55277","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions19-23\nChoose the correct researcher (A - D) for each statement. You may choose any letter more than once.\nList of Researchers\nA Colin Ellard\nB Brendan Walker\nC Rudd, Vohs and Aaker\nD Charles Montgomery"},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"7168:55277:23","type":"choice","text":"23 One particular building failed to provide visual stimulation.","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是“某特定建筑未能提供视觉刺激”是哪个专家提出的。\n定位关键信息：“building”、“visual stimulation”\n对应原文：B段，“Passing the monolithic Whole Foods Market, people's state of arousal plummeted.”\n解题思路：原文中提到经过Whole Foods Market时，人们的兴奋度下降（lack of stimulation），与题目一致。","options":["Colin Ellard","Brendan Walker","Rudd, Vohs and Aaker","Charles Montgomery"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55277","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions19-23\nChoose the correct researcher (A - D) for each statement. You may choose any letter more than once.\nList of Researchers\nA Colin Ellard\nB Brendan Walker\nC Rudd, Vohs and Aaker\nD Charles Montgomery"},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"7168:55278:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"facade","acceptedAnswers":["facade"],"explanation":"定位关键词：a striking impact on commuters and employees\n定位原文：F段，“From the outside, the facade jolts city dwellers from their daily commutes.”\n解题思路：原文提到“外墙（facade）给上班族带来震撼的效果”，与题目一致。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55278","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"7168:55278:25","type":"fill","text":"填写第 25 空","answer":"escalators","acceptedAnswers":["escalators"],"explanation":"定位关键词：carry employees up\n定位原文：F段，“Inside, workers travel upon diagonal escalators, up a three-story water sculpture, through the tower's historic atrium, flooded with light.”\n解题思路：原文提到“内部有斜向电梯（escalators）”供员工使用，符合题意。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55278","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"7168:55278:26","type":"fill","text":"填写第 26 空","answer":"atrium","acceptedAnswers":["atrium"],"explanation":"定位关键词：light-filled\n定位原文：F段，“Inside, workers travel upon diagonal escalators, up a three-story water sculpture, through the tower's historic atrium, flooded with light.”\n解题思路：原文提到“充满光线的中庭（atrium）”，与题目一致。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55278","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"55276","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 18\nLook at the six sections (A - F). Which section contains the following information?","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"55277","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions19-23\nChoose the correct researcher (A - D) for each statement. You may choose any letter more than once.\nList of Researchers\nA Colin Ellard\nB Brendan Walker\nC Rudd, Vohs and Aaker\nD Charles Montgomery","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":19},{"id":"55278","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 24 - 26\nComplete the summary. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Hearst Tower</strong></p><p style=\"line-height: 2em;\">Norman Foster&#39;s Hearst Tower was built in 2006. The 40-storey modern triangular-patterned building is made of glass and steel, contrasting with the base which is in the style of the 1920s. The sight of the building&#39;s <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong>&nbsp;has a striking impact on commuters and employees. Some passers-by may find the building&#39;s design confusing, as it mixes old and new elements. Inside the tower <strong class=\"source-blank\">[25] ____</strong> carry employees up past a large water sculpture in the light-filled <strong class=\"source-blank\">[26] ____</strong> .</p>","firstNumber":24}],"passage":"<p><strong>Boring buildings</strong></p><p><br/></p><p><em>There could be more than an economic or nostalgic price to impersonal retail and high-rise construction; boring architecture may take an emotional toll on the people forced to live with it</em></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>A growing body of research in cognitive science illuminates the physical and mental toll bland cityscapes take on residents. Generally, these researchers argue that humans are healthier when they live surrounded by variety or work in well-designed, unique spaces, rather than unattractive, generic ones. Urban policy professor Justin Hollander and architect Ann Sussman review scientific data to help architects and urban planners understand how, exactly, people respond to their built surroundings, particularly at work. People, they argue, function best in intricate settings, not &#39;big, blank, boxy offices&#39;.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>B&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Indeed, that&#39;s what Colin Ellard, a neuroscientist at the University of Waterloo in Canada, has found in his work. Five years ago, Ellard became interested in a certain building – the gigantic Whole Foods Market &#39;plopped into&#39; a notoriously textured part of lower Manhattan in New York. Ellard partnered with the Guggenheim Museum to analyze what happens when someone walks out of a tiny neighborhood restaurant and encounters a full city block with nothing but &#39;the long, blank facade of the Whole Foods Market&#39; building.</p><p><br/></p><p>In 2011, Ellard led small groups on Lower East Side walks to measure the effect of the urban environment on them. Participants recorded their response to questions at each stopping point and wore sensors that measured skin conductance, a response to emotional excitement. Passing the monolithic Whole Foods Market, people&#39;s state of arousal plummeted. Physiologically, Ellard explained, they were bored. To describe this place, they used words like &#39;bland&#39; and &#39;passionless&#39;. In contrast, one block east at the other test site – a &#39;lively sea of restaurants with lots of open doors and windows&#39; – people measured high levels of excitement, and they listed words like &#39;lively&#39;, and &#39;socializing&#39;. Ellard explains that the main objective of urban design should be to produce some kind of novelty or change every few seconds; otherwise, we become cognitively disengaged.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>The trick, it seems, is to design a world that excites but doesn&#39;t overload our faculties with a constant barrage of information. &#39;We are, as animals, programmed to respond to thrill,&#39; said Professor Brendan Walker. In Walker&#39;s &#39;thrill laboratory&#39; at the University of Nottingham in the UK, devices measure heart rate and skin conductance to see how people respond to adrenaline-producing experiences such as a roller-coaster ride. A thrilling encounter moves us quickly from a state of equilibrium to a desirable &#39;disorientation&#39;. &#39;Humans want a certain element of turmoil or confusion,&#39; he said. &#39;Complexity is thrilling whether in an amusement park or architecture.&#39;</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>D&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Psychologists have found that awe-inspiring moments can potentially improve our well-being. One study conducted by Melanie Rudd, Kathleen Vohs and Jennifer Aaker of Stanford University in the US showed that the feeling of &#39;awe&#39; can make people more patient and less materialistic. In an experiment, the researchers showed students 60-second clips of waterfalls, whales, or astronauts in space. After only a minute of virtual images, those who said they were awed also felt less pressed for time. And in another variation, people made hypothetical choices between physical and experiential goods of equal monetary value. Those who had just &#39;felt awe&#39; were more likely to choose an experience over a possession, a choice that is linked with greater satisfaction in the long run. In other words, a visual buzz – whether architectural or natural – might have the ability to change our frame of mind, making modern-day life more satisfying and interactive.</p><p><br/></p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>It&#39;s important to note, however, that architectural boredom isn&#39;t about how pristine a street is. People often confuse successful architecture with whether an area looks pleasant. On the contrary, when it comes to city buildings, people often focus too narrowly on aesthetics, said Charles Montgomery, author of Happy City: Transforming Our Lives Through Urban Design. Some of the happiest blocks in New York City, he argues, are &#39;kind of ugly and messy&#39;.</p><p><br/></p><p>In 2014, Montgomery&#39;s Happy City lab conducted an experiment in which he found a strong correlation between messier blocks and pro-social behavior. Montgomery sent researchers, posing as lost tourists, to places he coded as either &#39;active&#39; or &#39;inactive&#39; facades. He concluded that the former had a high level of interest, that is they were messy, while the latter had no special features such as long warehouse blocks. Pedestrians at active sites were nearly five times more likely to offer assistance than at inactive ones. Of those who assisted, seven times as many at the active site offered use of their phone.<br/></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p>Fortunately, it&#39;s not necessarily a dichotomy – new architecture can achieve the optimal level of cacophony and beauty. Take the 2006 Hearst Tower in midtown Manhattan. Designed by architect Norman Foster, Hearst Tower is a glass-and-steel skyscraper, 40 stories of which are designed in a triangular pattern, differing in style from the 1920s Art Deco base. From the outside, the facade jolts city dwellers from their daily commutes, while energizing employees who enter it each morning. For many who walk by, Hearst Tower&#39;s design may not be the easiest to understand; it&#39;s both sleek and old. The top looks like it traveled from the future. Inside, workers travel upon diagonal escalators, up a three-story water sculpture, through the tower&#39;s historic atrium, flooded with light. Few New Yorkers who pass by would find this building boring. And they&#39;re likely to be happier&nbsp;–&nbsp;maybe even nicer to each other – because of it.</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7168&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7169","type":"reading","title":"Passage 3 The Analysis of Fear","book":"阅读还原集Vol.9","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 1","part":3,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.9 · Test 1 · 14 题","questions":[{"number":27,"sourceQuestionId":"7169:55279:27","type":"choice","text":"In the first paragraph, the writer points out that","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是第一段中作者指出了什么。\n定位关键信息：“the first paragraph”\n对应原文：A段，“Over the years, the majority of people acquire a range of skills for coping with frightening situations.”\n解题思路：A段明确提到“大多数人都学会了处理恐惧情境的技巧”。\n同义替换：coping with=dealing with","options":["fear and stress are different feelings.","most humans develop strategies for dealing with fear.","business situations cause more fear than others.","some people never experience fear."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55279","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 30\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":28,"sourceQuestionId":"7169:55280:28","type":"choice","text":"When discussing the use of rhesus monkeys as experimental subjects, the writer notes that","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是关于“使用恒河猴作为实验对象”时，作者提到的特征。\n定位关键信息：“rhesus monkeys”和“mental growth”\n对应原文：B段，“These animals undergo many of the same physiological and psychological developmental stages that humans do, but in a more compressed time span.”\n解题思路：原文提到恒河猴的“心理发展阶段”与人类相似，这表明恒河猴的心理成长与人类相似，因此选项C是正确的。","options":["they react more quickly to fear than humans.","they are more influenced by fear than humans.","their mental growth resembles that of humans.","their brains work more slowly than those of humans."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55280","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 30\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":29,"sourceQuestionId":"7169:55281:29","type":"choice","text":"Which of the following did Kalin and Shelton outline as the second stage in their research project?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是Kalin和Shelton在研究项目中定义的第二阶段。\n定位关键信息：“Kalin and Shelton”和“second stage”。\n对应原文：C段，“Kalin and Shelton knew that they would first have to find cues that elicit fear and identify behaviors that reflect different types of anxiety. With such information in hand, they could then proceed to determine the age at which monkeys begin to match defensive behaviors selectively to specific cues.”\n解题思路：原文中明确表示，第一步是“找到引发恐惧的线索”，接着才是分析猴子的行为与年龄之间的关系。","options":["the identification of expressions of anxiety in monkeys","the identification of situations that arouse stress in monkeys","an analysis of brain development in monkeys","the study of reactions to fear in monkeys of different ages"],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55281","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 30\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":30,"sourceQuestionId":"7169:55282:30","type":"choice","text":"In the fourth paragraph, the writer notes that the three related situations","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是第四段中提到的三种情境反映了什么。\n定位关键信息：“the fourth paragraph”和“three related situations”。\n对应原文：D段，“These positions are no more frightening than those that primates encounter frequently in the wild, or those that human infants encounter every time they are left at a day-care center.”\n解题思路：原文提到这三种情境类似于“人类婴儿在托儿所时遇到的情境”，因此A选项是正确答案。","options":["reflect common experiences for infant humans and monkeys.","highlight the similarities between monkey and human infant care.","were predicted to cause monkeys more distress than human infants.","were graded in terms of their potential effect on young monkeys."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D"],"sourceGroupId":"55282","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 30\nChoose the correct answer."},{"number":31,"sourceQuestionId":"7169:55283:31","type":"choice","text":"31 aggressive facial expressions","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"对应原文：E段，“So the stare condition evoked a third set of responses. The monkeys made several hostile gestures: \"barking\" (forcing air from the abdomen through the vocal cords to emit a harsh, growl-like sound) and staring back.”\n解题思路：原文描述了“stare condition”情境下猴子表现出的攻击性行为（如“barking” 和“staring back”），这符合题目中“aggressive facial expressions”的描述。","options":["the alone condition","the no-eye-contact condition","the stare condition"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"55283","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 31 - 35\nChoose the correct condition (A - C) for each response of monkey. You may choose any correct condition more than once.\nList of Conditions\nA the alone condition\nB the no-eye-contact condition\nC the stare condition"},{"number":32,"sourceQuestionId":"7169:55283:32","type":"choice","text":"32 prolonged stillness","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"对应原文：E段，“In the more frightening no-eye-contact situation, the monkeys reduced their activity greatly and sometimes froze for extended periods of time.”\n解题思路：原文明确提到“no-eye-contact condition”情境下猴子表现出“froze for extended periods of time”（长时间静止）的行为，这与题目描述完全一致。","options":["the alone condition","the no-eye-contact condition","the stare condition"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"55283","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 31 - 35\nChoose the correct condition (A - C) for each response of monkey. You may choose any correct condition more than once.\nList of Conditions\nA the alone condition\nB the no-eye-contact condition\nC the stare condition"},{"number":33,"sourceQuestionId":"7169:55283:33","type":"choice","text":"33 a combination of contradictory signals","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"对应原文：E段，“Sometimes the animals mixed the threatening displays with submissive ones, such as fear grimaces, which look something like wary grins, or grinding of teeth.”\n解题思路：原文中描述了猴子在“stare condition”情境下表现出“threatening displays（威胁性展示）”和“submissive ones（顺从的表现）”的混合行为，这些行为相互矛盾，正好符合题干“contradictory signals”的描述。","options":["the alone condition","the no-eye-contact condition","the stare condition"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"55283","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 31 - 35\nChoose the correct condition (A - C) for each response of monkey. You may choose any correct condition more than once.\nList of Conditions\nA the alone condition\nB the no-eye-contact condition\nC the stare condition"},{"number":34,"sourceQuestionId":"7169:55283:34","type":"choice","text":"34 appeals for maternal protection","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"对应原文：E段，“In the alone condition, most monkeys became very active and emitted frequent gentle ‘coo’ calls made with pursed lips. These responses help to draw the mother's attention.”\n解题思路：原文提到“emitted frequent gentle ‘coo’ calls”行为是为了“draw the mother’s attention（吸引母亲的注意）”，即“寻求母亲保护”，这与题目描述一致。","options":["the alone condition","the no-eye-contact condition","the stare condition"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"55283","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 31 - 35\nChoose the correct condition (A - C) for each response of monkey. You may choose any correct condition more than once.\nList of Conditions\nA the alone condition\nB the no-eye-contact condition\nC the stare condition"},{"number":35,"sourceQuestionId":"7169:55283:35","type":"choice","text":"35 the production of soft sounds","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"对应原文：E段，“In the alone condition, most monkeys...emitted frequent gentle 'coo' calls made with pursed lips.”\n解题思路：原文中描述了“emitted frequent gentle 'coo' calls（发出轻柔的‘咕咕’声）”，这正是题干“soft sounds”的描述。","options":["the alone condition","the no-eye-contact condition","the stare condition"],"optionValues":["A","B","C"],"sourceGroupId":"55283","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 31 - 35\nChoose the correct condition (A - C) for each response of monkey. You may choose any correct condition more than once.\nList of Conditions\nA the alone condition\nB the no-eye-contact condition\nC the stare condition"},{"number":36,"sourceQuestionId":"7169:55284:36","type":"fill","text":"填写第 36 空","answer":"age","acceptedAnswers":["age"],"explanation":"审题与定位：题目中“grouped the monkeys according to”提示我们寻找分组的标准。关键词是“grouped”和“according to”，可以定位到F段描述分组方法的句子。\n对应原文：\nF段，“To establish the critical period of development, they examined four groups of infant monkeys ranging in age up to 12 weeks old.”\n解题思路：原文明确指出，他们是根据“age”（年龄）将猴子分成四组。因此，答案为“age”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55284","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":3},{"number":37,"sourceQuestionId":"7169:55284:37","type":"fill","text":"填写第 37 空","answer":"two weeks old/2 weeks old","acceptedAnswers":["two weeks old","2 weeks old"],"explanation":"审题与定位：题目中的关键词是“Monkeys as young as”和“haphazard fashion”。我们需要找到描述年龄最小的猴子反应的段落，定位到F段。\n对应原文：\nF段，“The infants in the youngest group (no more than two weeks old) engaged in defensive behaviors. But they lacked some motor control and seemed to act randomly.”\n解题思路：这里明确提到“the youngest group”（最小组别的猴子）的年龄是“两周以下”（no more than two weeks old）。该组猴子表现出了随机行为（acted randomly），这正好对应“haphazard fashion”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55284","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":3},{"number":38,"sourceQuestionId":"7169:55284:38","type":"fill","text":"填写第 38 空","answer":"human beings","acceptedAnswers":["human beings"],"explanation":"审题与定位：关键词是“unaware of”和“who were around them”。\n我们要找猴子对周围存在无反应的描述，可以定位到F段的最小组别反应描述。\n对应原文：\nF段，“But they lacked some motor control and seemed to act randomly, as if they had not noticed the human beings that were present.”\n解题思路：原文中明确提到，这些猴子好像没有注意到在场的“human beings”（人类）。因此答案是“human beings”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55284","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":3},{"number":39,"sourceQuestionId":"7169:55284:39","type":"fill","text":"填写第 39 空","answer":"good motor control","acceptedAnswers":["good motor control"],"explanation":"审题与定位：题目中“demonstrating”提示我们寻找描述猴子有某种能力的句子。关键词是“middle groups”和“failed to react”。可以定位到描述中间组（intermediate-age groups）猴子行为的句子。\n对应原文：\nF段，“Babies in the two intermediate-age groups had good motor control, but their actions seemed unrelated to the test condition.”\n解题思路：原文描述了中间组的猴子表现出了“good motor control”（良好的运动控制能力），但是他们的行为与实验情境无关。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55284","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":3},{"number":40,"sourceQuestionId":"7169:55284:40","type":"fill","text":"填写第 40 空","answer":"mature monkeys","acceptedAnswers":["mature monkeys"],"explanation":"审题与定位：题目中的关键词是“oldest group”和“reacted in the same way as”。\n定位到F段描述最老组（oldest group）猴子行为的句子。\n对应原文：\nF段，“Only animals in the oldest group...conducted themselves differently in each situation, and their reactions were both appropriate and identical to those of mature monkeys.”\n解题思路：原文明确指出，最老组猴子的反应与“mature monkeys”（成熟的猴子）一致。因此答案是“mature monkeys”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55284","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","maxWords":3}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"55279","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 30\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>In the first paragraph, the writer points out that</strong></p>","firstNumber":27},{"id":"55280","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 30\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>When discussing the use of rhesus monkeys as experimental subjects, the writer notes that</strong></p>","firstNumber":28},{"id":"55281","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 30\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>Which of the following did Kalin and Shelton outline as the second stage in their research project?</strong></p>","firstNumber":29},{"id":"55282","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 27 - 30\nChoose the correct answer.","html":"<p><strong>In the fourth paragraph, the writer notes that the three related situations</strong></p>","firstNumber":30},{"id":"55283","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 31 - 35\nChoose the correct condition (A - C) for each response of monkey. You may choose any correct condition more than once.\nList of Conditions\nA the alone condition\nB the no-eye-contact condition\nC the stare condition","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":31},{"id":"55284","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 36 - 40\nComplete the summary. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","html":"<p>Once they had identified three types of defensive behaviour, Kalin and Shelton grouped the monkeys according to their <strong class=\"source-blank\">[36] ____</strong>&nbsp;in order to discover precisely when they were able to respond appropriately to different fear-related cues. They videotaped their results and found that monkeys as young as <strong class=\"source-blank\">[37] ____</strong> reacted to the cues but in a haphazard fashion. The researchers noted that they seemed to be unaware of the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[38] ____</strong> who were around them. Despite demonstrating <strong class=\"source-blank\">[39] ____</strong> the monkeys in the middle groups failed to react in ways corresponding to the experimental situation. The oldest group, however, reacted in the same way as <strong class=\"source-blank\">[40] ____</strong> and the researchers concluded that monkeys are capable of selective responding between nine and 12 weeks old.</p>","firstNumber":36}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>The Analysis of Fear</strong></p><p><br style=\"-webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); font-size: 1.14286rem;\"/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><em>Researchers are investigating the processes in the brain that give rise to fear in animals. The results may lead to new ways to treat human anxiety.</em></p><p><br style=\"-webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); font-size: 1.14286rem;\"/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br style=\"-webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); font-size: 1.14286rem;\"/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Over the years, the majority of people acquire a range of skills for coping with frightening situations. They will attempt to placate a vexed teacher or boss and will shout and run when chased by a hostile stranger. But some individuals become overwhelmed in circumstances others would consider only minimally stressful: fear of ridicule might cause them to shake uncontrollably when called on to speak in a group, or terror of strangers might lead them to hide at home, unable to work or shop for groceries. Why do certain people fall prey to excessive fear?</p><p><br style=\"-webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); font-size: 1.14286rem;\"/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong></p><p><br style=\"-webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); font-size: 1.14286rem;\"/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Ned H. Kalin and Steven E. Shelton at the University of Wisconsin-Madison are addressing this problem by identifying specific brain processes that regulate fear and its associated behaviors. Despite the availability of non-invasive computer imaging techniques. such information is still extremely difficult to obtain in humans. Hence, they have turned their attention to another primate, the rhesus monkey. These animals undergo many of the same physiological and psychological developmental stages that humans do, but in a more compressed time span. As we gain more insight into the nature and operation of neural circuits that modulate fear in monkeys, it should be possible to pinpoint the brain processes that cause inordinate anxiety in people, and to devise new therapies to counteract it. Effective interventions would be particularly valuable if they were applied at an early age, as growing evidence suggests overly fearful youngsters are at high risk of later emotional distress.</p><p><br style=\"-webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); font-size: 1.14286rem;\"/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong></p><p><br style=\"-webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); font-size: 1.14286rem;\"/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">When they began their studies two decades ago, Kalin and Shelton knew that they would first have to find cues that elicit fear and identify behaviors that reflect different types of anxiety. With such information in hand, they could then proceed to determine the age at which monkeys begin to match defensive behaviors selectively to specific cues. Finally, by determining the parts of the brain that reach maturity during the same time span, they could gain clues to the regions that underlie the regulation of fear and fear-related behavior.</p><p><br style=\"-webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); font-size: 1.14286rem;\"/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong></p><p><br style=\"-webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); font-size: 1.14286rem;\"/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The experiments were carried out at the University of Wisconsin-Madison. Kalin and Shelton discerned varied behaviors by exposing monkeys between six and 12 months old to three related situations. In the alone condition, an animal was separated from its mother and left by itself in a cage for ten minutes. In the no-eye-contact condition, a person stood motionless outside the cage and avoided looking at the solitary infant. In the stare condition, a person was again present and motionless but, assuming a neutral expression, peered directly at the animal. These positions are no more frightening than those that primates encounter frequently in the wild, or those that human infants encounter every time they are left at a day-care center.</p><p><br style=\"-webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); font-size: 1.14286rem;\"/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br style=\"-webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); font-size: 1.14286rem;\"/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">In the alone condition, most monkeys became very active and emitted frequent gentle &#39;coo&#39; calls made with pursed lips. More than 40 years ago it was deduced that when an infant monkey is separated from its mother, it yearns to regain the closeness and security provided by nearness to the parent. These responses help to draw the mother&#39;s attention. In contrast, in the more frightening no-eye-contact situation, the monkeys reduced their activity greatly and sometimes froze for extended periods of time. When an infant spots a potential predator, its goal shifts from attracting the mother to becoming inconspicuous. Inhibiting motion and freezing are common attempts to achieve this in many species. If the infant perceives that it has been detected, its aim shifts to warding off an attack. So the stare condition evoked a third set of responses. The monkeys made several hostile gestures: &quot;barking&quot; (forcing air from the abdomen through the vocal cords to emit a harsh, growl-like sound) and staring back. Sometimes the animals mixed the threatening displays with submissive ones, such as fear grimaces, which look something like wary grins, or grinding of teeth.</p><p><br style=\"-webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); font-size: 1.14286rem;\"/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F</strong></p><p><br style=\"-webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); font-size: 1.14286rem;\"/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Having identified three categories of defensive behaviors, Kalin and Shelton set about determining when infant monkeys first begin to apply them effectively. Several lines of work had led them to surmise that the ability to make such choices emerges when an infant is around two months old. To establish the critical period of development, they examined four groups of infant monkeys ranging in age up to 12 weeks old. The babies were separated from their mothers, left to acclimatize to a cage, and then exposed to the alone, no-eye-contact and stare conditions. All sessions were videotaped for analysis. They found that the infants in the youngest group (no more than two weeks old) engaged in defensive behaviors. But they lacked some motor control and seemed to act randomly.as if they had not noticed the human beings that were present. Babies in the two intermediate-age groups had good motor control, but their actions seemed unrelated to the test condition. Only animals in the oldest group (nine- to 12-week-olds) conducted themselves differently in each situation, and their reactions were both appropriate and identical to those of mature monkeys. This finding meant motor control was not the prime determinant of selective responding and that nine to 12 weeks is the critical age for the appearance of a monkey’s ability to adaptively modulate its defensive activity to meet changing demands.</p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7169&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7163","type":"reading","title":"Passage 1 A survivor's story","book":"阅读还原集Vol.8","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":1,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.8 · Test 4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":1,"sourceQuestionId":"7163:55236:1","type":"choice","text":"Early European settlers made detailed studies of the morepork.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问早期欧洲定居者是否对morepork进行了详细研究。\n定位关键信息：European settlers，morepork，detailed studies\n解题思路：文章中并没有提到早期欧洲定居者对morepork的详细研究。文章更多介绍的是laughing owl和morepork的生态特点和现存情况，并没有提到早期定居者的相关研究。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55236","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":2,"sourceQuestionId":"7163:55237:2","type":"choice","text":"The Polynesian rat had a negative effect on the number of laughing owls.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问波利尼西亚鼠是否对笑鸮数量产生了负面影响。\n定位关键信息：\"Polynesian rat\"和“negative effect”\n对应原文：A段，“Where other native birds suffered from predation by the Polynesian rat, the laughing owl turned the tables and adapted its diet to include the rodent.”\n解题思路：原文指出波利尼西亚鼠对其他鸟类有负面影响，但笑鸮通过将波利尼西亚鼠纳入其食谱而适应，因此波利尼西亚鼠对笑鸮并无负面影响。\n同义替换：题目中的“negative effect”替换为“suffered from predation”。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55237","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":3,"sourceQuestionId":"7163:55238:3","type":"choice","text":"The laughing owl was larger than the morepork.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问笑鸮是否比morepork体型更大。\n定位关键信息：\"laughing owl\"（笑鸮）和\"larger\"（更大）。\n对应原文：A段，“However, the laughing owl was wiped out around the beginning of the 20th century. Its demise was caused by specimen collectors, habitat changes, and non-native predators including cats and stoats. Surprisingly, it is the smaller owl, the morepork, that has managed to survive until this day.”\n解题思路：原文中提到laughing owl在20世纪初灭绝，而体型更小的morepork生存至今。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55238","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":4,"sourceQuestionId":"7163:55239:4","type":"choice","text":"Rats pose a risk to young moreporks.","answer":"TRUE","acceptedAnswers":["TRUE"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问老鼠是否对幼年morepork构成威胁。\n定位关键信息：\"rats\"和“young morepork”\n对应原文：F段，“As the female is a hole-nester, she is vulnerable to predators such as stoats and possums during the breeding season, and eggs and chicks will also be at risk from rats.”\n解题思路：原文明确表示老鼠会对morepork的蛋和幼崽造成威胁。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55239","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":5,"sourceQuestionId":"7163:55240:5","type":"choice","text":"The New Zealand Department of Conservation is hoping to limit the population of moreporks.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问新西兰保护部是否希望限制morepork的数量。\n定位关键信息：\"New Zealand Department of Conservation\"和\"limit the population\"\n对应原文：G段，“The department is involved in measuring the population of moreporks... it is hoped that the morepork will continue to survive and thrive.”\n解题思路：原文提到保护部希望morepork种群能够继续生存并繁衍，而不是限制其数量。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55240","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":6,"sourceQuestionId":"7163:55241:6","type":"choice","text":"Other bird species are frightened away when they hear the morepork's cry.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","acceptedAnswers":["NOT GIVEN"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问是否有其他鸟类听到morepork的叫声后感到害怕而逃离。\n定位关键信息：\"Other bird species\"和\"frightened away\"\n对应原文：没有明确提到其他鸟类因为morepork的叫声而逃走的内容。\n解题思路：文章只提到morepork的捕猎策略和叫声在毛利文化中的象征意义，但没有说明其他鸟类听到叫声后的反应。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55241","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":7,"sourceQuestionId":"7163:55242:7","type":"choice","text":"In Maori tradition, the low call of the morepork had negative associations.","answer":"FALSE","acceptedAnswers":["FALSE"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问在毛利传统中，morepork的低音叫声是否具有负面意义。\n定位关键信息：\"Maori tradition\"、\"low call\"和“negative associations”\n对应原文：H段，“The occasional high, piercing call of the morepork signified bad news, but the lower-pitched and more common 'ruru' call heralded good news.”\n解题思路：原文提到morepork的高音叫声预示坏消息，而低音叫声预示好消息，因此低音叫声没有负面意义。","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"optionValues":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"sourceGroupId":"55242","allowNumber":false,"section":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this."},{"number":8,"sourceQuestionId":"7163:55243:8","type":"fill","text":"填写第 8 空","answer":"29 centimeters/29 centimetres","acceptedAnswers":["29 centimeters","29 centimetres"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问morepork的长度。\n定位关键信息：关键词为\"length\"（长度）。\n对应原文：B段，“they are around 29 centimeters long from head to tail。”\n解题思路：原文直接描述了morepork的长度为29厘米。\n同义替换：题目中的“in length”替换为“29 centimeters long”","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55243","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap."},{"number":9,"sourceQuestionId":"7163:55244:9","type":"fill","text":"填写第 9 空","answer":"rocks","acceptedAnswers":["rocks"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问morepork的筑巢地点。\n定位关键信息：\"nests\"和\"roots\"\n对应原文：C段，“Moreporks nest in tree hollows, in clumps of plants, or in cavities among rocks and roots.”\n解题思路：原文明确列出了morepork的筑巢地点，包括“岩石和树根中的缝隙”。\n同义替换：题目中的“spaces in roots”与“cavities among rocks and roots”同义。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55244","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap."},{"number":10,"sourceQuestionId":"7163:55245:10","type":"fill","text":"填写第 10 空","answer":"bill","acceptedAnswers":["bill"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问morepork用什么携带猎物。\n定位关键信息：\"transports its prey\"\n对应原文：D段，“which it then carries away in its bill”。\n解题思路：原文直接提到morepork用“嘴”来携带猎物。\n同义替换：题目中的“transports”替换为“carries away”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55245","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap."},{"number":11,"sourceQuestionId":"7163:55246:11","type":"fill","text":"填写第 11 空","answer":"day","acceptedAnswers":["day"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问morepork在何时被其他鸟类驱逐。\n定位关键信息：\"chased away by other birds\"。\n对应原文：D段，“In the day, these small birds sometimes mob drowsy moreporks and chase them away from their roosts.”\n解题思路：原文指出morepork在白天被其他小鸟驱逐。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55246","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap."},{"number":12,"sourceQuestionId":"7163:55247:12","type":"fill","text":"填写第 12 空","answer":"plovers","acceptedAnswers":["plovers"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问morepork攻击了什么被引入Motuora岛的生物。\n定位关键信息：“attacked”和\"Motuora island\"\n对应原文：E段，“Scientists trying to establish a population of plovers…The culprits turned out to be five pairs of moreporks。”\n解题思路：原文提到morepork攻击了被引入的plovers（鸻鸟）。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55247","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap."},{"number":13,"sourceQuestionId":"7163:55248:13","type":"fill","text":"填写第 13 空","answer":"poison","acceptedAnswers":["poison"],"explanation":"审题：题目询问morepork在猎物中可能接触到什么。\n定位关键信息：“exposed to”和\"prey\"\n对应原文：F段，“As moreporks are at the top of the food chain, they could be affected by an accumulative poison by consuming prey that has ingested poison.”\n解题思路：原文明确提到morepork可能通过猎物接触到“累积性毒素”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55248","allowNumber":true,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap."}],"questionGroups":[],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"55236","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>Early European settlers made detailed studies of the morepork.</strong></p>","firstNumber":1},{"id":"55237","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The Polynesian rat had a negative effect on the number of laughing owls.</strong></p>","firstNumber":2},{"id":"55238","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The laughing owl was larger than the morepork.</strong></p>","firstNumber":3},{"id":"55239","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong><span style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">Rats pose a risk to young moreporks.</span></strong></p>","firstNumber":4},{"id":"55240","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>The New Zealand Department of Conservation is hoping to limit the population of moreporks.</strong></p>","firstNumber":5},{"id":"55241","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong><span style=\"text-wrap: wrap;\">Other bird species are frightened away when they hear the morepork&#39;s cry.</span></strong></p>","firstNumber":6},{"id":"55242","title":"判断／选择","instruction":"Questions 1 - 7\nChoose TRUE if the statement agrees with the information given in the text, choose FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, or choose NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","html":"<p><strong>In Maori tradition, the low call of the morepork had negative associations.</strong></p>","firstNumber":7},{"id":"55243","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>The Morepork</strong></p><p><strong>Appearance</strong></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; – approximately <strong class=\"source-blank\">[8] ____</strong>&nbsp;in length</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; – feathers with fringes to enable quiet flight</p>","firstNumber":8},{"id":"55244","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>Nesting</strong></p><p><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>– nests in trees, plants or spaces in roots and&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[9] ____</strong></p><p><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>– after about 35 days, baby moreporks are capable of leaving the nest</p>","firstNumber":9},{"id":"55245","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>Hunting</strong></p><p><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>–&nbsp;transports its prey using its&nbsp;<strong class=\"source-blank\">[10] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":10},{"id":"55246","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","html":"<p><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>– can be chased away by other birds during the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[11] ____</strong></p>","firstNumber":11},{"id":"55247","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","html":"<p><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>–&nbsp;attacked <strong class=\"source-blank\">[12] ____</strong> that had been introduced to Motuora island</p>","firstNumber":12},{"id":"55248","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 8 - 13\nComplete the notes. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER in each gap.","html":"<p><strong>Threats</strong></p><p><span style=\"text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>– may be exposed to <strong class=\"source-blank\">[13] ____</strong> in their prey</p>","firstNumber":13}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A survivor&#39;s story</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><em>One native bird in New Zealand that has managed to survive the introduction of non-native species</em></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>A&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">As an island country with a fauna dominated by birds, New Zealand was once home to an owl species which is now extinct, the &#39;laughing owl&#39;, named for its distinctive cry. This bird was widespread throughout the islands when European settlers arrived in the middle of the 19th century and it remained in good numbers for some years thereafter. Where other native birds suffered from predation by the Polynesian rat, the laughing owl turned the tables and adapted its diet to include the rodent. It was also capable of catching and killing the other New Zealand owl, the morepork, and even larger birds, such as the weka. However, the laughing owl was wiped out around the beginning of the 20th century. Its demise was caused by specimen collectors, habitat changes, and non-native predators including cats and stoats. Surprisingly, it is the smaller owl, the morepork, that has managed to survive until this day.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>B</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Speckled dark brown, with yellow eyes and long tails, they are around 29 centimeters long from head to tail and 175 grams in weight. Moreporks have fringes on the edge of their feathers, so they can fly almost silently and not alert potential prey. They have acute hearing and their large eyes are very sensitive to light.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>C</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Moreporks nest in tree hollows, in clumps of plants, or in cavities among rocks and roots, in the wild. Moreporks usually start nesting in October, although zoo specimens have been recorded nesting in midwinter, possibly stimulated by an ample food supply. The female lays up to three white eggs, which she incubates for 20 to 30 days. During this time, she rarely hunts, and the male brings food to her. Once the chicks hatch, she stays mainly on the nest until the young owls are fully feathered. When hatched, chicks are covered in light grey down, and have their eyes closed. The eyes do not open until the eighth day after hatching. They can fly at around 35 days.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>D</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">By day, moreporks sleep in roosts. By night, they hunt a variety of animals – mainly large invertebrates including scarab and huhu beetles, moths, caterpillars and spiders. They also take small birds and mice. They can find suitable food in pine forests as well as native forest. A morepork uses its sharp talons to catch or stun its prey, which it then carries away in its bill. Moreporks are clever hunters, and birds such as robins, grey warblers and fantails can end up as their prey. In the day, these small birds sometimes mob drowsy moreporks and chase them away from their roosts. They force the sleepy predators to search for a more peaceful spot.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>E</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Moreporks have proved to be ungracious hosts. Scientists trying to establish a population of plovers on Motuora island in New Zealand&#39;s Hauraki Gulf were mystified as to why only two birds survived out of 75 placed there. The culprits turned out to be five pairs of moreporks that ate or chased away the new arrivals.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>F&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">Although moreporks are still considered to be relatively common, it is likely that numbers are in gradual decline due to predation and loss of habitat. As the female is a hole-nester, she is vulnerable to predators such as stoats and possums during the breeding season, and eggs and chicks will also be at risk from rats. The use of pesticides is another possible threat to the owls though not a direct one. As moreporks are at the top of the food chain, they could be affected by an accumulative poison by consuming prey that has ingested poison.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>G</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">The New Zealand Department of Conservation is taking steps to ensure the preservation of New Zealand&#39;s only native owl. The department is involved in measuring the population of moreporks and has put transmitters on a number of birds to determine survival and mortality. As well as being New Zealand&#39;s only native owl, the morepork has symbolic and spiritual importance, so in monitoring the birds it is hoped that the morepork will continue to survive and thrive.</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><strong>H</strong></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\">At dusk, the melancholy sound of the morepork can be heard in forests and parks as it calls to other moreporks and claims territory. Its Maori name (ruru) echoes its two-part cry. In the tradition of the Maori people of New Zealand, the morepork, or ruru, was often seen as a careful guardian. A number of sayings referred to the bird&#39;s alertness. As a bird of the night, it was associated with the spirit world. Moreporks were believed to act as messengers to the gods in the heavens, flying along spiritual paths in the sky. They were the mediums used to communicate with the gods. The occasional high, piercing call of the morepork signified bad news, but the lower-pitched and more common &#39;ruru&#39; call heralded good news.</p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7163&scene=%E7%94%9F%E7%89%A9%E7%A0%94%E7%A9%B6&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-reading-7165","type":"reading","title":"Passage 2 Biophilic Design","book":"阅读还原集Vol.8","collection":"离线题库","testLabel":"Test 4","part":2,"description":"阅读还原集Vol.8 · Test 4 · 13 题","questions":[{"number":14,"sourceQuestionId":"7165:55250:14","type":"fill","text":"14 a description of how rapid change has a negative effect on people","answer":"C","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"explanation":"题目意思：哪个段落描述描述了快速变化对人类产生负面影响。\n定位关键信息：“rapid change”和“negative effect”\n对应原文：C段，“The rates of technological progress are far exceeding rates of psychological evolution, leaving us ill-equipped to cope with our lifestyle, which in turn leads to increased stress.”\n解题思路：原文提到科技进步的速度超过了心理进化的速度，导致我们无法适应当前的生活方式，增加了压力，符合“快速变化对人类的负面影响”。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55250","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the eight paragraphs (A - H). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nYou may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":15,"sourceQuestionId":"7165:55250:15","type":"fill","text":"15 a reference to an architect whose designs were uncharacteristic of biophilia","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"题目意思：哪个段落提到了一位设计风格不符合生物亲和设计理念的建筑师。\n定位关键信息：“architect”和“uncharacteristic of biophilia”\n对应原文：B段提到，“though not technically a biophilic design, Fallingwater – the stunning house in rural Pennsylvania designed in the 1930s by Frank Lloyd Wright – arguably speaks to the human soul much more than the box-like blocks of flats designed by his contemporary Le Corbusier.”\n解题思路：Le Corbusier设计的建筑风格不符合生物亲和设计，而Frank Lloyd Wright的作品却更符合该理念。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55250","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the eight paragraphs (A - H). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nYou may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":16,"sourceQuestionId":"7165:55250:16","type":"fill","text":"16 a definition of the two main aims of biophilia","answer":"A","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"explanation":"题目意思：哪个段落描述了生物亲和设计的两个主要目标。\n定位关键信息：“main aims”和“biophilia”\n对应原文：A段，“The premise of biophilic design seeks both to avoid or minimize harmful impacts on the natural environment, and equally importantly, to provide and restore beneficial contacts between people and nature in the built environment.”\n解题思路：原文中明确提到生物亲和设计的两个主要目标：减少对自然环境的有害影响，以及恢复人与自然的联系。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55250","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the eight paragraphs (A - H). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nYou may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":17,"sourceQuestionId":"7165:55250:17","type":"fill","text":"17 a positive claim about early forms of architecture","answer":"H","acceptedAnswers":["H"],"explanation":"题目意思：哪个段落描述了对早期建筑形式的积极评价。\n定位关键信息：“positive claim”和“early forms of architecture”\n对应原文：H段，“They mimicked nature’s forms, producing magnificent structures with which we are still awed.”\n解题思路：原文对早期建筑形式进行积极评价，提到这些建筑模仿自然形态，并且至今令人惊叹。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55250","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the eight paragraphs (A - H). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nYou may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":18,"sourceQuestionId":"7165:55250:18","type":"fill","text":"18 a reference to the fact that many architects are too focused on innovation","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"题目意思：哪个段落提到了许多建筑师过于注重创新。\n定位关键信息：“too focused on innovation”\n对应原文：B段，“All too often, architects have put creative originality before the needs of the people who have to live and work in their futuristic constructions.”\n解题思路：原文提到建筑师将“创造性”放在了人们需求之前，过度关注设计创新。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55250","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the eight paragraphs (A - H). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nYou may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":19,"sourceQuestionId":"7165:55250:19","type":"fill","text":"19 a description of features which conserve energy in a biophilic design","answer":"F","acceptedAnswers":["F"],"explanation":"审题：题目问的是哪个段落讲述了在生物亲和性设计中的节能特性。\n定位关键信息：“features which conserve energy”\n对应原文：F段，“The Lewis Center is sustainable in a broader sense than in the typical application of the word. It harnesses solar power, utilizes both active and passive air systems, and monitors the weather to adapt to conditions.”\n解题思路：F段提到Lewis Center利用太阳能，使用主动和被动空气系统，并监测天气以适应条件，这些都是节能特性。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55250","allowNumber":false,"section":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the eight paragraphs (A - H). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nYou may choose any letter more than once."},{"number":20,"sourceQuestionId":"7165:55251:20","type":"fill","text":"填写第 20 空","answer":"technological","acceptedAnswers":["technological"],"explanation":"题目意思：在现代世界中，什么进步速度太快，人类难以适应。\n定位关键信息：“modern world”和“advancements”\n对应原文：C段，“The rates of technological progress are far exceeding rates of psychological evolution.”\n解题思路：原文提到“technological progress”超过了“心理进化”的速度，说明人类难以适应科技进步的速度。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55251","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20 - 24\nComplete the sentences. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":21,"sourceQuestionId":"7165:55253:21","type":"fill","text":"填写第 21 空","answer":"stress","acceptedAnswers":["stress"],"explanation":"题目意思：生物亲和设计可以帮助我们应对由当前生活方式带来的什么。\n定位关键信息：“deal with”和“current lifestyles”\n对应原文：C段，“The rates of technological progress are far exceeding rates of psychological evolution, leaving us ill-equipped to cope with our lifestyle, which in turn leads to increased stress.”\n解题思路：原文提到“biophilia”可以缓解由当前生活方式引起的“stress”（压力）。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55253","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20 - 24\nComplete the sentences. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":22,"sourceQuestionId":"7165:55254:22","type":"fill","text":"填写第 22 空","answer":"sunlight","acceptedAnswers":["sunlight"],"explanation":"题目意思：人们本能地在有充足什么的地方感到更舒适。\n定位关键信息：“comfortable”和“plenty of”\n对应原文：C段，“We are evolutionarily programmed to respond positively to sunny areas over dark or overcast ones.”\n解题思路：原文提到人类对“sunny areas”有积极反应，表明阳光充足的地方使人更舒适。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55254","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20 - 24\nComplete the sentences. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":23,"sourceQuestionId":"7165:55255:23","type":"fill","text":"填写第 23 空","answer":"tree","acceptedAnswers":["tree"],"explanation":"题目意思：一个测试自然对病人恢复时间影响的实验发现，能够看到什么的病人恢复更快。\n定位关键信息：“experiment”和“effect of nature”和“recovery”\n对应原文：D段，“One group had a view of tree; the others had a window looking onto a brick wall. The first group had shorter hospital stays, received fewer negative comments from the nurses, required fewer analgesics, and had slightly fewer post-operative complications.”\n解题思路：原文提到能够看到树的病人恢复更快。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55255","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20 - 24\nComplete the sentences. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":24,"sourceQuestionId":"7165:55256:24","type":"fill","text":"填写第 24 空","answer":"air","acceptedAnswers":["air"],"explanation":"题目意思：在Guelph-Humber大学建筑中有一个生物亲和设计的特点，可以改善什么的质量。\n定位关键信息：“ the University of Guelph-Humber”和“biophilic design feature”和“quality”\n对应原文：G段，“The wall purifies the air and has the potential to fulfill the building's fresh air intake requirements.”\n解题思路：原文提到“the wall purifies the air”，说明该设计特征可以改善空气质量。","options":[],"optionValues":[],"sourceGroupId":"55256","allowNumber":false,"section":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20 - 24\nComplete the sentences. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","maxWords":1},{"number":25,"sourceQuestionId":"7165:55252:25-26","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following statements does the writer make about the Adam Joseph Lewis Center at Oberlin College?","answer":"B","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"explanation":"题目意思：以下哪个选项是关于Oberlin学院的Adam Joseph Lewis中心的描述？\n定位关键信息：“Adam Joseph Lewis Center at Oberlin College”\n对应原文：F段，“The director of Oberlin’s Environmental Studies at Oberlin Studies Program, David Orr, explained the building’s goals were ‘to create not just a place for classes but rather a building that would help to redefine the relationship between humankind and the environment – one that would expand our sense of ecological possibilities’. The Lewis Center is sustainable in a broader sense than in the typical application of the word. It harnesses solar power, utilizes both active and passive air systems, and monitors the weather to adapt to conditions.”\n解题思路：原文中提到建筑不仅有利于学生，还保护了环境；同时，该建筑旨在重新定义人与环境的关系，启发新的环保思维。","options":["It was the first educational establishment designed with biophilic principles.","It is beneficial for both students and the environment.","It has established new concepts for classroom design.","It aims to inspire new ways of thinking about the environment.","It provides solar power to other buildings in the surrounding area."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"55252","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 25-26\nChoose TWO correct answers.","groupId":"55252-7165:55252:25-26"},{"number":26,"sourceQuestionId":"7165:55252:25-26","type":"choice","text":"Which TWO of the following statements does the writer make about the Adam Joseph Lewis Center at Oberlin College?","answer":"D","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"explanation":"题目意思：以下哪个选项是关于Oberlin学院的Adam Joseph Lewis中心的描述？\n定位关键信息：“Adam Joseph Lewis Center at Oberlin College”\n对应原文：F段，“The director of Oberlin’s Environmental Studies at Oberlin Studies Program, David Orr, explained the building’s goals were ‘to create not just a place for classes but rather a building that would help to redefine the relationship between humankind and the environment – one that would expand our sense of ecological possibilities’. The Lewis Center is sustainable in a broader sense than in the typical application of the word. It harnesses solar power, utilizes both active and passive air systems, and monitors the weather to adapt to conditions.”\n解题思路：原文中提到建筑不仅有利于学生，还保护了环境；同时，该建筑旨在重新定义人与环境的关系，启发新的环保思维。","options":["It was the first educational establishment designed with biophilic principles.","It is beneficial for both students and the environment.","It has established new concepts for classroom design.","It aims to inspire new ways of thinking about the environment.","It provides solar power to other buildings in the surrounding area."],"optionValues":["A","B","C","D","E"],"sourceGroupId":"55252","allowNumber":false,"section":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 25-26\nChoose TWO correct answers.","groupId":"55252-7165:55252:25-26"}],"questionGroups":[{"id":"55252-7165:55252:25-26","numbers":[25,26],"selectionCount":2,"answers":["B","D"]}],"sourceGroups":[{"id":"55250","title":"信息匹配","instruction":"Questions 14 - 19\nLook at the eight paragraphs (A - H). Which paragraph contains the following information?\nYou may choose any letter more than once.","html":"<p></p>","firstNumber":14},{"id":"55251","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20 - 24\nComplete the sentences. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>In the modern world, <strong class=\"source-blank\">[20] ____</strong> advancements are happening so quickly that humans are unable to adjust to them.</p>","firstNumber":20},{"id":"55253","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20 - 24\nComplete the sentences. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>Biophilia can help us deal with the <strong class=\"source-blank\">[21] ____</strong> caused by the difficulties of our current lifestyles.</p>","firstNumber":21},{"id":"55254","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20 - 24\nComplete the sentences. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>People instinctively feel more comfortable in places which have plenty of <strong class=\"source-blank\">[22] ____</strong>.</p>","firstNumber":22},{"id":"55255","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20 - 24\nComplete the sentences. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>An experiment designed to test the effect of nature on patient recovery times found that those who could see a <strong class=\"source-blank\">[23] ____</strong> made a faster recovery.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>","firstNumber":23},{"id":"55256","title":"填空题","instruction":"Questions 20 - 24\nComplete the sentences. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","html":"<p>There is a biophilic design feature in the University of Guelph-Humber building which improves the quality of the&nbsp; <strong class=\"source-blank\">[24] ____</strong>.</p>","firstNumber":24},{"id":"55252","title":"选择题","instruction":"Questions 25-26\nChoose TWO correct answers.","html":"<p>Which <strong>TWO</strong>&nbsp;of the following statements does the writer make about the Adam Joseph Lewis Center at Oberlin College?</p>","firstNumber":25}],"passage":"<p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Biophilic Design</strong></span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Biophilic design, a movement related to green architecture, has gained much momentum within the building community in recent years. The premise of biophilic design seeks both to avoid or minimize harmful impacts on the natural environment, and equally importantly, to provide and restore beneficial contacts between people and nature in the built environment.</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">People have a psychologically developed need to commune with nature but this has frequently been neglected. All too often, architects have put creative originality before the needs of the people who have to live and work in their futuristic constructions, with scant regard for emotional, as well as practical, considerations. Biophilic design does not advocate tree houses or cave-dwelling, but it does provide the nature-based features that maximize human functioning and health. Though not technically a biophilic design, Fallingwater – the stunning house in rural Pennsylvania designed in the 1930s by Frank Lloyd Wright – arguably speaks to the human soul much more than the box-like blocks of flats designed by his contemporary Le Corbusier.</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">In the modern world, much of our built environment is obstructing the age-old connection between humans and nature. The rates of technological progress are far exceeding rates of psychological evolution, leaving us ill-equipped to cope with our lifestyle, which in turn leads to increased stress. Because biophilia attempts to integrate basic and current needs, it can alleviate the difficulties caused by the brain&#39;s constant attempts to function in a modern environment it has not yet evolved to handle. For example, one crucial element of the natural landscape to human health is sunlight. We are evolutionarily programmed to respond positively to sunny areas over dark or overcast ones, and sense that they will foster restoration, improve emotional well-being and promote health.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>D</strong>\t</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Because of its tremendous impact biophilic design plays a vital role in healthcare and healthcare delivery. The current healthcare system contains many flaws, especially in its physical clinics, and offices are high-stress environments for patients, visitors and healthcare professionals alike. One well-known study looked at the impact of nature on patients after surgery. One group had a view of tree; the others had a window looking onto a brick wall. The first group had shorter hospital stays, received fewer negative comments from the nurses, required fewer analgesics, and had slightly fewer post-operative complications</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">As a consequence of this and other studies, nature and nature-based design have been integrated into the physical design of many hospitals. For example, Dartmouth Hitchcock Medical Center (DHMC) in New Hampshire boasts an atrium design, illuminating the entire facility. Natural elements also permeate the building, including wood, stone, and numerous live plants. While DHMC was built to incorporate these qualities, other hospitals have had biophilic features added to existing structures. The application of biophilia’s concepts to interior design in hospitals has increased substantially as administrators have witnessed patients&#39; positive responses to nature.</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Many existing buildings contain biophilic elements, but only a few have been built with the specific idea of biophilic design in mind. One such building is the Adam Joseph Lewis Center for Environmental Studies at Oberlin College, in Ohio. The director of Oberlin’s Environmental Studies at Oberlin Studies Program, David Orr, explained the building’s goals were ‘to create not just a place for classes but rather a building that would help to redefine the relationship between humankind and the environment – one that would expand our sense of ecological possibilities’. The Lewis Center is sustainable in a broader sense than in the typical application of the word. It harnesses solar power, utilizes both active and passive air systems, and monitors the weather to adapt to conditions. The Center&#39;s ‘Living Machine’ treats wastewater by combining traditional wastewater technology with wetland ecosystems’ purification processes, producing water that can be used in the toilets and for irrigation. In their design, Orr and his team of architects engineered a healthy and comfortable space for students, while ensuring the surrounding environment was undamaged.</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>G</strong></span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Another example is the University of Guelph-Humber building in Ontario, Canada. It contains a centrally located bio-wall, vertically spanning the building. The wall is covered in dense foliage which not only connects people to nature on the inside of the building, but also functions as a new filtration system prototype. The wall purifies the air and has the potential to fulfill the building&#39;s fresh air intake requirements. This is another example of how biophilic design principles can be applied in a variety of contexts. These examples prove that the built environment need does not interfere with biological human needs to commune with nature, nor with existing ecological systems.</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>H</strong></span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5em;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Ancient architects built for their cultures, which were almost always more in touch with the earth than western society of the present. They mimicked nature’s forms, producing magnificent structures with which we are still awed – though biophilic design is a novel concept, they certainly employed some of its recommendations. Today, we can add another layer to this tradition and ensure maximal benefit for our planet and ourselves.</span></p><p><br/></p>","source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/igotangDetailedExplanationOfExercises?topicId=7165&scene=%E8%87%AA%E7%84%B6%E7%A7%91%E6%8A%80&subjectName=2&smarterPracticeRecordId=","answers":"用户提供的题库答案与解析","note":"题目来源 igopx；沿用来源分类，不代表官方认证"},"library":true}]);